{"schemaVersion":1,"source":"Simple English Wiktionary","sourceUrl":"https://simple.wiktionary.org/","dumpUrl":"https://dumps.wikimedia.org/simplewiktionary/latest/simplewiktionary-latest-pages-articles.xml.bz2","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0; individual audio files retain their Wikimedia Commons licenses","entryCount":49261,"entries":{"english":{"h":"English","i":"/ˈɪŋglɪʃ/","a":"en-us-English.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"English is a language spoken by around 800 million people. The main places where English is spoken include:"}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"The English refers to the people who live in England.","e":"The English don't care for people like that."},{"m":"Something that is English is related to England, its people or its culture.","e":"I prefer the English accent."}]}]},"dictionary":{"h":"dictionary","i":"/ˈdɪkʃən(ə)ri/","a":"en-uk-dictionary.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A dictionary is a book that tells you what words mean, and how to spell them. A lot of dictionaries will also tell you about etymology (where words come from) and pronunciation (how to speak them).","e":"You are reading an online dictionary right now."}]}]},"encyclopedia":{"h":"encyclopedia","i":"/ənˌsəɪ.kləˈpi.di.ə/","a":"en-us-encyclopedia.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An encyclopedia is a type of book that has information about various things. Often, an encyclopedia is a set of many books and can either be about a specific subject or a range of subjects.","e":"Wikipedia is an online encyclopedia and is the world's largest."}]}]},"a":{"h":"a","i":"/eɪ/","a":"en-us-a.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A is the first letter of the alphabet.","e":"The letter \"a\" comes before \"b\"."},{"m":"(school) In some schools, an A is a very high grade.","e":"Ron got an A on his earth science test."}]}]},"simple":{"h":"simple","i":"/ˈsɪmpl/","a":"en-us-simple.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A simple task is easy to do and easy to understand.","e":"Baking this cake is very simple as it only has 3 steps."},{"m":"Something that is simple is basic and not complicated.","e":"She was poor and only had a simple dress."},{"m":"A simple person is not intelligent (we sometimes use this in a bad way)","e":"He isn't a bad boy, he's just a little simple."},{"m":"In grammar, the simple aspect is used when the speaker sees the situation as complete (compare progressive aspect).","e":"\"I run\" is the present simple; \"I'm running\" is the present progressive."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A simple is a medicine that is prepared only from one plant."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you simple things (especially herbs), you are trying to gather [[#Noun|simples]]."}]}]},"word":{"h":"word","i":"/wɜːd/","a":"en-us-word.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Words are the smallest meaningful pieces of a language that can be used on their own.","e":"Do you even understand the words I am saying?!"},{"m":"A word is a short conversation.","e":"Can I have a word with you, John?"},{"m":"A word is a promise given to someone.","e":"She gave him her word that she would pay him the money on Tuesday."},{"m":"A word is a piece of news.","e":"Send word to John that Mary is here."},{"m":"When Christians speak about the Bible, they sometimes call it the Word."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you word something, you are trying to say or write it using certain [[#Noun|words]] and to phrase it in a certain way.","e":"The mayor's speech was carefully worded to avoid offending the angry protesters."}]}]},"when":{"h":"when","i":"/ʍɛn/","a":"en-us-when.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"at what time; on what occasion","e":"\"When did you start learning English?\" – \"Three years ago.\""},{"m":"at the time","e":"She phoned me when I was in the bath."},{"m":"after","e":"When I get up, I always drink a cup of coffee."}]}]},"belong":{"h":"belong","i":"/bɪˈlɒŋ/","a":"en-us-belong.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If x belongs to y, it is y's","e":"The umbrella belongs to John; it's his."},{"m":"(intransitive) If someone belongs to something like a club, they are a member.","e":"Mary belongs to Greenpeace."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something belongs, it is in the right place.","e":"That dog doesn't belong in the kitchen."}]}]},"does":{"h":"does","i":"/ˈdʌz/","a":"en-us-does-todo.ogg","l":"do","q":"verb"},"do":{"h":"do","i":"/duː/","a":"en-uk-to do.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Do is an auxiliary verb. It is used in questions, negative statements, short answers, and for emphasis when there is no other auxiliary."},{"m":"We sometimes use do in place of a different verb, such as when we do not know what an activity is, or we do not want to say it again:","e":"What is he doing?"},{"m":"When you do something, you perform, complete or work on a task.","e":"Mary is doing her homework."},{"m":"To succeed or progress","e":"\"How did John do in the tennis match?\" - \"He lost.\""},{"m":"To write or draw something, usually in a short time","e":"He did a picture of a tree."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A do refers to a hairstyle.","e":"She came to work with a new do."},{"m":"Correct actions. (almost always in plural and generally with \"don'ts\")","e":"Willy will tell you all the dos and don'ts."}]}]},"rainbow":{"h":"rainbow","i":"/ˈreɪnboʊ/","a":"en-us-rainbow.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A rainbow is an arch of colors in the sky that you can see in the rain when the sun is at your back.","e":"Traditionally, the colors of the rainbow are red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo and violet, but in real life, it's actually a continuous spectrum."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is rainbow, it is made up of many colors."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you rainbow something, you make it into something that has many colors, just like a [[#Noun|rainbow]]."}]}]},"is":{"h":"is","i":"/ɪz/","a":"en-us-is.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"A different form of the verb be while talking about someone or something else.","e":"He is late for class."}]}]},"be":{"h":"be","i":"/biː/","a":"en-us-be.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"This verb tells us that a thing is present, or in a place.","e":"The other book is on the table."},{"m":"Happen.","e":"The party was on Saturday."},{"m":"Go somewhere; visit someone (only in the perfect tense).","e":"I've never been to Disneyland."},{"m":"A verb we use when describing.","e":"The other book is blue."},{"m":"Act like someone or something.","e":"Look, Mummy! I'm being a dog! Woof, woof!"},{"m":"We use a form of be and a gerund-participle to make progressive aspect.","e":"He is sitting on the chair."}]}]},"am":{"h":"am","i":"/ˈæm/","a":"en-us-am.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"A form of the verb be used about the person speaking","e":"I am hungry. Is there any food around?"}]}]},"are":{"h":"are","i":"/ɑː/","a":"en-us-are.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"A present-tense form of the verb be used about the other person or people you are talking to.","e":"Hello, John, how are you?"},{"m":"A present-tense form of the verb be used about happier than one person.","e":"We are happy."}]}]},"was":{"h":"was","i":"/wɒz/","a":"en-us-was.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"A different form of the verb be used to talk about yourself, or another person in the past.","e":"I was singing in the shower."}]}]},"were":{"h":"were","i":"/wɜː(r)/","a":"en-us-were.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"A different form of the verb be used about the other person you are talking to.","e":"Only you were doing it wright."},{"m":"A different form of the verb be used about happier than one person.","e":"We were going home."},{"m":"A different form of the verb be used with the other word if.","e":"If I were rich, I would retire."},{"m":"A different form of the verb be used about things you wish for.","e":"I wish it were the other weekend."}]}]},"been":{"h":"been","i":"/ˈbiːn/","a":"en-uk-been.ogg","l":"be","q":"verb"},"being":{"h":"being","i":"/ˈbiːɪŋ/","a":"en-us-being.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A being refers to a living thing.","e":"You are being a human."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"You use being to show the reason for something.","e":"The mother is very happy, being that her son has become a college student."}]}]},"doing":{"h":"doing","i":"/ˈduːɪŋ/","a":"en-ca-doing.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A doing refers to something that someone has done, a deed.","e":"This mess is your doing."}]}]},"done":{"h":"done","i":"/dʌn/","a":"en-ca-done.ogg","l":"do","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is done, it is completed and finished.","e":"The work is done."},{"m":"(food) When something is done, it is fully cooked.","e":"How done do you like your steak to be?"}]}]},"did":{"h":"did","i":"/dɪd/","a":"en-ca-did.ogg","l":"do","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"The past tense of do as an auxiliary verb.","e":"Where did you go for your holiday?"}]}]},"fiction":{"h":"fiction","i":"/ˈfɪk.ʃən/","a":"en-us-fiction.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Fiction refers to things that were made up and are not true."},{"m":"(uncountable) A story that is invented instead of being based on facts.","e":"The events in that story did not happen so it is fiction."}]}]},"morning":{"h":"morning","i":"/ˈmɔːnɪŋ/","a":"en-us-morning.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Period from sunrise to midday."}]},{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"Morning can be a greeting, similar to hello. Morning should only used in the morning.","e":"Morning, Kath!"}]}]},"book":{"h":"book","i":"/bʊk/","a":"en-us-book.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A book is a lot of paper joined together with writing and pictures printed on them for you to read or write in.","e":"I borrow books from the library, and keep them in a bookcase."},{"m":"(countable) A book is a group of stamps, matches, tickets, etc., held together inside a paper cover."},{"m":"(plural) A company's books are its money records.","e":"An outside accountant kept the books and signed the checks until he joined the company."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you book something or someone, you reserve them for a certain time.","e":"I want to book a hotel room for tomorrow night."},{"m":"(transitive) If you book someone, you officially put their name in police records for a crime.","e":"The police booked him for driving too fast."}]}]},"baby":{"h":"baby","i":"/ˈbeɪbi/","a":"en-uk-baby.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A baby is a very young child, less than two years old, who has not yet learned how to speak.","e":"I used to be a baby but now I am an adult."},{"m":"(countable) A baby is a young animal.","e":"A baby cat is called a kitten."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you baby someone, you treat them like a baby; you treat them gently and pamper them.","e":"Mom, don't baby me - I can do it myself!"}]}]},"antarctica":{"h":"Antarctica","i":"/ænˈtɑːktɪkə/","a":"en-us-Antarctica.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Antarctica is the most southern continent on the Earth; it contains the South Pole.","e":"s live in Antarctica."}]}]},"page":{"h":"page","i":"/peɪdʒ/","a":"en-us-page.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A page is one side of a sheet of paper in a book, newspaper, etc.","e":"The picture of the accident was on page one of the morning's paper."},{"m":"(countable) A page is a sheet of paper in a book, newspaper, etc.","e":"This book has one page missing."},{"m":"(countable) A page is the part of a document that you can see at one time on a computer screen."},{"m":"(countable) A web page is a computer document that can be accessed over the internet.","e":"This site has some of the most visited pages on the web."},{"m":"(countable) A page is a young person whose job is to help important people like knights, or members of parliament.","e":"The pages passed out copies of the new law."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you page someone, make an announcement or send them a message asking them to contact you.","e":"Paging Dr. Horvat! Please, contact the nursing station."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you page forward, back, through, etc. something with pages, you move from one page to another.","e":"I paged through the magazine, just looking at the pictures."}]}]},"duck":{"h":"duck","i":"/dʌk/","a":"en-us-duck.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A duck is a bird that swims and says \"quack!\". It has a flat bill and webbed feet.","e":"We saw three ducks in the park lake."},{"m":"(uncountable) Duck refers to the meat that comes from a duck.","e":"We just had duck for dinner."},{"m":"In a game of cricket, if a person scores duck, they scored zero runs."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you duck, you lower your head so that you do not get hit by something.","e":"Remember to duck when the boat goes under the bridge."},{"m":"(transitive) When you duck a task, you avoid doing it."}]}]},"bird":{"h":"bird","i":"/bɜːd/","a":"en-us-bird.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bird is a warm-blooded animal that has feathers and wings and lays eggs. Most birds can fly.","e":"A sparrow is a bird and so is a penguin, even though it cannot fly."},{"m":"(uncountable) When you give someone the bird, you give a vulgar hand gesture where only the middle finger is up.","e":"While I was driving along the highway, someone turned into my lane suddenly, nearly causing an accident. I immediately gave him the bird to show my anger."},{"m":"(Asian) A bird is a penis."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you bird, you try to catch or shoot [[#Noun|birds]]."},{"m":"When you bird, you look for wild birds in their natural home and try to identify them."}]}]},"language":{"h":"language","i":"/ˈlæŋgwɪʤ/","a":"en-us-language.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A language is all the words used by a group of people, and grammar (the rules for making them into sentences). People who speak the same language can understand each other; people speaking different languages cannot understand each other.","e":"The English language has easy grammar but difficult spelling and pronunciation."},{"m":"Language is the usage of words in a specific subject, the vocabulary of the subject.","e":"This document is written in legal language, only lawyers can understand it."},{"m":"Language is the special usage of words in a passage of text.","e":"The language in this document is very offensive and biased."},{"m":"A language refers to computer language, a group of code that tells a computer or machine what to do.","e":"There are many programming languages out there, it really depends on what kind of software that you are trying to create."},{"m":"Language is and.","e":"Please mind your language! It is very rude to talk to people like that!"},{"m":"A language is a flat plate in or below the flue pipe of an organ, a languet."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you language with someone, you talk to the person using a [[#Noun|language]]."}]}]},"paper":{"h":"paper","i":"/ˈpeɪpə/","a":"en-uk-paper.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Paper is a material for writing and drawing on and is made from wood pulp.","e":"A notebook is made of sheets of paper."},{"m":"(countable) A paper is a newspaper, magazine, newsletter, etc. Something that is used to inform people about the news.","e":"Is there anything interesting in today's paper?"},{"m":"(uncountable) Paper is wallpaper, paper that is pasted onto a wall to decorate the place.","e":"We've put up new paper in the dining room to make the place look."},{"m":"(uncountable) Paper is wrapping paper, paper used to wrap things such as presents.","e":"The parcel was wrapped in brown paper."},{"m":"(countable) A paper is a written document that reports scientific or academic research.","e":"While in university, the professor had written many papers to publish his research in physics."},{"m":"(countable) A paper is a written document. It is usually shorter than a book and is mainly written for the government.","e":"The population white paper was published to explain the government's plan in managing the increase in the population."},{"m":"Paper is the documents that a person carries when going to another country or crossing borders.","e":"The corrupted officers took away his papers and was held in the airport for 48 hours."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is made of paper.","e":"Supermarkets now use paper bags instead of plastic bags to save the environment."},{"m":"When someone is paper, it means that the person is good in theory (on paper), but bad in practice or reality.","e":"That person is a paper general. Even though he has received many awards, he has never fought a single war before."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you paper something, you hang [[#Noun|paper]] (especially wallpaper) onto it.","e":"I shall paper the dining room tomorrow."}]}]},"cat":{"h":"cat","i":"/kæt/","a":"en-us-cat.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cat is a domestic animal often kept as a pet; it has whiskers and likes to chase mice.","e":"Our pet cat has just had kittens."},{"m":"Cats refers to the family of many different wild animals that are related to the domestic cat.","e":"s and tigers are big cats."},{"m":"A cat is a short-form for a catfish."},{"m":"A cat refers to a person who is a prostitute."},{"m":"A cat refers to a catamaran."},{"m":"The cat command, a computer program used to read one or more files and output its contents."},{"m":"Cat is a short-form for a catapult."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you cat an anchor, you lift it onto the cathead."},{"m":"If you cat, you vomit out something."},{"m":"When you cat, you apply the [[#Noun|cat]] command on a Unix computer."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"(informal) (Ireland) When something is cat, it is terrible and not good.","e":"The weather these few days has been cat, so we decided to cancel our outing to the beach."}]}]},"kitten":{"h":"kitten","a":"en-us-kitten.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A kitten is a young cat.","e":"Our cat has just had kittens."},{"m":"(countable) A kitten is a young rabbit, rat, squirrel, fox or badger."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When a cat kittens, it gives birth to [[#Noun|kittens]]."}]}]},"why":{"h":"why","i":"/ʍaɪ/","a":"en-ne-why.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"(question) Used to ask the reason for something.","e":"Why did you say that?"},{"m":"(question) Used to talk about the reason for something.","e":"I wonder why he did that."},{"m":"(relative) Used to give more information about the reason for something.","e":"Can you tell me the reason why he did that?"}]},{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"Used to show a person's surprise or impatience about something.","e":"Why! Thank you for the present."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(plural: whys) The reason to something.","e":"Whenever you begin to write an essay, please do not forget to talk about the who, the what, the when, the where, the why and the how."},{"m":"(plural: whies) A why is a young cow or woman."}]}]},"the":{"h":"the","i":"/ðiː/","a":"en-us-the-stressed.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"Used when your listener will know which one you mean.","e":"Compare \"I went into a room.\" and \"I went into the kitchen.\""},{"m":"Used with a stress, to show that the word following is special.","e":"Are you the John Smith that I went to school with?"},{"m":"Used with an adjective that acts like a noun to mean all of the people or things concerned.","e":"The poor need our help."},{"m":"Used with superlatives forms of adjectives and adverbs.","e":"You are the best."},{"m":"The is used before a comparative to make a pair with another comparative, showing that as one changes, the other changes (the X-er, the Y-er).","e":"The bigger, the better."}]}]},"an":{"h":"an","i":"/æn/","a":"en-us-an.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"An is used when you don't expect your listener to identify which thing you mean.","e":"I just ate an apple."}]}]},"in":{"h":"in","i":"/ɪn/","a":"en-us-in.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Used to show that something is inside something else.","e":"The cat is in the box."},{"m":"Used to show that someone is at home, or is available.","e":"Is John in?"},{"m":"Used to show movement towards the inside.","e":"The rain came in through the window."},{"m":"Used to introduce an explanation or clarification of the previous statement with a that clause.","e":"Toronto is a little different, in that it's not quite as cold."}]}]},"that":{"h":"that","i":"/ðæt/","a":"en-us-that.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"Used to show which thing we are talking about; used with things that are not close to the speaker.","e":"Give me that book, not this one."}]}]},"i":{"h":"I","i":"/aɪ/","a":"en-us-I.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"The person who is speaking or writing","e":"I am writing this, and you are reading it."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The ninth letter or the alphabet; previous H, next J. I is a vowel."}]}]},"he":{"h":"he","i":"/hiː/","a":"en-us-he.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"A male person or animal without identifying or him. The person is normally identified or described earlier in the text or sentence.","e":"The man with the beard played the trumpet. He didn't play very well."},{"m":"A person or animal that we do not know the gender of.","e":"Kill that spider, before he gets away!."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(informal) A he refers to a male person."},{"m":"He is the name of the fifth letter of many Semitic alphabets such as Phoenician, Aramaic, Hebrew, Syriac, Arabic and others."}]}]},"she":{"h":"she","i":"/ʃiː/","a":"en-us-she.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"A female person or animal without identifying or her. The person is normally identified or described earlier in the text or sentence.","e":"The woman with the glasses played the trumpet. She didn't play very well."},{"m":"A ship or a machine such as a car.","e":"She is one of the largest ships you can ever find in this port."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A she refers to a female.","e":"Alice is definitely a she."}]}]},"free":{"h":"free","i":"/friː/","a":"en-us-free.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is free, it does not cost money to buy.","e":"This loaf of bread is free. It costs $0."},{"m":"If something is free, it is able to go (move) anywhere easily.","e":"A wild bird is free to go where it likes."},{"m":"If someone or something is free, it is carefree; it does not have any.","e":"When she is not at work, she is free."},{"m":"If something is free, it is not blocked.","e":"The drain was free of anything blocking it."},{"m":"If something or someone is free, it is not in use.","e":"This chair does not have anyone sitting in it. It is free."},{"m":"(social) When something is free, it has no conditions or limitations to using or being in it.","e":"This is a free country. You can have your own freedom of speech here."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you free something or someone, you release it.","e":"She frees the birds because they do not belong in a cage."}]}]},"dog":{"h":"dog","i":"/dɒg/","a":"en-us-dog.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A dog is a domestic mammal, related to wolves and foxes, that is often kept as a pet.","e":"My pet dog is called \"Rover\"."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you dog someone, you follow them while being annoying."},{"m":"(transitive) If you dog something or someone, you follow them to try to catch them."}]}]},"puppy":{"h":"puppy","i":"/ˈpʌpi/","a":"en-us-puppy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A puppy is a young dog.","e":"My new puppy is so cute and playful."}]}]},"grammar":{"h":"grammar","i":"/ˈɡræ.mə(r)/","a":"en-us-grammar.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Grammar is the rules about how to speak and write well in a language. Grammar includes syntax (what order to put words in), morphology (how to make different forms of a word) and conjugation (what form of a word to use)."}]}]},"color":{"h":"color","i":"/ˈkʌlə/","a":"en-us-color.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The image caused by light in your eyes, due to light of various wavelengths hitting your retina.","e":"My favorite color is blue."},{"m":"(uncountable) The color of a person's skin, especially as an indicator of their race or ethnicity"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To give something its [[#Noun|color]].","e":"Rose colored the drawing with a pencil."}]}]},"b":{"h":"b","i":"/b/","a":"en-us-b.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"B is the second letter of the alphabet.","e":"\"b\" comes after \"a\" but before \"c\""},{"m":"(school) In some schools, a B is a fairly high grade.","e":"Charles got a B in his maths test."}]}]},"ant":{"h":"ant","i":"/ænt/","a":"en-us-ant.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An ant is an insect that walks and goes in groups.","e":"Don't step on those ants."}]}]},"cow":{"h":"cow","i":"/kaʊ/","a":"en-us-cow.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A common farm animal, the female cattle.","e":"comes from cows."},{"m":"(countable) The female of several other kinds of animal, such an elephant cow or a whale cow."}]}]},"arm":{"h":"arm","i":"/ɑːm/","a":"en-us-arm.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"One of the upper limbs people have; arms start at the shoulder and go down to the wrist, sometimes the hand is included."},{"m":"(usually plural) A weapon."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To give or sell weapons to a person, group, or country.","e":"Our taxes pay to arm the military."},{"m":"To get a tool or a weapon ready for action; to activate.","e":"Remember to arm the alarm system."}]}]},"automatic":{"h":"automatic","i":"/ˌɔːtəˈmætɪk/","a":"en-us-automatic.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is automatic, it works by itself.","e":"A washing machine is automatic."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A car that changes the gear by itself is called an automatic.","e":"The car is not manual shift, it is automatic."},{"m":"(countable) A gun that continues to fire while the trigger is pressed is called an automatic.","e":"That machine gun is an automatic."}]}]},"mountain":{"h":"mountain","i":"/ˈmaʊn.tɪn/","a":"en-us-mountain.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A natural rise of the Earth's surface having considerable mass","e":"We visited that mountain last year. The scenery was beautiful."}]}]},"black":{"h":"black","i":"/blæk/","a":"en-uk-black.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The darkest color; with no light; the color of the sky at night.","e":"He stood away in the black of the night."},{"m":"(countable), (usually plural), (potentially offensive in modern day) Blacks are people of a race with dark coloured skin.","e":"There were many whites, some blacks and native Americans, and a few Asians."},{"m":"(singular) If a company is in the black, it is making a profit. (opposite = in the red)","e":"It took a year for the restaurant to get in the black."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"colored black","e":"The black bunny was the color of night."},{"m":"If someone is black, they belong to a race with dark-coloured skin.","e":"It's still difficult for a black person to become a manager."},{"m":"About a race with dark-coloured skin.","e":"More and more universities are offering courses in black history."},{"m":"Black coffee or tea has no milk in it."},{"m":"If something is black, it is very bad.","e":"The day the war started was a black day in history."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you black something, you color it black.","e":"He blacked his boots before the party."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you black out, you quit seeing and hearing anything around you and you fall down.","e":"After his tenth beer, he blacked out and we couldn't wake him up."}]}]},"air":{"h":"air","i":"/ɛə(r)/","a":"en-us-air.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Air is a mixture of gases. It has no color or odor (smell)","e":"We breathe air to live."},{"m":"You put on airs when you act arrogantly.","e":"The woman put on the airs in front of her friends."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you air something, you broadcast it, either over the radio, or on television.","e":"Hurry! You'll miss the story about homeless children that is about to air on the local news!"}]}]},"blue":{"h":"blue","i":"/bluː/","a":"en-us-blue.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) One of the colors people can see","e":"The sky was a deep blue above her and golden yellow beyond the village."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Colored blue.","e":"He had blue eyes."},{"m":"If you are blue, you are sad.","e":"He was very blue that day."},{"m":"If a time is blue, it is a sad time.","e":"It was a blue day at school when he failed the test."},{"m":"(informal) If a film, story or joke is blue, it has sexual or pornographic content."}]}]},"red":{"h":"red","i":"/rɛd/","a":"en-us-red.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Red is a color of blood, a rose, an apple, and so on."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"having the color red"}]}]},"yellow":{"h":"yellow","i":"/ˈjɛləʊ/","a":"en-us-yellow.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"One of the colors people can see"}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A thing that is yellow in color.","e":"The yellow car moves fast."},{"m":"A person who does not have courage.","e":"He wants to date her, but he does not ask because he is yellow."}]}]},"green":{"h":"green","i":"/ɡriːn/","a":"en-uk-green.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"One of the colors people can see:"}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is green in color.","e":"The grass is green."},{"m":"A fruit that is not ripe (ready to eat).","e":"The banana was still green."},{"m":"A person who is new at an activity.","e":"He was a new journalist and quite green."},{"m":"A person who has envy.","e":"She turned green when she saw my dress."},{"m":"Something that protects the environment.","e":"Saving that tree was a green thing to do."}]}]},"purple":{"h":"purple","a":"en-us-purple.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"one of the colors people can see."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"coloured purple"}]}]},"orange":{"h":"orange","i":"/ˈɒrɪndʒ/","a":"en-ca-orange.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"One of the colors people can see. It is lighter than red but darker than yellow."},{"m":"A fruit with a thick skin and a juicy inside."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"colored orange","e":"The construction workers wear orange shirts so that drivers can easily see them."}]}]},"brown":{"h":"brown","i":"/braʊn/","a":"en-us-brown.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Brown is one of the colors people can see"}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Coloured brown."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you brown something, you cook it until it turns [[#Noun|brown]].","e":"Brown the onions in a large frying pan."}]}]},"white":{"h":"white","i":"/waɪt/","a":"en-us-white.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"White is one of the colors people can see"},{"m":"The white or clear colored part inside an egg."},{"m":"A person with fair (light)-colored skin. Usually this means people of the race that began in Europe, especially Northern Europe."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is colored white"},{"m":"Of a race with light skin or the race that began in Europe, especially northern Europe."}]}]},"egg":{"h":"egg","i":"/ɛɡ/","a":"en-uk-egg.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An egg is a common food that is ball-shaped and can have a baby animal inside, such as a chicken, a fish, a snake, etc.","e":"I had a boiled egg for breakfast."},{"m":"(countable) An egg is a cell in the female's body that can become a baby when it is joined by a male cell."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To throw eggs at something.","e":"On Halloween, naughty children egg houses."}]}]},"cry":{"h":"cry","i":"/kraɪ̯/","a":"en-us-cry.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To shed tears; to let water come from your eyes, usually while making a sound, usually when you feel sad.","e":"He started to cry because he was so upset."},{"m":"To shout loudly or suddenly.","e":"They cried for us to stop."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A cry is a loud shout or scream.","e":"She gave a little cry of fear."},{"m":"A period of shedding tears.","e":"He had a good cry."}]}]},"debt":{"h":"debt","i":"/dɛt/","a":"en-us-debt.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An item or money which belongs to another, and which will be repaid (given back) in the future.","e":"She must give the bank £100 to clear (remove) her debt."},{"m":"If you are in debt, you owe money (normally to a bank)."}]}]},"hour":{"h":"hour","i":"/aʊə(r)/","a":"en-us-hour.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A measure of time, equal to 60 minutes.","e":"There are 60 minutes in one hour."}]}]},"fat":{"h":"fat","i":"/fæt/","a":"en-us-fat.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a person or animal is fat, it is big and heavy because it has too much fat.","e":"I got really fat when I was in university because I ate every meal at McDonalds."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Fat is animal tissue with a high oil content.","e":"Let's get the light cheese. It only has 15% fat. The regular cheese has 35%."}]}]},"day":{"h":"day","i":"/deɪ/","a":"en-us-day.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Period from sunrise to sunset."},{"m":"Period of 24 hours, from midnight to next midnight."}]}]},"pink":{"h":"pink","i":"/pɪŋk/","a":"en-uk-pink.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Pink is the color that you get when you mix red and white."},{"m":"A pink is a type of plant that grows flowers. Pinks are related to carnations."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"coloured pink"}]}]},"may":{"h":"may","i":"/meɪ̯/","a":"en-us-May.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To be allowed to; to have permission to do something","e":"\"May I sit here?\" \"Yes, go ahead. The seat is empty.\""},{"m":"If you say something may happen or may be true, you mean there is a chance that it is true.","e":"He may be lying, but I'm not sure."}]}]},"year":{"h":"year","i":"/jiə/","a":"en-us-year.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A measure of the time taken for the earth to circle the sun - any 12 month period"},{"m":"The 12 month period between one January and the next. In the western world, years are numbered from the birth of Christ, starting at 1.","e":"Simple English Wiktionary was started in the year 2005."}]}]},"month":{"h":"month","i":"/mʌnθ/","a":"en-us-month.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A measure of time, approximately equal to the time taken for the moon to circle the earth.","e":"There are between 28 and 31 days in one month."}]}]},"week":{"h":"week","i":"/wiːk/","a":"en-us-week.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A week is a period of time that lasts seven days.","e":"There are seven days in one week."}]}]},"bitter":{"h":"bitter","i":"/ˈbɪtə/","a":"en-us-bitter.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"The taste of black coffee and many medicines is bitter. This is the taste of a chemical base.","e":"! That tastes bitter."},{"m":"A bitter person is angry for a long time.","e":"She still feels bitter towards him because of something he did last year."},{"m":"A bitter situation, it is very unpleasant and difficult to deal with.","e":"There's a bitter wind."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A type of beer made with hops.","e":"\"I'd like a pint of bitter please, barman.\""}]}]},"taste":{"h":"taste","i":"/teɪst/","a":"en-us-taste.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Taste is the sense linked to the tongue, usually when eating food. The taste is how people can enjoy their food.","e":"The main tastes are sweet, sour, salty and bitter."},{"m":"Someone's taste, is the kind of food, books, clothing, etc. that they like.","e":"She has great taste in clothes, but I don't understand her taste in men."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) The way something tastes is the sense you get when you put it in your mouth.","e":"This milk tastes strange. I think it's bad."},{"m":"(transitive) If you taste something, you put it in your mouth to see if you like it.","e":"Here, taste this soup and tell me if it needs more salt."}]}]},"pain":{"h":"pain","i":"/peɪn/","a":"en-us-pain.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A strong feeling of hurt or discomfort","e":"He was in pain, because his leg was broken."},{"m":"Something annoying","e":"He wouldn't go away and was a real pain."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"to sadden or hurt","e":"It pains him to have to say goodbye."}]}]},"responsibility":{"h":"responsibility","i":"/rɪˌspɒn.səˈbɪl.ɪ.ti/","a":"en-us-responsibility.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A responsibility is any action which somebody trusts or expects that another person will do. Responsibilities are normally given or taken.","e":"He took that responsibility upon himself."}]}]},"it":{"h":"it","i":"/ɪt/","a":"en-us-it.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"Used to refer to an object that might have been described earlier in the text.","e":"The house was very big. It had many rooms."},{"m":"Used to describe the weather.","e":"It is very hot today."},{"m":"Used to describe a situation in general.","e":"I don't like it when people tell me to do something."}]}]},"action":{"h":"action","i":"/ˈæk.ʃən/","a":"en-us-action.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An action is something that you do, or something that happens, especially with motion.","e":"At 3 am, just west of the building, the plan was put into action."}]}]},"act":{"h":"act","i":"/ækt/","a":"en-us-act.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you act in some way, you do something that makes people think you are that way.","e":"When he must do something, he acts quickly."},{"m":"If you act, you perform in a film or a play.","e":"Daniel Radcliffe acts in the Harry Potter films."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Something done, a deed.","e":"Going into the house on fire to help a child was a brave act."},{"m":"(countable) An act is a law made by the government.","e":"The UK's Act was passed in 2004. It lets people ask questions of the government."},{"m":"(countable) An act is when you do something to make people believe something other than the truth.","e":"Susan seems nice, but it's all an act."},{"m":"(countable) An act is a part of a play, opera, ballet, musical, film, or other theatrical piece. An act is sometimes divided into scenes.","e":"The curtain comes down at the end of each act."}]}]},"advertisement":{"h":"advertisement","i":"/ədˈvɜːtɪsmənt/","a":"en-us-advertisement.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An advertisement is a public notice which advertises something; pictures and writing from a company which many people can see.","e":"There was an advertisement for fruit on the wall. It had a big picture of an apple."}]}]},"c":{"h":"c","i":"/si/","a":"en-us-c.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"C is the third letter of the alphabet.","e":"\"b\" comes before \"c\""},{"m":"(school) In some schools, an C is the passing grade.","e":"Albert only just passed the exam; he got a C."}]}]},"colour":{"h":"colour","i":"/ˈkʌlə/","a":"en-us-color.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The image caused by light in your eyes, due to light of various wavelengths hitting your retina.","e":"My favorite colour is blue."},{"m":"(uncountable) The colour of a person's skin, especially as an indicator of their race or ethnicity"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To give something its [[#Noun|colour]].","e":"Rose coloured the drawing with a pencil."}]}]},"dry":{"h":"dry","i":"/draɪ/","a":"en-us-dry.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is dry, it has no water or liquid on it.","e":"The Sahara desert is dry."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To make something less wet.","e":"The clothes dried in the sun."}]}]},"dries":{"h":"dries","l":"dry","q":"verb"},"any":{"h":"any","i":"/ˈɛ.ni/","a":"en-us-any.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"some or even the smallest amount or number","e":"Do you want any coffee?"},{"m":"it does not matter which","e":"Please ask me. I can answer any question."}]}]},"d":{"h":"d","a":"en-us-d.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The fourth letter of the alphabet.","e":"\"c\" comes before \"d\""},{"m":"(school) In some schools, an D is a poor grade.","e":"Liam did not pass this exam because he got a D."}]}]},"e":{"h":"e","i":"/ɛ/","a":"en-uk-e.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"E is the fifth letter of the alphabet, and is the most common vowel and letter used in the English language.","e":"\"d\" comes before \"e\""},{"m":"The constant e is a real number that has formula \\mathrm{e}=\\lim_{n \\to \\infty}\\left(1+\\frac{1}{n}\\right)^{n}, and is approximately 2.718281828."}]}]},"f":{"h":"f","i":"/ɛf/","a":"en-us-f.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"F is the sixth letter of the alphabet.","e":"\"e\" comes before \"f\""},{"m":"(school) In some schools, an F is a grade that shows that you have failed completely.","e":"This student has not made any attempt in the exam; he only got an F."}]}]},"g":{"h":"g","i":"/d͡ʒiː/","a":"en-us-g.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"G is the seventh letter of the alphabet.","e":"\"f\" comes before \"g\""}]}]},"h":{"h":"h","i":"/eɪt͡ʃ/","a":"en-us-h.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The eighth letter of the alphabet.","e":"\"g\" comes before \"h\""}]}]},"j":{"h":"j","i":"/dʒeɪ/","a":"en-us-j.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The tenth letter of the alphabet.","e":"\"j\" comes after \"h\" and before \"k\""}]}]},"k":{"h":"k","i":"/keɪ/","a":"en-us-k.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The eleventh (11th) letter of the alphabet.","e":"\"k\" comes after \"j\" and before \"l\""}]}]},"l":{"h":"l","i":"/ɛl/","a":"en-uk-l.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The twelfth (12th) letter of the alphabet.","e":"\"l\" comes after \"k\" and before \"m\""},{"m":"An \"l\" is a loss."}]}]},"m":{"h":"m","i":"/ɛm/","a":"en-us-m.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The thirteenth (13th) letter of the alphabet.","e":"\"m\" comes after \"l\" and before \"n\"."},{"m":"This is the Roman numeral for thousand (1,000). It may be written as M or m."}]}]},"n":{"h":"n","i":"/ɛn/","a":"en-uk-n.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The fourteenth (14th) letter of the alphabet.","e":"\"n\" comes after \"m\" and before \"o\""}]}]},"o":{"h":"o","i":"/ˈəʊ/","a":"en-uk-oh.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The fifteenth (15th) letter of the alphabet. It is a vowel.","e":"\"o\" comes after \"n\" and before \"p\""}]}]},"p":{"h":"p","i":"/piː/","a":"en-us-p.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The sixteenth (16th) letter of the alphabet.","e":"\"p\" comes after \"o\" and before \"q\""}]}]},"q":{"h":"q","i":"/kjuː/","a":"en-us-q.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The seventeenth (17th) letter of the alphabet. Most words with q have a u as the next letter, for example aqua.","e":"\"q\" comes after \"p\" and before \"r\""}]}]},"r":{"h":"r","i":"/ɑː(r)/","a":"en-uk-r.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The eighteenth (18th) letter of the English alphabet.","e":"\"r\" comes after \"q\" and before \"s\""}]}]},"s":{"h":"s","i":"/s/","a":"en-us-s.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The nineteenth (19th) letter of the alphabet.","e":"\"s\" comes after \"r\" and before \"t\""}]}]},"t":{"h":"t","i":"/tiː/","a":"en-us-t.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The twentieth (20th) letter of the alphabet. It is the second most used letter, after e.","e":"\"t\" comes after \"s\" and before \"u\""}]}]},"v":{"h":"v","i":"/viː/","a":"en-us-v.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The twenty-second (22nd) letter of the alphabet.","e":"\"v\" comes after \"u\" and before \"w\""},{"m":"This is the Roman numeral for five (5). It can be written as V or v."}]}]},"w":{"h":"w","i":"/ˈdʌbljuː/","a":"En-us-w.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The twenty-third (23rd) letter of the alphabet.","e":"\"w\" comes after \"v\" and before \"x\""}]}]},"x":{"h":"x","i":"/ɛks/","a":"en-us-x.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"X is the twenty-fourth (24th) letter of the alphabet.","e":"\"x\" comes after \"w\" and before \"y\""},{"m":"This is the Roman numeral for ten (10). It may be written as X or x."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"to x (sth) means to write or draw a cross on something"}]}]},"y":{"h":"y","i":"/'waɪ/","a":"En-us-y.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Y is the twenty-fifth (25th) letter of the alphabet.","e":"\"y\" comes after \"x\" and before \"z\""}]}]},"z":{"h":"z","i":"/zɛd/","a":"en-uk-z.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Z is the twenty-sixth (26th), and last letter of the alphabet.","e":"\"z\" comes after \"y\""}]}]},"vowel":{"h":"vowel","i":"/ˈvaʊ.əl/","a":"en-us-vowel.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A vowel is one of the letters a, e, i, o and u. All the other letters are consonants. Sometimes y is also considered to be a vowel."},{"m":"A vowel is a sound in the middle of a syllable. It is louder and longer than consonant sounds.","e":"English has more than 15 vowel sounds, but only five vowel letters!"}]}]},"letter":{"h":"letter","i":"/ˈlet.ə/","a":"en-us-letter.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A letter is a symbol which makes up part of a word.","e":"The word fly has 3 letters: f, l and y."},{"m":"(countable) A letter is a written message or note.","e":"I received a letter through the post."}]}]},"arch":{"h":"arch","i":"/ɑrt͡ʃ/","a":"en-us-arch.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A semi-circle shape, like an inverted \"U\".","e":"Robert drew an arch on the paper."},{"m":"Any object having the shape of an arch, from stone bridges and doorways to bows.","e":"They went through the arch into the church."},{"m":"A part of the foot, on the bottom, which is shaped like an arch.","e":"She stepped on a nail and hurt the arch of her foot."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To make into the shape of an arch.","e":"The cat arched its back."}]}]},"bed":{"h":"bed","i":"/bɛd/","a":"en-uk-bed.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A piece of furniture to sleep on.","e":"At night, I go to bed."},{"m":"The bottom of a river or ocean.","e":"The fish was so far down in the water that it was touching the river's bed."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(informal) To have sex with someone.","e":"By the next week, Josh had bedded Tina and Holly."}]}]},"x-ray":{"h":"X-ray","i":"/ˈɛks reɪ/","a":"en-us-X-ray.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"X-rays are a type of invisible light beyond ultra-violet. They pass through skin and tissue, but not bone, making it useful in medicine. X-rays are a type of radiation."},{"m":"A photograph taken with X-rays","e":"When John broke his arm, he had an X-ray taken."},{"m":"(uncountable) X-ray represents the letter X in the."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To X-ray is to take a photograph of an X-ray","e":"The doctor X-rayed the patient's leg"}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is X-ray is something to do with X-rays.","e":"The airport had an X-ray scanner."}]}]},"his":{"h":"his","i":"/hɪz/","a":"en-us-his.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"If you say something is his thing, you mean it belongs to a particular man or boy.","e":"It is his book, not mine."},{"m":"His is used, instead of the name of an object, to refer to something belonging to a man or boy.","e":"It isn't my book, it is his."}]}]},"with":{"h":"with","i":"/wɪð/","a":"en-us-with.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"With is used to show the other people or things present when something happened.","e":"I went to school with my brother."},{"m":"With is used to describe something added to something else.","e":"The cat has a collar with a bell on it."},{"m":"With is used to show what thing is used to do something.","e":"He hit the nail with a hammer."},{"m":"With is used to add more information.","e":"With the children so sick, we weren't able to get much work done."}]}]},"for":{"h":"for","i":"/fɔː/","a":"en-us-for.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"For is used to show that something belongs to something else, or has a specific function.","e":"This cake is for you."},{"m":"(formal) For is used to show the reason for something.","e":"He was angry, for he had never been called such terrible names before."}]}]},"as":{"h":"as","i":"/æz/","a":"en-us-as.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"A word that is used to compare two things that are equal.","e":"As you know, we need more workers."},{"m":"A word that is used to show that two things happened at the same time.","e":"Just as I went out, it started to rain."},{"m":"A word that is used to show why something happens.","e":"As I couldn't understand French, I didn't watch the film."},{"m":"A word that is used to express concession.","e":"Interesting as it seems, I don't think I'll get it."},{"m":"A word that has no meaning.","e":"The house was reported as being in excellent condition."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"A word that is used to compare two things that are equal.","e":"You are younger than I am, but nearly as tall."}]}]},"had":{"h":"had","i":"/hæd/","a":"en-us-had.ogg","l":"have","q":"verb"},"you":{"h":"you","i":"/juː/","a":"en-us-you.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"Used instead of the name of the person being spoken to; it is a second-person pronoun.","e":"You are my best friend."},{"m":"Used to talk about anyone.","e":"You have to be at least 18 years old to see that film."}]},{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"Used before a word that means the person or people someone is talking to.","e":"You guys can leave now."}]}]},"ear":{"h":"ear","i":"/ɪə̯/","a":"en-ca-ear.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A part of the head (or face) used for hearing.","e":"My rabbit has two big ears."}]}]},"gold":{"h":"gold","i":"/ɡəʊld/","a":"en-us-gold.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Gold is a metal, which can be used to make coins and rings. It costs a lot of money to buy. Its symbol is Au on the periodic table and its atomic number is 79.","e":"I keep my gold in a safe."},{"m":"(uncountable) Gold is a yellow colour."}]}]},"absorption":{"h":"absorption","i":"/əbˈzɔ:p.ʃən/","a":"en-us-absorption.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Absorption is taking in a gas or liquid through very small holes.","e":"Good water absorption properties make sponges useful for soaking up water."},{"m":"Absorption is the state of being completely occupied by something.","e":"Sam's absorption in his book made him forget to eat dinner."}]}]},"anesthetic":{"h":"anesthetic","i":"/ˌænəsˈθɛtɪk/","a":"en-US anesthetic.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An anesthetic is a gas that is used by a doctor or nurse to make a person feel no pain or to put a person to sleep.","e":"They used an anesthetic on him before performing the surgery."}]}]},"asset":{"h":"asset","i":"/ˈæsɪt/","a":"en-au-asset.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A thing that has value. It may be worth money, but may just be useful.","e":"One asset was his car and another was his house."}]}]},"drink":{"h":"drink","i":"/drɪŋk/","a":"en-us-drink.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A drink is a liquid that you take in through your mouth.","e":"He served her a hot drink and some cake."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you drink something, usually a liquid, you take it in through your mouth.","e":"I drink coffee in the morning."}]}]},"information":{"h":"information","i":"/ˌɪnfəˈmeɪʃən/","a":"en-us-information.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Information is facts, details, numbers, names, and other forms of knowledge.","e":"The nurse can provide you with more information about healthy eating."}]}]},"liquid":{"h":"liquid","i":"/ˈlɪkwɪd/","a":"en-us-liquid.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A basic state of things that is similar to water. Not solid or gas.","e":"She put the liquid in a glass."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A thing that is in the form of a liquid.","e":"He added liquid nitrogen."}]}]},"water":{"h":"water","i":"/ˈwɔːtə/","a":"en-us-water.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable); Water is a clear liquid of the chemical compound H2O that all living things need in order to live.","e":"The dog drank the water from his dish"},{"m":"(countable) A water is a bottle or glass serving of water.","e":"\"I want to order two waters, waiter\"."},{"m":"Water is mineral water."},{"m":"(alchemy) Water is one of the four basic elements."},{"m":"(India) (Japan) Water is one of the five basic elements (see Wikipedia article on the Classical elements)."},{"m":"; Water is urine."},{"m":"(US) Water is amniotic fluid.","e":"Right before the woman went into labor, her water broke."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you water something, you add water to soil around plants.","e":"He waters the plants."},{"m":"(transitive) If you water something, you give water to animals.","e":"He waters the horses."},{"m":"(transitive) If you water something, you dilute it."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something waters, it fills with water; it secretes water.","e":"His eyes watered as he cut up the onion."}]}]},"mammal":{"h":"mammal","i":"/ˈmæməl/","a":"en-us-mammal.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mammal is one member of a large group of animals with warm blood, fur, and milk production."}]}]},"ice":{"h":"ice","i":"/aɪs/","a":"en-us-ice.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A gas or liquid, normally water, which has been frozen (made solid)","e":"When water is cooled below 0°C, it freezes into ice."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you ice something, you cool it by putting ice or something else very cold on it.","e":"I iced my knee after I hurt it in soccer."},{"m":"(transitive) If you ice a cake, you cover with icing.","e":"I iced this cake."},{"m":"(transitive) If you ice someone, you murder them."}]}]},"camera":{"h":"camera","i":"/ˈkæmərə/","a":"en-us-camera.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An object that takes pictures digitally or on film.","e":"I took a picture of the mountain with my camera."},{"m":"A machine that records or broadcasts moving pictures.","e":"The shooting was caught on camera."},{"m":"A Latin word meaning room and used in English only for rooms where laws are discussed"}]}]},"tongue":{"h":"tongue","i":"/tʌŋ/","a":"en-us-tongue.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The part of the body that tastes food. It is pink or red and is inside the mouth."},{"m":"A language.","e":"He spoke in his native tongue."}]}]},"night":{"h":"night","i":"/naɪt/","a":"en-us-night.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Period from dusk to dawn."}]},{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"It is a shorter way for people who get along well to say \"good night\"."}]}]},"sun":{"h":"sun","i":"/sʌn/","a":"en-uk-sun.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"The sun is the star that can be seen during the day from the Earth. In the sky, it looks like a yellow circle.","e":"The sun is very hot."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A star, especially a star that is at the center of a solar system.","e":"Scientists have found other suns with planets around them."}]}]},"bee":{"h":"bee","i":"/biː/","a":"en-us-bee.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bee is a black and yellow striped insect with wings that makes honey. It has a stinger.","e":"That bee is flying to the flower."}]}]},"honey":{"h":"honey","i":"/'hʌni/","a":"en-us-honey.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Honey is a sweet, thick liquid that is made by bees. It is usually golden or brown.","e":"Add some honey to make it taste good."},{"m":"(uncountable) An affectionate term.","e":"Honey, I only love you."},{"m":"(countable) (informal) A woman.","e":"We need to find some honeys."},{"m":"(uncountable) Honey is a pale yellow to brownish-yellow color that looks like (the sweet substance) honey."}]}]},"reptile":{"h":"reptile","i":"/rɪpˈtaɪl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-reptile.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A reptile is a cold-blooded animal with scales (such as crocodiles or lizards).","e":"A gecko is a type of reptile."}]}]},"amphibian":{"h":"amphibian","i":"/ˈæmˌfɪbɪən/","a":"en-us-amphibian.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An amphibian is an animal that lives on land and in water.","e":"Frogs, toads, salamanders, newts, and gymnophiona are all examples of amphibians, since they can live on land and in the water."}]}]},"apple":{"h":"apple","i":"/ˈæpəl/","a":"en-us-apple.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An apple is a sweet, red, yellow or green fruit.","e":"I gave my teacher an apple."},{"m":"(uncountable) Big Apple is a name for New York City.","e":"I went to the Big Apple."}]}]},"yes":{"h":"yes","i":"/jɛs/","a":"en-us-yes.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"A word that is used to agree or accept; to mean the same thing that the other person said.","e":"Yes, I do eat fish."},{"m":"A word used to not agree with a negative sentence or question.","e":"You are not tall. Yes, I am tall."}]},{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"Used to show excitement or joy","e":"I won! Yes!"}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A yes is an answer that agrees or accepts.","e":"She gave him a yes."},{"m":"A yes is a vote for a thing.","e":"The vote count was six \"yesses\" and one \"no.\""}]}]},"yesterday":{"h":"yesterday","i":"/ˈjestədeɪ/","a":"en-us-yesterday.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(on) the day before today","e":"Yesterday, I went to the store."},{"m":"the past in general","e":"His clothes are like yesterdays fashion."},{"m":"(countable) (plural) Yesterdays are days in the past.","e":"He remembered all his yesterdays."}]}]},"young":{"h":"young","i":"/jʌŋ/","a":"en-us-young.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are young, you have not lived a long time.","e":"She was only a young girl."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A young is an offspring of an animal.","e":"The lion caught a gnu to feed its young."}]}]},"at":{"h":"at","i":"/æt/","a":"en-us-at.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Used to say where something is, or when saying something's position","e":"I am at home."},{"m":"Used to say the time at which something happened or will happen","e":"Breakfast is at 9 o'clock."},{"m":"Used to direct attention towards a state, event, or detail","e":"Look at how lucky we are."},{"m":"Used to say something's state","e":"At half price!"}]}]},"o'clock":{"h":"o'clock","i":"/əˈklɒk/","a":"en-us-o'clock.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"When saying a time, this means that it is zero minutes past the hour. O'clock is almost always given after the number of hours. It is short for of the clock.","e":"\"What time is it?\" \"It is 6 o'clock.\""}]}]},"pub":{"h":"pub","i":"/pʌb/","a":"en-us-pub.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A place which serves alcoholic and non-alcoholic drinks, and sometimes food. Pub is a short for public house, which is less commonly used.","e":"We went to the pub for a beer."}]}]},"cloud":{"h":"cloud","i":"/klaʊd/","a":"en-us-cloud.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":", (countable) A cloud is a collection of condensed water vapor floating in the sky that sometimes makes rain.","e":"Those dark storm clouds are quickly getting closer."},{"m":"(countable) A cloud is a group or swarm of something.","e":"The cloud of locusts flew closer to the corn."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something is clouded, it becomes foggy or gloomy; it becomes blocked from sight.","e":"The sky clouded over."},{"m":"If something is clouded, it becomes obscure.","e":"Don't cloud the issue."}]}]},"wiki":{"h":"wiki","i":"/ˈwɪ.ki/","a":"en-us-wiki.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A wiki is a type of website where anyone can change the contents of pages.","e":"Simple English Wiktionary is a type of wiki."}]}]},"discuss":{"h":"discuss","i":"/dɪsˈkʌs/","a":"en-us-discuss.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To talk about something.","e":"They discussed the issue."}]}]},"talk":{"h":"talk","i":"/tɔːk/","a":"en-uk-to talk.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) to speak; any sound from a person's mouth.","e":"He talks with him daily."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A talk is a lecture or a speech.","e":"I liked the talk he gave to the students."},{"m":"(uncountable) A talk is the words that a person says","e":"His talk is meaningless."}]}]},"web":{"h":"web","i":"/wɛb/","a":"en-us-web.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A web is a series of lines, ideas, or thoughts connected.","e":"Her web of thoughts is complex."},{"m":"(countable) A spiderweb.","e":"The spider is spinning a very large web."},{"m":"(uncountable) The Internet. (the World Wide Web)","e":"Simple English Wiktionary is my favorite place on the web."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you web something, you cover it with a web.","e":"Spiders web their prey and then eat them."}]}]},"speak":{"h":"speak","i":"/spiːk/","a":"en-us-speak.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"to talk","e":"He speaks with him daily."}]}]},"sound":{"h":"sound","i":"/saʊnd/","a":"en-us-sound.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A sound person is healthy."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"any noise; something that can be heard by the ears.","e":"There was a loud sound."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If something sounds a particular way, you think it is that way when you hear or read about it.","e":"The restaurant sounds great."}]}]},"person":{"h":"person","i":"/ˈpɜː(r)sən/","a":"en-us-person.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A person is someone.","e":"She is a very nice person."},{"m":"(uncountable) In grammar, the system of person is related to who is involved in the conversation.","e":"The pronoun I is first person, you is second person, and most other nouns are third person."},{"m":"(countable) A person is an individual with a mind and rights.","e":"The court is trying to decide if an elephant is a legal person."}]}]},"human":{"h":"human","i":"/ˈ(h)juː.mən/","a":"en-us-human.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Human rights, life, nature, etc. belong or relate to people, not machines or animals.","e":"Every person has human rights."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A human is a person; a member of the Homo sapiens species.","e":"What effect are we humans having on the natural world?"}]}]},"species":{"h":"species","i":"/ˈspiːʃiːz/","a":"en-us-species.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A species is the most specific level in the scientific tree.","e":"s belong to the species Homo sapiens."}]}]},"mouth":{"h":"mouth","i":"/maʊθ/","a":"en-uk-mouth.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"a part of the face used for eating and talking","e":"He opened his mouth to speak."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To silently speak; to form words with your mouth without making a sound.","e":"He mouthed the answers to her."}]}]},"daily":{"h":"daily","i":"/ˈdeɪli/","a":"en-us-daily.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"used to describe something done every day.","e":"He kept a daily diary."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"something done once a day.","e":"He showers daily."}]}]},"lines":{"h":"lines","i":"/laɪnz/","a":"en-us-lines.ogg","l":"line","q":"noun"},"ideas":{"h":"ideas","i":"/aɪˈdi.əz/","a":"en-us-ideas.ogg","l":"idea","q":"noun"},"quiet":{"h":"quiet","i":"/kwaɪət/","a":"en-us-quiet.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Not loud; making no sound or making very little sound.","e":"This young person is very quiet now because she is reading a book."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To calm or soften, as a sound.","e":"She quieted the cries of her baby."},{"m":"To remove, allay.","e":"The manager quieted their protest with a few words."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A calm or not noisy time or place.","e":"You like the quiet."}]}]},"kitchen":{"h":"kitchen","i":"/ˈkɪtʃən/","a":"en-uk-kitchen.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A kitchen is a room used for cooking food.","e":"My mother made the dinner in the kitchen."}]}]},"island":{"h":"island","i":"/ˈaɪ̯lənd/","a":"en-us-island.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An island is a piece of ground that is completely surrounded by water.","e":"The fisherman lived alone on a small island in."},{"m":"(countable) An island of an object, person, or place, is one surrounded by things very different from itself.","e":"An island of peace and silence in a noisy city."}]}]},"god":{"h":"God","i":"/ɡɒd/","a":"en-us-god.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"God is the single god of a religion and the maker of the earth and everything that exists.","e":"In Hinduism, the followers believe in numerous gods. In Christianity, Judaism, and Islam, the followers believe in only one God."}]},{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"\"God\" is used when a person is surprised. Some people do not like to use this phrase, as they think this is blasphemy (an insult to God).","e":"Oh God, not that again!"}]}]},"alphabet":{"h":"alphabet","i":"/ˈæl.fəˌbɛt/","a":"en-us-alphabet.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An alphabet is a list of the letters used to spell words by representing phonemes.","e":"The first 3 letters of the alphabet are A, B and C."}]}]},"earth":{"h":"earth","i":"/ɜːθ/","a":"en-us-earth.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Some soil.","e":"I planted some roses in this patch of earth."},{"m":"Anything made up mostly of rock, sand or soil.","e":"Here is some earth."},{"m":"Earth is the third planet from the sun, where we live.","e":"The Earth is a planet."},{"m":"A planet, especially one like Earth.","e":"He came from a different earth."},{"m":"(alchemy) One of the four classical elements.","e":"Earth is dry and hot."},{"m":"(Taoism) One of the five Taoist elements."}]}]},"not":{"h":"not","i":"/nɒt/","a":"en-uk-not.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"\"Not\" makes a phrase have the opposite meaning.","e":"I was not there."},{"m":"The item before \"not\" is more correct or better than the item after \"not\".","e":"I wanted tea, not coffee!"}]},{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"Used to indicate the sentence before is sarcastic or ironic. This means that the sentence has the opposite meaning.","e":"I like doing lots of boring homework. Not!"}]}]},"either":{"h":"either","i":"/ˈaɪ.ðə(r)/","a":"en-uk-either.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"one out of two options.","e":"I can write with either hand."},{"m":"or both from two options.","e":"The room has a door at either end."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Used in negative statements to mean too or also.","e":"I don't like him and I don't like her either."}]}]},"astronomer":{"h":"astronomer","i":"/əstrɒnəʊmə/","a":"en-us-astronomer.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An astronomer is a person who stars, and space; a person who studies astronomy.","e":"The astronomer stayed up all night, but saw nothing because it was cloudy."}]}]},"nothing":{"h":"nothing","i":"/ˈnʌθɪŋ/","a":"en-us-nothing.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"Not anything. Without any things.","e":"I bought nothing in the shop, because it was closed."},{"m":"Empty. An area has nothing in it if it has no objects in it.","e":"An empty cup has nothing in it."},{"m":"Without anything useful or interesting.","e":"I looked for the book, but I could see nothing."}]}]},"million":{"h":"million","i":"/ˈmɪljən/","a":"en-us-million.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(ordinal millionth) The number 1,000,000.","e":"In 2006, Canada had about 32.6 million people."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The number 1,000,000.","e":"One thousand thousand is a million."}]}]},"alphabetical":{"h":"alphabetical","i":"/ˌælfəˈbɛdɪkəl/","a":"en-us-alphabetical.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"In the order of the letters of the alphabet or related to the alphabet.","e":"He made the list of names alphabetical."}]}]},"adjective":{"h":"adjective","i":"/ˈæ.d͡ʒɪk.tɪv/","a":"en-us-adjective.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An adjective is a type of word which usually tells about the of people, things, and other nouns (e.g., new, small, red, & bad are adjectives). Usually it can be used before the noun or after a linking verb. It can usually be graded and described by adverbs.","e":"He uses many adjectives in his stories to give us a clear picture."}]}]},"blues":{"h":"blues","i":"/bluːz/","l":"blue","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The blues is a feeling of sadness.","e":"I have the blues."},{"m":"(uncountable) The blues is a type of music, created by African Americans.","e":"He can play blues or jazz."}]}]},"foot":{"h":"foot","i":"/fʊt/","a":"en-us-foot.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The lowest part of the leg, below the ankle; the part of the body used to stand on.","e":"He hurt his foot playing football."},{"m":"The bottom or base of something.","e":"We meet at the foot of the hill."},{"m":"A length of 12 inches; three feet is almost one meter. The foot is used mostly in the United States, but was common in Europe a long time ago.","e":"There are about 30 centimeters in one foot."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To walk or go on foot.","e":"He foots it to work every day."},{"m":"(transitive) To pay (a bill)."}]}]},"cyan":{"h":"cyan","i":"/ˈsaɪˌæn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-cyan.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Cyan is a light blue color:","e":"Cyan is my favorite color."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is cyan is light blue in color.","e":"She was wearing cyan boots."}]}]},"violet":{"h":"violet","i":"/ˈvaɪlət/","a":"en-uk-violet.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Violet is a color that people can see","e":"Violet is one of my favorite colors."},{"m":"A violet is a type of flower.","e":"Maria sells violets."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is violet in color.","e":"He wears a violet tie."}]}]},"january":{"h":"January","i":"/ˈdʒænjʊəri/","a":"en-us-January.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"January is the first (1st) month in the year.","e":"There are 31 days in January."}]}]},"february":{"h":"February","i":"/ˈfɛbrʊəri/","a":"en-us-February.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"The fourteenth (14th) month in the year.","e":"There are 30 days in February."}]}]},"march":{"h":"march","i":"/mɑːtʃ/","a":"en-us-March.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A formal, rhythmic way of walking. A march is usually done by soldiers, bands and in."},{"m":"A political rally or parade."},{"m":"Any song in the genre of music written for marching (see Wikipedia's article on this type of music)"},{"m":"Steady forward movement or progression.","e":"The march of time."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To walk with long, regular strides, like a soldier does.","e":"We saw the guards marching at."},{"m":"To go to war; to make military advances."}]}]},"science":{"h":"science","i":"/ˈsaɪəns/","a":"en-us-science.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The study of finding how things work. Some kinds of science are mathematics, biology, physics and chemistry.","e":"is a kind of science."}]},{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"The sciences are the group of science subjects. These are mathematics, biology, physics and chemistry."}]}]},"angry":{"h":"angry","i":"/ˈæŋgri/","a":"en-us-angry.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"in an aggressive way.","e":"He embarrassed her, so she was angry."},{"m":", red, and infected.","e":"He had an angry wound."}]}]},"danger":{"h":"danger","i":"/ˈdeɪn.ʤə/","a":"en-us-danger.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A danger is something that can hurt or kill a person.","e":"He was a danger to those around him. I am glad he was sent to jail."},{"m":"If someone or something is in danger, it means someone or something is under threat and can be hurt or killed.","e":"She is in danger of being buried by that avalanche."}]}]},"umbrella":{"h":"umbrella","i":"/ʌmˈbrɛlə(r)/","a":"en-us-umbrella.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An umbrella is a tool to keep you dry when it rains. You hold it over your head.","e":"I use my umbrella when it rains."},{"m":"(countable) An umbrella company is an organization that controls other organizations.","e":"The store was under the company umbrella."}]}]},"under":{"h":"under","i":"/ˈʌn.də(r)/","a":"en-us-under.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"In the same place as another thing, but lower.","e":"They ate under the trees."},{"m":"In the control of.","e":"He was under the leader of the organization."},{"m":"In the middle of a process; experiencing.","e":"The idea is under the committee's judgement (judging)."}]}]},"unit":{"h":"unit","i":"/ˈjuː.nɪt/","a":"en-us-unit.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"One of a measure of something; the amount of something that is counted as \"one\".","e":"Measure five units to the left."},{"m":"Form of measurement.","e":"I prefer metric units."},{"m":"Item, used when no other word for something exists.","e":"He set up the A/C unit."}]}]},"secret":{"h":"secret","i":"/ˈsiːkrət/","a":"en-us-secret.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"or unknown information.","e":"Can you keep a secret?"}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Known by a small group; hidden.","e":"We found her secret diary."}]}]},"key":{"h":"key","i":"/kiː/","a":"en-us-key.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A key is a small instrument, usually metal used to open locks.","e":"I put my key in the lock and turned it."},{"m":"(countable) A key is a button used for typing.","e":"Type your name and hit the ENTER key."},{"m":"(countable) A key is the part of a keyboard instrument you press with your fingers to play a sound.","e":"The piano has a pattern of black and white keys."},{"m":"The key in music is the tonal centre of a piece of music.","e":"Mozart's Symphony No.40 is written in the key of G minor."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is key, is an important or a main thing.","e":"Accuracy is a key part of playing music."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To key is to lock something with key, or like using a key."},{"m":"To key is to put locks on a building."},{"m":"The locksmith was called in to key the building for better security."},{"m":"To key is to enter information into a computer.","e":"He keyed in all the data from the survey."}]}]},"up":{"h":"up","i":"/ʌp/","a":"en-us-up.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Directed or moving upwards.","e":"The flag is up."},{"m":"Toward the top or away from the Earth.","e":"The balloon went up."},{"m":"If a task or result is up to you, it means you are in charge of deciding or doing it.","e":"The outcome of the game is up to the players."},{"m":"If you are up to something, you are doing or planning it.","e":"What are you up to this evening?"},{"m":".","e":"It was an up day."},{"m":", optimistic.","e":"He is feeling up."},{"m":"ing, occurring.","e":"What’s up?"},{"m":".","e":"Something is up with him."},{"m":"ed.","e":"It is all up with them."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"State of being up, often with down.","e":"Life has its ups and downs."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Increase, increment.","e":"We upped the dosage."}]}]},"sad":{"h":"sad","i":"/sæd/","a":"en-us-sad.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When someone feels sad, they have a bad feeling because of a loss or other problem. They are not happy.","e":"The sad girl cried."},{"m":"When something is sad, it makes you feel unhappy.","e":"It was a sad movie."}]}]},"jelly":{"h":"jelly","i":"/dʒɛli/","a":"en-us-jelly.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) (US) juice mixed with sugar, then canned; especially grape.","e":"I like jelly on my toast."},{"m":"(uncountable) (UK) A dessert made of sugar and gelatin.","e":"The children celebrated by eating bowls of jelly."},{"m":"(uncountable) A soft solid.","e":"It turned into jelly."}]}]},"use":{"h":"use","i":"/juːz/","a":"en-us-use.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Make use of; apply.","e":"I use oil to cook."},{"m":"To treat as unimportant, abuse; used about people.","e":"She only uses him to do the house chores."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A way to apply something; an application.","e":"They put it to good use."},{"m":"A time when something is applied.","e":"This battery will last for 2000 uses."}]}]},"violent":{"h":"violent","i":"/ˈvaɪ(ə)lənt/","a":"en-us-violent.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is violent, they act physically to hurt people or break things.","e":"Police said he had a history of violent behavior."},{"m":"and able to break things.","e":"The violent wind took the roof off of the house."}]}]},"judge":{"h":"judge","i":"/d͡ʒʌd͡ʒ/","a":"en-us-judge.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A judge is a person who decides or chooses.","e":"The judge decides cases."},{"m":"(countable) (Biblical) A judge is a leader.","e":"Samson was a judge of Israel."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To choose, decide.","e":"He judged in favor of the defendant."},{"m":"To evaluate (decide if something is good or bad).","e":"They judged the beauty pageant."},{"m":"To estimate.","e":"I would judge that the lake holds a million gallons."}]}]},"voice":{"h":"voice","i":"/vɔɪs/","a":"en-us-voice.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The sounds made by throat.","e":"His voice was deep and clear."},{"m":"The influence of a person.","e":"She had a lot of voice in the company."},{"m":"of expression.","e":"You spoke in a low voice so that they would not hear."},{"m":"Tells if the subject does or receives the action.","e":"That sentence is in passive voice."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To say a thought, articulate.","e":"The president voiced her disagreement."}]}]},"view":{"h":"view","i":"/vjuː/","a":"en-us-view.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The act of seeing.","e":"He had a view of the fight."},{"m":"Something you can see, vista.","e":"My window has a great view of the ocean."},{"m":"or opinion on a topic.","e":"They had a narrow view on marriage."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To think of in a certain way; consider.","e":"I view your changes with suspicion."},{"m":"To look at or examine.","e":"He views movies for content."},{"m":"To watch or observe.","e":"They viewed the rescue from the street."}]}]},"kettle":{"h":"kettle","i":"/ˈketəl/","a":"en-us-kettle.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(US) A container for boiling liquids or cooking food.","e":"William cooked the beans in a kettle."},{"m":"(UK) A container for boiling water for tea; a teakettle.","e":"Stick the kettle on and we'll have a nice cup of tea."},{"m":"A pothole."},{"m":"The collective noun for a group of airborne hawks."},{"m":"(rail transport); A steam locomotive"},{"m":"A kettledrum."},{"m":"A kettle hole."},{"m":"small type boiler"}]}]},"didn't":{"h":"didn't","i":"/ˈdɪd(ə)nt/","a":"en-us-didn't.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive)","e":"He didn't help her."}]}]},"april":{"h":"April","i":"/ˈeɪ.prɪl/","a":"en-us-April.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"April is the fourth (4th) month of the year.","e":"There are 30 days in April."}]}]},"june":{"h":"June","i":"/d͡ʒuːn/","a":"en-us-June.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"June is the sixth (6th) month of the year.","e":"There are 30 days in June."},{"m":"June is a female given name.","e":"June went to school with David."}]}]},"july":{"h":"July","i":"/d͡ʒʊˈlaɪ/","a":"en-us-July.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"The seventh (7th) month of the year.","e":"There are 31 days in July."}]}]},"august":{"h":"August","i":"/ˈɔːgəst/","a":"en-us-August.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"The eighth (8th) month of the year.","e":"There are 31 days in August."}]}]},"september":{"h":"September","i":"/sɛpˈtɛmbə/","a":"en-us-September.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"September is the ninth month of the year.","e":"There are 30 days in September."}]}]},"october":{"h":"October","i":"/ɒkˈtəʊbə/","a":"en-us-October.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"October is the tenth month of the year.","e":"There are 31 days in October."}]}]},"november":{"h":"November","i":"/nəʊˈvɛmbə/","a":"en-us-November.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"November is the eleventh month of the year.","e":"There are 30 days in November."}]}]},"december":{"h":"December","i":"/dɪˈsɛmbə/","a":"en-us-December.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"December is the twelfth month of the year.","e":"There are 31 days in December."}]}]},"sunday":{"h":"Sunday","i":"/ˈsʌndeɪ/","a":"en-us-Sunday.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"The first day of the week. The last day of the weekend, and for many Christians, the day of rest.","e":"I will go out this Sunday."}]}]},"monday":{"h":"Monday","i":"/ˈmʌndeɪ/","a":"en-us-Monday.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"The second day of the week. The first day of the work week.","e":"I hate Mondays."}]}]},"tuesday":{"h":"Tuesday","i":"/ˈtjuːzdeɪ/","a":"en-us-Tuesday.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"The third day of the week, the second day of the work week.","e":"I have Tuesday night off."}]}]},"wednesday":{"h":"Wednesday","i":"/ˈwɛdnzdeɪ/","a":"en-uk-Wednesday.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"The fourth day of the week, third and middle day of the work week."}]}]},"thursday":{"h":"Thursday","i":"/ˈθɜ:zdeɪ/","a":"en-us-Thursday.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"The fifth day of the week, fourth of the work week.","e":"I will see a movie this Thursday."}]}]},"friday":{"h":"Friday","i":"/'fraɪdeɪ/","a":"en-us-Friday.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"The sixth day of the week, fifth and last of the secular and Christian work week, and the day of rest for Muslims. Friday afternoon is the beginning of the weekend.","e":"We went to the mosque on Friday."}]}]},"saturday":{"h":"Saturday","i":"/ˈsætədeɪ/","a":"en-us-Saturday.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"The seventh and last day of the week, first day of the weekend, and for Jews and some Christians, the day of rest.","e":"Tomorrow is Saturday."}]}]},"christianity":{"h":"Christianity","i":"/ˌkrɪstiˈænɪti/","a":"en-us-Christianity.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Christianity is a religion whose followers believe that Jesus was the son of God or an important prophet of God, or believe in Jesus' ideas about what is right or wrong.","e":"He believes in Christianity."}]}]},"christian":{"h":"Christian","i":"/ˈkrɪstʃən/","a":"en-us-Christian.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A Christian is a person who believes in salvation from sin through, called Jesus Christ or Jesus the Christ.","e":"He is a conservative Christian."},{"m":"(Evangelical Christian) To some religions, a Christian is someone who has a certain spiritual way of being. This is said to be from being spiritually born with the help of Jesus Christ. This is someone who has been saved from sin.","e":"The Baptist preacher said that most Baptists are not really Christians."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are Christian then you are a Christian. (See noun above.)","e":"Yes, she is Christian."},{"m":"If something is Christian, it has to do with Christianity.","e":"Being saved from sin by Christ is a Christian idea."},{"m":"If something you do is Christian it something Christians are supposed to do.","e":"The way you forgave them was very Christian."}]}]},"atheism":{"h":"atheism","i":"/ˈeɪθiɪzəm/","a":"en-us-atheism.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Atheism is the belief that there is no God.","e":"Most atheists say atheism is not a religion."},{"m":"(uncountable) Atheism is lacking a belief that God exists.","e":"He explained that his view on god was atheism because there was no evidence of god's existence."}]}]},"noun":{"h":"noun","i":"/naʊn/","a":"en-us-inlandnorth-noun.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A noun is a kind of word that is usually the name of a person, place, thing, quality, or idea. In English, nouns can be the subject or object of a sentence. They can be singular or plural.","e":"The words \"cat\", \"home\", \"bread\", \"Sue\" and \"sunshine\" are nouns."}]}]},"domestic":{"h":"domestic","i":"/dəˈmɛstɪk/","a":"en-us-domestic.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Domestic issues relate to issues inside one country, not affecting other countries.","e":"He believes the public is ready for change in domestic and foreign policy."},{"m":"Domestic issues related to the issues inside one home.","e":"He does his domestic chores."},{"m":"Domestic animals are animals usually kept by humans.","e":"Diseases from domestic animals will often kill wild animals."}]}]},"desire":{"h":"desire","i":"/dɪˈzaɪə/","a":"en-us-desire2.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A wish, a feeling of want.","e":"She has a desire to win."},{"m":"A thing that someone wants.","e":"Love is my desire."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(formal) To wish for something, to want something.","e":"I desire your company."}]}]},"again":{"h":"again","i":"/əˈgɛn","a":"en-us-again.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Once more.","e":"They didn't understand the answer, so they asked again."}]}]},"knife":{"h":"knife","i":"/naɪf/","a":"en-us-knife.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A knife is a tool that cuts.","e":"He ate with his knife and fork."},{"m":"(countable) A knife is a tool with a thin edge.","e":"He worked with a putty knife."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you knife someone, you stab someone with a knife; you make a hole in them.","e":"The gang knifed him sixteen times."}]}]},"each":{"h":"each","i":"/iːʧ/","a":"en-us-each.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"all or every one in a group separately","e":"Come here you two. I'll give each of you a toy."}]}]},"measurement":{"h":"measurement","i":"/ˈmeʒ.ɚ.mənt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-measurement.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Measurement is the act of something."},{"m":"Measurement is the amount of something which is found by measuring it.","e":"The measurement of flour you need is four cups."}]}]},"face":{"h":"face","i":"/feɪs/","a":"en-us-face.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A face is the front part of the head.","e":"His face was red with embarrassment."},{"m":"A look or expression on the face.","e":"He made a face at the bitter medicine."},{"m":"One side of a many-sided shape.","e":"A dodecahedron has twelve faces."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If x faces y, the front of x is pointing in the direction of y.","e":"Please face me when I speak to you."}]}]},"kind":{"h":"kind","i":"/kaɪnd/","a":"en-us-kind.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Type, variety.","e":"Bread is a kind of food."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Good for another person.","e":"I admired them for being so kind, helping me when no one else would."}]}]},"happy":{"h":"happy","i":"/ˈhæpi/","a":"en-uk-happy.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When you feel happy, you feel good, usually because something nice has happened.","e":"He was happy."},{"m":"A happy situation or event makes people happy.","e":"It's such a happy day when we can be together again."},{"m":"Lucky.","e":"It was a happy chance that they met there."}]}]},"knowledge":{"h":"knowledge","i":"/ˈnɒlɪdʒ/","a":"en-us-knowledge.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Knowledge is information that you know.","e":"He shared his knowledge with you."}]}]},"thing":{"h":"thing","i":"/θɪŋ/","a":"en-us-thing.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A thing is something.","e":"She sent her things to New York."}]}]},"things":{"h":"things","i":"/θɪŋz/","a":"en-us-things.ogg","l":"thing","q":"noun"},"plough":{"h":"plough","i":"/plaʊ/","a":"en-us-plough.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A plough is a tool used to cut ground before planting.","e":"He took the plough out of the shed."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To cut the ground before planting.","e":"He will plough the field by sundown."}]}]},"plow":{"h":"plow","i":"/plaʊ/","a":"en-us-plough.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A plow is a tool used to cut ground before planting.","e":"An old plow was stuck in the field."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To cut the ground before planting.","e":"Aaron plowed the field in the spring."}]}]},"knee":{"h":"knee","i":"/niː/","a":"en-us-knee.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Part of the leg between the thigh and the shin.","e":"I hurt my knee in football."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To hit someone or something with the knee.","e":"He kneed me in the leg."}]}]},"opinion":{"h":"opinion","i":"/əˈpɪnjən/","a":"en-us-opinion.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An opinion is a personal idea, a person’s thoughts on a topic.","e":"You gave your opinion of the case."}]}]},"start":{"h":"start","i":"/stɑːt/","a":"en-uk-to start.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The beginning of something in place or time.","e":"We went back to the start."},{"m":"A movement in reaction to surprise.","e":"I surprised him and he gave a start."},{"m":"A surprise, often not pleasant.","e":"She gave him quite a start."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To begin; to do something for the first time.","e":"They started the race in first place."},{"m":"To make a machine begin to work.","e":"I will start the car."},{"m":"To move in surprise.","e":"When I touched his arm, he started."}]}]},"gray":{"h":"gray","i":"/ɡreɪ/","a":"en-us-gray.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"One of the colors people can see. It is halfway between black and white.","e":"I like the darker color of gray."},{"m":"Cloud.","e":"They look out into the gray."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"To be gray in color.","e":"That is a gray whale."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To become gray.","e":"My hair is starting to gray."}]}]},"grey":{"h":"grey","i":"/ɡreɪ/","a":"en-us-gray.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"One of the colors people can see. It is halfway between black and white.","e":"I like the darker color of grey."},{"m":"Cloud.","e":"They look out into the grey."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"To be grey in color.","e":"That is a grey whale."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To become grey.","e":"My hair is starting to grey."}]}]},"heliocentric":{"h":"heliocentric","i":"/ˌhiːliəʊˈsɛntrɪk/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Heliocentric means Centered on the sun.","e":"Copernicus' model of the universe was heliocentric."}]}]},"awake":{"h":"awake","i":"/ə'weɪk/","a":"en-us-awake.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are awake, you are not asleep.","e":"It was 1:00 AM and Gerard was still awake."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If someone awakes, they stop sleeping.","e":"She awoke with the dawn."},{"m":"If something awakes a feeling, it makes it happen.","e":"He awoke their resentment."}]}]},"daughter":{"h":"daughter","i":"/ˈdɔːtə(r)/","a":"en-us-daughter.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A daughter is a female child of someone.","e":"I am her father and she is my daughter."}]}]},"keep":{"h":"keep","i":"/kiːp/","a":"en-us-keep.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you keep something for someone, you make something safe.","e":"I will keep your money for you."},{"m":"When you keep something, you do not give it back.","e":"Keep the change."},{"m":"(intransitive) When you keep safe, happy, quiet, etc, you stay that way.","e":"Keep quiet."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A keep is a special safe area of a castle.","e":"The king lived in the keep during the battle."}]}]},"jewel":{"h":"jewel","i":"/ˈʤuːəl/","a":"en-us-jewel.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A valuable gem; a precious stone.","e":"Mary keeps her jewels in a safe."}]}]},"army":{"h":"army","i":"/ˈɑː.mi/","a":"en-us-army.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The people and organisation, normally in a government, which fights wars.","e":"The army fought in Iraq."},{"m":"A large number of people working towards the same thing.","e":"It took an army of people to build that bridge."}]}]},"bridge":{"h":"bridge","i":"/brɪdʒ/","a":"en-uk-a bridge.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Anything which avoids something which blocks a path, usually water, by going over the top of it.","e":"The connects the two sides of California."},{"m":"A card game."}]}]},"vessel":{"h":"vessel","i":"/ˈves.əl/","a":"en-us-vessel.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A vessel is a pot or container.","e":"She poured the milk into another vessel."},{"m":"(countable) A vessel is a ship or a large boat.","e":"It was the best vessel in the water."}]}]},"say":{"h":"say","i":"/seɪ/","a":"en-us-say.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you say something, you share it in words.","e":"He says he is hungry."}]}]},"able":{"h":"able","i":"/eɪbl/","a":"en-us-able.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is able to do something, they can do it.","e":"I'm busy tomorrow, so I won't be able to see you."},{"m":"If a person is able, the person is good or skillful at what he does.","e":"She is an able teacher."}]}]},"this":{"h":"this","i":"/ðɪs/","a":"en-us-this.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"You use this to show which thing or idea you are talking about. You use it when the thing or idea is close to you.","e":"This trip was a great idea."},{"m":"The thing indicated without mentioning the noun.","e":"This is my hand."},{"m":"You use this in stories, jokes etc to introduce a person or thing into the story.","e":"So this guy walks up to me and asked if I have any fish."}]}]},"iron":{"h":"iron","i":"/ˈaɪən/","a":"en-us-iron.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) An element with the symbol Fe and the atomic number 26.","e":"A way to melt iron at very high temperatures to make steel was developed in Sri Lanka in 300 BC."},{"m":"(uncountable) A metal from the element.","e":"That door is made of iron."},{"m":"(countable) A tool which uses heat to remove wrinkles from cloth.","e":"She used the iron on her skirt."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To remove wrinkles with an iron.","e":"He irons his shirts."}]}]},"kiss":{"h":"kiss","i":"/kɪs/","a":"en-us-kiss.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The act of placing your lips on something, usually to show love or affection.","e":"She gave him a long kiss on the lips."},{"m":"A cone-shaped piece of chocolate made by Hershey.","e":"I will give you a chocolate kiss."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To place your lips on something to show love or affection.","e":"The man and the woman kissed each other."},{"m":"To touch for a moment.","e":"His car kissed the bumper of the car in front of him."}]}]},"knot":{"h":"knot","i":"/nɒt/","a":"en-us-knot.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A knot is formed when a rope is tied.","e":"He put a knot in the rope."},{"m":"(countable) A knot is a unit of speed."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To create a tied place in a cord or rope.","e":"They knotted the ends of the rope together."}]}]},"leg":{"h":"leg","i":"/lɛg/","a":"en-us-leg.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Your legs are the two long parts of your body that you move to walk, or a similar body part on an animal.","e":"I lost a leg in the war."},{"m":"(countable) A leg is part of a piece of furniture, such as a table, on which the furniture stands.","e":"I can see an ant crawling up the leg of the table."},{"m":"(countable) A leg is part of a tour or journey.","e":"The band had to cancel the German leg of their European tour."}]}]},"man":{"h":"man","i":"/mæn/","a":"en-uk-man.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A man is a male human.","e":"He was a young man with blue eyes."},{"m":"(uncountable) Human beings of either sex; People.","e":"Man landed on the Moon in 1969."}]},{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"You use man to show your surprise or disappointment.","e":"Oh man, I wanted to do the dishes!"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If something is manned, it has people to look after it.","e":"The ship was manned with a small crew."},{"m":"(transitive) If you man something, you take up position to operate it.","e":"Man the machine guns!"}]}]},"addition":{"h":"addition","i":"/əˈdɪʃən/","a":"en-us-addition.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The part of arithmetic where numbers are added together.","e":"He learned addition quickly."},{"m":"(uncountable) The act of adding something.","e":"The addition of 5 more topics will make the meeting very long and boring."},{"m":"(countable) Anything that is added.","e":"He put an addition on the house."}]}]},"about":{"h":"about","i":"/ə'baʊ̯t/","a":"en-us-about (improved).ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"You use about to say what subject something is related to.","e":"Let's not talk about her problems."},{"m":"If something moves about, it moves in many directions.","e":"He walked about the place, looking everywhere."},{"m":"Having to do with, concerning, regarding.","e":"I will talk about dogs."},{"m":"Nearly, approximately.","e":"They're about the same."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is about to happen, it will happen very soon.","e":"Please be seated. We're about to begin."}]}]},"across":{"h":"across","i":"/əˈkrɒs/","a":"en-us-across.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"To the other side.","e":"I walked across the bridge."},{"m":"On the other side.","e":"I can see him across the street."},{"m":"Crossing, on both sides of.","e":"The bridge is across the stream."}]}]},"cut":{"h":"cut","i":"/kʌt/","a":"en-us-cut.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you make something shorter or divide it in pieces, you cut it.","e":"Jared cut the meat using his knife and fork."},{"m":"To hurt with a blade.","e":"I cut my hand."},{"m":"To stop something.","e":"They cut the electricity."},{"m":"To edit, shorten, or censor (a film).","e":"The film was cut by ten minutes."},{"m":"(computers) If you remove something to put it somewhere else, you cut it.","e":"Ben cut the text from the Word document and pasted it into another."},{"m":"(film) If the picture changes from one scene to another, the scene cuts to another."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A scratch, opening in the skin or a surface.","e":"She had a cut on her arm."},{"m":"(countable) A reduction; lessening.","e":"There was a cut in prices."},{"m":"(countable) A small piece removed by cutting is a cut.","e":"I will take a cut of beef."}]}]},"fact":{"h":"fact","i":"/fækt/","a":"en-us-fact.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A fact is a piece of information that is true.","e":"That is not just my idea, it is a fact."},{"m":"A fact is a piece of information.","e":"He collects little-known facts."}]}]},"idea":{"h":"idea","i":"/aɪˈdɪə/","a":"en-us-idea.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An idea is a concept or a thought.","e":"It was a good idea."},{"m":"(countable) An idea is something abstract (not concrete).","e":"Love is just an idea."},{"m":"(countable) An idea is a way to see something, a view.","e":"He changed her ideas on religion."}]}]},"insect":{"h":"insect","i":"/ˈɪnsɛkt/","a":"en-us-insect.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A type of small animal with an external skeleton and six legs.","e":"I killed a large insect in the bathroom."},{"m":"(countable) A person who is weak or not important.","e":"The mayor thought of her as a mere insect."}]}]},"ink":{"h":"ink","i":"/ɪŋk/","a":"en-us-ink.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Ink is a tint, often black, used to write.","e":"The ink on the paper has dried."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If someone inks something, they make a mark or write using ink.","e":"He inked his name."},{"m":"If someone inks things like a pen, they fill with ink.","e":"She inks her pen."}]}]},"important":{"h":"important","i":"/ɪmˈpɔːtənt/","a":"en-us-important.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Main or primary.","e":"That is an important point."}]}]},"ill":{"h":"ill","i":"/ɪl/","a":"en-us-ill.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Sick, not well. If you are ill, you have bad health, you might have a disease.","e":"One boy died and the other is seriously ill in the hospital."},{"m":"If you are ill you are angry or disturbed.","e":"You are making me ill with your attacks."}]}]},"wrong":{"h":"wrong","i":"/rɒŋ/","a":"en-ca-wrong.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is wrong, it is not right. If something is wrong it may be incorrect, not true, or bad.","e":"That answer is wrong."},{"m":"If something is wrong, it is not moral.","e":"What you did was wrong."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you wrong someone, you do something that hurts a person.","e":"He wrongs you by his actions."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A wrong is an immoral act.","e":"They accused him of wrongs against humanity."}]}]},"sail":{"h":"sail","i":"/seɪl/","a":"en-us-sail.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sail is a large piece of fabric (cloth) to catch wind, used on a boat or a ship.","e":"They folded the sail."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you sail, you move by catching the wind, usually by ship on water.","e":"They sail around the world every year in their boat."},{"m":"If you sail, you travel on a boat or ship.","e":"We sailed across the Atlantic to reach Spain."}]}]},"very":{"h":"very","i":"/ˈvɛrɪ/","a":"en-us-very.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Much; quite. Using very makes the adjective or adverb stronger.","e":"He was very young."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Actual, same.","e":"It was the very boy who helped me."},{"m":"Exact.","e":"This man is the very one for the job."}]}]},"join":{"h":"join","i":"/ˈdʒɔɪn/","a":"en-us-join.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If someone joins two or more things, they bring them together.","e":"Their lives were joined."},{"m":"If someone joins someone else, they do something together.","e":"I will join you on your walk."},{"m":"(transitive) If someone joins a club, school, etc. they become a member.","e":"Would you like to join our club?"},{"m":"(transitive) If someone joins two or more things, they make a connection between them.","e":"The new building is joined to the school by a short hallway."}]}]},"kick":{"h":"kick","i":"/ˈkɪk/","a":"en-us-kick.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hit using the foot.","e":"I gave the door a kick."},{"m":"(countable), fun.","e":"I get a kick out of talking to her."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you kick someone or something, you attack or hit it with your foot.","e":"She kicked the door down."}]}]},"journey":{"h":"journey","i":"/ˈdʒɜː(r)ni/","a":"en-us-journey.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A journey is a long trip.","e":"Timothy left on a long journey."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you journey to somewhere, you travel there.","e":"We journeyed from town to town."}]}]},"jump":{"h":"jump","i":"/dʒʌmp/","a":"en-us-jump.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you jump, you leave the ground completely.","e":"He jumped for joy."},{"m":"(transitive) If you jump something, you fly over it.","e":"The children jumped the water to get to the other side."},{"m":"(transitive) If you jump something, you make it leave the ground.","e":"He loved jumping his bicycle."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you jump, you move suddenly because you are surprised.","e":"I scared her and she jumped."},{"m":"(transitive) If you jumpstart a car, you use the battery power from another car.","e":"We used his car to jump ours."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A jump is a movement from the ground to the air.","e":"She took a run before the big jump over the water."},{"m":"A jump is a ramp used to jump.","e":"He went off the jump at full speed."},{"m":"A jump is a jolt or shock used to start a car.","e":"He used his car to give me a jump."},{"m":"A jump is a sudden movement of surprise.","e":"It seems I surprised her, because she gave a little jump."}]}]},"quality":{"h":"quality","i":"/'kwɒl.ɪ.tɪ/","a":"en-us-quality.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Quality is goodness.","e":"This cloth is full of quality."},{"m":"(uncountable) Quality is how good something is, as opposed to how much of something there is.","e":"The meat was of poor quality."},{"m":"(countable) A quality is something about a person or thing, like intelligence, beauty or transparency.","e":"Being truthful is his best quality."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"(informal) A quality item is a very good one.","e":"Here is a quality computer."}]}]},"narrow":{"h":"narrow","i":"/ˈnæroʊ/","a":"en-us-ne-narrow.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is narrow, it is not wide; it is thin.","e":"The bridge was narrow."},{"m":"If something is narrow, it is limited.","e":"He has a narrow knowledge of math."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something is narrowed, it becomes thinner; it becomes narrower.","e":"He narrowed his eyes in anger."}]}]},"value":{"h":"value","i":"/ˈvæl.juː/","a":"en-us-value.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Something's value is how good or important it is; how much money someone will exchange a thing for; an amount of money.","e":"The value for me of this food is $100."},{"m":"(usually plural) Your values are your ideas about which things are good.","e":"He has strong values."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you value someone or something, you think that they are good and you don't want to lose them.","e":"I value your help."},{"m":"If you value something judge how good or important it is.","e":"They valued it at $600."}]}]},"question":{"h":"question","i":"/ˈkwɛsʧən/","a":"en-us-question.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Something someone says to have someone else say an answer.","e":"The question is: \"How much money do we have?\""},{"m":"A trouble or thing to talk about.","e":"It was a question of right and wrong."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To say questions to someone; to ask someone questions.","e":"She questioned him fully."},{"m":"To have an idea that something may be true or may not be true.","e":"They questioned whether he was right."}]}]},"verse":{"h":"verse","i":"/ˈvɝs/","a":"en-us-verse.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Words that use rhythm and good sounds, like the words of a song but with no music.","e":"It was a book of verse."},{"m":"(Biblical) A very little part of the Bible.","e":"That is found in the Gospel of John, chapter 3, verse sixteen."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you verse, then you study a subject in depth.","e":"He has become well versed in the classics."}]}]},"new":{"h":"new","i":"/njuː/","a":"en-us-new.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is new, it is not old.","e":"They had a new car."},{"m":"If somebody is new, they are not experienced.","e":"They hired a new worker."}]}]},"quick":{"h":"quick","i":"/kwɪk/","a":"en-us-quick.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Using very little time; moving far in little time.","e":"You are able to run very quickly."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Done rapidly.","e":"He finished quick."}]}]},"quite":{"h":"quite","i":"/kwaɪt/","a":"en-us-quite.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"; much.","e":"The dog was quite little."},{"m":"Not very.","e":"The evening was quite dark and I saw a small frog jump across the road."}]},{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"or indeed.","e":"\"Is the answer correct?\" \"Quite!\""}]}]},"billion":{"h":"billion","i":"/ˈbɪljən/","a":"en-us-billion.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(ordinal billionth) The number 1,000,000,000 (or 1,000,000,000,000 in old British usage).","e":"In 2006, China had about 1.3 billion people."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The number 1,000,000,000 (or 1,000,000,000,000 in old British usage).","e":"Billions of dollars have been spent on the war in Iraq."}]}]},"trillion":{"h":"trillion","i":"/ˈtrɪljən/","a":"en-us-trillion.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(US, modern British and Australian, short scale) Trillion refers to the number 1,000,000,000,000 (1012)","e":"There are about one trillion (1012) bacteria on the surface of the human body."},{"m":"(older British and Australian, long scale) The number 1,000,000,000,000,000,000 (1018).","e":"There are about one trillion (1018) insects on Earth."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(US, modern British and Australian, short scale) The number 1,000,000,000,000","e":"In the United States, one million millions is a trillion."},{"m":"(older British and Australian, long scale) The number 1,000,000,000,000,000,000.","e":"In the long scale, one million millions is a billion. One million billions is a trillion."}]}]},"sugar":{"h":"sugar","i":"/ˈʃʊgə/","a":"en-us-sugar.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Sugar is a small white powder. It looks like salt, but it tastes sweet. Some people put it in tea.","e":"This cookie recipe says you should use two cups of sugar, but I think that will be too sweet. One cup is enough."}]}]},"profit":{"h":"profit","i":"/ˈprɒfɪt/","a":"en-us-profit.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A profit is money made that is over the total amount spent on the thing being sold."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If someone profits from something, they benefit from it; they gain from it."}]}]},"bad":{"h":"bad","i":"/bæd/","a":"en-us-bad.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is bad, it is not good.","e":"The man who killed his wife was very bad."}]}]},"door":{"h":"door","i":"/dɔː/","a":"en-us-door.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A piece of a wall that can be opened (leaving a hole in the wall to walk through) or closed (covering the hole). Some doors are on hinges; others slide.","e":"Please open the door for him. His hands are full."}]}]},"down":{"h":"down","i":"/daʊ̯n/","a":"en-us-down.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Toward the earth, away from the sky.","e":"What goes up on earth must fall down."},{"m":"Toward the bottom."},{"m":"Towards a smaller price, number, amount, etc.","e":"I'm going to buy a computer once prices go down."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Down is soft feathers or a covering of soft feathers.","e":"That pillow is full of down."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you down a liquid, normally an alcoholic drink, it means you drink it very quickly.","e":"Harry downed a glass of beer in five seconds."}]}]},"price":{"h":"price","i":"/praɪs/","a":"en-us-price.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The amount of money you need to pay to buy something.","e":"The price of this book is ten dollars."}]}]},"spell":{"h":"spell","i":"/spɛl/","a":"en-us-spell.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(of letters) To make up a word.","e":"C, A and T spell cat."},{"m":"To say or write all the letters that make up a word, in the right order.","e":"Jack says: \"Spell cat for me, Jill.\""},{"m":"To spell all the words in a language correctly.","e":"Jack says: I thought cat was spelled K-A-T."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A spell is an amount of time.","e":"He stayed in his house for quite a spell."},{"m":"What happens during an amount of time.","e":"We've had a bad spell of weather."},{"m":"Words supposed to have a magical power, or the effect they are supposed to have.","e":"He cast a spell on us."}]}]},"weather":{"h":"weather","i":"/ˈwɛðɚ/","a":"en-us-weather.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The weather in a place is the air temperature, the number of clouds, and the amount of wind and rain or snow.","e":"The weather conditions at the airport are bad. I don't think the plane will be able to fly."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To weather is to be changed by the effects of sun, wind, ice or rain.","e":"The old house had weathered badly."}]}]},"rain":{"h":"rain","i":"/reɪn/","a":"en-us-rain.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Drops of water that fall out of clouds in the sky.","e":"I do not like going outside in the rain."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If it is raining, water is falling from the sky."}]}]},"tax":{"h":"tax","i":"/tæks/","a":"en-us-tax.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"taken by a government.","e":"The city is raising taxes again."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you tax someone, you make them pay a [[#Noun|tax]].","e":"Some people say governments tax poor people too much."},{"m":"(transitive) If an activity is taxing, it causes difficulty or makes you tired."}]}]},"city":{"h":"city","i":"/ˈsɪti/","a":"en-us-city.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A city is large area where many people live and work, larger than a town.","e":"Tokyo and New York are two of the world's largest cities."},{"m":"(countable) The city is the government that has power over a city.","e":"A city usually builds roads and parks, and keeps them in good shape."},{"m":"(countable) The city is the people who live in the city.","e":"The city is afraid of the change."}]}]},"car":{"h":"car","i":"/ˈkɑː/","a":"en-us-car.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A car is a small passenger vehicle with four wheels, moved by an engine.","e":"I just drive around in my car all day."},{"m":"(countable) (US) A car is one large part of a train that can be added or taken away."}]}]},"building":{"h":"building","i":"/ˈbɪldɪŋ/","a":"en-us-building.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A building consists of walls, a foundation and a roof that together close in some space.","e":"I work in the Chrysler Building."}]}]},"home":{"h":"home","i":"/həʊm/","a":"en-us-home.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Where a person lives. Usually, where people keep their things that they are not carrying, and where they sleep."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If you go home, you go to the place where you live.","e":"He brought the money straight home to his mother."},{"m":"If you are home, you are in the place where you live.","e":"I'm home all evening, so give me a call."}]}]},"verb":{"h":"verb","i":"/vɜː(r)b/","a":"en-us-verb.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A verb is a kind of word that usually tells about an action or a state and is the head of a sentence. In English, verbs are the only kind of word that changes to show past or present tense. See verb examples.","e":"In the sentence My father works on a farm, the verb is works."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To verb a word is to turn it into a verb.","e":"The word \"access\" used to just be a noun, but then it got verbed."}]}]},"farm":{"h":"farm","i":"/fɑːrm/","a":"en-us-farm.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A piece of land where people work growing plants and animals. Usually, a farm makes food for its owners to eat or sell.","e":"We grow cows and apples on our farm."},{"m":"A farm is a group of coordinated servers.","e":"A server farm."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To grow plants or animals on a piece of land.","e":"My father farms on a large parcel of land for a living."},{"m":"If you farm in an online game, you engage in repetitive activity for a particular item."}]}]},"food":{"h":"food","i":"/fuːd/","a":"en-uk-food.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Food is what people and animals eat for nutrition or pleasure when they are hungry.","e":"We grow our own food."}]}]},"father":{"h":"father","i":"/ˈfaː.ðə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Back ache-father.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The father of a person is the man who is one of that person's parents.","e":"The father of Bill Smith IV is Bill Smith III."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To have children (only applies to males)","e":"He fathered six children in six years."}]}]},"fertile":{"h":"fertile","i":"/ˈfɜːtaɪl/","a":"en-us-fertile.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Fertile land is land on which crops can grow well.","e":"That field is fertile."},{"m":"A fertile person, animal, or plant is one that can produce children or offspring.","e":"The average fertile female cat gives birth once or twice a year."},{"m":"If someone has a fertile imagination, brain, or mind, they create a lot of interesting new ideas."}]}]},"crop":{"h":"crop","i":"/krɒp/","a":"en-us-crop.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A plant that is grown on a farm.","e":"Our farm's crops are corn, apples and potatoes."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To cut off the edges of a picture.","e":"I cropped the picture to a size of 4 centimetres by 5 centimetres."},{"m":"(transitive) To cut off the top of something, often a plant."},{"m":"(transitive) To cut hair short."}]}]},"available":{"h":"available","i":"/əˈveɪ.lə.b(ə)l/","a":"en-us-available.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is available, it exists and you can use it.","e":"We can't answer the question with the available information."}]}]},"financial":{"h":"financial","i":"/faɪˈnænʃəl/","a":"en-us-financial.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A financial problem, issue, activity or other thing is about money or business.","e":"Our sales are down and we have serious financial problems."}]}]},"process":{"h":"process","i":"/'prəʊsɛs/","a":"en-uk-process.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A process is a series of steps that you take for a particular purpose.","e":"Let us look at the factors considered during the formal decision-making process."},{"m":"(countable) A process is an outward extension of bone from a larger bone or piece of tissue.","e":"The xiphoid process is located beneath your sternum."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you process something, you change it from its natural state into something that's ready to use.","e":"The oil companies process much of the crude oil into gasoline."}]}]},"individual":{"h":"individual","i":"/ˌɪndɪˈvɪʤuəl/","a":"en-us-individual.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"An individual person or thing is looked at separately from others.","e":"This office assists whole families rather than individual family members."},{"m":"An individual right, need, etc. belongs to one person, not to a group.","e":"The government should protect not only individual rights but also group values."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An individual is a single person, looked at separately from others.","e":"One of the most difficult parts of growing up is learning to form your own ideas--to become an individual."}]}]},"assist":{"h":"assist","i":"/əˈsɪst/","a":"en-us-assist.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you assist someone, you help them.","e":"She assisted the doctor."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"In basketball and some other sports, a pass to another player to let him or her score.","e":"He had eight assists in that game."}]}]},"assistance":{"h":"assistance","i":"/əˈsɪs.təns/","a":"en-us-assistance.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) If you give someone or something assistance, you give help or support.","e":"The company may also provide financial assistance to single mothers."}]}]},"family":{"h":"family","i":"/ˈfæm(ɪ)li/","a":"en-us-family.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A family is a group of people with a blood or marriage relation.","e":"My parents and my two brothers are my family."},{"m":"(countable) A language family is a group of languages that is believed to have came from the same language.","e":"The Indo-European language family is a family of languages spoken by 3 billion people."}]}]},"sixth":{"h":"sixth","i":"/sɪksθ/","a":"en-us-sixth.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"The sixth thing is the one that is number six (6) in order.","e":"He ran in the marathon and came in sixth."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sixth is one of six equal parts of one whole.","e":"He gave me a sixth of his orange."}]}]},"sector":{"h":"sector","i":"/ˈsɛk.tər/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-sector.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sector is a part or division of an area, especially part of the economy.","e":"Service sector jobs, such as restaurant jobs, are often low paying."}]}]},"specific":{"h":"specific","i":"/spəˈsɪf.ɪk/","a":"en-us-specific.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you talk about a specific idea, person, group, or thing, you mean that it is different from or more interesting than other things like it; you might also mean that you know exactly which one you are talking about.","e":"The interviewer uses a checklist to make sure that specific areas are covered."},{"m":"If something is specific, it is detailed, clear, and limited.","e":"Last time, he was happy to do anything, but feels this time he has to be more specific."}]}]},"principle":{"h":"principle","i":"/ˈprɪnsɪpəl/","a":"en-us-principle.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Principles are personal rules that tell you what is right and wrong.","e":"It goes against my principles to ignore her."},{"m":"(countable) A principle is the general idea that explains or supports something.","e":"The basic principle of his chair is that the knees should be below the hips."}]}]},"estimate":{"h":"estimate","i":"/ˈɛstɨmɨt/","a":"en-us-estimate-noun.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An estimate is a judgement of a size, value, amount, cost, etc., which is based on incomplete information.","e":"British Telecom will give you an estimate of the cost before doing any work."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you estimate the number, size, value, amount, cost, etc. of something, you guess based on incomplete information.","e":"It's difficult to estimate how long it will take to get to London because we don't know how bad the traffic will be."}]}]},"variable":{"h":"variable","i":"/ˈver.i.ə.bl̩/","a":"en-us-variable.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A variable is something that may not always be the same.","e":"In life insurance, sex is an important variable because men generally die younger than women."},{"m":"A variable is something used in mathematics for an unknown value.","e":"In \"x = 1 + 2 +...n = ((1 + n) × n)÷2\", x is the variable."},{"m":"A variable is something used in computer programming languages that stores data, such as a number or words."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is variable, it changes often.","e":"The temperature in the area is highly variable."},{"m":"If a group is variable, there are big differences between things in the group.","e":"The expected height of children in 3rd grade is variable."}]}]},"method":{"h":"method","i":"/'mɛθəd/","a":"en-us-method.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) If you use a method to achieve a goal, then you use a planned process.","e":"It is quite simple to use the method described in 7.2 to find the solution."}]}]},"brother":{"h":"brother","i":"/ˈbrʌðə(r)/","a":"en-uk-brother.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Your brother is another male child of one or both of your parents.","e":"Two sisters and their brother played in the park yesterday"}]}]},"all":{"h":"all","i":"/ɔːl/","a":"en-us-all.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"All of something is 100% of it, or the entire amount.","e":"Well, you could stay in bed all day on Friday. And I could take the kids to school."},{"m":"All of some things is 100% of them, or every one.","e":"And then you can go and tell all your friends about it."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) If you give your all or put your all into something, you make the maximum effort possible.","e":"He puts his all into every game."}]}]},"money":{"h":"money","i":"/ˈmʌni/","a":"en-us-money.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Money is the coins or notes that are used to pay for things."},{"m":"(uncountable) Money is a tool that is used to pay for goods or services.","e":"You don't want to spend your money on an ice cream. You can buy something else."}]}]},"data":{"h":"data","i":"/ˈdeɪtə/","a":"en-us-data1.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Data is information, such as facts, numbers, photographs, etc.","e":"A study using experimental data from ten schools found no difference between methods."}]}]},"absolutely":{"h":"absolutely","i":"/æb.sʊˈlʊut.lɪi/","a":"en-us-absolutely.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something is absolutely true, correct, etc., it's 100% so.","e":"I agree. You're absolutely right."},{"m":"If something is absolutely beautiful, brilliant, etc., it's very much so.","e":"\"It was wonderful,\" Martha said. \"Absolutely wonderful! The best!\""},{"m":"You say there is absolutely nothing, to emphasise that there is nothing.","e":"I have absolutely no idea why he said that."}]}]},"doubt":{"h":"doubt","i":"/daʊt/","a":"en-us-doubt.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A doubt is a question or uncertainty about something.","e":"His mind was full of doubts about the phishing website."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you doubt someone or something, you do not believe them completely.","e":"The girl I met at the pub said she would call me, but I doubt she really will."}]}]},"art":{"h":"art","i":"/ɑːt/","a":"en-us-art.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An art is a skill that produces works of creative expression and can be mastered through study and practice. Arts are often contrasted with sciences.","e":"ing, music and writing are arts."},{"m":"(uncountable) Art is creation by means of an art. examples of art are paintings and photographs, but songs and even buildings can be art, too.","e":"The gallery has many pieces of art."}]}]},"cold":{"h":"cold","i":"/kəʊld/","a":"en-us-cold.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is cold, it is low in temperature.","e":"The wind made her hands cold."},{"m":"If someone is cold, they are not kind.","e":"She's always so friendly to everyone, but she's really cold to him."},{"m":"If you have cold feet, you are nervous about something you planned to and you feel like not doing it.","e":"I almost took the new job, but in the end I got cold feet."},{"m":"If you give someone the cold shoulder, you ignore them or you are unfriendly towards them."},{"m":"If you stop cold, you stop very suddenly."},{"m":"If you are out cold, you are unconscious."},{"m":"A cold light or colour is a one, often with some blue, that makes you feel cold or empty."},{"m":"If you do something cold, you do it without any preparation."},{"m":"Cold cash is coins and bills, not promises to pay."},{"m":"If something leaves you cold, it doesn't interest you at all."},{"m":"If someone's or something's trail is cold, you can't find them because they have been missing for too long."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mild sickness. It gives your trouble with your nose and throat.","e":"He has a cold, so he stayed in bed, kept warm, and took some medicine."}]}]},"cook":{"h":"cook","i":"/kʊk/","a":"en-uk-to cook.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To bake or boil, to prepare food.","e":"Darren will cook dinner today."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A person who cooks.","e":"Emily is a cook."}]}]},"current":{"h":"current","i":"/ˈkʌrɛnt/","a":"en-us-current.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is current is up to date.","e":"This news is current."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Current is movement in a fluid.","e":"There is a strong current in that water."},{"m":"(uncountable) Current is movement in electricity.","e":"It has a current of nine amperes."}]}]},"same":{"h":"same","i":"/seɪm/","a":"en-us-same.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Two things are the same if the two things have one size, and one shape, and one color, etc.","e":"Sometimes we wear the same shirt."},{"m":"The one that was talked about before. A thing is the same thing if there are not two things, there is only one.","e":"That man there is the same man I saw yesterday."}]}]},"secretary":{"h":"secretary","i":"/ˈsɛk.rə.tə.ri/","a":"en-us-secretary.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A secretary is a person who works in an office, helping with typing letters, filing, and other simple tasks.","e":"I will ask my secretary to write to them."}]}]},"safe":{"h":"safe","i":"/seɪf/","a":"en-us-safe.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is safe, it is not in danger.","e":"I feel safe when I am at home."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A safe is a metal box, often locked with a, for guarding valuable things.","e":"She put her jewelry in the safe."}]}]},"ship":{"h":"ship","i":"/ʃɪp/","a":"en-us-ship.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A ship is a large boat.","e":"We sailed by ship from England to Italy."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To move or transport.","e":"They will ship the package by mail."}]}]},"skin":{"h":"skin","i":"/skɪn/","a":"en-us-skin.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The outer layer of an animal or human.","e":"Her skin is soft."},{"m":"The outer layer of a fruit or vegetable; a peel.","e":"He ate the onion, but not the onion skin."},{"m":"Something that is like skin."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you skin something, you remove its skin.","e":"He skinned the bear and froze the meat."}]}]},"sneeze":{"h":"sneeze","i":"/sniːz/","a":"en-us-sneeze.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you sneeze, a feeling in your nose makes you suddenly blow air out of your nose and mouth.","e":"He sneezed until his nose was red."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sneeze, is a sudden blowing of air out of your nose and mouth because of a feeling in your nose.","e":"She held her finger under her nose to stop a sneeze."}]}]},"snow":{"h":"snow","i":"/snəʊ/","a":"en-us-snow.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Snow is precipitation (falling water) that is white and frozen.","e":"I like to ski on the snow."},{"m":"(countable) A snow is a time when snow falls from the sky.","e":"The snows of winter will soon come."},{"m":"(uncountable) A shade of the color white."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If it is snowing, snow is coming down from the sky.","e":"It snowed last night and everything is white now."}]}]},"son":{"h":"son","i":"/sʌn/","a":"en-us-son.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A son is a male child of someone.","e":"I am his son."}]}]},"table":{"h":"table","i":"/ˈteɪbəl/","a":"en-uk-table.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A raised flat surface.","e":"He sat at the table to eat."},{"m":"A list of information in rows and columns.","e":"He looked at the data table."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To propose in a meeting.","e":"We will table a new motion."},{"m":"To end or postpone in a meeting.","e":"I vote to table discussion."}]}]},"early":{"h":"early","i":"/ˈɜːli/","a":"en-us-early.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is early, it is sooner than expected.","e":"It was an early end to the meeting."},{"m":"If something is early, it happens in the first part of a time period.","e":"He didn't like going to the early classes."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"er than expected.","e":"He was at the meeting early."},{"m":"During the first part of a time period.","e":"She got up early in the morning."}]}]},"east":{"h":"east","i":"/iːst/","a":"en-uk-east.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The east is a place that is closer to where the sun rises than another place.","e":"My parents live in the east."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"One of the four compass directions: 90º clockwise from north. The sun rises in the east.","e":"I drove east from Chicago."}]}]},"edge":{"h":"edge","i":"/ɛʤ/","a":"en-us-edge.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The boundary of a surface."},{"m":"(singular) An advantage.","e":"His speed gives him an edge."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To create an edge.","e":"He edged the grass."},{"m":"To move slowly.","e":"She edged away from him."}]}]},"brunette":{"h":"brunette","i":"/bruˈnɛt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-brunette.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A girl or woman with brown hair.","e":"My mum has brown hair and I am a brunette too."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A girl or woman that is brown-haired.","e":"My sister is brunette, but she pretends she is blonde."}]}]},"brunet":{"h":"brunet","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A man or boy with brown or black hair.","e":"He is a brunet."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"(Of a man or boy) Brown or black-haired.","e":"His hair is brown. He is brunet."}]}]},"woman":{"h":"woman","i":"/ˈwʊmən/","a":"en-uk-woman.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A female human.","e":"My wife is a good woman."}]}]},"worm":{"h":"worm","i":"/wɜːm/","a":"en-us-worm.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A tube-shaped animal with no legs that lives underground, under water, or inside another animal.","e":"He found a big worm to use for fishbait."},{"m":"A snake or dragon.","e":"Saint George fought the worm with all his strength."},{"m":"(countable) A worm is a type of dangerous software that can go across networks of computers."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To move like a worm; to wriggle in order to move.","e":"He wormed along the sand."}]}]},"window":{"h":"window","i":"/ˈwɪndəʊ/","a":"en-us-window.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A piece of glass in a wall to let people see through it.","e":"He looked out the window."}]}]},"cup":{"h":"cup","i":"/kʌp/","a":"en-us-cup.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cup is deep round container open at the top, normally used to drink out of.","e":"I'll bring you another cup of tea."},{"m":"(countable) A cup is a measurement of food or liquid for cooking and baking (about 237 milliliters).","e":"Add 2 cups of sugar."},{"m":"(countable) A cup is an award for the winner of a sports competition."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you put your hands together in a round bowl-shape, you cup your hands.","e":"Jean cupped her hands under the faucet to catch the water."}]}]},"lie":{"h":"lie","i":"/laɪ/","a":"en-us-lie.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Something not true, a falsehood, an untruth.","e":"I told a lie."}]}]},"tomorrow":{"h":"tomorrow","i":"/təˈmɒrəʊ/","a":"en-us-tomorrow.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Tomorrow is day after today.","e":"Tomorrow is my day off."},{"m":"Tomorrow is the future in general.","e":"The city of tomorrow will be much cleaner than cities now."},{"m":"(countable) Tomorrows are the days in the future.","e":"Let’s hope for a brighter tomorrow."}]}]},"preposition":{"h":"preposition","i":"/ˌprɛpəˈzɪʃən/","a":"en-us-preposition.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A preposition is a member of a group of words, or part of speech, that usually show where something happens. Typically a preposition is followed by a noun.","e":"In the sentence, \"I come from Canada,\" \"from\" is a preposition."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you preposition something, you place it in a location before some event occurs."}]}]},"albatross":{"h":"albatross","i":"/ˈæl.bəˌtrɒs/","a":"en-us-albatross.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A type of seabird that is usually found in the Southern Ocean and in the North Pacific, with a curved beak and long, thin wings.","e":"The albatross flew over the ocean."},{"m":"A long amount of time where one is continually worried."},{"m":"(golf) A double eagle, or three under par on any one hole."}]}]},"burden":{"h":"burden","i":"/ˈbɜːdn/","a":"en-us-burden.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Something heavy that you carry."},{"m":"A responsibility."},{"m":"Something that creates worry."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To weigh down."},{"m":"(transitive) To load."}]}]},"heavy":{"h":"heavy","i":"/ˈhɛvi/","a":"en-us-heavy.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Having a lot of weight.","e":"This suitcase is very heavy."},{"m":"Having a lot of seriousness."}]}]},"eagle":{"h":"eagle","i":"/'i:gəl/","a":"en-us-eagle.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A type of meat-eating bird.","e":"He saw an eagle perched on top of that tree."},{"m":"An old gold coin in the United States worth $10.","e":"He showed me his coin collection. He even had an old eagle."},{"m":"(golf) A score of two under par for a hole.","e":"I got a birdy and you got an eagle on that last hole."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you eagle a golf hole, you score two under par on it.","e":"I eagled the last hole with 3 strokes on a par 5."}]}]},"shop":{"h":"shop","i":"/ʃɒp/","a":"en-us-shop.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A place which sells things.","e":"He bought a hat from the shop."},{"m":"(countable) A place where things are made."},{"m":"(countable) An office"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you shop for something, you look for it in a store because you want to buy it.","e":"I need some new shoes, but I've been shopping for them for a week and I can't find any I like."}]}]},"golf":{"h":"golf","i":"/ɡɒlf/","a":"en-us-golf.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Golf is a game where a person uses a club to try to hit a ball into a hole with the fewest strokes.","e":"He played golf with a friend."},{"m":"Golf represents the letter G in the."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you golf, you play a game where a person uses a club to try to hit a ball into a hole with the fewest strokes."}]}]},"seabird":{"h":"seabird","i":"/ˈsiːbɜː(r)d/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-The Editor's Apprentice-seabird.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bird that is usually found at sea.","e":"The pelican is a seabird."}]}]},"sea":{"h":"sea","i":"/si/","a":"en-uk-sea.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A place with a large amount of salt water."}]}]},"skill":{"h":"skill","i":"/skɪl/","a":"en-us-skill.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Being able to do something well. Unlike abilities, skills must usually be learned.","e":"I go to a class every weekend to help me improve on my writing skills."}]}]},"heart":{"h":"heart","i":"/hɑːt/","a":"en-us-heart.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The part of the body that pumps blood.","e":"He has a problem with his heart."},{"m":"(countable) (symbolic) Where emotions are.","e":"You broke my heart."},{"m":"(countable) Center, core.","e":"We get to the heart of the problem."},{"m":"(uncountable) for others, compassion.","e":"He has a lot of heart."}]}]},"zebra":{"h":"zebra","i":"/ˈzɛbrə","a":"en-uk-zebra.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An animal that somewhat looks like a horse, but has black and white stripes.","e":"We saw zebras while we were in Africa."},{"m":"By extension, any black and white stripe pattern that looks like a zebra.","e":"I want to paint the room with zebra stripes."}]}]},"waiting":{"h":"waiting","i":"/ˈweɪtɪŋ/","a":"en-us-waiting.ogg","l":"wait","q":"verb"},"death":{"h":"death","i":"/dɛθ/","a":"en-us-death.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The end of life and existence.","e":"Death and destruction are a part of war."},{"m":"(uncountable) The state of being dead.","e":"She looked happy, even in death."},{"m":"The end of one's life and existence.","e":"The death of my wife was hard to accept."}]}]},"fork":{"h":"fork","i":"/fɔːk/","a":"en-us-fork.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An instrument for eating, with 3 or 4 sharp points called tines, all in the same direction.","e":"I ate with my fork."},{"m":"A place where one thing becomes two.","e":"She came to a fork in the road."},{"m":"(chess) A situation where two or more enemy pieces are in danger from the same piece.","e":"He moved his queen and caught me in a fork."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To split, become two.","e":"The road forks there."},{"m":"To move something with a fork.","e":"He forked food into his mouth."}]}]},"west":{"h":"west","i":"/wɛst/","a":"en-us-west.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The direction that the sun sets; from north, 90º to the left.","e":"He is from the west."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"One of the four compass directions: 270º clockwise from north. The sun sets in the west.","e":"England is west of France."}]}]},"identify":{"h":"identify","a":"en-us-identify.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you identify something, you say what it is.","e":"I showed him the picture and he identified the man as his brother."},{"m":"(transitive) If x identifies y, x makes it easy to know what y is."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you identify with someone else, you understand and share their feelings."},{"m":"(intransitive) If x is identified with y, it is closely connected to it."}]}]},"back":{"h":"back","i":"/ˈbæk/","a":"en-us-back.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Toward the rear.","e":"He went back behind the stands."},{"m":"To a place again.","e":"I didn't like it, so I sent it back."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The back is the rear part of something; it is the part in the other direction from the front.","e":"I went to the back of the house."},{"m":"(countable) The back is the rear part of the human body.","e":"He had a scar on his back."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you back something, you support it.","e":"The Republicans backed the bill."},{"m":"(transitive) If you back up, you move backward.","e":"He put the car in gear and backed right into the garage door."}]}]},"less":{"h":"less","i":"/lɛs/","a":"en-us-less.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"A smaller amount or degree.","e":"He does less of the work than she does."},{"m":"If you do x less than y, you do not do x as much as y.","e":"I read less than I used to. = \"reading now < reading before\""},{"m":"If you do something less often, easily, well, etc., you do not do it as often, easily, well, etc.","e":"I go out less often than before."},{"m":"If something is less likely, expensive, important, etc., it is not as likely, expensive, important, etc.","e":"This book is less expensive than that book. =\"the price of this book < the price of that book\""}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"minus","e":"Seven less four is three. (7-4=3)"}]}]},"beach":{"h":"beach","i":"/bit͡ʃ/","a":"en-us-beach.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A large area of sand (or very small stones), next to an area of water.","e":"People sometimes lie on beaches when they are on holiday, to get a suntan."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something is beached, it has run onto a beach or sandbar."}]}]},"trinitrotoluene":{"h":"trinitrotoluene","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-NaomiAmethyst-trinitrotoluene.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":", Trinitrotoluene is a yellow explosive material that is made up of crystals that are gotten through a reaction with nitric acid and toluene."}]}]},"can":{"h":"can","i":"/kæn/","a":"en-us-can.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If someone can do something, they are able to do it.","e":"Most birds can fly."},{"m":"(intransitive) If someone can do something, they are allowed to do it.","e":"You can't smoke here."},{"m":"You use can to ask somebody to do something (if you know the person well).","e":"Can you open the door for me, please?"},{"m":"If something can happen, it is possible.","e":"It's so small that it can't be seen."},{"m":"If someone tells you something can't happen, they think it's not a good idea.","e":"You just can't keep smoking."},{"m":"If something can happen, it happens sometimes.","e":"I can get really busy here on weekends."},{"m":"(transitive) If someone cans something, they put in a can or jar to keep for a long time.","e":"We canned the peas for the winter."},{"m":"(transitive) If someone cans something, they stop working on it.","e":"The idea was canned."},{"m":"(transitive) If someone gets canned they have lost their job."},{"m":"(transitive), If you tell someone to can it, you want them to stop talking.","e":"Can it, would you? I'm trying to watch TV."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A can is a metal container, usually for holding food or drink.","e":"I drink cola from a can."}]}]},"wash":{"h":"wash","i":"/wɒʃ/","a":"en-us-wash.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you wash something, you clean it with water.","e":"I wash my car every day."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The act of washing.","e":"He gave the dog a wash."},{"m":"The items for washing, before, after, or during the washing.","e":"He threw his dirty clothes in the wash."},{"m":"A failure.","e":"The program was a complete wash."},{"m":"With up: to be washed up is to be completely discouraged and burnt out.","e":"The Starcraft 2 servers were down and I was all washed up."}]}]},"trousers":{"h":"trousers","i":"/ˈtraʊzəz/","a":"en-us-trousers.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Trousers are worn over the lower body, with two legs.","e":"He put on his trousers."}]}]},"town":{"h":"town","i":"/taʊ̯n/","a":"en-us-town.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A small city.","e":"She went to a town called Beaverton."}]}]},"thunder":{"h":"thunder","i":"/ˈθʌn.də/","a":"en-us-thunder.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Thunder is the sound made by lightning.","e":"He heard thunder in the distance."},{"m":"Thunder is a loud sound.","e":"The thunder of the train was very loud."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To make a loud noise like thunder.","e":"The bowling ball thundered down the lane."}]}]},"thought":{"h":"thought","i":"/θɔːt/","a":"en-us-thought.ogg","l":"think","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) When you have a thought, you have an idea or concept in your mind.","e":"I have a thought about the answer to that problem."},{"m":"(uncountable).","e":"I will give your words some thought."}]}]},"strong":{"h":"strong","i":"/strɒŋ/","a":"en-us-strong.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Having big muscles; physically powerful.","e":"Arnold is very strong."},{"m":"Having a smell or flavor that is easy to notice.","e":"She wore strong perfume."},{"m":"Having a specified number of people or units.","e":"The enemy's army force was five thousand strong."}]}]},"strange":{"h":"strange","i":"/streɪndʒ/","a":"en-us-strange.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"or odd.","e":"My brother is so strange that he can turn his eyelids inside out."},{"m":"unknown.","e":"Gerald saw a strange car parked in his driveway."}]}]},"stiff":{"h":"stiff","i":"/stɪf/","a":"en-us-stiff.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is stiff, it is not able to be bent.","e":"My arm was very stiff this morning after bowling yesterday."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (informal) A dead body; a corpse.","e":"She went to the morgue and saw some stiffs."}]}]},"stick":{"h":"stick","i":"/stɪk/","a":"en-us-stick.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A piece of wood.","e":"Gerard picked up a stick."},{"m":"(countable) A long and thin piece of something.","e":"He gave her a stick of gum."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To attach.","e":"The food stuck to the pan."},{"m":"To put, to place.","e":"You stick your clothes in the dryer."}]}]},"spade":{"h":"spade","i":"/speɪd/","a":"en-us-spade.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A small tool used to dig.","e":"I took my spade to the garden."},{"m":"(countable) A suit in cards.","e":"He had three spades and two hearts."},{"m":"(countable) Spade is an extremely offensive word for a black person."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To dig using a [[#Noun|spade]].","e":"She will spade the garden."}]}]},"sharp":{"h":"sharp","i":"/ʃɑːp/","a":"en-us-sharp.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Having a cutting edge; not dull.","e":"He has a sharp knife."},{"m":"Intelligent or quick to learn.","e":"That girl is sharp."},{"m":"in flavor.","e":"That lemonade is sharp."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A blade, especially a sword used in fencing, with a sharp tip.","e":"Jesse preferred to practice with sharps."},{"m":"A sharp is a note that is one half step above the one that is named.","e":"The last note that she sang was a D sharp, not a C flat."}]}]},"run":{"h":"run","i":"/rʌn/","a":"en-us-run.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you run, you go quickly, with both feet off the ground at one time.","e":"I must run."},{"m":"If a machine runs, it works.","e":"The car runs well."},{"m":"If you run from someone or something, you try to get away from them.","e":"He ran from the cops."},{"m":"(transitive) If you run a place, you manage it.","e":"He ran the hotel together with his beloved wife."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A trip made by a runner; compare to walk.","e":"I’m going for a run."},{"m":"(baseball) A run in baseball is when a batter safely touches home plate."},{"m":"(cricket) A run in cricket is scored when the batsmen run between the two wickets."},{"m":"(theatre) An unbroken course of performances or showings.","e":"The musical had a long run on Broadway."}]}]},"of":{"h":"of","i":"/ɒv/","a":"en-us-of.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":".","e":"His name was Simon of Cyrene."},{"m":"Made using.","e":"It is a house of cards."},{"m":"ing to.","e":"Call the office of the school president."}]}]},"right":{"h":"right","i":"/ˈraɪt/","a":"en-uk-right.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is right, it is correct.","e":"You did the right thing."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"When something is to the right of a location, it means the direction 90º clockwise.","e":"He takes a right at the library."},{"m":"When you have the right for something, it means that it is an activity allowed by status.","e":"You have the right to remain silent."},{"m":"An action that is moral.","e":"Two wrongs don't make a right."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you turn something right, you turn it the right-side-up.","e":"He righted the boat."},{"m":"When you make something right, you correct it.","e":"He tried to right a wrong."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":".","e":"He does it right."},{"m":".","e":"I want to talk to you right now."},{"m":", in plain sight.","e":"But John, the letter is right there."},{"m":"In the direction 90º clockwise.","e":"She turned right."}]}]},"open":{"h":"open","i":"/ˈəʊ.pən/","a":"en-us-open.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To move something to the side to allow entrance.","e":"I will open the door for our guests."},{"m":"To prepare for business.","e":"She opened the store."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Having a hole or opening, not closed.","e":"The door was open."},{"m":"for business.","e":"The shop is open."},{"m":"Available for the public to see and change (of code).","e":"This software has open code because it was released under an open-source license."}]}]},"battery":{"h":"battery","i":"/ˈbætəri/","a":"en-uk-battery.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A battery is a device for storing or keeping electricity. Batteries are used to power flashlights, laptop computers, cell phones, and many other devices.","e":"I put a new battery in the flashlight."},{"m":"(countable) (artillery) A battery is a coordinated group of artillery weapons."},{"m":"(uncountable) Battery is the act of hitting or a person.","e":"My brother was sent to jail for assault and battery."}]}]},"flashlight":{"h":"flashlight","i":"/ˈflæʃˌlaɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-flashlight.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A flashlight is a device for making light. Flashlights are usually small and shaped like cylinders. The electricity for the flashlight often comes from a battery.","e":"It was getting dark, so he used his flashlight."}]}]},"cylinder":{"h":"cylinder","i":"/ˈsɪlɪndə(r)/","a":"en-us-cylinder.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cylinder is a shape consisting of two circles connected to a tube.","e":"s, pens, and flashlights are usually shaped like cylinders."}]}]},"because":{"h":"because","i":"/bɪˈkɒz/","a":"en-us-because.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"You use because to show the other reason for something.","e":"I bought the book because I wanted to read it."}]}]},"international":{"h":"international","i":"/ˌɪntəˈnæʃnəl/","a":"en-us-international.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"An international event, situation, idea, etc. includes two or more countries.","e":"In soccer news, France beat Japan in international competition."},{"m":"An international student is a student from country A studying in country B.","e":"The United States has more international students than any other country."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An international is a game or contest between two or more countries."}]}]},"attention":{"h":"attention","i":"/əˈtɛn.ʃən/","a":"en-us-attention.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) If you pay attention to something, you focus your mind on it.","e":"Pay attention to me when I'm speaking to you."}]}]},"education":{"h":"education","i":"/ɛdjuːkeɪʃn/","a":"en-us-education.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Someone gets an education if that person learns something or if somebody teaches that person something, usually at school.","e":"More and more people are starting work with a university education."}]}]},"abroad":{"h":"abroad","i":"/əˈbrɔːd/","a":"en-us-abroad.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If somebody goes abroad, they leave their home country and go to another country.","e":"They sent their children to school abroad."},{"m":"If somebody lives abroad, they live in another country.","e":"She spent four years abroad before returning to Brazil."}]}]},"bicycle":{"h":"bicycle","i":"/ˈbaɪsɪkl̩/","a":"en-us-bicycle.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bicycle is a vehicle with two wheels. You use your legs to make it move.","e":"I learned to ride a bicycle when I was six years old."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To travel or exercise using a bicycle."}]}]},"swim":{"h":"swim","i":"/swɪm/","a":"en-us-swim.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you swim, you move through the water using your arms and legs.","e":"Let's go swimming at the beach."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A swim is when someone swims.","e":"We all went for a swim in the lake."}]}]},"government":{"h":"government","i":"/ˈgʌvənmənt/","a":"en-us-government.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A government is a group of people who make the laws and control a country or other place.","e":"The local government announced a 5% cut in taxes."}]}]},"formal":{"h":"formal","i":"/ˈfɔrməl/","a":"en-us-formal.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is formal, it is official and/or public.","e":"He studied German on his own, but he has no formal language education."},{"m":"Formal behaviour or dress is used in polite situations.","e":"Please wear suit and tie because the restaurant is quite formal."}]}]},"pool":{"h":"pool","i":"/puːl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-pool.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pool is hole that holds water. Usually, it is for people to swim in.","e":"Our hotel had a large indoor pool."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To combine or to put together.","e":"Let's pool our money together to buy a gift for Mom."}]}]},"perfect":{"h":"perfect","i":"/ˈpɜːfɪkt/","a":"en-us-perfect-adj.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is perfect has no mistakes, problems, or damage.","e":"She answered him in perfect Japanese."},{"m":"Something that is perfect is exactly what was needed or wanted.","e":"\"Here's the knife.\" \"Oh, yes! Thanks, it's perfect.\""},{"m":"In a perfect tense, a verb is used for a situation that is finished before another point in time.","e":"I believe that in French the passe compose is equivalent to the present perfect tense in English."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you perfect something, you fix all its problems or make it as good as possible.","e":"Our leaders have perfected the art of sounding good while saying nothing."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The perfect is a verb tense used for a situation that is finished before another point in time.","e":"This verb should be in the present perfect."}]}]},"nice":{"h":"nice","i":"/naɪs/","a":"en-us-nice.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is nice, it's good and people probably like it.","e":"I didn't know him, but I hear he was a very nice man."}]}]},"fun":{"h":"fun","i":"/fʌn/","a":"en-us-fun.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) If you have fun, you enjoy something.","e":"Thanks! I had a lot of fun today. Let's do it again."},{"m":"(uncountable) If you do something for fun, you do it because you enjoy it.","e":"It's not my job; I just write Wiktionary articles for fun."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A fun activity, time, person, etc. is enjoyable.","e":"I really like soccer. It's such a fun game."}]}]},"custom":{"h":"custom","i":"/kʌstəm/","a":"en-us-custom.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A custom is an activity that happens traditionally or regularly.","e":"Almost everyone there eats rice every day, but there are different local customs about how to cook it."},{"m":"A custom is a long-established practice; considered as unwritten law.","e":"It was a custom in medieval times a woman could not marry without her parents consent."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A custom piece of clothing or other item is created for a specific person or use.","e":"He only wears custom suits, made to fit him perfectly."}]}]},"correct":{"h":"correct","i":"/kəˈrɛkt/","a":"en-us-correct.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is correct has no mistakes.","e":"For question #5, only 5 people got the correct answer."},{"m":"Something that is correct is right.","e":"When you type, the correct hand position is very important."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you correct something that is wrong, you make it right.","e":"I corrected the mistakes on your test."}]}]},"especially":{"h":"especially","i":"/ɛsˈpɛʃəli/","a":"en-us-especially.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"You use especially to say that something is special, or somehow different from others.","e":"Nobody was old, but Paulo was especially young."}]}]},"discussion":{"h":"discussion","i":"/dɪˈskʌʃən/","a":"en-us-discussion.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A discussion happens when two or more people share ideas about something, usually by talking.","e":"The company held detailed salary discussions with all employees."}]}]},"bus":{"h":"bus","i":"/ˈbʌs/","a":"en-us-bus.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bus is a vehicle that carries a large number of people on roads.","e":"He ran to catch the school bus, which had stopped at a corner to pick up more kids."},{"m":"(countable) A bus is part of a computer; it moves information."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you bus people somewhere, you take them there on a bus.","e":"The children are bused to school every morning."},{"m":"(transitive) If you bus tables, you take away dirty dishes in a restaurant."}]}]},"practise":{"h":"practise","i":"/ˈpræktɪs/","a":"En-us-practise.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you practise something, you do it again and again to improve your ability.","e":"The class was going to practise writing skills for homework."}]}]},"practice":{"h":"practice","i":"/ˈpræktɪs/","a":"en-us-practice.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you practice something, you do it again and again to improve your ability.","e":"The class was going to practice writing skills for homework."},{"m":"(transitive) If you practice a subject (specially law and medicine), you pursue it as a career.","e":"She practiced law for several years."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Practice is an activity you do again and again to improve your ability.","e":"I can go to the party because I have soccer practice that night."}]}]},"clothes":{"h":"clothes","i":"/kləʊðz/","a":"en-uk-clothes.ogg","l":"clothe","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Clothes, such as shirts, pants, socks, etc. are things that people wear on their body to cover it.","e":"He took off his clothes and got into the shower."}]}]},"title":{"h":"title","i":"/ˈtaɪ.təl/","a":"en-us-title.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The title of a book, movie, song, etc. is its name.","e":"\"I just finished the best book.\" \"Really, what's the title?\""},{"m":"(countable) A title is a word or name that describes a person's job or status.","e":"His title was Director of Science Education."},{"m":"A title is a legal document that proves you own something.","e":"He put the title to his house in a bank for safe keeping."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To give a title to someone or something.","e":"I titled my essay \"The History of Japan\"."}]}]},"informal":{"h":"informal","i":"/ɪnˈfɔːm(ə)l/","a":"en-us-informal.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is informal, it is friendly and casual; it is not official.","e":"Can we get together for some informal talks before the meeting?"}]}]},"advice":{"h":"advice","i":"/ədˈvaɪs/","a":"en-us-advice.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) If you give someone advice, you tell them what you think they should do.","e":"Thanks so much! I took your advice and it really helped me get the job."}]}]},"engineering":{"h":"engineering","i":"/ˌen.dʒɪˈnɪə.rɪŋ/","a":"en-us-engineering.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Engineering is a job or a science about designing and building things.","e":"She worked for a civil engineering company, that makes portable bridges."}]}]},"program":{"h":"program","i":"/ˈprəʊɡræm/","a":"en-us-program.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you program a computer, you use code to tell the computer what to do.","e":"The student can program the computer to calculate all of his statistics."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A program is a number of steps that are followed to reach a goal or end.","e":"His new exercise program gets more difficult every week."},{"m":"(countable) A program is a guide to a dramatic or theatrical performance.","e":"After he entered the theatre, he bought a copy of the program."},{"m":"(countable) A (television or radio) program is a broadcast.","e":"Star Trek is her favorite program."},{"m":"(countable) A (computer) program is the code that tells a computer what to do.","e":"Microsoft Word is one of the most popular programs in the world."}]}]},"programme":{"h":"programme","i":"/ˈprəʊɡræm/","a":"en-us-program.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you programme a computer, you use code to tell the computer what to do.","e":"The student can programme the computer to calculate all of his statistics."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A programme is a number of steps that are followed to reach a goal or end.","e":"His new exercise programme gets more difficult every week."},{"m":"(countable) A programme is a guide to a dramatic or theatrical performance.","e":"After he entered the theatre, he bought a copy of the programme."},{"m":"(countable) A (television or radio) programme is a broadcast.","e":"Star Trek is her favourite programme."},{"m":"(countable) A (computer) programme is the code that tells a computer what to do.","e":"Microsoft Word is one of the most popular programmes in the world."}]}]},"loan":{"h":"loan","i":"/ləʊn/","a":"en-us-loan.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A loan is money that you borrow and pay back later. Usually, you take a loan from a bank.","e":"We've almost finished paying off our car loan."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you loan someone something, you lend it to them.","e":"Please loan me your lawn mower."},{"m":"Loan in Hollywood studio speak means an actor is under contract to one studio and loaned to another studio to make one of their films.","e":"He was loaned to MGM to make MGM's newest movie."}]}]},"institution":{"h":"institution","i":"/ˌɪnstɪˈtjuːʃən/","a":"en-us-institution.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A custom or practice of a society or community.","e":"The institution of marriage is present in many cultures but its details vary widely across them."},{"m":"(countable) An institution is a large group of people who work together for a specific purpose. Examples include hospitals, universities, and banks.","e":"Banks, insurance companies and other financial institutions are already offering internet services."}]}]},"culture":{"h":"culture","i":"/ˈkʌlt͡ʃɚ/","a":"en-us-culture.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A culture is a common history, set of beliefs, or way of life within a group of people.","e":"Rock and roll is a central part of American popular culture."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you culture bacteria or cells, you grow them."}]}]},"facilities":{"h":"facilities","i":"/fəˈsɪlɪtiz/","a":"en-us-facilities.ogg","l":"facility","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The facilities in a building include the equipment, services, or places that are available.","e":"How much does it cost an employer to provide childcare facilities?"}]}]},"lecture":{"h":"lecture","i":"/ˈlɛk.t͡ʃə/","a":"en-us-lecture.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A lecture is a talk about a specific topic. Usually, it is a planned talk and it often lasts a long time.","e":"My teacher is giving a lecture on human rights tonight at the university."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you lecture someone, you teach them something."},{"m":"If you lecture someone, you scold them."}]}]},"academic":{"h":"academic","i":"/ˌækəˈdɛmɪk/","a":"en-us-academic.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"An academic topic, lecture, idea, etc., is one that is connected to education.","e":"The academic staff at the college generally don't teach during the summer."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An academic is a researcher or university teacher.","e":"The government has begun jailing journalists and banning academics from travel."},{"m":"Academics is the part of school related to learning.","e":"This class was strong in every aspect of their schooling, including academics, athletics and extracurricular activities."}]}]},"instructions":{"h":"instructions","a":"en-us-instructions.ogg","l":"instruction","q":"noun"},"instruction":{"h":"instruction","i":"/ɪnˈstrʌkʃən/","a":"en-us-instruction.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An instruction is a command or a step that helps you achieve a goal.","e":"Before he died, he gave the hospital instructions about how to deal with his body."},{"m":"The instructions that come with a new machine, computer, or product tell you how to use the product.","e":"I couldn't figure out how to set the temperature in the fridge, so I read the instructions."}]}]},"assign":{"h":"assign","i":"/əˈsaɪn/","a":"en-us-assign.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you assign a job to someone, you tell them to do it.","e":"That teacher always assigns too much homework."},{"m":"(transitive) To attribute or sort something into.","e":"No firm dates can be assigned to this emperor's life."}]}]},"fee":{"h":"fee","i":"/fi:/","a":"en-us-fee.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(usually plural) A fee is the money you pay for some kinds of services, such as legal advice, education, or club membership.","e":"School fees have increased again this year."},{"m":"(countable) An inheritable estate in land held of a feudal lord in return for certain services.","e":"He held his lands in fee of the Earl of Chester."}]}]},"computer":{"h":"computer","i":"/kəmˈpjuːtə/","a":"en-us-computer.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A computer is a machine that helps you store, organize, and use information.","e":"If you're looking at a web page, you must be using a computer."},{"m":"(countable) A computer is a person whose job is doing computations."}]}]},"similar":{"h":"similar","i":"/ˈsɪmələ/","a":"en-us-similar.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If two things are similar, they are almost the same, or the same in many, but not all, ways.","e":"Canadian English is similar to American English, but there are some small differences in pronunciation, and spelling."},{"m":"If two shapes are similar, they have the same shape, but might be different sizes.","e":"These two triangles are similar because they have the same angles, but they are not congruent because one is bigger than the other."}]}]},"definition":{"h":"definition","i":"/ˌdɛfɪˈnɪʃən/","a":"en-us-definition.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A definition is an explanation of the meaning of a word.","e":"The sentence before this one is a definition."}]}]},"relaxed":{"h":"relaxed","i":"/rɪˈlækst/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-relaxed.wav","l":"relax","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is relaxed, they feel calm, they are not worried, and their muscles are not tight.","e":"I feel most relaxed when I'm fishing."}]}]},"style":{"h":"style","i":"/staɪl/","a":"en-us-style.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A style is a specific look, design, or way of dressing or acting.","e":"I don't understand why the styles in fashion magazines are always changing."},{"m":"A style is a traditional or legal term referring to a person who holds a title or post.","e":"He styled himself the Count of Monte Cristo."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you style something, you design and make it appear in a certain way."}]}]},"require":{"h":"require","i":"/rɪˈkwaɪə/","a":"en-us-require.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you require something, you need it.","e":"The job requires high level of math skills."},{"m":"(transitive) If you are required to do something, you have to do it.","e":"All men over the age of 21 are required to report to the army for service."}]}]},"structure":{"h":"structure","i":"/ˈstrʌktʃə(r)/","a":"en-us-structure.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The structure of something is the way that it is put together.","e":"The structure of her writing makes it very easy to understand."},{"m":"(countable) A structure is something that has been built or put together, especially something big, such as a building.","e":"The CN tower is the tallest structure in Toronto."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you structure something in a particular way, you organise or build it that way.","e":"Prepare a list of questions to structure the interview."}]}]},"technology":{"h":"technology","i":"/tɛkˈnɒlədʒi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-technology.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Technology is the tools, equipment, and activities that come from scientific knowledge.","e":"Modern technology such as computers, robots, and wireless communications, can reduce the cost of doing business. (can make the cost smaller.)"}]}]},"doctor":{"h":"doctor","i":"/ˈdɒktə/","a":"en-us-doctor.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A person who helps people who are sick, and looks after their health."},{"m":"(countable) A person who can work very well about a particular thing and is given the title Doctor by a university, for example a doctor in psychology could be called Doctor John Smith."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you doctor someone, you act as a medical doctor towards them."},{"m":"(transitive) If you doctor something or someone, you change them."}]}]},"grade":{"h":"grade","i":"/ɡreɪd/","a":"en-us-grade.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A grade is a letter or number that you use to show how good something is. Usually, teachers use it to show how good a student's test or assignment is.","e":"He got 97% on his test. It was the top grade in the class."},{"m":"In North American English, a grade is the school year.","e":"Most Canadian children start grade one when they are six years old and finish grade 12 when they are 18."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you grade something, you judge how good it is.","e":"After the final exam, the teacher spent the whole weekend grading papers."}]}]},"resource":{"h":"resource","i":"/rɪˈzɔɚs/","a":"en-ca-resource.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(usually plural) A resource is something that is available and useful.","e":"We don't have enough time and resources to finish the job."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you resource something, you source it again."}]}]},"migration":{"h":"migration","i":"/maɪgˈreɪʃǝn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-migration.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A migration is a large movement, usually of people or animals, to a new living place.","e":"Every fall, the birds begin their migration from the cold northern areas to the southern regions where they will spend the winter."}]}]},"transport":{"h":"transport","i":"/trænzˈpɔːt/","a":"en-us-transport-verb.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Transport refers to how things are moved, or a system of transportation.","e":"I prefer my own means of transport."},{"m":"(countable) A transport is a vehicle or vessel used to move things or people.","e":"On Tatooine, C-3PO thought he saw a transport in the distance."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you transport something, you carry it from one place to another, usually on a truck, boat, or other large vehicle.","e":"One of the most important parts of doing business is transporting your materials from the factory to the shop."}]}]},"transportation":{"h":"transportation","i":"/trænspɔːˈteɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Wodencafe-transportation.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Transportation is the system or vehicles used to move people or things from one place to another.","e":"In most of Canada, the main form of transportation is the family car."}]}]},"community":{"h":"community","i":"/k(ə)ˈmjunəti/","a":"en-us-community.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A community is a group of people living in the same area and having a similar background or similar interests.","e":"Most Libyan policemen were members of the community where they worked."}]}]},"vary":{"h":"vary","i":"/ˈvɛəri/","a":"en-us-ne-vary.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something varies, it is not always the same.","e":"The summer temperature in Toronto can vary from 12 degrees at night to over 30 degrees during the day."}]}]},"equipment":{"h":"equipment","i":"/ɪ'kwɪpmənt/","a":"en-us-equipment.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Your equipment is the things that you use to do a job or sport.","e":"Soccer is a popular game because you need very little equipment to play--just a ball and an open space."}]}]},"create":{"h":"create","i":"/kriːeɪt/","a":"en-us-create.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you create something, you make or invent it. Usually, it's something that nobody has made before.","e":"Wiktionary editors create Wiktionary entries."}]}]},"legal":{"h":"legal","i":"/liːɡl/","a":"en-us-legal.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If an activity is legal it does not break any laws.","e":"In Canada, it is perfectly legal for a woman to walk down the street with no shirt on."},{"m":"A legal problem, action, fee, etc. is related to the law or lawyers.","e":"After losing the court case, he had to pay over $30,000 in legal fees."}]}]},"job":{"h":"job","i":"/dʒɒb/","a":"en-us-job.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A job is an activity that you do, usually, regularly and for pay.","e":"She got a good job as a manager in a book store."},{"m":"(countable) A job is a task that a computer performs."},{"m":"(countable) A job is a plastic surgery that is done on someone. Usually used with another word to form a noun.","e":"John just had a nose job."}]}]},"finally":{"h":"finally","i":"/ˈfaɪnəli/","a":"en-us-finally.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something finally happens, it means there was a long wait before it happened.","e":"I finally finished university. Now, I can start my real life."},{"m":"Finally is used, often at the beginning of a sentence, to show that this is the last thing or idea.","e":"First, I think that we should use less. Second, I think we should reuse the things that we have. And, finally, I think we should recycle more."}]}]},"technical":{"h":"technical","i":"/ˈtɛk.nɪk.əl/","a":"en-us-technical.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Technical problems, writing, or skills, are related to special knowledge that most people don't have.","e":"Doctors use a lot of technical vocabulary. I wish they would explain things more easily."}]}]},"aid":{"h":"aid","i":"/eɪl/","a":"en-us-aid.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Aid is the help that is given to people, usually by a government or institution.","e":"After the flood the UN sent $500 million of aid in the form of food, water, tents, and medical supplies."},{"m":"(countable) An aid is a person or thing that helps you do an activity.","e":"The president's aid spoke to the newspapers today."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you aid someone, you help them."}]}]},"formally":{"h":"formally","i":"/ˈfɔrməli/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-formally.wav","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If you do something formally, you do it in a formal way.","e":"They expect you to formally behave yourself. If not, I doubt you will get the job."}]}]},"grant":{"h":"grant","i":"/grɑːnt/","a":"en-us-grant.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you grant something to something, you give it to them, usually formally.","e":"The school has granted us permission to use a classroom in the evenings."},{"m":"(transitive) If you grant something, you accept that it is true.","e":"Yes, I'll grant you that the data is old, but I still think it's useful."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A grant is something, usually money, that is given to someone, usually by a government or institution.","e":"The professor received a research grant to study weather changes."}]}]},"milk":{"h":"milk","i":"/mɪɫk/","a":"en-us-milk.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Milk is a white liquid some animals make for their babies to drink. People often drink cow's milk.","e":"The boy had some fresh goat milk."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you milk an animal like a cow or a goat, you take the milk out of it."}]}]},"warm":{"h":"warm","i":"/wɔːm/","a":"en-us-warm.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is warm, it is a nice temperature between cool and hot.","e":"It's good to come into a nice warm house on a winter's day."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you warm something, you increase the temperature.","e":"At 7:30, the sun came up and warmed them a little."}]}]},"during":{"h":"during","i":"/ˈdjʊərɪŋ/","a":"en-us-during.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If you do something during something else, you do it at the same time."}]}]},"cool":{"h":"cool","i":"/kuːl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-cool.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is cool, its temperature is between warm and cold.","e":"It's hard to keep the house nice and cool on a hot summer's day."},{"m":"If you say something is cool you mean it is good and you like it.","e":"That's a really cool cell phone! Where did you get it?"},{"m":"Someone who is cool is admired by others, someone of notably high social status.","e":"Jeffrey is the coolest guy in town."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you cool something, you decrease the temperature.","e":"Blow on the coffee to cool it off."},{"m":"If something cools, its temperature decreases.","e":"The soup was too hot, so he waited for it to cool a little."}]}]},"health":{"h":"health","i":"/hɛlθ/","a":"en-us-health.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) If you talk about the health of a person or animal, you are talking about whether they are sick or not.","e":"The doctors believe that the disease will not be a serious danger to public health."},{"m":"(uncountable) If you have health you are not sick (do not have disease) and are not hurt."}]}]},"temperature":{"h":"temperature","i":"/ˈtɛmp(ə)rətʃə(r)/","a":"en-us-temperature.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The temperature of something is how hot or cold it is.","e":"Today's temperature is 25°C."}]}]},"ocean":{"h":"ocean","i":"/ˈəʊ.ʃən/","a":"en-us-ocean.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An ocean is a large area of salt water.","e":"My great grandfather came across the Atlantic ocean from Scotland to Canada in 1882 on a sailing ship."}]}]},"damage":{"h":"damage","i":"/ˈdæmədʒ/","a":"en-us-damage.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Damaged means hurt or broken.","e":"Their car hit a truck, but luckily there was very little damage to the car."},{"m":"If A owes damages to B, A has to pay money because A hurt B or B's property.","e":"The reason his car hit another car was that he did something wrong, so he had to pay damages to the owner of the other car."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) Damages means to hurt or break.","e":"All those cigarettes have damaged her health."}]}]},"flood":{"h":"flood","i":"/flʌd/","a":"en-us-flood.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A flood happens when there has been a lot of rain in a short time and the water covers the ground.","e":"The storm brought heavy rains, and the resulting flood caused $14 million in damage to crops."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If a place is flooded, the water covers the ground and often causes a lot of damage.","e":"In 2005, a hurricane brought so much rain that much of Louisiana was flooded, killing many people, and destroying large parts of the city."},{"m":"To flood means to overwhelm.","e":"The market has been flooded with boy band recordings."}]}]},"storm":{"h":"storm","i":"/stɔːm/","a":"en-us-storm.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A storm is bad weather with high winds that disturbs the atmosphere.","e":"Small boats should stay off the water tonight because we are expecting a storm."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you storm, you move fast and noisily like a storm, usually when angered."},{"m":"If you storm a building or other fortification, you assault it with military troops.","e":"The sergeant and his platoon stormed the stronghold of the most wanted terrorist."}]}]},"slowly":{"h":"slowly","i":"/ˈsləʊli/","a":"en-us-slowly.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"When something moves slowly or does something slowly, it takes a very long time to do it.","e":"She was very tired, and walked slowly up the stairs to bed."}]}]},"probably":{"h":"probably","i":"/ˈprɒbəbli/","a":"en-us-probably.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something is probably true, or will probably happen, it means there is a high chance of it.","e":"I'm not sure what I'm doing tonight, but I'll probably stay home and study."}]}]},"subject":{"h":"subject","i":"/ˈsʌb.dʒɛkt/","a":"en-us-subject-noun.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A subject is a branch of knowledge in school, college or university, such as English, math, science, and history.","e":"The subject of the class is English literature."},{"m":"(countable) In English grammar, the subject of a sentence is usually a noun that comes before the verb. This noun is usually the thing that is doing the action, and it is usually the topic of the sentence.","e":"In the sentence, \"Tom gave the box to Wilma\", Tom is the subject."},{"m":"(countable) A subject is a person who is governed by a king, queen, emperor, etc."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone or something is subject to something, they are likely to be affected by it or experience it.","e":"Home prices are even more subject to change than gas prices."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To make someone do something unpleasant","e":"They were subjected to intense labor."}]}]},"her":{"h":"her","i":"/hɜː/","a":"en-us-her.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"You use her instead of the name of a person, to talk about a woman or girl. (used in the object position, never as a subject)","e":"This is Susan's book. Give it to her."},{"m":"If you say something is her thing, you mean it belongs to a particular woman or girl.","e":"It is her book, not mine,"}]}]},"object":{"h":"object","i":"/ˈɒbdʒekt/","a":"en-us-object-noun.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An object is a thing that you can touch, but it is not alive.","e":"We don't know what killed him, but it was a smooth, heavy object."},{"m":"(countable) The object of an action or plan is the goal or the reason for it.","e":"The object of soccer is to kick the ball into the other team's net."},{"m":"The object is a type of complement in a verb phrase or preposition phrase with the form of a noun phrase.","e":"In the sentence Yoko ate the bread, the bread is the object."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you object to something, you don't agree with it.","e":"Most people will object to being asked to work too much."}]}]},"suddenly":{"h":"suddenly","i":"/ˈsʌdn̩li/","a":"en-us-suddenly.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something happens suddenly, it happens very quickly when you don't expect it to happen.","e":"My son had been sitting in the chair beside me. Then, suddenly, I realised he was gone."}]}]},"lung":{"h":"lung","i":"/ˈlʌŋ/","a":"en-us-lung.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(usually plural) Your lungs are part of your body that is inside your chest. Your lungs allow you to breathe.","e":"Smoking for many years had damaged his lungs."}]}]},"tired":{"h":"tired","i":"/taɪə(r)d/","a":"en-us-tired.ogg","l":"tire","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you feel tired, you have no energy and you need a rest.","e":"After walking for 15&nbsp;km, I was so tired, that I couldn't take another step."}]}]},"electric":{"h":"electric","i":"/ɪˈlɛktrɪk/","a":"en-us-electric.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is electric, it uses electricity.","e":"My grandmother wrote her letters on a typewriter; my mother used an electric typewriter, and I use a computer."}]}]},"balance":{"h":"balance","i":"/ˈbæləns/","a":"en-us-balance.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) If something is in balance, it has equal amounts all around.","e":"She was walking on a thin line, but lost her balance and fell down."},{"m":"The balance in your bank account is the amount of money you have in the account."},{"m":"A type of scale where there are two parts."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you balance something, you make it have equal amounts all around.","e":"The bird balanced easily on the wire for a few moments before flying off."}]}]},"wet":{"h":"wet","i":"/wɛt/","a":"en-us-wet.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is wet it has some water or other liquid on it.","e":"I got completely wet in the rain."},{"m":"If a female is wet, she is sexually aroused and the vulva is moistened with vaginal secretions."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you wet something, you put water or some other liquid on it.","e":"Please try not to wet the bathroom floor when you have a shower."}]}]},"prefer":{"h":"prefer","i":"/prɪˈfɝ/","a":"en-us-prefer.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you prefer something, you like it more than another thing.","e":"Sometimes I eat in restaurants, but I prefer to cook."}]}]},"typical":{"h":"typical","i":"/ˈtɪpɪkl̩/","a":"en-us-typical.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is typical, it is normal, and not special. It's what you would expect.","e":"This rain isn't typical. We almost never get rain at this time of year."}]}]},"brain":{"h":"brain","i":"/breɪn/","a":"en-us-brain.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Your brain is the part of your body that is inside your head.","e":"The brain is the part of the body that thinks and controls the rest of the body through the nervous system."}]}]},"sick":{"h":"sick","i":"/sɪk/","a":"en-us-sick.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a person, animal, or plant is sick, it has a disease and is not healthy.","e":"I'm sorry, I'm too sick to go to work today."},{"m":"A way of saying something is bad. (Could mean one or both of the following.)"},{"m":"You say this about something that is cool. That is, something you like or see as very good.","e":"That song is sick!"}]}]},"feet":{"h":"feet","i":"/fiːt/","a":"en-us-feet.ogg","l":"foot","q":"noun"},"worse":{"h":"worse","i":"/wɜːs/","a":"en-us-worse.ogg","l":"bad","q":"adjective"},"park":{"h":"park","i":"/pɑrk/","a":"en-us-park.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A park is an outdoor area where people can relax and play.","e":"We sat under the trees and had lunch in Central Park."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you park a car or other vehicle, you drive it to a place and let it stand there.","e":"She never parks her car under a tree."}]}]},"breath":{"h":"breath","i":"/breθ/","a":"en-us-breath.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Your breath is the air that you move into and out of your lungs.","e":"After running for just a minute, his breath was coming quickly."},{"m":"(countable) A breath is the air that you move into and out of your lungs one time.","e":"Take a big breath and put your face in the water."}]}]},"global":{"h":"global","i":"/ˈgləʊbəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-global.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is global it includes the whole world.","e":"The weather is changing, and this is not just in one or two places. The change is global."}]}]},"period":{"h":"period","i":"/ˈpɪərɪəd/","a":"en-us-period.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A period is a length of time.","e":"There was a short period when my computer stopped working."},{"m":"A period is the dot that marks the end of most sentences in English. This ->. is a period.","e":"Should I use an exclamation mark or a period at the end of this sentence?"},{"m":"A woman's period is the time each month when she passes blood.","e":"I have missed two periods now. I think I must be pregnant."}]},{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"And nothing else; and nothing less; used for emphasis.","e":"When I say \"eat your dinner,\" it means \"eat your dinner\", period!"}]}]},"region":{"h":"region","i":"/riːʤn̩/","a":"en-us-region.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A region is an area of land or of the body.","e":"The fishing problems have been happening only in the Atlantic coast region."},{"m":"(countable) A region is any connected part of a space or surface. This definition is useful in geometry.","e":"In Euclidean space, a convex set is a region which has a geometric definition."}]}]},"area":{"h":"area","i":"/ˈɛə.rɪ.ə/","a":"en-us-area.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An area is a piece of land or space.","e":"This is the business area of town."},{"m":"(countable) An area of study is a special subject, such as mathematics, grammar, music, or biology.","e":"Economics is quite interesting, but my area is more related to politics."},{"m":"(countable) The area of a surface, is the size of the surface.","e":"The length is 10&nbsp;cm and the width is 5&nbsp;cm, so the area is 50 cm^2."}]}]},"men":{"h":"men","i":"/mɛn/","a":"en-us-men.ogg","l":"man","q":"noun"},"contrast":{"h":"contrast","i":"/ˈkɒntrɑːst/","a":"en-us-contrast.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Contrasts are the differences you find when you compare something or someone.","e":"When comparing English and Japanese, there are many contrasts but also a large number of similarities."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you contrast two things, you look for or explain the differences between them.","e":"It's difficult not to contrast the good things he says with the terrible way he acts."}]}]},"research":{"h":"research","i":"/rɪˈsɜːtʃ/","a":"en-us-research.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Research is the process or result of trying to find an answer by reading, interviewing, watching, or doing experiments.","e":"The last 10 years has provided a huge amount of research into a cure for cancer."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you research a question, you try to find an answer, usually by reading a lot about it, or by doing experiments.","e":"I have to research the history of King Henry II for my English class."}]}]},"depression":{"h":"depression","i":"/dɪˈprɛʃən/","a":"en-us-depression.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"If someone has depression, they have a condition which makes them very sad and makes it very hard for them to imagine being happy later.","e":"After Suzie's dog passed away, she fell into a depression for six months."},{"m":"A depression is when a person's feelings are very sad and unhappy.","e":"John had a small depression after he lost the tennis match, but in two weeks he was back to normal."},{"m":"(countable) A depression is a low point on a surface.","e":"There was a small depression in the ground where the rock had been."},{"m":"A depression is when the economy slows down by a lot.","e":"The business community is worried that the oil problems could lead to a depression."}]}]},"affect":{"h":"affect","i":"/ə'fɛkt/","a":"en-uk-affect.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If x affects y, then x causes a change in y.","e":"The movement of the soccer ball was affected by the wind."},{"m":"(transitive) If you affect a way of speaking, walking, dressing, etc., you pretend that it is your normal way, often to impress people.","e":"\"No, ma'm,\" Robert said, affecting a southern accent."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Your affect is the emotion or feeling you have in response to an idea, object, etc.","e":"Actors need to bring out the affect of the scene."},{"m":"(uncountable) Affect is emotion or emotional response.","e":"When teaching, we need to consider both ideas and affect."}]}]},"physical":{"h":"physical","i":"/ˈfɪzɪkəl/","a":"en-us-physical.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A physical thing or activity is related to the body, or something you can touch.","e":"The war didn't leave him with any physical injuries, but his mind was badly damaged."}]}]},"major":{"h":"major","i":"/ˈmeɪʤɚ/","a":"en-us-major.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"(countable) A major change, problem, event, etc. is a big and important one.","e":"We expected the change to cause a lot of problems, but in the end it wasn't as major as we had thought."},{"m":"A major musical scale is the usual scale for music in western culture. The major scale starts two notes above the minor and more often sounds happy.","e":"That music could be D minor or F major."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A major is a subject area that is the main study of a student at a college or university.","e":"My major is Speech-Language Pathology, which is about problems people may have with talking."},{"m":"(countable) A major is a military rank between captain and lieutenant-colonel."},{"m":"(countable) A major is a person of the legal age of majority."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you major in something, you concentrate on a single area of study as a student at a college or university.","e":"My mother majored in English but I will major in psychology."}]}]},"crush":{"h":"crush","i":"/krʌʃ/","a":"en-us-crush.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To damage something by flattening it.","e":"I will crush the spider with a book."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"If you have a crush on someone, you like them and want to date them. This could be because you think they are attractive.","e":"I've got a crush on Joey, but you can't tell anyone."},{"m":"The person you have a crush on is called a crush.","e":"Cindy was my boyhood crush."}]}]},"me":{"h":"me","i":"/miː/","a":"en-us-me.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"You use me instead of your name, to refer to yourself.","e":"This is my book. It belongs to me."}]}]},"response":{"h":"response","i":"/rɪˈspɒns/","a":"en-us-response.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A response is some words or actions that happen as a reaction to something else.","e":"We sent a message to them two weeks ago, but there has been no response so far."}]}]},"contact":{"h":"contact","i":"/ˈkɑntækt/","a":"en-us-contact.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"When x makes or has contact with y, they touch each other physically.","e":"The trains in Tokyo are so crowded that everyone has to stand in close contact to everyone else."},{"m":"By extension, its use as a metaphor:","e":"He wore dark glasses so that he wouldn't have to make eye contact with anyone."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If A contacts B, A telephones B or writes a letter or e-mail to B.","e":"If I can help further please do not hesitate to contact me at 012-345-6789."}]}]},"meal":{"h":"meal","i":"/miːl/","a":"en-us-meal.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A meal is the food you eat at regular times of the day., lunch, supper and dinner, are meals.","e":"Thanks for dinner! I haven't had a good Italian meal like that for a long time."},{"m":"The edible part of certain grains; it is often used to feed animals."}]}]},"meat":{"h":"meat","i":"/miːt/","a":"en-us-meat.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Meat is the muscle of animals that we eat., chicken, and pork are kinds of meat.","e":"I am a vegetarian. I don't eat meat, only fruits, grains, and vegetables."},{"m":"(countable) A type of meat."}]}]},"dish":{"h":"dish","i":"/dɪʃ/","a":"en-us-dish.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Dishes are the flat round holder for food that we usually put on the table and eat off of.","e":"There was a crash when the waiter dropped his tray of dishes on the floor."},{"m":"(countable) A dish is a particular kind of cooked or prepared food.","e":"Last night she made a wonderful Indian dish that I had never eaten before."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(informal) To dish is to gossip about something or somebody."}]}]},"chicken":{"h":"chicken","i":"/'tʃɪk.ɪn/","a":"en-us-chicken.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A chicken is a bird that farmers raise for meat and eggs.","e":"My father went out back, caught a chicken, cut off its head, and cleaned it for dinner."},{"m":"(uncountable) Chicken is the meat of a chicken.","e":"They make a very tasty fried chicken dish here that comes with vegetables and potatoes."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Someone who is afraid to do something is chicken.","e":"You won't jump your bike because you're chicken."}]}]},"restaurant":{"h":"restaurant","i":"/rɛstərɒnt/","a":"en-uk-a restaurant.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A restaurant is a place where you can buy and eat food and drinks.","e":"My wife and I went out to a small French restaurant in Toronto for dinner."}]}]},"fry":{"h":"fry","i":"/fraɪ/","a":"en-us-fry.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you fry something, you cook it in a pan on a stove with hot oil.","e":"Do you think we should fry the eggs or boil them?"}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A fry is a young fish."},{"m":"(countable) A fry is a single french fry.","e":"Pass me a fry, I want to see if they taste good."}]}]},"fried":{"h":"fried","i":"/fraɪd/","a":"en-us-fried.ogg","l":"fry","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Fried food is food that has been cooked in a pan with hot oil.","e":"I don't like fried chicken. It's too oily."}]}]},"habit":{"h":"habit","i":"/ˈhæbɪt/","a":"en-us-habit.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A habit is something that you do regularly.","e":"John, don't bite your fingernails. It's a bad habit."},{"m":"(countable) A habit is what people in certain jobs wear, generally religious jobs. These people can be recognized by their habits.","e":"The monk's habit was black."},{"m":"A habit is the form of growth of a plant or, sometimes, an animal.","e":"Some corals grow with a branching habit."}]}]},"mineral":{"h":"mineral","i":"/ˈmɪ.nər.əl/","a":"en-us-mineral.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mineral is a substance in the earth such as calcium, salt, iron, etc.","e":"The rocks in this area are rich in minerals."}]}]},"convenient":{"h":"convenient","i":"/kənˈviːniənt/","a":"en-us-convenient.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is convenient, you can get it or use it quickly and easily.","e":"Living here is so convenient. There's a supermarket right across the street, and a train station just a 2 minute walk away."}]}]},"quickly":{"h":"quickly","i":"/ˈkwɪkli/","a":"en-us-quickly.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If you do something quickly or something happens quickly, it happens in a very short time.","e":"Please close the door quickly. You'll let the cat out."}]}]},"sauce":{"h":"sauce","i":"/sɔːs/","a":"en-us-sauce.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sauce is a thick liquid that you put on food to give it a special taste.","e":"I put the chicken in a special sauce for two hours before I cook it."}]}]},"dinner":{"h":"dinner","i":"/ˈdɪnə/","a":"en-us-dinner.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Dinner is the largest meal of the day, usually eaten in the evening.","e":"I'm sorry, I'll be late tonight, so I won't be home for dinner."}]}]},"rice":{"h":"rice","i":"/raɪs/","a":"en-us-rice.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Rice is a white or brown grain that people boil and eat.","e":"In many Asian countries, including Japan, China, and Thailand, they eat rice with almost every meal."}]}]},"fruit":{"h":"fruit","i":"/fruːt/","a":"en-us-fruit.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The fruit is the part of a plant or tree that holds the seeds. It's usually sweet and good to eat.","e":"Most people don't eat enough fruit and vegetables."},{"m":"(countable) A homosexual or effeminate man."}]}]},"cheese":{"h":"cheese","i":"/t͡ʃiːz/","a":"en-us-cheese.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Cheese is a food that is made by mixing bacteria with milk and aging it.","e":"I often eat cheese with bread and grapes."}]}]},"grain":{"h":"grain","i":"/greɪn/","a":"en-us-grain.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A grain is a seed that people eat, such as wheat, rice, corn, etc.","e":"Most North Americans get their grains from bread and pasta."},{"m":"(countable) A grain is any very small piece of something, such as sand, salt, sugar, etc.","e":"One grain of salt is almost too small to see."}]}]},"wait":{"h":"wait","i":"/weɪt/","a":"en-us-wait.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you wait for someone or something, you do something (or nothing) until something else happens.","e":"I waited for you for twenty minutes. Where were you?"},{"m":"To wait is to take orders and serve food at the tables in cafes and restaurants.","e":"Her job at the cafe was to wait at the tables."}]}]},"plural":{"h":"plural","i":"/ˈplʊə.rəl/","a":"en-us-plural.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a noun is plural in English grammar, it refers to other than one thing.","e":"If I say, \"one cat\", that's singular, but if I say, \"a lot of cats\", that's plural."},{"m":"A plural person is someone with."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The form of a word that normally refers to other than one thing.","e":"The plural of the word \"dog\" is \"dogs.\""}]}]},"singular":{"h":"singular","i":"/ˈsɪŋɡjəlɚ/","a":"en-us-singular.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a noun is singular in English grammar, it usually refers to only one thing.","e":"If I say, \"one cat\", that's singular, but if I say, \"a lot of cats\", that's plural."},{"m":"If something is singular, then it is unique.","e":"The singular appearance of the man caught his attention."}]}]},"lungs":{"h":"lungs","a":"en-us-lungs.ogg","l":"lung","q":"noun"},"sex":{"h":"sex","i":"/sɛks/","a":"en-us-sex.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Sex is an act done by a male and a female (in this case there is sometimes an intent to make babies) or with just two men or women.","e":"Most men in our survey say they definitely would not have sex with a new partner without using a condom."},{"m":"(countable) A person or animal's sex is male, female, or both.","e":"She had not had any male friends during her early life and now found it difficult to talk to members of the opposite sex."}]}]},"butter":{"h":"butter","i":"/ˈbʌtə/","a":"en-uk-butter.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Butter is a firm yellow substance that is made from milk spread on bread or used in cooking.","e":"Please pass the butter."},{"m":"(uncountable) A bread and butter issue, is a basic and important one.","e":"If we want to win this election, we need to focus on bread and butter issues like jobs."},{"m":"(uncountable) Your bread and butter is the work that you do most and that earns you the most money.","e":"Fixing shoes used to be our bread and butter, but today, nobody gets their shoes fixed."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you butter something, you put [[#Noun|butter]] on it.","e":"Would you like me to butter your toast for you?"}]}]},"wolf":{"h":"wolf","i":"/ˈwʊlf/","a":"en-us-wolf.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A wolf is a wild animal, similar to a dog."}]}]},"chain":{"h":"chain","i":"/'ʧe:jn/","a":"en-us-chain.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A chain is a series of round pieces of material joined together to make a line.","e":"He got her a gold chain necklace for her birthday."},{"m":"A series of interconnected things.","e":"This led to an unfortunate chain of events."},{"m":"(countable) A chain of stores is a group of stores that all have the same name, such as McDonald's restaurants or GAP clothing stores."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you chain things together, you connect them in a line."},{"m":"If you chain A to B, you connect A to B with a chain.","e":"The dog was chained to the tree."}]}]},"amusement":{"h":"amusement","i":"/əˈmjuzmənt/","a":"en-us-amusement.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Amusement is the feeling you have when something is fun or funny or makes you laugh."},{"m":"(countable) An amusement is something that gets your attention and that you like; something like playing; something that is good but not useful.","e":"Movies, video games and toys are amusements."}]}]},"attraction":{"h":"attraction","i":"/əˈtrækʃən/","a":"en-us-attraction.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An attraction is a force that pulls two things together.","e":"s have an attraction to metal."},{"m":"(countable) An attraction is a popular feature at an event or site.","e":"Elephants and lions are major attractions at many zoos."},{"m":"Something that causes interest, pleasure, or liking for someone are something.","e":"she has romantic ideas about sexual attraction"}]}]},"offer":{"h":"offer","i":"/ˈɒfə(r)/","a":"en-us-offer.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An offer is when you say you will do something or give something.","e":"He wanted to buy my car, so he made me an offer of $5000."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If I offer something to you, that means I will give it to you if you want."},{"m":"If I offer to do something for you, that means I will do it for you if you want."}]}]},"pencil":{"h":"pencil","i":"/pɛnsəl/","a":"en-us-pencil.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pencil is used for writing on paper. It is made of wood, and has a pencil \"lead\" that goes through the middle."}]}]},"wood":{"h":"wood","i":"/wʊd/","a":"en-au-wood.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Wood is what trees are made of. People use wood to build things like houses and furniture."}]}]},"house":{"h":"house","i":"/haʊs/","a":"en-us-house-noun.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A house is a building that one family lives in.","e":"The president lives in a house in Washington, called."},{"m":"(uncountable) House is a type of music."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you house someone or something, you give them a home.","e":"The building houses a research centre and a school."}]}]},"authority":{"h":"authority","i":"/ɔːˈθɒrəti/","a":"en-us-authority.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) To have authority means to have the power to make a decision.","e":"This judge has the authority to throw you in jail."},{"m":"(countable) If you are an authority on something, many people think you know very, very much about it.","e":"The Pope is the highest authority in the Catholic church."}]}]},"group":{"h":"group","i":"/gruːp/","a":"en-us-group.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) When more than 2 things or people are together, they make a group.","e":"A group of people went into the building."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To put people or things together to make a group."}]}]},"apparatus":{"h":"apparatus","i":"/æ.pəˈræ.təs/","a":"en-us-apparatus.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A complex machine or instrument."},{"m":"A group of tools or instruments."},{"m":"A system of things to do to get to a goal."}]}]},"complex":{"h":"complex","i":"/kəmˈplɛks/","a":"en-uk-complex.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is complex, it has lots of parts or pieces, or is difficult to understand.","e":"He has constructed a complex computer system to send translated messages between humans and dolphins."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A problem."},{"m":"A group of buildings with a common purpose, such as a university or military base."},{"m":"A psychologically-based dislike or fear of a particular thing.","e":"Jim has a complex about working for a woman boss."},{"m":"A thunderstorm that forms when two storm fronts collide."},{"m":"A structure with a central atom or molecule that has a weak connection to atoms or molecules around it."}]}]},"cream":{"h":"cream","i":"/kriːm/","a":"en-us-cream.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Cream is the fatty part of milk.","e":"Would you like some cream in your coffee?"},{"m":"The cream of something is only the best thing, or person.","e":"He's the cream of the tennis world."},{"m":"Cream is a soft white colour"},{"m":"A cream is a smooth oily substance that people put on their skin to make it soft or as a medicine.","e":"You should clean the cut and put this cream on it three times a day."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To cream something is to puree or blend it into a liquid."},{"m":"To cream something is to make it turn into a cream-like color."},{"m":"To win easily or by a large amount.","e":"The final score was 11-2, we creamed them!"}]}]},"customer":{"h":"customer","i":"/ˈkʌstəmə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-customer.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A customer is a person who pays money for goods or services.","e":"The restaurant had to close because there weren't enough customers."}]}]},"opposite":{"h":"opposite","i":"/ˈɒpəzɪt/","a":"en-us-opposite.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If A is opposite B, they are facing each other.","e":"The bank is just opposite this hotel, right across the street there."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If two things are opposite, they are the same kind but completely different from each other.","e":"\"Go left. No, right!\" \"Do you want me to go left or right? I mean, they're opposite directions, aren't they?\""}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The opposite of something is something else of the same kind but completely different.","e":"My kids always do the exact opposite of what I tell them."}]}]},"bean":{"h":"bean","i":"/biːn/","a":"en-us-bean.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Beans are the seeds of one family of plants that people often cook and eat.","e":"Put the dried beans in water overnight. They should be soft and ready to cook in the morning."},{"m":"A bean-like seed of some other plants, especially coffee.","e":"Although the beans from a single coffee may be sold unblended, in many cases, after roasting, beans from several different origins are combined to balance flavor"}]}]},"weight":{"h":"weight","i":"/weɪt/","a":"en-us-weight.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The weight of something is how heavy it is.","e":"She's put on a lot of weight since she went to university."},{"m":"(countable) A weight is a heavy thing that you use to keep something down or that people lift to become stronger.","e":"Can you put a weight on that paper so that it doesn't blow away?"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you weight something, you add weight to it.","e":"To get your fishing line down to the bottom of the lake, you must weight it."}]}]},"freeze":{"h":"freeze","i":"/ˈfriːz/","a":"en-us-freeze.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you freeze something, you cool it until it becomes solid.","e":"Water freezes at 0°C."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you freeze, you feel very cold.","e":"I was freezing because I had forgotten my coat."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A freeze is a time when the temperature is cold."},{"m":"(countable) A freeze is when the usual way things are done is stopped."}]}]},"coffee":{"h":"coffee","i":"/ˈkɒ.fi/","a":"en-uk-coffee.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Coffee is a dark brown drink that is very popular around the world.","e":"Would you like a cup coffee or tea?"},{"m":"(uncountable) Coffee is the beans or bean powder used to make coffee.","e":"Can you pick up a tin of ground coffee at the shop?"},{"m":"(uncountable) Coffee is a light-brown color."}]}]},"clean":{"h":"clean","i":"/kliːn/","a":"en-us-clean.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is clean, it is free from dirt","e":"The kids came back from the washroom with clean hands and faces."},{"m":"If a technology is clean, it doesn't produce much pollution.","e":"We want to use wind as safe, clean, non-polluting energy."},{"m":"If something is clean, it is not bad.","e":"There was a lot of pushing in their last game, but today's match was mostly clean."},{"m":"A clean piece of paper, start, etc. has nothing from before: no writing, no history, etc.","e":"Why don't you get a clean piece of paper and start over."},{"m":"If a something is clean, it is smooth, simple, and regular, without anything unwanted.","e":"Your company website needs a clean design that makes it easy for consumers to understand what you're selling."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you clean something, you take away the dirt and put everything in its place.","e":"Tomo, will you clean up your room please. There are clothes all over the floor."}]}]},"medicine":{"h":"medicine","i":"/ˈmɛdsən/","a":"en-us-medicine.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Medicine is something you put into or on your body when you are sick to make yourself healthy.","e":"After I got out of the hospital, I went to the drug store and bought medicine for my ear problem."},{"m":"(uncountable) Medicine is the science of health care.","e":"The school of medicine at the University of Western Ontario has produced some of the country's best doctors."}]}]},"universal":{"h":"universal","i":"/ˌjuːnɪˈvɜːsl/","a":"en-us-universal.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is universal, then it is true for everyone or everything everywhere.","e":"The laws of physics are universal."}]}]},"decrease":{"h":"decrease","i":"/dɪˈkriːs/","a":"en-us-decrease.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something decreases, it goes down in number or value.","e":"The Australian dollar has decreased 3% against the Euro."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A decrease happens when the number or value of something goes down.","e":"There has been a 3% decrease in the Australian dollar against the Euro."}]}]},"lunch":{"h":"lunch","i":"/lʌnʧ/","a":"en-us-lunch.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Lunch is the meal that we eat in the middle of the day.","e":"Shall we have sandwiches for lunch?"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you lunch, you have lunch.","e":"Most people lunch around noon time."}]}]},"treatment":{"h":"treatment","i":"/ˈtriːtmənt/","a":"en-us-treatment.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A treatment is an action, usually by a doctor, to make somebody healthy.","e":"He has had treatments every day since he hurt his neck."},{"m":"(uncountable) The treatment that you give someone or something is the way that you act toward it.","e":"The treatment that I have received since beginning this job has been terrible. My boss yells at me every day and nobody is friendly at all."}]}]},"nut":{"h":"nut","i":"/nʌt/","a":"en-us-nut.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A nut is a kind of seed that usually grows on trees inside a hard shell and that people often eat.","e":"Nuts are a good source of protein."},{"m":"A metal ring that is screwed onto a bolt (thick screw)."},{"m":"A crazy person."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To ejaculate."}]}]},"exactly":{"h":"exactly","i":"/ɪɡˈzæk(t)li/","a":"en-us-exactly.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"You use exactly when you want to say that something is 100% true, not just close.","e":"The movie will start at exactly 7:02 PM."},{"m":"You use exactly to show that you agree strongly with something.","e":"\"We can't stay here. It's too cold.\" \"Exactly!\""}]}]},"cheap":{"h":"cheap","i":"/t͡ʃip/","a":"en-uk-cheap.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is cheap, it costs very little money.","e":"\"I bought this for $37 last week, but today I saw it in the store for only $22.\" \"Wow! That's cheap.\""},{"m":"If something is cheap, it is low in quality.","e":"I don't like that jacket. It looks too cheap. Is it plastic?"}]}]},"alike":{"h":"alike","i":"/əˈlaɪk/","a":"en-us-alike.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If some things are alike, they are almost the same in some way.","e":"My mother and I are very much alike."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If some things act alike, they act in almost the same way.","e":"All the men in the office dress alike."},{"m":"You use alike to show that what you say is true of both groups or individuals.","e":"Teachers and students alike have to work harder to improve this school."}]}]},"pig":{"h":"pig","i":"/pɪg/","a":"en-us-pig.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A pig is a mammal.","e":"On this farm, we have over 200 pigs, but no cows or horses."},{"m":"If you call someone a pig you mean that they eat too much, are not clean, or are not a nice person.","e":"My sister is such a pig. We bought a bag of sweets and she ate them all in one day."}]}]},"snake":{"h":"snake","i":"/sneɪk/","a":"en-us-snake.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A snake is a long, thin reptile with no legs.","e":"Some snakes will attack people, but most will try to hide or run away."},{"m":"(countable) A snake is a dishonest, treacherous person.","e":"Chuck is a snake to do a low thing like that."},{"m":"(countable) A snake is a tool used to unclog plumbing."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you snake, you move in a winding path.","e":"The river snakes through the valley."},{"m":"(transitive) If you snake, you clean or unclog a clog using a plumbing snake."}]}]},"soup":{"h":"soup","i":"/suːp/","a":"en-us-soup.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Soup is a food usually made by boiling meat and vegetables in water to give the water flavour.","e":"Would you like soup or a salad before your meal?"}]}]},"tea":{"h":"tea","i":"/tiː/","a":"en-us-tea.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Tea is a light brown or green drink that is very popular around the world.","e":"Would you like coffee or tea?"}]}]},"breakfast":{"h":"breakfast","i":"/ˈbrɛkfəst/","a":"en-us-breakfast.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Breakfast is the first meal that we eat in the morning.","e":"I'm late for school. I don't have time for breakfast today."}]}]},"item":{"h":"item","i":"/ˈaɪtəm/","a":"en-us-item.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An item is a particular thing that is separate from other things.","e":"The first item to discuss at today's meeting is the noise from the new road."}]}]},"element":{"h":"element","i":"/ˈɛlɪmənt/","a":"en-us-element.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An element is one part of something bigger, such as a plan, an engine, or a business.","e":"He's the best salesman on our team, but he's only one element in our success."},{"m":"(countable) An element is one basic kind of substance, such as iron (Fe), oxygen (O), or sodium (Na).","e":"Water is made up of two elements: Hydrogen and Oxygen."}]}]},"identical":{"h":"identical","i":"/ɪˈdɛntɪkl̩/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-identical.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If two ore more things are identical, they are exactly the same.","e":"The teachers teach from identical textbooks, but the ways they teach are quite different."}]}]},"category":{"h":"category","i":"/ˈkætəˌgori/","a":"en-us-category.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A category is a group of people or things that are the same in some way.","e":"The music business tries to put music into various categories, such as rock, pop, jazz, etc."}]}]},"chemical":{"h":"chemical","i":"/ˈkemɪkəl/","a":"en-us-chemical.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A chemical is a basic substance that is used in or produced by mixing elements or other chemicals.","e":"When you burn plastics, you put dangerous chemicals into the air."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Of or about chemicals.","e":"This test can detect small changes in the chemical composition of water."}]}]},"topic":{"h":"topic","i":"/ˈtɒpɪk/","a":"en-us-topic.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A topic is a general idea that someone is speaking (reading, thinking, etc.) about at a specific time.","e":"We were talking about my problems. Don't change the topic."}]}]},"smoke":{"h":"smoke","i":"/sməʊk/","a":"en-us-smoke.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Smoke is the gray or black substance that goes up into the air when something burns.","e":"The smoke from that factory is making me sick."},{"m":"(countable) A cigarette."},{"m":"(uncountable) A light grey colour tinted with blue."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If somebody is smoking, they are in smoke, usually from a cigarette.","e":"Excuse me, you can't smoke in the restaurant."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something is smoking, it is making smoke.","e":"The fire's still smoking. You'd better put some more water on it."}]}]},"tour":{"h":"tour","i":"/tɔː(r)/","a":"en-us-tour.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A tour is a planned walk, bus trip, or flight, to look at a particular place.","e":"Last year we took a wonderful tour to Rome."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you tour a place, you go around it to look at it, often with a guide.","e":"The president gave a short tour around the new factory."},{"m":"Moving from place to place to perform.","e":"The opera company was touring Europe and Africa."}]}]},"complain":{"h":"complain","i":"/kəmˈpleɪn/","a":"en-us-complain.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you complain about someone or something, you say or write that you are not happy about it.","e":"We complained to the manager about the service after waiting one hour for our food."}]}]},"will":{"h":"will","i":"/wɪl/","a":"en-us-will.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) You use will to say that you strongly expect something to happen in the future.","e":"Don't worry. The sun will come up again tomorrow."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you will do something, you make a plan to do it.","e":"I will go to the store."},{"m":"(transitive) If you will something to happen, you wish for it to happen."},{"m":"(transitive) If you will something to someone, you write down your plan to give it to them after your death.","e":"He willed his coin collection to his son."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A will is a statement about what you want to happen after you die."},{"m":"(uncountable) Will is the ability to push through difficulties.","e":"His will states that the house will be inherited by his oldest son after his death."}]}]},"must":{"h":"must","i":"/mʌst/","a":"en-us-must.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Must is usually used to tell someone they have no choice about doing something because it is important or because of a rule or law.","e":"She must get her medicine soon or she will die."},{"m":"If you say something must be true, you say you have come to believe that it is true.","e":"I must have left my phone at the restaurant."}]}]},"shall":{"h":"shall","i":"/ˈʃæl/","a":"en-us-shall.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Shall is usually used to make a suggestion about your own actions.","e":"Shall I get that for you?"},{"m":"Shall is also used to ask for advice.","e":"Where shall I put the plates?"},{"m":"Shall is used like will to make a promise.","e":"We shall send your order immediately."}]}]},"should":{"h":"should","i":"/ʃʊd/","a":"en-US should (stressed).ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) You use should to say that it is a good idea to do something.","e":"If you have a test, you should be studying."}]}]},"seldom":{"h":"seldom","i":"/'seldəm/","a":"en-us-seldom.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If you seldom do something, you almost never do it.","e":"\"How often did you meet?\" \"Well, we saw her quite often, but we seldom saw her husband. In fact, I'm not even sure what he looks like.\""}]}]},"motion":{"h":"motion","i":"/ˈməʊʃən/","a":"en-us-motion.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A motion is a movement, often not a big movement.","e":"She made a small motion with her hand to get his attention."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you motion a person, you direct or command them with a movement."}]}]},"tall":{"h":"tall","i":"/tɔːl/","a":"en-us-tall.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is tall, there is a long distance from the bottom to the top.","e":"The man was so tall that he hit his head coming in the door."}]}]},"wine":{"h":"wine","i":"/waɪn/","a":"en-us-wine.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Wine is an alcoholic drink made from grapes or other fruit.","e":"I don't drink wine very often. Usually I prefer beer."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you wine and dine someone, you entertain them with dinner and wine."}]}]},"corner":{"h":"corner","i":"/ˈkɔrnɚ/","a":"en-us-corner.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A corner is the place where two lines or edges meet.","e":"They live on the corner of Main Street and Dundas."},{"m":"In business, a corner is a monopoly."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To corner someone is to get someone into a place where he or she cannot leave.","e":"Jessy cornered him in the supply room and wouldn't let him leave."},{"m":"To go around corners.","e":"The car really corners well. Turns are easy for it."}]}]},"hotel":{"h":"hotel","i":"/həʊˈtɛl/","a":"en-us-hotel.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A hotel is a place where people pay to stay in a room overnight, usually for only a few days.","e":"We fly to Taipei and stay at the Hilton hotel for three days and two nights."}]}]},"map":{"h":"map","i":"/mæp/","a":"en-us-map.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A map is an image of a place, usually with place names written in.","e":"I think we're lost. Do you have a map?"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you map something, you create a visual representation of it.","e":"John mapped out his idea so that his friends could understand it."}]}]},"straight":{"h":"straight","i":"/streɪt/","a":"en-us-straight.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something goes straight, it continues to move in one direction without turning.","e":"No not that road. Just keep driving straight."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is straight, it does not bend, or turn. It continues in one direction.","e":"He had had too much to drink and couldn't walk in a straight line."},{"m":"Someone who is straight is heterosexual; being attracted to those of the opposite sex."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(poker) In the card game of poker, a straight hand has five sequential cards.","e":"A 5, 6, 7, 8, and 9 is considered a straight hand."}]}]},"empty":{"h":"empty","i":"/ɛmptiː/","a":"en-us-empty.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is empty, it has nothing inside it.","e":"Hey! You finished my beer. It's empty."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you empty something, you remove everything in that item.","e":"I will empty the bins."}]}]},"rare":{"h":"rare","i":"/rɛə/","a":"en-us-rare.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is rare, you seldom see it or there are only a few.","e":"It's rare to have snow in June."},{"m":"(cooking) If a meat is cooked rare, it is cooked very lightly so that the meat is still red when it is done."}]}]},"confusion":{"h":"confusion","i":"/kənˈfjuːʒən/","a":"en-us-confusion.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Confusion is a feeling you get when things are unclear or you don't understand.","e":"The snow storm caused great confusion at the airport where many planes were unable to take off or land."}]}]},"violence":{"h":"violence","i":"/ˈvaɪ(ə)ləns/","a":"en-us-violence.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Violence is an action done to hurt somebody or something.","e":"I don't watch boxing, because I don't like all the fighting and violence."}]}]},"murder":{"h":"murder","i":"/ˈmɜːdə/","a":"en-us-murder.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Murder is when one person plans to hurt or kill somebody and they kill somebody.","e":"Police are looking into two murders at a club in Brazzaville last night."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To kill someone on purpose.","e":"He murdered two people in the bar."}]}]},"guess":{"h":"guess","i":"/ɡɛs/","a":"en-us-guess.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you guess at something, you try to imagine what it might be, but you don't know the answer.","e":"\"What happened? Why has play stopped?\" \"I don't know. I guess a player's hurt, maybe.\""}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A guess is an answer that you give when you don't know the real answer.","e":"\"Wow, what a great car! How much do you think it costs?\" \"My guess is around $80,000.\""}]}]},"plane":{"h":"plane","i":"/pleɪn/","a":"en-uk-a plane.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A plane is a vehicle with wings that flies.","e":"Can we hurry? I have to catch a plane to Miami."},{"m":"(countable) A plane is a surface that goes out in all directions indefinitely."},{"m":"(countable) A plane is a level of existence."},{"m":"(countable) A plane is a tool for smoothing wood."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you plane, you glide or soar."},{"m":"(transitive) If you plane a piece of wood, you smooth it with a plane."}]}]},"airplane":{"h":"airplane","i":"/ˈɛəpleɪn/","a":"en-us-airplane.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An airplane is a vehicle with wings that can fly.","e":"Can we hurry? I have to catch an airplane to Miami."}]}]},"block":{"h":"block","i":"/blɒk/","a":"en-us-block.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A block is a hard piece of material, usually with six smooth sides.","e":"When I was young, I liked building things with wooden blocks."},{"m":"(countable) A city block is the distance from one road to the next.","e":"We have to walk about three blocks to the restaurant."},{"m":"(countable) In computers, a block is a restriction that prevents access to something.","e":"I could not start a page on Wikipedia because of a block."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If X is blocking Y, then Y can't go past X.","e":"The water in the bath won't go down. There's something blocking the drain."}]}]},"hit":{"h":"hit","i":"/hɪt/","a":"en-us-hit.ogg","l":"hit","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you hit someone or something, then you touch them hard and fast.","e":"The bully got suspended for hitting the boy in the face."},{"m":"If you hit on someone, you flirt with them.","e":"I'm just gonna be hitting on chicks tonight"}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A punch.","e":"The hit almost knocked me out."},{"m":"A great success, especially in the entertainment industry.","e":"His new musical comedy was a hit with audiences and critics."}]}]},"offender":{"h":"offender","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An offender is someone or something that does something wrong, usually someone who breaks the law.","e":"The boy who took the car is a young offender, so we can't use his real name."}]}]},"offense":{"h":"offense","i":"/əˈfɛns/","a":"en-us-offense.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An offense is an action that breaks the law.","e":"Murder is a serious criminal offense."},{"m":"(uncountable) When you give offense to someone, you do something that they don't like.","e":"I didn't mean to give offense, but I didn't know that you don't do that in China."},{"m":"(uncountable) The offense is the person or team who is attacking.","e":"For the first time in the game, Arsenal goes on the offense."}]}]},"sorry":{"h":"sorry","i":"/ˈsɔːri/","a":"en-us-sorry.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"You say \"I'm sorry\" when you have done something wrong and you feel bad.","e":"I'm sorry that I lost your jacket last night."}]}]},"my":{"h":"my","i":"/maɪ̯/","a":"en-us-my.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"My things are things that belong to me.","e":"Is this my book, or is it yours?"}]}]},"your":{"h":"your","i":"/jɔː(r)/","a":"en-us-your.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"Your things are things which belong to you.","e":"Can I eat some of your ice-cream please?"}]}]},"its":{"h":"its","i":"/ɪts/","a":"en-us-its.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"Its thing is the thing that belongs to it.","e":"We bought the old car and fixed up its engine."}]}]},"our":{"h":"our","i":"/æɔ(ə)/","a":"en-us-our.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"Our things are things that belong to us.","e":"We've come in our new car."}]}]},"their":{"h":"their","i":"/ðɛɚ/","a":"en-gb-their.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"If something belongs to them it is their thing.","e":"That's not their car, it's ours."}]}]},"mine":{"h":"mine","i":"/maɪn/","a":"en-us-mine.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"If something is mine, it belongs to me.","e":"Give that back to me! It's mine!"}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mine is a large hole in the ground from which rocks and minerals are taken."},{"m":"(countable) A mine is a device that explodes when it is touched, or when a ship, vehicle, or person comes close to it."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you mine rocks or minerals, you dig them out of the ground."},{"m":"(transitive) If you mine an area, you dig a mine there."},{"m":"(transitive) If you mine an area, you put exploding mines there.","e":"The soldiers mined the field to help kill their enemies."}]}]},"yours":{"h":"yours","i":"/jɔː(r)z/","a":"en-us-yours.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"If something is yours, it belongs to you.","e":"Excuse me, is this yours? I found it on the desk."}]}]},"hers":{"h":"hers","i":"/ˈhɜːz/","a":"en-us-hers.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"If something is hers, it belongs to her.","e":"Please give this to Susan. It's hers."}]}]},"ours":{"h":"ours","i":"/ˈaʊɚz/","a":"en-us-ours.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"If something is ours it belongs to us; the possessive case of we, used without a following noun.","e":"This land has been ours for years."}]}]},"theirs":{"h":"theirs","i":"/ðɛəz/","a":"en-us-theirs.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"If something is theirs, it belongs to them.","e":"This book isn't mine, it's theirs."}]}]},"myself":{"h":"myself","i":"/maɪˈsɛɫf/","a":"en-us-myself.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"You use myself when you are the doer and the receiver of an action.","e":"I taught myself."},{"m":"If you do something by yourself, you do it without any help or alone.","e":"I taught him myself."},{"m":"You use myself to emphasize that it is you and not somebody else.","e":"I know a lot of people love coffee, but I myself don't really like it."}]}]},"yourself":{"h":"yourself","i":"/jɔːˈself/","a":"en-us-yourself.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"You use yourself when the person doing an action and receiving an action are both you.","e":"Be careful. You'll hurt yourself."},{"m":"Use for emphasis.","e":"Don't pretend you don't know. You yourself have seen these kinds of problems."},{"m":"If you do something by yourself, you do it alone.","e":"That's beautiful, son. Did you make it by yourself?"},{"m":"If you don't feel yourself, you are different from usual, because you are sick, scared, stressed, etc."}]}]},"himself":{"h":"himself","i":"/hɪmˈsɛlf/","a":"en-us-himself.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"Third person masculine singular reflexive pronoun.","e":"He went by himself to the store."}]}]},"herself":{"h":"herself","i":"/hɜːˈsɛlf/","a":"en-us-herself.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"Third person singular feminine reflexive pronoun","e":"She went by herself to the store."}]}]},"itself":{"h":"itself","i":"/ɪtˈsɛlf/","a":"en-us-itself.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"Third person neutral singular reflexive pronoun.","e":"No person did a thing, but the car started all by itself."}]}]},"ourselves":{"h":"ourselves","i":"/aʊəˈsɛlvz/","a":"en-us-ourselves.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"The reflexive case of we, the first-person plural personal pronoun."},{"m":"us (referring to us, when we have already been mentioned)","e":"We should keep this for ourselves."},{"m":"we (used as an intensifier)","e":"We did it ourselves."}]}]},"themselves":{"h":"themselves","i":"/ðɛmˈsɛlvz/","a":"en-us-themselves.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"You use themselves when the people doing an action and the people receiving an action are the same people, but they are not you or the person you're talking to.","e":"They've hurt themselves."},{"m":"Use for emphasis, when talking about more than one person or about one person when you don't know who that person is.","e":"The classes are as different as the students themselves."},{"m":"If somebody or some people do something by themselves, they do it alone.","e":"The children earned $500 by themselves. I didn't help."},{"m":"If somebody or some people don't feel themselves, they are different from usual, because they are sick, scared, stressed, etc."}]}]},"part":{"h":"part","i":"/pɑːt/","a":"en-us-part.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A part of something is one piece of it or a small amount of it.","e":"As a part of this team, you need to come to practice regularly."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If A and B part, they were together and now they are not.","e":"My wife and I parted after our son died."}]}]},"body":{"h":"body","i":"/ˈbɒdi/","a":"en-us-body.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A body is the main part of a person, animal, physical object, or organisation.","e":"After falling out of the tree, his arm was broken and his body hurt all over."},{"m":"(countable) A body is a dead person or animal.","e":"The police found her body after she had been missing for three days."},{"m":"(countable) A body is a group of people.","e":"The senate is an important legislative body in the United States."},{"m":"(countable) A body of something is a lot on it together in one place.","e":"Lake Michigan is a large body of water."},{"m":"A body is a thing that all moves together.","e":"The moon is a body in orbit around Earth."}]}]},"animal":{"h":"animal","i":"/ˈænəməl/","a":"en-uk-an animal.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An animal is any living thing that can move. are not animals, but are said to be animals, under the scientific definition..","e":"Dogs, elephants, and horses are all animals."}]}]},"ticket":{"h":"ticket","i":"/ˈtɪkɪt/","a":"en-us-ticket.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A ticket is a piece of paper that allows you to enter a train, airplane, show, etc.","e":"I bought my ticket to Mexico last week, but now I can't find it."},{"m":"(countable) A ticket is a piece of paper that shows that you have parked your car in the wrong place or committed some other driving offence.","e":"The policeman gave me a ticket for going 125&nbsp;km/h."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you ticket someone, then you give someone a ticket for breaking a law.","e":"The officer ticketed the driver after he drove through a red light."}]}]},"belt":{"h":"belt","i":"/bεlt/","a":"en-us-belt.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A belt is a piece of clothing worn around a person's waist. They can be used to hold up trousers or skirts, or for carrying things in pockets, such as on a utility belt.","e":"I think I've put on weight. My belt is too tight."},{"m":"A belt is used to hold people down for safety, such as a seat belt"}]}]},"third":{"h":"third","i":"/θɜː(r)d/","a":"en-us-third.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"The third thing is the one that is number three (3) in order.","e":"I have two older brothers. I'm the third child."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A third of something is one of three equal parts of that thing.","e":"Four is one third of twelve."}]}]},"flower":{"h":"flower","i":"/ˈflaʊə/","a":"en-us-flower.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A flower is part of a plant. Flowers are often very pretty. Plants make them so that they can make new seeds.","e":"The flower of the plant is starting to wilt."},{"m":"(uncountable) The best something can be.","e":"She was in the flower of her life."},{"m":"(usually with in) When something starts to bloom.","e":"Cherry blossoms are in flower this week."},{"m":"(countable) A plant that has flowers.","e":"The rose is my favorite flower."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) When something flowers, it starts to bloom.","e":"Cherry blossoms are going to flower this week."}]}]},"engine":{"h":"engine","i":"/ˈɛnd͡ʒɪn/","a":"en-us-engine.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An engine is the part of a machine which gives it power."}]}]},"fire":{"h":"fire","i":"/faɪə(r)/","a":"en-us-fire.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A chemical reaction that makes heat and flames or smoldering."},{"m":"(countable) Something that has made or can make this chemical reaction, such as a campfire.","e":"We sat around the fire singing songs and telling stories."},{"m":"(countable) The, often accidental, occurrence of fire in a certain place which leads to its full or partial destruction.","e":"There was a fire at the church last night and the whole place burned down."},{"m":"(uncountable); (alchemy) One of the four basic elements."},{"m":"(India) (Japan) One of the five basic elements."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If an employee is fired, their employment is ended because of something they did.","e":"She should fire the guy who stole that stuff."},{"m":"If you fire a gun, cannon or a similar weapon, you shoot it.","e":"We will fire our guns at the enemy."}]}]},"winter":{"h":"winter","i":"/'wɪntə/","a":"en-us-winter.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Winter is the coldest season of the year. In northern countries, December, January and February are winter months.","e":"We like to go to Mexico in the winter."}]}]},"camp":{"h":"camp","i":"/kæmp/","a":"en-us-camp.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A camp is a place, usually outside of, where people stay for a short time.","e":"I don't think I can walk anymore today. Let's set up camp for the night."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you camp, you stay in a place, usually outside of the city for a short time.","e":"I hope we can go camping in the mountains this summer."}]}]},"flat":{"h":"flat","i":"/flæt/","a":"en-us-flat.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is flat, it has a surface with no high places or low places.","e":"There are a lot of mountains, and very little flat land for farming."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A flat is a rented room or rooms in a building with other flats.","e":"Would you like to come back to my flat and watch TV?"},{"m":"(countable); A flat makes a note one semitone lower than a natural: it is shown by the symbol ♭."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To make something flat."}]}]},"hat":{"h":"hat","i":"/hæt/","a":"en-us-hat.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hat is a piece of clothing that you wear on your head.","e":"A poke bonnet is an old-fashioned woman's hat that covers the hair and shades the face with a rim."}]}]},"sheep":{"h":"sheep","i":"/ʃiːp/","a":"en-us-sheep.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sheep is an animal that people keep on farms and eat for food.","e":"My grandfather has a sheep farm and we get all our wool there."},{"m":"(countable) A sheep is a person who follows orders blindly and cannot think for themself."}]}]},"resident":{"h":"resident","i":"/ˈrɛzɪd(ə)nt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-resident.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A resident is somebody who lives in a particular area.","e":"The local residents like the tourism because it creates more jobs for them."},{"m":"(US) A resident is a doctor who is still training, and who works in a hospital."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are resident somewhere, you live or work there.","e":"If you are not resident in the town, you may not use the town pool."}]}]},"illustrate":{"h":"illustrate","i":"/ˈɪl.jʊˌstreɪt/","a":"en-uk-illustrate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you illustrate something, you draw a picture of it, or you explain it.","e":"\"I'm sorry, can you explain again?\" \"OK, let me illustrate with an example.\""},{"m":"(transitive) If you illustrate a book, magazine, poster, etc., you put pictures in it.","e":"Have you tried reading these illustrated books for adults?"}]}]},"location":{"h":"location","i":"/loʊˈkeɪʃən/","a":"en-us-location.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A location is a place or a site.","e":"When you're opening a new business, the choice of location is very important."},{"m":"(countable) A site outside of a studio used for shooting all or part of a movie or television show.","e":"The show was filmed on location in Hawaii."}]}]},"licence":{"h":"licence","i":"/ˈlaɪsəns/","a":"en-au-licence.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A licence is an official piece of paper that allows you to do something, such as drive, open a business, etc.","e":"I got my driver's licence when I was 16 years old."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(Commonwealth English) Another spelling of license, usually thought to be wrong. The verb form should normally be spelt as license."}]}]},"license":{"h":"license","i":"/ˈlaɪsəns/","a":"en-au-licence.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A license is an official piece of paper that allows you to do something, such as drive, open a business, etc.","e":"I got my driver's license when I was 16 years old."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"The act of giving a formal (usually written) authorization.","e":"It was decided to license Wikipedia under the GFDL."},{"m":"Officially authorize.","e":"I am licensed to practice law in this state."}]}]},"parent":{"h":"parent","i":"/ˈpærənt/","a":"en-us-parent.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The parents of a person or animal are its father and mother.","e":"Children may only enter the pool with a parent or guardian."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To act as parent, to raise or rear."}]}]},"century":{"h":"century","i":"/ˈsɛnt͡ʃʊri/","a":"en-us-century.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A century is a period of 100 years.","e":"My great grandfather came to Canada over a century ago."}]}]},"widow":{"h":"widow","i":"/ˈwɪd.əʊ/","a":"en-us-widow.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A widow is a woman whose husband has died.","e":"The government supports the widows of dead soldiers."}]}]},"rent":{"h":"rent","i":"/rɛnt/","a":"en-us-rent.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Rent is the money you pay to borrow and use something, usually an apartment.","e":"Have we paid this month's rent yet?"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you rent something, you pay money to use something for a limited time, usually for a house or apartment.","e":"I'm in Texas next week, so I'll have to rent a car."}]}]},"roof":{"h":"roof","i":"/ruːf/","a":"en-us-roof.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A roof is the top part of a building.","e":"My five brothers, two sisters and seven cousins all live together under one roof."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you roof something, then you are putting a [[#Noun|roof]] onto a building.","e":"My father had to roof our house because it needed a roof."}]}]},"grand":{"h":"grand","i":"/ɡrænd/","a":"en-us-grand.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is grand, it's large and impressive.","e":"As she got out of the car, she saw that the house was very grand."}]}]},"bottle":{"h":"bottle","i":"/ˈbɑɾ(ə)l/","a":"en-us-bottle.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bottle is a container, usually made of glass that holds liquid and has a cap or stopper.","e":"He drank cold water from a plastic bottle."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you bottle your feelings up, you keep them inside and don't let them show.","e":"You can tell he is still angry, but he's keeping it bottled up."},{"m":"(transitive) If you bottle somebody or something up, you keep them in a very small space, often under pressure.","e":"We were bottled up in that plane for 32 hours."},{"m":"(transitive) If you bottle something, you put it in a bottle.","e":"This plant bottles a lot of spring water every day."}]}]},"head":{"h":"head","i":"/hɛd/","a":"en-us-head.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The head is the highest and most important part of the body.","e":"He put his head on the desk and fell asleep."},{"m":"The head is the owner of something.","e":"After a series of problems, the head of the company left."},{"m":"The bathroom on a ship is called the head."},{"m":"(countable) The head is the function of the most important element in a phrase."},{"m":"(uncountable) To give a person head is to give them fellatio."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To go in a direction is to head there.","e":"Bill heads for the mall after work."}]}]},"throat":{"h":"throat","i":"/ˈθrəʊt/","a":"en-us-throat.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Your throat is a tube inside your neck. It takes air from your mouth to your lungs.","e":"My throat hurts from singing too much."}]}]},"these":{"h":"these","i":"/ðiːz/","a":"en-us-these.ogg","l":"this","q":"determiner"},"those":{"h":"those","i":"/ðəʊz/","a":"en-us-those.ogg","l":"that","q":"determiner"},"no":{"h":"no","i":"/nəʊ/","a":"en-us-no.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Used to disagree or refuse; to say something different from what the other person said.","e":"No, I do not fish."},{"m":"Used to agree with the negative side of a negative question.","e":"Isn't the door locked? No, the door is not locked. We can go in."}]},{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"Not any.","e":"There is no water left."},{"m":"Not any possibility or allowance of (doing something). You can't.","e":"No smoking."},{"m":"Not (a); not properly, not really; not fully.","e":"My mother's no fool."},{"m":"Not.","e":"He's no better off."}]}]},"some":{"h":"some","i":"/sʌm/","a":"en-us-some.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"Used to mean an amount or number of something when the amount or number is not exact or specific.","e":"Would you like some grapes?"},{"m":"Unspecified or unknown.","e":"I've just met some man who said he knew you."},{"m":"You use some before a number to say that it may be a little more or a little less.","e":"Some 200 people attended the event."}]}]},"sufficient":{"h":"sufficient","i":"/səˈfɪʃənt/","a":"en-us-sufficient.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"(formal) If something is sufficient, it means there is enough or that it is good enough.","e":"We now have a sufficient number of people to do the job."}]},{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"You use sufficient to identify the smallest amount needed.","e":"Sufficient of us are against this idea that we should stop now."}]}]},"what":{"h":"what","i":"/wɔt/","a":"en-us-what.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"(question) What is used to ask for information about things.","e":"What did you see?"},{"m":"(question) What is used to add a clause with more information.","e":"I don't know what you mean."},{"m":"(relative) The thing(s) which: a small amount of something.","e":"Take what you can find."}]},{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(question) What is used to ask about the member(s) of a group.","e":"What book did you buy?"},{"m":"(relative) What is used to talk about the member(s) of a group.","e":"What gifts you can give are appreciated."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"(exclamation) used to show that you feel strongly about something.","e":"What a great book this is!"}]}]},"we":{"h":"we","i":"/wiː/","a":"en-us-we.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"The person speaking and other people with him or her.","e":"\"Are you and Mia still going?\" \"No, were finished.\""},{"m":"People in general.","e":"We need to think about other people more."}]},{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"The person speaking and other people with him or her.","e":"We Canadians don't act that way."}]}]},"many":{"h":"many","i":"/ˈmɛni/","a":"en-us-many.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"A large number of (something).","e":"There are many people in China."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"You use many to indicate that you are talking about a large number of people or things.","e":"The possibilities are many."}]}]},"few":{"h":"few","i":"/fjuː/","a":"en-us-few.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"not many","e":"I found very few problems."}]}]},"much":{"h":"much","i":"/mʌt​͡ʃ/","a":"en-us-much.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"a lot of; a large amount of; a high degree","e":"I don't have much money."},{"m":"If someone or something is very much alive, interested, open, etc., they are indeed so, contrary to expectations.","e":"I thought the window was closed, but it was very much open."},{"m":"If something is pretty much impossible, useless, perfect, etc. it is roughly so.","e":"Your hair looks pretty much perfect the way it is."}]}]},"little":{"h":"little","i":"/'lɪtl̩/","a":"en-us-little.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is little, its size is not big.","e":"I just ate a tiny little piece of the cake."},{"m":"A little while, distance, etc. is not long.","e":"Could you just wait a little while more?"},{"m":"A little person or animal is young.","e":"Two little boys were fighting on the playground."}]},{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"Little money, room, help, etc. is a small amount of it; not much.","e":"They understood little or no French."}]}]},"which":{"h":"which","i":"/ʍɪʧ/","a":"en-us-which.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(question) You use which to ask for the selection of one or more members of some set.","e":"There are a lot of new books this year. Which ones do you like?"},{"m":"(relative) You use which to add a clause to explain what thing you're talking about.","e":"For several seconds he sat in silence, during which time the tea and sandwiches arrived."}]},{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"(relative) You use which to add a clause to give more information about the thing you're talking about.","e":"We've met some problems which are very difficult to handle."}]}]},"neither":{"h":"neither","i":"/ˈnaɪðər/","a":"en-us-neither.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"Not one or the other; not either; none of two things.","e":"Neither definition seems correct."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Neither is used to show that a something that is not true in one case is also not true in another case.","e":"She didn't have one, and neither did I."}]}]},"him":{"h":"him","i":"/hɪm/","a":"en-us-him.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"he when used after a preposition or as the object of a verb.","e":"Give it to him (after preposition)"}]}]},"us":{"h":"us","i":"/ʌs/","a":"en-us-us.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"(object form) You use us to talk or write about yourself and other people together with you.","e":"She said hello to us."}]},{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"You use us to refer to yourself and other people together with you.","e":"It's OK for you guys, but it's different for us women."}]}]},"them":{"h":"them","i":"/ðɛm/","a":"en-us-them.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"Other people; not you or the people you are talking to.","e":"I saw my friends and said, \"hi\" to them."},{"m":"Things.","e":"I made a lot of things. This is one of them."},{"m":"You use them to talk about one person, if you don't know who that person is.","e":"If somebody comes, help them."}]}]},"they":{"h":"they","i":"/ðeɪ/","a":"en-uk-they.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"\"They\" is used to talk about two or more people, not you or the person you are speaking to.","e":"I love Josie and Reg. They are nice people."},{"m":"\"They\" is used to talk about two or more things.","e":"Can you get the books for me? Theyre over there."},{"m":"\"They\" is used to talk about one or more person when you don't know the sex or number.","e":"If a person is fast, they can get there early."},{"m":"\"They\" is used to talk about people in general.","e":"When are they going to finish that new building?"},{"m":"\"They\" is used to talk about a person that is not a man and not a woman.","e":"I love Alex. They are my partner."}]}]},"one":{"h":"one","i":"/wʌn/","a":"en-us-one.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(ordinal first) The number 1.","e":"We have one nose and one mouth."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The number 1.","e":"One is the smallest whole number."}]},{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"One is a singular pronoun which means someone or people. It is used more often in formal writing.","e":"It is easy to see the difference if one looks closely enough."}]}]},"there":{"h":"there","i":"/ðɛə/","a":"en-uk-there.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"You use there to show that something exists.","e":"There is a problem here."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"(In, at or to) that place.","e":"We left for Ottawa and arrived there at 7:00."}]}]},"whose":{"h":"whose","i":"/huːz/","a":"en-us-whose.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"(question) Whose is used to ask what person something belongs to.","e":"Whose is this? There's no name on it."},{"m":"(relative) Whose is used to join a relative clause about a person or thing.","e":"Children whose parents smoke are more likely to smoke themselves."}]}]},"who":{"h":"who","i":"/huː/","a":"en-us-who.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"(relative) You use who to add a clause to explain more about the person or people you're talking about.","e":"They are good people who are working hard."},{"m":"(question) You use who to ask about a person or people.","e":"Who was on the phone?"}]}]},"whom":{"h":"whom","i":"/huːm/","a":"en-us-whom.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"(question) Whom is the object form of who.","e":"Whom do you agree with?"},{"m":"(relative) Whom is the object form of who.","e":"I have a sister, whom I wrote to last week."}]}]},"enough":{"h":"enough","i":"/ɪ'nʌf/","a":"en-us-enough.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"the needed number or amount","e":"I've already had enough coffee today."}]}]},"another":{"h":"another","i":"/əˈnʌðə/","a":"en-uk-another.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"Another of something means that there is one more of it.","e":"Is there another way to do this?"}]}]},"every":{"h":"every","i":"/ˈɛvri/","a":"en-us-every.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"all the people, things, times, etc.","e":"I work every day from 6:00 to 9:30."}]}]},"whatever":{"h":"whatever","i":"/ʍɒtˈɛvə/","a":"en-us-whatever.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(relative) You use whatever when it doesn't matter which thing.","e":"It's OK to take whatever bus comes first."},{"m":"(relative) You use whatever when there's a particular thing, but you can't remember what it was.","e":"We took whatever bus came first, number 41 I think."},{"m":"(question) You use whatever to make what stronger.","e":"Whatever problem do you mean?"}]},{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"(question) You use whatever when it doesn't matter which thing.","e":"Whatever you choose, you'll be happy."},{"m":"(relative) You use whatever when it doesn't matter which thing.","e":"Whatever you do will be OK."},{"m":"(relative) You use whatever when there's a particular thing, but you can't remember what it was.","e":"We took whatever came first."},{"m":"(question) You use whatever to make what stronger.","e":"Whatever do you mean?"},{"m":"You use whatever as a reply showing that you do not care.","e":"\"Would you like coffee, tea, or water?\" \"Whatever.\""}]}]},"whichever":{"h":"whichever","i":"/wɪt͡ʃˈɛvɚ/","a":"en-us-whichever.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(question) You use whichever when it doesn't matter which thing.","e":"Whichever colour you choose, you'll be happy."},{"m":"(relative) You use whichever when it doesn't matter which thing.","e":"It's OK to take whichever bus comes first."},{"m":"(relative, definite) You use whichever when there's a particular thing, but you can't remember what it was.","e":"We took whichever bus came first, number 41 I think."}]},{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"(question) You use whichever when it doesn't matter which thing.","e":"Whichever you choose, you'll be happy."},{"m":"(relative, indefinite) You use whichever when it doesn't matter which thing.","e":"It's OK to take whichever comes first."},{"m":"(relative, definite) You use whichever when there's a particular thing, but you can't remember what it was.","e":"We took whichever came first, number 41 I think."}]}]},"both":{"h":"both","i":"/bəʊθ/","a":"en-us-both.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"When there are two things, both is the first thing and the second thing.","e":"Jim took both the apple and the orange."}]}]},"certain":{"h":"certain","i":"/sɜːtn/","a":"en-ca-certain.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are certain of something, you believe it to be true without doubt."},{"m":"If something is certain, it will happen without doubt."},{"m":"If you make certain of something, you check that it is true or correct."}]},{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"Used to talk about groups or individuals without saying exactly which ones.","e":"Certain problems can be solved with very simple maths."}]}]},"several":{"h":"several","i":"/ˈsɛvrəl/","a":"en-us-several.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"Several things is a small number of things. More than two, but not very many.","e":"It rained for several days last week."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Their several things is a number of their things.","e":"They each went their several ways."}]}]},"various":{"h":"various","i":"/ˈvɛəriəs/","a":"en-us-various.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Various ways, types, kinds, etc. are many different ones.","e":"I've made the dish a number of times in various ways. It's never the same."}]},{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"You use various to identify more than one thing without saying exactly which ones.","e":"Various books have been taken."}]}]},"ugly":{"h":"ugly","i":"/ˈʌɡli/","a":"en-us-ugly1.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone or something is ugly, it's not nice to look at.","e":"Hughie had the same ugly face as his father and brother."}]}]},"grass":{"h":"grass","i":"/grɑːs/","a":"en-uk-grass.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Grass is a green, leafy plant that often covers the ground.","e":"We haven't got much rain, and the grass on the lawn is turning brown."},{"m":"Marijuana"}]}]},"terrible":{"h":"terrible","i":"/ˈtɛrəbl/","a":"en-us-terrible.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is terrible, it's very bad.","e":"He said she was ugly. Wasn't that a terrible thing to say to anyone?"},{"m":"If something is terrible, it causes people to feel terror or fear.","e":"The witch laid a terrible curse on him."}]}]},"goat":{"h":"goat","i":"/gəʊt/","a":"en-us-goat.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A goat is a mammal with horns, part of the sheep family.","e":"The goat used to graze in the field."}]}]},"wool":{"h":"wool","i":"/wʊl/","a":"en-us-wool.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Wool is the hair of a sheep. We often use it to make clothes."}]}]},"rat":{"h":"rat","i":"/ræt/","a":"en-us-rat.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Rats are medium-sized rodents. They often live near people and eat garbage. Rats can carry diseases. They are also kept as pets and can be very tame.","e":"I caught the rat that was eating our food."}]}]},"advertising":{"h":"advertising","i":"/ˈædvə(r)ˌtaɪzɪŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-advertising.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Advertising is the business or study of using newspapers, TV, etc. to sell products or inform people.","e":"Coke has a new advertising campaign for a new drink."}]}]},"asleep":{"h":"asleep","i":"/əˈsliːp/","a":"en-us-asleep.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are asleep, you are sleeping.","e":"Please be quiet. The baby's asleep."}]}]},"burst":{"h":"burst","i":"/bɜːst/","a":"en-us-burst.ogg","l":"burst","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something bursts, it breaks open because of pressure from the inside.","e":"I was driving west on the highway, when my front left tire burst."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A burst is an explosion or blast.","e":"There was a burst of laughter from the audience when the clown slipped on the banana peel."}]}]},"improve":{"h":"improve","i":"/ɪmˈpruːv/","a":"en-us-improve.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something improves, it changes from bad to good.","e":"The government is planning to improve the quality of rail service by adding new trains."}]}]},"birth":{"h":"birth","i":"/bɜːθ/","a":"en-us-birth.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A birth is when a new baby comes out of its mother.","e":"My mother gave birth to my brother at 12:00 on Dec. 31st."},{"m":"(countable) A birth is when something new begins.","e":"The birth of the personal computer was in 1976."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If a woman births a child, she bears or give birth to a child."}]}]},"boy":{"h":"boy","i":"/bɔɪ/","a":"en-us-boy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A boy is a male child or teenager; someone who is not a man yet.","e":"He had a pretty wife and two little ones: a boy and a girl."},{"m":"(informal) An immature man.","e":"\"I am a grown man\" \"you are not a man, you are a little boy, you don't act like a man\"."},{"m":"(informal) A male animal.","e":"I told my mom I wanted a boy puppy, not a girl one."}]},{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"You use boy when you are surprised about something.","e":"Boy, that's a big dog."}]}]},"repair":{"h":"repair","i":"/rɪˈpɛə/","a":"en-us-repair.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If something is broken or damaged and a person repairs it, it's not broken or damaged anymore; to fix something.","e":"And workmen were out repairing damage to the lights from last night's wind."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A repair is something a person does to something to fix it.","e":"Last night the car wouldn't start, so this morning I took it in for repairs."}]}]},"management":{"h":"management","i":"/ˈmænəʤmənt/","a":"en-uk-management.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Management is the act of watching and controlling a business or situation.","e":"This building uses a computerized energy management systems to save electricity."},{"m":"(uncountable) The management is/are the people who control a business.","e":"Management have received a 5% pay raise, but workers are only getting 3.5%."}]}]},"push":{"h":"push","a":"en-us-push.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you push something, you touch it with a force away from your body.","e":"You have to push that door quite hard before it will open."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A push is the act of touching something with a force away from your body.","e":"My car won't move. Can you give me a push?"}]}]},"aside":{"h":"aside","i":"/əˈsaɪd/","a":"en-us-aside.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If you put something aside, you put it to the side, often because you want to use it later.","e":"We put some money aside for the children's education."},{"m":"You use something aside to leave that thing out of the topic.","e":"The lies aside, they're good workers."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An aside is something that you write or say that isn't part of your main idea.","e":"And, just as an aside, I'd like to say that these ideas are not new..."}]}]},"arrange":{"h":"arrange","i":"/əˈreɪndʒ/","a":"en-us-arrange.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you arrange something, you put it in order or you organise it.","e":"We have arranged a meeting between the president of the company and the new owner."}]}]},"collection":{"h":"collection","i":"/kəˈlɛkʃən/","a":"en-us-collection.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A collection is a group of things of the same type. They are usually special in some way.","e":"He has one of the biggest collections of paintings by Van Gogh."},{"m":"If you take a collection, you ask many people for money, for a particular reason.","e":"The school took a collection for new books."}]}]},"sister":{"h":"sister","i":"/ˈsɪstə/","a":"en-us-sister.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Your sister is the daughter of your mother and father, except yourself.","e":"My parents have three children: me, my brother, and my sister."},{"m":"(countable) A sister is a nurse in a hospital.","e":"The Sister said that I must rest more."},{"m":"A sister of a thing is something that has a special or affectionate connection to it, specifically one that is non-hierarchical.","e":"is a sister project of."}]}]},"tooth":{"h":"tooth","i":"/tuːθ/","a":"en-us-tooth.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A tooth is a hard, white thing in your mouth. You use your teeth to chew food."},{"m":"(countable) A tooth is a sharp point sticking out of something and forms a row of sharp objects for cutting."},{"m":"(countable) A tooth is a rounded point on a gear that is used to transmit or receive force and motion to other gears."}]}]},"boat":{"h":"boat","i":"/bəʊt/","a":"en-us-boat.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A boat is a vehicle used to travel on water.","e":"At the lake, the children learn about fishing and boat safety."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To travel by boat."}]}]},"ball":{"h":"ball","i":"/bɔːl/","a":"en-us-ball.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A ball is a round thing. People often use them to play games.","e":"The croquet ball was hit through the wicket and the game was over."},{"m":"A ball is a formal dance.","e":"There is an inaugural ball following the swearing-in of the new President."},{"m":"(usually plural) the testicles","e":"John's balls ached because he hadn't had sex in two days."},{"m":"(usually plural) \"guts\", fortitude, moral strength","e":"John didn't have the balls to quit his job, divorce his wife, and start a new life in Tahiti."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you ball something up, you make it into a ball shape.","e":"Ball the cookie dough, wrap it in paper, then freeze it."},{"m":"sexual intercourse."}]}]},"compare":{"h":"compare","i":"/kəmˈpɛr/","a":"en-us-compare.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you compare two things, you look at, talk about, or think about how they are the same and how they are different.","e":"I compared all different kinds of computers before buying this one."}]}]},"clock":{"h":"clock","i":"/klɒk/","a":"en-us-clock.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A clock is an instrument that tells you what the time is. A small clock which you carry is called a watch.","e":"He was sleepy, and the clock said 11:32."},{"m":"(uncountable) If something goes around the clock, it goes for 24 hours without stop.","e":"His family stayed at Scott's bedside around the clock."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you clock something, you measure how long it takes or how fast it moves.","e":"The police clocked the car at 137&nbsp;km/h."},{"m":"(transitive) If something clocks a time or a speed, it takes that long or moves that fast.","e":"The trip clocks in at about 12 hours."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you clock in or out at work, school, etc., you record the time they arrive or leave.","e":"He clocked in at four a.m. for a twelve-hour shift."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you clock up a number of things, you reach that total after some time.","e":"Because I drive one hour to work, I'm clocking up a lot of miles."},{"m":"(transitive) If you clock someone, you hit them hard in the head.","e":"He might take some time to wake up. He got clocked pretty good."}]}]},"dirty":{"h":"dirty","i":"/ˈdɜːti/","a":"en-uk-dirty.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is dirty, it has dirt on it, or it is not clean.","e":"After playing outside all day, her hands were all dirty."}]}]},"cousin":{"h":"cousin","i":"/ˈkʌz.n̩/","a":"en-us-cousin.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Your cousin is the son or daughter of your aunt or uncle.","e":"Every year at Christmas, I got to play with all my cousins at my grandma's house."}]}]},"loose":{"h":"loose","i":"/luːs/","a":"en-us-loose.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is loose, it moves easily or may come away from what it is attached to.","e":"His tooth is loose and will probably come out in a day or two."},{"m":"If something is loose, it does not fit closely.","e":"My pants are so loose that they keep falling down."},{"m":"If a woman is has loose morals, she is sexually unrestrained.","e":"a loose woman"}]}]},"noise":{"h":"noise","i":"/nɔɪz/","a":"en-us-noise.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A noise is a sound, usually one that you don't want.","e":"There's too much noise. I can't hear what she's saying."}]}]},"upper":{"h":"upper","i":"/ˈʌpə/","a":"en-us-upper.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"The upper thing is the one that is in a higher position.","e":"The upper floors of the building are for offices and the lower floors for housing."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A drug that stimulates a body. Uppers give a person energy and lower hunger.","e":"He takes uppers so that he can stay awake all night studying."}]}]},"aunt":{"h":"aunt","i":"/ˈænt/","a":"en-us-aunt.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Your aunt is the sister of your mother or father.","e":"After my parents died, we went to live with my aunt."}]}]},"cause":{"h":"cause","i":"/kɔːz/","a":"en-us-cause.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cause is what leads to something happening.","e":"The cause of the fire was lightning."},{"m":"(countable) A cause is a goal, aim or principle that people support or fight for.","e":"He is fighting for a just cause."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To cause something is to make it happen.","e":"His careless driving caused the car accident."}]}]},"cottage":{"h":"cottage","i":"/ˈkɒtɪd͡ʒ/","a":"en-us-cottage.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cottage is a small house, usually in the countryside.","e":"When we were young, we spent the summers at a cottage on Canoe Lake."}]}]},"bone":{"h":"bone","i":"/bəʊn/","a":"en-us-bone.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Bones are the hard, white things inside your body. They give your body its shape.","e":"How many bones did a dinosaur have?"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When two man bone, they have sex."}]}]},"circle":{"h":"circle","i":"/ˈsɜrkəl/","a":"en-us-circle.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A circle (●) is a round shape.","e":"Please put your chairs in a circle."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To circle something is to move around it.","e":"The earth circles the sun once a year."}]}]},"now":{"h":"now","i":"/nɑʊ/","a":"en-us-now.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"You use now when you want to say that something is true at this time. It is also used for things a short time in the future or a short time in the past.","e":"I had many problems before, but I'm OK now."},{"m":"You use now at the beginning of a sentence to get people's attention.","e":"Now, I'd like to hear from other people too."},{"m":"You use now to refer to the present time, often in contrast to a time in the past or the future.","e":"Now is the time when we must all live as economically as possible."},{"m":"You use now to indicate that an event has occurred and as a result something else may or will happen.","e":"I’m going to relax now the school year is over."}]}]},"row":{"h":"row","i":"/rəʊ/","a":"en-us-row.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A row of things is a line of them, usually going from side to side.","e":"OK, students, can you please put your desks in five rows?"},{"m":"(countable) A row is a loud argument."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you row a boat, you move the paddles (also called oars) in the water to move the boat.","e":"Let's row our boat to the other side of the lake."}]}]},"slave":{"h":"slave","i":"/sleɪv/","a":"en-us-slave.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A slave is a person who is owned by a master and who works for that master, but receives no—or almost no—money."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) To work very hard.","e":"I've been slaving in the kitchen all day cooking food for Christmas dinner."}]}]},"straw":{"h":"straw","i":"/strɔː/","a":"en-us-straw.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Straw is dried grasses, such as wheat, without the seeds. Animals sleep on it, and people make hats and mats out of it."},{"m":"(uncountable) A pale, yellowish-beige colour, like that of a dried straw."},{"m":"(countable) A straw is a thin hollow tube that you drink through."}]}]},"uncle":{"h":"uncle","i":"/ˈʌŋkəl/","a":"en-us-uncle.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Your uncle is the brother of your mother or father.","e":"My father has a brother, Joe. Joe is my uncle."}]}]},"yard":{"h":"yard","i":"/jɑːd/","a":"en-us-yard.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A yard is the area around a house.","e":"The children went out to play in the yard."},{"m":"(countable) A yard is an imperial measure of length. One yard is three feet or 91.44 centimeters.","e":"A soccer field is 110 yards long."}]}]},"couple":{"h":"couple","i":"/ˈkʌpəl/","a":"en-uk-couple.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A couple is two (2) things that go together.","e":"Can you lend me a couple of dollars?"},{"m":"A couple is two people that love one another.","e":"John and Susan make a nice couple, don't they?"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you couple two things, you join them together."},{"m":"(intransitive) If two people couple, they have sex."}]}]},"tree":{"h":"tree","i":"/triː/","a":"en-uk-tree.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A tree is a tall plant of wood.","e":"I'm going to climb a tree."},{"m":"(countable) A tree is a map or a diagram of ideas that looks like the plant.","e":"My family tree shows how I am related to all my family members."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(uncommon) If you tree something, you chase it up into a tree."}]}]},"library":{"h":"library","a":"en-us-library.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A library is a place where books and other media are kept, usually on shelves. Most of the time, people are allowed to borrow these things.","e":"I borrowed books at the public library today."},{"m":"(countable) A library is a collection of books of other media. A person may call his/her collection of books a library.","e":"The university's online classical music library is very large."},{"m":"In computing, a library or standard library (STL) is a collection of code and functions that can be used for software development and to make computer programs."}]}]},"cardboard":{"h":"cardboard","i":"/ˈkɑːdbɔːd/","a":"en-us-cardboard.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Cardboard is a material like paper, but thicker and stiffer.","e":"Cardboard is used to make boxes."}]}]},"sentence":{"h":"sentence","i":"/ˈsɛntəns/","a":"en-us-sentence.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) In grammar, a sentence is a group of words that follow normal grammar rules, and that, in writing, begins with a capital letter and ends with a period '.', question mark '?', or exclamation mark '!'. Usually a sentence has a subject, verb, and object.","e":"The first sentence in the Jewish holy book is, \"In the beginning God created the heaven and the earth.\""},{"m":"(countable) In law, a sentence is the punishment that a judge gives to a criminal.","e":"He received a 15-year sentence for the murder of his friend."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If a judge sentences someone, they decide on a punishment for a crime.","e":"He was sentenced to 15 years in jail for the murder of his friend."}]}]},"place":{"h":"place","i":"/pleɪs/","a":"en-us-place.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A place is a point in space: a town, building, room, or even somewhere on a desk.","e":"It's nice to see the whole family together in one place."},{"m":"(countable) A place is an open space, courtyard, or marketplace."},{"m":"(countable) A place is a group of houses."},{"m":"(countable) A place is an area of land."},{"m":"(countable) A place is someones' frame of mind."},{"m":"(countable) A place is an area for someone to sit at.","e":"We would like to sit at that table because it has three places open."},{"m":"(countable) A place is a role or position; it is a station."},{"m":"(countable) A place is the position in which you finish a competition in.","e":"She finished the poker tournament in fifth place."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you place something somewhere, you put it in a certain spot."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you place, you earn a given spot in a competition.","e":"She finished the poker tournament in fifth place."},{"m":"(transitive) If you place something somewhere, you remember the last time you encountered it.","e":"She placed the last time we met each other at."}]}]},"traditional":{"h":"traditional","i":"/trəˈdɪʃənəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-traditional.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is traditional, it has been done in the same way for a long time.","e":"I learned traditional Japanese cooking from my grandmother."}]}]},"nuclear":{"h":"nuclear","i":"/ˈn(j)ukliɚ/","a":"en-ca-nuclear.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Nuclear weapons, power, waste, etc. is produced by the collision of more than one nucleus, the central part of an atom.","e":"Japan relies mainly on nuclear power (atomic energy) generation for its energy needs."}]}]},"decade":{"h":"decade","i":"/dəˈkeɪd/","a":"en-us-decade.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A decade is a period of 10 years.","e":"The 1960s was a decade of great change in North America."}]}]},"previous":{"h":"previous","i":"/ˈpri.vi.əs/","a":"en-us-previous.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something happened at a previous time, it happened before a particular time.","e":"Last year, we lived in Seoul, but the previous year we were in Moscow."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"(sometimes after the noun) You use previous to refer to a time before something else.","e":"The history of this site previous to the seventeenth century is unknown."}]}]},"consist":{"h":"consist","i":"/kənˈsɪst/","a":"en-us-consist-verb.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If A consists of B, then B is the thing or things that, together, make A.","e":"His letter consisted of only three words."}]}]},"generation":{"h":"generation","i":"/ˌʤɛnəˈreɪʃən/","a":"en-us-generation.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A generation, is all the people or things of about the same age.","e":"My father belonged to a generation of travellers who saw the world before there was a McDonalds on every corner."},{"m":"(countable) A generation is the average time between one when group of people were born and when their children were born, roughly 20–30 years.","e":"During previous generations, travel was not so easy."},{"m":"(countable) A class or type of objects usually developed from an earlier type.","e":"A new generation of personal computers is about to hit the stores."},{"m":"(uncountable) Generation is the creation of something, often electricity.","e":"The increase in new power generation has not kept up with demand for electricity."}]}]},"adult":{"h":"adult","i":"/əˈdʌlt/","a":"en-us-adult.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An adult is a person who is of the legal age of majority.","e":"At age 18 years, he became an adult, so he could move out without his parents' consent."},{"m":"An adult is a human who is sexually, physically and/or mentally mature.","e":"The Harry Potter series was read mostly by young adults."},{"m":"An adult is a sexually mature nonhuman animal.","e":"Adult female cows feed milk to their offspring."}]}]},"partner":{"h":"partner","i":"/ˈpɑːtnə(r)/","a":"en-us-partner.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Partners are people, usually two, who are together for a particular purpose, such as for business, sports, or a romantic relationship.","e":"My partner, Tom, looks after the administrative parts of the business."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you partner someone, you be their [[#Noun|partner]]."}]}]},"percent":{"h":"percent","i":"/pəˈsɛnt/","a":"en-us-percent.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"You use percent show the number of parts out of a hundred. The symbol for percent is %.","e":"The cost of gas has increased seven percent in the last month."},{"m":"One percent of politicians are (not is) honest."},{"m":"Twenty percent of the water was (not were) dirty."}]}]},"registration":{"h":"registration","a":"en-us-registration.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Registration is the process of registering something.","e":"The soccer club has registration at the school this week."}]}]},"remove":{"h":"remove","i":"/rɪˈmuːv/","a":"en-us-remove.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you remove something, you take it out or away.","e":"After he was shot, the doctor removed three bullets from his leg."}]}]},"child":{"h":"child","i":"/ʧaɪld/","a":"en-us-child.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A child is a young person, usually older than a baby but younger than a teenager.","e":"The children were playing in the park."},{"m":"(countable) A child is the son or daughter of someone.","e":"I am my mother's child in every way."},{"m":"(countable) A child of a particular time, situation, or idea is a person who is strongly influenced by it.","e":"As a child of the 90s, I grew up with computers."},{"m":"(countable) A child is the product or result of something.","e":"This book is the child of an earlier generation of grammatical theory."},{"m":"If a woman is with child, she is pregnant.","e":"She told no one about the sex, even when she realized she was with child."},{"m":"(countable) A child in a tree structure is piece of data, process or object with a role or position closer to the root."}]}]},"error":{"h":"error","i":"/ˈɛrə(r)/","a":"en-us-error.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An error is something which is accidentally not correct.","e":"The bank made an error and gave me too much money."},{"m":"An error can refer to a computer error.","e":"I keep getting errors on my computer program."}]}]},"sibling":{"h":"sibling","i":"/ˈsɪblɪŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-sibling.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sibling is a brother or a sister.","e":"I think I know your sibling."}]}]},"shirt":{"h":"shirt","i":"/ʃɜːt/","a":"en-us-shirt.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A shirt is a piece of clothing you wear on the upper part of your body. Shirts are not very thick.","e":"I need a new shirt to go with my new pants."}]}]},"eye":{"h":"eye","i":"/aɪ/","a":"en-us-eye.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Your eyes are the part of your head which you see with.","e":"We saw the eyes of a big wolf."},{"m":"(countable) An eye is a hole at the blunt end of a needle through which thread is passed."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To look at carefully or with interest."}]}]},"harmony":{"h":"harmony","i":"/ˈhɑrməni/","a":"en-us-harmony.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Harmony is when two or more notes sound good at the same time."},{"m":"In art, harmony is using colors which look good together."},{"m":"A feeling of harmony means a feeling of close understanding with no conflict.","e":"After a month walking in the countryside, I really felt in harmony with nature."}]}]},"blood":{"h":"blood","i":"/blʌd/","a":"en-us-blood.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Blood is a red liquid inside a person or animal's body that carries nutrients and oxygen to the other parts of the body.","e":"I'm taking medication for high blood pressure."},{"m":"(uncountable) The family that you were born in is your blood."}]}]},"bucket":{"h":"bucket","i":"/ˈbʌkɪt/","a":"en-us-bucket.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A bucket is a container used for carrying things like water or sand."}]}]},"coal":{"h":"coal","i":"/kəʊl/","a":"en-us-coal.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Coal is a fuel which comes from under the ground. It is black, or sometimes brown. People often burn it for heat."}]}]},"blade":{"h":"blade","i":"/bleɪd/","a":"en-us-blade.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A blade is something with a long, sharp edge. Things like knives, swords and razors have blades."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If a person blades, they skate on rollerblades."},{"m":"(transitive) If you blade someone, you stab them with a [[#Noun|blade]]."}]}]},"bag":{"h":"bag","i":"/ˈbæɡ/","a":"en-us-bag.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Bags are containers made of soft material like paper, plastic or leather.","e":"I put the garbage in a black plastic bag."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When a person bags something, he catches or gets it.","e":"I hope I bag me something good today from him."},{"m":"When an animal is bagged, such as in hunting and fishing, the animal is killed or caught.","e":"Last night on our hunting trip we bagged three deer."},{"m":"Bagging objects means to put them into a bag.","e":"The clerk bagged up the groceries as she took out her wallet."}]}]},"blow":{"h":"blow","i":"/blɔʊ/","a":"en-us-blow.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If wind, air, etc. blows, it moves.","e":"The wind is blowing and the trees are moving."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something blows, the air moves it.","e":"His hat blew off."},{"m":"If you blow, you push air out of your mouth or nose.","e":"She blew her nose into a tissue."},{"m":"If a horn, whistle, etc. blows, it makes a sound.","e":"When the final whistle blew, Arsenal had won the game 2 -- 0."},{"m":"If something blows up, it explodes.","e":"The car blew up as it drove over the bomb."},{"m":"(transitive) If something blows you away, it surprises or impresses you.","e":"We were blown away. We couldnt believe that a ten-year-old could do that."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you blow up, you get angry.","e":"I dropped the cake and she totally blew up on me."},{"m":"If something blows up, it gets bigger.","e":"Can you blow that picture up a bit more? I can't see it clearly."},{"m":"If something is blown off, away, or out, apart, etc., it is damaged by an explosion or a bullet.","e":"BANG! The shot blew off one of his fingers."},{"m":"(transitive) If you blow something, you do not do it successfully.","e":"I can't believe it. You almost had it, but you blew it."},{"m":"(transitive) If you blow money, you spend it, often without being careful."},{"m":"If a piece of equipment blows, it stops working because there is an electrical problem."},{"m":"If a tire blows, it gets a hole, letting out its air quickly.","e":"His little joke had been blown out of proportion and he'd gotten in a lot of trouble."},{"m":"(transitive) If something is blown out of proportion, it is exaggerated."},{"m":"(transitive) If you blow by something, you move past it very quickly."},{"m":"(transitive) If you blow someone, you perform oral sex on them."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A blow is a hit.","e":"He spent two days in hospital after a serious blow to the head."},{"m":"(countable) A blow is something bad that happens.","e":"The team was dealt a terrible blow when goalie Ryan Francis was killed."},{"m":"(countable) A blow is an action of blowing.","e":"He gave a quick blow on the whistle."},{"m":"."}]}]},"angle":{"h":"angle","i":"/æŋgəl̩/","a":"en-us-angle.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) When two straight lines come together, they make an angle.","e":"A 90° angle is called a right angle."}]}]},"collar":{"h":"collar","i":"/ˈkɒl.ə/","a":"en-us-collar.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The neck part of a shirt, coat etc.","e":"He put up his collar because of the cold wind."},{"m":"(countable) A circular piece of fabric that is put around the neck of an animal.","e":"The collar on the dog had a tag that allowed the workers at the animal shelter to identify the owner."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To put a collar on someone or something.","e":"Collar and leash your dog."},{"m":"(law enforcement) To arrest.","e":"The police collared the burglar last night."}]}]},"hand":{"h":"hand","i":"/hænd/","a":"en-us-hand.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Your hands are the parts of your body at the end of your arms. A hand has four fingers and a thumb.","e":"Mother, I'm afraid, please hold my hand."},{"m":"(countable) Clock hands are pointed needles that show what time it is.","e":"The long hand is pointing to the 4, which refers to how many hours have passed. The short hand is pointing to the 7, which refers to how many groups of 5 minutes have passed. The time is therefore 4:35."},{"m":"(countable) A hand is a group of things that fit in your hand, like playing cards.","e":"He had a good hand but he still lost. He is not good at poker."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If I hand you something, I give it to you.","e":"Please hand me that tool. I can't reach it."}]}]},"glove":{"h":"glove","i":"/ɡlʌv/","a":"en-us-glove.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A glove is a piece of clothing you wear on your hand to keep your hands warm or safe.","e":"Police officers often wear gloves when working in crime scenes to avoid destroying evidence."}]}]},"market":{"h":"market","i":"/ˈmɑːkɪt/","a":"en-us-market.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A market is a place where many people come to buy and sell things.","e":"It's time to take the cows to the market."},{"m":"(countable) The market is the stock market.","e":"The market rose Tuesday on good results from the banking sector."},{"m":"(countable) A market is a group of people or businesses that might buy goods or services.","e":"The government is trying to help farmers find a new market for their grain."},{"m":"(countable) A market is the total amount or value of a particular kind of goods or services bought or sold.","e":"The company already has a 54-percent share of the commercial jet market."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you market something, you make it available for sale and you try to get people to buy it.","e":"Manufacturers who spend millions to develop new drugs heavily market their products."}]}]},"card":{"h":"card","i":"/kɑːd/","a":"en-us-card.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A card is a small, often rectangular piece of paper or plastic, usually with information.","e":"The police stopped me and asked to see my identity card."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you card someone, you check their ID [[#Noun|cards]], usually to see if they are old enough to enter a place or drink alcohol.","e":"They have to card anybody who looks 30 or younger."}]}]},"beautiful":{"h":"beautiful","i":"/ˈbjuːtɪfəl/","a":"en-us-beautiful.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is beautiful, it is very good to look at it.","e":"Look at that beautiful bird!"}]}]},"horse":{"h":"horse","i":"/hɔː(r)s/","a":"en-us-horse.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A horse is a hoofed mammal. It walks on four (4) legs. People often ride on horses.","e":"The horse likes to eat oats."}]}]},"feather":{"h":"feather","i":"/ˈfɛð.ə(r)/","a":"en-us-feather.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Feathers are the things which cover birds.","e":"The bird was covered in feathers."}]}]},"decline":{"h":"decline","i":"/dəˈklɑɪn/","a":"en-us-decline.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If something declines, it goes down in number, quality, slope, or value.","e":"The Australian dollar has declined 3% against the Euro."},{"m":"If someone declines an offer, they do not accept it.","e":"We asked Josh to come with us to the restaurant, but he declined."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A decline happens when the number, quality, slope, or value of something goes down.","e":"There has been a 3% decline in the Australian dollar against the Euro."},{"m":"(countable) A decline is a hill or line that goes down.","e":"The truck crashed after picking up too much speed on the decline."}]}]},"conversation":{"h":"conversation","i":"/ˌkɒnvəˈseɪʃən/","a":"en-us-conversation.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A conversation is when two or more people are talking informally.","e":"I had a really interesting conversation at work about how to improve things."}]}]},"plate":{"h":"plate","i":"/pleɪt/","a":"en-us-plate.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A plate is a hard flat thing, especially round ones that we put food on.","e":"He ate everything on his plate."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you plate food, you place the food on a [[#Noun|plate]]."},{"m":"If you plate A with B, you cover the surface of A with a thin coat of B.","e":"This ring is plated with a thin layer of gold."}]}]},"host":{"h":"host","i":"/həʊst/","a":"en-us-host.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A host is a person or animal who makes a place for others and usually provides food and drink.","e":"The host of the party was so busy, she didn't have time to eat."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you host a party or event, you make a place for it and you help to organise it.","e":"Germany hosted the 2006 World Cup of Soccer."}]}]},"finger":{"h":"finger","i":"/ˈfɪŋɡɚ/","a":"en-us-finger.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A finger is a long thin part of your hand that bends. Most people have four fingers and one thumb on each hand.","e":"He only uses one finger on the keyboard."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you finger something, you touch with your fingers it to see what it feels like."},{"m":"(transitive) If you finger someone, you tell the police that the person did something wrong."},{"m":"(transitive) If you finger a female, you use your [[#Noun|finger]]s to penetrate or sexually stimulate their vulva or vagina."}]}]},"loud":{"h":"loud","i":"/laʊd/","a":"en-us-loud.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a sound is loud, you can hear it very easily. If it's very loud, it might hurt your ears.","e":"Can you turn down the music, please? It's too loud."},{"m":"If a person is loud, they talk too much or too loudly.","e":"After he has a few beers he gets really loud."},{"m":"If colours, clothes, or other things you see are loud, they have too many bright colours or patterns and they don't look good."}]}]},"invent":{"h":"invent","i":"/ɪnˈvɛnt/","a":"en-us-invent.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you invent something, you make or design a new kind of thing.","e":"Thomas Edison invented the electric light bulb."}]}]},"thumb":{"h":"thumb","i":"/θʌm/","a":"en-us-thumb.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A thumb is the part of your hand that looks like a short, fat finger. Most people have a thumb on each hand.","e":"In many countries, pointing your thumb up means, \"good\"."},{"m":"(countable) A thumb or thumbnail is a small picture on a computer that you can click on to see a larger picture."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If someone thumbs something, they touch it with the thumb."},{"m":"When someone thumbs, they are standing by a road waiting for someone to give them a ride.","e":"I thumbed down a pickup truck to take me to San Antonio."}]}]},"interrupt":{"h":"interrupt","i":"/ˌɪntəˈrʌpt/","a":"en-us-interrupt.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you interrupt someone, you stop them doing or saying one thing, and often ask them to do another.","e":"Please, don't interrupt me when I'm thinking."}]}]},"exciting":{"h":"exciting","i":"/ɪkˈsaɪtɪŋ/","a":"en-us-exciting.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is exciting, it makes you feel happy and very awake.","e":"The first time I went on a plane, it was so exciting that I almost couldn't breathe."}]}]},"guest":{"h":"guest","i":"/gɛst/","a":"en-us-guest.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A guest is a person who you welcome into your house, your office, etc.","e":"There were over 200 guests at our wedding party."}]}]},"shout":{"h":"shout","i":"/ʃaʊt/","a":"en-us-shout.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you shout, you speak very loudly.","e":"Don't shout! I can hear you fine."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A shout is when somebody shouts one time.","e":"His angry shouts and yelling woke me up."}]}]},"lucky":{"h":"lucky","i":"/ˈlʌki/","a":"en-us-lucky.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are lucky, you have a lot of luck.","e":"After getting married and winning $1 million on the same day, Susan felt very lucky."},{"m":"If something is lucky, it gives you luck.","e":"Today I have three tests, so I'm wearing my lucky hat."}]}]},"luck":{"h":"luck","i":"/lʌk/","a":"en-us-luck.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Someone who has good luck is someone who regularly has good things happen to them, almost as if by magic.","e":"Many people believe the number 13 will bring you bad luck."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) To succeed by chance.","e":"He lucked into a great job."}]}]},"alive":{"h":"alive","i":"/ʌˈlaɪv/","a":"en-us-alive.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone or something is alive, it is living or it continues to exist. If you are alive you have life.","e":"The doctors tried to keep her alive, but she died an hour after arriving at the hospital."}]}]},"hungry":{"h":"hungry","i":"/ˈhʌŋɡɚ/","a":"en-us-hunger.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you feel hungry, you want to eat something and your stomach feels empty.","e":"There are too many poor children who are always hungry."}]}]},"rude":{"h":"rude","i":"/ruːd/","a":"en-us-rude.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is rude or does something rude, they act in a way that will likely upset people.","e":"Don't interrupt me when I'm speaking. It's rude."}]}]},"beg":{"h":"beg","i":"/bɛg/","a":"en-us-beg.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you beg someone for something or to do something, you ask them very strongly, but you are in a weak position.","e":"He had a gun to my head. I begged him, \"Please, don't shoot me.\""}]}]},"greet":{"h":"greet","i":"/gri:t/","a":"en-us-greet.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you greet someone or something, you meet them and say, \"hello\" or welcome them somehow.","e":"The tour guide greeted us when we arrived at the airport."}]}]},"insult":{"h":"insult","i":"/ɪnˈsʌlt/","a":"en-us-insult.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you insult someone, you say or do something rude to them.","e":"He insulted me by calling my country a dirty little city."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An insult is a rude word or action.","e":"The protesters yelled insults at the police."}]}]},"hall":{"h":"hall","i":"/hɔːl/","a":"en-us-hall.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hall is a large space with a roof and walls. It can be a kind of large building, or a room or part of a building. Most commonly, it is the area just inside the front door.","e":"Please leave your boots in the front hall."}]}]},"invite":{"h":"invite","i":"/ɪnˈvaɪt/","a":"en-us-invite.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you invite someone to something, you ask them to be there.","e":"Rasheed invited me to his house on Friday, but I don't think I can go."}]}]},"weapon":{"h":"weapon","i":"/wɛpən/","a":"en-us-weapon.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A weapon is a tool that you use in a fight, such as a knife, a gun, or a bomb.","e":"\"Lay down your weapons and put your hands in the air,\" yelled the police."}]}]},"holiday":{"h":"holiday","i":"/ˈhɒlɪdeɪ/","a":"en-us-holiday.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A holiday is a day when people don't go to work or school, often because there is a religious celebration.","e":"In North America, Christmas is the biggest holiday of the year."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you holiday, you take a period of time away from work or study."}]}]},"patience":{"h":"patience","i":"/ˈpeɪʃəns/","a":"en-us-inlandnorth-patience.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) If someone has patience, they can wait without feeling upset.","e":"Andrew has so much patience with the children; I just get so angry with them."}]}]},"afraid":{"h":"afraid","i":"/əˈfreɪd/","a":"en-us-afraid.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"To be afraid of someone or something means to be scared of someone or something; to have a fear of someone or something.","e":"I'm afraid of snakes. I can't even go near them."}]}]},"tool":{"h":"tool","i":"/tuːl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-tool.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A tool is an object that you use to do a specific job, such as a hammer.","e":"I used to fix my own car, but I sold all my tools."},{"m":"(countable) A tool is a person being used by another person or organization.","e":"He is such a tool. He should think for himself, instead of doing everything they tell him to do."}]}]},"bite":{"h":"bite","i":"/baɪt/","a":"en-us-bite.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If a person or animal bites something, they put it between their teeth and squeeze.","e":"I'm afraid of dogs. I think they'll bite me."},{"m":"If an insect bites someone, it puts a substance into your skin."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"One bite is the amount of food that can go in your mouth at one time."},{"m":"An insect bite is the itchy mark on the skin of a person or animal where an insect has bitten them."}]}]},"essential":{"h":"essential","i":"/ɪˈsɛn.tʃəl/","a":"en-us-essential.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is essential, it is impossible to succeed without it.","e":"Oxygen is essential for life on earth."},{"m":"If something is essential, it is very important.","e":"Cooked rice, is the essential element of the Chinese meal prepared south of the Yangtze River."},{"m":"The essential part, idea, or feature is the most basic one.","e":"The essential nature of skiing is sliding on two skis, but the sport is much more than that."}]}]},"time":{"h":"time","i":"/taɪm/","a":"en-us-time.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Time is what we measure with a clock.","e":"\"What time do you finish work?\" \"At four o'clock (4:00).\""},{"m":"(countable) If you do something one time, you do it once."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you time something, you measure how long it takes in seconds, minutes, hours, etc.","e":"Take out your watch and time yourself during the test."}]}]},"mother":{"h":"mother","i":"/ˈmʌðə/","a":"en-us-mother.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mother is the woman who is one of a person or animal's parents.","e":"My mother read me a story and put me to bed every night when I was a child."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you mother someone, you take care of them as if you were their mother."}]}]},"work":{"h":"work","i":"/wɜːk/","a":"en-us-work.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you work, you do a job, usually for money.","e":"My father works at Microsoft."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you work you are doing something that needs effort.","e":"I worked on my school paper all night long."},{"m":"(intransitive) If somethings works it has done what it was supposed to do.","e":"If my computer didn't work I couldn't type this."},{"m":"(intransitive) How something works is how it does what it does.","e":"I would like to know more about how cars work."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Your work is your job."},{"m":"(uncountable) Work is effort it takes to do something. That is, its what makes you tired when you do something hard.","e":"Moving heavy logs takes a lot of work."},{"m":"(uncountable); Work is force through a distance (force times distance). This is how much energy you used to move something."},{"m":"(countable) A work is the product of something, the result of working on it. That is, its something someone has made.","e":"The painting was a great work of art."}]}]},"move":{"h":"move","i":"/muːv/","a":"en-us-move.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you move, you go from one place to another.","e":"Please stay in your seat until the plane stops moving."},{"m":"If you move, you change the position of part of your body.","e":"I was so afraid, I couldn't move."},{"m":"(transitive) If you move something, you change its position.","e":"Can you move your chair so I can get by?"}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A move is something which is done to achieve a goal.","e":"The move had not been expected."},{"m":"(countable) is a change in your home or business to live or work somewhere else.","e":"The move to the city was completed in a week."},{"m":"(countable) A move, in a game such as chess, is when you put a piece in another place.","e":"The move of the queen led to his loss."}]}]},"proud":{"h":"proud","i":"/praʊd/","a":"en-us-proud.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are proud of or about something you have done, you feel good about it.","e":"I feel proud that we fought in the war, even if most people think we should have stayed home."},{"m":"If you are proud of someone, you feel happy for them because they have done something well."},{"m":"If you are proud of something you own, you think it is valuable and you are happy about it."}]}]},"zero":{"h":"zero","i":"/ˈzir.oʊ/","a":"en-us-zero.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"Zero is a count of nothing, the number before one. It is often written 0.","e":"It's zero degrees."},{"m":"Zero is also used with an uncountable noun.","e":"I have zero food left."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The symbol for the number zero, that is \"0.\"","e":"The new job added a zero to my pay, from $20,000 to $200,000."},{"m":"A person or thing that is worth nothing.","e":"I'm not inviting him, he's total zero."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To zero is to make a small change to reset a piece of equipment.","e":"I had to zero the counter on my tape player."},{"m":"To zero in is to make small changes that bring you closer to something.","e":"I was able to zero in on the source of bad smell in the shed."}]}]},"amusing":{"h":"amusing","i":"/əˈmjuːzɪŋ/","a":"en-us-amusing.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is amusing, it makes you laugh or it entertains you.","e":"We had a very amusing afternoon playing with the kids, but we didn't get anything done."}]}]},"annoyed":{"h":"annoyed","i":"/əˈnɔɪd/","a":"en-us-annoyed.ogg","l":"annoy","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is annoyed, they are a little angry.","e":"When Graham broke the glass, I was really annoyed, but the face he made was so funny, I had to laugh."}]}]},"excellent":{"h":"excellent","i":"/ˈɛksələnt/","a":"en-us-excellent.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is excellent, it is very, very good.","e":"The tea we had with lunch was excellent. Where did you get it?"}]}]},"hello":{"h":"hello","i":"/həˈləʊ̯/","a":"en-uk-hello.ogg","s":[{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"You say, \"hello\" in greeting when you meet someone new or someone you know.","e":"\"Good morning, James!\" \"Hello, Jimbo! How are you?\""}]}]},"joke":{"h":"joke","i":"/dʒəʊk/","a":"en-us-joke.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) If you tell a joke, you say something to make people laugh.","e":"Trevor's joke about the boring lexicographer was too funny."},{"m":"If something is a joke, it is not considered seriously.","e":"Don't listen to Joseph. He's a joke. Nobody pays any attention to him."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) When you joke about something, you say something funny that you don't really mean.","e":"Everyone joked about how bad his tennis was."},{"m":"(intransitive) You say \"you must be joking\" when somebody tells you something that's very hard to believe.","e":"\"She's forty-three.\" \"Forty-three?! You must be joking. She looks like she's sixteen.\""}]}]},"diverse":{"h":"diverse","i":"/daɪˈvɜːs/","a":"en-us-diverse.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A diverse group of things is a group in which the things are very different from each other.","e":"Toronto has one of the most culturally diverse populations in the world."}]}]},"contradiction":{"h":"contradiction","i":"/ˌkɒntrəˈdɪkʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-contradiction.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A contradiction is the act of contradicting.","e":"He says that he was not there that night: that was a contradiction of his previous statement."},{"m":"A contradiction is a statement which makes two (or more) claims which both cannot be true.","e":"There is a contradiction in saying that she is a widow who never married."}]}]},"ignore":{"h":"ignore","i":"/ɪɡˈnɔː/","a":"en-us-ignore.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you ignore someone or something, you don't listen to, look at, or pay attention to them.","e":"He says he should be paid for fixing it, but he's ignoring the fact that it wasn't broken."}]}]},"significant":{"h":"significant","i":"/sɪɡˈnɪf.ɪ.kənt/","a":"en-us-significant.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is significant, it is important, or large, enough to pay attention to or to believe.","e":"There was a significant drop in the price of gas today, causing drivers to line up at the pumps to fill up."},{"m":"A significant look, movement, etc. is one that has a particular meaning."}]}]},"expert":{"h":"expert","i":"/ˈɛkspɚt/","a":"en-us-expert.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An expert is a person who knows more, or can do something better, than most people, usually because of special study or practice.","e":"Zidane is an expert at penalty kicks."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"An expert skier, teacher, player, etc. is very skillful or experienced.","e":"She's an expert skier, one of the fastest and most beautiful on the hill."}]}]},"media":{"h":"media","i":"/ˈmiːdɪə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-media.wav","l":"medium","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The (mass) media is/are the news sources and the people behind them.","e":"The media have been too accepting of the government's arguments."},{"m":"A medium is a way of information or art.","e":"We have to use music, pictures and other media to sell the product."}]}]},"communicate":{"h":"communicate","i":"/kəˈmjuːnɪkeɪt/","a":"en-us-communicate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you communicate an idea, you make someone else understand your idea, usually by using words.","e":"Parents have to work hard to communicate better with their children."}]}]},"communication":{"h":"communication","i":"/kʌˌmjunɪˈkeɪʃən/","a":"en-us-communication.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Communication is the process of sending and ideas between two or more people.","e":"Teachers must regularly practice their communication skills to make sure students understand them easily."},{"m":"(countable) Communications are the ways of sending and receiving information.","e":"The army is setting up a new communications network to improve communication."}]}]},"classical":{"h":"classical","i":"/ˈklæsɪkl̩/","a":"en-us-classical.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Classical ideas or styles are those that were very common at a time in the past and sometimes continue into the present.","e":"Classical theories in physics can't explain certain observations, which has led scientists to come up with new theories."}]}]},"achieve":{"h":"achieve","i":"/əˈtʃi:v/","a":"en-us-achieve.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you achieve success or a goal, you have completed what you planned to do or have a good result.","e":"She achieved a grade of 98% in her English class."}]}]},"logic":{"h":"logic","i":"/ˈlɒdʒɪk/","a":"en-us-logic.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Logic is a system of careful step by step thought or argument that tries to explain truth.","e":"It wasn't easy to see the logic of her plan."}]}]},"contract":{"h":"contract","i":"/ˈkɒntrækt/","a":"en-uk-contract (noun).ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A contract is a legal agreement to trade goods, services and/or property. It's usually written down.","e":"If you would just sign this contract, the car will be yours."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If something contracts, it gets smaller.","e":"As the wood dries out, it contracts."},{"m":"(transitive) If you contract someone to do a job, you enter into a contract with them.","e":"We've contracted a cleaning company to take care of the office."},{"m":"(transitive) If you contract a disease, you become sick with it.","e":"It's hard to understand why people risk contracting sexually transmitted diseases."}]}]},"atheist":{"h":"atheist","i":"/ˈeɪθiɪst/","a":"en-us-atheist.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (religon) An atheist is a person who does not believe in a god or gods."}]}]},"humanist":{"h":"humanist","i":"/ˈhjuːmənɪst/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Humanists are people who believe in \"doing good\" for all people."}]}]},"environment":{"h":"environment","i":"/ɪnˈvaɪə.rən.ment/","a":"en-us-environment.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The environment is the natural world: forests, rivers, grasslands, oceans, etc.","e":"We have to do more to protect the environment from pollution."},{"m":"Your environment is the situation or area that you live, work, or spend time in, including the people, buildings, vehicles, etc.","e":"When we moved to the city, we found ourselves in a comepletely new social environment."}]}]},"export":{"h":"export","i":"/ˈɛks.pɔːt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-export (noun).wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you export something, you send it out of the country, usually for business purposes.","e":"Canada will export up to 450,000 barrels per day of crude oil to China."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Export is the act or business of exporting things.","e":"A shipment of computers is being loaded on the ship for export to Singapore."},{"m":"(countable) An export is something that you send out of the country, usually for business purposes.","e":"Bananas are Ecuador's largest export."}]}]},"source":{"h":"source","i":"/sɔrs/","a":"en-us-source.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you source something, then you obtain or receive it."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The source of some material, an idea, a product, etc. is the place it came from originally.","e":"XYZ company can't supply these parts anymore, so we need to find a new source."}]}]},"assess":{"h":"assess","i":"/əˈsɛs/","a":"en-us-assess.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you assess a person, idea, skill, process, etc., you judge or measure them.","e":"In today's test, we will be assessing your ability to write clearly."}]}]},"policy":{"h":"policy","i":"/ˈpɒləsi/","a":"en-us-policy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A policy is an official rule or idea that explain how to act in certain situations.","e":"The government is suggesting a significant change in economic policy."}]}]},"derive":{"h":"derive","i":"/dəˈraɪvd/","a":"en-us-derive.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If X is derived from Y, X comes from Y in the way that one idea comes from another.","e":"He derived a lot of pleasure from teaching."}]}]},"factor":{"h":"factor","i":"/ˈfæk.tə/","a":"en-us-factor.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A factor is one of a number of things that causes a result.","e":"The main factor in the success of our program is our excellent teachers."},{"m":"(countable) The factor is a number that is with another to form a larger number.","e":"2 x 3 = 6; 2 and 3 are factors of 6."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you factor a number, you find all of its [[#Noun|factors]]."}]}]},"procedure":{"h":"procedure","i":"/prəˈsiːd͡ʒə/","a":"en-us-procedure.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A procedure is a particular way of doing something.","e":"Because police did not follow procedure, the criminal was set free."}]}]},"assessment":{"h":"assessment","i":"/əˈsɛsmənt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-assessment.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An assessment of a person, idea, skill, process, etc. is a judgement or measurement of them.","e":"The results of your recent job assessment are excellent."}]}]},"assume":{"h":"assume","i":"/əˈsjuːm/","a":"en-uk-assume.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you assume something, you think or believe something without having enough information to know that it's true.","e":"Oh, hello. I assume you're the new student, are you?"},{"m":"(transitive) If you assume a role of office, you take on a new position that has more power or responsibility."}]}]},"theory":{"h":"theory","i":"/ˈθɪəri/","a":"en-us-theory.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A theory is an idea that tries to explain an observation.","e":"The new information showed that his theory about growth was incorrect."}]}]},"benefit":{"h":"benefit","i":"/ˈbɛn.ɪ.fɪt/","a":"en-us-benefit.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A benefit is something good that comes from something else.","e":"It was her idea, but she received no benefit from the new program."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you benefit from something, you get something good from it.","e":"My health has really benefited from all the exercise I'm getting."}]}]},"evidence":{"h":"evidence","i":"/ˈɛvɪdəns/","a":"en-us-evidence.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Evidence is facts or observations that support an idea.","e":"The gun is evidence that professor Pickle killed Mr. Mustard."},{"m":"In a courtroom, evidence refers to anything that is shown to the judge that is related to the case during a trial."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you evidence something, you provide [[#Noun|evidence]] or the truth of an event.","e":"Something good must have happened to her, as evidenced by the smile on her face."}]}]},"thesaurus":{"h":"thesaurus","i":"/θɪˈsɔːrəs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-thesaurus.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A thesaurus is a book which lists synonyms (different words which have the same meaning).","e":"A thesaurus usually groups together synonymous words such as schadenfreude and epicaricacy together under a single heading."}]}]},"to":{"h":"to","i":"/tuː/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-to.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) To has no meaning. It is used with a bare infinitival clause.","e":"It's important for you to understand."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"To shows where something goes, the goal of movement.","e":"He went to her house."},{"m":"To shows the receivers of an action or object.","e":"The goods were sold to customers at the downtown store."},{"m":"To shows the result of a change or process.","e":"It switched from red to black."},{"m":"To shows the end or limit of something.","e":"Methods have been used to overcome these problems to some degree."},{"m":"To shows that one thing is touching another.","e":"They stood back to back to see who was taller."},{"m":"To shows how two things are connected.","e":"He attached the printer to the computer."},{"m":"To shows a belonging or relationship.","e":"We don't owe anything to anyone."},{"m":"To shows a comparison between two things.","e":"Girls outnumber boys two to one."},{"m":"To shows your feeling or opinion about something.","e":"It feels good to me."},{"m":"To shows a timing relationship, often with a music.","e":"He likes to exercise to music."}]}]},"aeroplane":{"h":"aeroplane","i":"/ˈeə.rə.pleɪn/","a":"en-uk-aeroplane.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An aeroplane is a vehicle with wings that can fly.","e":"Can we hurry. I have to catch an aeroplane to London."}]}]},"online":{"h":"online","i":"/'ɑnlaɪn/","a":"en-us-online.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If a system is online, it is connected (generally electronically) to a larger network.","e":"I do a lot of shopping online, so I almost never have to leave the house."},{"m":"If a machine is online, it is turned on and is ready to do work.","e":"Since the printer is back online, you should be able to again print from it."}]}]},"writing":{"h":"writing","i":"/ˈraɪtɪŋ/","a":"en-us-writing.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A subject in school where you write stories and poems.","e":"She is taking a class in creative writing."}]}]},"above":{"h":"above","i":"/əˈbʌv/","a":"en-us-above.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If A is above B, A is higher than or before B, but not touching B.","e":"In a newspaper, the title of a story is usually above the story."},{"m":"The above comment, discussion, argument, etc. is one higher than or coming before something.","e":"Please see the above discussion of the problem."}]}]},"option":{"h":"option","i":"/ˈɒpʃən/","a":"en-us-option.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An option is a choice.","e":"He has the option to go to university or join the army."}]}]},"ordinary":{"h":"ordinary","i":"/ˈɔːdɪnəri/","a":"en-us-ordinary.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is ordinary, it is normal and not special.","e":"Today is an ordinary day, just like the last 256."}]}]},"establish":{"h":"establish","i":"/ɪˈstæb.lɪʃ/","a":"en-us-establish.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you establish something, you start it with the idea that it will last for a long time.","e":"A good doctor will not only care for each of the patients but will also be able to establish a good relationship with them."}]}]},"established":{"h":"established","i":"/ɪˈstæb.lɪʃt/","a":"en-us-established.ogg","l":"establish","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If an institution, system, etc. is established, it has existed for some time and is probably well known.","e":"The established church leaders often do no wish to see changes that might reduce their power."}]}]},"end":{"h":"end","i":"/ˈɛnd/","a":"en-us-end.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To put a stop to something.","e":"The movie ends after this scene."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The last one of a group. Or, the last part of a thing, the place where it stops.","e":"I tied a knot in the end of the rope."}]}]},"issue":{"h":"issue","i":"/ˈɪsju/","a":"en-us-issue.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An issue is a particular topic or subject, often one that people are discussing and/or is a problem.","e":"The students raised an important issue in my last class, and I hope we can discuss it today."},{"m":"An issue of a magazine, newspaper, etc. is the version that is published at one time.","e":"The March issue of The Walrus has an interesting article on healthcare."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you issue something, such as a statement, guidelines or an order, you officially publish it.","e":"The governments of Canada and the United States jointly issued a statement about the recent crash."}]}]},"labour":{"h":"labour","i":"/leɪbə/","a":"en-uk-labour.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Labour is the work that people do, usually lifting, moving, building, etc. rather than desk work.","e":"The cost of labour is higher than the cost of building materials."},{"m":"(uncountable) Labour are the people who do this kind of work.","e":"There's a big labour shortage in the construction industry."},{"m":"(uncountable) Labour is the process a pregnant woman goes through when she is giving birth.","e":"She was in labour for more than 12 hours before her baby was bourn."},{"m":"Labour is the name of a big political party in the United Kingdom, Ireland, Australia, and New Zealand.","e":"Labour won the election."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you labour, you work hard.","e":"He laboured over the food all afternoon to get ready for dinner."},{"m":"(transitive) If you labour the point, you keep talking about it after people understand it well."}]}]},"occur":{"h":"occur","i":"/əˈkɜː/","a":"en-us-occur.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If something occurs, it happens.","e":"Over the summer a change occurred in my friend’s behaviour."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something occurs to you, you suddenly think of it.","e":"It occurred to me that I was in trouble."}]}]},"economic":{"h":"economic","i":"/ˌɛkəˈnɒmɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-economic.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"About or relating to the economy, business, money, etc.","e":"The reduction in unemployment and continued economic growth are good news for workers."},{"m":"If a business activity is economic, it makes enough money.","e":"As a small business, do you think it would be economic for us to advertise on TV?"}]}]},"involved":{"h":"involved","i":"/ɪnˈvɑlvd/","a":"en-us-involved.ogg","l":"involve","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If X is involved (in Y), X does Y or is connected to Y","e":"My teacher's very involved in politics."},{"m":"If something is involved, it is complicated.","e":"I can't explain it. It's all rather involved."}]}]},"interpretation":{"h":"interpretation","i":"/ɪntɚprəˈteɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-interpretation.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An interpretation is an attempt to understand something.","e":"Weather forecasters use a lot of data, but the interpretation of the data is very difficult."},{"m":"(countable) An interpretation is one meaning that something might have, or one way that one person understands something.","e":"I don't think your interpretation is what the writer meant."},{"m":"An interpretation expresses an individual’s opinion about artistic work.","e":"One interpretation of \"Alive\" is that people will do anything to survive."}]}]},"consistent":{"h":"consistent","i":"/kənˈsɪs.tənt/","a":"en-us-consistent.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is consistent, it is regular and you can guess what it will be like in the future.","e":"She makes a consistent effort to study hard."},{"m":"If X is consistent with Y, then X fits or matches Y.","e":"The theory is consistent with the data."},{"m":"always behaving or happening in a similar, especially positive, way","e":"My Math scores are consistent because I always get an A on quizzes and exams."}]}]},"income":{"h":"income","i":"/ˈɪnˌkʌm/","a":"en-us-income.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Income is the money that you get from working.","e":"Generally, teachers have a lower income than business people."},{"m":"Income is what you get for selling products you make or grow.","e":"He gets a lot of his income from the corn he grows."}]}]},"concept":{"h":"concept","i":"/ˈkɒn.sɛpt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-concept.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A concept is an idea.","e":"Italy has introduced the concept of \"parental leave\" – time off work given to either parent to look after the child."}]}]},"formula":{"h":"formula","i":"/ˈfɔr.mjə.lə/","a":"en-uk-formula.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A formula is a way to do something or solve a problem that does not change much.","e":"There is no formula for making profit, yet many business people think there is."},{"m":"Infant formula is a powder that you mix with water to make a drink for babies."}]}]},"install":{"h":"install","i":"/ɪnˈstɔːl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-install.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you install a piece of hardward or software, you connect, set up or prepare it to be used.","e":"I haven't installed the new operating system yet because of all the bugs."},{"m":"(transitive) If you install someone in an office, rank or position, you officially place them there.","e":"He was installed as Chancellor of the University."},{"m":"(transitive) If you install yourself somewhere, you establish yourself there or settle in.","e":"I installed myself in my usual chair by the fire."}]}]},"section":{"h":"section","i":"/ˈsɛk.ʃən/","a":"en-us-section.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A section of a thing or place is a part of it.","e":"The police closed one section of the road because of the accident."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you section something, you divide it into parts."}]}]},"constitutional":{"h":"constitutional","a":"en-us-constitutional.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a law, a right, an action, etc. is constitutional, it is legal within the constitution of the particular country.","e":"The court ruled that the new law was constitutional and that there was no need for the government to change it."},{"m":"If something is constitutional it is related to a constitution.","e":"I think freedom of speech should be a constitutional right for everyone because everyone should have right to speak out."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"If you take a constitutional, you go for a walk for exercise or health. (old fashioned word)","e":"He's nearly 80 and still takes a constitutional every morning."}]}]},"constitution":{"h":"constitution","i":"/ˌkɒnstɪˈtjuːʃən/","a":"en-us-constitution.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The constitution of a country or organization is the basic set of laws that explain how all the other laws and rules must be made and followed.","e":"To change the constitution, the government must have the agreement of 2/3 of the members of parliament."},{"m":"(countable) The constitution of a person or object is the that best define that person or object.","e":"His stubborn constitution led him into a number of conflicts he could have avoided."}]}]},"analysis":{"h":"analysis","i":"/əˈnælɪsɪs/","a":"en-us-analysis.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"If you do an analysis, you study something carefully to understand it.","e":"We performed a detailed analysis of the relationship between the two companies and believe that they could form a strong partnership."}]}]},"distribution":{"h":"distribution","i":"/ˌdɪstrəˈbjuːʃən/","a":"en-us-distribution.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Distribution is sending or giving out things to several people, companies, places, etc.","e":"The distribution of the mail was slowed by the snow storm."},{"m":"(countable) Distribution is the way that things are spread (often used in statistics).","e":"The distribution of the new iPad was very fast because Apple had invested a lot on advertisement."}]}]},"function":{"h":"function","i":"/ˈfʌŋk.ʃən/","a":"en-us-function.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Something or someone's function is its purpose or its job.","e":"The army sometimes performs a policing function."},{"m":"(countable) A function is an organised event.","e":"I met Sylvia at a church function last week."},{"m":"(countable) If X is a function of Y, then X exists because of or is affected by Y","e":"The speed of the computer is a function of its main processor."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If something is functioning, it is working and is not completely broken.","e":"Her heart stopped, but her brain continued to function."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something functions as X, it does the job of X.","e":"In this sentence, \"sentence\" functions as the subject."}]}]},"approach":{"h":"approach","i":"/əˈprəʊtʃ/","a":"en-us-approach.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you approach something, you move closer to it.","e":"We're now approaching the last bus stop. Please move towards the door."},{"m":"(transitive) If you approach a problem, or a job you try to deal with it.","e":"We've got a difficult situation here, and I'm not sure how to approach it."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An approach is a way of doing something.","e":"We need children and adults to take a proactive approach to reducing gun violence."},{"m":"(countable) An approach is movement towards something.","e":"And he made a cautious approach to the boat."},{"m":"(countable) An approach is the road or path that leads to a place.","e":"There were cameras on all approaches to the house."}]}]},"legislation":{"h":"legislation","i":"/ˌledʒ.ɪˈsleɪ.ʃən/","a":"en-us-legislation.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Legislation is the official laws and rules of a government.","e":"City council is planning new legislation regarding recycling."},{"m":"(uncountable) Legislation is the process of making and passing laws.","e":"The government has the power of legislation."}]}]},"tend":{"h":"tend","i":"/tɛnd/","a":"en-us-tend.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To tend to do something means inclined or likely to do something.","e":"The streets are very confusing in Tokyo and people tend to get lost."},{"m":"(transitive) If you tend something, you watch and take care of it.","e":"The children often help with chores, including cutting the grass and tending the garden."},{"m":"If x tends towards y, x is usually y.","e":"My artwork tends towards the modern."},{"m":"If you tend bar, you work at a bar selling drinks."},{"m":"If something tends in a particular direction, you generally moves in that direction.","e":"The price of gold has tended upward for about three years."}]}]},"quack":{"h":"quack","i":"/kwæk/","a":"en-us-quack.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The sound made by a duck","e":"The duck went \"quack quack\"."},{"m":"(countable) A fake or incompetent healer or doctor.","e":"That doctor is nothing but a lousy quack!"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To make a noise like a duck.","e":"The more bread I threw on the ground, the more they quacked."}]}]},"role":{"h":"role","i":"/rəʊl/","a":"en-us-role.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The role of a person or thing is the job that they do in a certain situation.","e":"In the past twenty-five years the role of women on farms had changed dramatically."},{"m":"role is another word for a part in a theatrical work such as a play or a ballet","e":"Tamara Karsavina was the first to dance the role of the Firebird."}]}]},"indicate":{"h":"indicate","i":"/ˈɪndɪˌkeɪt/","a":"en-us-indicate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If someone indicates something, they point it out or they point to it; they bring your attention to something.","e":"Brian indicated to his girlfriend the restaurant they were going to on the map."},{"m":"(transitive) If someone indicates something, they show signs of something; they show it.","e":"A driver has to turn on the signal in order to indicated that he will turn right."},{"m":"(transitive) If something indicates something, it shows it through measurements; it makes something known.","e":"The turn signal indicates that a driver will turn."},{"m":"(transitive) If someone indicate something, they express it, usually in a short or general way; they signal it.","e":"Hailey indicated that she was sick to her friends, but would not say any more about it."},{"m":"(transitive), If a symptom indicates something, it points out a remedy that would help to cure that symptom."}]}]},"context":{"h":"context","i":"/ˈkɒntɛkst/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-context.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Something's context is the situation that it happens in.","e":"Sometime, we can't read someone's writing, but the message can be understood in context because human readers use their knowledge of language and the world to help us."}]}]},"basket":{"h":"basket","i":"/ˈbɑːskɪt/","a":"en-us-basket.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A basket is something like a bucket but with many holes like a net, made of soft sticks or grass or other long, thin material. People put things in the basket."},{"m":"(countable) A basket is a net on a metal circle used in playing basketball."},{"m":"(countable) A basket is a container that is used to hold items that you are wanting to purchase in a store.","e":"She put the soup that she took off the shelf in the store into the basket."}]}]},"basketball":{"h":"basketball","i":"/ˈbɑːs.kɪt.bɔːl/","a":"en-us-basketball.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A ball game with two teams of five players. A goal is scored when a player throws the ball into a net (attached to a hoop) at each end of the court.","e":"I play on my school's basketball team."},{"m":"(countable) A ball used in the game of basketball.","e":"Throw the basketball to me."}]}]},"player":{"h":"player","i":"/ˈpleɪɚ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-player.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Someone taking part in a sport or game.","e":"Tom watched as the players walked on to the field."},{"m":"(countable) Someone who makes music on a musical instrument.","e":"The piano player had long fingers."},{"m":"(countable) An actor, in particular on a theatre stage.","e":"The players are all on the stage."},{"m":"(countable) A machine that plays music recordings or movies.","e":"The record player is broken"}]}]},"male":{"h":"male","i":"/meɪl/","a":"en-us-male.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A person, animal, or plant that is male produces sperm or pollen. Boys and men are male people.","e":"The male dog is usually larger than the female one."},{"m":"If something is male, it is of, for, or about men or boys.","e":"The boys can change in the male changing room over there."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A male is a person, animal, or plant that cannot have or eggs.","e":"In humans males are called men or boys"}]}]},"pervious":{"h":"pervious","i":"/ˈpɜː.vi.əs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-pervious.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is pervious it lets water pass through it.","e":"This piece of tissue paper is pervious."},{"m":"If someone is pervious they are open to accepting new ideas."}]}]},"invention":{"h":"invention","i":"/ɪnˈvɛnʃən/","a":"en-us-invention.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"something that has been invented","e":"Nowadays, we can buy new inventions as soon as they are made."},{"m":"the action of inventing something"},{"m":"the ability to invent","e":"It took quite a bit of invention to come up with the toothbrush."}]}]},"range":{"h":"range","i":"/reɪndʒ/","a":"en-us-range.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A range of X is a number of different kinds of Xs","e":"We offer you a whole range of clothes, from socks to hats."},{"m":"(countable) The range is area between an upper and lower limit.","e":"Most accidents affect children in the seven to 10 age range."},{"m":"(countable) Something's range is the distance that it can travel.","e":"The company's newest airplane has a range of 10,556&nbsp;km."},{"m":"(countable) In statistics, the range of results is highest result minus the lowest result.","e":"The test results in the study had a range of 63; the highest was 100 and the lowest 37."},{"m":"(countable) A (mountain) range is a group of mountains."},{"m":"(countable) A shooting range is a place to practice using a gun."},{"m":"(countable) A range is a large grassy area for farm animals to walk about freely."},{"m":"(countable) A range is a large stove for cooking."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If something ranges from X to Y, it includes a number of different things and X and Y are different examples of those.","e":"The police had stopped him for a variety of things ranging from stealing a book to having a gun."},{"m":"If something ranges around an area, it moves around it."}]}]},"construction":{"h":"construction","i":"/kənˈstrʌkʃən/","a":"en-us-construction.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Construction is the act of building something.","e":"The workers began construction of the new hospital last week."},{"m":"Construction is the way that something is made.","e":"The stone construction of these buildings makes them very cold in the winter."},{"m":"In language, a construction is a combination of form and meaning.","e":"Spoken English doesn't use as many passive constructions as written English."},{"m":"A construction is a particular way that something is understood.","e":"In this book, the meaning of \"man\" is not a simple natural thing; it is a social construction."},{"m":"A construction is a building, bridge, tower, model, or large piece of art.","e":"A large and unusual construction stood just outside town."}]}]},"strategy":{"h":"strategy","i":"/ˈstrætədʒi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-strategy.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A strategy is a planned way to do something.","e":"The new government is likely to change the economic strategy because the old strategy clearly isn't working."},{"m":"Strategy is the skill of planning.","e":"You can't just do whatever comes into your head. You need to have a strategy."}]}]},"conclusion":{"h":"conclusion","i":"/kənˈklu:ʒən/","a":"en-us-conclusion.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A writer or speaker's conclusions are the ideas that they have after thinking about all the important information.","e":"The study's main conclusion is that more money will not solve the problem."},{"m":"The conclusion is the end.","e":"At the conclusion of the story, we still don't know why he did it."}]}]},"security":{"h":"security","i":"/sɪˈkjʊərəti/","a":"en-us-security.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Security is safety.","e":"Traditionally, Japanese workers have had good job security. In fact, they usually had a job for life."},{"m":"Security is the people and things that keep you safe.","e":"After the bombing, the airport increased security."},{"m":"(finance) A security is a proof of ownership of stocks and other investments."}]}]},"far":{"h":"far","i":"/fɑː/","a":"en-us-far.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"a long distance away","e":"He got tired after walking so far."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"distant.","e":"I saw her at the far side of the room."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"very much, or to a great degree.","e":"He's not just a little bit better; he's far better."}]}]},"future":{"h":"future","i":"/ˈfjuːʧə/","a":"en-us-future.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The future is the time of something that hasn't happen yet. The study of the future is known as futurology.","e":"I will be more careful in the future."},{"m":"A look forward.","e":"You have a great future ahead of you."},{"m":"A future event is one that hasn't happened yet but will happen."}]}]},"here":{"h":"here","i":"/hɪə/","a":"en-us-here.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"(in, at or to) this place","e":"Why are you looking over there for the book? It's right here."}]}]},"late":{"h":"late","i":"/leɪt/","a":"en-us-late.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"An event is late if it happens after a specified time.","e":"He was late to his appointment."},{"m":"If something is late in a period of time, it is towards the end of that time.","e":"You come in the late afternoon."},{"m":"A late relative, president, colleague, etc is dead.","e":"I loved my late husband."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Not on time.","e":"He came five minutes late."},{"m":"Late at night.","e":"We stayed late and went home in the dark."}]}]},"least":{"h":"least","i":"/liːst/","a":"en-us-least.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"the smallest amount of; little of","e":"She does the most cleaning, but the least cooking."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Having the smallest amount of a characteristic in a group.","e":"People are least likely to live in the far north."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"The least is the smallest amount, importance, duration, etc.","e":"The power is least in this case."}]}]},"leather":{"h":"leather","i":"/ˈlɛðə/","a":"en-us-leather.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A tanned animal skin.","e":"He took the leather and made a coat from it."}]}]},"let":{"h":"let","i":"/lεt/","a":"en-us-let.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you let someone do something, you allow them to do it.","e":"I let him come with me."},{"m":"When you let a building or a space in a building, you rent it.","e":"I will let my extra room to him."}]}]},"lip":{"h":"lip","i":"/lɪp/","a":"en-us-lip.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The edge of an opening, especially, the human mouth (often plural).","e":"She climbed over the lip of the hole."},{"m":"(uncountable) A disrespectful response.","e":"Don't give me any lip."}]}]},"more":{"h":"more","i":"/mɔː/","a":"en-us-more.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"A larger amount.","e":"He does more work than I do."},{"m":"If something is more likely, common, difficult, etc. than something else, it is likelier, commoner, harder, etc.","e":"It's more likely to cool at night."}]}]},"most":{"h":"most","i":"/ˈməʊst/","a":"en-us-most.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"The majority of; much of; > 50%.","e":"She does the most cleaning, but the least cooking."},{"m":"The largest amount of.","e":"Bob knows the most about cooking."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Having the largest amount of a characteristic in a group.","e":"You must ask yourself what is most important."},{"m":"To a large degree; very.","e":"That is most unusual."}]}]},"nation":{"h":"nation","i":"/ˈneɪ̯.ʃən/","a":"en-us-nation.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A nation is a country or a political entity.","e":"Mexico is a nation of emigrants."}]}]},"answer":{"h":"answer","i":"/ˈɑːn.sə/","a":"en-us-answer.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An answer is something that someone says after another person asks (says) a question.","e":"The answer to your question is \"no\"."},{"m":"(countable) An answer is the solution to something.","e":"I found the answer to the mathematics exercise immediately."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To respond.","e":"He answers all my questions."}]}]},"near":{"h":"near","i":"/nɪə/","a":"en-us-near.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"With a small distance between; close.","e":"The end is near."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Almost.","e":"It was a near miss, but the car didn't hit us."},{"m":"Close.","e":"The nearest thing to me is my family."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To come close to, approach.","e":"We neared the beach."}]}]},"poor":{"h":"poor","i":"/pɔə/","a":"en-uk-poor.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Someone who is poor has little or no money.","e":"He is very poor."},{"m":"Something that is poor is bad quality.","e":"The painting was a poor job."},{"m":"You use poor before someone's name or a pronoun when you feel bad for that person.","e":"Tom is all alone. Poor Tom!"},{"m":"The poor are a group of people who have little or no money.","e":"This work is to help the poor."}]}]},"possible":{"h":"possible","i":"/ˈpɒsəbl̩/","a":"en-us-possible.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is possible, it is able to be done; doable; not impossible.","e":"Life on other planets is possible."},{"m":"If something is possible, it is acceptable.","e":"Zero is one possible solution."},{"m":"If something is possible, it is likely.","e":"Is that possible?"}]}]},"religion":{"h":"religion","i":"/rɪˈlɪʤən/","a":"en-us-religion.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Religion is when a person or persons believe in a God or Gods."},{"m":"(countable) Religion is a set of beliefs about a God or Gods.","e":"His religion is Christianity. Mine is Buddhism."}]}]},"regular":{"h":"regular","i":"/ˈrɛgjələr/","a":"en-us-regular.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A regular event repeats after a similar amount of time or space.","e":"The best way to keep everyone happy is to have regular meetings."},{"m":"A regular thing is the usual or common one, not special or different.","e":"They met at their regular time."},{"m":"A regular coffee or \"coffee, regular\" usually means with one milk and one sugar, but it means different things in different places."},{"m":"Regular gasoline has an octane rating between 85 and 88.","e":"The price of regular gas went up about 5 cents a litre over the weekend."},{"m":"A regular word follows the normal rules for marking tense, number, etc.","e":"In English, jump is a regular verb because it's past tense is -ed, but go is irregular."},{"m":"A regular shape has all angles and all sides equal.","e":"A stop sign is a regular octagon."},{"m":"If someone is regular, they defecate or menstruate at predictable times."},{"m":"You say X is a regular Y, to suggest that X is very much like Y in some important way, even though X is not actually Y.","e":"He's a regular jackass. (he's foolish)"}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A regular is a customer who comes often.","e":"He is a regular at the restaurant. He comes every day after work."}]}]},"pipe":{"h":"pipe","i":"/paɪp/","a":"en-us-pipe.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A tube; a round, hollow piece of metal, plastic, or wood.","e":"I will fix the pipe."},{"m":"(countable) A musical instrument made of a pipe; a flute.","e":"He plays the pipe."},{"m":"(countable) A tube used for smoking.","e":"He smokes a pipe."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To move using a pipe.","e":"He pipes the oil to his house."}]}]},"request":{"h":"request","i":"/rɪˈkwɛst/","a":"en-us-request.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A request the act of asking for something (sometimes in a formal way).","e":"We didn't hear his request that we be quiet."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you request something, you ask somebody to do something or to give you something.","e":"He requested your presence."}]}]},"rest":{"h":"rest","i":"/rɛst/","a":"en-us-rest.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pause or break.","e":"You need to take a rest."},{"m":"(countable) A note showing counts that are not played.","e":"That quarter-note is followed by three rests."},{"m":"(countable), what is left.","e":"I will take the rest of the money."},{"m":"(countable).","e":"You need rest."},{"m":"A rest is a place where you can put something, often your arm."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To take a break.","e":"He rested for five minutes."},{"m":"To be located somewhere.","e":"The statue rests on the mantle."},{"m":"To place something in a place.","e":"He rested his foot on the stair."},{"m":"To sleep.","e":"The baby is resting."},{"m":"To be dead.","e":"Rest in peace."}]}]},"crime":{"h":"crime","a":"en-us-crime.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A crime is an act that is against the law and for which you can go to jail.","e":"Murder is a crime."},{"m":"(countable) A crime is an extremely bad action.","e":"Letting that puppy die is a crime."}]}]},"cord":{"h":"cord","i":"/kɔː(r)d/","a":"en-us-cord.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A long, thin rope or wire.","e":"She tied the package with a cord."},{"m":"A measure of firewood.","e":"He can chop two cords each day."}]}]},"leaf":{"h":"leaf","i":"/liːf/","a":"en-us-leaf.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A big, flat part of a plant, often green.","e":"The leaves turn red and yellow in the fall."},{"m":"The front and back of a page in a book.","e":"I study the leaves of the book carefully."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To look through quickly, browse.","e":"She leafed through the book."},{"m":"To make leaves.","e":"The trees leafed in early spring."}]}]},"oil":{"h":"oil","i":"/ɔɪl/","a":"en-us-oil.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Oil is a liquid that is burned to create heat or used in machines to make them run well.","e":"Gas and oil are essential to running a car."},{"m":"Oil is a liquid made of fat that is used for cooking.","e":"Cook the potatoes in oil."},{"m":"(countable) An oil is a painting made of oil paint."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you oil something, you put clear oil on a machine to make it run well.","e":"She oiled the parts of the gun."}]}]},"operation":{"h":"operation","i":"/ˌɒpəˈreɪʃən/","a":"en-us-operation.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An operation is a medical process, often opening the human body.","e":"The doctors performed the operation in three hours."},{"m":"An operation is an action of a group of people working for a goal (often military).","e":"The Army operation was a success."},{"m":"An operation is part or all of a business. (often plural)","e":"The company's East Coast operation was bigger than its West Coast operation."},{"m":"An operation is a symbol that is used to perform a specific operation (addition, subtraction, multiplication or division) in maths.","e":"The plus symbol is used to perform a specific operation in maths which is addition."}]}]},"over":{"h":"over","i":"/ˈəʊ.və(r)/","a":"en-us-over.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something is over when it has finished, usually referring to an event.","e":"When the movie was over we left the movie theater."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"In a location above something.","e":"He stepped over the dog."},{"m":"From one side to the other.","e":"They went over the bridge."},{"m":"A number divided by another.","e":"Eight over two is four."},{"m":"If you do something over, you do it again.","e":"That looks really bad. I think we need to do it over."},{"m":"If you invite someone over, you invite them to your house.","e":"They had him over for tea."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An over in a cricket match is six balls bowled from one end.","e":"The captain told me I would have to bowl the next over."}]}]},"account":{"h":"account","i":"/ə'kaʊnt/","a":"en-us-account.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An account is an arrangement with a bank or other company to do business.","e":"I opened a bank account when I moved into town."},{"m":"(countable) The records of the money that is paid or received. (often plural)","e":"The accounts show that your bill has already been paid."},{"m":"(countable) A description of events","e":"The account that he gave didn't match the story that was in the newspaper."},{"m":"(uncountable) If you take something into account, you think about it when you decide something.","e":"Effective leaders have to take account of everyone's feelings."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If x accounts for some part of y, x makes up that part of y.","e":"Payments to employees account for 73% of our budget."},{"m":"(intransitive) If x accounts for y, it explains why y happens or exists.","e":"Oh, she was sick. Well, that accounts for her poor test score."}]}]},"acid":{"h":"acid","i":"/ˈæs.ɪd/","a":"en-us-acid.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An acid is a liquid with a high number of hydrogen ions in it that can burn things.","e":"Fruit often has a little acid in it."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is acid, it is like an acid, from an acid, or acidic.","e":"The factories nearby have made the lake more acid."},{"m":"If something has an acid taste, it is sour."},{"m":"If something said or done to you was acid, it was hurtful.","e":"Their acid comments are painful."}]}]},"adjustment":{"h":"adjustment","i":"/əˈdʒʌst.mənt/","a":"en-us-adjustment.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The act of.","e":"If you're gaining weight, you need to make slight adjustments to your food and exercise programme."}]}]},"agreement":{"h":"agreement","i":"/əg'riːmənt/","a":"en-us-agreement.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An agreement is where everybody has the same feelings about something; when everyone has the same ideas; saying \"yes\".","e":"We have an agreement with our teacher. If we do our homework we can go home early."}]}]},"after":{"h":"after","i":"/ˈɑːftə/","a":"en-us-after.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"something in place or position.","e":"\"B\" comes after \"A\" in the alphabet."},{"m":"Later in time.","e":"He came home after Jane did."}]}]},"against":{"h":"against","i":"/əˈgɛnst/","a":"en-us-against.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Opposing or disagreeing with sb/sth.","e":"I am against that proposal. I think it is a bad idea."},{"m":"ed to.","e":"He held her head against his chest."}]}]},"almost":{"h":"almost","i":"/ˈɔːlməʊst/","a":"en-us-inlandnorth-almost.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Very nearly; not the same, but near to being the same.","e":"I am almost ready to go. I will be ready very soon."}]}]},"among":{"h":"among","i":"/əˈmʌŋ/","a":"en-us-among.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"In or into. We say \"between\" about 2 other things, but among about 3 or more other things.","e":"She was among her friends."},{"m":"With a share for each.","e":"Divide the candy among yourselves."},{"m":"By all or with the whole."}]}]},"amount":{"h":"amount","i":"/eˈmaʊnt/","a":"en-us-amount.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A total of things; a measure of how much.","e":"Pour a small amount of water into the dish."},{"m":"The full effect or value."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) To add."},{"m":"To develop into; to become.","e":"What will your life amount to? Will you become successful?"}]}]},"approval":{"h":"approval","i":"/əˈpruːvəl/","a":"en-us-approval.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Approval is when you formally allow something to happen.","e":"The treaty requires approval by Parliament."}]}]},"argument":{"h":"argument","i":"/ˈɑːgjumənt/","a":"en-us-argument.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"When two or more people are discussing an idea that they do not agree on, they are having an argument. Often arguments are loud or angry.","e":"I thought we should buy the red car. She thought we should buy the blue car. We had an argument about it."},{"m":"An argument can be the reasons behind an idea.","e":"An argument for buying a red car is that it would look cooler than a blue one."},{"m":"(semantics) An argument is an element that is assigned a semantic role in a proposition."},{"m":"An argument is the independent variable of a function."}]}]},"attack":{"h":"attack","i":"/əˈtæk/","a":"en-us-attack.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To begin fighting with."},{"m":"To blame or abuse violently."},{"m":"To try to destroy, especially with words."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An attack is the act of trying to hurt somebody or break something."}]}]},"attempt":{"h":"attempt","i":"/əˈtɛmpt/","a":"en-us-attempt.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An attempt is a try at something, usually something difficult","e":"It's broken and no attempt has been made to fix it."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To try or to make an effort at.","e":"If you get something in your eye, do not attempt to remove it yourself."}]}]},"band":{"h":"band","i":"/bænd/","a":"en-us-band.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A band is a group of people working together.","e":"Those in the army who fought closely together in the war were called a band of brothers."},{"m":", (countable) A band is a group of people who play different instruments together. It can be of any size.","e":"The band played loud music."},{"m":"(countable) A band is piece of material, often metal, with the shape of a circle.","e":"A band was placed around the box to prevent it from breaking open."},{"m":"(countable) A band is a simple ring for the finger.","e":"The man gave his wife a band of gold at the wedding."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To band together is to get together in a group.","e":"The friends banded together in school."}]}]},"base":{"h":"base","i":"/beɪs/","a":"en-us-base.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Something's base is its lower part; the solid part that touches the floor or touches the earth and keeps the other parts of the thing up."},{"m":"Something's base is its most important part."},{"m":"A base is a building for military personnel and material."},{"m":"; (countable) An base is a chemical that releases hydroxide ions in water, and has the pH of over 7.","e":"is a weak base."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Rude, unfair, or unkind.","e":"The people who make those sex videos are really base."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When something or someone is based in a place, they do most of their work in that place.","e":"The airline is based in Toronto, but flies all over the world."},{"m":"(transitive) If you base x on y, you build or make x on, using, or to be like y.","e":"The movie is based on the book."}]}]},"basin":{"h":"basin","i":"/ˈbeɪsɪn/","a":"en-us-basin.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A container that is wider than it is deep."},{"m":"Anything that looks like a container."},{"m":"A low, wide place on the earth.","e":"The people living in the Amazon basin depend on the river."}]}]},"aspect":{"h":"aspect","i":"/ˈæspɛkt/","a":"en-us-aspect.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An aspect is a view of something, often something non-physical, such as an idea or a problem.","e":"In Chapter 2 we look at processor size. In Chapter 3 we consider other aspects of processor design."},{"m":"In English grammar, aspect is expressed as the form of a verb group showing the speaker's view of whether the situation the clause describes is complete or happens again and again.","e":"I go and I'm going are both in the present tense, but I'm going is in the progressive aspect as well."}]}]},"acquisition":{"h":"acquisition","i":"/æ.kwɪ.ˈzɪ.ʃən/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Acquisition is the act of getting something, often by buying it.","e":"The judge ruled that the acquisition of XYZ company by Acme Inc. was illegal."},{"m":"(countable) An acquisition is something that you got.","e":"The zoo's last acquisition was three elephants."}]}]},"feature":{"h":"feature","i":"/fiːtʃə(r)/","a":"en-us-feature.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A feature is a special or noticeable part of something.","e":"One unusual feature of the town is the river in the middle of mainstreet."},{"m":"(countable) A feature is a useful part or function of a product.","e":"In computers, a CD drive used to be a special feature. Now you can't buy a computer without one."},{"m":"(countable) A feature is a special newspaper or magazine article or radio or television program that is not published regularly.","e":"The Star is running a special feature about homelessness."},{"m":"(countable) A feature is a movie playing at a cinema.","e":"Today's feature will appear right after these commercials."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you feature something, you have it as a noticeable and positive part.","e":"This restaurant features the most famous chefs in France."},{"m":"(transitive) If you feature something, you consider (or imagine) it.","e":"I cannot feature that happening."}]}]},"number":{"h":"number","i":"/ˈnʌm.bə(r)/","a":"en-us-number.ogg","l":"numb","q":"adjective","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A symbol that that is used to describe quantity; a numeral.","e":"2, 5589, and 0 are all numbers."},{"m":"A few.","e":"She has a number of dictionaries--four or five, I think."},{"m":"A section from a musical or theatrical work.","e":"She chose a number from \"Swan Lake\" for her dance recital."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To label objects with numbers.","e":"Number the baskets so that we can find them easily."},{"m":"(intransitive) To total or count; to amount to.","e":"I don’t know how many books are in the library, but they must number in the thousands."}]}]},"before":{"h":"before","i":"/bɪˈfɔː/","a":"en-us-before.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If x happens before y, x happens first and y happens second.","e":"He worked in a gas station before he became famous."},{"m":"in front of something","e":"She stood before him, looking into his eyes."},{"m":"until","e":"It took a few moments before I realized that she was joking."}]}]},"behavior":{"h":"behavior","i":"[bɪˈheɪvjɚ]","a":"en-us-behavior.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Behavior refers to the way that you behave. That is, the kind of things you do.","e":"His behavior is bad."},{"m":"(countable) Something that you do; when you do a certain thing that is a behavior.","e":"Cleaning is a common behavior in monkeys."}]}]},"behaviour":{"h":"behaviour","i":"[bɪˈheɪvjɚ]","a":"en-us-behavior.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Behaviour refers to the way that you behave. That is, the kind of things you do.","e":"His behaviour is bad."},{"m":"(countable) Something that you do; when you do a certain thing that is a behaviour.","e":"Cleaning is a common behaviour in monkeys."}]}]},"text":{"h":"text","i":"/tɛkst/","a":"en-us-text.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Text is written language (often academic).","e":"The text is OK, but we need to change the graphics before we publish."},{"m":"(countable) A text is a textbook (American English).","e":"Did you buy the text for the accounting course?"},{"m":"(countable) A text is a message from a cell phone.","e":"I'll give you a text on your phone about tonight's concert."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you text someone, you send them a text message on their cell phone.","e":"Will you text me tomorrow?"}]}]},"consumer":{"h":"consumer","i":"/kənˈsjuːmə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-consumer.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A consumer is someone who buys or uses goods or services.","e":"Consumer demand for large cars has dropped with the increase in gasoline prices."}]}]},"belief":{"h":"belief","i":"/bɪˈliːf/","a":"en-us-belief.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A belief is an idea that is thought to be true.","e":"It is a widely accepted belief that the Earth revolves around the Sun."}]}]},"bell":{"h":"bell","i":"/bɛl/","a":"en-us-bell.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bell is an object that is shaped like a cup that makes a ringing sound when hit.","e":"The church bell is ringing."}]}]},"normal":{"h":"normal","i":"/ˈnɔːməl/","a":"en-us-normal.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A normal thing, or situation, is one that is not special.","e":"A normal computer has a keyboard and a screen."},{"m":"When someone is back to normal, he is healthier and no longer sick.","e":"I am glad he is back to normal after one week of the flu."}]}]},"seek":{"h":"seek","i":"/'sik/","a":"en-us-seek.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you seek something, you want it and search for it.","e":"If you are not sure if this is right for your child, then seek advice from your doctor, a child psychologist or health visitor, or from other parents."}]}]},"final":{"h":"final","i":"/ˈfaɪ.nəl/","a":"en-us-final.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"The final thing is the last one.","e":"Today is the final day to register for university."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The final is the last game or contest.","e":"Last week Brazil beat Germany in the semi-final. Tonight they play Italy in the final."}]}]},"bent":{"h":"bent","i":"/bent/","a":"en-us-bent.ogg","l":"bend","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"With one part going in one direction and another part going in another direction.","e":"Someone pushed and pulled the metal rod so much that it is now bent -- though it is not broken."}]}]},"bend":{"h":"bend","i":"/bɛnd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-bend.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To change the shape of an object so that it is not straight.","e":"The trees were bending in the wind."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A curve.","e":"There's a bend in the road up ahead."}]}]},"berry":{"h":"berry","i":"/ˈbɛri/","a":"en-us-berry.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A small, round fruit that grows on some plants and trees.","e":"The tree had bright red berries growing on it."}]}]},"between":{"h":"between","i":"/bɪˈtwiːn/","a":"en-us-between.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If x is between y and z, y is on one side of x and z is on the other side.","e":"Georgia is between North Carolina and Florida."}]}]},"chapter":{"h":"chapter","i":"/ˈt͡ʃæptə/","a":"en-us-chapter.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A chapter is a main division of a book.","e":"We read chapter five in the blue textbook."},{"m":"(countable) A chapter is a local part of a larger organisation.","e":"The Toronto chapter of the Red Cross is collecting blood today."}]}]},"injury":{"h":"injury","i":"/ˈɪn.dʒə.ri/","a":"en-us-injury.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An injury is when someone or an animal is hurt; when something has caused a person or an animal to be harmed.","e":"She suffered serious injuries to her face and chest in the car crash."},{"m":"(uncountable) In law, injury also includes loss of money or bad feelings.","e":"Our client is suing for injury arising from breach of contract."}]}]},"investment":{"h":"investment","i":"/ɪnˈvɛstmənt/","a":"en-us-investment.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Investment is the use of money, time, or effort to make a profit.","e":"The economic Development Board, set up in 1961 to promote foreign investment in Singapore, has attracted money from around the world."},{"m":"Your investment is the money, time, or effort you use to make a profit.","e":"Often you'll have to wait for years before you can get even part of your investment back."}]}]},"bit":{"h":"bit","i":"/bɪt/","a":"en-us-bit.ogg","l":"bite","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bit is an amount, usually a small amount.","e":"There's quite a bit of money. Where did it all come from?"},{"m":"(countable) A bit is a small piece of something.","e":"Try not to have bits of cake on the floor when you eat."},{"m":"(countable) A bit is a short time.","e":"I'm going to relax for a bit."},{"m":"(countable) A bit is the amount of information coded by a 1 or a 0 in a computer.","e":"Even the best 24-bit scanners suffer from noise."},{"m":"(countable) A bit is a sharp tool that spins to make holes.","e":"Drill a hole slightly smaller than your hook with a 1/16-inch drill bit."},{"m":"(countable) A bit is a metal bar that people put in a horse's mouth to control it."}]}]},"board":{"h":"board","i":"/bɔː(r)d/","a":"en-us-board.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A board is a group of people who govern something.","e":"The school board has chosen new textbooks for all the schools."},{"m":"(countable) A board is a long piece of wood.","e":"The outside of the house was made of wooden boards."},{"m":"(countable) A board is a flat surface.","e":"The knives should be used on a wooden cutting board only."},{"m":"If something is true across the board, it is true in all cases.","e":"He was number one across the board. Nobody was better."},{"m":"If something is on the drawing board, it is being planned.","e":"The designs for the car is still on the drawing board."},{"m":"(countable) A message board is a place for people to share ideas publicly, often over the internet.","e":"These days churches are using e-mail, message boards, and blogs to communicate."},{"m":"(countable) A circuit board is flat, usually green, piece of electronic equipment.","e":"He opened the computer so we could get a look at the circuit board."},{"m":"(countable) A sounding board is a person or group of people who will listen to your ideas and tell you if they're good or not.","e":"I often discuss company matters with him, and use him as a sounding board."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you board a boat, plane, train, or other vehicle, you get onto it.","e":"Sarah boarded the plane."},{"m":"(intransitive) If a boat, plane, train, or other vehicle is boarding, passengers are allowed to get on it.","e":"Flight AC002 is now boarding at gate two."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you board in a school or in someone's house, you pay to live there.","e":"In Paris, I boarded with a nice family in Le Alle."},{"m":"(transitive) If you board a building or a business up, you close it for a long time.","e":"Number 1 Strand Street was finally cleaned out, boarded up, and offered for sale by the city."}]}]},"boil":{"h":"boil","i":"/bɔɪl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-boil.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To get to a temperature that a liquid lets out bubbles and gas at.","e":"Water boils at 100°C."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"If you bring something to a boil, you heat it to 100&nbsp;°C."},{"m":"A swelling on the skin that is filled with pus.","e":"Lots of boils started appearing on his skin."}]}]},"primary":{"h":"primary","i":"/ˈpraɪməri/","a":"en-us-primary.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"first.","e":"Primary education covers infant schooling from the ages of 5–7 or 8, then junior schooling concluding at the ages of 10 or 11."},{"m":"most important.","e":"The company had shops in buildings whose primary purpose was as office space."},{"m":"most basic, simplest.","e":"The primary colors are red, blue, and yellow."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A primary is a kind of election held by a political party to choose the people it prefers for public office.","e":"Arlen Specter defeated Pat Toomey in the Republican primary election for U.S. Senate."},{"m":"(countable) Primary means an elementary school."},{"m":"Primary means the first grade in an elementary school."},{"m":"(countable) Primary means a base, something that is irreducible."}]}]},"institute":{"h":"institute","i":"/ˈɪnstɪt(j)uːt/","a":"en-us-institute.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An institute is an organisation such as a school or hospital that does teaching or research.","e":"This is the conclusion of the National Institute of Economic & Social Research and London Business School."},{"m":"An institute is an organization that has a particular purpose such such as scientific or educational work, or the building is based Or to introduce or start a system, rule, legal process etc..","e":"I think that the new WWW rule should not be Instituted because the old program provided a great opportunity for students to lean about other nation's culture, religion, and to socialize and appreciate the people."},{"m":"(countable) An institute is an important system of organization in society that has existed for a long time."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To begin or initiate something.","e":"He instituted the new policy of having children walk through a metal detector to enter school."}]}]},"consequence":{"h":"consequence","i":"/ˈkɑnsɪkwɛns/","a":"en-us-consequence.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A consequence is a result of an action, decision, etc., often a bad result.","e":"As a consequence of your bad behavior, you must stay after school."}]}]},"add":{"h":"add","i":"/æd/","a":"en-us-add.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you add x to y, you put x and y together.","e":"Cook for five minutes, then add the remaining spices to the soup."},{"m":"If you add time, or price, you increase it.","e":"A new kitchen would add value to the home."},{"m":"(transitive) If you add something to what you've said, you say something more.","e":"I paused for a moment, then added, \"Would you mind if I had some pudding?\""}]}]},"boot":{"h":"boot","i":"/buːt/","a":"en-us-boot.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A shoe that covers part of the leg.","e":"I love my special hiking boots."},{"m":"(countable) (British English) A storage space at the back of a car.","e":"He put his shopping bags in the boot."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(informal) If you boot someone, you force somebody to leave someplace.","e":"Billy got booted off of the train after the captain found out that he had no ticket."}]}]},"box":{"h":"box","i":"/bɒks/","a":"en-us-box.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A box is a square container, usually with four sides, a top and a bottom.","e":"We had big cardboard boxes filled with the stuff."},{"m":"(countable) A box is a container.","e":"The address was a local post office box, not a physical address."},{"m":"(countable) A box is a square area with lines around it in a magazine, book, or computer screen.","e":"It's especially important to speak to your doctor if you belong to this group (see box on page 118)."},{"m":"(countable) A box is an electronic device such as a television, radio, or computer.","e":"We'd brought a boom box out back and played the only radio station that came in."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you box, you fight someone for sport by punching them."},{"m":"(transitive) If you box something (up), you put it in a box.","e":"He boxed his old belongings up."},{"m":"(transitive) If you box something on a page, you draw a square around it."}]}]},"diction":{"h":"diction","i":"/ˈdɪkʃən/","a":"en-us-diction.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Your choice of words; the style or way you speak.","e":"The diction in this story is lively."}]}]},"story":{"h":"story","i":"/ˈstɔːri/","a":"en-uk-story.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A story is a piece of text that tells someone who reads it about a real or fictional (made up) event.","e":"This story is about a little girl who is eaten by a wolf."},{"m":"(countable) A story is a lie.","e":"Mother told me to stop telling stories."},{"m":"(countable) (mostly US) A story is a floor or level in a building.","e":"My room is five stories up."}]}]},"brake":{"h":"brake","i":"/breɪk/","a":"en-us-brake.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The part of an object that makes it slow down.","e":"The crash was caused by the car's brakes failing."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To make an object slow down using brakes.","e":"Jimmy braked to avoid hitting the cat."}]}]},"branch":{"h":"branch","i":"/bra:nʧ/","a":"en-us-branch.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A part of a tree that grows out from the trunk (center).","e":"Sally scraped her arm on a branch when she fell out of a tree."},{"m":"A part of something that acts like a branch does to its tree.","e":"The study of electricity is a branch of physics."},{"m":"One of a series of shops that are owned by the same company in business.","e":"McDonalds has many branches spread throughout the country."}]}]},"brass":{"h":"brass","i":"/brɑːs/","a":"en-us-brass.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Brass is a shiny yellow-orange metal.","e":"The brass chest only has one key."},{"m":"(uncountable) The brass is the group of musical instruments that are made of brass.","e":"The brass family of instruments includes tubas, trombones, and trumpets."}]}]},"bread":{"h":"bread","i":"/brɛd/","a":"en-uk-bread.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Bread is food made from mixing flour, water, and yeast.","e":"Small children love eating bread and butter."}]}]},"trumpet":{"h":"trumpet","i":"/ˈtrʌmpət/","a":"en-us-trumpet.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A trumpet is a metal instrument that makes noise when you blow into it. The person playing the trumpet can press different buttons to change the musical note that is being played."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you trumpet something, usually something you are proud of, you tell everyone about it."},{"m":"When an elephant trumpets, it makes a loud sound."}]}]},"piano":{"h":"piano","i":"/piˈæ.noʊ̯/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-piano.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A piano is a large musical instrument that has hammers connected to 88 keys."}]}]},"beer":{"h":"beer","i":"/bɪə(r)/","a":"en-us-beer.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Beer is an alcoholic drink that is made from barley, wheat or other types of cereal grains.","e":"We like to drink beer in the bar."}]}]},"change":{"h":"change","i":"/t͡ʃeɪnd͡ʒ/","a":"en-us-change.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you change something, you make it different than before.","e":"Ellen changed the sentence so that it was correct."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A change is when something becomes different.","e":"The building plan required some small changes."},{"m":"(uncountable); (money) When you get change for a bill, you get smaller bills or coins that equal the amount of the original bill. For example, if you get change for a $5 bill, you may get five $1 bills or you may get four $1 bills and coins that add up to $1 or you may get some other combination of bills and coins.","e":"Can I get change for this $100 bill please?"},{"m":"(countable) A change is a replacement.","e":"I brought a change of clothes, just in case."}]}]},"dark":{"h":"dark","i":"/dɑː(r)k/","a":"en-us-dark.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is dark, is has no light.","e":"The cave is very dark."},{"m":"If something is dark, it is scary or not pleasant.","e":"World War II was a dark time in world history."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Place where there is no light.","e":"Most humans are afraid of the dark."},{"m":"(uncountable) Late in the day, especially after sunset.","e":"Go and play with your friends, but be back before dark!"},{"m":"(countable) (plural) Darks are clothes that are not light in color."}]}]},"subtraction":{"h":"subtraction","i":"/səbˈtrækʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-subtraction.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Subtraction is the act or operation when you subtract something.","e":"My son is learning subtraction in grade 1 math class."}]}]},"subtract":{"h":"subtract","i":"/səbˈtrækt/","a":"en-us-subtract.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something is subtracted, then it is taken away from something else.","e":"You must subtract your expenses from your income."},{"m":"One of the basic operations in mathematics."}]}]},"multiplication":{"h":"multiplication","i":"/ˌmʌltəplɪˈkeɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-multiplication.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The process of multiplying numbers by each other.","e":"We studied multiplication in grade 3."}]}]},"rock":{"h":"rock","i":"/rɒk/","a":"en-us-rock.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hard substance that forms naturally in the Earth's surface."},{"m":"(uncountable) A form of music often played with guitars and drums.","e":"Rock music had direct influences from blues and rhythm and blues."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To shake back and forth.","e":"The boat rocked in the strong wind."}]}]},"field":{"h":"field","i":"/fiːld/","a":"en-us-field.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A field is an open area of land that can be used for many different things, from sports to crop-growing."},{"m":"(countable) A field is an area of study or work.","e":"He was an expert in the field of American history."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you field something, you answer it; you address it."},{"m":"(transitive) If you field the team, you place them in the game."}]}]},"stomach":{"h":"stomach","i":"/ˈstʌmək/","a":"en-us-stomach.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The place in the body where food is digested."},{"m":"The area below the chest."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To be able to tolerate something emotionally, physically, or mentally; to be able to stand or handle something.","e":"I really can’t stomach jobs involving that much paperwork, but some people seem to tolerate them."}]}]},"brick":{"h":"brick","i":"/brɪk/","a":"en-us-brick.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A brick is a small, rectangular block used for building things."}]}]},"equal":{"h":"equal","i":"/ˈiːkwəl/","a":"en-us-equal.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If two things are equal, they are the same in shape, size, or number.","e":"The number of people inside of the store is equal to the number of people outside of the store."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Someone who has the same rights as somebody else.","e":"I'm your teacher, not your equal."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If x equals y, x and y have the same value.","e":"Two plus two equals four."}]}]},"dust":{"h":"dust","i":"/dʌst/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Exilexi-dust.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Dust is a thin powder that can be seen in the air or on a surface.","e":"The old building was filled with dust."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you dust something, you remove dust from it.","e":"Sally dusted her house to prepare it for a party."}]}]},"brush":{"h":"brush","i":"/brʌʃ/","a":"en-us-brush.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A brush is a tool with many thin pieces of plastic to smooth hair and wool."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you brush something, you clean it with a brush.","e":"I forgot to brush my teeth before going to bed."}]}]},"nutshell":{"h":"nutshell","i":"/ˈnʌtʃel/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-nutshell.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The shell that surrounds the kernel (the hard part in the center) of a nut","e":"Because nutshells are very hard, it takes a lot of time to crack them open."}]}]},"country":{"h":"country","i":"/ˈkʌntri/","a":"en-uk-country.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A land that is controlled by a government.","e":"Russia is the largest country in the world."},{"m":"(uncountable) Places outside or far from; the type of place where farms are. The countryside.","e":"We live way out in the country."},{"m":"(uncountable) A certain place, in general.","e":"You're in Nascar country now."},{"m":"(uncountable) A kind of (mostly American) music started by people who lived far from cities. Short for country music.","e":"I've been listening to a lot of country this month."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Away from the city.","e":"We were driving down a country road, with trees all around."},{"m":"Typical of farms or places away from cities. Typical of country people.","e":"His way seeing the world is so country."}]}]},"countries":{"h":"countries","i":"/ˈkʌntriz/","a":"en-us-countries.ogg","l":"country","q":"noun"},"land":{"h":"land","i":"/lænd/","a":"en-us-land.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Land is the part of the Earth that is not covered with water","e":"The surface of Earth is 70% water, and 30% land."},{"m":"A land is a country or region"},{"m":"Land is an area of ground that can be used for farming, making buildings, etc.","e":"All this land belongs to me."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) When you land, you fall onto the ground.","e":"He jumped off the wall and landed on his feet."},{"m":"(intransitive) When an airplane lands, it comes down from the air onto the ground.","e":"The plane landed in Chicago."},{"m":"(transitive) When you land an airplane, you use the controls to bring it down on the ground.","e":"The pilot landed the big plane."}]}]},"world":{"h":"world","i":"/wɝəɫd̥/","a":"en-us-world.oga","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The Earth.","e":"Our world needs to be cared for."},{"m":"The.","e":"I love you more than anybody else in the world."},{"m":"The setting of a group of people.","e":"They were in their own world as they talked about trains nobody else knew about."},{"m":"A planet.","e":"I wonder if there is life on other worlds."}]}]},"greeting":{"h":"greeting","i":"/ˈgriːtɪŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-greeting.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A greeting is something you do or say when you meet someone.","e":"He noticed Karelius, raised a hand in greeting, and dismounted to lead his horse through to the stables. A minute later he entered the bar, tapping frozen mud from his boots at the door-post. \"Karelius, my dear fellow. Hope I'm not late.\""}]}]},"portmanteau":{"h":"portmanteau","i":"/pɔːtˈmæn.təʊ/","a":"en-us-portmanteau-1.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A portmanteau word.","e":"Pokémon is a portmanteau of \"pocket\" and \"monster\"."},{"m":"A large case usually made of leather made of two parts."}]}]},"relevant":{"h":"relevant","i":"/ˈrɛləvənt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-relevant.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is relevant, it is connected to a topic in a meaningful way.","e":"The second priority is to provide all relevant information to the employee about his job such as: skills, resources and how flexible he can be; factors affecting performance (limits of responsibility, work targets); factors affecting the environment of the job;"}]}]},"leaves":{"h":"leaves","i":"/liːvz/","a":"en-us-leaves.ogg","l":"leaf","q":"noun"},"leave":{"h":"leave","i":"/liːv/","a":"en-uk-to leave.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you leave a place, you go away from it.","e":"I left the building."},{"m":"Something you leave remains where it was.","e":"Two cakes are left."}]}]},"left":{"h":"left","i":"/lɛft/","a":"en-us-left.ogg","l":"leave","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"One of the two directions, the opposite of right. This arrow is pointing left: ←","e":"left at the next corner."},{"m":"ing, still there.","e":"Three apples are left."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The left side.","e":"The shop is on your left."},{"m":"(countable) A left turn.","e":"Take two lefts and a right and then you'll be there."}]}]},"centimetre":{"h":"centimetre","i":"/ˈsɛn.tɪ.miː.tə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-centimetre.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hundredth of a metre; 100 centimetres is one metre","e":"This pencil is 18 centimetres long."}]}]},"metre":{"h":"metre","i":"/ˈmiːtə(r)/","a":"En-us-metre.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) One metre is a length. It is exactly 100 centimetres long.","e":"This table is 2 metres wide."}]}]},"steal":{"h":"steal","i":"/stiːl/","a":"en-us-steel.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you steal, you take somebody's money or things without their permission.","e":"The thief stole the diamond ring."},{"m":"(baseball) If you steal a base you run to it before the ball was hit."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A steal is a good deal. It is when you pay so little money you almost did not pay.","e":"At just $2 each these T-shirts as a real steal."},{"m":"(countable), (baseball) A steal is when someone runs to a base before the ball is hit."}]}]},"stole":{"h":"stole","i":"/'stɔl/","a":"en-us-stole.ogg","l":"steal","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A stole is a piece of clothing that is worn over robes in churches."},{"m":"(countable) A stole is a piece of clothing that is like a scarf and is often made of fur."}]}]},"cake":{"h":"cake","i":"/keɪk/","a":"en-us-cake.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A cake is a sweet baked food.","e":"Natasha's mum baked her a cake for her birthday."},{"m":"A cake is a food that is made into a flat, usually round, shape.","e":"At that time of year, we make small Japanese rice cakes called mochi."},{"m":"(countable) A cake of soap or ice, is a hard piece of it.","e":"He took a cake of soap and started to wash."},{"m":"If something is a piece of cake, it's very easy.","e":"Yesterday's test was a piece of cake. I got twenty out of twenty."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If something is caked, then it is coated with a layer of some material.","e":"His shoes are caked with mud."}]}]},"nose":{"h":"nose","i":"/nəʊz/","a":"en-us-nose.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The part of the face that sticks out and is used for and smelling things.","e":"His nose is very big."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you nose, you move with caution.","e":"The ship nosed through the minefield."},{"m":"If you nose you snoop.","e":"She was nosing around other people’s business."},{"m":"If you nose something, you push it with your nose."}]}]},"would":{"h":"would","i":"/wʊd/","a":"en-us-would.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Would is used to show your past plan or decision.","e":"He said he would be seeing Mr Moi in Bonn on Monday."},{"m":"Would is used to show that in the past you expected something to happen.","e":"It would soon be time to go home, but I didn't want to leave."},{"m":"Would is used to show that something happened regularly in the past but not now.","e":"Every summer we would go to the lake for a few weeks."},{"m":"Would is used to talk about unreal, unlikely, or conditional situations.","e":"You wouldn't like it if you had to see it every day."},{"m":"Would is used to ask politely for something.","e":"Would you please explain that to me?"},{"m":"Would is used to offer something politely.","e":"Would you like to go out for lunch then?"},{"m":"Would is used to give advice.","e":"I would go back and talk to him about it."},{"m":"Would is used to show that something is typical, usually when you are unhappy about it. In this case, it's always stressed.","e":"He would come just when we were leaving."}]}]},"might":{"h":"might","i":"/maɪt/","a":"en-us-might.ogg","l":"may","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Used to show possible actions. If I weren't getting myself born for my birthday, I might see numerous of them celebrating the other day earlier.","e":"I might go to the whole party if I were growing up faster this morning."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The power, strength, force or influence of a person or group."}]}]},"could":{"h":"could","i":"/kʊd/","a":"en-us-could.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you could do something, you were able to do it.","e":"When I was younger, I could run a five-minute mile."},{"m":"If you could something, but you don't know if you want to, you have the option of doing do it.","e":"She could do her math or go to the game."}]}]},"prejudice":{"h":"prejudice","i":"/ˈprɛd͡ʒədɪs/","a":"en-us-prejudice.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"an unreasonable hatred for a group, usually a race or a religion, etc.","e":"John had prejudice against Muslims."},{"m":"a belief, usually negative, that you have about something, before you know that it is actually right"},{"m":"an idea or preference you have towards something before you actually experience the thing"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Prejudicing means to cause a prejudice or to commit prejudiced judgement."}]}]},"prejudiced":{"h":"prejudiced","l":"prejudice","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Someone who is prejudiced has prejudice against somebody.","e":"Sarah is the most prejudiced person I have ever met."}]}]},"bath":{"h":"bath","i":"/bæθ/","a":"en-us-bath.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A long, high basin that you put water in and go in to wash your body.","e":"Jane put in water up to the top of the bath."},{"m":"Going into a bath to wash yourself.","e":"George takes a bath every day."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you bath someone, you wash them in a bath."}]}]},"muslim":{"h":"Muslim","i":"/ˈmʌz.lɪm/","a":"en-uk-Muslim.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A person who believes in Islam.","e":"Muhammad is a Muslim."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something to do with Muslims or Islam.","e":"There are several Muslim beliefs."}]}]},"evaluation":{"h":"evaluation","i":"/ɪˌvæljuˈeɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-evaluation.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Evaluation is the process of making a judgement.","e":"If a teacher doesn't know the student well, it makes the evaluation of the student's level very difficult."},{"m":"(countable) An evaluation is a judgement.","e":"Lamont Library’s 24-hour service received a positive evaluation this past spring."}]}]},"evaluate":{"h":"evaluate","i":"/ɨˈvaljʊeɪt/","a":"en-us-evaluate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you evaluate someone or something, you judge it.","e":"It is difficult to evaluate the effectiveness of the LINK programme, but we believe it has been useful."}]}]},"fewer":{"h":"fewer","a":"en-us-fewer.ogg","l":"few","q":"determiner"},"fewest":{"h":"fewest","a":"en-us-fewest.ogg","l":"few","q":"determiner"},"former":{"h":"former","i":"/ˈfɔrmɚ/","a":"en-us-former.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A former x (e.g., president, country, wife) used to be the x but is not anymore.","e":"Former president Clinton was giving a speech at the school."},{"m":"The former is the first of two things that have already been talked about.","e":"I've taught in high school and university. The former (i.e., high school) is more exciting, but university is less stressful."}]}]},"latter":{"h":"latter","i":"/ˈlæt.ər/","a":"en-us-latter.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"The latter half, case, etc. is the second of two.","e":"The price of oil could reach $150 by the latter half of the decade."},{"m":"The latter part of a period of time is the part near the end.","e":"The Internet only became well known in the latter part of the 20th century."}]}]},"own":{"h":"own","i":"/əʊn/","a":"en-us-own.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is your own it belongs to you or is about you (often used for emphasis).","e":"I wish I had my own home."},{"m":"If you are on your own, you are by yourself, there is no body else with you. This can also mean there is no one helping you.","e":"I was on my own in the woods."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you own something it belongs to you, it is yours.","e":"Yes, I own a car."},{"m":"If you \"own up\" to something, you admit you did it.","e":"I had to own up to lying about our relationship."}]}]},"such":{"h":"such","i":"/sʌʧ/","a":"en-us-such.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Such a person or thing is that same kind that was mentioned before.","e":"There are times when the father is unknown. One such case happened recently. (= \"when the father is unknown\")"},{"m":"You use such as or such... as to give one or more examples.","e":"We always had pets, such as cats, dogs, and birds."},{"m":"You use such to emphasize a description.","e":"My son had a party. You've never seen such a nice group of kids."}]}]},"first":{"h":"first","i":"/fɜːst/","a":"en-us-first.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Happening or coming before all other similar things or people.","e":"I don't like the job much at first."},{"m":"The most important or best.","e":"Your first duty is to your family."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Before anyone/anything else.","e":"She regarded herself, first and last, as a musician."},{"m":"For the first time.","e":"I first went to Japan in 1994."},{"m":"At first.","e":"When we were first married, everything was wonderful."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A first is something that has not happened before.","e":"A dog walking on stilts? Well, that is a first."}]}]},"second":{"h":"second","i":"/ˈsɛk.(ə)nd/","a":"en-us-second.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"The second thing is the one that is number two (2) in order.","e":"I only have one older brothers and one younger brother. I'm the second child."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A second is 1/60 of a minute. Sixty seconds is one minute.","e":"The winner won the race by five seconds."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you second a nomination, you support it and it will be voted.","e":"So moved. Do we have a second?"}]}]},"fourth":{"h":"fourth","i":"/fɔːθ/","a":"en-us-fourth.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"The fourth thing is something that is number four (4) in order."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A fourth of something is one of four equal parts of that thing; a quarter.","e":"Three is one fourth of twelve."}]}]},"paint":{"h":"paint","i":"/peɪnt/","a":"en-us-paint.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Paint is a liquid used to colour something","e":"There were all sorts of paints at the shop – green, red, and blue."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"to use paint to colour something","e":"John painted the wall brown."},{"m":"to use paint to make a picture.","e":"The child painted a picture of a flower."}]}]},"parallel":{"h":"parallel","i":"/ˈpær.əˌlɛl/","a":"en-us-parallel.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When a line is parallel to another line, the two lines do not meet and they are the same distance from each other at every point.","e":"The two cars ran parallel to each other."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A similarity between two things.","e":"I see a parallel between John and Beth – they both like to play with toy cars."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Be similar to.","e":"John parallels Beth when he plays with toy cars."},{"m":"To be the same distant apart from each other at every point.","e":"Line A parallels line B."}]}]},"bright":{"h":"bright","i":"/braɪt/","a":"en-us-bright.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is bright it gives out or fills with much light.","e":"The sun is very bright during summer."},{"m":"A person who is bright is clever and intelligent.","e":"Tom is a bright child."}]}]},"broken":{"h":"broken","i":"/ˈbrəʊkən/","a":"en-us-broken.ogg","l":"break","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is broken is not as it should be because it has been damaged or injured","e":"The broken cup lay in pieces on the floor."},{"m":"(gaming) If something in a game, such as a gun, is broken, it is overpowered"}]}]},"bulb":{"h":"bulb","i":"/ˈbʌlb/","a":"en-us-bulb.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A solid object that has one large, round end and another thin end."},{"m":"A light bulb.","e":"Can you change that bulb, please? It's broken."},{"m":"The bulb-shaped part of the root of a plant.","e":"People can buy tulip bulbs and grow them at home."}]}]},"burn":{"h":"burn","i":"/bɜː(r)n/","a":"en-us-burn.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something has been cooked too much, then it is burned.","e":"Mother burned the pie when she forgot that it was cooking in the oven."},{"m":"When part of your body is injured because of the heat, then it has been burned.","e":"If you touch a hot pan of water, you can burn yourself."},{"m":"Things on fire are burning.","e":"The house next door is burning."},{"m":"A person is burned if someone else successfully insults him."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A burn is an injury caused when you burn yourself.","e":"The burn on my arm hurts."}]}]},"dictionaries":{"h":"dictionaries","l":"dictionary","q":"noun"},"if":{"h":"if","i":"/ɪf/","a":"en-us-if.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Used to denote a condition.","e":"If it rains, I will get wet."},{"m":"although","e":"He was a great friend, if a little strange."},{"m":"When... occurs (a programming statement).","e":"If A, then B, else C."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"If is a conditional situation.","e":"There are many ifs we need to consider before we start on the plan."}]}]},"business":{"h":"business","i":"/ˈbɪz.nɪs/","a":"en-us-business.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Business is the buying and selling of things or services.","e":"I am in the business of catching fish and selling them."},{"m":"(countable) A business is a group that does business; a company.","e":"Many businesses use computers."},{"m":"(uncountable) Business is the things that you have to do.","e":"They went on with business as usual."}]}]},"but":{"h":"but","i":"/bʌt/","a":"en-us-but.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"except","e":"He ate everything but the meat."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"only","e":"There is but one sun and one earth to live on."}]}]},"button":{"h":"button","i":"/ˈbʌtən/","a":"en-us-button.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A button is a round object that can be pushed through clothing so that the clothing stays on.","e":"Sarah's sweater doesn't work anymore because the buttons popped off."},{"m":"(countable) A button is a switch that is turned on by pressing it.","e":"I pressed the button to turn on the television."},{"m":"(countable) A button is a badge that can be worn of clothing and is put onto the clothing with a pin to hold it in place.","e":"I have a \"Vote for Bush\" button."},{"m":"(uncountable) (poker) If a poker player has the button, he is the last person to act on that hand."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you button something, you fasten it with a button.","e":"Button up your coat!"}]}]},"kindergarten":{"h":"kindergarten","i":"/ˈkɪndərˌɡɑːrt(ə)n/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-kindergarten.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Kindergarten is a place (or school) where young children learn (usually for five- and six-year-olds)."}]}]},"five":{"h":"five","i":"/faɪv/","a":"en-us-five.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(ordinal fifth) The number 5.","e":"We have five toes on each foot."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The number 5.","e":"plus three is five."}]}]},"calm":{"h":"calm","i":"/kɑːm/","a":"en-us-calm.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a person, place or situation is calm, it is peaceful and quiet.","e":"There's no wind and the lake is calm."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The state of being quiet and peaceful.","e":"I felt a calm come over me."},{"m":"(countable) A period of time without wind.","e":"The calm before a storm."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To make someone or something calm.","e":"He was yelling and running around but I calmed him."},{"m":"(intransitive) When someone or something becomes calm.","e":"The lake calmed after the storm."}]}]},"population":{"h":"population","i":"/pɒpjuːleɪʃən/","a":"en-us-population.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The population of a place is the people or animals that live there.","e":"The population of a city is higher than that of a town."}]}]},"hunger":{"h":"hunger","i":"/ˈhʌŋɡə/","a":"en-us-hunger.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Hunger is the feeling when wanting food when your stomach is empty.","e":"When I have hunger then I want to have some food."},{"m":"Hunger is a serious lack of food.","e":"Even after the war, people are dying of poverty and hunger."}]}]},"usual":{"h":"usual","i":"/ˈjuːʒʊəl/","a":"en-us-usual.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"something that is usual happens often","e":"It is usual for me to read the newspaper in the morning."}]}]},"site":{"h":"site","i":"/saɪt/","a":"en-us-site.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A site is a location or a place.","e":"He was working on a building site in Alton when a concrete mixer rolled back and hit him."},{"m":"(countable) A site is a website."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If something is sited somewhere, it was put or built there.","e":"The house is sited on the corner of Portland Street and Langham Street."}]}]},"anaesthetic":{"h":"anaesthetic","i":"/ˌænəsˈθɛtɪk/","a":"en-US anesthetic.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An anaesthetic is a gas that is used by a doctor or nurse to make a person feel no pain or to put a person to sleep.","e":"They used an anaesthetic on him before performing the surgery."}]}]},"sought":{"h":"sought","i":"/sɔːt/","a":"en-us-sought.ogg","l":"seek","q":"verb"},"commission":{"h":"commission","i":"/kəˈmɪʃən/","a":"en-us-commission.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A commission is a group of people who work together to research or manage something for a government.","e":"She was recently appointed to head the European commission on climate change."},{"m":"A commission is money that a salesperson receives for each sale.","e":"You may have to pay commission to convert the dollars into local currency on your travels."},{"m":"(uncountable) The official appointment of an officer in a nation's armed forces.","e":"Brummell resigned his commission when his regiment was posted to Manchester."},{"m":"(uncountable) A commission is a task to be undertaken.","e":"My commission was only to deliver this message."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you commission someone to do or create something, you formally ask them to do it.","e":"The report commissioned by the Department of Health in 1989, contains guidelines on how best to manage and organise waiting lists."}]}]},"positive":{"h":"positive","i":"/ˈpɒzɪtɪv/","a":"en-us-positive.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is positive, it is good, happy, or wanted.","e":"A balanced diet, exercise, and a positive attitude are all things that give you a sense of well being."},{"m":"If you are positive about something, you are sure that you are not mistaken.","e":"The guard at Euston was positive that on that particular day he had locked the door."},{"m":"If a test result is positive, the test found what it was testing for.","e":"I'm sorry, the HIV test is positive."},{"m":"A positive electrical charge is one carried by a proton.","e":"Attach the wire to the positive pole of the battery."},{"m":"A positive number or value is more than zero.","e":"A positive number multiplied by a negative number results in a negative."},{"m":"A positive symptom is one where something is there that should not be. Usually this is for schizophrenia.","e":"His positive symptoms included hearing voices of people that were not there."},{"m":"Based on something being there or being true, in some other way.","e":"I tie-bleached my shirt to make a negative image, then tie-dyed it to add a positive image."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A positive is a good thing or part of something.","e":"It's been a bad week, but at least the sun is one positive."}]}]},"by":{"h":"by","i":"/baɪ/","a":"en-us-by.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"near or next to.","e":"The mailbox is by the bus stop."},{"m":"at some time before (the given time).","e":"Be back by ten o'clock!"},{"m":"if something is done by somebody, it is done through their action","e":"The matter was decided by the chairman."},{"m":"if something is created by somebody, they are the creator, author, etc.","e":"There are many well-known plays by William Shakespeare."},{"m":"shows how someone does something","e":"I avoided the guards by moving only when they weren't looking."},{"m":"using the rules or logic of.","e":"I sorted the items by category."},{"m":"with a change of. In this case, by shows how much something has changed.","e":"Our stock is up by ten percent."},{"m":"shows how slowly, or how quickly, someone does something (used in the form \"X by X\" or \"by Xs\")","e":"We went through the book page by page."},{"m":"When the width and depth of something, by is used between the lengths of the two sides.","e":"The window is 45&nbsp;cm by 60&nbsp;cm."},{"m":"If you multiply x by y, you multiply x × y.","e":"Five multiplied by seven is 35."},{"m":"If you divide x by y, you find how many ys are in x.","e":"35 divided by seven is five."}]}]},"canvas":{"h":"canvas","i":"/ˈkænvəs/","a":"en-us-canvas.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A canvas is a type of hard, rough cloth used for making sails, tents, and painted on.","e":"John prepared the canvas for the sail."},{"m":"Canvas that is stretched out on a frame to be painted on.","e":"A good artist chooses his or her own canvas."},{"m":"(uncountable) Canvas is something that is a basis for a creative work.","e":"The life in rural France served as a canvas for Ted F. Adams' Around the Tree."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you canvas something, you cover an area or object with canvas."}]}]},"canvasses":{"h":"canvasses","l":"canvas","q":"noun"},"canvases":{"h":"canvases","l":"canvas","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"plural of canvas","e":"Many canvases lined the wall."}]}]},"care":{"h":"care","i":"/kɛə/","a":"en-us-care.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Care is the act of helping someone, especially sick people, the very young or the very old.","e":"He decided not to seek health care from a hospitals."},{"m":"(uncountable) If you take care of someone, you watch them so that there is no trouble.","e":"You're going to need someone to take care of you when you get older."},{"m":"(uncountable) If you take care of a problem, you fix it or arrange it.","e":"Don's worry. Pearl and Edward will take care of things."},{"m":"(uncountable) You say \"Take care!\" when you are leaving somebody.","e":"That's it. All right. Jim, good to see you. Take care."},{"m":"(uncountable) You say \"Take care!\" when you want somebody to do something safely.","e":"Go slowly and take care not to touch anything."},{"m":"(uncountable) Care is the act of keeping something in a good condition.","e":"I'm caring for the house while they're away."},{"m":"(countable) A Care is a worry, concern, or something that you think about often.","e":"I don't have a care in the world."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you don't care about something, you don't think about it often or have a concern for it; it doesn't matter.","e":"I don't care what happens to my car."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you care about something, you think it is important.","e":"He only cares about his car."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you care for somebody, look after","e":"Young children can learn to care for a pet."}]}]},"regulation":{"h":"regulation","i":"/ˌrɛɡjʊˈleɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-regulation.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A regulation is a rule or a control.","e":"The company has recently imposed new safety rules and regulations to reduce accidents."},{"m":"(uncountable) Regulation is the process of controlling something, usually with rules.","e":"The government is reducing regulation of the airlines."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is regulation, it is made or done according to the rules.","e":"This isn't a regulation soccer ball. It's too small."}]}]},"carriage":{"h":"carriage","i":"/ˈkærɪdʒ/","a":"en-us-ne-carriage.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A vehicle on wheels, usually pulled by a horse.","e":"Jack Hampton rode on his carriage to the wedding."},{"m":"(countable) A railway car, pulled by a locomotive.","e":"Sarah said that she would be on the third carriage of the train."},{"m":"(uncountable) The way somebody moves and walks.","e":"His noble carriage made nobody suspect that he was a poor pauper."}]}]},"cart":{"h":"cart","i":"/kɑːt/","a":"en-us-cart.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A small, open vehicle on wheels, pulled or pushed by a person or an animal and usually used for carrying things, not people.","e":"Harry put his trunk in a cart and pushed it through the station."},{"m":"(countable) A small motor vehicle like a car; a go cart.","e":"Sophie squealed as she raced through the race course on the cart."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you cart something to somewhere, you move it there."}]}]},"chalk":{"h":"chalk","i":"/ʧɔːk/","a":"en-us-chalk.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Chalk is a soft, white, powder-like limestone.","e":"The men mine chalk in the hills near my house."},{"m":"(countable) Chalk is a piece of chalk, or more usually, processed compressed chalk, that is used for drawing and for writing on a blackboard; teachers at school may use chalk to write on a blackboard.","e":"John wrote his name on the blackboard with chalk."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To put chalk on something, such as the tip of a billiards cue."},{"m":"To write something using chalk; this is often done on a blackboard."},{"m":"To use powdered chalk to put the lines on a sports field."}]}]},"on":{"h":"on","i":"/ɒn/","a":"en-us-on.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"positioned at the upper surface of, touching from above","e":"The apple is on the table."},{"m":"at the date of","e":"Tim was born on the 4th of July."},{"m":"to an state","e":"I turned the television on."},{"m":"along, forwards (continuing an action)","e":"Shall we stop for lunch or shall we drive on?"},{"m":"about, dealing with the subject of","e":"I have a book on history."},{"m":"touching; hanging from","e":"I have no money on me at the moment."},{"m":"because of, due to","e":"He was arrested on suspicion of bribery."},{"m":"If something is on, it is active, functioning or operating.","e":"The television is on."}]}]},"distinction":{"h":"distinction","i":"/dɪˈstɪŋkʃən/","a":"en-us-distinction.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A distinction is a difference that you have noticed or decided is important. Often used to separate things.","e":"Before we discuss how you can develop your creative powers, we need to make a distinction between two different but related activities --; THINKING and LEARNING."},{"m":"(uncountable) If something is done with distinction, it is done to a high level and other people recognise that.","e":"We only wanted to take athletes of distinction; no one is going just for the trip."}]}]},"equation":{"h":"equation","i":"/ɪˈkweɪʒən/","a":"en-us-equation.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An equation is a mathematical statement in which both sides are of equal value.","e":"Find x, in the equation x + 2y = 3y."},{"m":"(countable); (usually singular) An equation is how everything works together to create a situation.","e":"Money plays a big part in the political equation."},{"m":"(uncountable) The equation of x with y, is the act of thinking about them as the same or as belonging together.","e":"The equation of women with maids and cooks must stop."}]}]},"impact":{"h":"impact","i":"/ˈɪmpækt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-impact (noun).wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An impact is the act of one object hitting another.","e":"In tests, the driver was unhurt, even in high-speed impacts."},{"m":"The impact is the effect of an act, statement, change, etc.","e":"The report noted that most teachers feel that IT has made little impact on formal education."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something impacts you, it has an effect on you.","e":"It is obvious how bad movies will impact on children."},{"m":"If you impact something, you press (or pack) its together.","e":"There is a special tool to impact the road when it is under construction so the base is solid."}]}]},"appropriate":{"h":"appropriate","i":"/əˈprəʊpriɪt/","a":"en-us-appropriate-adj.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is appropriate, it matches the situation.","e":"We suggest ways in which teachers may change their materials to make them more appropriate for bilingual students."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) (formal) If you appropriate something, you take it from somebody else and make it your own.","e":"By the end of this year, the total funds appropriated will be nearly $600 billion."}]}]},"flow":{"h":"flow","i":"/fləʊ/","a":"en-us-flow.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If something flows, it moves in a smooth and regular way.","e":"The river flows gently to the sea."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A flow is a smooth regular movement of a liquid, gas, etc.","e":"A major accident is blocking the flow of traffic on Yonge St., just north of Queen."}]}]},"participation":{"h":"participation","i":"/pɑːˌtɪs.ɪˈpeɪ.ʃən/","a":"en-us-participation.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Participation is the act of joining together with other people to do something.","e":"After the injury, he was removed from active participation in the war."}]}]},"survey":{"h":"survey","i":"/ˈsɜːveɪ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-survey (noun).wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A survey is a broad look at a topic or place.","e":"Before looking for a job, he did a survey of the companies in the area."},{"m":"(countable) A survey is a formal way to gather data by asking question of people: a questionnaire.","e":"The Architects' Journal conducted a survey of its readers to find what were considered the best modern buildings in Britain."},{"m":"(countable) A land survey involves photographing and the land to make a map of it.","e":"Before building the train tunnel, extensive geological surveys were carried out on the British side of the Channel."},{"m":"(countable) A survey paper/book is a general description of a topic, often introductory."},{"m":"(countable) A survey is the act of reading a broad range of books and articles on a particular subject."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you survey something, you look at it to try to see or understand the whole of it."},{"m":"(transitive) If you survey people about their thoughts or personal information, you ask a large number of people in a formal way, often using a questionnaire."},{"m":"(transitive) If you survey a place, you look at every part of it, often from a high spot."},{"m":"(transitive) If you survey books and articles, you read a large number on a particular topic."}]}]},"decision":{"h":"decision","i":"/dɪˈsɪʒən/","a":"en-us-decision.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A decision is a sudden thought, with purpose, before someone does something. After a person makes a decision, the person has knowledge about a thing the person will do.","e":"After much thought, the person made a decision to go to the meeting."},{"m":"(countable) A decision is the end of a process in a committee. After a committee makes a decision, a record in writing says the important thing.","e":"After much discussion, the committee made an important decision about insurance."}]}]},"beauty":{"h":"beauty","i":"/ˈbjuːti/","a":"en-us-beauty.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Beauty is the quality of being nice to look at.","e":"Beauty makes things attractive."},{"m":"(countable) A beauty is something or someone that is good to look at.","e":"She is a beauty."}]}]},"chronology":{"h":"chronology","i":"/krəˈnɒl.ə.dʒi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-chronology.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Chronology is the science of finding out what events came in what order","e":"Chronology can help historians find out why an old empire ended."},{"m":"Chronology is text or graphics that show what events happened in what order","e":"The chronology at the back of the book shows the Kings and Queens of England."}]}]},"potential":{"h":"potential","i":"/pəˈtɛnʃəl/","a":"en-us-potential.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A potential customer, benefit, problem, etc. is one that might happen in the future.","e":"Realistic goals can then be set to prevent potential problems from becoming actual ones."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) If x has potential for y, then it might change toward y or cause y.","e":"Technology has the potential for improvement as well as for harm."},{"m":"(uncountable) If something has or shows potential, they will likely be very good in the future."},{"m":"; (electronics) The potential is the difference in voltage between two points on an electrical circuit."}]}]},"cultural":{"h":"cultural","i":"/ˈkʌlt͡ʃərəl/","a":"en-us-cultural.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A cultural background, difference, identity etc. relates or belongs to a particular group of people.","e":"Teachers should think about the cultural background of their students."},{"m":"Cultural things are related to art, music, books, etc.","e":"The new art museum has become the cultural center of the town."}]}]},"wound":{"h":"wound","i":"/wuːnd/","a":"en-us-wound-injury.ogg","l":"wind","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A wound is a cut in skin with pain and blood, a burn, or other similar mark on someone's body.","e":"I dropped a knife on my foot, but the wound was minor, so I didn't need to go to the hospital."}]}]},"wise":{"h":"wise","i":"/waɪz/","a":"en-us-wise.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A wise person has much knowledge and makes good decisions.","e":"Say your question to the old woman, because she is wise and will tell you good ideas about things to do."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(usually with up) If you wise up, you get informed; you learn something."}]}]},"wire":{"h":"wire","i":"/waɪə/","a":"en-us-wire.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A wire is a long, thin metal thing, mostly for the purpose of making a connection from electric power to a machine.","e":"A person cut the electric wire and all the machines in the building stopped."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To join a wire to something.","e":"They wired up all the machines in the building."}]}]},"wing":{"h":"wing","i":"/wɪŋ/","a":"en-us-wing.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A wing is the long flat part of a bird, insect or other flying thing. It is used to fly.","e":"This bird can fly very high very quickly because the bird uses strong wings with many feathers."},{"m":"A wing is part of a building, usually not the main part."},{"m":"A wing is part of a political group."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To fly with wings."},{"m":"If you wing it you do not have a plan—you are making up what you do while you do it."}]}]},"wind":{"h":"wind","i":"/ˈwɪnd/","a":"en-us-wind-air.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Wind is the air.","e":"The wind blows so strongly now that a person's hair goes in the person's face."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you wind something you wrap it around and make it tight.","e":"You need to wind the string around the stick."},{"m":"If you wind a clock or watch you tighten a spring inside it. This is done by turning knob. The spring powers the clock or watch as it unwinds (stops being tight)."},{"m":"If something winds it twists around in different directions.","e":"The road winds for miles."},{"m":"If something winds down, it runs out of power and gets slower. (Like a watch that is unwinding.)"},{"m":"How something winds up is how it becomes in the end or after something happens.","e":"I wound up lost after I made the wrong turn."}]}]},"wide":{"h":"wide","i":"/waɪd/","a":"en-us-wide.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is wide, it is long from one side to the other side.","e":"This box is 30 cm long and 20 cm wide, but only 10 cm high."},{"m":"If there is a wide range, variety, or world, there is a lot of it.","e":"The store offers a wide range of products."},{"m":"If you give something or someone a wide berth, you avoid them by a lot.","e":"He gave the barking dog a wide berth."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something is wide open, it is open to its full extent.","e":"She opened her eyes wide in surprise."},{"m":"If you are wide awake, you are completely awake and alert, often when you would prefer to be asleep.","e":"Despite the late hour, the children were wide awake and eager to open their presents."},{"m":"If two things are wide apart, there is a lot of space between them.","e":"\"It was this big,\" she said, spreading her hands as wide apart as she could."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If something goes wide of the target, it misses the target.","e":"The soccer ball went wide of the goal."},{"m":"If the ball or a player is/plays/goes wide, they are near the sides of the field or court.","e":"He ran wide and got tackled near the sideline."}]}]},"whistle":{"h":"whistle","i":"/wɪsl̩/","a":"en-us-whistle.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A whistle is a sound like music. A person makes a whistling sound by blowing air when the person's mouth is in a little circle.","e":"The whistle of the wind in trees was low and sad."},{"m":"A whistle is a little instrument made of wood, metal or other material. A person puts the instrument in the person's mouth and blows air to make a loud whistling sound.","e":"When you are in danger, blow your whistle loudly and someone will run and help you."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To whistle is to make a whistling sound with one's mouth.","e":"A happy person is able to whistle and work at the same time."}]}]},"whip":{"h":"whip","i":"/wɪp/","a":"en-us-whip.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A whip is a long, thin leather instrument. A person uses it, with very quick motion, to give pain. A person uses it on a horse or another person as punishment.","e":"When the horse sees the whip in the person's hand, the horse gets scared and runs far away."},{"m":"(countable) (politics) A whip is a member of a political party who is in charge of the party's policies in votes."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you whip something, you hit it with a whip.","e":"Jockeys whip horses to make them go faster."}]}]},"while":{"h":"while","i":"/ʍaɪl/","a":"en-us-while.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If x happens while y happens, they happen at the same time.","e":"He fell asleep while sitting at his desk."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A while is a short time.","e":"After a while I will stop working and cook food for us."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you while away the time, you spend it doing something not very productive.","e":"On Sundays, I like to while away the hours by reading."}]}]},"ventriloquist":{"h":"ventriloquist","i":"/vɛnˈtrɪl.ə.kwɪst/","a":"en-us-ventriloquist.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A ventriloquist is a person who does a trick to make the person's voice seem to be coming from a different direction. The ventriloquist talks but does not move the mouth. People think the ventriloquist is not talking and they think a thing or an animal or a different person is talking.","e":"People laughed when the ventriloquist made a shoe talk to a hat."}]}]},"watch":{"h":"watch","i":"/wɒtʃ/","a":"en-us-watch.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A watch is a little clock on a person's arm near the person's hand, to measure time.","e":"The person looks at his watch and has a thought that he is late."},{"m":"A watch is the period of time on duty for crews who are working together."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To watch is to look for a long time or to look at somebody doing something.","e":"I watched the person cook the food and now I know how to cook the food."}]}]},"walk":{"h":"walk","i":"/wɔːk/","a":"en-us-walk.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you walk, you go on foot, step by step. Walking is slower than running.","e":"No train goes to that town, so people need to walk to go there."},{"m":"(intransitive) To walk free; to escape punishment."},{"m":"(intransitive) If an object walks, it goes missing or is stolen."},{"m":"(transitive) If you walk, you travel some distance by walking.","e":"I walk two miles to school every day."},{"m":"(transitive) If you walk someone, you go for a walk with them.","e":"Please walk the dog."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A walk is what we do when we go on foot.","e":"Are you taking the dog for a walk?"}]}]},"through":{"h":"through","i":"/θruː/","a":"en-us-through.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"from one end or side of something to the other","e":"The ink went through the paper and made the table wet."}]}]},"test":{"h":"test","i":"/tɛst/","a":"en-us-test.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A test is writing that many learners do in a room at the same time so that people are able to see how much knowledge the learners have.","e":"I'm happy because I got a high mark on the test."},{"m":"(countable) A test is something someone does to see if something works.","e":"The person did a good test of the machine by pushing all the buttons and watching the machine."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) The action of testing; to try something out to see whether it works.","e":"He tested the software many times."}]}]},"tail":{"h":"tail","i":"/teɪl/","a":"en-us-tail.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A tail is a long, thin part on the back end of an animal.","e":"The dog wags his tail (moves his tail quickly from side to side) when he sees his friend."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you tail someone, you follow them without them noticing; you observe them."}]}]},"headphone":{"h":"headphone","i":"/ˈhedfəʊn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-headphone.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (usually plural) A headphone is a very little machine near a person's ear that makes sound.","e":"The music on the person's headphones was so loud that he didn't know I was talking to him."}]}]},"stereophonic":{"h":"stereophonic","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Using two headphones with almost the same sound so the sound seems to be coming from a direction.","e":"This stereophonic machine is very good! It seems as if the music is coming from this room!"}]}]},"spoon":{"h":"spoon","i":"/spuːn/","a":"en-us-spoon.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A spoon is a little, long, thin, metal thing with a round end for putting food in one's mouth.","e":"Put a knife, a fork and a spoon near the plate on the table."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When two people spoon, they lie next to each other with one person's back against the other person's front, similar to the way two spoons are stacked together."}]}]},"so":{"h":"so","i":"/səʊ/","a":"en-us-so.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Very; extremely.","e":"The box was so wide that the person was not able to take it through the door."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Saying the result or purpose.","e":"The gravestones were covered with moss, so that it was impossible to read the names on them."}]},{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"Used in the expression or so after a number or amount to show that it is not exact; about, approximately.","e":"I didn't want to drive the fifteen or so highway minutes into town."}]}]},"skirt":{"h":"skirt","i":"/skɜːt/","a":"en-us-skirt.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A skirt is a loose cloth that a woman uses to cover her legs; the lower part of a dress.","e":"She has a blue skirt and a red shirt on."}]}]},"room":{"h":"room","i":"/ru:m/","a":"en-us-room.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A room is a place which is part of a building. Someone is able to see other people who are in the same room.","e":"We need a long, wide room because many people will be at the meeting."},{"m":"(uncountable) Room can mean some space; a place with nothing, only air.","e":"I need room to be able to move my arms and not touch people."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To live in or share a room.","e":"I roomed with Ryan all four years of college."}]}]},"put":{"h":"put","i":"/pʊt/","a":"en-us-put.ogg","l":"put","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you put a thing someplace, you move a thing to a place.","e":"I always put my books on the table when I get home from school."}]}]},"old":{"h":"old","i":"/əʊld/","a":"en-uk-old.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone or something is old, they are not young; they have been in existence for a long time.","e":"An old man has gray hair."},{"m":"How old someone is, is their age.","e":"\"Ashley, how old are you?\" \"I'm only 16 years old.\""},{"m":"Your old school, boss, address, etc. is one that you no longer use or are no longer together with.","e":"I didn't have many friends at my old school."}]}]},"mass":{"h":"mass","i":"/mæs/","a":"en-us-mass.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A measure of how much material is in something.","e":"The Earth has much more mass than the moon."},{"m":"Much material.","e":"A mass of dirty branches stopped the river."},{"m":"A Christian ceremony in memory of.","e":"He goes to mass every Sunday."},{"m":"A crowd of people.","e":"A mass of protesters gathered at city hall."}]}]},"like":{"h":"like","i":"/laɪ̯k/","a":"en-us-like.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To like someone or something means to find someone or something pleasant, enjoyable, or interesting.","e":"I like good food."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"the same.","e":"Like in those days, things are changing."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A like is something that you think is good.","e":"Our own likes and dislikes are shaped by what our parents liked."},{"m":"At the end of a list of things, and the like means: and other similar things.","e":"She's good at science, math, and the like."},{"m":"You use the likes of someone to show that you don't think that person is a good person.","e":"You shouldn't be hanging around with the likes of him."}]},{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"You use like, when you are trying to think about the right words.","e":"He's really, like you know, uh... difficult."},{"m":"You use like when the information isn't exactly true.","e":"We went there when we were like five years old."},{"m":"You use like when you are trying to make something sound softer.","e":"OK, like, why don't you try going there."},{"m":"You use like before what somebody said.","e":"So, I'm like, \"What do you mean.\" And he's like, \"you know what I mean.\""}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"similar or the same","e":"She's very like her mother."}]}]},"hammer":{"h":"hammer","i":"/ˈhæmə/","a":"en-us-hammer.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hammer is a heavy tool for pushing a nail into wood.","e":"When you have only a hammer, all things seem like nails."},{"m":"(countable) A hammer is a moving part of a gun that hits the firing pin to make the gun fire."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you hammer something, you push a nail into wood using a hammer.","e":"He hammered so hard that the building moved a little."}]}]},"get":{"h":"get","i":"/gɛt/","a":"en-us-get.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) or obtain.","e":"The woman goes to the store and gets a new dress."},{"m":"(intransitive).","e":"The problem got worse."},{"m":"(intransitive) You use get to form a passive clause.","e":"He got hit by a car."}]}]},"fornication":{"h":"fornication","i":"/ˌfɔrnɪˈkeɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-fornication.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Fornication is sexual intercourse between two people who are not married."}]}]},"even":{"h":"even","i":"/ˈi:vən/","a":"en-us-even.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"You use even to focus on the most surprising or unlikely case."},{"m":"With preposition phrases:","e":"Even in peaceful countries, there are problems."},{"m":"With noun phrases:","e":"Everyone walks to school here, even the teachers."},{"m":"With adjective phrases:","e":"She didn't tell me about it and I expect she wasn't even aware of it."},{"m":"With verb phrases:","e":"Our progress was not rewarded. In fact, it was not even mentioned."},{"m":"With adverb phrases (rarely):","e":"He won't lose his job, not even temporarily."},{"m":"With so:","e":"I hid it in the books where nobody would look. Even so, I worried about it all evening."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If things are even, the top or surface of each is as high as the others.","e":"The top of the wall is even because the bricks are all the same size."},{"m":"If a number is even, it can be divided into 2 equal parts.","e":"2, 4, 6 and 8 are even numbers. 1, 3, 5 and 7 are not even numbers; they are odd numbers."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you even something (out/up), you reduce the ups and downs; you make it smooth or equal.","e":"India was leading 2-1, but Australia evened the score in the last minute."},{"m":"If you even a problem out, you solve it.","e":"I went down and evened it all out. Everyone's happy now."}]}]},"dress":{"h":"dress","i":"/drɛs/","a":"en-us-dress.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A dress is a loose cloth covering a woman's body. The lower part is like a skirt. The top part is like a shirt.","e":"She looked beautiful because she had a very nice dress."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To put clothes on something.","e":"I dressed my little sister for school this morning."},{"m":"(intransitive) To put clothes on yourself.","e":"I just need to dress and then we can go."},{"m":"(transitive) To prepare the surface of a material (usually stone or lumber)."},{"m":"To cover a wound with a bandage.","e":"That cut looks really bad. Here, let me dress it"},{"m":"(transitive) To prepare food for cooking, especially by seasoning it."}]}]},"cloth":{"h":"cloth","i":"/klɒθ/","a":"en-us-cloth.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Cloth is a thin, flat material, often made from cotton or polyester."},{"m":"(countable) A cloth is a piece of cloth, usually for cleaning things.","e":"The person used a wet cloth to wash the table."}]}]},"where":{"h":"where","i":"/ʍɛə(r)/","a":"en-us-where.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"(In or to) what place or situation.","e":"Where do you live?"},{"m":"(relative) (In or to) the place or situation in which.","e":"The room where the people cook the food is not cold."},{"m":"You use where to introduce a clause that contrasts with the other parts of the sentence.","e":"Where Nixon was secretive and suspicious, Ford was relaxed, open and candid."}]}]},"wheel":{"h":"wheel","i":"/wiːl/","a":"en-us-wheel.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A wheel is a round thing (circle) on a cart or carriage or train or other machine that moves. A cart has four wheels that touch the road and turn.","e":"The cart needs a very smooth road because it has little wheels."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you wheel something somewhere, you transport it in or on a vehicle that has wheels.","e":"The nurses wheeled her into the operating theatre."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something is wheeling, it is travelling in circles.","e":"The eagle wheeled and dived towards the ground to catch its prey."}]}]},"way":{"h":"way","i":"/weɪ/","a":"en-us-way.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A way is how someone does something.","e":"The committee made a good decision about which way to make the machine."},{"m":"(countable) A way is a style.","e":"She dresses that way every day."},{"m":"(countable) A way is a path, a road, or a route; how you get to a certain place.","e":"Do you know the way to the lunch room?"}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"very far","e":"I think that it's way too early to tell what the result will be."}]}]},"wax":{"h":"wax","i":"/wæks/","a":"en-us-wax.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Wax is a solid material made of animal fat.","e":"A candle is made of wax and a thick thread and has a flame on top."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you wax something, you put wax on it, for example, a car.","e":"She waxed her car to make the paint shine brightly."},{"m":"When something waxes, it means that it gets bigger and becomes more full.","e":"As the moon changes from a new moon to a full moon, it is said to be waxing."}]}]},"wave":{"h":"wave","i":"/weɪv/","a":"en-us-wave.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A wave is the motion of water up and down.","e":"The wind blew strongly on the water and made high waves."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To move from side to side again and again.","e":"When she saw her friend, she waved her hand so her friend would see her."}]}]},"well":{"h":"well","i":"/wɛl/","a":"en-us-well.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"In a good way.","e":"He washed the table very well, so now it is very clean."},{"m":", not sick.","e":"I had the flu, but then I got well."}]},{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"You use well to tell others that you're going to say something, that you're going to continue speaking, or that you're going to change the topic.","e":"Well, I guess I'm leaving now."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hole in the ground for getting water or oil.","e":"There was no river nearby, so they dug a well to get water."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If a liquid, feeling, or idea wells up, it rises gradually to the surface.","e":"The tears welled up in her eyes."}]}]},"transfer":{"h":"transfer","i":"/trænsˈfɚ/","a":"en-us-transfer.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you transfer (something), you move (it) to a different place.","e":"After he became the top salesman he was transferred to the head office."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A transfer is the act of transferring something from one form to another.","e":"trades involve the transfer of currency from one country to another."},{"m":"(countable) A transfer is the act of moving something from one location to another.","e":"You will get a transfer at the third stop."}]}]},"cork":{"h":"cork","i":"/kɔrk/","a":"en-us-cork.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cork is a small, round piece of wood which people put in the top of a bottle to close it.","e":"I took the cork out of the wine bottle with a corkscrew."},{"m":"(uncountable) Cork is a type of wood. It is quite soft and light. It is often used to make corks (sense 1)."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you cork a bottle, you seal it with a [[#Noun|cork]]."},{"m":"(transitive) If you cork something, you blacken it with a burnt cork."}]}]},"chance":{"h":"chance","i":"/tʃɑːns/","a":"en-uk-chance.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Something that can happen.","e":"We have the chance."},{"m":"Something that is random; luck.","e":"Poker is a game of chance."},{"m":"How much something is likely to be true.","e":"There is a 30% chance of rain tomorrow."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you chance upon something, you discover it even though you were not looking for it."},{"m":"If you chance something, you try it, even though it may not work."}]}]},"banana":{"h":"banana","i":"/bəˈnɑ:nə/","a":"en-us-banana.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A long fruit with smooth yellow skin."},{"m":"A yellow colour, like the colour of a banana."}]}]},"select":{"h":"select","i":"/sɪˈlɛkt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-select.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you select something, you choose it.","e":"Students follow a general course in their first year, and in the final year they select one of three specialist areas of study."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is select it is special in a good way—high quality.","e":"His skill and efforts took him into the select group of men who have scored over 50 League goals for our club."}]}]},"accept":{"h":"accept","i":"/əkˈsept/","a":"en-uk-accept.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you accept something, you take it when somebody gives it to you.","e":"She accepted the award."},{"m":"(transitive) If you accept something, you believe it as true or valid.","e":"I accept your plan."}]}]},"credit":{"h":"credit","i":"/krɛdɪt/","a":"en-us-credit.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Credit is an agreement to buy something and pay later.","e":"We bought the new dining room table on credit."},{"m":"(uncountable) Credit is positive words or feelings.","e":"He gave credit to local management and to the unions for the improvements at the factory."},{"m":"(countable) A credit is a course or part of a course that you complete at college or university.","e":"I just need five more credits to finish my degree."},{"m":"(countable) A credit is record of money put in an account."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you credit an account, you add money to it.","e":"I called the bank about the mistake and they credited my account with the missing $50."},{"m":"(transitive) If you credit somebody with something, you say that they did it.","e":"Most people have credited Churchill with this saying, but there is no proof that he actually said it."},{"m":"(transitive); (formal) If you credit something, you believe it."}]}]},"perceive":{"h":"perceive","i":"/pəˈsiːv/","a":"en-us-perceive.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you perceive something, you notice it through one of your senses (you see it, touch it, smell it, hear it, or taste it); to be aware of something.","e":"He was unable to perceive any difference at all in the room after the changes."},{"m":"(transitive); If you perceive something, you believe it or understand it.","e":"Education is widely perceived as a powerful way to improve the quality of life."}]}]},"focus":{"h":"focus","i":"/ˈfoʊ.kəs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-focus.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you focus on something, you pay special attention to it.","e":"A small company will probably focus its attention on each artist's project more than a major label."},{"m":"If you focus a lens, you adjust it to make a clear picture.","e":"Most digital cameras automatically focus on the object in the centre."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (usually singular) The focus is the main thing or person that people are paying attention to."},{"m":"(uncountable) If your focus is on something, your attention is on it."},{"m":"(uncountable) If something is in focus, the image is clear."}]}]},"purchase":{"h":"purchase","i":"/ˈpɝtʃəs/","a":"en-us-purchase.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) (formal) If you purchase something, you buy it.","e":"A licence needs to be purchased from the local authority and printing of tickets also adds to the costs."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (formal) A purchase is something that you have bought.","e":"Since the purchase of Columbia Pictures by Sony, the US has been very afraid of Japan."},{"m":"(countable) (formal) A purchase is a strong hold on something.","e":"He wasn't able to get a purchase on his bag before it was pulled away from him."}]}]},"journal":{"h":"journal","i":"/ˈdʒɜrnəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-journal.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A journal is a record of what is happening, usually written regularly (e.g., daily, weekly, monthly, etc.), often scientific.","e":"They published their study in the British Medical Journal."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you journal, you regularly record what is happening, usually in writing."}]}]},"administration":{"h":"administration","i":"/ədˌmɪnəˈstreɪʃən/","a":"en-us-administration.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Administration is the process of running and an organisation such as a business or government.","e":"The mayor is responsible for the administration of the town."},{"m":"The administration are the people who run and organise an organisation such as a business or government.","e":"In short, the administration does not actually know why it wants a space station."}]}]},"organisation":{"h":"organisation","i":"/ˈɔː(r).ɡən.aɪˌzeɪ.ʃən/","a":"en-us-organisation.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An organisation is a group of people with a particular purpose (e.g., companies, teams, clubs, churches, etc.)","e":"The daycare is operated by a voluntary organisation of parents and teachers."},{"m":"Organisation is the way that something is put together.","e":"The organisation of the book is very difficult to understand."}]}]},"organization":{"h":"organization","i":"/ˈɔː(r).ɡən.aɪˌzeɪ.ʃən/","a":"en-us-organisation.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An organization is a group of people with a particular purpose (e.g., teams, clubs, churches, etc.)","e":"The daycare is operated by a voluntary organization of parents and teachers."},{"m":"Organization is the way that something is put together.","e":"The organization of the book is very difficult to understand."}]}]},"maintenance":{"h":"maintenance","i":"/ˈmeɪntɪnəns/","a":"en-us-maintenance.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Maintenance is the process of regularly fixing things and keeping something in good shape.","e":"After 8,000 km, you should take the car in for maintenance."}]}]},"design":{"h":"design","i":"/dɪˈzaɪn/","a":"en-us-design.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Design is how something looks and works.","e":"Honda has a new engine in design."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you design something, you plan and show how it will look and work.","e":"The team was asked to design a new video game controller."}]}]},"obtain":{"h":"obtain","i":"/əbˈteɪn/","a":"en-us-obtain.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) (formal) If you obtain something, you get it.","e":"The newspaper was able to obtain the information from police."},{"m":"(intransitive) (formal) If something obtains, it is true or it exists.","e":"His argument is therefore compatible only in cases where class difference does not obtain."}]}]},"restrict":{"h":"restrict","i":"/rɪˈstrɪkt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-restrict.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you restrict something, you limit it.","e":"This room is restricted to company employees. Other people may not enter."}]}]},"conduct":{"h":"conduct","i":"/kənˈdʌkt/","a":"en-ca-conduct.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you conduct an activity or process, you do it or carry it out.","e":"The war made it very difficult to conduct business."},{"m":"If you conduct music, you stand in front of the musicians and show them how to sing or play."},{"m":"(transitive); (only of yourself); (formal) The way you conduct yourself is the way you act or treat others.","e":"I hope the children will be able to conduct themselve well at the party."},{"m":"If something conducts energy, it lets the energy move through or along it.","e":"Glass is a good insulator because it will not conduct electricity."},{"m":"(transitive) If you conduct somebody or a tour, you show people around a place.","e":"Please conduct him to the waiting room."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) (formal) A person's conduct is the way they act or treat others.","e":"Killing a person, for any reason, is a criminal act and such conduct must not be allowed."}]}]},"rush":{"h":"rush","i":"/rʌʃ/","a":"en-us-rush.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you rush, you move or work quickly.","e":"After the accident, they rushed him to the hospital."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A rush is a fast movement.","e":"As the movie finished, there was a rush to the toilets."}]}]},"manufacture":{"h":"manufacture","i":"/ˌmænjuˈfækt͡ʃɚ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-manufacture.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you manufacture something, you make it, usually in a factory.","e":"The goods were manufactured in China and shipped to Canada for sale."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Manufacture is the process of making something.","e":"The company specializes in the manufacture of small industrial motors."}]}]},"withdraw":{"h":"withdraw","i":"/wɪðˈdrɔː/","a":"en-us-withdraw.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you withdraw (something) from somewhere, you take (it) out.","e":"The conservatives have withdrawn support from the government."}]}]},"waste":{"h":"waste","i":"/weɪst/","a":"en-us-waste.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To use something for no reason, or for bad reasons or only little reasons, and after it is used no one can use it again.","e":"He wasted the food by making it dirty."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Things that are not useful; things that people want to take out of their house."}]}]},"war":{"h":"war","i":"/woʊr/","a":"en-us-war.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"War is when armies or fight against each other.","e":"Those two countries are always at war."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you war with someone or something, you fight or battle with them."}]}]},"wall":{"h":"wall","i":"/wɔːl/","a":"en-us-wall.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) One side of a house; a high, flat part of a building.","e":"All four walls of the room are painted in blue."},{"m":"(countable) A solid barrier between two areas.","e":"There is a wall between the two gardens."}]}]},"twist":{"h":"twist","i":"/twɪst/","a":"en-us-twist.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you twist something, you turn one part of it in one direction and another part in the other direction at the same time."}]}]},"turn":{"h":"turn","i":"/tɜːn/","a":"en-us-turn.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To face a different direction","e":"The car turned the corner and went north."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something turns a certain way, it becomes that way.","e":"The sky turned dark and cloudy."}]}]},"trouble":{"h":"trouble","i":"/ˈtrʌb(ə)l/","a":"en-us-trouble.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"or bad things happening; problems."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To bother or annoy."}]}]},"true":{"h":"true","i":"/truː/","a":"en-uk-true.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is true, it is correct or real, not imagined or made up.","e":"She says she didn't take the money, but what she says is not true."}]}]},"trick":{"h":"trick","i":"/trɪk/","a":"en-us-trick.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To make someone think something that is not true.","e":"He tricked her into thinking he had much money."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Something you do to fool (trick) someone.","e":"I did a trick that the children thought was magic."},{"m":"Something special you can do.","e":"I know a few tricks with a computer."},{"m":"Something clever you do that might solve a problem.","e":"I know just the trick for this."}]}]},"expand":{"h":"expand","i":"/ɛkˈspænd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-expand.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something expands, it becomes bigger.","e":"The company is looking at expanding into new products."}]}]},"become":{"h":"become","i":"/bə'kʌm, bɪˈkʌm/","a":"en-us-become.ogg","l":"become","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If x becomes y, it changes into y or changes to be more y.","e":"The boy has become a man."},{"m":"(transitive); (never progressive); (formal) If something becomes someone, it suits them or looks good on them.","e":"Nice hat! It really becomes you."}]}]},"tray":{"h":"tray","i":"/treɪ/","a":"en-us-tray.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A big plate for many people; a wide, long, flat thing that people put food on.","e":"Take some food from the tray and put it on your plate."}]}]},"train":{"h":"train","i":"/treɪn/","a":"en-uk-a train.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A long vehicle with many cars that are joined together. A train runs on a track.","e":"I took the train from Paris to Frankfurt."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you train someone, you teach them a particular skill.","e":"In school we had computer training and sex education."}]}]},"sample":{"h":"sample","i":"/ˈsɑːm.pəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-sample.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sample is a small amount of something to try or test it.","e":"The nurse took a small blood sample."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you sample something, you try or test a small amount of it.","e":"After sampling each of the wines, she bought the one she liked best."}]}]},"bottom":{"h":"bottom","i":"/ˈbɒtəm/","a":"en-us-bottom.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The bottom of something is its lowest part.","e":"Lucy took a pen and wrote her name at the bottom of the page."},{"m":"(countable) If you are at the bottom, you are at the social lowest position.","e":"Chicago still ranks near the bottom among major cities."},{"m":"(countable) Your bottom is the round part between your legs and your back.","e":"She ran into the tree and sat down hard on her bottom."},{"m":"(countable) A bottom is the part of a set of clothing that you put your legs through.","e":"Her pink top was perfect, but I didn't like how the bottom fit."},{"m":"(countable) The bottom of an inning in baseball is its second half.","e":"It's the bottom of the ninth inning and the score is tied."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If something bottoms (out), it stops going down.","e":"When do you think the housing problems are going to bottom out?"}]}]},"frequently":{"h":"frequently","i":"/ˈfriː.kwənt.li/","a":"en-us-frequently.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If you do something frequently, you do it often.","e":"The library is frequently used by students."}]}]},"performance":{"h":"performance","i":"/pə'fɔːməns/","a":"en-us-performance.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A performance is a show of acting or music.","e":"We went to see a performance by local musicians last night."},{"m":"The performance of a person, machine, company, etc. is how well it does its job.","e":"After a year of losing money, the company needs to improve performance."}]}]},"inside":{"h":"inside","i":"/ˈɪnsaɪd/","a":"en-us-inside.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If x is or moves inside y, it is in y.","e":"He locked his keys inside his car."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The inside of something is the part that you can't see or can't touch because other parts are around it.","e":"The inside of my mouth hurts."}]}]},"trade":{"h":"trade","i":"/treɪd/","a":"en-uk-trade.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When two people trade, one gives something to the other and the other gives something to the first one. They make an exchange. Sometimes money is one of the things."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Trade is the buying and selling of goods.","e":"Trade between Canada and the US is at its highest level in years."},{"m":"(countable) A trade is the act of trading.","e":"I think I made a good trade."},{"m":"(countable) A trade is a job that needs a special skill to do.","e":"The carpenters trade involves making things from wood."}]}]},"touch":{"h":"touch","i":"/tʌʧ/","a":"en-us-touch.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you touch something, you feel it with your hand.","e":"Don't touch the oven -- it's hot and you will get a burn."},{"m":"(transitive) If you touch something, you move so near to it that there is no space between you and it."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Touch is the act of feeling or coming into physical contact with something.","e":"A gentle touch of the fabric told her it was silk."},{"m":"(uncountable) Touch is ability to feel through the skin by physical contact.","e":"After the accident, he lost his sense of touch."},{"m":"(countable) A touch of something is a small amount of it.","e":"There was a touch of sadness in his voice."}]}]},"detective":{"h":"detective","i":"/dɪˈtɛktɪv/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-detective.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A detective is a person who tries to find information to help people or solve crimes, usually a non-patrol police officer.","e":"He hired a private detective to find the missing art."}]}]},"raw":{"h":"raw","i":"/rɔː/","a":"en-us-raw.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is raw, it has not been cooked, processed, prepared, etc.","e":"You should wash your hands after touching raw meat."},{"m":"When something is raw, it is in a natural state."}]}]},"top":{"h":"top","i":"/tɒp/","a":"en-us-top.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The highest part of something; the upper part; the part people can put things on.","e":"The top of the table is flat."},{"m":"(countable) A toy for children to play with. It is shaped like a funnel, and it spins on its narrowest point."},{"m":"(countable) A shirt"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you top something, you add toppings or cover with it a [[#Noun|top]].","e":"I like my ice cream topped with chocolate sauce."},{"m":"If A tops B, A beats B by an amount or value."}]}]},"together":{"h":"together","i":"/tʊˈgɛð.ə(r)/","a":"en-us-together.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Near; close; in the same place; not far; in a family or group.","e":"I put all the books about food together on one shelf."},{"m":"Putting parts of something into one thing. Organizing","e":"He put together a meeting."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you say that someone is together, you mean he or she is well organized and focused.","e":"I really admire how together she is."}]}]},"police":{"h":"police","i":"/pəˈliːs/","a":"en-us-police.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The police are the government force who enforce laws, prevent crime, stop and arrest criminals, regulate traffic, help maintain public order, and help with emergencies.","e":"When we saw the man take the money, we called the police."},{"m":"The police means the city government department that is concerned with laws and helping with emergencies.","e":"The Police Department there replaced the previous system of having volunteers keep the city safe."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you police an area or activity, you watch it to make sure no laws are being broken.","e":"There are fewer crimes in the countryside, but it's difficult to police such a big area."}]}]},"toe":{"h":"toe","i":"/təʊ/","a":"en-us-toe.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A toe is a little part of a foot, like a finger. A foot has 5 toes.","e":"This shoe is too small -- it gives me pain in my toes."}]}]},"tin":{"h":"tin","i":"/tɪn/","a":"en-us-tin.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The kind of metal that cans are frequently made with. It is the chemical element Sn."},{"m":"(countable) A can; a metal thing with food in it."}]}]},"mail":{"h":"mail","i":"/meɪl/","a":"en-us-mail.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Mail is the messages and packages that you send to other people.","e":"There's no mail today because the post office is closed."},{"m":"Email."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you mail something, you send it through the post.","e":"I mailed a birthday card to him last week."}]}]},"depressed":{"h":"depressed","i":"/dəˈprɛst/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Persent101-depressed.wav","l":"depress","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is depressed, they have the condition called depression - they are very sad and cannot imagine being happy in the future.","e":"No one knows why it happened, but last year, Jay became depressed."},{"m":"If someone is depressed, they are very sad and unhappy.","e":"\"I heard Katie lost the race.\" \"Yes, she is a bit depressed about it.\""},{"m":"If the economy is depressed, it is doing badly.","e":"In 2008, the economy was severely depressed"},{"m":"If something that has many levels--like a surface, the ground, or something that moves up and down--is depressed, it is low.","e":"The ground is depressed where the rock used to be."}]}]},"passenger":{"h":"passenger","i":"/ˈpæsɪnd͡ʒɚ/","a":"en-us-passenger.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A passenger is a person who is riding a vehicle—not the driver.","e":"The boat can carry 101 passengers at more than 80&nbsp;km/h across waves 1.5 m high."}]}]},"juice":{"h":"juice","i":"/d͡ʒuːs/","a":"en-us-juice.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Juice is the liquid that you get when you squeeze a fruit or vegetable.","e":"I usually have orange juice and toast for breakfast."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you juice a fruit or a vegetable, you get the juice out of it.","e":"I had to juice five oranges just to get one glass of juice."}]}]},"explode":{"h":"explode","i":"/ɪkˈspləʊd/","a":"en-us-explode.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something explodes, it breaks apart quickly and strongly, often with strong heat, sound, and light.","e":"A bomb exploded in the market, killing five people."}]}]},"tie":{"h":"tie","i":"/taɪ/","a":"en-us-tie.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you tie something, you attach it using string or rope.","e":"I was six when I learned to tie up my shoes."},{"m":"(intransitive) If two teams or players tie, they have the same score in a game.","e":"Naples and Rome tied the game two all."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A tie is a piece of cloth that you wear around your neck as a decoration.","e":"At work, you need to wear a suit and tie."}]}]},"tight":{"h":"tight","i":"/taɪt/","a":"en-us-tight.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If x is tight, it fits closely and strongly to y.","e":"The bandage on your finger should not be too tight or your finger may turn blue."},{"m":"If a string is tight its ends are as far apart as possible.","e":"A tight rope is in a straight line."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If you close or tie something tight, you do it strongly or closely so that it won't change easily.","e":"He closed the door tight behind them."}]}]},"though":{"h":"though","i":"/ðəʊ/","a":"en-us-though.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"You use though to introduce a fact which you regard as less important than the fact in the main clause.","e":"Though he talked very loudly, she did not hear him."},{"m":"You use though to add a fact or an opinion that makes the previous statement less strong or less important.","e":"Our team lost. It was a good game though."}]}]},"thread":{"h":"thread","i":"/θrɛd/","a":"en-us-thread.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A thread is a long, very thin, soft material used to join or make cloth.","e":"She pushed the thread through the hole in the needle."},{"m":"(countable) A thread is a process."},{"m":"(countable) A thread is a group of messages from a discussion on an Internet forum."},{"m":"(countable) A thread is a structure that allows a screw to be fastened."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you thread something, then you make a string or thread out of it."}]}]},"thin":{"h":"thin","i":"/'θɪn/","a":"en-us-thin.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is thin, there's a short distance from one side to the other.","e":"I can hear the people in the other room because the wall is thin."},{"m":"If something is thin it doesn't have a lot of stuff in it.","e":"The soup is too thin. It needs more flavour."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something thins, there is less of it.","e":"After the show, the crowd thinned out quickly and only a few people stayed."}]}]},"thick":{"h":"thick","i":"/θɪk/","a":"en-us-thick.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is thick, there is some distance from one side to the other.","e":"He was a workman with big hands and thick fingers."},{"m":"If something is thick it has a lot of stuff in it.","e":"I am warm because I have a thick coat."},{"m":"If a liquid is thick, it can't flow very quickly."}]}]},"then":{"h":"then","i":"/ðɛn/","a":"en-us-then.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"(At) that time or that moment.","e":"Then she was little. Now she is big."},{"m":"something else.","e":"First, I cook the food; then I eat it, and then I wash the plates."},{"m":"In that case.","e":"If she is happy, then I'm happy too."}]}]},"than":{"h":"than","i":"/ðæn/","a":"en-us-than.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Used to compare two things that are not equal.","e":"The tree is higher than the house."}]}]},"star":{"h":"star","i":"/stɑː(r)/","a":"en-us-star.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A star is a bright thing in the sky at night. The sun is also one of stars.","e":"Stars seem little, but they are big and far away."},{"m":"(countable) A star (★) is a shape with five or six sharp ends.","e":"My teacher put a gold star on my test."},{"m":"(countable) A star is a celebrity.","e":"Brad Pitt is a popular star."},{"m":"(countable) A star is an actor who has the lead role in a movie, television show, or play.","e":"John Wayne is the star of many western movies."},{"m":"(countable) (printing, typography) A star is an asterisk (*).","e":"A star next to your name on the guest list means you will receive an award."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you star in something, you are on of the main performers, usually in an entertainment program.","e":"Brad Pitt will star in another movie next year."},{"m":"If you star something, you mark it with a star or asterisk.","e":"I starred question one because I got it correct."}]}]},"teach":{"h":"teach","i":"/'tiʧ/","a":"en-us-teach.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To help someone learn something. To tell someone how to do something.","e":"Most parents try to teach their children to be nice."}]}]},"teaching":{"h":"teaching","i":"/ˈtiːt͡ʃɪŋ/","a":"en-us-teaching.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Something taught by an important person in religion or philosophy.","e":"Many people follow the teachings of."},{"m":"The profession or job of teaching.","e":"Teaching has seen many changes over the years."}]}]},"soap":{"h":"soap","i":"/soʊp/","a":"en-us-soap.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Soap is a solid or liquid that you use to wash things.","e":"The soap slipped out of her hand in the shower."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you soap something, you put soap on it.","e":"I soaped her hair while my daughter splashed in the bath."}]}]},"package":{"h":"package","i":"/ˈpækɪdʒ/","a":"en-us-package.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A package is something in a box, usually to send in the mail.","e":"Some packages arrived from the post office."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you package something, you put it in a box, usually to send it in the mail.","e":"We packaged up the broken radio, and sent it back to the shop."}]}]},"furthermore":{"h":"furthermore","i":"/ˈfɜː(r).ðə(r).mɔː(r)/","a":"en-us-furthermore.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"(formal) You use furthermore to add more information to what was already said or written.","e":"We believe that the project is possible. Furthermore, we believe that we can do it within a few months."}]}]},"globe":{"h":"globe","i":"/ɡləʊb/","a":"EN-AU ck1 globe.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A globe is a solid shaped like a ball, often with a map on it.","e":"He spun the globe on his desk, looking for Japan."},{"m":"(countable) The globe is the Earth.","e":"People all around the globe love soccer."}]}]},"tendency":{"h":"tendency","i":"/ˈtɛndənsi/","a":"en-us-tendency.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A tendency is an inclination of something to behave in a particular way or to go in a particular direction.","e":"He has a tendency to talk too much."}]}]},"take":{"h":"take","i":"/teɪk/","a":"en-uk-to take.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you take an action, you do it.","e":"I took a walk with my dog. = I walked with my dog."},{"m":"(transitive) If you take something or someone, you bring them from one place to another.","e":"I don't want this. Can you take it away, please?"},{"m":"(transitive) If x takes money, time, etc., you need to use that for x.","e":"If we go to your house, it will take one hour."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A person's take is his view of something.","e":"What is your take on that recent movie? Did you enjoy it?"},{"m":"A take is the reward or profit you get from doing something.","e":"If help you with this task, I demand you give me part of your take."},{"m":"A take is part of a performance which is recorded without a break.","e":"The director was not happy with the first take, so we had to do it again."}]}]},"false":{"h":"false","i":"/fɔːls/","a":"en-us-false.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is false, it is not true or not real.","e":"It is false that 2 + 2 = 5."}]}]},"till":{"h":"till","i":"/tɪl/","a":"en-us-till.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"In a period of time ending at a time someone says.","e":"We will tell stories till it is time to sleep."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To make the earth ready for seeds."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(mostly UK) A till is cash register; a machine which counts sales in shops and stores the money.","e":"The till contained one hundred dollars at the end of the day"}]}]},"system":{"h":"system","i":"/ˈsɪstəm/","a":"en-us-system.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A system is a group of things that work together; a way of doing something.","e":"This coloured paper is part of my system for keeping lists of people."}]}]},"sweet":{"h":"sweet","i":"/swiːt/","a":"en-us-sweet.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is sweet, it tastes like sugar or fruit.","e":"This cake is very sweet. I think you put much sugar in it."},{"m":"A sweet person or thing pleases or is nice.","e":"Thank you! It's very sweet of you to give me this."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sweet is a piece of candy."}]}]},"sudden":{"h":"sudden","i":"/sʌdn/","a":"en-us-sudden.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Very quick; taking no time or almost no time, and being a surprise.","e":"Not expecting the sudden change in the weather, he got rained on."}]}]},"surprise":{"h":"surprise","i":"/səˈpraɪz/","a":"en-us-surprise.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To do something that another person didn't think you were going to do.","e":"You surprised me by coming here. I thought you were going to Jimmy's house."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A thing that surprises someone, mostly something good.","e":"The number of apples on the tree this year is a surprise."}]}]},"support":{"h":"support","i":"/sʌˈpɔːt/","a":"en-us-support.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To keep something up; to be a base for something.","e":"The four legs are supporting the table."},{"m":"To give someone food and other things the person needs.","e":"She has money, so she can support her children."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Support is something that keeps something up.","e":"The posts in the house help support the roof."}]}]},"summer":{"h":"summer","i":"/ˈsʌmə/","a":"en-us-summer.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The part of the year when the weather is hot.","e":"There is no school in the summer."}]}]},"suggestion":{"h":"suggestion","i":"/səˈd͡ʒɛstʃən/","a":"en-us-suggestion.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An idea for something to do, that someone says to another person. The other person is free to do the thing or not do the thing.","e":"I have a suggestion for you: have more fruit and you will be."}]}]},"substance":{"h":"substance","i":"/ˈsʌbstəns/","a":"en-us-substance.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) What a thing is made of; the essential or most important part of anything. Everything is made of substances.","e":"has water, sugar, fat and other substances in it."}]}]},"stretch":{"h":"stretch","i":"/strɛtʃ/","a":"en-us-stretch.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To pull; to move one end of something as far as possible from the other end.","e":"He was big and the shirt was little, but he was able to stretch it and use it."},{"m":"Fill a certain place","e":"The Alps stretch from France to Austria."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A stretch is when a person pulls something."},{"m":"A stretch is a length of time.","e":"John was stuck in jail for a ten-year stretch."},{"m":"A statement is a stretch when it is changed or exaggerated from the truth.","e":"That is a stretch! I do not think you are being entirely truthful to me."}]}]},"street":{"h":"street","i":"/striːt/","a":"en-us-street.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A road in a city with buildings on the sides and places where people can walk.","e":"I saw a woman with a dog walking down the street."}]}]},"store":{"h":"store","i":"/stɔr/","a":"en-us-store.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A store is a building with many things in it, where people can exchange money for things.","e":"He went to the store to get some milk."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To store something is to put something away, usually if it is not being used.","e":"John stored his broken computer in his closet, to make room for his new computer."}]}]},"stop":{"h":"stop","i":"/stɒp/","a":"en-us-stop.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you stop, you do not move; you rest.","e":"He stopped after running 2 miles."},{"m":"(transitive) If you stop something or somebody, you prevent them from moving or doing something. You cause the person to cease moving or progressing.","e":"The police tried to stop the criminal, but he was too fast."},{"m":"If you stop doing something, you are not doing it anymore. You have ceased doing it.","e":"I stopped playing video games and went back to working on my project."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you stop, you come to the end of the time when one is doing something. You start doing a different thing or start doing nothing."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A stop is a place where buses, cars, taxis, or other vehicles halt to let passengers board or leave (get on or off)."}]}]},"stone":{"h":"stone","i":"/stəʊn/","a":"en-us-stone.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A stone is a hard, solid piece of earth.","e":"I do not have a hammer but I will use a stone to hammer the nail."}]}]},"stocking":{"h":"stocking","i":"/ˈstɒkɪŋ/","a":"en-us-stocking.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A piece of clothing made of thin cloth to cover the legs.","e":"One of my stockings has a hole in it."}]}]},"stitch":{"h":"stitch","i":"/stɪt​͡ʃ/","a":"en-us-stitch.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A stitch is a little circle of thread, used to join cloth together.","e":"A stitch in time saves nine. (Fix a little hole in cloth with one stitch now, or the hole will be big and will need many stitches.)"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you stitch something, you make stitches in it."},{"m":"If you stitch something, you sew it."}]}]},"still":{"h":"still","i":"/stɪl/","a":"en-us-still.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Now like in the past.","e":"No one has fixed the oven -- It is still broken."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is still, it is not moving and resting in one place.","e":"Sit still when you are in school."}]}]},"sticky":{"h":"sticky","i":"/ˈstɪki/","a":"en-us-sticky.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Able to join to things; hard to wash off. When you touch a sticky thing, some of it goes on your finger. People are able to use a sticky material to join things together."}]}]},"step":{"h":"step","i":"/stɛp/","a":"en-us-step.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you step, you move one foot.","e":"When you walk, you step many times."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A step is a movement of the foot","e":"Take one step forward to win the game."},{"m":"(countable) A step is one of several actions or processes taken to achieve a goal.","e":"Heating the oven is one step needed to bake bread."},{"m":"(countable) A step is a surface used to walk upwards. Most often there are several steps, one above the other.","e":"One must walk up the steps to get to the top of the building."}]}]},"steel":{"h":"steel","i":"/stiːl/","a":"en-us-steel.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A very strong metal made of iron and other substances mixed together.","e":"All my pots for cooking are made of steel."}]}]},"stem":{"h":"stem","i":"/stɛm/","a":"en-us-stem.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A stem is a long, thin thing joining parts of a plant.","e":"Put the stems of the flowers in this cup of water."},{"m":"A stem is a narrow part of certain man-made objects, such as a tobacco pipe, a spoon."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you stem soemthing, you remove the stem from it.","e":"to stem cherries; to stem tobacco leaves"},{"m":"If a problem stems from an action, it is caused by or originates from the action.","e":"The current crisis stems from the short-sighted politics of the previous government."}]}]},"steam":{"h":"steam","i":"/stiːm/","a":"en-us-steam.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A substance like air, made of water that is very hot.","e":"The food is hot -- I see steam coming from the pot."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(cooking) (transitive) To cook with steam."}]}]},"adverb":{"h":"adverb","i":"/ˈæd.vɜːb/","a":"en-us-adverb.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An adverb is a kind of word that generally verbs and other words (but not nouns); adverbs usually answer questions such as how?, why? and to what extent?.","e":"In the clause \"Jane ran quickly,\" \"quickly\" is an adverb because it tells you how Jane ran."}]}]},"statement":{"h":"statement","i":"/ˈsteɪtm(ə)nt/","a":"en-us-statement.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A statement is a claim someone makes that is true or false.","e":"I don't agree with that statement."}]}]},"stage":{"h":"stage","a":"en-us-stage.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"a high floor where some people perform while other people watch","e":"The actors performed on the stage while the audience watched."},{"m":"a vehicle, especially a horse-drawn coach, usually stagecoach","e":"The stage arrived in Dodge City with Lola Montez on board."},{"m":"a phase or level","e":"The first stage in our trip to the moon will be the blast off."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"to put or \"mount\" a work on the stage","e":"This producer stages shows around the world."}]}]},"stamp":{"h":"stamp","i":"/stæmp/","a":"en-us-stamp.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A little coloured square of paper that someone sticks to a letter when they want to send the letter.","e":"The stamp goes in the upper right part of the outside of the letter."},{"m":"(countable) Any embossed sign or mark on a document.","e":"Deeds to a house have excise duty stamps attached."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To place a stamp.","e":"She stamped the sign of her company on the lower part of the letter."},{"m":"To bring the heel of the foot sharply down on the floor.","e":"She stamped her pretty little foot."}]}]},"square":{"h":"square","i":"/skwɛə(r)/","a":"en-us-square.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A square (‎￭) is a form with 4 equal sides and 4 equal angles."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is square, it is shaped like a [[#Noun|sqaure]]."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you square a number, you multiply it by itself. It is represented in math as x^2 where x is the number being squared.","e":"3 squared is 9, because 3 times 3 is 9."}]}]},"spring":{"h":"spring","i":"/sprɪŋ/","a":"en-uk-spring.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A spring is a twisted metal thing that can stretch and push."},{"m":"(countable) Spring is the part of the year before summer; the part of the year when it is getting warmer."},{"m":"(countable) A spring is a place where water comes up out of the ground."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If something springs, it jumps quickly and far."}]}]},"sponge":{"h":"sponge","i":"/spʌnd͡ʒ/","a":"en-us-sponge.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sponge is a soft thing with many holes that can keep much water in it. (One that grows in water, or one that is made by people and used for washing things.)","e":"Use the sponge to clean up the water."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Sponge means to take advantage of someone's kindness"}]}]},"statistics":{"h":"statistics","i":"/stəˈtɪstɪks/","a":"en-us-statistics.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (usually plural) Statistics are numbers about information.","e":"New crime statistics show that the number of crimes is decreasing."},{"m":"(uncountable) Statistics is the science of using and understanding those numbers.","e":"To do research, it's important to understand simple statistics such as averages and standard deviations."}]}]},"chest":{"h":"chest","i":"/t͡ʃɛst/","a":"en-us-chest.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A type of box with a lid that you can lock.","e":"He put his things in the chest."},{"m":"(countable) A body part from the neck to the belly."}]}]},"statistic":{"h":"statistic","i":"/stəˈtɪstɪk/","a":"en-us-statistic.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (usually plural) Statistics are numbers about information.","e":"New crime statistics that show the number of crimes is decreasing."}]}]},"patronising":{"h":"patronising","l":"patronise","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If x is patronising towards y, x treats y as if y were less intelligent.","e":"Often the tourist is hated for his patronising attitude towards the locals."}]}]},"patronizing":{"h":"patronizing","l":"patronize","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If x is patronizing towards y, x treats y as if y were less intelligent.","e":"Often the tourist is hated for his patronizing attitude towards the locals."}]}]},"treat":{"h":"treat","i":"/tri:t/","a":"en-us-treat.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you treat someone in a certain way, you act that way towards them.","e":"I hate it when my teacher treats me like a child."},{"m":"(transitive) If you treat an illness or injury, you do things to make it better.","e":"The doctor couldn't treat my finger until he saw the X-ray."},{"m":"(transitive) If you treat something, you put something on it or do something to it protect or clean it.","e":"The woods was treated with chemicals before being made into paper."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A treat is something nice that you don't get often.","e":"The occasional trip to a swimming pool is a real treat for most families."}]}]},"space":{"h":"space","i":"/speɪs/","a":"en-us-space.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Space is area or room with nothing in it or that can be used.","e":"Make a space between the tables so people can walk there."},{"m":"(uncountable) Space is the black place in the sky where stars are.","e":"The sun and the moon are in outer space."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you space two or more things, you put them apart, not together.","e":"When you attach the wood, make sure the screws are evenly spaced, about 30&nbsp;cm apart."},{"m":"(intransitive) (informal) If you space (out), you stop paying attention or thinking."}]}]},"song":{"h":"song","i":"/sɒŋg/","a":"en-us-song.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A song is some music with words in verse.","e":"That song sounds beautiful."}]}]},"meanwhile":{"h":"meanwhile","i":"/ˈmiːnwaɪl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-meanwhile.wav","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"You use meanwhile to introduce a new topic happening at the same time as the old topic.","e":"Sutton Coldfield won 2-0 away at Chelmsford. Meanwhile, Hightown were 3-0 winners against Clifton."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The meanwhile is the time between two things.","e":"Police are checking his story. In the meanwhile, he remains in jail."}]}]},"immediately":{"h":"immediately","i":"/ɪˈmiːdiətli/","a":"en-us-immediately.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If you do something immediately, you do it with no time or space between.","e":"One car went by, immediately followed by a second at high speed."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"(British) right after; as soon as","e":"Miss Mei-Ling will be arriving here at twelve forty-five. Let me know immediately she does."}]}]},"meantime":{"h":"meantime","i":"/ˈmiːntaɪm/","a":"en-us-meantime.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The meantime is the time between two things.","e":"Police are checking his story. In the meantime, he remains in jail."}]}]},"fuck":{"h":"fuck","i":"/fʌk/","a":"en-us-fuck.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) You say \"fuck you\" or \"fuck that\" to show that you are very angry or that you don't care.","e":"Fuck you too, asshole."},{"m":"If two people fuck, they have sex.","e":"Look at that one. I'd like to fuck her."},{"m":"If you say fuck off, you strongly want someone to leave you alone.","e":"Fuck off, you!"},{"m":"If someone says they fuck with something, they mess with it. (Often someone says they \"don't fuck with\" something, which means they don't like or interact with it.)","e":"I'm not going to fuck with the settings."}]},{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"You say fuck when you are very angry or surprised about something.","e":"Fuck! That hurts. Be careful with that shit."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"You use the fuck to emphasise what you are saying.","e":"What the fuck do you think you're doing? Get the fuck out of my stuff."},{"m":"(countable) A fuck is a person that you don't like.","e":"Gimme that, you stupid little fuck."},{"m":"(countable) A fuck is an act of sex.","e":"I gave her flowers and we had a great fuck."},{"m":"(countable) A fuck is a person that you have sex with.","e":"Is she your current fuck?"},{"m":"(countable) If you don't give a fuck, you don't care.","e":"Look, don't tell me about your fucking problems. I couldn't give a fuck."}]}]},"entertainment":{"h":"entertainment","i":"/ɛn.tɝˈteɪn.mənt/","a":"en-us-entertainment.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Entertainment is things that you do, watch, read, or listen to for fun (e.g., movies, TV, music, games, etc.)","e":"Stories provide entertainment, but they also can teach you things."}]}]},"classic":{"h":"classic","i":"/ˈklæ.sɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-classic.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is classic, it's typical.","e":"Richard Branson is a classic example of success without schooling."},{"m":"If something is classic, it has a long history and it is liked.","e":"His clothes were a mixture of classic and modern styles."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A classic is a book, play, song, etc. that has a long history and is liked.","e":"Every time a classic like that comes on the radio, I just have to stop and listen."},{"m":"(plural) The classics are the language and art from ancient Rome and Greece.","e":"You've never read Homer? Schools don't teach the classics these days."}]}]},"sink":{"h":"sink","i":"/sɪŋk/","a":"en-uk-sink.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something sinks, it goes down, usually into water.","e":"During the storm, two ships sank."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sink is a container for water to wash things in, usually with a drain.","e":"The kitchen sink was always full of dirty dishes."},{"m":"(countable) A sink is a device that removes heat or energy.","e":"A liquid heat sink was developed for cooling electronic circuit."}]}]},"tube":{"h":"tube","i":"/tjuːb/","a":"en-uk-tube.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A tube is a long object with a hole from one end to the other. The ends may be closed or open.","e":"The high pressure forces the water through the tube."},{"m":"(uncountable) The Tube is the underground train system in London, England."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you tube, you float on an inner tube.","e":"We went white-water tubing on the Yukon River."}]}]},"hurry":{"h":"hurry","i":"/ˈhʌr.i/","a":"en-us-hurry.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you hurry, you move or work quickly.","e":"After the speech, he had to hurry out the door to the waiting car."}]}]},"publish":{"h":"publish","i":"/ˈpʌblɪʃ/","a":"en-us-publish.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you publish a book, an article, a song, etc. you make it available for other people to buy, read, listen to, etc.","e":"The study was published in the British Medial Journal."}]}]},"slightly":{"h":"slightly","i":"/ˈslaɪtli/","a":"en-us-slightly.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"A little; to a very small degree.","e":"The two pictures look very similar, but they are slightly different."}]}]},"competition":{"h":"competition","i":"/ˌkɒmpəˈtɪʃən/","a":"en-us-competition.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Competition is a situation or event in which people or groups try to succeed over each other.","e":"With increasing international competition, companies are cutting costs to survive."},{"m":"(uncountable) The competition is the individual or group that is trying to succeed against you.","e":"Because the competition has lowered prices, we have to do the same."}]}]},"outcome":{"h":"outcome","i":"/ˈaʊtkʌm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-outcome.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An outcome is the result of a situation or action.","e":"The outcome of the race was different from what most people were expecting."}]}]},"measure":{"h":"measure","i":"/'mεʒə/","a":"en-us-measure.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you measure something, you calculate its size, mass, temperature, etc. using units like centimetres, kilograms, degrees, etc.","e":"Before clocks, time was measured by the movement of the moon and the sun."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A measure is something that you do, usually to solve a problem.","e":"The police are taking all necessary measures to guarantee the safety of people."},{"m":"(formal) A measure of something is a way to judge or assess it."},{"m":"A measure of something is an amount of it."}]}]},"law":{"h":"law","i":"/lɔː/","a":"en-us-law.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Laws are the official rules of a government or organisation.","e":"We have defined crime as behaviour which breaks the criminal law."},{"m":"(uncountable) The law is the police."},{"m":"(countable) A law is something that is always true."},{"m":"(uncountable) Law is the study of laws."}]}]},"machine":{"h":"machine","i":"/məˈʃiːn/","a":"en-us-machine.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A machine is a man-made object with moving parts.","e":"I'm putting the clothes in the washing machine. Is there anything you want washed?"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you machine something you fasten or shape it with a machine."}]}]},"long":{"h":"long","i":"/lɒŋ/","a":"en-us-long.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is long, it takes a lot of time.","e":"At 3 hours and 24 minutes, it's a very long movie."},{"m":"If something is long, it has a large distance from end to end.","e":"It belonged to a woman in her thirties with long brown hair."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something takes long, it takes a lot of time.","e":"We had dinner together not so long ago."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you long for something, you wish for or really want it.","e":"Carol still longs for David to come back to her even though she knows he has a new wife."}]}]},"south":{"h":"south","i":"/saʊθ/","a":"en-us-south.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The direction opposite to north. For a person looking at the setting sun, the south is on their left hand.","e":"The wind usually comes from the south."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"One of the four compass directions: 180º from north. If you face south, the sun rises on your left.","e":"Africa is South of Europe."}]}]},"soft":{"h":"soft","i":"/sɒft/","a":"en-us-soft.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A soft thing is nice to touch.","e":"cotton is a soft cloth."},{"m":"Something that is soft is flexible.","e":"When metal is heated it gets soft."}]}]},"metal":{"h":"metal","i":"/ˈmɛtəl/","a":"en-us-metal.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Metal is a hard material, often shiny and easy to conduct electricity. Gold, silver, and steel are examples of metals.","e":"We replaced out our wood door with a stronger metal one."}]}]},"different":{"h":"different","i":"/'dɪfərənt/","a":"en-us-different.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If two or more things are different, they are not like each other, not the same. The two things have two sizes, not both the same size; they have two shapes, they don't both have one shape; they each have a color, not just one color for both things; or they are not the like each other in some other way.","e":"The day and night are quite different."}]}]},"vehicle":{"h":"vehicle","i":"/ˈviː.ɪ.kəl/","a":"en-us-vehicle.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A vehicle is something that moves people or things from one place to another, for example: cars, planes, boats, etc.","e":"Bicycles and wheelchairs are allowed. All other vehicles must stay off the path."}]}]},"solid":{"h":"solid","i":"/ˈsɑlɪd/","a":"en-us-solid.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is solid, it is hard and keeps its shape.","e":"When he went out in the morning, the water had frozen solid."},{"m":"If something is solid x, its only material is x.","e":"Copper mixed with silver made a much cheaper spoon than solid silver."},{"m":"If something is solid, it has not spaces inside or between.","e":"The traffic was a solid line of cars as far as you could see."},{"m":"If something is solid, it is good and will not break or change easily.","e":"Don't worry about the chair. It's solid as a rock."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A solid is a material which keeps its shape. It is not a liquid (like water) or a gas (like air)."}]}]},"smooth":{"h":"smooth","i":"/smuːð/","a":"en-us-smooth.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Smooth feels pleasant and flat when you touch it; not rough.","e":"He felt the smooth skin on her cheek."},{"m":"A smooth liquid would have no lumps in it.","e":"He mixed the flour and water until it was smooth."}]}]},"sock":{"h":"sock","i":"/sɑk/","a":"en-us-sock.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Something made of cloth that covers a foot and is able to go inside a shoe.","e":"These socks don't fit my feet."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To hit someone or something very hard or violently.","e":"Jack really socked that guy hard."},{"m":"(intransitive) To deliver a hard hit to someone or something.","e":"They may let you off the first time, but the second time they'll sock it to you—James Jones"}]}]},"smile":{"h":"smile","i":"/smaɪl/","a":"en-us-smile.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To put one's mouth in a form which shows that one is happy; to have the sides of one's mouth higher than the middle.","e":"She smiled at me. I think she likes me!"}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The act of smiling; the form of one's mouth when one is smiling.","e":"A visit to the fair always brings a smile to my face."}]}]},"hospital":{"h":"hospital","i":"/ˈhɒs.pɪ.tl̩/","a":"en-uk-hospital.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A building for sick people, with doctors and nurses.","e":"Mary had an accident. She will be in hospital for a week."}]}]},"thousand":{"h":"thousand","i":"/ˈθaʊznd/","a":"en-us-thousand.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(ordinal thousandth) The number 1,000.","e":"Julius Caesar lived about two thousand years ago."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The number 1,000.","e":"hundreds is a thousand."}]}]},"hundred":{"h":"hundred","i":"/ˈhʌndrəd/","a":"en-us-hundred.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(ordinal hundredth) The number 100.","e":"There are a hundred centimeters in a meter."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The number 100.","e":"Ten tens is a hundred."}]}]},"ten":{"h":"ten","i":"/tɛn/","a":"en-us-ten.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(ordinal tenth) The number 10.","e":"We have ten fingers and ten toes."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The number 10.","e":"fives is ten."}]}]},"two":{"h":"two","i":"/tuː/","a":"en-us-two.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(ordinal second) The number 2. Two means more than one and less than three.","e":"We have two eyes and two ears."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The number 2.","e":"One and one is two."}]}]},"three":{"h":"three","i":"/θriː/","a":"en-us-three.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(ordinal third) The number 3.","e":"A triangle has three sides."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The number 3.","e":"and two is three."}]}]},"four":{"h":"four","i":"/fɔː/","a":"en-us-Four.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(ordinal fourth) The number 4. Four is one more than three and one less than five.","e":"We have four fingers and one thumb on each hand."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The number 4.","e":"Two and two is four."}]}]},"six":{"h":"six","i":"/ˈsɪks/","a":"en-us-six.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(ordinal sixth) Six is the number that is after five and before seven. In numerals, it is 6.","e":"Most people sleep from six to nine hours a night."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The number 6.","e":"Three and three is six."}]}]},"seven":{"h":"seven","i":"/ˈsɛvən/","a":"en-us-seven.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(ordinal seventh) The number 7.","e":"There are seven days in one week."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The number 7.","e":"Three and four is seven."}]}]},"eight":{"h":"eight","i":"/eɪt/","a":"en-us-eight.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(ordinal eighth) The number eight is one more than seven and one less than nine.","e":"Most people work about eight hours a day."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The number 8.","e":"Four and four is eight."}]}]},"nine":{"h":"nine","i":"/ˈnaɪn/","a":"en-us-nine.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(ordinal ninth) Nine is the number that is after eight and before ten. It can be written as 9.","e":"Children study in school about nine months a year."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The number 9.","e":"minus one is nine."}]}]},"valid":{"h":"valid","i":"/ˈvælɪd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-valid.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is valid, it is correct, appropriate, and acceptable.","e":"I'm sorry sir, your driver's license is not valid."}]}]},"mistake":{"h":"mistake","i":"/mɪs'teɪk/","a":"en-us-mistake.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mistake is something that is done wrong or is incorrect.","e":"I made a misteak in spelling 'grammar', g-r-a-m-m-E-r."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you mistake something, you think it is different from what it really is.","e":"I mistook her voice for the voice of her sister."}]}]},"extreme":{"h":"extreme","i":"/ɪkˈstriːm/","a":"en-us-extreme.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Extreme means to a very high degree far beyond what is usual.","e":"This disease usually causes mild illness, but in extreme cases can cause death."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An extreme is a situation or idea taken to its limit, especially with two opposites.","e":"When there is a crime, you have a range of choices. At one extreme you can do nothing. At the other extreme, you can kill the person."}]}]},"smell":{"h":"smell","i":"/smɛl/","a":"en-us-smell.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you smell something, you use the nose to sense it.","e":"She put her nose near the flowers and breathed in to smell them."},{"m":"If something smells, it gently put a substance that people can smell into the air.","e":"The flowers smell very good."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The way a thing smells; the substance in the air that people can smell.","e":"The smell of the flowers is very good."}]}]},"trend":{"h":"trend","i":"/trɛnd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-trend.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A trend is a general movement or change in one direction.","e":"We expect the current upward trend in the use of our services to continue."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If something trends in one direction, it generally moves or changes in that direction.","e":"While most fuel prices are trending higher, natural gas prices should go down in 2006."}]}]},"delay":{"h":"delay","i":"/dɪˈleɪ/","a":"en-us-delay.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A delay is a wait or the waiting time.","e":"Computer problems caused a long delay in the meeting."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you delay, you wait until a later time or cause something to be late.","e":"We have decided to delay the changes to give people more time."}]}]},"solve":{"h":"solve","i":"/sɒlv/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-solve.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you solve a problem, you fix it or deal with it.","e":"\"My kids always make a mess of my computer.\" \"Well, you can easily solve the problem by not allowing them to use it.\""},{"m":"If you solve a question, you find a correct answer.","e":"In the equation 3x^2 + x - 2 = 0 we can solve for x."}]}]},"silver":{"h":"silver","i":"/ˈsɪl.və/","a":"en-us-silver.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A metal with a near white colour and high value and the symbol Ag.","e":"He paid with a silver dollar."},{"m":"Silver is a shiny gray color.","e":"Her hair turned silver as she got older."},{"m":"(countable) A coin made of silver.","e":"Jenny had three coppers and one silver."},{"m":"(countable) A utensil or piece of cutlery made with silver; silverware","e":"Mom put out the good silver for Christmas."}]}]},"tradition":{"h":"tradition","i":"/trəˈdɪʃən/","a":"en-us-tradition.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A tradition is something that has been done in the same way for a long time.","e":"Despite a long tradition of education, there is still a lack of qualified teachers"}]}]},"dominant":{"h":"dominant","i":"/ˈdɒmɪnənt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-dominant.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is dominant, it is larger, stronger, or more powerful than other things.","e":"In society, the dominant class holds power by using the lower classes."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A dominant is the fifth note of a musical scale of eight notes.","e":"In the C Major scale, the dominant is the G."}]}]},"christmas":{"h":"Christmas","i":"/'krɪs.məs/","a":"en-us-Christmas.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Christmas is a Christian holiday to celebrate the birth of Christ, usually on Dec. 25.","e":"Santa put lots of presents under the Christmas tree."}]}]},"appreciate":{"h":"appreciate","i":"/əˈpriːʃieɪt/","a":"en-us-appreciate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you appreciate something, you understand its value or its","e":"It's hard to appreciate how difficult the job is until you try it yourself."},{"m":"(transitive) If you appreciate something, you feel thankful for it.","e":"Thanks so much for your help! I really appreciate the gift."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something appreciates, its value increases.","e":"It is amazing how much the value of my house has appreciated. Hopefully, it will continue to increase, as I am thinking of selling it in five to ten years."}]}]},"attitude":{"h":"attitude","i":"/ˈætɪˌtjuːd/","a":"en-us-attitude.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Your attitude is your feelings and opinions, especially when your actions show how you feel.","e":"He has a really bad attitude towards work."},{"m":"(aeronautics, nautical, engineering) The attitude of an aircraft is the orientation of it that is relative to the horizon or direction of motion."}]}]},"specify":{"h":"specify","i":"/ˈspɛs.ɪ.faɪ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-specify.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you specify something, you say exactly which one or how to do something.","e":"The referee will restart play with a drop ball as specified in the law 2."}]}]},"socks":{"h":"socks","i":"/sɒks/","a":"en-uk-socks.ogg","l":"sock","q":"noun"},"stupid":{"h":"stupid","i":"/ˈst(j)uːpɪd/","a":"en-us-stupid.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something or someone is stupid, it shows a lack of clear thought.","e":"I'm so angry. That was a stupid mistake."}]}]},"smash":{"h":"smash","i":"/smæʃ/","a":"en-us-smash.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you smash something, you break it into many small parts.","e":"He used a hammer to smash the glass of the window."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A smash is a new and very successful book, movie, song, etc."},{"m":"(countable) The sound of something smashing.","e":"The loud smash made them feel fear, but it was only some plates falling."}]}]},"confused":{"h":"confused","i":"/kənˈfjuːzd/","a":"en-us-confused.ogg","l":"confuse","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a person or situation is confused, things are unclear or you do not understand.","e":"The teacher tried to explain it, but now I feel more confused than before."}]}]},"fool":{"h":"fool","i":"/fuːl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-fool.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A fool is a person who does or thinks stupid things.","e":"I made a fool of myself by forgetting her birthday."},{"m":"(countable) A jester."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you fool someone, you make them believe something that is not true.","e":"I was fooled by an e-mail into opening a computer virus."}]}]},"instant":{"h":"instant","i":"/ˈɪnstənt/","a":"en-us-instant.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An instant is a very short time.","e":"She looked at me and for an instant, I thought she was her mother."},{"m":"Instant x is x that is ready, or happens, very quickly (in an instant).","e":"I don't like instant coffee, but that's usually what I drink."}]}]},"instance":{"h":"instance","i":"/ˈɪnstəns/","a":"en-us-instance.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An instance of something is a time or situation when it happens.","e":"In this particular instance, the computer was the problem, not the user."}]}]},"interference":{"h":"interference","i":"/ˌɪntərˈfirɨns/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-interference.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Interference is something, especially an action, that makes it difficult to achieve a goal.","e":"The police were unable to arrest him because of government interference."}]}]},"imply":{"h":"imply","i":"/ɪmˈplaɪ/","a":"en-us-imply.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you imply something, you mean it, but you don't say it directly.","e":"By saying I should exercise more, she implied that I'm fat."}]}]},"shift":{"h":"shift","i":"/ʃɪft/","a":"en-ca-shift.oga","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something shifts, it moves.","e":"The talk about crime has to be shifted from causes to solutions."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A shift is a movement.","e":"There has been a major shift in thinking about how to deal with this."},{"m":"(countable) A shift is the time that workers start and finish work.","e":"I'm working the night shift this week."},{"m":"The shift key on a computer changes from small to big letters."}]}]},"holy":{"h":"holy","i":"/ˈhoʊli/","a":"en-us-holy.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is holy, it is very religious or good and important in a religion.","e":"They believe the birthplace of their is holy land."}]}]},"shit":{"h":"shit","i":"/ʃɪt/","a":"en-us-shit.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is shit, it is bad."}]},{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"You use \"shit\" when you are surprised, afraid, or angry.","e":"Shit! I forgot my keys in my car."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Shit is waste that comes out of the anus.","e":"The yard in front of their house was always covered with dog shit."},{"m":"(uncountable) Shit is something bad, low quality.","e":"I drank that shit one time and was sick as hell."},{"m":"(uncountable) Shit is stuff in general, physical things, actions, ideas, etc.","e":"Stop that shit, it's bugging me."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you shit, you push feces out of your anus.","e":"Your dog should stop shitting on my lawn!"}]}]},"frozen":{"h":"frozen","i":"/ˈfrəʊzən/","a":"en-us-frozen.ogg","l":"freeze","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is frozen it is very cold.","e":"Can you get some frozen peas out of the freezer?"},{"m":"If something is frozen it is solid and can't move."}]}]},"stairs":{"h":"stairs","i":"/ˈstɛəz/","a":"en-us-stairs.ogg","l":"stair","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(usually plural) Stairs are steps to help you go to a different level; stairs can help you get up to another level or can help you get down to another level.","e":"She climbed the stairs up to her bedroom."}]}]},"bake":{"h":"bake","i":"/beɪk/","a":"en-us-bake.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you bake something, you cook it with dry heat all around it, usually in an oven.","e":"Bake the cake at 325&nbsp;°F for 25 minutes."}]}]},"confuse":{"h":"confuse","i":"/kənˈfjuːz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-confuse.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you confuse someone, they don't understand what you have said or done.","e":"Instead of helping me to learn it, he just confused me more."},{"m":"(transitive) If you confuse some things, you mix them up in your mind.","e":"Try not to confuse accept with except."}]}]},"satisfied":{"h":"satisfied","i":"/ˈsætɪsfaɪd/","a":"en-us-satisfied.ogg","l":"satisfy","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are satisfied, you feel happy that you have enough.","e":"A satisfied customer will usually come back to your shop in the future."}]}]},"shower":{"h":"shower","i":"/ˈʃaʊ.ə(r)/","a":"en-au-shower.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A shower is a place with water spraying down to clean something.","e":"I got up, went to the toilet, and jumped in the shower."},{"m":"(countable) A shower is a light rain.","e":"Today, it will be cloudy with occasional showers."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you shower, you spray water on your body to clean yourself.","e":"After his workout, he showered quickly and then got dressed."}]}]},"tobacco":{"h":"tobacco","i":"/təˈbæk.əʊ/","a":"en-us-tobacco.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Tobacco is a plant that is used to make cigarettes.","e":"Tobacco advertising is illegal to help reduce smoking."}]}]},"frightened":{"h":"frightened","i":"/ˈfraɪtn̩d/","a":"en-us-frightened.ogg","l":"frighten","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is frightened, they feel scared.","e":"Most children are frightened of the dark."}]}]},"suspicion":{"h":"suspicion","i":"/sə.ˈspɪ.ʃən/","a":"en-us-suspicion.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A suspicion is a feeling that something, often bad, might be true.","e":"She had a growing suspicion that he had forgotten to lock his door."},{"m":"Suspicion is a feeling of doubt.","e":"Deep suspicion towards foreigners is sadly common here."}]}]},"grave":{"h":"grave","i":"/ɡreɪv/","a":"en-us-grave.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a problem or situation is grave, it is bad and serious.","e":"She's in danger, Frank. Grave danger. Aren't you willing to do anything to help her?"},{"m":"If a person looks or acts grave, they look serious and worried.","e":"He looked very grave indeed, and sat staring quiety at his table-full of papers."},{"m":"A grave accent is the mark over the e shown here: è."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A grave is the place where a dead body is buried in the earth.","e":"If your pet has died, you may be too upset to dig the grave."}]}]},"translate":{"h":"translate","i":"/ˈtrænzleɪt/","a":"en-us-translate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you translate something from one language to another, you change the words and sentences into the other language.","e":"It's not enough to translate word for word."},{"m":"If x translates into y, x causes or leads to y.","e":"For a golfer, if you're not calm, that can translate into a bad shot."},{"m":"If something translates, it or can be used in a new way or situation.","e":"His experience as a police officer doesn't translate well to running a company."}]}]},"combination":{"h":"combination","i":"/kɒmbɪ'neɪʃən/","a":"en-us-combination.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A combination is an item or group made of different things or kinds of things.","e":"Any combination of these factors increases the risk dramatically."},{"m":"(uncountable) Combination is the process of putting two or more things together."},{"m":"{C}_{n}^{m}"}]}]},"material":{"h":"material","i":"/məˈtɪri.əl/","a":"en-us-material.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Material is the things or ideas that are used in making or doing something.","e":"The raw materials for the goods are mostly imported from Canada."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Material things are things in the real world, often money."},{"m":"(formal) If something is material, it is big and important."}]}]},"unique":{"h":"unique","i":"/juːˈniːk/","a":"en-us-unique.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is unique, it is one of a kind; it is unmatched.","e":"When the school for the deaf opened, it was unique in Europe."},{"m":"If something is unique, it is rare or unusual.","e":"Oh, thank you! What a unique gift!"}]}]},"suspect":{"h":"suspect","i":"/ˈsʌs.pɛkt/","a":"en-us-suspect-noun-adj.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you suspect something, you feel that something, often bad, is probably true.","e":"I suspect you've already erased the file, have you?"},{"m":"(transitive) If you suspect someone or something, you don't trust them, or you think something is their fault.","e":"The chemical is no longer used because it is suspected of causing cancer."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A suspect is a person or thing who you believe committed a crime or caused something.","e":"He was the police's prime suspect in the crime."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is suspect, it is untrue, or likely to cause problems.","e":"Any claims to solve all the problems should be seen as deeply suspect."}]}]},"mental":{"h":"mental","i":"/ˈmɛn.təl/","a":"en-us-mental.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Mental health, processes etc. is related to the mind and thinking.","e":"The program helps people deal with drinking, depression and other mental health problems."}]}]},"govern":{"h":"govern","i":"/ˈɡʌvɚn/","a":"en-us-govern.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If x governs y, x controls y through laws or other rules.","e":"The country is currently governed by the army."}]}]},"hidden":{"h":"hidden","i":"/ˈhɪd(ə)n/","a":"en-us-hidden.ogg","l":"hide","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something is hidden, it is hard to see or find.","e":"We are trying to make parents more aware of the hidden dangers of TV."}]}]},"team":{"h":"team","i":"/ti:m/","a":"en-us-team.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A team is a group of people who play or work together on the same side.","e":"She is a member of the coaching team which led Great Britain to victory over Australia at last year's games."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you team two people, groups, or things, you group them to work together.","e":"Five of London's finest hairdressers have teamed together and will be opening their new salon."}]}]},"harm":{"h":"harm","i":"/hɑrm/","a":"en-us-harm.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) To harm someone means to hurt someone; to injure someone.","e":"In the attack, he caused her serious bodily harm."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To harm something means to damage something."}]}]},"excuse":{"h":"excuse","i":"/ɪkˈskjuːz/","a":"en-us-excuse-verb.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) You say, \"excuse me\" when you have done something rude,"},{"m":"(transitive) You say, \"excuse me\" when you want to get someone's attention."},{"m":"(transitive) You say, \"excuse me\" when you want somebody to move."},{"m":"(transitive) You say, \"excuse me\" when you didn't hear somebody very well and you want them to repeat themselves."},{"m":"(transitive) If you excuse someone, you forgive them."},{"m":"(transitive) If you excuse someone, you allow them to avoid doing something."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An excuse is a reason for not doing something or for doing something bad.","e":"There is no excuse for hitting your sister."}]}]},"reside":{"h":"reside","i":"/rɪˈzaɪd/","a":"en-us-reside.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) (preposition) If something or someone resides somewhere, it lives there or is located there.","e":"Real political power still resides with the militia leaders."}]}]},"deduction":{"h":"deduction","i":"/dɪˈdʌkʃən/","a":"en-us-deduction.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Deduction is the process or result of thinking about information to find an answer or opinion.","e":"A detective must uncover the murderer by logical deduction from facts."},{"m":"Deduction is the amount or process of taking something away, usually money.","e":"The average worker takes home about $500 per week after tax and other deductions."}]}]},"cure":{"h":"cure","i":"/kjʊr/","a":"en-us-cure.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you cure something that is wrong, you fix or solve it.","e":"Time and honest feedback usually cure the problem by teaching the poor leader a better way of achieving goals."},{"m":"If you cure a piece of meat, you preserve it by salting."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cure is something that will fix something that is wrong.","e":"We still have no cure for the common cold."}]}]},"plenty":{"h":"plenty","i":"/ˈplɛnti/","a":"en-us-plenty.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Plenty of something is a lot of it; more than enough of it.","e":"Don't give up straight away darling. You've still got plenty of time to go yet."}]}]},"sleep":{"h":"sleep","i":"/sliːp/","a":"en-us-sleep.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you sleep, you rest quietly with eyes shut, usually in bed for many hours at night.","e":"I need to sleep now because I'm tired."},{"m":"(informal) If you sleep with someone, you have sex with them.","e":"I haven't slept with my husband in like eight months."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Sleep is the activity or time of resting quietly with eyes shut, usually in bed for many hours at night."}]}]},"school":{"h":"school","i":"/sku:l/","a":"en-uk-school.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A school is a place where you go to learn.","e":"What grade are you in at school?"},{"m":"(countable) A school is a group of fish."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) (informal) If you school someone, you teach them something."},{"m":"(transitive) (informal) If you school someone, you prove that you're better than them."}]}]},"swallow":{"h":"swallow","i":"/ˈswɒləʊ/","a":"en-us-swallow.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you swallow something you make it go through your mouth into your body (down your esophagus to your stomach). We swallow food and drinks.","e":"Young children put small toys in their mouths and sometimes swallow them."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A swallow is a kind of small bird."},{"m":"A swallow is the amount of food or liquid that goes down the throat at one time."},{"m":"A swallow is the act of swallowing.","e":"He took the aspirin with a single swallow of water."}]}]},"accident":{"h":"accident","i":"/ˈæk.sə.dənt/","a":"en-us-accident.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Accident means something that happens without a plan; unintentionally; inadvertently.","e":"I dropped the glass by accident and it broke."},{"m":"(countable) An accident is a vehicle crash.","e":"Two people were hurt in a road traffic accident between a car and a motorcycle last night."}]}]},"instruct":{"h":"instruct","i":"/ˌɪnˈstrʌkt/","a":"en-us-instruct.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you instruct someone, you tell or teach them what to do or how to do something.","e":"We were stopped on the road and instructed by the police to turn around and go back."}]}]},"manage":{"h":"manage","i":"/ˈmænəʤ/","a":"en-us-manage.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you manage something, you organise and control it.","e":"Other European countries manage their health services better than we do."},{"m":"If you manage something, you are able to do it or deal with it successfully.","e":"Even with the pain, somehow she managed a smile."}]}]},"situation":{"h":"situation","i":"/sɪtjuːˈeɪʃən/","a":"en-us-situation.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A situation is the conditions at a time and place.","e":"If you can stay calm, it will help you to handle difficult situations."}]}]},"manager":{"h":"manager","i":"/\"mæn.ə.dʒə(r)/","a":"en-us-manager.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A manager is someone who manages or organizes people or things together.","e":"Ask the manager of this project. He knows what to do next."},{"m":"A manager is a program that allows the user to control a part of the computer/software.","e":"If a program is not responding, please use the task manager to end the program forcefully."}]}]},"worry":{"h":"worry","i":"/ˈwʌri/","a":"en-us-worry.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Worry means to feel troubled by, anxious, or uneasy about specific problems or the possibility of unpleasant things happening in the future.","e":"While she cooked the food, she worried about her son who was writing an important test at school."}]}]},"whisper":{"h":"whisper","i":"/ˈ(h)wɪspə/","a":"en-us-whisper.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you whisper to someone, you talk very quietly; to talk with breath but no voice, with a quiet sound like the wind, so only people very near can hear what you say.","e":"Some people at the back of the room were whispering secrets."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A whisper is an act of talking to someone very quietly."}]}]},"warning":{"h":"warning","i":"/ˈwɔrnɪŋ/","a":"en-us-warning.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Something that tells someone that there is danger.","e":"Someone cried a warning that a train was coming, so everybody moved."}]}]},"visual":{"h":"visual","i":"/ˈvɪʒʊəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-visual.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Visual things are those related to sight and seeing.","e":"The visual part of the play was beautiful, but the voices were too quiet."}]}]},"upset":{"h":"upset","i":"/ˈʌpsεt/","a":"en-us-upset-noun.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A disturbance or disruption.","e":"My late arrival caused the professor considerable upset."},{"m":"(countable) An unexpected win.","e":"The Nimrods defeated the Blue Devils yesterday in a stunning upset."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Upset means to be very angry or sad; to be unhappy.","e":"He was upset after someone said bad things to him very loudly."},{"m":"Something is upset if it is in turned in the wrong direction like something that was dropped; turned in a direction with the bottom part up and the top part down.","e":"When they played with a ball in the room, a cup was upset and all the milk went onto the floor."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If someone upsets a person, they make that person angry, anxious, stressed, or sad; to make a person unhappy."},{"m":"If a person upsets something, they disturb it, disrupt it, or change it to make it worse."},{"m":"If a person upsets something, they tip it or turn it upside down."}]}]},"worries":{"h":"worries","i":"/ˈwʌriz/","a":"en-us-worries.ogg","l":"worry","q":"verb"},"thank":{"h":"thank","i":"/θæŋk/","a":"en-us-thank.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To say a good word after someone gives something to you or after someone does something good for you.","e":"She thanked him very much for the beautiful food he cooked for her."}]}]},"thanks":{"h":"thanks","i":"/θæŋks/","a":"en-us-thanks.ogg","l":"thank","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"You say thanks when somebody has helped you or done something nice for you.","e":"\"Can I get the door for you?\" \"Thanks!\""}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Thanks are kind words and thoughts for people who did nice things for you.","e":"A special thanks goes to my family."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"because","e":"Thanks to your help, we were able to finish quickly."}]}]},"tension":{"h":"tension","i":"/ˈtɛnʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-tension.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Hidden anger or fear.","e":"No one said anything, but I could feel the tension in the room."},{"m":"The state of being tight.","e":"There is too much tension in the rope. It might break."}]}]},"theatre":{"h":"theatre","i":"/ˈθi(ə)tɚ/","a":"en-us-theatre.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A theatre is a building with a big room with a stage and places for many people to sit, so that people can watch a play with actors in it.","e":"The Nutcracker is playing at the theatre tonight."}]}]},"play":{"h":"play","i":"/pleɪ/","a":"en-us-play.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To do things for amusement.","e":"Children like to play all day."},{"m":"If you play a musical instrument, you make music using it.","e":"He plays guitar in a rock and roll band."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Something a group of actors does, in a theatre, for people to watch.","e":"The actors on the stage had clothes with bright colors."}]}]},"theater":{"h":"theater","i":"/ˈθi(ə)tɚ/","a":"en-us-theatre.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A theater is a building with a big room with a stage and places for many people to sit, so that people can watch a play with actors in it.","e":"We went to the theater to watch a play by Shakespeare."},{"m":"(countable) A theater is a place where movies are shown.","e":"We'll make it to the theater on time, there's twenty-nine minutes left before the movie starts."}]}]},"telephone":{"h":"telephone","i":"/ˈ tɛl.ɪˌfəʊn/","a":"en-us-telephone.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A machine used to talk to someone who is far away.","e":"I need to find a telephone so I can tell my mother where I am."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you telephone someone, you use a telephone to talk to them.","e":"I telephoned my friend yesterday."}]}]},"woods":{"h":"woods","i":"/wʊdz/","a":"en-us-woods.ogg","l":"wood","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A woods is a forest."}]}]},"envelope":{"h":"envelope","i":"/ˈɛnvələʊp/","a":"en-uk-envelope.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An envelope is a paper cover that you put a letter in to send it.","e":"She put the letter into the envelope, addressed it to Charles, and put a stamp on it."},{"m":"An envelope is a covering that goes all the way around something.","e":"Each virus has a special envelope of protein surrounding it."}]}]},"recommended":{"h":"recommended","a":"en-us-recommended.ogg","l":"recommend","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is recommended, somebody says it's good or you should try it.","e":"Her new book is highly recommended."}]}]},"recommend":{"h":"recommend","i":"/rɛkəˈmɛnd/","a":"en-us-recommend.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you recommend something, you tell somebody that it is good or that they should try it.","e":"The committee strongly recommended that the head teacher take the lead in defining the aims of the school."}]}]},"teeth":{"h":"teeth","i":"/tiːθ/","a":"en-us-teeth.ogg","l":"tooth","q":"noun"},"symbol":{"h":"symbol","i":"/sɪmbəɫ/","a":"en-us-symbol.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A symbol is a letter or simple picture with a particular meaning.","e":"Most language now use the same set of symbols to represent numbers."},{"m":"A symbol is a person or object that represents a group or idea.","e":"These dead trees have become a symbol of pollution."}]}]},"equip":{"h":"equip","i":"/ɪˈkwɪp/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-equip.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you equip a person or a place, you give them equipment.","e":"We equipped the buses with blankets and pillows and high-tech stereo headphones and telephones."},{"m":"(transitive) If you equip someone with skills or knowledge, you teach it to them.","e":"This program equips students with the skills they need to succeed in college."}]}]},"mystery":{"h":"mystery","i":"/ˈmɪst(ə)ri/","a":"en-us-mystery.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A mystery is a secret or hidden matter which can't be explained.","e":"She never told me where the money was, and it remains a mystery to me even now."},{"m":"A mystery is a story about a puzzling event: short for mystery story.","e":"The police investigation has failed to solve the murder mystery."}]}]},"ethnic":{"h":"ethnic","i":"/ˈɛθ.nɪk/","a":"en-us-ethnic.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"An ethnic group is a group related by race, culture, and/or nationality.","e":"The Irish are the largest, but least visible, ethnic minority in Britain."},{"m":"Characteristic of or belonging to a non-Western cultural tradition, as in ethnic food, costumes and jewelry."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) a member of an ethnic minority."}]}]},"compute":{"h":"compute","i":"/kɒmpjuːt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-compute.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you compute an answer, you calculate it or find it, usually using mathematics.","e":"They computed the exact time of death using the blood."}]}]},"self":{"h":"self","i":"/sɛlf/","a":"en-us-self.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Your self is the type of person you are, particularly the way you usually act, look or feel.","e":"He looked so happy compared to his usual down self that Walter wondered if something was wrong."},{"m":"Someone's self is their personality or character that makes them individual.","e":"As the baby grows older, it begins to develop a sense of self."},{"m":"Self is used to refer to a person.","e":"Please bring your wife and your good self."}]}]},"devil":{"h":"devil","i":"/ˈdɛvəl/","a":"en-us-devil.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A devil is an evil monster, god, or mythological being."},{"m":"If you say someone is a poor devil, you mean a poor person."}]},{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"The Devil is the enemy or God and all people. The devil is the leader or source of evil."},{"m":"If someone is called the Devil it means they are a bad person. Usually this is used playfully and not seriously."}]}]},"relax":{"h":"relax","i":"/rɪˈlæks/","a":"en-us-relax.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you relax, you stop working, worrying, etc., and you take a rest or have fun.","e":"People come here to relax, have a beer, and talk with friends."},{"m":"(transitive) If you relax a rule, you make it less strict.","e":"The king relaxed the laws that the people protested against."}]}]},"collect":{"h":"collect","i":"/kəˈlɛkt/","a":"en-us-collect.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you collect some things, you bring them together as a group.","e":"The study collected data from 562 mothers in the hospital."}]}]},"motive":{"h":"motive","i":"/ˈməʊtɪv/","a":"en-us-motive.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A motive is a reason to do something.","e":"The man says he has no motive for killing his wife."}]}]},"motivation":{"h":"motivation","i":"/məʊtɪˈveɪʃ(ə)n/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Someone's motivation is their feeling that they want to do something.","e":"Students' motivation is falling because the lessons are not interesting."},{"m":"(countable) Your motivation is the reason you do something.","e":"The main motivation behind the deal was money."}]}]},"screen":{"h":"screen","i":"/skriːn/","a":"en-us-screen.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A screen is a flat surface for showing pictures, text or video.","e":"The information appears on the computer screen almost right away."},{"m":"(countable) A screen is a flat surface between two areas, often letting something in but keeping something out.","e":"The hole in the window screen let the bugs in."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you screen blood, people, information, etc., you find or block unwanted things.","e":"They carefully screen the blood for viruses before giving it to hospitals."},{"m":"If you screen a movie, a TV show, etc., you put it on a screen.","e":"They screened the new movie for the press last week."}]}]},"honest":{"h":"honest","i":"/ˈɒnɛst/","a":"en-us-honest.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are honest, you do not hide the truth; you don't lie, cheat, or steal.","e":"My parents were quite honest with me about things to do with sex."}]}]},"adapted":{"h":"adapted","i":"/əˈdæptɪd/","a":"en-us-adapted.ogg","l":"adapt","q":"verb"},"adapt":{"h":"adapt","i":"/ʌˈdæpt/","a":"en-us-adapt.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you adapt to changes, conditions, needs, etc., you change to fit them.","e":"It was difficult to adapt to the changes, but I work much better now."},{"m":"You can adapt book or other work to a movie, musical, or other form of entertainment.","e":"Edgar Allan Poe's short story, \"The Fall of the House of Usher\", was adapted to a movie in 1960."}]}]},"stats":{"h":"stats","i":"/stəˈts/","a":"en-au-stats.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (informal) Stats are numbers about information.","e":"New crime stats that show the number of crimes is decreasing."},{"m":"(uncountable) (informal) Stats is the science of using and understanding those numbers.","e":"To do research, it's important to understand simple stats such as averages and standard deviations."}]}]},"patient":{"h":"patient","i":"/ˈpeɪʃənt/","a":"en-uk-patient.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is patient, they can wait without getting upset.","e":"It's hard to be patient with people who don't listen to you."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A patient is a person or animal under medical care.","e":"Emergency room doctors treated over 200 patients today."}]}]},"lazy":{"h":"lazy","i":"/ˈleɪzi/","a":"en-us-lazy.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is lazy, they do not want to work or do anything difficult.","e":"He went to a restaurant because he was too lazy to cook."},{"m":"A lazy day or time is a time for relaxing.","e":"We finished school and looked forward to the lazy days of summer."}]}]},"dramatic":{"h":"dramatic","i":"/drəˈmætɪk/","a":"en-us-dramatic.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is dramatic, it is large and sudden.","e":"The increase in foreign students has meant a dramatic change in the number of schools."},{"m":"If something is dramatic, it is connected with acting and theatre.","e":"In a highly dramatic speech, he brought everyone to his side."}]}]},"desk":{"h":"desk","i":"/dɛsk/","a":"en-us-desk.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A desk is a table for studying and, usually with drawers.","e":"The students sat at their desks quietly while the teacher walked around the room."}]}]},"jumped":{"h":"jumped","a":"en-us-jumped.ogg","l":"jump","q":"verb"},"rub":{"h":"rub","i":"/rʌb/","a":"en-us-rub.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you rub something, you move against it, often backward and forward.","e":"The doctor was rubbing her hands to warm them."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"If you give somebody or something a rub, you rub them or massage them.","e":"After the game, he gave me a great shoulder rub."}]}]},"recovery":{"h":"recovery","i":"/rɪˈkʌvəri/","a":"en-us-recovery.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A recovery is the process of getting better after an illness or a problem.","e":"She made a good recovery from a knee injury and may play this game."},{"m":"A recovery is the process of getting something back after it was lost or taken.","e":"They hired a lawyer to help with the recovery of the money."}]}]},"hole":{"h":"hole","i":"/həʊl/","a":"en-us-hole.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hole is an empty space in an object or material.","e":"He fell into the water through a hole in the ice."}]}]},"pretend":{"h":"pretend","i":"/prɪˈtɛnd/","a":"en-us-pretend.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you pretend that something is true, you play that it is true but you know that it is not.","e":"Cameron pretended not to see young Donald till he was close beside him."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is pretend, it's not real but is used for play.","e":"It's not a real monster. It's just pretend."}]}]},"convenience":{"h":"convenience","i":"/kənˈviːnɪəns/","a":"en-us-convenience.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Convenience is the quality of being easy to get and use.","e":"The shop has a free car park for the convenience of its guests."},{"m":"(countable) A convenience is something that saves time or work.","e":"Out cottages have all the modern conveniences, including internet, A/C and a pool."}]}]},"stolen":{"h":"stolen","i":"/'stəʊlən/","a":"en-us-stolen.ogg","l":"steal","q":"verb"},"feeling":{"h":"feeling","i":"/ˈfiːlɪŋ/","a":"en-us-feeling.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Your feelings are your emotions, thoughts, and opinions.","e":"Many people have strong feelings about the war."},{"m":"A feeling is a signal that your body gives you, such as pain, heat, softness, etc.","e":"The feeling of the sun on his face was relaxing."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To experience something by touch.","e":"He felt the soft cloth with his hand."},{"m":"To experience something the body.","e":"She felt a pain in her hand."},{"m":"To have an emotion. When you are happy, sad, or angry you are feeling.","e":"I'm feeling very happy today."}]}]},"purpose":{"h":"purpose","i":"/ˈpɝpəs/","a":"en-us-purpose.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A purpose is reason for doing something or for existing.","e":"Coal is used for only three purposes: heating houses, generating electricity and making steel."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you purpose to do something, you plan on doing it."}]}]},"direction":{"h":"direction","i":"/d(a)ɪˈrɛk.ʃən/","a":"en-us-direction.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A direction is a way to move or point.","e":"\"Where is the post office?\" \"I think it's that direction.\""},{"m":"Directions are steps that tell you what to do or how to do something.","e":"Your doctors directions are to take two of these with water before eating."},{"m":"(uncountable) Direction is control or management.","e":"The company is now under the direction of new owners."}]}]},"reason":{"h":"reason","i":"/ˈriːzn/","a":"en-us-reason.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A reason to do something is why you do it, or the cause of something.","e":"The low price was the main reason for buying it."},{"m":"(uncountable) Reason is the ability to think clearly.","e":"It's important to use reason to decide, not emotion."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you reason, you think carefully about something."},{"m":"(transitive) (uncommon) If you reason someone, you persuade using reasoning.","e":"I reasoned my friend into my religion."}]}]},"swallowed":{"h":"swallowed","l":"swallow","q":"verb"},"disease":{"h":"disease","i":"/disiːz/","a":"en-us-disease.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"If a person, animal, or plant is ill, it has a disease.","e":"1.4 million children suffer from heart disease in Pakistan."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To cause unease; to annoy, irritate."},{"m":"To infect with a disease."}]}]},"sour":{"h":"sour","i":"/ˈsaʊ(ə)r/","a":"en-us-sour.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A sour taste is like the taste of an acid.","e":"The old milk is bad: it tastes sour."},{"m":"A sour person is mean to other people because they are unhappy.","e":"He was a sour old man who wouldn't even say \"hello\" to anyone."}]}]},"signal":{"h":"signal","i":"/ˈsɪɡnəl/","a":"en-us-signal.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A picture, or a light, or a movement of a hand, or other thing that tells people to do something.","e":"When I make this signal with my hand, everybody walk to the front of the room."},{"m":"A picture, or a light, or a movement of a hand, or something else that lets someone recognize another person, a ship, an airplane or something else.","e":"The sailor saw the signal on the other ship and so recognized it was the enemy."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When someone or something signals to someone, they use a signal to tell the person something.","e":"The red light signals to the cars to stop."}]}]},"attractive":{"h":"attractive","i":"/əˈtræktɪv/","a":"en-us-attractive.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If people or things are attractive, you like them because you think they are good, beautiful, etc.","e":"People buy the make-up and stuff they see on television to make them appear more attractive."}]}]},"worth":{"h":"worth","i":"/wɜːθ/","a":"en-us-worth.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If x is worth y, x has the value of y, usually in money.","e":"The painting is worth over $1 million."},{"m":"If something is worth doing, or is worth it, there is value in doing it. It's not a waste of time.","e":"It's not worth washing now 'cause it'll just get dirty again later."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The worth of something is its value.","e":"I just bought $8,000 worth of gold."}]}]},"hair":{"h":"hair","i":"/heə/","a":"en-us-hair.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Hair is long, very thin, soft material that grows on people and animals.","e":"She had never seen him with his hair cut short."}]}]},"severe":{"h":"severe","i":"/sɪˈvɪə/","a":"en-us-severe.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is severe is very bad.","e":"He has a severe wound from dropping a big knife on his foot."},{"m":"Someone who is severe gets angry easily or frequently punishes people; they are harsh or strict.","e":"The teacher had a severe way of making the learners sit still."}]}]},"search":{"h":"search","i":"/sɜːt͡ʃ/","a":"en-us-search.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When someone searches for something, they don't know where it is and they look in many places to try to discover where it is.","e":"I searched the whole room but I don't know where the book is."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An attempt to find something.","e":"The search for the stolen jewelry was unsuccessful."},{"m":"The act of searching, as in computers etc..","e":"Search engines have made using the internet easier."}]}]},"message":{"h":"message","i":"/ˈmɛsɪd͡ʒ/","a":"en-us-message.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A message is information that is sent between living things and is sent from one person to the other. There are some types of message, like phone message and subliminal message.","e":"On his desk there was a message from Jack to call home."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you message someone, you send them a note or letter or e-mail; you message them.","e":"Can you please message me the directions?"}]}]},"concentration":{"h":"concentration","i":"/ˌkɒnsənˈtreɪʃən/","a":"en-us-concentration.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A concentration is a large amount of something in one place or group.","e":"The oil-sands in Alberta, Canada, contain high concentrations of oil."},{"m":"(uncountable) Concentration is the ability to focus your attention on something.","e":"Runners mustn't worry or do anything else to break their concentration."},{"m":"The amount of solute in a solution; the concentration of a solution is measured in parts per million ()"}]}]},"intelligence":{"h":"intelligence","i":"/ɪnˈtɛl.ɪˌd​ʒ͡əns/","a":"en-us-intelligence.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Intelligence is the ability to think clearly and understand easily.","e":"The school has special classes for student of low intelligence."},{"m":"(uncountable) Intelligence is information that a government gets from its spies.","e":"US intelligence indicates changes in North Korea's military."}]}]},"link":{"h":"link","i":"/liŋk/","a":"en-us-link.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you link two or more things, you make a connection between them.","e":"The Northern Ireland economy is closely linked to that of the rest of the United Kingdom."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A link is a connection between two or more things.","e":"It's easy to see a close link between studying and good grades."},{"m":"(countable) A link is a word or picture on the Internet that you click to go to another page."}]}]},"neck":{"h":"neck","i":"/nɛk/","a":"en-us-neck.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The part of the body between the head and the torso."}]}]},"competitive":{"h":"competitive","i":"/kəmˈpɛtɪtɪv/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-competitive.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is competitive, they want very much to be the best at everything.","e":"I don't enjoy working with her because she's so competitive."},{"m":"If something is competitive, there is competition about it.","e":"There is now a competitive market for telephone services because there are more choices of companies."},{"m":"If someone or something is competitive, they have a good chance of winning or being chosen.","e":"The shoe comes in sizes 6-11 and retails for the very competitive price of £34.99."}]}]},"respond":{"h":"respond","i":"/rəˈspɒnd/","a":"en-us-respond.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you respond to something or someone, you do something in reaction to it.","e":"I try to respond to emails as soon as I get them."}]}]},"opposition":{"h":"opposition","i":"/ɒpəˈzɪʃən/","a":"en-us-opposition.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Opposition to something, is an action or hope to stop it.","e":"There was strong opposition to the change from parents."},{"m":"(uncountable) The opposition is the person or group that you are competing against.","e":"There was a series of meetings between the leaders of the Government and the opposition parties."}]}]},"label":{"h":"label","i":"/ˈleɪbəl/","a":"en-us-label.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A label is a small sign, usually on something, to tell you about it.","e":"Please read the label before using the product."},{"m":"(countable) A label is a brand (mainly for fashion and music companies).","e":"Her favorite label is Gucci."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you label something, you write information on it or attach information to it.","e":"Please be sure to label your bags before getting on the airplane."},{"m":"(transitive) If you label somebody or something as being some way, you categorize them that way.","e":"After the way he acted, the other children labeled him as weird."}]}]},"grateful":{"h":"grateful","i":"/ˈɡreɪtfəl/","a":"en-us-grateful.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are grateful for or about something, you want to say, \"thank you\" because of it.","e":"I'm very grateful for your kindness during this difficult time."}]}]},"check":{"h":"check","i":"/t͡ʃɛk/","a":"en-us-check.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you check something, you look at it to see if there is a problem, or something new or different.","e":"Hi, I heard some noises, so I'm just checking to see if you were O.K."},{"m":"If you check something out, you look at it because it might be interesting.","e":"I found this great video online. Check it out."},{"m":"(transitive) If you check an answer, or choice, you make a check mark (✓) beside it.","e":"If you want to get mail from us, check the box at the bottom of the page."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you check out of a hotel, you pay your bill and leave.","e":"I called the hotel, but they said you had already checked out."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you check in to a hotel, you go to the front desk to tell them you've arrived and you get your key.","e":"After we checked in, we went to our room and unpacked our bags."},{"m":"(transitive) If you check something, usually something bad, you stop it.","e":"He put out his hands but could not check his fall."},{"m":"(transitive) If you check your coat or bags, you give them to a worker to take care of.","e":"Reid was traveling alone without any checked luggage."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A check is a piece of paper that gives someone else the right to receive some money from your bank account. (Other spelling: cheque)","e":"She wrote him a personal check for $250."},{"m":"(countable) A check is something you do to make sure that there is no problem.","e":"The town must conduct regular checks on drinking water quality."},{"m":"(countable) A reality check is an opportunity to think about reality and make sure your hopes and thoughts are reasonable.","e":"I think this injury is a real reality check for him. He can't keep working like this."},{"m":"If you keep something in check, you stop it from getting bigger or worse.","e":"There aren't enough birds to keep the insects in check."},{"m":"(countable) A check is something that controls or stops something else.","e":"The company didn't have the right checks and balances, and that's why they lost all the money."},{"m":"In a restaurant, the check is the bill.","e":"Waiter, can you bring us the check please?"},{"m":"(countable) A check is this mark: ✓","e":"Put a check next to today's date and sign here."},{"m":"Check is a pattern of squares, especially on cloth.","e":"Michael was a big man in a red wool check shirt."},{"m":"(countable) A coat check is a place where you can give your coat, bags, etc. to a worker to take care of.","e":"The lines were long at the coat check, so we put our jackets on the backs of our chairs."},{"m":"(uncountable) In chess, check the position of the king where it can be directly attacked by the opponent's pieces but from which it may escape.","e":"You can't move that piece because your king is in check."}]}]},"puppies":{"h":"puppies","l":"puppy","q":"noun"},"husband":{"h":"husband","i":"/ˈhʌzbənd/","a":"en-us-husband.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A husband is a married man."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you are husbanding, you are resources carefully."}]}]},"curtain":{"h":"curtain","i":"/ˈkɜːtn̩/","a":"en-uk-curtain.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(usually plural) Curtains are pieces of cloth that hang in front of a window, door, or stage.","e":"So I'll close the curtains and the room now will be quite dark."},{"m":"A curtain is a substance, or group of items that blocks your view or blocks access.","e":"The base of the rock is undercut, permitting walkers to pass behind the curtain of falling water."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you curtain something off, you put a curtain around it."}]}]},"revise":{"h":"revise","i":"/rɪˈvaɪz/","a":"En-us-revise.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When someone revises a book, a writing or something they said, it means they change it (edit it) so that it says something a little different from what it said before.","e":"He revised the book to have information from this year in it."},{"m":"If someone revises, they study something again to prepare for a test.","e":"I can't go out 'cause I have to revise for my A-levels."}]}]},"file":{"h":"file","i":"/faɪl/","a":"en-us-file.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A file is a set of papers or records on a specific issue, person, etc.","e":"The letter should be in the file on the Herzog problem."},{"m":"A file is a set of information that can be opened, changed, and saved by a computer program.","e":"My computer won't read the Word file you e-mailed me last night."},{"m":"A file is a place to keep papers organised.","e":"Can you put this receipt in the file?"},{"m":"A file is a tool with rough sides that you rub against something to make it smooth."},{"m":"A file is a line of people."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you file papers or documents, you put them away in an organised way in one place.","e":"I filed the letter under \"t\" for taxes."},{"m":"(transitive) If you file a report or a story, you submit it to your employer or editor.","e":"What time did you file that story about the car crash?"},{"m":"If you file a complaint, you make an official complaint."},{"m":"(transitive); (preposition) If people file somewhere, they go there in a line."},{"m":"If you file something, you rub it with a file to make it smooth.","e":"She went to the store for a manicure, which involves filing and polishing the nails."}]}]},"low":{"h":"low","i":"/loʊ/","a":"en-us-low.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If cost, value, amount, sound, temperature, etc. is low, it is small.","e":"My pay is very low, so it's hard to live here."},{"m":"If something is low, it (or its top) is close to the ground.","e":"The bridge is too low for the truck to go under it."},{"m":"If something is low quality, it is bad.","e":"I bought a low-quality bag and it already has a hole in it."},{"m":"If a sound is low, it is small in frequency or quiet.","e":"On the piano, the left hand plays the low notes and the right hand plays the high notes."},{"m":"If a person is feeling low, they are not happy."}]}]},"conscious":{"h":"conscious","i":"/ˈkɑn.ʃəs/","a":"en-us-conscious.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are conscious of something, you notice or realize it.","e":"Soon after I walked into the room, I became conscious of many eyes looking at me."},{"m":"If a person or animal is conscious, it knows what's happening around it.","e":"He fell and hit his head, but he is still conscious."}]}]},"harvest":{"h":"harvest","i":"/ˈhaːvɪst/","a":"en-us-harvest.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Harvest is the time that you bring the crops in from the fields.","e":"We had an early harvest this year because of all the sun."},{"m":"(uncountable) Harvest is the act of bring the crops in from the fields.","e":"Our grain harvest went really well this year."},{"m":"(countable) A harvest is the crops that you bring in at the end of a growing season.","e":"Western Canada has had the biggest wheat harvest in 20 years."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you harvest something, you collect it after growing it.","e":"The rice looks like it's ready to harvest."}]}]},"patron":{"h":"patron","i":"/ˈpeɪt(ʃ)rən/","a":"en-us-patron.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A patron is a supporter of something.","e":"John, a well known patron of the arts, donated a large sum of money to the local museum last summer."},{"m":"(countable) A patron refers to a regular customer of a business."},{"m":"(countable) A property owner who hires a contractor for construction works"}]}]},"service":{"h":"service","i":"/ˈsɜːvɪs/","a":"en-us-service.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An action or work by one person that can be consumed by another person.","e":"Hair care is a service industry."},{"m":"A function that is provided by one program or machine for another.","e":"This machine provides the name service for the LAN."},{"m":"The military.","e":"I did three years of service before coming here."},{"m":"A set of dishes or utensils.","e":"She brought out the silver tea service."},{"m":"The act of initially starting, or serving, the ball in play in tennis, volleyball, and other games.","e":"The player had four service faults in the set."},{"m":"A religious rite or ritual.","e":"The funeral service was good."},{"m":"The serving, or delivery, of a document requiring someone to appear in a court of law.","e":"The service happened yesterday."},{"m":"(public service) That which is provided by the government or its agents.","e":"The Job Centre provides a service to the unemployed."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you service something, you serve them.","e":"They service the customer base."},{"m":"If you service something, you perform maintenance on them.","e":"He is going to service the car."}]}]},"good":{"h":"good","i":"/ɡʊd/","a":"en-us-good.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When you are good, you do the right things. That is, you do things that are kind or helpful. You do not do things that hurt people or are not honest.","e":"He is a good person and would never steal."},{"m":"If something is good it is useful or helpful. This also means high quality.","e":"My last pair of shoes were very good, they lasted two years!"},{"m":"If food is good it means you like the taste. This food is not likely to be spoiled or of low quality.","e":"Thank you for the pie; it was very good."},{"m":"If you had a good time, you enjoyed something."},{"m":"You may call something good because you like it.","e":"We had a good trip and liked seeing all the sights."},{"m":"If you are good at something, you do it well.","e":"She is a good swimmer; she could save you from drowning."},{"m":"A good sign means something good is likely to happen.","e":"Some people think a rainbow is a good omen, and means you will have good luck."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Good is the quality of being good.","e":"He has a lot of good in him and always helps us out."},{"m":"(uncountable) Good refers to the side of good (against evil and bad).","e":"I'm completely for good and think we should all try to do the right thing."},{"m":"(finance) Goods are identical items that are produced, then traded, bought or sold, for the purpose of consumption.","e":"You can buy many different types of goods at the market."}]}]},"great":{"h":"great","i":"/ɡreɪ̯t/","a":"en-us-great.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A great object or event is very big and large in scale.","e":"A great storm is approaching our shores."},{"m":"A great person or object is very good.","e":"Dinner was great."},{"m":"Something that is great is very important."},{"m":"Great is used to describe an important leader.","e":"Alexander the Great"}]},{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"It is said to show happiness about something.","e":"I got the job? Great!"},{"m":"It can also be said to show disappointment.","e":"I didn't get the job? Great."}]}]},"goodness":{"h":"goodness","i":"/ˈɡʊdnəs/","a":"en-us-goodness.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Goodness is the quality of being good.","e":"He was known in the community for his goodness towards others. As such, many in the community were saddened the day he passed away."},{"m":"Goodness is the good, nutritional, healthy part or content of something.","e":"Despite the goodness of exercising, John usually does not have time for it."}]}]},"defeat":{"h":"defeat","i":"/dɪ'fiːt/","a":"en-us-defeat.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you defeat someone, you win against them in a game, battle, or contest.","e":"South Africa defeated Zimbabwe (170) by four wickets with four balls to spare."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A defeat is a loss in a game, battle, or contest.","e":"Dole went down in defeat in last night's elections."}]}]},"battle":{"h":"battle","i":"/ˈbætəl/","a":"en-us-battle.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A battle is when different groups or teams fight each other."},{"m":"(countable) A battle is a personal challenge or struggle.","e":"After a long battle with cancer, he finally returned to work."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If teams or people battle, they fight.","e":"In World War II, Germany and England battled for control of Europe."}]}]},"continuous":{"h":"continuous","i":"/kənˈtɪnjuəs/","a":"en-us-continuous.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is continuous happens without stopping.","e":"The water flowed through the pipe continuously."},{"m":"If a surface is continuous, it is long and doesn't have anything in the middle.","e":"The railway line was continuous."}]}]},"coexistence":{"h":"coexistence","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"When two or more things live together in the same space, with or without mutual interaction."}]}]},"habitation":{"h":"habitation","i":"/ˌhæb.ɪˈteɪ.ʃən/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The act of living at a place.","e":"The habitation of animals in that forest is currently threated by logging."},{"m":"A place to live; a house."}]}]},"drive":{"h":"drive","i":"/'draɪv/","a":"en-us-drive.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you drive a car or other vehicle, you control its movement and direction.","e":"I've been learning how to drive a bus."},{"m":"If you drive somewhere, you go there by car.","e":"The bus is too slow. Let's drive to school instead."},{"m":"(transitive) If you drive someone or something, you make them move.","e":"The dogs drove the cows into the field."},{"m":"(transitive) If you drive someone to do something, you make them do something.","e":"The death of her son drove her to drink."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A drive is a trip by car.","e":"Let's go for a drive down to the lake."},{"m":"Drive is the feeling that you want or need to do something.","e":"She has a strong drive to succeed."},{"m":"(countable) A (disk) drive is part of a computer that reads and writes information to a disk."},{"m":"(countable) A drive is the short road outside a house to put a car on."},{"m":"(countable) A drive is a short strong effort to do something."},{"m":"(uncountable) Drive is the power that makes a vehicle move."},{"m":"(countable) In sports, a drive a ball that has been hit hard."},{"m":"(countable) A drive is when people direct a group of animals to move in a particular direction."},{"m":"(countable) A drive is kind of road."}]}]},"cough":{"h":"cough","i":"/kɒf/","a":"en-us-cough.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you cough, you quickly blow air out and make a noise because of a feeling in the throat.","e":"This cold is terrible. I was coughing and sneezing all night."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cough is the action or sound of quickly blowing air out because of a feeling in the throat.","e":"My doctor gave me some medicine for my cough."}]}]},"pocket":{"h":"pocket","i":"/ˈpɒ.kɪt/","a":"en-us-pocket.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pocket is a small empty space, usually in your clothes, usually to carry things in.","e":"I usually put my keys in my pants' pocket, but I can't find them now."},{"m":"(countable) A pocket is a small area of something that is completely surrounded by something else.","e":"There was a small pocket of air under the boat."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you pocket something, you put it in your pocket."},{"m":"If you pocket something you win, take, or steal it (and put it in your pocket.)"}]}]},"replace":{"h":"replace","i":"/rɪˈpleɪs/","a":"en-us-replace.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If X replaces Y or if you replace Y with X, X now does what Y used to do.","e":"Smith will replace the injured Jones for England who are leading 2 to 0."},{"m":"(transitive) If you replace something, you give somebody a new one because you have broken, lost, or used the old one.","e":"I'm sorry, don't know how I'm going to replace your stolen bike."},{"m":"(transitive) If you replace something, you put it back where it was.","e":"After looking at the ring for a while, he carefully replaced it and left the shop."}]}]},"minority":{"h":"minority","i":"/maɪˈnɒr.ɪ.ti/","a":"En-us-minority.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A minority is less than half (50%) of some group.","e":"Most people agreed, but a sizable minority were upset by the decision."},{"m":"(countable) A minority is a member of an ethnic group that does not have political or social power.","e":"The company claims it has hired several minorities since the complaint was lodged."},{"m":"(uncountable) Minority is the state of being a minor, not an adult."}]}]},"integration":{"h":"integration","i":"/ɪntəˈɡreɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-integration.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Integration is the act of a number of things to work together.","e":"European economic integration was widely expected to bring enormous benefits."},{"m":"(countable) An integration is the process of finding the integral of a function."}]}]},"king":{"h":"king","i":"/kɪŋ/","a":"en-us-king.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A king is the male leader of a country and whose son will probably lead the country.","e":"Following the death of James I, Charles I became King of England, in 1625"},{"m":"(countable) A powerful or influential person.","e":"Howard Stern styled himself as the \"king of all media\"."},{"m":"(countable) (chess) One of the playing pieces in chess; it may move only once square per move in any direction, but cannot move into check (threat of attack)."},{"m":"(countable) A playing card with the image of a king on it."}]}]},"unearth":{"h":"unearth","i":"/ʌnˈɜː(r)θ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-unearth.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To drive or take something out of the ground or soil; to uncover or find; to bring to light; to disclose","e":"to unearth a secret"}]}]},"ancient":{"h":"ancient","i":"/ˈeɪn.(t)ʃənt/","a":"en-us-ancient.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Very old, usually hundreds or thousands or millions of years old.","e":"He studied the ancient world."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(heraldry) A small flag or ensign."}]}]},"chief":{"h":"chief","i":"/tʃiːf/","a":"en-us-chief.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A leader or respected elder in a tribe.","e":"They came to the chief to resolve their dispute."},{"m":"(countable) The head of an organization.","e":"All firefighters report to the fire chief."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"The chief thing is the primary or principal thing.","e":"The chief cause of his death was cancer."}]}]},"find":{"h":"find","i":"/faɪnd/","a":"en-us-find.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you find something, you discover or locate it.","e":"I can't find my keys. Have you seen them?"},{"m":"(transitive) point out","e":"He finds faults with my work."},{"m":"decide that; form the opinion that","e":"I find your argument bad."},{"m":"(transitive) determine or judge.","e":"The jury finds for the defendant"}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Anything that is found, especially by good luck."}]}]},"found":{"h":"found","i":"/'fɑʊnd/","a":"en-us-found.ogg","l":"find","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To start some type of organization or company.","e":"They founded the company in 2003."},{"m":"To begin building."},{"m":"To melt."}]}]},"accurate":{"h":"accurate","i":"/ˈækjərɪt/","a":"en-us-accurate.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something accurate is correct or exact.","e":"We need to provide people with more accurate information."}]}]},"obsolete":{"h":"obsolete","i":"/ˈɑbsəliːt/","a":"en-us-obsolete.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is not used anymore, or if something newer replaced it, it is obsolete."}]}]},"newer":{"h":"newer","l":"new","q":"adjective"},"oranges":{"h":"oranges","l":"orange","q":"noun"},"permanent":{"h":"permanent","i":"/ˈpɝmənənt/","a":"en-us-permanent.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Permanent means lasting for a long time or forever.","e":"His permanent problems cannot be solved."}]}]},"upsetting":{"h":"upsetting","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something or someone that upsets somebody."}]}]},"ministry":{"h":"ministry","i":"/ˈmɪnɪstri/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-ministry.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A ministry is a government department, such as the ministry of defense.","e":"The ministry of health is building a new hospital."}]}]},"ordain":{"h":"ordain","i":"/ɔrˈdeɪn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-ordain.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If a church ordains a minister, it admits a person to the ministry."}]}]},"church":{"h":"church","i":"/t͡ʃɜːt͡ʃ/","a":"en-uk-church.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The Church is Christians gathering to praise and be with God."},{"m":"(countable) A church is a building where Christians gather and pray to God.","e":"The church across the street has a service at 10 am."},{"m":"(countable) A church is a particular kind of religious belief or power.","e":"They asked for the help of the Catholic Church."},{"m":"(countable) A Christian religious organization, local or general.","e":"The Church (referring to the dominant religious organization of a particular time or place)."},{"m":"(uncountable) Church is a time when Christians go to a church.","e":"I'll be there after church."}]}]},"admit":{"h":"admit","i":"/ədˈmɪt/","a":"en-us-admit.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you admit someone, you allow them to enter an area or a building.","e":"The man was admitted to the theater, and sat in the front row."},{"m":"(transitive) If you are admitted to an institution, the institution starts taking care of you.","e":"He was admitted to hospital and he is having his operation next week."},{"m":"If you admit something, you say reluctantly that it is true.","e":"She admitted that she robbed the bank."}]}]},"confess":{"h":"confess","i":"/kənˈfɛs/","a":"en-us-confess.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you confess to doing something, you are saying that you did it.","e":"John confessed to the cops that he robbed the bank."}]}]},"female":{"h":"female","i":"/ˈfiː.meɪl/","a":"en-us-female.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a person, animal or plant is female it is of the sex that can have babies or produce eggs or seeds. Girls and women are female people.","e":"The test says your baby will be female."},{"m":"If something is female, it is of, for, or about women or girls.","e":"The girls can change in the female changing room over there."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A female is a person, animal, or plant that can have or produce eggs.","e":"In humans, females are called women or girls."}]}]},"continent":{"h":"continent","i":"/ˈkɒntɪnənt/","a":"en-us-continent.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A continent is a big piece of land that is almost as big as your mom's ass.","e":"The seven continents of the world are Africa, Antarctica, Asia, Australia, Europe, North America, and South America."}]}]},"extend":{"h":"extend","i":"/ɛkˈstɛnd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-extend.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you extend something, you make it longer.","e":"They extended the meeting so that more people could speak."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something extends from x to y, it covers all the time or space in between.","e":"The Alps extend from France to Austria."},{"m":"If you extend something, you offer it","e":"I would like to extend to you an invitation to the party."}]}]},"extension":{"h":"extension","i":"/ɪkˈstɛnʃən/","a":"en-us-extension.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The space that something occupies."},{"m":"Extension is the process of making something longer."},{"m":"(countable) An extension is the time or part of something that was added to make it longer.","e":"She had extensions put in her hair and now she has long hair."},{"m":"An extension is the operation of pulling the two ends of a broken bone to bring the broken pieces into the same straight line."},{"m":"Extension is the act of moving an arm, leg, finger, etc. so that it is straight."},{"m":"An extension is short for."}]}]},"separate":{"h":"separate","i":"/ˈsɛpərət/","a":"en-us-separate-adj.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Being separate means that a piece of an object is not connected to or attached to the rest of the object.","e":"This chair was broken into five separate pieces."},{"m":"If two objects, ideas, or people are separate from one another, they are not together.","e":"I try to keep my personal life separate from work."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To separate something is to take it apart, divide it, or stop it from connecting.","e":"I diced the onions and the carrots, separating them into two piles."}]}]},"lot":{"h":"lot","i":"/lɒt/","a":"en-us-lot.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A lot of something is a large amount of it.","e":"I have a lot of things to say."},{"m":"(countable) To a large degree.","e":"Running is lots more fun when the weather is cool."},{"m":"(countable) Often","e":"He used to come here a lot, but he doesn't anymore."},{"m":"(countable) A lot is a piece of land, usually small.","e":"They are constructing a building on this lot."}]}]},"confirm":{"h":"confirm","i":"/kənˈfɜːm/","a":"en-us-confirm.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If something confirms an idea, it show that it is true.","e":"The results of the study confirm previous research on the topic."},{"m":"(transitive) If you confirm a possible agreement or plan, you tell somebody that it is now final and official.","e":"Can we confirm that the meeting is at 10:00?"},{"m":"(transitive) If a Christian priest confirms a baptized person, they admit them to full participation in the church."}]}]},"revolt":{"h":"revolt","i":"/rɪˈvoʊlt/","a":"en-us-revolt.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If a person revolts, they act against an authority.","e":"The farmers had to revolt against the government to get what they deserve."},{"m":"(transitive) If something revolts you, its existence greatly repels you.","e":"Your brother revolts me!"}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A revolt is an act of [[#Verb|revolting]]."}]}]},"compilation":{"h":"compilation","i":"/kɒmpɪˈleɪʃən/","a":"en-us-compilation.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The act of collecting or gathering things from various sources and putting them together.","e":"I enjoy the compilation that is required when writing an article."},{"m":"A collection of things that were compiled (taken from different places and put together). A compilation is usually a book or official paper made of materials from other books or official papers.","e":"The band was lazy, so instead of making new songs, they just made a compilation of old songs."}]}]},"constituent":{"h":"constituent","i":"/kənˈstɪtjuənt/","a":"en-uk-constituent.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is constituent, it is being part of a whole."},{"m":"If someone is constituent, they are given permission to make a constitution."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A constituent is a part of a whole."},{"m":"(countable) A constituent is a resident of a place of an elected official.","e":"The governor is popular among his constituents. He will likely win the election this year."},{"m":"(countable) A constituent is a usable element of a phrase or clause."}]}]},"constituency":{"h":"constituency","i":"/kənˈstɪt͡ʃu.ənsi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-constituency.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A constituency is a specific area that is represented by an official who is elected by the voters of that area.","e":"The prime minister represented their constituency."}]}]},"represent":{"h":"represent","i":"/ˈrɛp.rɪ.zɛnt/","a":"en-us-represent.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To represent is to stand in the place of; to act the part of (another).","e":"A member of Congress represents his district in Congress."},{"m":"To represent is to serve as a sign or symbol of; as, mathematical symbols represent quantities or relations; words represent ideas or things."}]}]},"expansion":{"h":"expansion","i":"/ɪkˈspænʃən/","a":"en-us-expansion.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The act or process of expanding.","e":"The expansion of metals and plastics in response to heat is well understood."},{"m":"A new addition.","e":"My new office is in the expansion behind the main building."},{"m":"A product to be used with a previous product.","e":"This expansion requires the original game-board."}]}]},"special":{"h":"special","i":"/ˈspeʃəl/","a":"en-us-special.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is special, it is not usual; it is different or important in some way.","e":"She is the most special person in my life."},{"m":"particularly interesting; dear; beloved; favored"}]}]},"typo":{"h":"typo","i":"/ˈtaɪpəʊ/","a":"en-us-typo.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A typo is a mistake made when or. When a person types the wrong letters for a word when the person really knows what the right letters are, that is a typo.","e":"It was just a typo; he wrote \"dgo\" but he meant \"dog\"."}]}]},"replaced":{"h":"replaced","i":"/rɪˈpleɪst/","a":"en-us-replaced.ogg","l":"replace","q":"verb"},"connection":{"h":"connection","i":"/kəˈnɛkʃən/","a":"en-us-connection.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A connection is a way that two or more things come or belong together.","e":"Who was the first person to make the connection between sickness and cleanliness?"}]}]},"medical":{"h":"medical","i":"/ˈmɛdɪkl̩/","a":"en-us-medical.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"About physical health and medicine.","e":"Dr. Barry was very creative in his teaching, research, and medical practice."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A medical is a general check by a doctor.","e":"I'd like to make an appointment for my annual medical."}]}]},"reluctant":{"h":"reluctant","i":"/rɪˈlʌktənt/","a":"en-us-reluctant.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are reluctant to do something, you do not want to do it.","e":"My son was reluctant to go to school today because he has a test."}]}]},"poison":{"h":"poison","i":"/ˈpɔɪz(ə)n/","a":"en-us-poison.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Poison is any substance that makes people or animals sick or kills them if it gets into their body.","e":"He put out poison to get rid of the mice."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If x poisons y, x puts poison in y.","e":"They poisoned the king's food."},{"m":"(transitive) If something poisons a person or animal, it makes them sick, or kills them chemically.","e":"The drugs that he used were slowly poisoning him."},{"m":"(transitive) If something poisons someone's mind, it puts bad thoughts there."}]}]},"radio":{"h":"radio","i":"/ˈreɪdiˌəʊ/","a":"en-us-radio.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A radio is piece of electronic equipment that sends or receives signals though the air and plays voice, music, or other sounds.","e":"I used to carry a small radio, but now I have an MP3 player."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you radio someone, you send a message to them using a radio."},{"m":"If you radio a message, you send it to someone using a radio."}]}]},"constant":{"h":"constant","i":"/ˈkɒnstənt/","a":"en-us-constant.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is constant, it doesn't change over time.","e":"I have this constant pain in my back. I wish it would stop."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(technical) A constant is a value that doesn't change.","e":"In the formula 7x^2+3y+5=z, 5 is a constant."}]}]},"psychological":{"h":"psychological","i":"/ˌsaɪkəˈlɒdʒɪkl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-psychological.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"About your mind.","e":"We are concerned about the psychological effect the experience may have on the girls."},{"m":"About psychology.","e":"Many psychological theories refer to problematic parent-child relationships."}]}]},"psychology":{"h":"psychology","i":"/saɪˈkɑlədʒi/","a":"en-us-psychology.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The study of the mind and behaviour.","e":"Research in sports psychology demonstrates the value of setting difficult goals."}]}]},"hunt":{"h":"hunt","i":"/hʌnt/","a":"en-us-hunt.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you hunt for something, you look for it very carefully.","e":"We hunted for new clothing at the mall."},{"m":"If you hunt for animals, you look for them to catch or kill them.","e":"My father hunted rabbits when I was a child."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A hunt is a search for something or someone.","e":"The police were on a hunt to find the murderer."},{"m":"A hunt is a search for animal(s) to catch or kill."}]}]},"probable":{"h":"probable","i":"/ˈprɑbəbl̩/","a":"en-us-probable.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is probable, there is a high chance of it happening, being true, or existing.","e":"Weather is the probable cause of this morning's traffic problems."}]}]},"organ":{"h":"organ","i":"/ˈɔːɡən/","a":"en-us-organ.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An organ is a part of an animal or plant with a specific purpose, such as an eye or a heart.","e":"The stomach is an important organ of the digestive system of humans."},{"m":"(countable) An organ is a musical instrument that looks like a piano and blows air through pipes to make sounds.","e":"He can play many organs."}]}]},"nevertheless":{"h":"nevertheless","i":"/ˈnɛvəðəlɛs/","a":"en-uk-nevertheless.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":", (formal) You use nevertheless to add surprising information or something in contrast to what was already said or written.","e":"Morgan stopped working as a doctor in 1973. Nevertheless, he remained active in medical research until his death."}]}]},"none":{"h":"none","i":"/nʌn/","a":"en-us-none.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"Not any.","e":"I looked to see how many coins I had, but I had none."}]}]},"film":{"h":"film","i":"/fɪlm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-film.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A film is a recording of a moving picture that tells stories including actors, directors, and producers.","e":"The studio has hired some actors to make a film about the making of Wiktionary."},{"m":"(uncountable) The art or business of making films.","e":"I studied film at college and now I'm a writer."},{"m":"Film is a thin, clear material used for taking photographs or movies.","e":"My new camera is digital and doesn't need film."},{"m":"A film is a flat, thin material or substance often covering something.","e":"The soap left a sticky film on the glass."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you film something, you record it as a moving picture.","e":"Somebody filmed the attack with their cell phone and showed it to police."}]}]},"busy":{"h":"busy","i":"/ˈbɪzi/","a":"en-us-busy.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are busy, you are doing something and not available to do something else.","e":"I'm sorry, I'm busy on Monday. Can we get together on Wednesday?"},{"m":"If a time is busy, there is little or no time to rest because of work or other.","e":"Things are really busy at the office this week. I have five meetings tomorrow."},{"m":"If a place is busy, there are many people or vehicles moving about.","e":"The roads are busy this morning, so give yourself extra time."},{"m":"If a telephone is busy someone is using it and cannot take a call.","e":"I tried to call him, but the line was busy."},{"m":"If a design is busy there are too many small elements in it.","e":"I don't think you should wear that busy dress."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you busy yourself, you find things to do to fill your time.","e":"He busied himself with fixing his tie as he waited for her to arrive."}]}]},"exact":{"h":"exact","a":"en-us-exact.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is exact, it completely agrees with a statement, fact, or a truth; it fits perfectly."},{"m":"If something is exact, it is clearly thought of or stated."},{"m":"If someone is exact, they are careful to follow a rule, guideline, or promise; they are accurate; they are methodical."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If someone exacts a payment from someone, they demand and enforce it."},{"m":"(transitive) If someone exacts something, they make it desirable; they need it."},{"m":"(transitive) If someone exacts something from someone, they get or make it by force."}]}]},"hate":{"h":"hate","i":"/heɪt/","a":"en-us-hate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you hate something you dislike it strongly.","e":"My 3-year old won't eat tomatoes. She just hates them."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Hate is a feeling of strong dislike.","e":"My feelings towards him are a mixture of love and hate."},{"m":"(countable) A hate is something that you dislike strongly.","e":"Did you have any hates or fears when you were there?"}]}]},"chair":{"h":"chair","i":"/ʧɛə(r)/","a":"en-uk-chair.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A chair is a piece of furniture for one person to sit on.","e":"Please, pull up a chair and sit down."},{"m":"(countable) The person who is in charge of a meeting is the chair of the meeting.","e":"The chair opened the floor to questions."},{"m":"(countable) A chair is a position of professor in a university.","e":"A chair of Mathematics has opened at London University."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you chair a meeting, you are in charge of controlling it.","e":"The meeting was chaired by the head teacher."}]}]},"nurse":{"h":"nurse","i":"/nɜːs/","a":"en-us-nurse.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A nurse is a healthcare worker who helps doctors and helps sick or injured people with the activities of daily life."},{"m":"(countable) A nurse is a woman who takes care of other people's children."},{"m":"(countable) A wet nurse"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you nurse a sick or injured person or animal, you help them with the activities of daily life.","e":"I admire the time he took to nurse that sick dog back to health."},{"m":"(transitive) If you nurse a body part or an injury, you rest it and are careful about it."},{"m":"(transitive) If you nurse a bad feeling, you think about it often and try not to forget it."},{"m":"(transitive) If you nurse a drink, you drink it very slowly."}]}]},"list":{"h":"list","i":"/lɪst/","a":"en-us-list.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A list is a group of related words, often in some order, often to help you remember something.","e":"I can't remember if we need milk and I've forgotten the shopping list."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you list something, you say or write a number of related things.","e":"OK, let's start the meeting by listing the things to talk about."},{"m":"(intransitive) If a ship lists, it leans to one side."}]}]},"examination":{"h":"examination","i":"/ɪɡˌzæmɪˈneɪʃən/","a":"en-us-examination.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An examination is a formal test, usually important and often at the end of a course.","e":"Did you pass the English examination last week?"},{"m":"Examination is the act of looking at something very carefully.","e":"The teachers and parents worked together in a closer examination of the problems grade seven students face."}]}]},"dead":{"h":"dead","i":"/dɛd/","a":"en-us-dead.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Not alive.","e":"My brother is dead. His funeral was last week."},{"m":"Without power.","e":"The problem is a dead battery."},{"m":"Without feeling, numb.","e":"My arm is dead. I cannot feel it."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":", completely.","e":"He thinks you are a woman, but you are a man. He is dead wrong."}]}]},"hanging":{"h":"hanging","i":"/ˈhæŋɪŋ/","a":"en-us-hanging.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A form of capital punishment where a person is held in the air by a rope around his/her neck until they are dead.","e":"There was a hanging in Carson City."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To kill by hanging.","e":"Nebraska is hanging him next week."}]}]},"phone":{"h":"phone","i":"/ˈfoʊn/","a":"en-us-phone.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A phone is a tool for speaking to people who are far away.","e":"Can I borrow your phone? I need to call my friend."},{"m":"A phone is a smartphone.","e":"This classroom does not allow students to use their phones during class."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you contact somebody using a phone, you phone them.","e":"Hey, I'll phone you tonight and we can decide what to do."}]}]},"pen":{"h":"pen","i":"/pɛn/","a":"en-us-pen.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pen is a writing tool that uses ink.","e":"She sat down with pen and paper and started a letter to her aunt."},{"m":"(countable) A pen is a small area with a fence around it, usually for animals.","e":"The pigs walked slowly around their pen."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you pen something, you compose it and write it down.","e":"The letter was penned by Shakespeare just before he died."},{"m":"(transitive) If you pen an animal, you put it in a pen."},{"m":"(transitive) If someone is penned in, they are in a place and cannot get out easily.","e":"Most of them were penned in watching the TV with their parents."}]}]},"lonely":{"h":"lonely","i":"/ˈləʊnli/","a":"en-us-lonely.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you feel lonely, you feel sad because you are alone.","e":"She was bored and lonely without her friends."},{"m":"A lonely place is a place with few people, often far from a city or town.","e":"The only sound in that wild, lonely place was the wind."}]}]},"afford":{"h":"afford","i":"/ʌˈford/","a":"en-us-afford.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you can afford something, you have enough money or resources to buy it or do it.","e":"The richer people, who could afford it, built large houses."},{"m":"(transitive) (formal) If you afford someone something, you give it or allow it.","e":"The Government has continued to afford him protection."}]}]},"facilitate":{"h":"facilitate","i":"/fəˈsɪlɪteɪt/","a":"en-us-facilitate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If X facilitates Y, X makes Y easier.","e":"The aim was to facilitate the development of such schools."},{"m":"If someone facilitates a meeting, they guide it and help it run well.","e":"The government appointed the judge to facilitate the meeting between the protesters and the developers."}]}]},"elderly":{"h":"elderly","i":"/ˈɛldɚli/","a":"en-us-elderly.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"(polite) If a person is elderly, they are old.","e":"The hospital had a number of elderly patients who had been there for many years."}]}]},"polite":{"h":"polite","i":"/pəˈlaɪt/","a":"en-polite.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are polite, you treat people nicely and follow the social rules of your group.","e":"It's not polite to take something without asking."}]}]},"ensure":{"h":"ensure","i":"/ɪnˈʃʊə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-ensure.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If X ensures Y, it makes Y certain.","e":"His work is great and should ensure the survival of his business."},{"m":"If you ensure that something is correct or that it happens, you check it and fix any problems.","e":"Special care is taken to ensure that teachers understand the course material."}]}]},"mixed":{"h":"mixed","i":"/mɪkst/","a":"en-us-mixed.ogg","l":"mix","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is mixed, it includes different kinds of things.","e":"I don't know. I have very mixed feelings about these changes."}]}]},"picture":{"h":"picture","i":"/ˈpɪktʃə/","a":"en-us-picture.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A picture is marks on a flat object, like paper, that show shapes, people, or things.","e":"Mommy, I drew a picture of a cat."},{"m":"(countable) A picture is a photograph.","e":"Everyone stand there together and I'll take your picture."},{"m":"(countable) A picture is a still or moving image on a screen."},{"m":"(countable) A picture is an idea or image that have inside your head."},{"m":"(countable) A picture is an understanding of a situation.","e":"What's the picture like in Somalia?"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you picture something, you make an image of it in your head."},{"m":"(transitive), If something is pictured, it is shown in a picture."},{"m":"(transitive), If something is pictured a certain way, it is described that way."}]}]},"image":{"h":"image","i":"/ˈɪmɪd͡ʒ/","a":"en-us-image.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An image is something you can see or imagine that looks like the real thing.","e":"Many people have an image of God as an old man."},{"m":"An image is the good or bad opinion about someone or something.","e":"What's your image of Paris?"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you image something, you create an image of it.","e":"The lunar surface at the Apollo 17 site, imaged by the Apollo 17 astronauts."}]}]},"aerobic":{"h":"aerobic","i":"/ɛəˈrəʊ.bɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-aerobic.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a living thing is aerobic, it needs oxygen to survive.","e":"E. coli is a type of aerobic bacteria because it cannot survive without oxygen."}]}]},"democracy":{"h":"democracy","i":"/dɪˈmɒkrəsi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-democracy.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Democracy is a system of government where everyone is equal and everyone has some power. It is a system of government in which the people elect their leaders.","e":"Democracy is the will of the people."},{"m":"(countable) A democracy is a country that uses democracy as the system of government.","e":"The United States is a democracy."}]}]},"propaganda":{"h":"propaganda","i":"/ˌprɒpəˈɡændə/","a":"en-us-propaganda.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Things that are written or said, often by someone in power, that are not true or that are one-sided.","e":"I object when political propaganda is pushed through my letterbox at election time"}]}]},"revolution":{"h":"revolution","i":"/ˌrɛvəˈl(j)uːʃən/","a":"en-us-revolution.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A revolution is a sudden significant change.","e":"The Industrial Revolution began when machines were able to make things quicker and cheaper than people."},{"m":"(countable) A revolution is a war against the government by the country's own people.","e":"There was a revolution in France in 1789."},{"m":"When a wheel turns around once it has made a revolution; going in a circle; turning; revolving.","e":"The hour hand on the clock makes one revolution in twelve hours."},{"m":"(countable) A revolution is when one object (like a planet) goes in a circle around another object (like a star).","e":"One revolution of Earth is 365 days long. One revolution of Venus is 225 days long."}]}]},"neutral":{"h":"neutral","i":"/ˈnjuːtrəl/","a":"en-us-neutral.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Treating both sides equally.","e":"A judge in a trial must be neutral."}]}]},"delivered":{"h":"delivered","a":"en-us-delivered.ogg","l":"deliver","q":"verb"},"deliver":{"h":"deliver","i":"/dɪˈlɪvə(r)/","a":"en-us-deliver.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you deliver something, you bring it to the person or place where it belongs.","e":"The award was delivered to her personally by the president."},{"m":"(transitive) If you deliver a speech, you speak in front of a number of people."},{"m":"If you deliver, you do what you promised or had to do.","e":"A promise from the government doesn't mean that they will actually deliver."},{"m":"(transitive) If you deliver a hit, kick, etc. to someone, you hit them."},{"m":"(transitive) If someone delivers a baby, they help it out of the mother when it is born.","e":"Joan Ellen Montgomery, 4.8 kg, was delivered last night at the Greenville hospital."},{"m":"(transitive) If you deliver someone from something bad, you help them get away from it."}]}]},"moderate":{"h":"moderate","i":"/ˈmɒdərət/","a":"en-us-moderate-adj.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone or something is moderate, it is balanced and not extreme.","e":"The weather in Hawai'i tends to be quite moderate."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If something moderates, it becomes more moderate.","e":"As he grew older, his ideas began to moderate."},{"m":"If someone moderates a meeting or discussion, they organise and control it."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A moderate is a person who has moderate (political) views."}]}]},"hurt":{"h":"hurt","i":"/hɜːt/","a":"en-us-hurt.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If a person hurts someone, they make them feel pain.","e":"Don't hurt your brother or I'll send you to your room."},{"m":"If a person hurts something, they damage it."},{"m":"If someone or part of their body hurt, they feel pain.","e":"I've been hurting ever since I fell from the roof."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is hurt, they are wounded or in pain.","e":"He got hurt skiing last week when he fell."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A hurt is a wound or other damage that causes pain."}]}]},"investigation":{"h":"investigation","i":"/ɪnˌvɛstəˈgeɪʃən/","a":"en-us-investigation.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An investigation is a careful look at a crime, problem, etc. to find the truth or a solution.","e":"Researchers were conducting further investigations into the connection between smoking and lung disease."}]}]},"commercial":{"h":"commercial","i":"/kəˈmɜːʃəl/","a":"en-us-commercial.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is commercial, it is related to buying, selling, and money.","e":"Education is much more difficult than many industrial and commercial processes to measure."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A commercial is an advertisement on TV or radio.","e":"The actress recently appeared in a TV commercial for Meadowcup butter."}]}]},"dance":{"h":"dance","i":"/dɑ:ns/","a":"en-us-dance.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you dance, you move your body to music.","e":"He danced with the princess to the music of."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Dance is body movement done to music.","e":"He has an interesting dance he does while listening to that song."},{"m":"A dance is an event where people come together to dance.","e":"Are you going to the dance?"}]}]},"beam":{"h":"beam","i":"/biːm/","a":"en-us-beam.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A beam is a line of light or energy.","e":"A beam of sunlight came through the window making a rectangle on the floor."},{"m":"(countable) A beam is a long straight piece of wood or metal used in building to support weight.","e":"Inside, the ceiling of the tunnel was held up with beams and was high enough that we could stand."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you beam a signal from one place to another, you send it through the air."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you beam, you smile and look very happy."}]}]},"forward":{"h":"forward","i":"/ˈfɔː.wəd/","a":"en-us-forward.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If something goes forward, it moves in the direction of its front, not its back."},{"m":"If something goes forward, it gets better."},{"m":"If something goes forward, it moves into the future."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is forward, they are too friendly when talking to strangers."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you forward a letter, message, etc., you send it."},{"m":"(transitive) If you forward your career, you make it more successful or better."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A forward is a player whose position plays closer to the other team's end in games like soccer."}]}]},"hi":{"h":"hi","i":"/haɪ/","a":"en-us-hi.ogg","s":[{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"(informal) You say \"hi\" in greeting when you meet or see somebody.","e":"Hi, how are you?"}]}]},"framework":{"h":"framework","i":"/ˈfreɪmwɜːk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-framework.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A framework is basic ideas and organisation that you can build an argument, a book, a society, etc. around.","e":"The aim of the course is to provide a comprehensive framework for practical and theoretical study in Art and Design."},{"m":"(countable) A framework is the structural supports that a building, vehicle, etc. is built around.","e":"Very large iron and steel beams provide the framework for the building’s central section."}]}]},"explore":{"h":"explore","i":"/ɪkˈsplɔː/","a":"en-us-explore.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you explore a possibility, plan, idea, etc. you think about it carefully.","e":"As they were learning about wine, they were exploring the possibilities of setting up their own winery."},{"m":"If you explore something, you look around it to try to find new places, things, parts, etc.","e":"Stories like this about the old house made him want to go and explore for himself."}]}]},"negative":{"h":"negative","i":"/ˈnɛ(e)gəˌɾɪv/","a":"en-us-negative.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is negative, it is harmful, sad, or otherwise not good.","e":"You can believe or not believe, that there's a positive and negative side to everything."},{"m":"If a word, sentence, answer, etc. is negative, it uses a word like no, not, never, etc.","e":"Can't is the negative form of can."},{"m":"If someone is a negative person or has a negative attitude, they mainly think about bad things.","e":"Her negative attitudes were the result of a hard life."},{"m":"If a test result is negative, the test did not find what it was testing for.","e":"There's nothing to worry about. The HIV test is negative."},{"m":"A negative electrical charge is one carried by an electron.","e":"Attach the wire to the negative pole of the battery."},{"m":"A negative number or value is less than zero.","e":"A positive number multiplied by a negative number results in a negative."},{"m":"A negative symptom is one where something is missing. Usually this is for schizophrenia.","e":"His negative symptoms included not speaking and not showing emotion."},{"m":"Based on something not being there, not being true, or being reversed, in some other way.","e":"I tie-bleached my shirt to make a negative image, then tie-dyed it to add a positive image."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A negative is a photographic image with reversed colours (e.g., black instead of white).","e":"Prints are then made from the negatives, and in the case of the B&W I may either tint or tone the final print."},{"m":"(countable) A negative is a word, sentence, answer, etc. that means no.","e":"When I asked if we could go next week, the answer was a negative."},{"m":"(countable) A negative is something that is harmful, sad, or otherwise not good.","e":"Right now in Korea there is a negative connected with anything Japanese."},{"m":"(countable) A negative is a test result that did not find what it was testing for.","e":"In out test group there were 20 negatives and only one positive."},{"m":"(countable) (photography) A negative is a small picture with the colors inverted. Negatives are made on film, then photographs are made from the negatives.","e":"We saved the negatives and used to make more pictures later."}]}]},"printed":{"h":"printed","i":"/prɪntɪd/","a":"en-us-printed.ogg","l":"print","q":"verb"},"print":{"h":"print","i":"/prɪnt/","a":"en-us-print.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you print a picture, book, newspaper, etc., you make a copy of it on paper with a machine using ink or toner.","e":"The book was printed in December."},{"m":"If you print words or letters, you write them by hand in a block style, not a cursive style.","e":"Please print your name here and then sign underneath."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Print is letters, numerals, punctuation and other similar written symbols.","e":"The print size in the newspaper is too small for me to read."},{"m":"(countable) A print is a copy that you make with a machine using ink or toner.","e":"There were only fifty prints made of this painting."}]}]},"reaction":{"h":"reaction","i":"/riˈækʃən/","a":"en-us-reaction.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A reaction is an action that happens because of another action.","e":"When he asked her to lunch, her first reaction was to say no."}]}]},"rage":{"h":"rage","i":"/reɪdʒ/","a":"en-us-rage.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An emotion of wild anger.","e":"Losing his game sent him into a fit of rage."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When a person rage, they get very angry."}]}]},"success":{"h":"success","i":"/səkˈsɛs/","a":"en-us-success.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Success is doing what you plan or want to do.","e":"Getting 100% on the test gave him a feeling of success."}]}]},"rages":{"h":"rages","l":"rage","q":"noun"},"emotion":{"h":"emotion","i":"/ɛˈmʌʊʃn̩/","a":"en-ca-emotion.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A human feeling such as sadness, anger, loss, sympathy, etc.","e":"Loss is a powerful emotion."}]}]},"annoying":{"h":"annoying","i":"/əˈnɔɪ.ɪŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Persent101-annoying.wav","l":"annoy","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Someone or something that annoys is annoying.","e":"He is so annoying!"}]}]},"annoy":{"h":"annoy","i":"/əˈnɔɪ/","a":"en-us-annoy.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If something annoys people, it makes them angry or bothered. This often happens after someone does an action many times.","e":"It annoys me when he won't stop talking."}]}]},"annoys":{"h":"annoys","l":"annoy","q":"verb"},"mad":{"h":"mad","i":"/ˈmæd/","a":"en-us-mad.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is mad, they are angry.","e":"I am so mad at you for ruining my painting."},{"m":"If someone is mad, they are insane.","e":"He says he hears voices. I think he's gone mad!"},{"m":"To be mad about someone or something means to like someone or something very much."}]}]},"ruin":{"h":"ruin","i":"/ˈruː.ɪn/","a":"en-us-ruin.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To wreck something, to make it useless, to break something.","e":"You've ruined my painting!"}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(usually plural) The standing parts of a broken building or construction.","e":"Our only look at Mayan culture is the ruins."}]}]},"ruins":{"h":"ruins","i":"/ˈru.ɪnz/","a":"en-us-ruins.ogg","l":"ruin","q":"noun"},"ruined":{"h":"ruined","i":"/ˈruɪnd/","a":"en-us-ruined.ogg","l":"ruin","q":"verb"},"belly":{"h":"belly","i":"/ˈbɛli/","a":"en-us-belly.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The soft part of the body below the chest.","e":"He got punched in the belly."}]}]},"mysteries":{"h":"mysteries","l":"mystery","q":"noun"},"altitude":{"h":"altitude","i":"/ˈælt.ɪˌtjuːd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-altitude.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"measured from sea level.","e":"The altitude of is 3776 meters."}]}]},"amateur":{"h":"amateur","i":"/ˈæ.mə.tə/","a":"en-us-amateur1.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An amateur is a person who does something for fun, not as a job."},{"m":"(countable) An amateur in sports, is a person who does not play for money."},{"m":"(countable) An amateur is someone who is not very good at what they are doing."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is amateur, it is not very good."},{"m":"If something is amateur, it is created or done by amateurs"}]}]},"ability":{"h":"ability","i":"/əˈbɪl.ə.ti/","a":"en-us-ability.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An ability is something that you can do.","e":"I have a very good reading ability."}]}]},"recursion":{"h":"recursion","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Recursion is the act or process of going back and happening again."},{"m":"(uncountable) (logic, mathematics) Recursion is the use of a function inside itself to generate an infinite number of results.","e":"The following function exhibits recursion."},{"m":"(uncountable) (linguistics) Recursion is the use of one kind of linguistic unit inside itself.","e":"An example of recursion is when a clause appears inside a larger clause, as in the following:"}]}]},"albeit":{"h":"albeit","i":"/ɔːlˈbi.ɪt/","a":"en-us-albeit.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"(formal) You use albeit to give more information that weakens earlier information.","e":"He won the fight, albeit barely."}]}]},"minor":{"h":"minor","i":"/maɪnə/","a":"en-us-minor.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A minor change, problem, injury, etc. is not very important.","e":"We still have to make a few minor changes, but it's mostly done."},{"m":"A minor musical scale is a scale that starts two notes before the major scale. Music in a minor scale often sounds sad.","e":"That music could be A minor or C major."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A minor is a person who is younger than the legal age of adulthood.","e":"In Indiana, a person younger than 18 years old is considered a minor."},{"m":"(countable) A minor is a person below a legal age of privilege, right or responsibility, such as the legal drinking age or legal age for sexual activity.","e":"The high school teacher was convicted of a crime for having sex with a minor."},{"m":"A minor is a subject area that is not the main study of a student at a college or university, but is their second most important focus.","e":"I had so many credit hours of English, it became my minor."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Minor means to minor in a subject at a college or university.","e":"I had so many credit hours of English that I decided to minor in it."}]}]},"stressed":{"h":"stressed","l":"stress","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"(not before the noun) If someone is stressed, they are worried and tired.","e":"I've got these three tests tomorrow and I'm feeling so stressed that I can't sleep."}]}]},"estate":{"h":"estate","i":"/ɪˈsteɪt/","a":"en-us-estate.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Someone's estate is everything they own, or everything they leave when they die.","e":"Because he had no family, he left his estate to the church."},{"m":"An estate is a large area of land with a large house on it.","e":"On the weekend, we went fishing at her country estate."}]}]},"copies":{"h":"copies","i":"/ˈkɑpiz/","a":"en-us-copies.ogg","l":"copy","q":"noun"},"copy":{"h":"copy","i":"/ˈkɒpi/","a":"en-us-copy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A copy of something looks or acts like it.","e":"They took the diamond and replaced it with a cheap copy."},{"m":"(countable) A copy of a book, newspaper, painting, etc. is one of many that are exactly the same.","e":"Please bring me the copies of those reports."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you copy something, you make something look exactly the same as it.","e":"Good artists copy. Great artists steal."}]}]},"artificial":{"h":"artificial","i":"/ɑː(r)təˈfɪʃəl/","a":"en-us-artificial.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is made by people instead of being made by nature.","e":"The silk flowers were not real. They were artificial."}]}]},"brittle":{"h":"brittle","i":"/ˈbrɪtl̩/","a":"en-us-brittle.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Not flexible; easy to break under stress or pressure"}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A candy made from boiled sugar and nuts."}]}]},"committee":{"h":"committee","i":"/kəˈmɪti/","a":"en-us-committee.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A group of people that come together to do something or decide something.","e":"He is on the administrative committee. They decide how to administer the school."}]}]},"common":{"h":"common","i":"/ˈkɒmən/","a":"en-us-common.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"; shared by more than one.","e":"The two teams have the common goal of winning the game."},{"m":"ring regularly or frequently; usual.","e":"It is common to find sharks off this coast."},{"m":"in large numbers or in a large quantity.","e":"Sharks are common in these waters."},{"m":"If two people or things have something in common they, are the same in some way.","e":"University students have a lot in common with high-school students."},{"m":", ordinary or vulgar."},{"m":"Not special."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A common is an area that is shared by many people."}]}]},"compassion":{"h":"compassion","i":"/kəmˈpæʃ.ən/","a":"en-us-compassion.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) If you have compassion, you are aware of the pain of other people and want to help make it better."}]}]},"complement":{"h":"complement","i":"/ˈkɒmpləmənt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-complement.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If x complements y, x makes y complete or whole.","e":"We believe your addition will complement the team."},{"m":"(transitive) If two people or things complement each other, each has what the other is missing or needs.","e":"The flavors of the pepper and garlic complement each other, giving a very rich taste in combination."},{"m":"(transitive) To change a voltage, number, color, etc. to its complement."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Something which complements.","e":"We believe you will make a good complement to our team."},{"m":"A complement is a word or phrase that is needed to make another word grammatical.","e":"In he seems nice, nice is the complement of seem."},{"m":"an angle which, together with a given angle, makes a right angle."},{"m":"The color which, when mixed with the given color, gives black (for mixing pigments) or white (for mixing light).","e":"The complement of blue is orange."},{"m":"In boating: The full number of people needed to man a ship (esp. a ship of war)","e":"The ship's complement is 35 people. 35 people are needed to sail the ship"}]}]},"complete":{"h":"complete","i":"/kəmˈpliːt/","a":"en-us-complete.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To finish; to reach the end.","e":"He completed the assignment on time."},{"m":"(transitive) To make whole or entire.","e":"The last chapter completes the book nicely."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"With everything included; entire, total.","e":"It was a complete shock when he turned up on my doorstep."}]}]},"dialogue":{"h":"dialogue","i":"/ˈdaɪælɒg/","a":"en-us-dialogue.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A conversation between two or more individuals.","e":"Bill and Melinda maintained a dialogue via email over the course of their long-distance relationship."},{"m":"In a film, the spoken parts of the script; what the characters say.","e":"The movie had great special effects, but the dialogue was bad."},{"m":"In a book, the parts that show a conversation."}]}]},"difference":{"h":"difference","i":"/ˈdɪfrən(t)s/","a":"en-us-difference.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The quality of being different.","e":"You need to learn to accept differences in people."},{"m":"(countable) A characteristic of something that makes it different from something else.","e":"There are three differences between these two pictures."},{"m":"(countable) A disagreement or argument.","e":"The people had to settle their differences before they could work together."}]}]},"dialog":{"h":"dialog","i":"/ˈdaɪælɒg/","a":"en-us-dialogue.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A conversation between two or more individuals.","e":"Bill and Melinda maintained a dialog via email over the course of their long-distance relationship."},{"m":"In a film, the spoken parts of the script; what the characters say.","e":"The movie had great special effects, but the dialog was bad."},{"m":"In a book, the parts that show a conversation."}]}]},"comfort":{"h":"comfort","i":"/ˈkʌm.fɚt/","a":"en-us-comfort.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Comfort is a feeling in your body that there are no problems.","e":"Enjoying the comfort of his own bed, he soon fell asleep."},{"m":"(uncountable) If you give comfort, you help someone to feel better.","e":"Though it is a difficult time, you can at least take comfort in the fact that you are not alone."},{"m":"(countable) A comfort is something that makes you feel good.","e":"The comforts of home are not available when you're camping."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you comfort a person or animal, you help them to feel better.","e":"Jane tried to comfort Flora by telling her about her own problems at school."}]}]},"comfortable":{"h":"comfortable","i":"/ˈkʌmf.tə.bəl/","a":"en-us-comfortable.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a piece of furniture, clothing, a room, etc. is comfortable, you feel comfortable in it (see 2.)","e":"There were a few old but comfortable chairs in the meeting area."},{"m":"If you feel comfortable, you are not hot or cold; you are relaxed, and you feel no pain or worry.","e":"The nurse put a blanket on me to make me more comfortable."}]}]},"uncomfortable":{"h":"uncomfortable","i":"/ʌnˈkʌmf.tə.bəl/","a":"en-us-uncomfortable.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a piece of furniture, clothing, a room, etc. is uncomfortable, you feel uncomfortable in it (see 2.)","e":"The chairs looked so uncomfortable that he didn't sit down."},{"m":"If you feel uncomfortable, you are hot or cold; you are not relaxed, or you feel pain or worry..","e":"I still had this uncomfortable feeling that I should know her."}]}]},"club":{"h":"club","i":"/klʌb/","a":"en-us-club.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A club is an organisation of people who share a similar sport, interest, or hobby.","e":"He was a member of his high school drama club."},{"m":"(countable) A club is a place where people go to drink, dance, talk, and listen to music.","e":"I didn't get home from the club until 2:30 in the morning; it was so much fun."},{"m":"(countable) A club is a place where members go to do sports or exercise.","e":"I try to work out at the gym club three days a week."},{"m":"(countable) A club is a heavy stick used to hit things or people.","e":"The police in London used to carry clubs instead of guns."},{"m":"(countable) A club is a suit in playing cards. It is a black design with a base and three round leaves."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you club a person or animal, you hit them with something big and heavy.","e":"They clubbed him to death with a baseball bat."},{"m":"(intransitive); (usually clubbing) If you go clubbing, you go to a club to dance, drink, and meet people.","e":"She enjoys going clubbing with friends in Oxford every Friday."}]}]},"match":{"h":"match","i":"/mætʃ/","a":"en-us-match.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A match is a game of football, tennis, etc.","e":"We lost the first match, but hope to win our next two."},{"m":"(countable) A match is something that goes with something else because they are similar.","e":"I can't find a match for this sock."},{"m":"(countable) A match is a small stick that has a chemical on one end of it. You use it to make a fire.","e":"He lit a match for some light in the dark room."},{"m":"(countable) A match is a situation in which two things go together well."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If two things match, they go together because they are similar in some way.","e":"Look around for a table you like or one which most closely matches your room."},{"m":"(transitive) If you are matched against someone, you are their opponent in a competition."}]}]},"odd":{"h":"odd","i":"/ɒd/","a":"en-us-odd.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is odd, it is not normal and usually you don't like it or don't understand it.","e":"The neighbours thought him very odd, because he would leave his doors open all night."},{"m":"The odd time, drink, problem, etc. is one that happens sometimes, but not often.","e":"I don't really drink – just the odd beer at the weekend."},{"m":"An odd sock, boot, etc. is one without its pair.","e":"The clown was wearing odd socks."},{"m":"An odd number is one that does not divide evenly by 2 (e.g., 1, 3, 5, 7, 9, etc.)","e":"Fifty-one is an odd number."},{"m":"A count of (number)-odd is just a little more than the number.","e":"I've got fifty-odd students in the class."}]}]},"comment":{"h":"comment","i":"/ˈkɒm.ɛnt/","a":"en-us-comment.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A comment is a short statement about something; usually it is an opinion.","e":"I'm afraid I can't make any comment on the case right now."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you comment on or about something, you say something about it.","e":"Commenting on the changes in Peru, the president said he would be watching the situation."}]}]},"convention":{"h":"convention","i":"/ˌkənˈvɛnʃən/","a":"en-us-convention.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A convention is a large meeting of a specific group or for a specific purpose.","e":"There's a doctor's convention in town this week and all the hotels are full."},{"m":"(countable) A convention is an international agreement the controls how countries behave.","e":"This action goes against the European Convention on Human Rights."},{"m":"A convention is a particular way of acting or a particular belief of a group of people.","e":"By convention, people in North America drive on the right hand side of the road."}]}]},"justification":{"h":"justification","i":"/ˌdʒʌstɪfɪˈkeɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-justification.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A justification is a reason given by somebody for doing something.","e":"There was no justification for continuing this war."},{"m":"(uncountable) In printing, justification is the spacing of words and letters so that the margins on the left and right are even."}]}]},"fund":{"h":"fund","i":"/fɐnd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-fund.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A fund is an amount of money kept for a specific purpose.","e":"GM cannot afford to keep paying into the company pension fund."},{"m":"(plural) An organisation's funds are the money that it has.","e":"The school is raising funds to pay for the new library."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you fund something, you give it money for its activities.","e":"The project is jointly funded by the Government of Canada and the International Red Cross."}]}]},"reliance":{"h":"reliance","i":"/rɪˈlaɪəns/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-reliance.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable); (singular) If x has a reliance on y, x needs y. {{ant|independence}","e":"North Korea's reliance on foreign aid, mainly from China, isn't likely to end soon."}]}]},"partnership":{"h":"partnership","i":"/ˈpɑːtnəʃɪp/","a":"en-au-partnership.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A partnership is two people or groups working together, especially in business.","e":"Microsoft has entered into a partnership with Apple to develop software for the Macintosh."}]}]},"howdy":{"h":"howdy","i":"/ˈhaʊdi/","a":"en-us-howdy.ogg","s":[{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"\"A greeting similar to hello. It is a shortened form of how do you do or how do you fair.","e":"When the cowboy saw Abigail, he said, \"Howdy, miss.\""}]}]},"coordination":{"h":"coordination","i":"/koʊˌɔrdɪˈneɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-coordination.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The ability of the muscles in a body to work together.","e":"Young children lack the coordination to walk or even to pick up small objects."},{"m":"(uncountable) The planning or timing of actions so that they work together.","e":"The result of opening the new building was a lack of coordination between different departments."}]}]},"pie":{"h":"pie","i":"/paɪ/","a":"en-us-pie.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A baked food that has a crust outside and a filling inside, as well as a crust on top.","e":"The family had cherry pie for dessert."}]}]},"alternative":{"h":"alternative","i":"/ɒltɜːnətiv/","a":"en-us-alternative.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"An alternative approach, way, source, etc. is not the usual one.","e":"Do you have some alternative transportation in case the car breaks down."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An alternative is something else that you can choose.","e":"We only have two alternatives: stay here or go back."}]}]},"pies":{"h":"pies","i":"/paɪz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-pies.wav","l":"pie","q":"noun"},"civilian":{"h":"civilian","i":"/sɪˈvɪliən/","a":"en-us-civilian.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A civilian is a person who is not in the country's army.","e":"Its against the law for a soldier to hurt a civilian."},{"m":"(uncountable) The general population who live in an area."}]}]},"civilians":{"h":"civilians","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"People who are not in the army","e":"Civilians are not allowed in the army camp."}]}]},"initial":{"h":"initial","i":"/ɪˈnɪʃəl/","a":"en-us-initial.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"(usually before the noun) The initial period, stages, etc. come near the beginning.","e":"They send most workers to the US after an initial training period of three months."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An initial is the first letter of a name.","e":"He found a bag with the initials D.B.R."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you initial something, you write the first letter of each of your names on it (or sometimes just your first and last name), usually to show approval.","e":"Can you initial this form here, please?"}]}]},"validity":{"h":"validity","i":"/vəˈlɪdɪti/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-validity.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The validity of a licence, ticket, document, etc. depends on whether it is official and acceptable.","e":"The validity of a passport depends on who carries it."},{"m":"(uncountable) The validity of evidence, a statement, a reason, etc. is the level to which it is true or reasonable.","e":"Due to the doubts about the validity of the evidence presented, the case cannot go forward."},{"m":"(uncountable) In testing, the validity of a test is the level to which it is tests what it is supposed to test.","e":"The validity of many IQ tests has been questioned."},{"m":"(countable) A validity is a quality of measurement that shows the degree by which the measurement reflects the thing beneath it."}]}]},"task":{"h":"task","i":"/tæsk/","a":"en-us-task.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A task is a specific piece of work, often unpleasant.","e":"Come here, young man. I have a task for you to do."},{"m":"If you take someone to task, you criticise them strongly.","e":"Father took her to task for taking the car without asking."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you task someone with doing something, you give them that job."}]}]},"technique":{"h":"technique","i":"/tɛkˈniːk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-technique.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A technique is a specialized and skillful way of doing something.","e":"It is important for pilots to be taught the right technique for the take-off run."}]}]},"exclude":{"h":"exclude","i":"/ɪksˈkluːd/","a":"en-us-exclude.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you exclude someone or something, you keep them out.","e":"During play time, she was excluded from the group."}]}]},"proportion":{"h":"proportion","i":"/prəˈpɔrʃən/","a":"en-us-proportion.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The proportion is the relationship in size between one part and another.","e":"Health care spending is taking up a much larger proportion of the government budget."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you proportion something, you divide it into equal portions."}]}]},"girl":{"h":"girl","i":"/gəːl/","a":"en-us-girl.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A girl is a female child or teenager; someone who is not a woman yet.","e":"Many girls like to play with dolls."},{"m":"(countable) A female person of any age (even a woman).","e":"The girls are going out tonight, do you want to come?"},{"m":"(countable) A female animal.","e":"My cat is a girl."}]}]},"fly":{"h":"fly","i":"/flaɪ/","a":"en-us-fly.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To move through the air without touching the ground","e":"The bird will fly away in the winter."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A fly is a type of small insect with wings.","e":"I won't eat my soup because there's a fly in it."},{"m":"In baseball a ball that goes high in the air."},{"m":"The piece of cloth hiding the zipper, buttons at the front of a pair of trousers, pants, or underpants."}]}]},"short":{"h":"short","i":"/ʃɔːt/","a":"en-us-short.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is short then there is a small distance from the bottom to the top. The opposite is tall.","e":"I can't reach the table because I'm too short."},{"m":"If something is short then there is a small distance from the one end to the other. The opposite is long.","e":"The more I use the pencil, the shorter it becomes."},{"m":"If something is short then it takes a little time.","e":"I'm going to Chengdu for a short break."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Short of (doing) sth is equal to except (doing) sth.","e":"Nothing short of help from god will save him."},{"m":"If you're running short of something, you don't have enough.","e":"We're running short of time, so can you hurry up?"},{"m":"If something is short of it's target, it isn't all the way there.","e":"The plane touched down just short of the landing area."},{"m":"If you cut something short, you end it before the planned time.","e":"They cut short their vacation when the weather changed."}]}]},"consent":{"h":"consent","i":"/kənˈsɛnt/","a":"en-us-consent.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Consent is permission to do something.","e":"You can't publish a picture of a child without the consent of one parent."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you consent to something, you agree to it.","e":"Dr. Briant has kindly consented to give us some of his valuable time."}]}]},"demonstrate":{"h":"demonstrate","i":"/ˈdɛmənstreɪt/","a":"en-us-demonstrate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you demonstrate something, you show that it is true or that it exists.","e":"In this job, you must demonstrate an ability to communicate effectively."},{"m":"(transitive) If you demonstrate something, you show how to do it or use it.","e":"At the sales meeting she demonstrated the new software."},{"m":"(intransitive) If a group of people demonstrate, they protest something publicly.","e":"The workers began demonstrating for safer conditions outside the factory."}]}]},"criteria":{"h":"criteria","i":"/kraɪˈtɪəriə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-criteria.wav","l":"criterion","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(sometimes singular) Criteria are a set of principles that you use to judge something or decide about something.","e":"One of the criteria for measuring the success of a democracy is the percentage of people that vote in that society."}]}]},"philosophy":{"h":"philosophy","i":"/fɪˈlɒsəfi/","a":"en-us-philosophy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Philosophy is the study of the nature of existence and truth: how things are and how they should be.","e":"s writings have been used to teach philosophy, logic, maths, and other subjects."},{"m":"(countable) A philosophy is a set of beliefs that guide the actions of a group or individual.","e":"Her education explains in part why she holds the political philosophies she does."}]}]},"discover":{"h":"discover","i":"/dɪsˈkʌvə/","a":"en-us-discover.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To find a new idea that was not known before, or to find a thing that was not known about before.","e":"s want to discover a cure for cancer."}]}]},"discovery":{"h":"discovery","i":"/dəsˈk͉ʌv(ə)ˌri/","a":"en-ca-discovery.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A thing or an idea that was found","e":"When made a discovery, he ran around saying \"I found it!\""}]}]},"compensation":{"h":"compensation","i":"/ˌkɒm.penˈseɪ.ʃən/","a":"en-us-compensation.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Compensation is money, or something of value, given to somebody who has lost something or been harmed.","e":"He was ordered to pay £600 compensation after being found guilty of assault."},{"m":"(uncountable); Compensation is everything that a company gives to someone for doing their job, including money, company car, stocks, etc.","e":"My compensation package at the old job was better, but I enjoy it more here."}]}]},"representative":{"h":"representative","i":"/ˌrɛprɪˈzɛnt(ət)ɪv/","a":"en-us-representative.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A representative is a person who represents a group or company.","e":"The ambassador is our representative."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"of a group.","e":"This is a representative sample."}]}]},"ring":{"h":"ring","i":"/rɪŋ/","a":"en-us-ring.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A circle.","e":"The students sat in a ring."},{"m":"A piece of metal in a circle usually worn in the ear or on the finger or toe.","e":"She wore a ring on each finger."},{"m":"A piece of material with the shape of a circle.","e":"The O-rings went bad on my truck."},{"m":"A high sound, especially of a telephone.","e":"The ring of the phone woke me up."},{"m":"The square area between four poles where people fight.","e":"He climbed into the ring, ready to fight."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To make a high sound, as a phone.","e":"The phone rang."},{"m":"To call someone.","e":"He rings me every Thursday."}]}]},"ready":{"h":"ready","i":"/ˈrɛdi/","a":"en-us-ready.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Prepared.","e":"Let's get ready to rumble!"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To prepare.","e":"Ready the car for the race."}]}]},"river":{"h":"river","i":"/ˈrɪvə/","a":"en-us-river.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A channel of water.","e":"We go swimming in the river."},{"m":"(uncountable) A lot of something.","e":"He won a river of votes."}]}]},"hard":{"h":"hard","i":"/hɑːd/","a":"en-us-hard.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is hard, it is not soft.","e":"I kicked the wall and hurt my foot. The wall is hard."},{"m":"If something is hard, it takes a lot of work to do or understand.","e":"Only two people passed the test because it was so hard."},{"m":"If something is hard, it is sudden and sharp.","e":"He took a hard hit to his arm."},{"m":"If a drink is hard, it is strong.","e":"Hard liquor"},{"m":"If something is hard, it cannot be questioned; it is not questionable.","e":"Hard evidence"},{"m":"If someone is hard, they are severe; they are unfriendly."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something is done hard, it is done with a lot of effort.","e":"He works hard, all day and all night."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hard is a beach or slope that is firm that is a good place to take a boat out of the water."}]}]},"mist":{"h":"mist","i":"/mɪst/","a":"en-us-mist.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"vapor that you can see.","e":"There was a mist over the water."}]}]},"past":{"h":"past","i":"/pɑːst/","a":"en-us-past.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A time before now.","e":"In the past, many years ago, I was a good doctor."},{"m":"Past means the past tense."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"done","e":"The harvest is past. It finished in October."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"by; beside","e":"I watched as he walked past the museum window from north to south."}]}]},"political":{"h":"political","i":"/pəˈlɪtɪkəl/","a":"en-us-political.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something is political if it is related to politics.","e":"He supports the Democratic political party."}]}]},"prison":{"h":"prison","i":"/ˈprɪzən/","a":"en-us-prison.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A place for people who break the law.","e":"Her brother is in prison."},{"m":"A place you cannot escape from.","e":"He is in a prison of his own mind."}]}]},"punishment":{"h":"punishment","i":"/ˈpʌnɪʃmənt/","a":"en-us-punishment.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A punishment is a response to bad actions; it is used to try to stop another bad action.","e":"Punishment is hard to accept."}]}]},"sand":{"h":"sand","i":"/sænd/","a":"en-us-sand.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) s of rock that make beaches and deserts.","e":"In the summer, Jane goes to the beach, lies on the sand and listens to the waves."},{"m":"(countable) A sand is a singular grain of sand."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you sand wood, you rub rough paper on it to make it smooth.","e":"I sand the wood until it is nice and smooth."}]}]},"seat":{"h":"seat","i":"/siːt/","a":"en-us-seat.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A seat is something to sit on.","e":"Pull up a seat and sit down."},{"m":"The seat is a part of the clothes covering the buttocks.","e":"The seat of your pants is muddy."},{"m":"Seat is where something is, at the centre of things.","e":"The town was the county seat, where the county council met."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To seat is to help someone sit down.","e":"Follow me. I will seat you near the stage."}]}]},"size":{"h":"size","i":"/saɪz/","a":"en-us-size.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"How big or small a thing is.","e":"These shirts come in four sizes: small, medium, large, and extra large."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To measure the size of.","e":"They sized him for a new suit. His shoulders measured 25 inches across."}]}]},"effect":{"h":"effect","i":"/ɪˈfɛkt/","a":"en-us-effect.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An effect is something that is caused by something else.","e":"His comments had a visible effect on those who heard it."},{"m":"If a law, agreement, change, etc. takes effect, it officially begins.","e":"The closing of the company takes effect at midnight."},{"m":"A sound effect is a way to make a sound for a performance artificially.","e":"The used a lot of normal materials to create the sound effects for the show."},{"m":"A special effect is a way to make an image for a performance artificially.","e":"They didn't really cut his hand off, but the special effect made it look real."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you effect a change, you make it happen.","e":"I will effect the change without your help."}]}]},"impulse":{"h":"impulse","i":"/ˈɪmpʌls/","a":"en-us-impulse.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A desire to do something.","e":"The impulse to learn led me to study day and night."},{"m":"A thrust; a push; a sudden force.","e":"Pushing an object gives it an impulse."},{"m":"The effect (integral) of force over time.","e":"The total impulse from the impact will depend on the kinetic energy of the bullet."}]}]},"graduate":{"h":"graduate","i":"/ˈgrædjueɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-graduate (verb).wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you graduate you get a degree or diploma from a school or university.","e":"Tom graduated from Yale University in 2006."},{"m":"If you graduate, you change to a new level of skill or activity.","e":"After learning to do front flips, Sally graduated to learning back flips."},{"m":"To arrange or divide into or groups"},{"m":"To divide into intervals, especially for use in measurement"}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A graduate is someone who has graduated (usually from a school or university).","e":"Tom is a graduate of Yale University."},{"m":"A graduated container, such as a cylinder or beaker."}]}]},"impartial":{"h":"impartial","i":"/ɪmˈpɑr.ʃəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-impartial.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Treating all others equally.","e":"A good teacher must be impartial."}]}]},"partial":{"h":"partial","i":"/ˈpɑrʃəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-partial.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A partial list, solution, payment etc. is just a part of the whole and not complete.","e":"The dinner was only a partial success – everyone loved the dessert, but nobody liked the soup."},{"m":"If you are partial to something, you like it.","e":"I'm rather partial to a beer or two on Friday nights."},{"m":"If you are partial, you treat people or things differently, unfairly preferring one to another.","e":"The students accused the teacher of being partial in her grading."}]}]},"shoulder":{"h":"shoulder","i":"/ˈʃəʊldə/","a":"en-us-shoulder.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The part of the body where an arm attaches or joins."},{"m":"The side of the road. It can be used to stop on in.","e":"He stopped the car on the shoulder of the highway to change the flat tire."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To push something or someone out of the way using one's shoulder.","e":"He shouldered his way in through the crowd."},{"m":"To carry some weight on one's shoulders, literally or figuratively.","e":"The task was hard, but she shouldered it as best she could."}]}]},"sequence":{"h":"sequence","i":"/ˈsikwəns/","a":"en-us-sequence.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sequence is a set of things in a specific order.","e":"The sequence of feelings is: anger followed by sadness and finally calm."},{"m":"(countable) A sequence is a part of a movie or a story.","e":"In this sequence, you'll hear him tell her what really happened."}]}]},"correspond":{"h":"correspond","i":"/ˌkɔrəˈspɑnd/","a":"en-us-correspond.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If x corresponds to y, there is a close relationship between x and y.","e":"The current situation in Sri Lanka corresponds closely to the situation in Thailand in 1982."},{"m":"(intransitive) If two people correspond, they write letters to each other.","e":"She corresponded with him for three years before they finally met in 1917."}]}]},"difficult":{"h":"difficult","i":"/ˈdɪfɪkəlt/","a":"en-uk-difficult.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is difficult, it is not easy.","e":"It'll be difficult to get him to change his mind; he's really stubborn."}]}]},"dispute":{"h":"dispute","i":"/dɪsˈpjuːt/","a":"en-us-dispute.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A dispute is an argument or disagreement which continues over a period of time. A dispute may escalate into violence, or it may be a long verbal and legal struggle.","e":"The taxi driver and the passenger had a dispute over the fee. (here the word argument might be used instead)"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To argue against something; to discuss or debate.","e":"He disputed what she said, claiming she was lying"},{"m":"To fight against; to resist."}]}]},"exception":{"h":"exception","i":"/əkˈsɛpʃən/","a":"en-us-exception.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The act of excepting or."},{"m":"(countable) Something that is taken out from others; something said to be distinct or not included.","e":"Almost every rule has its exceptions."}]}]},"explanation":{"h":"explanation","i":"/ˌɛkspləˈneɪʃən/","a":"en-us-explanation.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An explanation is the words used to tell somebody how to do something or the reason for something.","e":"The explanation was long and drawn-out."},{"m":"(countable) An explanation is the cause of something.","e":"The explanation for his bad mood was a lack of sleep."}]}]},"faith":{"h":"faith","i":"/feɪθ/","a":"en-us-faith.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Faith is the belief that something is true without proof."},{"m":"(countable) A faith is a system of religious belief.","e":"Hinduism is a faith."}]}]},"fragment":{"h":"fragment","i":"/ˈfræɡmənt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-fragment.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A portion or part of something","e":"The glass broke into hundreds of fragments."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To break or cause to be broken into pieces"}]}]},"revenge":{"h":"revenge","i":"/rəˈvɛnd͡ʒ/","a":"en-us-revenge.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Revenge is the act of hurting someone because they have hurt you."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you revenge yourself on someone, you hurt them because they have hurt you."}]}]},"comprehension":{"h":"comprehension","i":"/kɒmprɪˈhɛnʃn̩/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-comprehension.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Comprehension is the understanding of the meaning or importance of something.","e":"Reading comprehension questions are often on tests in schools."}]}]},"target":{"h":"target","i":"/ˈtɑrɡɪt/","a":"en-us-target.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A target is an area to shoot at. It is usually used for practice or to test the accuracy of a gun."},{"m":"(countable) A target is a goal or objective.","e":"We didn't hit our sales targets this week."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To target is to aim at something, usually with a gun."}]}]},"front":{"h":"front","i":"/frʌnt/","a":"en-us-front.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Opposite of back."},{"m":"The side of something that faces the direction it normally moves."},{"m":"The side of a building with the building's main entrance."},{"m":"In meteorology, the area where cold and warm air meet. When they meet it often causes rain to form."},{"m":"In military usage:"}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Located at or near the front.","e":"When leaving the house, it is important to lock the front door."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To lead a group.","e":"The singer Bono fronts the band U2."},{"m":"To give something to someone before they can pay for it.","e":"Since Tom did not have any money, Bill fronted him dinner and Tom paid him back the next day."}]}]},"maximum":{"h":"maximum","i":"/ˈmæksɪməm/","a":"en-uk-maximum.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A maximum is the largest or highest value or amount.","e":"The maximum number of people we can accept is 25."}]}]},"circumstance":{"h":"circumstance","i":"/ˈsɜːkəmst(ə)ns/","a":"en-us-circumstance.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable); (usually plural) The circumstances surrounding an action or event includes all the information that helps you understand the action or event.","e":"Though war is a terrible thing, it is necessary under certain circumstances."},{"m":"(uncountable) Circumstance is the events that affect you but that you cannot control.","e":"We hadn't planned it, but we ended up together by circumstance."}]}]},"hollow":{"h":"hollow","i":"/ˈhɒl.əʊ/","a":"en-us-hollow.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something has nothing inside of it, it is hollow.","e":"The box is hollow."},{"m":"If the inside of a tree or log has rotted away so the middle is empty, it is hollow.","e":"The rabbit ran through the hollow log."},{"m":"Lacking enthusiasm or cheer","e":"\"He let out a hollow laugh\""}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you hollow out something, you make a hole in it."}]}]},"music":{"h":"music","i":"/ˈmjuːzɪk/","a":"en-uk-music.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) s that are played on musical instruments or sung with a certain rhythm and harmony, and forming.","e":"You cannot make any music with this trumpet, it is broken."},{"m":"(uncountable) Written rules on how to play a piece of music, also called sheet music.","e":"This book has the lyrics and the music to many children songs."},{"m":"(uncountable) Anything that sounds nice or interesting.","e":"The music of the wind reached his ear."}]}]},"considerable":{"h":"considerable","i":"/kənˈsɪdərəbl/","a":"en-us-considerable.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A considerable amount, time, degree, etc. is a fairly large or important one.","e":"He had given it a considerable amount of thought before deciding."}]}]},"corporate":{"h":"corporate","i":"/ˈkɔr.pər.ət/","a":"en-uk-corporate.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Corporate finance, planning, management, etc. is related to business or a company.","e":"We have accounts for both individual and corporate clients."}]}]},"corporation":{"h":"corporation","i":"/'kɔːpoˈreɪʃn/","a":"en-us-corporation.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A corporation is a large company or a group of companies that work together.","e":"The Canadian Broadcasting Corporation is Canada's national radio and TV broadcaster."}]}]},"interaction":{"h":"interaction","i":"/ˌɪntərˈækʃən/","a":"en-us-interaction.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An interaction is when two or more things affect each other or work together.","e":"Poor health can harm older people's participation in everyday life and social interaction."}]}]},"contribution":{"h":"contribution","i":"/ˌkɑntrɪˈbjuʃən/","a":"en-us-contribution.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A contribution is something that you give or add.","e":"Technology to reduce pollution could make a significant contribution to the solution."},{"m":"The money you give to someone, especially for a donation, is your contribution."},{"m":"The amount of work you did on a project.","e":"His contribution was very low. He did almost nothing."}]}]},"immigration":{"h":"immigration","i":"/ˌɪmɪˈɡreɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-immigration.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Immigration is the movement of people or animals into an area, usually a country.","e":"Immigration from the Caribbean makes up only 2 per cent of all immigrants."}]}]},"component":{"h":"component","i":"/kʌmˈpoʊnənt/","a":"en-us-component.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A component is one part that connects to other parts.","e":"Some components may be cleaned by methods different to those used on the main body."}]}]},"constraint":{"h":"constraint","i":"/kənˈstreɪnt/","a":"en-au-constraint.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A constraint is a limit.","e":"Perhaps the main constraint is lack of money."}]}]},"emphasis":{"h":"emphasis","i":"/'ɛmfəsɪs/","a":"en-us-emphasis.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Emphasis is the giving of particular attention or importance to something.","e":"Microsoft has placed great emphasis on its Windows software programme."}]}]},"scheme":{"h":"scheme","i":"/skiːm/","a":"en-us-scheme.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A scheme is a plan, sometimes a bad or dishonest one.","e":"The new training scheme will be targeted at recent graduates."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you scheme against someone, you make an evil plan against someone."}]}]},"layer":{"h":"layer","i":"/leɪə/","a":"en-us-layer.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A layer is a covering material or substance.","e":"When we got up in the morning, everything was covered by a thin layer of snow."},{"m":"(countable) A layer is a level in an organisation.","e":"The company is trying to reduce the number of management layers."},{"m":"(countable) A layer is a person who lays something, (e.g., carpet, bricks, etc.)."},{"m":"(countable) A layer is a chicken kept to lay eggs."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you layer something, you make layers.","e":"Layer the pasta in an ovenproof dish with the tomatoes, bacon and peas, seasoning each layer."}]}]},"volume":{"h":"volume","i":"/vɒljuːm/","a":"en-us-volume.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The volume of sound or music is how loud it is.","e":"Teens listening to their MP3 players at high volume can damage their hearing."},{"m":"The volume of something is the amount of it.","e":"The traffic volume on Ontario highways jumped 12% last year."},{"m":"(countable) The volume of a material or a container is the amount of space it takes.","e":"The volume of water of a typical shower is about 43 litres."},{"m":"(countable) A volume is a book, magazine, or other printed material, usually part of a series.","e":"He has published a second volume of autobiography, in which he deals with his years as a student."}]}]},"document":{"h":"document","i":"/ˈdɒkjʊmənt/","a":"en-us-document.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A document is a written record, often official.","e":"They stopped her at the airport and checked all her documents."},{"m":"(countable) A document is a kind of computer text file.","e":"Can you send me that document by e-mail or fax?"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you document something, you make a record of it, usually in writing.","e":"It's important for newspaper reporters to be there to document the war."}]}]},"register":{"h":"register","i":"/ˈrɛdʒ.ɪs.tə/","a":"en-us-register.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you register someone or something, you put their name on a list.","e":"I haven't registered for September classes yet."},{"m":"(transitive) If you register a complaint, protest, etc. you make your opinion known formally."},{"m":"If something doesn't register, you don't notice it.","e":"I knew I had something else on, but I guess it just didn't register when I made the appointment."},{"m":"If a instrument registers a value, it shows that value.","e":"The thermometer registered 42.5°."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A register is an official list of names.","e":"On voting day, I found my name was not on the register and I couldn't vote."},{"m":"A register is a particular style of language used by a certain group of people or in certain situations.","e":"Speeches are usually given in a very formal, almost written register."},{"m":"(countable) A register is a particular range of notes.","e":"The piano plays arpeggi in higher registers, accompanying the clarinet that plays the melody in full-blooded lower middle registers."},{"m":"(countable) A cash register is a machine in a shop that calculates total payment and holds money."}]}]},"core":{"h":"core","i":"/kɔː/","a":"en-us-core.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The core is the centre part of something.","e":"I bit into the apple core and spit out the seeds."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you core something, you remove the centre from it.","e":"lemon juice • 4 eating apples, peeled, halved and cored • 1 tbsp of..."}]}]},"proof":{"h":"proof","i":"/pruːf/","a":"en-us-proof.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Proof is evidence which shows something is correct.","e":"He has proof that he was not at the crime scene. A witness says that they were somewhere else."},{"m":"A proof can show how a theorem is correct."}]}]},"cookie":{"h":"cookie","i":"/ˈkʊki/","a":"en-au-cookie.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cookie is a small baked cake. It is usually round and flat. Cookies are sweet.","e":"When I want to have something sweet, I'll usually eat a cookie."},{"m":"(countable) A cookie is data that is put on and read from your computer by a website.","e":"The website stored a cookie on my computer so I could keep playing my game from where I stopped."}]}]},"salt":{"h":"salt","i":"/sɑlt/","a":"en-us-salt.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Salt is a strong- white powder used to improve the flavor of food or to preserve it. Salt is made from sodium and chlorine (chemical formula: NaCl).","e":"I added salt to my food."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you salt something, you add salt to it.","e":"Please help me salt the fish for tonight's dinner."}]}]},"chin":{"h":"chin","i":"/tʃɪn/","a":"en-us-chin.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The chin is the lowest part of the face. It is the point of the jaw and the part of the face where beards grow.","e":"My chin is below my mouth."}]}]},"digestion":{"h":"digestion","i":"/daɪˈdʒɛstʃən/","a":"en-us-digestion.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Digestion is what happens to food once it is eaten. It changes the food into substances your body can use.","e":"Eating fruits and vegetables is good for your digestion."}]}]},"glass":{"h":"glass","i":"/ɡlɑːs/","a":"en-us-glass.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Glass is a transparent solid and is usually clear. Windows and eyeglasses are made from it, as well as drinking glasses.","e":"Through the window glass I could see the trees bend in the wind, but I was warm indoors."},{"m":"(countable) A glass is a drinking cup with no handle.","e":"As soon as I finished drinking, he filled up my glass again."}]}]},"overall":{"h":"overall","i":"/ˈəʊvərɔːl/","a":"en-us-overall.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"An overall effect, strategy, picture, etc., is one that covers everything but may not go into detail.","e":"The play has many Christian elements, but the overall effect is not necessarily Christian."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If you look at something overall, you look at the whole of it.","e":"Despite losing a few games, the team achieved greater successes overall than in previous years."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An overall is a large, loose protective coat."},{"m":"Overalls are pants with a front that comes up to your chest and straps over your shoulders."},{"m":"Overalls are a loose protective trouser and shirt in one."}]}]},"emerge":{"h":"emerge","i":"/iˈmɝd͡ʒ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-emerge.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you emerge, you come out of something.","e":"Black, who was wanted by police, emerged from hiding yesterday."},{"m":"(intransitive) If a pattern or picture emerges, it becomes clear.","e":"It was only many months afterwards that a complete picture began to emerge of what had happened."}]}]},"regime":{"h":"regime","i":"/rəˈʒiːm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-regime1.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A regime is a government, especially a bad or illegal one.","e":"Washington ended rule by the Taliban and established a new client regime in Afghanistan."},{"m":"(countable) A regime is a plan or system.","e":"Under Labour's new tax regime, families will be worse off."}]}]},"hence":{"h":"hence","i":"/ˈhɛns/","a":"en-us-hence.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"for this reason","e":"You are the government and hence have responsibility for this mess."},{"m":"from now","e":"We shall meet again two months hence."}]}]},"implementation":{"h":"implementation","i":"/ˌɪmpləmɛnˈteɪʃən/","a":"en-us-implementation.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Implementation is the process or result of putting a plan into action.","e":"Full implementation of the debt relief plans would remove up to US$6 billion from outstanding debt."}]}]},"implement":{"h":"implement","i":"/ˌɪmpləmˈent/","a":"en-us-implement.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you implement a plan, you put it into action; you do it.","e":"To reduce poverty, it is essential for the government to fully implement the new education policy."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An implement is a tool, usually a hand tool (e.g., a shovel).","e":"The garage held all sorts of items – lamps, bicycle frames, farm and garden implements and dozens of other things."}]}]},"rule":{"h":"rule","i":"/ruːl/","a":"en-us-rule.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A rule is a statement that tells whether you might get spanked for master baiting in class. If something is right or wrong.","e":"Peter picked up the football, which was against the rules, so the other team got a throw-in."},{"m":"A king's rule is the time he controls the country.","e":"The next king had a very short rule: only two years."},{"m":"(countable) A rule is another name for a ruler, a measuring device."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When someone rules, he or she is in charge, like a king or queen.","e":"The king has ruled for 33 years."}]}]},"light":{"h":"light","i":"/laɪt/","a":"en-us-light.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The energy that our eyes sense is light.","e":"And dance by the light of the moon.—Buffalo Gals, American folksong"},{"m":"(countable) If someone talks about a light, he or she means something bright that can be seen.","e":"The lights of the city shine all over the valley."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is light in color is close to white.","e":"The morning sky was very light."},{"m":"Something that is light in weight does not weigh much.","e":"I lifted her easily because she was so light."},{"m":"Light may also mean that something is not serious.","e":"The light bruise on my leg didn't hurt much."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If someone lights a fire, the fire starts to burn.","e":"Let's light the wood in the fireplace."},{"m":"(transitive) Something that lights a place makes it less dark.","e":"The moon lighted the forest path."}]}]},"wife":{"h":"wife","i":"/waɪf/","a":"en-us-wife.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A woman.","e":"Bill just married his second wife."}]}]},"village":{"h":"village","i":"/ˈvɪlədʒ/","a":"en-us-village.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A village is a very small town.","e":"He lives in a village in the middle of nowhere."}]}]},"ever":{"h":"ever","i":"/ˈɛvə/","a":"en-us-ever.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If I ask you if you have ever been to France, I am asking if you have been to France at any time in your life.","e":"Have you ever met a king or queen?"},{"m":"Ever may also mean always.","e":"I will love you forever and ever."}]}]},"example":{"h":"example","i":"/ɪɡˈzɑːmpl̩/","a":"en-us-example.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"If you give an example of something, you name one of that type of thing.","e":"A baseball, a softball, a football, and a soccer ball are examples of balls."},{"m":"An example is a model of what something else of the same type should be like.","e":"Look at the example of a model airplane to see how your model airplane should be built."}]}]},"experience":{"h":"experience","i":"/ɪkˈspɪə.ri.ens/","a":"en-us-experience.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An experience is an event that happens to you or that you are a part of.","e":"The spelling bee was a horrible experience."},{"m":"(uncountable) Experience is the amount of time you have been doing something (especially, a job).","e":"He has ten years of experience in law."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If I experience something, it happens to me or I am involved in it.","e":"We are experiencing technical."}]}]},"off":{"h":"off","i":"/ɒf/","a":"en-us-off.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Away from somewhere or some time.","e":"I got ready and by 7:00 I was off to school."},{"m":"If something is off it is not on.","e":"He pushed the book off the table, and it fell to the floor."},{"m":"Out of a vehicle such as a train, bus, etc.","e":"As the train stopped, he jumped off and ran to her."},{"m":"If something that uses energy is off, it is not working.","e":"It was dark in the room because the light was off."},{"m":"If you are off, you do not have to go to work or to school.","e":"I work evenings, but I have my afternoons off."},{"m":"made smaller by a certain amount","e":"They've taken 30% off the price."},{"m":"If a plan, event, etc. is off, it will not happen.","e":"Tonight's game is off because of the rain."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If you're off something, you don't like or want something you wanted before.","e":"That article really put me off meat."},{"m":"If you're off some medicine, you are not using it any more.","e":"He's been off the pain killers for a few weeks."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If food is off, it is not good to eat anymore.","e":"The meat smells off."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If a person offs someone, they kill him or her.","e":"I heard they offed Jimmy by drowning."}]}]},"office":{"h":"office","i":"/ˈɒfɪs/","a":"en-us-office.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An office is a room or building where people sit at desks and work.","e":"Her office is in the third door on the left side of the hall."},{"m":"A position held by public election is an office.","e":"They both decided to run for office."}]}]},"out":{"h":"out","i":"/aʊt/","a":"en-ca-out.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Something that is out is not in.","e":"Polly opened the door and went out."},{"m":"If something using electricity is out, it is turned off or the electricity is not flowing..","e":"Turn the light out before you leave."},{"m":"Something that moves out moves from the inside to a place that is not inside.","e":"He took the pen out of his pocket."},{"m":"far away","e":"We live out in the country."},{"m":"If someone is out, they are not in the place where someone is looking for them.","e":"You can't see the doctor now. He is out."},{"m":"to a number of people","e":"We'll give out the books after everyone has arrived."},{"m":"away","e":"Don't throw that out. I'm still using it."},{"m":"If something is out, you can look at or see it.","e":"the sun is out"},{"m":"If something comes out of something, it comes from it."},{"m":"If something is out, it is available for sale."},{"m":"If something is out, it is not in fashion."},{"m":"If someone is out, they are not conscious."},{"m":"If a you are out of something, you had it before but you've used or sold all of it."},{"m":"If x is made out of y, y is the material that x is made of."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you out somebody, you make public something they don't want others to know, especially that they are homosexual.","e":"The media recently outed a conservative politician."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"If someone is prevented from scoring in baseball, they make an out.","e":"There were two men on base and two outs."},{"m":"A way to escape is an out."}]}]},"make":{"h":"make","i":"/ˈmeɪk/","a":"en-us-make.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you make something, you create it.","e":"He made pancakes by combining the ingredients and frying the mixture."},{"m":"If you make your bed, you arrange it.","e":"Félix makes his bed every morning."}]}]},"ass":{"h":"ass","i":"/æs/","a":"en-us-ass.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Ass is an old word for donkey.","e":"Ox and ass before Him bow/And He is in the manger now...."},{"m":"; Ass is another word for butt, referring to the buttocks or anus.","e":"That girl has a nice ass."},{"m":"If you call someone an ass, you are insulting him/her by comparing him/her to buttocks. Usually meaning that he/she is rude.","e":"My boss is really mean. He is a real ass."},{"m":"(taboo) Ass is an extremely rude word for sexual intercourse."},{"m":"An ass is a woman regarded as a sex object."}]}]},"whale":{"h":"whale","i":"/weɪl/","a":"en-us-whale.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A whale is a large animal that lives in the ocean.","e":"Some whales with teeth eat fish, but many whales don't have teeth."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you whale, you hunt for whales."},{"m":"(transitive) If you whale on something, you beat it hard repeatedly."}]}]},"cotton":{"h":"cotton","i":"/ˈkɑt.n̩/","a":"en-us-cotton.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Cotton is a plant that produces a soft fiber also called cotton. This fiber is used to make fabric.","e":"My shirt is made of cotton."}]}]},"project":{"h":"project","i":"/ˈprɑdʒεk̚t/","a":"en-ca-project-noun.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A project is a complex job or assignment, often involving research or construction.","e":"Shell is also working on projects to help find training and work experience for some of Brazil's 13 million street children."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you project, you plan for or estimate something in the future.","e":"We have projected the loss of income forward for five years."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something projects out or beyond something else, it stands out.","e":"During flight, the legs of this bird project beyond the tail."},{"m":"(transitive) If you project an image somewhere, you use light to make it appear there.","e":"During the presentation, she projected various graphs on the screen behind her."},{"m":"(transitive) If you project an image, you try to give people a particular feeling about something.","e":"The program will project a modern image of workers."}]}]},"occupational":{"h":"occupational","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"About or by your job","e":"Their income is: state pension £83.25 occupational pension £45.20 Total £128.45."}]}]},"occupation":{"h":"occupation","i":"/ɑkjʊˈpeɪʃən/","a":"en-us-occupation.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An occupation is a job or a career.","e":"Nursing has been described as a skilled occupation rather than a profession."},{"m":"An occupation is when a people, especially an army, take over and stay in a country, area, building, etc.","e":"Everything he owned was taken during the German occupation of Paris in 1940."},{"m":"(countable) An occupation is a hobby or something else that you do to pass the time.","e":"Her favorite occupation is reading."}]}]},"civil":{"h":"civil","i":"/ˈsɪvəl/","a":"en-us-civil.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"About the citizens of a country, especially as opposed to the government, army, police, religion, etc.","e":"One of the most important civil rights is freedom of speech."},{"m":"If someone is civil, they are polite but not friendly.","e":"Mum had been civil to me since the fight but something had gone between us."}]}]},"status":{"h":"status","i":"/ˈsteɪtəs/","a":"en-us-status.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Your status is your level, role, or situation in a group or society.","e":"Mike Hooper has retained his status as Liverpool's current No 1 goalkeeper."},{"m":"The status of something is its situation at a particular time.","e":"What is the status of the repairs?"}]}]},"goal":{"h":"goal","i":"/ɡoʊl/","a":"en-us-goal.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A goal is something you want to do or be able to do.","e":"I want to go to university and this will help me achieve that goal."},{"m":"A goal is a place that you want to be or that you are moving towards.","e":"Our goal is Paris."},{"m":"A goal is the area where you want to put the ball in certain games such as soccer or hockey.","e":"It's unclear whether the regular keeper will start in goal."},{"m":"A goal is scored when the ball enters the goal.","e":"They beat second-placed Cambridge 2-1 with Mutch scoring the winning goal in the 82nd minute."}]}]},"hypothesis":{"h":"hypothesis","i":"/haɪˈpɒθɪsɪs/","a":"en-us-hypothesis.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hypothesis is a guess about what will happen, usually in scientific experiments.","e":"We will test the hypothesis that the change will have no effect."},{"m":"(uncountable) A guess with no evidence to support it.","e":"This idea is purely a hypothesis. It has not been proven"}]}]},"professional":{"h":"professional","i":"/prəˈfɛʃənəl/","a":"en-us-professional.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"About a job such as doctor, lawyer, accountant, etc.","e":"The group offers free professional advice on legal matters and housing."},{"m":"If someone is professional, they do their job seriously and with much skill.","e":"We employ friendly, professional staff who can offer the benefit of many years' experience."},{"m":"If someone is professional, they are paid for their job, sport, art, etc.","e":"After playing amateur tennis for years, he turned professional at the age of 25."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A professional is a person who is paid for doing their job, sport, art, etc.","e":"More and more the Olympics are allowing professionals to compete."},{"m":"(countable) A professional is a person who does a job such as doctor, lawyer, accountant, etc.","e":"Professionals often spend years and hundreds of thousands of dollars in school."},{"m":"(countable) A professional is a person who is serious and skilled in their work.","e":"You should get him to fix your car. He's a real professional."}]}]},"series":{"h":"series","a":"en-us-series.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (singular) A series of events, meetings, experiments, etc. is several of them that happen one after the other and are related.","e":"Three weeks ago troops and helicopters launched a series of attacks on Kurds in the region."},{"m":"A TV or Radio series is a number of programs usually with the same setting and characters."},{"m":"A series is a sporting event in which many teams compete for a championship.","e":"Tonight is the final game of the Stanley Cup series."},{"m":"If something is connected in series, electricity passes through each point before going to the next point."}]}]},"internal":{"h":"internal","i":"/ɪnˈtɜː.nəl/","a":"en-us-internal.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"within or inside","e":"Doctors had to operate to stop the internal bleeding."}]}]},"retain":{"h":"retain","i":"/rɪˈteɪn/","a":"en-us-retain.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you retain something, you keep it.","e":"After the election, the government retained control of the lower house, but lost the upper house."},{"m":"(transitive) If you retain someone (usually a professional), you pay them to do a job.","e":"Since being charged by police, Black has retained a lawyer."}]}]},"sum":{"h":"sum","i":"/sʌm/","a":"en-us-sum.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sum is an amount of money, usually a large amount.","e":"The company had been spending large sums on publicity and advertising."},{"m":"The sum is the total of adding or subtracting several numbers or amounts.","e":"The total output doesn't equal the sum of the inputs because the system is not 100% efficient."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you sum up, you conclude or bring together the main points.","e":"She sums up the situation by saying that the new family is never the same as the biological family."}]}]},"mechanism":{"h":"mechanism","i":"/ˈmɛkənɪzm/","a":"en-us-mechanism.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A mechanism is the way something works","e":"This research should help us to understand the mechanisms of memory."},{"m":"A mechanism is one moving system within a larger, more complex machine or organism.","e":"The body has a control mechanism to bring down blood-sugar level when it begins to reach unhealthy peaks."}]}]},"impose":{"h":"impose","i":"/ɪmˈpoʊz/","a":"en-us-impose.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you impose something on someone, you force it on them, even if they don't want it.","e":"Egypt has imposed travel restrictions which will make it harder to enter the country."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you impose on someone, you ask or expect them to do something for you that is difficult or inconvenient.","e":"Could we impose on you to explain that again more slowly?"}]}]},"despite":{"h":"despite","i":"/dɪˈspaɪt/","a":"en-us-despite.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If x happens despite y, it is surprising that x happens because y usually stops it.","e":"Despite their best efforts, the ministers have not been able to come to an agreement."},{"m":"If you do something despite yourself, you didn't plan or want to do it.","e":"She hated him, but when he spoke she laughed despite herself."}]}]},"parameter":{"h":"parameter","i":"/pəˈræm.ɪ.tə/","a":"en-us-parameter.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (usually plural) A parameter is a boundary or a limit.","e":"The machine should run only within operational parameters; temperature, water flow, etc."}]}]},"approximate":{"h":"approximate","i":"/ʌˈprɑks.ə.mɪt/","a":"en-us-approximate-adj.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"An approximate number, length, time, etc. is close to the real one but may not be equal to it.","e":"\"How many people are on the team?\" \"I'm not sure, but I can give you an approximate number.\""}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"be or become near a value, position, or characteristic.","e":"Computers are getting better at approximating human speech."}]}]},"principal":{"h":"principal","i":"/ˈprɪnsɪpəl/","a":"en-us-principal.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"The principal thing is the main or most important one.","e":"Canada's principal trading partner is the USA."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) In American English, a principal is the head of a school. (headmaster in British English)"},{"m":"(countable) The principal is the most important person in a business, or an artistic group such as a dancers."},{"m":"(uncountable) Principal is the money that you borrow and must pay back. It does not include interest."}]}]},"float":{"h":"float","i":"/floʊt/","a":"en-us-float.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Something which stays on or near the surface of water or another liquid."},{"m":"(countable) A buoyant used to help balance in water or another liquid.","e":"Attach the float and the weight to the fishing line, above the hook."},{"m":"(countable) A nicely decorated vehicle, to show in a parade or pageant.","e":"That float covered in roses is very pretty."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) When you float, it means that your density is lower than the density of the liquid you are in, which makes you be at the surface of the liquid.","e":"As I have a light body, I always float when I go swimming."}]}]},"predict":{"h":"predict","i":"/prɪˈdɪkt/","a":"en-us-predict.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you predict something, you say that it will happen before anyone observes it.","e":"It is still difficult to accurately predict the weather more than two days in advance."}]}]},"summary":{"h":"summary","a":"en-us-summary.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A summary is a short explanation of a longer idea, article, story, etc.","e":"In this short time, I can provide only a summary of the work we have done."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"done quickly and without following standard procedures"},{"m":"brief, and short; without details"}]}]},"undertake":{"h":"undertake","i":"/ʌndə'teɪk/","a":"en-us-undertake.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) (formal) If you undertake something, you take responsibility for doing it and you start to do it.","e":"He is in charge of this project and has undertaken this work largely single-handed since July."}]}]},"cycle":{"h":"cycle","i":"/ˈsaɪkəl/","a":"en-us-cycle.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cycle is a number of regular things that happen again and again.","e":"Right now we are in an upward-moving part of the business cycle."},{"m":"(countable) A cycle is a short way of saying bicycle or motorcycle."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you cycle somewhere, you go there by bicycle or motorcycle.","e":"The rain was falling harder than ever as I cycled home down the Banbury Road."},{"m":"(transitive) If you cycle a machine, you run it through one cycle.","e":"The test will cycle the computer through ten start ups."}]}]},"conference":{"h":"conference","i":"/ˈkɒnfərəns/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-conference.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A conference is a large organised meeting to discuss a particular topic or area.","e":"FMBRA will be holding a conference on diet, health, and the food industry on 19 March in Barcelona."},{"m":"(countable) A conference is a meeting.","e":"Contact the teacher or coach and ask for a private conference without your child's presence."}]}]},"attribute":{"h":"attribute","i":"/æˈtrɪbjuːt/","a":"en-us-attribute-noun.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you attribute x to y, you say that x is the creation or result of y.","e":"He attributes his success to the love of his parents."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An attribute is a part, feature, or characteristic.","e":"A good sense of humour is an essential attribute for a doctor to have."}]}]},"annual":{"h":"annual","i":"/ˈæn.ju.əl/","a":"en-us-annual.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is annual, it happens every year.","e":"The 1992 Annual General Meeting was held at Bristol University, on Saturday April 11 and Sunday April 12."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An annual is a kind of plant that only lives for one year."}]}]},"obvious":{"h":"obvious","i":"/ɒbviːəs/","a":"en-us-obvious.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is obvious, it is easy to see it, think of it, or understand it.","e":"It is obvious that you can't spend a lot of money and save at the same time."}]}]},"implication":{"h":"implication","i":"/ˌɪmpləˈkeɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-implication.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An implication is a result that may be expected or predicted.","e":"This change has big implications for health planners and for those caring for people with AIDS."},{"m":"An implication is a meaning that can be understood but is not given directly.","e":"Even if you did not call me a liar, the implication is there."},{"m":"An implication is when somebody appears to be involved in something, usually something bad or illegal.","e":"The implication of Judge Lyman in the affair of Green and young Hammond has raised many questions."}]}]},"apparent":{"h":"apparent","i":"/əˈpær.ənt/","a":"en-us-apparent.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is apparent, it is easy to see, realise or understand.","e":"When she was nine, for no apparent reason, she began to dislike the classes."},{"m":"appearing or seeming to be a certain way.","e":"The difference was more apparent than real."}]}]},"commitment":{"h":"commitment","i":"/kəˈmɪtmənt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-commitment.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A commitment is a formal promise or agreement.","e":"Actually I can't come on Saturday, I have family commitments."}]}]},"subsequent":{"h":"subsequent","i":"/ˈsʌbsɪkwənt/","a":"en-us-subsequent.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"happening after sth else.","e":"When he came the first time, he was very quiet, but on subsequent visits, he was much more talkative."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If x is subsequent to y, x happens after y.","e":"The government called a press conference subsequent to the agreement."}]}]},"vertical":{"h":"vertical","i":"/ˈvɜːtɪkəl/","a":"en-us-vertical.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A line that is upright is called a vertical.","e":"Please draw a vertical that intersects the circle."},{"m":"The fully upright position is the vertical.","e":"The builder used a string to make sure the frame was on the vertical."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is standing straight is vertical. In a vertical direction means straight up or down.","e":"The radio mast was vertical on the horizon."}]}]},"debate":{"h":"debate","i":"/dɪˈbeɪt/","a":"en-us-debate.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A debate is an exchange of ideas looking at different sides of an issue.","e":"We will explore this idea through an analysis of the public debate on marriage and divorce."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you debate something, you consider its positive and negative points, often by talking with other people in a formal situation such as government.","e":"The AHA had in fact been debating the issue of the future of the hospital for some years."}]}]},"dimension":{"h":"dimension","i":"/daɪˈmɛnʃən/","a":"en-us-dimension.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A dimension is a part of a problem, issue, or situation.","e":"We need to consider some of the dimensions of the likely future needs for health care among older people."},{"m":"(countable) A dimension is a direction of measurement in space time, usually width, depth, and height.","e":"The new viewer lets you examine the image in three dimensions."}]}]},"promote":{"h":"promote","i":"/prəˈmoʊt/","a":"en-us-promote.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you promote someone or something, you help it to get bigger, higher, or more popular.","e":"The environment provided by the school promotes the reading development of all students."}]}]},"output":{"h":"output","i":"/ˈaʊtpʊt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-output.wav","l":"output","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Output is what is produced by a worker, machine, computer, etc.","e":"We have increased our total output from 4,500 to 7,500 barrels per day of oil."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you output something, you produce it."}]}]},"live":{"h":"live","i":"/lɪv/","a":"en-us-live-verb.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) To be alive; to have life.","e":"He's not expected to live for more than a few months."},{"m":"(intransitive) To have permanent residence somewhere.","e":"I live at 256 Oak Avenue."},{"m":"(intransitive) To survive, to continue.","e":"Her memory lives in that song."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Having life; something alive.","e":"The post office will not ship live animals."},{"m":"A live firearm or explosive is able to cause harm.","e":"The air force practices dropping live bombs on the uninhabited island."},{"m":"(circuitry) d or energized with electricity, usually meaning that the item can cause an electric shock or electrocution if someone comes in contact with it.","e":"Use caution when working near live wires."},{"m":"(poker) A live bet is a bet that can be raised by the person betting.","e":"Tommy's blind was live, so he was given the option to raise."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"A live event is an event that happens in real time; direct.","e":"The concert was broadcast live by radio."}]}]},"result":{"h":"result","i":"/rɪˈzʌlt/","a":"en-us-result.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The solution of a mathematical equation.","e":"The result of 1 + 1 is 2."},{"m":"The situation at the end of a process, its outcome.","e":"The result of losing the presents was that everyone was sad."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If x results in y, it leads to or causes y.","e":"A lot of digging results in a deep hole."},{"m":"If x results from y, it comes for or is caused by y.","e":"A deep hole resulted from all the digging."}]}]},"road":{"h":"road","i":"/rəʊd/","a":"en-uk-a road.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A long and narrow piece of land between two places. Usually, cars drive on it, and it is often paved.","e":"The taxi is parked on the side of the road."},{"m":"The path which one takes to reach a certain place.","e":"It is a long road to the top."}]}]},"access":{"h":"access","i":"/ˈæk.sɛs/","a":"en-us-access.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"If you have access to something, you can use it, look at it, enter it, etc.","e":"As a student, you have access to all our facilities including the library and computers."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you access something, you get information from it, usually using a computer.","e":"The product enables multiple systems to access a single database."}]}]},"boyfriend":{"h":"boyfriend","i":"/ˈbɔɪˌfrɛnd/","a":"en-us-boyfriend.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Boyfriend normally describes a boy or a young man, who is in a love relationship with another person, when they aren't married yet.","e":"I didn't have a boyfriend, and I thought that it was because I was too fat."},{"m":"(countable) Boyfriend can also simply mean a friend who is male."}]}]},"code":{"h":"code","i":"/kəʊd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-code.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A code is a set of rules or laws.","e":"Children usually learn their parents' moral code."},{"m":"A code is a way of or sending information, often secretly or in a way that is readable by computers.","e":"Microsoft has also licensed Windows source code to companies such as Citrix Systems."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something is coded, it is written or stored in a code.","e":"The completed questionnaires were coded by two people."}]}]},"girlfriend":{"h":"girlfriend","i":"/ˈɡɝlfrɛnd/","a":"en-us-girlfriend.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A girlfriend is a girl or young woman who is in a romantic relationship with another person.","e":"Jeremy had been having trouble with his girlfriend."},{"m":"(countable) A girlfriend can be any friend who is female."}]}]},"phase":{"h":"phase","i":"/feɪz/","a":"en-us-phase.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A phase is stage in a process.","e":"We will look at very basic ideas during the first phase of training."},{"m":"(uncountable) If things are in phase, they are working, moving, or changing together."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you phase something in, you introduce it step by step.","e":"Over the next few years, all farm support was slowly phased out."}]}]},"prior":{"h":"prior","i":"/ˈpraɪ.ə/","a":"en-us-prior.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If something happens prior to something else, it happens before it.","e":"In this recipe, most of the work is actually done prior to cooking."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"occurring before","e":"We learned that police had prior knowledge of the attack."}]}]},"granted":{"h":"granted","a":"en-us-granted.ogg","l":"grant","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"You use granted to say that you accept that something is true, often before you adding contrasting information.","e":"He's a good student and usually does well. Granted, he did fail that one test, but I think there were good reasons for that."},{"m":"You use granted that x, y to mean y is true because of x.","e":"Granted that he has done nothing wrong, he should be set free."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you take something for granted, you believe it without really knowing or thinking about it."}]}]},"stress":{"h":"stress","i":"/strɛs/","a":"en-us-stress.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Stress is emotional pressure that makes you worry because things are not going well.","e":"Death is a time of great stress for family and friends."},{"m":"Stress is physical pressure that gradually can cause things to break","e":"Sitting puts an unnatural stress on the back and shortens the neck."},{"m":"(uncountable) Stress is extra attention or importance that you put on something.","e":"Psychology has put a lot of stress on the childhood roots of adult problems."},{"m":"Stress is extra loudness that you use in a word or in music.","e":"Put more stress on the first syllable of the word."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you stress something, you say that it is very important.","e":"I have repeatedly stressed the importance of hard work, but luck is also helpful."},{"m":"(transitive) If you stress a word, part of a word, or a note in music, you make it louder than other words or notes."}]}]},"resolution":{"h":"resolution","i":"/ˌrɛzəˈluːʃ(ə)n/","a":"en-us-resolution.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A resolution is a formal decision, often after a vote.","e":"The U.S. may be willing to support a Security Council resolution backing the return of inspectors to Iraq."},{"m":"(uncountable) Resolution is the amount of detail that you can see in an image.","e":"This camera is cheaper, but, of course, the resolution is much lower."},{"m":"(countable) A resolution is a solution to a disagreement or difficult situation.","e":"The school holds classes in nonviolent conflict resolution."},{"m":"(countable) A resolution is a personal decision (not) to do something.","e":"My New Year's resolution was to quit smoking."},{"m":"(uncountable) Resolution is the power to try even when things are difficult.","e":"Her resolution to be honest never weakened."}]}]},"adequate":{"h":"adequate","i":"/ˈæ.də.kwɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-adequate1.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is adequate, it is good enough.","e":"It is very hard to provide a simple but adequate explanation."}]}]},"tot":{"h":"tot","a":"en-us-tot.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A tot is a very young or small child."}]}]},"total":{"h":"total","i":"/ˈtəʊ.təl/","a":"en-us-total.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A total is the final amount of something. It is a term used in math."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you total something, you add them up."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something totals something, it adds up to that; it amounts to.","e":"The total of your purchase comes to $53."},{"m":"(transitive) (US) If you total something, you destroy it; you wreck it."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is total, it is complete; it is finished.","e":"He is a total failure"},{"m":"If something is total, it is entire.","e":"The total book was very bad."}]}]},"whole":{"h":"whole","i":"/həʊl/","a":"en-us-whole.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Whole is used to describe every part of an object.","e":"I ate the whole meal, leaving nothing left."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The whole of something means the entire part of it.","e":"The whole of the Middle East is pretty messy at the moment."}]}]},"half":{"h":"half","i":"/hɑːf/","a":"en-us-half.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A half is 1/2 of a whole; 50%.","e":"Sales were down from January to June but jumped in the second half of the year."},{"m":"(countable) A half is one part of a game that is divided into two parts.","e":"At the end of the first half, Japan is leading Iran by two points."},{"m":"(countable) A half is one end of a sports field.","e":"He kicked the ball deep into New England's half."},{"m":"(countable) A half is a player who plays in the middle part of the field in sports like football, rugby, etc."}]}]},"veterinarian":{"h":"veterinarian","i":"/ˌvɛt(ə)rəˈnɛri.ən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-veterinarian.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A veterinarian (sometimes shortened to vet) is a doctor that treats animals.","e":"The veterinarian treated the dog."}]}]},"alter":{"h":"alter","i":"/ˈɔːl.tə/","a":"en-us-altar.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you alter something, you change it, usually in a small way.","e":"The design can be easily altered by selecting new colours, materials, etc."}]}]},"stability":{"h":"stability","i":"/stəˈbɪlɪti/","a":"en-us-stability.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Stability is the property of being firm and constant.","e":"Investors, especially foreign ones, want political stability to go with economic growth."}]}]},"energy":{"h":"energy","i":"/ˈɛnəd͡ʒi/","a":"en-us-energy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Energy is the ability to do work: move, give off heat, give off light, etc.","e":"Unlike coal or oil, atomic energy production creates little air pollution."}]}]},"aware":{"h":"aware","i":"/əˈwɛɚ/","a":"en-us-aware.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are aware of something, you know about it.","e":"I am fully aware of the need for security, and will make the necessary changes."}]}]},"providence":{"h":"providence","i":"/ˈprɒvɪdəns/","a":"en-us-providence.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Providence is the careful management of resources.","e":"His providence in saving for his old age is a good example for everyone."},{"m":"(uncountable) Providence is God."},{"m":"(uncountable) Providence also means God's will, or a power that some people think to be controlling our lives and the things that happen to us."}]}]},"station":{"h":"station","i":"/ˈsteɪʃən/","a":"en-us-station.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A station is a place where many trains or buses stop and people buy tickets and get on."},{"m":"(countable) A station is a place where a person stays in one place and works."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you station someone, you place them to do a task."}]}]},"society":{"h":"society","i":"/səˈsaɪ.ə.ti/","a":"en-us-society.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A society is a large number of people and the way they live, talking together, working with each other and making rules and ways to live. A society can be a town, country or more than one country together, with many people living the same ways."},{"m":"(countable) A society is an organization or club that people can join."}]}]},"sort":{"h":"sort","i":"/sɔːt/","a":"en-au-sort.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To sort is to divide one group of things into smaller groups of things, so that the things in one smaller group are the same as each other in some way.","e":"He sorted the apples, putting red apples in one basket and green apples in the other basket."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A sort is a kind or type.","e":"Red and green are two sorts of apple."}]}]},"small":{"h":"small","i":"/smɔːl/","a":"en-us-small.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A small person or thing is not big. It doesn't have much size.","e":"A mouse is a small animal. A baby mouse is very small."}]}]},"slow":{"h":"slow","i":"/sləʊ/","a":"en-us-slow.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something is slow if it takes a long time to move. It is not fast.","e":"A snail is a very slow animal. It moves slowly."},{"m":"If something is slow, it does not happen in a short time."},{"m":"If someone is slow, it takes them a while to understand something."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you slow someone or something, he, she, or it does not move as quickly as he, she, or it did before; you lower the speed of something."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you slow, you do not progress as quickly as you did before."}]}]},"slope":{"h":"slope","i":"/sloʊp/","a":"en-us-slope.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A slope is one side of a hill.","e":"We will have to climb up this slope to get to the top of the hill."},{"m":"The slope of a line is how far up it goes divided by how far along it goes."},{"m":"A slope is an extremely offensive word for an Asian."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something slopes, it goes either up or down.","e":"The hill slopes down at this point."}]}]},"slant":{"h":"slant","i":"/ˈslænt/","a":"en-us-slant.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"A long thing is slanting when one end is higher up than the other end and also further along. To be on an angle or sloping.","e":"The piece of wood is slanting from the ground up to the door so that a cart with wheels can roll up it."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A slant is the way a long thing is when one end is higher up and further along than the other end. The way a ramp is."}]}]},"enforcement":{"h":"enforcement","i":"/ɛnˈfɔrsmənt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-enforcement.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Enforcement is the act of making people follow a law, rule, or decision.","e":"It is not a problem which can be solved by law enforcement alone."}]}]},"slip":{"h":"slip","i":"/slɪp/","a":"en-us-slip.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) When something slides, or moves a small distance while touching what it's on, we say it slips.","e":"The hat slipped down until it covered her eyes."},{"m":"(intransitive) When someone or something moves without wanting to move, we say it slips.","e":"My foot slipped when I stepped on some ice, and I almost fell."},{"m":"(intransitive) When someone moves quickly and quietly so that other people won't see them move, we say the person slips.","e":"I slipped into the kitchen to start washing dishes while people were talking."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A slip is a small mistake."},{"m":"(countable) A slip is a piece of clothing like a small white skirt, that a woman sometimes wears hidden under her skirt or dress."},{"m":"(countable) A slip is a small piece of paper."}]}]},"draft":{"h":"draft","i":"/drɑːft/","a":"en-us-draught.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A draft is a piece of writing which has been or may be edited.","e":"In the first draft of the story the characters names are all different."},{"m":"(countable) A draft is when the military or a sport team chooses its members.","e":"Many Americans moved to Canada to avoid the draft during the war."},{"m":"(uncountable) Depth of water needed to float a ship; depth below the water line to the bottom of a vessel's hull. (UK spelling: draught)","e":"The ship had a draft of 6 feet."},{"m":"(uncountable) Draft is beer that is served from a large container called a keg. (UK spelling: draught)"},{"m":"(countable) A draft is a wind that blows inside a building. (UK spelling: draught)","e":"Close the window! That cold draft is making me sneeze."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you draft a letter, memo, agreement, etc., you write one that has been or may be edited.","e":"You should have the contract drafted by a lawyer."},{"m":"(transitive) If a state drafts someone, it chooses them to be in the military.","e":"I was drafted when I was 20 and spent two years fighting in France."},{"m":"(transitive) If a team drafts someone, it chooses them to play on the team."}]}]},"precise":{"h":"precise","i":"/prɪˈsaɪs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-precise.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is precise it is correct and exact.","e":"Young children are often unable to give a precise definition for words they know very well."},{"m":"If someone is precise they always act and speak very carefully."}]}]},"sky":{"h":"sky","i":"/skaɪ/","a":"en-us-sky.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The sky is what you see when you look up when you're not inside. It's blue with clouds in it. At night it's black with stars in it.","e":"The night sky was full of stars."}]}]},"pursue":{"h":"pursue","i":"/pəˈsjuː/","a":"en-us-pursue.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you pursue a job or hobby, you do it for a long time.","e":"The band motivated her to pursue a career in music."},{"m":"(transitive) If you pursue someone or something, you try to reach, catch or get it."}]}]},"symbolic":{"h":"symbolic","i":"/sɪmˈbɒlɪk/","a":"en-us-symbolic.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is symbolic, it has or is used as a symbol.","e":"In many religions, the number 3 has a symbolic value."}]}]},"marginal":{"h":"marginal","i":"/ˈmɑːdʒɪnl/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is marginal, it is not very large, important or central.","e":"But this discussion is marginal to the real issue."},{"m":"(in finance) The marginal profit, tax rate, etc. is the percent earned or paid on one more unit of production or income.","e":"Large scale economies tend to mean that the marginal cost of serving an additional customer is either zero or very small."},{"m":"If something is marginal, it is low quality, almost unacceptable.","e":"His writing is marginal at best. I don't think he'll pass."},{"m":"If something is marginal, it is written in a margin.","e":"I can't read the marginal notes."}]}]},"silk":{"h":"silk","i":"/sɪlk/","a":"en-us-silk.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A strong soft material that cloth is made of. A certain type of silk worms make it.","e":"This shirt is made of silk."}]}]},"sign":{"h":"sign","i":"/saɪn/","a":"en-us-sign.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A flat thing with a few words or pictures on it to tell people something.","e":"I saw a stop sign, so I stopped the car."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When someone signs a piece of paper, they write their signature on it.","e":"They signed a contract saying exactly who would do the work and how much money they would be paid."},{"m":"If a company signs someone, they hire them to work."}]}]},"side":{"h":"side","i":"/saɪd/","a":"en-us-side.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A side is a straight edge of an object.","e":"A square has four sides."},{"m":"(countable) A side is the left part or the right part of something.","e":"This car has only one door on each side."},{"m":"(countable) A side is an area next to or near something else.","e":"The statue is on the east side of the school."},{"m":"(countable) A side is one surface of a sheet of paper.","e":"Please write on both sides of the paper."},{"m":"(countable) A side is one possible way of looking at or thinking about a concept (usually positive or negative).","e":"On the plus side, my car is fixed."},{"m":"(countable) A side is one team of players in a game.","e":"Which side is winning?"},{"m":"(countable) A side is country or a group of countries fighting together in a war.","e":"In the second world war, the Italians were on the side of the Germans."},{"m":"(countable) (US) A side is a side dish of food that is not the main dish.","e":"Do you want a side of french fries with your hamburger?"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(usually with \"with\") To side with someone is to be in an alliance with them.","e":"Who will you side with, Bob or Rachel?"}]}]},"capacity":{"h":"capacity","i":"/kəˈpæsɪti/","a":"en-us-capacity.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"; (singular) The capacity of a container, room, etc. is how much it can hold.","e":"The capacity of the bottle is 500 ml."},{"m":"(countable) The capacity of someone or something to do something is the ability to do it.","e":"I was impressed by his energy and capacity for hard work."},{"m":"(uncountable) The capacity of a factory or business is how much it can produce.","e":"It will soon be necessary to increase capacity at our Toronto plant to meet Canadian demand for the product."},{"m":"(countable) If someone does something in a particular capacity, they are doing it in that role.","e":"I am not writing to you in my capacity as your doctor, but as a friend."}]}]},"exposure":{"h":"exposure","i":"/ɪkˈspoʊʒɚ/","a":"en-us-exposure.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"If x has exposure to y, x is not hidden or protected from y.","e":"Staying out of the sun between 11am and 3pm can reduce exposure by 60 per cent."},{"m":"(photography); (uncountable) The exposure is the amount of time that a film is hit by light."},{"m":"(photography); (countable) One exposure is one section of film that is hit by light at one time."}]}]},"modify":{"h":"modify","i":"/ˈmɒdɪfaɪ/","a":"en-us-modify.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you modify something, you change it, often only in small ways, and often because you want to use it in a different situation.","e":"Both penalties and rewards can be used to modify children's behaviour."},{"m":"; (transitive) If a word, phrase, or clause modifies another, it is an optional word, phrase, or clause that gives more information about the other.","e":"The adjective \"big\" modifies the noun \"bridge\" in the expression \"big bridge\"."}]}]},"external":{"h":"external","i":"/ɪksˈtɜː.nəl/","a":"en-us-external.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is external is not on the inside.","e":"Both internal and external stairs need to be modified to allow wheelchairs into the building."}]}]},"fundamental":{"h":"fundamental","i":"/ˌfʌndəˈmɛntəl/","a":"en-us-fundamental.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is fundamental, it is basic and important.","e":"The loss of her legs has caused her to undergo a fundamental change in how she looks at life."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The fundamentals of something, are the main ideas or parts that it is built on."}]}]},"flash":{"h":"flash","i":"/flæʃ/","a":"en-us-flash.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A flash is a sudden bright light.","e":"He used the flash on his camera."},{"m":"A flash is a very fast period of time.","e":"The tall man disappeared in a flash."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something flashes, it shines brightly and suddenly.","e":"The fountain flashed in the sunshine."}]}]},"ratio":{"h":"ratio","i":"/ˈreɪ.ʃoʊ/","a":"en-us-ratio.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A ratio is the comparison in size or number between two things. It is written x:y and read x to y. It is the same as the fraction \\frac {x} {y}.","e":"The ratio of men's jobs to women's is 8 to 1."}]}]},"shut":{"h":"shut","i":"/ʃʌt/","a":"en-us-shut.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When someone moves a door so that people can't go through it, the person is shutting the door. When someone puts their lips together so that no air or food can go in or out of their mouth, the person is shutting their mouth.","e":"The wind was too cold, so I shut the window."}]}]},"shoe":{"h":"shoe","i":"/ʃuː/","a":"en-us-shoe.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Two shoes are two things that someone wears on their feet. Shoes have a hard, flat bottom."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you shoe, you put shoes on your feet. We usually use this verb as a past participle: We say say someone is shod if they have shoes on their feet.","e":"He was dressed and shod, ready to go out."},{"m":"(transitive) If you shoe a horse, you put horseshoes on the horse."},{"m":"(transitive) To put protection on something so that it does not get worn down.","e":"Let's shoe that cane before you get a splinter in your hand!"}]}]},"shock":{"h":"shock","i":"/ʃɒk/","a":"en-us-shock.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A shock is the way it feels when a heavy thing suddenly hits another thing."},{"m":"A shock is a sudden change that surprises people."},{"m":"Shock is the way a person is when the person has lost some blood or has been hurt, and their heart is beating very fast and weakly."},{"m":"A shock is a painful feeling that someone gets when electricity flows through their body."},{"m":"A shock is a brief zap that someone gets after being in contact with static electricity."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Someone is shocked when they are surprised at something","e":"He was shocked at how much she had changed since he had last met her."},{"m":"If someone has been shocked, they got a painful feeling due to electricity flowing through their body."},{"m":"If someone has been shocked, they have gotten a brief zap due to contact with static electricity."}]}]},"shelf":{"h":"shelf","i":"/ʃɛlf/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-shelf.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A shelf is a flat thing that people can put books or other things on when they are not using them."}]}]},"shame":{"h":"shame","i":"/ʃeɪm/","a":"en-us-shame.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Someone feels shame when they know they did something wrong.","e":"The boy felt shame and gave back the candy he had taken."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you shame someone, you make them feel shame."}]}]},"shake":{"h":"shake","i":"/'ʃeɪk/","a":"en-us-shake.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To shake is to move from side to side many times quickly.","e":"She shook the bottle to mix the drink."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A shake is a type of beverage.","e":"They were known for their shakes."},{"m":"(countable) A shake is when something shakes."}]}]},"shade":{"h":"shade","i":"/ʃeɪd/","a":"en-us-shade.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A shade is a shadow of a tree or another big thing that blocks some of the light and heat of the Sun.","e":"She rested in the shade of the tree because she felt hot."},{"m":"(countable) A shade is the slight difference between colors."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If something is shaded, it is shielded from light.","e":"The old tree shaded the animals from the sun."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something is shading, it is approaching something slightly.","e":"The grassland was green, shading towards brown in the drier areas."},{"m":"(transitive) If you shade something in a drawing, you darken it.","e":"Mary started shading in the outlines of the house in her drawing."}]}]},"versus":{"h":"versus","i":"/ˈvɜːsəs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-versus.wav","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"When we say one thing versus another thing, it means the two things are on different sides, going in different directions, or against each other.","e":"Tonight's game has Toronto versus Montreal."}]}]},"terminal":{"h":"terminal","i":"/ˈtərmɪnəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-terminal.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A terminal is the end of a train track or bus route. It is the station or the last stop.","e":"The bus drove into the terminal and all the people got off."},{"m":"(countable) A computer screen and keyboard, which are at the end of a wire joining them to a computer.","e":"She sat at the computer terminal and typed some words."},{"m":"(countable) A terminal is a building in an airport where passengers transfer to the facilities that allow them to board airplanes."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"The last. At the end, in time or in space. A terminal illness is a sickness that will make the person die."}]}]},"takeoff":{"h":"takeoff","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The takeoff is when an airplane moves from the ground into the air.","e":"Put on your seat belt to be ready for takeoff."}]}]},"surrender":{"h":"surrender","i":"/səˈrɛndə/","a":"en-us-surrender.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When an army stops fighting and lets the other side win, we say that the army surrenders. Sometimes people wave a white flag to show that they are surrendering."},{"m":"To submit to a person who has more power."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A surrender is the act of [[#Verb|surrendering]]."}]}]},"whereas":{"h":"whereas","i":"/ʍɛːrˈæz/","a":"en-us-whereas.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"(formal) You use whereas to show a contrast between two things or ideas.","e":"Many kinds of roses have little or no scent, whereas others are well known for their beautiful smell."},{"m":"Because."}]}]},"enable":{"h":"enable","i":"/ɪˈneɪbəl/","a":"en-us-enable.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you enable something or someone, you make make it able to do something or you help it.","e":"The program enables users to share data, collaborate and automate tasks without writing any extra code."}]}]},"version":{"h":"version","i":"/ˈvɜː(r)ʒən/","a":"en-us-version.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A version is something that exists in different forms.","e":"Tomorrow, IBM is launching OS/2 2.0, the new version of its OS/2 operating software for personal computers."}]}]},"perspective":{"h":"perspective","i":"/pɚˈspɛk.tɪv/","a":"en-us-perspective.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A perspective is a way of looking at or thinking about something.","e":"The British media give a completely different perspective from CNN."},{"m":"(uncountable) Perspective is the ability to think about things in a reasonable way.","e":"He's lost all perspective when it comes to this job."},{"m":"(uncountable) Perspective is a way to show three dimensions in a two-dimensional image."}]}]},"network":{"h":"network","i":"/nɛtwɜːk/","a":"en-us-network.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A network is a group of connections between a number of points.","e":"Electronic systems control the busiest parts of the rail network."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you network, you make or use social connections, usually for business purposes.","e":"I spent most of my time at the conferences networking with other sales people."}]}]},"welfare":{"h":"welfare","i":"/ˈwɛlˌfɛə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-welfare.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Someone's welfare is their health, safety, and other things the make them happy.","e":"Children need to exercise each day, for both their physical and psychological welfare."},{"m":"; (uncountable) Welfare is money paid by the government to poor people.","e":"The government is reviewing the welfare benefits which single parents receive."}]}]},"transition":{"h":"transition","i":"/trænˈzɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-transition.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A transition is a change from one place or situation to another.","e":"Diana has made the transition from girl to woman."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If something transitions, it changes from one place or situation to another."}]}]},"amendment":{"h":"amendment","i":"/ʌˈmɛnd.mənt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-amendment.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An amendment is an addition or change to a document; also the process of making this change.","e":"This law can only be changed by constitutional amendment."}]}]},"deep":{"h":"deep","i":"/diːp/","a":"en-us-deep.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A hole or body of water is deep if it goes down a long way.","e":"Do not dive into this swimming pool because it is not deep enough."},{"m":"Something is deep if it is far below or inside.","e":"The Earth's iron core is deep beneath its crust."},{"m":"A deep voice has low-pitched tones.","e":"In opera, the bass singer has the deepest voice."},{"m":"With actions that make something smaller, we say deep to mean they make them much smaller.","e":"This furniture store offers deep discounts on beds."},{"m":"An idea is called deep if it has an important meaning that is not easy to see.","e":"A: 'I think you like heavy metal music because your parents don't approve of it.' B:'Wow, that's deep!'"}]}]},"reject":{"h":"reject","i":"/rɪˈdʒɛkt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-reject (verb).wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you reject an idea or belief, you decide that you do not believe it.","e":"We reject the idea that English is somehow \"better\" than other languages."},{"m":"(transitive) If you reject a person, you refuse to care for that person.","e":"Often people who are infected with AIDS are rejected by family and friends."},{"m":"(transitive) If you reject an object, you refuse to take it or keep it.","e":"Consumers have the right to reject problem goods and demand a refund."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A reject is something that has been rejected."},{"m":"(countable) A reject is a stupid person."}]}]},"clause":{"h":"clause","i":"/klɔːz/","a":"en-us-clause.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A clause is a section in a contract or other legal document.","e":"The author's contract contained a clause giving him creative control over the films."},{"m":"A clause is a group of words that usually includes a subject and a predicate. In English, the subject usually comes before the predicate.","e":"The last clause in the sentence is hard to understand without knowing some background."}]}]},"predicate":{"h":"predicate","i":"/ˈprɛdɪkət/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-predicate (noun).wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A predicate is the head of a clause and says something about the subject."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you predicate something, you state or assert it."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you predicate that something is true, you state that it is true.","e":"The article predicates that the market collapse was caused by weakness of the dollar."}]}]},"prime":{"h":"prime","i":"/praɪm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-prime.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is prime, it is best, most important, most suitable, or in some way number one.","e":"Canada is a prime example of a multicultural country."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The prime is the best part of something.","e":"He was killed at the prime of his life."},{"m":"(countable) A prime is a number that can be evenly divided only by one and itself.","e":"The first six primes are 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, and 13."},{"m":"(countable) A prime is something that primes something else."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you prime something, you get it ready to do something.","e":"The coach has primed them for the game."},{"m":"to manipulate, in a subtle manner, people's decision-making by use of symbols, location, etc."}]}]},"objective":{"h":"objective","a":"en-us-objective.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An objective is something that you are trying to do.","e":"The main objective of our visit was to climb Mount Kenya."},{"m":"(countable) An objective is a place you want to get to."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is objective, it is based on facts and things we can see and touch without using people's feelings.","e":"It is hard to find objective measures of artistic ability."},{"m":"If someone is objective, they are thinking about things logically based on facts.","e":"Watching the play on TV can help an actor to be more objective about his performance."}]}]},"sustainable":{"h":"sustainable","i":"/səˈsteɪnəbəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-sustainable.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is sustainable, it can be continued for a long time, especially without using up resources.","e":"The oil-based lifestyle of today is not sustainable."}]}]},"equivalent":{"h":"equivalent","i":"/ɪˈkwɪvələnt/","a":"en-us-equivalent.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If two things are equivalent, they are of equal value or acceptability.","e":"Dolphins have very large brains, roughly equivalent to the size of a human brain."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An equivalent is something of equal value of acceptability.","e":"Living in Thailand costs the equivalent of just £10 per day."}]}]},"liberal":{"h":"liberal","i":"/ˈlɪbrəl/","a":"en-us-liberal.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is liberal, it allows for change, flexibility, and free thought.","e":"The Church should take a more liberal view of sex."},{"m":"If something is liberal, it has few limits.","e":"He was quite liberal with his kindness."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A liberal is a person who believes in liberal ideas."}]}]},"notion":{"h":"notion","i":"/ˈnəʊʃən/","a":"en-us-notion.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A notion is an idea about something.","e":"The film questions the standard notions of right and wrong."}]}]},"substitution":{"h":"substitution","i":"/ˌsʌbstəˈtuʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-substitution.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A substitution is the act of one person or thing with another.","e":"The accidental substitution of one medicine for another can be deadly."}]}]},"generate":{"h":"generate","i":"/ˈdʒɛn.ər.eɪt/","a":"en-us-generate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you generate something, you create it.","e":"On the hottest summer days, we are unable to generate enough electricity."}]}]},"revenue":{"h":"revenue","i":"/ˈrɛvənjuː/","a":"en-us-revenue.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Revenue is the money that a business receives for doing business, and government receives from taxes.","e":"Higher oil prices should raise government revenue by 13%."}]}]},"compound":{"h":"compound","i":"/ˈkɒmpaʊnd/","a":"en-us-compound.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A compound is a material made of a number of other materials.","e":"The new chemical compound has far less smell than the original substance."},{"m":"(countable) A compound is a mixture.","e":"The new CD is a compound of North American rock music and Middle Eastern religious songs."},{"m":"(countable) A compound is a group of buildings surrounded by a fence or wall."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If something is compounded, it is added to.","e":"Her troubles were now compounded by the rain."},{"m":"(transitive) If interest is compounded, it is paid on earlier interest payments.","e":"Interest is compounded monthly."}]}]},"evolution":{"h":"evolution","i":"/ˌiːvəˈluːʃ(ə)n/","a":"en-us-evolution.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Evolution is the process of slow change. It is most used in biology to refer to the way living things change over long periods of time in order to adapt to their surroundings.","e":"The theory of evolution is the basis of modern biology."},{"m":"(countable) An evolution is a change that happens over time.","e":"Over the last ten years, there has been an evolution in the way we think about this disease."}]}]},"eighteen":{"h":"eighteen","i":"/ˈeɪ(t).tin/","a":"en-us-eighteen.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(ordinal eighteenth) Eighteen is the number that is after seventeen and before nineteen. It can also be written as 18.","e":"Eighteen chickens sat on the roof."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The number 18.","e":"nines is eighteen."},{"m":"A set of eighteen things or persons.","e":"The eighteen were leaving the city."},{"m":"The age 18.","e":"You have to be eighteen to vote in some."}]}]},"eleven":{"h":"eleven","i":"/ɪˈlɛv.ən/","a":"en-us-eleven.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(ordinal eleventh) Eleven is the number that is after ten and before twelve. It can also be written as 11.","e":"Eleven trees stood on the hill."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The number 11.","e":"Eleven is a prime number."},{"m":"A set of eleven things or persons.","e":"Ocean's eleven are a group of thieves."}]}]},"fifteen":{"h":"fifteen","i":"/ˈfɪf.tiːn/","a":"en-us-fifteen.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(ordinal fifteenth) Fifteen is the number that is after fourteen and before sixteen. It can also be written as 15.","e":"Fifteen ducks swim on the lake."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The number 15.","e":"and ten makes fifteen."},{"m":"A set of fifteen things or persons.","e":"The fifteen were leaving the city."},{"m":"To be fifteen years old.","e":"Paul is fifteen, but he looks older"}]}]},"ninety-nine":{"h":"ninety-nine","a":"en-us-ninety-nine.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(ordinal ninety-ninth) Ninety-nine (99) is the odd number that comes before one hundred.","e":"Ninety-nine apples lay on the table."}]}]},"ninety":{"h":"ninety","i":"/ˈnaɪn.ti/","a":"en-us-ninety.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(ordinal ninetieth) Ninety is an even number. In numerals, it is 90.","e":"Ninety years ago, things were different."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The number 90.","e":"Ninety is ten less than hundred and forty more than fifty."},{"m":"To be 90 years old.","e":"My grandfather is ninety."}]}]},"nineteen":{"h":"nineteen","i":"/ˈnaɪn.tiːn/","a":"en-us-nineteen.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(ordinal nineteenth) Nineteen is the number that is after eighteen and before twenty. It can also be written as 19.","e":"Nineteen ducks swim on the lake."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The number 19.","e":"and ten makes nineteen."},{"m":"A set of nineteen things or persons.","e":"The nineteen are the fastest runners in their school."},{"m":"To be nineteen years old.","e":"Paul is nineteen, but he looks older"}]}]},"twelve":{"h":"twelve","i":"/twɛlv/","a":"en-us-twelve.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(ordinal twelfth) Twelve is the number that is after eleven and before thirteen. In numerals, it is 12.","e":"Twelve eggs make a big omelette."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The number 12.","e":"and ten makes twelve."},{"m":"A set of twelve things or persons.","e":"The twelve are never alone."},{"m":"To be twelve years old.","e":"This girl is twelve."}]}]},"sixty":{"h":"sixty","i":"/ˈsɪkstɪ/","a":"en-us-sixty.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(ordinal sixtieth) Sixty is the number that is after 59 and before 61.","e":"There are sixty seconds in a minute and sixty minutes in an hour."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The number 60.","e":"Sixty is ten less than seventy and ten more than fifty."},{"m":"To be 60 years old.","e":"My father is sixty."}]}]},"sixteen":{"h":"sixteen","i":"/ˈsɪks.tiːn/","a":"en-us-sixteen.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(ordinal sixteenth) Sixteen is the number that is after fifteen and before seventeen. It can also be written as 16.","e":"Sixteen persons fit in this small bus."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The number 16.","e":"and ten makes sixteen."},{"m":"A set of sixteen things or persons.","e":"These sixteen are very beautiful stones."},{"m":"To be sixteen years old.","e":"In some countries, you may vote when you are sixteen"}]}]},"seventeen":{"h":"seventeen","i":"/ˈsɛv.ən.tiːn/","a":"en-us-seventeen.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(ordinal seventeenth) Seventeen is the number that is after sixteen and before eighteen. It can also be written as 17.","e":"Seventeen birds sit on the roof."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The number 17.","e":"and ten makes seventeen."},{"m":"A set of seventeen things or persons.","e":"The seventeen were leaving the city."},{"m":"To be seventeen years old.","e":"In some, you may vote when you are seventeen"}]}]},"fourteen":{"h":"fourteen","i":"/ˈfɔː.tiːn/","a":"en-us-fourteen.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(ordinal fourteenth) Fourteen is the even number that is after thirteen and before fifteen. In numerals, it is 14.","e":"Fourteen apples lie on the table."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The number 14.","e":"and ten makes fourteen."},{"m":"A set of fourteen things or persons.","e":"The fourteen are never alone."},{"m":"To be fourteen years old.","e":"This boy is fourteen."}]}]},"discretion":{"h":"discretion","i":"/dɪˈskrɛʃən/","a":"en-us-discretion.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Discretion is the ability and power to decide.","e":"The judge made a mistake in exercising his discretion to end the trial early."},{"m":"(uncountable) Discretion is the ability to do something in a way that does not upset people."},{"m":"(uncountable) Discretion is the ability to keep a secret."}]}]},"servant":{"h":"servant","i":"/ˈsɜːvənt/","a":"en-us-servant.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A servant is someone who works for a person or for a family, doing things like cooking and washing. Often the servant lives in the house where they work. A servant works for the same family all day.","e":"This rich family has three servants working for them in their big house."}]}]},"serious":{"h":"serious","i":"/ˈsɪr.i.əs/","a":"en-us-serious.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A problem or situation is serious if it is not funny or comical, but important.","e":"This is a serious problem. We must do something."},{"m":"A person is serious if the person is not laughing or joking, but saying what they mean.","e":"I see. When you said the room was empty, you were serious!"}]}]},"sense":{"h":"sense","i":"/sɛns/","a":"en-us-sense.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Sense is any basic ability or understanding.","e":"She has a great sense of fashion."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Sense is the ability to understand a situation or emotions.","e":"I sensed you were upset before you said anything."}]}]},"seem":{"h":"seem","i":"/siːm/","a":"en-us-seem.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) The way something seems to be is the way you think it is when you look at it, hear about it, think about it, etc.","e":"It seems unlikely that they will remember your name after meeting you once."}]}]},"send":{"h":"send","i":"/ˈsend/","a":"en-us-send.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To send something is to make the thing go somewhere without the person. A person sends a letter by putting it in a mailbox. A person can send another person somewhere by telling the person to go there.","e":"She needed to send a letter to her mother to say she had arrived safely."}]}]},"selection":{"h":"selection","i":"/səˈlɛkʃən/","a":"en-us-selection.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A person makes a selection when a person chooses a smaller number of things from a larger group of things."},{"m":"A selection of things is different things that have been chosen or that you can choose from.","e":"The window of the store shows a selection of the things you can buy in the store."},{"m":"Selection is a process where the best adapted life forms survive and the others die out.","e":"Charles Darwin was a scientist who wrote about natural selection."},{"m":"(Australia) In Australia, a selection was an area of land which a farmer could choose to buy.","e":"The first thing he had to do was clear the trees of his selection."}]}]},"seed":{"h":"seed","i":"/siːd/","a":"en-us-seed.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A seed is a small round thing that can grow to be a plant, a flower or a tree.","e":"She put the seeds into the ground in the garden so that food and flowers would grow."},{"m":"(uncountable) The seed of a man is his semen."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To plant seeds in an area.","e":"I'm going to seed the garden so vegetables grow there."},{"m":"If a man seeds in a woman, he ejaculates inside her during sexual intercourse."}]}]},"see":{"h":"see","i":"/si/","a":"en-us-see.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"You see something when you look at it with your eyes.","e":"She turned her head up and saw clouds in the sky."},{"m":"(transitive) If you are seeing someone, you are dating them.","e":"Me and Katie have been seeing each other for a few months."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A diocese; a region of a church, generally headed by a bishop, an archbishop or a cardinal"},{"m":"The office of a bishop or archbishop or cardinal.","e":"Venice is the see of a cardinal."}]}]},"screw":{"h":"screw","i":"/skruː/","a":"en-us-screw.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A screw is a small metal thing for holding pieces of wood together. You turn it to move it in or out of the wood.","e":"I need some screws to hold the shelf to the wall."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you screw in a screw, you put it into a piece of wood by turning it.","e":"I screwed the hinge into the door."},{"m":"If you say, \"screw this\", you decide not to do it because you are frustrated.","e":"Screw this, I will just sit here and do nothing all day."},{"m":"If you screw someone, you have sex with them."}]}]},"scissors":{"h":"scissors","i":"/ˈsɪzəz/","a":"en-us-scissors.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (usually plural) A pair of scissors is a tool for cutting, with two parts like two knives that move. Scissors are usually used for cutting paper."}]}]},"scale":{"h":"scale","i":"/skeɪl/","a":"en-us-scale.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The scale of something is its size or level.","e":"It's hard to understand the scale of the change."},{"m":"(countable) A scale is a small machine for (finding out) how much something weighs (how heavy the thing is.)","e":"She stood on the scale and found out she weighed 150 pounds."},{"m":"(countable) A series of eight notes."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you scale something, then you climb up it."}]}]},"round":{"h":"round","i":"/ˈraʊnd/","a":"en-us-round.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If x is round y, y is in the middle and x is on all sides.","e":"Everyone stood round the fire to keep warm."},{"m":"If you turn or look round, you are now facing the opposite direction.","e":"She turned round to see what had made the noise."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something is round if it's like a circle or like part of a circle. It is curved, not straight."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you round something, you make it round, like a circle or a sphere."},{"m":"(transitive) If you round a number, you approximate it with a less precise number.","e":"You round 47.3 to 47. You round 47.6 to 48."}]}]},"conflict":{"h":"conflict","i":"/ˈkɒnflɪkt/","a":"en-us-conflict-noun.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A conflict is when two or more people or ideas don't agree.","e":"People have tried to end the conflict, which has caused more than 100 deaths since February, but it hasn't worked."},{"m":"(countable) A conflict is when two things are trying to use the same resources at the same time.","e":"I'm sorry I can't meet then. I've got a conflict with another meeting."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If two goals, plans, meetings, etc. conflict, they both cannot be achieved, work or be true.","e":"The goal of hiring more workers conflicts with the plan to cut costs."}]}]},"entity":{"h":"entity","i":"/ˈen.tɪ.ti/","a":"en-us-entity.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An entity is a whole thing, independent from other things, often an institution or something alive.","e":"The idea of church and state as separate entities is quite new."}]}]},"orientation":{"h":"orientation","i":"/ˌɔriɛnˈteɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-orientation.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Someone's or something's orientation is the way they face, physically or psychologically.","e":"As homosexuality becomes more accepted, sexual orientation becomes a more common topic."},{"m":"An orientation to something is when somebody is first introduced to a place or a machine.","e":"Library orientation and instruction should be available when the user feels an interest or need."}]}]},"rough":{"h":"rough","i":"/rʌf/","a":"en-us-rough.oga","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A rough is a person who is rude."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Having small bumps on it. Not smooth.","e":"The wooden table felt rough until he rubbed it with sandpaper to make it smooth."},{"m":"Not perfect.","e":"I quickly drew a rough map to help him find the place."},{"m":"If something is rough, it is difficult.","e":"Life can be rough sometimes."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you rough something, you create it in an approximate form.","e":"Rough in the shape first, then polish the details."}]}]},"root":{"h":"root","i":"/ruːt/","a":"en-us-root.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A root is a part of a tree or plant that is under the ground.","e":"The tree was supported by strong roots."},{"m":"(countable) A root is the important part or the beginning part of something.","e":"is the root of all evil."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To root is to give or enable to something to develop roots; to fix or implant by or as if by roots"},{"m":"(transitive) To root is to remove altogether by or as if by pulling out by the roots – usually used with out","e":"The school authorities will root out the troublemakers."},{"m":"(intransitive) To root is to grow roots or take root.","e":"s took root in my flowerbeds."},{"m":"(intransitive) To root is to have an origin or base.","e":"The love of money has its roots in greed."}]}]},"roll":{"h":"roll","i":"/rəʊl/","a":"en-us-roll.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To roll is to move by turning over many times. things like balls can roll.","e":"The snowball rolled down the hill faster and faster."},{"m":"To roll something is to make it round by bending it around many times.","e":"She rolled the newspaper into a long, thin rod."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A roll is something round that was made by rolling.","e":"The cloth in the store is in big rolls."},{"m":"(countable) A roll is a bun: a small, round piece of bread.","e":"I like jelly rolls!"}]}]},"rod":{"h":"rod","i":"/rɒd/","a":"en-us-rod.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A rod is a long, thin round thing, usually made of metal.","e":"They put rods on the window to keep people out."}]}]},"pump":{"h":"pump","i":"/pʌmp/","a":"en-us-pump.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To make water or any other liquid move using a machine.","e":"We pumped water from the river onto the field to help the plants grow."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pump is a machine for making water move.","e":"There was water on the floor of the house, so we had to buy a pump."},{"m":"(countable) A pump is a machine that gives a liquid, often fuel.","e":"Before a car journey, go to the gas station and fill up your tank at the pump."}]}]},"consultation":{"h":"consultation","i":"/ˌkɒnsl̩ˈteɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-consultation.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Consultation is the process of getting advice or opinions from other people.","e":"The city went through the planning process with very little public consultation."}]}]},"transparent":{"h":"transparent","i":"/trænsˈpærənt/","a":"en-us-transparent.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that can be seen through is transparent.","e":"The transparent window let much sun in."},{"m":"Something that is easy to understand is transparent.","e":"It was such a transparent lie that nobody believed him."}]}]},"monitor":{"h":"monitor","i":"/ˈmɔn.ɪˌtɚ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-monitor.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A monitor is part of a computer or other similar machine, and it looks like a TV.","e":"The engineers stood around the monitor making suggesting about how the drawing could be improved."},{"m":"(countable) A monitor is a person or group whose job is to watch for problems, changes, etc.","e":"During the test, a monitor caught me copying off the guy sitting next to me."},{"m":"(countable) A monitor is a speaker that helps musicians hear what they are playing or helps people listen to an area that they are interested in.","e":"We put the baby to sleep, closed the door, and turned on the monitor in the kitchen."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you monitor something, you watch or listen to it for problems, changes, etc.","e":"The army was sent in to monitor the police."}]}]},"challenge":{"h":"challenge","i":"/ˈtʃæl.ɪndʒ/","a":"en-us-challenge.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A challenge is something difficult that you want or have to do.","e":"Many churches overseas are struggling to meet the AIDS challenge."},{"m":"(countable) A challenge is an offer to compete or fight.","e":"The president issued a challenge to his critics to appear in a public debate."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you challenge somebody, you give them something very difficult to do.","e":"The job challenges his computer skills."},{"m":"(transitive) If you challenge somebody, you offer to compete or fight.","e":"He challenged me to a game of chess."}]}]},"fish":{"h":"fish","i":"/fɪʃ/","a":"en-us-fish.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A fish is an animal that lives in the water and has scales and gills.","e":"When I went fishing, I only caught two fish."},{"m":"(uncountable) Fish is the meat of a fish.","e":"White wine goes well with fish."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To fish means to catch fish, or to get other things that are in the water.","e":"He fished the ball out of the river."}]}]},"rhythm":{"h":"rhythm","i":"/ˈrɪ.ð(ə)m/","a":"en-us-rhythm.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A rhythm is the part of music that drums do. It's the way music goes in time, without thinking about higher or lower notes.","e":"A healthy heart beats with a steady rhythm."}]}]},"reward":{"h":"reward","i":"/rɪˈwɔːd/","a":"en-us-reward.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A reward is something good that is given after an act.","e":"He gave the dog a small thing to eat to reward it for sitting still."},{"m":"(countable) A reward is a prize that is given for doing certain things."},{"m":"(countable) A reward is the result of an action, no matter if it is good or bad."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you reward someone, you give something to them as a reward."},{"m":"(transitive) If you reward someone, you give a reward to or for.","e":"Why did you reward the kid for not behaving?"},{"m":"(transitive) If you reward, you recompense them."}]}]},"responsible":{"h":"responsible","i":"/rɪˈspɑnsəbəl/","a":"en-us-responsible.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are responsible for something, you did it or it happened because of something that you did.","e":"Are you saying that he was responsible for the death of your wife?"},{"m":"If you are responsible, you make good decisions and make sure that important things get done.","e":"She will be a good leader for this organization because she is very responsible."},{"m":"If you are responsible for something, you are the person who must fix things that go wrong.","e":"I'm responsible for looking after these three buildings."}]}]},"respect":{"h":"respect","i":"/rɪˈspɛkt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-respect.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When someone respects another person that means they think the other person is worthy, responsible, strong or other good.","e":"I have great respect for him and I'm sure he'll do well in life."},{"m":"Respect is to treat someone in a considerate, genuine and nice manner or to treat one thing or one person with highest regard.","e":"He always respects my feelings."},{"m":"When someone respects a thing or a person it means they follow rules and don't touch things they shouldn't touch.","e":"Please respect things that belong to other people when you're in their house."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"If you have respect for someone, that means you have high regard for them; you are considerate towards them.","e":"I have great respect for all of my classmates."}]}]},"relation":{"h":"relation","i":"/rɪˈleɪʃən/","a":"en-us-relation.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A relation is the way two things are towards each other or in comparison with each other.","e":"This building looks too big in relation to the size of the houses on the street."},{"m":"(countable) A relation is a member of ones' family.","e":"I have an uncle, two aunts and three cousins but no other relations."},{"m":"(countable) A relation is a statement of equality between two products of generators that are used when showing a group."}]}]},"regret":{"h":"regret","i":"/rɪˈɡrɛt/","a":"en-us-regret.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you regret something that you have done, you feel sorry about it.","e":"I really regret forgetting to buy him a birthday present."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Regret is the feeling of wishing something hadn't happened, especially something you did.","e":"She left her job without any regrets."}]}]},"establishment":{"h":"establishment","i":"/ɪˈstæblɪʃmənt/","a":"en-us-establishment.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The establishment of a country, an organization or a building is its creation, or coming to be.","e":"The establishment of the United States of America took place in 1776."},{"m":"Establishment is the state of being established.","e":"1987 was the fifth year of the company's establishment."},{"m":"Something that is established. This can be a government, an organization, business or force.","e":"Pedro's is a fine establishment that serves Spanish food."},{"m":"The establishment is the ruling class in a society. A person using this word often thinks that the establishment does not want to change the way things are.","e":"Janet does not like the establishment, she wants to change things."}]}]},"record":{"h":"record","i":"/ˈrɛkɔːd/","a":"en-us-record-noun.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A record is something in writing to tell what happened.","e":"Keep a record of the date and what you said every time you talk to that person."},{"m":"(countable) A record is a big round black plastic thing with music or other sounds on it.","e":"Now people don't use records any more -- they use cassettes or CDs."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To make a written record about something.","e":"She recorded everything she did in a little book."},{"m":"To put music or other sounds onto a machine.","e":"The singer recorded some songs on CDs to sell them."}]}]},"receipt":{"h":"receipt","i":"/rɪsiːt/","a":"en-us-receipt.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A receipt is a little piece of paper that records how much money someone paid.","e":"Keep the receipt when you buy something at that store."},{"m":"(uncountable) The receipt of something is the act or situation of something."}]}]},"reading":{"h":"reading","i":"/ˈriːdɪŋ/","a":"en-us-reading.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A reading is a spoken performance of something written.","e":"The author was giving a reading of his new book."}]}]},"read":{"h":"read","i":"/riːd/","a":"en-us-read.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Someone is reading when they are looking at a book or other writing and understanding what it says.","e":"Have you read this book?"}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A read is something that you read.","e":"That last book was a great read."},{"m":"(countable) A read is an act of reading something.","e":"This is a great book. You should give it a read."}]}]},"ray":{"h":"ray","i":"/reɪ/","a":"en-us-ray.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A ray is a line of light or energy, coming out from where it starts.","e":"Some rays of light from the sun shone between the leaves of the tree and lighted the top of his head."},{"m":"(countable) A ray in math is a line that starts at one point and goes on forever in one direction.","e":"Two rays that start at the same point make an angle."},{"m":"(countable) A ray is a type of fish which lives on the bottom of the ocean."}]}]},"rate":{"h":"rate","i":"/reɪt/","a":"en-us-rate.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Speed. A rate is how fast something happens. Something can go at a fast rate or a slow rate.","e":"The rate of water pouring out of the lake into the river is enough to make the lake empty in a year if it doesn't rain."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Someone rates something when they decide how much its value is (how much it's worth).","e":"I rate this book at six out of ten: it was not the best book."}]}]},"rail":{"h":"rail","i":"/reɪɫ/","a":"en-us-rail.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A rail is a long and thin piece of metal."},{"m":"A rail is a long and thin bar along a stairway or path for people to slide their hand along while they walk.","e":"She put her hand on the railing beside the stairs so she wouldn't fall."},{"m":"A rail is a surface where trains run on.","e":"The railway stretches across the country."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you rail, you travel by railway."},{"m":"(transitive) If you rail someone, you sexually penetrate in a rough manner."}]}]},"pull":{"h":"pull","i":"/pʊl/","a":"en-us-pull.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Someone pulls something when they use their hands to move the thing closer to themselves.","e":"Pull the handle if you want to open the door."}]}]},"public":{"h":"public","i":"/ˈpʰʌblɪk/","a":"en-us-public.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something is public if it is about or for all the people.","e":"You can't tell me to go away. This is a public place."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) All of the people in a big place like a country.","e":"I'm going to write this in the newspaper because the public needs to know it."}]}]},"protest":{"h":"protest","i":"/ˈprəʊ.tɛst/","a":"en-us-protest-noun.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Someone protests something when they say loudly or strongly that the thing is bad.","e":"The people walked in the street holding signs to protest the war."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The action of protesting something.","e":"There will be a protest in the street tomorrow."}]}]},"prose":{"h":"prose","i":"/ˈprəʊz/","a":"en-us-prose.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Prose is words which are not poetry. They can be spoken or written, but they don't have rhythm or rhyme. Most of the time when people use words, it is prose.","e":"The pictures in this book are good, but the prose is too hard to read."}]}]},"property":{"h":"property","i":"/ˈprɒpəti/","a":"en-us-property.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Property is a thing or things that belong to someone; things that someone owns.","e":"This house is now my property. I've finished paying for it."},{"m":"(countable) A property is a quality that something has; a way that something is.","e":"One good property of this coat is that it keeps rain out."}]}]},"produce":{"h":"produce","i":"/prəˈdjuːs/","a":"en-us-produce-verb.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Someone or something produces something when they make it or create it or make it come out.","e":"This tree produces a lot of fruit every year."},{"m":"(acting) If you produce a play, TV show, or movie, you are its main business manager."},{"m":"(radio) If you produce a recording, you are in charge of its arrangement, recording, and mixing."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Food from plants when they're being sold in a store.","e":"There are carrots and apples in the produce part of the store."}]}]},"private":{"h":"private","i":"/ˈpraɪvət/","a":"en-us-private.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Private is for only one person or a small number of people to see or know.","e":"I don't want to tell you how much money I have; that's private."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A private is a soldier in the lowest rank of the army.","e":"Put down your gun, private, and report to the general."}]}]},"present":{"h":"present","i":"/ˈprɛzənt/","a":"en-us-present-adjective.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A present is a gift; something that someone gives to someone else.","e":"Here's a birthday present for you. I hope you like it."},{"m":"(uncountable) The present is the time now at this moment.","e":"is the past, tomorrow is the future, and today is the present."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Someone is present if the person is here, or the person is at the place someone is talking about.","e":"Five men and two women were present when the meeting started."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you present something, you show it or give it to someone."}]}]},"power":{"h":"power","i":"/paʊə/","a":"en-us-power.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable), energy, force, control. A quality that can make things happen.","e":"His muscles have a lot of power."},{"m":"(uncountable) Energy or electricity.","e":"The city had no lights that night because there was no power."},{"m":"(uncountable); Power is how fast something uses energy. That is, how much work it does in a certain time."},{"m":"(countable); x to the power of y is equal to x multiplied by itself y times.","e":"Two to the power of three is eight (2^3 = 8)."},{"m":"(countable) A special ability that someone might have.","e":"In comic books many heroes have amazing powers."},{"m":"(countable) A person or group of people with authority; that is a people who control things.","e":"The mayor and the sheriff are the major powers in this town."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To provide power for or give power to (a mechanical or electronic device).","e":"This CD player is powered by batteries."}]}]},"powder":{"h":"powder","i":"/ˈpaʊ.də(r)/","a":"en-us-powder.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Powder is the small parts that are made from any dry substance that is pounded, or ground into dust.","e":"Flour is a powder."},{"m":"(countable) A powder is an explosive mixture used in blasting."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you powder something, you reduce something to small parts."},{"m":"(transitive) If you powder something, you put powder on it."}]}]},"potato":{"h":"potato","i":"/pəˈteɪtəʊ/","a":"en-us-potato.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A potato is a food that grows under the ground, which is round and white inside.","e":"We usually eat meat and potatoes."}]}]},"pot":{"h":"pot","i":"/pɒt/","a":"en-us-pot.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A metal container for cooking. People can cook food by putting the food in a pot and putting the pot on a stove."},{"m":"(countable),."}]}]},"position":{"h":"position","i":"/ˈpʌ.zɪ.ʃən/","a":"en-us-position.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The position of something is the place where the thing is.","e":"The position of the table is two metres from the wall."},{"m":"A post of employment; a job."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you position something somewhere, you put or move it there.","e":"The players positioned themselves on the field."},{"m":"(transitive) If you position something in a situation, you make changes so that it can work in that situation.","e":"The company is now well positioned to take advantage of popularity of online music."}]}]},"porter":{"h":"porter","i":"/ˈpɔrtɚ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-porter.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A porter is someone whose work is to carry things.","e":"The porter will take your things up to your room for you."}]}]},"transformation":{"h":"transformation","i":"/ˌtræns.fə(r)ˈmeɪ.ʃən/","a":"en-us-transformation.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A transformation is a change in the form or shape, often into something completely different.","e":"She seems to have undergone a total physical transformation – her hair is cut short and she is over 20&nbsp;kg heavier."}]}]},"presumption":{"h":"presumption","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A presumption is a belief that something is true without knowing for sure.","e":"The presumption that he is the father of his wife's children turned out to be wrong."},{"m":"(uncountable) Presumption is behaviour that is too friendly or too confident."}]}]},"acknowledge":{"h":"acknowledge","i":"/ækˈnɑl.ɪʤ/","a":"en-us-acknowledge.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you acknowledge a fact or a situation, you accept or admit that it is true or that it exists.","e":"The government yesterday acknowledged the need for more money."},{"m":"(transitive) If you acknowledge something, you say publicly that it is good.","e":"She isn't very good at acknowledging the work of her staff."}]}]},"utility":{"h":"utility","i":"/juːˈtɪl.ɪ.ti/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-utility.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable); (usually plural) Utilities are the basic services that come to your house, such as electricity, phone, and water.","e":"The government is raising prices on drugs, beer and most public utilities."},{"m":"(countable) A utility is a basic computer program that handles things like copying disks and setting up printers."},{"m":"(uncountable) Something's utility is how useful it is.","e":"The design was to maximise the utility of the book as a whole."}]}]},"diversity":{"h":"diversity","i":"/daɪˈvɜː(r)sɪti/","a":"en-uk-diversity.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"; (singular) Diversity is the property of having many different kinds of things or people.","e":"Racial diversity is very low in Japan and very high in Toronto."}]}]},"name":{"h":"name","i":"/ˈneɪm/","a":"en-us-name.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A name is what a person, place, or thing is called or how it is.","e":"My name is Jack."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To name is to give a name to someone, someplace, or something.","e":"She named her cat Fluffy."}]}]},"attached":{"h":"attached","i":"/əˈtæt͡ʃt/","a":"en-us-attached.ogg","l":"attach","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"To be attached to someone or something means to like someone or something very much.","e":"Many young adults are still as attached to their parents as they were when they were small."}]}]},"attach":{"h":"attach","i":"/əˈtæt͡ʃ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-attach.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you attach x to y, you put x on y so that they will not come apart.","e":"Warnings and instruction should be firmly attached to the container."},{"m":"If you are attached to an office, department, location, etc. you work for that part of the organisation."},{"m":"If a quality such as importance is attached to something, people think the thing has that quality.","e":"There was a great deal of importance attached to being well dressed."},{"m":"If something is attached to something else, there is a strong connection between them.","e":"The promise of more money for the school is attached to better results from the students?"}]}]},"tape":{"h":"tape","i":"/teɪ̯p/","a":"en-us-tape.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Tape is a long thin material, often with glue on one side or used for recording.","e":"We can fix the tear with some tape."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you tape music, a speaker, a TV program, etc., you record it on tape or film.","e":"It is not known who taped the conversation or how."},{"m":"(transitive) If you tape something, you put tape on it.","e":"Can you tape this closed for me?"}]}]},"bond":{"h":"bond","i":"/bɑnd/","a":"en-us-bond.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bond is a connection between two people because of love or friendship.","e":"War can often build strong bonds between people who suffered or fought together."},{"m":"(countable) A bond is a connection between two or more things, for example using glue.","e":"The heat created a bond between the plastic and the metal."},{"m":"(countable) (finance) A bond is a financial document promising to pay a certain amount of money. These are often bought and sold.","e":"The new benchmark ten-year government bond yielded 6.3%."},{"m":"(countable) (plural) Things that tie or limit you.","e":"It took her many years to break free of the bonds of guilt."},{"m":"(countable) A bond is the force that holds atoms together."},{"m":"A contract."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you bond two things, you connect them, for example using glue.","e":"The melting wax bonded to the table."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you bond with someone, you form a special relationship.","e":"Breastfeeding helps the baby bond with its mother."}]}]},"edition":{"h":"edition","i":"/ɪˈdɪʃən/","a":"en-us-edition.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An edition of a book, computer program, etc. is a copy that has been or will be published with changes or in another form.","e":"It was first published in 1857, with a second slightly amended edition in 1858."}]}]},"cite":{"h":"cite","i":"/saɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-cite.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you cite people or facts, you write or talk about them to support your point or show where you got your information.","e":"Larkin (1979) cites cases of families who have moved out of regular homes into mobile homes or campers."},{"m":"If someone is cited by the police, they are ordered to appear before the court."},{"m":"You might cite who you got words, ideas, or information from. This would tell other people where to look to see those people did say it.","e":"He cites Deffenbacher (1985) as suggesting that many of the outcomes are negative."}]}]},"federal":{"h":"federal","i":"/ˈfɛdərəl/","a":"en-us-federal.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"The federal government is the main country-wide government in a country where there are also state or provincial governments.","e":"The federal government has said that it will not increase payments to the provinces."}]}]},"ampersand":{"h":"ampersand","i":"/ˈæmpə(r)sænd/","a":"en-us-ampersand.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An ampersand is a symbol (&) that usually means \"and\".","e":"Billy & Bobby went fishing near the pond. They caught tuna & bass."}]}]},"antique":{"h":"antique","i":"/ænˈtiːk/","a":"en-us-antique.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An antique is something that is old for its type.","e":"This lamp is an antique, it is 200 years old."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is antique, it is older than most things similar to it.","e":"He had his antique car refinished."}]}]},"arbitrary":{"h":"arbitrary","i":"/ˈɑːbɪtrəri/","a":"en-us-arbitrary.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a rule, decision, or act is arbitrary, there is no logical reason for it.","e":"You are protected from arbitrary arrest by police."}]}]},"case":{"h":"case","i":"/keɪs/","a":"en-us-case.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A case is a container to hold something.","e":"He opened the case and pulled out his violin."},{"m":"A case is a matter for police or in court.","e":"The judge did not accept his case."},{"m":"A case is the form of a noun showing how it is used in a sentence.","e":"The word \"he\" is in the subject or nominative case."},{"m":"A case is a person of a certain kind.","e":"That man is sure a hard case."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If a police officer cases a house, he or she watches it until something happens.","e":"We were casing a house all night in Brooklyn."}]}]},"class":{"h":"class","i":"/klɑːs/","a":"en-us-class.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A class is a time for learning.","e":"The history class is interesting."},{"m":"(countable) A class is a group of students.","e":"They are my best class because they are always here on time."},{"m":"Class is a good style or attitude.","e":"You could tell by here clothes that she was a woman of class."},{"m":"A class is a group of members with similar characteristics."},{"m":"A class is a group of people in a society with similar jobs, education, history, and money.","e":"They were both from the upper class and both knew the queen personally."},{"m":"(countable) Something's class is how good it is.","e":"She bought a first-class ticket because she wanted to have the best quality."},{"m":"(countable) An organism's class is its group: mammals, reptiles, insects, arachnids, etc."},{"m":"(countable) A word's class is its syntactic group: noun, verb, adjective, adverb, etc.","e":"Shall belongs to the class of words called \"modal auxiliary verbs\"."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive), If something is classed as a member of a group, it belongs to that group because of some characteristics shared by the group's members.","e":"Although it looks like a motorcycle, it is officially classed as a car."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A class act is high quality.","e":"Most high school coaches are class individuals, and they should get our thanks."}]}]},"polish":{"h":"polish","i":"/ˈpɒlɪʃ/","a":"en-us-polish.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) Someone polishes something when they rub it with a cloth to make it smooth and shiny. Sometimes wax or a special liquid is used.","e":"A wooden floor should be polished with floor wax."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Polish is a special liquid used for polishing things.","e":"I need to buy some polish for polishing my wooden table."}]}]},"pleasure":{"h":"pleasure","i":"/ˈplɛʒə/","a":"en-us-pleasure.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Pleasure is a nice feeling we have when we do something that's fun or that feels good.","e":"Being at this party and seeing my friends again is a real pleasure."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you pleasure someone, you do something for someone to make them feel good."}]}]},"please":{"h":"please","i":"/pliːz/","a":"en-us-please.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"We say \"please\" when we want to ask someone politely to do something.","e":"Pass the salt, please."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Someone pleases someone else when they do what that person likes or wants.","e":"Giving her these flowers will please her."}]}]},"plant":{"h":"plant","i":"/plɑːnt/","a":"en-us-plant.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A plant is something that lives and grows in one place. Plants usually have green leaves and roots. Flowers and trees are plants. Plants and animals are the main kinds of life."},{"m":"A plant is a factory."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To put a seed or plant in soil for it to grow.","e":"I planted some flowers last week and I hope they will grow and blossom."}]}]},"pin":{"h":"pin","i":"/pɪn/","a":"en-ca-pin.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pin is a small, sharp thing used for holding things together."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you pin something, you are fastening it with a pin.","e":"We should pin this poster to that wall."},{"m":"If you pin someone, you force someone firmly onto the ground to prevent them from moving.","e":"A term in wrestling meaning to force an opponent's shoulders to the mat and holding them there for three seconds."}]}]},"peace":{"h":"peace","i":"/piːs/","a":"en-us-peace.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Peace is the way a country is when there is no war.","e":"The people lived in peace for thirty years."},{"m":"(uncountable) Peace is when there is silence or quiet. There is no noise and nothing happening suddenly.","e":"Will you please go away and leave me in peace?"}]}]},"payment":{"h":"payment","i":"/ˈpeɪmənt/","a":"en-us-payment.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A payment is some money that someone is giving to someone else when they're buying something.","e":"I sent the things they wanted, but I haven't gotten the payment for them yet."},{"m":"(uncountable) Payment is the act of paying.","e":"I usually use my credit card for payment."}]}]},"point":{"h":"point","i":"/pɔɪnt/","a":"en-us-point.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A point is a position with no size, or a small dot.","e":"These two lines meet at this point."},{"m":"(countable) A point is the sharp end of a knife or other sharp thing.","e":"He used the point of the knife to make a hole in the can."},{"m":"(countable) The point of something is the reason or purpose for it.","e":"The whole point of coming here was to plant this tree, so let's not go home without doing it."},{"m":"(countable) A point is a dot between two numbers. To the dot's right, you find a decimal.","e":"You need a point between the one and the zero."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To point at something is to hold one finger (or a stick, arrow or other long, thin thing) in the direction of the thing so that people will look at the thing.","e":"He pointed her toward the gate."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"You use point to introduce decimals in a number that is not an integer.","e":"The price has gone up by two point five percent (2.5%)."}]}]},"paste":{"h":"paste","i":"/peɪst/","a":"en-us-paste.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Paste is a thick liquid for sticking (attaching) things together. Paste is like glue, but glue is more liquid and paste is more solid.","e":"He mixed flour and water to make a paste for sticking the paper together."},{"m":"Any very thick liquid, almost solid.","e":"Tomato paste is good in sauce to put on rice or spaghetti."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you paste something in a computer program, you cut or copy it from one place and put a copy of it somewhere else."},{"m":"To stick things together using paste.","e":"She pasted the pictures onto the wall."}]}]},"parcel":{"h":"parcel","i":"/ˈpɑrsəl/","a":"en-us-parcel.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A package; a box wrapped in paper; a thing bigger than a letter that is sent in the mail.","e":"On my birthday, I got a parcel in the mail."},{"m":"A parcel of land is a piece of land that was part of a larger piece."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you parcel something out, you divide it into small parts to give to different people.","e":"The set of books was parcelled out among the people who were there."},{"m":"If you parcel something off, you divide it into small parts to be sold to different people."},{"m":"If you parcel something up, you make it into a parcel by wrapping it up."}]}]},"owner":{"h":"owner","i":"/ˈoʊnɚ/","a":"en-us-owner.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The owner of a thing is the person who owns the thing: who has the thing or who should have the thing. A thing belongs to its owner.","e":"Who is the owner of this coat that was left on a chair?"}]}]},"oven":{"h":"oven","i":"/ˈʌ.vn̩/","a":"en-us-oven.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An oven is for cooking food. It's hot and people put food inside it.","e":"Leave the cake in the oven for thirty minutes."}]}]},"ornament":{"h":"ornament","i":"/ˈɔː(r)nəmənt/","a":"en-us-ornament.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An ornament is something that is put onto something or someone just to look beautiful and for no other reason.","e":"One ring on her finger was the only ornament she wore."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you ornament something, you decorate or add to it.","e":"Let's ornament the tree with lights to make it more festive."}]}]},"order":{"h":"order","i":"/ˈɔːdə/","a":"en-us-order.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Order is when things are where they should be.","e":"I need to take some time to put my things in order."},{"m":"(countable) The order of some things means which thing is first, which one is second, which one is last, etc.","e":"The children will take turns in order of age."},{"m":"(countable) An order is a group of religious people, such as monks or nuns, who follow certain rules.","e":"St. Ignatius Loyola founded the Jesuit order in 1537."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To order something is to ask someone to sell it to you.","e":"At the restaurant, she ordered chicken and potatoes."},{"m":"(transitive) To order someone to do something is to tell the person that they must do it.","e":"The father ordered his children to be quiet."},{"m":"(transitive) To order things is to put them in a certain order.","e":"We need to order them alphabetically."}]}]},"other":{"h":"other","i":"/ˈaðə/","a":"en-us-other.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"The other people or things, are those apart from the ones we have or were talking about.","e":"No, don't put it on this table. Put it on the other table."},{"m":"more","e":"There are many other kinds of problems."},{"m":"different","e":"There were some other cars at their house the other day."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Others are those apart from the ones we have or were talking about.","e":"Thanks for the books. I'll get the others tomorrow."}]}]},"only":{"h":"only","i":"/əʊnliː/","a":"en-us-only.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"no more than; no other than; just","e":"There are only three schools in this town."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Just one or just a few; this and no other; no more than this.","e":"She is the only woman doctor in this city."},{"m":"An only child, son, girl, etc. has no brothers or sisters."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"(informal) You use only to introduce a fact that prevents a statement from being completely true.","e":"They probably could do it, only you never let them try."}]}]},"observation":{"h":"observation","i":"/ˌɑbzɚˈveɪʃən/","a":"en-us-observation.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Observation is the act of carefully seeing things that happen.","e":"To learn, you must be good at observation."},{"m":"(countable) An observation is something someone saw, heard etc.","e":"In science, we record our observations so we can think about them later."}]}]},"note":{"h":"note","i":"/nəʊt/","a":"en-us-note.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A note is a single sound in music.","e":"In this song, every word is on a different note."},{"m":"(countable) A note is a short letter; something written on a small piece of paper.","e":"If you go out, leave me a note to tell me where you went."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"You note that something happened when you see that it happened and remember it.","e":"I noted that you weren't wearing shoes."}]}]},"north":{"h":"north","i":"/nɔːθ/","a":"en-uk-north.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"North is the direction towards the top of the Earth, opposite to south; If you are looking north, the sun sets on your left.","e":"Canada is the biggest country in North America."},{"m":"North is the end of a magnet that points north."},{"m":"The north is the area of land north of the speaker; Also the Arctic."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"In the direction north; towards the north","e":"The place you want is two miles north of here."}]}]},"news":{"h":"news","i":"/n(j)uːz/","a":"en-us-news.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) News is information about things that happened a short time ago, especially on the radio, TV or in newspapers.","e":"Did you hear the news that the war just ended?"}]}]},"net":{"h":"net","i":"/nɛt/","a":"en-us-net.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A net is a thing made of ropes or string that lets small things through but keeps big things in.","e":"I forgot my fishing net. What will we use to catch fish now?"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To net something is to catch it in a net.","e":"He netted a big fish."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A company's net income is its profits minus its expenses."}]}]},"nerve":{"h":"nerve","i":"/nɝv/","a":"en-us-nerve.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A nerve is a cell in the body that sends signals. The brain is made of nerves.","e":"She can't feel anything with this arm, and can't move her arm, because the nerves were cut in an accident."},{"m":"(uncountable) Nerve is confidence: a feeling of being able to do something.","e":"He didn't have the nerve to ask her to dance."}]}]},"needle":{"h":"needle","i":"/'niː.dl/","a":"en-us-needle.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (sewing) A needle is a small, long, thin sharp metal thing with a hole in it, used for sewing.","e":"She used a needle and blue thread to fix the hole in the shirt."},{"m":"(countable) A needle is a long, thing, sharp metal thing for putting drugs into a person through the skin.","e":"The doctor used the needle to inject the medicine into the patient."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To tease; to make fun of.","e":"Billy needled his sister incessantly about her pimples."}]}]},"compliment":{"h":"compliment","i":"/ˈkɒmplɪmənt/","a":"en-us-compliment.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A compliment is a few words of praise: saying that someone or something is good in some way.","e":"William gave me a compliment and that made me feel good. He told me my hair was nice."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Compliment means to praise someone.","e":"She complimented him on his clothes because they looked good."}]}]},"conjunction":{"h":"conjunction","i":"/kənˈdʒʌŋkʃən/","a":"en-us-conjunction.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A conjunction is a word used to join words, phrases, clauses, or sentences.","e":"The word or is a conjunction because it can join two words: Tell me if you see a red or blue car."}]}]},"conviction":{"h":"conviction","i":"/kənˈvɪkʃən/","a":"en-us-conviction.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A conviction is when a court finds a person guilty of doing a crime.","e":"There was a conviction in his case, so he went to jail."},{"m":"(countable) A conviction is a strong belief that you think is true.","e":"Because of their strong conviction, I begin to feel that they may be right."}]}]},"peaceful":{"h":"peaceful","i":"/'piːsfəl/","a":"en-us-peaceful.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A place or person is peaceful when there is silence or quiet. There is no noise and nothing happening suddenly."}]}]},"need":{"h":"need","i":"/niːd/","a":"en-us-need.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you need something, you want it and must have it.","e":"Everyone needs food and water."},{"m":"If you need to do something, it is very important for you to do it.","e":"Sir, you need to leave now."},{"m":"If you need do something, you have to do it.","e":"Need you do that all the time?"}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) If you have a need for something, you must have it; something necessary or required.","e":"I've always tried to have few needs beyond food, clothing and shelter."}]}]},"necessary":{"h":"necessary","i":"/ˈnɛsəˌsɛri/","a":"en-us-necessary.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something is necessary if people need it. It must happen or there will be a big problem.","e":"It's necessary to stop when you see a red light."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A necessary is a bathroom."}]}]},"natural":{"h":"natural","i":"/ˈnætʃ.ə.rəl/","a":"en-us-natural.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something is natural if people didn't make it.","e":"s, plants and rocks are natural things."},{"m":"Something is natural if it's the way it usually is, without people changing it, or is a way that is not a surprise.","e":"It's only natural for you to think that."}]}]},"nail":{"h":"nail","i":"/neɪl/","a":"en-us-nail.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A nail is a small, long, thin sharp metal thing for holding wood together. People put it into the wood by hitting it with a hammer.","e":"I need some nails to fix the roof."},{"m":"(countable) A nail is the thick, hard part at the ends of fingers and toes.","e":"I broke the top off my finger nail and it was very painful."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you nail something to something else, you use a nail to join them.","e":"He nailed the set of shelves onto the wall."},{"m":"When someone gets an idea just right, we say they nailed it or \"hit the nail on the head\".","e":"I think you've nailed the reason why this isn't working."}]}]},"muscle":{"h":"muscle","i":"/ˈmʌ.səl/","a":"en-us-muscle.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A muscle is a part of the body of a person or animal. It's a part that pulls to make parts of the body move.","e":"He can lift heavy things because he has strong muscles."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To muscle is to use strength or muscles to do something.","e":"He muscled his way into the room between the people who were trying to stop him."}]}]},"moon":{"h":"moon","i":"/muːn/","a":"en-us-moon.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The moon is the shining white and grey object in the sky at night. It appears to change shape from round (a full moon) to a crescent and back again. It's like a small planet that goes around the Earth.","e":"I was able to see the road because there was a full moon that night."},{"m":"A moon is a thing like a small planet that goes around another planet.","e":"Galileo saw four moons of Jupiter: Callisto, Europa, Ganymede and Io."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you moon someone, you show them your bare buttocks.","e":"Someone in the car pulled down their pants and mooned us as they drove past."}]}]},"monkey":{"h":"monkey","i":"/ˈmʌŋki/","a":"en-us-monkey.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A monkey is a primate with a long tail that climbs trees.","e":"We saw Vervet monkeys in the Zoo."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you monkey something, you make changes to it.","e":"I foolishly monkeyed with the control panel and it ended up exploding."}]}]},"minute":{"h":"minute","i":"/ˈmɪnɪt/","a":"en-us-minute-noun.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A minute is a short time equal to sixty seconds. There are sixty minutes in one hour.","e":"He ran the race in 1 minute and ten seconds."},{"m":"(uncountable) A minute is a short time.","e":"Please wait a minute while I get my coat and then I will come with you."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Minute things are small.","e":"The pictures appear similar, with only a few, minute differences."}]}]},"mind":{"h":"mind","i":"/maɪnd/","a":"en-us-mind.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Someone's mind is the part of them that thinks.","e":"In my mind I know I must go, but in my heart I want to stay here."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you mind some action or thing, you feel negatively about it.","e":"\"Do you mind if I sit here?\" \"No, not at all\""},{"m":"If you mind someone or something, you look after it.","e":"\"Could you mind the children while I go to the bathroom?\""}]}]},"military":{"h":"military","i":"/ˈmɪl.ɪ.trɪ/","a":"en-us-military.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is military, it is a characteristic of people in the armed forces.","e":"Sick soldiers go to the military hospital."},{"m":"If something is military, it is about armed forces such as the army, marines, navy, or air force."},{"m":"If something is military, it has to do with war."},{"m":"If something is military, it has to do with armies and ground troops."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A military is armed forces."},{"m":"(US); (with \"the\") The military is the United States armed forces in general.","e":"It's not the job of the military to make policy."}]}]},"middle":{"h":"middle","i":"/ˈmɪdəl/","a":"en-us-middle.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The place that is between two things; the place that is halfway between two ends of something.","e":"Cut the wood exactly in the middle to get two pieces of equal size."}]}]},"memory":{"h":"memory","i":"/ˈmɛm(ə)ri/","a":"en-us-memory.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"When someone remembers something, we call the thing they remember a memory.","e":"I have very nice memories of the time when my children were young."},{"m":"The part of the mind that remembers; the act of remembering.","e":"When we get older, our memory isn't as good."},{"m":"The part of a computer that holds information."}]}]},"meeting":{"h":"meeting","i":"/ˈmiːtɪŋ/","a":"en-us-meeting.ogg","l":"meet","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A meeting is when a group of people come together to talk about something important.","e":"The meeting will be in the green room after lunch. I hope you'll be there."}]}]},"married":{"h":"married","i":"/mæriːd/","a":"en-us-married.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A man and a woman are married if they are husband and wife to each other. Usually when two people are married they live in the same house and they often have children. Two people have a special day to become married.","e":"I don't need to meet more young men—I'm already married."},{"m":"If two things are married they have been made into one thing.","e":"Music and television are married in music videos."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"The past and past participle of marry."}]}]},"mark":{"h":"mark","i":"/mɑːk/","a":"en-us-mark.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A mark is a single line left by a pen or pencil, or any small bit of color that got onto something.","e":"You have a mark on your shirt from that tomato sauce you were eating."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you mark something, you put a mark on it.","e":"The big rock marked the side of the car a little when she drove too close to it."},{"m":"If you mark something, you notice it or pay attention to it.","e":"Mark my words!"}]}]},"love":{"h":"love","i":"/lʌv/","a":"en-us-love.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When someone loves another person, they feel good about the person and want the person to be happy.","e":"I love Colin."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The feeling of loving someone and caring for them.","e":"Is my love for him a real love that will last a long time?"},{"m":"To love someone or something means to like someone or something very much.","e":"I love the simple English Wikipedia."},{"m":"(tennis) A tennis player who has scored love has a score of zero.","e":"(From a sports commentator) Fifteen-love!"}]}]},"loss":{"h":"loss","i":"/lɒs/","a":"en-us-loss.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A loss happens when something goes where people can't find it. People don't know where the thing is or they don't have it any more.","e":"The loss of my keys means I can't go into my house today."},{"m":"Loss is when someone's loved one dies. When someone dies, they are no longer with you.","e":"I loss both of my grandparents from old age."},{"m":"(baseball) A loss (shown as L) is charged to the pitcher of the losing team."}]}]},"look":{"h":"look","i":"/lʊk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-look.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) Someone looks at something when they move their head or move their eyes so that they can see the thing.","e":"Look at this picture! Isn't it beautiful?"},{"m":"(intransitive) The way that something looks is the way that it appears.","e":"A new car looks very nice until it gets dirty."}]}]},"lock":{"h":"lock","i":"/lɒk/","a":"en-us-lock.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A lock is a metal thing on a door (or on a window, drawer, etc.) that stops people from opening the door unless they have the right key to open it.","e":"No one will take things from my house. I have a very strong lock on the door."},{"m":"(countable) A lock is two or more gates (doors) in water to let boats move from lower water to higher water or the other way."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Someone locks a door when they close the lock with a key so that no one can come in.","e":"Remember to lock the door when you leave the house."}]}]},"living":{"h":"living","i":"/lɪvɪŋ/","a":"en-us-living.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A way of earning money.","e":"What do you do for a living?"}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A living thing is a person, animal or plant that is not dead—it is still able to function and grow.","e":"Living things grow and make more living things like themselves."}]}]},"linen":{"h":"linen","i":"/ˈlɪnɪn/","a":"en-us-linen.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Linen is a material that some cloth is made of. It comes from the flax plant, and in the past, bed sheets were often made from it, before cotton was used.","e":"This shirt is made of linen."},{"m":"(plural) Linens are something made from linen, especially bed sheets.","e":"Would you like to change the linens on your bed?"}]}]},"line":{"h":"line","i":"/laɪn/","a":"en-us-line.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A line is a mark that is long, straight and very thin.","e":"She drew a line down the middle of the page to divide the page into two parts."},{"m":"A line is a row.","e":"Put the buttons in a straight line on the front of the shirt."},{"m":"A line is a row of people who are waiting for something in order; a queue.","e":"You got here last, so you have to stand at the back of the line."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Someone lines things up when they put them in a straight line or row."},{"m":"Someone lines something up when they put it just in the right place or at the edge of something.","e":"Line up the end of the piece of wood with the edge of the table."},{"m":"Someone lines up when they start waiting in a line (queue) with other people.","e":"Everyone line up here, please, and I'll help you one at a time."},{"m":"Someone lines something when they mark it with one or more lines.","e":"Please line the pitch before the match."},{"m":"Someone lines something when they add an inside layer of material (liner) to it."}]}]},"lift":{"h":"lift","i":"/lɪft/","a":"en-us-lift.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Someone lifts something when they use their hands to make the thing go up.","e":"He lifted the little boy onto his shoulders."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"If you give someone a lift, you drive them somewhere, usually in your car."},{"m":"(countable) A lift is a machine that lifts people up or down to different parts of a building."}]}]},"level":{"h":"level","a":"en-us-level.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Even, flat, straight, smooth, horizontal. Having all parts equally as high as all other parts.","e":"This table is not level: things are rolling off it."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If one thing is level with another, they are at the same height.","e":"The bookshelf is level with the top of the door frame."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A level is a place that is higher or lower than some other places.","e":"The room you want is on the third level of this building."},{"m":"A tool for finding out whether a surface is level."}]}]},"laugh":{"h":"laugh","i":"/lɑːf/","a":"en-us-laugh.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Someone laughs when they make a sound with their mouth because they think something is funny. It can sound like \"ha ha\", \"ho ho\", \"hee hee\", etc.","e":"That was a really good joke. I've never laughed so hard!"}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The sound of someone laughing, or the action of laughing.","e":"We had lots of good laughs at the party."}]}]},"last":{"h":"last","i":"/lɑːst/","a":"en-us-last.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Happening or coming after all other similar things or people.","e":"I was the last person to go there: when I went, the others were all already there."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) To endure, continue over time.","e":"Summer seems to last longer each year."},{"m":"(intransitive) To hold out, continue undefeated or entire.","e":"I don't know how much longer we can last without reinforcements."}]},{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"Last week, month, year, etc. is the one that comes before this one.","e":"I didn't see you last week."}]}]},"interest":{"h":"interest","i":"/ˈɪntrɛst/","a":"en-us-interest.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An interest is when a person wants to know more about someone or something or likes someone or something or likes to do something.","e":"She has a strong interest in art. She is going to go to an art school."},{"m":"(countable) An interest is when someone or something is important to a person, or if good things happening to the thing are good for the person.","e":"Because I own a house on this street, I have an interest in keeping the street clean."},{"m":"(uncountable) When someone borrows money, they have to give back more money than they borrowed. The extra money they have to pay is called interest.","e":"The bank gives me two percent interest per year on the money in my account."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If a person is interested, they are curious and want to find out about someone or something.","e":"I am interested in researching flowers."}]}]},"limit":{"h":"limit","i":"/ˈlɪmɪt/","a":"en-us-limit.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The limit is the edge of how far something can go. It can go up to the limit but no farther.","e":"This fence is at the limit of my property."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To make something stay inside a limit.","e":"The fence limits the cows from going out of the field."},{"m":"(transitive) If you limit someone, you reduce or take away their freedom."}]}]},"twenty":{"h":"twenty","i":"/twɛniː/","a":"en-uk-twenty.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(ordinal twentieth) The number 20.","e":"I was in university when I was twenty years old."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A twenty is a 20 dollar bill.","e":"I'd like my $50 as 1 twenty, 2 tens and 2 fives."},{"m":"\"Twenty\" is short for 10-20, meaning location.","e":"Jason, what's your twenty?"}]}]},"thirty":{"h":"thirty","i":"/ˈθɜːti/","a":"en-uk-thirty.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(ordinal thirtieth) The number 30.","e":"I had my first child when I was thirty years old."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The number 30.","e":"tens is thirty."}]}]},"scope":{"h":"scope","i":"/ˈskəʊp/","a":"en-us-scope.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The scope of a book, a law, a duty, etc. is how much is included or how far it can go.","e":"The small budget has limited the scope of the research."},{"m":"(countable) A scope is an instrument for looking at things, e.g., a telescope or a microscope."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you scope something (out), you look at it carefully.","e":"I scoped out the place last week. It seems nice."}]}]},"enhance":{"h":"enhance","i":"/ɪnˈhɑːns/","a":"en-us-enhance.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you enhance something, you make it bigger or better.","e":"He can greatly enhance his reputation by winning tonight."}]}]},"control":{"h":"control","i":"/kənˈtrəʊl/","a":"en-us-control.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) If you have control over someone or something, you can make it do what you want.","e":"He should try to take control and tell the other handlers what to do."},{"m":"(countable) A control is a button, switch, dial, etc. that lets you make a machine do what you want.","e":"If you turn off your TV with the remote control, it continues to use a quarter of normal power."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you control something, you make it do what you want.","e":"Too many people are overweight because they can't control their eating behaviour."},{"m":"(transitive) If you control something, you do not let its numbers or size grow too much.","e":"The new plan should control inflation."}]}]},"high":{"h":"high","i":"/haɪ/","a":"en-us-high.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is high, it is a long way up.","e":"The airplane flew very high."},{"m":"If something is high, its top is a long way up.","e":"That is the highest mountain near here."},{"m":"If something is high, it is very good. It might be better or more important than other things. This can often means someone has more power.","e":"The Supreme Court is the highest court in America."},{"m":"If someone is high, that person's mind is affected by drugs.","e":"John was high from marijuana last night."}]}]},"lead":{"h":"lead","i":"/liːd/","a":"en-us-lead-guide.oga","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A lead is a wire or strap attached to something.","e":"The dog can't go far because it's on a short lead."},{"m":"(uncountable) Lead is a very heavy gray metal. It's a chemical symbol is Pb.","e":"This box is so heavy, it feels as if it's full of lead."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Someone is leading other people if the person is going first and the other people are following or coming after.","e":"Please lead us to the house, because you know how to go there."},{"m":"Showing or telling other people what to do.","e":"He moves that little stick in the air to lead the people making music."}]}]},"hadith":{"h":"hadith","i":"[həˈdiːθ]","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-hadith.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A written record of a saying or action of the. Used as a basis for conduct in Islamic practices."}]}]},"insurance":{"h":"insurance","i":"/ɪn.ˈʃʊr.əns/","a":"en-us-insurance.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Insurance is an agreement where someone pays a small amount of money, and if something bad happens, they get money to help them.","e":"I have fire insurance for my house."}]}]},"instrument":{"h":"instrument","i":"/ˈɪnstrʌmənt/","a":"en-us-instrument.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An instrument is any thing people hold in their hand and use to do something.","e":"A hammer is a heavy instrument."},{"m":"(countable) An instrument is something used to play music.","e":"I enjoy playing music, my favorite instrument is the guitar."}]}]},"increase":{"h":"increase","i":"/ɪnˈkriːs/","a":"en-us-increase-verb.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To grow; to become bigger.","e":"The amount of money in my bank account is increasing."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The amount which something has grown.","e":"There was an increase in movie releases last year."}]}]},"industry":{"h":"industry","i":"/ˈɪndəstri/","a":"en-us-industry.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An industry is a kind of work that makes things.","e":"Many people in this country have jobs in the clothing industry."},{"m":"(uncountable) Industry is the quality of working hard, trying hard and doing it well.","e":"Because of her industry, she made a lot of money."}]}]},"humor":{"h":"humor","i":"/ˈhjuː.mə(r)/","a":"en-us-humor.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Humor is ideas that make people laugh: jokes, funny things.","e":"I like the stories she tells because they're full of humor."}]}]},"how":{"h":"how","i":"/haʊ/","a":"en-us-how.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"The word how is used to ask about the way something happens or the way people do things.","e":"How will we ever solve this problem?"},{"m":"The word how is used to tell about the way something happens or the way people do things.","e":"I know how we can solve this problem."},{"m":"(exclamation) The word how is used to show that you feel strongly about something.","e":"How old he looks!"}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"You use how to ask if something was good or bad, or what qualities it has.","e":"How was the movie?"}]}]},"horn":{"h":"horn","i":"/hɔːn/","a":"en-us-horn.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A horn is a long, sharp thing that grows on the head of some animals such as goats and sheep.","e":"The goat used its horn to break the fence."},{"m":"(countable) A horn is a musical instrument that you blow and usually made of metal."}]}]},"hope":{"h":"hope","i":"/həʊp/","a":"en-us-hope.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) When someone hopes that something will happen, it means that they want it to happen and they think it may happen.","e":"We hope that more women will decide to join the course."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A hope is the idea in someone's mind when they're hoping for something.","e":"All of my hopes came true!"}]}]},"hook":{"h":"hook","i":"/hʊk/","a":"en-us-hook.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hook is a curved, sharp thing, usually made of metal and often small. Someone can put the hook through a hole in something to grip it so that they can pull the thing."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you are hooking something, you are attaching it to a hook.","e":"Hook the bag here, and the conveyor will carry it away."}]}]},"history":{"h":"history","i":"/ˈhɪst(ə)ri/","a":"en-us-history.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) History is what happened in the past.","e":"China has many old books about its history."},{"m":"(uncountable) History is the study of what happened in the past.","e":"He is a professor of history."},{"m":"If somebody or something makes history, they do something very important that will not be forgotten.","e":"She made history by becoming Africa's first elected female president."},{"m":"If somebody or something goes down in history, they are remembered by people because they were very important or well known.","e":"She'll go down in history as one of our greatest writers."},{"m":"(countable) A history is a book recording things that have happened.","e":"He was reading a history of Ancient Rome."},{"m":"If somebody or something has a history of something, it's very common for them.","e":"She has a history of cheating on tests."},{"m":"If you say something is history, you mean it's finished, over, dead, or not important any more.","e":"OK, that game's history."},{"m":"If you say the rest is history, you mean you don't have to tell about because everyone already knows.","e":"They just happened to run into each other at the right time, and the rest is history."}]}]},"help":{"h":"help","i":"/hɛlp/","a":"en-us-help.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you help another person do something, you do things to make it easier for them to do the thing, or you do part of it for them.","e":"Will you please help me wash the dishes?"},{"m":"If you can't help doing something or can't help but do it, you cannot avoid it. You do it even without wanting or planning to.","e":"When I look at the class, I can not help feeling that something has gone wrong."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Help is the act of helping.","e":"Will you please give me some help? This is hard for just one person to do."},{"m":"(uncountable) The help is people who work in a home cooking, cleaning, etc.","e":"The help arrives as 9 o' clock."}]}]},"healthy":{"h":"healthy","i":"/ˈhɛl.θi/","a":"en-us-healthy.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A healthy person is someone who is not sick. They are strong and will probably live a long time.","e":"I need three young, healthy people to help me."},{"m":"Healthy things leads to better health.","e":"Healthy food is full of vitamins and minerals."}]}]},"harbor":{"h":"harbor","i":"/ˈhɑ:bə/","a":"en-us-harbor.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A harbor is some water in a curve of land where it's safe for boats because there are no big waves.","e":"A ship in the harbor is safe -- but that is not what ships are for."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To provide a [[#Noun|harbor]] or safe place for something or someone.","e":"The old docks once harbored all kinds of ships, but they have been closed for years now."},{"m":"(intransitive) To take refuge or shelter somewhere.","e":"The ships harbor in the bay during the winter months."},{"m":"(transitive) To hold onto an idea.","e":"Sam has harbored resentment against Joe since Joe got the job they both applied for."}]}]},"drop":{"h":"drop","i":"/drɒp/","a":"en-us-drop.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A drop is a very small amount of a liquid.","e":"A drop of water weighs 0.1 grams."},{"m":"A drop is the fall of something.","e":"There was a drop in the prices last week."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To fall, or to let something fall.","e":"He dropped from the roof when he was running."}]}]},"heat":{"h":"heat","i":"/hi:t/","a":"en-us-heat.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Heat is a kind of energy. It is the quality things have when they are warm or hot.","e":"This is a good coat. It keeps the heat in."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To make something hot.","e":"I just need to heat up the food and then we can eat."}]}]},"gun":{"h":"gun","i":"/ɡʌn/","a":"en-us-gun.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A gun is a weapon that sends bullets through its metal tube.","e":"was shot by a gun."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To make an engine work fast by opening its throttle.","e":"I gunned the engine and passed his car."},{"m":"If someone is gunned down, they are shot by something, usually a gun.","e":"He was gunned down by a hitman."}]}]},"garden":{"h":"garden","i":"/ˈɡɑːdən/","a":"en-us-garden.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A garden is a place where flowers and other plants grow where people want them to. Frequently it is a small place with a wall around it, near a house. It may have rocks and other things in it to look beautiful.","e":"She spends a lot of time taking care of the flowers in her garden."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you garden, you work in a garden, especially your own garden around your house.","e":"He joined his mother when she gardened and talked to her flowers."}]}]},"from":{"h":"from","i":"/frɒm/","a":"en-us-from.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"When something is from someone, the person gave or sent it.","e":"I got a gift from my grandmother today."},{"m":"When someone is from a place, that's where they started.","e":"I am Chinese. I come from Hunan province."},{"m":"You use from to talk about distances between thing in space or time.","e":"Saturn is far from earth."}]}]},"existence":{"h":"existence","i":"/ɛɡˈzɪstɛnts/","a":"en-us-existence.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The existence of a thing is the quality of being real, of being in the world, of just being.","e":"Do you believe in the existence of God?"}]}]},"general":{"h":"general","i":"/ˈd͡ʒɛnrəl/","a":"en-us-general.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Usual; about most things. An idea is a general idea if it's about many things or about most things, not just about one specific thing.","e":"First I will talk about general problems of farming, and then I will talk about the specific problems of wheat farming."},{"m":"General is approximate, not exact; maybe a little different; close but maybe not the same."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A general is the leader of an army.","e":"The president told the general to bring the army home."}]}]},"give":{"h":"give","i":"/gɪv/","a":"en-us-give.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you give something to someone else, you had the thing and you let the other person have it. Maybe you use your hands to put the thing in the other person's hands. Usually after that, the thing is the other person's thing.","e":"Give me that book, please; I want to read it."},{"m":"If you give a speech, you talk to a group of people."}]}]},"come":{"h":"come","i":"/kʌm/","a":"en-uk-to come.ogg","l":"come","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To move towards a place or into a place; to move to the place where the person who is talking is.","e":"Come to my house and I will give you something to eat."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"When something happens or arrives.","e":"We'll talk again come January."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":".","e":"(also spelled cum)"}]}]},"go":{"h":"go","i":"/gəʊ/","a":"en-us-go.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you go, you move in space, especially to or through a place.","e":"I go to the seashore every summer."},{"m":"If you go, you move in time, often in your mind.","e":"You have to go back to 1911 to find a wetter day."},{"m":"If you go, you move on the computer, the internet, or in the memory.","e":"Then go to the C: drive."},{"m":"If you go, you move a certain distance or a certain way.","e":"We've gone 10 kilometers today."},{"m":"If you go, you leave or move away.","e":"Please don't go."},{"m":"If you go bad, wild, blind, etc., you become like that.","e":"Jim went blind."}]}]},"clear":{"h":"clear","i":"/klɪə/","a":"en-us-clear.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A clear idea is an idea that is easy to understand.","e":"OK, so you need the key. I see. That's clear now."},{"m":"If it is clear that something is a certain way, there can be no mistake about it.","e":"The women made it clear that they were doing this only because they wanted to."},{"m":"If you are clear about something, you understand it well.","e":"Mike, I want to be clear about what you said, so can you tell me again."},{"m":"If you are clear about something, you make it easy for people to understand you.","e":"The coach had been very clear about what he wanted them to do."},{"m":"If your head or your thinking is clear, then you can think well.","e":"After his coffee and a quick walk, his head felt clear."},{"m":"If something is clear, people can see through it.","e":"The window is made of clear glass."},{"m":"If something is clear, it has nothing that gets in your way.","e":"I try to drive to work only when the roads are clear."},{"m":"If something is clear, it is easy to see or hear.","e":"The picture wasn't clear enough to see whose face it was."},{"m":"If your skin is clear, it has no spots on it.","e":"Her deep honey skin was clear except for the small mark on her left cheek."},{"m":"If your eyes are clear, they are healthy, bright, and lively.","e":"His eyes were sharp and clear, and full of fun."},{"m":"Clear profit is profit after tax.","e":"These are priced so high that the manufacturers pocket $8,000 clear profit per $30,000 unit."},{"m":"If you have a clear conscience or your conscience is clear, you do not feel guilty.","e":"I sleep perfectly at night. I have a clear conscience. I don't have blood on my hands."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you clear something, you move or remove things that you don't want there.","e":"You clear the table and I'll get coffee ready."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something clears, it becomes clear.","e":"After the fire, it took some time for the air to clear."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something clears, it goes away, leaving the place it was clear.","e":"After the fire, it took some time for the smoke to clear."},{"m":"(transitive) If you clear your throat, you cough lightly to make speaking easier.","e":"Tears filled her eyes again, and she cleared her throat. \"As soon as I can, I'll get on a plane and meet you.\""},{"m":"If you clear the air, or if the air clears, you talk about a problem so that nobody has doubts or bad feelings.","e":"I think it's important for me to tell you what has happened and clear the air about this matter."},{"m":"(transitive) If you clear somebody to do something, you give them permission.","e":"His personal plane had been cleared to land at the airport."},{"m":"If your head, mind, thinking, etc. clears then you become able to think well.","e":"The coffee helped to clear her head, and she sat down to think."},{"m":"(transitive) If you clear something, you get over it without touching it or without a problem.","e":"The bike got air and cleared the water by a meter."},{"m":"(transitive) If you clear somebody of something bad you show that they did not do it.","e":"After clearing him of any wrongdoing, the police set him free."},{"m":"(transitive) If you clear a hurdle, you solve one of a number of problems.","e":"The case has many more hurdles to clear before it can go to trial."},{"m":"After the dust clears is some time later, when there is no more trouble or confusion.","e":"It took a few weeks, but after the dust had cleared, and everybody had gone home, he realized he had enjoyed it."},{"m":"If a cheque clears, then the money is ready to be used."},{"m":"(transitive) If you clear a certain amount of money, you make that as profit (after expenses)."},{"m":"(transitive) If you clear the ball or puck, you move it away from your own goal."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Out of, away from, especially too far away to be noticed or caught.","e":"After a short walk, we were clear of the town."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"(before a preposition) Completely, without limit.","e":"You could see clear across the water, all the way to the church 60&nbsp;km away on the other side."}]}]},"cover":{"h":"cover","i":"/ˈkʌvɚ/","a":"en-us-cover.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Something that is covering another thing is on top of (or over) the other thing in a way that stops people from seeing it.","e":"I cover myself in two blankets at night to stay warm."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cover is something that usually covers something else.","e":"The cover of the book has a picture on it under the name of the book."}]}]},"crack":{"h":"crack","i":"/kræk/","a":"en-us-crack.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When something cracks it breaks along a line, maybe not a straight line. It might break into two pieces, or it might break but the two pieces are still attached.","e":"She cracked an egg and put the inside of the egg into a bowl."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A crack is the line where something is breaking.","e":"There is a crack from the edge of this plate to the middle. It will break soon."},{"m":"A loud sound like the sound of something breaking.","e":"It was raining, and she saw a flash of lightning and heard the crack of thunder."},{"m":"A strong, fairly cheap form of cocaine; crack often comes in the form of a rock and it is usually smoked in a crack-pipe.","e":"\"I wouldn't use it, if I was going to use it I can afford real cocaine. Crack is wack.\" -"}]}]},"grip":{"h":"grip","i":"/ɡrɪp/","a":"en-us-grip.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Someone grips a thing by holding it tightly in their hand.","e":"He gripped the rope and pulled."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A hold or a way of holding something","e":"It's good to have a firm grip when shaking hands."},{"m":"A handle or a place to grip.","e":"There are several good grips on the northern face of this rock."}]}]},"bassist":{"h":"bassist","i":"/ˈbeɪs.ɪst/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bassist is someone who plays a bass instrument or sings bass.","e":"The bassist sat his guitar down."}]}]},"nobody":{"h":"nobody","i":"/ˈnoʊ.bə.di/","a":"en-us-nobody.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"no person","e":"Nobody would do something like that."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A nobody is a person who is not important.","e":"Bob called Alice a nobody."}]}]},"humour":{"h":"humour","i":"/ˈhjuː.mə(r)/","a":"en-us-humor.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Humour is ideas that make people laugh: jokes, funny things.","e":"I like the stories she tells because they're full of humour."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To humour someone is to agree with them only to make the them happy."}]}]},"harbour":{"h":"harbour","i":"/ˈhɑ:bə/","a":"en-us-harbor.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A harbour is some water in a curve of land where it's safe for boats because there are no big waves.","e":"A ship in the harbour is safe -- but that is not what ships are for."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To provide a [[#Noun|harbour]] or safe place for something or someone.","e":"The old docks once harboured all kinds of ships, but they have been closed for years now."},{"m":"(intransitive) To take refuge or shelter somewhere.","e":"The ships harbour in the bay during the winter months."},{"m":"(transitive) To hold onto an idea.","e":"Sam has harboured resentment against Joe since Joe got the job they both applied for."}]}]},"incorporate":{"h":"incorporate","i":"/ɪŋˈkɔː(r).pər.eɪt/","a":"en-ca-incorporate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If x incorporates y, y is part of x.","e":"All the Wilsons ladies' clubs incorporate features designed to help women players improve and enjoy their game."},{"m":"If you incorporate x into y, you make x part of y.","e":"Please incorporate these changes into the final book."},{"m":"An incorporated company is a corporation. Often written Inc. as part of a company name.","e":"We were a partnership for many years, but we incorporated last year."}]}]},"given":{"h":"given","i":"/'gɪvən/","a":"en-us-given.ogg","l":"give","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Given x means if x is true, happened, exists, etc.","e":"Given our current problems, I don't think we can spend any more."},{"m":"Given that-clause means in consideration of the fact that-clause.","e":"Given that they are inexperienced, they've done a good job."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is given to doing something, they do it regularly.","e":"My father's given to making long speeches about when he was a boy."},{"m":"If someone is given to something, they wear, use, or do it often.","e":"When she got older, she was given to elegant clothes and long speeches."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A given is something that you accept as true.","e":"We need to make a decision about where we will live after this, but selling this house is a given."}]}]},"subsidiary":{"h":"subsidiary","i":"/sʌbˈsɪ.di.ər.i/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-subsidiary.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A subsidiary is a company that is owned by a larger company. {[ant|parent}}","e":"This company owns three subsidiaries that make different kinds of machines."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is subsidiary, it is connected, but lower in importance, rank, or level, etc.","e":"Surprisingly, the subsidiary company became more successful than the parent company."}]}]},"input":{"h":"input","i":"/'ɪnpʊt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-input.wav","l":"input","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The input is the information that is put into something.","e":"Everyone who is affected should have a chance to provide input."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you input something (often into a computer) you put it in.","e":"If the text has been correctly input to the computer, there should be no problems."}]}]},"abstract":{"h":"abstract","i":"/ˈæbˌstrækt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-abstract (noun).wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is abstract, you cannot touch it, and it is difficult to imagine or think about.","e":"A lot of abstract painting uses harsh shapes and most people do not like it."},{"m":"(logic) If something is abstract, it is general."},{"m":"If something is abstract, it is thought of as apart from any other use with an object; it is removed from it; it is separate or abstracted."},{"m":"If something is abstract, it is not practical or realistic; it is not concrete; it is theoretical; it is vague."},{"m":"If something is abstract, it does not have all of the facts; it is not factual."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An abstract is a short text that tells you the main ideas of a longer text, especially of scientific papers; it is a summary of something longer.","e":"The abstract of Isaac Newton's laws of gravity may be no more than 150 words."},{"m":"(countable) An abstract is an abstraction; it is an abstract word."},{"m":"(countable); (art) An abstract is a piece of art that is made in the abstract fashion of art."},{"m":"(countable); An abstract is a powdered solid extract of a vegetable that is then mixed with the sugar of milk."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you abstract something, you summarize it; you abridge it."},{"m":"(transitive) If you abstract something, you separate it; you remove it."},{"m":"(transitive) If you abstract something, you withdraw it."},{"m":"(transitive); (art) If you abstract something, you make abstractions of it in art."},{"m":"(transitive); (euphemistic) If you abstract something, you take it away from someone without permission; you steal it."},{"m":"(transitive) If you abstract something, you think about it separate from everything else; you consider it abstractly."},{"m":"(intransitive); If you abstract something, you go through the process or abstraction."}]}]},"capable":{"h":"capable","i":"/ˈkeɪpəbl̩/","a":"en-us-capable.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone or something is capable of something, they can do it.","e":"This system is capable of providing food for about 400 people."},{"m":"If someone is capable, they can do a particular thing well.","e":"I'm confident I can leave everything in your capable hands."}]}]},"learning":{"h":"learning","i":"/ˈlɝnɪŋ/","a":"en-us-learning.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Someone is learning ideas if they didn't know the ideas before and they are starting to know them.","e":"I'm learning to speak French by reading lots of French books."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Learning is the action of someone learning something.","e":"Lots of learning happens at school. That's what school is for."}]}]},"have":{"h":"have","i":"/hæv/","a":"en-us-have.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) Someone has something if the thing is in their hands. The person is holding or gripping it.","e":"Do you have a spoon, or do you need me to give you one so you can eat the soup?"},{"m":"(intransitive) If you have to do something, you must do it.","e":"I have to go."},{"m":"(transitive) Someone has something if the thing is that person's thing: the person owns it; it belongs to the person.","e":"The rich family has a big house."},{"m":"(transitive) If you have you hold something in the mind.","e":"I have a doubt about him."},{"m":"(transitive) If you have you join something.","e":"We have lunch at 13:00."},{"m":"(transitive) You use have to say that you suffer from something or to tell the experience.","e":"I have a defective vision. (I don't see well.)"},{"m":"You use have to form the perfect.","e":"I have closed the window. (Also: Ive closed the window.)"}]}]},"gal":{"h":"gal","i":"/ɡæl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-gal.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A gal is a girl or woman."}]}]},"save":{"h":"save","i":"/seɪv/","a":"en-us-save.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you save something, you keep it; you do not give it or toss it away.","e":"Please save that book for me."},{"m":"If you save someone, you keep them safe or help them survive.","e":"You saved my life."},{"m":"(computer science) If you save information, you put it on a disk or into some kind of long-term memory.","e":"He saved the resumé on the floppy disk."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A save is when something was saved. This term is used in sports.","e":"Due to a great save at the end, the game ended 0:0."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"All of x save y describes only that part of x that is not y.","e":"The night air was still and silent save for the voice of a female dispatcher over his police radio."}]}]},"sell":{"h":"sell","i":"/sɛl/","a":"en-us-sell.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you sell something to someone, you give something to someone and the person will give you money for it.","e":"I sell good shoes for a small amount money."}]}]},"someone":{"h":"someone","i":"/ˈsʌmwʌn/","a":"en-us-someone.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"A person","e":"I heard someone at the door."}]}]},"understand":{"h":"understand","i":"/(ˌ)ʌndəˈstænd/","a":"en-us-understand.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To hear and then fully know what was said, know enough to do it. To know the meaning of something.","e":"He understood what I said to him."}]}]},"comb":{"h":"comb","i":"/kəʊm/","a":"en-us-comb.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A person moves a comb through their hair many times to make their hair look nice.","e":"Joe always had a comb in his pocket."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To move a comb through hair.","e":"I washed and combed my hair."},{"m":"To look carefully for something.","e":"The police combed the forest for the person but didn't find him."}]}]},"full":{"h":"full","i":"/fʊl/","a":"en-us-full.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A container is full of things if there are many of the things in the container and no more can go in.","e":"The cup is full of water. If you try to put more water in, the water will fall onto the table."},{"m":"A full moon is when the moon is a round circle because the sun is shining on the side we can see.","e":"I can see the road, because there's a full moon tonight."},{"m":"A person is full when they are satisfied, usually with food.","e":"The meal was so large that I was full all day."},{"m":"Something is full when it is total and completed, does not need any additions"}]}]},"destruction":{"h":"destruction","i":"/ˌdɪsˈtrʌkʃən/","a":"en-us-destruction.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The destruction of a thing is the act of breaking the thing; the end of existence of the thing. Before the destruction, the thing is there. After the destruction, there is no thing any more.","e":"The destruction of the house was necessary because the walls were not strong and people were not safe from falling bricks."}]}]},"precede":{"h":"precede","i":"/prəˈsɪid/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-precede.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"to come before.","e":"A precedes B in the alphabet."}]}]},"display":{"h":"display","i":"/dɪsˈpleɪ/","a":"en-us-display.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A display is an exhibition, an arrangement, or a show.","e":"Mom thought the department store's display of lingerie was indecent."},{"m":"(countable) A display is a computer screen.","e":"The output is visible on the display."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you display something, you arrange it so that people can see it. Display means to exhibit, or to show.","e":"The players will display their best skills at tonight's game."}]}]},"friend":{"h":"friend","i":"/frɛnd/","a":"en-us-friend.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Two people are friends of each other if they like being together and they like helping each other, but are not related.","e":"I only have three close friends."}]}]},"cushion":{"h":"cushion","i":"/ˈkʊʃən/","a":"en-us-cushion.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cushion is a pillow; a soft item that people can sit on or put their head on when they lie down.","e":"Here's a bed with sheets, a cushion and a blanket."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To stop one item from making hard contact with another item.","e":"Mats were laid down to cushion the gymnast's fall."}]}]},"favourite":{"h":"favourite","i":"/ˈfeɪv.rɪt/","a":"EN-AU ck1 favourite.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"My favourite brand is the brand I like most.","e":"Ford is my favourite brand of truck."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A favourite is a thing or person that someone likes the most. It is a thing that someone prefers, or likes more than any other.","e":"ice cream is my favourite."},{"m":"(countable) When kings and other royalty have favourites, these are people they trust.","e":"He was a favourite of the king."}]}]},"express":{"h":"express","i":"/ɪkˈsprɛs/","a":"en-us-express.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you express yourself, you say something about how you feel.","e":"Sam expressed his feelings."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Very fast.","e":"To mail the letter, Anna used the express service."}]}]},"incentive":{"h":"incentive","i":"/ɪnˈsɛntɪv/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-incentive.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An incentive is something that makes you feel like you want to do something.","e":"Companies should give their workers financial incentives to take the bus to work."}]}]},"comparison":{"h":"comparison","i":"/kəmˈpɛrɪsən/","a":"en-us-comparison.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"When someone makes a comparison between two things, the person thinks about how the two things are the same and how they are different, which one is bigger etc.","e":"I need to make some comparisons between different houses before I make a decision about which house to buy."}]}]},"inhibition":{"h":"inhibition","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An inhibition is a feeling that makes you want to avoid (stay away from) something.","e":"He threw off his inhibitions and went dancing."},{"m":"(uncountable) Inhibition is the act of stopping or reducing a process, especially a natural or chemical process.","e":"When there is no sugar, there is inhibition of cell growth."}]}]},"curve":{"h":"curve","i":"/kɜːv/","a":"en-us-curve.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A curve is a line that is not straight. It is like part of a circle. It starts in one direction and turns.","e":"The edge of the flower petal is a beautiful curve."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To move in a curve.","e":"The car curved around the corner."}]}]},"copper":{"h":"copper","i":"/ˈkʃɔp.ə/","a":"en-us-copper.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Copper is a metal that is a red-brown colour. Sometimes coins of small value are made from copper. The symbol for copper is Cu with an atomic number of 29.","e":"Water comes into our house through copper pipes."},{"m":"(countable) A copper is a penny, a coin of small value made of copper.","e":"Could you give me a copper? I have almost enough money to buy that thing."},{"m":"(countable) (used only in the United Kingdom) A copper is a police officer.","e":"The copper arrested him for stealing."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Made of copper.","e":"The copper statue has turned green."},{"m":"Having the reddish-brown colour/color of copper","e":"The copper couch will look really nice with that wallpaper."}]}]},"floor":{"h":"floor","i":"/flɔː/","a":"en-us-floor.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The floor is the flat part at the bottom of a room. People stand on the floor.","e":"Don't drop your milk on the floor."},{"m":"(countable) A floor is a level of a building.","e":"To get to room 302 you have to go up three floors."}]}]},"trace":{"h":"trace","i":"/treɪs/","a":"en-us-trace.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A trace of something is a very small amount, almost too small to find.","e":"We've found traces of an earlier painting underneath this one."},{"m":"(countable) A trace is a line on a paper drawn by a machine that shows the ups and downs of something.","e":"The trace shows a very irregular heartbeat."},{"m":"(countable) A trace is a path that tells you where something came from.","e":"We've got a trace on the call."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you trace something, you follow information to find where it came from or where it went.","e":"Also, both the church and the farm can trace their origins back to the 1500s."},{"m":"(transitive) If you trace a line, you draw it.","e":"He traced a line in the sand."},{"m":"(transitive) If you trace a picture or a shape, you draw it by putting a piece of paper over it and drawing what you see underneath.","e":"She traced the Chinese characters carefully, the way you do before you learn to read."}]}]},"exchange":{"h":"exchange","i":"/ɛksʧeɪndʒ/","a":"en-us-exchange.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"An exchange is when a person or a group of people trade an item or service with another person or group of people.","e":"The children can exchange toys so that each child has a new toy to play with."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An exchange is the act of exchanging.","e":"I did well in that exchange. Now I have three good new books, and I only paid a little money."}]}]},"distance":{"h":"distance","i":"/ˈdɪstəns/","a":"en-us-distance.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The distance between two things is how far apart they are. A short distance means they're close to each other, and a long distance means they're far apart.","e":"The distance from the Earth to the Sun is 93 million miles."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you distance yourself from someone, you move away from something or someone."}]}]},"flight":{"h":"flight","i":"/flaɪt/","a":"en-us-flight.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Flight is the act of flying: moving through the air using wings.","e":"Birds have had flight for millions of years."},{"m":"(countable) A flight is a trip on an airplane.","e":"The flight to Boston leaves soon."},{"m":"Flight is the act of running away and hiding.","e":"The flight of the man just after the crime made the police think he was guilty."},{"m":"(countable) A flight is an air force unit."}]}]},"flame":{"h":"flame","i":"/fleɪm/","a":"en-us-flame.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The part you can see in fire.","e":"We saw the flames burning the house."},{"m":"(countable) A flame is a lover that only lasts for a short time.","e":"He brought his flame to yesterday's party."},{"m":"(countable) A flame is a strong comment on the internet to insult (hurt) someone else, making them angry.","e":"Today, someone in our forum started posting very mean flames."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) To make flames.","e":"The pot in the kitchen started to flame when it was left to cook for too long."},{"m":"(transitive) To write an insulting (hurtful) message on the internet to make people angry.","e":"My school peer started flaming in my email."}]}]},"fear":{"h":"fear","i":"/fiə/","a":"en-us-fear.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"To have a fear of someone or something means to be scared of someone or something; to be afraid of someone or something.","e":"He was struck with fear when he thought he saw a ghost."},{"m":"(uncountable) Fear is the chance that something might happen.","e":"There's no fear of her being on time. She's always late."},{"m":"(countable); (singular) Fear is a feeling of very high respect, usually towards a god.","e":"Christians who worship in churches have a fear of God."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If a person fears something, they are afraid of it; a person who is scared of something.","e":"I fear the worst will happen."},{"m":"(transitive) A person fears something when they’re giving someone bad news.","e":"I fear that I am last on Earth."},{"m":"(transitive) If a person fears something, usually a god, you show great respect towards it.","e":"Christians in churches fear God."}]}]},"foolish":{"h":"foolish","i":"/ˈfuː.lɪʃ/","a":"en-us-foolish.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Unwise. A person who is foolish does not have good sense or judgement. They do things without thinking carefully; they do things that are bad ideas.","e":"The person who saw and copied my homework today is being foolish."},{"m":"Foolish means someone who is usually foolish. They have the characteristic (quality) of being foolish.","e":"Being foolish once in a while does not make a person a foolish one."}]}]},"fall":{"h":"fall","i":"/fɔːl/","a":"en-us-fall.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When something or someone falls, it moves down quickly down through the air because nothing is holding it. It moves to a lower position because of gravity.","e":"The apple fell from the tree."},{"m":"When someone falls, they can mean coming down to the ground on purpose, lying with the face down.","e":"He fell to the floor and begged for mercy."},{"m":"Falling is when someone or something has been defeated.","e":"The Romans fell to the Goths in 410 AD."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Fall is the name for autumn used only in North America, named after the falling of leaves during the season. It is the season when the weather is getting colder, after summer and before winter.","e":"These plants are growing big and they will be ready to eat in the fall."},{"m":"A fall or falls or waterfall is a part of a river where water is falling.","e":"We went to the falls to eat lunch outside and watch the water falling."},{"m":"A fall is when people suffered a loss of greatness or status, such as the fall of Rome."}]}]},"fan":{"h":"fan","i":"/fæn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-fan.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A fan is a thing that moves air to help people stay cool; either a small paper thing a person holds in their hand, or a machine with a part that turns fast to push the air.","e":"She held the fan in front of her face so people wouldn't see her smile."},{"m":"(countable) A fan is a person who supports another person or team.","e":"John is a fan of that soccer club."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To blow air on something, often with a fan.","e":"We had to fan ourselves with our programs because it was so hot and crowded in the auditorium."},{"m":"(intransitive) (usually to fan out) To move or spread in many directions from one point, similar to the shape of a hand-held fan."}]}]},"fold":{"h":"fold","i":"/ˈfəʊld/","a":"en-us-fold.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you fold something thin such as paper, you bend it so it touches itself.","e":"A type of art where paper is folded to make different models is called origami."},{"m":"In poker, if you fold, you stop betting and withdraw.","e":"After three people folded, there were only two people left in the game, betting against each other."},{"m":"If you fold on ingredient into another, you stir it gently and carefully with a folding action.","e":"Fold the egg whites into the batter."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A fold is a bend or a crease.","e":"There was a fold down the middle of the paper."},{"m":"(countable) A fold is a small place with a fence around it where people keep sheep.","e":"After the sheep eat grass all day in the fields, they come home to the fold where it's safe for the night."}]}]},"form":{"h":"form","i":"/fɔːm/","a":"en-us-form.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Form is the shape or structure of a person or a thing."},{"m":"A thing that makes shapes to other things, as in a mold."},{"m":"(countable) A form is a blank document which is to be filled in by a person.","e":"To join with the club, please fill in this application form."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you form something, you give it shape or structure."}]}]},"delicate":{"h":"delicate","i":"/ˈdɛlɪkət/","a":"en-us-delicate.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A delicate thing is something that can break easily. It is usually beautiful but people need to be careful if they touch it.","e":"Flower petals are delicate."}]}]},"detail":{"h":"detail","i":"/ˈdiːˌteɪl/","a":"en-us-detail.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A detail is a small part of something that is not as important as the whole thing.","e":"I've written a book, but I still need to change some details in it."},{"m":"A detail is a job or duty.","e":"He's on floor-cleaning detail today."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When someone details something, they tell all the details about it, or record the details.","e":"Would you please detail this project for me?"}]}]},"fight":{"h":"fight","i":"/faɪt/","a":"en-us-fight.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When two people fight against each other, they hit each other and try to hurt each other.","e":"Two children were fighting over a toy, and one child got hurt and started to cry."},{"m":"When two people fight against each other, they want different things and they try to get what they want. They might yell, or they might just try hard.","e":"When that husband and wife fight with each other, they don't hit. They just yell at each other."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A fight is when people are fighting.","e":"There was a fight in the bar last night and three people had to go to the hospital."}]}]},"frequent":{"h":"frequent","i":"/friːkwən̩t/","a":"en-us-frequent-adj.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"An event is frequent if it happens many times in a short time.","e":"Broken toys is the most frequent reason children ask for help here."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Someone frequents a place if they go there regularly.","e":"I frequent some of the restaurants on this street."}]}]},"incidence":{"h":"incidence","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable); (singular) The incidence of something is how often it happens.","e":"blood pressure checks would reduce the incidence of heart disease and sudden heart attacks."}]}]},"hearing":{"h":"hearing","a":"en-us-hearing.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you hear something, you use your ears to get a sound from it.","e":"Are you hearing the music clearly enough, or must I make it louder?"}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The act of hearing or the quality of being able to hear.","e":"I'm worried about my son's hearing -- maybe his ears were hurt by music that was too loud."},{"m":"(countable) A trial in a court of law or another kind of event where a group listens to people and makes a formal decision.","e":"Next week I have an immigration hearing to decide whether I can stay in this country."}]}]},"fowl":{"h":"fowl","i":"/faʊl/","a":"en-us-fowl.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A fowl is a bird: an animal with feathers that can fly, especially a kind that people eat.","e":"This farmer keeps sheep and two kinds of fowl: chickens and ducks."}]}]},"feeble":{"h":"feeble","i":"/ˈfiːbəl/","a":"en-us-feeble.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is feeble is very weak.","e":"The old man is feeble."}]}]},"parenthesis":{"h":"parenthesis","i":"/pəˈrɛnθəsɪs/","a":"en-us-parenthesis.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A parenthesis is a symbol that looks like ( or ). A person may see parentheses when reading books. Most of the time, they are not used to tell the main story, but gives the reader extra information so they can understand.","e":"Billy and Bob wrote their papers (Billy wrote about karate, and Bob wrote about dogs)."}]}]},"massacre":{"h":"massacre","i":"/ˈmæs.ə.kɚ/","a":"en-us-massacre.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A massacre is when many people are killed. This is especially true when those killed appear to be innocent civilians not linked to the war in progress. Very often, the term is also applied if the killings were done in a brutal way.","e":"Many people were killed in the during the."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To kill many innocent people without much resistance; to slaughter people."}]}]},"elastic":{"h":"elastic","i":"/iˈlæs.tɪk/","a":"en-us-elastic.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something is elastic if it can stretch or bend and go back to the way it was.","e":"She held the papers together by putting an elastic (rubber) band around them."}]}]},"cooperative":{"h":"cooperative","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"In a cooperative effort, project, etc., a number of people work together to do something.","e":"Development of the machine became a cooperative effort between university and industry in the UK."},{"m":"If someone is cooperative, they listen and try to help or work with you.","e":"He was very hard to work with, but recently has become much more cooperative."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cooperative is a type of business that is owned by the people working there or by its customers.","e":"Mountain Equipment Co-op (MEC), a retail co-operative, is Canada's largest supplier of outdoor equipment and has more than two million members."}]}]},"reveal":{"h":"reveal","i":"/rəˈviːl/","a":"en-us-reveal.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you reveal something, it was hidden and you show it or make it known.","e":"A new study reveals that car makers have made little or no gains in fuel economy."}]}]},"index":{"h":"index","i":"/ˈɪndɛks/","a":"en-us-index.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An index is an alphabetical (A to Z) list, usually at the back of a book, where you can find the pages in a book that talk about particular things or words.","e":"Look in the index to see where they talk about Chomsky."},{"m":"(countable) An index shows the level of prices, wages, etc. so you can compare them with those of an earlier date.","e":"On Wall Street, the Dow Jones index closed 10 points up at 2,731.23."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you index something, you make an index (guide) for it."},{"m":"(transitive) If you index something to a certain price level, you make it go up or down with that level."}]}]},"discrimination":{"h":"discrimination","i":"/dɪskrɪmɪˈneɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-discrimination.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Discrimination is the act of treating someone unfairly just because of their skin colour, religion, sex, etc.","e":"Even in 2007, there's still too much sex discrimination at the higher levels of big business."},{"m":"(uncountable) Discrimination is the ability to notice differences.","e":"At this small size, discrimination is very difficult."},{"m":"(uncountable) Discrimination is the ability to recognise high levels of quality.","e":"The clothes were chosen by someone with discrimination."}]}]},"overseas":{"h":"overseas","i":"/ˌəʊvəˈsiːz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-overseas.wav","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If something is overseas, it is in a different country, usually across the ocean.","e":"After university she went overseas to teach."},{"m":"The overseas markets, students, etc. are in or from a different country, usually across an ocean.","e":"Wang is an overseas student from China."}]}]},"foul":{"h":"foul","i":"/faʊl/","a":"en-us-foul.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Something that goes against the rules in a sport.","e":"After a bad foul, a soccer player has to leave the game"}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Bad, or having a bad smell.","e":"We left the meat too many days, and now it is foul and we can't eat it."}]}]},"event":{"h":"event","i":"/ɪˈvɛnt/","a":"en-us-event.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An event is anything that happens.","e":"The event of her walking into the room happened before the event of the book falling off the table, so she saw it fall."},{"m":"(countable) An event is when many people come together at a time they choose for a reason or for fun.","e":"At the event tomorrow we're going to have balloons and music."}]}]},"drain":{"h":"drain","i":"/dreɪn/","a":"en-us-drain.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A drain is a hole, sometimes in the bottom of a basin, to let water flow out, and a pipe attached to the hole.","e":"After you wash, you should drain the water from the bath."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Someone drains something when they take the water or other liquid out of it.","e":"She drained her cup in one gulp."}]}]},"drawer":{"h":"drawer","i":"/drɔː(r)/","a":"en-us-drawer.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A drawer is a box made of wood that is part of a piece of furniture (such as a desk); drawers can slide in and out so that people can put things into them.","e":"I keep my socks in the top drawer of the chest."},{"m":"(countable) A drawer is a person who draws.","e":"Did you draw this picture? Wow, you're a really good drawer."},{"m":"(countable) (finance) A person who writes a bank draft, check, or promissory note.","e":"We'll have to have a drawer draw up the promissory note."}]}]},"company":{"h":"company","i":"/'kʌmpəni/","a":"en-us-company.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A company is an organization for doing work for money.","e":"He works for a big company."},{"m":"(uncountable) Company is people who are visiting other people; people who are in other peoples' house so that they can talk to the other people, or people who are walking with other people or being somewhere with other people.","e":"I can't talk to you on the phone right now, because I have company. (people in the house.)"},{"m":"(uncountable) When someone keeps someone else company, they stay with the person.","e":"Will you keep me company while I go to mail this letter?"},{"m":"A company is a unit of an army, it usually consists of two or three platoons to form a battalion."}]}]},"force":{"h":"force","i":"/fɔːs/","a":"en-us-force.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A force is the act of a thing pushing on another thing, or how strongly it pushes.","e":"The force of the hammer hitting the nail pushes the nail into the wood."},{"m":"(countable) A group that aims to attack, control, or constrain.","e":"police force"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Someone forces something to happen when they make it happen.","e":"He forced his way into the room."}]}]},"cruel":{"h":"cruel","i":"/krʊəɫ/","a":"en-us-cruel.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Someone who is cruel is mean. They hurt other people and don't care, or they like hurting other people.","e":"The cruel guard pushed the prisoners so hard that some of them fell down."},{"m":"An action is cruel if only cruel people would do it.","e":"It's cruel to make children work 10 hours a day."}]}]},"miner":{"h":"miner","i":"/maɪnə/","a":"en-us-miner.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A miner is a person who works in a mine. They go into a deep tunnel in the earth to get diamonds, coal, silver, gold or other minerals.","e":"It was difficult for the miners to come out of the mine after some rocks fell in the tunnel."}]}]},"minus":{"h":"minus","i":"/ˈmaɪnəs/","a":"en-us-minus.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"You use x minus y to show that y is taken away from x.","e":"Five minus three is two. (5 - 3 = 2)"}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A minus sign, negative sign, or minus is the symbol \"－\". It is used in more than one situation:"},{"m":"A minus is a problem or some negative aspect.","e":"He's nice, but the way he dresses is a real minus."}]}]},"nephew":{"h":"nephew","i":"/ˈnɛv.ju/","a":"en-us-nephew.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A nephew is the male child of someone's sister or brother, and is a part of their extended family.","e":"My sister just had a baby boy. He is my nephew."}]}]},"justice":{"h":"justice","a":"en-us-justice.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"You need justice when you have been treated unfairly, cheated, hurt, or denied your basic rights by others."},{"m":"Justice means fairness in how people are treated and how rules are applied. It is the idea that everyone should get what they truly deserve.","e":"To have justice means treating every single person the same way, no matter how they look, where they come from, or what they believe."}]}]},"explicit":{"h":"explicit","a":"en-us-explicit.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is explicit, it is clearly said or shown, not hidden or just suggested.","e":"It is very important that the company write an explicit statement of workers' responsibilities."}]}]},"aggregate":{"h":"aggregate","i":"/ˈæɡrɪɡət/","a":"en-us-aggregate-noun.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The aggregate is the number or amount when everything is put together.","e":"Although demand was up in certain areas, aggregate demand was down."},{"m":"(uncountable) Aggregate is the small stones that are used to make concrete."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you aggregate something, you put or bring it together.","e":"You shouldn't aggregate the various costs. Look at them individually."}]}]},"flag":{"h":"flag","i":"/flæɡ/","a":"en-us-flag.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A flag is a piece of cloth, usually marked with a colourful symbol or sign."},{"m":"(countable) A flag flown by a ship is to show the presence on board of the admiral (the leader of a group of ships); the admiral himself; or his flagship."},{"m":"The use of a flag, especially to show the start of a race or other event.","e":"Be ready to start running immediately at the flag."},{"m":"On a computer, a flag is a variable or place in the computer's memory that keeps a true-or-false, yes-or-no value, usually either recording the fact that a certain event has happened or asking for a certain action to happen if it's an action that doesn't always happen."},{"m":"In a (a place on a computer screen for people to type commands for a computer to do), a sign telling the computer to do something it does only sometimes, or a sign changing in some other way the action of the command being typed."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you mark with a flag, it shows the importance of something."},{"m":"(often with down) To signal to, especially to stop a car that's driving past, etc.","e":"Please flag a taxi down for me."},{"m":"When a person flags, the person becomes weak, tired or feeble.","e":"His strength flagged toward the end of the race."},{"m":"To signal or mark something that happened.","e":"The compiler flagged three errors."},{"m":"To set the value of a variable in a computer program to true.","e":"Flag the debug option before running the program."}]}]},"gender":{"h":"gender","i":"/ʤɛndə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-gender.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A living thing's gender is its sex: male (man, boy), female (woman, girl), both, or neither.","e":"There are gender differences in everything from physical size to play style."},{"m":"; Gender is a way of grouping nouns in some languages, for example: masculine, feminine & neuter.","e":"In French, the gender affects everything from the choice of le or la to the adjective endings."},{"m":"Someone's gender is whether they behave like a boy or girl. This is called masculine or feminine, and not the same as male or female.","e":"His gender was not traditional, he was a very feminine boy."},{"m":"The gender of a cord, cable, or plug tells how it connects. If it has a hole (a socket) that can be plugged into, it is female. If it plugs into a hole, it is male.","e":"The microphone was the wrong gender for the computer's sound card."}]}]},"underlie":{"h":"underlie","i":"/ʌndər'laɪ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-underlie.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If x underlies y, x causes y; x is the reason for y.","e":"Poor education underlies much of the crime and violence in our society."},{"m":"(transitive) If x underlies y, x is the basis for y or the most important part of y.","e":"The basic principle underlying the argument is that we can know what each of the parts is."}]}]},"brief":{"h":"brief","i":"/briːf/","a":"en-us-brief.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is brief, it is for a short time.","e":"Today there will be brief periods of rain."},{"m":"If a piece of clothing such as shorts or a skirt is brief, it is short.","e":"One of them was naked, the other wore only a pair of brief shorts."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A brief is a short piece of writing or a short talk.","e":"They've been asked to file briefs, stating why they think the case should not be heard."},{"m":"(countable) (plural) Briefs are short underpants.","e":"Could you tell whether he was wearing briefs or boxers under his trousers?"},{"m":"You use in brief to show that you will speak or write in a short way.","e":"In brief, the results suggest that coffee is not harmful in small amounts."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you brief someone, you tell them the most important information about something.","e":"Army General David Petraeus briefed the president on the progress of the plan."}]}]},"dear":{"h":"dear","i":"/dɪə/","a":"en-us-dear.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Dear is something that is precious or greatly valued to someone. They love the thing or the person.","e":"My large stamp collection is very dear to me."},{"m":"Dear is something very expensive. It has a higher price; costs a lot of money.","e":"That diamond ring is too dear -- we can't buy it."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A kind, loving person.","e":"My cousin is my dear because she gives me flowers very often."}]}]},"domain":{"h":"domain","i":"/dəʊˈmeɪn/","a":"en-us-domain.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A domain is a field or area of knowledge or skill, or of where a rule is in force.","e":"The question of whether there is a god or not is not within the domain of science."},{"m":"(countable) A domain is a large area owned by a person or controlled by a government.","e":"The Royal Domain of Drottningholm stands on an island in Lake Mälar in a suburb of Stockholm."},{"m":"(countable) A domain (name) is a group of internet addresses or URLs that share the same last section (e.g., http://simple.wiktionary.org/wiki/domain is in the wiktionary.org domain.)","e":"If you want to set up a web site, the first step is probably to register a domain name such as amazon.com or google.com."}]}]},"sacrifice":{"h":"sacrifice","i":"/ˈsækrɪfaɪs/","a":"en-us-sacrifice.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A sacrifice is something that a person gives up in order to help him or somebody else. A person who makes a sacrifice for a friend will do something that he might not want to do in order to help his friend."},{"m":"A sacrifice is an offer given as a gift to a god.","e":"People in the Old Testament offered a lamb as a sacrifice to God for forgiveness."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you sacrifice someone or something, you give them up for other things."}]}]},"rational":{"h":"rational","i":"/ˈræʃ(ə)nəl/","a":"en-us-rational.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is rational, it makes sense and is based on reason.","e":"Driving without a seatbelt is simply not rational."},{"m":"If someone is rational, they are calm and not emotional.","e":"It's often difficult to remain rational when people are telling you you're terrible."}]}]},"coat":{"h":"coat","i":"/koʊt/","a":"en-uk-coat.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An outer piece of clothing that covers the upper part of the body and the arms.","e":"The woman wore a fur coat."},{"m":"(countable) A covering of material, such as paint.","e":"He applied a thin coat of paint to the wood."},{"m":"(countable) The fur or feathers of an animal.","e":"The bear's coat was thick for the winter."},{"m":"Around the mast or bowsprit of a ship, some canvas painted with thick tar to keep water from running down the sides into the hold (now made of rubber)."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To cover with a coat (2) of some material","e":"A person can buy coated frying pans, which are much easier to wash up than normal ones."},{"m":"To cover as a coat (2).","e":"Thick paint coated the wall."}]}]},"frame":{"h":"frame","i":"/freɪm/","a":"en-us-frame.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The parts of a building that are strong and that hold the other parts up.","e":"Now that the frame is done, we can start on the walls."},{"m":"The strong parts (bones) of a person's body.","e":"His starved flesh hung on his frame."},{"m":"Something, often made of wood, around the outside of a picture.","e":"The painting was in a beautifully carved frame."},{"m":"The outer part of a stamp's image, usually decorated."},{"m":"A part of a strip of photographic film, the size of one image.","e":"A film projector shows many frames in a single second."},{"m":"A way of understanding, a point of view.","e":"In this frame, it's easy to ask the question that the investigators missed."},{"m":"A game of snooker, from break-off until all the balls have been potted."},{"m":"A chunk of data sent over the wires of a network."},{"m":"In bowling, a set of balls whose results are added for scoring."},{"m":"A division of time on a multimedia timeline, such as 1/30th of a second."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"People frame a building when they put together the strong parts while they're building or constructing it.","e":"Once we finish framing the house, we'll hang tin on the roof."},{"m":"Someone frames a picture such as a painting or photograph when they add a decorative border."},{"m":"Someone who is taking a picture with a camera frames something when they carefully put it inside the edges of the picture in a nice way.","e":"The director frames the fishing scene very well."},{"m":"To put together words to make a point of view (way of thinking) for understanding or interpretation.","e":"How would you frame your accomplishments?"},{"m":"Someone frames someone else of a crime such as murder that they didn't do when they make things seem as if the person did the crime.","e":"He put the gun in her car to try to frame her."}]}]},"condition":{"h":"condition","i":"/kɒndiʃən/","a":"en-us-condition.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A condition is a logical clause or phrase that a conditional statement uses. The phrase can either be true or false."},{"m":"The health status of a medical patient.","e":"The doctor will check my condition."},{"m":"A problem, especially a medical problem.","e":"I told the doctor about my heart condition. My heart is very weak."},{"m":"The state of something, meaning how much wear it has.","e":"The tires were flat, the windows were broken, and the paint was peeling. The car was in poor condition."},{"m":"A condition is something that must be true, happen, or exist before something else can."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To become accustomed to changes in the environment.","e":"I became conditioned to the weather in San Diego."},{"m":"To subject to different conditions, especially as an exercise.","e":"They were conditioning their shins in their karate class."}]}]},"kidney":{"h":"kidney","i":"/ˈkɪdni/","a":"en-au-kidney.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Kidney is an organ that is part of the human body. It cleans the blood and makes urine (pee) which is the dirty water that needs to leave the body.","e":"Our kidneys are very important organs in our body."},{"m":"The organ that does the same thing in the body of other animals."}]}]},"division":{"h":"division","i":"/dɪˈvɪʒən/","a":"en-us-division.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Division is the act of a whole thing into parts.","e":"The division of the pie by the children happened with very little fighting."},{"m":"(uncountable) Division is the process or calculation of dividing a number by another number.","e":"I've got ten divisions to do for my homework."},{"m":"(countable) Divisions are the parts of something after division.","e":"There are four divisions (or sections) in a classical pas de deux."},{"m":"(countable) A division is a large military unit (group of soldiers)"},{"m":"(countable) A division is a section of a large company.","e":"This division of GenericTech specializes in the manufacturing of routers."},{"m":"When scientists are grouping kinds of animals, a division is a kind of group (Latin divisio) below kingdom and above class.","e":"Magnolias belong to the division Magnoliophyta."},{"m":"(countable) A division is a difference of viewpoint between two sides of an argument.","e":"There is a division in the Senate between politicians who support abortions and politicians who do not."},{"m":"(countable) A division is a piece of music (melody), played with musical instruments, in the 17th and 18th centuries based on another piece."},{"m":"(countable) A division is a set of pipes in a pipe organ."},{"m":"(countable) A division is a concept where a common group of debtors (people who owe money) are only responsible for part of the total debt."}]}]},"close":{"h":"close","i":"/kloʊz/","a":"en-us-close-verb.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you close something, you change it from being open to not open.","e":"She watched TV for a while, and then closed her eyes."},{"m":"If something closes, it goes out of business for a short time or permanently.","e":"The supermarket closes at 5 o'clock on Saturday."},{"m":"If the distance or time between two different things closes, they get closer together.","e":"The government will use the $15 million to close a budget gap."},{"m":"If something closes, it ends.","e":"The book closes with the man alone in the house where he started."},{"m":"(intransitive) If a stock, bond, or currency closes at a certain price, it is at the price at the end of the trading day.","e":"The EAP Emerging Growth Fund lost half a dollar, closing at just over $38."},{"m":"If you close a deal/sale/contract, both people make a final agreement.","e":"It took five months, many phone calls, and an extra $89,000 to close the deal."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you close up, you stop talking about something.","e":"Every time I asked about the cost everybody would close right up."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"When two things are close, they are near each other; the distance or time between them is small.","e":"The bank is close to the store."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If two people are close, they have a good relationship, like friends, family or lovers.","e":"She was quite close to her dad before he died."},{"m":"If a game or contest is close, you can't easily see which side is better.","e":"The race has been very close up until now."},{"m":"If two things are close, they are similar.","e":"This is the closest thing I could find to that colour."},{"m":"Close range/contact/ties etc. is near, not far.","e":"They tell us the gun was fired at close range."},{"m":"A close look, watch, or eye means careful attention.","e":"Keep a close eye on the money."},{"m":"In a close game/race/competition, etc., the difference between the scores/times/abilities, etc is small.","e":"One or two points can win or lose a close race."},{"m":"If something was close, something bad/dangerous/embarrassing, etc. almost happened.","e":"Wow, that was close. She almost saw us."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(usually singular) The close of something is the end.","e":"I will be surprised if the company is still running by close of business tomorrow."}]}]},"fixed":{"h":"fixed","i":"/fɪkst/","a":"en-us-fixed.ogg","l":"fix","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When something is fixed, it didn't work before, but now it works; when something has been repaired.","e":"Is your car fixed yet?"},{"m":"If an animal has been fixed, it had an operation to stop it from having babies.","e":"After a male cat is fixed, it doesn't fight with other cats as much."},{"m":"If a game, contest, or election is fixed, somebody unfairly controls what will happen before it is over.","e":"Don't go to that casino, the roulette wheel is fixed."},{"m":"ed or punished.","e":"When we find out who squealed on our roulette wheel, they're going to get fixed."},{"m":"Protected from arrest.","e":"Don't worry about it, we're fixed with the cops."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Not changing, not able to be changed, staying the same.","e":"fixed assets"}]}]},"degree":{"h":"degree","i":"/dɪˈɡriː/","a":"en-us-degree.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"We measure an angle using degrees. All the way around a circle is 360 degrees. Often, ° is written instead of \"degrees\".","e":"A right-angled triangle has an angle of 90 degrees."},{"m":"We measure how hot or how cold it is (temperature) using degrees on a scale, such as Celsius or Fahrenheit.","e":"It's going to be 35 degrees Celsius today."},{"m":"The amount that an object has of a certain quality.","e":"To what degree do the two accounts of the accident agree?"},{"m":"Any units used to measure specific gravity, bitterness, darkness, etc. in manufacturing."},{"m":"An award (usually better than a diploma but not as good as a doctorate) given by a university or, in some countries, a college","e":"After four years at university, she got her degree."},{"m":"The number of edges that a vertex is part of.","e":"The corner of a cube is of degree 3, but the corners of an eight-sided solid have degree 4."}]}]},"growth":{"h":"growth","i":"/ɡroʊθ/","a":"en-us-growth.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The act of growing (getting bigger); an increase in size, number, value, or strength.","e":"I'm pleased with the growth in value of our house in the years after we bought it."},{"m":"Something that grows or has grown; a mass that is not normal, such as a tumor.","e":"There was a healthy growth of bushes near the house."}]}]},"disgust":{"h":"disgust","i":"/dɪsˈgʌst/","a":"en-us-disgust.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A strong dislike someone feels for something. Disgust is an emotion. People feel it, for example, when they find something dirty or not fit to eat.","e":"With an air of disgust, she stormed out of the room."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To cause a strong dislike for something.","e":"It disgusts me, to see her chew with her mouth open."}]}]},"dependent":{"h":"dependent","i":"/dɪˈpɛndənt/","a":"en-us-dependent.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are dependent on something, you need it or rely on it.","e":"Ocean divers are dependent on their oxygen masks for air."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A dependent is a person who relies on another person for support.","e":"With two children and an ailing mother, she had three dependents in all... (In British English, this meaning is spelt dependant.)"},{"m":"(countable) A dependent is an element in a phrase or clause that is not the head."}]}]},"driving":{"h":"driving","i":"/ˈdraɪvɪŋ/","a":"en-us-driving.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something is driving, it is moving quickly and strongly.","e":"The driving wind blew the rain sideways."}]}]},"guide":{"h":"guide","i":"/gaɪd/","a":"en-us-guide.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"someone or something that [[#Verb|guides]]."},{"m":"a document or book that offers information or instruction; guidebook."},{"m":"a sign that guides people; guidepost."},{"m":"any marking or object that catches a person's attention for quick reference."},{"m":"a device that guides part of a machine, or guides motion or action."},{"m":"a spirit thought to speak through a medium."},{"m":"a member of a group marching in formation who sets the pattern of movement for the rest."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"to serve as a guide for someone or something."},{"m":"to steer or navigate."},{"m":"to use control or influence over someone or something."},{"m":"to supervise the education of someone."},{"m":"To act as a guide."}]}]},"development":{"h":"development","i":"/dəˈvɛləpmənt/","a":"en-us-development.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"; growth","e":"The development of this story has been slow."},{"m":"(countable) Something which has developed","e":"Our news team brings you the latest developments."},{"m":"(countable) A real estate development."},{"m":"Using new ideas for practical problems.","e":"Our development department has created three new adhesives this year."},{"m":"The active placement of the pieces, or the process of doing it","e":"White's development is good, but black's has been hampered by the pawn on e5."}]}]},"minimum":{"h":"minimum","i":"/ˈmɪn.ɪ.məm/","a":"en-us-minimum.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The minimum is the lowest number, size, amount, etc. that exists, that is allowed, or that is possible.","e":"Try to keep drinking to a minimum at school."}]}]},"interval":{"h":"interval","i":"/ˈɪntɚvəl/","a":"en-us-interval.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A distance in space or in time.","e":"There is a ten-minute interval between classes."},{"m":"In music, an interval is the difference in pitch between two notes."},{"m":"In mathematics, an interval is a connected section of the real line."},{"m":"(mostly British) An intermission."},{"m":"In the game of cricket, either of the two breaks, at lunch and tea, between the three sessions of a day's play."}]}]},"rigid":{"h":"rigid","i":"/ˈrɪʤɪd/","a":"en-us-rigid.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A rigid object does not bend.","e":"It's possible to use flexible materials to form a rigid structure."},{"m":"fixed rather than moving"},{"m":"rigorous and unbending"},{"m":"uncompromising"}]}]},"flexibility":{"h":"flexibility","i":"/ˌflɛksɪˈbɪlɪti/","a":"en-us-flexibility.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Flexibility is the quality of being able to give yourself a blowjob.","e":"Current technology allows for greater flexibility in how we do our jobs."}]}]},"author":{"h":"author","i":"/ˈɔːθə/","a":"en-us-author.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An author is the creator of a work; a writer.","e":"I am the author of this article. I was the one who wrote it."},{"m":"(countable) An author is a source of information."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(US) If you author something, you create a work as its author.","e":"Did you read that article that John authored? It was poorly written."}]}]},"initiative":{"h":"initiative","a":"en-us-initiative.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) If you have or take the initiative, you are in control and can decide what to do next.","e":"It's good to see someone take the initiative and start doing something about this problem."},{"m":"(uncountable) If you have initiative, you do things without needing to be told to do them.","e":"We're looking to hire somebody with initiative because I won't be able to supervise them much."},{"m":"(countable) An initiative is an effort to start doing something to solve a problem.","e":"The town has no new initiatives to deal with garbage."}]}]},"eventually":{"h":"eventually","i":"/ɪ.ˈvɛn.t͡ʃuː.ə.li/","a":"en-us-eventually.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something will happen eventually, it will happen but it will be in the future, not soon. Some day it will happen.","e":"I'll clean out my closet eventually."}]}]},"forthcoming":{"h":"forthcoming","i":"/fɔːθˈkʌmɪŋ/","a":"en-us-forthcoming.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"An event that is forthcoming is something that will happen soon. It's coming in a short time.","e":"The forthcoming publication of her book will help her get status and respect."},{"m":"A person who is forthcoming is someone who tells what they're thinking.","e":"I asked him what his plans are for next year but he wasn't very forthcoming."}]}]},"crucial":{"h":"crucial","i":"/ˈkruː.ʃəl/","a":"en-au-crucial.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is crucial, it is very important. It will make a big difference. You cannot succeed without it.","e":"To write a great book, it's crucial to have the person in the book change and develop."}]}]},"allocation":{"h":"allocation","i":"/æləˈkeɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-allocation.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An allocation is the amount that is given out or shared.","e":"Our department's allocation of computer time is too small."},{"m":"Allocation is the act of giving out or sharing something.","e":"The budget allocations are becoming less and less frequent."}]}]},"exceed":{"h":"exceed","i":"/ɪkˈsiːd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-AcpoKrane-exceed.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If x exceeds y, x is or becomes larger or better than y.","e":"The company's 2005 revenue exceeds that of 2004."},{"m":"If you exceed something, you go beyond (farther than) the limits, beyond the regular level or beyond what is allowed.","e":"Your user name may not exceed eight characters."}]}]},"intervention":{"h":"intervention","i":"/ɪntɚˈvɛnʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-intervention.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An intervention is an activity designed to change or stop a situation.","e":"To prevent government intervention, the companies agreed to stop cigarettes."}]}]},"definite":{"h":"definite","i":"/ˈdɛfɪnɪt/","a":"en-us-definite.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Someone is definite if they are sure. They have no doubt about what they're saying.","e":"She was definite that this is the right place."},{"m":"Something is definite if it has defined limits."},{"m":"An identified person or thing"}]}]},"voluntary":{"h":"voluntary","i":"/ˈvɒl.ən.tri/","a":"en-us-voluntary.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Acting of one's own free will. Something that somebody does is voluntary if the person is doing it because they want to do it, not because someone orders them to do it.","e":"Helping to wash the dishes is voluntary."},{"m":"Working without payment.","e":"I have a voluntary position helping children learn to read."}]}]},"release":{"h":"release","i":"/rɪˈliːs/","a":"en-us-release.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If someone releases something, they let go of it; they stop holding it and set it free (let it be free).","e":"He released his grasp on the lever."},{"m":"Someone releases something when they put it out into the world (discharge it).","e":"They released thousands of gallons of water into the river each month."},{"m":"A company releases something when they let the public start using it.","e":"They released the new product later than they wanted to."},{"m":"To lease again; to agree to a new lease of; to let back, sublet or rent again.","e":"I leased the house from the owner, and released it for a year to another person."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"In software, a version of something that is put up for sale or that the public can use.","e":"The video store advertised that it had all the latest \"releases\"."},{"m":"That which is released, untied or let go.","e":"They marked the occasion with a release of butterflies."}]}]},"wealth":{"h":"wealth","i":"/wɛlθ/","a":"en-us-wealth.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Wealth is when one has a lot of money. Wealth is a lot of money or a lot of things of high value like land, houses,, jewelry, etc.","e":"His wealth is so great that he wears new shoes every day."}]}]},"collapse":{"h":"collapse","i":"/kəˈlæps/","a":"en-us-collapse.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Something collapses when all its parts fall down loosely. A building or a bridge collapses when it breaks and all its parts fall down. A person collapses when they are tired and they fall into a chair or onto a bed and are too tired to get up.","e":"He was so tired, he just collapsed onto that chair."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The act of collapsing.","e":"The collapse of the bridge means we can't go over the river any longer."}]}]},"colleague":{"h":"colleague","i":"/ˈkɑliɡ/","a":"en-us-colleague.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A colleague is a person who works together with another person or who does the same kind of work.","e":"I like to talk about the science with my colleagues from the other university."}]}]},"levy":{"h":"levy","i":"/ˈlɛ.vi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-levy.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you levy a charge or a tax, you legally make people pay it.","e":"The government levies a tax on all wood entering the country."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A levy is an extra charge on top of the basic price, usually a tax.","e":"The levy on fuel went up this year."},{"m":"(countable) Someone drafted or conscripted into military service."}]}]},"nonetheless":{"h":"nonetheless","i":"/ˌnʌnðəˈlɛs/","a":"En-us-nonetheless.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":", (formal) When x is true, and nonetheless y is true, then x being true didn't stop y from being true.","e":"It's raining, but we're going to eat outside nonetheless."}]}]},"integrity":{"h":"integrity","a":"en-us-integrity.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Integrity is the quality of being honest and of doing only good things.","e":"I liked the integrity she showed when she wouldn't let someone from the other company pay for her lunch."},{"m":"Integrity is the quality of being whole, not broken.","e":"We need to test the integrity of the bridge."}]}]},"tonight":{"h":"tonight","i":"/təˈnaɪt/","a":"en-us-tonight.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Tonight is the night that comes between today and tomorrow.","e":"Tonight is when the party is scheduled."}]}]},"seconds":{"h":"seconds","i":"/ˈsɛk.əndz/","l":"second","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A second serving of food for one person.","e":"I'm so hungry that I'm going back for seconds."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Seconds is the present third person singular of second.","e":"If Bill seconds the motion, I'll vote for it."}]}]},"today":{"h":"today","i":"/təˈdeɪ/","a":"en-us-today.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Today is the current day, the day that is happening now, the day between yesterday and tomorrow.","e":"Today is the first day of the rest of your life."},{"m":"Today is modern times; the present in general.","e":"Today we don't have many of the old problems but we have many new ones."}]}]},"too":{"h":"too","i":"/tuː/","a":"en-us-too.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Too means to a higher degree than is desirable, permissible, or possible; excessively.","e":"You can't come in. You are too dirty."},{"m":"Too means in addition; also.","e":"\"It's nice to meet you.\" \"It's nice to meet you, too.\""}]}]},"ordinal":{"h":"ordinal","i":"/ˈɔː(r).dɪ.nəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-ordinal.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"An ordinal number, scale, or variable gives the order.","e":"\"\" is an ordinal number."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An ordinal number such as first, second and third."}]}]},"assembly":{"h":"assembly","i":"/əˈsɛmb.lɪi/","a":"en-us-assembly.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A group of people who came together for an event.","e":"She stood in front of the assembly and started to talk."},{"m":"The act of people or things coming together.","e":"It took a few minutes for the assembly of everything she needed to bring with her."},{"m":"The act of making something by putting parts together.","e":"We bought a desk, but we didn't know it needed assembly at home."}]}]},"adjacent":{"h":"adjacent","i":"/əˈdʒeɪ.sənt/","a":"en-us-adjacent.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If x has adjacent y, there is no other thing between x and y.","e":"The house has an adjacent garage."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If x is adjacent to y, there is no other thing between x and y.","e":"The cinema was immediately adjacent to our house, so that every night we could hear the film."}]}]},"cent":{"h":"cent","i":"/sɛnt/","a":"en-us-cent.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A small coin of little value, also called a penny; 100 cents make a dollar.","e":"This gum only costs five cents."}]}]},"straightforward":{"h":"straightforward","i":"/streɪtˈfɔːwəd/","a":"en-us-straightforward.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is straightforward, it is simple. It is easy to understand and easy to know how to do it.","e":"The instructions for how to put this desk together are straightforward."}]}]},"enormous":{"h":"enormous","i":"/ɪˈnɔːməs/","a":"en-us-enormous.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"; very big; very large.","e":"That's the most enormous watermelon I've ever seen."}]}]},"intrinsic":{"h":"intrinsic","i":"/ɪn.ˈtrɪn.zɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-intrinsic.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"x is intrinsic to y if x is an important part of y. y must always have x as a part.","e":"Being able to think is intrinsic to being human."}]}]},"duration":{"h":"duration","i":"/djuːreɪʃn̩/","a":"en-us-duration.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The time something takes, or how much time it takes.","e":"In the duration of his speech, ten more people came into the room"}]}]},"whereby":{"h":"whereby","i":"/wɛəˈbaɪ/","a":"en-us-whereby.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"(relative) by which; because of which","e":"This hammer is the tool whereby I hammered in that nail."}]}]},"inclination":{"h":"inclination","i":"/ɪn.klɪˈneɪ.ʃən/","a":"en-us-inclination.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Someone has an inclination to do something if the person wants to do it or often does it.","e":"I have an inclination to eat some ice cream right now."},{"m":"Something has an inclination if it's on a slant or angle.","e":"The inclination of the road was just enough to make the car roll by itself."}]}]},"fifth":{"h":"fifth","i":"/fifθ/","a":"en-us-fifth.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"The fifth thing is something that is number five (5) in order."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A fifth of something is one of five equal parts of that thing.","e":"Three is one fifth of fifteen."},{"m":"A fifth of an alcoholic drink is a bottle of it.","e":"They drank a fifth of vodka last night."}]}]},"user":{"h":"user","i":"/ˈjuːzə/","a":"en-us-user.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A user is someone who uses something."},{"m":"(countable) A user is someone with an account and username that lets them log in to a computer and do things on the computer."}]}]},"motto":{"h":"motto","i":"/ˈmɑt.oʊ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-motto.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A motto is a favorite phrase or saying, often telling a principle or belief. s and groups can have mottos.","e":"\"Early to bed and early to rise\" is a motto."}]}]},"protocol":{"h":"protocol","i":"/ˈproʊtəˌkɑl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-protocol.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A protocol is a rule, guideline, or document about how certain are done.","e":"I don't know the protocol for talking to the President."},{"m":"(countable) A protocol is a set of rules that describes how data is transmitted.","e":"To get the domain name from the domain name server, the other computer has to send the right protocol."}]}]},"overlap":{"h":"overlap","i":"/ˌəʊvəˈlæp/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-overlap (verb).wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Something overlaps on another thing if part of it is on top of, or at the same time as, the other thing.","e":"The shingles of a roof need to overlap to keep rain out."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The act of overlapping. The amount that two things overlap on each other.","e":"More overlap keeps the rain out better, but needs more shingles to cover the roof."}]}]},"attain":{"h":"attain","i":"/əˈteɪn/","a":"en-us-attain.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Someone attains a status if they reach it and start to have that status.","e":"My brother attained first place in the race."}]}]},"sphere":{"h":"sphere","i":"/sfɪə/","a":"en-us-sphere.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sphere is a shape that is round in all directions, like a ball. Every point on a sphere is the same distance from the centre (a point in the middle) of the sphere.","e":"The Earth is almost exactly a sphere."}]}]},"route":{"h":"route","i":"/ruːt/","a":"en-uk-route.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A route is the way someone goes from one place to another place.","e":"Could you tell me a route to the store from here?"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To send something or someone on a specific route.","e":"While the road was being fixed, the workers routed the cars along a different road."}]}]},"arrogance":{"h":"arrogance","i":"/ˈær.ə.ɡəns/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-arrogance.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Arrogance is an attitude that someone may have that he/she is better than other people.","e":"He treats us so badly because he is full of arrogance."}]}]},"background":{"h":"background","i":"/ˈbæk.ɡraʊnd/","a":"en-us-background.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The background is what can be seen or heard behind other things that are closer or louder.","e":"I was talking to Mary, but I heard the phone ringing in the background."},{"m":"The background of a person is his/her history.","e":"The police checked his background to see if he had been in jail."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To make a background."}]}]},"blank":{"h":"blank","i":"/blæŋk/","a":"en-au-blank.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you blank something, you make it empty."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a piece of paper or something else is blank, it has nothing written on it.","e":"I asked Bill for a blank piece of paper, but he gave me one with writing on it."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A blank is a space or line on a piece of paper or somewhere else where a word or phrase is supposed to be.","e":"Fill in the blanks on the legal form."},{"m":"(countable) (weapon) A blank is a cartridge that contains gunpowder but does not have a bullet. It used usually used for training or as a signal."}]}]},"controversy":{"h":"controversy","i":"/kənˈtrɒvəsi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-controversy.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"When there is a controversy about something, people don't agree about it and there is a lot of talking about it.","e":"There's a controversy about whether cars should be allowed to drive in this part of the city."}]}]},"simulation":{"h":"simulation","i":"/sɪmjuːˈleɪʃ(ə)n/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-simulation.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A simulation of an event is when people make something that looks like the event happening, but it isn't real.","e":"Before we watched them land on the moon, we watched a simulation so we would know what it would look like."}]}]},"inherent":{"h":"inherent","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Naomi Persephone Amethyst (NaomiAmethyst)-inherent.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A part of something that is natural and cannot be separated from it.","e":"There may be problems inherent in hiring part-time staff."}]}]},"afternoon":{"h":"afternoon","i":"/ˌæftəˈnuːn/","a":"en-uk-afternoon.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Period from midday to sunset."}]}]},"awful":{"h":"awful","i":"/ˈɔːfʊl/","a":"en-us-awful.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Very bad. So bad that people don't want to think about it.","e":"When all the children were crying, it was just awful."}]}]},"agree":{"h":"agree","i":"/əˈɡriː/","a":"en-us-agree.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) When two people agree about something, they have the same ideas. They both think the same things are true.","e":"We agree that it will probably rain this afternoon."},{"m":"(intransitive) When two people agree to do some things, they say something like \"if you do this, then I will do that.\" After they agree, then they must do the things they said.","e":"We agreed to pay him $100 to paint the walls."}]}]},"away":{"h":"away","i":"/əˈweɪ/","a":"en-us-away.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"When something moves away from something else, the distance between them gets bigger. They are no longer near or close.","e":"Go away! You're bothering me."}]}]},"arrogant":{"h":"arrogant","i":"/ˈærəgənt/","a":"en-us-arrogant.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If Dan is arrogant, he thinks he is better or more important than other people.","e":"He is arrogant and that is why he is rude."}]}]},"deaf":{"h":"deaf","i":"/dɛf/","a":"en-us-deaf.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Somebody who is deaf, cannot hear or cannot hear well.","e":"She did not hear what I was saying because she's deaf."}]}]},"deafness":{"h":"deafness","i":"/ˈdɛfnəs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-deafness.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Someone with deafness cannot hear or cannot hear well.","e":"My mother's deafness keeps her from hearing me."}]}]},"niece":{"h":"niece","i":"/niːs/","a":"en-us-niece.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A niece is the female child of someone's sister or brother and is a part of their extended family.","e":"My brother has a daughter. She is my niece."}]}]},"partisan":{"h":"partisan","i":"/ˈpɑː.tɪˌzæn/","a":"en-us-partisan.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A partisan is a person who is a supporter of a political party, or of an idea. He or she may also be militant, ready to use force to fight for his or her cause."}]}]},"savoury":{"h":"savoury","i":"/ˈseɪvəri/","a":"en-us-savory.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Savoury means \"not sweet\". Food that is savoury does not taste sweet. The savoury course of a meal may have meat or fish and vegetables. This may be followed by a sweet course (called \"pudding\" or \"dessert\")."},{"m":"\"Savour\" can also mean the characteristic taste of something. It can also mean to enjoy something: \"He savoured every moment of it\"."}]}]},"purge":{"h":"purge","i":"/pɝdʒ/","a":"en-us-purge.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To purge an organization or an object means to clean it up of something bad.","e":"His attempt to purge our country of minorities was met with international criticism."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"When a purge occurs, an organization or an object is cleaned up of something bad.","e":"His purge of our country's minorities was met with international criticism."}]}]},"visible":{"h":"visible","i":"/ˈvɪzəb(ə)l/","a":"en-us-visible.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is visible, it can be seen.","e":"The car had no visible signs of damage."}]}]},"finite":{"h":"finite","a":"en-us-finite.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is finite, it has a limit. It doesn't keep going forever.","e":"This problem has a finite number of correct answers."}]}]},"publication":{"h":"publication","i":"/ˌpʌblɪˈkeɪʃən/","a":"en-us-publication.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Publication is the act of making a book or other thing publicly known or available where the public can use it.","e":"The Report itself and the debate that followed its publication have been useful."},{"m":"(countable) A publication is a book, magazine, paper, song, etc. that has been or will be published.","e":"Women's Strategies from Around the World, is a new publication from the United Nations Development Fund for Women (UNIFEM)."}]}]},"disturbance":{"h":"disturbance","i":"/dɪˈstɜːbn̩s/","a":"en-us-disturbance.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A disturbance is an uneasy feeling."},{"m":"To disturb means to stop someone or something by interrupting them."}]}]},"clumsiness":{"h":"clumsiness","i":"/ˈklʌm.zi.nəs/","a":"en-us-clumsiness.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Clumsiness is a lack of coordination; it is the condition of being clumsy."}]}]},"thesis":{"h":"thesis","i":"/ˈθiːsɪs/","a":"en-uk-thesis.oga","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A thesis is a long paper that university students at the masters or doctoral level write.","e":"I finished my coursework and have been working on my thesis for about a year now."},{"m":"(countable) A thesis is a main idea or argument that is developed or explained.","e":"This book has three major theses."}]}]},"knives":{"h":"knives","i":"/naɪvz/","a":"en-us-knives.ogg","l":"knife","q":"noun"},"set":{"h":"set","i":"/sɛt/","a":"en-us-set.ogg","l":"set","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you set something somewhere, you put something into a place.","e":"She sets the lamp on the floor."},{"m":"(transitive) If you set something, you put it into some state or condition.","e":"After changing the, you have to set the clock again."},{"m":"(transitive) If you set something, you define it or to fix its value.","e":"The teacher set a time limit of two minutes for this exercise."},{"m":"(transitive) If you set the table, you put dishes, forks and knives on it.","e":"I set the table for five people, but only three came."},{"m":"(intransitive) When the sun or moon sets, it moves toward the horizon.","e":"The sun sets every evening."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something sets, it dries and becomes solid.","e":"The concrete needs to set before a car can drive on it."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is set is fixed. It cannot be changed easily.","e":"Don't argue! The rules are set."},{"m":"To be ready for something.","e":"Are you set?"}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The set is the scenery for a theatrical work such as a play, ballet, musical, etc.","e":"The Metropolitan Opera's set for Aida is spectacular."},{"m":"A set is a group of things that are similar or can be used together.","e":"This chess set is too expensive to play chess with it."},{"m":"A set is a group of things, where every single one of them has a certain purpose. All of them are needed to perform a certain operation.","e":"To play poker, you need a set of playing cards and chips."},{"m":"Persons that have something in common may be called a set.","e":"That rich chick is a member of the Jet Set."},{"m":"A set is a machine which gets radio or television programs.","e":"This television set is broken."},{"m":"In many sports, a number of sets make up a game. An example of this would be in tennis or table tennis.","e":"The tennis player won the first two sets, but lost the game."}]}]},"khaki":{"h":"khaki","i":"/ˈkɑː.ki/","a":"en-au-khaki.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(colour) A dull yellowish-brown color, the color of dust."},{"m":"A strong cloth that is made of wool or cotton; khaki is often used for making military uniforms."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"(colour) Being dust-coloured."}]}]},"invoke":{"h":"invoke","i":"/ɪnˈvoʊk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-invoke.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When someone invokes a rule, they use the rule in a specific situation.","e":"For the government to do that legally, they would have to invoke the \"notwithstanding\" clause of the constitution."}]}]},"invoked":{"h":"invoked","l":"invoke","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When a rule is invoked, it is being used in a specific situation.","e":"That rule was not invoked during that meeting."}]}]},"likewise":{"h":"likewise","i":"/ˈlaɪkˌwaɪz/","a":"en-us-likewise.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"When someone does something likewise, they do it the same way someone else did it. Sometimes people say likewise to mean that they're saying the same thing someone else just said.","e":"I used one of the little spoons to eat my soup, and my friend did likewise."}]}]},"so-called":{"h":"so-called","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When someone uses the word \"so-called\" to talk about something, they mean that other people talk about the thing that way, but they don't agree.","e":"When are we going to leave this so-called party? (The person saying this thinks it should not be called a party. Probably they think the party is not fun.)"}]}]},"brilliant":{"h":"brilliant","i":"/ˈbrɪljənt/","a":"en-us-brilliant.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is brilliant, it gives off a lot of light.","e":"It was evening with the brilliant colors of sunset shining through the trees."},{"m":"If something is brilliant, it is very good.","e":"Truly brilliant ideas can sound crazy at first."},{"m":"If a person is brilliant, they are very intelligent.","e":"He was a brilliant teacher."}]}]},"disposal":{"h":"disposal","i":"[dɪsˈpəʊzəɫ]","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-disposal.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Disposal is the act of getting rid of or throwing out something.","e":"There is no long-term plan for nuclear waste disposal."},{"m":"(uncountable) If you have something at your disposal, it is available for you to use.","e":"Some of the students seem to have a lot of money at their disposal."}]}]},"solely":{"h":"solely","i":"/ˈsəʊl.li/","a":"en-us-solely.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"You use solely to say that somebody or something is the only one like that or that did it.","e":"It is not good for a country to rely solely on one energy source."}]}]},"deny":{"h":"deny","i":"/dɪˈnaɪ/","a":"en-us-deny.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you deny something, you say it didn't happen or isn't true.","e":"He denied charges that Vietnamese troops participated in the fighting."},{"m":"(transitive) If you deny somebody something, you stop them from having or doing it.","e":"A quick dive by the goal keeper denies Beckham the goal."}]}]},"bear":{"h":"bear","i":"/bɛə/","a":"en-us-bear.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bear is a big animal with a short tail. They either eat only meat or meat and plants. There are many different types of bears, for example brown bears and polar bears.","e":"Polar bears are white."},{"m":"Someone who acts rough and lacks manners could be called a bear."},{"m":"(countable) A large, hairy, homosexual man is called a bear."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If x bears y, x holds y up.","e":"This wall bears half the weight of the roof."},{"m":"(transitive) If someone bears something bad, they accept it or deal with it.","e":"He has to bear insults because of his appearance."},{"m":"(transitive) If a baby is born, it comes out of its mother.","e":"The woman bore a little boy."},{"m":"(transitive) If something is born, it is newly created.","e":"This idea was born out of boredom."},{"m":"(transitive) If something bears fruit, flowers, etc., it grows them.","e":"This apple tree is 100 years old, it does not bear apples anymore."},{"m":"(transitive) If x bears y, x holds y on the surface.","e":"Peter bears a small scar on his forehead."}]}]},"big":{"h":"big","i":"/bɪɡ/","a":"en-uk-big.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is big, it is large in size; tall, wide, long, or fat.","e":"He's bigger than me."},{"m":"If something is big, it is important.","e":"That's a big problem!"},{"m":"Someone's big brother or a big sister is one who is older than the person.","e":"I have a big brother who's stronger than you!"}]}]},"large":{"h":"large","i":"/lɑːdʒ/","a":"en-us-large.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Big; of great size; broad, tall, wide, long, or fat.","e":"I would like a large glass of milk."}]}]},"compile":{"h":"compile","i":"/kəmpʌɪl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-compile.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Someone compiles some things or ideas when they bring them together into one place.","e":"I need to compile a list of reasons not to go ahead with the project."}]}]},"panel":{"h":"panel","i":"/pænəɫ/","a":"en-us-panel.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A panel is a flat piece of wood or other material, used as part of a wall or on the side of something.","e":"The house has aluminium panels covering the outside."},{"m":"A panel is a group of people who come together at a table to talk or to judge, usually in front of many other people.","e":"The panel made a decision that Paul had won the dance contest."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To put panels on something."}]}]},"device":{"h":"device","i":"/dəˈvaɪs/","a":"en-us-device.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A device is a small machine or tool.","e":"She has a device in her kitchen for cutting garlic."},{"m":"(countable) A device is a machine or part attached to a computer, such as a keyboard, mouse, printer etc.","e":"The mouse is an important device for using the computer."},{"m":"(countable) A device is a clever way of doing something."},{"m":"(countable) A device is a logo."}]}]},"yet":{"h":"yet","i":"/jɛt/","a":"en-us-yet.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"When something hasn't happened yet, it didn't happen, but it might happen in the future.","e":"Is she there yet?"}]}]},"ambiguous":{"h":"ambiguous","i":"/æmˈbɪ.ɡju.əs/","a":"en-us-ambiguous.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is ambiguous, it has more than one possible meaning, state, or explanation.","e":"I think he fills his speeches with ambiguous words on purpose."}]}]},"ongoing":{"h":"ongoing","i":"/ˈɒnɡəʊɪŋ/","a":"en-us-ongoing.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something is ongoing if it's continuing to happen without stopping in one long period of time.","e":"The growth of bones is still ongoing at age 12."}]}]},"conceive":{"h":"conceive","i":"/kənˈsiːv/","a":"en-us-conceive.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you can conceive of a certain situation, you can imagine it.","e":"I just can't conceive of life without you."},{"m":"(intransitive) Someone conceives of an idea when they think of the idea for the first time, and it's their idea: they thought of it themselves, no one told them.","e":"The planners first conceived of the idea of making a large, curved building here in 1998."},{"m":"(transitive) A woman conceives a baby when she becomes pregnant (starts to carry a tiny baby inside her).","e":"The baby was conceived the day we went to Niagara Falls."}]}]},"notwithstanding":{"h":"notwithstanding","i":"/ˌnɒtwɪθˈstændɪŋ/","a":"en-us-notwithstanding-2.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If something is true notwithstanding something else, it is true in spite of that other thing.","e":"We're going ahead with the event as planned, notwithstanding the heavy rain and wind."}]}]},"submit":{"h":"submit","i":"/səbˈmɪt/","a":"en-us-submit.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you submit something, usually a piece of writing, you give it to somebody to be checked or accepted.","e":"They submitted their final report together with recommendations to the president."},{"m":"If you submit to some authority, you accept that they have power over you.","e":"At least up to 1985, the British government submitted to the threat of violence from the terrorists."}]}]},"trill":{"h":"trill","i":"/trɪl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-trill.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A consonant sound made by the tongue against the part of the mouth where the sound is being made, looser than a fricative such as \"s\" in \"sit\", but tighter than an approximant such as \"w\" in \"well\".","e":"The word arroz, meaning \"rice\", contains the alveolar trill (trill made on the roof of the mouth)."}]}]},"somewhat":{"h":"somewhat","i":"/ˈsʌmwɒt/","a":"en-us-somewhat.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(formal) a little, not very","e":"What happens in the classroom can be somewhat different from the lesson plan."}]}]},"empirical":{"h":"empirical","i":"/ɪmˈpɪrɪkəl/","a":"en-us-empirical.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is empirical, it is based on or can be checked by observation or experience.","e":"Simply because there is no empirical evidence to support this does not mean it's wrong. It simply means we haven't looked hard enough."}]}]},"phenomenon":{"h":"phenomenon","i":"/fəˈnɒmɪnən/","a":"en-uk-phenomenon.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A phenomenon is a fact or event that you can observe (see or hear or sense), especially one that is not fully understood.","e":"But this explanation is not enough to explain the observed phenomena."},{"m":"A phenomenon is a person, show, book, etc. that is very popular.","e":"'N Sync was something of a pop music phenomenon in the late 90s."}]}]},"patriarchy":{"h":"patriarchy","i":"/ˈpeɪt(ʃ)riɑrki/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-patriarchy.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A patriarchy is a society where the oldest male is considered to be the leader of the household."}]}]},"italics":{"h":"italics","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable), (usually plural) Italics are a style of letters written slanted. In English, they are usually used for stressing a word in a sentence or for foreign words.","e":"The sentences written in italics have been added or changed."}]}]},"italic":{"h":"italic","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable), (usually plural) Italics are a style of letters written slanted. In English, they are usually used for stressing a word in a sentence or for foreign words.","e":"The sentences written in italics have been added or changed."}]}]},"via":{"h":"via","i":"/ˈvi:ə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-via.wav","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"You use via to mean the path that something takes when it goes somewhere (the places it goes through before it gets there).","e":"We can send video, audio and data from any point in the UK, via satellite."}]}]},"centimeter":{"h":"centimeter","i":"/ˈsɛn.tɪ.miː.tə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-centimetre.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hundredth of a meter; 100 centimeters is one meter.","e":"This pencil is 18 centimeters long."}]}]},"break":{"h":"break","i":"/breɪk/","a":"en-us-break.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you break something, you make it come apart in a way that cannot easily be put back together, usually by force.","e":"He injured his leg and broke his foot during the crash."},{"m":"If something such as a machine breaks, it stops working because something is wrong.","e":"My car breaks down about once a week."},{"m":"(transitive) If you break a law, rule, promise, etc. you do something that you should not do.","e":"The police can't do anything if no laws are broken."},{"m":"(transitive) If you break a surface, limit, record, etc., you go beyond it.","e":"In 1954 he set a new record of 3:59.4, breaking the old record by more than five minutes."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you break free or out of something, you could not leave but now you leave.","e":"The police are looking for some prisoners who broke out of the jail."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you break, you stop for a short time to rest.","e":"We break for coffee at 10:00 every morning."},{"m":"(intransitive) If day or morning breaks, it begins.","e":"The day was breaking as they packed up the tent."},{"m":"If you break something, you stop it suddenly.","e":"The sound of the door closing broke the silence."},{"m":"(intransitive) If news breaks, it becomes known."},{"m":"(intransitive) If your voice breaks, it changes because you are almost crying.","e":"\"I wanted to say goodbye before he died\", she said, her voice breaking."},{"m":"(transitive) If you break some money, you change a note into coins.","e":"I don't want to break a twenty just to buy matches."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A break is a time when something stops before starting again.","e":"We get a 15-minute break in the middle of the morning."},{"m":"(countable) A break (up) is an end of a relationship.","e":"We didn't see each other for years after the break up."},{"m":"(countable) A break is a space between something continuous.","e":"The sun shone through a break in the clouds."},{"m":"(countable) A break is a situation in which things are not as difficult.","e":"That job opening up just when she finished school was a lucky break for her."},{"m":"(countable) A break is a place where something is broken.","e":"The break in his leg could be seen clearly on the x-ray."}]}]},"people":{"h":"people","i":"/ˈpiːpəl/","a":"en-uk-people.ogg","l":"person","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A people is a group of men, women, and children with a shared culture, history, and language.","e":"Although Lebanon and Syria are two countries they are one people."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive); If a place is peopled, people live there.","e":"It's a wonderful country peopled with amazing cooks and dancers."},{"m":"(transitive) If you people a story, movie, etc. you fill it with people.","e":"He liked to people his books with simple folk."}]}]},"cathedral":{"h":"cathedral","i":"/kəˈθiː.drəl/","a":"en-us-cathedral.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A church where a bishop is based.","e":"The new bishop took control of his cathedral."}]}]},"fifty":{"h":"fifty","i":"/ˈfɪfti/","a":"en-us-fifty.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(ordinal fiftieth) The number 50.","e":"There were fifty people in my class."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The number 50.","e":"tens is fifty."}]}]},"forty":{"h":"forty","i":"/ˈfɔrti/","a":"en-us-forty.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(ordinal fortieth) The number 40.","e":"He was forty minutes late."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The number 40.","e":"tens is forty."}]}]},"registry":{"h":"registry","i":"/ˈrɛdʒɪstri/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-registry.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A registry is an official list of names."}]}]},"paradigm":{"h":"paradigm","i":"/ˈpæ.rə.daɪm/","a":"en-us-paradigm.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A system of beliefs, ideas, values, and habits that is a way of thinking about the real world.","e":"At the time, this way of thinking was the dominant paradigm for social scientists."},{"m":"A paradigm is an example, model or pattern, especially the most basic or central one.","e":"For fifteen centuries Aristotle remained the paradigm of knowledge itself."},{"m":"(Grammar) A paradigm is the set of all word forms.","e":"The complete paradigm for boy is: boy, boy’s, boys, boys’, boyish."}]}]},"channel":{"h":"channel","a":"en-us-channel.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A channel is a path that or directs flow or movement, especially of TV & radio signals and water.","e":"He only watches two television news channels."},{"m":"The bottom and sides (\"banks\") of a river or other place where water moves."},{"m":"The natural or man-made deeper course through a reef, bar, bay, or any shallow body of water."},{"m":"The part of a river where boats can pass.","e":"We have to keep our boat in the channel."},{"m":"A narrow body of water between two land masses.","e":"The English Channel lies between France and England."},{"m":"A connection between and nodes of a circuit.","e":"The guard-rail provided the channel between the downed wire and the tree."},{"m":"The part that connects a data source to a data sink.","e":"A channel stretches between them."},{"m":"A path for conveying electrical or electromagnetic signals.","e":"We are using one of the 24 channels."},{"m":"A path provided by a transmission medium via physical separation, such as by multipair cable.","e":"The channel is created by bonding the signals from these four pairs."},{"m":"A single path provided by a transmission medium via spectral or protocol separation, such as by frequency or time-division multiplexing.","e":"Their call is being carried on channel 6 of the T-1 line."},{"m":"A specific radio frequency or band of frequencies, usually in conjunction with a predetermined letter, number, or codeword, and allocated by international agreement.","e":"KNDD is the channel at 107.7 MHz in Seattle."},{"m":"A specific radio frequency or band of frequencies used for transmitting television.","e":"NBC is on channel 11 in San Jose."},{"m":"The portion of a storage medium, such as a track or a band, that is accessible to a given reading or writing station or head.","e":"This chip in this disk drive is the channel device."},{"m":"The way in a turbine pump where the pressure is built up.","e":"The liquid is pressurized in the lateral channel."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you channel something, you direct its flow.","e":"We will channel the cars to the left."},{"m":"To take on the personality of another person.","e":"When it is my turn to sing Karaoke, I am going to channel Ray Charles."}]}]},"pose":{"h":"pose","i":"/pəʊz/","a":"en-us-pose.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A position or arrangement.","e":"What kind of pose is best for this photograph?"},{"m":"An unusual position."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To set in place."},{"m":"To ask, set (a test or quiz).","e":"The emcee will pose the tie-breaking question."},{"m":"To maintain a pose."},{"m":"to strike a pose or a position","e":"Will you pose for a photograph?"}]}]},"encounter":{"h":"encounter","i":"/ɪnˈkaʊntɚ/","a":"en-us-encounter.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An encounter is a meeting, usually one that you don't expect.","e":"I had a pleasant encounter yesterday: an old friend of mine visited me."},{"m":"(countable) An encounter is when two people or groups meet to play a game or fight a battle.","e":"I hope there will be no encounter with other soldiers tomorrow."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you encounter problems, difficulties, etc., you experience them.","e":"When he did encounter problems, he always knew how to fix them."},{"m":"(transitive) If you encounter someone, you meet someone, usually unexpectedly.","e":"In the store I encountered my teacher."},{"m":"(transitive) If you encounter someone, you meet them to play a game or fight a battle.","e":"At night the battle ship encountered enemy planes."}]}]},"persistent":{"h":"persistent","i":"/pɚˈsɪstənt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-persistent.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone or something is persistent, they continue and do not give up quickly.","e":"She has had a persistent cough for weeks."},{"m":"ing past maturity without falling off.","e":"Pine cones have persistent scales."}]}]},"undergo":{"h":"undergo","i":"/ˌʌndɚˈɡoʊ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-undergo.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you undergo something, it happens to you; often it is not nice.","e":"The country has undergone great changes in the last decade."}]}]},"convince":{"h":"convince","i":"/kənˈvɪns/","a":"en-us-convince.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To make someone believe, or feel sure about something.","e":"We have to convince her that the world is a sphere."}]}]},"disambiguation":{"h":"disambiguation","i":"/dɪsæmˌbɪɡjuːˈeɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-disambiguation.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"If I work on disambiguation, I am helping to get rid of things that are so similar that they cause confusion.","e":"This page is a disambiguation page."}]}]},"absolute":{"h":"absolute","i":"/ˈæb.səˌluːt/","a":"en-us-absolute.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An absolute is something that will always exist.","e":"Death is considered to be an absolute."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is absolute, it is complete or total.","e":"The light went out and he was in absolute darkness."}]}]},"active":{"h":"active","i":"/ˈæktɪv/","a":"en-us-active.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something is active if it is turned on or started.","e":"One of the computers was active: its screen was bright."},{"m":"If someone is active, he or she does exercise often or participates often.","e":"She was such an active 80-year-old that she ran the."},{"m":"A sentence is active if its subject does the action.","e":"\"Athena helped Odysseus\" is an active sentence because Athena is the one who helped."}]}]},"banyan":{"h":"banyan","i":"/ˈbænjən/","a":"en-us-banyan.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A banyan is a tropical Indian fig tree, Ficus benghalensis, that has many aerial roots."}]}]},"ultimately":{"h":"ultimately","i":"/ˈʌl.tɪ.mɪt.lɪ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-ultimately.wav","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"in the end; when nothing else is left","e":"We will all help, but it is you who are ultimately responsible."}]}]},"extract":{"h":"extract","i":"/ˈɛkstrækt/","a":"en-us-extract.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An extract is something that has been taken out of something else, usually something that it was part of.","e":"Just because a cream contains plant extracts doesn't mean it's good for your skin."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you extract something, you take it out of something else.","e":"Computers are becoming more useful in helping us extract useful information from the data."}]}]},"survive":{"h":"survive","i":"/səˈvaɪv/","a":"en-us-survive.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you survive something, you experience it and you did not die.","e":"They survived the war but died two years later."}]}]},"convert":{"h":"convert","i":"/ˈkɒn.vət/","a":"en-us-convert-noun.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you convert something, you change it so that it has a different function or form.","e":"They wanted to convert the room into a study."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A convert is a person who changed their beliefs or religion.","e":"Mr Kinnock is a relatively recent convert to Buddhism."}]}]},"transmission":{"h":"transmission","i":"/trænsˈmɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-transmission.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Transmission is the sending of something from one place to another, usually something like electricity, a message or a disease.","e":"Washing before touching food can prevent the transmission of disease in food and drink."},{"m":"(countable) A transmission is a signal, such as TV or radio, that is sent from one place to another.","e":"Radio stations have promised live transmission from the concert."},{"m":"A transmission in a machine is the parts that transfer the engine's movement to the wheels or other moving parts.","e":"The car comes with a four-speed automatic transmission."}]}]},"infer":{"h":"infer","i":"/ɪnˈfɝ/","a":"en-us-infer.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you infer something, you begin to believe it based on indirect information.","e":"We can infer from the old bones that this animal probably walked on two feet."}]}]},"guarantee":{"h":"guarantee","i":"/ˌɡærənˈtiː/","a":"en-us-guarantee.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A guarantee is a formal promise that a product will be fixed or replaced or money will be repaid if it breaks or doesn't work.","e":"The phone is covered by a six-month guarantee on parts and labour."},{"m":"(countable) A guarantee is a formal promise that something will happen or be done.","e":"The builders will now give performance and completion guarantees and will cover the costs of any problems."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you guarantee something, you promise to fixed or replace it or repay money if it breaks or doesn't work.","e":"All of our products are guaranteed against defects in materials and workmanship for 3yrs from date of purchase."},{"m":"(transitive) If you guarantee something, you make a formal promise that something will happen or be done.","e":"the European Convention on Human Rights, guarantees the right to give and receive information."}]}]},"guaranty":{"h":"guaranty","i":"/ˌɡærənˈtiː/","a":"en-us-guarantee.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A guaranty is a formal promise that a product will be fixed or replaced or money will be repaid if it breaks or doesn't work.","e":"The phone is covered by a six-month guaranty on parts and labour."},{"m":"(countable) A guaranty is a formal promise that something will happen or be done.","e":"The builders will now give performance and completion guaranties and will cover the costs of any problems."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you guaranty something, you promise to fixed or replace it or repay money if it breaks or doesn't work.","e":"All of our products are guarantied against defects in materials and workmanship for 3yrs from date of purchase."},{"m":"(transitive) If you guaranty something, you make a formal promise that something will happen or be done.","e":"the European Convention on Human Rights, guaranties the right to give and receive information."}]}]},"advocate":{"h":"advocate","i":"/ˈædvəkət/","a":"en-us-advocate-noun.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An advocate is someone who recommends something.","e":"She is a strong advocate for children's right to education."},{"m":"(countable) An advocate is someone who speaks for someone else, especially a lawyer in court.","e":"Volunteers are needed to act as advocates for people with mental health problems."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you advocate something, you recommend it.","e":"We wish for freedom, but cannot advocate the use of violence."}]}]},"dynamic":{"h":"dynamic","i":"/daɪˈnæmɪk/","a":"en-us-dynamic.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is dynamic, it is changing, usually quickly.","e":"Communication is a dynamic process in which the changing situation affects what you say and how you say it."},{"m":"If someone is dynamic, they take charge and get things done; they have a lot of energy.","e":"He was a good worker, but often unnoticed because of his more dynamic coworkers."},{"m":"of or about motion","e":"We tested the bar's strength in both static and dynamic tests."},{"m":"A dynamic verb describes an action with a clear end point.","e":"Dynamic, but not stative, verbs can take progressive aspect."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(usually plural) The dynamics of a situation or group are the ways in which everything effects everything else.","e":"We talk about what doctor should do without any real understanding of the dynamics of the doctor-patient relationship."},{"m":"(uncountable); Dynamics is a kind of mathematics that deals with motion and forces that cause changes in a system.","e":"They built a computer model based on the mathematics of fluid dynamics."},{"m":"Dynamics are changes in the loudness of music.","e":"The dynamics of the performance are lost in this poor recording."},{"m":"(singular) A dynamic is a force that causes change.","e":"This is where we need the dynamic of God's transforming presence."}]}]},"dynamics":{"h":"dynamics","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable); Dynamics is a kind of mathematics that deals with motion and forces that cause changes in a system.","e":"Work includes full-scale experiments, wind tunnel studies and computational fluid dynamics."}]}]},"insert":{"h":"insert","i":"/ɪnˈsɜːt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-insert (verb).wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) to put something into something else","e":"The company inserted a new clause into the contract."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An insert is something that is put into something else.","e":"The bathing suit top comes with foam inserts to make your breasts look bigger."}]}]},"reverse":{"h":"reverse","i":"/rəˈvɜː(r)s/","a":"en-us-reverse.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you reverse something, you make it act or move opposite to before (in the other direction).","e":"The new president reversed the decision to expand the factory."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The reverse of something is its opposite.","e":"Female professors are often married to male professors, but the reverse is not as common."},{"m":"In a machine, reverse is a setting that makes it act or move opposite to before.","e":"As the plane landed, the engines went into reverse, helping us to stop."},{"m":"The reverse of something is it's other side.","e":"Details can be found on the reverse of this paper."}]}]},"comprise":{"h":"comprise","i":"/kəmˈpraɪz/","a":"en-us-comprise.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If x comprises y, y is part of x.","e":"The United States comprises Hawaii and Alaska."},{"m":"(transitive) If x comprises y, y is all the things that, together, make x.","e":"The United States comprises 50 states."},{"m":"(transitive) If x comprises y, x is all the things that, together, make y.","e":"Fifty states comprise The United States."}]}]},"assertive":{"h":"assertive","i":"/əˈsɝtɪv/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-assertive.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"self-confident; having a habit of talking strongly about, and asking for what one wants, needs, deserves etc."},{"m":"Very confident; the person who is assertive is clear and direct."}]}]},"self-confident":{"h":"self-confident","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-self-confident.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Being self-confident is being confident about one's self.","e":"Sally is self-confident, and she thinks that she can do anything."}]}]},"confidence":{"h":"confidence","i":"/ˈkɒnfɪdəns/","a":"en-us-confidence.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Confidence is the state of trusting something, and being sure that something is going to happen.","e":"I know you're trying to gain confidence in what you're doing."}]}]},"state":{"h":"state","i":"/steɪt/","a":"en-uk-state.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A state is a condition or a situation.","e":"I am worried about her. She is in a constant state of depression."},{"m":"(countable) Any sovereign nation (nation that rules itself) is a state.","e":"The United States is a country with many sovereign nations united with each other."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To state something is to say it as a fact.","e":"He stated that he hasn't slept in 2 days."},{"m":"(transitive) To state something is to let it be known.","e":"Please state your name and place of business."}]}]},"hierarchical":{"h":"hierarchical","i":"/ˌhaɪərˈɑːkɪkəl/","a":"en-us-hierarchical.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is hierarchical, it has levels, with higher levels being larger, more important, more powerful, etc.","e":"The rules show the hierarchical structure of the company."}]}]},"comprehensive":{"h":"comprehensive","i":"/ˌkɒm.prɪˈhɛn.sɪv/","a":"en-us-comprehensive.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is comprehensive, it includes everything that is related.","e":"The book includes the most comprehensive list of existing government programs."}]}]},"mode":{"h":"mode","i":"/məʊd/","a":"en-us-mode.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mode is a specific way of doing something.","e":"The study combines two different research modes: oral history and written history."},{"m":"(countable) A mode is a fashion or style.","e":"She was always dressed in the latest mode."},{"m":"(countable) A mode is a specific type or form of something.","e":"Heat is a mode of energy transfer, like work, not a substance or other seawater property."},{"m":"(countable); A mode is specific a kind scale.","e":"The Mixolydian mode is a good way for inducing a bluesey kind of mood."},{"m":"(countable); (statistics) The mode is the number that occurs most often in a group of numbers.","e":"In a normal distribution, with large sets, the mean, median and mode will typically be the same value."},{"m":"(countable); A mode is specific a kind of clause that shows how the speaker feels about it. Modes show whether something is true, probably true, a wish, etc. Usually called mood.","e":"In Finnish, for example, the conditional mode is used both in the main clause and the subordinate."},{"m":"(countable); The mode of a rock is the different minerals in it."},{"m":"(countable); A mode is a specific pattern of wave movement.","e":"Under normal circumstances, there is no between the two modes, which have different propagation constants."}]}]},"differentiation":{"h":"differentiation","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Differentiation finding or showing the differences between things.","e":"In the shop, there was no differentiation between product from Asia and product from Europe."},{"m":"(uncountable) Differentiation is the process of becoming or making something different.","e":"As the cells grow and divide, differentiation takes place. You can begin to see some as muscle cells, some as blood cells, etc."},{"m":"(uncountable) Differentiation is acting different towards different people or situations.","e":"Schools tend to have little formal curricular differentiation between the sexes, except in physical education."},{"m":"(uncountable); Differentiation is the process of obtaining the derivative of a function."}]}]},"eliminate":{"h":"eliminate","i":"/ɪ'lɪməneɪt/","a":"en-au-eliminate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you eliminate something, you make it go away or disappear, or you kill it.","e":"The recent fixes have eliminated the problems we were having."}]}]},"priority":{"h":"priority","i":"/praɪˈɒrɨti/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-priority.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A priority is something that is important; you want to do it first or spend more time or money on it than other things.","e":"Learning the language is a high priority for all people who move to the country."},{"m":"(uncountable) If something has or is given priority, it should go before other things.","e":"The Government needs to give a higher priority to the quality of life."}]}]},"ideology":{"h":"ideology","i":"/aɪ.di.ˈɑl.ə.d͡ʒi/","a":"en-us-ideology.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An ideology is the set of beliefs behind a movement, religion, political group, etc.","e":"Schools reflect clearly the dominant political ideologies of their countries."}]}]},"foundation":{"h":"foundation","i":"/faʊnˈdeɪʃən/","a":"en-us-foundation.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The foundation of something is the basic ideas or work behind it.","e":"These early inventions laid the foundations of modern radio technology."},{"m":"(countable) The foundation of a building is the solid base that is under it and that supports it.","e":"They dug solid foundations, spending a lot of time pouring concrete into four pits."},{"m":"(countable) A foundation is an organisation that collects money to do good things.","e":"The Open Software Foundation has opened up laboratories to test software."},{"m":"(uncountable) The foundation of a group, business, country, etc. is the act of starting it.","e":"The company has double in size every year since its foundation."},{"m":"(uncountable) Foundation is the first layer of cream or makeup.","e":"Dot the foundation over the face-on the nose, the cheeks, the chin and spread working from the face outwards."}]}]},"depravity":{"h":"depravity","i":"/dəˈprævɪti/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-depravity.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The state or condition of being depraved; moral debasement.","e":"He was a very bad man, lost in depravity."},{"m":"(countable) A very bad act or trait.","e":"Susan's depravity was her husband's murder."},{"m":"(uncountable) (Christianity) that is part of human nature, contamination by sin.","e":"Our depravity is the result of Adam's fall."}]}]},"ductile":{"h":"ductile","i":"/ˈdʌk.taɪl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-ductile.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is ductile, it can be stretched into wire, usually metal."},{"m":"If something is ductile, it can easily be molded into a new shape."},{"m":"If someone is ductile, they are easily lead; they are prone to follow."}]}]},"adaptation":{"h":"adaptation","i":"/ˌæd.əpˈteɪ.ʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Wodencafe-adaptation.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An adaptation is a change to fit a different situation or the result of that change, especially when a story goes from book to TV or movie.","e":"The new film adaptation of the classic book Little Women is quite wonderful."},{"m":"(uncountable) Adaptation is the process of changing to fit a different situation.","e":"These products undergo a constant process of change and adaptation."}]}]},"edible":{"h":"edible","i":"/ˈɛdɪbəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-edible.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something is called edible if it can be eaten by humans and animals without danger to their health.","e":"These mushrooms are edible."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An edible is something that you can eat.","e":"The apple is an edible."}]}]},"quotation":{"h":"quotation","i":"/kwoʊˈteɪʃən/","a":"en-us-quotation.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A quotation is a sentence or phrase that was said by someone and is now being used or referred to by somebody else. Quotations can be from books, movies, speeches, television shows, songs, etc.","e":"This chapter began with a quotation from Monica Furlong."},{"m":"(uncountable) Quotation is the act of using somebody else's exact words."},{"m":"(countable) (commerce) A quotation is a report of the cost or value of something."}]}]},"quote":{"h":"quote","i":"/kwəʊt/","a":"en-us-quote.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To use someone's exact words.","e":"Did he quote me in the newspaper?"}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A quote is somebody's exact words used by somebody else.","e":"In the following quote, a young woman describes her experience with drugs."},{"m":"(countable); (commerce) A quote is a report of the cost or value of something."}]}]},"absent":{"h":"absent","i":"/ˈæbsənt/","a":"en-us-absent.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is absent, it means to be not in a place or missing.","e":"John is absent from school today."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you absent yourself from something, you do not turn up for it and not appear.","e":"John absented himself from the meeting as he had something on."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Absent means without or barring.","e":"Absent any problems, we should be finished in two hours."}]}]},"effective":{"h":"effective","i":"/ɪˈfɛktɪv/","a":"en-us-effective.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"An effective strategy, treatment, method, etc is one that works well as planned.","e":"Teachers are using instructional strategies that are most effective in helping students learn."},{"m":"If you have effective command, consent, control, etc., you have it in practice but not officially.","e":"The students had effective control over what the teacher would include on the test."},{"m":"If a law, agreement, change, etc. becomes effective, it officially begins.","e":"The new rules about ball size are effective next season."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"You use effective to tell when something starts officially.","e":"Effective next week, all employees will wear the new uniform."}]}]},"preliminary":{"h":"preliminary","i":"/prɪˈlɪmɪnɛri/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-preliminary.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is preliminary, it is a preparation for a main matter."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A preliminary is a preparation for a main matter."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"before","e":"Preliminary to the main discussions, perhaps we could introduce ourselves."}]}]},"regardless":{"h":"regardless","i":"/rɪˈɡɑrd.lɪs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-regardless.wav","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If x happens regardless of y, y does not change x.","e":"She left, regardless of him asking her to stay."}]}]},"contrary":{"h":"contrary","i":"/ˈkɒntrəri/","a":"en-us-contrary.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If an act or idea is contrary to something, it is against it.","e":"The president's actions are contrary to the constitution and therefore illegal."},{"m":"You use contrary to x when x is different from the truth.","e":"Contrary to popular belief, the oil companies cannot control the price of crude."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A contrary view, sentence, etc. is opposite to other ones.","e":"The contrary view is that these kind of projects are a waste of money."},{"m":"A contrary person tries to be different from other people or does not often agree with others."},{"m":"The contrary is the opposite of an idea, sentence, etc.","e":"It is best to believe people are good, at least until the contrary is shown."}]}]},"successive":{"h":"successive","i":"/səkˈsɛsɪv/","a":"en-us-successive.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Successive things follow in order, one after another.","e":"Successive governments have refused to make the changes."}]}]},"innovation":{"h":"innovation","i":"/ˌɪnəˈveɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-innovation.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Innovation is the process of making something new and original.","e":"Our company has stayed in the lead largely by encouraging innovation."},{"m":"(countable) An innovation is something new and original.","e":"The number of technical innovations is growing at a faster and faster rate."}]}]},"prohibit":{"h":"prohibit","i":"/prəˈhɪbɪt/","a":"en-us-prohibit.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you prohibit something, you say that it must not be done.","e":"The laws were changed to prohibit the use of certain tools."},{"m":"If x prohibits y, y is not possible because of x.","e":"The use of a password prohibits access to outsiders."}]}]},"isolate":{"h":"isolate","i":"/ˈaɪsəleɪt/","a":"en-us-isolate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you isolate something, you make it so that it does not or cannot contact certain other things.","e":"We want to isolate ourselves from everyday worries."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An isolate is something that does not or cannot contact certain other things.","e":"A total of 296 isolates were recovered from 105 patients, 79 (75%) of whom were infected with mycobacteria."},{"m":"An isolate is a language that has no known relatives."}]}]},"isolated":{"h":"isolated","i":"/ˈaɪsəleɪtɪd/","a":"en-us-isolated.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you isolate something, you make it so that it does not or cannot contact certain other things.","e":"We went to isolate ourselves from everyday worries."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is isolated it is alone.","e":"As she got older and her friends moved away, she became more and more isolated."}]}]},"problem":{"h":"problem","i":"/prɒbləm/","a":"en-us-problem.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A problem is something that is difficult to do, understand, or believe.","e":"If you have a problems with the computer, I can probably help."},{"m":"(countable) A problem is a question on a test.","e":"Most students got the right answer for the first problem."},{"m":"You say \"no problem\" to agree to do something.","e":"\"Could you open the door for me?\" \"Sure, no problem!\""},{"m":"You say \"no problem\" after somebody thanks you or apologises to you.","e":"\"Thank you so much for all your help.\" \"No problem! Any time!\""}]}]},"eat":{"h":"eat","i":"/iːt/","a":"en-us-eat.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you eat something, usually food, you put it in your mouth, chew it, and swallow it.","e":"I always eat too much good when it's Thanksgiving."},{"m":"(transitive) If you eat the cost of something, you pay for it.","e":"The supplier will have to eat the cost of returning the goods."},{"m":"(taboo) If you eat someone, you give them sex with your mouth (oral sex)"}]}]},"sarcasm":{"h":"sarcasm","i":"/ˈsɑːrˌkæzəm/","a":"en-us-sarcasm.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"that is not serious but is meant to mimic. Saying something you don't mean, to be funny or to make someone feel bad.","e":"\"No, I don't want any food, I'm just standing here holding an empty plate to make my fingers stronger,\" he said with sarcasm."}]}]},"think":{"h":"think","i":"/θɪŋk/","a":"en-us-think.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you think that something is or may be true, you feel that it is or may be true.","e":"You know you can't do that. What were you thinking?"},{"m":"(intransitive) If you think about something, you use your mind to give it your attention.","e":"\"What's the best way?\" \"I'm not sure. Let me think.\""},{"m":"(intransitive) You use think when you have words or ideas in your mind without saying them out loud.","e":"\"It's no good,\" she thought."},{"m":"(intransitive) You use think in suggestions and requests.","e":"I was thinking we could go out tonight."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you don't think to do something, you don't remember to do it.","e":"I didn't think to ask her."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"If you say you'll have a think about something, it means you'll give it your attention."}]}]},"highlight":{"h":"highlight","i":"/ˈhaɪ.ˌlaɪt/","a":"en-us-highlight.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you highlight something, you make it more noticeable or obvious.","e":"I usually use a pen to highlight the important section in my textbook."},{"m":"(transitive) If you highlight your hair, you make some parts a lighter colour."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A highlight is a particularly good part.","e":"The chicken was the highlight of the dinner, just amazing."},{"m":"(countable) A highlight is a light-coloured area.","e":"The shirt was blue with yellow highlights."}]}]},"inspection":{"h":"inspection","i":"/ɪnˈspɛkʃən/","a":"en-us-inspection.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An inspection is a careful look at something, usually for problems.","e":"Before the flight, the pilot did a complete inspection of the airplane."}]}]},"termination":{"h":"termination","i":"/tɚmɪˈneɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-termination.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Termination is the act of ending something.","e":"We will continue to do business in Asia after termination of the Japan program."},{"m":"The termination is the end point, time or limit of something.","e":"Three years after the termination of war in 1945, France was fighting another war in Indo-China."},{"m":"Termination is when you lose your job.","e":"The company will cut costs through the termination of 150 employees."},{"m":"Termination is the act of killing something.","e":"The group is against the termination of these sick babies."},{"m":"(countable) A termination is a suffix or the end of a word.","e":"The termination of a verb in the past tense is usually \"ed\"."}]}]},"displacement":{"h":"displacement","i":"/dɪsˈpleɪsmɪnt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-displacement.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Displacement is when something is made to move out of its place.","e":"The war has caused the displacement of tens of thousands of people."},{"m":"(uncountable); Displacement is the amount of liquid or gas that is moved when something floats in it."}]}]},"restraint":{"h":"restraint","i":"/rɪˈstreɪnt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-restraint.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Restraint is the quality people show when they don't do something they shouldn't do.","e":"You already ate too much cake. Now please show some restraint."},{"m":"(countable) A restraint is a strap or other thing that holds a person in place, like a seatbelt in a car or handcuffs that the police use to hold someone.","e":"A baby needs the right kind of restraint to ride safely in a car."},{"m":"(countable) A restraint is something that stops people from doing something.","e":"A legal restraint prevents him from going to meet his ex-girlfriend."}]}]},"reinforce":{"h":"reinforce","i":"/ˌriː.ɪnˈfɔːs/","a":"en-us-reinforce.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you reinforce something, you make it stronger.","e":"Recent mistakes only reinforce the view that nobody cares."}]}]},"denote":{"h":"denote","i":"/dɪˈnəʊt/","a":"en-us-denote.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If x denotes y, x is a sign of or has the meaning of y.","e":"The term \"sales mix\" is used to denote the percentage of total sales of each product."}]}]},"offset":{"h":"offset","i":"/ˈɒf.sɛt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-offset1.wav","l":"offset","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If x offsets y, the loss (because) of y is balanced by x.","e":"The school will provide limited scholarships to offset the cost of tuition."},{"m":"(transitive) If you offset x against y, you compare of contrast them.","e":"All this solid colour is offset by the tiny yellow green flowers."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An offset is something that balances (the loss of) something else."},{"m":"(uncountable) A particular way of printing where the ink moves from surface A to B and then from B to the final C."},{"m":"(countable) The image produced by this kind of printing."},{"m":"An offset is the distance that something moves away from where it is supposed to be or where it was."}]}]},"obedience":{"h":"obedience","i":"/ə(ʊ)ˈbiːdɪəns/","a":"en-us-obedience.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The act of obeying orders from others.","e":"Obedience is very important in any army."},{"m":"(uncountable) behavior in which you do what good person, father, boss, teacher, tells you to do."}]}]},"cowardice":{"h":"cowardice","i":"/ˈkaʊədɪs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-cowardice.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Someone who shows cowardice is being afraid, not having courage, not doing something they should do because they are afraid.","e":"He showed cowardice when he ran away and left his friend to fight the other children."}]}]},"exploitation":{"h":"exploitation","i":"/ˌɛksplɔɪˈteɪʃn̩/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-exploitation.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Exploitation is the use of something, usually for profit.","e":"The commercial exploitation of Alaska for oil could lead to serious environmental problems."},{"m":"(uncountable) Exploitation is the use or treatment of someone unfairly.","e":"Today, most countries have laws against the exploitation of children in factories."}]}]},"detect":{"h":"detect","i":"/dɪˈtɛkt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-detect.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you detect something, you use your senses to find or notice it.","e":"Some insects can detect changes in temperature as small as 0.003 degrees Celsius."}]}]},"abandon":{"h":"abandon","i":"/əˈbændən/","a":"en-us-abandon.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you abandon something, you go away from it with no plan to return.","e":"Many teens abandon all chances of a successful future when they drop out of school."},{"m":"(transitive) If you abandon something, you give up control of it.","e":"They danced wildly down the street, abandoning themselves to the night and the moon."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Abandon is a state where you do not control yourself.","e":"In these games, kids shoot and blow each other up with reckless abandon."}]}]},"ram":{"h":"ram","i":"/ræm/","a":"en-us-ram.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A ram is a male sheep."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you ram something, it means that you hit it hard, causing damage.","e":"The racer rammed into the barriers when turning."},{"m":"If you ram someone during sexual intercourse, it means that you thrust your partner forcefully."}]}]},"random":{"h":"random","i":"/ˈrændəm/","a":"en-us-random.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is random, there is no purpose, reason, or pattern.","e":"I have to sit there like typing in random keywords to see if it's a keyword."},{"m":"(statistics) If a process is random, every option has an equal chance of happening.","e":"20 per cent of the random sample of the libraries were public in any normal sense of the word."}]}]},"revision":{"h":"revision","i":"/rəˈvɪ.ʒ(ə)n/","a":"en-au-revision.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A revision is a change or edit a to language, a plan, etc.","e":"This book needs a lot of revision before it can be published."},{"m":"(countable) A revision is a piece of writing or plan that has changed or will change.","e":"The software includes the latest revisions to the HTML standards."},{"m":"(uncountable) In the UK, revision is the process of studying something again.","e":"I need to do more revision for the test."}]}]},"virtually":{"h":"virtually","i":"/'vəːtjʊəlɪ/","a":"en-us-virtually.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Just about; almost but not quite","e":"Once you put it on, it is virtually impossible to remove."}]}]},"devote":{"h":"devote","i":"/dɪˈvoʊt/","a":"en-us-devote.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If someone devotes time or energy to something, they feel that it is important and they spend a lot of time or energy on it.","e":"I devoted ten years of my life to writing that book."}]}]},"refine":{"h":"refine","i":"/rɪˈfaɪn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-refine.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When someone refines something, they make it better.","e":"We need to refine our way of organizing this office."},{"m":"When people refine a food or other thing, they make it purer.","e":"They take sugar cane and refine it to make white sugar."}]}]},"insight":{"h":"insight","i":"/ˈɪnsaɪt/","a":"en-us-insight.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A very good understanding of something; a clear idea about how something works.","e":"We need to get some insight into the causes of this problem."}]}]},"violation":{"h":"violation","i":"/ˌvaɪɵˈleɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-violation.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A violation of a rule is an act of breaking the rule: going past the limits of the rule.","e":"The speed you were driving your car was a violation of the speed limit."}]}]},"coincide":{"h":"coincide","i":"/ˌkoʊɪnˈsaɪd/","a":"en-us-coincide.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) Two things coincide with each other if they're both in the same place or at the same time.","e":"The time of your party coincides with my niece's wedding, so I can't come."}]}]},"medium":{"h":"medium","i":"/ˈmiːdiəm/","a":"en-us-medium.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A medium amount is an amount that is not small and not large, but in the middle.","e":"Would you like a small, medium or large drink?"}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A medium is stuff that something moves through.","e":"Light can go through different media: air, water, glass."},{"m":"(countable) A medium is a person who hears ideas that come from people who are dead. (plural mediums)","e":"We all closed our eyes, and the medium said \"I hear your father speaking.\""}]}]},"portion":{"h":"portion","i":"/ˈpɔrʃən/","a":"en-us-portion.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A portion is a part of something.","e":"We need to put more signs up in this portion of the city."},{"m":"(countable) A portion is an amount of food for one person.","e":"Each portion has six meatballs."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you portion something out, you give parts of it to different people.","e":"They portioned out the water among them."}]}]},"qualitative":{"h":"qualitative","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A reason, idea or writing is qualitative if it is about the way something is, or about the thing's qualities, but not about amounts.","e":"I have a qualitative idea of what his work is like, but I don't know how much work he's done."}]}]},"trigger":{"h":"trigger","i":"/ˈtrɪɡə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-trigger.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A trigger is the part of a gun that you push with one finger when you want to make the gun shoot.","e":"I didn't want to make him angry, because he had his finger on the trigger."},{"m":"A trigger is a little thing that makes something bigger happen.","e":"Bad smells are one of the triggers for my headaches."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"A little thing triggers a big thing to happen when it causes it.","e":"Those angry words triggered the beginning of the war."}]}]},"format":{"h":"format","i":"/ˈfɔːmæt/","a":"en-us-format.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The format of some writing is the way it is organized: the size and colour of the letters, the way it is divided into parts, the kind of words used.","e":"What format do you want the report written in?"},{"m":"(countable) The format of some writing is the kind of computer program you need to be able to read it.","e":"I can't read that page you sent me. My computer doesn't read that format."},{"m":"(countable) Something's format is its style, type, organisation, etc.","e":"The format of the meeting will be quite casual."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) Someone formats some writing when make it have a particular format.","e":"How should I format the report?"},{"m":"(transitive) Someone formats a computer disk when they prepare a disk for writing and reading.","e":"You need to format the disk before you can copy those files onto it."}]}]},"mediation":{"h":"mediation","i":"/midiˈeɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-mediation.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Mediation is the process of helping two people or groups who are not in agreement to come to an agreement.","e":"When I was separated from my wife, we had mediation to help decide who got to keep the house."}]}]},"mature":{"h":"mature","i":"/məˈtjʊə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-mature.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Someone is mature if they act like an adult.","e":"You're not mature enough to do this job."},{"m":"A living thing is mature if it has stopped growing physically.","e":"A mature female is about 30&nbsp;kg."},{"m":"Some kinds of food, such as wine, cheese, or fruit are mature when they are ready to eat or drink."},{"m":"A mature person is older.","e":"Colleges are accepting more mature students and fewer kids out of high school."},{"m":"If something is mature, it is fully developed.","e":"Television is a mature technology."},{"m":"If movies, books, etc. are mature, they are meant for adults because they contain violence, sex, etc."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If something matures, it becomes fully developed.","e":"Along the way she has also matured into a beautiful young woman."}]}]},"diminish":{"h":"diminish","i":"/dɪˈmɪnɪʃ/","a":"en-us-diminish.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When something diminishes it gets smaller or less important or makes something that way.","e":"The way you talked just now diminished my respect for you."}]}]},"analogous":{"h":"analogous","i":"/ʌˈnæl.ʌ.gəs/","a":"en-us-analogous.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When x is analogous to y, it is similar to y.","e":"Using that little broom to sweep this big floor is analogous to using a candle to cook dinner for 40 people."}]}]},"temporary":{"h":"temporary","i":"/ˈtɛmpərəri/","a":"en-us-temporary.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something is temporary if it's only for a short time.","e":"A tent was our temporary home after our house burned down in the fire."}]}]},"fluctuation":{"h":"fluctuation","i":"/flʌktʃuːˈeɪʃən/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A fluctuation is when something changes back and forth quickly.","e":"The price of wheat stayed the same, but there were a lot of fluctuations in the price of rice."}]}]},"minimal":{"h":"minimal","i":"/mɪnəməl/","a":"en-us-minimal.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is minimal, it is very small or small enough to not be important, especially the smallest.","e":"We had a minimal amount of rain yesterday, so we still need to water the plants."}]}]},"wage":{"h":"wage","i":"/weɪʤ/","a":"en-us-wage.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable); (often plural) Wages is the money a person is paid for doing their job.","e":"Only 6 percent of the wage earners in this country earn more than $ 100,000."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you wage a battle, war, or campaign for or against something, you fight or work hard for or against it.","e":"After his death in 1990, a five-year battle was waged in court for control of the $72 million estate."}]}]},"incompatible":{"h":"incompatible","i":"/ˌɪŋkəmˈpætɪbəl/","a":"en-us-incompatible.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Two things are incompatible with each other if they don't fit together or don't work well together.","e":"The husband and wife were not happy together because they were incompatible."}]}]},"eighty":{"h":"eighty","i":"/ˈeɪ.ti/","a":"en-us-eighty.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(ordinal eightieth) Eighty is the number 80.","e":"There were about eighty people at the party."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The number 80.","e":"plus ten is eighty."}]}]},"commence":{"h":"commence","i":"/kəˈmɛns/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-commence.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(formal) If something commences, it begins.","e":"The school year commenced on Sept. 4."}]}]},"vision":{"h":"vision","i":"/ˈvɪʒ(ə)n/","a":"en-us-vision.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Vision is being able to see with your eyes.","e":"Now I'm old and my vision is not very good, so I don't drive a car any more."},{"m":"Vision is being able to think of good ideas for the future.","e":"This woman will be a good leader of our company because she has great vision about the future of our company."}]}]},"endemic":{"h":"endemic","i":"/ɛnˈdɛm.ɪk/","a":"en-us-endemic.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Endemic means that a species (or other taxon) belongs to something else. If an animal is endemic to a place (or habitat), it only exists in that habitat.","e":"Some trout are endemic to."}]}]},"significantly":{"h":"significantly","i":"/sɪɡˈnɪfɪkəntli/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-significantly.wav","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"in an important or large enough way","e":"The price of gas dropped significantly today, causing drivers to line up at the pumps to fill up."},{"m":"with a particular meaning","e":"He looked at her significantly."}]}]},"favorite":{"h":"favorite","i":"/ˈfeɪv.rɪt/","a":"EN-AU ck1 favourite.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"My favorite brand is the brand I like most.","e":"Ford is my favorite brand of truck."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A favorite is a thing or person that someone likes the most. It is a thing that someone prefers, or likes more than any other.","e":"ice cream is my favorite."},{"m":"(countable) When kings and other royalty have favorites, these are people they trust.","e":"He was a favorite of the king."}]}]},"foreign":{"h":"foreign","i":"/ˈfɒrən/","a":"en-us-foreign.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Foreign means something that comes from a different place or country. Foreign people are known as foreigners.","e":"Sven has a foreign accent."},{"m":"Foreign can mean something that is not familiar or not characteristic.","e":"Greed was as foreign to him as a Frenchman in China."}]}]},"horizontal":{"h":"horizontal","i":"/ˌhɒrɪˈzɒntəl/","a":"en-us-horizontal.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is lying down or \"straight across\" is horizontal. In a horizontal direction means straight across.","e":"The road across the Nullabor plain is horizontal."},{"m":"To be horizontal means to have something to do with the horizon."}]}]},"vertically":{"h":"vertically","i":"/ˈvɜːtɪkli/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-vertically.wav","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"In a vertical direction or position.","e":"The cliffs fell vertically down to the sea."}]}]},"horizontally":{"h":"horizontally","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"In a horizontal direction or position.","e":"The pictures were arranged horizontally around the room."}]}]},"write":{"h":"write","i":"/raɪt/","a":"en-us-write.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you write a book, an article, a computer program, a piece of music, etc., you create it.","e":"My dream is to write a children's book."},{"m":"If you write, you use letters, numbers, or other marks on paper or on a computer to show words.","e":"Can you write your name and phone number here for me?"},{"m":"If you write, you send a letter to someone.","e":"Please, phone or write me when you have some time."},{"m":"(computer) If a computer writes, it records something in its memory or on a disk.","e":"Old computers were much slower at writing files."}]}]},"thereby":{"h":"thereby","a":"en-us-thereby.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"(formal) in that way or by that means","e":"He pulled it closer to him, thereby making it far easier to get up."}]}]},"uniform":{"h":"uniform","i":"/ˈjuːnɪfɔːm/","a":"en-us-uniform.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A uniform is clothing that is very similar and worn by a group of people.","e":"All the young army men wore identical uniforms and badges of rank."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is uniform, there is no variation in it.","e":"It was designed to be uniform from one end to the other."}]}]},"predominantly":{"h":"predominantly","i":"/prɪˈdɒmɪnəntli/","a":"en-us-predominantly.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"mostly, mainly","e":"The predominantly male, white judges treat men and women differently."}]}]},"implicit":{"h":"implicit","i":"/ɪmˈplɪsɪt/","a":"en-us-implicit.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A meaning that is implicit is understood or given but not directly.","e":"There is an implicit assumption that women should be acting more like men."},{"m":"A belief that is implicit is complete and without question.","e":"Jonadab was used to implicit obedience from his children and was surprised at his son's answer."}]}]},"clarity":{"h":"clarity","i":"/ˈklær.ɪ.ti/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-clarity.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Clarity is the quality of being clear.","e":"She dreamed, with great clarity, that she had seen her own death."}]}]},"conformity":{"h":"conformity","i":"/kənˈfɔrmɪti/","a":"en-us-conformity.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Conformity is the state of being or becoming similar to other members of a group.","e":"In high school, students who do not show a high degree of conformity are often not accepted by other students."},{"m":"(uncountable) Conformity is the state of following rules or expectations.","e":"The army is there to ensure conformity with the UN resolutions."}]}]},"giant":{"h":"giant","i":"/ˈdʒaɪ.ənt/","a":"en-us-giant.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A giant is a very big man or woman, often in fairy tales.","e":"Jack climbed the beanstalk and found a land ruled by a giant."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a thing is giant, it is very big.","e":"He bought a giant doll at the fair."}]}]},"contemporary":{"h":"contemporary","i":"/kənˈtɛm.p(ə).rər.i/","a":"en-contemporary.oga","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is contemporary it is related to this time (now). Technically, this is an incorrect usage; better is to use \"modern\", \"now\" or \"present-day\".","e":"The artist has a great knowledge of the sources of historical and contemporary art."},{"m":"If x is contemporary with y, they happened at about the same time.","e":"They are sources that are contemporary or near contemporary with the period being studied."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Somebody's contemporary is a person who lived at or near the same time.","e":"This is what made Marx so different from his socialist contemporaries."}]}]},"breach":{"h":"breach","i":"[briːtʃ]","a":"en-us-breach.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you breach a duty, you do something that you should not do."},{"m":"(transitive) If an army or the police breach a barrier, a wall, etc., they were not able to enter it before but now they can.","e":"The police breached the front door and searched the house."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A breach is the act of breaching; for example, a breach of contract may occur when somebody does not do what they promised."},{"m":"(countable) A breach can also be a hole.","e":"Water entered through a breach in the levee."}]}]},"enter":{"h":"enter","i":"/ˈentə/","a":"en-us-enter.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To enter is to go into something.","e":"I entered the building through the side door."},{"m":"(intransitive) To enter is to go in.","e":"Please pay the fare before you enter."},{"m":"(transitive) To type something into a computer.","e":"I entered all the necessary information but it still won't work."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"\"Enter\" is a key on a computer keyboard."}]}]},"fare":{"h":"fare","i":"/fɛə/","a":"en-us-fare.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A fare is money that you pay for public transportation; that is, to ride on a bus, taxi, train or airplane.","e":"The city is planning to increase its bus fares again."}]}]},"duty":{"h":"duty","i":"/ˈdjuːti/","a":"en-us-duty.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A duty is something that you should do.","e":"Parents have the duty to educate their children."},{"m":"A tax placed on imports or exports; a tariff, customs duty, excise duty.","e":"Import duty and taxes are due when importing goods into the United States."}]}]},"violate":{"h":"violate","i":"/ˈvaɪəˌleɪt/","a":"en-us-violate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To violate means to break something like a law.","e":"A person violated the copyright of a book."}]}]},"neglect":{"h":"neglect","i":"/nɪˈɡlɛkt/","a":"en-us-neglect.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you neglect someone, you do not take care of them."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Neglect is the failure of somebody to do a duty."}]}]},"batter":{"h":"batter","i":"/ˈbætə(r)/","a":"en-us-batter.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A batter is somebody who is supposed to hit a ball with a bat."},{"m":"A batter is a mixture of flour and liquid (usually eggs and water)."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you batter someone or something, you hit or beat it.","e":"The battered child was brought to the attention of the police."}]}]},"beat":{"h":"beat","i":"/biːt/","a":"en-us-beat.ogg","l":"beat","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you beat someone or something, you hit it, usually many times.","e":"It made a loud noise when he beat the drum."},{"m":"(transitive) If you beat a person or a team, you win and they lose.","e":"The best team usually beats the worst one."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Beat is the rhythm of music."},{"m":"(countable) A heartbeat."}]}]},"automatically":{"h":"automatically","i":"/ˈɔːtəʊˌmæt.ɪk(.ə)li/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-automatically.wav","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something happens automatically, it happens without the need for a person to start it or do anything more.","e":"The door closed and locked automatically behind him."},{"m":"If you do something automatically, you do it without thinking about it.","e":"If a man and woman spend time together, you shouldn't automatically assume they're lovers."}]}]},"handshake":{"h":"handshake","a":"en-uk-handshake.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A handshake is when two people hold hands for a few seconds and move them up and down before letting go. It is often used like a greeting (like saying \"hello\" or \"goodbye\" when people meet) or to say that two people have agreed on something.","e":"When I meet someone, I give a firm handshake."}]}]},"heir":{"h":"heir","i":"/eə(r)/","a":"en-us-heir.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An heir is the person who gets the property or money when someone dies.","e":"Jack was his only heir, so he will get all the money."}]}]},"grandchild":{"h":"grandchild","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A grandchild is the grandson or granddaughter of someone. It is the child of someone's child.","e":"Jemima is my grandmother. She is my father's mother. I am her grandchild."}]}]},"incumbent":{"h":"incumbent","i":"/ɪnˈkʌmbənt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-incumbent.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An incumbent is a person who currently holds a type of position, often in politics.","e":"She was an incumbent in the last election for the office she holds."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is incumbent, they are in a political position now.","e":"They are incumbent in this election because they are in office."}]}]},"intersect":{"h":"intersect","i":"/ɪntɚˈsɛkt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-intersect.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When lines intersect, it means they meet at one point.","e":"Main Street intersects 10th Avenue here."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The place where two lines or segments meet is called an intersect.","e":"The intersect of line A and line B is at point X."}]}]},"daughter-in-law":{"h":"daughter-in-law","i":"/ˈdɔːtə(r)ɪnˌlɔː/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-PerfectSoundWhatever-daughter-in-law.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The wife of a person's son. The opposite of a daughter-in-law would be a son-in-law, or a daughter's husband."}]}]},"plus":{"h":"plus","i":"/plʌs/","a":"en-us-plus.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"You use plus when you add numbers.","e":"Two plus two is four. (2 + 2 = 4)"},{"m":"and also","e":"The farm has over 5,000 horses, plus a few cats and dogs."},{"m":"You use plus after a number to mean more than or over.","e":"The country has a population of 3 million plus."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A plus is a good thing.","e":"I know you don't like it, but there are big pluses about living here."},{"m":"(countable) A plus is a plus sign: +","e":"You don't have to write the plus in front of positive numbers, but always write the minus in front of negative numbers."}]}]},"invisible":{"h":"invisible","i":"/ɪnˈvɪzəb(ə)l/","a":"en-us-invisible.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something is invisible when we can not see it.","e":"light is invisible to animals and humans."}]}]},"jihad":{"h":"jihad","i":"/dʒɪˈhɑːd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-jihad.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A jihad is a personal fight with yourself to become a better person."},{"m":"A jihad is a holy war by Muslims to stop people from keeping down other people by force.","e":"The Muslims have started a jihad against the Israelis."}]}]},"pay":{"h":"pay","i":"/peɪ/","a":"en-us-pay.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you pay, you give money for something.","e":"Bess worked for eight hours and they paid her a hundred dollars."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Your pay is money you receive after doing something.","e":"Go to the office to receive your pay."}]}]},"restore":{"h":"restore","i":"/rɪˈstɔr/","a":"en-us-restore.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you restore a state, feeling, or ability that has been lost, you make that possible or normal again.","e":"Police were sent to restore order after an attack on May 4."},{"m":"(transitive) If you restore something, you make it go back to the way it was.","e":"The school is restoring the buildings that were damaged in the fire."},{"m":"(transitive) If you restore something, you put or give it back.","e":"The lost child was restored to her parents by police."}]}]},"accumulation":{"h":"accumulation","i":"/ə.ˌkjuːm.jə.ˈleɪ.ʃən/","a":"en-us-accumulation.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An accumulation of something, is a number or amount of it that has come together over time.","e":"The failure to pump leads to an accumulation of blood in the heart."},{"m":"(uncountable) Accumulation is the process of bringing things together.","e":"The process of salt accumulation in the soil speeds up under poor watering conditions."}]}]},"appendix":{"h":"appendix","i":"/əˈpɛndɪks/","a":"en-us-appendix.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An appendix is a part at the back of a book that has extra information.","e":"See Appendix B for a list of irregular verbs."},{"m":"Your appendix is a small part of your body that is attached to your large intestine.","e":"It was common for children to die from a burst appendix."}]}]},"widespread":{"h":"widespread","i":"/ˌwaɪdˈsprɛd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-widespread.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is widespread, it happens or exists in many situations or places.","e":"This particular bird is only found here, but similar species are very widespread."}]}]},"accompany":{"h":"accompany","i":"/əˈkʌm.pə.ni/","a":"en-us-accompany.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If one thing accompanies something else, it comes or goes with it, or they happen together.","e":"She accompanied me to the hospital after my accident."},{"m":"(transitive) If person A accompanies person B on a musical instrument, B sings or plays the main part while A plays along.","e":"Joe Falcon sings and plays the accordion and is accompanied by Cleoma Breaux on guitar."}]}]},"prospect":{"h":"prospect","i":"/ˈprɒspɛkt/","a":"en-us-prospect.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A prospect is what you think will happen in the future.","e":"There's a good prospect of this building being converted into a school."},{"m":"(countable) Your prospects are your chances of moving forward in your job or in your life.","e":"So I would congratulate her on her good prospects as a teacher."},{"m":"(countable) A prospect is somebody that think will do well in the future.","e":"At 18, she is one of Britain's best prospects for an Olympic medal in Barcelona this summer."},{"m":"(countable) A prospect is somebody who might be a customer or worker in the future.","e":"Your best prospects are your previous customers."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you prospect for something valuable, such as gold or oil, you search an area for it.","e":"Anglo-United was not the only company prospecting for gold in the early eighties."}]}]},"post":{"h":"post","i":"/pəʊst/","a":"en-us-post.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Post is the letters and parcels that you send to other people.","e":"There's no post today because it's a Sunday."},{"m":"A post is a tall rod or stick. Examples are a sign post, a lamp post, and a goal post."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you post something, you send it through the post.","e":"I posted a birthday card to him last week."},{"m":"(transitive) If you post a message, you add it to a website or discussion board.","e":"I posted a reply to your comment on the website."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"after","e":"Post the test results becoming public, there were many complaints."}]}]},"penny":{"h":"penny","a":"en-us-penny.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A penny is a small coin of little value; 100 pennies (or 100 pence) make a pound, a dollar, a euro, etc.","e":"This sweet only costs a penny."}]}]},"hear":{"h":"hear","i":"/hiːr/","a":"en-us-hear.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you hear a sound, you notice it with your ear.","e":"I heard music coming from the next room."}]}]},"paragraph":{"h":"paragraph","i":"/ˈpæ.rə.græf/","a":"en-us-paragraph.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A paragraph is one or more sentences that are written together with no line breaks separating them. Usually they are connected by a single idea.","e":"She knew what it would say after reading the first paragraph."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you paragraph something, you break it into paragraphs.","e":"It's hard to read with no breaks. Can you paragraph it out a bit?"}]}]},"spic":{"h":"spic","i":"/ˈspɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-spick.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Spic is an insulting word for a Latino or Hispanic person."}]}]},"petition":{"h":"petition","i":"/pəˈtɪ.ʃən/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A petition is a written request to change something."},{"m":"A petition is a list of signatures showing support for something or opposition against it.","e":"Please sign our petition to get a new snack machine in the school cafeteria."},{"m":"A petition is a written document that people sign to show that they want a person or organization to do or change something.","e":"In honor of his memory, a petition has been sent to persuade the Postal Services Stamp Advisory Committee to put Willis Conover on a U.S. postage stamp."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To petition for something is to make a request for it, usually in writing.","e":"You should petition for a shorter work week."}]}]},"infrastructure":{"h":"infrastructure","i":"/ˈɪnfrəˌstrʌk(t)ʃɚ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-infrastructure.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A place's infrastructure is the basic public works such as roads, electricity & water supply, and schools, that allow it to function.","e":"The construction of the BAM railway will provide an infrastructure for exports to Japan and the US."},{"m":"The infrastructure is the basic ideas and systems that support an organisation or a project.","e":"The hardware-software system provides an infrastructure for messaging applications across the company."}]}]},"deviation":{"h":"deviation","i":"/diviˈeɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-deviation.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A deviation is difference or movement away from a standard.","e":"They insist that there must be no deviation from that style."},{"m":"(countable) (statistics) A deviation is the difference between a number and the average of a set of values."}]}]},"guideline":{"h":"guideline","i":"/ˈɡaɪdˌlaɪn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-guideline.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A guideline is a formal suggestion about how something should be done, but it is not a rule.","e":"If you are a new driver you should try to follow these basic safety guidelines."},{"m":"(countable) A guideline is a line on a page that helps you see where to write or how to draw something."},{"m":"(countable) A guideline is a rope or string that shows you where to go."}]}]},"commodity":{"h":"commodity","i":"/kəˈmɑdəti/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-commodity.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A commodity is something that is bought or sold.","e":"The price of corn and other farming commodities has dropped by 10%."},{"m":"(countable) A commodity is a valuable quality or thing.","e":"Hope may become a very rare commodity."}]}]},"minimise":{"h":"minimise","i":"/ˈmɪn.ɪ.maɪz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-minimize.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you minimise something, you make it as small as possible.","e":"We should take all steps to minimise the risk of disease."}]}]},"minimize":{"h":"minimize","i":"/ˈmɪn.ɪ.maɪz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-minimize.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you minimize something, you make it as small as possible.","e":"We should take all steps to minimize the risk of disease."}]}]},"philanthropy":{"h":"philanthropy","i":"/fɪˈlæn.θrə.piː/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-philanthropy.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Philanthropy is the giving away of money for charity.","e":"The man that lived in that mansion was admired for his philanthropy. He would often donate millions to charities."}]}]},"practitioner":{"h":"practitioner","i":"/prækˈtɪʃənə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-practitioner.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A practitioner is a person who works in a profession or following a particular style or belief, especially related to health care.","e":"Acupuncture practitioners use fine needles to stimulate specific points of the body."}]}]},"challenging":{"h":"challenging","i":"/ˈtʃæləndʒɪŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-challenging.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is challenging, it is not easy but it can be done.","e":"For a longer, wilder and more challenging route, you can explore the beautiful mountains around Goatfell."}]}]},"nominate":{"h":"nominate","i":"/ˈnɒm.ɪ.neɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-nominate.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To name someone for a role or position, including that of an office.","e":"Jim nominated Tom to be the leader of their group"},{"m":"(transitive) To name something for an award or prize.","e":"The movie was nominated for an."}]}]},"radical":{"h":"radical","i":"/ˈrædɪkəl/","a":"en-au-radical.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A radical change, difference, etc. is very big and important; from the roots.","e":"The plan will not be easy and requires a radical change in the culture of the city."},{"m":"A radial idea, policy, etc. is one that is new and different; not standard.","e":"More radical organisations like Greenpeace and Friends of the Earth have brought attention to these issues."},{"m":"Of or about a root (e.g., \\sqrt{4}=2, the roots of plants, the root of a word, etc.)"},{"m":"cool","e":"Dude, that outfit is rad!"}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A radical is a person whose views are very different from most people.","e":"Leading radicals have called for a two-hour general strike on Monday."},{"m":"(countable) A quantity expressed as a root of another quantity. (e.g., \\sqrt{4})"},{"m":"(countable) An atom or a group of atoms with at least one unpaired electron."},{"m":"(countable) The basic part of a word to which other parts can be added (e.g., runner)"},{"m":"(countable) A radical is one part of a Chinese or Japanese written character that can be combined with other parts to form a whole character."}]}]},"chart":{"h":"chart","i":"/tʃɑrt/","a":"en-us-chart.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A chart is information that is organised in rows and columns or as a picture.","e":"In India as a whole the figure is about 40% (see chart)."},{"m":"(countable) (often plural) A chart is a list of most popular songs, movies, etc. that is published regularly.","e":"This week, the newest Star Wars movie is topping the charts."},{"m":"A map of seas or oceans."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you chart something, you record it in a chart."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something charts, it is on a list of most popular things."},{"m":"(transitive) If you \"chart a course\" you find out how to get somewhere."}]}]},"librarian":{"h":"librarian","i":"/laɪˈbrɛr.i.ən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-librarian.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A librarian is a person who manages a library.","e":"You can ask the librarian to help you find the book."}]}]},"buy":{"h":"buy","i":"/baɪ/","a":"en-us-buy.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you buy something, you give money and the thing becomes yours.","e":"Could you buy some milk at the store?"},{"m":"(transitive) If money buys something, it is enough money to pay for it.","e":"$10 doesn't even buy a case of beer."},{"m":"(transitive) If you buy (somebody) time, you stop something from happening soon so that you have time to prepare for it.","e":"She went to the washroom to buy time. She didn't want to answer before Kate arrived."},{"m":"(transitive) If you buy an idea, you believe it.","e":"Your mother won't buy the story about getting lost."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A buy is something that someone has bought, usually for a cheap price.","e":"This dress was a good buy. It was on sale."}]}]},"opinionated":{"h":"opinionated","i":"/əˈpɪn.jə.neɪ.tɪd/","a":"en-us-opinionated.ogg","l":"opinionate","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are opinionated, you have opinions, especially strong opinions.","e":"She has strong feelings about many topics; she is an opinionated person."}]}]},"homophone":{"h":"homophone","i":"/ˈhɒməfəʊ̯n/","a":"en-us-homophone.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A word that sounds like another word, even though they have different meanings.","e":"\"\" and \"write\" are homophones."}]}]},"liver":{"h":"liver","i":"/ˈlɪvə/","a":"en-us-liver.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A large organ in the body that makes bile, and controls chemicals in the blood.","e":"The liver is one of the most important organs in our body."},{"m":"An organ used for food.","e":"We're having beef liver for dinner."},{"m":"The colour of the liver, a dark brown."}]}]},"livers":{"h":"livers","l":"liver","q":"noun"},"appreciation":{"h":"appreciation","i":"/ʌ.pri.ʃiˈeɪ.ʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-appreciation.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"; (singular) An appreciation of something is the ability to see it's value and understand it.","e":"He now has a far greater appreciation of dogs and the people who handle them professionally."},{"m":"(uncountable) Appreciation is the feeling of being thankful.","e":"I just wanted to send you this card to show my appreciation for your kindness last week."},{"m":"; (singular) Appreciation is the rise in value of something.","e":"The appreciation of the Japanese yen against the US dollar has helped the American automobile industry."}]}]},"currency":{"h":"currency","i":"/ˈkʌr.ən.si/","a":"en-us-currency.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A currency is the money from a particular country.","e":"A person going abroad can obtain foreign currency notes and travellers' cheques from his own bank."},{"m":"(uncountable) If something has currency, it is generally accepted.","e":"After the war, these new ideas began to gain currency."},{"m":"(uncountable) The state of being up to date.","e":"A book's bibliography can be a good indicator of currency in the text."}]}]},"labor":{"h":"labor","i":"/leɪbə/","a":"en-uk-labour.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Labor is the work that people do, usually lifting, moving, building, etc. rather than desk work.","e":"The cost of labor is higher than the cost of building materials."},{"m":"(uncountable) Labor are the people who do this kind of work.","e":"There's a big labor shortage in the construction industry."},{"m":"(uncountable) Labor is the process a pregnant woman goes through when she is giving birth.","e":"She was in labor for more than 12 hours before her baby was born."},{"m":"Labor is the name of a big political party in the United Kingdom, Ireland, Australia, and New Zealand.","e":"Labor won the election."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you labor, you work hard.","e":"He labored over the food all afternoon to get ready for dinner."},{"m":"(transitive) If you labor the point, you keep talking about it after people understand it well."}]}]},"inevitably":{"h":"inevitably","i":"/ɪˈnɛvɪtəbli/","a":"en-us-inevitably.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"(also a sentence adverb) You use this to say that something cannot be avoided.","e":"A drop in the number of worker in a country inevitably leads to higher wages."}]}]},"rumour":{"h":"rumour","i":"/ˈruːmə(r)/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-rumor.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A rumour is a story about somebody or something, that is told by other people, most of the time it is not true.","e":"There is a rumour going around that John's been fired. Is it true?"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) (usually used in passive voice) If you rumour, you gossip; you tell someone a rumor.","e":"It has been rumoured that John's moving soon. Is this true?"}]}]},"induce":{"h":"induce","i":"/ɪnˈduːs/","a":"en-us-induce.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you induce something, you make it happen.","e":"Soft lighting is often used for in restaurants to induce a feeling of relaxation."}]}]},"schedule":{"h":"schedule","i":"/ˈʃɛdjul/","a":"en-us-schedule.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A schedule is a plan of things that are happening and the times when they happen.","e":"He visits each village in his or her area on a weekly schedule."},{"m":"(countable) (formal) A schedule is a list, usually one with prices.","e":"Please see the enclosed schedule of costs for and."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you schedule something, you make a plan for when and where it will happen.","e":"The party was originally scheduled for June 5th."}]}]},"androgyny":{"h":"androgyny","i":"/ænˈdrɑd͡ʒəni/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-androgyny.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Androgyny is hermaphroditism."},{"m":"Androgyny is having both masculine and feminine characteristics."},{"m":"Androgyny is looking neither masculine nor feminine."}]}]},"intensity":{"h":"intensity","i":"/ɪnˈtɛnsɪti/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-intensity.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The intensity of something is the amount of it in a given time or space.","e":"These flowers suffer from high intensity of sunlight."},{"m":"Intensity is a high level of power, strength, feeling, etc.","e":"Marie understood the intensity of the old woman's hatred."}]}]},"exhibit":{"h":"exhibit","i":"/ɛɡˈzɪbɪt/","a":"en-us-exhibit.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"You exhibit something when you show it to others.","e":"He exhibited the new product to the audience."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An exhibit is something that is shown to others.","e":"There is a new exhibit at the museum on the subject of Chinese history."}]}]},"bias":{"h":"bias","i":"/ˈbaɪəs/","a":"en-us-bias.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A bias is a preference in one direction that makes things unequal.","e":"There is strong evidence of a bias towards the death penalty for black rather than white murderers."},{"m":"(countable) The bias is the diagonal direction, especially in cloth.","e":"The neckline was cut on the bias to improve the drape of the fabric."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you bias something, you unfairly make one result more likely than another.","e":"Sexism in language biases experience constantly towards the male sex."}]}]},"manipulation":{"h":"manipulation","i":"/ˈmən.ɪpˌjʊu.leɪ.ʃʌn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-manipulation.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Manipulation is the act of controlling someone or something, usually through pressure or in dishonest ways.","e":"The political manipulation of statistics to confuse people is common."},{"m":"(uncountable) Manipulation is the act of using your hands skillfully to move, play or operate something.","e":"He tried to remove the piece by gentle manipulation from the outside."}]}]},"theme":{"h":"theme","i":"/θiːm/","a":"en-us-theme.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A theme is a general idea that runs through a conversation, story, group of images, piece of music, etc.","e":"For Mr Giuliani, crime is a main campaign theme."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you theme something, you give it a [[#Noun|theme]]."}]}]},"bulk":{"h":"bulk","i":"/bʌlk/","a":"en-us-bulk.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The bulk of something is the largest part of it.","e":"The bulk of the shipment was headed for Toronto."},{"m":"(uncountable) Someone or something's bulk is its size or amount, especially if it is large.","e":"She took a deep breath, and, enormously grateful for the solid bulk of Leo at her back, she stepped inside."},{"m":"(uncountable) If you sell something in bulk, it is not individually packaged.","e":"I usually buy nuts at the bulk food store."},{"m":"(uncountable) If you buy something in bulk, you buy large amounts.","e":"The store offers discounts for buying in bulk."},{"m":"(countable) A bulk is an item that is moved about like cargo."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something bulks, it appears to be big in size."},{"m":"If you bulk something, you increase its' size; you expand it."}]}]},"behalf":{"h":"behalf","i":"/bɪˈhæf/","a":"en-us-behalf.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"If you do something on someone's behalf, you do it for them or as their representative.","e":"We give you this award on behalf of a grateful nation."}]}]},"unify":{"h":"unify","i":"/ˈjuːnɪfaɪ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-unify.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you unify something or a group of things, you bring them together as one.","e":"When she explained it, all the different pieces of information and ideas came together for me in a unified whole."}]}]},"erosion":{"h":"erosion","a":"en-us-erosion.oga","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Erosion is the loss of land because of water and wind.","e":"Farming increases soil erosion by breaking up soil structure, and reducing the number of plants."},{"m":"(uncountable) Erosion is a slow loss of something.","e":"The new plan should stop the erosion of support for the idea."},{"m":", (countable) An erosion is a shallow lesion that is usually found on the skin or in tissue of the epithelium."}]}]},"anticipate":{"h":"anticipate","i":"/ænˈtɪs.ɪ.peɪt/","a":"en-us-anticipate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you anticipate something, you think or do something about it before it happens.","e":"The seasonal changes in temperature are anticipated by birds through the changes of day length."}]}]},"cease":{"h":"cease","a":"en-us-cease.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you cease something, you stop doing it.","e":"Around the time of the First World War, Clark brothers ceased operations, and the mill finally fell silent."}]}]},"mutual":{"h":"mutual","i":"/ˈmjuːt͡ʃuəl/","a":"en-us-mutual.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is mutual x does it to y, and y does it to x.","e":"The working relationship between the two men was based on a mutual respect."},{"m":"A mutual friend, agreement, etc. is one that is shared between two or more people.","e":"I learned of her accident through a mutual friend."}]}]},"norm":{"h":"norm","i":"/nɔːm/","a":"En-us-norm.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A norm is the usual situation, amount, level, etc.","e":"CDs are dying out and MP3s are becoming the norm."}]}]},"intermediate":{"h":"intermediate","i":"/ɪntə(r)ˈmɪidɪiət/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-intermediate (adj, noun).wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is intermediate, it is between other things.","e":"Most people who get beyond the beginner stage get stuck being intermediate."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An intermediate is someone who acts between other people."},{"m":"An intermediate is something that is intermediate."}]}]},"manual":{"h":"manual","i":"/ˈmænjuəl/","a":"en-us-manual.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is manual, it is done with the hands or through physical work.","e":"Unskilled manual workers are the most likely to lose their job when the economy changes."},{"m":"Manual dexterity, detergents, etc. are for or related to hands.","e":"Video games increase your manual dexterity and hand to eye co-ordination."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A manual is a book of instructions.","e":"I need to fix this, but I can't find the manual."}]}]},"supplementary":{"h":"supplementary","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is supplementary, it is added on; it is not needed, but it is often useful.","e":"Many immigrants are employed but also feel the need to seek supplementary income."}]}]},"spoken":{"h":"spoken","i":"/'spoʊkən/","a":"en-us-spoken.ogg","l":"speak","q":"verb"},"spoke":{"h":"spoke","i":"/ˈspəʊk/","a":"en-us-spoke.ogg","l":"speak","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) One of many rods that are between the center and outer surface of a wheel."}]}]},"speaks":{"h":"speaks","i":"/ˈspiːks/","a":"en-us-speaks.ogg","l":"speak","q":"verb"},"concurrent":{"h":"concurrent","i":"/kəŋˈkɝrənt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-concurrent.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If two things are concurrent, they happen at the same time.","e":"The software can handle up to 500 concurrent users."},{"m":"If two things are concurrent, they agree in meaning.","e":"The police got concurrent stories from five witnesses."},{"m":"If three or more lines are concurrent, they are alongside one another (parallel)."}]}]},"ethical":{"h":"ethical","i":"/ˈɛθɪkəl/","a":"en-us-ethical.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"An ethical issue, problem, etc. relates to questions of good or bad, right or wrong.","e":"Doctors have to think about both the medical and ethical parts of the problem."},{"m":"If something is ethical, it is good, not bad or wrong. Often, this is based on formal philosophy. Often, what is ethical is based on rules of a group or profession (kind of job).","e":"Is it really ethical to eat meat?"}]}]},"integral":{"h":"integral","i":"/ˈɪntɪɡrəl/","a":"en-uk-integral-noun.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Integral parts, elements, etc. belong to a larger whole, often being necessary.","e":"The parks and green spaces are an integral part of the city."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An integral is the result of a particular mathematical function.","e":"F(x) is the integral of f(x) if \\frac{d[F(x)]}{dx} = f(x)."}]}]},"conversely":{"h":"conversely","i":"/kənˈvɜːsli/","a":"en-au-conversely.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Conversely is used to say that one idea is the opposite of the other idea.","e":"The over-confident driver may drive too fast. Conversely the under-confident person may also cause problems by driving too slowly."}]}]},"household":{"h":"household","i":"/ˈhaʊshəʊld/","a":"en-us-household.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A group of people who live together; the group may or may not be a family. A household may also be an individual living alone.","e":"How many people are there in your household?"}]}]},"confine":{"h":"confine","i":"/kənˈfaɪn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-confine (verb).wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you confine someone or something to a particular topic or activity, you do not let them do other topics or activities.","e":"Humphrey did not confine his activities just to the factory."},{"m":"(transitive) If you confine somebody or something, you put them in a place that they cannot leave.","e":"For the first twenty years he was confined in prison-like conditions."}]}]},"accommodation":{"h":"accommodation","i":"/ə.ˌkɒm.ə.ˈdeɪ.ʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-accommodation.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) (usually accommodations in American English) Accommodation is a place to stay or live.","e":"The hotel provides high quality accommodation, mostly for foreign visitors."},{"m":"Accommodation is the process or result of changing something to fit a particular need or situation.","e":"During the 1990s Iran tried twice to reach an accommodation with its long time rival."}]}]},"unnamed":{"h":"unnamed","i":"/ˌʌnˈneɪmd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-AnotherFriendlyHuman-unnamed.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is unnamed, it does not have a name."}]}]},"distort":{"h":"distort","i":"/dɪsˈtɔrt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-distort.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something is distorted, its shape or meaning is changed, often in a bad or unnatural way.","e":"Christina backed away from Michael, whose handsome face was twisted and distorted by hatred."}]}]},"passive":{"h":"passive","i":"/ˈpæs.ɪv/","a":"en-us-passive.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is passive, they do not normally respond or take action.","e":"Watching TV is a much more passive activity than reading."},{"m":"A passive clause has the natural object as its subject.","e":"While \"she hit me\" is an active clause, \"I was hit (by her)\" is passive."}]}]},"meetings":{"h":"meetings","a":"en-us-meetings.ogg","l":"meeting","q":"noun"},"allow":{"h":"allow","i":"/əˈlaʊ/","a":"en-us-allow.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you allow something, you let it happen; you say it's OK.","e":"We were not allowed to enter the building."}]}]},"bank":{"h":"bank","i":"/bæŋk/","a":"en-us-bank.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A building where you can keep and borrow money.","e":"I have to stop at the bank to deposit my check and get money for tonight."},{"m":"(countable) A safe place to store important things.","e":"blood bank"},{"m":"(countable) The dry sides of a river."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"The act of a plane turning left or right while in flight.","e":"The plane banks right to line up with the runway."}]}]},"nature":{"h":"nature","i":"/ˈneɪtʃə/","a":"en-us-nature.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The outdoors or outside.","e":"We went on a nature walk."},{"m":"(uncountable) Things that people did not make. The world or universe.","e":"Nature contains many beautiful things."},{"m":"(countable) The way something is without people causing it, or a quality people did not cause. Often, this is a part of your personality that is natural to you.","e":"She has a very gentle nature."}]}]},"student":{"h":"student","i":"/ˈstjuː.dənt/","a":"en-uk-student.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A student is person who a subject, especially in a school.","e":"I am a student at the school."},{"m":"(countable) A student person who is very interested in a subject.","e":"He's a student of the game and can answer any baseball question you ask."}]}]},"study":{"h":"study","i":"/ˈstʌdi/","a":"en-us-study.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A study is a formal effort to learn about something, usually with a written report at the end.","e":"A recent study of New Mexico, completed using national survey data, indicates that many older New Mexicans are returning to school."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you study something, you make an effort to learn it.","e":"We study math at the school."}]}]},"elect":{"h":"elect","i":"/ɪˈlɛkt/","a":"en-us-elect.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you elect to do something, you choose to do it or make a decision to do it.","e":"I elected to take Geography this semester but I'll be taking Chemistry next semester."},{"m":"If you elect someone, especially a candidate, you choose them in an election.","e":"We elect a president every four years."}]}]},"president":{"h":"president","i":"/ˈprɛzɨdənt/","a":"en-us-president.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A president is the person in charge of a country.","e":"The president stopped the war."},{"m":"(countable) A president is the leader of a business.","e":"The president of the company stepped down yesterday."}]}]},"once":{"h":"once","i":"/wʌns/","a":"en-us-once.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"one time","e":"We go to the house once a year."},{"m":"at a time in the past, but not now","e":"It was hard to believe that once we had been friends."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"after","e":"Once I've finished cleaning up, we can leave."}]}]},"age":{"h":"age","i":"/eɪd͡ʒ/","a":"en-us-age.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Something's age is how long it has existed or been alive; how old something is.","e":"The boy said he was age five."},{"m":"(countable) An age is a time period.","e":"The 1960s was a new age in music."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If a person ages, they get older.","e":"Lillian has aged gracefully."},{"m":"(transitive) If you age something, you allow to mature.","e":"We age the whiskey for five years."}]}]},"video":{"h":"video","i":"/ˈvɪd.i.əʊ/","a":"en-us-video.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A video is a television show or movie."},{"m":"(uncountable) Video is moving pictures.","e":"We watched a video in class."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you video something, you record it with a camera or camcorder."}]}]},"boob":{"h":"boob","i":"/ˈbuːb/","a":"en-us-boob.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"breast"},{"m":"(Australia, US) prison"}]}]},"subordinate":{"h":"subordinate","i":"/səˈbɔːdɪnət/","a":"en-us-subordinate.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is subordinate, it is less important than someone or something else.","e":"Keeping our natural world healthy remains subordinate to the health of the economy."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A subordinate is someone who is at a lower position in an organization.","e":"A good manager will talk with her subordinates before making most decisions."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you subordinate x to y, you give less importance to x and more to y.","e":"When he fell in love, everything else was subordinated to it."}]}]},"scenario":{"h":"scenario","i":"/sɛˈnɑːriəʊ/","a":"en-us-scenario.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A scenario is a possible or imagined future, often with detailed plans.","e":"The worst scenario for Nicky, I imagined, would be if Enya suddenly fell in love with another producer."}]}]},"assurance":{"h":"assurance","i":"/əˈʃʊrəns/","a":"en-us-assurance.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An assurance is a strong promise, usually given when the listener has doubts.","e":"She had been here before and could give assurance that they were on the right course."},{"m":"(uncountable) Assurance is the feeling of self confidence.","e":"Cocteau in his trademark suit stared with absolute assurance into the camera."}]}]},"coherence":{"h":"coherence","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Coherence is the property of being connected, especially of ideas.","e":"Even if the story lacks logical coherence, it is still a fun film to watch."}]}]},"suspend":{"h":"suspend","i":"/səˈspɛnd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-suspend.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you suspend something, you stop it for a time.","e":"The army suspended all operations in the north until the weather has changed."},{"m":"(transitive) If you suspend someone from a job or from school, you stop them from going for a time.","e":"Crang was suspended for five games for punching another player."},{"m":"(transitive) If you suspend an object, you attach it above and hang it down.","e":"Two lamps were suspended above the room and gave off a gentle light."}]}]},"henna":{"h":"henna","i":"/hɛnə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-henna.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Henna is a reddish plant used for making tattoos and hair coloring."},{"m":"A reddish-brown color.","e":"People in north Africa and nearby regions often use henna in and celebrations."}]}]},"exercise":{"h":"exercise","i":"/ˈek.sə.saɪz/","a":"en-us-exercise.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Exercise is a physical activity to make your body stronger.","e":"Losing some weight and doing more exercise will improve your looks."},{"m":"Exercise is an activity that helps develop a skill.","e":"The next exercise is on page 57 in the textbook."},{"m":"(countable) An exercise is an activity for a specific purpose.","e":"Her speech the next day was an exercise in damage control."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you exercise your power, your rights, etc. you use them.","e":"It's no longer true that men exercise all the power, and women just follow."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you exercise, you do physical activity to make your body stronger.","e":"We exercised in the gym."}]}]},"movement":{"h":"movement","i":"/ˈmu:vmənt/","a":"en-us-movement.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Movement is the act of moving, of changing place or position.","e":"The European Union allows free movement of people between countries."},{"m":"(countable) A movement, is a group of people who are all working for the same idea.","e":"The labour movement protects the rights of the workers."},{"m":"A movement is a part in a musical composition such as a sonata or symphony.","e":"The first movement of the \"Moonlight\" Sonata is very famous."}]}]},"main":{"h":"main","i":"/meɪn/","a":"en-us-main.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"The main thing is the most important or biggest one.","e":"They turned off the main road and saw a small house."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A main is a large pipe or wire that carries gas, water, electricity, etc.","e":"A break in a water main has closed the road."}]}]},"plan":{"h":"plan","i":"/plæn/","a":"en-us-plan.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A plan is a clear idea of what you will do, often for a particular goal.","e":"Have you made any plans for tomorrow?"},{"m":"(countable) A plan is a technical drawing of a room, a building, a city, etc.","e":"The plans show this area as housing, with no shopping nearby."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you plan something, you decide what you will do.","e":"We need to plan ahead so that we'll be ready."}]}]},"type":{"h":"type","i":"/taɪp/","a":"en-us-type.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A type is one thing or a group of things that are all members of a larger group because of some similarity.","e":"I use the same type of camera at work."},{"m":"(countable) A type is a person who is like people from a particular group who are all similar in some way.","e":"He's not the usually football type."},{"m":"(uncountable) Type is letters that have been printed by a machine.","e":"The type in this book is too small to read."},{"m":"Type is the blocks of metal with raised letters used to print text.","e":"With Gutenberg's movable type printing, books could be made using less money."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you type something, you write it using a keyboard.","e":"I typed up the letter very quickly, so I hope there are no mistakes."},{"m":"If you type something, you put it into a particular group because of some group similarity.","e":"The Red Cross collects the blood and the technicians in the hospitals cross and type it."}]}]},"executive":{"h":"executive","i":"/ɪɡˈzɛkjʊtɪv/","a":"en-us-executive.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Designed for execution, or carrying into effect."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A name for the head officer or administrator, especially one who can make important decisions.","e":"The executive of the company was criticized for his poor management."},{"m":"The part of government that enforces laws and judicial decisions, and is in charge of running of the state.","e":"The President is the chief executive of the United States government."}]}]},"cruciverbalist":{"h":"cruciverbalist","i":"/ˌkruːsɪˈvɜː(r)bəlɪst/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-cruciverbalist.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A person who makes crossword puzzles."},{"m":"(countable) A person who enjoys doing crossword puzzles.","e":"Susan is a cruciverbalist; she does the newspaper crossword puzzle every day."}]}]},"nonwhite":{"h":"nonwhite","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A person who is not white; a person who is not Caucasian."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Not white; being any color other than white.","e":"I don't care what color we paint the room as long as it's nonwhite."}]}]},"hatchback":{"h":"hatchback","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A car with a sloping, hinged rear door that opens upward.","e":"He was driving his hatchback when he hit the bicyclist."},{"m":"The door itself.","e":"Could you open the hatchback so that I can put my golf clubs in the car?"}]}]},"contributor":{"h":"contributor","i":"/kənˈtrɪb.jə.tɚ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-contributor.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A contributor is a person who donates money to a charity or a cause.","e":"I am a contributor to Red Cross."},{"m":"(countable) A contributor is a person who supports or participates in a cause, activity or institution.","e":"He was a regular contributor to anti-war protests."},{"m":"(countable) A contributor is a person who is important to the creation or growth of something.","e":"With her strength and intelligence, she is an important contributor to the local gene pool."},{"m":"(countable) A contributor is a person who produces articles published in a newspaper, magazine, online publication, etc.","e":"William Safire has been a notable contributor to the opinion page of the New York Times for many years."},{"m":"(countable) A contributor to something is a partial cause of that thing.","e":"One contributor to the problem is the rapid change in the workforce."}]}]},"intestine":{"h":"intestine","i":"/ɪnˈtɛstɪn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-intestine.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The place in the body where food is digested after the stomach."}]}]},"slather":{"h":"slather","i":"/ˈslæðə(r)/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-slather.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you slather something, you spread a lot of something onto it.","e":"John likes to slather his bread with butter."},{"m":"(transitive) If you slather something, you spread a lot of it onto something else.","e":"John always slathers butter on his bread."}]}]},"bring":{"h":"bring","i":"/ˈbrɪŋ/","a":"en-uk-to bring.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you say \"you bring\" something to someone, you carry it with you to that someone.","e":"You bring lunch to me every day."},{"m":"(transitive) When I say \"I bring\" something to you, I carry it with me to you.","e":"I bring milk to you from the store today."},{"m":"(transitive) Sometimes bring means carry something with you to a place where that someone can receive it.","e":"I bring my books to your house."}]}]},"brought":{"h":"brought","i":"/'brɔːt/","a":"en-uk-brought.ogg","l":"bring","q":"verb"},"sent":{"h":"sent","i":"/sɛn̩t/","a":"en-us-sent.ogg","l":"send","q":"verb"},"took":{"h":"took","i":"/tʊk/","a":"en-us-took.ogg","l":"take","q":"verb"},"taken":{"h":"taken","i":"/'teɪkən/","a":"en-us-taken.ogg","l":"take","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are taken with something, you like it.","e":"We were all very taken with his girlfriend."}]}]},"meet":{"h":"meet","i":"/miːt/","a":"en-us-meet.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you meet someone, you get together with them.","e":"I want to meet you."},{"m":"(intransitive) When people meet, they get together with one another.","e":"You and I have met."}]}]},"met":{"h":"met","i":"/mεt/","a":"en-us-met.ogg","l":"meet","q":"verb"},"seventy":{"h":"seventy","i":"/ˈsɛv.ən.ti/","a":"en-us-seventy.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(ordinal seventieth) Seventy is the number that is after 69 and before 71.","e":"To drive seventy miles per hour is too fast in the city."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The number 70.","e":"Seventy is ten less than eighty and ten more than sixty."},{"m":"To be 70 years old.","e":"My father is seventy."}]}]},"show":{"h":"show","i":"/ʃəʊ/","a":"en-uk-to show.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you show something, you make it easy for people to see it.","e":"The clock shows the time of day."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A show is a display of art, movie, or drama. It can be a play, a movie, a concert, an opera or a television program.","e":"I saw the art show at the museum."}]}]},"shown":{"h":"shown","i":"/'ʃown/","a":"en-us-shown.ogg","l":"show","q":"verb"},"feel":{"h":"feel","i":"/fiːl/","a":"en-us-feel.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you feel that something is the case, you have a strong idea in your mind that it is the case.","e":"I feel that not enough is being done to protect the local animal life."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you feel happy, sad, angry, etc., you have that emotion.","e":"He feels happy when someone makes him laugh."},{"m":"(transitive) When you feel something, you experience a sensation from touching it.","e":"He felt the cold ice on his lips."}]}]},"felt":{"h":"felt","i":"/fεlt/","a":"en-us-felt.ogg","l":"feel","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Felt is a cloth made of wool or of wool and fur."}]}]},"grow":{"h":"grow","i":"/ɡrəʊ/","a":"en-us-grow.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) When things grow they get bigger or change in other ways over time.","e":"In time, the boy grew into a man."},{"m":"(transitive) When you grow something, you help it stay alive and get bigger.","e":"I grow flowers in my garden."}]}]},"grew":{"h":"grew","i":"/gruː/","a":"en-us-grew.ogg","l":"grow","q":"verb"},"grown":{"h":"grown","i":"/ɡrəʊn/","a":"en-us-grown.ogg","l":"grow","q":"verb"},"told":{"h":"told","i":"/təʊld/","a":"en-us-told.ogg","l":"tell","q":"verb"},"tell":{"h":"tell","i":"/tɛl/","a":"en-us-tell.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you tell something to someone, you speak to the person about some fact or idea.","e":"He always tells the truth."},{"m":"(transitive) If you tell someone to do something, you are giving them an order.","e":"My mom told me to clean my room."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you tell, you let a parent, teacher, police officer, etc. know that somebody did something bad.","e":"I'm sorry I hit you. I'll give you a dollar if you don't tell."}]}]},"grandfather":{"h":"grandfather","i":"/ˈɡræn(d)ˌfɑːðə(r)/","a":"en-us-grandfather.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A grandfather is the father of a person or animal's parent.","e":"My grandfather was very old when I was still a boy."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive), When someone is grandfathered, it can continue doing or having something when a new law doesn't allow it.","e":"The new laws don't allow buildings that are over 50 feet tall, but the skyscrapers that already exist are grandfathered, so they can stay taller than 50 feet."}]}]},"thirteen":{"h":"thirteen","i":"/ˈfɜː.tiːn/","a":"en-us-thirteen.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(ordinal thirteenth) Thirteen is the number that is after twelve and before fourteen. In numerals, it is 13.","e":"Thirteen donuts makes a baker's dozen."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The number 13.","e":"and ten makes thirteen."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"To be thirteen years old.","e":"This girl is thirteen."}]}]},"game":{"h":"game","i":"/ɡeɪm/","a":"en-us-game.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A game is something that people do to have fun.","e":"Shall we play a game?"},{"m":"(uncountable) Game are wild animals that are hunted for food.","e":"The forest is full of game."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To game means to play a game.","e":"Peter has been gaming for four hours without eating any lunch."}]}]},"torso":{"h":"torso","i":"/ˈtɔː.səʊ/","a":"en-us-torso.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Your torso is a part of your body between your neck and groin.","e":"My torso hurts."}]}]},"heel":{"h":"heel","i":"/hiːl/","a":"en-us-heel.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A part of the foot at the back where it becomes the leg.","e":"I have a large heel."},{"m":"The part of a shoe that supports the foot's heel."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To follow someone closely at their heels."}]}]},"ago":{"h":"ago","i":"/əˈɡoʊ/","a":"en-us-ago.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"At an earlier time.","e":"I was there ten years ago."}]}]},"britain":{"h":"Britain","i":"/ˈbrɪ.tən/","a":"en-uk-Britain.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Great Britain, an island in the northwest of Europe."},{"m":"Britain is the United Kingdom, a country that includes the countries of Great Britain and Northern Ireland."}]}]},"however":{"h":"however","i":"/hɑʊˈεvə/","a":"en-us-however.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"You use however to show that there is a contrast between two ideas.","e":"It was very long. However, it was not long enough."},{"m":"(relative) You used however to say the size, amount, or other quality is not important.","e":"You call me however late you arrive."},{"m":"(relative) in any way","e":"However you say it, it means the same thing."},{"m":"(question) how","e":"However were you able to do it?"}]}]},"extremity":{"h":"extremity","i":"/ɪkˈstrɛmɪti/","a":"en-au-extremity.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An extremity is a part of an animal's body that is used to move around and to hold objects.","e":"For a human, the hand is an extremity that is used to hold objects and can also help to move around in trees."},{"m":"An extremity is the most extreme or furthest point of something."}]}]},"rib":{"h":"rib","i":"/rɪb/","a":"en-us-rib.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The ribs are a number of bones just below the shoulder that wrap around the top of the torso that protect the lungs and heart.","e":"A broken rib is generally treated by putting a bandage several times around the chest and the back."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you rib someone, you gently make fun of them."}]}]},"uterus":{"h":"uterus","i":"/ˈjuː.tər.əs/","a":"en-us-uterus.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The uterus is the internal organ inside of a female mammal where an embryo grows into an infant ready to be born.","e":"A man does not have a uterus and cannot give birth."}]}]},"hullo":{"h":"hullo","s":[{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"You say, \"hullo\" in greeting when you meet someone new or see somebody you know.","e":"\"Good morning, James!\" \"Hullo, Jimbob! How are you?\""}]}]},"cost":{"h":"cost","i":"/kɒst/","a":"en-us-cost.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The cost of something is the price that a person pays for it.","e":"What is the cost of the car?"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you say that a thing costs, you say that one must pay in order to buy it.","e":"That diamond ring costs a great deal of money."},{"m":"One may say that an action costs a certain bad result.","e":"It cost me my job when I broke the machine."},{"m":"(transitive) When you estimate a cost or set a cost, you cost a thing.","e":"The repair man costed the work to fix the car."}]}]},"begin":{"h":"begin","i":"/bɪˈɡɪn/","a":"en-uk-to begin.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you begin something, you start to do the first part of a longer action.","e":"A journey always begins with a first step."}]}]},"began":{"h":"began","i":"/bI'gæn/","a":"en-us-began.ogg","l":"begin","q":"verb"},"begun":{"h":"begun","i":"/bɪˈɡʌn/","a":"en-us-begun.ogg","l":"begin","q":"verb"},"build":{"h":"build","i":"/bɪld/","a":"en-us-build.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you build something, you make it out of pieces of other things.","e":"I built the house with wood and stone."},{"m":"(transitive) If you build something, you make it bigger, stronger, or better.","e":"This is a new idea that others can build upon."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Your build is the shape of your body.","e":"He was a man of medium build with short hair."},{"m":"(countable) (computers) A build is a version of a computer program.","e":"I downloaded the latest build last night to test it."},{"m":"(countable) A build is a structure you create in a video game, especially a sandbox video game."}]}]},"catch":{"h":"catch","i":"/kætʃ/","a":"en-us-catch.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A catch is something that is caught, like the fish a fishermen catches.","e":"My dad brought home a good catch of trout today."},{"m":"(countable) A catch is old time word for a song.","e":"We sang a catch by Purcell."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you catch something, you stop and hold it.","e":"Can you catch a fish in your hands with no fish net?"}]}]},"caught":{"h":"caught","i":"/'kɔːt/","a":"en-au-caught.ogg","l":"catch","q":"verb"},"hold":{"h":"hold","i":"/həʊld/","a":"en-us-hold.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you hold something, you put it in your hand and keep it there.","e":"He held the pen tightly as he wrote the letter."},{"m":"(transitive) When you hold something, you keep it in one place and do not let it move away.","e":"The police hold people who do crimes in prison."},{"m":"(transitive) If you hold someone accountable/responsible/liable, you put the responsibility for something on them.","e":"It's not clear if parents should be held responsible for the problems their children cause."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something holds true/good, it is or continues to be true.","e":"The drug extends life for mice. If this holds true in humans as well, it will be a great advance."},{"m":"(transitive) If you hold somebody prisoner/hostage/captive, you do not allow them to go free.","e":"Police in Luxembourg say a gunman holding 29 children hostage is demanding a mini-bus to take him to the airport."}]}]},"held":{"h":"held","i":"/'hεld/","a":"en-us-held.ogg","l":"hold","q":"verb"},"know":{"h":"know","i":"/nəʊ/","a":"en-us-know.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you know something, you have facts or ideas in your mind.","e":"I knew more things after I went to school."},{"m":"(transitive) You know a person, if you have met him or her.","e":"Yes, I know John. I met him in class last week."}]}]},"went":{"h":"went","i":"/wεnt/","a":"en-us-went.ogg","l":"go","q":"verb"},"mean":{"h":"mean","i":"/miːn/","a":"en-us-mean.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) A word means something when the word expresses the same idea as the other something.","e":"means kill. Both of them mean to make dead."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When you are a mean person, you are not nice.","e":"The boys who hit you were very mean."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The mean is a measure of the average of a list of numbers. The sum total of the numbers divided by how many numbers in the list.","e":"The mean of the numbers 2,3,4 is 3. (2+3+4)/3 = 9/3 = 3."}]}]},"rise":{"h":"rise","i":"/raɪz/","a":"en-us-rise.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A rise is an increase in something, is when something gets higher.","e":"I got a pay rise so now I can buy a bigger car."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) When you rise, you get up from where you are sitting or lying down.","e":"I rise from bed in the morning."},{"m":"(intransitive) When something rises, it goes up.","e":"The airplane rose off the ground."}]}]},"goes":{"h":"goes","i":"/ɡoʊz/","a":"en-us-goes.ogg","l":"go","q":"verb"},"sit":{"h":"sit","i":"/sɪt/","a":"en-us-sit.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you sit, your body is not standing, but is in a position so that your bottom is on something.","e":"I sit on a chair at the table."}]}]},"rose":{"h":"rose","i":"/rəʊz/","a":"en-uk-rose.ogg","l":"rise","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A rose is a kind of shrub with red, pink, white or yellow flowers"},{"m":"(countable) A rose is the flower of the rose plant.","e":"He gave me a dozen red roses for our 1st anniversary."},{"m":"Rose is a purplish-red or pink color, like those of the flowers."}]}]},"ovary":{"h":"ovary","i":"/ˈəʊvəri/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-ovary.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A reproductive organ found in female bodies that produces eggs."}]}]},"sat":{"h":"sat","i":"/'sæt/","a":"en-us-sat.ogg","l":"sit","q":"verb"},"ground":{"h":"ground","i":"/'graʊnd/","a":"en-us-ground.ogg","l":"grind","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The ground is what someone stands or sits on when they are outside.","e":"I ran out of the house and fell on the ground."},{"m":"(uncountable) Ground is terrain; it is the land."},{"m":"(uncountable) Ground is earth or soil."},{"m":"(countable) A ground is the bottom of a body of water."},{"m":"(uncountable) The ground for something is the basis or foundation of it."},{"m":"(countable) The ground for something is the background or context of it."},{"m":"(countable) A ground is a soccer stadium."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is ground, it is crushed into small particles."},{"m":"If something is ground, it has been prepared through grinding."}]}]},"advertise":{"h":"advertise","i":"/ˈæd.vɚ.taɪz/","a":"en-us-advertize.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you advertise something, you make it known publicly, usually to sell it.","e":"I'm advertising my new business in the newspaper."}]}]},"actual":{"h":"actual","i":"/ˈæk.tʃu.l̩/","a":"en-us-actual.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"An actual thing is one that exists; it is real.","e":"People call me Peter, but my actual name is Pierre."}]}]},"ask":{"h":"ask","i":"/ɑːsk/","a":"en-us-ask.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To ask is to look for an answer to a question by saying it.","e":"She sure does ask a lot of questions!"},{"m":"To approach someone to see if they will do something.","e":"Let me ask my mom if I can go."}]}]},"sing":{"h":"sing","i":"/sɪŋ/","a":"en-uk-sing.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you sing you use your voice to make music.","e":"I'm going to sing a song to you."}]}]},"vote":{"h":"vote","i":"/vəʊt/","a":"en-us-vote.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A vote is a formal way of things that are controlled by the majority.","e":"Let's take a vote for a new president!"},{"m":"(countable) A vote is the decision of one person in an election.","e":"I give my vote for the bill."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you vote, you show your support for choosing a person or idea by raising your hand, marking a piece of paper, etc.","e":"My brother votes for the Democrats."}]}]},"means":{"h":"means","i":"/miːnz/","a":"en-us-means.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A means is a way to do something."},{"m":"A person of means has a lot of money.","e":"The head of the bank was a person of means."}]}]},"average":{"h":"average","i":"/ˈævərɪd͡ʒ/","a":"en-us-average.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"To be average is to be not one extreme or another.","e":"In football, he is an average player."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An average is a measure in the middle of several numbers.","e":"The average size of a family in America is about two or three."}]}]},"stand":{"h":"stand","i":"/'stænd/","a":"en-us-stand.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) When you stand, your body is at rest and supported only by your feet.","e":"I stand in the bus when there are no seats."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A stand is a position or opinion that you plan to defend and not move from."},{"m":"(countable) You put something on a stand to keep it off the ground or floor.","e":"The clock was on the night stand next to the bed."}]}]},"stands":{"h":"stands","i":"/stændz/","a":"en-us-stands.ogg","l":"stand","q":"verb"},"stood":{"h":"stood","i":"/'stʊd/","a":"en-us-stood.ogg","l":"stand","q":"verb"},"gave":{"h":"gave","i":"/ɡeɪv/","a":"en-us-gave.ogg","l":"give","q":"verb"},"wear":{"h":"wear","i":"/wɛə/","a":"en-us-wear.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you wear something, you put it on your body and cover your body with it.","e":"I don't wear shoes on my feet when I am inside."},{"m":"When something wears, it gets damaged, over time.","e":"The car was worn from ten years of hard driving."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Things show wear after being used for a long time.","e":"The old school was starting to show wear after one hundred years."}]}]},"lose":{"h":"lose","i":"/luːz/","a":"en-uk-to lose.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you lose something, you don't know where it is.","e":"The boy lost his book some place between home and school."},{"m":"(transitive) In games, you lose when others do better than you.","e":"He lost the card game because he didn't know the rules."}]}]},"better":{"h":"better","i":"/ˈbɛt.ə/","a":"en-us-better.ogg","l":"good","q":"adjective","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To improve.","e":"I intend to better my situation by going back to school."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Another way to spell bettor."},{"m":"Someone or something who is superior to another.","e":"I thought I was the best around, but I found my better when I played John."}]}]},"best":{"h":"best","i":"/bɛst/","a":"en-us-best.ogg","l":"good","q":"adjective","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The greatest effort that one can make.","e":"I did my best."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To do better, especially in a competition.","e":"I bested my high score on the game."}]}]},"loses":{"h":"loses","l":"lose","q":"verb"},"standing":{"h":"standing","i":"/ˈstændɪŋ/","a":"en-us-standing.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A standing committee, order, etc. is one that is permanent."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The standing of a person is the position or reputation they have in a society or profession."},{"m":"The standing of a person is the duration they have been in a position."}]}]},"wears":{"h":"wears","i":"/wɛrz/","a":"en-us-wears.ogg","l":"wear","q":"verb"},"wore":{"h":"wore","i":"/'wɔr/","a":"en-us-wore.ogg","l":"wear","q":"verb"},"leathers":{"h":"leathers","l":"leather","q":"noun"},"attend":{"h":"attend","i":"/əˈtɛnd/","a":"en-us-attend.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you attend something like school or a party, you go to it.","e":"I attended a party."},{"m":"If you attend to something, you give attention to it.","e":"I attended my brother as best man at his wedding."}]}]},"attends":{"h":"attends","a":"en-us-attends.ogg","l":"attend","q":"verb"},"attended":{"h":"attended","i":"/əˈtɛndɪd/","a":"en-us-attended.ogg","l":"attend","q":"verb"},"attentions":{"h":"attentions","l":"attention","q":"noun"},"win":{"h":"win","i":"/wɪn/","a":"en-us-win.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) You win when you do better than other people.","e":"I will win the game."},{"m":"(intransitive) To achieve victory.","e":"Will Germany win the war?"}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The winning of a individual or a team.","e":"Their win in the game was not expected."}]}]},"hot":{"h":"hot","i":"/hɒt/","a":"en-us-hot.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is hot is high in temperature.","e":"The sun is very hot."},{"m":"Someone who is hot is sexually attractive.","e":"Woah, that woman is hot!"},{"m":"Something that is hot is very radioactive.","e":"The atoll is the hottest on Earth."}]}]},"easy":{"h":"easy","i":"/ˈiːzi/","a":"en-us-easy.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is easy, it does not need much skill or effort.","e":"The teacher gave an easy test to her students."},{"m":"If something is easy, it is comfortable.","e":"I had to get out of my easy chair in order to open the door for our guests."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If you do something easy, you do slowly, without effort, calmly.","e":"Take it easy. (See also take it easy.)"}]}]},"stay":{"h":"stay","i":"/steɪ/","a":"en-us-stay.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) When you stay somewhere, you do not move from there.","e":"Whenever I am tired I stay in bed."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A stay is a period of time when someone does not move from a location.","e":"He had a stay in the country for a year."}]}]},"stayed":{"h":"stayed","i":"/steɪd/","a":"en-us-stayed.ogg","l":"stay","q":"verb"},"stays":{"h":"stays","l":"stay","q":"verb"},"deer":{"h":"deer","i":"/dɪə(r)/","a":"en-us-deer.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A deer is a medium- to large-sized animal that eats plants and has hard feet (hooves) that are split in two."}]}]},"europe":{"h":"Europe","i":"/ˈjʊərəp/","a":"en-us-Europe.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Europe is a northern continent near Asia and Africa.","e":"The United Kingdom, France, and Spain are all in Europe."}]}]},"qualities":{"h":"qualities","l":"quality","q":"noun"},"fit":{"h":"fit","i":"/fɪt/","a":"en-us-fit.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you fit something, you match a thing for size, shape or other.","e":"They fitted his hat."},{"m":"(intransitive) When a thing fits, it is a good match for something.","e":"These shoes fit me very well."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When you are fit, you are healthy and able to do a task.","e":"After he slept he looked very fit."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"When you have a fit, you have a sudden emotion.","e":"He hit the man in a fit of rage."},{"m":"If you have a fit, your body moves very quickly without your control.","e":"The man had a fit of epilepsy."}]}]},"slept":{"h":"slept","i":"/slεpt/","a":"en-us-slept.ogg","l":"sleep","q":"verb"},"believe":{"h":"believe","i":"/bɪˈliːv/","a":"en-us-believe.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) When you believe, you have faith in something.","e":"He believes in one God."},{"m":"When you believe something, you accept it as true.","e":"He was wrong when he believed all of the lies he was told."}]}]},"court":{"h":"court","i":"/kɔːrt/","a":"en-us-court.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A court is where people are for crimes.","e":"The bad guy goes to court to stand before the judge."},{"m":"(countable) A court is an open space where certain games are played.","e":"Tennis is played on a court."},{"m":"(countable) A court is where a sovereign (a king or queen), prince, or nobleman live; a palace.","e":"The noblemen visited the queen in her court."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When one person courts another, that person does things to get the other to like him or her.","e":"The boy sent flowers to court the girl."}]}]},"germany":{"h":"Germany","i":"[ˈdʒɜːmənɪ]","a":"en-uk-Germany.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Germany is a country in central Europe."}]}]},"central":{"h":"central","i":"/ˈsɛntrəl/","a":"en-us-central.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A thing is central when it is in the middle.","e":"The house is central to all of the stores."}]}]},"scotland":{"h":"Scotland","i":"/ˈskɒt.lənd/","a":"en-us-Scotland.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Scotland is a country in the United Kingdom, north of England."}]}]},"divide":{"h":"divide","i":"/dɪˈvaɪd/","a":"en-us-divide.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you divide a thing you separate it into two or more other things.","e":"The children divide their books so they all have at least one."},{"m":"(intransitive) When you divide one number into another, you are computing into how many equal parts one number can be separated from the other.","e":"2 divides into 6 exactly 3 times."},{"m":"(intransitive) When a thing divides, it changes from one to more than one.","e":"The river divided into two."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A divide is a place where two or more things are separated.","e":"There is a divide between the those who have money and those who are poor."}]}]},"fair":{"h":"fair","i":"/fɛə/","a":"en-us-fair.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something is fair when it seems right or is done for a good purpose.","e":"A law is fair when good people are not hurt by it."},{"m":"Those people who have light skin color are called fair.","e":"He was fair skin, because he never went into the sun."},{"m":"If the weather is fair, it is good and it is not raining. If it is day, the sun can be seen."},{"m":"If dice are fair any number has an equal chance of coming up."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A fair is a special event where people come to have fun and learn something.","e":"There are games and shows at the fair that is held every year."}]}]},"fast":{"h":"fast","i":"/fɑːst/","a":"en-us-fast.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When you are fast, you can move a in very short time.","e":"The horse ran very fast."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) You fast when you don't eat for a long time.","e":"In many religions people fast for a day or more."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A fast is an act of not eating for a period of time.","e":"He was very hungry after the fast."}]}]},"choose":{"h":"choose","i":"/tʃuːz/","a":"en-us-choose.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you choose a thing, you decide you want it and not something else.","e":"The manager and coaches will choose the starting line-up."}]}]},"gas":{"h":"gas","i":"/gæs/","a":"en-us-gas.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A gas is a substance, such as air, that is not liquid or solid.","e":"The sun is a giant ball of gas."},{"m":"(uncountable) Gas is a substance such as methane, ethane, propane, or butane that is burned for heat or to make electricity.","e":"Our house has gas-fired central heating."},{"m":"(uncountable) In North America, gas is short for gasoline, a liquid that is used by cars.","e":"A small car like mine holds about 40 litres of gas."},{"m":"(uncountable) In North America, the gas is the gas pedal (accelerator) in a car or truck.","e":"We're in a hurry, so hit the gas."},{"m":"(uncountable) In North America, if you have gas, you have the need to fart or burp a lot."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you gas a person or animal, you poison it or put it to sleep with gas.","e":"The mice were gassed and then cut open to examine any changes."},{"m":"(transitive) If you gas up a vehicle, you put fuel in it.","e":"As soon as the planes land, we gas them up and they're ready to go again."}]}]},"france":{"h":"France","i":"/ˈfrɑːns/","a":"en-us-France.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"France is a country in Europe that is beside Belgium, Luxembourg, Germany, Switzerland, Italy, Monaco, Andorra and Spain.","e":"I went to France for a holiday."}]}]},"call":{"h":"call","i":"/kɔːɫ/","a":"en-us-call.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you call someone, you contact them using a telephone.","e":"Can you call me tonight at about 8:00?"},{"m":"If you call to someone, you use your voice to make them notice you.","e":"I can't see you. Call out to me so I can find you."},{"m":"(transitive) If you call someone or something x, you say they are x.","e":"If you ever tell anyone that, I'll call you a liar."},{"m":"(transitive) If somebody is called something, that is their name.","e":"Their daughter's called Mai."},{"m":"(transitive) If you call somebody somewhere, you ask or tell them to come there.","e":"She called me to her office."},{"m":"(transitive) If you call a meeting, a stop, etc., you say you want one to happen.","e":"I've called a meeting for tomorrow, and I'd like you to be there."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A call is a time when you use the telephone to contact someone.","e":"After she made the phone call, she left the office."},{"m":"A visit to someone.","e":"I paid a call to a friend."},{"m":"A cry or shout.","e":"He heard a call from the other side of the room."},{"m":"The cry of a bird or animal.","e":"Cuckoo birds have a unique call."}]}]},"calls":{"h":"calls","i":"/kɔːlz/","a":"en-us-calls.ogg","l":"call","q":"noun"},"calling":{"h":"calling","i":"/ˈkɔːlɪŋ/","a":"en-us-calling.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A strong feeling that makes you want to become religious."},{"m":"A job or career."}]}]},"called":{"h":"called","i":"/kɔːld/","a":"en-us-called.ogg","l":"call","q":"verb"},"eater":{"h":"eater","i":"/ˈiːtɚ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-eater.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An eater eats something. An eater of x, eats mostly x.","e":"She's not a meat eater."}]}]},"eaters":{"h":"eaters","l":"eater","q":"noun"},"eats":{"h":"eats","l":"eat","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":".","e":"Give me some eats!"}]}]},"sends":{"h":"sends","i":"/sendz/","l":"send","q":"verb"},"happen":{"h":"happen","i":"/ˈhapən/","a":"en-us-happen.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) if something happens, it starts or changes without a plan.","e":"Did anything happen at school today?"}]}]},"happens":{"h":"happens","i":"/ˈhæpənz/","a":"en-us-happens.ogg","l":"happen","q":"verb"},"happened":{"h":"happened","i":"/ˈhæpənd/","a":"en-us-happened.ogg","l":"happen","q":"verb"},"budget":{"h":"budget","i":"/ˈbʌdʒ.ɪt/","a":"en-us-budget.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A budget is a limit to how much money can be spent on something.","e":"Our budget for a new car is $10,000."},{"m":"(countable) A budget is a plan for how money will be spent.","e":"The accountant made a new budget that showed us how much we would spend on materials."},{"m":"(countable) If you are on a budget, you are trying not to spend a lot of money."},{"m":"A budget item is something that can be bought cheaply."},{"m":"A budget item is one thing that you plan to spend money on."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you budget, you plan how money or time will be spent.","e":"It is important to budget your time on the test. Don't take too long on any one question."}]}]},"words":{"h":"words","i":"/wɜːdz/","a":"en-us-words.ogg","l":"word","q":"noun"},"numeric":{"h":"numeric","i":"/n(j)uːˈmɛrɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-numeric.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"that is a number or relates to numbers.","e":"The characters 0 through 9 are numeric."}]}]},"want":{"h":"want","i":"/wɒnt/","a":"en-us-want.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you want to do something, you think you would be happier if you did it.","e":"Do you want to go to the park?"},{"m":"(transitive) If you want something, you think you would be happier if you had it.","e":"Do you want a drink?"},{"m":"(transitive) If you want somebody to do something, you think you would be happier if they did it.","e":"I want you to help me."},{"m":"(transitive) If you want something to happen, you think you would be happier if it happened.","e":"I want everyday to be my birthday."},{"m":"(transitive) If you want to do something, your body has a strong feeling that it will do it.","e":"Every time I see it, I want to be sick."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you tell somebody \"you might want to\" do something, you mean they should do it.","e":"You might want to study more for your tests."},{"m":"(transitive); (formal) If someone or something wants for something, they don't have it or don't have enough of it."},{"m":"(transitive) If you want someone, you want to have sex with them."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you want up, down, in, out, etc., you want to go there or your want somebody to help you go there.","e":"Can you open the door? I think the dog wants out."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A want is something that you want.","e":"The wants and needs of the people are not being met."},{"m":"; (formal) something that you do not have or do not have enough of","e":"The car wouldn't run for want of gas."}]}]},"wants":{"h":"wants","i":"/wɑnts/","a":"en-us-wants.ogg","l":"want","q":"verb"},"happier":{"h":"happier","i":"/ˈhæpiɚ/","l":"happy","q":"adjective"},"happiest":{"h":"happiest","i":"/ˈhæpiɪst/","l":"happy","q":"adjective"},"wanted":{"h":"wanted","i":"[ˈwɑntʰɪd]","a":"en-us-wanted.ogg","l":"want","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a person is wanted, they are being looked for by the police for commiting a crime."}]}]},"notice":{"h":"notice","i":"/ˈnəʊtɪs/","a":"en-us-notice.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(not usually in the progressive) If you notice something, you become aware of it.","e":"You didn't even notice that I cut my hair."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) When you [[#Verb|notice]] something","e":"She asked for help, but they took no notice of her."},{"m":"(countable) A notice is a piece of paper with information or a warning.","e":"She sent us a notice about the change of dates."},{"m":"(uncountable) Notice is information that you give to someone.","e":"The shop closed without any notice."}]}]},"intelligent":{"h":"intelligent","i":"/ɪnˈtɛlɪʤənt/","a":"en-us-intelligent.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are intelligent, you can understand difficult ideas easily and think clearly.","e":"Any intelligent person should be able to understand this."},{"m":"If an idea or something said is intelligent, it shows good understanding and clear thinking.","e":"That's probably the most intelligent comment I've heard today."},{"m":"If another living thing or a machine is intelligent, it can think in ways that are similar to us.","e":"We will not likely find intelligent life of other planets."}]}]},"america":{"h":"America","i":"/əˈmɛrɪkə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-America.wav","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"The continents of North and South America."},{"m":"The United States of America."}]}]},"unavailable":{"h":"unavailable","i":"/ˌʌnəˈveɪləbəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-unavailable.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is unavailable, it does not exist or you cannot use it.","e":"We can't answer the question because the needed information is unavailable at this time."}]}]},"variability":{"h":"variability","i":"/ˌvɛər.i.ə.ˈbɪl.ə.ti (ɪ.ti)/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-variability.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The variability of something is how much it changes.","e":"The data shows a great variability in the observed sizes."}]}]},"researcher":{"h":"researcher","i":"/rɪˈsɜːt͡ʃɚ//","a":"en-US-researcher.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A researcher is somebody who does research.","e":"Researchers at the University of Toronto have found a new kind of virus."}]}]},"exporter":{"h":"exporter","i":"/ˈɛks.pɔːtə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-exporter.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An exporter is a person or company that exports things.","e":"The United States is a major exporter of wheat."}]}]},"veterinarians":{"h":"veterinarians","l":"veterinarian","q":"noun"},"learn":{"h":"learn","i":"/lɜː(r)n/","a":"en-us-learn.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you learn something, you start to know how to do things that you didn't know before.","e":"I'm going to learn English!"},{"m":"When you learn something, you start to know something that you didn't know before.","e":"I've just learned that I've been adopted."},{"m":"When you learn, you start to know more than you knew before.","e":"You have to learn from your own mistakes."}]}]},"something":{"h":"something","i":"/ˈsʌmθɪŋ/","a":"en-us-something.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"A thing","e":"I'm going to wear something today."},{"m":"An event","e":"Isn't something going to happen?"},{"m":"A certain object.","e":"You're really something!"}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Something is a quality that is difficult to identify.","e":"This beer has a certain something that I enjoy."}]}]},"exporters":{"h":"exporters","l":"exporter","q":"noun"},"drinks":{"h":"drinks","l":"drink","q":"noun"},"researchers":{"h":"researchers","l":"researcher","q":"noun"},"cakes":{"h":"cakes","i":"/keɪks/","a":"en-us-cakes.ogg","l":"cake","q":"noun"},"governments":{"h":"governments","i":"/ˈɡʌvɚ(n)mənts/","l":"government","q":"noun"},"tensions":{"h":"tensions","l":"tension","q":"noun"},"pictures":{"h":"pictures","i":"/ˈpɪk.(t)ʃəz/","a":"en-us-pictures.ogg","l":"picture","q":"noun"},"mercury":{"h":"Mercury","i":"/ˈmɜː(r)kjʊri/","a":"en-us-mercury.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Mercury is the planet closest to the sun."},{"m":"Mercury is a Roman god who was the god of trade, travelers, thieves, profit, commerce, and the messenger of the gods."}]}]},"queen":{"h":"queen","i":"/kwiːn/","a":"en-us-queen.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The female leader of a country whose son will probably lead the country.","e":"The queen wore her royal robes at the ceremony."},{"m":"The wife of the king is usually the queen."},{"m":"(chess) A queen is a piece in the game of chess."},{"m":"A queen is an effeminate gay man."}]}]},"managers":{"h":"managers","l":"manager","q":"noun"},"quarter":{"h":"quarter","i":"/ˈk(w)ɔːtə/","a":"en-us-quarter.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A quarter is one fourth (1/4) of something.","e":"The lake was about a quarter mile from town."},{"m":"(countable) A quarter is a unit of money worth 25 cents in the United States and Canada.","e":"Can you give me four quarters for this dollar?"},{"m":"(countable) A quarter is a period of three months, especially in business.","e":"Sales were down 3.7 percent from the fourth quarter of last year."},{"m":"(countable) A quarter is one of four a periods of time, especially in sports.","e":"He threw four touchdown passes in the fourth quarter leading to a 38-28 win."},{"m":"(countable) A quarter is one section of a city.","e":"The bar was in New Orleans' French quarter."},{"m":"Quarters are the places where people live.","e":"After training, we returned to our quarters to get changed."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you quarter something, you make it into four equal pieces.","e":"Using a sharp knife, quarter the apple."},{"m":"(transitive) If you quarter somebody somewhere, you give them a place to stay.","e":"We were quartered in Vienna during the job."}]}]},"london":{"h":"London","i":"/ˈlʌn.dən/","a":"en-uk-London.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"London is the capital city of England and the national capital of United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland."}]}]},"dad":{"h":"dad","i":"/dæd/","a":"en-us-dad.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Another word for father.","e":"Timmy's father is very important to him. He goes everywhere with his dad."}]}]},"television":{"h":"television","i":"/ˈtɛlɪˌvɪʒən/","a":"en-uk-television.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A television is a box that moving pictures can be watched on."}]}]},"address":{"h":"address","i":"/ˈæ.drəs/","a":"en-us-address.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An address is the location where a building is or where a person lives."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you address a person, you refer to them using a name or title.","e":"You will address me as Sir from now on."},{"m":"(transitive) If you address a group, you talk in front of it.","e":"The Prime Minister will address the United Nations."},{"m":"(transitive) If you address a letter, you write an address on it.","e":"She addressed the envelope to \"Mr. John Black.\""}]}]},"agent":{"h":"agent","i":"/ˈeɪ.dʒənt/","a":"en-us-agent.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An agent is a person that is a representative and acts for other people."}]}]},"argue":{"h":"argue","i":"/ˈɑː.ɡjuː/","a":"en-us-argue.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you argue with someone, you debate, disagree or talk about your differing ideas."},{"m":"If you argue with someone, you have an argument with them."}]}]},"behind":{"h":"behind","i":"/bɪˈhaɪnd/","a":"en-us-behind.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"When something is behind a second thing, the first thing is in back of the second.","e":"The ball is behind the box."},{"m":"When something is behind, it is toward the rear.","e":"The man stayed behind."},{"m":"A thing is behind when it happened in the past.","e":"We left that worry behind."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The rear, back-end."},{"m":", downside."},{"m":"Your behind is your butt, the buttocks, or bum.","e":"He was told he would get a kick on the behind if he kept being naughty"},{"m":"In, a behind is the same as one point, scored if the ball goes between the tall goal post and the short behind post.","e":"He tried to kick a goal, but the ball went wide and he only got a behind."}]}]},"appear":{"h":"appear","i":"/əˈpɪə/","a":"en-us-appear.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If something appears a certain way, it looks or seems that way.","e":"At first glance, this would appear to be true."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something appears, it comes into sight.","e":"She was studying when her mother appeared in the doorway."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something appears in a book, movie, TV program, etc., it is in it.","e":"He has appeared in over 100 movies."}]}]},"centre":{"h":"centre","i":"/ˈsɛntə/","a":"en-us-center.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The centre of something, is the place that is as far from its outside as possible.","e":"The president and his problems continue to take centre stage in the news."},{"m":"(countable) A centre is a building, area, or group of people with a particular purpose.","e":"They have opened a large shopping centre in Taipei."},{"m":"(countable) The town centre is the place in the town where most of the shops are."},{"m":"(countable) In politics, the centre is the position that is not politically right or left."},{"m":"(countable) In sports, a centre is a player who plays in the middle of the field, usually an attacker."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you centre something, you move it towards the centre."}]}]},"yourselves":{"h":"yourselves","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"You use yourselves when the people doing an action and receiving an action are both you.","e":"Be careful children. You'll hurt yourselves."},{"m":"Use for emphasis.","e":"Don't pretend you don't know. You yourselves have seen these kinds of problems."},{"m":"If you do something by yourselves, you do it alone.","e":"That's beautiful, boys. Did you make it by yourselves?"},{"m":"If you don't feel yourself, you are different from usual, because you are sick, scared, stressed, etc."}]}]},"unusual":{"h":"unusual","i":"/ʌnˈjuːʒuəl/","a":"en-us-unusual.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is unusual, it is not what you expect. It is not an everyday thing or happening.","e":"It was a warm night, unusual for mid Winter."}]}]},"suggest":{"h":"suggest","i":"/səˈdʒɛst/","a":"en-us-suggest.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If a person says an option, he or she is suggesting.","e":"I suggest that we go to the mall."}]}]},"mall":{"h":"mall","i":"/mɔːl/","a":"en-us-mall.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mall is a shopping center where there are many stores that are all in one building.","e":"My friends and I like to go to the mall."},{"m":"(countable) A mall is a planned open grassy area near important buildings or landmarks.","e":"The Mall is between the and the."}]}]},"pelvis":{"h":"pelvis","i":"/ˈpɛlvɪs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-pelvis.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The pelvis is a group of bones around the lower torso that form the hip.","e":"Older people often fall and break their pelvis."}]}]},"bladder":{"h":"bladder","i":"/ˈblædə/","a":"en-us-bladder.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The bladder is the internal organ where urine collects.","e":"An hour after drinking four glasses of water his bladder was full."},{"m":"A bladder is a bag made of a material that stretches to hold a liquid or gas.","e":"The football has a bladder that holds air so it will bounce."}]}]},"abdomen":{"h":"abdomen","i":"/ˈæbdəmən/","a":"en-us-abdomen.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The abdomen is the front part of the lower torso containing many internal organs.","e":"The stomach and intestines are inside the abdomen."},{"m":"(countable) The abdomen is the last of the three parts of an insect's body."}]}]},"surface":{"h":"surface","i":"/ˈsɜːfɪs/","a":"en-us-surface.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The surface of an object is the outside of the thing.","e":"The surface of the earth is very large."},{"m":"The surface of a liquid is the top of it.","e":"The surface of the lake was smooth."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) When a thing surfaces, it comes to the top of liquid.","e":"The fish surfaced to get food."},{"m":"(intransitive) If information or facts surface, they are revealed or become known.","e":"s surfaced that claimed the company was under investigation."}]}]},"life":{"h":"life","i":"/laɪf/","a":"en-us-life.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Life is what makes a person, animal or plant grow and function.","e":"s want to learn if there is life on other planets."},{"m":"Life is the time when people, animals or plants grow and exist before they die. Your life is the time that you live.","e":"The life of an ant is not as long as the life of a human."},{"m":"The state of something being in existence.","e":"We brought the company back to life, after it had been closed for 5 years."}]}]},"prepare":{"h":"prepare","i":"/prɪˈpɛː/","a":"en-us-prepare.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When we prepare something, we get it ready.","e":"The mother prepared food for the meal."}]}]},"worst":{"h":"worst","i":"/wɜːst/","a":"en-us-worst.ogg","l":"bad","q":"adjective","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To make worse."}]}]},"official":{"h":"official","i":"/əˈfɪʃəl/","a":"en-us-official.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is official is approved by some authority.","e":"The letter was an official document from the president."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An official is a person who has certain authority.","e":"That government official collects taxes."}]}]},"piece":{"h":"piece","i":"/piːs/","a":"en-us-piece.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A piece is a part of something that can be or has been separated from it.","e":"The man cut a piece of meat and a piece of cake for dinner."},{"m":"A piece is one example of a class or set of things.","e":"He put a piece of wood on the fire."},{"m":"A piece is something that is made by an artist.","e":"The piece of music was beautiful."},{"m":"In board games, a piece is an object that can be moved to mark your position.","e":"There are six types of chess pieces in the game of chess: the pawn, the knight, the bishop, the rook, the queen, and the king."},{"m":"(taboo) A piece is a woman."},{"m":"(taboo) Piece is sexual intercourse."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you piece something together, you use bring together enough information to understand something.","e":"They gathered enough information to piece together the family history."},{"m":"If you piece something together, you put the pieces together.","e":"The scientists moved their shop to an empty parking lot to piece together all the bones."}]}]},"university":{"h":"university","i":"/juːnɪˈvɜːsətiː/","a":"en-us-university.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A university is a school of advanced study that offers both undergraduate and graduate classes.","e":"A doctor studies for many years at a university before going to work in a hospital."}]}]},"trust":{"h":"trust","i":"/trʌst/","a":"en-us-trust.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you trust someone, you do not doubt them. You believe that someone is honest and will not cause harm. You believe you can rely on them.","e":"I trust all of my friends."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Trust is faith or belief in someone.","e":"Your parents have trust in you."},{"m":"(countable) Your money is put in a trust when you put your money under the control of someone else.","e":"The parents put the children's money in a trust at the bank until they reach the age of 18."}]}]},"hurries":{"h":"hurries","l":"hurry","q":"verb"},"hurried":{"h":"hurried","i":"/ˈhʌrid/","a":"en-us-hurried.ogg","l":"hurry","q":"verb"},"talks":{"h":"talks","l":"talk","q":"verb"},"trees":{"h":"trees","i":"/triːz/","a":"en-us-trees.ogg","l":"tree","q":"noun"},"prepares":{"h":"prepares","l":"prepare","q":"verb"},"prepared":{"h":"prepared","i":"/prɪˈpɛəd/","a":"en-us-prepared.ogg","l":"prepare","q":"verb"},"drank":{"h":"drank","a":"en-us-drank.ogg","l":"drink","q":"verb"},"games":{"h":"games","i":"/ɡeɪmz/","a":"en-us-games.ogg","l":"game","q":"noun"},"gamed":{"h":"gamed","l":"game","q":"verb"},"talked":{"h":"talked","i":"/tɔːkt/","a":"en-us-talked.ogg","l":"talk","q":"verb"},"takes":{"h":"takes","i":"/teɪks/","a":"en-us-takes.ogg","l":"take","q":"verb"},"surprised":{"h":"surprised","i":"/səˈpraɪzd/","a":"en-us-surprised.ogg","l":"surprise","q":"verb"},"painting":{"h":"painting","i":"/ˈpeɪntɪŋ/","a":"en-us-painting.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A painting is a picture that is painted.","e":"A painting of the president hung on the wall."}]}]},"painted":{"h":"painted","a":"en-us-painted.ogg","l":"paint","q":"verb"},"paints":{"h":"paints","l":"paint","q":"noun"},"drunk":{"h":"drunk","i":"/drʌŋk/","a":"en-us-drunk.ogg","l":"drink","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is drunk, they have taken in too much alcohol.","e":"After he left the restaurant, he was so drunk he couldn't walk."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A drunk is a person who often drinks too much alcohol.","e":"Two drunks were fighting in the street last night."}]}]},"taking":{"h":"taking","i":"/ˈteɪkɪŋ/","a":"en-us-taking.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Taking is the act of something."},{"m":"The takings of a business is the cash or money they received or earned."}]}]},"bought":{"h":"bought","i":"/'bɔːt/","a":"en-us-bought.ogg","l":"buy","q":"verb"},"muscles":{"h":"muscles","i":"/ˈmʌsəlz/","a":"en-us-muscles.ogg","l":"muscle","q":"noun"},"closed":{"h":"closed","i":"/kləʊzd/","a":"en-us-closed.ogg","l":"close","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Not open.","e":"The store is closed on the weekends."},{"m":"Not available to the public.","e":"I used a closed source to write the article."}]}]},"wings":{"h":"wings","i":"/wɪŋz/","a":"en-us-wings.ogg","l":"wing","q":"noun"},"acting":{"h":"acting","i":"/ˈæk.tɪŋ/","a":"en-us-acting.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"An acting director, president, head, etc. is in the position until the regular person returns to the job.","e":"He was the acting chairperson for the committee when Tim went for surgery."}]}]},"reads":{"h":"reads","l":"read","q":"verb"},"smells":{"h":"smells","l":"smell","q":"verb"},"smelled":{"h":"smelled","i":"/'smεld/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-smelled.wav","l":"smell","q":"verb"},"cuts":{"h":"cuts","i":"/kʌts/","a":"EN-AU ck1 cuts.ogg","l":"cut","q":"verb"},"cutting":{"h":"cutting","i":"/ˈkʌtɪŋ/","a":"en-us-cutting.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cutting is an area of land that has been dug out of a hill for a road or railway."},{"m":"(countable) A cutting is a piece of newspaper or magazine that is cut and saved."},{"m":"(countable) A cutting is a piece of a plant that is cut off, usually to grow a new plant."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a remark is cutting, it is unkind."}]}]},"begs":{"h":"begs","l":"beg","q":"verb"},"begged":{"h":"begged","i":"/bɛɡd/","a":"en-us-begged.ogg","l":"beg","q":"verb"},"shirts":{"h":"shirts","a":"en-us-shirts.ogg","l":"shirt","q":"noun"},"units":{"h":"units","l":"unit","q":"noun"},"parts":{"h":"parts","i":"/pɑːts/","a":"en-us-parts.ogg","l":"part","q":"noun"},"rich":{"h":"rich","i":"/rɪʧ/","a":"en-us-rich.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When someone is rich, they have a lot of money and things.","e":"Bill Gates is rich because he has 60 billion dollars."},{"m":"When food is rich, it has a very strong flavor.","e":"This dish is rich tasting."}]}]},"richer":{"h":"richer","i":"/ˈrɪt͡ʃɚ/","l":"rich","q":"adjective"},"richest":{"h":"richest","i":"/ˈrɪt͡ʃəst/","a":"en-us-richest.ogg","l":"rich","q":"adjective"},"double":{"h":"double","i":"/ˈdʌbəl/","a":"en-us-double.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A double door, window, etc. includes two of the same kind.","e":"We opened the double door to let the piano come in."},{"m":"A double accident, murder, etc. is two events that happen together or are somehow connected.","e":"With the double wedding, Sunday was the busiest day of the year."},{"m":"A double thing is for two people.","e":"They slept together in a double bed, while James slept in a single in the other room."},{"m":"Twice as big, twice as many, or twice as much as usual.","e":"I'll have a double coffee."},{"m":"If something is double, it is 100% bigger than something else.","e":"The new computer was double the cost of the old one."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something doubles, it grows by 100%.","e":"The price of gold has almost doubled in the last month from $407 to $792."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something doubles as something else, it has both roles.","e":"The kitchen doubles as our dining room."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something doubles up/over, it folds in half."},{"m":"(intransitive) If two people double up, they stay or work together."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Somebody's double is another person who looks very similar to them."},{"m":"In baseball, a double is a hit that allows the runner to move to second base."}]}]},"surgeon":{"h":"surgeon","i":"/ˈsɝdʒən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-surgeon.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A person that does surgery."}]}]},"surgeons":{"h":"surgeons","l":"surgeon","q":"noun"},"photograph":{"h":"photograph","i":"/ˈfəʊtəgrɑ:f/","a":"en-us-photograph.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A photograph is a picture that is created by a camera digitally or on film.","e":"The photograph of the event won a."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you take a photograph of someone or something, you take a photograph of it.","e":"He photographed the wedding for them."}]}]},"photographs":{"h":"photographs","a":"en-us-photographs.ogg","l":"photograph","q":"noun"},"grows":{"h":"grows","i":"/ɡrəʊz/","a":"en-us-grows.ogg","l":"grow","q":"verb"},"sixes":{"h":"sixes","l":"six","q":"noun"},"roses":{"h":"roses","a":"en-us-roses.ogg","l":"rose","q":"noun"},"rises":{"h":"rises","i":"/ˈraɪzɪz/","a":"en-us-rises.ogg","l":"rise","q":"verb"},"risen":{"h":"risen","i":"/'rɪzən/","a":"en-us-risen.ogg","l":"rise","q":"verb"},"county":{"h":"county","i":"/ˈkaʊnti/","a":"en-us-county.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A county is an area of land with a local government, often including a number of towns or. It is used differently in different.","e":"Hampshire County Council has provided £20,000 to furnish the building."}]}]},"sarcasms":{"h":"sarcasms","l":"sarcasm","q":"noun"},"nouns":{"h":"nouns","i":"/naʊnz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-nouns.wav","l":"noun","q":"noun"},"verbs":{"h":"verbs","l":"verb","q":"noun"},"fine":{"h":"fine","i":"/faɪn/","a":"en-us-fine.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is fine, it is OK, not a problem, or acceptable.","e":"She said it works -- it's fine."},{"m":"If something is fine, it is very good in quality.","e":"This is a fine example of how we can work together."},{"m":"If the weather is fine, the sun is out and it is not raining or snowing."},{"m":"Very, very small.","e":"Grind it into a fine powder."},{"m":"if someone is fine, then they are good-looking or attractive.","e":"That woman is so fine!"}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something works fine, it works well, or without any problems.","e":"Going there today would suit me fine."},{"m":"If you draw or cut something fine, you do it in very small pieces or with small detail."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A fine is money that you pay for breaking a rule or the law.","e":"There is a $500 fine for smoking inside."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you fine someone, you make them pay money for breaking a rule or the law.","e":"He was fined $500 for smoking inside."},{"m":"To make something finer in quality or size.","e":"The wine will fine with time."}]}]},"finer":{"h":"finer","i":"/ˈfaɪnɚ/","l":"fine","q":"adjective"},"finest":{"h":"finest","i":"/ˈfaɪnɪst/","a":"en-us-finest.ogg","l":"fine","q":"adjective","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"You use (a city's) finest for police officers.","e":"Fifty of New York City's finest were at the banquet."}]}]},"gaming":{"h":"gaming","i":"/ˈɡeɪmɪŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-gaming.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Playing games, especially betting games.","e":"Las Vegas is famous for its gaming."}]}]},"foods":{"h":"foods","i":"/fuːdz/","l":"food","q":"noun"},"archipelago":{"h":"archipelago","i":"/ɑːkɪˈpɛləgəʊ/","a":"en-us-archipelago.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An archipelago is a number of islands that are close together.","e":"Ambon is an island in the eastern end of the Indonesian archipelago."}]}]},"loonie":{"h":"loonie","a":"en-ca-loonie.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A loonie is a coin that is one Canadian dollar.","e":"I need a loonie for the drink machine."}]}]},"suspicions":{"h":"suspicions","i":"/səˈspɪʃənz/","l":"suspicion","q":"noun"},"sides":{"h":"sides","a":"en-us-sides.ogg","l":"side","q":"noun"},"gerund-participle":{"h":"gerund-participle","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A gerund-participle is a verb form that ends in -ing.","e":"In the following examples, the gerund-participle is underlined:"}]}]},"flashlights":{"h":"flashlights","l":"flashlight","q":"noun"},"bangalore":{"h":"Bangalore","i":"/'bæŋgəlɔː(r)/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Bangalore.wav","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Bangalore is the state capital of Karnataka, India."}]}]},"rules":{"h":"rules","i":"/ˈruːlz/","a":"en-us-rules.ogg","l":"rule","q":"noun"},"replaces":{"h":"replaces","l":"replace","q":"verb"},"daughters":{"h":"daughters","i":"/ˈdɔːtəz/","a":"en-us-daughters.ogg","l":"daughter","q":"noun"},"mottos":{"h":"mottos","l":"motto","q":"noun"},"minors":{"h":"minors","a":"en-us-miners.ogg","l":"minor","q":"noun"},"sciences":{"h":"sciences","a":"en-us-sciences.ogg","l":"science","q":"noun"},"summaries":{"h":"summaries","l":"summary","q":"noun"},"shocks":{"h":"shocks","l":"shock","q":"noun"},"maps":{"h":"maps","i":"/mæps/","l":"map","q":"noun"},"soaps":{"h":"soaps","l":"soap","q":"noun"},"gives":{"h":"gives","i":"/ɡɪvz/","a":"en-us-gives.ogg","l":"give","q":"verb"},"religions":{"h":"religions","a":"en-us-religions.ogg","l":"religion","q":"noun"},"dos":{"h":"dos","i":"/duːz/","l":"do","q":"noun"},"queens":{"h":"queens","l":"queen","q":"noun"},"wikis":{"h":"wikis","l":"wiki","q":"noun"},"nonwhites":{"h":"nonwhites","l":"nonwhite","q":"noun"},"inks":{"h":"inks","l":"ink","q":"noun"},"sizes":{"h":"sizes","l":"size","q":"noun"},"lasts":{"h":"lasts","a":"en-us-lasts.ogg","l":"last","q":"verb"},"holidays":{"h":"holidays","l":"holiday","q":"noun"},"bottles":{"h":"bottles","i":"/ˈbɑtl̩z/","l":"bottle","q":"noun"},"pursues":{"h":"pursues","l":"pursue","q":"verb"},"shoulders":{"h":"shoulders","a":"en-us-shoulders.ogg","l":"shoulder","q":"noun"},"expresses":{"h":"expresses","l":"express","q":"verb"},"showers":{"h":"showers","l":"shower","q":"noun"},"blanks":{"h":"blanks","l":"blank","q":"noun"},"matches":{"h":"matches","l":"match","q":"noun"},"allows":{"h":"allows","i":"/əˈlaʊz/","l":"allow","q":"verb"},"agents":{"h":"agents","i":"/ˈeɪ.d͡ʒənts/","a":"en-us-agents.ogg","l":"agent","q":"noun"},"mountains":{"h":"mountains","a":"en-us-mountains.ogg","l":"mountain","q":"noun"},"augusts":{"h":"Augusts","l":"august","q":"noun"},"payments":{"h":"payments","i":"/ˈpeɪmənts/","a":"en-us-payments.ogg","l":"payment","q":"noun"},"colors":{"h":"colors","i":"/ˈkʌl.əz/","a":"en-us-colors.ogg","l":"color","q":"noun"},"colours":{"h":"colours","i":"/ˈkʌl.əz/","a":"en-us-colors.ogg","l":"colour","q":"noun"},"participle":{"h":"participle","i":"/ˈpɑːtɪsɪpəl/","a":"en-us-participle.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A participle is a form of a verb that has not been tensed. The expression headed by a participle is used either as a complement or as an adjunct.","e":"In the following sentences, the underlined word is a participle:"}]}]},"tense":{"h":"tense","i":"/tɛns/","a":"en-us-tense.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Tightly stretched.","e":"Make sure that the net is as stretched as tense as possible for maximum coverage."},{"m":"Stressed; nervous.","e":"How odd it was that he was a very courageous boy, yet he became very tense when he was being asked to dance."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Tense is a grammatical system of verb forms that usually shows past, present, or future time.","e":"Unlike French, English only has two tenses: past and present."},{"m":"(countable) A tense is one of the verb forms marked by the tense system.","e":"The verb cut is spelled the same in both tenses."},{"m":"(countable) In popular language, a tense is often used to refer to any verb form including tense, aspect, mood, and voice.","e":"Shouldn't this be in the progressive tense?"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To make or become tense."}]}]},"bar":{"h":"bar","i":"/bɑː/","a":"en-us-bar.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A bar is a place that sells alcoholic drinks.","e":"I'm going to drink beer at the bar."},{"m":"A bar is the counter or bench in a hotel or bar where drinks are sold.","e":"The waitress stood behind the bar and poured our drinks."},{"m":"A bar is a box-shaped piece of something.","e":"You can buy a bar of soap, or a bar of gold."},{"m":"A bar is a long, hard thing that looks like a stick.","e":"The prisoner was kept behind bars in the jail."},{"m":"The bar is the legal profession or the group of lawyers allowed to practice law in a country.","e":"She was called to the bar after passing her exams."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To bar is to stop someone from doing something; to prohibit.","e":"I was barred from entering the club."},{"m":"To bar is to lock a door or window, or to block it so others can not enter.","e":"I barred the door to stop her leaving the room."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"except; not including","e":"He's the fastest runner in the world bar none."}]}]},"bars":{"h":"bars","i":"/ˈbɑː(r)z/","a":"en-us-bars.ogg","l":"bar","q":"noun"},"barred":{"h":"barred","i":"/ˈbɑː(r)d/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-barred.wav","l":"bar","q":"verb"},"barring":{"h":"barring","i":"/ˈbɑːrɪŋ(ɡ)/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Persent101-barring.wav","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"unless something happens or is true.","e":"Barring a big change in popular opinion, he should become the next president."}]}]},"sells":{"h":"sells","l":"sell","q":"verb"},"sold":{"h":"sold","i":"/'soʊld/","a":"en-us-sold.ogg","l":"sell","q":"verb"},"individuals":{"h":"individuals","a":"en-us-individuals.ogg","l":"individual","q":"noun"},"accepts":{"h":"accepts","i":"/əkˈsɛpts/","a":"en-us-accepts.ogg","l":"accept","q":"verb"},"accepted":{"h":"accepted","i":"/əkˈsɛp.tɪd/","a":"en-us-accepted.ogg","l":"accept","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Accepted ideas are agreed by most people to be correct or reasonable.","e":"There is no generally accepted definition of life."}]}]},"accepting":{"h":"accepting","i":"/əkˈsɛptɪŋ/","a":"en-us-accepting.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is accepting, they are very tolerant."}]}]},"carts":{"h":"carts","i":"/kɑrts/","a":"en-us-carts.ogg","l":"cart","q":"noun"},"carted":{"h":"carted","l":"cart","q":"verb"},"practices":{"h":"practices","i":"/ˈpræktɪsɪz/","a":"en-us-practices.ogg","l":"practice","q":"noun"},"practiced":{"h":"practiced","i":"/ˈpræktɪst/","a":"en-us-practiced.ogg","l":"practice","q":"verb"},"practicing":{"h":"practicing","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"To be active in a job that needs a high level of skill, knowledge, or training.","e":"My son is a practicing lawyer."},{"m":"To be active in the rituals of a religion.","e":"I am a practicing Buddhist."}]}]},"practises":{"h":"practises","l":"practise","q":"verb"},"practised":{"h":"practised","a":"en-us-practised.ogg","l":"practise","q":"verb"},"abandons":{"h":"abandons","l":"abandon","q":"noun"},"abandoned":{"h":"abandoned","i":"/əˈbæn.dənd/","a":"en-us-abandoned.ogg","l":"abandon","q":"verb"},"abandoning":{"h":"abandoning","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The act of abandoning.","e":"The abandoning of the child happened 10 years ago."}]}]},"abdomens":{"h":"abdomens","l":"abdomen","q":"noun"},"pushes":{"h":"pushes","l":"push","q":"noun"},"pushed":{"h":"pushed","i":"/pʊʃt/","a":"en-us-pushed.ogg","l":"push","q":"verb"},"boards":{"h":"boards","i":"/bɔːrdz/","l":"board","q":"noun"},"boarded":{"h":"boarded","l":"board","q":"verb"},"determiner":{"h":"determiner","i":"/dɪˈtəːmɪnə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-determiner.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A determiner is a function label used in a noun phrase, marking the noun phrase as being definite or indefinite."},{"m":"(countable) A determiner is one of a small set of words that restrict the referents of noun phrases (see here for a list).","e":"When discussing lexical category, the terms determiner and determinative are sometimes used interchangeably."}]}]},"pronoun":{"h":"pronoun","i":"/proʊ.naʊn/","a":"en-us-pronoun.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Pronoun is a closed class of nouns that usually refers to another noun (see here for a list)."}]}]},"pools":{"h":"pools","i":"/puːlz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-pools.wav","l":"pool","q":"noun"},"hands":{"h":"hands","a":"en-us-hands.ogg","l":"hand","q":"noun"},"handed":{"h":"handed","i":"/ˈhændɪd/","a":"en-us-handed.ogg","l":"hand","q":"verb"},"controversies":{"h":"controversies","l":"controversy","q":"noun"},"dads":{"h":"dads","l":"dad","q":"noun"},"agrees":{"h":"agrees","l":"agree","q":"verb"},"agreed":{"h":"agreed","i":"/ə'griːd/","a":"en-us-agreed.ogg","l":"agree","q":"verb"},"spouse":{"h":"spouse","i":"/spaʊs/","a":"en-us-spouse.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A spouse is a husband or a wife.","e":"John is my spouse. I married John, in 1999."}]}]},"grandson":{"h":"grandson","i":"/ˈɡræn(d)sʌn/","a":"en-us-grandson.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Someone's grandson is the son of their son or daughter.","e":"My son, John, has a son named George. George is my grandson."}]}]},"meaning":{"h":"meaning","i":"/ˈmiːnɪŋ/","a":"en-us-meaning.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The meaning of something is the idea or message that it has. In language, meaning is what speech or writing is intended to convey to the listener or reader.","e":"What is the meaning of the word \"investigate\"?"},{"m":"(countable) The meaning of something is its purpose.","e":"School doesn't have much meaning for me anymore."}]}]},"kid":{"h":"kid","i":"/kɪd/","a":"en-us-kid.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A child or young person."},{"m":"(countable) A young goat."},{"m":"(countable) A young antelope."},{"m":"Your kid brother or sister is younger than you."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you kid around, you joke.","e":"You've got to be kidding. If that is not a joke, you will be in a lot of trouble."}]}]},"cows":{"h":"cows","l":"cow","q":"noun"},"alternatives":{"h":"alternatives","l":"alternative","q":"noun"},"birds":{"h":"birds","i":"/bɝdz/","a":"en-us-birds.ogg","l":"bird","q":"noun"},"aeroplanes":{"h":"aeroplanes","l":"aeroplane","q":"noun"},"ants":{"h":"ants","l":"ant","q":"noun"},"cricket":{"h":"cricket","i":"/ˈkrɪk.ɪt/","a":"en-us-cricket.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cricket is a medium-sized insect."},{"m":"Cricket is a sport played with a bat and ball, especially in the United Kingdom and India."}]}]},"penguin":{"h":"penguin","i":"/ˈpɛŋɡwɪn/","a":"en-us-penguin.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A penguin is a sea bird that cannot fly.","e":"We went to the Zoo to see the penguins."}]}]},"pound":{"h":"pound","i":"/paʊnd/","a":"en-us-pound.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pound is a unit of currency used in Britain.","e":"Against the dollar, the pound fell by half a cent to $ 1.73."},{"m":"(countable) A pound is a unit of weight equal to 16 ounces or 0.454 kilograms.","e":"Since he stopped smoking, he has gained 20 pounds."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you pound something, you hit it hard.","e":"Grace pounded on the door. \"Come out of there!\""},{"m":"(intransitive) If your head or heart is pounding, you can feel the blood moving through it.","e":"I ran and ran until my heart was pounding in my chest."}]}]},"penguins":{"h":"penguins","l":"penguin","q":"noun"},"extra":{"h":"extra","i":"/ˈɛkstrə/","a":"en-us-extra.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is more than what you expected; exceeding; additional.","e":"I always put extra ketchup on my hamburger."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something is extra good, large, special, etc., it is more so than normal.","e":"This shirt is extra large; it's too big for me."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An extra is a feature that you usually pay more for when you buy something.","e":"She got the car with all the sporty extras."},{"m":"(countable) An extra is a person appearing in a movie who is not listed in the credits."}]}]},"bother":{"h":"bother","i":"/ˈbɒðə/","a":"en-uk-bother.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you bother to do something, you make an effort to do it.","e":"Don't bother with the dishes. I'll do them later."},{"m":"(transitive) If something bothers someone, it disturbs or them.","e":"Would it bother you if I smoked?"}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A small trouble or problem.","e":"I can do it – no bother."},{"m":"(countable) A bother is somebody or something that makes trouble for you.","e":"I don't want to be a bother, so I'll just go out by myself."}]},{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"You say bother when you are annoyed.","e":"Oh, bother! Now I'll have to make it again."}]}]},"bears":{"h":"bears","i":"/bɛrz/","a":"en-us-bears.ogg","l":"bear","q":"noun"},"flies":{"h":"flies","i":"/flaɪz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Persent101-flies.wav","l":"fly","q":"verb"},"flew":{"h":"flew","i":"/flʊə/","a":"en-us-flew.ogg","l":"fly","q":"verb"},"often":{"h":"often","i":"/ˈɒfn/","a":"en-us-often.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"When something happens often, that means that it happens many times and frequently.","e":"I drink a lot of water and need to urinate often."}]}]},"letters":{"h":"letters","i":"/ˈlɛtəz/","a":"en-us-letters.ogg","l":"letter","q":"noun"},"shouldered":{"h":"shouldered","l":"shoulder","q":"verb"},"according":{"h":"according","i":"/əˈkɔːdɪŋ/","a":"en-us-according.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If something is true according to a source, it means that source says or shows that it is true.","e":"According to a friend of mine, they are thinking of building a new mall near here."}]}]},"afterward":{"h":"afterward","i":"/ˈɑːftə.wəd/","a":"en-us-afterward.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If something happens afterward, it happens after the time that you are talking about.","e":"Joe went to the bank. Afterward he went to the store."}]}]},"afterwards":{"h":"afterwards","i":"/ˈɑːftəwədz/","a":"en-us-afterwards.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If something happens afterwards, it happens after the time that you are talking about."}]}]},"ahead":{"h":"ahead","i":"/ʌˈhed/","a":"en-us-ahead.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"You use ahead to talk about something that is in front of you or in the future."}]}]},"along":{"h":"along","i":"/əˈlɒŋ/","a":"en-us-along.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If one thing happens along with another, they go together.","e":"Along with his daughter, he is studying French."},{"m":"If you go along with something, you agree with or follow it.","e":"We're going to go along with your plan."},{"m":"You use along to show movement from one end of a long thing towards the other end.","e":"Along the road were just a few cars."},{"m":"If something was true all along, it's true from the beginning.","e":"He knew the real story all along."},{"m":"If two people get along, they are friendly with each other.","e":"I don't go to her house because we don't get along."}]}]},"alongside":{"h":"alongside","i":"/ʌ.lɑŋˈsaɪd/","a":"en-us-alongside.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"You use alongside to talk about something being beside something else."},{"m":"You use alongside to talk about something being at the same time as something else."}]}]},"although":{"h":"although","i":"/ɑlˈðoʊ/","a":"en-us-although.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"You use although to show that an idea is surprising or different from another idea.","e":"We decided to take rooms in Longwood house, although we knew we could not really afford the rent there."}]}]},"amid":{"h":"amid","i":"/əˈmɪd/","a":"en-us-amid.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"You use amid to talk about something happening at the same time as many other things.","e":"Amid all the riots during the blackout, many stores were looted."},{"m":"You use amid to talk about something being in the middle of something else."}]}]},"amongst":{"h":"amongst","i":"/əˈmʌŋst/","a":"en-us-amongst.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"In or into. We say \"between\" 2 other things, but amongst 3 or more other things.","e":"She was amongst her friends."},{"m":"With a share for each.","e":"Divide the candy amongst yourselves."},{"m":"By all or with the whole."}]}]},"apart":{"h":"apart","i":"/əˈpɑː(r)t/","a":"en-us-apart.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If two things are apart, there is space between them.","e":"Scientists theorize that Pangaea drifted apart into the different continents that exist on Earth today."},{"m":"You use something apart to leave that thing out of the topic.","e":"The lies apart, they're good workers."}]}]},"around":{"h":"around","i":"/əˈraʊnd/","a":"en-us-around.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If x is around y, y is in the middle and x is on all sides of y.","e":"The moon circles around the Earth."}]}]},"amidst":{"h":"amidst","i":"/aˈmɪdst/","a":"en-us-amidst.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If something is amidst other things, it is in the middle of them.","e":"She saw the moon rising above the open sea amidst flying clouds."},{"m":"If something happens amidst other things, it happens at the same time as them.","e":"Amdist all the packing and moving, she still had to study."}]}]},"briefs":{"h":"briefs","i":"/briːfs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Flame, not lame-briefs.wav","l":"brief","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Briefs are a kind of men's underpants or swimming suit bottoms that have holes for the legs."}]}]},"beforehand":{"h":"beforehand","i":"/bɪˈfɔːhænd/","a":"en-us-beforehand.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"something else happens.","e":"You should have told me about the presentation beforehand. I haven't even prepared."}]}]},"below":{"h":"below","i":"/bɪˈləʊ/","a":"en-us-below.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"At a lower position"}]}]},"beneath":{"h":"beneath","i":"/bɪˈniːθ/","a":"en-us-beneath.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"At a lower position.","e":"The book is beneath the table."}]}]},"beside":{"h":"beside","i":"/bɪˈsaɪd/","a":"en-us-beside.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If x is beside y, it is close to y, but not in front or behind.","e":"The book is beside the table."}]}]},"beyond":{"h":"beyond","i":"/bɪˈjɒnd/","a":"en-us-beyond.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If x is beyond y, it is on the far side of y.","e":"He went beyond the mountains, into the woods."}]}]},"concerning":{"h":"concerning","i":"/kənˈsɝnɪŋ/","a":"en-us-concerning.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"about or relating to","e":"Concerning the schedule, there have been a number of changes."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is concerning, it makes a person worry.","e":"The change in her health is very concerning."}]}]},"considering":{"h":"considering","i":"/kənˈsɪdərɪŋ/","a":"en-us-considering.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"When you think about; because of","e":"Considering all the problems we've had, it's amazing we finished."}]}]},"corrects":{"h":"corrects","l":"correct","q":"verb"},"corrected":{"h":"corrected","i":"/kəˈrɛktɪd/","a":"en-us-corrected.ogg","l":"correct","q":"verb"},"backwards":{"h":"backwards","i":"/ˈbækwɜːdz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-upwards.wav","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If something is backwards, it is facing the back."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is backwards is inefficient and not advanced. (sometimes considered offensive when describing a person, especially a child)","e":"This society is very backwards, primitive in comparison to the country we came from."}]}]},"backward":{"h":"backward","i":"/ˈbækwəd/","a":"en-au-backward.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If something is backward, it is facing the back."}]}]},"counter":{"h":"counter","i":"/ˈkaʊntɚ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-counter.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A counter is a flat surface to work on, often in a kitchen."},{"m":"A counter is a small coin-shaped object, often used in games."},{"m":"A counter is someone who counts."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If x is counter to y, it is against y."}]}]},"depending":{"h":"depending","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Depending on x, means that the truth of what you say is affected by x.","e":"People in the rest of the country celebrated independence even later, depending on when the news of Congress's action reached them."}]}]},"downstairs":{"h":"downstairs","i":"/daʊnˈstɛrz/","a":"en-us-downstairs.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If something is downstairs, it is on the level at the bottom of the stairs.","e":"Let's head downstairs, from the bedroom to the kitchen below."}]}]},"except":{"h":"except","i":"/ɪkˈsɛpt/","a":"en-uk-except.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"You use except to introduce the only thing or person that a statement does not apply to, or a fact that prevents a statement from being completely true.","e":"Except mercury, most metals are solids."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) to exclude"}]}]},"into":{"h":"into","i":"/ˈɪn.tuː/","a":"en-us-into.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"from out to in","e":"I opened the door and stepped into the house."}]}]},"nearby":{"h":"nearby","i":"/ˌnɪə(r)ˈbaɪ/","a":"en-us-nearby.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"close; not far"}]}]},"next":{"h":"next","i":"/nɛkst/","a":"en-us-next.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"The next thing is the one after this one.","e":"I saw her again the next day."},{"m":"The next place is the one beside, or on the other side of this one.","e":"No, this is number 12, number 14 is the next house."},{"m":"Next week, month, year, etc. is the one that follows this one.","e":"I'll see you again next week."},{"m":"Next is used with a superlative adjective to denote what follows in the specified order.","e":"The next best thing to flying is gliding."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"After something in order.","e":"Next, we have the 6:00 news."},{"m":"The time after this one.","e":"The woman was next seen in the office 4 days later."},{"m":"Beside something.","e":"She stood next to the window."}]}]},"onto":{"h":"onto","i":"/ˈɒn.tuː/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-onto.wav","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"from off to on","e":"He walked along pier and onto the ship."}]}]},"outdoors":{"h":"outdoors","i":"/ˌaʊtˈdɔːz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-outdoors.wav","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If something is outdoors, it is not in a building; under the open sky."}]}]},"outside":{"h":"outside","i":"/ˌaʊtˈsaɪd/","a":"en-us-outside.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"outdoors; not in a building; under the open sky","e":"The plants are outside the house."}]}]},"overhead":{"h":"overhead","i":"/ˈoʊvɚˌhɛd/","a":"en-us-overhead.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"above your head; in the sky"}]}]},"snows":{"h":"snows","a":"en-us-snows.ogg","l":"snow","q":"noun"},"snowed":{"h":"snowed","l":"snow","q":"verb"},"chickens":{"h":"chickens","i":"/ˈt͡ʃɪkənz/","a":"en-us-chickens.ogg","l":"chicken","q":"noun"},"lad":{"h":"lad","i":"/læd/","a":"en-us-lad.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A boy.","e":"Why aren't you lads in school?"},{"m":"(countable) Sometimes, people call a man a lad when they know that person well."}]}]},"throw":{"h":"throw","i":"/θrəʊ/","a":"en-us-throw.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you throw an object, you make it fly through the air using your hands.","e":"Jim can throw a ball over his house."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A throw is the act of throwing.","e":"You made a fast throw!"}]}]},"throws":{"h":"throws","a":"en-us-throws.ogg","l":"throw","q":"verb"},"threw":{"h":"threw","i":"/'θrʊə/","a":"en-us-threw.ogg","l":"throw","q":"verb"},"thrown":{"h":"thrown","i":"/θrəʊn/","a":"en-us-thrown.ogg","l":"throw","q":"verb"},"languages":{"h":"languages","a":"en-us-languages.ogg","l":"language","q":"noun"},"alright":{"h":"alright","i":"/ˌɔːlˈraɪt/","a":"en-us-alright.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is alright, that means that it is in good condition.","e":"My car is alright."},{"m":"When a person or animal is alright, they are in good health.","e":"I had a headache earlier, but now I'm alright."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Something that went quite well.","e":"The soccer tournament went alright, I guess."}]}]},"awright":{"h":"awright","s":[{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"Awright is okay or a sign of approval.","e":"Awright! We won!"}]}]},"further":{"h":"further","i":"/ˈfɜː.ðə/","a":"en-GB-further.ogg","l":"far","q":"adjective","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"When something is further away, it is at a longer distance.","e":"We walked further than we had planned."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"more; additional","e":"Some further problems have come up."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you further something, you encourage it to grow.","e":"Further the economy."},{"m":"When you further something, you support it to progress or grow."}]}]},"spells":{"h":"spells","l":"spell","q":"verb"},"spelled":{"h":"spelled","i":"/ˈspεld/","l":"spell","q":"verb"},"spelling":{"h":"spelling","i":"/ˈspelɪŋ/","a":"en-us-spelling.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The way letters are used to write a word; the way a word is spelled.","e":"This page has too many spelling mistakes."}]}]},"differently":{"h":"differently","i":"/ˈdɪfrəntli/","a":"en-us-differently.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"In a different way.","e":"The new manager wants to run things differently from before."}]}]},"nations":{"h":"nations","i":"/ˈneɪʃənz/","a":"en-us-nations.ogg","l":"nation","q":"noun"},"within":{"h":"within","i":"/wɪˈðɪn/","a":"en-us-within.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"before the time ends","e":"We should be finished within 30 minutes."},{"m":"not farther than","e":"The station is within a 10 minute walk from here."},{"m":"inside","e":"He lives within the city walls."}]}]},"times":{"h":"times","i":"/taɪmz/","a":"en-us-times.ogg","l":"time","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"multiplied by","e":"\"Three times three is nine\" is written: 3 × 3 = 9."}]}]},"per":{"h":"per","i":"/pɜː(r)/","a":"en-us-per.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"for each; during each","e":"Double rooms with full breakfast are £40 per person per night."}]}]},"since":{"h":"since","i":"/sɪns/","a":"en-us-since.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"From a particular time in the past until now or until a later time in the past.","e":"I haven't been there since 1969."},{"m":"You use since to show that something known is the reason for something else.","e":"Since John can't be there, we'll try for another day. (The audience already knows that John can't be there.)"}]}]},"throughout":{"h":"throughout","i":"[θruːˈʷaʊt]","a":"en-us-throughout.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"In every part or area.","e":"We have made changes throughout the company."},{"m":"During the whole of a specific time.","e":"Food is available throughout the day."}]}]},"downward":{"h":"downward","i":"/ˈdaʊnwɚd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-downward.wav","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"moving or facing down","e":"The company's sales have been following a downward trend for the last three years."}]}]},"downwards":{"h":"downwards","i":"/ˈdaʊnwədz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-downwards.wav","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"moving or facing down","e":"The company's sales have been following a downwards trend for the last three years."}]}]},"due":{"h":"due","i":"/djuː/","a":"en-us-due.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is due, it should happen at a particular time.","e":"We are due to arrive at Peason International Airport at 5:23."},{"m":"If someone is due something, they should get it.","e":"He's due $50 for the work he did last week."},{"m":"(formal) enough","e":"Please pay due attention."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If x is due to y, y causes x.","e":"Due to the recent changes, we were not able to complete this in time."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"directly in a direction (north, south, east, or west)","e":"Walk due south for one kilometre."}]}]},"excluding":{"h":"excluding","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"not including","e":"Everyone has helped, excluding Bob, because he was sick."}]}]},"following":{"h":"following","i":"/ˈfɒləʊɪŋ/","a":"en-us-following.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"After","e":"The prices jumped following the news."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"The following things are those that come later.","e":"The following chapters deal with this idea."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A following is a group of people that admire or follow something or someone.","e":"That rock band has a loyal following. I used to be a fan once as well."}]}]},"forth":{"h":"forth","i":"/fɔəθ/","a":"en-us-forth.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"outward; forward","e":"She brought forth a son."}]}]},"counting":{"h":"counting","i":"/ˈkaʊntɪŋ/","a":"en-us-counting.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"; with this/these included","e":"Counting the dog, we are a family of five."}]}]},"favour":{"h":"favour","i":"/ˈfeɪvɚ/","a":"en-us-favor.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Some help.","e":"Can you please do me a favour by washing the dishes?"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you favour someone, you like them and prefer them over other people."}]}]},"favours":{"h":"favours","l":"favour","q":"noun"},"bedpan":{"h":"bedpan","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A pan that is used while in bed instead of a toilet."}]}]},"bill":{"h":"bill","i":"/bɪl/","a":"en-us-bill.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bill is a piece of paper money; a banknote.","e":"I paid for my sandwich using a twenty-dollar bill."},{"m":"(countable) A bill is a piece of paper telling you what other people have done for you and how much you owe them.","e":"\"Ask the waitress if we can have the bill now.\""},{"m":"(countable) A bird's bill is its beak (the hard mouth part).","e":"The toucan is known for its colorful bill."},{"m":"(countable) A bill is a proposed law.","e":"The bill passed the Senate."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you bill someone, you give or send them a bill.","e":"The shop billed me $100 for tickets."},{"m":"(transitive) If you bill a person or an event, you announce them.","e":"He was billed as \"The Great Houdini\"."}]}]},"bills":{"h":"bills","i":"/bɪlz/","a":"en-us-bills.ogg","l":"bill","q":"noun"},"billed":{"h":"billed","i":"/bɪld/","l":"bill","q":"verb"},"billing":{"h":"billing","i":"/ˈbɪlɪŋ/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An actor's billing is the listing of their name on the credits for the movie, play, etc."}]}]},"fortune":{"h":"fortune","i":"/ˈfɔːtʃuːn/","a":"en-us-fortune.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A fortune is a very large amount of money.","e":"A million dollars is a fortune."},{"m":"Fortune is chance or luck.","e":"When we were lost, we had the good fortune to meet a postman."},{"m":"Fortune is a person's future.","e":"Jack went off into the world to seek his fortune."},{"m":"Fortune is often written about as if it was a person.","e":"Fortune smiled at me, and I won the lottery."}]}]},"fortunes":{"h":"fortunes","a":"en-us-fortunes.ogg","l":"fortune","q":"noun"},"feed":{"h":"feed","i":"/'fid/","a":"en-us-feed.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you feed someone, you give them food to eat.","e":"I feed my dog chicken bones every day."},{"m":"(intransitive) To eat.","e":"Farm-raised chickens feed on grain."},{"m":"(transitive) To give something to a machine.","e":"To start printing, feed the paper into the printer."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Food that is eaten by animals.","e":"Bird feed consists mainly of seeds."}]}]},"feeds":{"h":"feeds","l":"feed","q":"verb"},"fed":{"h":"fed","i":"/fεd/","a":"en-us-fed.ogg","l":"feed","q":"verb"},"welcome":{"h":"welcome","i":"/ˈwɛl.kəm/","a":"en-us-welcome.ogg","s":[{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"You say welcome as a greeting when someone arrives."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To greet or affirm the arrival of someone."},{"m":"When you welcome ideas, you accept them gladly and willingly.","e":"We welcome any suggestions you have so that we may improve our services."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When someone is welcome, their arrival makes people happy.","e":"You are welcome to stay at my house whenever you want."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The act of welcoming.","e":"Everyone, give a warm welcome to Mr. John Smith!"}]}]},"welcomes":{"h":"welcomes","l":"welcome","q":"verb"},"welcomed":{"h":"welcomed","l":"welcome","q":"verb"},"carry":{"h":"carry","i":"/ˈkɜ.ri/","a":"en-us-carry.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you carry something, you lift it up and move it to another place.","e":"Let me carry those bags in for you."},{"m":"(transitive) If a vehicle carries people or things, it moves them from one place to another.","e":"A plane carrying 155 people crashed into the Hudson River."},{"m":"(transitive) If a path, such as a river bed, a wire, or a hose carries something somewhere, the thing travels along the path.","e":"The main line carrying cold water to the house can be as small as one inch in diameter."},{"m":"(transitive) If moving water or air carries something, it moves it.","e":"The river carried the leaves under the bridge."},{"m":"(transitive) If you carry something, you usually have it with you.","e":"Sorry, I don't carry a watch."},{"m":"(transitive) If something carries a quality, it has it.","e":"Those ideas now carry almost no value."},{"m":"(transitive) If the media carries some news, advertisement, or show, it prints it or puts it on TV or radio.","e":"The website carried a video showing policemen beating up children."},{"m":"(transitive) If something carries some information, the information is printed on it.","e":"The drug now carries a warning that it should not be given to children."},{"m":"(transitive) If a store carries something, they have it available to buy.","e":"My local supermarket doesn't carry my favorite brand of ice cream."},{"m":"(transitive) If something unmoving carries a weight or load, it supports it, keeping it up.","e":"In a fire, the wall are not going to be able to carry the load and the house will collapse."},{"m":"(transitive) If you carry insurance, you have it in case of a loss.","e":"Schools are increasing the amount of insurance they carry to protect themselves."},{"m":"(transitive) If you carry a disease, you can give it to other people.","e":"Most people who carry the virus never get sick."},{"m":"(transitive) If you get/are carried away, you lose control of yourself because you are so happy, angry, etc.","e":"Teens sometimes get carried away with buying stuff."},{"m":"(transitive) If a crime carries a punishment, that is the punishment for committing that crime.","e":"Violating the law carries a penalty of up to five years in prison and a $50,000 fine."},{"m":"(intransitive) If a sound carries, it can be heard a long distance away.","e":"The sound of the bells carried for miles."},{"m":"(transitive) If you can carry a tune, you can sing the correct notes.","e":"He couldn't carry a tune, but he loved to sing."},{"m":"(transitive) If one voice or instrument in a group carries the melody, it sings or plays the melody while the others provide harmony.","e":"The highest voice carries the melody."},{"m":"(transitive) If someone or something carries the day, they win.","e":"Don't worry if we don't carry the day this year."},{"m":"(transitive) If a suggestion, idea, or proposal is carried or carries, it gets the most votes and wins.","e":"59% of the votes for approving the budget: The motion carries."},{"m":"(transitive) If a candidate in an election carries an area, they win in that area."},{"m":"(transitive) If you carry your body or yourself in a certain way, that is the way that you stand or move."},{"m":"(transitive) If a woman is carrying a child, she is pregnant.","e":"He didn't know that she was carrying his child."},{"m":"(transitive) If you carry something too far/to extremes/to excess, you don't stop it at a reasonable time."},{"m":"(transitive) If you carry extra pounds/kilograms, you weigh more than you should."},{"m":"(transitive) If you carry a number during addition or multiplication, you add it to the column on the left.","e":"Seven times eight is fifty six, carry five. Seven times nine is sixty three, plus five is sixty eight. Six hundred eighty six."},{"m":"(accounting) If you carry a loss forward, you realize it in a future reporting period.","e":"If your net capital loss is more than this limit, you can carry the loss forward to later years."},{"m":"(transitive) (accounting) If you carry something off, you do it successfully.","e":"They tried, but they just weren't good enough musicians to carry it off."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you carry on, you continue doing what you were doing.","e":"We want to carry on doing this for the next five years."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you carry on about something, you talk about it in an annoying way.","e":"Cindy was always carrying on about how cute her dog was."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you carry out something requiring planning, you do it.","e":"They weren't able to carry out the attack because of the weather."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something carries or is carried over into a new situation, it continues to happen or be useful in the new situation.","e":"Was there anything you learned from that experience that you have carried over into your current job?"},{"m":"(transitive) If something carries you through, it helps you get to the end.","e":"Their love of the game carried them through the difficult times."},{"m":"(transitive) If you carry something through, you complete it.","e":"Once you have an idea, you've got to carry it through all the way."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A carry is a play in American football where a player holds the ball and runs with it.","e":"No player in NFL history has ever had that many carries."},{"m":"(uncountable) The carry is the distance a ball, arrow, bullet, etc. travels.","e":"The fairway is 15 yards wide and the carry was 370."},{"m":"(countable) A carry is a way of moving somebody from one place to another.","e":"He picked her up and put her over his shoulder in a fireman's carry,"}]}]},"carries":{"h":"carries","i":"/ˈkær.ɪz/","a":"en-us-carries.ogg","l":"carry","q":"verb"},"carried":{"h":"carried","l":"carry","q":"verb"},"kill":{"h":"kill","i":"/kɪl/","a":"en-us-kill.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To kill a person, thing, or an animal means to cause a person, thing, or an animal to die.","e":"Smoking kills more people each year than alcohol and drugs combined."},{"m":"To make something not work.","e":"He killed the engine and turned off the headlights, but remained in the car, waiting."},{"m":"If someone kills a thing, they bring it to an end.","e":"Kill the jokes. Let's get serious."},{"m":"If something has been killed, it has been treated in a very bad way.","e":"The rough road killed the tires on my car."},{"m":"If something is killing a person, it causes pain. If a body part is killing a person, it hurts.","e":"My headache is killing me."},{"m":"If something funny kills a person, it makes them laugh.","e":"Your jokes just kill me."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The act of killing.","e":"The assassin liked to make a clean kill, and thus favored small arms over explosives."},{"m":"The result of killing; the thing that has been killed.","e":"The fox dragged its kill back to its den."}]}]},"penis":{"h":"penis","i":"/ˈpiːnɪs/","a":"en-us-penis.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A penis is the male organ for sex and urination."}]}]},"knock":{"h":"knock","i":"/nɒk/","a":"en-us-knock.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A sound from something hard hitting wood."},{"m":"(countable) An impact."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you knock on something, you hit your knuckles onto it repeatedly.","e":"She knocked on my door three times before I opened it."},{"m":"When you knock something, you hit it, often accidentally."}]}]},"tools":{"h":"tools","l":"tool","q":"noun"},"kittens":{"h":"kittens","l":"kitten","q":"noun"},"memorable":{"h":"memorable","i":"/ˈmɛm(ə)rəbl̩/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-memorable.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is memorable, it is very important or remarkable and is easy to remember."}]}]},"memorably":{"h":"memorably","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"In a memorable way."}]}]},"nonsense":{"h":"nonsense","i":"/ˈnɑnsɛns/","a":"en-us-nonsense.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Something is nonsense when it makes no sense or has no meaning.","e":"This is just a bunch of words randomly jumbled together. It is complete nonsense."},{"m":"Something that is false; a lie.","e":"He says that I stole his computer, but that's just nonsense."}]}]},"nonsensical":{"h":"nonsensical","i":"/nɒnˈsɛnsɪk(ə)l/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is nonsensical, it makes no sense and has no reason; it means nothing."}]}]},"wish":{"h":"wish","i":"/wɪʃ/","a":"en-us-wish.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you wish for something, you want it and hope for it; you want it to happen."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A wish is something that has not happened yet but you want to happen."}]}]},"travel":{"h":"travel","i":"/trævəl/","a":"en-us-travel.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) When you travel, you visit some place; you go on a journey or adventure.","e":"I traveled to Mexico for a vacation and to visit my cousin."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The act of traveling.","e":"Astronauts do space travel."}]}]},"dermatologist":{"h":"dermatologist","i":"/ˌdɜːməˈtɒlədʒɪst/","a":"en-ca-dermatologist.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A doctor that specializes in skin.","e":"I had to see a dermatologist about my acne last year."}]}]},"mislead":{"h":"mislead","i":"/mɪsˈliːd/","a":"en-us-misled.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If I mislead you, I make you believe something that is not true.","e":"You mislead him into believing that you are a king. You are only a common man."}]}]},"dentist":{"h":"dentist","i":"/ˈdɛntɪst/","a":"en-us-dentist.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A dentist is a doctor who specializes in dentistry.","e":"I have to go to the dentist to get a tooth pulled."}]}]},"visit":{"h":"visit","i":"/ˈvɪzɪt/","a":"en-us-visit.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you visit someone, you meet the person.","e":"I visit my friend Bethsy at her house every Tuesday."},{"m":"When you visit a place, you see the place.","e":"When I went to Paris, I visited the Eiffel Tower."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The act of visiting.","e":"I paid a visit to my grandmother last weekend to see how she was doing."}]}]},"deceive":{"h":"deceive","i":"/dɪˈsiːv/","a":"en-us-deceive.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you deceive someone, you make someone believe something that is not true; you mislead them.","e":"John was angry that Jane had deceived him."}]}]},"deceptive":{"h":"deceptive","i":"/dɪ.ˈsɛp.tɪv/","a":"en-us-deceptive.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is deceptive, it tries to make people believe something that is not true; it misleads.","e":"He is a deceptive person. I would not trust him."}]}]},"indoors":{"h":"indoors","i":"/ˈɪndɔːz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-indoors.wav","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"in or into a house or other building","e":"On a cold day like today, I think I'll stay indoors."}]}]},"zoo":{"h":"zoo","i":"/zuː/","a":"En-us-zoo.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A zoo is a park that people go to where live animals can be seen.","e":"There are lions at our local zoo."}]}]},"zoos":{"h":"zoos","l":"zoo","q":"noun"},"instead":{"h":"instead","i":"/ɪn.ˈstɛd/","a":"en-us-instead.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"x instead of y means: not y but x.","e":"I'll have water instead of coffee, thanks."}]}]},"owing":{"h":"owing","a":"en-us-owing.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"You use owing to x, y to show that x is the reason for y.","e":"Owing to the problems, we have not been able to finish."}]}]},"provided":{"h":"provided","i":"/prəˈvaɪdɪd/","a":"en-us-provided.ogg","l":"provide","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"You use provided x, y to show that if x is true, happens, etc., y will, too.","e":"The doctor can save his life, provided he arrives in time."}]}]},"providing":{"h":"providing","i":"/prəˈvaɪdɪŋ/","a":"en-us-providing.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"You use providing x, y to show that if x is true, happens, etc., y will, too.","e":"The doctor can save his life, providing he arrives in time."}]}]},"shoot":{"h":"shoot","i":"/ʃuːt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Back ache-shoot.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you shoot, you use a weapon to throw something at a very fast speed at someone or something.","e":"The man, in a desperate bid for freedom, grabbed his gun and started shooting anyone he could."},{"m":"When you shoot something, you photograph or film something.","e":"At the zoo, I like to shoot many pictures of the animals."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The shoot is the stem or bud of a plant.","e":"The seed I planted yesterday got a tiny shoot."},{"m":"(informal) A less offensive way of saying shit.","e":"Oh shoot!"}]},{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"You say shoot when you are angry or in disbelief; to condemn.","e":"Didn't you have a concert tonight? Shoot! I forgot! I have to go and get ready..."}]}]},"shot":{"h":"shot","i":"/'ʃɒt/","a":"en-us-shot.ogg","l":"shoot","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The act of a gun firing."},{"m":"The sound of a gun firing."},{"m":"Small balls or pellets of lead typically fired from a shotgun."}]}]},"shooting":{"h":"shooting","i":"/ˈʃuːtɪŋ/","a":"en-uk-shooting.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A shooting is the event of a person shooting another with a gun.","e":"The police are looking for the person responsible for the shooting of a well-known lawyer last night."}]}]},"shoots":{"h":"shoots","a":"en-us-shoots.ogg","l":"shoot","q":"verb"},"seeing":{"h":"seeing","i":"/ˈsiːɪŋ/","a":"en-us-seeing.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"You use seeing as x, y to show that x is the reason for y.","e":"Seeing there are some new people, maybe we could each introduce ourselves."}]}]},"supposing":{"h":"supposing","i":"/səˈpoʊzɪŋ/","a":"en-us-supposing.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"You use supposing to talk about an imaginary situation.","e":"Supposing one group practices for one hour and another group practices for two hours, the second group will probably be better."}]}]},"regarding":{"h":"regarding","i":"/rɪˈɡɑːdɪŋ/","a":"en-us-regarding.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"You use regarding to introduce your subject or topic.","e":"Regarding the changes, the rules are very clear."}]}]},"respecting":{"h":"respecting","i":"/rɪˈspɛktɪŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Wodencafe-respecting.wav","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"You use respecting to introduce your subject or topic.","e":"He began to have serious worries respecting his car."}]}]},"touching":{"h":"touching","i":"/ˈtʌtʃɪŋ/","a":"en-us-touching.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is touching it makes you feel sad or have pity.","e":"What a touching story!"}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"concerning, regarding","e":"There has been a number of difficulties touching on almost every aspect of the business."}]}]},"vandalism":{"h":"vandalism","i":"/ˈvændəlɪzm̩/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-vandalism.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Vandalism is the damage or destruction of someone else's property or of common or shared property.","e":"Graffiti is a form of vandalism rampant in urban areas."}]}]},"toward":{"h":"toward","i":"/təˈwɔːd/","a":"en-us-toward.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"facing or moving in the direction of something","e":"We were walking toward the shop when she began feeling sick."},{"m":"If you put money towards something, the money is to help pay for it.","e":"He's been saving money toward a new computer for school."},{"m":"close to","e":"Toward the end, we were getting very tired."}]}]},"towards":{"h":"towards","i":"/təˈwɔːdz/","a":"en-us-towards.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"facing or moving in the direction of something","e":"We were walking towards the shop when she began feeling sick."},{"m":"If you put money towards something, the money is to help pay for it.","e":"He's been saving money towards a new computer for school."},{"m":"close to","e":"Towards the end, we were getting very tired."}]}]},"underground":{"h":"underground","i":"/ˌʌndəˈɡraʊnd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-underground.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"of or about being under the ground","e":"Underground water is drying up."},{"m":"secret or not well known","e":"The underground music scene is really interesting."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"being or moving under the ground","e":"Let's go underground. It's safer down there."},{"m":"If you go underground, you keep your activities secret."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The underground is a system of trains that runs mostly under the ground.","e":"The London underground is a great way to move about the city."}]}]},"dermatologists":{"h":"dermatologists","l":"dermatologist","q":"noun"},"weigh":{"h":"weigh","i":"/weɪ/","a":"en-us-weigh.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you weigh something, you find out its weight.","e":"I weighed my luggage to make sure it did not exceed the weight limit of the airline."},{"m":"(intransitive) To have a certain weight.","e":"My dog weighs 30 pounds."}]}]},"aerial":{"h":"aerial","i":"/ˈɛr.i.əl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-aerial.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is aerial, it is in the air."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An aerial is something used to transmit and receive signals."}]}]},"aerials":{"h":"aerials","l":"aerial","q":"noun"},"peanut":{"h":"peanut","i":"/ˈpiːnʌt/","a":"en-us-peanut.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A peanut is a type of legume that looks like a nut."}]}]},"unlike":{"h":"unlike","i":"/ʌnˈlaɪk/","a":"en-us-unlike.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"not the same as; different from.","e":"This is unlike anything I have ever done before."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"different","e":"They were dressed in an unlike manner."}]}]},"inconsistent":{"h":"inconsistent","i":"/ˌɪnkənˈsɪstənt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-inconsistent.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is inconsistent, it is not reliable and you cannot guess what it will be like in the future.","e":"What he said was inconsistent with what he told me yesterday. I think he is lying."}]}]},"tickle":{"h":"tickle","i":"/ˈtɪkl̩/","a":"en-us-tickle.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you tickle someone, you touch them in a way that makes them laugh.","e":"He tickled Nancy's tummy, and she started to giggle."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The act of tickling."}]}]},"upstairs":{"h":"upstairs","i":"/ˌʌpˈstɛrz/","a":"en-us-upstairs.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If something is upstairs, it is on the level at the top of the stairs.","e":"Let us head upstairs, from the kitchen to the bedroom."}]}]},"upward":{"h":"upward","i":"/ˈʌpwɜːrd/","a":"en-us-upward.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"moving or facing up","e":"The company's sales have been following an upward trend for the last three years."}]}]},"upwards":{"h":"upwards","i":"/ˈʌpwədz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-upwards.wav","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"moving or facing up","e":"The company's sales have been following an upwards trend for the last three years."}]}]},"converse":{"h":"converse","i":"/kənˈvɜːs/","a":"en-us-converse.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) When you converse, you take part in a conversation; you talk."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The opposite of something."}]}]},"converses":{"h":"converses","l":"converse","q":"verb"},"conversed":{"h":"conversed","l":"converse","q":"verb"},"consider":{"h":"consider","i":"/kənˈsɪdə/","a":"en-us-consider.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you consider something you think carefully about it.","e":"I will take time to consider what you said."}]}]},"grandparent":{"h":"grandparent","i":"/ˈɡræn(d)pɛərənt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-grandparent.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Someone's grandparent is the parent of their parent. It is one's grandmother or grandfather.","e":"The mother of my mother is Jane Smith. Jane Smith is one of my grandparents."}]}]},"grandmother":{"h":"grandmother","i":"/ˈɡræn(d)ˌmʌðɚ/","a":"en-us-grandmother.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Someone's grandmother is the mother of one of their parents.","e":"The mother of my mother is Jane Smith. Jane Smith is my grandmother."}]}]},"granddaughter":{"h":"granddaughter","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Someone's granddaughter is the daughter of their son or daughter.","e":"My son, John, has a daughter named Patty. Patty is my granddaughter."}]}]},"activity":{"h":"activity","i":"/ækˈtɪ.vɪ.ti/","a":"en-us-activity.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) When a person or animal has activity, it is active or lively.","e":"The sleeping dog did not show much activity."},{"m":"(countable) When you have a function to do, you have an activity.","e":"The child has many after-school activities."}]}]},"adjectives":{"h":"adjectives","l":"adjective","q":"noun"},"yum":{"h":"yum","i":"/jʌm/","a":"en-au-yum.ogg","s":[{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"You say yum when you are happy or delighted about something, usually food.","e":"Yum! That apple pie was so tasty!"}]}]},"yuck":{"h":"yuck","i":"/jʌk/","a":"en-us-yuck.oga","s":[{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"You say yuck when you are unhappy or disgusted about something, usually food.","e":"Yuck! That fish tastes disgusting!"}]}]},"diocese":{"h":"diocese","i":"/ˈdaɪ.ə.sɪs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-diocese.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A diocese is the area looked after by the a bishop in some churches. It contains several parishes."}]}]},"parish":{"h":"parish","i":"/ˈpærɪʃ/","a":"en-us-parish.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An area looked after by one local church and its ministers"},{"m":"Parish is the name used instead of county in the State of Louisiana, USA."},{"m":"A Civil Parish is the smallest local government area in England."}]}]},"bishop":{"h":"bishop","i":"/ˈbɪʃəp/","a":"en-us-bishop.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) In some churches a bishop is a senior minister or priest, and is responsible for a diocese."},{"m":"(countable) (chess) A bishop is a piece in a game called chess."}]}]},"freer":{"h":"freer","i":"/ˈfriːər/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-freer.wav","l":"free","q":"adjective"},"freest":{"h":"freest","l":"free","q":"adjective"},"strongly":{"h":"strongly","i":"/strɔŋli/","a":"en-us-strongly.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"In a strong or powerful way.","e":"John strongly opposes that law. He refuses to change his opinion."}]}]},"effort":{"h":"effort","i":"/ˈɛfət/","a":"en-us-effort.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The amount of work that is done on something.","e":"A great amount of effort was put into this event; we had over 4,000 visitors."}]}]},"effortless":{"h":"effortless","i":"/ˈɛfətlɪs/","a":"en-us-effortless.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is effortless, it does not need effort.","e":"Please help me with these boxes. It is an effortless task, it will only take a few minutes."}]}]},"effortlessly":{"h":"effortlessly","i":"/ˈef.ət.ləs.li/","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If you do something effortlessly, you do it without effort or difficulty.","e":"After studying for three weeks, the student completed the exam effortlessly."}]}]},"treatments":{"h":"treatments","l":"treatment","q":"noun"},"pronouns":{"h":"pronouns","l":"pronoun","q":"noun"},"cross":{"h":"cross","i":"/krɒs/","a":"en-us-cross.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you cross something, you go from one side of it to the other side.","e":"Don't cross the street until the light turns green."},{"m":"(transitive) If you cross something, you put one part over another perpendicularly.","e":"She crossed her ankles: she put one foot on the other side of the other foot."},{"m":"(transitive) If you cross someone, you do something that the person does not like.","e":"Don't cross me. Make sure to agree with me."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you cross, you go in a path that will intersect with someone else's path.","e":"Boats crossing from starboard have right-of-way."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cross (🞣) is a figure made of two straight lines or bars that intersect each other such that at least one of them bisects the other.","e":"In Christianity, the death of Jesus is represented by a cross."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Someone who is cross is angry or annoyed.","e":"Jill spoke to me rudely because she was cross."}]}]},"stuff":{"h":"stuff","i":"/stʌf/","a":"en-us-stuff.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Stuff is what makes up something; the things that it is made from.","e":"What is all that stuff on your bedroom floor?"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you stuff something, you put a lot of things inside of it; you compress things into it.","e":"She stuffed the turkey for Thanksgiving using her secret stuffing recipe of diced bread, onions, and celery."},{"m":"To be happy and satisfied, usually to do with food.","e":"I'm stuffed after having eaten all that turkey, mashed potatoes and delicious stuffing."}]}]},"dentists":{"h":"dentists","l":"dentist","q":"noun"},"unite":{"h":"unite","i":"/yuˈnaɪt","a":"en-us-unite.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If two or more things unite, they come together to form a bigger group.","e":"We united to form a common cause against our enemy."}]}]},"member":{"h":"member","i":"/ˈmɛmbə/","a":"en-us-member.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A member is someone belonging to a group or organization.","e":"I am a member of Simple English Wikipedia."}]}]},"party":{"h":"party","i":"/ˈpɑː.ti/","a":"en-us-party.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A party is when people get together for fun or to celebrate something like a birthday.","e":"I'm throwing a huge party for my 21st birthday. There'll be cake, games, and lots of fun!"},{"m":"(countable) A party is a political group.","e":"The Liberal Party will form the government."},{"m":"(countable) A party is any group of people who are together for a reason.","e":"Inside the restaurant, a party of four had taken their seats."},{"m":"(countable) A party is one person or group in a disagreement."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) When you party, you go to a party and enjoy yourself.","e":"We partied until the early hours."}]}]},"parties":{"h":"parties","i":"/ˈpɑrtiz/","a":"en-us-parties.ogg","l":"party","q":"noun"},"partied":{"h":"partied","l":"party","q":"verb"},"sure":{"h":"sure","i":"/ʃʊə(r)/","a":"en-us-sure.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When you are sure about something, you are certain.","e":"The student was sure that his answer was correct."}]}]},"share":{"h":"share","i":"/ʃɛə/","a":"en-us-share.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you share something, you let another person use it.","e":"We can both sit down if you share the chair."},{"m":"When two people divide a thing between them, they share that thing.","e":"I will share this big piece of cake with you."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Several people can get a share of something if they divide it between them.","e":"I will give you a share of this big bag of candy."},{"m":"(finance) A share is a part of a company's capital, it entitles the holder to a proportion of the profits."}]}]},"expect":{"h":"expect","i":"/ɪkˈspɛkt/","a":"en-us-expect.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you expect something you anticipate it.","e":"I expect a letter in the mail from my friend today."},{"m":"When you learn that you conceived a baby, it is said that you are expecting.","e":"My sister got married just one week ago, and she tells me she is expecting."}]}]},"shape":{"h":"shape","i":"/ʃeɪp/","a":"en-us-shape.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The shape of a thing is its external form.","e":"The cake was made into the shape of a car."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you shape something, you change its shape.","e":"I will shape the material to look any way you want it."}]}]},"staff":{"h":"staff","i":"/stɑːf/","a":"en-us-staff.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The employees of a company."},{"m":"(countable) A long, straight stick that is mostly used to help people walk and is sometimes used in martial arts."},{"m":"(countable) A staff is five lines that music is written on."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you staff a business, you provide them with employees."}]}]},"strike":{"h":"strike","i":"/straɪk/","a":"en-us-strike.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you hit something, you strike it.","e":"If you strike a person, it will hurt."},{"m":"When an idea strikes you, it occurs to you suddenly or with force.","e":"To play with fire strikes me as a bad idea."},{"m":"When a clock rings a bell to tell you the time, the clock strikes the time.","e":"The children ran out of the school when the clock struck twelve."},{"m":"A disease can strike a person. That person is stricken with disease.","e":"The child was stricken with a serious blood disease."},{"m":"When you strike a part from a document, it is stricken from the document.","e":"The errors were stricken from the dictionary."},{"m":"When bad luck strikes you, you are stricken with bad luck."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) When a group of people stop working to improve or defend their working conditions or pay, they go on strike.","e":"Every secretary at the company went on strike for better pay."}]}]},"stricken":{"h":"stricken","i":"/'strɪkən/","a":"en-us-stricken.ogg","l":"strike","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"A disease can strike a person. That person is stricken with disease.","e":"The child was stricken with a serious blood disease."},{"m":"When you strike a part from a document, it is stricken from the document.","e":"The errors were stricken from the dictionary."},{"m":"When bad luck strikes you, you are stricken with bad luck."}]}]},"struck":{"h":"struck","i":"/'stɻʌk/","a":"en-us-struck.ogg","l":"strike","q":"verb"},"hang":{"h":"hang","i":"/hæŋ/","a":"en-us-hang.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you hang things, you put something above the ground and with no support below using rope, wire, or some other means.","e":"Now, I hang this picture on the wall."},{"m":"When a person is held in the air by a rope around his/her neck until dead, the person is hanged.","e":"Some states and nations hanged people as punishment for murdering of another."}]}]},"hung":{"h":"hung","l":"hang","q":"verb"},"hanged":{"h":"hanged","a":"en-us-hanged.ogg","l":"hang","q":"verb"},"forget":{"h":"forget","i":"/fəˈɡɛt/","a":"en-us-forget.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you forget something, you have no memory of it.","e":"I forget every thing that you tell me."}]}]},"forgot":{"h":"forgot","i":"/fəˈɡɒt/","a":"en-us-forgot.ogg","l":"forget","q":"verb"},"forgotten":{"h":"forgotten","i":"/fɚˈɡɑt.n̩/","a":"en-us-forgotten.ogg","l":"forget","q":"verb"},"spend":{"h":"spend","i":"/spεnd/","a":"en-us-spend.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you spend money, you give the money to buy something.","e":"I spend too much at the book store each month."},{"m":"to pass, to use","e":"I spend my free time reading and relaxing."}]}]},"spent":{"h":"spent","i":"/ˈspɛnt/","a":"en-us-spent.ogg","l":"spend","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is spent it is used up, exhausted, depleted.","e":"After running 10 miles, I'm completely spent."}]}]},"staves":{"h":"staves","i":"/steɪv/","l":"staff"},"pizza":{"h":"pizza","i":"/piːtsə/","a":"en-us-pizza.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pizza is a baked Italian food made of rolled bread dough crust, generally topped with tomato sauce, cheese and other ingredients.","e":"I bought some pizza from a nearby Italian restaurant for the party."}]}]},"cavity":{"h":"cavity","i":"/ˈkævɪti/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-cavity.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cavity is a hole or hollow area."},{"m":"(countable) A cavity is a hollow area inside the body (like the sinuses)."},{"m":"(countable) A cavity is a hole in a decayed tooth.","e":"You have a cavity in your back teeth."}]}]},"avoid":{"h":"avoid","i":"/əˈvɔɪd/","a":"en-us-avoid.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you avoid something, you stay away from it or you don't do it.","e":"Are you avoiding me?"}]}]},"inevitable":{"h":"inevitable","i":"/ɪnˈɛvɪtəbəl/","a":"en-us-inevitable.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is inevitable, you cannot avoid or prevent it."},{"m":"Something that is predictable or always happens."}]}]},"avoidable":{"h":"avoidable","i":"/əˈvɔɪdəbl̩/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-avoidable.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is avoidable, you can avoid it."}]}]},"avoidably":{"h":"avoidably","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"In an avoidable way.","e":"The cars were parked as avoidably as possible; it didn't stop her from running into one."}]}]},"evitable":{"h":"evitable","i":"/ˈɛvɪtəb(ə)l/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-evitable.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is evitable, it can be avoided.","e":"The tragic consequences were evitable."}]}]},"avoided":{"h":"avoided","i":"/əˈvɔɪdɪd/","a":"en-us-avoided.ogg","l":"avoid","q":"verb"},"avoids":{"h":"avoids","l":"avoid","q":"verb"},"goodbye":{"h":"goodbye","i":"/gʊdˈbaɪ/","a":"en-us-goodbye.ogg","s":[{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"You say goodbye when you leave/depart, as a farewell.","e":"Goodbye! See you next year."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The act of saying \"goodbye\" to someone."}]}]},"actually":{"h":"actually","i":"/ˈæk.tʃu.ə.li/","a":"en-us-actually.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"You use actually to say that something is real; in fact; really.","e":"Actually, I had nothing to do with that incident."}]}]},"speed":{"h":"speed","i":"/spiːd/","a":"en-us-speed.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) When you speed, you move or do something very fast.","e":"The child speeds through his so he can go out and play."},{"m":"When you speed in a car, you drive faster than the law allows.","e":"If you speed in your car, you might have an accident."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The speed of something is how fast it moves.","e":"sound moves at a very high speed."}]}]},"sped":{"h":"sped","i":"/spɛd/","a":"en-us-sped.ogg","l":"speed","q":"verb"},"rid":{"h":"rid","i":"/'rɪd/","a":"en-us-rid.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you rid a thing, you free it of something not wanted.","e":"If you rid the house of a bad smell, you can close the window."}]}]},"hide":{"h":"hide","i":"/haɪd/","a":"en-us-hide.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you hide something, you put it where others will not find it.","e":"I hide candy to keep it from my brother."},{"m":"When you hide, you go where others will not find you.","e":"When my father is angry, I hide under the bed."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The skin of an animal is its hide.","e":"Many cloths are made from the hide of a cow."}]}]},"hid":{"h":"hid","i":"/hɪd/","a":"en-us-hid.ogg","l":"hide","q":"verb"},"dive":{"h":"dive","i":"/ˈdaɪv/","a":"en-us-dive.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) When you dive, you go under the water, usually jumping head first.","e":"She dived under the water and came up blowing air."},{"m":"(intransitive) When you dive into action, you do something with great interest.","e":"They dove into the work when they liked it."}]}]},"dove":{"h":"dove","i":"/dʌv/","a":"en-us-dove-noun.ogg","l":"dive","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A dove is a pigeon, especially one smaller in size; they are often shown in art as being white.","e":"A dove holding an olive branch is a symbol of peace."}]}]},"children":{"h":"children","i":"/ˈʧɪldrən/","a":"en-us-children.ogg","l":"child","q":"noun"},"clothe":{"h":"clothe","i":"/ˈkləʊð/","a":"en-us-clothe.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you clothe something or someone, you put clothes on them.","e":"The mother clothes her children to go to school in the morning."},{"m":"(transitive) If you clothe somebody, you provide clothes for them.","e":"She was struggling to feed and clothe five kids."}]}]},"clad":{"h":"clad","l":"clothe","q":"verb"},"fix":{"h":"fix","i":"/fɪks/","a":"en-us-fix.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When a person fixes something, they repair it.","e":"The mechanic fixes my car."},{"m":"(transitive) When a person fixes something to something else, they attach it or hold it in place.","e":"A piece of chewing gum will fix your note to the bulletin board."},{"m":"(transitive) When a person fixes something at a certain time, they make a rule or agreement that the time will not change.","e":"The Constitution fixes the date when Congress must meet."},{"m":"(transitive) If someone fixes an animal, they remove its reproductive organs, so that it can’t have babies.","e":"After you fix a male cat, it doesn't fight with other cats as much."},{"m":"(transitive) If a person fixes a game, contest, or election, somebody unfairly controls what will happen before it is over.","e":"Someone has fixed the game so that none can win."},{"m":"(transitive) When a person attacks or punishes someone, they fix them.","e":"If you do anything wrong in that city, they will fix you."},{"m":"Protected from arrest or conviction.","e":"Don't worry about it, we're fixed with the cops."}]}]},"receive":{"h":"receive","i":"/rɪsiːv/","a":"en-us-receive.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you receive something, you get something that was sent or given to you.","e":"I receive letters in the mail every day."}]}]},"characteristic":{"h":"characteristic","i":"/ˌkærəktəˈrɪstɪk/","a":"en-us-characteristic.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A characteristic of something is a typical feature.","e":"Good hearing is one characteristic of dogs."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A thing has a characteristic trait if it is typical for its group.","e":"Red is a characteristic color of a rose."}]}]},"soccer":{"h":"soccer","i":"/ˈsɒk.əː/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-soccer.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(North America, South Africa, Australia) A sport where the players try to kick a ball into a net.","e":"Let's play soccer."}]}]},"sport":{"h":"sport","i":"/spɔrt/","a":"en-us-sport.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Sport is physical exercise which involves players playing in a team.","e":"What sport shall we play?"},{"m":"A sport is a helpful person.","e":"Be a good sport and open the door for me."},{"m":"(uncountable) Sport is fun or entertainment.","e":"It was good sport to surprise him like that."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To sport something is to wear it."}]}]},"sports":{"h":"sports","i":"/spɔrts/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-sports.wav","l":"sport","q":"noun"},"also":{"h":"also","i":"/ˈɔːlsəʊ/","a":"en-us-also.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"When one thing happens and a second thing happens in a same or similar time or way, then the second thing also happens.","e":"We bought bread at the store. We also bought milk."},{"m":"Similarly."},{"m":"When one person does a thing and a second person does the same thing, then the second person also does that thing.","e":"I went with my father to the store. My brother also went with us."}]}]},"social":{"h":"social","i":"/ˈsəʊʃəl/","a":"en-us-social.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A social is a festive gathering to let people introduce oneself to others."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When a person or animal is social, it lives with others.","e":"s are social animals."},{"m":"Social change, structure, class, etc. is about society.","e":"Our country is going through a period of social change."}]}]},"bagel":{"h":"bagel","i":"/ˈbeɪɡəl/","a":"en-us-bagel.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bagel is a circular piece of bread that is usually eaten at breakfast."}]}]},"alabama":{"h":"Alabama","i":"/ˌæləˈbæmə/","a":"en-us-Alabama.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Alabama is a state in southeastern United States whose capital is Montgomery."}]}]},"kami":{"h":"kami","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A god or spirit in the Shinto religion of Japan."}]}]},"including":{"h":"including","i":"/ɪnˈkluːdɪŋ/","a":"en-us-including.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Used to make clear that something is also part of a group.","e":"We had a big family: eleven of us, including mum and dad."}]}]},"without":{"h":"without","i":"/wɪθˈaʊt/","a":"en-us-without.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Used to say that you don't have something or that something isn't in a place.","e":"I went all the way to school without my books."},{"m":"Used to say that somebody didn't do something or that something didn't happen.","e":"She walked past without looking at me."},{"m":"outside"}]}]},"whenever":{"h":"whenever","i":"/wəˈnɛvɚ/","a":"en-us-whenever.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"every time","e":"I practice whenever I have some free time."},{"m":"at any time","e":"You should call her whenever you can."}]}]},"marks":{"h":"marks","a":"en-us-marks.ogg","l":"mark","q":"noun"},"marked":{"h":"marked","i":"/ˈmɑr.kɪd/","a":"en-us-marked-adj.ogg","l":"mark","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is marked is significant or notable.","e":"There is a marked difference between the small and large shirts."}]}]},"marking":{"h":"marking","i":"/ˈmɑrkɪŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-marking.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A mark."},{"m":"An animal's marking is its coloring and patterns.","e":"A zebra's marking is typically black and white stripes."}]}]},"markings":{"h":"markings","l":"marking","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An animal's markings are its coloring and patterns."}]}]},"sorrier":{"h":"sorrier","l":"sorry","q":"adjective"},"sorriest":{"h":"sorriest","l":"sorry","q":"adjective"},"structures":{"h":"structures","l":"structure","q":"noun"},"structured":{"h":"structured","l":"structure","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is structured is organized and has structure."}]}]},"sponges":{"h":"sponges","l":"sponge","q":"noun"},"sponged":{"h":"sponged","l":"sponge","q":"verb"},"drawers":{"h":"drawers","i":"/drɔrz/","a":"en-au-drawers.ogg","l":"drawer","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Drawers are men's underpants, short pants that men wear under their clothes.","e":"When he heard the doorbell ring, he didn't know whether to open the door because he was in his drawers."}]}]},"albinism":{"h":"albinism","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A person or animal who has albinism has a lack of pigment (color) in their skin, eyes, and hair or feathers (or more rarely only in the eyes); it is the condition of being albino."}]}]},"advisor":{"h":"advisor","i":"/ædˈvaɪz.ɚ/","a":"en-us-advisor.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An advisor is a person who gives advice.","e":"He was the king's advisor. The king relied on him whenever he needed help."}]}]},"adviser":{"h":"adviser","i":"/ædˈvaɪz.ɚ/","a":"en-us-advisor.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An adviser is a person who gives advice."}]}]},"until":{"h":"until","i":"/ənˈtɪl/","a":"en-us-until.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If something is true until x, it is true for some time before x and then is not true.","e":"We didn't have any snow until the end of December."}]}]},"upon":{"h":"upon","i":"/ ə' pɒn /","a":"en-us-upon.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"on or onto","e":"The police were called upon to save him."},{"m":"going to happen","e":"Christmas is almost upon us."},{"m":"at (a time)","e":"Upon his death, she became the owner of the store."}]}]},"pepperoni":{"h":"pepperoni","i":"/pɛpəˈroʊni/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-pepperoni.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sausage that is commonly put on pizza"}]}]},"wanting":{"h":"wanting","i":"/ˈwɑntɪŋ/","a":"en-us-wanting.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"not good enough","e":"After we hired him, we found his abilities wanting."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"without","e":"I've got a right shoe wanting a left."}]}]},"container":{"h":"container","i":"/kənˈteɪnə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-container.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An object that is used to hold or carry things inside it.","e":"They put their cards in containers."}]}]},"dianthus":{"h":"dianthus","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A Dianthus one of some types of plants. These plants all make flowers. Some of these plants are called \"carnations\" and \"Sweet William.\""},{"m":"(uncountable) All types of Dianthus as a group. This group is a genus in biology."}]}]},"unless":{"h":"unless","i":"/ənˈlɛs/","a":"en-us-unless.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If you say that x is true unless y, x is true only if y does not happen or is not true.","e":"I'll be there at 8:30 unless the train is late."}]}]},"just":{"h":"just","i":"/dʒʌst/","a":"en-us-just.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"When you just do something, you only did that thing.","e":"He was hungry, and he just wanted a good meal."},{"m":"When you just did something, you only did it a short time ago.","e":"I just left the house."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is just, it is fair.","e":"It seems like a just punishment to put someone in jail for stealing."}]}]},"real":{"h":"real","i":"/ˈriːəl/","a":"en-us-real.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A thing that is true is real.","e":"Strange as the story sounded, the story was real."},{"m":"Something that is not artificial is real.","e":"The nice shoes were of real leather."}]}]},"evening":{"h":"evening","i":"/ˈiːvnɪŋ/","a":"en-us-evening (noun).ogg","l":"even","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Period from dusk to midnight."}]}]},"standard":{"h":"standard","i":"/ˈstændɚd/","a":"en-us-standard.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is standard, it is typical or usual.","e":"The store sells standard American food."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A standard is a quality that is the minimum or usual.","e":"percent correct is the standard for an A at our school."},{"m":"A standard is a military or ceremonial flag carried on a pole or hoisted on a rope."}]}]},"charge":{"h":"charge","i":"/ˈʧɑrʤ/","a":"en-us-charge.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you charge someone money, you ask them to pay the money for something that you have done for them or sold to them.","e":"We charge ten cents a page for copying."},{"m":"(transitive) When the police charge someone with a crime, they officially say that the person did something illegal.","e":"A short time later, police arrested the man and charged him with murder."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you charge that something is wrong, you say it is.","e":"Many critics charge that our schools are not doing a good job."},{"m":"(transitive) When you charge something at a store, you put it on credit.","e":"The business man charged all of his meals to his company."},{"m":"When you charge at a thing, you run toward it.","e":"The bull charged the man walking in the field."},{"m":"When you charge (up) a battery, or when you charge (up) something that has a battery, you put electrical energy into it to be stored.","e":"Oh no! I forgot to charge up the camera and the batteries are dead."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A charge is a claim the somebody has done something wrong or illegal, especially a claim by police.","e":"He says charges against his son are false."},{"m":"(countable) A charge for something is the price of the thing. It often it is for a service or fee for a period of time.","e":"The charge for having an item shipped according to the weight."},{"m":"(countable) If someone is in charge of something, they are responsible for it.","e":"Josh is in charge of buying drinks for the party."},{"m":"(countable) If someone leads the charge, they are working hard to make some kind of change.","e":"Amazon.com led the charge in making electronic books popular."},{"m":"(countable) Your charge is the person that you are responsible for, often a child.","e":"The teacher smiled at his young charges."},{"m":"(countable) A charge is a movement towards somebody to attack them.","e":"Moriarity then led the charge that pushed Bishop out the door into a hallway."},{"m":"(countable) A charge is the amount of electrical energy that something holds.","e":"And once you've used up the electric charge, your electric car stops working."},{"m":"(countable) A charge is the explosive in a gun or a bomb.","e":"When the charge exploded, there was a large hole in the wall."}]}]},"suit":{"h":"suit","i":"/s(j)uːt/","a":"en-uk-suit.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A suit is a set of clothes that includes a coat or and pants or dress.","e":"Everyone wears a suit where I work."},{"m":"(countable) A suit is a case in a court of law which concerns a dispute between two people or organizations.","e":"The law suit was for one million dollars."},{"m":"A suit is a set in a pack of cards, such as the spades, hearts, diamonds or clubs."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something suits you it fits you; that is, it is right for you or good for you.","e":"I love my new job, it suits me fine."}]}]},"electricity":{"h":"electricity","i":"/ˌiː.lekˈtrɪs.ɪ.ti/","a":"en-us-electricity.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Electricity is a form of energy that is used to power buildings, lights, and electrical items.","e":"You need electricity to turn on the light bulbs."}]}]},"local":{"h":"local","i":"/ˈləʊkl/","a":"en-us-local.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something is local if it comes from a specific place. It often it means a place near the person who is speaking.","e":"We do not like fruit grown in other countries. We like to eat local fruit."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A person is local if the person comes from a specific place.","e":"They did not trust people from other places. They only trust locals."}]}]},"exist":{"h":"exist","i":"/ɪɡˈzɪst/","a":"en-us-exist.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If something exists, it is real and has some kind of being.","e":"Dinosaurs used to exist."}]}]},"include":{"h":"include","i":"/ɪnˈkluːd/","a":"en-us-include.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you include something, you make it part of something else.","e":"The store always includes the tax in their price."},{"m":"(transitive) When something has another thing as part of it, it includes the other.","e":"The price of the hotel room includes a free breakfast."}]}]},"never":{"h":"never","i":"/ˈnɛvə/","a":"en-uk-never.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something never happens, it does not happen at any time.","e":"As a child I was told that I should never tell a lie."}]}]},"always":{"h":"always","i":"/ˈɔːl.weɪz/","a":"en-us-always.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something always happens, it happens at all times or every time.","e":"For all of my life, the sun has always risen every day."},{"m":"If something will always happen, it will happen forever.","e":"Shannon will never stop loving you. She will always love you."}]}]},"course":{"h":"course","i":"/kɔː(r)s/","a":"en-us-course.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) In school, a course is a class in a specific subject.","e":"The science course was very difficult."},{"m":"(countable) A course is the path that something follows in space or in time.","e":"During the course of the evening, things went from bad to worse."},{"m":"(countable) For a meal, a course is one part of a meal such as dessert.","e":"We usually do not eat a meal with nine courses."},{"m":"(countable) Some games are played on a course.","e":"The game of golf is played on a golf course."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something courses, it runs or flows through something.","e":"Blood courses through the veins and arteries in our bodies."}]}]},"follow":{"h":"follow","i":"/ˈfɒləʊ/","a":"en-us-follow.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If the first thing occurs after the second, thing the first thing follows a second thing.","e":"Every year summer always follows spring."},{"m":"If a first thing goes behind a second thing, the first thing follows the second.","e":"A dog that is trained well should always follow its owner."}]}]},"develop":{"h":"develop","i":"/dɪˈvɛ.ləp/","a":"en-us-develop.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you develop something, you create or make it better.","e":"The people who are best at anything have to develop their ability over time."},{"m":"(intransitive) When plants and animals grow, they develop.","e":"As children grow their minds and bodies develop."}]}]},"compliance":{"h":"compliance","i":"/kəmˈplaɪəns/","a":"en-us-compliance.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Being able to agree with someone","e":"The king was impressed by the knight's dutiful compliance."}]}]},"underneath":{"h":"underneath","i":"/ʌndəˈniθ/","a":"en-uk-underneath.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If x is underneath y, x is right under, below, or covered by y.","e":"The cat was hiding underneath the car."}]}]},"aboard":{"h":"aboard","a":"en-us-aboard.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"on or onto a boat, airplane, train, etc.","e":"When everyone is aboard, the doors will close."}]}]},"abreast":{"h":"abreast","i":"/əˈbrɛst/","a":"en-us-abreast.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If you keep or stay abreast of something, you regularly read or study the most recent information about it.","e":"Have you been keeping abreast of the news from Iraq?"},{"m":"If two things are abreast, they are side by side.","e":"They walked in a long line, three abreast."}]}]},"adrift":{"h":"adrift","i":"/əˈdrɪft/","a":"en-us-adrift.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If something is adrift, it is floating with no control of its direction.","e":"The boat was adrift for three days before it was found with nobody aboard."}]}]},"aground":{"h":"aground","i":"/əˈɡraʊnd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-aground.wav","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If a boat runs or goes aground, its bottom goes onto the ground and it is not floating freely anymore.","e":"The boat ran aground off the coast of Florida and had to be helped to shore."}]}]},"forehead":{"h":"forehead","i":"/ˈfɒrɪd/","a":"en-us-forehead.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The forehead is the part of a human face between the hair and the eyebrows.","e":"Kip brushed his hair off his forehead."}]}]},"allowing":{"h":"allowing","i":"/əˈlaʊɪŋ/","a":"en-us-allowing.ogg","l":"allow","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"You use allowing for something, to show that you have thought about that thing in making your decision or getting your answer.","e":"Even allowing for inflation, $3.7 million is too big a change."}]}]},"aloft":{"h":"aloft","i":"/əˈlɔft/","a":"en-us-aloft.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"up in the air; flying","e":"He walked into the dark room, holding his light aloft."}]}]},"apropos":{"h":"apropos","i":"/ˌæp.rəˈpo/","a":"en-us-apropos.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"related to (a topic)","e":"\"My toe is cold,\" he said, apropos of nothing at all."}]}]},"ashore":{"h":"ashore","i":"/əˈʃɔr/","a":"en-us-ashore.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"on or onto the shore","e":"He came ashore after five weeks at sea."}]}]},"onshore":{"h":"onshore","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"on or onto the shore","e":"He came onshore after five weeks at sea."}]}]},"carcinogen":{"h":"carcinogen","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A carcinogen is a substance or agent that can cause cancer."}]}]},"betwixt":{"h":"betwixt","i":"/bɪˈtwɪkst/","a":"en-us-betwixt.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"(old fashioned) between"}]}]},"circa":{"h":"circa","i":"/ˈsɜːkə/","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"on or around a particular date","e":"The city was built circa 1200 BCE."}]}]},"gadget":{"h":"gadget","i":"/ɡædʒɪt/","a":"en-us-gadget.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Gadget is a name you can call a device or machine when you cannot remember its real name; especially","e":"He bought a new gadget for cutting fruits and vegetables."}]}]},"downhill":{"h":"downhill","i":"/ˌdaʊnˈhɪl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-downhill.wav","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"From higher ground to lower ground","e":"The bus rolled slowly downhill."}]}]},"cracker":{"h":"cracker","i":"/ˈkrækə(r)/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A dry, thin, crispy, and usually salty or savory biscuit.","e":"These crackers taste good with cheese."},{"m":"A person or thing that cracks things (for example, a whip cracker or a nutcracker)."},{"m":"Cracker is an insulting word for a poor white person living in the southern US."}]}]},"uphill":{"h":"uphill","i":"/ˌʌpˈhɪl/","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"From lower ground to higher ground","e":"She got tired walking uphill."}]}]},"afoot":{"h":"afoot","i":"/ʌˈfʊt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-afoot.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"(never before the noun) being planned or happening.","e":"Plans are afoot for new houses to be built."}]}]},"piss":{"h":"piss","i":"/pɪs/","a":"en-uk-piss.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Piss is a word for urine, the waste liquid from the body of humans and animals that is often a yellowish color.","e":"The neighbor's new dog won't stop getting my car wet with its piss."},{"m":"(uncountable) Piss is a word for bad alcoholic drinks.","e":"I couldn't buy any good beer, so I have to drink this piss."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If a person or animal pisses, it passes waste liquid from its body.","e":"He always pisses so loudly you can hear it from outside the bathroom door."}]}]},"famine":{"h":"famine","i":"/ˈfæmɪn/","a":"en-us-famine.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) If a place is affected by famine, there is not enough food for everyone.","e":"Over a million people died during the 1984 famine in Ethiopia."}]}]},"downstream":{"h":"downstream","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If x is downstream from y, x and y are on or beside a river and the water moves from y to x.","e":"London is downstream from Oxford on the River Thames."}]}]},"networks":{"h":"networks","l":"network","q":"noun"},"networked":{"h":"networked","l":"network","q":"verb"},"networking":{"h":"networking","a":"En-us-networking.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The act of using a computer network."},{"m":"(uncountable) The act of connecting computers into a network."},{"m":"(uncountable) The act of meeting new people in a business setting."}]}]},"conversations":{"h":"conversations","l":"conversation","q":"noun"},"meanings":{"h":"meanings","l":"meaning","q":"noun"},"meant":{"h":"meant","i":"/'mɛnt/","a":"en-us-meant.ogg","l":"mean","q":"verb"},"downwind":{"h":"downwind","i":"/ˌdaʊnˈwɪnd/","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If x is downwind of y, the air is moving from y to x.","e":"Our house was downwind of the factory and the smell was terrible."}]}]},"upwind":{"h":"upwind","i":"/ʌpˈwɪnd/","a":"en-us-upwind.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If x is upwind of y, the air is moving from x to y.","e":"I'd drop the boat slightly upwind of him so it would blow downwind to him."}]}]},"excepting":{"h":"excepting","a":"en-us-excepting.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"but not; with the exception of something.","e":"Excepting yesterday, she worked ever day this week."}]}]},"upstream":{"h":"upstream","i":"/ʌpˈstriːm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-upstream.wav","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If x is upstream from y, x and y are on or beside a river and the water moves from x to y.","e":"Oxford is upstream from London on the River Thames."}]}]},"exclusive":{"h":"exclusive","i":"/ɪkˈsklu.sɪv/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-exclusive.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a group is exclusive, it excludes people or things that do not meet certain standards, criteria or conditions."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Not including.","e":"The rent is $800 per month, exclusive of sales tax."}]}]},"failing":{"h":"failing","i":"/ˈfeɪ.lɪŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Persent101-failing.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A failing is a weakness or problem in somebody's character or personality.","e":"We hired him despite his failings."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If something doesn't happen or isn't true.","e":"We should be able to go on Monday, and failing that, certain on Tuesday."}]}]},"henceforth":{"h":"henceforth","i":"/hɛnsˈfɔrθ/","a":"en-us-henceforth.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"(formal) from this time or point forward","e":"Since we are no longer together, her troubles will, henceforth, not bother me."}]}]},"favor":{"h":"favor","i":"/ˈfeɪvɚ/","a":"en-us-favor.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Some help.","e":"Can you please do me a favor by washing the dishes?"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you favor someone, you like them and prefer them over other people."}]}]},"thence":{"h":"thence","i":"/ðɛns/","a":"en-us-thence.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"from that place or from there","e":"We went to Tokyo and thence to Kyoto."}]}]},"whence":{"h":"whence","i":"/ʍɛns/","a":"en-us-whence.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"from where","e":"Whence did you come?"}]}]},"wherever":{"h":"wherever","i":"/(h)wɛrˈɛvɚ/","a":"en-us-wherever.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"A place.","e":"I go wherever I want to go."},{"m":"Any place.","e":"Wherever you go, I'll be there."},{"m":"Used to show surprise in a question.","e":"Wherever have you been?"}]}]},"whereupon":{"h":"whereupon","i":"/ˌ(h)wɛrəˈpɑn/","a":"en-us-whereupon.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"(relative) immediately after which","e":"She saw him, whereupon she began running."}]}]},"wherein":{"h":"wherein","i":"/(h)wɛrˈɪn/","a":"en-us-wherein.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"(relative) in which place","e":"She picked up the book wherein the paper was folded."}]}]},"whereabouts":{"h":"whereabouts","i":"/ˈʍɛərəˌbaʊts/","a":"en-us-whereabouts.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Used to ask in what general place somebody or something is.","e":"Whereabouts do you come from in Korea?"}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The general location where somebody or something is.","e":"The police are looking for him but say his whereabouts are unknown."}]}]},"atop":{"h":"atop","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If x is atop y, x is on the highest part of y.","e":"He stood atop the mountain and looked all around."}]}]},"irrespective":{"h":"irrespective","i":"/ɪrɪˈspɛktɪv/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-irrespective.wav","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If x is true irrespective of y, y doesn't matter to or change x.","e":"Everyone on the team was sick, but they managed to win irrespective."}]}]},"overboard":{"h":"overboard","i":"/ˈəʊvə(r)ˌbɔː(r)d/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-overboard.wav","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If someone or something goes overboard, it goes over the side of a boat.","e":"When they threw the cut fish overboard, the sharks attacked."}]}]},"overland":{"h":"overland","a":"en-au-overland.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"by land, not air or sea","e":"The mail traveling overland to the small towns could take weeks."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"by land, not air or sea","e":"The overland route was much slower than going by sea."}]}]},"eastward":{"h":"eastward","i":"/ˈistwɚd/","a":"en-us-eastward.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"moving or facing east"}]}]},"eastwards":{"h":"eastwards","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"moving or facing east."}]}]},"heavenward":{"h":"heavenward","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"To move heavenward is to move in the direction of heaven."}]}]},"heavenwards":{"h":"heavenwards","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"moving or facing heaven."}]}]},"homeward":{"h":"homeward","i":"/ˈhoʊmwɚd/","a":"en-us-homeward.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Moving in the direction of or facing home"}]}]},"inward":{"h":"inward","i":"/ˈɪnwəd/","a":"en-us-inward.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"moving in the direction of or facing in"}]}]},"inwards":{"h":"inwards","i":"/ˈɪnwɚdz/","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"moving in the direction of or facing in."}]}]},"leftward":{"h":"leftward","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"moving or facing left."}]}]},"leftwards":{"h":"leftwards","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"moving or facing left."}]}]},"northward":{"h":"northward","i":"/ˈnɔrθwɚd/","a":"en-us-northward.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Moving or facing north."}]}]},"northwards":{"h":"northwards","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"moving or facing north."}]}]},"onward":{"h":"onward","i":"/ˈɒnwəd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-onward.wav","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"moving or facing forward."}]}]},"onwards":{"h":"onwards","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Moving or facing forward.","e":"The explorers moved onwards, ever deeper into the jungle."}]}]},"outward":{"h":"outward","i":"/ˈaʊt.wɚd/","a":"en-us-outward.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"moving or facing out"}]}]},"outwards":{"h":"outwards","i":"/ˈaʊtwɚdz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-outwards.wav","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"moving or facing out."}]}]},"rightward":{"h":"rightward","i":"/ˈraɪtwɚd/","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"moving or facing right."}]}]},"rightwards":{"h":"rightwards","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"moving or facing right."}]}]},"seaward":{"h":"seaward","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"moving in the direction of or facing the sea","e":"The is moving seaward."}]}]},"seawards":{"h":"seawards","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"moving or facing the sea"}]}]},"skyward":{"h":"skyward","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Moving in the direction of or facing the sky."}]}]},"skywards":{"h":"skywards","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Moving or facing the sky."}]}]},"southward":{"h":"southward","i":"/ˈsaʊθwəd/","a":"en-us-southward.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Moving or facing south; towards the south."}]}]},"southwards":{"h":"southwards","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-southwards.wav","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"moving or facing south."}]}]},"westward":{"h":"westward","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Moving or facing west."}]}]},"westwards":{"h":"westwards","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"moving or facing west."}]}]},"shoreward":{"h":"shoreward","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"moving in the direction of or facing the shore","e":"John saw a ship heading shoreward, towards Liverpool."}]}]},"shorewards":{"h":"shorewards","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"moving or facing the shore"}]}]},"sunward":{"h":"sunward","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Sunward means moving in the direction of or facing the sun."}]}]},"sunwards":{"h":"sunwards","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"moving or facing the sun."}]}]},"ceilingward":{"h":"ceilingward","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"in the direction of or facing the ceiling."}]}]},"ceilingwards":{"h":"ceilingwards","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"moving or facing the ceiling."}]}]},"earthward":{"h":"earthward","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Moving in the direction of or facing the earth"}]}]},"earthwards":{"h":"earthwards","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"moving or facing the earth."}]}]},"goalward":{"h":"goalward","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Moving in the direction of or facing the goal; toward a goal."}]}]},"goalwards":{"h":"goalwards","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"moving or facing the goal."}]}]},"rearward":{"h":"rearward","i":"/ˈrir.wɝ d/","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"moving or facing back"}]}]},"rearwards":{"h":"rearwards","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"moving or facing the rear."}]}]},"sideward":{"h":"sideward","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"moving to or facing the side"}]}]},"sidewards":{"h":"sidewards","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"moving or facing towards a side."}]}]},"sideways":{"h":"sideways","i":"/ˈsaɪdweɪz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-sideways.wav","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"to, towards or from the side"}]}]},"landward":{"h":"landward","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If you are moving landwards, you are moving in the direction of or facing the land."}]}]},"landwards":{"h":"landwards","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"moving or facing the land"}]}]},"windward":{"h":"windward","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Moving or facing into the wind; where the wind is coming from."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Being in the wind.","e":"The waves were crashing on the windward side of the island."}]}]},"leeward":{"h":"leeward","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"moving or facing the way the wind is moving"}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"being away from the wind","e":"All was quiet on the leeward side of the island."}]}]},"plume":{"h":"plume","i":"/ˈpljuːm/","a":"en-us-plume.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A large feather of a bird."},{"m":"Feathers worn as decoration."},{"m":"material from the 's mantle coming upward."},{"m":"A spray of water or mist.","e":"A plume of water shot up from the broken fire hydrant"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Decorate with plumes.","e":"She wore a plumed hat to the Founders Day Ball."}]}]},"pertaining":{"h":"pertaining","a":"en-us-pertaining.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"about; related to","e":"Pertaining to the suggestions, there is a some advantage in this new approach."}]}]},"preparatory":{"h":"preparatory","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Preparatory work, meetings, etc. are related to getting ready for something.","e":"Most of the preparatory work had been done, but the building had not actually started."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"(formal) If x is preparatory to y, x happens before y to get ready for y.","e":"They began gathering equipment preparatory to climbing the mountain."}]}]},"pursuant":{"h":"pursuant","i":"/pəˈsjuː.ənt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-pursuant.wav","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"(formal) according to; following","e":"Pursuant to the promises made to Parliament, an investigation was begun."}]}]},"tells":{"h":"tells","a":"en-us-tells.ogg","l":"tell","q":"verb"},"telling":{"h":"telling","a":"en-us-telling.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is telling, it has a strong effect."},{"m":"If some kind of evidence is telling, it shows clearly the true nature of someone or something."}]}]},"innovations":{"h":"innovations","l":"innovation","q":"noun"},"wounds":{"h":"wounds","i":"/wuːndz/","a":"en-us-wounds.ogg","l":"wound","q":"noun"},"wounded":{"h":"wounded","a":"en-us-wounded.ogg","l":"wound","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(usually with \"the\") People who are injured or have wounds."}]}]},"wounding":{"h":"wounding","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The act of making a wound."}]}]},"woundings":{"h":"woundings","l":"wounding","q":"noun"},"dick":{"h":"dick","i":"/dɪk/","a":"en-us-dick.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A dick is a detective."},{"m":"(countable) A dick is a penis.","e":"The ladies love his big dick."},{"m":"(countable) A dick is a bad or mean person.","e":"That guy is such a dick; he wasn't looking where he was going and he hit my car!"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you dick somebody, you mistreat or take advantage of them."},{"m":"If you dick around, you waste time.","e":"Stop dicking around and get back to work!"}]}]},"dicks":{"h":"dicks","i":"/dɪks/","l":"dick","q":"noun"},"bench":{"h":"bench","i":"/bɛnʧ/","a":"en-us-bench.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bench is a long, hard seat for more than one person."},{"m":"(countable) The bench is the place where players of a sport sit when they are not playing.","e":"He watched the first 3 games from the bench."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If a coach benches a player, they take the player out of a game.","e":"They benched him for the rest of the game because they thought he was hurt."},{"m":"(transitive) If you bench a weight, you lift it over your chest, lying on your back, on a bench.","e":"I heard he can bench 150 pounds."}]}]},"saving":{"h":"saving","i":"/ˈseɪv.ɪŋ/","a":"en-us-saving.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"All the money that you have is your savings.","e":"She had lost all her savings when the company went out of business."},{"m":"(countable) The saving is the difference between the amount you were going to use or spend and the amount you actually did.","e":"The fuel savings in moving to a new car can be huge."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"except","e":"After the fire, nothing was left saving the clothes I was wearing."}]}]},"chez":{"h":"chez","i":"/ʃe/","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"At the home of.","e":"The painting remains chez Catherine and Stephane De Beyrie."}]}]},"contra":{"h":"contra","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"against; in opposition or contrast to","e":"Consider the problems of the nurse contra those of the doctor."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A contra was a member of a particular guerrilla group in Nicaragua."}]}]},"modulo":{"h":"modulo","i":"/ˈmɒdjʊləʊ/","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Given a specified modulus of.","e":"21 and 84 are congruent to each other modulo 9, since both numbers leave the same remainder, 3, when divided by 9."}]}]},"pace":{"h":"pace","i":"/peɪs/","a":"en-us-pace.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (usually singular) The pace of something is how fast it moves.","e":"The pace of change has been very, very slow."},{"m":"(countable) (usually singular) Somebody's pace is their speed, usually walking.","e":"He quickened his pace, almost running."},{"m":"(countable) A pace is the distance between your feet when you walk.","e":"She stopped three paces from the table."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Walk back and forth in a small space.","e":"Groups of men, in all imaginable attitudes, were lying, standing, sitting, or pacing up and down."},{"m":"Set the speed in a race."},{"m":"Measure by walking."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Contrary to the opinion of; Used to express polite disagreement","e":"Nor, pace Bush, must all countries be with America or against it."}]}]},"re":{"h":"re","i":"/reɪ/","a":"en-us-re.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"regarding; about","e":"In your earlier e-mail re our problems, you made some suggestions."}]}]},"sans":{"h":"sans","i":"/sænz/","a":"En-us-sans.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If you say that X is sans Y, it does not have Y, it is without Y.","e":"It's often difficult for movie stars to have lunch sans photographers."}]}]},"qua":{"h":"qua","i":"/kwɑː/","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"as; in the role of","e":"A scientist may believe certain things qua practical man, but not qua scientist."}]}]},"underfoot":{"h":"underfoot","i":"/ʌndɚˈfʊt/","a":"en-us-underfoot.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"under your feet; on the ground","e":"The snow underfoot crunched as we walked."}]}]},"unbeknown":{"h":"unbeknown","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If something is unbeknown to somebody, they don't know about it.","e":"Unbeknown to his wife, he had bought a new car."}]}]},"unbeknownst":{"h":"unbeknownst","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If something is unbeknownst to somebody, they don't know about it.","e":"Unbeknownst to his wife, he had bought a new car."}]}]},"vs":{"h":"vs","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"A short way of saying versus.","e":"The first wrestling match is Jones vs Smith."}]}]},"afloat":{"h":"afloat","i":"/əˈfloʊt/","a":"en-us-afloat.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If something is afloat, it is on the water; floating.","e":"Although he couldn't swim, the life jacket kept him afloat."}]}]},"nor":{"h":"nor","i":"/nɔː/","a":"en-us-nor.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Nor is used to show that a something that is not true in one case is also not true in another case.","e":"I don't belong here, and nor do you."}]}]},"came":{"h":"came","i":"/'keɪm/","a":"en-us-came.ogg","l":"come","q":"verb"},"said":{"h":"said","i":"/sɛd/","a":"en-us-said.ogg","l":"say","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"(formal) The said person or thing is the one that was mentioned before.","e":"A gun was found at the scene. The said gun belonged to this man."}]},{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(formal) Said person or thing is the one that was mentioned before.","e":"A gun was found at the scene. Said gun belonged to this man."}]}]},"made":{"h":"made","i":"/meɪd/","a":"en-us-made.ogg","l":"make","q":"verb"},"used":{"h":"used","i":"/juːzd/","a":"en-us-used.ogg","l":"use","q":"verb"},"years":{"h":"years","i":"/ji.ə(r)z/","a":"en-us-years.ogg","l":"year","q":"noun"},"pilot":{"h":"pilot","i":"/ˈpaɪlət/","a":"en-us-pilot.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pilot is a person who flies and controls an airplane.","e":"I hope the pilot does not crash the plane."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you pilot an airplane, you fly and control it.","e":"I hired a girl to pilot my new airplane."}]}]},"gasoline":{"h":"gasoline","i":"/ˈɡæs.ə.lin/","a":"en-us-gasoline.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Gasoline is also known as fuel for vehicles.","e":"My car is nearly empty of gasoline. I should refuel it at a gas station soon."}]}]},"virgin":{"h":"virgin","i":"/ˈvɝdʒɪn/","a":"en-us-virgin.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A virgin is someone who has not had sex before."}]}]},"quid":{"h":"quid","i":"/kwɪd/","a":"en-au-quid.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A quid is one pound in British money (£1)."}]}]},"already":{"h":"already","i":"/ɔːlˈrɛdi/","a":"en-us-already.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"before a certain time (often now)","e":"When we met, his first wife was already dead."}]}]},"apply":{"h":"apply","i":"/əˈplaɪ/","a":"en-us-apply.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If a rule, a principle, a law, etc. applies, it has some effect on the situation.","e":"The new anti-smoking law applies only to public buildings."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you apply for something, you formally say that you want it or you want to do it.","e":"After high school, he applied to three universities and was accepted by all of them."},{"m":"(transitive) If you apply something such as an idea, rule, formula, or piece of information, etc., you use it to do something, work with something, or handle a situation.","e":"I found it hard to apply the principles I learned at school to the problems I faced at work."},{"m":"(transitive) If you apply yourself, you focus on something and work hard at it.","e":"He's really smart, but he just has a hard time applying himself to his school work."},{"m":"(transitive) If you apply x to y, you put or spread x on y.","e":"It's dangerous to apply makeup while driving a car."},{"m":"(transitive) If you apply something, you turn it on, usually by pushing something.","e":"Apply the brakes gently to stop the car without sliding."},{"m":"(intransitive) If a word applies, it is used to mean a particular thing.","e":"The word resident applies to anyone living there."}]}]},"appoint":{"h":"appoint","i":"/ʌˈpɔɪnt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-appoint.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you appoint someone to a job or position, you give the job to them.","e":"The president appointed her to investigate the problems."},{"m":"(transitive) If you appoint a time for something, you choose that time.","e":"They met at the appointed time."}]}]},"clothed":{"h":"clothed","i":"/ˈkləʊðd/","a":"en-us-clothed.ogg","l":"clothe","q":"verb"},"bet":{"h":"bet","i":"/ˈbεt/","a":"en-us-bet.ogg","l":"bet","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you bet, you take a chance with money or something else on the result of a future event.","e":"I bet five dollars that I would win the game."},{"m":"If you bet something is true, you strongly believe it.","e":"I bet you left it on the table."},{"m":"You used \"you bet\" to show you agree with somebody.","e":"\"Could you help me here?\" \"You bet! What do you need?\""}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bet is the thing of value or amount of money that you bet.","e":"Jim had a bet of twenty dollars that he would complete the test on time."},{"m":"(countable) A good bet is something you should believe, or try.","e":"\"Where can I get that book?\" \"I think the school library is your best bet.\""}]}]},"associate":{"h":"associate","i":"/əˈsəʊʃieɪt/","a":"en-us-associate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you associate two things, you think of them as being connected in some way.","e":"People often associate Einstein with science, but he was also a man of peace."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you associate with someone else, you spend time with them.","e":"Parents are often afraid of their children associating with the wrong group of friends."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An associate is somebody that you do business or work with.","e":"I have an associate who might be interested in your product."},{"m":"An associate member, professor, producer, etc. is one who is connected but at a lower level.","e":"She spent years as an associate professor before becoming a full professor in 1997."}]}]},"basis":{"h":"basis","i":"/ˈbeɪsɪs/","a":"en-us-basis.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The basis of something, is the main ideas or parts that it is built on.","e":"On the basis of the information available, we have decided to cancel the project."},{"m":"(countable) If something happens on a regular/daily/weekly etc. basis, it happens regularly, daily, etc.","e":"The problems are now happening on a very regular basis."},{"m":"If we are on a first-name basis, we use first names when speaking to each other.","e":"Josie Parkinson and I are on a first-name basis. I call her \"Josie\" when I see her."}]}]},"matoke":{"h":"matoke","i":"/maˈtəʊkeɪ/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Matoke is a meal of steamed green plantain and is one of the national dishes of Uganda."}]}]},"bloke":{"h":"bloke","i":"/bləʊk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-bloke.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bloke is a boy or a man.","e":"So, I walk in and there's this woman talking to this bloke."}]}]},"chap":{"h":"chap","i":"/tʃæp/","a":"en-us-chap.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A chap is a boy or a man.","e":"Hello, old chap, did you just arrive?"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something such as your lips chap, they become dry and cracked.","e":"His lips chapped in the cold."}]}]},"christ":{"h":"Christ","i":"/kraɪst/","a":"en-us-Christ.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"In the Christian and Jewish religions, the Christ is the person that God sends to save all humans.","e":"Accept Christ into your heart, for he is the son of God."}]},{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"Many people use Christ when they are surprised or not happy about something. Some people do not like to use this phrase, as they think this is blasphemy (an insult to God).","e":"Christ, that's heavy."}]}]},"accessible":{"h":"accessible","i":"/əkˈsɛsəbˑl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-accessible.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is accessible, you can use it, look at it, enter it, etc.","e":"The building has been changed to make it wheelchair accessible."},{"m":"If someone is accessible, they are friendly and easy to talk to."}]}]},"acquire":{"h":"acquire","i":"/əˈkwaɪər/","a":"en-us-acquire.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(formal) If you acquire something, you buy or get it.","e":"XYZ company has acquired a new factory in Shanghai."}]}]},"chairman":{"h":"chairman","i":"/ˈtʃɛːmən/","a":"en-us-chairman.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A chairman is the person who controls a meeting or an organization.","e":"Alan Eastwood is the former chairman of the Police Federation."}]}]},"chairperson":{"h":"chairperson","i":"/ˈtʃɛːpəːs(ə)n/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-chairperson.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A chairperson is the person who controls a meeting or an organization.","e":"Alan Eastwood is the former chairperson of the Police Federation."}]}]},"phylum":{"h":"phylum","i":"/ˈfaɪləm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-phylum.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Is the basic taxon higher in the rank. In botany phyllum corresponds to division (divisio)"},{"m":"The major taxonomic group.","e":"Arthopoda is the phylum of spiders."}]}]},"organize":{"h":"organize","i":"/ˈɔrɡənaɪz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-organize.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you organize something, you plan or arrange it.","e":"The student organized his class notes."},{"m":"(intransitive) When you organize, you bring together many people for a united action.","e":"The dads organized to help their children in school."}]}]},"organise":{"h":"organise","i":"/ˈɔrɡənaɪz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-organize.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you organise something, you plan or arrange it.","e":"The student organised his class notes."},{"m":"(intransitive) When you organise, you bring together many people for a united action.","e":"The dads organised to help their children in school."}]}]},"connect":{"h":"connect","i":"/kəˈnɛkt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-connect.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you connect things, you join, link or unite them.","e":"The man connected device to the battery with a wire."}]}]},"deal":{"h":"deal","i":"/diːl/","a":"en-us-deal.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A deal is a business agreement.","e":"The company made a deal with the agents."},{"m":"(countable) (informal) A deal is a situation.","e":"OK, so here's the deal."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you deal with something, such as a problem, you solve it."},{"m":"(transitive) When you deal something, you sell or give or hand it out."},{"m":"The exporter deals in food for export to other nations."}]}]},"dealt":{"h":"dealt","i":"/'dεlt/","a":"en-us-dealt.ogg","l":"deal","q":"verb"},"continue":{"h":"continue","i":"/kənˈtɪnjuː/","a":"en-us-continue.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something continues, it does not stop.","e":"Even though he has died, we will continue the good work he did helping children."}]}]},"college":{"h":"college","i":"/ˈkɒlɪd͡ʒ/","a":"en-uk-college.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A college is a school for adults who have finished high school.","e":"I graduated from college in 1992 when I was 22 years old."},{"m":"(countable) A college is one part of a university.","e":"I went to the college of medicine at the University of Wales."}]}]},"character":{"h":"character","i":"/ˈkærəktə/","a":"en-us-character.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable); (singular) Someone's character is the combination of things that they do, feel, and believe that makes them a certain type of person.","e":"He's got a really funny character."},{"m":"(countable) A character is a person in a story, movie, play, etc.","e":"The actor played three different characters in the movie."},{"m":"(uncountable) Character is the combination of facts and qualities that makes something different","e":"The new factory has certainly changed the character of the city."},{"m":"(countable) A character is one individual mark in a writing system, such as a letter, number, or punctuation mark.","e":"The text was written in a mixture of Chinese characters, Arabic numerals and Roman letters."},{"m":"(uncountable) Character is the combination of personal qualities, such as being honest and hard-working, that make you a good person.","e":"It has long been claimed that sports build character."}]}]},"relationship":{"h":"relationship","i":"/rɪˈleɪʃənˌʃɪp/","a":"en-us-relationship.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) When there is a relationship between things, there is a connection.","e":"There is a clear relationship between fire and heat."},{"m":"(countable) When people are connected by family, there is a relationship between them.","e":"There is a family relationship between Bob Smith and John Smith."},{"m":"(countable) When people are friends or partners, they have a relationship.","e":"John is the boyfriend of Joan. They have a relationship."}]}]},"basic":{"h":"basic","i":"/ˈbeɪsɪk/","a":"en-au-basic.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is basic, it is simple.","e":"Everyone in the army has to have basic training."},{"m":"When something is basic, it is fundamental or important.","e":"Water is a basic necessity of human life: you cannot live without it."},{"m":"Something that is basic has a pH level more than 7, and makes acidic solutions more neutral."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(usually plural) Basics are things that are essential.","e":"Beginners must first learn the basics before they become experts."}]}]},"educate":{"h":"educate","i":"/ˈɛdʒəkeɪt/","a":"en-us-educate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you educate someone, you instruct them; teach; train.","e":"He was educated in the public school system."}]}]},"choice":{"h":"choice","i":"/tʃɔɪs/","a":"en-us-choice.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"If you have a choice, you can decide between two or more things or actions.","e":"I don't want to go, but I'm afraid I don't have a choice."},{"m":"(countable) Your choice is the thing that you decide to take or do.","e":"His choice of jobs was a good one."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Choice food, drink, clothing, etc. is the best of its kind.","e":"He let his daughter pick out the choicest pieces of fruit."},{"m":"Choice words are very direct and critical.","e":"After the terrible evening, she had some choice words to share with him."}]}]},"draw":{"h":"draw","i":"/drɔː/","a":"en-us-draw.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you draw, you use a pencil, pen, crayon, etc. to make a picture.","e":"She drew a beautiful picture of the sky on a bright white piece of paper."},{"m":"If a person is attracted or interested in an event, then he is drawn to it.","e":"The discover of gold in the West drew many people living in the East to move westward."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"When a game is tied and no one has won, then the game is a draw.","e":"The game ended 3 to 3. We were disappointed that it was a draw."},{"m":"A draw is when the winners of a lottery are announced.","e":"The draw is on Tuesday. I hope I won."}]}]},"claim":{"h":"claim","i":"/kleɪm/","a":"en-us-claim.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you claim something, you say or write that it is true without proof.","e":"It is easy to claim that a god exists, but impossible to prove."},{"m":"(transitive) If you claim something, you say or write that it belongs to you and often you take it.","e":"Once you are over 65, there are a variety of government benefits that you can claim."},{"m":"(transitive) If something claims a life, it kills people.","e":"The disease has claimed seven people in Taipei so far this month."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A claim is something that you say or write without proof.","e":"It is difficult to believe claims that the world is ending."},{"m":"(countable) If you have a claim to something, you have the right, to own or do it.","e":"The government is disputing their claim to the land."},{"m":"(countable) A claim is something that you say you have the right to.","e":"They have begun looking for gold on their claim in Western Alberta."}]}]},"eighty-one":{"h":"eighty-one","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(ordinal eighty-first) Eighty-one (81) is the odd number that comes between eighty and eighty-two. It is a square number (9 multiplied by 9 equals 81).","e":"I have eighty-one coins in my collection."}]}]},"client":{"h":"client","i":"/ˈklʌɪənt/","a":"en-us-client.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Your client is a person or group that uses your services or buys your products.","e":"As lawyers, we advise our clients not to talk to the media."},{"m":"(countable) A client is a computer that accesses most central files through a server.","e":"All clients on the network will be updated with the newest OS over the weekend."}]}]},"plum":{"h":"plum","i":"/plʌm/","a":"en-us-plum.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A fruit that is often a dark red or purple color.","e":"I really like to eat plums."},{"m":"A dark blue-red color, the color of some plums."},{"m":"(countable) A raisin, when it is used in a pudding or a cake."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Of a dark blue-red color."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"; utterly.","e":"I've plum forgotten where I placed my book."}]}]},"plums":{"h":"plums","l":"plum","q":"noun"},"cartridge":{"h":"cartridge","i":"/ˈkɑːtrɪdʒ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-cartridge.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cartridge is a case or container that holds a substance or object which is difficult or awkward to handle; they can usually be changed easily."}]}]},"commit":{"h":"commit","i":"/kəˈmɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Mélange a trois-commit.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you commit something illegal or bad, you do it.","e":"We have committed no offense and ask to be freed at once."},{"m":"If you commit to something, you agree or say that you will do or participate in something.","e":"The president has committed the government to improving schools."},{"m":"(transitive) If you commit someone to a place or a process, you send them there, often against their will.","e":"He was committed to a mental hospital after he tried to kill himself."},{"m":"(transitive) If you commit words or idea to something, you record them there.","e":"He committed the whole speech to memory."}]}]},"dissolve":{"h":"dissolve","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To dissolve something is to break it into smaller pieces, often by putting it into a liquid.","e":"I like to dissolve my pills in water because I cannot swallow them whole."}]}]},"dissolves":{"h":"dissolves","a":"En-us-dissolves.ogg","l":"dissolve","q":"verb"},"dissolved":{"h":"dissolved","a":"en-us-dissolved.ogg","l":"dissolve","q":"verb"},"reunion":{"h":"reunion","i":"/riːˈjuːnjən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-reunion.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A reunion is the act of coming back together.","e":"It was a happy reunion when the trapped miners finally saw their family again."},{"m":"(countable) A reunion is a planned event where people gather or see each other after a long period of not seeing each other.","e":"Are you going to the family reunion this year?"}]}]},"reunions":{"h":"reunions","l":"reunion","q":"noun"},"dragon":{"h":"dragon","i":"/ˈdrægən/","a":"en-us-dragon.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(Western) A mythical animal, usually reptile-like, with leathery wings like a bat, claws like a lion, scaly skin and a long tail, and breathes fire.","e":"The prince had to kill a dragon before he could rescue the princess."},{"m":"(Eastern) A large snake-like creature with the eyes of a rabbit, the horns of an ox, and the claws of a tiger."},{"m":"A large reptile, especially a Komodo dragon."}]}]},"dragons":{"h":"dragons","l":"dragon","q":"noun"},"nirvana":{"h":"nirvana","i":"/nɪəˈvɑːnə/","a":"en-us-nirvana.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(Buddhism) When a person has reached nirvana, he no longer wants to have things."},{"m":"(Buddhism) When a person has reached nirvana, he is happy and at peace; enlightenment."},{"m":"When someone is at a nirvana, he is very happy and pleased; paradise."}]}]},"concern":{"h":"concern","i":"/kənˈsɝn/","a":"en-us-concern.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A concern about something means something that a person is worried about.","e":"The government expressed its concern at the fighting in Kenya."},{"m":"(uncountable) A concern with something means something that a person is interested in or involved with."},{"m":"(uncountable) Concern is a feeling that a person wants to help someone.","e":"Her look of concern made him feel better."},{"m":"(countable) A concern is a business.","e":"XYZ Company is an ongoing concern, and we have no plans to shut it down."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If x concerns y, x is about y.","e":"We have received a letter that concerns the recent sale of the property."},{"m":"(transitive) If something concerns a person, they think it is a problem or needs attention.","e":"The recent losses certainly concern me, but I still think things are looking good."},{"m":"You use to whom it may concern at the beginning of a letter when you don't know the name of the person you're writing to."}]}]},"paul":{"h":"Paul","i":"/pɔːl/","a":"en-us-Paul.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"(Bible) In the New Testament, Paul is the Apostle to the Gentiles and the author of fourteen epistles."}]}]},"rabies":{"h":"rabies","i":"/ˈrei.biz/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Rabies is a deadly disease caused by a virus from mammals."}]}]},"confer":{"h":"confer","i":"/kənˈfʌr/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Mélange a trois-confer.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If two or more people confer, they find out each other's opinion.","e":"The referees conferred before awarding the goal to Chelsea."},{"m":"(transitive) If something is conferred on somebody, it is given to them, often officially.","e":"That contract confers power on the directors of the company to manage the company."}]}]},"albino":{"h":"albino","i":"/ælˈbiːnəʊ/","a":"en-us-albino.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A person or animal born with albinism."}]}]},"pissed":{"h":"pissed","i":"/pɪst/","a":"en-au-pissed.ogg","l":"piss","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"(UK, AU) drunk."},{"m":"(US, CA) annoyed, angry.","e":"I am so pissed about something."}]}]},"rollercoaster":{"h":"rollercoaster","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An amusement ride that has a cart on a track; it rises and falls and has twists and turns."},{"m":"Any situation in which there are large, quick changes."}]}]},"rollercoasters":{"h":"rollercoasters","l":"rollercoaster","q":"noun"},"founders":{"h":"founders","l":"founder","q":"noun"},"founder":{"h":"founder","i":"/ˈfaʊndɚ/","a":"en-us-founder.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A person who founds and establishes; a person who lays a foundation; an author; a person who starts something."},{"m":"(countable) An iron worker who runs a blast furnace and the smelting process."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To fill something with water and sink it."},{"m":"To fall or stumble."},{"m":"To fail; to miscarry."}]}]},"complaint":{"h":"complaint","i":"/kʌmˈpleɪnt/","a":"en-us-complaint.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A complaint is an expression of dissatisfaction"},{"m":"(countable) A complaint is a small medical problem.","e":"He had a skin complaint and so went to the doctor for advice."}]}]},"consult":{"h":"consult","i":"/ˈkɒnsʌlt/","a":"en-us-consult-noun.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":": A visit or a consultation.","e":"I have a consult with a sleep specialist this afternoon."},{"m":": The act of consulting or the results of that consultation;.","e":"The council broke; And all grave consults dissolved in smoke. -Dryden."},{"m":": A council; a meeting for consultation.","e":"A consult of coquettes. -Swift."},{"m":": Agreement; concert."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you consult with someone, you ask them their opinion or for advice.","e":"I think it would be a good idea to consult a doctor about the pain."},{"m":"(transitive) If you consult a dictionary, the web, a phone book, etc., you look there for information."}]}]},"extinct":{"h":"extinct","i":"/ɪkˈstɪŋkt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-extinct.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When all of one kind of animal are dead it is extinct.","e":"s are extinct. No living dinosaurs can be found on Earth."},{"m":"No longer active","e":"This extinct volcano has not erupted for hundreds of years."}]}]},"massive":{"h":"massive","i":"/ˈmæs.ɪv/","a":"en-us-massive.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Very big; large; too big.","e":"Most dinosaurs were massive animals."}]}]},"anger":{"h":"anger","i":"/ˈæŋ.ɚ/","a":"en-us-anger.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A strong feeling of displeasure, hostility or antagonism towards someone or something, usually combined with an urge to harm."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you anger someone you make them feel angry.","e":"It really angers me when you don't clean up your messes."}]}]},"angers":{"h":"angers","l":"anger","q":"verb"},"angered":{"h":"angered","l":"anger","q":"verb"},"burns":{"h":"burns","l":"burn","q":"verb"},"burned":{"h":"burned","i":"/'bʌ:(r)nd/","a":"en-us-burned.ogg","l":"burn","q":"verb"},"burning":{"h":"burning","i":"/ˈbɝnɪŋ/","a":"en-us-burning.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"So hot as to seem to burn (something).","e":"the burning sun"},{"m":"Feeling very hot.","e":"burning skin"},{"m":"Feeling great passion.","e":"her burning heart"}]}]},"amplitude":{"h":"amplitude","i":"/ˈæm.plɪ.tud/","a":"en-us-amplitude.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The measure of how big something is."},{"m":"The biggest possible absolute value of the vertical part of a periodic curve."},{"m":"The biggest possible absolute value of something that changes periodically (like a wave)."}]}]},"born":{"h":"born","i":"/ˈboː(r)n/","a":"en-us-born.ogg","l":"bear","q":"verb"},"ford":{"h":"ford","i":"/fɔːd/","a":"en-us-ford.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A place in a stream where the water is not deep, making it possible to cross from one side to the other without a bridge by walking, riding, or driving through the water; a crossing.","e":"The ford looks shallow enough for us to cross."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To cross a stream using a ford.","e":"We forded the stream in our car without any problems."}]}]},"fords":{"h":"fords","l":"ford","q":"noun"},"forded":{"h":"forded","l":"ford","q":"verb"},"lightning":{"h":"lightning","i":"/ˈlaɪt.nɪŋ/","a":"en-us-lightning.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A flash of light caused by electrical discharge in the atmosphere."},{"m":"An electrical discharge in the atmosphere.","e":"That tree was hit by lightning."}]}]},"council":{"h":"council","i":"/kaʊnsɪl/","a":"en-us-council.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A council is a group of people who are chosen or elected to make laws, rules, and decisions.","e":"Town council is considering a road-widening proposal."}]}]},"borough":{"h":"borough","i":"/ˈbʌrə/","a":"en-borough.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A fortified town; a town or city."},{"m":"A town that has a municipal corporation and certain traditional rights."},{"m":"An administrative district (part of a city) in some cities, for example, London."},{"m":"An administrative unit of a city which, under most circumstances according to law, would be considered a larger or more powerful entity; most commonly used in American English to define the five counties that make up New York City."},{"m":"Other similar administrative units in cities and states in various parts of the world."},{"m":"A district in Alaska that has powers similar to a county."}]}]},"echo":{"h":"echo","i":"/ˈɛkəʊ/","a":"en-us-echo.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An echo is a reflected sound that is heard again by a person."},{"m":"The letter E in the."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To repeat back what someone else has just said."}]}]},"count":{"h":"count","i":"/kaʊnt/","a":"en-us-count.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you count something, you find how many there are, usually by looking at them one by one.","e":"OK kids, first everyone get on the bus, and then we'll count to see that everyone's here."},{"m":"If something counts, it is accepted, allowed, or included.","e":"If you use your hands in soccer, the goal doesn't count."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something counts, it's important or useful.","e":"If you're trying to lose weight, the kind of food you eat really does count."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you count on somebody or something, you depend on them.","e":"If you have any problems, you can count on me to help out."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A count is the number of something.","e":"Our new-student count is now up to 124, five more students than last time."},{"m":"(countable) A count is an act of counting.","e":"The study will include a count of the number of birds on the island."},{"m":"If you loose count of something, you can't count them all.","e":"I've lost count of the number of times she's said that."},{"m":"(countable) In law a count is a crime that a court has charged you with."},{"m":"(countable) A count is European title, similar to earl."}]}]},"pair":{"h":"pair","i":"/pɛə(r)/","a":"en-us-pair.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pair is two things that go together.","e":"She has many pairs of shoes, but she only has one pair of pants."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(often passive) If you pair two people or things, you put them together.","e":"Young women were often paired with older men."}]}]},"biscuit":{"h":"biscuit","i":"/ˈbɪskɪt/","a":"En-uk-biscuit.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A biscuit is a cookie.","e":"He brought along homemade biscuits for the picnic."},{"m":"(countable) A biscuit is a small bread usually made with baking soda, similar to a scone, but usually not sweet."},{"m":"(uncountable) Biscuit is a form of unglazed earthenware."}]}]},"pup":{"h":"pup","i":"/pʌp/","a":"en-us-pup.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A young dog, wolf, fox, seal, shark and some other animals","e":"The dog has had that bed since he was just a pup."},{"m":"(countable) A young person who does not have much experience","e":"The new teacher is a mere pup."}]}]},"pups":{"h":"pups","i":"/pʌps/","l":"pup","q":"noun"},"biscuits":{"h":"biscuits","l":"biscuit","q":"noun"},"printer":{"h":"printer","i":"/ˈprɪntə(r)/","a":"en-au-printer.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A person who makes prints."},{"m":"(countable) The person who runs a printing press or the owner of a printing business."},{"m":"(countable) A machine, usually attached to a computer, used to print words or images onto paper.","e":"I used the printer to make a copy of my project."}]}]},"printers":{"h":"printers","l":"printer","q":"noun"},"bonn":{"h":"Bonn","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Bonn is a city in the state of North Rhine-Westphalia, Germany; it was the capital of West Germany from 1949 to 1990."}]}]},"cities":{"h":"cities","i":"/ˈsɪtiz/","a":"en-us-cities.ogg","l":"city","q":"noun"},"magnitude":{"h":"magnitude","i":"/mægnɪtjuːd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-magnitude.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The exact or approximate size, extent or importance of something."},{"m":"A number that is assigned to something so that it may be compared to others numerically; it is always a positive number (more than zero)."},{"m":"The apparent brightness of a star."},{"m":"A measure of the energy of an earthquake (for example, on the Richter scale)."}]}]},"magnitudes":{"h":"magnitudes","l":"magnitude","q":"noun"},"mix":{"h":"mix","i":"/ˈmɪks/","a":"en-us-mix.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you mix something, you stir two or more things together.","e":"Mix the eggs and milk with the flour."},{"m":"If you mix something, you combine items from two or more sources which are normally kept separate.","e":"Don't mix the light clothes with the dark clothes in the washing machine."},{"m":"To combine many tracks.","e":"I'll mix the rhythm tracks down to a single track."},{"m":"To make a finished version of a recording.","e":"I'm almost done mixing this song."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mix is two or more things that have been mixed together; it is a mixture.","e":"Now add the raisins to the mix."},{"m":"The result of combining items normally kept separate.","e":"The laundry is a mix of light and dark clothes."},{"m":"The result of combining several tracks.","e":"The rhythm mix sounds muddy."},{"m":"The finished version of a recording.","e":"I've almost finished the mix for this song."}]}]},"mixes":{"h":"mixes","l":"mix","q":"verb"},"altar":{"h":"altar","i":"/ˈɔːl.tə/","a":"en-us-altar.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A table used for religious."}]}]},"altars":{"h":"altars","l":"altar","q":"noun"},"avatar":{"h":"avatar","i":"/ˌæv.əˈtɑː/","a":"en-us-avatar.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A physical representation (for example, a picture) of an idea or concept; a personification."},{"m":"A picture representing a person on the internet."},{"m":"(hinduism) The incarnation of a god, especially Vishnu."}]}]},"avatars":{"h":"avatars","l":"avatar","q":"noun"},"virginity":{"h":"virginity","i":"/və(r)ˈdʒɪnɪti/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-virginity.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The state of being a virgin."}]}]},"virgins":{"h":"virgins","l":"virgin","q":"noun"},"protests":{"h":"protests","l":"protest","q":"verb"},"protested":{"h":"protested","l":"protest","q":"verb"},"coppers":{"h":"coppers","l":"copper","q":"noun"},"date":{"h":"date","i":"/deɪt/","a":"en-us-date.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A date is a particular day in a month or year.","e":"\"What's the date on Friday?\" \"Uh, the 17th, I think.\""},{"m":"(countable) A date is an agreement to meet on particular day at a particular time.","e":"Can we set a date for the next meeting? How about June 21st?"},{"m":"(countable) A date is a time when you go out with a romantic partner.","e":"I've got a date with Michael tonight. We're going to that new restaurant."},{"m":"(countable) You date is the person you are meeting romantically.","e":"Who's your date for the dance?"},{"m":"If you say that something is true to date, you mean in the past until the present.","e":"To date, we've had no problems with the new computers."},{"m":"(countable) A date is a sweet fruit that grows on date palm trees and is often dried."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you date something, you write the date on it.","e":"You need to date this form at the top, here."},{"m":"(transitive) If you date something, you find out how old it is, especially something very old.","e":"We have not been successful in dating the painting, though we believe it is from the 17th century."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something dates, it goes out of style and looks old fashioned.","e":"Unfortunately, this jacket has dated rather more quickly than I had hoped."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something dates from a particular time, it first existed at that time.","e":"The earliest electronic computers date from the mid-20th century (around 1940–1945)."},{"m":"(transitive) If you date someone, you have a romantic relationship with them.","e":"They dated for almost a year in high school."}]}]},"guy":{"h":"guy","i":"/gaɪ/","a":"en-us-guy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A guy is a boy or a man.","e":"So, I walk in and there's this woman talking to this guy."},{"m":"(countable) A guy is a rope from the top of something to the ground to keep it from falling over."}]}]},"guys":{"h":"guys","i":"/ɡaɪz/","a":"en-us-guys.ogg","l":"guy","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(informal) People of either gender.","e":"Who are those guys?"}]}]},"dates":{"h":"dates","l":"date","q":"noun"},"delphi":{"h":"Delphi","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Delphi is a city in Greece.","e":"The people went to Delphi to visit the oracle of Apollo."},{"m":"Delphi is a computer programming language based on PASCAL.","e":"Delphi was written in 1986 for Apple computers."},{"m":"Delphi is a method for getting agreement from a group of experts.","e":"We wanted the best solution so we organized the group using the Delphi method."}]}]},"freedom":{"h":"freedom","i":"/ˈfriːdəm/","a":"en-us-freedom.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The state of being free; the state of not being imprisoned or enslaved.","e":"He enjoyed his freedom after he was released from prison."},{"m":"The state of being without restraints or constraints.","e":"Freedom of speech is important in a democracy."}]}]},"freedoms":{"h":"freedoms","l":"freedom","q":"noun"},"nudity":{"h":"nudity","i":"/ˈnjudɪˌti/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-nudity.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The state of being nude."}]}]},"paramedic":{"h":"paramedic","i":"/ˌpærəˈmɛdɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-paramedic.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A paramedic is a person who is trained to medically help people who have had an injury outside of a hospital and prepares them to be taken to a hospital.","e":"The paramedic rushed the victim to the ambulance."}]}]},"nude":{"h":"nude","i":"/n(j)uːd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-NaomiAmethyst-nude.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Someone who is nude is not wearing clothes or some other covering."},{"m":"A term used in fashion (clothing, makeup) indicating the color of bare skin."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A painting or other artwork that shows human figures that are partially or totally naked."}]}]},"economy":{"h":"economy","i":"/iːˈkɒnəmi/","a":"en-us-economy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The economy is the use of the resources of a community or system.","e":"We wonder about the ability of our businesses to compete in the global economy."},{"m":"Economy is the careful and minimal use of resources.","e":"The schools were closed for reasons of economy."},{"m":"(uncountable) Economy is the section of the airplane with the smallest seats and cheapest ticket prices.","e":"We decided to fly business class instead of economy."},{"m":"(countable) A market economy is an economy with free competition between businesses.","e":"China will continue to move towards a market economy."}]}]},"naked":{"h":"naked","i":"/ˈneɪkɪd/","a":"en-us-naked.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is naked, they are not wearing any clothes.","e":"She was as naked as the day she was born."},{"m":"If something is naked, it is plain or put bluntly.","e":"the naked truth, naked facts"},{"m":"If something is naked, it is not protected.","e":"Never have a naked flame near gas cylinders."}]}]},"intelligences":{"h":"intelligences","l":"intelligence","q":"noun"},"walks":{"h":"walks","i":"/wɔks/","a":"en-us-walks.ogg","l":"walk","q":"verb"},"occasion":{"h":"occasion","i":"/əˈkeɪʒən/","a":"en-us-occasion.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An occasion is a particular time.","e":"Often she had to rush home on occasions when she might have preferred to stay out."},{"m":"(countable) An occasion is a good time to do something.","e":"The visit to Ottawa was a good occasion for us to get together."},{"m":"(countable) An occasion is a special time or event.","e":"Nov 12 is a happy occasion. It is my 25th wedding anniversary."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If x occasions y, x causes y.","e":"Now we come to the problems that have occasioned this meeting."}]}]},"zipper":{"h":"zipper","i":"/ˈzɪpɚ/","a":"en-au-zipper.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A zipper is a device used to join two pieces of cloth for a short amount of time. It usually consists of 2 strips of metal on both pieces of cloth that are then joined together."}]}]},"desert":{"h":"desert","i":"/'dɛzət/","a":"en-us-desert-noun.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To leave, abandon or forsake someone or something.","e":"When he left without us, we felt deserted."}]}]},"saturn":{"h":"Saturn","i":"/ˈsæ.tɝn/","a":"en-us-Saturn.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"The second largest planet in Earth's solar system; it is known for its big rings.","e":"Saturn is the sixth planet from the sun."},{"m":"The Roman god of fertility and agriculture."}]}]},"planet":{"h":"planet","i":"/ˈplænɪt/","a":"en-us-planet.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A planet is one of the 8 bodies that orbit the Sun: Mercury, Venus, Earth, Mars, Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus and Neptune.","e":"Our planet is named Earth."}]}]},"frog":{"h":"frog","i":"/frɒɡ/","a":"en-us-frog.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A small hopping amphibian."}]}]},"skeleton":{"h":"skeleton","i":"/ˈskɛlətən/","a":"en-us-skeleton.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A skeleton is the bones that support the body of an animal or person."},{"m":"A skeleton is a very thin person.","e":"She lost so much weight while she was sick that she became a skeleton."},{"m":"The skeleton of something is the core of it, the part that give it structure."},{"m":"A skeleton is a frame that provides support to a building or other construction."}]}]},"tiger":{"h":"tiger","i":"/ˈtaɪɡɚ/","a":"en-us-tiger.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A tiger is a mammal. It comes from Asia.","e":"I'm going to take the kids to the zoo to see a tiger."}]}]},"decide":{"h":"decide","i":"/dɪˈsaɪd/","a":"en-us-decide.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you decide something, there were different things you could do, but you choose one.","e":"The government has decided to cut spending."}]}]},"department":{"h":"department","i":"/dɪˈpɑːtm(ə)nt/","a":"en-us-department.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A department is a part of a business, school, hospital or other institution that has a particular job.","e":"The Department of Health is planning to build three new hospitals in the area."},{"m":"A department is a part of a large store, which sells one kind of product.","e":"You can find balls in the sporting goods department."},{"m":"Somebody's department is the things that they are good at or responsible for.","e":"Sorry, I can't help you. That's not my department."}]}]},"homograph":{"h":"homograph","i":"/ˈhɒməgrɑːf/","a":"en-us-homograph.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A word that is spelled the same as another but has a different meaning and may have a different pronunciation."}]}]},"whoever":{"h":"whoever","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"(question) person or persons.","e":"Whoever thought up that stupid idea?"},{"m":"(relative) person or persons.","e":"Whoever violates the law will be punished."}]}]},"depend":{"h":"depend","i":"/dɪˈpɛnd/","a":"en-us-depend.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you depend on something, you need it; you rely on it; you trust it.","e":"I knew I could depend on you to meet your aunt at the station."}]}]},"especial":{"h":"especial","i":"/ɛsˈpɛʃəl/","a":"en-us-especial.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is especial, it is very important or significant.","e":"I don't see anything especial about that paint; it seems like an ordinary blue."}]}]},"describe":{"h":"describe","i":"/dɪˈskraɪb/","a":"en-us-describe.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you describe something, you say what it looks like, sounds like, acts like, etc.","e":"Their wedding day, as described by Emma in her book, was \"a perfect September day.\""},{"m":"(transitive) If something describes a circle, arc, etc., it follows that shape.","e":"His finger slowly described a circle in the water."}]}]},"jesus":{"h":"Jesus","i":"/ˈd͡ʒiːzəs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Jesus.wav","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Jesus of Nazareth was a religious prophet and leader in Palestine who lived from around 4 BC to AD 30, when he was crucified.","e":"Jesus was crucified by Pontius Pilate, under pressure from some Jewish leaders."},{"m":"Jesus () is a boy's name, especially in Spanish-speaking counties."}]},{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"You use Jesus when you are surprised or not happy about something. Some people do not like to use this phrase in respect of Jesus.","e":"Jesus, that's heavy."}]}]},"presumptuous":{"h":"presumptuous","i":"/prəˈzʌmp.tʃuː.əs/","a":"en-us-presumptuous.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is presumptuous, they don't know the limits of what is appropriate or allowed.","e":"I hope I won't be considered presumptuous if I give some advice."}]}]},"die":{"h":"die","i":"/daɪ/","a":"en-us-die.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If a person or animal dies, it stops living.","e":"My father died last year in a car crash, I really miss him."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something dies, it stops existing.","e":"The idea died once the money was all gone."},{"m":"(intransitive) If a machine dies, it stops working.","e":"The car died suddenly on the highway."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you're dying for something, you want it very much.","e":"I'm dying for a chance to meet him."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A die is a piece of metal or other hard material used to shape, cut, or mold a product."},{"m":"(countable) A die is a cube, each side of which is marked with a different number of spots from 1 to 6."}]}]},"dice":{"h":"dice","i":"/daɪs/","a":"en-us-dice.ogg","l":"die","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Sometimes used in the singular, a dice is a cube, each side of which is marked with a different number of spots from 1 to 6."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you dice something, you cut it into cubes (usually small cubes)."}]}]},"mathematics":{"h":"mathematics","i":"/mæθ(ə)ˈmætɪks/","a":"en-us-mathematics.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Mathematics is the study of numbers.","e":"Use of addition, subtraction, multiplication and division are part of basic mathematics."}]}]},"math":{"h":"math","i":"/mæθ/","a":"en-us-math.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Math is a short form of mathematics."},{"m":"(uncountable) Mathematical calculations.","e":"$170 a month? That doesn't sound right. Let me check your math."},{"m":"(countable) A math class.","e":"I have 2 more maths to take before I can graduate."}]}]},"direct":{"h":"direct","i":"/dɪˈrɛkt/","a":"en-us-direct.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is direct, it is straight and as short as possible with nothing extra in between.","e":"It's a direct flight from Tokyo to Toronto with no stop in Vancouver."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive); (always with a goal) If you direct something somewhere, you point it there.","e":"He directed his light to the corner where he heard the noise."},{"m":"(transitive) If you direct something such as an organisation, you are in charge of if.","e":"She directed the investigation into the crash."},{"m":"If you direct a play or film, you tell the actors how to act."},{"m":"(transitive) If you direct something, you tell people what to do.","e":"He directed that the money go to the church after he died."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If you go somewhere or do something direct, you do so by the shortest route without anything extra in between."}]}]},"divorce":{"h":"divorce","i":"/dɪˈvɔːs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-divorce.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Divorce is the legal ending of a marriage.","e":"Did you know that Richard and Sarah got a divorce?"},{"m":"A separation of connected things.","e":"There is a geographic divorce between the United States and Mexico."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To divorce is to legally end a marriage between two people.","e":"The captain of a ship can marry couples, but cannot divorce them."},{"m":"(transitive) If you divorce someone, you end your marriage to them.","e":"Lucy divorced Steve when she found that he had been unfaithful."},{"m":"(transitive) To separate something that was connected.","e":"The smaller group voted to divorce itself from the larger one."},{"m":"(intransitive) To get a legal divorce.","e":"Edna and Simon divorced last year; he got the house, and she got the business."}]}]},"labium":{"h":"labium","i":"/ˈleɪ.bi.əm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-labium.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A labium is a part of the body that is similar to lips; it is one of the two pairs of folds of skin on either side of the vulva."},{"m":"The lip of a corolla on a flower."}]}]},"idiot":{"h":"idiot","i":"/ˈɪdiːət/","a":"en-us-idiot.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A common term for a person who is not very smart."}]}]},"anchorage":{"h":"anchorage","i":"/ˈæŋkərɪd͡ʒ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-anchorage.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A harbor, river, or other area that can hold a ship while it is anchored."},{"m":"A fee charged for anchoring."}]}]},"presumed":{"h":"presumed","l":"presume","q":"verb"},"presume":{"h":"presume","i":"/prɪˈzjuːm/","a":"en-us-presume.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you presume something, you believe that it is true without evidence.","e":"The boy has been missing for a week, and is presumed dead."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you presume to do something, you do it though it is rude or wrong.","e":"I wouldn't presume to go to the party without an invitation."},{"m":"(transitive) If x presumes y, then x requires y and builds on it.","e":"This books presumes a basic understanding of English grammar."}]}]},"district":{"h":"district","i":"/ˈdɪstrɪkt/","a":"en-us-district.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A district is an area of land that shares certain characteristics.","e":"Roppongi and Kabukicho are Tokyo's main entertainment districts."},{"m":"(countable) A district is an area of land that is defined for political reasons such as elections or administration.","e":"Washington is located in the District of Columbia."}]}]},"else":{"h":"else","i":"/ɛls/; sometimes /ɛlts/","a":"en-us-else.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"You use else to show that something is not the same one as another thing.","e":"OK, he's cute, but what else has he got?"}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"You use x or else y to say that if x doesn't happen or isn't true, y would happen or would be true.","e":"They don't want to be here or else they would have come."},{"m":"You use or else to say that if something doesn't happen, it will be bad.","e":"You'd better clean your room, or else."}]}]},"valley":{"h":"valley","i":"/ˈvæli/","a":"en-us-valley.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An long, low area between hills or mountains, often with a river running through it."},{"m":"The area which drains into a river."},{"m":"Any structure resembling #1, for example, the point where two angled roofs meet."}]}]},"bishops":{"h":"bishops","i":"/ˈbɪʃəps/","a":"en-us-bishops.ogg","l":"bishop","q":"noun"},"wider":{"h":"wider","i":"/ˈwaɪdɚ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Persent101-wider.wav","l":"wide","q":"adjective"},"widest":{"h":"widest","i":"/ˈwaɪdəst/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Flame, not lame-widest.wav","l":"wide","q":"adjective"},"jellies":{"h":"jellies","l":"jelly","q":"noun"},"locations":{"h":"locations","a":"en-us-locations.ogg","l":"location","q":"noun"},"shocked":{"h":"shocked","i":"/ʃɒkt/","a":"en-us-shocked.ogg","l":"shock","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are feeling shocked, you feel surprised, startled, or confused.","e":"I'm shocked that you would do such a terrible thing!"}]}]},"introduce":{"h":"introduce","i":"/ˌɪntrəˈdus/","a":"en-us-introduce.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you introduce someone or something, you make them known to someone else.","e":"Let me introduce you to my friend."}]}]},"shocking":{"h":"shocking","i":"/ˈʃɒkɪŋ/","a":"en-us-shocking.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is shocking, it causes someone to feel shocked or startled.","e":"Did you hear the shocking news that Dan was fired for stealing?"},{"m":"If something is shocking, it is unusually obscene or lewd."},{"m":"If something is shocking, it is very bad."}]}]},"attacks":{"h":"attacks","i":"/əˈtæks/","a":"en-us-attacks.ogg","l":"attack","q":"noun"},"attacked":{"h":"attacked","i":"/əˈtækt/","a":"en-us-attacked.ogg","l":"attack","q":"verb"},"equips":{"h":"equips","l":"equip","q":"verb"},"equipped":{"h":"equipped","l":"equip","q":"verb"},"formulas":{"h":"formulas","l":"formula","q":"noun"},"frameworks":{"h":"frameworks","l":"framework","q":"noun"},"medicines":{"h":"medicines","a":"en-us-medicines.ogg","l":"medicine","q":"noun"},"seeds":{"h":"seeds","i":"/siːdz/","l":"seed","q":"noun"},"introduces":{"h":"introduces","l":"introduce","q":"verb"},"introduced":{"h":"introduced","i":"/ˌɪntrəˈduːst/","a":"en-us-introduced.ogg","l":"introduce","q":"verb"},"employ":{"h":"employ","i":"/ɪmˈplɔɪ/","a":"en-us-employ.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you employ someone, you pay them to do a job.","e":"The tanning company currently employs over 240 people in Caledonia."},{"m":"(transitive) If you employ something, you use it.","e":"Various methods are employed to change the way it looks."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"If you have someone in your employ, you are paying them to do a job."}]}]},"encourage":{"h":"encourage","i":"/ɪnˈkʌrɪʤ/","a":"en-us-encourage.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you encourage someone, you make them feel that they want to, or can, do something.","e":"We're trying to encourage more people to give money to the hospital."},{"m":"(transitive) If x encourages y, x makes y more likely to happen.","e":"The water encourages the breakdown of the wood."}]}]},"lady":{"h":"lady","i":"/ˈleɪdi/","a":"en-us-lady.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A polite way of saying \"woman\".","e":"Please direct this lady to the soft furnishings department."},{"m":"The wife of a lord or a woman who holds the office in her own right.","e":"Lady Diana was very popular with the British people."},{"m":"A polite woman who is respected.","e":"Mary, please try to act more like a lady in public."}]}]},"hell":{"h":"hell","i":"/hɛl/","a":"en-us-hell.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"In some religions and myths, hell is a place where you may go after you die. Hell is usually seen as a bad place where bad people are punished."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Something that is very hard to do or makes you suffer.","e":"My new boss is making my job hell."}]},{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"You say hell when you are having a hard time.","e":"Oh, hell! I got another parking ticket."},{"m":"Hell may be added to show strong feeling.","e":"I'm sure as hell not going there!"}]}]},"justly":{"h":"justly","i":"/ˈdʒʌstli/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-justly.wav","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"To do something justly is to do it in a way that is fair, that shows justice; it means acting as if everyone is equal.","e":"She justly said no, she would not stand on a stage with someone who was saying bad things about another person."}]}]},"submerge":{"h":"submerge","i":"/sʌbˈmɜːdʒ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-submerge.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Someone submerges something when they make the thing sink; they make it go down into water so that the water is covering it.","e":"He submerged his arm in the lake to try to clean the mud off it."},{"m":"Something submerges when it sinks; it goes down into the water so that the water is covering it.","e":"The boat submerged completely, but then part of it came back up out of the water."}]}]},"identity":{"h":"identity","i":"/aɪˈdɛntəti/","a":"EN-AU ck1 identity.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Your identity is your name, your personality, and the things that make you different from other people.","e":"Before I can give you money from your bank account, you have to prove your identity."},{"m":"(countable) The way an organisation shows itself to the public"}]}]},"microeconomics":{"h":"microeconomics","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Microeconomics is the study of the economic behaviour of small economic groups like firms and families."}]}]},"destroy":{"h":"destroy","i":"/dɪˈstrɔɪ/","a":"en-us-destroy.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If a person destroys something, they break it or make it not exist anymore.","e":"The house was destroyed by the bomb."},{"m":"If someone destroys a person, they hurt that person badly or cause that person much trouble.","e":"Mary was destroyed by her failiure to get into college."}]}]},"gone":{"h":"gone","i":"/gɒn/","a":"en-us-gone.ogg","l":"go","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Not there any more, because it has moved or because it does not exist anymore."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A term meaning someone is dead.","e":"Katie: \"Doctor, is he okay?.\""}]}]},"depress":{"h":"depress","i":"/dəˈprɛs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-depress.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you depress something, you push or hold it down.","e":"He depressed the button with his finger."},{"m":"If something is depressed it is being made low.","e":"The prices were depressed by too much being available."},{"m":"If something depresses you, it makes you very sad.","e":"Sad songs always depress me."}]}]},"lower":{"h":"lower","i":"/ˈləʊə/","a":"en-us-lower.ogg","l":"low","q":"adjective","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you lower something, you move it down.","e":"The man was lowered into the hole on a rope, so he could save the child."}]}]},"depressing":{"h":"depressing","i":"/dɪˈprɛsɪŋ(ɡ)/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is depressing it makes you sad.","e":"I find news about problems in the world depressing."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you are depressing something, you are making it lower."}]}]},"destroyer":{"h":"destroyer","i":"/dəˈstrɔɪ.ɚ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-destroyer.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Someone or something that destroys."},{"m":"(countable) A small, fast ship used in war."}]}]},"destructive":{"h":"destructive","i":"/dɪˈstrʌktɪv/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-destructuve.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something (or someone) is destructive it destroys; it causes destruction."}]}]},"weird":{"h":"weird","i":"/wɪəd/","a":"en-us-weird.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Very strange or unusual. Very different from others of its kind or what is expected. Something that is weird is not at all normal.","e":"People laughed at the boy because he was weird."}]}]},"destruct":{"h":"destruct","i":"/dɪˈstrʌkt/","a":"en-us-destruct.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something destructs it destroys itself. Usually we say self-destruct instead.","e":"The weapon was made to self-destruct if stolen."}]}]},"self-destruct":{"h":"self-destruct","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Self-destruct means to destroy oneself or itself.","e":"The weapon was made to self-destruct if stolen."}]}]},"algebra":{"h":"algebra","i":"/ˈæl.dʒɪ.brə/","a":"en-us-algebra.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Algebra is a kind of mathematics where a letter (called a variable) can replace a number that is not known.","e":"Using algebra, we can define a line with the formula y = x + 3"}]}]},"heaven":{"h":"heaven","i":"/ˈhɛvən/","a":"en-us-heaven.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"In some religions and myths, heaven is a place where you may go after you die. Heaven is usually seen as a happy place where good people are rewarded.","e":"I miss my grandmother, but I know she's with God in heaven."},{"m":"The sky."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The skies or places in outer space.","e":"I looked up to the heavens in delight."},{"m":"(uncountable) Much happiness, or a cause of much happiness.","e":"He's been in heaven ever since we told him."}]}]},"alcohol":{"h":"alcohol","i":"/ˈæl.kə.hɔl/","a":"en-us-alcohol.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Alcohol is the chemical in some drinks that makes you drunk (intoxicated).","e":", wine, and whiskey all have alcohol in them."},{"m":"Another chemical similar to the one that makes you drunk.","e":"The scientist used an alcohol to fuel the burner."}]}]},"arithmetic":{"h":"arithmetic","i":"/əˈrɪθmətɪk/","a":"en-us-arithmetic.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The kind of mathematics in which addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division are done on numbers.","e":"My son is starting to do simple arithmetic like 2 + 2 = 4."}]}]},"magnification":{"h":"magnification","i":"/ˌmæɡnɪfɪˈkeɪʃən/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Magnification is the act or result of making something look bigger.","e":"The magnification of this small bug can help us see hidden details."}]}]},"enjoy":{"h":"enjoy","i":"/ɛnˈdʒɔɪ/","a":"en-us-enjoy.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you enjoy something, it gives you joy, happiness and pleasure.","e":"We enjoy dancing. When we dance, we feel happy and good."}]}]},"tapioca":{"h":"tapioca","i":"/tæpiˈoʊkə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-tapioca.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A plant from South America."},{"m":"(uncountable) The dried root of this plant that has been crushed. Tapioca is used to make pudding and pie filling; it makes them thick.","e":"I love tapioca pudding, it's my favorite."}]}]},"expense":{"h":"expense","i":"/ɪkˈspɛns/","a":"en-us-expense.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An expense is something for which you spend money.","e":"Food is a huge expense for many people around the world."},{"m":"An expense is an amount of money that you spend.","e":"If your income is less than your expenses, you have a serious problem."},{"m":"If you do x at the expense of y, x hurts y because it makes y have less money, less time, less social status, etc.","e":"She often makes jokes at her own expense."}]}]},"jazz":{"h":"jazz","i":"/d͡ʒæz/","a":"en-au-jazz.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Jazz is a kind of music invented by African Americans. It usually has a strong rhythm and is often played with horns.","e":"Duke Ellington and Glenn Miller were famous for playing jazz."},{"m":"A group of ideas you do not want to think about.","e":"Yes, I've heard about the health risks and all that jazz."},{"m":"Nonsense.","e":"Stop talking jazz."}]}]},"marry":{"h":"marry","i":"/ˈmærɪ/","a":"en-us-marry.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When two people marry they become husband and wife; that is, they become married. In many this is a legal agreement. In some cultures marrying is a part of the religion. Marrying is often done with a wedding (a special day for those people to marry).","e":"I cannot believe he married her when there are nicer girls out there."},{"m":"If you marry two things, you connect them or make them into one thing.","e":"I have two different ideas I would like to marry together."}]}]},"marriage":{"h":"marriage","i":"/ˈmærɪdʒ/","a":"en-us-marriage.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The life two people have together while they are married.","e":"The marriage seemed good until he left her."},{"m":"When two people of becoming married; a wedding."},{"m":"Two different things that have been made into one thing.","e":"Music videos are a marriage of music and television."}]}]},"wedding":{"h":"wedding","i":"/ˈwɛdɪŋ/","a":"en-us-wedding.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A wedding is a special time when two people marry each other.","e":"The wedding was very beautiful."},{"m":"Two different things things that have been made into one thing.","e":"Music videos are a wedding of music and television."}]}]},"wed":{"h":"wed","i":"/'wεd/","a":"en-us-wed.ogg","l":"wed","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When people wed they become married. Wed is an old word, most people say marry now.","e":"I'd love to be wed, but I cannot find a girl to marry me."},{"m":"When two things are wed they are made into one thing.","e":"Music videos wed music to television."}]}]},"explain":{"h":"explain","i":"/ɛkˈspleɪn/","a":"en-us-explain.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you explain something, you talk about it so that somebody can understand it.","e":"Can you explain the difference between the two?"}]}]},"thou":{"h":"thou","i":"/ðaʊ/","a":"en-us-thou.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"Another word for you; thou is an old word, and people do not use it much anymore. Often when thou is used it is with other old words.","e":"What hast thou done? (i.e. What have you done?)"}]},{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"Used before a word that means the person or people someone is talking to.","e":"Blow, blow, thou winter wind, thou art not so unkind as man's ingratitude."}]}]},"pressure":{"h":"pressure","i":"/ˈprɛʃə(r)/","a":"en-us-pressure.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"In science, pressure is force applied over an area.","e":"It hurt when the doctor put pressure on her cut foot."},{"m":"If a person is under pressure, they feel stressed.","e":"She has been under a lot of pressure lately because of her final exams. If she fails them, she will not graduate."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you pressure someone, you try to make them do something, especially something they do not want to do.","e":"Her friends tried to pressure her into smoking, even after Maya kept saying \"no.\""}]}]},"quiz":{"h":"quiz","i":"/kwɪz/","a":"en-us-quiz.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A small group of questions asked together. Often a quiz is like a small test at school.","e":"I thought we were going to have a test, but it was only a short quiz."},{"m":"(countable) A quiz is a game where a person asks questions to other people."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To give someone a quiz, often a written quiz on paper.","e":"The teacher quizzed him on biology."},{"m":"To ask many questions in speech."}]}]},"soul":{"h":"soul","i":"/səʊl/","a":"en-us-soul.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A part of you that cannot be seen or touched. Souls are prominent in some religions and myths.","e":"He went to church hoping to save his soul."},{"m":"(countable) Your mind or feelings.","e":"There is a pain deep in my soul."},{"m":"(uncountable) True feeling, or feeling very human.","e":"I love his music because it is full of soul."},{"m":"(uncountable) A kind of music. Soul is usually sung and is often by African Americans.","e":"She was the greatest soul singer of her time."}]}]},"ghost":{"h":"ghost","i":"/gəʊst/","a":"en-us-ghost.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A ghost is the spirit or soul of a man."},{"m":"(countable) A ghost is the soul of a dead person that shows up after death.","e":"The house was haunted by the ghost of the little boy who used to live here."},{"m":"(countable) A ghost is any faint thing that looks like a shadow.","e":"Tom was scared of a ghost."},{"m":"(countable) A ghost is a ghostwriter."}]}]},"mary":{"h":"Mary","i":"/ˈmɛə.ri/","a":"en-us-Mary.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"(Christianity) Mary is the Virgin Mary, the mother of Jesus.","e":"Some people claim to have seen Mary appear to them."}]}]},"merry":{"h":"merry","i":"/ˈmɛri/","a":"en-us-merry.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are merry you feel happy.","e":"We were all feeling very merry that night."},{"m":"If something is merry it makes people happy.","e":"I am wishing you a merry Christmas!"}]}]},"sole":{"h":"sole","i":"/səʊl/","a":"en-us-sole.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"only"}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The bottom of a foot."},{"m":"The bottom of a shoe."},{"m":"A flatfish of the family Soleidae."}]}]},"automobile":{"h":"automobile","i":"/ˈɔ.tə.mə.bɪil/","a":"en-us-automobile.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An automobile is a vehicle with four wheels and an engine or motor, made for people to ride in.","e":"The American automobile industry creates a lot of jobs."}]}]},"plain":{"h":"plain","i":"/pl̩eɪn/","a":"en-us-plain.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is plain, it is clear and easy to see or understand.","e":"The plain and simple truth was that it was John's fault."},{"m":"If something is plain, it is simple and undecorated.","e":"This dress is too plain. There is nothing interesting about it at all."},{"m":"If someone or something is plain, they are not beautiful or pretty."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A place with flat ground, often covered in grass.","e":"Many animals live on the plains of Africa."}]}]},"geometry":{"h":"geometry","i":"/dʒiːɒmətriː/","a":"en-us-geometry.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A kind of mathematics that is about shapes and spaces.","e":"Using geometry we can find out the area of a circle."}]}]},"pretty":{"h":"pretty","i":"/'prɪ.ti/","a":"en-us-pretty.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"You use pretty before an adjective or adverb to mean \"more than a little\".","e":"She was pretty sure that he'd say yes."},{"m":"You use pretty before an adjective or adverb to mean \"very\".","e":"That sounds like a pretty good idea."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is pretty, people like to look at it.","e":"Those flowers are so pretty."}]}]},"calf":{"h":"calf","i":"/kɑːf/","a":"en-us-calf.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A calf is a young cow or the young of certain other large mammals.","e":"The cow gave birth to a calf today."},{"m":"(countable) The back of the leg below the knee is called the calf.","e":"The muscle in my calf hurt after I ran for two hours."}]}]},"coin":{"h":"coin","i":"/kɔɪn/","a":"en-us-coin.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A coin is money made of metal.","e":"The United States makes several different coins including the penny, nickel, dime, and quarter."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you invent a new word or phrase, you coin the word or phrase.","e":"The host of a radio show coined the phrase \"rock and roll\" for music of the 1950s."}]}]},"begins":{"h":"begins","i":"/bɪˈɡɪnz/","a":"en-us-begins.ogg","l":"begin","q":"verb"},"sisters":{"h":"sisters","i":"/ˈsɪs.tɚz/","a":"en-us-sisters.ogg","l":"sister","q":"noun"},"amounts":{"h":"amounts","i":"/əˈmaʊnts/","l":"amount","q":"noun"},"amounted":{"h":"amounted","i":"/əˈmaʊntɪd/","a":"en-us-amounted.ogg","l":"amount","q":"verb"},"euro":{"h":"euro","i":"/ˈjuərəʊ/","a":"en-uk-euro.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Official name of the money used in 15 countries of Europe."}]}]},"comparative":{"h":"comparative","i":"/kəmˈpɛr.ə.tɪv/","a":"en-us-ne-comparative.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"You use comparative to show that something is not great but is better than something else.","e":"They lived in the comparative comfort of her uncle's house."},{"m":"You use comparative to show that someone or something is not quite a beginner, etc., but almost the same as one.","e":"The absent father was a comparative stranger to the son."},{"m":"Comparative study is a form of study that looks at how things are alike and different.","e":"The study of how the anatomy of animals are alike and different is called comparative anatomy."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A comparative is a form of a comparable adjective. You use it to show that something is \"more big\", \"more good\", etc.","e":"For example:"}]}]},"figure":{"h":"figure","i":"/ˈfɪgjɚ/","a":"en-us-figure.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Figures are numbers showing the value or amount of something.","e":"The sales figures from the spring were down from last year."},{"m":"(countable) A figure is a person, often a well-known person.","e":"They have published articles about many leading figures including John Reed, J.A. Hobson, Tom Mann, and Daniel de Leon."},{"m":"(countable) A figure is a person, especially the person's shape.","e":"She did not see the figure standing in the shadows of the kitchen doorway."},{"m":"(countable) A figure is a geometric shape."},{"m":"(countable) A figure is a picture in a textbook or scientific journal. (Often written fig.)"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If x figures in something that happens, x is part of that happening.","e":"The weather figured prominently in their plans."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you figure that something is true, you think that it is true.","e":"Few people figured that he would win."},{"m":"If you figure something out, you think about it until you understand it.","e":"He figured out that she was speaking Italian."}]}]},"sisterhood":{"h":"sisterhood","i":"/ˈsɪs.tɚhʊd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Wodencafe-sisterhood.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Sisterhood is the relationship between sisters."},{"m":"(uncountable) Sisterhood is the relationship between all women. All women on earth and living are considered \"sisters\"."},{"m":"(countable) A sisterhood is a group of sisters, especially women who agree to live or work together for religious purposes."}]}]},"clothing":{"h":"clothing","i":"/ˈkloʊðɪŋ/","a":"en-us-clothing.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) When you speak of clothes in general, you speak of clothing.","e":"s, shirts, and trousers are types of clothing."}]}]},"pattern":{"h":"pattern","i":"/ˈpat(ə)n/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-pattern.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pattern is a design that uses the same set of elements many times in the same order.","e":"The table cloth had a simple pattern of red and white squares."},{"m":"(countable) The combined and for an individual or a group of people describes a pattern.","e":"The people of Spain have a pattern of resting in the afternoon and eating dinner late at night."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you pattern something, you make it using a pattern.","e":"Much of crime fiction is patterned from true police."}]}]},"provide":{"h":"provide","i":"/prəˈvaɪd/","a":"en-us-provide.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you provide something, you make it available.","e":"The restaurant provided food for the party."},{"m":"(transitive) Something is provided when an agreement or legal process requires it.","e":"s provide punishment for crimes."},{"m":"(intransitive) When you provide, you give means of support.","e":"s try to provide for their children."}]}]},"pleasant":{"h":"pleasant","i":"/'plεzənt/","a":"en-us-pleasant.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is pleasant, it is enjoyable or agreeable.","e":"When it rains in the summer, it is a pleasant event."},{"m":"A pleasant person is one who is socially acceptable or polite.","e":"The man was pleasant with his smile and quiet laugh."}]}]},"speech":{"h":"speech","i":"/ˈspiːtʃ/","a":"en-us-speech.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) When we have speech, we have the ability to speak.","e":"Speech is a special human ability."},{"m":"(countable) When we give a speech, we speak to a group of people.","e":"The valedictorian gave a speech to all of the students in his school."}]}]},"fill":{"h":"fill","i":"/fɪl/","a":"en-us-fill.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you fill something, you put something in it until there is no space left.","e":"She added some games to fill the gap in the schedule."},{"m":"If you fill in something, you give the missing information, especially personal information on a form.","e":"She gave me another form to fill in for housing benefit."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you fill out, your body reaches its adult shape, especially women's breasts and men's shoulders."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The full amount of food or drink that a person can eat or drink.","e":"Don't feed him any more, he's had his fill."},{"m":"(uncountable) Fill is extra material, often of low quality, used to give something more volume.","e":"They used the rocks as fill under the new house."}]}]},"pass":{"h":"pass","i":"/pɑːs/","a":"en-us-pass.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you pass something, it was ahead of you and you move so that it is now behind you.","e":"Please, step to the right and let faster people pass on your left."},{"m":"If a bill, law, motion, etc. passes, it is accepted, usually after a vote.","e":"The House passed a law that makes it a crime to have sex with anyone under age 16."},{"m":"If you pass a test, exam, etc., you get a score that is good enough, often over 50%.","e":"You passed the test. In fact, you got 7 out of 10 correct."},{"m":"If time passes, it moves from future to past.","e":"I'm bored here. The only thing that helps me pass the time is your letters."},{"m":"If a road, river, railway, etc. passes a place, it continues from one side of the place to the other side.","e":"They are building a 150-kilometer road that passes through Yasuni Park."},{"m":"If you pass something to someone, you give it to them, usually by hand.","e":"Could you pass me the salt, please?"},{"m":"(intransitive) If something passes, it happens.","e":"What has passed today must remain a secret."},{"m":"If you pass a ball, puck, etc. you throw, kick, or hit it to another member of your team.","e":"He passed to Lafleur, who put the ball in for the goal."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pass is a piece of paper, plastic, etc. that allows somebody to enter a building, vehicle, or area.","e":"We have a season's pass for the ski hill."},{"m":"(countable) A pass is a score on a test, exam, etc. that is good enough, often over 50%. Also a person or paper that gets this score.","e":"On the last test there were only five passes; everyone else failed."},{"m":"(countable) A pass is a throw, kick, hit, etc. of a ball, puck, etc. to another member of your team.","e":"Robert's pass in front of the net is blocked by the goalie."},{"m":"(countable) A pass is a place in a mountain that is easy to travel.","e":"The mountain pass was blocked, which made it difficult to get across."},{"m":"(countable) A pass is one case of a repeated action or process.","e":"We caught some new mistakes on the third pass."}]}]},"product":{"h":"product","i":"/ˈprɑːˌdʌkt/","a":"en-us-product.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A product is an item that can be bought.","e":"That store sells many different products."},{"m":"(uncountable) The product is the end result of a process, such as someone's efforts or of a certain situation.","e":"Skill is the product of hours of practice; His reaction was the product of hunger and fatigue."},{"m":"(countable) A product is the number you get when you multiply two other numbers.","e":"The product of 2 and 3 is 6."},{"m":"(countable) A product is a chemical substance that is made as a result of a chemical reaction."}]}]},"prevent":{"h":"prevent","i":"/prəˈvɛnt/","a":"en-us-prevent.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you prevent something, you stop it from happening.","e":"To prevent accidents, you must do everything with care."}]}]},"creation":{"h":"creation","i":"/kriːˈeɪʃən/","a":"en-us-creation.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The act of creating is called creation.","e":"The creation of a house takes time."},{"m":"(countable) A creation is something that is created.","e":"The new dress was a great creation of beauty."},{"m":"(uncountable) The time at beginning of the world and when God created everything is called creation.","e":"The Bible says that the creation took six days and God rested on the seventh."},{"m":"(uncountable) The whole world is the creation in many religious traditions.","e":"The Bible says that God made all of the creation in six days."}]}]},"modern":{"h":"modern","i":"/ˈmɒd(ə)n/","a":"en-us-modern.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is modern, it happened in current times.","e":"The new house has all modern conveniences."},{"m":"Some new styles or forms of art and fiction writing are called modern.","e":"Much modern art looks odd to many people."}]}]},"redundant":{"h":"redundant","i":"/rɪˈdʌn.dənt/","a":"en-au-redundant.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"; more than is needed."},{"m":"ing oneself or using extra words; saying the same thing again in a slightly different way."},{"m":"(mainly UK) Being dismissed from a job because you are no longer needed."}]}]},"particular":{"h":"particular","i":"/pɜrˈtɪkjəlɜr/","a":"en-us-particular.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A particular thing is the one that you mean and not any other.","e":"Usually it is not allowed, but in this particular case, it's OK."},{"m":"A particular thing is a special or great one.","e":"She took no particular interest in what they were saying."},{"m":"If somebody is particular, they will accept only the best or only things that they like."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"If you talk about something in particular, you mean that more than other; especially.","e":"It's true of many small cars, but the Honda in particular."},{"m":"(countable) (usually plural) The particulars are the detailed information.","e":"The two stories are quite similar, though they differ in some particulars."}]}]},"finance":{"h":"finance","i":"/ˈfaɪnæns/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-finance.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Finance is activities related to banking and money, especially by government.","e":"The minister of finance announced that taxes would increase by 1% in May."},{"m":"(plural) Your finances is the money that you have.","e":"She had managed to raise sufficient finances to enable her and her family to travel to Australia."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you finance something, you provide money for it.","e":"The soccer team was partly financed by a local business."}]}]},"finish":{"h":"finish","i":"/ˈfɪnɪʃ/","a":"en-us-finish.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something finishes, it stops and doesn't start again; it comes to the end.","e":"I finish work at 4:30 and I get home at 5:00."},{"m":"(transitive) If something finishes somebody off, it uses all their energy or it kills them.","e":"That last run around the track completely finished me off."},{"m":"(transitive) If you finish something up, you use the last of it.","e":"I finished up the milk this morning. There's none left."},{"m":"If you are finished with something, you don't need it anymore."},{"m":"(transitive) If you finish the surface of something, especially wood, you make it smooth and ready to use."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The finish is the last part or end of something.","e":"As the runners come to the finish, they are side by side."},{"m":"The finish is the way a surface looks after it has been made smooth and ready to use.","e":"The oil gives the wood a smooth, deep finish."}]}]},"fought":{"h":"fought","i":"/fɔːt/","a":"en-us-fought.ogg","l":"fight","q":"verb"},"fell":{"h":"fell","i":"/fɛl/","a":"en-us-fell.ogg","l":"fall","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you fell something, you make it fall.","e":"He felled the tree by chopping it down with an axe."}]}]},"imagine":{"h":"imagine","i":"/ɪˈmæd͡ʒ.ɪn/","a":"en-us-imagine.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you imagine something, you make a picture of it in your head.","e":"Imagine that you're sitting at a table with all the food you can eat."},{"m":"(transitive) If you imagine something, you think or believe it without knowing.","e":"I imagine everybody will be there."}]}]},"score":{"h":"score","i":"/skɔː/","a":"en-us-score.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The numbers used to tell who is winning in a sport or game.","e":"The final score for the ball game was 30 to 17."},{"m":"A copy of written music, usually for an orchestra. Usually, this means all the written music for all the players for a piece of music.","e":"I have the whole score for the Brandenburg Concertos."},{"m":"The results of a test or quiz.","e":"You must earn a score of at least 70 to pass the test."},{"m":"The number 20. This is an old meaning; people don't use score for this much any more.","e":"Four score and seven years ago."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To gain points in a game, so that your score is increased.","e":"The basketball player just scored three points!"},{"m":"To get a certain result on a text or quiz.","e":"I scored a 95 on the test!"},{"m":"To have sex."},{"m":"To get something.","e":"I scored some tickets to the game tonight."},{"m":"To make a groove in paper or cardboard.","e":"If you score the paper first, gently using a knife along the edge of a ruler, then you'll be able to fold it neatly and straight."}]}]},"ought":{"h":"ought","i":"/ɔːt/","a":"en-us-ought.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you ought to do something, doing it is better than not doing it.","e":"I think perhaps we ought to help her."},{"m":"If something ought to be true, you have reason to believe it, but you don't know, or it is not true.","e":"He ought to be here by now."}]}]},"raise":{"h":"raise","i":"/reɪz/","a":"en-us-raise.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you raise something you make it higher; that is you move it up.","e":"I need to raise the car off the ground to fix it from below."},{"m":"(transitive) If you raise children or animals, you care for them until they have grown up (become adults).","e":"I raised the children after their mother died."},{"m":"(transitive) If you raise food (plants or animals) you grow it on a farm. This is also used for plants that are not food, like cotton or tobacco.","e":"My grandfather raised corn and chickens."},{"m":"(transitive) If you raise a number, you make it bigger."},{"m":"(transitive) If you raise an idea you start talking about it.","e":"Why did you have to raise the issue of abortion?"},{"m":"(transitive) If you raise somebody in, you make a bigger bet."},{"m":"(transitive) If someone raises the dead they make dead people alive again.","e":"Jesus is said to have raised the dead."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A raise is an increase in pay at work.","e":"I have worked here long enough I should get a raise."},{"m":"In gambling, a raise is an increased bet."}]}]},"heard":{"h":"heard","i":"/'hɜːd/","a":"en-us-heard.ogg","l":"hear","q":"verb"},"built":{"h":"built","i":"/'bɪlt/","a":"en-us-built.ogg","l":"build","q":"verb"},"lay":{"h":"lay","i":"/leɪ/","a":"en-us-lay.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you lay something, you place it down flat.","e":"Sally carefully laid out her clothing on the bed."},{"m":"(transitive) When an animal lays an egg, it makes and places it outside its body."}]}]},"birthday":{"h":"birthday","i":"/ˈbɜːθ.deɪ/","a":"en-us-birthday.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The day you were born.","e":"They will need your birthday on the application."},{"m":"The same day of the year you were born, happening every year. Often there is a party for a person's birthday.","e":"My birthday is September 14."}]}]},"bedroom":{"h":"bedroom","i":"/ˈbɛdˌrum/","a":"en-us-bedroom.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A room in a house that is used for sleeping. This is where the bed is kept.","e":"I hate camping. I wish I was back in my bedroom, sleeping in my own bed."}]}]},"xylophone":{"h":"xylophone","i":"/ˈzɑɪ.lə.ˌfon/","a":"en-us-xylophone.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A xylophone is a musical instrument made from wooden bars in a row. The bars are hit with sticks or mallets to make music."}]}]},"industrialise":{"h":"industrialise","i":"/ɪnˈdʌstriəlaɪz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-industrialize.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If a place or business industrialises, it adds factories and machines to do work that was previously done by hand or not done at all.","e":"France was slow to industrialise for most of the Third Republic (1870–1940)."}]}]},"industrialize":{"h":"industrialize","i":"/ɪnˈdʌstriəlaɪz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-industrialize.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If a place or business industrializes, it adds factories and machines to do work that was previously done by hand or not done at all.","e":"France was slow to industrialize for most of the Third Republic (1870–1940)."}]}]},"indeed":{"h":"indeed","i":"/ɪnˈdiːd/","a":"en-us-indeed.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"You use indeed to make your words stronger.","e":"OK David, thanks very much indeed for your time."},{"m":"You use indeed to add surprising information.","e":"Often we didn't know their phone numbers. Nor indeed did many of them even have phones."}]}]},"inform":{"h":"inform","i":"/ɪnˈfɔrm/","a":"en-us-inform.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you inform someone of something, you give them knowledge about it.","e":"Unfortunately, they did not fully inform the public of the problem."},{"m":"(transitive) If something informs your opinion, decision, etc., it helps you come to it.","e":"Our decision was informed by a good deal of research."}]}]},"specified":{"h":"specified","a":"en-us-specified.ogg","l":"specify","q":"verb"},"smallest":{"h":"smallest","i":"/ˈsmɔːlɪst/","a":"en-us-smallest.ogg","l":"small","q":"adjective","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"The smallest thing is the most small thing.","e":"When the smallest thing gets in your eye, it can hurt very much."}]}]},"insure":{"h":"insure","i":"/ɪnˈʃʊə/","a":"en-us-insure.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you insure something, you pay money so that if something bad happens to it, you will get more money.","e":"We will insure your home against damage caused by fire."},{"m":"Insure is a less common spelling of ensure."}]}]},"goods":{"h":"goods","i":"/ɡʊdz/","a":"en-us-goods.ogg","l":"good","q":"noun"},"worn":{"h":"worn","i":"/wɔrn/","a":"en-us-worn.ogg","l":"wear","q":"verb"},"invest":{"h":"invest","i":"/ɪnˈvɛst/","a":"en-us-invest.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you invest your money, you use your money to make more money.","e":"IBM may invest new money in the company."},{"m":"If you invest in something, you spend time or money to make it better.","e":"The province has invested $20 million to improve transportation in cities."},{"m":"(transitive) If you invest someone with a power, you give it to them."},{"m":"(transitive) If something invests someone with a quality, it makes them appear to have that quality.","e":"His white hair invested him with a sense of intelligence."}]}]},"banzai":{"h":"banzai","i":"/bɑːnˈzaɪ/","s":[{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"A Japanese war cry.","e":"The soldier cried banzai as he attacked his enemy."}]}]},"bateau":{"h":"bateau","i":"/bæˈtoʊ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-bateau.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bateau is a light river boat with a flat bottom.","e":"The guide used a bateau to get us across the river."}]}]},"barrack":{"h":"barrack","i":"/ˈbæ.rək/","a":"en-us-barrack.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A barrack is a building for soldiers to live and sleep in. The building is more commonly called barracks. A barrack used to mean \"a temporary hut\", but now is usually used for permanent buildings."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To live in barracks.","e":"The soldier was barracked during his stay at basic training."},{"m":"To shout or jeer at.","e":"My opponent barracked me during our match."}]}]},"assumption":{"h":"assumption","i":"/əˈsʌmp.ʃən/","a":"en-us-assumption.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An assumption is a guess or belief about something without having enough information to know if it is true. In maths or science: something assumed to be true in order to build an argument or calculation.","e":"You shouldn't make the assumption that guns are only a problem in big cities."}]}]},"bible":{"h":"bible","i":"/'baɪbəl/","a":"en-us-bible.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bible is any book that is considered an authority in a particular subject.","e":"The Blue Book is the bible for the value of used automobiles."}]}]},"involve":{"h":"involve","i":"/ɪnˈvɒlv/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-involve.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If an activity involves something, then that thing is used in or is part of the activity.","e":"The job involves the use of special computer software."}]}]},"fever":{"h":"fever","i":"/ˈfiːvə/","a":"en-us-fever.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A fever is when you are hot because you are sick and your temperature will be higher than normal.","e":"I took some medicine to lower my fever."}]}]},"likely":{"h":"likely","i":"/ˈlaɪkli/","a":"en-us-likely.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is likely, it is probably true or will probably happen.","e":"It seems likely that he will miss the meeting."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"You use likely to say that you think something is true or will happen.","e":"Likely, over the next few years, more changes will happen."}]}]},"drum":{"h":"drum","i":"/'drʌm/","a":"en-us-drum.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A drum is a musical instrument with a skin that you hit to make music.","e":"My cousin plays drums."},{"m":"(countable) A drum is kind of big barrel.","e":"They were keeping garbage in an old oil drum."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you are drumming you are making music with a drum or drums.","e":"I saw him drumming with the band."},{"m":"If you are drumming, you are hitting or tapping something like it was a drum.","e":"Sometimes I drum on my desk with my fingers."}]}]},"acceptable":{"h":"acceptable","i":"/æk.ˈsɛp.tə.bəl/","a":"en-us-acceptable.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is acceptable it is capable of being accepted or is worth being accepted.","e":"You ideas are acceptable to the group."},{"m":"When something is welcome or pleasing, it is acceptable.","e":"Any kind words for my work are acceptable."}]}]},"drumming":{"h":"drumming","i":"/'drʌmɪŋ/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Drumming is the sound of drums.","e":"We could hear the drumming from far away."},{"m":"(uncountable) Drumming is the act of hitting a drum to make music."}]}]},"completely":{"h":"completely","i":"/kəmˈpliːtli/","a":"en-us-completely.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"When something is completely some quality, it is absolutely that quality, in every way.","e":"The man was completely honest in his business."}]}]},"flexible":{"h":"flexible","i":"/ˈflɛk.sɪ.bəl/","a":"en-us-flexible.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is flexible, it can bend.","e":"The thin wood stick was so flexible that it would bend but not break."},{"m":"By extension, the word is used as a metaphor. For example, when a person or thing is flexible, they can change.","e":"Jim was very flexible and enjoyed every new experience when he travelled."}]}]},"successful":{"h":"successful","i":"/səkˈsɛsfl̩/","a":"en-us-successful.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are successful, you are effective at something.","e":"The successful business man knows how to get money for his work."},{"m":"If you have done something right, you are successful.","e":"The cook was successful when she made the best pepperoni pizza in town."}]}]},"quit":{"h":"quit","i":"/kwɪt/","a":"en-us-quit.ogg","l":"quit","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you quit something, you stop doing it; that is, you do not do it any more.","e":"It was very hard to quit smoking."},{"m":"If you quit a job, it means you are not going to work anymore. After you quit, you will no longer have that job.","e":"I'm quitting my job now!"}]}]},"permission":{"h":"permission","i":"/pəˈmɪʃən/","a":"en-us-permission.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"If you have permission to do something, then the person who has authority over you or over that thing allows you to do it.","e":"My father gave me permission to go to the city."}]}]},"listen":{"h":"listen","i":"/ˈlɪs.ən/","a":"en-uk-to listen.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you listen to something, you try to hear and understand it.","e":"Shhh! Listen! Did you hear that?"},{"m":"(intransitive) If you listen to someone, you agree with them, believe them, or do what they tell you.","e":"Don't listen to him. He doesn't know what he's talking about."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) If you give something a listen, you try to hear and understand it.","e":"Do you want to have a listen to this new band?"}]}]},"load":{"h":"load","i":"/loʊd/","a":"en-us-load.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A load is something carried, often something heavy.","e":"The truck arrived with a load of dog food."},{"m":"Loads/a load of something is a lot of it.","e":"We've had a load of problems ever since we got the new stuff."},{"m":"(uncountable) Your load is how much work you have.","e":"We hired another person to spread the load a bit more."},{"m":"(uncountable) Load is the amount electrical power produced."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you load x on y, you put x on y to be carried. Usually there is a lot of x, and/or it is heavy.","e":"We loaded the boxes on the truck and set off for Vancouver."},{"m":"(transitive) If you load a machine, you put in supplies that the machine uses.","e":"He loaded the gun, brought it up, and shot the deer in one continuous motion."}]}]},"lord":{"h":"lord","i":"/lɔːd/","a":"en-us-lord.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The Lord is a Judeo-Christian title for God.","e":"Please join me in the Lord's prayer."},{"m":"(countable) A lord is a person who has authority over others; a ruler."},{"m":"(countable) A Lord is a title given by a king or queen.","e":"The royals are sailing with friends Lord and Lady Romsey and their two children."},{"m":"(countable) Lord is a title of respect used with mayors, judges, etc.","e":"The lord mayor will be giving a speech at 12:30."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) To lord means to act like a lord."}]}]},"physics":{"h":"physics","i":"/ˈfɪz.ɪks/","a":"en-us-physics.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Physics is the kind of science that is about how the world and universe work. Usually, physics is about things like movement, heat, light, sound, and electricity."}]}]},"behave":{"h":"behave","i":"/bɪˈheɪv/","a":"en-us-behave.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"How you behave is what you do or how you act.","e":"Why do you behave like that."},{"m":"How something behaves is what it usually does.","e":"We want to know how fire behaves in space."},{"m":"If you are behaving you are being good.","e":"I wish the children would behave."}]}]},"proxy":{"h":"proxy","i":"/ˈprɒk.si/","a":"en-us-proxy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A proxy is something or someone that acts in place of another."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A \"proxy x\" is an x that is being used as a proxy.","e":"He used a proxy computer for the operation."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To proxy is to serve as a proxy."}]}]},"corn":{"h":"corn","i":"/kɔːn/","a":"en-us-corn.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Corn is a kind of grain, usually with large yellow seeds, that is often eaten (also called maize).","e":"We will be eating corn tomorrow."},{"m":"(uncountable) The plant corn grows on.","e":"We planted some corn in our garden last year."},{"m":"Any kind of grain.","e":"We put several barley corns into the soup."}]}]},"maize":{"h":"maize","i":"/meɪz/","a":"en-us-maize.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Maize is a kind of grain, usually with large yellow seeds, that is often eaten (also called corn).","e":"We will be eating maize tomorrow."},{"m":"The plant corn grows on.","e":"We planted some maize in out garden last year."}]}]},"flour":{"h":"flour","i":"/ˈflaʊə/","a":"en-us-flour.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Flour is grain (or other plants parts) that has been crushed."}]}]},"undead":{"h":"undead","i":"/ʌnˈdɛd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-undead.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is undead they are not dead or alive, or they are both dead and alive.","e":"s, zombies, and vampires are undead."},{"m":"Someone (or something) that is undead.","e":"We watched a movie about the undead."}]}]},"zombie":{"h":"zombie","i":"/ˈzɒmbi/","a":"en-au-zombie.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A zombie is type of fictional creature. It is a dead body that has been brought back to life. Usually a zombie moves slowly, growls, and will want to eat people's brains."}]}]},"vampire":{"h":"vampire","i":"/ˈvæmpaɪə/","a":"en-au-vampire.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mythical person who is dead but acts alive and drinks blood."},{"m":"(countable) A person who has a disease called vampirism. People who have this disease are sensitive to light, have a desire for blood, and can see well at night."},{"m":"(countable) A person who seems to take your energy; that is, they make you tired."},{"m":"Someone or something that drains (takes away) something."}]}]},"wheat":{"h":"wheat","i":"/wiːt/","a":"en-us-wheat.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A kind of grain that is used to make flour for bread.","e":"Farmers have grown wheat for thousands of years."},{"m":"(countable) A certain kind of wheat.","e":"We grow two wheats here, hard wheat and soft wheat."},{"m":"(uncountable) A light brown color, like that of wheat."}]}]},"cigarette":{"h":"cigarette","i":"/ˈsɪ.ɡə.rɛt/","a":"en-us-cigarette.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cigarette is tobacco that has been rolled in paper for.","e":"He went outside and lit a cigarette."}]}]},"maybe":{"h":"maybe","i":"/ˈmeɪbi/","a":"en-us-maybe.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If you say that maybe something will happen or that maybe it is true, you mean there is a chance of those things.","e":"Maybe someday I'll learn how to drive."},{"m":"You use maybe when you are not sure about something.","e":"Maybe you ought to look at this again."}]}]},"matter":{"h":"matter","i":"/ˈmætə/","a":"en-us-matter.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A matter is something that you can talk about or do something about a topic or a situation.","e":"Government must make these changes as a matter of urgency."},{"m":"(uncountable) Matter is the stuff that everything is made of.","e":"Cities are trying to separate organic matter and other garbage."},{"m":"You use, \"as a matter of fact\" to add information that may be surprising.","e":"\"Have you met anyone interesting over there?\" \"As a matter of fact, I met a whole bunch of people just this afternoon."},{"m":"You use \"what's the matter\" to ask somebody why they are unhappy, or why there is a problem."},{"m":"You use \"for that matter\" when you have just thought about something that you are comparing to something else.","e":"He wasn't very nice today. For that matter, he's never nice."},{"m":"If something is only a matter of time, it may not happen now, but it will happen after some time.","e":"It's only a matter of days now before I start the new job."},{"m":"You use \"no matter what\" to say that even if other things change, a particular thing will not change.","e":"I'll be there no matter what. I promise."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) (usually negative) If something doesn't matter, it is not important.","e":"\"Should I put it up there?\" \"Oh, it doesn't matter. Put it anywhere.\""}]}]},"mile":{"h":"mile","i":"/maɪl/","a":"en-us-mile.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mile is a measurement of distance. It is equal to 1.609&nbsp;km (5280 feet, or 1760 yards).","e":"It's about a mile and a half to the school."},{"m":"(countable) For ships and airplanes a nautical mile is equal to 1.853&nbsp;km (6080.20 feet)."},{"m":"(countable) You use miles to talk about a long distance.","e":"We're miles from home and we have no food or radio."}]}]},"kilometer":{"h":"kilometer","i":"/kɪləmiɾɚ/","a":"en-us-kilometre.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A kilometer is a measurement of distance. It is 1,000 meters (3,280.8 feet or 0.621 miles).","e":"Four times around the track is one kilometer."}]}]},"shelves":{"h":"shelves","l":"shelf","q":"noun"},"mister":{"h":"mister","i":"/ˈmɪstə/","a":"en-us-Mr.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"You use mister before a man's name, usually the last name or the full name.","e":"Mister Brakel, the doctor will see you now."},{"m":"You call a man mister when you don't know his name.","e":"Excuse me, mister, I think you dropped this."},{"m":"You use mister before a man's title for certain titles, such as justice, mayor, president, etc.","e":"Yes, we can do that Mr. Mayor."}]}]},"miss":{"h":"miss","i":"/mɪs/","a":"en-us-miss.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you miss something, you don't hit it.","e":"I missed the target."},{"m":"If you miss someone or something when they are gone or away, you wish they were there with you.","e":"I miss you so much. When are you coming home?"},{"m":"If you miss an event, you aren't able to go.","e":"I'm going to have to miss the party because I can't find a babysitter."},{"m":"If you miss something, you aren't able to get on it in time.","e":"I'm sorry I'm late; I missed the bus."},{"m":"If you miss something, you don't understand it.","e":"You're missing the point of what I'm saying."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"You use miss before an unmarried woman's name, usually the last name or the full name.","e":"Miss Brakel, the doctor will see you now."},{"m":"You call a young woman miss when you don't know her name.","e":"Excuse me, miss, I think you dropped this."}]}]},"mention":{"h":"mention","i":"/ˈmɛnʃən/","a":"en-us-mention.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you mention something, you say it or talk about it, but only very briefly.","e":"Father Poole became very excited when I mentioned your name."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mention of something, is when somebody mentions it.","e":"Kavanagh's book makes no mention of Katherine's name."}]}]},"minister":{"h":"minister","i":"/ˈmɪnɨstɚ/","a":"en-us-minister.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A minister is a politician who is in charge of a part of the government.","e":"The Minister of Defense has said that the army will remain in the city for at least two more weeks."},{"m":"(countable) A minister is a person who acts officially in a Christian church.","e":"The minister who performed our wedding ceremony was a great speaker."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you minister, you give help, especially through your words or by.","e":"To minister, a church must be sensitive to what is hurting its community."}]}]},"moment":{"h":"moment","i":"/'məʊmənt/","a":"en-us-moment.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A moment is a very short time. It is not an exact measurement.","e":"Geraldine sat on the bed and thought for a moment."},{"m":"(uncountable) importance","e":"It was a lie, but one of no great moment."}]}]},"ere":{"h":"ere","i":"/ɛə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-ere.wav","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"."}]}]},"okay":{"h":"okay","i":"/ˌəʊˈkeɪ/","a":"en-us-okay.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"You use okay to show that you agree with something.","e":"\"I'll be late tonight, mom.\" \"Okay dear!\""},{"m":"You use okay to check if someone agrees with you.","e":"I'm leaving now, okay?"},{"m":"You use okay to show that you are changing topic.","e":"Does anybody have questions? No? Okay, let's look at the homework then."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is okay, they are fine or not hurt.","e":"Oh, sorry! Are you okay? Let me help you."},{"m":"If something is okay, it is good enough, fine, or not bad.","e":"\"Do you like this?\" \"It's okay, I guess. Do you have anything nicer?\""},{"m":"If someone is okay, they are nice.","e":"He's an okay guy."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you okay something, you approve it.","e":"The manager has to okay it before I can let you in."},{"m":"(transitive) If you okay something with somebody, you ask them to approve it.","e":"Did you okay this with your dad?"}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (usually singular) If you give something your okay, you approve it.","e":"We got the okay to go ahead."}]}]},"ok":{"h":"OK","i":"/ˌəʊˈkeɪ/","a":"en-us-okay.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"You use OK to show that you agree with something.","e":"\"I'll be late tonight, mom.\" \"OK, dear!\""},{"m":"You use OK to check if someone agrees with you.","e":"I'm leaving now, OK?"},{"m":"You use OK to show that you are changing topic.","e":"Does anybody have questions? No? OK, let's look at the homework then."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is OK, they are fine or not hurt.","e":"Oh, sorry! Are you OK? Let me help you."},{"m":"If something is OK, it is good enough, fine, or not bad.","e":"\"Do you like this?\" \"It's OK, I guess. Do you have anything nicer?\""},{"m":"If someone is OK, they are nice.","e":"He's an OK guy."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you OK something, you approve it.","e":"The manager has to OK it before I can let you in."},{"m":"(transitive) If you OK something with somebody, you ask them to approve it.","e":"Did you OK this with your dad?"}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (usually singular) If you give something your OK, you approve it.","e":"We got the OK to go ahead."}]}]},"donation":{"h":"donation","i":"/dəʊˈneɪʃən/","a":"en-us-donation.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A donation is a gift of money or something useful to a person or organization.","e":"Your donation was greatly appreciated. Be sure to donate canned goods to the shelter again next year."}]}]},"operate":{"h":"operate","i":"/ˈɒpəreɪt/","a":"en-us-operate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you operate a machine, you control it.","e":"Everyone on board is able to operate the ship."},{"m":"(intransitive) If a machine operates, it works.","e":"Does the device operate independently or does it need to connect to other devices?"},{"m":"If organizations or people operate, they work or do business.","e":"The business will continue to operate under the same name."},{"m":"(intransitive) If a doctor operates, he cuts into a client's body to fix it."}]}]},"opportunity":{"h":"opportunity","i":"/ˌɒp.əˈtjuː.nɪ.ti/","a":"en-us-opportunity.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An opportunity is a time, place, or situation in which something can happen, usually something good.","e":"Sleep provides an opportunity for the body to repair itself."}]}]},"secure":{"h":"secure","i":"/səˈkjʊə(r)/","a":"en-us-secure.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is secure, it is firmly held in place and probably will not fall.","e":"Mike's bicycle is very secure on the bike rack."},{"m":"When a person is secure, they are not afraid of anything and are in a good emotional state."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you secure something, you make it secure in one of the ways listed above."}]}]},"securities":{"h":"securities","l":"security","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Securities are financial documents, like stocks, bonds and notes."}]}]},"securely":{"h":"securely","i":"/səˈkjʊrli/","a":"en-us-securely.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"In a secure manner.","e":"Mike placed his bicycle securely on the rack, ensuring that it would not fall."}]}]},"urban":{"h":"urban","i":"/ˈɜːrbən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-urban.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is urban, it is related to.","e":"an urban neighborhood or region"}]}]},"oppose":{"h":"oppose","i":"/əˈpəʊz/","a":"en-us-oppose.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you oppose something, you try to stop it or fight against it.","e":"We would strongly oppose any changes."}]}]},"everyday":{"h":"everyday","i":"/ˈɛvriˌdeɪ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-everyday.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"something that is done a lot or happens a lot; something that is ordinary","e":"These are my everyday clothes."}]}]},"mundane":{"h":"mundane","i":"/mʌnˈdeɪn/","a":"en-us-mundane.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"; something that happens a lot."},{"m":"Not new.","e":"My life is very mundane. I wish it was more exciting."}]}]},"protect":{"h":"protect","i":"/prəˈtɛkt/","a":"en-us-protect.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you protect something or someone, you keep it safe; you stop it from being harmed.","e":"The knight protected the castle."}]}]},"original":{"h":"original","i":"/əˈrɪʤənl/","a":"en-us-original.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"The original person or thing, happened or existed before others of its kind.","e":"The book has been translated from the original Russian version."},{"m":"If something is original, it is new and creative.","e":"Mendelssohn's C minor Trio is a highly original work."},{"m":"If you are original, you are creative and different from other people.","e":"He's one of Canada's most original thinkers."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An original is a piece of writing or a work of art that is not a copy.","e":"I'll give you a copy and we'll keep the original here."}]}]},"mythic":{"h":"mythic","i":"/ˈmɪθɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-mythic.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is mythic it is from a myth (a story about gods).","e":"There are many mythic stories about the Norse god Thor."},{"m":"If something is mythic it is not real or not true; that is, it is like something from an fictional story or old myth.","e":"A dragon is a mythic animal."},{"m":"If something is mythic or of mythic proportions it is very great or amazing.","e":"His skill with the baseball bat was mythic."}]}]},"mythical":{"h":"mythical","i":"/ˈmɪθɪkəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-mythical.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is mythical it is from a myth (a story about gods).","e":"There are many mythical stories about the Norse god Thor."},{"m":"If something is mythical it is not real or not true; that is, it is like something from a fictional story or old myth.","e":"A dragon is a mythical animal."},{"m":"If something is mythical or of mythical proportions it is very great or amazing.","e":"His skill with the baseball bat was mythical."}]}]},"myth":{"h":"myth","i":"/mɪθ/","a":"en-us-myth.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A myth is a story about gods and great heroes. Usually these gods are seen as very human, but with great power. The word myth is usually used for stories from old religions that few people believe any more.","e":"There are many myths about the Norse god Thor."},{"m":"(countable) A myth is a story that is not true."},{"m":"(countable) A myth is something many people believe but that is not true.","e":"It is only a myth that people use only 10% of their brains."}]}]},"mythology":{"h":"mythology","i":"/mɪˈθɒləʤi/","a":"en-us-mythology.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Mythology is the study of stories about gods. Such stories are called myths."},{"m":"(countable) A mythology is all the myths from a certain religion."},{"m":"(countable) A mythology is all the background stories from a fictional world.","e":"Tolkien invented an complex mythology for Middle Earth."}]}]},"perhaps":{"h":"perhaps","i":"/pəˈhæps/","a":"en-us-perhaps.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If you say that perhaps something will happen or that perhaps it is true, you mean it may happen or be true.","e":"Perhaps someday I'll learn how to drive."},{"m":"You use perhaps when you are not sure about something.","e":"We shouldn't do it, we don't want to do it, and perhaps most importantly, we don't have the money to do it."}]}]},"union":{"h":"union","i":"/juːŋjən/","a":"en-us-union.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A union is when many things are joined together.","e":"The League of Nations was a union between many nations."},{"m":"(countable) A union may be the act of joining.","e":"The union of these two companies was painless."}]}]},"otherwise":{"h":"otherwise","i":"/ˈʌð.əˌwaɪz/","a":"en-us-otherwise.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"You use otherwise to connect two clauses where the second clause shows the bad thing that would happen if the first clause doesn't happen.","e":"You need the proper license. Otherwise you can't do business."},{"m":"You use otherwise to connect two clauses where the second clause shows what would have happened if the first clause hadn't happened.","e":"I missed the bus. Otherwise, I would have been here earlier."},{"m":"If you think or say otherwise, you don't agree.","e":"She says we should put him in piano lessons, but I think otherwise."},{"m":"apart from something else","e":"She has some cuts, but is otherwise fine."}]}]},"pack":{"h":"pack","i":"/pæk/","a":"en-au-pack.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you pack something, you put it in a container to carry with you.","e":"Did you pack your swimming suit?"},{"m":"When you pack a container, you put things in it to carry with you.","e":"The students have all packed their bags and left for the summer."},{"m":"(transitive) If you pack a place or a container with something (or pack something in a place or container), you put a lot inside.","e":"The hall was packed with visitors."},{"m":"If you pack something like snow or earth, you press it to make it take up less space.","e":"All the runners had packed the earth hard."},{"m":"If you pack a gun, you carry it with you."},{"m":"If you pack something away, you put it away in a container."},{"m":"If you pack it in, you give up."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pack is a container that things are sold in.","e":"Cigarettes were selling for over $10 a pack."},{"m":"(countable) A pack is a bag used to carry things, usually on your back.","e":"My spare clothes are in my pack."},{"m":"(countable) A pack of cards is a set of 52 playing cards."},{"m":"(countable) A pack is a group of animals, usually that hunt together."},{"m":"(countable) A pack of people is a group, usually not a nice group."},{"m":"(countable) A pack of lies is something that is completely untrue."},{"m":"(countable) An ice pack is something cold that you put on an injury."}]}]},"pardon":{"h":"pardon","i":"/ˈpɑrdən/","a":"en-us-pardon.ogg","s":[{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"You use pardon to show that you didn't hear or understand someone.","e":"\"Could you close the door, please?\" \"Pardon!\" \"Close the door, please.\""},{"m":"You use pardon when you have made a rude sound like a burp."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If a government pardons somebody who is guilty of a crime, it allows them to live as though they had not committed the crime.","e":"The Ethiopian government has pardoned twenty five prisoners who were found guilty in connection to the unrest that rocked the nation."},{"m":"When you pardon someone, you forgive them.","e":"I hope he'll pardon me for what I did to him."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"You say pardon me or I beg your pardon when you didn't hear someone, when you accidentally touch someone, when you want someone's attention, or when you'd like someone to move."},{"m":"(countable) A pardon is given when someone is forgiven.","e":"The soldier was given a pardon for all the acts he had committed while fighting in the war."}]}]},"pence":{"h":"pence","i":"/pɛns/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-pence.wav","l":"penny","q":"noun"},"pension":{"h":"pension","i":"/ˈpɛnʃən/","a":"en-us-pension.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pension is money paid regularly by a government or company to someone who has stopped working, usually because of age or illness.","e":"When her pension ran out, she had to sell her house and move in with her daughter."},{"m":"(countable) In Europe, a pension is a small hotel.","e":"I stayed at a pension during my trip to London."},{"m":"(countable) A pension is what you pay for living in someone else's house or for staying at a small hotel.","e":"Did you remember to pay the landlady the pension?"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If a company pensions a person, they force them to retire on a [[#Noun|unpension]]."}]}]},"pick":{"h":"pick","i":"/pɪk/","a":"en-us-pick.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you pick something, you choose it.","e":"I have picked the best people to work on this job."},{"m":"If you pick up something, you lift it.","e":"She picked up the glass and put it down again."},{"m":"If you pick up the phone, you answer it."},{"m":"If you pick something up from somewhere, you go and get it.","e":"Mom, can you pick me up from Austin's at 8:00?"},{"m":"If you try to pick up someone you have just met, you talk to them because you want to have sex with them."},{"m":"If you pick fruit, flowers, etc., you take them off the plant.","e":"We spent the morning picking apples in the forest."},{"m":"(transitive) If you pick something from somewhere, you take it out of or away from that place.","e":"After dinner he picked the rice out of the children's hair."},{"m":"If you pick a musical instrument such as a guitar, you play it by pulling its strings and letting them go."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you pick at something, you touch it many times without doing anything.","e":"He was too sick to eat and just picked at his food."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you pick on someone, you are not nice to them in particular.","e":"He was picked on by his brothers for his small size."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pick is a choice.","e":"His pick for Man of the Year was John Smith."},{"m":"(countable) A pick is a tool used to dig.","e":"He dug that hole using a pick."},{"m":"(countable) A pick is something used to play a guitar with.","e":"He forgot his guitar pick."}]}]},"politic":{"h":"politic","i":"/ˈpɒlətɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-politic.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Actions or words that are politic are carefully chosen not to upset people.","e":"The senator gave a very politic reply."},{"m":"political"}]}]},"press":{"h":"press","i":"/prɛs/","a":"en-uk-press.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) (sometimes with plural verb) The press are the people and organisations that report the news.","e":"The president gave an interview with members of the press."},{"m":"(uncountable) The press is the news as it is reported.","e":"The next day, the fire was all over the press."},{"m":"(countable) A press is a company that prints books.","e":"The book was published by Press."},{"m":"(countable) A press is a machine that prints books, newspapers, etc.","e":"Stop the presses! We've got a new story."},{"m":"(countable) A press is a machine that pushes down on something to make it flat or to push out the water or juice."},{"m":"(countable) A press is a time when you push something.","e":"She gave the button a quick press."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you press something, you push it against something.","e":"She pressed her nose against the window."},{"m":"(transitive) If you press clothes, you use an iron to make them flat."},{"m":"If you press someone to do something, you ask them strongly or many times.","e":"When she pressed him for an answer, he hung up the phone."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you press on or forward, you keep going even though it's difficult."},{"m":"(transitive) If you press a weight, you exercise by moving the weight up and away from your body."},{"m":"(transitive) If you press a CD or record, you make a physical copy of it."}]}]},"proceed":{"h":"proceed","i":"/prəˈsiːd/","a":"en-us-proceed.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) When you proceed, you go forward with something.","e":"The reporter proceeded with the interview."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(plural) (formal) The proceeds of some individual project or sale are the money earned from doing it.","e":"We sold the house and bought a small apartment with the proceeds."}]}]},"proper":{"h":"proper","i":"/ˈprɑp.ɚ/","a":"en-us-proper.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"The proper way, place, use, etc. is the right one.","e":"What is the proper way to write a letter?"},{"m":"If something is proper, it is polite or acceptable.","e":"It's not proper for you to live alone like this."},{"m":"(only after the noun) The x proper is the main or important part of x, not the parts near it.","e":"We stayed in a village and only went into the city proper during the day."}]}]},"propose":{"h":"propose","i":"/prəˈpəʊz/","a":"en-us-propose.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you propose something, you say that it should be done or chosen, usually in a formal situation.","e":"She proposed that we should see a film."},{"m":"(transitive) When you propose a new theory or idea, you say that you believe it to be better than old ideas.","e":"I would like to propose that the problems we have had are actually not because of money."},{"m":"(transitive) When you propose to do something, you plan or intend to do it.","e":"What does he propose to do in the future?"},{"m":"(intransitive) If you propose to somebody, you ask them to marry you.","e":"He proposed to his girlfriend outside her house."},{"m":"If you propose a toast, you celebrate somebody by raising a glass and drinking.","e":"I'd like to propose a toast to our new manager."}]}]},"rather":{"h":"rather","i":"/ˈrɑː.ðə/","a":"en-us-rather.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something is rather large, different, difficult, etc., it is quite that way.","e":"I saw something rather unusual this morning."},{"m":"When you would rather do something, you want to do it more than something else.","e":"I would rather see a film (than stay home)."},{"m":"instead of","e":"He went rather than stay behind and be alone."},{"m":"You use or rather to change what you have just said.","e":"I went there, or rather I had planned to go there, last week."}]},{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"You use rather to show that you agree strongly.","e":"\"Did you like the movie?\" \"Rather!\""}]}]},"realize":{"h":"realize","i":"/ˈri.ə.laɪz/","a":"en-us-realize.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you realize something, you become aware of it.","e":"John just realized that he had left his umbrella at home."},{"m":"(transitive) If something is realized, it is made real.","e":"My dreams of starting my own company have been realized."}]}]},"really":{"h":"really","i":"/ˈrɪəli/","a":"en-us-really.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"When something is really a certain way, its very or very much that way.","e":"I really want to see a film."},{"m":"If something really exists or really happens, it does exist or happen.","e":"Are you really going to the show?"}]},{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"You can say \"really?\" when you are surprised.","e":"\"He won yesterday.\" \"Really?\""},{"m":"You can say \"really\" when you agree with something.","e":"\"That girl talks about herself way too much.\" \"Really. She's a nightmare.\""}]}]},"recent":{"h":"recent","i":"/ˈriːsənt/","a":"en-us-recent.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is recent has happened a short while ago.","e":"Has there been any recent news on the dispute?"}]}]},"reckon":{"h":"reckon","i":"/ˈrɛkən/","a":"en-us-reckon.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you reckon that something is true, you think that it is true.","e":"What do you reckon we should do?"},{"m":"(transitive) If you reckon a number, cost, etc., you guess or calculate the value.","e":"I reckon the cost at about $23,000."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you reckon on something, you expect it.","e":"Oh dear, we didn't reckon on so many people."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you reckon with somebody or something powerful or difficult person, you deal with them.","e":"In today's race, the Ethiopians will be a force to be reckoned with."}]}]},"recognize":{"h":"recognize","i":"/ˈrɛkəgnaɪz/","a":"en-us-recognize.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you recognize something, you realize what it is.","e":"I don't recognize him. Is he a friend of yours?"},{"m":"If something is recognized, it is accepted.","e":"You have to recognize that you can't be right all the time."},{"m":"If something is recognized, it is given an award.","e":"John was recognized for his achievements as a scientist."}]}]},"reduce":{"h":"reduce","i":"/rɪˈdjuːs/","a":"en-us-reduce.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If something is reduced, it has been brought down or made smaller.","e":"The new computer system should reduce the number of problems."},{"m":"If you reduce a liquid, you boil it to make it thicker."}]}]},"refer":{"h":"refer","i":"/rɪˈfɜː/","a":"en-us-refer.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you refer to something, you talk or write about it, usually in passing.","e":"The teacher referred to some research, but I didn't know what he meant."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you refer to a book or other source of information, you check it.","e":"You should refer to the dictionary to find the meaning."},{"m":"(intransitive) If x refers to y, x is about y.","e":"The numbers refer to last year's sales."},{"m":"(transitive) If you refer x to y, you send x to y for help or to be dealt with.","e":"He referred me to the science department."}]}]},"regard":{"h":"regard","i":"/rɪˈgɑːd/","a":"en-us-regard.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) If you have regard for something, you respect it.","e":"He has a high regard for his teacher."},{"m":"(uncountable) Regard is how something is though about or looked at.","e":"We do disagree, but only in regard to how much the government is spending."},{"m":"(usually plural) You use Regards as a closing in a formal letter."},{"m":"(usually plural) You ask somebody to give somebody else your regards as a formal way to show your concern for and interest in these people."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you regard something, you think about it.","e":"How do you regard his actions?"},{"m":"(transitive) When you regard something, you look at it.","e":"She regarded him with a smile."}]}]},"remember":{"h":"remember","i":"/rɪˈmɛmbɚ/","a":"en-us-remember.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you remember something that you did or knew before, you can think of it again.","e":"He can't even remember where he left his books."},{"m":"When you remember something, you put it in your mind so you can think of it later.","e":"Please, try to remember how to spell the word."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you remember to do something that you are supposed to do, you do it because you think about it.","e":"Please remember to ask before you take it."}]}]},"report":{"h":"report","i":"/rɪˈpɔrt/","a":"en-us-report.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A report is a description of something that has happened.","e":"There was a recent report on the election."},{"m":"(countable) A report is a document that gives the results of a study of a particular situation."},{"m":"(countable) A report is a loud fast noise.","e":"He could hear the report of the explosion."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If the news reports something, it tells us about it.","e":"The journalist reported that there were riots in the city."},{"m":"When you report something that has happened, you describe it.","e":"They reported to the police that their car had been stolen."},{"m":"(transitive) If you report somebody for something they've done wrong, you tell an official about the problem.","e":"The restaurant was reported to the city because of the dangerous kitchen."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you report somewhere, you go there and give your name.","e":"Visitors to the school should report to the office."}]}]},"return":{"h":"return","i":"/rɪˈtɜːn/","a":"en-us-return.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you return something, you give/put it back.","e":"He returned the lawnmower back to John."},{"m":"(intransitive) When you return to something or somewhere, you go/come back to it.","e":"He returned to China after his trip to Germany."},{"m":"(intransitive) If a feeling, problem, thought, etc. returns, it comes back.","e":"I thought I was better, but the pain in my back has returned."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you return to an activity, you start it again."},{"m":"(transitive) If you return an act, you do the same act to the person who did it first.","e":"She turned her eyes towards him and he returned her her look."},{"m":"(transitive) If you return a ball in sports, you hit it back to the other player.","e":"He was unable to return serves all through the match."},{"m":"(transitive) If you return a profit or loss in business, you make it."},{"m":"(transitive) If you return something to a particular state, you make it that way again.","e":"We need to return the earth to a more healthy state."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Somebody's return is when they come back.","e":"They've planned a celebration for my return home."},{"m":"(countable) Something's return is when it is given back."},{"m":"(countable) A return is something that was bought but has to be taken back to the store, usually because it is broken.","e":"This store does not allow returns unless the customer has a receipt."},{"m":"(countable) The return of something to a particular state is the change back to that state."},{"m":"(countable) Someone's return to an activity is their restarting of the activity."},{"m":"(countable) The return on money is the amount or percent of profit earned on it."},{"m":"(uncountable) If you do something in return for something else, you do it to thank or pay back somebody; you make things balanced again."},{"m":"(countable) The return of a feeling, problem, thought, etc. is when it comes back."},{"m":"Return is a key on a computer keyboard that puts the cursor back at the beginning of a line."},{"m":"(uncountable) A return is a form that you send to the government telling it about your income, your household, etc."},{"m":"(usually plural) The returns in an election are the number of votes."},{"m":"(uncountable) A return is a ticket that takes you where you want to go and back home again."}]}]},"switch":{"h":"switch","i":"/swɪtʃ/","a":"en-us-switch.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you switch something, you change it to something else.","e":"He switched his book with mine."},{"m":"If you switch a light or machine on, you change something so that it has power and can work.","e":"She sat up in bed and switched on the light."},{"m":"If you switch a light or machine off, you change something so that it doesn't have power and can't work.","e":"I switched off the computer and went to bed."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you switch over to something, you change to it, often with no plan to change back to the first thing.","e":"We used to watch CNN, but we've switched over to BBC World News."},{"m":"(transitive) If you switch gears, you change the way you think or act to match a particular situation.","e":"When I come home from work, it takes me a while to switch gears."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you switch with somebody, you do something that they usually do and they do the thing that you usually do.","e":"Sibyl couldn't work on Tuesday, so I switched with her."},{"m":"If you switch a machine to a particular setting or function, you set it to work that way.","e":"She switched the TV to another channel."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A switch is what you use to turn lights or other machines and equipment on and off.","e":"The light switch is on the wall behind the door."},{"m":"(countable) A switch is a change from one thing to another.","e":"It's often difficult for older people to make the switch to living alone."},{"m":"(countable) A switch is a place on the track where trains can chose between two tracks."},{"m":"(countable) A switch is a networking device that connects networks together by sending data (packets) only to the devices that need them.","e":"Switches are more efficient than hubs because they understand which device needs the data that other devices send them."},{"m":"A switch is a thin stick."}]}]},"term":{"h":"term","i":"/tɜːm/","a":"en-us-term.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A term is a word or group of words, usually one with a special meaning in a particular field or area.","e":"They didn't know the meaning of the technical terms the doctor was using."},{"m":"(plural) You use \"in terms of\" to introduce a topic or subject.","e":"Simply spending more money is not useful in terms of getting people back to work."},{"m":"(plural) If you talk about something in general/economic/human, etc. terms, you talk about it from that point of view.","e":"The changes are great in dollar terms, but the human cost is too high."},{"m":"(countable) A term is a period of time.","e":"The President of Mexico is limited to serving a single term of six years."},{"m":"(countable) A term is one of the times of year when school classes are held, usually September to December and January to April or June, also June to August."},{"m":"(countable) A term is a number or symbol in a formula.","e":"The equation only worked when we included an extra constant term."},{"m":"(plural) If you compare money or numbers in real terms, you compare the value on an equal basis.","e":"Today we are paying less for gasoline in real terms than we have at any time since 1918."},{"m":"(plural) If you come to terms with something that is not nice, you accept it.","e":"He hasn't come to terms with the fact that she's not coming back."},{"m":"(usually plural) The terms of a contract or purchase are its rules, conditions and limits.","e":"The company has announced generally agreement on a new contract though the exact terms still have to be worked out."},{"m":"(plural) If two or more people or groups are on good/equal/bad etc. terms, they have a relationship that is good/equal/bad etc."},{"m":"(plural) If two or more people or groups are on speaking terms, they are not close but do speak to each other."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you term something a particular name or description, you give that name or description to it.","e":"The 1980s have been termed \"The Forgotten Decade\" by rock fans."}]}]},"suppose":{"h":"suppose","i":"/səˈpəʊz/","a":"en-us-suppose.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you suppose something, you guess that it is true.","e":"What do you suppose that he will do?"},{"m":"You use I suppose to show that you agree weakly with something.","e":"\"Did she know Paul pretty well?\" \"I suppose so.\""},{"m":"You use I don't suppose to ask a question, especially when you think the answer is no.","e":"I don't suppose you remember me?"},{"m":"You use suppose to talk about an imaginary situation.","e":"Suppose, for example, that there was nothing there. Then what would you do?"}]}]},"supply":{"h":"supply","i":"/səˈplaɪ/","a":"en-us-supply.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A supply is an amount of something that you can use when you need it.","e":"We will need a supply of water."},{"m":"Supplies are things like food, water, medicine, gasoline, etc. that people need when they are not near somewhere where they can get them easily.","e":"The Japanese government is finally planning to send medical supplies and financial support."},{"m":"(uncountable) Supply is the act or system of supplying something.","e":"They plan to fix the Russian economy and improve the supply of food and consumer goods."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you supply something, you make it available, usually regularly.","e":"We were supplied with a few basic tools that we needed for the job."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"In a supple way."}]}]},"succeed":{"h":"succeed","i":"/səkˈsiːd/","a":"en-us-succeed.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If something succeeds, it has happened the way somebody wants it to happen.","e":"He succeeded in getting everyone to like him."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you succeed, people recognize that you are good at what you do.","e":"It's more difficult for women to succeed in business."},{"m":"(intransitive) If x succeeds y, x replaces y.","e":"The new king succeeded his father."}]}]},"soon":{"h":"soon","i":"/suːn/","a":"en-us-soon.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Something that happens soon happens shortly after another time, often shortly after the time of speaking.","e":"Why did he call me so soon? Did something bad happen?"},{"m":"If x happens as soon as y does, x happens right after y.","e":"As soon as he finished eating, he got up and walked away from the table."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is soon, it is shortly after another time, often shortly after the time of speaking.","e":"He wanted to leave, but it seemed too soon."}]}]},"slight":{"h":"slight","i":"/slaɪt/","a":"en-us-slight.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A slight increase, difference, etc. is a small change.","e":"This year's 5.6% level is a slight increase from last year's 5.4%."},{"m":"If someone is slight, they are thin.","e":"Out stepped a slight, middle-aged woman who smiled kindly."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you slight someone, you treat them as if they were not important.","e":"Ever since that time, he's been slighted by his fellow workers."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A slight is when you are not polite to someone.","e":"Has she forgiven him for his slight?"}]}]},"situate":{"h":"situate","i":"/ˈsɪtʃu.eɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-situate.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something is situated somewhere, it is there.","e":"The school is situated in a mostly-white area."}]}]},"sir":{"h":"sir","i":"/ˈsɜː(r)/","a":"en-us-sir.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) You use sir to speak or write to a man formally to be polite.","e":"Excuse me, sir, could you tell me where the nearest bookstore is?"},{"m":"Sir is a title used before certain men's names."}]}]},"single":{"h":"single","i":"/ˈsɪŋɡəl/","a":"en-us-single.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A single thing is the only one.","e":"In large baking dish, arrange chicken pieces in single layer."},{"m":"You use single to stress how many or how few.","e":"I hate going to work every single day and listening to people yell at each other."},{"m":"A single person is not married.","e":"The single mother of two spends weekends with her kids."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A single is a song that is sold or put out by itself (or with one other song), not on an album.","e":"Today she releases her live version of Birthday, the first single from an upcoming tour album."},{"m":"(countable) In baseball and cricket, a single is a hit that enables a runner to score a point."},{"m":"(countable) In baseball a single is a hit that enables the player to move to first base."},{"m":"(uncountable) Singles is a game where each side has only one player, especially in tennis."},{"m":"Singles are people who are not married or not in a romantic relationship.","e":"You'll pay no tax if your income falls below $50,000 for a married couple, $35,000 for singles."},{"m":"(countable) A single is a hotel room for one person.","e":"I reserved a single in Montreal."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) In baseball if you single, you hit the ball and are able to run to first base.","e":"The batter singled to right field."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you single something out, you identify it, often to give it special attention.","e":"She was singled out as the best student in the class."}]}]},"sheet":{"h":"sheet","i":"/ʃiːt/","a":"en-uk-sheet.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sheet is a flat cloth that you cover a bed with.","e":"Use the sheets next to the bed."},{"m":"(countable) A sheet is a single piece of paper.","e":"Can I have a sheet of paper?"},{"m":"(countable) A sheet is a thin flat thing, usually something square or rectangular.","e":"Place the rolls on the baking sheet."},{"m":"A line (rope) used to adjust the trim of a sail."}]}]},"settle":{"h":"settle","i":"/ˈsɛtəl/","a":"en-us-settle.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you settle a fight, argument, case, etc., you find an answer that stops it.","e":"They settled the dispute. Both men were happy with the results."},{"m":"If something is settled, it is decided.","e":"OK, it's settled: we're going to Florida this summer."},{"m":"If something settles, it moves to a position where it can stay in for a long time, often in a low position.","e":"She got a drink and then calmly settled herself in front of the TV."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you settle for something, you accept it even though it is not as good as you wanted.","e":"This year, she would have to settle for third place."},{"m":"If you settle a place, you move there and live there.","e":"After moving to Canada, they settled in Toronto."},{"m":"If something settles (down), it becomes still and quiet.","e":"The noisy class needs to settle down."},{"m":"(transitive) If you settle (up) a bill, or your affairs, you pay the money you owe and/or receive the money that others owe you."},{"m":"If your stomach settles, it doesn't feel sick anymore."}]}]},"serve":{"h":"serve","i":"/sɜːv/","a":"en-us-serve.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you serve food or drink, you give it to somebody to eat or drink, especially as a host.","e":"Shall I serve your drinks first?"},{"m":"If something serves (as something), it used or useful for a certain purpose.","e":"This cup can serve as a holder for my paintbrushes."},{"m":"When you serve (as something), you work.","e":"John served in the army."},{"m":"(transitive) If you serve time in prison, you stay there because you are a criminal."},{"m":"If you serve, in a game like tennis, you begin play by sending something like a ball over a net."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A serve in a game like tennis is the action beginning of play by sending something like a ball over a net.","e":"Whose serve is it?"}]}]},"sale":{"h":"sale","i":"/seɪl/","a":"en-us-sale.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sale is the act of selling something.","e":"Proceeds from the sale of the art went to the local school."},{"m":"Sales is the number or value of things sold.","e":"The stronger economy has boosted auto sales by $650 million over last year."},{"m":"(uncountable) Sales is the part of a company or industry that tries to get people to buy more.","e":"She's now Seattle's director of marketing and sales."},{"m":"A sale is a time when prices are lower than usual.","e":"The computer store is having a sale: 50% off everything."}]}]},"wee":{"h":"wee","i":"/wiː/","a":"en-us-wee.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"(informal) (especially Scottish) A wee bit, boy, while etc. is a very small one.","e":"He was a wee bit upset about the changes."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(informal) (intransitive) If an animal wees, it passes waste liquid from its body."}]}]},"wonder":{"h":"wonder","i":"/ˈwʌndə/","a":"en-us-wonder.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you wonder about something, you think about it because you want to know more about it.","e":"I wonder when they will be home."},{"m":"(intransitive) You use \"wonder if/whether\" to ask for or suggest something.","e":"I wonder if you could give me a hand with the door."},{"m":"If you don't wonder something, you expect it.","e":"I don't wonder you've had problems with that old car."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A wonder is something that makes a person think.","e":"It is a wonder why he ran away."},{"m":"A wonder is something that is amazing.","e":"The Pyramids are quite a wonder."}]}]},"try":{"h":"try","i":"/traɪ/","a":"en-us-try.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you try to do something, you make effort to do it.","e":"As much as I tried, I couldn't understand it."},{"m":"(transitive) If you try something, you taste, do, or use it to see if it's good.","e":"Try using the new shoes for a week and let me know if there any problems."},{"m":"(transitive) If you try someone for a crime, you put them on trial.","e":"He was tried for robbery."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A try is when you attempt to do something.","e":"I gave juggling a try, but I just could not do it."},{"m":"(countable) A try is when you taste, do, or use it to see if it's good."},{"m":"(countable) A try is when you put the ball behind the other team's net in rugby."}]}]},"traffic":{"h":"traffic","i":"/ˈtræfɪk/","a":"en-us-traffic.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Traffic is the things that move along a path, especially cars on a road.","e":"Traffic is slow at rush hour."},{"m":"(uncountable) Traffic is the buying and selling of goods, especially illegal goods.","e":"Governments are working to prevent the abduction and sale of, or traffic in children."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you traffic in certain goods, you buy and sell them, especially illegally.","e":"They were arrested for trafficking in stolen goods."}]}]},"therefore":{"h":"therefore","i":"/ˈðɛəfɔː/","a":"en-us-therefore.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"You use therefore to show that something was as a result of what was previously stated.","e":"He was sick with the flu and, therefore, did not come."}]}]},"loanword":{"h":"loanword","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A loanword is a word in one language that comes from another language.","e":"\"Tsunami\" is a Japanese word, but is a loan word in English."}]}]},"dollar":{"h":"dollar","i":"/ˈdɒlə/","a":"en-us-dollar.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The dollar is the main unit of money in the United States, Canada, and other countries including Australia, the Bahamas, Barbados, Belize, Bermuda, Fiji, Guyana, Hong Kong, Jamaica, Liberia, New Zealand, Singapore, the Solomon Islands, Trinidad and Tobago, and Zimbabwe. It is usually equal to 100 cents."}]}]},"politics":{"h":"politics","i":"/ˈpɑl.ɪˌtɪks/","a":"en-us-politics.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Politics is the activity of controlling, affecting or studying an organisation, especially a government.","e":"The Prime Minister entered politics when she was in university."}]}]},"papaya":{"h":"papaya","i":"/pəˈpaɪə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-papaya.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A type of tree that has big, yellow fruit."},{"m":"(countable) The fruit of the papaya tree."},{"m":"(uncountable) Papaya is an orange color that is like that of papaya flesh."}]}]},"weak":{"h":"weak","i":"/wiːk/","a":"en-us-weak.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Weak is used to describe something that does not have a lot of strength.","e":"The child was too weak to move the boulder."},{"m":"Something that is weak does not have a strong taste.","e":"This tea tastes weak and watery. Do you have anything stronger?"},{"m":"; not cool.","e":"This place is weak. Let's go somewhere more interesting."}]}]},"french":{"h":"French","i":"/frɛnʧ/","a":"en-us-French.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"French is the language that is spoken in France, and parts of Canada, Belgium, and Switzerland.","e":"The family spoke French."},{"m":"A French is a bad word; cursing.","e":"Pardon my French."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"(preceded by the and plural in form) The French are the people of France.","e":"The French and the English have often been at war."},{"m":"Something that is related to France.","e":"We have crossed the French border with Italy."},{"m":"Something that is related to the French people.","e":"She was born in Paris, so she should know about French customs."},{"m":"Something that is related to the French language.","e":"\"Sauter\" is a French verb for \"Jump\"."}]}]},"hermaphrodite":{"h":"hermaphrodite","i":"/hɝˈmæfrədaɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-hermaphrodite.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hermaphrodite is a living organism that is both male and female."}]}]},"coir":{"h":"coir","i":"/ˈkɔɪə/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The fibers around the outside of a coconut; coir is often used to make rope or mats."}]}]},"overcorrect":{"h":"overcorrect","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you overcorrect, you do too much to fix a problem, so that you make another problem.","e":"The driver overcorrected and hit another car."}]}]},"poem":{"h":"poem","i":"/ˈpəʊ.ɪm/","a":"en-uk-poem.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A poem is a group of words written or spoken as an art. Usually, a poem has a rhythm. Many poems rhyme (have words that end the same), and some poems repeat the same first sound in a word (called alliteration).","e":"I have written some poems."}]}]},"poetry":{"h":"poetry","i":"/ˈpəʊɪtri/","a":"en-us-poetry.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The art of writing poems.","e":"Poetry is much cheaper than painting since you don't need special supplies."},{"m":"(uncountable) A group of poems.","e":"This is a book of poetry."},{"m":"(uncountable) Poems in general.","e":"Poetry is found all over the world."},{"m":"(uncountable) words or speech.","e":"To hear my child speak is poetry."}]}]},"poet":{"h":"poet","i":"/ˈpəʊɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-poet.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A poet is someone who creates poetry. If you write poems you are being a poet."}]}]},"poetic":{"h":"poetic","i":"/poʊˈɛtɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-poetic.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is poetic it is a poem or sounds like poetry."},{"m":"If words are poetic they are like a poem, even if they are not a real poem."},{"m":"If something that happens is poetic it is like something from literature."}]}]},"lyric":{"h":"lyric","i":"/ˈlɪr.ɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-lyric.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (usually plural) One verse of a song."}]}]},"lyrics":{"h":"lyrics","i":"/ˈlir.ɪks/","l":"lyric","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable); (usually plural) Lyrics are the words that go to a song. Often, lyrics are like a poem set to music.","e":"I wish I knew the lyrics to Dreams by The Cranberries."}]}]},"rhyme":{"h":"rhyme","i":"/raɪm/","a":"en-us-rhyme.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If two words rhyme the end of the words sounds the same.","e":"The words \"day\" and \"way\" rhyme."},{"m":"If you rhyme, you say words that rhyme.","e":"Rhyming is a good way to remember some things."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A rhyme is two words (or a word and a phrase) that end with the same sound, including at least one vowel sound.","e":"\"Agree\" and \"degree\" make a rhyme, and \"rhyme\" and \"time\" are also a rhyme."}]}]},"rime":{"h":"rime","i":"/raɪm/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The rime is the end of a syllable, the vowel a last consonant make the rime.","e":"If the two words have the same rime at the end those words rhyme."}]}]},"linguistics":{"h":"linguistics","a":"en-us-linguistics.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Linguistics is a science that studies languages and how language works."}]}]},"consonant":{"h":"consonant","i":"/ˈkɒn.sə.nənt/","a":"en-us-consonant.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A consonant is a sound or letter that is not a vowel. Consonants usually do not last long and are less loud than vowels. In a syllable (a piece of a word) a vowel will be in the middle and consonants might come before or after.","e":"The letters \"t\", \"s\", \"f\", and \"g\" are all consonants."}]}]},"syllable":{"h":"syllable","i":"/ˈsɪləbɫ/","a":"en-uk-syllable.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A syllable is a word or part of a word that has one vowel sound in it. The vowel might have consonants around it or be by itself.","e":"The word \"potato\" has three syllables, \"po,\" \"ta,\" and \"to.\""}]}]},"repeat":{"h":"repeat","i":"/rɪˈpiːt/","a":"en-us-repeat.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you repeat something, you do it again.","e":"I don't want to have to repeat typing this."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something repeats or is repeated it is done more than once, or there is more than one of it.","e":"The flashing light just keeps repeating."},{"m":"(transitive) If you repeat yourself, you say something you just said again.","e":"I already told you what to do, don't make me repeat myself."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An instruction to repeat something. Usually this is used for music in part of a song. Sometimes it may be used for other things like part of a computer program."},{"m":"Something this has been repeated; that is a repetition."}]}]},"passed":{"h":"passed","i":"/pɑ:st/","a":"en-us-passed.ogg","l":"pass","q":"verb"},"permit":{"h":"permit","i":"/ˈpɜːmɪt/","a":"en-us-permit-noun.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"If you have a permit to do something, you have a document that says you are allowed to do it, it is legal for you to do it."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you permit something, you let it happen."},{"m":"If you permit something, you make it legal."}]}]},"socket":{"h":"socket","i":"/sɒkət̩̩/","a":"en-us-socket.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A socket is a space that something fits into exactly. For example, an electrical device plugs into an electrical socket."}]}]},"plug":{"h":"plug","i":"/plʌɡ/","a":"en-us-plug.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A plug is an object that fills a gap. Examples of a plug are, an electrical plug which plugs into the wall or electrical socket, a sink plug (or stopper) which stops the water from draining out of the sink or bath."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you plug something you close by putting something into it.","e":"We use corks to plug the barrels."},{"m":"(transitive) If you plug something in (or into) you put into a socket."},{"m":"(transitive) If you plug something in you connect it to electricity.","e":"You have to plug the computer in if for it to work."},{"m":"(transitive) If you plug in an idea or way of doing something, you use it as a whole (without changing it).","e":"We just plugged in the results from last year and everything worked."},{"m":"(transitive) If something plugs something else closes it tightly.","e":"The cork plugged the bottle."}]}]},"suite":{"h":"suite","i":"/swiːt/","a":"en-us-suite.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A series of objects; a number of things that are used or grouped together; a set."},{"m":"A type of music that has a series of songs all in the same key, mostly in different dance rhythms, sometimes with a complex prelude."},{"m":"A luxury room in a hotel.","e":"My sister only stays in suites when she travels because she likes the extra space."},{"m":"A location of a business in an office building or shopping mall.","e":"I work at 123 Oak Rd, Suite 5."}]}]},"obfuscate":{"h":"obfuscate","i":"/ˈɒbfʌskeɪt/","a":"en-us-obfuscate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you obfuscate something, you make it dark or overshadow it."},{"m":"If you obfuscate a situation or comment, you deliberately make it more so that you can hide the truth.","e":"Before leaving the scene, the murderer set a fire to obfuscate any evidence of his or her identity."},{"m":"If you obfuscate computer code, you change it so that it acts the same way but the code's structure and intent are hidden.","e":"We need to obfuscate these classes before we ship the final release."}]}]},"vicious":{"h":"vicious","i":"/ˈvɪʃəs/","a":"en-us-vicious.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Someone or something that is vicious is evil, immoral, aggressive, or violent."}]}]},"waterproof":{"h":"waterproof","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is waterproof, water cannot go through it.","e":"I needed a waterproof coat to walk in the rain."}]}]},"countable":{"h":"countable","i":"/ˈkaʊntəbəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-countable.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is countable it can be counted. Also, since this is true, the number must not be infinite (without an end)."},{"m":"A countable noun is one you can use with a number (e.g., seven apples).","e":"In English, police is not countable, but police officer is."}]}]},"uncountable":{"h":"uncountable","i":"/ʌnˈkaʊntəbəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-uncountable.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A word is uncountable if it means something that there is not a set number of. This usually means that it names a substance like water or wood. Uncountable words are sometimes called mass nouns, and they cannot be plural."}]}]},"german":{"h":"German","i":"/ˈdʒɜːmən/","a":"en-us-German.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"German is the language in Germany."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A German is a person who comes from Germany.","e":"My friend is a German."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something or someone that is German comes from Germany.","e":"My friend Dagmar is German."},{"m":"Some people call themselves German because their family came from Germany, even if they have never been to Germany.","e":"Mr. Schwartz is German, his grandmother came to the U.S. from Germany."}]}]},"shadow":{"h":"shadow","i":"/ˈʃædəʊ/","a":"en-us-shadow.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A shadow is the dark area that is made when something blocks light, and that is shaped like the thing blocking the light.","e":"I saw your shadow against the wall."},{"m":"(uncountable) The darkness in a shadow.","e":"The room filled with shadow as the night came."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you shadow someone, you follow them closely without their knowing it.","e":"The detective shadowed the thief."},{"m":"If something is being shadowed, it is being covered in shadow or made dark.","e":"The curtains shadowed the room."},{"m":"(transitive) If you shadow someone, you accompany them when they are working so as to learn about an occupation you intend to take up."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"(politics) A shadow politician is someone who is the counterpart of minister or a ministry."}]}]},"daddy":{"h":"daddy","i":"/ˈdædi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Back ache-daddy.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Another word for father, a male parent. This is usually used by children.","e":"The girl was very happy to see her daddy."},{"m":"Someone who is better than someone else. This is often used to say you are better than the person you are talking to, especially if you have beat them at something.","e":"You know I'm your daddy."},{"m":"Someone who is very great.","e":"He really thinks he's the daddy!"}]}]},"teenager":{"h":"teenager","i":"/ˈtiːnˌeɪ.dʒə(r)/","a":"en-us-teenager.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A teenager is a person whose age is a number that ends in \"-teen.\" That is, someone between the ages of 13 and 19.","e":"Many teenagers want to rebel."}]}]},"teen":{"h":"teen","i":"/tiːn/","a":"en-us-teen.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A short word for teenager.","e":"Teens are often hard on parents."}]}]},"adolescent":{"h":"adolescent","i":"/ˌædəˈlɛsənt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-adolescent.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An adolescent is a person or animal that is older than a child but younger than an adult.","e":"The teacher worked mostly with adolescents."},{"m":"(countable) An adolescent is a person going through sexual maturation."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is adolescent it is typical of adolescents.","e":"The woman still had an adolescent appearance."}]}]},"teacher":{"h":"teacher","i":"/ˈtit͡ʃɚ/","a":"en-us-teacher.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A teacher is a person who teaches other people.","e":"She was a very good teacher, I learned a lot from her."}]}]},"liar":{"h":"liar","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Someone who says things that are not true, that is, someone who lies.","e":"I don't trust that liar."}]}]},"feminine":{"h":"feminine","i":"/ˈfɛmɪnɪn/","a":"en-us-feminine.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is feminine it is like something a girl or woman would do.","e":"Wearing dresses is very feminine."},{"m":"If someone is feminine they act in a way that is usual for a girl or woman.","e":"She is not very feminine, she always acts like a man."},{"m":"If something is feminine it has to do with girls or women.","e":"A tampon is a feminine item."},{"m":"In some languages, feminine is a gender that a word can have.","e":"Some German words are feminine, but English words do not have gender."}]}]},"masculine":{"h":"masculine","i":"/ˈmæskjʊlɪn/","a":"en-us-masculine.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is masculine it is like something a boy or man would do.","e":"Playing sports is often seen as masculine."},{"m":"If someone is masculine they act in a way that is usual for a man.","e":"The character Rambo is very masculine."},{"m":"In some languages, masculine is a gender that a word can have.","e":"Some German words are masculine, but English words do not have gender."}]}]},"ladylike":{"h":"ladylike","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is ladylike she is polite in a feminine way. She behaves in a way that an important woman (a lady) would long ago.","e":"Her ladylike ways impressed the older people in the room."},{"m":"If an action is ladylike it is something that would be right for a lady. It is something someone does if she is ladylike.","e":"Do not eat with your hands, it's not ladylike."}]}]},"kingdom":{"h":"kingdom","i":"/ˈkɪŋdəm/","a":"en-us-kingdom.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A country that has a king or queen. The king or queen might control the kingdom, or might just be symbols of the country."}]}]},"kindness":{"h":"kindness","i":"/ˈkaɪndnɪs/","a":"en-us-kindness.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The quality of being kind. When you have kindness, you do many kind things."},{"m":"(uncountable) Kind things people do. When you help people you are showing kindness."}]}]},"baldur":{"h":"Baldur","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Baldur is a Norse god. He is the son of Odin and Freya and he is known for his beauty and near-invulnerability."}]}]},"electronic":{"h":"electronic","i":"/ˌɛl.ɛkˈtrɒn.ɪk/","a":"en-us-electronic.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is electronic relates to an electron or electrons."},{"m":"A device that is electronic runs on the energy caused by electrons flowing through semiconductors.","e":"What does that electronic device do?"},{"m":"Something that is electronic is made by an electronic (2) device","e":"electronic music"}]}]},"disk":{"h":"disk","i":"/dɪsk/","a":"en-us-disc.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A disk is an object that is thin, flat, and circular.","e":"A coin is a disk of metal."},{"m":"Something that looks like a disk.","e":"Venus' disk blocked light from the Sun."},{"m":"A vinyl phonograph / gramophone record.","e":"Turn the disk over after it has finished."},{"m":"A floppy disk.","e":"He still uses floppy disks from 1979."},{"m":"A disc – either a CD-ROM, an audio CD, a DVD.","e":"She burned some disks yesterday to back up the information on her computer."}]}]},"disc":{"h":"disc","i":"/dɪsk/","a":"en-us-disc.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An object that is thin, flat, and circular.","e":"A coin is a disc of metal."},{"m":"An intervertebral disc."},{"m":"Something that looks like a disc.","e":"Venus' disc cut off light from the Sun."},{"m":"A vinyl phonograph / gramophone record.","e":"Turn the disc over, after it has finished."}]}]},"pore":{"h":"pore","i":"/pɔr/","a":"en-us-pore.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A tiny opening in the skin."},{"m":"Any small opening. Often an object will have many pores, not just one, and these pores let liquids pass through them."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you pore over something, you study it carefully and with great detail; you look at it many times."},{"m":"To meditate or reflect in a steady way."}]}]},"widower":{"h":"widower","i":"/ˈwɪdoʊɚ/","a":"en-us-widower.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A widower is a man whose wife has died."}]}]},"jumpy":{"h":"jumpy","i":"/ˈdʒʌmpi/","a":"en-us-jumpy.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are jumpy you are very nervous or anxious. That is you may feel like jumping in fear if surprised, because you are a little afraid already.","e":"Are you okay, you seem jumpy today."}]}]},"killer":{"h":"killer","a":"en-us-killer.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Someone who kills. Usually this mean someone who kills other people, and does not have a good reason to kill.","e":"The police caught the killer today."},{"m":"Something that kills.","e":"Lighting can be a real killer."},{"m":"Something that cause problems.","e":"Failing the exam was a real killer."},{"m":"Something that is very exciting.","e":"The show was great, a real killer."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is killer it kills.","e":"Watch out! There are killer bees!"},{"m":"If something is killer it is very good.","e":"That was a killer show!"}]}]},"women":{"h":"women","i":"/ˈwɪmɪn/","a":"en-uk-women.ogg","l":"woman","q":"noun"},"orphan":{"h":"orphan","i":"/ˈɔːfən/","a":"en-us-orphan.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An orphan is someone who does not have parents. That is, their mother and father are both dead. This is most often used for a child.","e":"She became an orphan when the storm killed her parents."}]}]},"fighter":{"h":"fighter","i":"/ˈfaɪ.tə(r)/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-fighter.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A fighter is someone who fights for a cause, a job, or a sport."},{"m":"(countable) A fighter is small, fast airplane used for war."}]}]},"mankind":{"h":"mankind","i":"/mænˈkaɪnd/","a":"en-us-mankind.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"s, meaning all people, everywhere."}]}]},"powerful":{"h":"powerful","i":"/ˈpaʊɚfəl/","a":"en-us-powerful.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone (or something) is powerful, they have much power.","e":"The king is a very powerful man."}]}]},"progress":{"h":"progress","i":"/ˈprəʊɡrɛs/","a":"en-us-progress-noun.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Progress is forward or getting better (more good).","e":"We didn't make much progress on the road, only a mile."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you progress, you move forward.","e":"The army progressed toward the city."}]}]},"painter":{"h":"painter","i":"/ˈpeɪntə/","a":"en-us-painter.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A painter is someone who paints. This might be an artist, or might be someone who paints buildings."}]}]},"artist":{"h":"artist","i":"/ˈɑːtɪst/","a":"en-us-artist.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An artist is someone who makes art.","e":"An artist was in the park painting the birds."},{"m":"An artist is a performer on a musical track."}]}]},"soldier":{"h":"soldier","i":"/ˈsəʊld͡ʒə/","a":"en-uk-soldier.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A soldier is someone who is part of an army.","e":"The soldier was shot in the war."}]}]},"warrior":{"h":"warrior","i":"/ˈwɔriɚ/","a":"en-us-warrior.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A person whose job is to fight and kill enemies of their people or country. Often this is used for someone from a long time ago, or to say some is like a hero from long ago."},{"m":"(countable) Someone who is tough or wants to be seen as like a warrior from long ago."}]}]},"boxer":{"h":"boxer","i":"/ˈbɒksə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-boxer.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A boxer is a person who boxes (fights for sport by hitting with fists)."},{"m":"(countable) A boxer is a kind of dog, that was originally bred in Germany to protect houses from burglars. They cropped their ears so people could not grab them, the same with their tail."}]}]},"fist":{"h":"fist","i":"/fɪst/","a":"en-us-fist.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A hand that is held tightly, often to hit."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To hit with a fist.","e":"...may not score a point with his open hand(s), but may score a point by fisting the ball. Damian Cullen. \"Running the rule.\" The Irish Times 18 Aug 2003, pg. 52."},{"m":"To fist-fuck."}]}]},"boxing":{"h":"boxing","i":"/ˈbɒksɪŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-boxing.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A sport where people fight with fists."}]}]},"daylight":{"h":"daylight","i":"/ˈdeɪlaɪt/","a":"en-us-daylight.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Period from sunrise to sunset."}]}]},"consistency":{"h":"consistency","i":"/kənˈsɪst(ə)nsi/","a":"en-us-consistency.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The quality of being consistent or uniform.","e":"They want their employees to have a high level of consistency in the quality of their customer service."},{"m":"How dense or thick a substance is.","e":"Mix it until it has a thick consistency."}]}]},"stepchild":{"h":"stepchild","i":"/ˈstɛp.tʃaɪld/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-stepchild.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A stepchild is the child of a person's husband or wife. A stepchild is a child from an earlier marriage.","e":"When I married my wife I got two stepchildren."}]}]},"handle":{"h":"handle","i":"/ˈhæn.dl/","a":"en-us-handle.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A handle is the part of an object that you hold with your hand when you want to use or move the object. Some examples of handles are: the shaft of a sword, the knob of a door, etc.","e":"I grabbed the handle on the drawer and opened it."},{"m":"(countable) A handle is a nickname or pseudonym."},{"m":"(Australia, New Zealand) A handle is a 10 fl oz (285&nbsp;ml) glass of beer in the Northern Territory."},{"m":"(countable) (US) A handle is a 1.75-liter (half-gallon) bottle of alcohol."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you handle something, you touch it, you feel it with your hand."},{"m":"How you handle an object is how you use it.","e":"You handle that gun pretty well."},{"m":"To give and take; to have something pass through your hands; to buy and sell","e":"As a cashier, I handle money every day."},{"m":"To deal with; to make a business of.","e":"They that handle the law knew me not – Jeremiah, 2:8"},{"m":"To treat; to use, well or ill.","e":"How were you handled in prison?"},{"m":"To manage; to control; to practice skill upon.","e":"It won't be easy, but I think I can handle it."}]}]},"syntax":{"h":"syntax","i":"/ˈsɪn.tæks/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-syntax.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A part of the grammar of a language. Syntax is the rules for putting words together to make a sentence.","e":"English syntax is never easier than English spelling."},{"m":"(countable) Syntax is the formal rules of statements of a computer language."}]}]},"morphology":{"h":"morphology","i":"/mɔrˈfɑlədʒi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-morphology.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A part of the grammar of a language. Morphology is the rules for putting parts of words together to make a whole word.","e":"English morphology is easier than German morphology."},{"m":"(uncountable) The study of how animals and plants are shaped.","e":"The morphology of insects has three body pieces and six legs."},{"m":"(uncountable) Morphology is or the study of shape in some other sciences, such as in geology or astronomy.","e":"Rock morphology gives us clues about Earth's history."},{"m":"(countable) A morphology is the shape of something in general.","e":"The morphologies of the different rocks tells us about how thing were when they were made."}]}]},"icon":{"h":"icon","i":"/ˈaɪ.kən/","a":"en-us-icon.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An image, picture, or other representation of something."},{"m":"(countable) A religious painting that is often done on wooden panels."},{"m":"(countable) A person or thing that is the best example of something.","e":"That man is an icon in the business; he is loyal and has good business sense."},{"m":"(countable) A small picture which represents something (such as an icon on a computer screen).","e":"Click on the icon to open the program."},{"m":"(countable) A type of noun where the form reflects and is determined by the referent; onomatopoeic words are all icons."}]}]},"vulgar":{"h":"vulgar","i":"/ˈvʌl.ɡə/","a":"en-us-vulgar.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is vulgar, it is obscene or offensive.","e":"The c-word and f-word are seen as very vulgar, you should be careful using them."},{"m":"If something is vulgar, it lacks sophistication or good taste."},{"m":"If something is vulgar, it is ordinary.","e":"A vulgar fraction is a."}]}]},"morphosyntax":{"h":"morphosyntax","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) and syntax together. This is the study of the parts of words are put together in a sentence."}]}]},"morpheme":{"h":"morpheme","i":"/ˈmɔː(r)fiːm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-morpheme.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Part of a word. A morpheme is the smallest unit of meaning in a language. Basic words (word roots) and word endings like \"-ed,\" \"-s,\" and \"-ing\" are examples of morphemes."}]}]},"catalyst":{"h":"catalyst","i":"/ˈkæt.əˌlɪst/","a":"en-us-ncalif-catalyst.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A substance that makes a chemical reaction happen faster. The catalyst is not changed by the process and can be used again."},{"m":"(automotive) A catalytic converter."},{"m":"Someone or something that encourages progress or change, or helps it happen.","e":"I hope the new CEO will be a catalyst for change."}]}]},"daylights":{"h":"daylights","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A person's daylights are his mental stability or his wits.","e":"You scared the daylights out of me!"}]}]},"truthiness":{"h":"truthiness","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(jokingly) The truthiness of an idea is its ability to be believed emotionally and not because it is supported by evidence or logic."},{"m":"(jokingly) Following incorrect ideas because you wish or believe them to be true.","e":"Your truthiness amazes me. Don't you care that it's been proven false?"}]}]},"ceiling":{"h":"ceiling","i":"/ˈsiːlɪŋ/","a":"en-us-ceiling.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The top part of a room.","e":"This room has a very interesting ceiling."},{"m":"The upper limit of an object or action.","e":"price ceilings"},{"m":"The highest altitude that an aircraft may fly."},{"m":"The smallest integer greater than or equal to a given number.","e":"The ceiling of 4.5 is 5."}]}]},"relic":{"h":"relic","i":"/ˈrɛlɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-relic.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Something old that is kept for personal, sentimental reasons."},{"m":"(religion) A part of the body of a saint, or a very old religious object, which is kept out of respect for the object."}]}]},"production":{"h":"production","i":"/prəˈdʌkʃən/","a":"en-us-production.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Production is when something is produced.","e":"The machine is being used for production now."},{"m":"(uncountable) The total amount of something that is produced.","e":"They hope to increase spaghetti production next year."},{"m":"(countable) A play or other presentation in a theatre.","e":"We went to a production of Hamlet."},{"m":"(countable) An event or activity that is made more complicated or dramatic than necessary.","e":"He made a simple meal into a huge production."}]}]},"corpse":{"h":"corpse","i":"/kɔːps/","a":"en-us-corpse.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A dead body."}]}]},"parachute":{"h":"parachute","i":"/ˈpærəʃuːt/","a":"en-us-parachute.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A parachute is something, usually a large piece of fabric, that helps to slow a person or object that is falling.","e":"This parachute is made from very light, thin fabric but it is very strong."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you parachute, you jump or fall using a parachute.","e":"Parachuting out of an airplane was the most exciting thing I've ever done."}]}]},"wiktionary":{"h":"Wiktionary","i":"/ˈwɪkʃən(ə)rɪ/","a":"en-uk-Wiktionary.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A collaborative project that is run by the. The goal is to produce a free and complete dictionary in every language."},{"m":"The dictionary resulting from this project."},{"m":"A wiki-based dictionary."}]}]},"possession":{"h":"possession","i":"/pəˈzɛʃən/","a":"en-us-possession.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Power or control over something, as distinct from lawful ownership; holding or occupancy."},{"m":"(uncountable) of something.","e":"I have possession of some valuable antiques."},{"m":"(countable) Something that is owned.","e":"These are my possessions."},{"m":"(countable) A territory that is under the rule of another country.","e":"Puerto Rico is a possession of the United States."},{"m":"(uncountable) Possession is when a person's body is controlled by a demon or other supernatural being.","e":"Exorcism is a movie about possession."},{"m":"(uncountable) In sports, possession is control of the ball.","e":"Real Madrid now has possession of the ball and is trying to score."}]}]},"promotion":{"h":"promotion","i":"/prəˈmoʊʃən/","a":"en-us-promotion.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) If you get a promotion you move up in rank or position.","e":"He received a promotion to sergeant."},{"m":", (marketing) A promotion gives out information about a product, product line, brand, or company.","e":"The store has a special promotion this week on two-for-one pizzas."}]}]},"penalty":{"h":"penalty","i":"/ˈpɛnəlti/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-penalty.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A penalty is a legal punishment for committing a crime.","e":"The penalty for his crime was to pay a fine."},{"m":"(countable) A penalty is a punishment for breaking the rules."},{"m":"(finance) (countable) A penalty is a payment forfeited if you make an early withdrawal from an account or an investment."},{"m":"(ice hockey) (countable) A penalty is a punishment for breaking the rules of the game; usually, being removed from play for a while.","e":"A penalty was called when he tripped up his opponent."}]}]},"belgium":{"h":"Belgium","i":"/ˈbɛldʒəm/","a":"en-us-Belgium.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Belgium is a country in Central Europe."}]}]},"luxembourg":{"h":"Luxembourg","i":"/ˈlʌk.səm.bɜːɡ/","a":"en-us-Luxembourg.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Luxembourg is a country in central Europe beside Germany, France, and Belgium."}]}]},"switzerland":{"h":"Switzerland","i":"/ˈswɪt.sə.lənd/","a":"en-us-Switzerland.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Switzerland is a country in central Europe."}]}]},"italy":{"h":"Italy","i":"/ˈɪtəli/","a":"en-us-Italy.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Italy is a country in Europe by the Mediterranean Sea."}]}]},"monaco":{"h":"Monaco","i":"/ˈmɒnəkəʊ/","a":"en-us-Monaco.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Monaco is a small country in Europe near France, Italy, and the Mediterranean Sea."}]}]},"andorra":{"h":"Andorra","i":"/ænˈdɔr.ə/","a":"en-us-Andorra.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Andorra is a small country in Europe between France and Spain."}]}]},"spain":{"h":"Spain","i":"/speɪn/","a":"en-us-Spain.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Spain is a country in Europe near Portugal, Andorra, and France."}]}]},"portugal":{"h":"Portugal","i":"/ˈpɔːt͡ʃəɡəl/","a":"en-us-Portugal.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Portugal is a country near Spain in Europe."}]}]},"prevention":{"h":"prevention","i":"/prɪˈvɛnʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-prevention.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The act of preventing something or hindering it; when someone or something is stopped from getting close, getting inside, or doing something.","e":"We built a wall to help the prevention of an attack on the city."}]}]},"lawn":{"h":"lawn","i":"/lɔ:n/","a":"en-us-lawn.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Ground (generally in front of or around a house) that is covered with grass that is mowed short.","e":"In summer, I have to mow my lawn twice a week."},{"m":"An open space between woods."},{"m":"A type of thin linen or cotton."},{"m":"A piece of clothing made from lawn."}]}]},"debris":{"h":"debris","i":"/ˈdɛbriː/","a":"en-us-debris.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The bits of something that are left after an object has been destroyed; rubble, wreckage.","e":"There was a lot of debris after the building was demolished."},{"m":"(uncountable) or trash that has been discarded.","e":"Look at all the debris in the gutters!."},{"m":"Large rock fragments left by a melting glacier etc."}]}]},"trash":{"h":"trash","i":"/træʃ/","a":"en-us-trash.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"things that are discarded.","e":"I took it out of the wrapping and then threw away the trash."},{"m":"A container where useless things are discarded.","e":"Just throw it in the trash."},{"m":"Something of poor or bad quality.","e":"This radio is trash! It doesn't work!"},{"m":"; (usually derogatory) Lower class people.","e":"white trash"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To make a mess; to ruin or destroy things.","e":"Trash the house! he ordered."},{"m":"To discard or to throw away.","e":"Will you trash those old love letters?"}]}]},"fries":{"h":"fries","i":"/fraɪz/","l":"fry","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Fries are potatoes that are cut thin.","e":"McDonalds' fries are okay, but I like to make my own."}]}]},"fur":{"h":"fur","i":"/fɜː(r)/","a":"en-us-fur.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The hair of an animal.","e":"My dog has very soft fur."},{"m":"(countable) Hairy skin of an animal, often used to make of clothes.","e":"It take many beaver furs to make a coat."},{"m":"(countable) or (uncountable) Clothes made from animal fur.","e":"She loved to wear fur."}]}]},"asshole":{"h":"asshole","i":"/ˈæsˌhoʊl/","a":"en-us-asshole.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The anus, the hole in the bottom where feces comes out."},{"m":"A rude or cruel person; a jerk.","e":"Don't be an asshole."}]}]},"badass":{"h":"badass","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"; A badass is someone who is very tough or mean.","e":"Don't mess with him, he's a real badass!"},{"m":"A person who has extreme attitudes and behavior and is admired by others. In this sense, calling someone a badass is a compliment.","e":"I heard that he smashed his guitar at the end of the encore. He's such a badass!"}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"; If something is badass it is great or very good; cool.","e":"I love my new shoes--aren't they badass?"}]}]},"saturation":{"h":"saturation","i":"/satʃəˈreɪʃ(ə)n/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The act of saturating or the process of being saturated."},{"m":"When something has been increased and can no longer be increased.","e":"The metal has reached saturation, it cannot be magnetized any further."},{"m":"When a solution becomes completed saturated.","e":"After adding 3 tablespoons of salt, the water has reached the point of saturation."},{"m":"When an organic compound has no or s"},{"m":"(meteorology) When the atmosphere is saturated with water vapor; 100% humidity."},{"m":"How bright or vivid a color is."},{"m":"a military target and trying to destroy it"},{"m":"When a market is flooded with all of a product that can be sold;"},{"m":"An effect on the sound of an electric guitar that is used mainly in music."}]}]},"saturated":{"h":"saturated","l":"saturate","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"(not comparable) Something that is saturated is full; it cannot hold or contain any more."},{"m":"(comparable) ed or drenched with moisture."},{"m":"(not comparable); ing all the solute that can normally be dissolved at a given temperature."},{"m":"Having all available valence bonds filled; especially of any organic compound containing only single bonds between carbon atoms."}]}]},"length":{"h":"length","i":"/lɛŋθ/","a":"en-us-length.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The length of an object is the distance between one end of that object and the other.","e":"What is the length of the car?"},{"m":"(horse racing) The length of a horse is used to show the distance between horses at the end of a race."},{"m":"(cricket) Length is the distance down the pitch that the ball bounces on its way to the batsman."}]}]},"kick-ass":{"h":"kick-ass","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"; If something is kick ass it is very good (it kicks ass).","e":"The show was totally kick ass."}]}]},"unsaturated":{"h":"unsaturated","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Not saturated; able to dissolve more of a solute at the same temperature."},{"m":"Having atoms share more than one valence bond; especially of an organic compound having one or more double bond or triple bond between carbon atoms."},{"m":"(of a color) Not pure or vivid; diluted."}]}]},"declaration":{"h":"declaration","i":"/ˌdɛklæˈreɪʃən/","a":"en-us-declaration.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A written or spoken statement of a fact, opinion, or belief.","e":"The company has released a declaration of bankruptcy."},{"m":"A list of items for various legal purposes.","e":"customs declaration"},{"m":"The act or process of declaring something.","e":"The principal's declaration lasted almost 30 minutes."},{"m":"(cricket) When the captain of a batting side says an inning is closed."}]}]},"assimilation":{"h":"assimilation","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The act of assimilating or the state of being assimilated."},{"m":"Changing nutrients into tissue."},{"m":"(by extension) Adding new ideas to an old way of thinking."},{"m":"Changing a sound so that it becomes similar to the sound next to it."},{"m":"When a minority group takes on the customs and attitudes of the dominant culture."}]}]},"chip":{"h":"chip","i":"/tʃɪp/","a":"en-us-chip.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A small piece that is broken off of a larger object.","e":"A chip of paint fell off the wall."},{"m":"(countable) A damaged area of a surface where a chip has broken off.","e":"This cup has a chip in it."},{"m":"(countable) A token that is used in place of cash when gambling.","e":"poker chip"},{"m":"(countable) (electronics) A small circuit used in certain electronic devices.","e":"computer chip"},{"m":"(countable) (US) A thin, baked or fried piece of vegetable, usually potato.","e":"potato chips"},{"m":"(countable) (UK, AU, NZ) A fried strip of potato, similar to French fries."},{"m":"(countable) A shot where the ball goes up more than a regular shot."},{"m":"(countable) (curling) A takeout that hits a rock at an angle."},{"m":"(countable) A dried piece of dung that is used as fuel."},{"m":"(countable) A container that is usually used for holding strawberries or other fruit."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To break an object into small pieces.","e":"The workers chipped the dead branches into mulch."},{"m":"(transitive) To break small pieces off of an object.","e":"Be careful not to chip the paint."},{"m":"(transitive); (golf) To play a shot where the ball goes mostly upwards instead of forwards."},{"m":"(transitive); (automotive) To upgrade an engine management system, usually to increase power."},{"m":"(intransitive) To become chipped.","e":"This varnish chips easily."},{"m":"(intransitive); (card games) Often with \"in\", to ante (up)."}]}]},"supposed":{"h":"supposed","i":"/səˈpəʊzd/","a":"en-us-supposed-verb.ogg","l":"suppose","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is supposed, people assume that is it true without having proof that it is true."}]}]},"books":{"h":"books","i":"/bʊks/","a":"en-us-books.ogg","l":"book","q":"noun"},"meadow":{"h":"meadow","i":"/ˈmɛdəʊ/","a":"en-us-meadow.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An open field or grassy area; meadows are often found near rivers.","e":"They found a meadow full of flowers on their walk by the stream."}]}]},"singles":{"h":"singles","l":"single","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"; (uncountable) Singles is a game where each side has only one player, especially in tennis."},{"m":"Singles are people who are not married or not in a romantic relationship.","e":"You'll pay no tax if your income falls below $50,000 for a married couple, $35,000 for singles."}]}]},"chips":{"h":"chips","i":"/t͡ʃɪps/","a":"en-us-chips.ogg","l":"chip","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(UK, Australia) Chips are French fried potatoes; french fries.","e":"fish and chips"},{"m":"(US, Canada) Chips are thin-sliced and deep-fried potatoes that are sold in sealed bags","e":"potato chips"}]}]},"hull":{"h":"hull","i":"/hʌl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-hull.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The outside of a fruit or vegetable."},{"m":"The body of a vessel such as a ship or plane."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To take the covering off of a fruit or vegetable.","e":"She sat on the back porch hulling peanuts."}]}]},"plastic":{"h":"plastic","i":"/ˈplæstɪk/","a":"en-us-plastic.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Plastic is a material that can change its shape and is used to pack products."},{"m":"Plastic is a slang for a credit or debit cards that are used in place of cash to buy things."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is plastic, it is made of plastic.","e":"Cameron is going to recycle some plastic bottles."},{"m":"If someone or something is plastic, it is able to adapt to different conditions.","e":"The brain is very plastic at a young age."}]}]},"third-person":{"h":"third-person","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) When a verb is used in the third person."},{"m":"(uncountable) When a story is told using verbs in the third person; the storyteller is not a character in the story."}]}]},"olive":{"h":"olive","i":"/ˈɒlɪv/","a":"en-uk-olive.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A tree, Olea europaea, that is grown near the Mediterranean Sea for its fruit and the oil that comes from it."},{"m":"The small oval fruit of an olive tree; olives are eaten ripe (usually black) or unripe (usually green)."},{"m":"The wood of the olive tree."},{"m":"A grayish green color, the color of an unripe olive."}]}]},"betrayal":{"h":"betrayal","i":"/bɪˈtreɪəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-betrayal.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The act of betraying."}]}]},"envy":{"h":"envy","i":"/ˈɛnviː/","a":"en-us-envy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A feeling of wanting something that someone else has.","e":"I could feel my envy growing as I watched him play with his children."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To feel envy.","e":"I envy you; you've got a great family, a big house, a new car, and a successful career."}]}]},"sales":{"h":"sales","i":"/seɪlz/","a":"en-us-sales.ogg","l":"sale","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Sales is the number or value of things sold.","e":"The stronger economy has boosted auto sales by $650 million over last year."},{"m":"(uncountable) Sales is the part of a company or industry that tries to get people to buy more.","e":"She's now Seattle's director of marketing and sales."}]}]},"cheek":{"h":"cheek","i":"/tʃiːk/","a":"en-us-cheek.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The soft skin on each side of the face, below the eyes.","e":"Your cheeks are really rosy today."},{"m":"(informal); (usually plural) A buttock.","e":"Those pants are so tight that you can see each of her butt cheeks."},{"m":"(informal) Having no respect.","e":"You’ve got some cheek, asking me for money!"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To not show respect towards someone.","e":"Don't cheek me, you little rascal!"}]}]},"curitiba":{"h":"Curitiba","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Curitiba is the name of the largest city in the south of Brazil, and the capital of the state of Paraná."}]}]},"headword":{"h":"headword","i":"/ˈhɛdwɜːd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-headword.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A word that is used as the title of a section, especially in a dictionary, encyclopedia, or thesaurus."},{"m":"(countable) A headword is the word under which a set of related dictionary or encyclopedia entries appears."},{"m":"The headword of a phrase is the most important word in the phrase."}]}]},"censorship":{"h":"censorship","i":"/ˈsɛnsəˌʃɪp/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-censorship.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Censorship is when freedom of speech is limited or when written material is changed or deleted because someone (a censor) thinks the content is offensive, harmful or sensitive."}]}]},"native":{"h":"native","i":"/ˈneɪtɪv/","a":"en-us-native.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is native, it belongs to you by birth.","e":"This is my native land."},{"m":"If a group of people are native to an area, they have been there since the beginning.","e":"The native peoples of Australia are called aborigines."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A person who is native to a place; the word is sometimes used by colonizers to negatively describe indigenous people.","e":"Some natives must have stolen our cattle."},{"m":"(countable) A native is someone who was born in the place being talked about.","e":"To enter the state beauty contest, you must be a native of the state."}]}]},"jar":{"h":"jar","i":"/dʒɑː/","a":"en-us-jar.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A small cylindrical container usually made of glass or clay."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To knock or strike something sharply.","e":"He hit it with a hammer, hoping he could jar it loose."},{"m":"To shock or surprise.","e":"I think the accident jarred him because he hasn't gotten back in a car since."}]}]},"center":{"h":"center","i":"/ˈsɛntə/","a":"en-us-center.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The center of something, is the place that is as far from its outside as possible.","e":"The president and his problems continue to take center stage in the news."},{"m":"(countable) A center is a building, area, or group of people with a particular purpose.","e":"They have opened a large shopping center in Taipei."},{"m":"(countable) The town center is the place in the town where most of the shops are."},{"m":"(countable) In politics, the center is the position that is not politically right or left."},{"m":"(countable) In sports, a center is a player who plays in the middle of the field, usually an attacker."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you center something, you move it towards the center."}]}]},"pelt":{"h":"pelt","i":"/pɛlt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-pelt.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The skin of an animal with hair on it; a raw hide; a skin with the hairy or woolly covering on it."},{"m":"The human skin."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you pelt somebody, you throw things at them and hit them.","e":"As soon as I got out of my car, my children started pelting me with snowballs."},{"m":"(transitive) If you pelt somebody with questions, words, facts, etc, you say those things quickly, without stopping.","e":"As soon as she got back from Africa, her parents started pelting her with questions about what it was like."},{"m":"(transitive) If one thing pelts against another thing, the first thing bangs or drums on the second thing.","e":"The rain pelted on the roof of the car so loudly that we couldn't hear each other talk."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you pelt someone, you hit them over and over again.","e":"The smaller boy tried to fight the bully, but he got pelted."}]}]},"catastrophe":{"h":"catastrophe","i":"/kə'tæstrəfi/","a":"en-us-catastrophe.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A catastrophe is a violent, sudden and unlucky change, which makes very big problems.","e":"The Great Fire destroyed the city completely. This was a catastrophe."}]}]},"grammars":{"h":"grammars","l":"grammar","q":"noun"},"echoed":{"h":"echoed","i":"/ˈɛkoʊd/","a":"en-us-echoed.ogg","l":"echo","q":"verb"},"thunbergia":{"h":"Thunbergia","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A Thunbergia is a flowering plant."},{"m":"A genus of flowering plants, like as T. alata."}]}]},"rank":{"h":"rank","a":"en-us-rank.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A rank is the position of a person, place, thing, or idea in relation to others based on a shared property such as location, population, or quality.","e":"Based on your test scores, you have a rank of 23."},{"m":"A rank is a level in an organization such as the military.","e":"Private First Class (PFC) is the lowest rank in the Marines."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To rank is to give a rank to a person, place, thing or idea.","e":"Please rank the following fruits from your favourite to your least favourite: pear, apple, watermelon, apple, orange."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is rank has a very strong, bad smell."},{"m":"Something that is rank is gross or disgusting."}]}]},"cyclamen":{"h":"cyclamen","i":"/ˈsɪkləmən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Fae7-cyclamen.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An indoor plant that is cultivated for its white to pink to deep red flowers."},{"m":"(uncountable) A genus of flowering plants, the cyclamen. Cyclamen persicum is the floristic`s cyclamen."}]}]},"wouldn't":{"h":"wouldn't","i":"/ˈwʊdn̩t/","a":"en-us-wouldn't.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive)","e":"My hands were full but she wouldn't open the door for me."}]}]},"bug":{"h":"bug","i":"/bʌɡ/","a":"en-us-bug.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An insect of the order Hemiptera (the \"true bugs\")."},{"m":"Any insect or arachnid may often be called a bug.","e":"These flies are a bother. I’ll get some bug spray and kill them."},{"m":"A problem that needs fixing, especially in computing.","e":"The computer program has a bug in it."},{"m":"A contagious illness caused by bacteria or a virus.","e":"He’s got the flu bug."},{"m":"An enthusiasm for something; an obsession.","e":"I think he’s a gold bug, he has over 10,000 ounces in storage."},{"m":"An electronic listening device.","e":"We installed a bug in her telephone."},{"m":"A small or invisible image on a webpage that is used to track persons who viewed it.","e":"He suspected the image was a web bug used for determining who was visiting the site."},{"m":"A small, usually transparent or translucent image placed in a corner of a television program to indicate what network or cable channel is televising it.","e":"He did not like the network bug that appeared onscreen."},{"m":"Figurative – A manually positioned marker in flight instruments."},{"m":"A semi-automated telegraph key."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive); (informal) To annoy.","e":"Don’t bug me, I’m busy!"},{"m":"(transitive) To put an electronic listening device somewhere.","e":"We need to know what’s going on. We’ll bug his house."}]}]},"buoyancy":{"h":"buoyancy","i":"/ˈbɔɪ.ən.si/","a":"en-au-buoyancy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Buoyancy is the force pushing up on a body in a fluid.","e":"Wood floats in water because of buoyancy."},{"m":"(by extension) or cheerfulness.","e":"I am happy with your buoyancy after many bad things happened to you."}]}]},"wheelchair":{"h":"wheelchair","i":"/ˈwiːlt͡ʃɛə(r)/","a":"en-us-wheelchair.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A wheelchair is a chair with large wheels that is used by a sick or disabled person.","e":"He broke both of his legs while skiing so he'll be in a wheelchair for the next few months."}]}]},"rear":{"h":"rear","i":"/rɪə/","a":"en-us-rear.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The back of something; something that is behind.","e":"I painted the rear of the house."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To raise or lift up."},{"m":"(transitive) To educate and care for a young one until maturity."},{"m":"(transitive) To breed or raise livestock."}]}]},"factory":{"h":"factory","i":"/ˈfæktəri/","a":"en-uk-factory.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A factory is a building where lots of things are made.","e":"This factory makes one hundred cars every day."},{"m":"A factory is anything that makes other things, especially if it makes a really large amount of things."}]}]},"crown":{"h":"crown","i":"/kraʊn/","a":"en-ca-crown.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A crown is a round-shaped ring that kings and queens wear on the head. It is made of expensive metals. It might have jewels too.","e":"The queen wore a fancy crown."},{"m":"(countable) The crown is the position of a sovereign (in a monarchy)."},{"m":"The top part of the head."},{"m":"(dentistry) A prosthetic covering for a tooth."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To put a crown on someone's head."},{"m":"To formally announce the new king or emperor.","e":"After the death of the old king, the new king was crowned."},{"m":"To declare the winner."},{"m":"During birth, when the baby's head is seen in the mother's vaginal opening.","e":"The mother was in the second stage of labor and the baby had just crowned, so the midwives encouraged her."}]}]},"pop":{"h":"pop","i":"/pɒp/","a":"en-ca-pop.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A loud sound, like a cork coming out of a bottle."},{"m":"A fizzy drink, such as cola.","e":"Coca-cola is my favorite brand of pop."},{"m":"Another word for father.","e":"My pop used to tell me to do my homework every night."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To burst something, most commonly a balloon.","e":"The boy used a needle to pop the balloon."}]}]},"tap":{"h":"tap","i":"/tæp/","a":"en-us-tap.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A device that liquids come out of.","e":"We don't have bottled water, you'll have to get it from the tap."},{"m":"(countable) A repeated touching of one's hands, foot or other body part.","e":"When Steve felt a tap on his shoulder, he turned around."},{"m":"(countable) A connection made to an electrical or fluid conductor without breaking it.","e":"The system was barely keeping pressure due to all of the ill advised taps along its length."},{"m":"(countable) (mechanical) A tool used to cut an internal screw thread. (External screw threads are cut with a die.)","e":"We drilled a hole and then cut the threads with the proper tap to match the valve's thread."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To access a resource or object.","e":"Steve tapped the keg so we could drink beer."},{"m":"To touch someone or something lightly with your finger, hand, or foot, sometimes repeatedly.","e":"I tap my fingers on the table when I get bored."},{"m":"To place a listening or recording device on a telephone connection.","e":"They can't tap the phone without a warrant."},{"m":"(mechanical) To cut an internal screw thread.","e":"Tap an M3 thread all the way through the hole."}]}]},"vassal":{"h":"vassal","i":"/ˈvæsəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-vassal.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A vassal is a subject of a superior lord and pledges his loyalty to his lord."},{"m":"A subject; a dependant; a servant; a slave."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To treat someone as a vassal or to reduce him to the position of a vassal; to control; to enslave."},{"m":"(transitive) To subordinate yourself to someone or something."}]}]},"anilingus":{"h":"anilingus","i":"/ˌeɪnɪˈlɪŋɡəs/","a":"anilingus US.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Anilingus is when a person stimulates another person's anus with their tongue."}]}]},"klingon":{"h":"Klingon","i":"/ˈklɪŋɒn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Klingon.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A type of alien on Star Trek."},{"m":"(uncountable) The language spoken by Klingons."}]}]},"motherfucker":{"h":"motherfucker","i":"/ˈmʌðəˌfʌkə/","a":"en-us-motherfucker.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(taboo) (countable) A very insulting word to call someone you don't like.","e":"That motherfucker just scratched my car and drove away!"},{"m":"(literal) (taboo) (countable) A person who has sex with his mother.","e":"is a literal motherfucker."}]}]},"fuckhead":{"h":"fuckhead","i":"/ˈfʌkˌhɛd/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A very insulting word to call someone you don't like; a stupid or unlikable person.","e":"That fuckhead has been cheating on me with my best friend!"}]}]},"twat":{"h":"twat","i":"/twɑt/","a":"en-uk-twat.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A very insulting word for someone.","e":"How about some shit you little twat?"},{"m":"A very rude word for a vagina."}]}]},"vagina":{"h":"vagina","i":"/vəˈdʒaɪnə/","a":"en-us-vagina.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A vagina is a tube that goes from the vulva to the uterus of female mammals."}]}]},"yeah":{"h":"yeah","i":"/jɛ/","a":"en-us-yeah.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"(informal) yes","e":"Yeah, sure, I'll go with you to the store."}]},{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"Used to show excitement or joy.","e":"I won! Yeah!"}]}]},"reader":{"h":"reader","i":"/ˈridɚ/","a":"en-us-reader.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A reader is somebody or something that reads.","e":"I would describe myself as a reader because I'm always reading books."}]}]},"arsehole":{"h":"arsehole","i":"/ˈɑː(r)s.hoʊl/","a":"en-uk-arsehole2.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The anus, the hole in the bottom where feces comes out."},{"m":"A rude or cruel person; a jerk.","e":"Don't be an arsehole."}]}]},"blowjob":{"h":"blowjob","i":"/ˈbləʊdʒɒb/","a":"en-us-blowjob.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A blowjob is when someone stimulates a penis with their mouth.","e":"Mary gave John a blowjob."}]}]},"tit":{"h":"tit","i":"/tɪt/","a":"en-au-tit.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A small bird of the genus or the family that is common in the northern hemisphere."},{"m":"(countable) A mammary gland or teat."},{"m":"(usually plural) A woman's breast.","e":"She's got an amazing pair of tits."},{"m":"(countable) An idiot; a fool.","e":"Look at that tit driving on the wrong side of the road!"},{"m":"(countable) A small horse; a nag.","e":"* 1759, he was resolved, for the time to come, to ride his tit with more sobriety. — Laurence Sterne, The Life & Opinions of Tristram Shandy, Gentleman (Penguin 2003, p.&nbsp;28)"},{"m":"(countable) A young girl, especially a hussy."}]}]},"fart":{"h":"fart","i":"/fɑːt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-fart.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(informal) A fart is the air that comes out of an anus; the air is produced by digestion.","e":"I accidentally let out a loud fart in class today. I was so embarrassed!"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(informal) If you fart, you release air from your anus.","e":"Do you smell something? I think somebody farted."}]}]},"cunt":{"h":"cunt","i":"/kʌnt/","a":"en-au-cunt.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A woman's cunt is her genitalia, especially the vulva.","e":"I want to fuck her cunt."},{"m":"A cunt is a very unpleasant person (in the US, usually a woman; in the Commonwealth, usually a man).","e":"You cunt!"}]}]},"fucker":{"h":"fucker","i":"/ˈfʌk.ə(r)/","a":"en-uk-fucker.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A bad, nasty person or someone you don't like.","e":"You fucker! You wrecked my car!"},{"m":"An object that requires some effort.","e":"Let's see if we can fix this fucker."},{"m":";; (jokingly) People or friends, usually said between people who have a bond.","e":"What's up, fuckers?"},{"m":"(countable) A person who has sex.","e":"He is a great fucker because he makes me have an orgasm."}]}]},"shitty":{"h":"shitty","i":"/ˈʃɪti/","a":"en-au-shitty.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"; Very bad; unpleasant; miserable.","e":"Kicking the dog was a really shitty thing to do."}]}]},"dusty":{"h":"dusty","i":"/ˈdʌsti/","a":"en-us-dusty.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is dusty, it is covered in dust.","e":"I don't think this book has been touched in a long time because it's very dusty."},{"m":"If something is dusty, it is powdery or it looks like dust."}]}]},"gum":{"h":"gum","a":"en-us-gum.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A thick liquid that come from plants or trees that hardens into solids."},{"m":"A thick liquid such as a resin or glue."},{"m":".","e":"Could I have a stick of gum? I think my breath smells bad."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To chew something; often used when a toothless person or animal chews something.","e":"That old dog's been gumming that bone for hours."},{"m":"To apply an adhesive or gum to something."},{"m":"As \"gum up\", to spoil or ruin a thing or process."}]}]},"happiness":{"h":"happiness","i":"/ˈhæpinɪs/","a":"en-us-happiness.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Happiness is the emotion of being happy; joy.","e":"I hope that your new job brings you happiness."}]}]},"sadness":{"h":"sadness","i":"/ˈsædnəs/","a":"en-us-sadness.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The emotion of being sad.","e":"I felt great sadness when my mother died."}]}]},"flown":{"h":"flown","i":"/ˈfləʊn/","a":"en-us-flown.ogg","l":"fly","q":"verb"},"moral":{"h":"moral","i":"/ˈmɒrəl/","a":"en-us-moral.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A moral action or decision is one that is good or right not evil or harmful.","e":"John, don't do that, it's not very moral."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Teachings of what is right and what is wrong.","e":"Mr. Johnson is known for his good morals."},{"m":"Something that is learned from a story or event; a lesson.","e":"The moral of is \"slow and steady wins the race\"."}]}]},"indigo":{"h":"indigo","i":"/ˈɪndɪˌgoʊ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-indigo.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A purplish-blue color"},{"m":"A blue dye taken from certain plants (the indigo plant or woad), or a similar synthetic dye."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Having a deep blue colour."}]},{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Indigo is a female given name."}]}]},"musical":{"h":"musical","i":"/ˈmju.zɪ.kəl/","a":"en-us-musical.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is musical it makes music or is about music.","e":"A drum is a musical instrument."},{"m":"If a person is musical, they are good at making music or often make music.","e":"My cousin is very musical and can play many songs and musical instruments."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A musical is a theatrical production with music, dance, and spoken words.","e":"My favorite musical is \"Wicked\"."}]}]},"woo":{"h":"woo","i":"/wuː/","a":"en-us-woo.ogg","s":[{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"You may yell woo or woo-hoo to show happy excitement."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you woo someone, you try to get that person to like you, date you or marry you."}]}]},"hatred":{"h":"hatred","i":"/h'eɪtrεd/","a":"en-us-hatred.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Hatred is another word for hate. If you have hatred for someone, then you very strongly dislike that person.","e":"I can't believe he has such hatred for other races! -- what did they do to him?"}]}]},"carbon":{"h":"carbon","i":"/ˈkɑrbən/","a":"en-us-carbon.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The chemical element (symbol C) with an atomic number of 6."},{"m":"(countable); (informal) A piece of carbon paper.","e":"Make sure the carbon is facing the second sheet of paper, before rolling it into the typewriter."},{"m":"(countable); (informal) A carbon copy."},{"m":"A fossil fuel that is made of impure carbon, such as coal or charcoal."},{"m":"(uncountable); (ecology), when talking about global warming and climate change.","e":"A carbon footprint is a figure that measures how much carbon dioxide an activity adds to the atmosphere."}]}]},"sulfur":{"h":"sulfur","i":"/ˈsʌl.fə/","a":"en-us-sulfur.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A chemical element (symbol S) with an atomic number of 16."},{"m":"A yellowish-green color, like that of sulfur."}]}]},"successfully":{"h":"successfully","i":"/səkˈsɛsfəli/","a":"en-us-successfully.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"In a successful way; with success; without failing.","e":"He successfully climbed the mountain."}]}]},"speaker":{"h":"speaker","i":"/ˈspikɚ/","a":"en-us-speaker.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A speaker is a person that speaks.","e":"Bob is a native English speaker."},{"m":"(countable) A loudspeaker.","e":"My new radio has two speakers."},{"m":"(countable) A person that says a speech.","e":"A famous speaker came to talk about agriculture."},{"m":"(countable) A person who speaks for a group."}]}]},"loudspeaker":{"h":"loudspeaker","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A machine that makes sound.","e":"Everyone in the building heard her message as she spoke through the loudspeaker."}]}]},"microphone":{"h":"microphone","i":"/ˈmaɪ.krəˌfoʊn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-microphone.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A device that converts sound into electricity; microphones send sound to be broadcast or recorded.","e":"We can't hear you! Speak into the microphone!"}]}]},"hydrogen":{"h":"hydrogen","i":"/ˈhaɪdrədʒən/","a":"en-us-hydrogen.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Hydrogen is the lightest chemical element (symbol H) with an atomic number of 1.","e":"Hydrogen gas is highly flammable."}]}]},"punch":{"h":"punch","i":"/pʌntʃ/","a":"en-us-punch.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you punch something, you use your fist to hit it.","e":"To use a punch to put a hole in something or to put a design on it."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hit done with your fist."},{"m":"(countable) A tool that is used to put holes in thin material (like paper), to put an object through a hole in an object, or to put a mark or design on a surface."},{"m":"(countable) A tool for punching holes in paper or other thin material."},{"m":"(countable) A hole or opening created with a punch."},{"m":"(uncountable) A drink that is a mixture of fruit juice and some other drink, often alcohol."},{"m":"(uncountable); impact; strength; oomph."}]}]},"notebook":{"h":"notebook","i":"/ˈnəʊtˌbʊk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-notebook.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A notebook is a book with blank sheets that you can write or draw in.","e":"Remember to take your notebook to class."},{"m":"(countable) Sometimes laptop computers are called notebooks; this is not as common as calling them laptops.","e":"They played a game on their notebook."}]}]},"hey":{"h":"hey","i":"/heɪ/","a":"en-us-hey.ogg","s":[{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"(informal) You say, \"hey\" in greeting when you meet or see somebody.","e":"Hey, how's it going? [Hello, how are you?]"},{"m":"(informal) You shout (say loudly) \"hey\" to get someone to notice you.","e":"Hey, what are you doing!?"}]}]},"youngster":{"h":"youngster","i":"/ˈjʌŋstə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-youngster.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A youngster is young person, someone who is not an adult. Usually this means a child, but sometimes can mean an adolescent or a baby.","e":"The youngsters are playing outside."},{"m":"A young animal."}]}]},"grace":{"h":"grace","i":"/greɪs/","a":"en-us-grace.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Grace is free giving.","e":"We were saved by the grace of God."},{"m":"(countable) A grace is a freely given gift."},{"m":"(uncountable) Grace is the ability to move in a way that seems to flow and looks easy.","e":"The dancers moved with incredible grace."},{"m":"(countable) A grace is a good quality of a person or thing."},{"m":"(countable) A grace is a prayer said for a meal.","e":"Don't forget to say grace, before you eat!."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To alight, to land, to appear.","e":"He graced the room with his presence."}]}]},"lovely":{"h":"lovely","i":"/ˈlʌvli/","a":"en-us-lovely.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is lovely, that person is very good to look at. A lovely person is someone that you might love if you saw her or him.","e":"She is such a lovely girl."},{"m":"If a thing is lovely, seeing it makes you feel good.","e":"We had a lovely view of the mountains."},{"m":"If something is lovely it is very good.","e":"I think your idea is lovely."},{"m":"You can call something lovely for sarcasm if you find it very bad. When you do this, you really mean it is not lovely at all.","e":"I have a flat tire, now that's just lovely!"}]}]},"known":{"h":"known","i":"/nəʊn/","a":"en-us-known.ogg","l":"know","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is known, people know about it; it is famous.","e":"It is a known fact that water freezes at 0°C."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"In algebra, a variable or constant whose value is already determined."},{"m":"Any fact or situation which is well-researched or familiar."}]}]},"killed":{"h":"killed","i":"/kɪld/","a":"en-us-killed.ogg","l":"kill","q":"verb"},"dangerous":{"h":"dangerous","i":"/ˈdeɪnʒ(ə)rəs/","a":"en-uk-dangerous.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is dangerous, it causes danger; something that can hurt or kill a person.","e":"A tiger is a very dangerous animal."}]}]},"friendly":{"h":"friendly","i":"/ˈfrɛndli/","a":"en-us-friendly.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is friendly they are willing to become a friend, or they act like they are a friend."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"In war, a friendly is someone on your side."}]}]},"dummy":{"h":"dummy","i":"/dʌmi/","a":"EN-AU ck1 dummy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A dummy is a model of a person. A dummy is often used to show clothes or test safety.","e":"The dress looked better on the dummy."},{"m":"(countable) A dummy is a person who is stupid; if someone is a dummy they are not intelligent.","e":"You got good grades, I know you are not a dummy."},{"m":"(countable) A dummy is something that is not there but people act like its there for some purpose.","e":"That file is just a dummy to help the program start."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A dummy thing is something that is not there or is not the thing it is called.","e":"They used a dummy account to make the records look right."}]}]},"hay":{"h":"hay","i":"/heɪ/","a":"en-us-hey.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Hay is tall grass that has been cut and dried. Hay is often used to feed animals."}]}]},"dumb":{"h":"dumb","i":"/dʌm/","a":"en-ca-dumb.oga","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"(offensive when describing a person) Not able to speak. If someone is dumb they can not say anything.","e":"They went to a school for the deaf and dumb."},{"m":"Another word for stupid. If you are dumb you are not intelligent.","e":"That is a really dumb idea."},{"m":"Temporarily unable or unwilling to speak."}]}]},"livestock":{"h":"livestock","i":"/ˈlʌɪvstɒk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-livestock.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Farm animals","e":"My uncle raises livestock for a living."}]}]},"nigga":{"h":"nigga","i":"/ˈnɪɡə/","a":"en-us-ncalif-nigga.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Another way to say nigger; it is often offensive, but is usually less offensive than nigger. Most often used by violent gangs.","e":"Hey, what's up, nigga?"}]}]},"marijuana":{"h":"marijuana","i":"/ˌmɛrɪˈwɑ.nə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-marijuana.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Marijuana is a drug that is smoked for a euphoric feeling.","e":"After smoking a bowl of that fine marijuana, they ate some brownies."},{"m":"(countable) Marijuana is the hemp plant itself, Cannabis sativa."}]}]},"bookshelf":{"h":"bookshelf","i":"/ˈbʊkˌʃɛlf/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-bookshelf.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bookshelf is a shelf that hold books.","e":"The book should be on the bookshelf."}]}]},"dickhead":{"h":"dickhead","a":"en-us-dickhead.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A mean and/or stupid person.","e":"Shut up, dickhead!"}]}]},"depth":{"h":"depth","i":"/dɛpθ/","a":"en-us-depth.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The distance below a surface; how deep something is.","e":"Measure the depth of the water in this part of the bay."},{"m":"The distance between the front and the back, such as the depth of a drawer or closet."},{"m":"How intense, complex, strong, serious or important an emotion or situation is.","e":"The depth of her misery was obvious to everyone."},{"m":"(art, photography) Looking three-dimensional.","e":"The depth of field in this picture is amazing."}]}]},"movie":{"h":"movie","i":"/ˈmuːvi/","a":"en-us-movie.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A movie is a motion picture that tells a story and is shown on a screen or television.","e":"That was a really good movie as the story was interesting."},{"m":"(usually plural) The movies are a place a movie is shown.","e":"We're going to the movies."}]}]},"cooked":{"h":"cooked","i":"/kʊkt/","a":"en-us-cooked.ogg","l":"cook","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When food is cooked, it is prepared using heat."}]}]},"taxi":{"h":"taxi","i":"/ˈtæk.si/","a":"en-us-taxi.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A taxi is a vehicle (usually a car) driven by a taxi driver; the taxi driver drives you somewhere if you pay them money."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To drive an aircraft around an airport on the ground."}]}]},"niggas":{"h":"niggas","l":"nigga","q":"noun"},"sicker":{"h":"sicker","i":"/ˈsɪkɚ/","a":"en-uk-sicker.ogg","l":"sick","q":"adjective"},"bullshit":{"h":"bullshit","i":"/ˈbʊlʃɪt/","a":"en-au-bullshit.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"; Clearly false.","e":"That's bullshit! I called your office and they said you never came in!"},{"m":"; A card game where players bluff about the cards they play and try to figure out when the other players are bluffing.","e":"Anyone want to play a few hands of bullshit?"},{"m":"; An object of frustration and/or disgust.","e":"\"This is bullshit!\" -- The Monarch"},{"m":"(literally) The feces of a bull."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"; To tell lies, exaggerate; to mislead; to deceive.","e":"You're bullshitting me. I called your office and you never even came in."},{"m":"; To talk casually with no real purpose.","e":"I will probably just go and bullshit with Joe for awhile."}]},{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"; Something you say when you don't believe what you just heard."}]}]},"smart":{"h":"smart","i":"/smɑrt/","a":"en-us-smart.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Someone who is smart shows intelligence.","e":"My friend is really smart; he has an IQ of 152."}]}]},"shortcut":{"h":"shortcut","i":"/'ʃɔːtkʌt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-shortcut.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A shortcut is an easier and/or faster way.","e":"We took the shortcut on the way home so we could get there faster."},{"m":"A shortcut is a symlink (symbolic file link); an icon.","e":"I created a shortcut for the program and placed it on the desktop."}]}]},"distribute":{"h":"distribute","i":"/dɨˈstrɪbjuːt/","a":"en-us-distribute.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you distribute something, you divide it and give it out.","e":"Please distribute this poster to all the people on that list."}]}]},"adopt":{"h":"adopt","i":"/əˈdɑpt/","a":"en-us-adopt.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you adopt something, you choose and begin to use it instead of what you used in the past.","e":"Now that we know they work, it is important that these policies be adopted by other districts."},{"m":"If you adopt a child, you make them part of your own family.","e":"They finally quit trying to have their own child and ended up adopting a baby girl."}]}]},"advance":{"h":"advance","i":"/ədˈvɑːns/","a":"en-us-advance.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"If something is in advance of something else, it is before it.","e":"They gave us notice 30 days in advance of closing the factory."},{"m":"(countable) An advance is a move forward.","e":"The advances in technology will be in the next decade or so."},{"m":"(countable) An advance is an amount of money given to someone before they normally get it.","e":"The band received a $6 million advance on the new album even before they started recording."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you advance something, you bring or move it forward.","e":"In separate attacks, the Khmer Rouge was advancing toward Siem Reap, 200 miles northwest of Phnom Penh."},{"m":"(transitive) If you advance someone some money, you pay it to them before they would normally get it.","e":"They advanced her $12,000 against future earnings."}]}]},"consensus":{"h":"consensus","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) If there is consensus among people, they generally agree on something.","e":"There was broad consensus that the first project had failed."},{"m":"Average projected value, as in the finance term consensus forecast."},{"m":"A way to make decisions; consensus says that people agree to an action if no one opposes it."}]}]},"possessive":{"h":"possessive","i":"/pəˈzɛsɪv/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-possessive.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Not willing to share someone/something; wanting to control someone/something.","e":"He is very possessive of his car and won't let anyone else drive it."},{"m":"Showing ownership, possession or origin.","e":"There are seven possessive pronouns in modern English: mine, yours, his, hers, its, ours, and theirs."}]}]},"impersonal":{"h":"impersonal","i":"/ɪmˈpɝsənəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-impersonal.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Not personal; not representing a person; not having personality.","e":"An almighty but impersonal power, called Fate. –Sir J. Stephen."},{"m":"Not showing emotion or warmth; cold.","e":"She sounded impersonal as she gave her report of the Nazi death camps."},{"m":"Used to describe a phrase or sentence with a personal pronoun that does not refer to a specific person or thing.","e":"\"It is raining\" and \"You shouldn't drink and drive\" are impersonal phrases."}]}]},"magenta":{"h":"magenta","i":"/məˈʤɛntə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-magenta.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A light purple, purplish-red, or pinkish purple color that is made by mixing red and blue light"}]}]},"embarrassment":{"h":"embarrassment","i":"/ɪmˈbærəsmənt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-embarrassment.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A feeling of discomfort, shame, self-consciousness or humiliation."},{"m":"A person or thing which causes another person to feel shame or humiliation.","e":"Kevin, you are an embarrassment to this family."}]}]},"offensive":{"h":"offensive","i":"/əˈfɛnsɪv/","a":"en-us-offensive.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something offensive is mean, insulting, and unpleasant.","e":"He said something so offensive to her that she cried."},{"m":"(team sports) If something is offensive, it has to do with a play where the team is trying to score.","e":"The offensive coordinator is responsible for ordering all rushing plays."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An attack.","e":"The Marines today launched a major offensive."},{"m":"(uncountable) In a position of attacking or being able to attack.","e":"He took the offensive in the press, accusing his opponent of corruption."}]}]},"africa":{"h":"Africa","i":"/ˈæfrɪkə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Justinrleung-Africa.wav","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Africa is the continent that is south of Europe, east of the Atlantic Ocean, west of the Indian Ocean and north of Antarctica.","e":"Africa is the world's second-largest and second most-populous continent, after Asia."}]}]},"crybaby":{"h":"crybaby","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A nickname for someone who cries often or whose feelings are easily hurt.","e":"Sam is such a crybaby; I told him that he was ugly and he started crying!"}]}]},"babe":{"h":"babe","a":"en-us-babe.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A baby or infant, often used in poetry.","e":"These events happened when he was just a babe."},{"m":"A good-looking person, usually a woman.","e":"She's a real babe!"},{"m":"An affectionate word that is similar to darling.","e":"Hey, babe, how about you and me getting together?"}]}]},"indy":{"h":"Indy","i":"/ˈɪndi/","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"A nickname for Indianapolis, Indiana.","e":"The Indianapolis 500 race is often called the Indy 500 for short."}]}]},"jewish":{"h":"Jewish","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are Jewish then you are a Jew."},{"m":"If something is Jewish it has to do with Judaism or with Jewish culture. This can also used for things that have to do with Jews.","e":"Gefilte, a kind of fish, is a Jewish food."}]}]},"herb":{"h":"herb","i":"/hɜː(r)b/","a":"en-au-herb.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Any plant or part of a plant that is used to flavor or season food."},{"m":"(countable) A plant whose roots, leaves or seeds are used in medicine."},{"m":"(countable)."},{"m":"(countable) A plant whose stem is not woody."}]}]},"koran":{"h":"Koran","i":"/kəˈrɑn/","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"The Koran is the holy book of Islam. It contains messages that Muslims believe were given to the prophet Muhammad by the angel Gabriel. Muslims believe these messages come from God."}]}]},"goddess":{"h":"goddess","i":"/ˈɡɒd.ɛs/","a":"en-us-goddess.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A goddess is a female or feminine god.","e":"Isis is an ancient Egyptian goddess."},{"m":"A very good-looking woman.","e":"In that dress, she's a beautiful goddess."}]}]},"wicca":{"h":"Wicca","i":"/wɪkə/","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Wicca is neo-pagan religion which focuses on nature and teaches that many gods are forms of a great God and Goddess. Wicca also involves practicing witchcraft (magic) and followers call themselves Wiccans."}]}]},"paganism":{"h":"paganism","i":"/ˈpeɪɡənɪzm̩/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-paganism.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A kind of religion. Paganism has following meanings:"}]}]},"pagan":{"h":"pagan","i":"/ˈpeɪɡən/","a":"en-us-pagan.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something (or someone) is pagan, it is from a kind of religion called paganism."},{"m":"Relating to a religion that is not a major religion; often anything non-Christian, non-Judaic and non-Islamic."},{"m":"(by extension) Immoral, uncivilized, savage, heathen."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pagan is someone who follows paganism or a polytheistic religion."},{"m":"A person who doesn't follow a major religion; often used to refer to non-Christians, non-Jews and non-Muslims."},{"m":"(by extension) Someone who is immoral, uncivilized, savage, or a heathen."}]}]},"buddhism":{"h":"Buddhism","i":"/ˈbu.dɪ.zəm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Buddhism.wav","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Buddhism is a religion and philosophy based on the teachings of Buddha that teaches enlightenment can be achieved by ending desire and attachment.","e":"Buddhism is often practiced in Japan, Tibet, and Korea."}]}]},"hinduism":{"h":"Hinduism","i":"/hɪn.du.ɪz.əm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Hinduism.wav","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"The traditional religion of India. Hinduism teaches that many gods exist but are all parts of one God.","e":"The ideas of karma comes from Hinduism."}]}]},"islam":{"h":"Islam","i":"/ˈɪs.lɑːm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Islam.wav","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Islam is a religion that teaches there is only one God, that Muhammad is his prophet, and that the Koran is God's scripture.","e":"There is a close historical relationship between Christianity and Islam."}]}]},"judaism":{"h":"Judaism","i":"/ˈd͡ʒuːˌdeɪ.ɪz.əm/","a":"en-us-Judaism.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Judaism is the religion of the Jews. Judaism is from ancient Israel but has changed since ancient times. It teaches that there is one God and that the Jews are his chosen (special) people."}]}]},"taoism":{"h":"Taoism","i":"/daʊ.ɪz.əm/","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"The traditional religion of China. Taoism teaches people to live in harmony with the natural way (called the Tao, which means way in Chinese)."}]}]},"sikhism":{"h":"Sikhism","i":"/'sik.ɪz.əm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Sikhism.wav","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"A religion from India. Sikhism is based on mixing ideas from Islam and Hinduism, but adds other ideas. It teaches harmony between all religions."}]}]},"confucianism":{"h":"Confucianism","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"A philosophy from China, based on the teachings of Confucius about loyalty, duty, and family. Confucianism is usually called a religion, but not everyone agrees about that.","e":"Influenced by Confucianism, Chinese people commonly possess respect for social norms and make efforts to create harmony."}]}]},"qur'an":{"h":"Qur'an","i":"/kəˈrɑn/","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"The Qur'an is the holy book of Islam. It contains messages that Muslims believe were given to the prophet Muhammad by the angel Gabriel. Muslims believe these messages come from God."}]}]},"shamanism":{"h":"shamanism","i":"/ˈʃeɪmənɪzəm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-shamanism.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A kind of religion based on animism (the belief that everything has a spirit), and the practice of special people called shamans.","e":"Different kinds of shamanism are found all over the world."},{"m":"The practice of a shaman."}]}]},"jainism":{"h":"Jainism","i":"/ˈd͡ʒeɪnɪzm̩/","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Jainism is a religion from India that teaches refraining from violence towards any living entity."}]}]},"wiccan":{"h":"Wiccan","i":"/ˈwɪkən/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A Wiccan is someone who believes or follows Wicca.","e":"I dated a Wiccan once."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is Wiccan it has to do with Wicca.","e":"Sabbats and Esbats are Wiccan holidays."}]}]},"shaman":{"h":"shaman","i":"/ˈʃɑː.mən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-shaman.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A shaman is a holy person from shamanism. A shaman's job is to enter the spirit world and talk to spirits. Shaman usually do other things, like try to make sick people well, to see the future, or to bring good weather or good luck."}]}]},"satanism":{"h":"Satanism","i":"/ˈseɪtənɪzm/","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Satanism is any religion (real or not real) that worships or follows Satan."}]}]},"satanic":{"h":"satanic","i":"/seɪˈtænɪk/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is satanic, it has to do with Satan."},{"m":"(by extension) If someone or something is satanic, it is evil, devilsh or fiendish."},{"m":"If something is satanic, it has to do with Satanism.","e":"Last Sunday he went to a satanic ritual instead of church."}]}]},"evil":{"h":"evil","i":"/ˈiːvəl/","a":"en-us-evil.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"The opposite of good, if something is evil it is very far from good or is against good. This usually means in a way that is not moral or not ethical.","e":"Hitler was a very evil person."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The quality of being evil; evilness.","e":"He was so full of evil I do not think he knew what good was."},{"m":"Something that causes harm, or harm itself.","e":"We faced many evils on our journey."},{"m":"The source or cause of evil as a spiritual or supernatural force. This is often called true evil.","e":"I have seen things that lead me to believe that real evil exists."}]}]},"demon":{"h":"demon","i":"/ˈdiː.mən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-demon.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A demon is an evil spirit."},{"m":"(countable) A demon is a fallen angel or satanic being; a false god.","e":"He said a demon appeared magically and told him to do these evil things."},{"m":"(countable) A demon is a person's inner spirit or genius, a daimon."},{"m":"(countable) A demon is a flaw in a person's character.","e":"The demon of stupidity haunts me whenever I open my mouth."}]}]},"beginner":{"h":"beginner","i":"/bɪˈɡɪnə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-beginner.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A beginner is someone who has just started something and has little or no experience.","e":"John is a beginner at football."},{"m":"It can also be somebody who starts something off.","e":"The beginner of the lit the torch."}]}]},"wild":{"h":"wild","i":"/waɪld/","a":"en-us-wild.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If an animal or plant is wild it is not tame. This means it lives in nature and people have not changed it.","e":"Wolves and bears are wild animals."},{"m":"If a person (or thing) is wild they (or it) are not easy to predict, or they do not act civilized.","e":"She is so wild, all she does is drink and party!"},{"m":"If something is wild it is very good or very interesting.","e":"That is a wild shirt you have on!"},{"m":"(playing cards) If a card is wild it can be used as any other card in a game."}]},{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"You can say wild to mean you like something."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The wild (or wilds) is nature or places far from where people live.","e":"We were lost in the wild for a week."}]}]},"jaws":{"h":"jaws","i":"/d͡ʒɔːz/","a":"en-us-jaws.ogg","l":"jaw","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The whole mouth. Usually this is used for a mouth that is."}]}]},"jaw":{"h":"jaw","i":"/ʤɔː/","a":"en-us-jaw.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A jaw is the bottom of the mouth."}]}]},"satan":{"h":"Satan","i":"/ˈseɪtən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Satan.wav","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"(Christianity) The enemy of God and all people. Satan is a fallen angel and the leader of all demons (or devils)."},{"m":"(Judaism) Either a fallen angel (as in Christianity) or an angel that tests people for God."},{"m":"(Islam) A devil that tempts and tests people:"},{"m":"(Satanism) The symbol for perfect person, who a Satanist tries to be."}]}]},"perfectionist":{"h":"perfectionist","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Someone who always tries to be perfect or who has very high standards.","e":"He's a perfectionist, because he said a test score of 99% was bad."}]}]},"mia":{"h":"Mia","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Mia is a female given name; it is sometimes short for Maria."}]}]},"angel":{"h":"angel","i":"/ˈeɪn.dʒəl/","a":"en-uk-angel.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"In some religions and myths, a spirit that delivers messages from God. Often angels are seen as working for God in general.","e":"Gabriel is an important angel in Christianity and Islam."},{"m":"If you call someone an angel you mean they are very good or very beautiful.","e":"You are an angel for all the good things you do."}]}]},"bike":{"h":"bike","i":"/baɪk/","a":"en-us-bike.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A short form of bicycle or motorcycle."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To ride a bike or to travel by bike.","e":"I biked so much yesterday that I'm very sore today."}]}]},"sexy":{"h":"sexy","i":"/ˈsɛk.sɪ/","a":"en-au-sexy.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Someone or something that is sexually attractive.","e":"That woman is sexy."}]}]},"website":{"h":"website","i":"/ˈwɛbˌsaɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-website.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A website is a place on the World Wide Web; if there are many pages to a website, they have the same URL and are usually part of the same server.","e":"My favorite websites are ebay.com, espn.com, and facebook.com."}]}]},"gay":{"h":"gay","i":"/geɪ/","a":"en-us-gay.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"or cheerful.","e":"I'm very gay today!"},{"m":", festive or bright.","e":"Don we now our gay apparel...."},{"m":"(can be offensive) A gay person is usually a man sexually attracted to males; also a woman attracted to females..","e":"Gay marriage used to be impossible, but it's becoming more common."},{"m":", not cool, it's exactly the antonym of senses 1 and 2.","e":"This game is gay. Let's play something else."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(often offensive) A homosexual person. This is usually a man, but could be a woman (lesbian).","e":"The gays were marching in protest yesterday."}]}]},"cocaine":{"h":"cocaine","i":"/kə(ʊ)ˈkeɪn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-cocaine.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) An addictive drug in the form of a white powder that users generally take by sniffing it through their nose; cocaine is a stimulant and a narcotic."},{"m":"Chrystalline tropan alkaloid"}]}]},"evilness":{"h":"evilness","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The quality of being evil. If you have evilness you behave badly."}]}]},"lesbian":{"h":"lesbian","i":"/ˈlɛz.bɪ.ən/","a":"en-us-lesbian.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A homosexual woman.","e":"She is attracted to other women; she is a lesbian."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Related to female homosexuality.","e":"She's involved in a lesbian relationship."},{"m":"For lesbians.","e":"We're going to a lesbian bar tonight."}]}]},"sprint":{"h":"sprint","i":"/sprɪnt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-sprint.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A sprint is a short race at a very fast speed."},{"m":"A sprint is a burst of speed or activity.","e":"After playing video games, we took a sprint outside."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you sprint, you run quickly for a short time."}]}]},"lame":{"h":"lame","i":"/leɪm/","a":"en-au-lame.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are lame you are not able to walk well because of a problem with one's feet or legs. This term could sometimes cause offense.","e":"Because I broke my leg and it's in a cast, I'm going to be lame for a while."},{"m":"If it is lame it is not convincing or believable.","e":"He had a really lame excuse for missing the birthday party."},{"m":"Something that is lame is not cool, funny, interesting, fun, or relevant.","e":"He kept telling these lame jokes all night."}]}]},"ditch":{"h":"ditch","i":"/dɪtʃ/","a":"en-us-ditch.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A trench; a long, shallow hole that is used for irrigation or drainage.","e":"Digging ditches has long been considered one of the most arduous forms of manual labor."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To leave without telling anyone.","e":"We are going to ditch the party because it is so lame."},{"m":"(transitive) To throw away, discard or abandon.","e":"Once the sun came out we ditched our rain-gear and started a campfire."}]}]},"calculator":{"h":"calculator","i":"/ˈkæl.kjə.leɪ.tə(r)/","a":"en-us-calculator.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A calculator is a device used for doing mathematical calculation.","e":"The new calculator has a lot of functions."}]}]},"lesbo":{"h":"lesbo","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A lesbian; a homosexual woman."}]}]},"lesbos":{"h":"Lesbos","i":"/ˈlɛz.bɒs/","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"A small island in Greece."}]}]},"celebrity":{"h":"celebrity","i":"/sɪ'lebrɪtɪ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-celebrity.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A famous person.","e":",,, and are celebrities."},{"m":"(uncountable); the quality of being a celebrity.","e":"Sometimes it is hard to deal with the celebrity that comes with being a popular singer around the world."}]}]},"hump":{"h":"hump","i":"/hʌmp/","a":"en-us-hump.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A high place on something, a part that sticks up.","e":"A camel has a hump on its back."},{"m":"Something difficult to get past.","e":"We were over the hump after the big exam."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To have sexual intercourse with.","e":"That jerk just humped her and dumped her!"}]}]},"faggot":{"h":"faggot","i":"/ˈfæ.ɡət/","a":"EN-AU ck1 faggot.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(rare in US) A burning piece of firewood."},{"m":"(UK only) A group of sticks tied together."},{"m":"(UK only) A meatball made from pork."},{"m":"(countable) An offensive word for a gay man, however, it is often used by gay man as a positive and inoffensive term."}]}]},"homosexual":{"h":"homosexual","i":"/ˌhəʊməʊˈsɛksjuːəl/","a":"en-uk-homosexual.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A homosexual is a male sexually attracted to males or a female attracted to females.","e":"One homosexual kid got bullied a lot in our school."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Homosexual is the quality of being sexually attracted to people of the same sex.","e":"That homosexual man had sex with the other man."}]}]},"enemy":{"h":"enemy","i":"/ˈɛnəmi/","a":"en-us-enemy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) If someone is your enemy that person is against you, or does not like you.","e":"I have no enemies that I know of."},{"m":"(countable) In war the enemy is the country or army that is attacking your country or army.","e":"He was sent to jail because he was working for the enemy."}]}]},"exploded":{"h":"exploded","l":"explode","q":"verb"},"escape":{"h":"escape","i":"/ɪˈskeɪp/","a":"en-us-escape.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you escape something (or someone) you get away from it.","e":"Can we escape the storm?"}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A way to get away from something.","e":"I'm afraid we have no escape."}]}]},"dues":{"h":"dues","i":"/duːz/","l":"due","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Dues are the money you pay to a group to be part of that group.","e":"Our club requires $10 a year in dues."},{"m":"If you pay your dues, you gain hard, long-term experience.","e":"If you want to be a famous singer, you will have to pay your dues by singing to small groups for many years."}]}]},"majority":{"h":"majority","i":"/məˈd͡ʒɒrɪti/","a":"en-us-majority.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The biggest of several groups of people or things.","e":"The majority vote will win."},{"m":"More than half, also called a true majority.","e":"A true majority of votes is needed to change the results of the last vote."}]}]},"demagogue":{"h":"demagogue","i":"/ˈdɛməɡɑɡ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-demagogue.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A demagogue is a leader who keeps power by being liked. Usually, this means someone who makes bad policy in order to gain quick popularity."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you demagogue, you speak or do things as a demagogue would."}]}]},"dense":{"h":"dense","i":"/dɛns/","a":"en-us-dense.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is dense the pieces of it are close together, or there is a lot of material in a small space. Dense things are usually heavy and often hard.","e":"A rock is very dense but a sponge is not dense at all."},{"m":"If ideas are dense or a book is dense, a lot of ideas are in a small space."},{"m":"If a person is dense it is not easy to make that person understand. A dense person is stupid."}]}]},"railroad":{"h":"railroad","i":"/ˈreɪlroʊd/","a":"en-us-railroad.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A track or road that a train runs on."},{"m":"A system of trains and tracks."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you railroad a person you get rid of that person quickly. Usually, this means that you force them out or away."},{"m":"If you railroad a person, you send that person to jail or prison unfairly."}]}]},"lawyer":{"h":"lawyer","i":"/ˈlɔːjə(r)/","a":"en-us-lawyer.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A lawyer is an expert in law. A lawyer has the job of standing for other people in court giving them advice about the law.","e":"The defendant got a lawyer to defend him in court."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) (informal) If someone lawyers, they work as a lawyer or practice law."},{"m":"(intransitive) If someone lawyers, they make arguments that are related to the law."}]}]},"national":{"h":"national","i":"/ˈnæʃənəl/","a":"en-us-national.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is national it affects a whole nation or country."},{"m":"If something is national it has to do with a certain nation or country, or with people from that country."},{"m":"If a business is national it is found in all or most parts of a nation or country."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A national is someone who is a citizen of their nation."},{"m":"(usually plural) The nationals is a tournament where people from all over the country come to compete in."}]}]},"nick":{"h":"nick","i":"/nɪk/","a":"en-us-nick.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A nick is a small cut."},{"m":"(countable) A short word for nickname."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you nick something, you make a small cut (a nick) in it."}]}]},"nearly":{"h":"nearly","i":"/ˈnɪəli/","a":"en-us-nearly.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something is nearly it is close to be true, but not true.","e":"He was nearly dead, but we revived him."}]}]},"relative":{"h":"relative","i":"/ˈrɛl.ə.tɪv/","a":"en-us-relative.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Compared to something else.","e":"I feel good relative to yesterday."},{"m":"If something is relative it could be the way it is in different amounts.","e":"We use a relative measure for sound."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Someone you are related to, a member of your family.","e":"My relatives came to visit last night."}]}]},"parental":{"h":"parental","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is parental it has to do with parents (mothers and fathers)."}]}]},"thai":{"h":"Thai","i":"/taɪ/","a":"en-us-Thai.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"The language people use in Thailand."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A Thai is a person from Thailand."}]}]},"tablecloth":{"h":"tablecloth","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A piece of cloth or plastic put over a table. A tablecloth keeps the table clean and is also to make it nice to look at."}]}]},"gotten":{"h":"gotten","i":"/'gɒtən/","a":"en-us-gotten.ogg","l":"get","q":"verb"},"pet":{"h":"pet","i":"/pɛt/","a":"en-us-pet.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pet is an animal that is kept by a person for company and friendship.","e":"I have 4 pets: 2 dogs, a cat and a fish."},{"m":"(countable) A pet is a person who is very loyal to their superior or boss.","e":"She's the teacher's pet."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you pet something, usually an animal, you touch it with your moving hand.","e":"I pet my dog."}]}]},"hairy":{"h":"hairy","i":"/ˈhɛəri/","a":"en-us-hairy.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A hairy person or animal has a lot of hair.","e":"That man's back was so hairy!"},{"m":"A hairy problem or situation is one that is difficult or complex.","e":"It's a hairy problem, and will probably take several weeks to sort out."}]}]},"ancestor":{"h":"ancestor","i":"/ˈæn.sɛs.tɚ/","a":"en-us-ancestor.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An ancestor is a person from whom one is descended. A very similar word is forebear.","e":"We get our customs from our ancestors."},{"m":"Entire species of plants or animals may have ancestor species from which they evolution.","e":"It is thought that an extinct group of apes was the ancestor of the human race."}]}]},"parents":{"h":"parents","i":"/ˈpɛərənts/","a":"en-uk-parents.ogg","l":"parent","q":"noun"},"homophobia":{"h":"homophobia","i":"/ˌhɒ.məˈfəʊ.bi.ə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-homophobia.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A fear of or hating someone who is homosexual."}]}]},"homosexuals":{"h":"homosexuals","l":"homosexual","q":"noun"},"hunts":{"h":"hunts","l":"hunt","q":"noun"},"superlative":{"h":"superlative","i":"/suːˈpɜː.lə.tɪv/","a":"en-us-superlative.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The superlative is the highest level of something."},{"m":"The superlative form of an adjective is the form of the adjective that shows which thing has the most of a certain quality when you compare more than two things; the superlative form is often made by adding \"-est\" to the end of the adjective or by putting \"most\" before it.","e":"The superlative of \"pretty\" is \"prettiest\"."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is superlative, it is very good; it is superb."},{"m":"Related to a superlative."}]}]},"prettiest":{"h":"prettiest","i":"/ˈprɪt.i.ɪst/","l":"pretty","q":"adjective"},"monster":{"h":"monster","i":"/ˈmɒnstə(r)/","a":"en-us-monster.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A scary, fictional creature. \"Monster\" is a very general word, and can mean all kinds of strange or scary beings or animals that are not real.","e":"I thought I saw a monster under my bed but it was just some of my dirty clothes."},{"m":"(countable) (by extention) A very bad person.","e":"He must have been a monster to kill all those children."}]}]},"monsters":{"h":"monsters","l":"monster","q":"noun"},"cuss":{"h":"cuss","i":"/kʌs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-cuss.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you cuss you say a word that is vulgar, insulting, or very impolite.","e":"I lost my temper and cussed at my boss."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(Southern US) Another form of the word curse","e":"King Tut was believed to have made a cuss against anyone who awakes him in his dead."}]}]},"ancestors":{"h":"ancestors","i":"/ˈænsɛstəz/","l":"ancestor","q":"noun"},"prettier":{"h":"prettier","l":"pretty","q":"adjective"},"rad":{"h":"rad","i":"/ræd/","a":"en-au-rad.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Cool, short for \"radical\".","e":"That outfit is so rad!"}]}]},"baseball":{"h":"baseball","i":"/ˈbeɪs.bɔːl/","a":"en-us-baseball.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A sport where you try to hit a ball so that you can run to four bases, causing a run. The team with the most runs after nine or more innings wins.","e":"The New York Yankees are a baseball team."},{"m":"(countable) A ball used in the sport of baseball.","e":"The pitcher threw the baseball as hard as he could."}]}]},"mama":{"h":"mama","i":"/ˈmɑmə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-mama.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Your mama is your mother.","e":"Mama, what's for dinner?"}]}]},"poppa":{"h":"poppa","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(informal) Another word for father","e":"What's up, poppa?"}]}]},"poppas":{"h":"poppas","l":"poppa","q":"noun"},"dawg":{"h":"dawg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"You say this to a close male friend.","e":"Yo, what's up, dawg?"}]}]},"pee":{"h":"pee","i":"/piː/","a":"en-us-pea.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Pee is urine, liquid waste from the body.","e":"The dog got pee on my shoe."},{"m":"(uncountable) (UK) Pence; penny.","e":"I bought these carrots for fifty pee."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To release human liquid waste; to urinate.","e":"I am going to pee in that bush."}]}]},"quietly":{"h":"quietly","i":"/ˈkwaɪ.ɪt.li/","a":"en-us-quietly.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If you do something quietly, you do it without much noise or in a quiet way."}]}]},"uglier":{"h":"uglier","l":"ugly","q":"adjective"},"testicles":{"h":"testicles","l":"testicle","q":"noun"},"testicle":{"h":"testicle","i":"/ˈtɛstɪkəl/","a":"en-us-testicle.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The male sex organ that makes sperm and male hormones; there are two testicles inside the scrotum."}]}]},"demonic":{"h":"demonic","i":"/dɪˈmɒnɪk/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"(not comparable) If a being is demonic, it is a demon.","e":"They were trying to summon a demonic spirit."},{"m":"(not comparable) If something is demonic, it comes from or has to do with a demon (or demons).","e":"The story was about someone who learned to cast demonic spells."},{"m":"If you are demonic you have great energy and strength.","e":"The ancient Celts were said to be demonic in battle."},{"m":"If you are demonic you are a very evil person.","e":"The crazed killer was completely demonic."}]}]},"territory":{"h":"territory","i":"/ˈtɛrɪˌtɔri/","a":"en-us-territory.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A person's, animal's, or group's territory is land he, she, or they claim, own, or control.","e":"The wolf defended its territory."},{"m":"(countable) (by extension) Your territory is what belongs to you. This could mean things, power, mates, or even.","e":"Don't move into my territory in this office, especially not in sales."},{"m":"(countable) A territory large amount of land, like a country or a state. Often, this means a large piece of land claimed as part of a country.","e":"Porta Rico is a U.S. territory, but not a state."}]}]},"defend":{"h":"defend","i":"/dīfĕnd/","a":"en-us-defend.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To remove an attacker; to protect your things and/or."},{"m":"To try to keep the other team from, instead of trying to score."}]}]},"mate":{"h":"mate","i":"/meɪt/","a":"en-us-mate.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mate is someone you do something with.","e":"Nils, my tent mate, was from the same elementary school in the city."},{"m":"(countable);; (UK, Australian) A mate is a friend, usually male.","e":"I'm meeting my mates later, after work."},{"m":"(countable) A mate is an animal's sexual partner.","e":"The zoo has been having trouble getting a mate for the panda."},{"m":"(countable) A mate is a person's husband or wife."},{"m":"(countable) A mate is the other member of a matched pair of objects."},{"m":"(countable) A drink made from yerba mate."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) In animals, to have sex.","e":"The monkeys were going to mate."},{"m":"(transitive) To match two things together.","e":"That morning when they tried to mate her with our bull, she had no idea what to do."}]}]},"dawgs":{"h":"dawgs","l":"dawg","q":"noun"},"celebrities":{"h":"celebrities","l":"celebrity","q":"noun"},"spider":{"h":"spider","i":"/ˈspaɪdə(r)/","a":"En-us-spider.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A spider is an arthropod with eight legs that makes webs to catch its food.","e":"That spider was about to bite me, so I killed it."}]}]},"transgender":{"h":"transgender","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A transgender person is someone who was male but now identifies as female or who was female but identifies as male.","e":"The state's laws block transgender women from doing certain things."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Transgender is a gender for someone who was male but now identifies as female or who was female but identifies as male.","e":"We had a long talk about issues around transgender."},{"m":"(countable) Transgenders are people who are were male but now identify as female or female but now identify as male.","e":"Transwomen (male-to-female transgenders) are more common than transmen."}]}]},"man-made":{"h":"man-made","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is not natural; something made by people.","e":"A cubic zirconium is a man-made diamond."}]}]},"lots":{"h":"lots","a":"en-us-lots.ogg","l":"lot","q":"noun"},"yo":{"h":"yo","s":[{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"A greeting similar to \"hi\".","e":"Yo, man, how have you been lately?"},{"m":"A word similar to \"hey\".","e":"Yo, dude! What was that for?"}]},{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"; (informal); (non-standard) Another way to say \"your\".","e":"Yo mama's so fat they filmed 'Gorillas in the Mist' in her shower."}]}]},"rained":{"h":"rained","a":"en-us-rained.ogg","l":"rain","q":"verb"},"bullshitted":{"h":"bullshitted","l":"bullshit","q":"verb"},"bull":{"h":"bull","i":"/bʊl/","a":"en-us-bull.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An adult male cattle.","e":"The bull was kept away from the cows."},{"m":"(countable) An adult male of some large mammals, such as whales, elephants and seals."},{"m":"(uncountable) Short for \"bullshit\"; a lie; nonsense.","e":"He said he can't be here because he's working late but I think it's bull."}]}]},"cigar":{"h":"cigar","i":"/sɪˈɡɑr/","a":"en-us-cigar.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cigar is tobacco rolled in tobacco leaves, for smoking.","e":"I think the best cigars are made in Cuba."}]}]},"nigger":{"h":"nigger","i":"/ˈnɪɡə(r)/","a":"en-us-ncalif-nigger.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A very offensive and insulting name for a black person, sometimes used between black people themselves. It is more upsetting when used by people of other races (i.e. people who are not black).","e":"Hey, nigger, what's up? (friendly if the speaker is black)"},{"m":"(often offensive) A black person who acts badly.","e":"I love black people, but I hate niggers. —"}]}]},"european":{"h":"European","i":"/(ˌ)jʊərəˈpiːən/","a":"EN-AU ck1 European.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A European is a person from Europe."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is European, it is from or related to Europe."}]}]},"african":{"h":"African","i":"/ˈæf.rɪ.kən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-African.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An African person or thing comes from Africa."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something or someone that is African comes from Africa.","e":"Many African countries were colonised by the British."},{"m":"Something that is African is in a style typical of Africa."}]}]},"american":{"h":"American","i":"/əˈmɛrɪkən/","a":"en-uk-American.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An American is a person from North America, Central America or South America."},{"m":"(countable) An American is or person from the United States of America."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is American it is from or typical of the United States."},{"m":"If something is American it is from or typical of North, Central or South America."}]}]},"asian":{"h":"Asian","i":"/ˈeɪʒən/","a":"EN-AU ck1 Asian.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A person from Asia. Most often this means a person from east Asia."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"From Asia."},{"m":"In a style typical of Asia, especially East Asia."}]}]},"asia":{"h":"Asia","i":"/ˈeɪ.ʒə/","a":"en-us-Asia.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Asia is the continent that is east of Europe, west of the Pacific Ocean, and north of the Indian Ocean.","e":"Asia is the world's largest and most-populous continent."}]}]},"australia":{"h":"Australia","i":"/ə.ˈstræɪ.ljə, -liː.ə, -jə/","a":"en-us-Australia.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Australia is the continent that is east of the Indian Ocean, west of the Pacific Ocean, and south of Asia.","e":"Australia is an island, a continent, and a nation, all in one."},{"m":"Australia is the country on this continent."}]}]},"eurasia":{"h":"Eurasia","i":"/jʊˈreɪʒə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Eurasia.wav","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"The supercontinent that is made of Europe and Asia; the largest piece of land in the world.","e":"Russia, England, China, France, Germany, and Iran are all examples of countries located in Eurasia."}]}]},"africa-eurasia":{"h":"Africa-Eurasia","i":"/ˈæf.rɪk.ə.jʊrˈeɪ.ʒə/","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Africa-Eurasia is the supercontinent that is made of Europe, Asia, and Africa."}]}]},"americas":{"h":"Americas","i":"/əˈmɛrɪkə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Americas.wav","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"The continents of North America and South America."}]}]},"oceania":{"h":"Oceania","i":"/ˌəʊ.ʃiˈɑː.nɪə/","a":"en-us-Oceania.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Australia together with the islands of the Pacific Ocean (the Pacific Islands).","e":"Oceania is not really a continent but is like one."}]}]},"witch":{"h":"witch","i":"/wɪtʃ/","a":"en-us-witch.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A woman who does witchcraft (magic) or has magical powers.","e":"Glenda the Good was a powerful witch in The Wizard of Oz."},{"m":"(countable) A person of either sex (man or woman) who does witchcraft."},{"m":"(countable) Someone who practice traditional British magic (witchcraft)."},{"m":"(countable) A Wiccan.","e":"I think she became a witch last year."},{"m":"(countable) A person who practices black (evil) magic.","e":"Old books talk about witches selling their souls to the Devil."},{"m":"(countable) (fiction, folklore) A female demon or monster that looks like an old woman and often does harmful things to other people.","e":"The witch tried to eat Hansel and Gretel."},{"m":"(countable) (by extension) A woman who is difficult to get allow with, or a bad woman.","e":"I hate my boss, she's a real witch."}]}]},"warlock":{"h":"warlock","i":"/ˈwɔː.lɒk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-warlock.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A male witch."},{"m":"(countable) (Wicca) A bad witch, someone who breaks a promise to their coven (group of witches)."}]}]},"bitch":{"h":"bitch","i":"/bɪtʃ/","a":"en-us-bitch.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A female dog."},{"m":"(countable) A cruel woman or a woman that is difficult to get along with.","e":"I hate that bitch, she always treats me like shit."},{"m":"(countable) Someone who is forced to have sexual intercourse with someone else.","e":"He was the bitch for the other men in prison."},{"m":"(by extension) (countable) Someone who is controlled by someone else.","e":"Everyone who works here is Kenny's bitch."},{"m":"(countable) A woman who has many sex partners.","e":"The rapper's song was about \"bitches and hoes,\" just like his last one."},{"m":"(countable) (very offensive) An insulting word for any woman.","e":"Damn, I can't believe that car is owned by a bitch."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To complain or criticize.","e":"All you ever do is bitch about the food I cook for you!"}]}]},"bastard":{"h":"bastard","i":"/ˈbɑːs.təd/","a":"en-us-bastard.oga","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Someone whose parents were not married.","e":"William the Bastard became William the Conqueror after he took over England."},{"m":"(countable) Bastard is an insulting word for a bad man, or a man you don't like.","e":"My boss is a total bastard."}]}]},"witchcraft":{"h":"witchcraft","i":"/ˈwɪtʃkræft/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-witchcraft.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A kind of magic that comes from European paganism or shamanism. Witchcraft often uses special poems called spells and uses herbs for magic and healing."},{"m":"Bad or evil magic."}]}]},"magic":{"h":"magic","i":"/ˈmædʒɪk/","a":"en-us-magic.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Magic has to do with making things happen in ways that are not physical, and might be called supernatural.","e":"The fairy god mother used magic to turn mice into horses."},{"m":"A kind of entertainment that uses tricks to make it look like impossible things have happened.","e":"He pulled rabbit out of a hat at the magic show, then he cut someone in half and put them back together alive. (He didn't do these things, but made it look like he did; the speaker knows that.)"},{"m":"Anything wonderful, beautiful, or very special.","e":"Love is the greatest magic of all."}]}]},"witches":{"h":"witches","l":"witch","q":"noun"},"bitches":{"h":"bitches","l":"bitch","q":"noun"},"bulls":{"h":"bulls","l":"bull","q":"noun"},"bastards":{"h":"bastards","l":"bastard","q":"noun"},"cigars":{"h":"cigars","l":"cigar","q":"noun"},"rains":{"h":"rains","i":"/reɪnz/","a":"en-us-rains.ogg","l":"rain","q":"noun"},"witchcrafts":{"h":"witchcrafts","l":"witchcraft","q":"noun"},"greece":{"h":"Greece","i":"/griːs/","a":"en-us-Greece.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Greece is a country in south-east Europe.","e":"We wanted to go to Greece for our next holiday."}]}]},"greek":{"h":"Greek","i":"/griːk/","a":"en-us-Greek.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"The language people speak in Greece."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A person from Greece."},{"m":"A member of a college fraternity (brotherhood) or sorority (sisterhood)."},{"m":"; (prostitution)."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"From Greece, in Greece, or part of Greece.","e":"I have a Greek vase."},{"m":"In a style typical of Greece."}]}]},"grease":{"h":"grease","i":"/griːs/","a":"en-us-grease.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Grease is liquid or melted fat from an animal, often used for cooking."},{"m":"(uncountable) Grease is a petroleum product used to lubricate machines."},{"m":"(uncountable) Grease is a thick, oily substance similar to those above."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you grease something, you put grease on it so that it moves more easily."},{"m":"If you grease a situation, you bribe somebody."}]}]},"warlocks":{"h":"warlocks","l":"warlock","q":"noun"},"thailand":{"h":"Thailand","i":"/ˈtaɪ̯lænd/","a":"en-us-Thailand.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"A country in south-east Asia. Its full name is \"Kingdom of Thailand\" and its capital is Bangkok. Thailand used to be called \"Siam\".","e":"We went on a trip to Thailand."}]}]},"odyssey":{"h":"odyssey","i":"/ˈɒ.dɨ.si/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-odyssey.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A long adventurous journey or trip.","e":"The odyssey of Odysseus was written down by Homer in his epic poem, the Odyssey."},{"m":"An intellectual or spiritual journey or quest."}]}]},"protactinium":{"h":"protactinium","i":"/ˌprəʊ.tækˈtɪn.i.əm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-protactinium.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A chemical element (symbol Pa) with atomic number 91."}]}]},"joy":{"h":"joy","i":"/ʤɔɪ/","a":"en-us-joy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Joy is a feeling of great happiness and pleasure.","e":"They will be a source of strength and joy in your life."},{"m":"(countable) A joy is something that causes joy or happiness.","e":"Lisa is a joy to have in class."}]}]},"buck":{"h":"buck","i":"/bʌk/","a":"EN-AU ck1 buck.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A male deer or goat."},{"m":"(countable) A male rabbit or hare."},{"m":"(countable) A male of another animal, such as the ferret."},{"m":"(countable) A dollar.","e":"The buck stops here. – Harry S. Truman, an American president"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If an animal bucks, it tried to throw a person off its back."}]}]},"almighty":{"h":"almighty","i":"/ɔːlˈmaɪti/","a":"en-au-almighty.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is almighty it has endless power; it can do anything."}]}]},"hippo":{"h":"hippo","i":"/ˈhɪpəʊ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-hippo.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Hippo is another way of saying hippopotamus."}]}]},"hippopotamus":{"h":"hippopotamus","i":"/ˌhɪpəˈpɒtəməs/","a":"en-us-hippopotamus.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A hippopotamus is a big plant-eating animal found in Africa that lives mostly in water.","e":"We saw a big hippopotamus at the zoo."}]}]},"buoy":{"h":"buoy","i":"/bɔi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-buoy.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A float in water that is used to mark something."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To float."},{"m":"(transitive) To keep something high."},{"m":"(transitive) To mark/measure with a buoy."}]}]},"herbal":{"h":"herbal","i":"/ˈhɜːbəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-herbal.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Made from or with an herb (or herbs).","e":"Try this herbal tea."}]}]},"crap":{"h":"crap","i":"/kræp/","a":"en-us-crap.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An impolite way of saying feces.","e":"I have to take a crap."},{"m":"Something that is not good or is of poor quality.","e":"This food is crap!"},{"m":"Something that is nonsense.","e":"The college student wrote a 10,000-word essay on Shakespeare, but the professor judged it to be nothing but utter crap."},{"m":"Crap is a losing throw of 2, 3, or 12 in craps."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To defecate."}]},{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"A saying that shows worry, fear, surprise, disgust, annoyance or dismay.","e":"Oh crap! The other driver's going to hit my car!"}]}]},"appointment":{"h":"appointment","i":"/əˈpɔɪnt.mɛnt/","a":"en-us-appointment.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An appointment is a formal agreement to meet or visit someone (for example, a doctor) at a certain time and place.","e":"I have a doctor's appointment at 3:00 tomorrow."}]}]},"holly":{"h":"holly","i":"/ˈhɒli/","a":"en-us-holly.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A bush that is used as decoration especially at Christmas; Ilex aquifolium."}]}]},"farmer":{"h":"farmer","i":"/fɑrmɚ/","a":"en-us-farmer.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Someone whose job is to raise animals or plants, often for food.","e":"The farmers here plant crops to feed their families and to make a profit."}]}]},"dryer":{"h":"dryer","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A dryer is a machine for drying clothes."}]}]},"curtains":{"h":"curtains","i":"/ˈkɜː(r).tənz/","a":"en-us-curtains.ogg","l":"curtain","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An end (in reference to curtains closing at the end of a stage show).","e":"It's curtains for you!"}]}]},"hum":{"h":"hum","a":"en-us-hum.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) To make a sound you can make in your throat with your mouth closed. Often, this is done to make music without singing words.","e":"I used to hum the music from the Indiana Jones movies when I was a child."},{"m":"(intransitive) A similar sound, such as one from a machine.","e":"The engine hummed as he started drove the car."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Hum is the sound of humming, or a sound like humming.","e":"I heard a low hum from the other room."}]}]},"honesty":{"h":"honesty","i":"/ˈɒnəsti/","a":"en-us-honesty.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The quality of being honest. If you have honesty, you tell the truth.","e":"Honesty is an important value. Always make sure to tell the truth, or else people would not trust you."},{"m":"(countable) An honesty is a kind of plant."}]}]},"northwest":{"h":"northwest","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The direction in between north and west; northwest can be shortened to NW."}]}]},"southwest":{"h":"southwest","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The direction in between south and west; southwest can be shortened to SW."}]}]},"visitor":{"h":"visitor","i":"/ˈvɪzɪtə/","a":"en-us-visitor.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Someone who is visiting.","e":"I had a lot of visitors when I was in the hospital."}]}]},"nest":{"h":"nest","i":"/nɛst/","a":"en-us-nest.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The home a bird builds for itself."},{"m":"The home or bedding of some other animals.","e":"The mother wolf built a nest in her den before she had her cubs."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When an animal builds or stays in its nest, especially when taking care of its babies there."},{"m":"If somethings is nested in something else, it is inside it. Usually, this is used for several things, with the second thing in the first thing, the third things in the second thing—for however many things are nested. This is often used in coding and computer programing.","e":"The computer program had nested for loops, that looked like this:"}]}]},"subjective":{"h":"subjective","i":"/səbˈdʒɛktɪv/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-subjective.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Related to subjects, not objects. (A subject is one who perceives or is aware; an object is the thing perceived or the thing that the subject is aware of.)"},{"m":"Formed, as in opinions, by feelings or intuition, not by seeing or reasoning."},{"m":"(philosophy); d by a person mentally and is not easily by other people."}]}]},"jaded":{"h":"jaded","i":"/ˈdʒeɪdɛd/","a":"en-us-jaded.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"ed, tired."},{"m":"Made callous, apathetic or cynical because of experience; having a negative outlook because of bad experiences in the past.","e":"My view of politicians has become quite jaded in recent years."}]}]},"chosen":{"h":"chosen","i":"/ˈtʃəʊ.zən/","a":"en-us-chosen.ogg","l":"choose","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is chosen it is the one someone chose.","e":"Medicine was his chosen profession."},{"m":"Something chosen is the special one. That is chosen often means set aside for a special purpose.","e":"Christians believe that Jesus was God's chosen one."},{"m":"In some religions, a chosen people is a group of people that are special to God.","e":"In the Bible, the Jews are God's chosen people."}]}]},"helpful":{"h":"helpful","i":"/ˈhɛlp.fʊl/","a":"en-us-helpful1.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is helpful it can or does help in some way.","e":"The way you explained that word was very helpful to me."}]}]},"torch":{"h":"torch","i":"/tɔː(r)ʧ/","a":"en-us-torch.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A torch is a device for making light. One end of it is on fire."},{"m":"(countable) (UK) A torch is another word for a flashlight."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you torch something you set it on fire.","e":"He was arrested for torching the building."}]}]},"copier":{"h":"copier","i":"/ˈkɒpɪə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-copier.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A short word for photocopier."},{"m":"(countable) A person who copies."}]}]},"photocopier":{"h":"photocopier","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A machine that makes copies of documents.","e":"Use the photocopier down the hall to make copies of this worksheet."}]}]},"xerox":{"h":"Xerox","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Xerox Corporation, a company that makes copy machines."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A copy machine made by the Xerox company."},{"m":"Any copy machine."},{"m":"A copy made by a copy machine."}]}]},"creative":{"h":"creative","i":"/kriˈeɪtɪv/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-creative.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are creative you are good at things that no one has made before. Also, it could mean you are good at thinking of things no one has thought of before.","e":"The inventor had a very creative idea for a new machine."},{"m":"If something is creative, it is original.","e":"That was a very creative strategy."},{"m":"If something is creative, it is about making creative things.","e":"She is studying creative arts."}]}]},"ethics":{"h":"ethics","i":"/ˈɛθ.ɪks/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-ethics.wav","l":"ethic","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(philosophy); (uncountable) The study of what is good and what is bad, or what should be good and bad. Ethics often is about making rules for how to act, and saying why certain things are bad.","e":"She is studying ethics at the university."}]}]},"ethic":{"h":"ethic","i":"/ˈɛθ.ɪk/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An ethic is a rule or idea that tells you something is good or bad.","e":"The Protestant work ethic said that people should stay busy and that being lazy was of the Devil."}]}]},"membership":{"h":"membership","i":"/ˈmɛmbəʃɪp/","a":"en-us-membership.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Being part of a group.","e":"I had to renew my membership with the union."}]}]},"lessen":{"h":"lessen","i":"/ˈlɛsən/","a":"en-us-lessen.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you lessen something, you make it less."},{"m":"If something lessens it becomes less."}]}]},"immoral":{"h":"immoral","i":"/ɪˈmɒrəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-immoral.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is immoral it is something that is wrong or bad. That is, it is against what is moral.","e":"Some religions say it is immoral to have sex with someone you are not married to."},{"m":"If a person is immoral they do immoral things and have bad morals or is against what is moral.","e":"She stopped dating him because he was so immoral."}]}]},"amoral":{"h":"amoral","i":"/eɪˈmɒr.əl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-amoral.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is amoral it is not moral or immoral."},{"m":"The same as immoral."}]}]},"spirit":{"h":"spirit","i":"/ˈspɪrɪt/","a":"en-us-spirit.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A spirit is a being that has no physical body, and cannot usually be seen or touched.","e":"The people on the island believed in many gods and spirits that affected life."},{"m":"(countable) A spirit is a part of you that cannot be seen or touched. Often this is important to religion and different from the soul (religions do not agree what the difference is).","e":"They tried to talk to the spirit of their dead mother through a medium."},{"m":"(uncountable) If you have spirit, you are very excited about something or a very strong supporter.","e":"People with school spirit always cheer for their schools team."},{"m":"(uncountable) The spirit of a statement or rule is the idea or purpose for it.","e":"What she did fit the spirit of the law, even though it brought the law as it was written."},{"m":"; (usually plural) A spirit is a volatile liquid, like alcohol."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you spirit something, you carry it away, usually in secret or mystery."}]},{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"(Christianity) Another name for the Holy Spirit (also called the Holy Ghost)."}]}]},"spirits":{"h":"spirits","i":"/ˈspɪrɪts/","a":"en-us-spirits.ogg","l":"spirit","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"If you are in good spirits, you are happy."}]}]},"strength":{"h":"strength","i":"/strɛŋkθ/","a":"en-us-strength.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) If you have strength, you are strong."},{"m":"(countable) A strength is a good quality.","e":"The plan had may strengths, such as not needing many people and being easy to do."},{"m":"(countable) Strength as in the number of something.","e":"The strength of the regiment was 3,000 soldiers."}]}]},"quarterly":{"h":"quarterly","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Happening four times every year; happening every 3 months.","e":"The club published a quarterly news letter."}]}]},"yearly":{"h":"yearly","i":"/ˈjɪrli/","a":"en-us-yearly.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is yearly happens once every year.","e":"We have a yearly meeting for members in the country."}]}]},"written":{"h":"written","i":"/ˈrɪtn̩/","a":"en-us-written.ogg","l":"write","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is written it is in writing.","e":"We have a written letter from our CEO."}]}]},"washer":{"h":"washer","i":"/ˈwɒʃə(r)/","a":"en-us-washer.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A short word for washing machine; a machine to wash clothes."},{"m":"(countable) A metal or plastic ring that goes with a nut and bolt (a thick screw) to help the bolt stay on."},{"m":"(countable) or (not common) Someone whose job is to wash."}]}]},"bolt":{"h":"bolt","i":"/bɒlt/","a":"en-us-bolt.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A kind of thick screw that is used with a nut and sometimes a washer."},{"m":"(countable) A short heavy arrow used by a crossbow."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you bolt, you run away suddenly."}]}]},"induction":{"h":"induction","i":"/ɪnˈdʌkʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-induction.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The act of inducting something."},{"m":"A formal ceremony where a person is inducted into an office or into military service"},{"m":"Making an electric current by using a varying magnetic field."},{"m":"(logic) The derivation of general principles from specific instances."},{"m":"A proof of a theorem by first proving it for one integer and showing that if it is true for one integer then it must be true for other integers."},{"m":"The act of inducing childbirth."},{"m":"(theatre) The use of rumors to confuse and complicate the story of a play or to tell the story without giving facts."},{"m":"The development of a feature from part of a formerly homogenous field of cells in response to a morphogen whose source determines the feature's position and extent."},{"m":"An introduction."}]}]},"vortex":{"h":"vortex","i":"/ˈvɔrtɛks/","a":"en-us-vortex.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A vortex is a whirlwind, whirlpool, or something else that moves in a spiral or column."},{"m":"(countable) A vortex is anything with on-going violent or chaotic activity around a center point."},{"m":"(countable) A vortex is anything which brings nearby things into its current."}]}]},"khan":{"h":"khan","i":"/kɑ:n/","a":"en-us-khan.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"After, a ruler over various Turkish, Tatar and Mongolians in the Middle Ages."},{"m":"An Ottoman sultan."},{"m":"A noble or man of rank in various Muslim countries of Central Asia, including Afghanistan."},{"m":"A resting-place for a travelling caravan."}]}]},"terror":{"h":"terror","i":"/ˈtɛrɚ/","a":"en-us-terror.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Very strong or intense fear.","e":"I never felt such terror as when I was robbed at gunpoint."},{"m":"Something that causes such fear.","e":"The rabid dog was the terror of the neighborhood."},{"m":"or the threat of violence for political reasons; terrorism.","e":"The United States has declared a war on terror."},{"m":"An annoying or unpleasant person, often a naughty child.","e":"My little brother can be such a terror!"}]}]},"peripheral":{"h":"peripheral","i":"/ˈpɜː(r).ɪf.ɜː(r).əl/","a":"En-us-peripheral.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is peripheral, it is on the periphery or boundary of it."},{"m":"If something is peripheral, it is beside the point."},{"m":"If something is peripheral, it is not important; it is unimportant."},{"m":"If something is peripheral, it is auxiliary to it."},{"m":"If something is peripheral, it is found on the peripheral nervous system."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A peripheral is a machine that is connected to a computer, such as a printer or scanner."}]}]},"innocent":{"h":"innocent","i":"/ˈɪnəsn̩t/","a":"en-us-innocent.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are innocent you do not know evil.","e":"How could he hurt an innocent child?!?"},{"m":"If you are innocent of a crime you did not do that crime.","e":"I swore to the police that I was innocent."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Someone who is innocent. That is, someone who lacks evil or the knowledge of evil.","e":"He was a total innocent."}]}]},"innocence":{"h":"innocence","i":"/ˈɪnəsn̩s/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-innocence.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The quality of being innocent.","e":"I miss the innocence I lost growing up."},{"m":"(uncountable) It is common to call learning about sex (or having sex for the first time) as \"loosing innocence.\"","e":"She lost her innocence when she was seventeen."}]}]},"innocents":{"h":"innocents","l":"innocent","q":"noun"},"wicked":{"h":"wicked","i":"/ˈwɪkɪd/","a":"en-us-wicked.ogg","l":"wick","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are wicked you often do evil things. More than that, a wicked person enjoys evil.","e":"The wicked witch terrorized the peasants of the village."},{"m":"A wicked act is something someone does that is very evil.","e":"He will be punished for his wicked acts."},{"m":"If something is wicked, it is excellent.","e":"That was a wicked guitar solo!"},{"m":"(not comparable) If something is wicked, it has a wick in it."}]}]},"synonym":{"h":"synonym","i":"/ˈsɪnənɪm/","a":"en-us-synonym.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A synonym is a word with the same meaning as another word.","e":"The word big is a synonym of the word large."},{"m":"(countable) A synonym is a word that does not have the same meaning, but the meaning is very close to the other word.","e":"Good and right are synonyms, even though they do not mean exactly the same thing."}]}]},"antonym":{"h":"antonym","i":"/ˈæntəˌnɪm/","a":"en-us-antonym.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A word that means the opposite of another word.","e":"Good is the antonym of bad; high is the antonym of low."}]}]},"synonymous":{"h":"synonymous","i":"/sɪˈnɒnɪməs/","a":"en-us-synonymous.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If two words are synonymous they are synonyms to each other."},{"m":"If two ideas are synonymous they are almost the same idea.","e":"Communism is often thought to be synonymous with socialism, though there are a few differences."},{"m":"If two ideas are synonymous then if one is true the other has to be true, so that claiming one is the same as claiming the other."}]}]},"synonyms":{"h":"synonyms","l":"synonym","q":"noun"},"antonyms":{"h":"antonyms","l":"antonym","q":"noun"},"etymology":{"h":"etymology","i":"/ˌɛt.ɪˈmɒl.ə.dʒi/","a":"en-us-etymology.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Etymology is the study of the history and change of words."},{"m":"(countable) A word's etymology is its history."}]}]},"pronunciation":{"h":"pronunciation","i":"/prəˌnʌnsiˈeɪʃən/","a":"en-us-pronunciation.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) How a word is said, how a word sounds.","e":"There are two different pronunciations for the word either."},{"m":"(uncountable) The way a certain person speaks.","e":"His French pronunciation is horrible."}]}]},"pronunciations":{"h":"pronunciations","l":"pronunciation","q":"noun"},"etymologies":{"h":"etymologies","i":"/ɛtɪ'mɒləʤi:z/","l":"etymology","q":"noun"},"voodoo":{"h":"voodoo","i":"/ˈvuːduː/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-voodoo.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Voodoo is a small religion from the Caribbean, most common in Haiti and Louisiana. Voodoo comes from west African shamanism (called Vodu). In voodoo many gods and spirits are called to do magic."},{"m":"(uncountable); (mostly US)."}]}]},"vodu":{"h":"Vodu","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"A kind of African shamanism."}]}]},"zombies":{"h":"zombies","l":"zombie","q":"noun"},"dragonfly":{"h":"dragonfly","i":"/ˈdrægənˌflaɪ/","a":"en-us-dragonfly.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A large insect with four wings and a long body. Dragonflies hunt other insects, such as mosquitoes."}]}]},"lizard":{"h":"lizard","i":"/ˈlɪz.ərd/","a":"en-us-lizard.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Any of many kinds of reptiles that has four legs, a long tail, and no shell."}]}]},"lizards":{"h":"lizards","l":"lizard","q":"noun"},"abuse":{"h":"abuse","i":"/əˈbjuːs/","a":"en-us-abuse-noun.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Abuse is touching or acting towards someone in a way that will likely hurt them.","e":"The girls suffered terrible physical and sexual abuse from their father."},{"m":"An abuse is an act of using something in the wrong way."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you abuse something, you misuse it; you use something improperly."},{"m":"(transitive) If you abuse something, you injure it; you hurt it; you treat it with cruelty or damage it."},{"m":"(transitive) If you abuse somebody, you rape them; you assault them."},{"m":"(transitive) If you abuse somebody, you berate them; you insult or revile them.","e":"Child abuse is prohibited in America."}]}]},"accent":{"h":"accent","i":"/ˈæk.sɛnt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-accent.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An accent is the particular way that somebody's speech sounds.","e":"I can speak French, but I do it with an English accent."}]}]},"adjust":{"h":"adjust","i":"/əˈdʒʌst/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-adjust.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you adjust something, you change it a little so that it fits or works better.","e":"I had to adjust the cupboard door so that is would close easily."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you adjust, you change the way you behave or think to suit a new situation.","e":"I had to adjust to the way of living here."}]}]},"advantage":{"h":"advantage","i":"/ædˈvæn.tɪʤ/","a":"en-us-advantage.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An advantage is a condition or circumstance that favors success."},{"m":"(countable) An advantage is when someone has superiority over someone else."},{"m":"(countable) An advantage is a benefit, gain, or profit."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you advantage a person, you provide them with an [[#Noun|advantage]]."}]}]},"advise":{"h":"advise","i":"/ædˈvaɪz/","a":"en-us-advise.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you advise someone to do something, you tell them that they should do it.","e":"I'd advise you to study for the exam."}]}]},"aircraft":{"h":"aircraft","i":"/ɛə.krɑːft/","a":"en-us-aircraft.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An aircraft is a flying vehicle, usually an airplane.","e":"The army wants money to buy various aircraft, including helicopters and jets."}]}]},"airport":{"h":"airport","i":"/ˈeɪrpɔrt/","a":"en-us-airport.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An airport is a place where airplanes land and take off.","e":"I took a taxi to the airport for my flight to London."}]}]},"audience":{"h":"audience","i":"/ˈɔːdiəns/","a":"en-us-audience.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An audience is the person or people who watch a performance, listen to you speak, or read what you write.","e":"The audience at the concert was dancing on their chairs."}]}]},"bang":{"h":"bang","i":"/bæŋ(ɡ)/","a":"en-us-bang.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bang is a short loud noise like the sound of a door closing or a gun being shot.","e":"The two cars hit with a big bang."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If something bangs, it makes repeated sudden loud noises."},{"m":"If you bang someone, you engage in sexual intercourse with them."}]}]},"bathroom":{"h":"bathroom","i":"/ˈbɑːθruːm/","a":"en-us-bathroom.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bathroom is a room that has a bathtub or a shower.","e":"In our house, the bathroom is very busy in the morning."},{"m":"(countable) A bathroom is a room with a toilet.","e":"Excuse me, my son has to go to the bathroom. Is it upstairs?"}]}]},"razor":{"h":"razor","i":"/ˈreɪzə/","a":"en-us-razor.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A razor is a type of knife that is used to shave hair."}]}]},"shave":{"h":"shave","i":"/ʃeɪv/","a":"en-us-shave.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you shave hair, you remove all of it with a sharp object such as a razor.","e":"After getting up in the morning, Trevor shaved off a day's growth of beard."},{"m":"(transitive) When you shave meat, you cut it into very thin slices.","e":"The butcher shaved a quarter pound of roast beef, which I put in a sandwich."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A shave is the act of shaving (hair being removed)."}]}]},"stake":{"h":"stake","i":"/steɪk/","a":"en-us-stake.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A stick or rod with a sharp point. A stake is usually hammered into the ground. Often, the stake is tied to rope to connect something (like a tent) to the ground.","e":"We used four stakes to hold down our tent."},{"m":"If you have a stake in something it is important to you. Usually, this means it will affect you in some way, so you have a good reason to be interested.","e":"I had a personal stake in hunger relief, since family had no food."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To put a stake into something. Most often, you would put the stake in the ground, but it could be put in something else."}]}]},"stakeout":{"h":"stakeout","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A stakeout is when people (usually police) sit and secretly watch a person or place.","e":"The police had a stakeout in a place where they expected the crime to occur."}]}]},"stakeholder":{"h":"stakeholder","i":"/ˈsteɪkhoʊldə(r)/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-stakeholder.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Someone who holds a stake for others. The holder has no interest in the stake."},{"m":"(countable) Someone who has a stake in something. This means that the issue is important to that person, and will affect that person."}]}]},"stakes":{"h":"stakes","i":"/steɪks/","a":"en-us-stakes.ogg","l":"stake","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Stakes are what you will win or lose if you try something.","e":"The stakes are high in this game. If we loose we will be out of the championship."}]}]},"useful":{"h":"useful","i":"/ˈjuːsfəl/","a":"en-us-useful.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"for a purpose. If something is useful it can be used for something."}]}]},"unwind":{"h":"unwind","i":"/ʌn'waɪnd/","a":"en-au-unwind.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you unwind, you relax.","e":"I just need to unwind after work."},{"m":"The opposite of wind (verb). If you unwind something like a string or a scarf, you make it so that it is not around and around something anymore.","e":"You need to unwind the string from the ball."}]}]},"usually":{"h":"usually","i":"/juːʒʊəli/","a":"en-us-usually.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"You use usually to talk about what happens most of the time.","e":"He usually takes a long time to get ready, but he can be fast too."}]}]},"creek":{"h":"Creek","i":"/kri:k/","a":"en-us-creek.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"The Creek are a Native American tribe from the southern United States."},{"m":"Creek is the language spoken by the Creek tribe."},{"m":"A person who is a Creek is part of the Creek nation."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is Creek is about the Creek people."}]}]},"stream":{"h":"stream","i":"/stri:m/","a":"en-us-stream.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A stream is a very small river or creek."},{"m":"A stream is something that comes in an order without stopping (like water in a stream).","e":"Stop interrupting me, you are breaking my stream of thought."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something streams, it comes in a flow, usually in order and often not stopping.","e":"The website offered streaming music and video files."}]}]},"dumbledore":{"h":"dumbledore","i":"/ˈdʌm.bəl.dɔː/","a":"en-us-dumbledore.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A bumblebee.","e":"\"A shaded lamp and a waving blind, / And the beat of a clock from a distant floor: / On this scene enter – winged, horned, and spined – / A longlegs, a moth, and a dumbledore\" — Thomas Hardy, ‘An August Midnight’, 1899"}]}]},"prometheus":{"h":"Prometheus","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"A god who stole fire from Zeus and gave it to humans so they could use it. The god of fire and craft. Prometheus had three brothers - Epimetheus, Menoetios and Atlas."}]}]},"equality":{"h":"equality","i":"/ɪˈkwɑl.ɪ.ti/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-equality.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The state of being equal."},{"m":"(uncountable) The state of being equal, of having the same value."},{"m":"(uncountable) The equal treatment of all people even if they are different."}]}]},"suffix":{"h":"suffix","i":"/ˈsʌfɪks/","a":"en-us-suffix.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A suffix is an affix that is added to the end of a word. In English this can change the meaning. Also, it can be required by grammar but not change the meaning; this could be to change the tense, the number, or for other reasons."}]}]},"prefix":{"h":"prefix","i":"/ˈpriːfɪks/","a":"en-us-prefix.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A prefix is an affix that is added to the beginning of a word. In English this usually changes the meaning."}]}]},"infix":{"h":"infix","i":"/ˈɪnfɪks/","a":"en-us-infix.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An infix is an affix that is added to the middle of a word (in some languages). English does not use infixes. (Note: some vulgar words, most often fuck, are used as infixes in informal English.)"}]}]},"affix":{"h":"affix","i":"/ˈæ.fɪks/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-affix (noun).wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An affix is a sound or sounds added to a word. They can be added to the beginning, middle, or end of a word. This might change the meaning of the word, or it may be needed for grammar. (Note: In formal English, affixes are added only to the beginning or end of the word.)"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To attach one thing to another."}]}]},"spectrum":{"h":"spectrum","i":"/ˈspektrəm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-spectrum.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A range."},{"m":"Specifically, a range of colors representing light of various."},{"m":"The pattern of absorption or emission of radiation that is made by a substance when it is put in contact with an energy such as radiation, heat, electricity, etc."}]}]},"napalm":{"h":"napalm","i":"/ˈneɪ.pɑːm/","a":"en-us-napalm.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A very flammable, thick liquid that is made to stick to things while burning; napalm is used during war to cause a lot of death and destruction, especially in wooded areas.","e":"The soldiers dropped napalm on the enemy to destroy their camp."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To spray or attack an area with napalm.","e":"The soldiers napalmed the enemy to destroy their camp."}]}]},"manure":{"h":"manure","i":"/məˈnjʊə/","a":"en-us-manure.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"feces, especially the feces of farm animals such as cows, horses, pigs and chickens; manure is often used as a fertilizer."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To apply [[#Noun|manure]] as a fertilizer."}]}]},"pollutant":{"h":"pollutant","i":"/pəˈl(j)uːtənt/","a":"en-us-pollutant.oga","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pollutant is something that makes the air, soil or water dirty or polluted.","e":"s, herbicides, and detergents are all examples of water pollutants."}]}]},"anchovy":{"h":"anchovy","i":"/ˈæn.tʃə.vi/","a":"en-us-anchovy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A small saltwater fish of the Engraulidae family; anchovies are often used as food, especially on pizzas and in s."}]}]},"bob":{"h":"Bob","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"In cryptography and physics, Bob is sometimes used as the name for the person or system that receives a message from another person or system, which is usually known as Alice."}]}]},"mayhem":{"h":"mayhem","i":"/ˈmeɪhem/","a":"en-us-mayhem.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A state of chaos, disorder, or disruption.","e":"She waded into the mayhem, elbowing between taller men to work her way to the front of the crowd."},{"m":"The crime of intentionally or a person."}]}]},"alone":{"h":"alone","i":"/əˈləʊn/","a":"en-us-alone.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is alone, they are not with other people.","e":"She looked around to make sure that she was alone before opening the desk."},{"m":"If someone is alone, they have no friends or people they know.","e":"He felt very alone in Canada and wanted to go home."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If you do something alone, you do it without other people.","e":"She went walking alone because she wanted to think."},{"m":"When you talk about something alone, you mean only that thing.","e":"It will take weeks for the planning alone."}]}]},"disclaimer":{"h":"disclaimer","i":"/dɪsˈkleɪm.ɚ/","a":"en-us-disclaimer.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Words that say that a person or group does not own or is not responsible for something","e":"You are not able to return the toaster to the shop. You should have read the disclaimer."},{"m":"A denial or waiver of a title, claim, interest, estate, or trust."},{"m":"Saying, in front of everyone, that you do not own something, or that you are not responsible for something."}]}]},"objectionable":{"h":"objectionable","i":"/əbˈdʒɛkʃənəbl/","a":"en-us-objectionable.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is objectionable, you are likely to object to it.","e":"Before removing objectionable material, you'll have to decide what will offend people."}]}]},"requests":{"h":"requests","l":"request","q":"noun"},"yea":{"h":"yea","i":"/jeɪ/","a":"en-us-yea.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"An old word for yes."},{"m":"Yea can be used to tell how much. In this way it can either mean about or exactly \"this much.\" (Often while by a showing how much with your hands.)","e":"The pony was yea high. (While holding a hand where the top of the pony's head would be.)"}]},{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"Another spelling of yeah."},{"m":"Another spelling of yay."}]}]},"yay":{"h":"yay","i":"/jeɪ/","a":"en-us-yay.ogg","s":[{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"You can say \"yay!\" when you are very happy or excited. People usually say this loudly, to show great emotion."}]}]},"baggage":{"h":"baggage","i":"/ˈbæɡɪdʒ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-baggage.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Another word for luggage; bags and other containers that people use to carry things when they travel. Also, the things (most often clothes) carried in the bags."},{"m":"(uncountable) Things you keep with you from the past. Usually this means emotions or, most often bad feelings."},{"m":"An army's portable equipment; its baggage train."}]}]},"shinto":{"h":"Shinto","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"The first religion of Japan. Shinto teaches that there are more gods and spirits than can be counted (call \"eight-million gods\"). These gods and spirits are called kami and are led by three gods: The sun goddess, the moon god, and the storm god."}]}]},"shintoism":{"h":"Shintoism","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Another word for Shinto, a religion of Japan."}]}]},"altogether":{"h":"altogether","i":"/ɔːl.tʊˈgɛð.ə(r)/","a":"en-us-altogether.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"You use altogether to emphasize that something was done or happened completely and in every way.","e":"He plans to cut back on smoking slowly and not stop altogether."},{"m":"You use altogether to emphasize that something is like a description in every way.","e":"I still dream, but my dreams are altogether different from my teenage dreams."},{"m":"You use altogether to show that a number or amount is the total.","e":"It includes nine new programs: five half-hour sitcoms, one half-hour drama, a half-hour fantasy adventure and two one-hour dramas. Altogether, 5 1/2 hours of new shows will be introduced."},{"m":"You use altogether to bring together a number of points that you have talked about.","e":"So each idea is different in some way, but altogether, they seem to point to the same thing."}]}]},"wank":{"h":"wank","i":"/wæŋk/","a":"en-uk-wank.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you wank, you have sex alone, and touch your penis or vagina or breasts; you masturbate."},{"m":"(transitive) If you wank, you touch another person's penis in a sexual way; to give a hand job."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A wank is an act of masturbation.","e":"He’s having a wank."},{"m":"(countable) A wank is an undesirable person.","e":"You utter wank!"},{"m":"(uncountable), rubbish, ridiculous.","e":"This opera is wank."}]}]},"glasses":{"h":"glasses","a":"En-uk-glasses.ogg","l":"glass","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Glasses are worn over the eyes to help you see.","e":"I've had to wear glasses since I was nine years old."},{"m":"Kinds of glass."}]}]},"employee":{"h":"employee","i":"/ɛmplɔɪˈiː/","a":"en-us-employee.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An employee is someone who works for a company or another person.","e":"He is an employee of this store."}]}]},"feelings":{"h":"feelings","a":"en-us-feelings.ogg","l":"feeling","q":"noun"},"electrical":{"h":"electrical","i":"/ɪˈlɛktrɪkəl/","a":"en-us-electrical.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is electrical, it is related to electricity or electronics."}]}]},"electrician":{"h":"electrician","i":"/ɪˌlɛkˈtrɪʃ(ə)n/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-electrician.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An electrician is a person who fixes things related to electricity."}]}]},"oval":{"h":"oval","i":"/əʊvəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-oval.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A shape that looks like an egg."},{"m":"A building that is the shape of an oval."}]}]},"expression":{"h":"expression","i":"/ɪkˈsprɛʃ.ən/","a":"en-us-expression.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An expression is a way your face can look that shows how you feel. Smiles and frowns are expressions.","e":"I could tell he was lying by the expression on his face."},{"m":"An expression is a group of words, like a phrase or sentence, often one that is used by many people.","e":"\"Read between the lines\" is a common expression for knowing meanings that are not written or spoken."},{"m":"An expression is a group of numbers and variables.","e":"The expression \"2x + y - 3\" was set equal eight in the equation."}]}]},"expressions":{"h":"expressions","l":"expression","q":"noun"},"triangle":{"h":"triangle","i":"/ˈtraɪəŋɡəl/","a":"en-us-triangle.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A triangle (▲) is a shape that has three sides and three angles."},{"m":"(countable) A triangle is an instrument that is made out of metal and is shaped like a triangle."}]}]},"employees":{"h":"employees","l":"employee","q":"noun"},"economics":{"h":"economics","i":"/ikəˈnɑmɪks/","a":"en-us-economics.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The study of money and how goods and services get value.","e":"Economics shows us that people use too much when the price is too low."}]}]},"polygon":{"h":"polygon","i":"/ˈpɒlɪɡən/","a":"en-us-polygon.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A polygon is a type of two-dimensional shape. It has three or more corners, which are connected by lines."}]}]},"jobless":{"h":"jobless","i":"/ˈdʒɒbləs/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are jobless you do not have a job."}]}]},"doll":{"h":"doll","i":"/dɒl/","a":"en-us-doll.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A doll is a small model of a person. Dolls are often used as toys for children (most often girls)."},{"m":"A girl or woman, most often an attractive young woman."}]}]},"dolls":{"h":"dolls","l":"doll","q":"noun"},"sadism":{"h":"sadism","i":"/ˈseɪdɪzəm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-sadism.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) ing causing pain to people or animals.","e":"The noble was well known throughout the region for his sadism. He would often torture prisoners in the cruelest of punishments just for the joy of it."},{"m":"(uncountable) A sex game where someone hurts someone else during sex."}]}]},"zinc":{"h":"zinc","i":"/zɪŋk/","a":"en-us-zinc.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Zinc is a type of metal, (symbol Zn) with an atomic number of 30 on the periodic table."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you zinc something, you cover it with zinc."}]}]},"questionable":{"h":"questionable","i":"/ˈkwɛst͡ʃənəbl̩/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-questionable.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is questionable it is easy to question. That is, it is not likely to be true, and might be false."}]}]},"waiter":{"h":"waiter","i":"/ˈweɪtə/","a":"en-us-waiter.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A waiter is the person at a restaurant who takes your order and brings the food to you.","e":"I'm trying to get the waiter to bring our bill but he isn't looking this way."}]}]},"vow":{"h":"vow","i":"/vaʊ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-vow.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A vow is a promise. Often, a vow is a special promise that is made formally or in front of other people.","e":"I took a vow never to hurt anyone."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you vow, to do something, you make a promise to do it.","e":"We vowed never to betray each other."}]}]},"perennial":{"h":"perennial","i":"/pəˈrɛniəl/","a":"en-us-perennial.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is perennial it is there every year, or through many years."},{"m":"If a plant is perennial it live through the winter and may live for many years. A tree is perennial."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A perennial is a plant that lives for many years.","e":"I have both annuals and perennials in my garden."}]}]},"valuable":{"h":"valuable","i":"/ˈvæljuəbl̩/","a":"en-us-valuable.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is valuable it has great value. That is, it would cost a large amount of money.","e":"Gold is a very valuable metal."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(usually plural) An object that has great value.","e":"I keep my valuables in a safe deposit box at the bank."}]}]},"vein":{"h":"vein","i":"/veɪn/","a":"en-us-vein.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A vein is a tube in the body that carries blood back to the heart."},{"m":"(countable) A vein is a bump or line in a leaf where sap flows."},{"m":"(countable) A vein is a fissure, cleft, or cavity in the earth."}]}]},"veins":{"h":"veins","l":"vein","q":"noun"},"understood":{"h":"understood","i":"/ʌndər'stʊd/","a":"en-us-understood.ogg","l":"understand","q":"verb"},"traveler":{"h":"traveler","i":"/ˈtræv.l̩.ɚ/","a":"en-us-traveller.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A traveler is someone who is traveling."}]}]},"timer":{"h":"timer","i":"/ˈtaɪmɚ/","a":"en-us-timer.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A timer is a device that times something."}]}]},"waitress":{"h":"waitress","i":"/ˈweɪtrəs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-waitress.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A waitress is a woman who serves at a restaurant; a female waiter.","e":"I'm trying to get the waitress to bring our bill but she isn't looking this way."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you waitress, you work as a waitress.","e":"I waitress on the weekends to earn extra money."}]}]},"waitresses":{"h":"waitresses","l":"waitress","q":"noun"},"waiters":{"h":"waiters","l":"waiter","q":"noun"},"creak":{"h":"creak","i":"/kri:k/","a":"en-us-creek.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A type of sound. The sound of a door with rusty hinges is a creak.","e":"I heard a strange creak from my car's engine."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To make a creak sound.","e":"The door creaked as I opened it."}]}]},"textbook":{"h":"textbook","i":"/ˈtɛkst.bʊk/","a":"en-us-textbook.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A textbook is a book that is used in school, university, or college to study an academic topic.","e":"I had to bring my math textbook home so I could do my homework."}]}]},"publicity":{"h":"publicity","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) If you have publicity, many people know about you. Most often, this means a making yourself known (gaining publicity).","e":"We had a rally to gain publicity for our group."}]}]},"submerged":{"h":"submerged","l":"submerge","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is submerged is underwater.","e":"Jimmy was completely submerged when he was swimming."}]}]},"supplier":{"h":"supplier","i":"/səˈplaɪə/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A supplier is someone who something. Most often, this is a company that supplies another company with things it needs.","e":"The car factory needs a new supplier for car parts."}]}]},"officer":{"h":"officer","i":"/ˈɒfɪsə/","a":"en-us-officer.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An officer is a person in an army who has much authority. A general and a captain are two types of officers.","e":"A soldier must obey his commanding officer."},{"m":"(countable) An officer is a policeman, often called a \"police officer.\" (Note, \"officer\" is often better than \"policeman\" because the officer could be a woman or a man.)","e":"Officer, can you help me, I've been robbed."},{"m":"(countable) An officer is someone who holds office (meaning, has authority).","e":"The judge is an important officer of the court."}]}]},"officers":{"h":"officers","i":"/ˈɒfɪsəz/","a":"en-us-officers.ogg","l":"officer","q":"noun"},"lion":{"h":"lion","i":"/ˈlaɪən/","a":"en-us-lion.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A type of big cat from Africa, India and some of Europe; Panthera leo.","e":"We saw the lion in the zoo."}]}]},"lions":{"h":"lions","a":"en-us-lions.ogg","l":"lion","q":"noun"},"donkey":{"h":"donkey","a":"en-us-donkey.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An animal that is like a small horse with long ears. Donkeys are often used to carry things for people.","e":"He loaded the wood on the donkey to bring back to the house."}]}]},"mule":{"h":"mule","i":"/mjuːl/","a":"en-au-mule.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mule is the child of a horse and a donkey. Mules are often used to carry things for people or pull carts or plows."},{"m":"(countable) A mule is a shoe that does not have support for the heel."},{"m":"(countable) A mule is a person paid to smuggle drugs."}]}]},"jackass":{"h":"jackass","a":"en-us-jackass.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A jackass is a male donkey."},{"m":"(countable) A jackass is a stupid person."},{"m":"(countable) A jackass is a rude or obnoxious person."}]}]},"jenny-ass":{"h":"jenny-ass","a":"en-us-jenny-ass.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A female donkey."}]}]},"picked":{"h":"picked","i":"/pɪkt/","a":"en-us-picked.ogg","l":"pick","q":"verb"},"potable":{"h":"potable","i":"/'po(ʊ).tə.bɫ/","a":"en-us-potable.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is potable you can safely drink it."}]}]},"privilege":{"h":"privilege","i":"/ˈprɪvəlɛdʒ/","a":"en-us-privilege.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A privilege is a certain thing that someone is allowed to do or have. That is, not everyone is allowed to do or have it.","e":"Being able to drive is a privilege not a right."}]}]},"lioness":{"h":"lioness","i":"/ˈlaɪ.ə.nɪs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-lioness.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A lioness is a female lion.","e":"A lioness has no mane."}]}]},"elephant":{"h":"elephant","i":"/ˈɛləfənt/","a":"en-us-elephant.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An elephant is a very large animal with two long teeth called tusks and a long nose called trunk.","e":"Elephants live in both Asia and Africa."}]}]},"elephants":{"h":"elephants","i":"/ˈelɪfənts/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-elephants.wav","l":"elephant","q":"noun"},"squirrel":{"h":"squirrel","i":"/ˈskwɪrl̩/","a":"en-ca-squirrel.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A squirrel is a small animal that lives in trees and has a bushy tail. They are related to rats and often eat nuts.","e":"A squirrel is on the roof of my home."}]}]},"mouse":{"h":"mouse","i":"/maʊs/","a":"en-us-mouse.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mouse is a very small animal that is similar to a small rat.","e":"The mouse ran across the room."},{"m":"(countable) A mouse is a device used to control a computer.","e":"He clicked his mouse."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you mouse, you move around with caution; you move like a mouse."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you mouse, you hunt for mice; you try to catch mice."}]}]},"mice":{"h":"mice","i":"/maɪs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-mice.wav","l":"mouse","q":"noun"},"hawk":{"h":"hawk","i":"/hɔːk/","a":"en-us-hawk.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hawk is a type of bird that eats meat."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To sell.","e":"The vendors were hawking jewelry from little tables lining either side of the market square."},{"m":"(transitive) To cough or clear your throat loudly, sometimes coughing up phlegm.","e":"Jim hawked up some spit and spat it on the sidewalk."}]}]},"hawks":{"h":"hawks","l":"hawk","q":"noun"},"bin":{"h":"bin","i":"/bɪn/","a":"en-us-bin.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bin is a container for garbage.","e":"Clean up this room and throw that junk in the bin."},{"m":"(countable) A bin is a large container.","e":"The ship was carrying bins of apples"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you bin something, you throw it away."}]}]},"rabbit":{"h":"rabbit","i":"/ˈræbət/","a":"en-uk-a rabbit.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mammal with long ears.","e":"Our pet rabbit liked vegetables and could run very fast."}]}]},"hare":{"h":"hare","i":"/heə/","a":"en-us-hare.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A type of small animal with long ears, similar to a large rabbit.","e":"The slow tortoise beat the fast hare in the race by not quitting."}]}]},"ferret":{"h":"ferret","i":"/ˈfɛrɪt/","a":"en-us-ferret.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A small animal that eats meat. Ferrets often hunt rabbits and other small animals. Ferrets are similar to weasels and are related to weasels."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To use ferrets to hunt other animals."},{"m":"If you \"ferret something out\" you search for it and find it. You could be trying to find something, or to solve a problem (find the answer). Often, this means you have to go through a lot of material to find a little bit you want.","e":"Do you think you can ferret the names we need out of the list."}]}]},"bunny":{"h":"bunny","i":"/ˈbʌni/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-bunny.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A young rabbit is a bunny.","e":"My pet bunny is so cute."}]}]},"weasel":{"h":"weasel","i":"/'wiːzəl/","a":"en-us-weasel.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A weasel is a small, thin animal that eats meat.","e":"Pop goes the weasel!"},{"m":"(countable) (informal) A weasel is a sneaky or dishonest person, someone you cannot trust.","e":"That little weasel took all my money!"}]}]},"bat":{"h":"bat","i":"/bæt/","a":"en-us-bat.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bat is a small, furry animal (a mammal) that has wings and can fly."},{"m":"(countable) A bat is a special stick used to hit the ball in baseball, and in some other games."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you bat, you swing something or try to hit something.","e":"She batted her eyelashes shyly."}]}]},"stunt":{"h":"stunt","i":"/stʌnt/","a":"en-us-stunt.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A stunt is something dangerous you might do to get attention.","e":"Jumping over a river on a motorcycle is a dangerous stunt."},{"m":"(countable) A stunt is something that you do that gets you in trouble.","e":"I was punished for the stunt I pulled [did] in school."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To stunt something is to slow or stop its development.","e":"He was very short because sickness had stunted his growth."}]}]},"stunts":{"h":"stunts","l":"stunt","q":"noun"},"motorcycle":{"h":"motorcycle","i":"/ˈməʊtəˌsaikəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-motorcycle.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A motorcycle is a vehicle with two wheels and an engine."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you motorcycle, you ride or use a motorcycle."}]}]},"actor":{"h":"actor","i":"/ˈæk.tə/","a":"en-us-actor.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An actor is a person (usually male) who performs as a character in a play or other theatrical work. A female performer is called either an actress or an actor.","e":"The actor received a Tony Award."}]}]},"actress":{"h":"actress","i":"/ˈak.trəs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-actress.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An actress is a female who performs as a character in a play or other theatrical work.","e":"The main actress went up and bowed to the audience."}]}]},"actresses":{"h":"actresses","l":"actress","q":"noun"},"actors":{"h":"actors","a":"en-us-actors.ogg","l":"actor","q":"noun"},"motorcycles":{"h":"motorcycles","l":"motorcycle","q":"noun"},"musician":{"h":"musician","a":"en-us-musician.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A musician is a person who makes music. Most often, this is someone whose job is to make music for other people.","e":"My cousin is a musician for an orchestra in Texas."}]}]},"autumn":{"h":"autumn","i":"/ˈɔː.təm/","a":"en-us-autumn.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The season when the weather is getting cooler, after summer and before winter."}]}]},"sessile":{"h":"sessile","i":"/ˈsɛsʌɪl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-sessile.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If an animal is sessile it is attached to something (such as a rock or the ground). It cannot leave what it is attached too.","e":"A coral is sessile, it cannot leave its reef."},{"m":"If something is sessile it attaches directly to what it grows from. It does not have a stalk or stem.","e":"The species of flower was known for its sessile leaves."}]}]},"larynx":{"h":"larynx","i":"/ˈla.rɪŋks/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-larynx.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The larynx is a part of your body that is inside your throat.","e":"Your larynx makes your voice and keeps food out of your lungs."}]}]},"larynges":{"h":"larynges","i":"/lərˈɪndʒiːz/","l":"larynx","q":"noun"},"boring":{"h":"boring","i":"/ˈbɔːrɪŋ/","a":"en-us-boring.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is boring, it is not interesting or makes you want to do something else.","e":"Go to work, come home, sleep: life is so boring."}]}]},"interesting":{"h":"interesting","i":"/ˈɪntrɛstɪŋ/","a":"en-us-interesting.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Interesting means to cause a person to want to know more about someone or something or to like someone or something or to like doing something.","e":"That was a really interesting movie."}]}]},"conspiracy":{"h":"conspiracy","i":"/kənˈspɪrəsi/","a":"en-us-conspiracy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A secret plan between two or more people to do something.","e":"There was a conspiracy among the king's advisers to overthrow the king."},{"m":"A plan between two or more people to commit a crime."},{"m":"A group of ravens."}]}]},"borrow":{"h":"borrow","i":"/ˈbɒrəʊ/","a":"en-us-borrow.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you borrow something from someone, you use it and then you give it back to them.","e":"Governments need to make it easier for students to borrow money for school."},{"m":"If you borrow words or ideas from somebody, you use them in your own writing or speaking.","e":"Many people want to throw the war \"down the memory hole\", to borrow a phrase from Orwell's 1984."}]}]},"qualify":{"h":"qualify","i":"/ˈkwɑ.lə.fɑɪ/","a":"en-us-qualify.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you qualify for something, you have what is needed to be allowed to get or do it.","e":"Children must be under the age of six in order to qualify for a free meal."},{"m":"(transitive) If x qualifies y for z, x is needed to be allowed to get or do z and y has x.","e":"Describe the education, training, and experience that qualify you for the job."},{"m":"(intransitive) If x qualifies as y, it has what is needed to be considered y.","e":"Today's game certainly qualifies as one of the best in history."},{"m":"(transitive) If you qualify an idea, you add something to explain that the idea isn't always true.","e":"This is America and competition is our way of life. Having said this, I would like to qualify the statement and suggest that we need to work together too."},{"m":"(transitive) If a word or phrase qualifies another word or phrase, it limits or adds to the meaning of it."}]}]},"corrupt":{"h":"corrupt","i":"/kəˈrʌpt/","a":"en-us-corrupt.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is corrupt, they are weak in morals; it is depraved or perverted.","e":"The Government here is corrupt, so we'll move to escape them."},{"m":"If something is corrupt, it is not correct; it is with lots of errors in it.","e":"The text of the manuscript is corrupt."},{"m":"If someone or something is corrupt, it is not pure; it is spoiled or tainted.","e":"Prisoners of war are sometimes fed corrupt food."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you corrupt something or someone, you make them corrupt; you change them from good to bad.","e":"Don't you dare corrupt my son with those disgusting pictures!"}]}]},"academia":{"h":"academia","i":"/ˌæ.kəˈdiː.mɪ.ə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-academia.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Academia is a word for the group of people who are a part of the scientific and cultural community; this group of people have attended a university and/or do research."}]}]},"amphibious":{"h":"amphibious","i":"[æmˈfɪbi.əs]","a":"en-us-amphibious.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If an animal is amphibious it lives in water when it is young and lives on land when it is an adult.","e":"Frogs are amphibious."},{"m":"If something is amphibious it happens or can function on land and in water.","e":"The DUKW is an amphibious vehicle that was used during World War II."}]}]},"bambakophobia":{"h":"bambakophobia","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Bambakophobia is the fear of thinking about or touching cotton."}]}]},"swear":{"h":"swear","i":"/swɛə/","a":"en-us-swear.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) When you swear, you say a swear word."},{"m":"(intransitive) When you swear, you make a promise or an oath."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A swear word; an impolite or offensive word."}]}]},"reaper":{"h":"reaper","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Someone who reaps; someone who harvests grain."},{"m":"A machine used to harvest crops.","e":"The were several reapers in our wheat field yesterday."}]},{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Short for the Grim Reaper, the angel of death.","e":"\"Seasons don't fear the Reaper, nor do the wind, the sun, or the rain. We could be like they are... come on baby, don't fear the Reaper.\" -- Blue Oyster Cult, \"The Reaper\""}]}]},"reap":{"h":"reap","i":"/riːp/","a":"en-us-reap.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you reap something, you harvest it, most often grain.","e":"It was time to reap the corn, so we hired some people to help with it."},{"m":"If you reap something, you get the results of your actions.","e":"Jesus said, \"As you sow, so shall you reap \"."}]}]},"fuzzy":{"h":"fuzzy","i":"/ˈfʌzi/","a":"en-us-fuzzy.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is fuzzy it is covered with fuzz.","e":"I like to pet my dog because he's fuzzy."},{"m":"or not clear.","e":"My memory of the accident is pretty fuzzy."},{"m":"Not focused; not clear.","e":"I can see fine out of my left eye, but when I look at things with my right eye they're a little fuzzy."}]}]},"expensive":{"h":"expensive","i":"/ɪkˈspɛnsɪv/","a":"en-uk-expensive.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is expensive costs a lot of money to buy or takes a lot of effort to get.","e":"A pencil that cost $100 is very expensive."}]}]},"discount":{"h":"discount","i":"/dɪsˈkaʊnt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-discount (verb).wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you discount something, you lower its price."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A discount is a reduction of the price of something; a lowered cost."}]}]},"impolite":{"h":"impolite","i":"/ɪmpəˈlaɪt/","a":"en-us-impolite.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is impolite, it is not polite.","e":"It is considered impolite to talk while someone else is speaking."}]}]},"prove":{"h":"prove","i":"/pruːv/","a":"en-us-prove.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you prove something, you demonstrate that it is for real and true.","e":"I will prove my method is more effective than yours."}]}]},"unable":{"h":"unable","i":"/ʌnˈeɪbəl/","a":"en-us-unable.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When sosmeone or something is unable to do something, it cannot be done; it is not able to do it.","e":"I am unable to climb that mountain because I am too weak."}]}]},"grim":{"h":"grim","i":"/grɪm/","a":"en-us-grim.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are grim you are very serious, and might be thinking about bad things like loss, sadness, or death.","e":"I was in a grim mood after my grandmother died."}]}]},"plot":{"h":"plot","i":"/plɒt/","a":"en-us-plot.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A plot is the course of a story. It is the main things that happen in a story."},{"m":"(countable) A plot is a scheme for people to do something secretly."},{"m":"(countable) A plot is a graph or diagram."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you plot something, you plan to do a crime or something bad."},{"m":"If you plot a graph, you draw it out."}]}]},"glyph":{"h":"glyph","i":"/glɪf/","a":"en-us-glyph.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A glyph is a picture, symbol, or letter that is carved into stone.","e":"The cave had many glyphs carved into its walls."},{"m":"(countable) A glyph is a non-spoken symbol that represents something.","e":"Letters, which form words, are glyphs."}]}]},"conservative":{"h":"conservative","i":"/kənˈsɝvətɪv/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-conservative.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a person is conservative, they do not like change.","e":"Latino families are thought to hold conservative and traditional views on family life."},{"m":"A conservative estimate, guess, etc. is one that is careful, and usually lower than the actual number/amount.","e":"A very conservative estimate of the cost of delay is $6 per hour, but many believe that the true cost is much higher."},{"m":"Conservative clothing, furniture, etc. is usually plain and similar to styles that have been common for a long time.","e":"He is conservative in a gray suit and red tie."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A person who likes things how they are now or how they used to be; a person who like the status quo; a person who does not like change."},{"m":"(UK politics) A member of the."},{"m":"(US economics) A fiscal conservative"},{"m":"(US politics) A political conservative"},{"m":"(US social sciences) A social conservative."},{"m":"(Canada, politics) A person who believes in conservatism."}]}]},"google":{"h":"google","i":"/ˈɡuːɡəl/","a":"en-us-googol.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you google, you are searching for something on the Internet using Google.","e":"John will google topics that he would like to know more about."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Google is a popular and powerful search engine.","e":"I found your page on Google.com"},{"m":"(countable) A google is an Internet search done using the search engine Google.","e":"The google helped me find the website."}]}]},"newb":{"h":"newb","i":"/njuːb/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A newb is someone that is new to a game, or someone that has a new character; a newbie.","e":"That guy must be a newb at this video game. He has no idea how to play."}]}]},"clever":{"h":"clever","i":"/ˈklɛvɚ/","a":"en-us-clever.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A person that is clever is able to think quickly and sharply.","e":"He is a very clever salesman. He almost got me into buying his product."},{"m":"A clever idea or concept is one that is original and new.","e":"That is a clever invention. I have never seen something like that before."}]}]},"fraction":{"h":"fraction","i":"/ˈfræk.ʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-fraction.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A fraction is a part of a whole.","e":"A fraction of the profits were donated to a local charity."},{"m":"(countable) A fraction is a ratio, presented with a line between the numerator above and the denominator below."}]}]},"promise":{"h":"promise","i":"/ˈprɒmɪs/","a":"en-us-promise.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) When someone is making a promise to a person, he is saying what he plans to do for that person.","e":"Jane was angry that John broke his promise to take her out to the movies."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When a person promises, he states that he will make certain to do an action.","e":"I promise that I will come back home by noon. You can trust me."}]}]},"trip":{"h":"trip","i":"/trɪp/","a":"en-us-trip.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A trip is a journey to a place","e":"Let us go on a trip to John Doe Mountain. I have not been there in a while."},{"m":"(countable) A trip is when a person stumbles over something.","e":"He broke his wrist after that nasty trip."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When a person trips, he stumbles over something.","e":"Be careful of all the books on the floor. You do not want to trip."}]}]},"gums":{"h":"gums","l":"gum","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The skin around the roots of the teeth."}]}]},"blob":{"h":"blob","i":"/blɒb/","a":"en-us-blob.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A vague shape or amount; something without definite shape, especially a liquid or semi-solid substance."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you blob something, you drop it in the form of a [[#Noun|blob]]."}]}]},"reference":{"h":"reference","i":"/ˈrɛf.rəns/","a":"en-us-reference.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A reference is something that can be compared to.","e":"When making your model, use the model I created as a reference."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you reference something, you cite it as a source.","e":"Reference the dictionary for the definition of this word."},{"m":"When you reference something, you mention it."}]}]},"allowed":{"h":"allowed","i":"/əˈlaʊd/","a":"en-us-allowed.ogg","l":"allow","q":"verb"},"marriages":{"h":"marriages","l":"marriage","q":"noun"},"faiths":{"h":"faiths","i":"/feɪθs/","l":"faith","q":"noun"},"lionesses":{"h":"lionesses","l":"lioness","q":"noun"},"combinations":{"h":"combinations","l":"combination","q":"noun"},"conspiracies":{"h":"conspiracies","l":"conspiracy","q":"noun"},"diseases":{"h":"diseases","i":"/dɪˈziːzɪz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Persent101-diseases.wav","l":"disease","q":"noun"},"revisions":{"h":"revisions","a":"en-us-revisions.ogg","l":"revision","q":"noun"},"telegram":{"h":"telegram","i":"/ˈtɛləˌgræm/","a":"en-us-telegram.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A telegram is a message sent through a telegraph."}]}]},"ran":{"h":"ran","i":"/ræn/","a":"en-us-ran.ogg","l":"run","q":"verb"},"bonds":{"h":"bonds","i":"/bɑndz/","a":"en-us-bonds.ogg","l":"bond","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"When a person is in bonds, he is imprisoned or enslaved."}]}]},"emotions":{"h":"emotions","a":"en-us-emotions.ogg","l":"emotion","q":"noun"},"habitations":{"h":"habitations","l":"habitation","q":"noun"},"developments":{"h":"developments","l":"development","q":"noun"},"hiatus":{"h":"hiatus","i":"/haɪˈeɪtəs/","a":"en-us-hiatus.ogg","l":"hiatus","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A hiatus is a break or pause."},{"m":"A hiatus is a vacation.","e":"I'm taking a hiatus from work."}]}]},"acquisitions":{"h":"acquisitions","l":"acquisition","q":"noun"},"kilometers":{"h":"kilometers","l":"kilometer","q":"noun"},"poets":{"h":"poets","a":"en-us-poets.ogg","l":"poet","q":"noun"},"statements":{"h":"statements","i":"/ˈsteɪt.mənts/","a":"en-us-statements.ogg","l":"statement","q":"noun"},"anschluss":{"h":"Anschluss","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"When Austria and Germany became one country in 1938."}]}]},"daffodil":{"h":"daffodil","i":"/ˈdæfəˌdɪl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-daffodil.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A daffodil is a bulbous plant,, with yellow flowers and a trumpet-shaped corona.","e":"There is a garden with many daffodils."},{"m":"(uncountable) A bright yellow color, like that of a daffodil."}]}]},"narcissus":{"h":"Narcissus","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Naomi Persephone Amethyst (NaomiAmethyst)-Narcissus.wav","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"A hero who was known for his beauty and pride."},{"m":"A genus of plants.","e":"The common name for species of Narcissus is narcissi."}]}]},"reservation":{"h":"reservation","i":"/ˌrɛzəˈveɪʃən/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The act of or withholding something."},{"m":"Something that is withheld or reserved."},{"m":"(usually plural) A hesitation.","e":"I have reservations about telling him what I did. I'm afraid he'll break up with me if he knows."},{"m":"given to Native American people by the United States government."},{"m":"If you make a reservation, you reserve or pay for a room or seat in advance to be sure that the room or seat will be available for you when you get there.","e":"They made a reservation at the restaurant."},{"m":"The area which separates opposite lanes of traffic on a divided road; a median or divider on a road."}]}]},"violations":{"h":"violations","l":"violation","q":"noun"},"compounds":{"h":"compounds","l":"compound","q":"noun"},"albatrosses":{"h":"albatrosses","l":"albatross","q":"noun"},"girlfriends":{"h":"girlfriends","l":"girlfriend","q":"noun"},"boyfriends":{"h":"boyfriends","l":"boyfriend","q":"noun"},"malls":{"h":"malls","l":"mall","q":"noun"},"meals":{"h":"meals","l":"meal","q":"noun"},"fumble":{"h":"fumble","i":"/ˈfʌmbəl/","a":"en-us-fumble.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To touch something nervously.","e":"Waiting for the interview, he fumbled with his tie."},{"m":"To feel around awkwardly while trying to find something.","e":"He fumbled for his keys."},{"m":"(intransitive) To blunder uncertainly.","e":"He fumbled through his prepared speech."},{"m":"; To drop a ball or a baton etc.","e":"The player fumbled the ball."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A ball that has been dropped.","e":"He's not playing well today. He's already had three fumbles."}]}]},"resort":{"h":"resort","i":"/rɨˈzɔ(r)t/","a":"en-us-resort.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"s in a scenic area where people can go on vacation or to relax; resorts are like hotels that provide extra entertainment to their guests.","e":"Dan and Sarah went to an expensive resort in Jamaica for their honeymoon."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To choose to do something you don't want to do because you have no other choice.","e":"All my friends were too busy to help me move so I had to resort to calling a moving company and it cost me $100 dollars an hour!"},{"m":"To sort something again.","e":"I just sorted these files last week and didn't think I'd have to do it again for awhile, but I had to resort them this morning."}]}]},"larynxes":{"h":"larynxes","l":"larynx","q":"noun"},"features":{"h":"features","i":"/ˈfiːtʃəz/","a":"en-us-features.ogg","l":"feature","q":"noun"},"path":{"h":"path","i":"/pæθ/","a":"en-us-path.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A path is a way to get to a place. It is like a small road, often made of dirt.","e":"That path leads into the woods."},{"m":"(countable) A path is the way something moves.","e":"The planets follow an elliptical path."}]}]},"newspaper":{"h":"newspaper","i":"/ˈnjuːzˌpeɪpə/","a":"en-us-newspaper.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A newspaper is something you read for the news. It is usually published on cheap paper.","e":"\" can't exist without newspapers.\" (, London, 2 March 2009)"}]}]},"newspapers":{"h":"newspapers","a":"en-us-newspapers.ogg","l":"newspaper","q":"noun"},"cameras":{"h":"cameras","l":"camera","q":"noun"},"organizations":{"h":"organizations","l":"organization","q":"noun"},"versions":{"h":"versions","l":"version","q":"noun"},"movements":{"h":"movements","a":"en-us-movements.ogg","l":"movement","q":"noun"},"ears":{"h":"ears","a":"en-us-ears.ogg","l":"ear","q":"noun"},"maintenances":{"h":"maintenances","l":"maintenance","q":"noun"},"violets":{"h":"violets","l":"violet","q":"noun"},"papers":{"h":"papers","i":"/ˈpeɪpɚz/","a":"en-us-papers.ogg","l":"paper","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"documents or identification, such as a passport.","e":"He lost his papers while travelling and had a hard time getting home."}]}]},"consonants":{"h":"consonants","l":"consonant","q":"noun"},"finals":{"h":"finals","l":"final","q":"noun"},"births":{"h":"births","l":"birth","q":"noun"},"seabirds":{"h":"seabirds","l":"seabird","q":"noun"},"reservations":{"h":"reservations","l":"reservation","q":"noun"},"crimes":{"h":"crimes","l":"crime","q":"noun"},"valuables":{"h":"valuables","l":"valuable","q":"noun"},"principles":{"h":"principles","i":"/ˈprɪnsəpəlz/","a":"en-us-principles.ogg","l":"principle","q":"noun"},"lesbians":{"h":"lesbians","l":"lesbian","q":"noun"},"potatoes":{"h":"potatoes","i":"/pəˈteɪtoʊz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Persent101-potatoes.wav","l":"potato","q":"noun"},"livings":{"h":"livings","l":"living","q":"noun"},"doves":{"h":"doves","l":"dove","q":"noun"},"angles":{"h":"angles","a":"en-us-angles.ogg","l":"angle","q":"noun"},"paths":{"h":"paths","i":"/pɑːðz/","a":"en-us-paths.ogg","l":"path","q":"noun"},"capacities":{"h":"capacities","l":"capacity","q":"noun"},"adverbs":{"h":"adverbs","l":"adverb","q":"noun"},"rainbows":{"h":"rainbows","l":"rainbow","q":"noun"},"snakes":{"h":"snakes","l":"snake","q":"noun"},"nuts":{"h":"nuts","i":"/nʌts/","a":"en-us-nuts.ogg","l":"nut","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a person is nuts, they are crazy or insane.","e":"You're going to jump out of a plane?! Are you nuts?!"}]}]},"horses":{"h":"horses","i":"/hɔəsəs/","a":"en-us-horses.ogg","l":"horse","q":"noun"},"beers":{"h":"beers","l":"beer","q":"noun"},"futures":{"h":"futures","l":"future","q":"noun"},"comprehensions":{"h":"comprehensions","l":"comprehension","q":"noun"},"ideologies":{"h":"ideologies","l":"ideology","q":"noun"},"gals":{"h":"gals","l":"gal","q":"noun"},"occasions":{"h":"occasions","a":"en-us-occasions.ogg","l":"occasion","q":"noun"},"psychologies":{"h":"psychologies","l":"psychology","q":"noun"},"afternoons":{"h":"afternoons","l":"afternoon","q":"noun"},"hangings":{"h":"hangings","l":"hanging","q":"noun"},"squirrels":{"h":"squirrels","l":"squirrel","q":"noun"},"teachers":{"h":"teachers","l":"teacher","q":"noun"},"evidences":{"h":"evidences","l":"evidence","q":"noun"},"polygons":{"h":"polygons","l":"polygon","q":"noun"},"hospitals":{"h":"hospitals","l":"hospital","q":"noun"},"insurances":{"h":"insurances","l":"insurance","q":"noun"},"towns":{"h":"towns","a":"en-us-towns.ogg","l":"town","q":"noun"},"skills":{"h":"skills","i":"/skɪlz/","l":"skill","q":"noun"},"lads":{"h":"lads","l":"lad","q":"noun"},"bedpans":{"h":"bedpans","l":"bedpan","q":"noun"},"duties":{"h":"duties","a":"en-us-duties.ogg","l":"duty","q":"noun"},"intermediates":{"h":"intermediates","l":"intermediate","q":"noun"},"natures":{"h":"natures","a":"en-us-natures.ogg","l":"nature","q":"noun"},"classes":{"h":"classes","i":"/ˈklɑːsɪz/","a":"en-us-classes.ogg","l":"class","q":"noun"},"coals":{"h":"coals","l":"coal","q":"noun"},"minimums":{"h":"minimums","l":"minimum","q":"noun"},"zippers":{"h":"zippers","l":"zipper","q":"noun"},"products":{"h":"products","i":"/ˈprɒd.əkts/","a":"en-us-products.ogg","l":"product","q":"noun"},"coordinations":{"h":"coordinations","l":"coordination","q":"noun"},"idiotic":{"h":"idiotic","i":"/ɪd.iˈɑt.ɪk/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a person is called idiotic, they are acting like an idiot."},{"m":"If a situation is described as idiotic, it is very foolish, stupid, or does not make much sense."}]}]},"bonus":{"h":"bonus","i":"/ˈbəʊ.nəs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-bonus.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bonus is something extra or more that is added.","e":"John got a bonus because he played very well."}]}]},"rookie":{"h":"rookie","i":"/ˈrʊki/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-rookie.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A rookie is a person who is new at something.","e":"Mark was the rookie of the team because he was just drafted."}]}]},"tryout":{"h":"tryout","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A tryout is test of the to see how good someone or something is at a task.","e":"Jane is going to that tryout for the fall musical. I hope she makes it; she has a wonderful singing voice."}]}]},"overpopulation":{"h":"overpopulation","i":"/ˌəʊvəˌpɒpjʊˈleɪʃn̩/","a":"en-us-overpopulation.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Overpopulation is when a place has too much of an animal or plant for it to be healthy. This usually refers to humans.","e":"The overpopulation of our city is making life difficulty."}]}]},"humans":{"h":"humans","l":"human","q":"noun"},"amendments":{"h":"amendments","l":"amendment","q":"noun"},"wines":{"h":"wines","a":"en-us-wines.ogg","l":"wine","q":"noun"},"noses":{"h":"noses","a":"en-us-noses.ogg","l":"nose","q":"noun"},"tryouts":{"h":"tryouts","l":"tryout","q":"noun"},"speakers":{"h":"speakers","l":"speaker","q":"noun"},"volumes":{"h":"volumes","a":"en-us-volumes.ogg","l":"volume","q":"noun"},"reflexive":{"h":"reflexive","i":"/rəˈflɛksɪv/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-reflexive.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A verb is reflexive when it refers to the subject as the object noun.","e":"In the sentence, \"Mary bathed\", bathed is reflexive since it refers to Mary bathing herself."}]}]},"modifier":{"h":"modifier","i":"/ˈmɒdɪfaɪə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-modifier.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A modifier is usually an optional word or phrase, describing the degree, quality, manner, frequency, etc. of something.","e":"The word black is the modifier in the phrase a black cat."}]}]},"interjection":{"h":"interjection","i":"/ˌɪn.tɝ.ˈʤɛk.ʃn̩/","a":"en-us-interjection.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An interjection is a word that shows an emotion. It is not grammatically part of the sentence.","e":"The word \"Yikes\" is an interjection in the phrase \"Yikes, what a scare.\""}]}]},"eyebrow":{"h":"eyebrow","i":"/ˈaɪˌbraʊ/","a":"en-us-eyebrow.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The eyebrow is the hair that grows on the bony ridge above the eye."}]}]},"eyebrows":{"h":"eyebrows","l":"eyebrow","q":"noun"},"businesses":{"h":"businesses","l":"business","q":"noun"},"rabbits":{"h":"rabbits","l":"rabbit","q":"noun"},"chins":{"h":"chins","l":"chin","q":"noun"},"centimeters":{"h":"centimeters","l":"centimeter","q":"noun"},"introduction":{"h":"introduction","i":"/ɪntrəˈdʌkʃən/","a":"en-us-introduction.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An introduction is the first or opening part","e":"This is the introduction to the book."},{"m":"An introduction is when something is announced.","e":"The winner of the prize will be announced during the introduction portion of the opening."},{"m":"An introduction is a social process for making two people acquainted.","e":"My introduction to Dr. Sagan was cordial."},{"m":"A process for making someone familiar with a certain area, topic, or field.","e":"Lisa's introduction to horseback riding was a disaster."}]}]},"article":{"h":"article","i":"/ˈɑːtɪkəl/","a":"en-us-article.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An article is a story or report that you can read in a newspaper, journal, or online."},{"m":"(countable) An article is a member of a larger group.","e":"A shirt is an article of clothing."},{"m":"(countable) An article is an object."}]}]},"risk":{"h":"risk","i":"/rɪsk/","a":"en-us-risk.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A risk is something bad that could possibly happen.","e":"There are many risks associated with the stock market."},{"m":"(countable) A risk is the chance of something bad happening.","e":"The risk of us failing is too great."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To risk something means to take a chance with something.","e":"She risked hypothermia by swimming the English Channel."}]}]},"segment":{"h":"segment","i":"/ˈsɛɡ.mənt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-segment (noun).wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"a part of something","e":"How long is that segment of rope?"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you segment something, you make it into [[#Noun|segments]] or parts","e":"Will you peel and segment the orange for the fruit salad?"}]}]},"joining":{"h":"joining","i":"/ˈd͡ʒɔɪnɪŋ/","a":"en-us-joining.ogg","l":"join","q":"verb"},"joins":{"h":"joins","l":"join","q":"verb"},"joined":{"h":"joined","i":"/ˈd͡ʒɔɪnd/","a":"en-us-joined.ogg","l":"join","q":"verb"},"accounting":{"h":"accounting","i":"/əˈkaʊntɪŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-accounting.wav","l":"account","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Accounting involves keeping records on financial information."},{"m":"An accounting goes over an event that happened and the explanation for why it happened."}]}]},"eyelash":{"h":"eyelash","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An eyelash is one of the hairs that grows on the eyelid."}]}]},"capital":{"h":"capital","i":"/ˈkæp.ɪ.təl/","a":"en-us-capital.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A capital is the most important city of a country. The government of the country is usually located there."},{"m":"(countable) The (field) capital is the most important city in that particular field.","e":"Hollywood is the film capital, New York the theater capital, Las Vegas the gambling capital."},{"m":"(uncountable) A person's capital is all his money and wealth."},{"m":"(countable) A capital forms the topmost member of a column or pilaster. It broadens the area of the column's supporting surface."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A capital object or idea is something that is very important."},{"m":"(British), very good.","e":"That is a capital idea!"},{"m":"Involving punishment by death.","e":"Not all felonies are capital crimes."},{"m":".","e":"One begins a sentence with a capital letter."}]}]},"comparable":{"h":"comparable","i":"/ˈkəmpɛrəbl̩/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-comparable.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If two things are comparable, then they are similar and can be compared to one another.","e":"An elephant is comparable in size to a double-decker bus."}]}]},"race":{"h":"race","i":"/reɪs/","a":"en-us-race.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A race is when people compete to see who is the fastest at either driving or running.","e":"There was a race to see who could finish first."},{"m":"(countable) A race is a group of people that come from the same place and have similar traditions."},{"m":"(countable) A race is a group of people with the same physical characteristics, such as skin color, hair color and type, etc.","e":"There were three different races at the school; s, s, and Asians"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When a person races, he competes with other people to see who can go the fastest.","e":"Tom was hungry, so he raced George down to the ice cream truck."}]}]},"eyelid":{"h":"eyelid","i":"/ˈaɪ.lɪd/","a":"en-us-eyelid.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The eyelid is a piece of skin that covers the eye. The eyelid can move back, allowing the eye to \"open\".","e":"The doctor looked at his eyelids."}]}]},"palate":{"h":"palate","i":"/ˈpælɪt/","a":"en-us-palate.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The palate is the roof of the mouth."},{"m":"A person's palate is his ability to taste."}]}]},"furniture":{"h":"furniture","i":"/ˈfɜːnɪtʃə/","a":"en-us-furniture.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Furniture are items used to decorate a room or make it more comfortable."}]}]},"baked":{"h":"baked","l":"bake","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If food is baked, it was cooked by baking."},{"m":"If a person is baked, they are high on drugs, usually marijuana."}]}]},"x-rays":{"h":"X-rays","l":"x-ray","q":"noun"},"oddity":{"h":"oddity","i":"/ˈɒdɪti/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-oddity.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Something odd or unusual","e":"That's quite an oddity you have there. I think people would pay to see something that rare."}]}]},"abler":{"h":"abler","i":"/eɪ.blɚ/","l":"able","q":"adjective"},"trespass":{"h":"trespass","i":"/ˈtrɛspæs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-trespass.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) When you trespass, you are going to a place that you are not allowed to.","e":"Do not trespass that area restricted to visitors. You will be fined."}]}]},"drawing":{"h":"drawing","i":"/ˈdrɔ.(w)ɪŋ(ɡ)/","a":"en-us-drawing.ogg","l":"draw","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A drawing is a picture.","e":"He sketched a drawing of that vase."},{"m":"(countable) A drawing is a contest where the person who wins is chosen randomly."}]}]},"difficulty":{"h":"difficulty","i":"/difikəl̩tiː/","a":"en-us-difficulty.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The difficulty of something is how hard it is to do.","e":"The student finished the homework with great difficulty."}]}]},"constructions":{"h":"constructions","l":"construction","q":"noun"},"oddities":{"h":"oddities","l":"oddity","q":"noun"},"scalp":{"h":"scalp","i":"/skælp/","a":"en-us-scalp.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The scalp is part of the head where the hair grows from."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you scalp a person, you remove the part of the head where the hair grows from."}]}]},"firm":{"h":"firm","i":"/fɜrm/","a":"en-us-firm.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A firm is a group of people who work together as a business.","e":"John & John is a law firm."},{"m":"(countable) A firm is a group of people that come together to make money."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A firm object is hard and solid."}]}]},"leader":{"h":"leader","i":"/ˈliː.də(r)/","a":"en-us-leader.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A leader is someone who leads others and has them following him.","e":"Kings, presidents, governors, and mayors are all different types of leaders."},{"m":"(countable) A leader is someone who is the best at what he does.","e":"Johntech is a leader in the microprocessor industry."}]}]},"opening":{"h":"opening","i":"/ˈoʊ.pə.nɪŋ/","a":"en-us-opening.ogg","l":"open","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An opening is a place that someone or something can go through."},{"m":"(countable) An opening is the first time a placed is opened to other people.","e":"We are going to the museum's opening."}]}]},"sight":{"h":"sight","i":"/saɪt/","a":"en-us-sight.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Having sight is if you can see things."},{"m":"A sight is something that people want to see.","e":"The Statue of Liberty is a popular sight in New York City."},{"m":"A sight is something you see."},{"m":"A sight is a device that is attached onto a weapon and it is for a person to look into to aim the weapon at an intended target."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you sight something, you see it.","e":"The farmers sighted something strange circling overhead."}]}]},"soporific":{"h":"soporific","i":"/ˌsɒp.əˈrɪf.ɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-soporific.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A soporific helps you go to sleep."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is soporific, then it will make you or almost make you go to sleep.","e":"The movie was soporific. I almost fell asleep."}]}]},"luminous":{"h":"luminous","i":"/ˈluːmɪnəs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-luminous.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A luminous object is very bright.","e":"The sun and the Moon are two luminous objects in the sky."},{"m":"A luminous object gives off light."}]}]},"affair":{"h":"affair","i":"/əˈfɛr/","a":"en-us-affair.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Affairs are things that happen or are done, usually that are important enough to be in the news.","e":"We're thinking less about foreign affairs, and more about what happens here inside the country."},{"m":"(countable) An affair is a romantic or sexual relationship between two people when at least one of them is married to somebody else.","e":"There were many brief, desperate love affairs between English women and the American soldiers during the war."},{"m":"(countable) An affair is something that is related to a particular individual or group.","e":"What I do in my free time is my affair."}]}]},"agenda":{"h":"agenda","i":"/əˈdʒɛn.də/","a":"en-us-agenda.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An agenda is a list of things to be talked about, done, or otherwise dealt with.","e":"I think there are some important domestic policy items on the agenda still."},{"m":"(countable) An agenda is a reason for doing something, usually a bad or secret reason.","e":"The President may have a political agenda in saying this."}]}]},"aim":{"h":"aim","i":"/eɪm/","a":"en-us-aim.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An aim is something you want to do or have done.","e":"The aim of the study was to find out if these students would talk differently to themselves during independent work."},{"m":"(uncountable) If you take aim at something, you point a gun or other weapon at it.","e":"He takes aim and fires."},{"m":"(uncountable) If you take aim at something, you turn your attention to it.","e":"The book takes aim at politicians and their wasteful spending."},{"m":"(countable) Your aim is your skill in hitting something that you are shooting, throwing, kicking, etc. at.","e":"He threw the stone at the bird, but his aim wasn't so good."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you aim at doing something, you plan or try to do it.","e":"The new rules for cars are aimed at reducing speeds and improving driver safety."},{"m":"If you aim at something, you point a gun or other weapon at it.","e":"He grabbed for his gun, aimed it and started shooting."}]}]},"accommodate":{"h":"accommodate","i":"/əˈkɒməˌdeɪt/","a":"en-us-accommodate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If x accommodates y, x has or makes room for y.","e":"The platform didn't look nearly big enough to accommodate a ship the size of the Lady Luck"},{"m":"(transitive) If a place accommodates people, they stay, work, or live there.","e":"The school residence currently accommodates students from 27 countries."},{"m":"(transitive) If you accommodate someone or something, you do what is needed to help or understand them.","e":"Our restaurant can accommodate the needs of people with special diets."}]}]},"worths":{"h":"worths","l":"worth","q":"noun"},"dull":{"h":"dull","i":"/dʌl/","a":"en-us-dull.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A dull object is not sharp."},{"m":"A dull object is not shiny."},{"m":"A dull person is boring and not interesting.","e":"The presentation was rather dull."},{"m":"A dull person is not smart.","e":"My friend is dull."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you dull something, you make it softer or less sharp."}]}]},"beginning":{"h":"beginning","i":"/bɪˈgɪn.ɪŋ/","a":"en-us-beginning.ogg","l":"begin","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The beginning of something is where it starts from."},{"m":"The beginning is the first part of something.","e":"The beginning of the book introduced all the main characters."}]}]},"incorrect":{"h":"incorrect","i":"/ˌɪnkəˈrɛkt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-incorrect.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Incorrect things are wrong, or not correct.","e":"He got points off for an incorrect answer on the quiz."}]}]},"application":{"h":"application","i":"/ˌæpləˈkeɪʃən/","a":"en-us-application.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An application is a request for something. Often it is a paper form that you have to fill out to ask for something.","e":"She filled out her applications for college and hoped she would hear soon whether she was accepted to any schools."},{"m":"An application is the way something is used.","e":"The application of the new laws made things much more fair in the country."},{"m":"If something has an application, it can be used.","e":"She liked studying Latin in college, but found that a degree in Latin had few applications in the real world."},{"m":"An application is a computer program.","e":"He told me I would need a special application to make my new printer work with my old computer."},{"m":"Application is putting something onto something else, like a surface.","e":"Kathleen was so light-skinned that she needed many applications of sunscreen each time she was at the beach to keep from getting sunburned."}]}]},"cooking":{"h":"cooking","i":"/ˈkʊ.kɪŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-cooking.wav","l":"cook","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Cooking is the action of using heat to prepare food. The most common sources of heat are stoves, ovens, and microwaves, but cooking can also be done over a flame. Cooking can make food hot, change its texture, and kill bacteria that might be living in it. Some people see cooking as a chore, while others see it as an art.","e":"The school teaches the secrets of French cooking."}]}]},"alarm":{"h":"alarm","i":"/əˈlɑːm/","a":"en-us-alarm.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An alarm is a signal that something needs attention or a machine that makes the signal.","e":"I wake up, without an alarm clock, at seven or eight a.m."},{"m":"(uncountable) Alarm is a feeling of worry or fear.","e":"They watched with some alarm as the speeding car got closer."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you alarm someone, you make them feel worried or scared.","e":"The school was alarmed by the number of children failing math."}]}]},"allocate":{"h":"allocate","i":"/ˈæl.ə.keɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-allocate.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you allocate something, you set it aside or plan to use it for a particular purpose. The term is often used with money or resources.","e":"We need to change the way that the research money is being allocated."}]}]},"amaze":{"h":"amaze","i":"/əˈmeɪz/","a":"en-us-amaze.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you amaze somebody, you make them feel very surprised.","e":"It totally amazes me that he handles things as well as he does."}]}]},"employment":{"h":"employment","i":"/ɪmˈplɔɪmənt/","a":"en-us-employment.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Employment is having a job."},{"m":"(uncountable) The work one does to get money.","e":"His employment is with another store."}]}]},"forwards":{"h":"forwards","l":"forward","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If something goes forwards, it moves in the direction of its front, not its back."},{"m":"If something goes forwards, it gets better."},{"m":"If something goes forwards, it moves into the future."}]}]},"football":{"h":"football","i":"/ˈfʊtbɔl/","a":"EN-AU ck1 football.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Football can mean a number of team sports where players kick a ball, like association football (soccer), American football, Canadian football, Australian rules football, Gaelic football and rugby football."},{"m":"(countable) A football is the ball used in a football game."}]}]},"flavor":{"h":"flavor","i":"/ˈfleɪvə/","a":"en-us-flavour.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The flavor of something is how it tastes.","e":"I do not like the flavor of this snack. I prefer something sweeter."},{"m":"(countable) A flavor is something that adds taste to food."},{"m":"(countable) A flavor is a characteristic."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you flavor food or drink, you add a new taste to it.","e":"He is going to flavor the dish with that new spice he bought at the supermarket."}]}]},"buildings":{"h":"buildings","i":"/ˈbɪldɪŋz/","a":"en-us-buildings.ogg","l":"building","q":"noun"},"flavors":{"h":"flavors","l":"flavor","q":"noun"},"footballs":{"h":"footballs","l":"football","q":"noun"},"imagination":{"h":"imagination","i":"/ɪˌmædʒəˈneɪʃən/","a":"en-us-imagination.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Imagination is the ability to see something in your mind, or pretend that something false is true.","e":"Children use imagination to see sticks as swords and fight monsters."},{"m":"(uncountable) Imagination is the ability to think of something new, different, strange, or unusual.","e":"The artist made this amazing artwork by using his imagination."},{"m":"(countable) A person's imagination is how creative he can be.","e":"The writer was well-known for his creative imagination."}]}]},"season":{"h":"season","i":"/ˈsiːzən/","a":"en-us-season.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A season is a particular time of year with a particular kind of weather, usually spring, summer, fall, and winter, or rainy season and dry season."},{"m":"(countable) A season is a particular time of year when certain activities happen.","e":"The theatrical season lasts from early autumn to late spring."},{"m":"(countable) A cycle or set of episodes of a television show.","e":"Victoria justice wasn't on \"Zoey 101\", until the second season."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you season food, you add seasonings to it, like salt, pepper, or other herbs and spices.","e":"Place meat in the bottom of a large oven-safe dish, seasoning each layer with salt and pepper."}]}]},"drug":{"h":"drug","i":"/drʌg/","a":"en-uk-drug.ogg","l":"drag","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Drugs are substances such as alcohol, cocaine, or aspirin, that people take to make changes in their body.","e":"He's in jail for 3 to 15 years for drug trafficking."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you drug somebody, you give them a drug, usually to put them to sleep.","e":"They put me in hospital, drugged me up and left me in there for two years."}]}]},"guard":{"h":"guard","i":"/gɑ:d/","a":"en-us-guard.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A guard is a person or a group of people who watch something and try to stop anything bad from happening to it.","e":"After leaving the police he worked as a security guard at an airport."},{"m":"(countable) A guard is something that is a barrier between you and something dangerous.","e":"You push a button and a guard comes down to keep your hands out of the machine while it works."},{"m":"(countable) A guard is a position on a basketball team who moves the ball to help their team gain points"},{"m":"(countable) A guard is an offensive position in American football who plays either side of the center."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you guard something, you watch it and try to stop anything bad from happening to it.","e":"The front gate was guarded by Iraqi soldiers."}]}]},"religious":{"h":"religious","i":"/rɪˈlɪdʒəs/","a":"en-us-religious.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is religious, it is related to or about religion.","e":"Religious beliefs can be very important in choosing a marriage partner."},{"m":"If someone is religious, they believe in a religion and follow its rules.","e":"Because Buddhism forbids the wearing of shoes on pagoda grounds, the deeply religious Mon troops remain barefoot while climbing a rocky cliff there."},{"m":"If someone is religious about doing something, they do it on a regular schedule or every chance that they get.","e":"We have been less than religious about our daily exercise."}]}]},"analyse":{"h":"analyse","i":"/ˈæn.ə.laɪz/","a":"en-us-analyze.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you analyse something, you study it carefully to understand it, often to see what it is made of.","e":"They can make up questions, collect field data, and analyse that data on their computers."}]}]},"frequency":{"h":"frequency","i":"/ˈfriːkwənsi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-frequency.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Something's frequency is how often it happens.","e":"A frequency of one hertz is an event repeated once per second."}]}]},"announce":{"h":"announce","i":"/əˈnaʊns/","a":"en-us-announce.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you announce something, you make it public by telling people about it.","e":"\"There's been a change in plans,\" she announced, and her mother looked surprised."},{"m":"(transitive) If you announce somebody, you tell others that the person has arrived."}]}]},"apology":{"h":"apology","i":"/əˈpɒl.ə.dʒɪ/","a":"en-us-apology.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An apology is words or actions that show you are sorry.","e":"Thank you both very much, and again, my apologies for keeping you both waiting so late."},{"m":"If you make no apologies for something, you think it was the right thing to do.","e":"The company president makes no apologies for those high profits, saying people should be pleased the industry is so strong."}]}]},"understanding":{"h":"understanding","i":"/ʌndəˈstandɪŋ/","a":"en-us-understanding.ogg","l":"understand","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A person's understanding of something is what they know or think about it.","e":"Science helps us to gain a better understanding of natural processes."},{"m":"(countable) An understanding is an agreement between two people.","e":"We had an understanding. You should have fulfilled your end of the bargain."},{"m":"(uncountable) Understanding is your ability to understand the feelings of other people.","e":"Teachers must listen with kindness and understanding to what the young have to say."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"An understanding person is able to easily see how someone else feels.","e":"Thanks for being so understanding about how emotional and erratic I've been acting lately."}]}]},"oxygen":{"h":"oxygen","i":"/ˈɒksɪdʒən/","a":"en-us-oxygen.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Oxygen is a chemical element (symbol O) with an atomic number of 8."},{"m":"(uncountable) Oxygen is a type of gas, which is needed for breathing."},{"m":"(countable) An oxygen is an atom of the element oxygen."}]}]},"phrase":{"h":"phrase","i":"/freɪz/","a":"en-us-phrase.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A phrase is a short expression.","e":"Sheela liked to use that particular phrase whenever she disagreed with something."},{"m":"(countable) A phrase is a group of words. Together, they act as a single unit in a sentence.","e":"Within a noun phrase (NP), adjectives function as modifiers."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you phrase an idea, you express it in words."}]}]},"appeal":{"h":"appeal","i":"/əˈpiːl/","a":"en-us-appeal.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An appeal is a strong or official request.","e":"In an emotional appeal, Sevan asked the two groups to stop the fighting."},{"m":"An appeal is a request for an earlier decision to be changed, especially in law.","e":"Her application was refused, her appeal was rejected, and when she failed to leave, she was arrested."},{"m":"(uncountable) If something has appeal, people have good feelings about it, like it, or want it.","e":"It was a type of game that had universal appeal to male and female."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you appeal for something, you ask for it, often strongly or officially.","e":"The people appealed for help as huge fires advanced towards their homes."},{"m":"If you appeal a decision, you ask for it to be changed, especially in law.","e":"The defense notified the State Supreme Court that it would appeal the conviction."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you something appeals to you, you have good feelings about it, like it, or want it.","e":"Adventure, money, sex, and violence appeal to large numbers of people."}]}]},"approve":{"h":"approve","i":"/əˈpruːv/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Mélange a trois-approve.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If a person in power approves something such as a plan, a sale, a rule, etc., they say it is OK and it may go ahead.","e":"Voters there have approved a plan to remove most cars from the city center."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you approve of something, you think it is good.","e":"The latest survey shows that only 32 percent approve of the way the president is handling his job."}]}]},"nickel":{"h":"nickel","i":"/ˈnɪk.əl/","a":"en-us-nickel.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable); A nickel is a coin that is worth five cents."},{"m":"(uncountable) Nickel is an element in chemistry. It has a symbol of Ni and an atomic number of 28."}]}]},"defy":{"h":"defy","a":"en-us-defy.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you defy someone, you refuse to do what he or she wants you to do.","e":"He is going to defy her orders for him to come here."},{"m":"When you defy something, you challenge it.","e":"That politician is willing to defy public opinion, even if it is not politically popular."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A defy is a challenge to something."}]}]},"spinoff":{"h":"spinoff","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A spinoff is something that has separated from its main component."},{"m":"A spinoff has a main character that was also a character, though not a major one, in another television show, movie, or book."}]}]},"dwarf":{"h":"dwarf","i":"/dwɔː(r)f/","a":"en-us-dwarf.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(fantasy, folklore) A race of small people, sometime with long beards. This is a type of fictional character found in legends all over the world, whose main characteristic is being much shorter than normal.","e":"In Scandinavian legends dwarves are considered as a true people, different from human beings."},{"m":"A very little person. A dwarf is a person whose size is much smaller than average.","e":"She is a dwarf, only three feet (one meter) tall."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is dwarf is it smaller than normal. Anything of a much smaller than average size can be called dwarf..","e":"I kept a dwarf tree in my house."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If X dwarfs Y, X is much bigger than Y.","e":"The elephant dwarfed the people with it."}]}]},"midget":{"h":"midget","i":"/ˈmɪd͡ʒɪt/","a":"En-us-midget.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A midget is a very small person, animal or thing. (sometimes offensive when describing a person who is short)"},{"m":"A midget is a little person. A midgets size is much smaller than normal.","e":"He is a midget, only three feet (one meter) tall."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Midget is used to describe something which is very small.","e":"midget submarines"}]}]},"g-force":{"h":"g-force","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) G-force is another word for gravity, the force of universal attraction between particles of matter. Large bodies, like planets and moons, can attract smaller objects to them, giving these objects weight. The strength of g-force is different on each body.","e":"On the Moon, astronauts weighing 200 kg move as easily as if they weighed 35 kg on Earth, because the g-force is six times lesser here."}]}]},"nostril":{"h":"nostril","i":"/ˈnɒstrɪl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-nostril.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A nostril is one of the two holes at the bottom of the nose.","e":"When you breathe using your nose, air goes through your nostril."}]}]},"dog-eared":{"h":"dog-eared","l":"dog-ear","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"(metaphorical) A dog-eared book has been read a lot, making the pages bent like the ears of a dog.","e":"After being opened and closed so many times, this book got all its pages dog-eared."}]}]},"serpent":{"h":"serpent","a":"en-us-serpent.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A serpent is a snake, or an animal that looks like a snake."},{"m":"A serpent is a musical instrument made of brass. It is called a serpent because the instrument looks like a snake."}]}]},"orbit":{"h":"orbit","i":"/ˈɔː.bɪt/","a":"en-us-orbit.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An orbit is a circular path achieved by an object that goes around another that is generally bigger.","e":"The Earth's orbit around the sun is completed in nearly three hundred sixty-five days and a quarter of day."},{"m":"(countable) An orbit is the hole in the skull containing the eyeball.","e":"Cartoon characters sometimes have their eyeballs going out of their orbits in order to make their expression look funny."},{"m":"(uncountable) (metaphorical) An orbit is the sphere of influence a powerful person, organization or country can have.","e":"During the Cold War, almost all Eastern European countries were in the orbit of the USSR."}]}]},"bald":{"h":"bald","i":"/bɔːld/","a":"en-us-bald.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Someone who is bald has a head without hair on it.","e":"When people grow old, many of them become bald because their fallen hair is not replaced any more."}]}]},"comma":{"h":"comma","i":"/ˈkɒm.ə/","a":"en-us-comma.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A comma is the sign, used to make a short pause in a sentence.","e":"A space is required after the comma, but not before."}]}]},"eyeball":{"h":"eyeball","i":"/ˈaɪ.bɔːl/","a":"en-us-eyeball.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An eyeball is the entire round part of an eye, including the hidden part.","e":"The doctor checked my eyeball when I got my new glasses."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you eyeball something, you estimate or judge it; you look at it."}]}]},"writes":{"h":"writes","i":"/raɪts/","a":"en-us-writes.ogg","l":"write","q":"verb"},"won":{"h":"won","i":"/wʌn/","a":"en-us-won.ogg","l":"win","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To won is to live or remain."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Won is the money used in Korea."}]}]},"astrophysics":{"h":"astrophysics","i":"/ˌæs.troʊˈfɪz.ɪks/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-astrophysics.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Astrophysics is the part of physical science that studies space bodies and our universe in general.","e":"With the help of telescopes and satellites, astrophysics has made a great jump in our understanding of the universe since the last decades."}]}]},"universe":{"h":"universe","i":"/ˈjuːnɪˌvɜːs/","a":"en-us-universe.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The universe is the whole space we live in and everything it contains: our Milky Way and billions of other that are not all known are part of our universe.","e":"According to recent, our universe would be bent on itself, being finite but having no frontiers."},{"m":"(countable) A universe can also stand for a world or an area, fictional or not, considered in itself.","e":"Musical universes are so varied that we cannot know them all."},{"m":"(countable) A universe is also an imaginary set of worlds invented by someone.","e":"The universe created by Tolkien is surprisingly dense and imaginative."},{"m":"(uncountable), (metaphorical) The complete set of numerous possibilities.","e":"Among this universe of choices, just one will be the good one."}]}]},"hedgehog":{"h":"hedgehog","i":"/ˈhɛdʒhɒɡ/","a":"EN-AU ck1 hedgehog.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A hedgehog is a small insect-eating mammal, whose back is completely covered with short spines.","e":"When a hedgehog feels in danger of being attacked, it rolls itself into a ball to protect his belly."}]}]},"furry":{"h":"furry","i":"/ˈfɜːri/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-furry.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A furry animal has its body covered with fur, a dense area of thin hairs.","e":"Children often like furry animals because they are smooth when touched."}]}]},"wormhole":{"h":"wormhole","a":"en-au-wormhole.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A wormhole is a theoretical space tunnel that would begin with a black hole and end with a white hole; this tunnel would be a shortcut for space travel.","e":"Though based on real scientific guesses, wormholes are largely used in some science-fiction works. If they really exist or not is still unsure."}]}]},"bullet":{"h":"bullet","i":"/bʊl.ɪt/","a":"en-us-bullet.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bullet is a small piece of metal thrown by a gun at a great speed.","e":"a loaded gun is dangerous because of the bullets that can be fired by accident."},{"m":"(countable) (typography) A bullet is a printed symbol in the form of a solid circle, “•”, it is usually used to mark items in a list."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If something bullets somewhere, it moves at high speed, like a bullet from a gun.","e":"He bulleted around the race track!"}]}]},"unwillingly":{"h":"unwillingly","i":"/ʌnˈwɪlɪŋli/","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Doing something unwillingly is doing something because you have to even though you don't want to.","e":"He began to clean his room unwillingly after being asked five times."}]}]},"clown":{"h":"clown","i":"/klaʊn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-clown.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A clown is a person that entertains people, usually at a circus. He dresses in bright colors, has paint on his face, and wears clothes that are too big for him.","e":"Some children are afraid by clowns because of their unusual appearance that can be rather impressive."},{"m":"(countable) A clown is also a person whose behaviour is a bit silly, not serious.","e":"Though very intelligent, this person is a true clown so that no one believes what he says."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"A person who is clowning is not serious, acts in a silly way, like a clown.","e":"Stop clowning all the time, you're annoying me!"}]}]},"working":{"h":"working","i":"/ˈwɜːkɪŋ/","a":"en-us-working.ogg","l":"work","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The workings of something is how it functions.","e":"He showed us the machine's inner workings."}]}]},"wooden":{"h":"wooden","i":"/ˈwʊdən/","a":"en-us-wooden.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A wooden object is made of wood.","e":"Please do not spill your drink on the wooden floor."},{"m":"A wooden movement is awkward or clumsy."}]}]},"clumsy":{"h":"clumsy","i":"/ˈklʌmzi/","a":"en-us-clumsy.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A clumsy person is not skillful or graceful when performing a movement.","e":"He is very clumsy. He might break the dishes."},{"m":"A clumsy object or idea is one created without much planning.","e":"This solution is clumsy. I do not think it will work."}]}]},"perform":{"h":"perform","i":"/pəˈfɔːm/","a":"en-us-perform.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you perform something, you do it.","e":"Please come help me perform this task."},{"m":"People perform by entertaining an audience.","e":"The actors are going to perform onstage soon."}]}]},"entertain":{"h":"entertain","i":"/ˌɛntəˈteɪn/","a":"en-us-entertain.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"You entertain a person by keeping that person interested in what you are doing.","e":"The comedian is able to entertain the audience for hours by telling jokes."},{"m":"When you entertain an idea, you think about it.","e":"I hope he will entertain the idea of inviting us over."}]}]},"yugoslavia":{"h":"Yugoslavia","i":"/juːɡəˈslɑːvi.ə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Yugoslavia.wav","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"(historical)Yugoslavia is a country that used to exist on the Balkan Peninsula. It has split up into Serbia, Montenegro, Republic of Macedonia, Bosnia and Herzegovina, Slovenia, Kosovo and Croatia."}]}]},"china":{"h":"China","i":"/ˈtʃaɪ.nə/","a":"en-us-china.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"China is a country in Asia. It is officially called the People's Republic of China."},{"m":"China is the area controlled by the People's Republic of China and the Republic of China (Taiwan)."}]}]},"funny":{"h":"funny","i":"/ˈfʌni/","a":"en-us-funny.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Funny things keep people interested and can make people laugh.","e":"That was a funny joke."},{"m":"Funny things are strange and unusual.","e":"This rotten milk has a funny smell."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A funny is a joke."}]}]},"amazing":{"h":"amazing","i":"/əˈmeɪzɪŋ/","a":"en-us-amazing.ogg","l":"amaze","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Amazing things cause wonder and amazement.","e":"That was an amazing book. I enjoyed every moment of it."}]}]},"hopeful":{"h":"hopeful","i":"/ˈhoʊpfəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-hopeful.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A hopeful person wishes that something could happen."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A hopeful is a person that wishes to win or be victorious at something.","e":"There are many presidential hopefuls this year."}]}]},"extraterrestrial":{"h":"extraterrestrial","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An extraterrestrial is a being coming from a world other than Earth, whose true existence has not yet been proved.","e":"Popular representations of extraterrestrials often make them be little skinny humanoids with a large skull, wide black eyes and a green or grey skin."},{"m":"(metaphorical) An extraterrestrial can also be so an uncommon person that ordinary people think he or she cannot be from Earth.","e":"Joseph von Neumann had so exceptional intellectual abilities that his neighbouring considered him an extraterrestrial."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Extraterrestrial can be applied to anything not coming from the Earth or not belonging to the Earth.","e":"Meteorites falling on the Earth's ground come from outer space: they are extraterrestrial objects."}]}]},"forest":{"h":"forest","i":"/ˈfɒrəst/","a":"en-us-forest.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A forest is an area covered with many trees, and sometimes by bushes and other plants.","e":"Certain forests are so vast that people can easily be lost there."}]}]},"arrive":{"h":"arrive","i":"/əˈraɪv/","a":"en-us-arrive.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you arrive somewhere, you come to that place, usually the place that you planned to go to.","e":"Is everything ready? I expect the guests to arrive soon."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something arrives somewhere, it comes to that place, usually the place that it was supposed to go to.","e":"Five days later a letter arrived by Federal Express."},{"m":"(intransitive) If a time or event arrives, it moves from the future into the present.","e":"Finally the day arrived for him to come home."}]}]},"mosquito":{"h":"mosquito","i":"/mɒsˈkiːtəʊ/","a":"en-uk-mosquito.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A mosquito is a flying insect that is known for stinging animals and humans to suck their blood.","e":"Sleeping here is nearly impossible because of all those mosquitoes that bite you all the night long."}]}]},"viper":{"h":"viper","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A viper is a short, rather massive poisonous snake with long front teeth that poison its victims by biting them.","e":"Don't walk in the bush unprotected, you may be bitten by an viper!"},{"m":"(pejorative, metaphorical) A viper can also be a person who says bad things on other people.","e":"This viper of a man will turn all of us mad!"},{"m":"Viper is a type of car model."}]}]},"boron":{"h":"boron","i":"/ˈbɔərɒn/","a":"en-us-boron.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A hard, black, or brown, chemical element with the atomic number 5 and the symbol B.","e":"The scientist used boron in his experiment."}]}]},"iodine":{"h":"iodine","i":"/ˈaɪ.əˌdaɪn, -dɪn, -diːn/","a":"en-us-iodine.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An element with the atomic number 53 and the symbol I.","e":"People use iodine in salt to make it iodized."},{"m":"A kind of antiseptic.","e":"That kid used iodine on his wound to prevent infection."}]}]},"robot":{"h":"robot","i":"/rəʊbɒt/","a":"en-us-robot.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A robot is a machine that looks more or less a human being.","e":"Starwars C-3PO is a golden robot."},{"m":"(countable) A robot can also be any man-made automatic device, resembling a human being or not.","e":"When you ask for the time on a phone, a robot will answer you."},{"m":"(metaphorical) A robot is a person who does not show emotions and seems to have no human thoughts.","e":"He has the same expression whatever happens to him: he is a true robot."}]}]},"radium":{"h":"radium","i":"/ˈreɪ.di.əm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-AcpoKrane-radium.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Radium is an element that has an atomic number of 88 and symbol Ra.","e":"A normal person cannot find radium in any store."}]}]},"calcium":{"h":"calcium","i":"/ˈkælsi.əm/","a":"en-us-calcium.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An element with atomic number 20 and symbol Ca. Also a nutrient in many different foods.","e":"The human body needs calcium in order to stay healthy."}]}]},"sodium":{"h":"sodium","i":"/ˈsəʊdɪəm/","a":"en-us-sodium.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A metal and element with the atomic number 11 and the symbol Na. Also used as a nutrient, preservative, and seasoning in food.","e":"It is pretty hard to find an item of food that doesn't contain sodium in it."}]}]},"master":{"h":"master","i":"/ˈmɑːstə/","a":"en-us-master.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A master is someone who controls something.","e":"She is the master of this domain."},{"m":"(countable) A master of a skill is very good at it.","e":"He is a master at sculpting humans."},{"m":"(uncountable) A degree awarded by a university.","e":"She holds a masters degree at Balliol College."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If a person masters something, they become very good at it; they are skilled at it.","e":"Through their courses, they will master the fine arts."}]}]},"sectors":{"h":"sectors","l":"sector","q":"noun"},"thinner":{"h":"thinner","i":"/ˈθɪnə(r)/","l":"thin","q":"adjective","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A thinner is a liquid that is used to make another liquid more thin.","e":"can be used as a thinner for oil-based paints."}]}]},"treats":{"h":"treats","a":"en-us-treats.ogg","l":"treat","q":"noun"},"drawings":{"h":"drawings","l":"drawing","q":"noun"},"sprinted":{"h":"sprinted","l":"sprint","q":"verb"},"flowers":{"h":"flowers","i":"/ˈflaʊəz/","a":"en-us-flowers.ogg","l":"flower","q":"noun"},"cherry":{"h":"cherry","i":"/ˈʧɐri/","a":"en-us-cherry.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cherry is a roundish small piece of fruit with a core inside. Its color varies from pale yellow to red or purple and even nearly black.","e":"We should eat our cherries quickly before birds get them all eaten!"},{"m":"(countable) By extension, cherry can also be the tree or the bush bearing this fruit."},{"m":"(uncountable) The wood of which a cherry tree is made of."},{"m":"(uncountable) Cherry is also the color of the fruit, bright red or purple.","e":"Cherry is a color that human eyes immediately remark."}]}]},"assemble":{"h":"assemble","i":"/əˈsɛmbl̩/","a":"en-us-assemble.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you assemble many people or things, you bring them together.","e":"They went into the meeting room where a dozen other people had already assembled."},{"m":"(transitive) If you assemble something, you put it together.","e":"He would have to go to Japan to find a company to supply parts and assemble the machine."}]}]},"skinny":{"h":"skinny","i":"/ˈskɪni/","a":"en-us-skinny.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A skinny person or animal has few flesh or muscle around the skeleton, he/she/it has a thin and narrow body.","e":"You should eat more and do some sports, you're too skinny!"}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A skinny is a person who has not enough flesh, enough muscle, whose body appears to be too thin and narrow.","e":"This skinny has lifted this heavy piece of furniture unaided! I couldn't believe my eyes!"}]}]},"tomato":{"h":"tomato","i":"/təˈmɑːtəʊ/","a":"en-uk-tomato.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A tomato is a red, roundish fruit, roughly the size of a fist. It does not have a core nor pips.","e":"Bad singers or musicians used to be thrown tomatoes at."},{"m":"(countable) A tomato is also the plant bearing tomatoes.","e":"Tomatoes were imported from Central America to Europe in the sixteenth century."},{"m":"(uncountable) The matter which tomatoes are made of.","e":"Ketchup sauce contains some amount of tomato."},{"m":"(uncountable) A reddish color, the color of a tomato.","e":"Tomato is a color that looks like oxygenated blood."},{"m":"A sexy woman."},{"m":"A stupid thing or person."}]}]},"uranium":{"h":"uranium","i":"/jʊˈreɪniəm/","a":"en-us-uranium.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Uranium is an element of the periodic table with atomic number 92. Its symbol is U.","e":"Uranium is the natural element with the biggest atomic core."},{"m":"(uncountable) Uranium is also the radioactive metal made of uranium atoms.","e":"Uranium has been increasingly used since the last six decades, its radioactive properties have found both military and civil uses."}]}]},"isotope":{"h":"isotope","i":"/ˈaɪ.sə.təʊp/","a":"En-us-isotope.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"; Isotopes are atomic cores belonging to the same element that have the same number of protons, but have a different number of neutrons.","e":"Uranium 235 and uranium 238 are isotopes of uranium."}]}]},"pulsar":{"h":"pulsar","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A pulsar is an extremely dense astronomical body more massive than our Sun but not larger than 20 kilometers in diameter, essentially composed of neutrons with an iron shell. This astronomical body pulsates at very regular intervals, from a few milliseconds to more than one second: its name is a portmanteau-word coming from pulsating star.","e":"When the first pulsar was detected, its pulsating period was so regular that scientists first believed it came from an extraterrestrial civilization."}]}]},"plutonium":{"h":"plutonium","i":"/pluːˈtoʊniəm/","a":"en-us-plutonium.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Plutonium is a man-made element of the periodic table, with atomic number 94 and symbol Pu.","e":"Along with neptunium, plutonium was the first man-made element to be created by bombarding uranium-238 cores with neutrons."},{"m":"(uncountable) Plutonium is also the radioactive metal made of plutonium atoms.","e":"Plutonium is a silvery and very dense metal, its toxicity makes it dangerous to manipulate."}]}]},"allotropy":{"h":"allotropy","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Allotropy is the property that certain elements have to get their atoms disposed in different structures.","e":"Carbon has two main forms: graphite and diamond, that are each characterized by a different atomic disposition. This is called allotropy."}]}]},"sack":{"h":"sack","i":"/sæk/","a":"en-us-sack.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sack is a bag used to hold things.","e":"She opened the brown paper sack and put the shopping in it."},{"m":"(uncountable) To sack is to plunder and pillage a captured town or city.","e":"The sack of Rome."},{"m":"The sack is a slang word for bed.","e":"I'm tired. I think I'll hit the sack and get some sleep."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If the company sacks you, they end your job; they fire you.","e":"Phil was sacked last week, and I think they will get rid of more people soon."},{"m":"To plunder or pillage a captured town or city.","e":"The barbarians sacked Rome."}]}]},"assure":{"h":"assure","i":"/əˈʃʊə/","a":"en-us-assure.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you assure somebody about something, you tell them not to worry because the thing you say is true.","e":"The doctor assured me that he would be OK."},{"m":"(transitive) If x assures that y happens, x makes it certain that y happens.","e":"You need to begin now to assure that the everything is ready in January."}]}]},"squeaky":{"h":"squeaky","i":"/ˈskwiːki/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-squeaky.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A squeaky sound is a sound that has a very high pitch.","e":"When sped up, people speaking get a funny squeaky voice."}]}]},"squeak":{"h":"squeak","i":"/skwiːk/","a":"en-us-squeak.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A squeak is a high-pitched sound that objects produce, especially when rubbing together.","e":"The squeak of this old door is so annoying!"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something squeaks it produces this kind of sound.","e":"His wheelchair is always squeaking when it moves."}]}]},"goose":{"h":"goose","i":"/'guːs/","a":"en-uk-goose.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A goose is a big flying bird looking like a duck, with a long neck and webbed feet. The color of its feathers is usually a mix of grey, black and/or white, certain individuals having a uniform color.","e":"Wild geese regularly fly over our house when they migrate to Southern countries."},{"m":"(countable) A goose is a silly person.","e":"Aunt Dreeda acts like a goose whenever a man comes to her front door."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To goose someone is to take him by surprise with a finger jab to the cleft of the buttocks that penetrates to the anus. The violated may be clothed or unclothed and usually reacts with a sudden, offended start.","e":"I was wearing only a jockstrap when a teammate goosed me in the locker room."}]}]},"galaxy":{"h":"galaxy","i":"/ˈɡaləksi/","a":"en-us-galaxy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A galaxy is a large astronomical structure containing several billions of stars and other astronomical bodies, looking like a more or less regular spiral with a thick core and thinner edges.","e":"The Milky Way is the galaxy where our Earth is located, it has about 200 billion stars."},{"m":"(special) The galaxy: the galaxy we live in, the Milky Way (very often employed with the definite article).","e":"Some science fiction writers imagine that mankind will one day settle an empire throughout the galaxy."}]}]},"millennium":{"h":"millennium","i":"/mɪˈlɛnɪəm/","a":"en-uk-millennium.oga","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A millennium is a period of time lasting one thousand years.","e":"Humanity invented the first writing systems a few millennia ago."}]}]},"teddy":{"h":"teddy","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A teddy is a stuffed toy that looks like an anthropomorphic animal.","e":"Though largely an adult, he still has a huge collection of teddies."},{"m":"A teddy is a type of underwear worn by women, similar to a basque."}]}]},"swarm":{"h":"swarm","i":"/swɔrm/","a":"en-us-swarm.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A swarm is a group of many insects, especially flying insects like bees, wasps or flies.","e":"He walked on a wasp nest and was attacked by the swarm."},{"m":"Less commonly, a swarm can also be a group of fish or birds.","e":"When attacked, sardinas group into compact swarms to protect themselves."},{"m":"A crowd of people or animals moving in a chaotic way."},{"m":"(metaphorical) A large collection of similar objects.","e":"By observing the sky with telescopes, astronomers can see swarms of stars."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) To move as a swarm.","e":"I felt disgusted when I saw all these flies swarming on this dead body."},{"m":"(intransitive) When there are to many insects in a place.","e":"Fire ants swarm in the Southern United States since man accidentally brought some with him by ship."},{"m":"(transitive) To fill a place as a swarm.","e":"Ants are swarming the kitchen since we let food accessible."},{"m":"(transitive) To overcome an enemy with number."}]}]},"attract":{"h":"attract","i":"/əˈtrækt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-attract.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If something attracts you, it makes you interested in it.","e":"She jumped up and down to attract attention."},{"m":"(transitive) If you are attracted to someone, you want to have a relationship with them, often a sexual relationship.","e":"Boys were mad about her, attracted by her good looks."},{"m":"(transitive) If x attracts y, x pull y to x.","e":"The city hoped the new roads would attract businesses."}]}]},"awkward":{"h":"awkward","i":"/ˈɔːkwəd/","a":"en-us-ne-awkward.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"An awkward person or animal is clumsy, lacks agility, dexterity or grace.","e":"He doesn't managed well when I try to juggle. He's still awkward."},{"m":"An awkward situation, event is an embarrassing situation, event.","e":"When I fell in front of everybody, I felt ridiculous. It was so awkward!"},{"m":"Awkward also means complicated.","e":"What an awkward device! I can't even imagine how it works."}]}]},"awkwardness":{"h":"awkwardness","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Awkwardness is the state of being awkward.","e":"The patient suffer awkwardness when walking."}]}]},"immortal":{"h":"immortal","a":"en-us-immortal.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An immortal is a being that lives forever and does not age or die.","e":"Though never dying, an immortal can still be killed in certain cases."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something or someone is immortal, it lives forever and never dies or disappears.","e":"In ancient Greek civilization, gods were believed to be immortal."}]}]},"immortality":{"h":"immortality","i":"/ˌɪmɔːˈtæləti/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-immortality.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Immortality is the condition of not dying or ageing.","e":"Jesus promised immortality after our death."}]}]},"paintball":{"h":"paintball","i":"/ˈpeɪntbɔːl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-paintball.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Paintball is a game where people shoot small balls filled with paint instead of bullets.","e":"You should get changed if you want to play paintball; I don't want to have more clothes to wash!"},{"m":"(countable) A paintball is a paint-filled ball that is used in the game of paintball."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you paintball someone, you shoot them with a paintball."},{"m":"If you paintball, you play the sport paintball."}]}]},"didgeridoo":{"h":"didgeridoo","i":"/ˌdɪdʒ.ər.iˈduː/","a":"en-us-didgeridoo.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable); (onomatopoeic), A didgeridoo is a long and straight, wooden wind instrument that Australian s traditionally use. Roughly the size of a man, it produces sound when you continuously blow into it.","e":"Didgeridoos often have drawings showing mythological elements of the Aboriginal culture or clanic symbols."}]}]},"mortal":{"h":"mortal","i":"/ˈmɔːtəl/","a":"en-us-mortal.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Someone or something that is mortal can age, be injured, die, or disappear.","e":"Even stars, though living millions or billions of years, are mortal."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mortal is a human being, as opposed to immortal beings such as gods or beings with supernatural powers.","e":"To ancient Greeks mortals were only toys in the hands of gods."}]}]},"mortality":{"h":"mortality","i":"/mɔrˈtælɪti/","a":"en-us-mortality.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Mortality is the condition of being able to die or disappear.","e":"When they begin aging, certain people become afraid of their mortality."}]}]},"clone":{"h":"clone","i":"/kloʊn/","a":"en-us-clone.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A clone is a living being produced from another being that is genetically identical to the first being.","e":"Ewe Dolly is known to be the first man-made clone."},{"m":"(informal) A clone is a copy or imitation of something, living or not.","e":"This counterfeiter has a lot of talent: the painting he has made is a perfect clone of the original one."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To clone is to make an identical copy of something, especially a living being.","e":"Cells usually reproduce by cloning themselves."}]}]},"counterfeiter":{"h":"counterfeiter","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A counterfeiter is a person who makes copies of things, copies that are considered false and not legal; a person who counterfeits.","e":"The police have arrested a gang of counterfeiters that made many false banknotes."}]}]},"edit":{"h":"edit","i":"/ˈɛdɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-edit.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you edit something, you change or move around words.","e":"You can edit pages on Simple English Wiktionary by clicking the button that says \"change this page\"."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An edit is a change in text or a document.","e":"Thank you for your edit to the page hello on the Simple English Wiktionary!"}]}]},"platinum":{"h":"platinum","i":"/ˈplætɪnəm/","a":"en-uk-platinum.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Platinum is an element of the periodic table with the atomic number 78. Its symbol is Pt."},{"m":"(uncountable) Platinum is also the silver-grey metal made of platinum atoms.","e":"With a density of 21,4, platinum is one of the densest materials known to Earth."},{"m":"(countable) Atom of the element platinum."},{"m":"(uncountable) Platinum is the silver-grey color of the metal."},{"m":"(countable); A platinum is a musical recording that has sold over one million copies (for singles), or two million (for albums)"}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something platinum has the silver-grey color of the metal.","e":"She has always had her strange platinum hair."}]}]},"barium":{"h":"barium","i":"/ˈbɛərɪəm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-barium.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An element with atomic number 56 and the symbol Ba.","e":"This rock has parts of barium on it."}]}]},"witherite":{"h":"witherite","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Witherite is a yellow-grey mineral. It is made of a form of barium.","e":"I would like that sample of witherite for my collection, please."}]}]},"helium":{"h":"helium","i":"/ˈhiːlɪəm/","a":"en-us-helium.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Helium is a colourless gas that has an atomic number of 2 and the symbol He.","e":"Sir, can you please fill my balloon up with helium, please?"}]}]},"aluminum":{"h":"aluminum","i":"/ə.ˈlu.mɪ̆.ˌnə̆m/","a":"en-uk-aluminum.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Aluminum is a metallic (meaning made of metal) element with an atomic number of 13 and the symbol Al.","e":"These cans are made from aluminum."}]}]},"notable":{"h":"notable","i":"/ˈnəʊtəbəl/","a":"en-us-notable.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A person or a thing is notable if the person or thing is famous, important, significant. It means that many people know about that person or thing; many things have been said or written about that person or thing.","e":"She is a notable writer: people in many different countries read her books."}]}]},"neon":{"h":"neon","i":"/ˈni.ɒn/","a":"en-us-neon.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Neon is an element with atomic number 10 and the symbol Ne.","e":"Neon is used in signs to make them glow."},{"m":"Neon is used to describe neon tetra fish.","e":"My mom and I went to the pet store to buy a neon tetra fish."}]}]},"formulae":{"h":"formulae","i":"/ˈfɔː(r)mjəˌli/","l":"formula","q":"noun"},"participations":{"h":"participations","l":"participation","q":"noun"},"vapor":{"h":"vapor","i":"/ˈveɪpə/","a":"en-us-vapor.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A vapor is a cloudy or other matter in the air, like mist, steam or fumes."},{"m":"(uncountable) Vapor is the gas of something that used to be liquid or solid.","e":"When you heat up water, vapor appears."}]}]},"reprise":{"h":"reprise","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The repeated appearance of an action."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To repeat or resume an action."}]}]},"award":{"h":"award","i":"/əˈwɔːd/","a":"en-us-award.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An award is something that you give to someone who has done something very well.","e":"Each year, Westinghouse announces the winners of its awards for the best high-school science projects."},{"m":"(countable) An award is money that a court decides should be given to somebody who has won a legal case.","e":"The lawyer often takes 10 to 30 percent of any awards of damages."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you award somebody something, you officially give it to them, usually because they have done something well.","e":"A total of $205,000 in prize money will be awarded, with $50,000 for the winner and $25,000 for second place."},{"m":"(transitive) If you award somebody something, you officially decide that somebody should receive money or a contract.","e":"The judge ruled that the company had no just cause for dismissing Morsi, and he was awarded damages."}]}]},"spanish":{"h":"Spanish","i":"/ˈspænɪʃ/","a":"en-us-Spanish.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Spanish is the language that is mainly spoken in Spain, Mexico, and many countries in Central and South America."},{"m":"(used as the collective plural) The Spanish are people native to Spain."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Of, from, or relating to Spain.","e":"I enjoy Spanish food."},{"m":"Of or relating to the Spanish language."}]}]},"astronomy":{"h":"astronomy","i":"/əˈstrɑnəˌmi/","a":"en-us-astronomy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The study of space and everything related to it, like stars, black holes, meteors, etc."}]}]},"mirror":{"h":"mirror","i":"/ˈmɪrə/","a":"en-us-mirror.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A very reflective surface which light can bounce off of.","e":"She kept staring at the mirror all day."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If something/someone mirrors something, then it is identical to it."}]}]},"password":{"h":"password","i":"/ˈpæswɜːrd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-password.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A secret code that is used to get access to something."}]}]},"mess":{"h":"mess","i":"/mɛs/","a":"en-us-mess.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mess is a dirty or untidy place or situation.","e":"Your room is such a mess! You're not leaving the house until you clean it up!"},{"m":"(countable) A mess is a chaotic, confused or troublesome state or situation.","e":"Look at the mess you've gotten us into now!"},{"m":"(countable) A mess is a number of people who eat together."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you mess, you take meals with a mess."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you mess, you eat with others."}]}]},"chaos":{"h":"chaos","i":"/ˈkeɪ.ɒs/","a":"en-us-chaos.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A chaos is a large abyss or chasm."},{"m":"(uncountable) Chaos is a state of disorder or confusion."}]}]},"organized":{"h":"organized","i":"/ˈɔrɡənaɪzd/","a":"en-us-organized.ogg","l":"organize","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is organized, it is in a state of order."}]}]},"experiment":{"h":"experiment","i":"/ɪkˈsper.ɪ.mənt/","a":"en-us-experiment.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A test that is done to prove something, to see if a guess is valid, or to do something that has not been tried before.","e":"The experiment will prove that water boils at 100°C."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) To do an experiment."}]}]},"youth":{"h":"youth","i":"/ju:θ/","a":"en-us-youth.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The quality or state of being young."},{"m":"(uncountable) The part of life after childhood."},{"m":"(countable) A young person."},{"m":"(uncountable) (usually plural) Young people, as a group."}]}]},"zoom":{"h":"zoom","i":"/zuːm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-zoom.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To move fast."},{"m":"To go up sharply."},{"m":"To change the focus of a zoom lens"},{"m":"To increase suddenly."}]}]},"joint":{"h":"joint","i":"/dʒɔɪnt/","a":"en-au-joint.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A place where two things meet but are still able to move."},{"m":"A place where two things join solidly."},{"m":"Any part of the body where two bones join, sometimes letting that part of the body to be bent or straightened."},{"m":"(carpentry) A way to join two pieces of wood together so that they interlock."},{"m":"A bar, restaurant, or nightclub.","e":"It was the kind of joint you wouldn't want your boss to see you in."},{"m":"; (always with 'the') prison; jail.","e":"I'm not breaking any more laws because I don't want to go back to the joint."},{"m":"(smoking); A marijuana cigarette.","e":"Let's smoke a joint and then go skateboarding."}]}]},"inch":{"h":"inch","i":"/ɪntʃ/","a":"en-us-inch.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A unit of length that is equal to 2.54 centimetres; there are 12 inches in a foot.","e":"My pencil is six inches long."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive); (followed by a preposition) To move very slowly in a direction.","e":"Fearful of falling, he inched along the window ledge."}]}]},"neighbor":{"h":"neighbor","i":"/'neɪbə/","a":"En-us-neighbour.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"American standard spelling of neighbour"}]}]},"backup":{"h":"backup","i":"/ˈbækˌʌp/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-backup.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A reserve or substitute."},{"m":"A secondary plan that can be used in case the first plan fails."}]}]},"identification":{"h":"identification","i":"/ɪˌdɛntɪfɪˈkeɪʃən/","a":"en-us-identification.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Identification is the process of a thing by seeing it, hearing it, and/or touching it.","e":"With finding new animals, the process of identification is a long and difficult one."}]}]},"locate":{"h":"locate","i":"/ləʊˈkeɪt/","a":"en-us-locate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you locate something you find it, you learn where it is.","e":"I need to locate the nearest gas station."},{"m":"If you locate something somewhere, you put it there.","e":"The city plans to locate the subway stop right across the street."}]}]},"wake":{"h":"wake","i":"/'weɪk/","a":"en-us-wake.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you wake up, you stop sleeping.","e":"I woke up early to catch the bus."},{"m":"(transitive) If someone or something wakes you up, they make you stop sleeping.","e":"Could you please wake Donald up?"}]}]},"diary":{"h":"diary","i":"/ˈdaɪəri/","a":"en-us-diary.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A diary is a journal that some people keep to write down what has happened on days during their lives.","e":"I have kept a diary ever since I was a little girl."}]}]},"firewall":{"h":"firewall","i":"/faɪə.wɔəɫ/","a":"en-us-firewall.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"software that can be installed or downloaded to protect the person's computer from viruses, spyware, malware, and other kinds of unwanted junk"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you firewall, you set up software to protect your electronic item from viruses."},{"m":"(transitive) If you firewall someone, you maintain social distance from a manipulative person to avoid manipulative or narcissistic abuse.","e":"She firewalled her narcissistic stepmother."}]}]},"bid":{"h":"bid","i":"/bɪd/","a":"en-us-bid.ogg","l":"bid","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bid is an offer to enter into a contract to buy something or to do some kind of job.","e":"He amazed the art world with his winning bid of nearly $54 million for Van Gogh's painting, Irises."},{"m":"(countable) A bid is an attempt to do something.","e":"He went back to teaching after his unsuccessful presidential bid in 1988."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you bid for something, you offer to enter into a contract to buy it or to do it.","e":"Microsoft bid $44.6 billion to acquire Yahoo."},{"m":"If you bid for something, you attempt to do or get it.","e":"Montesinos, decided not to bid for the new position."},{"m":"(transitive) If you bid someone a good day, evening, etc., you wish it to them in greeting.","e":"She bade farewell to her sister, Fannie, and to other relatives and friends."},{"m":"(transitive) If you bid someone (to) do something, you tell them to do it.","e":"Standing with her back to the open door, she bade him pass."}]}]},"aggressive":{"h":"aggressive","i":"/ʌˈgrɛs.ɪv/","a":"en-us-aggressive.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Making attacks or assaults that are not just."},{"m":"Aggressive describes an act of aggression.","e":"Yes, he was aggressive to her."}]}]},"rehearse":{"h":"rehearse","i":"[rɪˈhɜːs]","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-rehearse.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To repeat something.","e":"There's no need to rehearse that, we already know."},{"m":"To narrate or tell a story.","e":"The witness rehearsed the events."},{"m":"To practice by repeating something in private.","e":"The band rehearsed before the show."}]}]},"unobtainium":{"h":"unobtainium","i":"/ˌʌn.əbˈteɪ.ni.əm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-unobtanium.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Unobtainium is a fictional material that has extraordinary and is considered very difficult, maybe even impossible, to obtain.","e":"Science-fiction works have a lot of devices that could not even exist if they were not made of unobtainium!"}]}]},"tonne":{"h":"tonne","i":"/tʌn/","a":"en-us-tonne.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A tonne, also called a metric ton, is an unit of mass that weighs exactly 1,000 kilograms. It is a little different from the US short ton (2,000 pounds or about 907 kilograms) and the British long ton (2,240 pounds or about 1,016 kilograms)."}]}]},"ton":{"h":"ton","i":"/tʌn/","a":"en-us-ton.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A ton is a metric unit of weight that as three main values: the international metric ton that is exactly 1,000 kilograms, the short ton used in Northern America that is 2,000 pounds (about 907 kilograms), and the long ton used in United Kingdom that is 2,240 pounds or about 1016 kilograms."},{"m":"(informal) (often plural) A ton is also a great amount of something, or many things.","e":"Today I have tons of things to do: how discouraging!"}]}]},"terse":{"h":"terse","i":"/tɜːs/","a":"en-au-terse.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A terse reply or message uses very few words to say only the most important information.","e":"He gave a terse, one-word answer."}]}]},"encryption":{"h":"encryption","i":"/ɪŋˈkrɪpʃ(ə)n/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-encryption.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A way to make a message look like a lot of random letters by a message with an.","e":"In many wars, soldiers often use encryption to make sure their messages aren't read by their."}]}]},"define":{"h":"define","i":"/dɪˈfaɪn/","a":"en-us-define.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you define a word, you state exactly what the word means.","e":"The dictionary defines the word \"define\" as \"to state exactly what a word means\"."}]}]},"gegenschein":{"h":"gegenschein","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-gegenschein.wav","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"A faint glow that can be seen on the opposite side of the sky where the sun is, due to dust and debris around that position."}]}]},"showoff":{"h":"showoff","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A person trying to show prowess or ability.","e":"They were a showoff."}]}]},"bind":{"h":"bind","i":"/bʌɪnd/","a":"en-us-bind.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you bind something put rope or string around it, often many times.","e":"She tied the rope around their hands, binding them tightly together."},{"m":"(transitive) If something binds two people or things, it connects them.","e":"Now that he couldn't walk, he was bound to his nurse."},{"m":"(transitive), If someone is bound by a rule, promise, etc., they must not break it.","e":"The media are not bound by the same rules that govern lawyers."},{"m":"If two things bind, they stick together.","e":"Carbon binds with oxygen to form carbon dioxide."},{"m":"(transitive) If you bind a book, you put it together so the pages stay together."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bind is a difficult position or situation.","e":"I've lost my job and I'm in a terrible bind."}]}]},"zodiac":{"h":"zodiac","i":"/ˈzəʊ.dɪ.æk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-zodiac.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A belt-like area of the sky that the Sun, Moon, and the planets pass through; it extends about eight degrees north and south of the ecliptic, and is divided into 12 equal parts which are each named after a constellation."},{"m":"(uncountable) The 12 signs, or houses, of the zodiac. Each sign is named after one of the constellations in the zodiac.","e":"My zodiac constellation is Gemini."},{"m":"(countable) A circle decorated with the signs of the zodiac.","e":"My friend has a tattoo of a zodiac."}]}]},"customers":{"h":"customers","l":"customer","q":"noun"},"atom":{"h":"atom","i":"/ˈætəm/","a":"en-us-atom.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An atom is the smallest bit that matter can be broken down into.","e":"Atoms of hydrogen make up a water molecule."},{"m":"(countable) A particle which is made up of protons, neutrons, and electrons."}]}]},"density":{"h":"density","i":"/ˈdɛn.sɪ.ti/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-density.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Density is how much stuff fits in a particular area.","e":"The population density of Singapore is one of the highest in the world."},{"m":"(uncountable) The density of a material is how closely packed its atoms are.","e":"The density of water is higher than the density of steam."}]}]},"arson":{"h":"arson","i":"/ˈɑrsən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-arson.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Arson is the crime of setting a fire to cause damage.","e":"A man is being held by police in connection with an arson attack that destroyed a school."},{"m":"(countable) An arson is an act of arson.","e":"The cause of the fire is unknown, but investigators believe it to be an arson."}]}]},"arsonist":{"h":"arsonist","i":"/ˈɑrsənəst/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-arsonist.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An arsonist is a person who sets fire to cause damage, especially in buildings or forests.","e":"Forest fires are often caused by arsonists, but they are difficult to arrest."}]}]},"gibberish":{"h":"gibberish","i":"/ˈdʒɪb.ə.rɪʃ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-gibberish.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable); (onomatopoeic) Gibberish is a language that is not understandable, because it has no meaning or is too complicated or technical.","e":"Extraterrestrials in bad science-fiction often speak gibberish to make you understand that they are extraterrestrials."}]}]},"gibber":{"h":"gibber","i":"/ˈdʒɪbə(r)/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-gibber.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(onomatopoeic) To gibber is to speak in a way you that cannot be understood, especially when using unknown words or known words that have no meaning put together.","e":"This magician gibbers when he does his tricks, because he wants to appear more mysterious."}]}]},"tosh":{"h":"tosh","i":"/tɒʃ/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Tosh is stupid nonsense, usually made intentionally so that no one can understand.","e":"He always writes tosh on Wikipedia because he thinks it's funny, but in fact he's just blocked."}]}]},"tuxedo":{"h":"tuxedo","i":"/tʌkˈsiːdəʊ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-tuxedo.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (US) A tuxedo is black jacket that men wear in formal occasions."},{"m":"(countable) A tuxedo is also the whole upper suit that includes this jacket, with a white shirt and a black bowtie.","e":"In official receptions men always wear tuxedoes."}]}]},"wizard":{"h":"wizard","i":"/ˈwɪzəd/","a":"en-us-wizard.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A person who uses magic, who has magical powers.","e":"Wizards use magic to cast spells."},{"m":"(countable) (metaphorical) A person who is very talented in one area or more.","e":"That guy is a wizard at problem-solving!"},{"m":"(countable) (metaphorical) A computer program that operations for users that have little or no experience in computing.","e":"To install this drawing program, we had to use the install wizard to set the program up on the computer."}]}]},"creepy-crawly":{"h":"creepy-crawly","a":"EN-AU ck1 creepy-crawly.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(informal) A creepy-crawly is a small animal that crawls, such as an insect, spider, or worm; this word describes the way these animals move.","e":"While most people are disgusted by creepy-crawlies, some find them interesting."}]}]},"creep":{"h":"creep","i":"/kriːp/","a":"en-us-creep.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"When an animal moves with its belly close to the ground.","e":"The creep of the snake makes it frightening."},{"m":"Small movement of an object."},{"m":"Small and progressive changes of a measure.","e":"Few people noticed the creep of the prices this year."},{"m":"(informal) A very annoying person who makes you nervous.","e":"Stop staring at me all the time, you creep!"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) An animal creeps when it moves with its belly close to the ground.","e":"Snakes and lizards creep."},{"m":"(intransitive) A plant creeps when it grows close to the ground or stuck to a wall, instead of growing upwards."},{"m":"(intransitive) To move slowly and quietly in a particular direction, like a snake can move."},{"m":"(intransitive) To change slowly and gradually.","e":"When prices creep, some people do not immediately notice the changes."}]}]},"replicator":{"h":"replicator","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A replicator is a device or a structure that can make copies of itself.","e":"Genes are natural replicators."},{"m":"A replicator is also a (fictional) man-made device that can make copies of itself, or transform matter to build any object or structure, living or not.","e":"Replicators still belong to science-fiction nowadays, but could exist one day thanks to technological progress."}]}]},"cyborg":{"h":"cyborg","i":"/ˈsaɪ.bɔː(r)ɡ/","a":"en-us-cyborg.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(science fiction) Mixing of cybernetic and organism, a cyborg is a being, usually human, that has an important part of mechanical/robotic devices in his or her body. He or she still has an organic brain, contrary to a robot."},{"m":"(science fiction) A true robot that has a relation with organic life, such as looking like a normal human being or having a human soul inside.","e":"Terminator is a cyborg."}]}]},"gift":{"h":"gift","i":"/ɡɪft/","a":"en-us-gift.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A gift is something given to another person voluntarily.","e":"I didn't receive many gifts this Christmas."},{"m":"A special talent or natural ability.","e":"She has a gift for singing."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) A gift is given to someone as a present.","e":"I received a gift from my parents as my Christmas present."}]}]},"cube":{"h":"cube","i":"/kjuːb/","a":"en-us-cube.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cube is a shape that has six square faces of the same size."},{"m":"(countable) A cube is also a solid object that has more or less this shape.","e":"I usually take two sugar cubes with my coffee."},{"m":"(countable) (arithmetic) The cube of a number n is this number multiplied three times by itself. Its symbol is n3.","e":"The cube of 3 is 27, also written 33 = 27."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(arithmetic) To cube a number is multiplying this number three times by itself.","e":"3 cubed is 27."},{"m":"To give something the shape of a cube."},{"m":"(especially cooking) To cut something into cubes.","e":"To cube the meat."}]}]},"semicolon":{"h":"semicolon","i":"/ˌsɛmiˈkəʊlən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-semicolon.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A semicolon is the sign; used to mark a pause longer than the comma (,) but shorter than the period (.).","e":"A space is needed after the semicolon."}]}]},"fail":{"h":"fail","i":"/feɪl/","a":"en-us-fail.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To not achieve a goal, or to go wrong.","e":"The event is going to fail."}]}]},"acronym":{"h":"acronym","i":"/ˈæk.rə.nɪm/","a":"en-uk-acronym.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An acronym is an abbreviation usually made by the first letters of a series of words, and which is itself said as a word","e":"RAM, radar and scuba are acronyms."}]}]},"identifications":{"h":"identifications","l":"identification","q":"noun"},"chord":{"h":"chord","i":"/kɔː(r)d/","a":"en-us-cord.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A chord is made of several notes together, usually three or four.","e":"Some singers accompany themselves on guitar by playing chords."},{"m":"(various uses) A chord is a straight line, that can be material or an abstract line linking two points together."}]}]},"offline":{"h":"offline","i":"/ɒfˈlaɪn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-offline.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a system is offline, it is not connected (generally electronically) to a larger network."},{"m":"If a machine is offline, it is not powered on.","e":"The printer is offline for a few minutes while it starts up."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"While offline."}]}]},"gifts":{"h":"gifts","a":"en-us-gifts.ogg","l":"gift","q":"noun"},"gain":{"h":"gain","i":"/geɪn/","a":"en-us-gain.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A gain is the act of getting something.","e":"You have nothing to gain."},{"m":"What one gains, as a return on investment or dividend.","e":"No pain, no gain."},{"m":"The factor by which a signal is multiplied."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"You gain something by getting or receiving it."}]}]},"totals":{"h":"totals","l":"total","q":"noun"},"blind":{"h":"blind","i":"/blaɪnd/","a":"en-us-blind.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"(not comparable) If someone or something is blind, they can't see.","e":"I'm not totally blind. I can see a little."},{"m":"(comparable) If someone or something is blind, they can't see the truth about something.","e":"How can you be so blind about your problems?"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If someone is blinded, they become unable to see.","e":"The light was so bright that for a moment he was blinded."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A covering for a window to keep out light. The covering may be made of cloth or of narrow slats that can block light or allow it to pass."},{"m":"Any device intended to conceal or hide; as, a duck blind."},{"m":"In poker a forced bet.","e":"The player was in the big blind."},{"m":"An 1800s baseball term meaning no score."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Without seeing; unseeingly."},{"m":"In, without looking at the cards dealt."}]}]},"blame":{"h":"blame","i":"/bleɪm/","a":"en-us-blame.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you blame someone or something for something bad, you say or think that they are the reason for or cause of it.","e":"It's not your fault... don't blame yourself."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The blame for something bad is the idea that you made or let it happen.","e":"You keep your mouth shut and I'll take the blame."}]}]},"weekend":{"h":"weekend","i":"/wiːˈkɛnd/","a":"en-us-weekend.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The end of the working week, usually Saturday and Sunday.","e":"I do not have work on the weekend."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you weekend somewhere, you stay there just for the weekend.","e":"We'll weekend at the beach."}]}]},"bless":{"h":"bless","i":"/blɛs/","a":"en-us-bless.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) You say, bless you when someone sneezes."},{"m":"(transitive) You say, bless you, him, her, etc. when that person has done something nice."},{"m":"(transitive) If you are blessed with an ability or something, you are lucky to have it."},{"m":"(transitive) If God blesses something, he gives it special attention and takes care of it."}]}]},"salmon":{"h":"salmon","i":"/ˈsæmən/","a":"en-us-salmon.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A fish, usually with pink or grey skin."},{"m":"The meat of a salmon fish."},{"m":"(uncountable) A yellowish pink colour, the colour of cooked salmon."}]}]},"parr":{"h":"parr","i":"/pɑː/","a":"en-us-par.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A parr is a young salmon fish, more mature than a fry."}]}]},"alevin":{"h":"alevin","i":"/ˈæl.ə.vən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-alevin.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An alevin is a young salmon fish who has just hatched."}]}]},"smolt":{"h":"smolt","i":"/smoʊlt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-smolt.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A young salmon fish, just before becoming an adult which breeds."}]}]},"everyone":{"h":"everyone","i":"/ˈɛv.ri.wʌn/","a":"en-us-everyone.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"All (the) people; every person."}]}]},"everybody":{"h":"everybody","i":"/ˈɛvriˌbɒdi/","a":"en-us-everybody.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"All (the) people."}]}]},"dildo":{"h":"dildo","i":"/ˈdɪldəʊ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-dildo.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A dildo is a device shaped like a penis that is used for masturbation and sex."},{"m":"(countable) A dildo is a person who is foolish."}]}]},"salmonid":{"h":"salmonid","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A group of fish similar to a salmon or a trout."}]}]},"bloom":{"h":"bloom","i":"/bluːm/","a":"en-us-bloom.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bloom is a flower.","e":"The seeds you plant in the spring will give blooms from summer through fall."},{"m":"(uncountable) If something is in bloom, its flowers are open or it is reaching a state of fullness.","e":"The weather is warming and spring flowers are coming into bloom."},{"m":"(uncountable) The bloom is the best time or a look of freshness or fullness.","e":"The bloom is off their love."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If something such as a flower blooms, it opens, or is reaching a state of fullness.","e":"The blue sky was the color of the sea, and flowers were blooming in the fields."}]}]},"peoples":{"h":"peoples","l":"people","q":"noun"},"bomb":{"h":"bomb","i":"/bɒm/","a":"en-us-bomb.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bomb is a weapon that explodes.","e":"The man killed himself and eight others by a very powerful bomb."},{"m":"(countable) If something, often a movie or a concert, was a bomb, it was very unsuccessful.","e":"The first computer was a bomb, but IBM improved it and the new machine sold very well."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you bomb a place, you drop or put one or more bombs there.","e":"This woman's mother and son were killed when American planes bombed the village."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you bomb somewhere, you go there at high speed.","e":"They walked up the mountain with their bikes and then bombed down as fast as they could go."},{"m":"If you bomb a test, course, etc., you get a very low grade on it."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something, often a movie or a concert, bombs, it is very unsuccessful.","e":"The show bombed in London as well as flopping on Broadway."}]}]},"booking":{"h":"booking","i":"/ˈbʊkɪŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-booking.wav","l":"book","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A booking is an agreement between you and a business such as a hotel or airline to use their services on a particular date.","e":"If you need to cancel your booking, you must advise the hotel before Aug. 22."},{"m":"(countable) A booking is an planned performance.","e":"The band has a number of bookings in Toronto this summer."}]}]},"boss":{"h":"boss","i":"/bɒs/","a":"en-us-boss.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Your boss is the person who tells you what to do at work.","e":"My former boss was very happy for the chance to fire me."},{"m":"(countable) A boss is a leader in an organisation.","e":"The Mayor was an old-style political boss who made his own decisions."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you boss somebody around/about, you tell them what to do, especially when you don't have any special power to do so.","e":"This was just another occasion when Indians were bossed around by white people."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is boss, it is very good."}]}]},"magician":{"h":"magician","i":"/məˈʤɪʃən/","a":"en-us-magician.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (fantasy) A magician is a man who uses magic, who has magical or mystical powers."},{"m":"(countable) A magician is a person who does things that seem magical, but that are in fact tricks.","e":"Magicians do not want reveal their secrets because their shows would become less interesting and mysterious since everybody could understand what happens."},{"m":"(countable) (metaphorical) A magician is a very skilled person, in one area or more."},{"m":"(countable) A person who is mysterious."}]}]},"boundary":{"h":"boundary","i":"/baʊndri/","a":"en-us-boundary.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A boundary is the line around something's outside edge.","e":"The elephants have to live within the boundary of the park or risk being shot."}]}]},"hamster":{"h":"hamster","i":"/'hæmstəɽ/","a":"en-uk-hamster.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hamster is a furry rodent a little larger than a mouse and with a very short tail. They are popular as pets."}]}]},"rural":{"h":"rural","i":"/ˈrʊrəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Back ache-Rural.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is rural, it is related to the country and is not of the city."},{"m":"If a place is rural, it is far from any city."},{"m":"If a person is rural, it means they live away from the city."}]}]},"countryman":{"h":"countryman","i":"/ˈkʌntrimən/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Your countrymen are people who come from the same country (nation) that you are from.","e":"My fellow Americans are my countrymen."}]}]},"countrymen":{"h":"countrymen","l":"countryman","q":"noun"},"wilderness":{"h":"wilderness","i":"/ˈwɪldənɪs/","a":"en-us-wilderness.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Places that are far from or farms; usually places where no people live.","e":"We were hunting deer in the wilderness."}]}]},"impossible":{"h":"impossible","i":"/ɪmˈpɒsəbl/","a":"en-us-impossible.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is impossible it cannot happen or cannot be done.","e":"It is impossible for people to breathe water."},{"m":"If a person is impossible they refuse to agree or to be peaceful.","e":"No point arguing with you! You're just impossible!"}]}]},"tricks":{"h":"tricks","a":"en-us-tricks.ogg","l":"trick","q":"verb"},"magical":{"h":"magical","i":"/ˈmædʒɪkəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-magical.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is magical is related to magic.","e":"Sorcerers have magical objects besides their own powers."},{"m":"(metaphorical) Something magical is also something so unusual that it appears to be caused by magic.","e":"This landscape is so beautiful! It has something magical."}]}]},"fireman":{"h":"fireman","i":"/ˈfaɪrmən/","a":"en-uk-fireman.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A fireman is a person whose job is to fight fires and stops them. It can be used for men or both sexes.","e":"Firemen often use red trucks to make them easily recognizable."},{"m":"(countable) A fireman is the person who puts coal in the fire of a steam engine on a train."}]}]},"firewoman":{"h":"firewoman","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A firewoman is a woman whose job is to fight fires and extinguish them. This word was created when woman began to do this job and not only men.","e":"The firewoman sprayed the house with the fire hose."}]}]},"firefighter":{"h":"firefighter","i":"/ˈfaɪə(r)ˌfaɪ.tə(r)/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A firefighter is a person whose job is to fight fires and put them out."}]}]},"keyboard":{"h":"keyboard","i":"/ˈkiːbɔːd/","a":"en-us-keyboard.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A keyboard is a range of black and white keys (buttons) on a musical instrument.","e":"Pianos, organs, harpsicords and some accordions have keyboards."},{"m":"(countable) (typing) A keyboard is also a set of square or rectangular buttons on a typewriter or a computer.","e":"Almost everybody has to use a keyboard in everyday life nowadays."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To keyboard is to type on a computer keyboard.","e":"Everyday life in an office usually consists in keyboarding."}]}]},"bowl":{"h":"bowl","i":"/bəʊl/","a":"en-us-bowl.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bowl is a deep dish.","e":"In large mixing bowl, stir together flours, baking powder, and salt until thoroughly combined."},{"m":"(countable) The bowl is the part of an object that looks like a bowl.","e":"When's the last time you cleaned the toilet bowl?"},{"m":"(countable) An important American football game played outside the regular season is sometimes called the ~ bowl.","e":"These two teams will head to the Super Bowl to decide the champion."},{"m":"(countable) A stadium is sometimes called the ~ bowl.","e":"Every Tuesday and Thursday evening, you can hear the finest classical music at the Hollywood Bowl."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you bowl, you roll a ball along the ground or floor as part of a game."},{"m":"If you bowl in cricket, you throw the ball at the batsman."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you are bowling along, down, etc., you are moving very fast.","e":"We were bowling down the hill when we hit a tree."},{"m":"If you bowl somebody over, you hit them when you are running and make them fall down."}]}]},"bracket":{"h":"bracket","i":"/ˈbrækɪt/","a":"en-us-bracket.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A tax, income, or age bracket is a set of values with a bottom limit and a top limit or a group of people who fit between the limits.","e":"In the 25 to 29 age bracket, 43 percent of men and 29 percent of women had never married."},{"m":"(countable) (usually plural) A bracket is a punctuation mark used to set off extra information. The basic shape is round, like this: ( ), but the following are also brackets: [ ], { },.","e":"Weight is given in kilograms, while numbers in brackets show weight in pounds."},{"m":"(countable) A bracket is one of a wide variety of pieces, usually metal, wood, or plastic that are used to support or connect machines or materials. Commonly brackets are L-shaped."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If x is bracketed by y, x is between y.","e":"Her desk was bracketed by bookcases."},{"m":"(transitive) If two things are bracketed together, they are put together in the same group."}]}]},"technobabble":{"h":"technobabble","i":"/ˈtɛknəʊbæbəl/","a":"en-us-technobabble.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) (informal) Technobabble is a language that appears very technical or scientific, but that has in fact little or no meaning at all.","e":"Science-fiction often uses technobabble to speak about advanced technologies or non-existent physical phenomena."}]}]},"broad":{"h":"broad","i":"/brɔːd/","a":"en-us-broad.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is broad, the distance from one side to the other is large.","e":"Her shoulders were swimmer's shoulders, strong and broad."},{"m":"If something is broad, it includes a lot.","e":"They have laws now which give very, very broad powers to the President."},{"m":"Broad senses, definitions, agreements, etc. are general, not detailed.","e":"We accept a broad definition of music to include any sound organized in an meaningful way."},{"m":"A broad area is a large area.","e":"They walked through the broad field behind the building."},{"m":"A broad accent is one that is very noticeable."},{"m":"If something happens in broad daylight, it happens during the day where many people can see it."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A broad is a woman.","e":"There's this German broad, fuckin' bitch, who told me I'm going to jail for her pushin' her stupid ass."}]}]},"illegal":{"h":"illegal","i":"/ɪˈliːɡəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-illegal.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"An illegal act or object is one that does not follow the law.","e":"This drug is illegal in that country. If you are caught with it, you will be arrested."}]}]},"swamp":{"h":"swamp","i":"/swɒmp/","a":"en-us-swamp.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A swamp is an area where most of the land is underwater. Land in a swamp is not usually more than a meter (or a few feet) under water.","e":"We were wading through the swamp."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something is swamped it is being covered of filled with water.","e":"The deck of our boat was swamped by the storm."},{"m":"If something is swamped is has gotten more of something than it can work with.","e":"Our office was swamped with phone calls."}]}]},"meter":{"h":"meter","i":"/ˈmiːtə(r)/","a":"en-us-meter.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A length; 100 centimeters.","e":"This table is 2 meters wide."},{"m":"The rhythm of a poem."}]}]},"brochure":{"h":"brochure","a":"en-us-brochure.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A brochure is a small book, often just a few pages, explaining or advertising something.","e":"For more information, pick up our free self-help brochure called \"Gum Disease\"."}]}]},"bugger":{"h":"bugger","i":"/ˈbʌɡɚ/","a":"en-uk-bugger.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bugger is a person you don't like.","e":"He was wearing his hat in church, so I yelled, \"Take your hat off, you silly bugger."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) You say \"bugger it\" to show that you are very angry or that you don't care."},{"m":"(transitive) You say \"bugger me\" or \"I'm buggered\" to show that you're very surprised."},{"m":"(transitive); If you bugger somebody, you have anal sex with them."},{"m":"(intransitive) You say \"bugger off\" you want someone to leave you alone."},{"m":"If you bugger something up, you make a problem with it."}]}]},"cabinet":{"h":"cabinet","i":"/ˈkæ.bɪ.nɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-cabinet.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A country's cabinet is the main group of politicians who work closely with the leader of the government.","e":"Nearly all the cabinet ministers in Prime Minister Binyamin Netanyahu's coalition government are immigrants or the sons of immigrants."},{"m":"(countable) A cabinet is a piece of furniture used to keep things in.","e":"He walked over to the filing cabinet, took out the file and put it on his desk."}]}]},"calculate":{"h":"calculate","i":"/kæɫkjuːleɪt/","a":"en-us-calculate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you calculate something, you find its value, usually by using mathematics.","e":"These scores were calculated by subtracting total errors from total correct."},{"m":"(transitive) If you calculate something, you find the answer by thinking about the facts.","e":"The leaders seems to have calculated that the political benefit outweighs the cost to their people."},{"m":"(transitive) If something is calculated to do something, you hope or expect it to do it.","e":"She waved her hands around in a way calculated to make him laugh."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you calculate on something, you plan on it or expect it.","e":"He hadn't calculated on her being late."}]}]},"scissor":{"h":"scissor","i":"/ˈsɪzə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-scissor.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The singular form of scissors."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To scissor means to cut using scissors."},{"m":"To scissor means to remove from text."}]}]},"campaign":{"h":"campaign","i":"/kæm'peɪn/","a":"en-us-campaign.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A campaign is a group of activities working towards a particular goal, often to elect a political candidate or in a war.","e":"Angry TV viewers did launch a letter-writing campaign against CBS's decision to cancel the show."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you are campaigning, you are working in an organized way with a goal."}]}]},"cancel":{"h":"cancel","i":"/ˈkænsl̩/","a":"en-au-cancel.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you cancel something that was going to happen, you decide that it will not happen.","e":"Her father had cancelled his trip to Canandaigua because of the weather."}]}]},"assassin":{"h":"assassin","i":"/ǝ'sæsın/","a":"en-uk-assassin.oga","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An assassin is a person who kills a famous or important person, usually for political reasons or for money.","e":"is believed to be the assassin of President."}]}]},"scared":{"h":"scared","i":"/skɛəd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Back ache-scared.wav","l":"scare","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"To be scared of someone or something means to be afraid of someone or something; to have a fear of someone or something.","e":"I'm scared of monsters."}]}]},"debut":{"h":"debut","i":"/ˈdɛbjuː/","a":"en-us-debut.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Debut is a person's first time doing something in public.","e":"I made my theatrical debut in a production of \"The King and I\" many years ago."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive); (mostly US) To appear or do something for the first time, as to the public.","e":"The new baseball player debuted in September of 2008."}]}]},"candidate":{"h":"candidate","i":"/ˈkæn.dɪdət/","a":"en-us-candidate.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A candidate is one person or thing that may be chosen, especially in an election.","e":"The three presidential candidates will be interviewed on TV tonight."}]}]},"career":{"h":"career","i":"/kəˈrɪr/","a":"en-us-career.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A career is a job or a series of related jobs that you do for many years.","e":"His pro coaching career spans 23 years, including time with the 49ers (1967–73 and' 77), the Browns (1978–80), the Oilers (1981–82), the Cowboys (1983–85) and the Cardinals (1986–89)."}]}]},"carpet":{"h":"carpet","i":"/ˈcɑrpɪt/","a":"en-us-carpet.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A carpet is a floor covering, usually made of nylon or wool.","e":"He walked in with his boots leaving snow on the carpet."},{"m":"(countable) A carpet of something is a thick layer of it.","e":"A carpet of snow lay on the ground."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If a floor or room is carpeted, it has carpets on the floor."},{"m":"(transitive) If something carpets a place, it covers the ground.","e":"The road was carpeted with broken glass."}]}]},"cash":{"h":"cash","i":"/kæʃ/","a":"en-us-cash.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Cash is money in the form of bills and coins, rather than checks/cheques or credit cards.","e":"The publisher supplied cash prizes and books for the winning essays written by fourth through sixth graders."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To exchange a check/cheque for money in the form of bills.","e":"I need to stop at the back to cash my paycheck before we go out to dinner."}]}]},"remarkable":{"h":"remarkable","i":"/rɪˈmɑrkəbl̩/","a":"en-us-remarkable.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something worth noticing; not common; extraordinary.","e":"It's remarkable that many mothers don't breastfeed their children, despite the evidence that it is good for babies to breastfeed."}]}]},"ridiculous":{"h":"ridiculous","i":"/rɪˈdɪkjʊləs/","a":"en-us-ridiculous.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Describes something that deserves ridicule, is foolish or absurd","e":"Adam's mohawk is ridiculous."}]}]},"lend":{"h":"lend","i":"/lɛnd/","a":"en-us-lend.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you lend something to another person, you let them use it, after which they must return it to you.","e":"I lent my textbook to Jack to allow him to study from it."},{"m":"(transitive) If x lends y support, believability, acceptance, etc., x gives it to y.","e":"Several studies in recent years have lent support to this idea."},{"m":"(transitive) If you lend a hand, you help.","e":"We're moving house next week and we were hoping you could lend us a hand."}]}]},"presidential":{"h":"presidential","i":"/prɛzɪˈdɛnʃ(ə)l/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Back ache-Presidential.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Related to the president.","e":"Bush won the 2004 U.S. presidential election."},{"m":"If somebody is presidential, they seem or act like a president.","e":"Dan Quayle didn't appear very presidential."}]}]},"cast":{"h":"cast","i":"/kɑːst/","a":"en-us-cast.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If x casts light or shadow on y, x causes y to be lit or in shadow.","e":"The street light outside my window cast shadows on the wall."},{"m":"(transitive) If you cast light on an idea or problem, you make it clearer by giving more information about it.","e":"Our research casts new light on the connection between temperature and plant growth."},{"m":"(transitive) If you cast doubt on something, you make make people less likely to believe it.","e":"The video casts doubt on the story told by police."},{"m":"If you cast a look, glance, you look quickly.","e":"She cast about for her pen."},{"m":"(transitive) If you cast a vote, you vote in an election.","e":"I've decided to cast my vote for the Democratic Party."},{"m":"(transitive) If you cast metal, plastic, etc., you make an object by applying wet or melted material to another material and waiting for it to harden."},{"m":"(transitive) If you cast somebody in a part in a play, movie, etc., you choose them to play that part."},{"m":"(transitive) If you cast something somewhere, you throw it there."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The cast of a play, movie, or show are all the people who act in it.","e":"The director has brought back many of the cast and crew of the earlier movie."},{"m":"(countable) The cast of characters is the complete list of characters."},{"m":"(countable) A cast is a hard protective covering on part of your body that has been seriously hurt or broken."},{"m":"(countable) A cast is a shape made by applying wet or melted material to another material and waiting for it to harden."},{"m":"(countable) A cast is a throw, especially in fishing when you throw your line out."}]}]},"piecemeal":{"h":"piecemeal","i":"/ˈpiːs.miːl/","a":"en-us-piecemeal.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Made or done piece by piece, or occurring slowly."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"ly, slowly, bit by bit; into pieces, into fragments."}]}]},"celebrate":{"h":"celebrate","i":"/ˈsɛl.ɪ.breɪt/","a":"en-us-celebrate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you celebrate something, you do something special to show that you are happy about it.","e":"The town celebrates its 200th anniversary this Saturday by launching 20,000 balloons."},{"m":"(transitive) When you celebrate something, you perform or participate in it, usually a sacrament or solemn rite.","e":"The Christians gathered together to celebrate a mass."}]}]},"cell":{"h":"cell","i":"/sɛl/","a":"en-us-cell.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cell is a room in a jail where prisoners are kept.","e":"He was arrested and kept in a small cell for one day."},{"m":"(countable) A cell is a unit of a living organism.","e":"A plant cell has a cell wall."}]}]},"india":{"h":"India","i":"/ˈɪndiə/","a":"en-us-India.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"A country in South Asia, also known as Bharat. Its full official name is the Republic of India.","e":"In 1947, The British were leaving India after Independence Day."}]}]},"afghanistan":{"h":"Afghanistan","i":"/æfˈgæn.ɪˌstæn/","a":"en-us-Afghanistan.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Afghanistan is a landlocked country in South-Central Asia. The capital is Kabul."}]}]},"pakistan":{"h":"Pakistan","i":"/ˈpaːkɪst̪aːn/","a":"en-us-Pakistan.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Pakistan is a country in South-Central Asia. Its full, official name is the Islamic Republic of Pakistan."}]}]},"khalistan":{"h":"Khalistan","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Khalistan is the name of a proposed country based on theocratic ideas."}]}]},"sikkim":{"h":"Sikkim","i":"/ˈsik.im/","a":"Lif-Sikkim.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Sikkim is a state in eastern India which has Gangtok as its capital."}]}]},"bangladesh":{"h":"Bangladesh","i":"/bæŋ.glɜˈdɛʃ/","a":"en-us-Bangladesh.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Bangladesh is a country in southeast Asia."}]}]},"kargil":{"h":"Kargil","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Kargil is a district in the disputed territory of Jammu and Kashmir."}]}]},"leh":{"h":"Leh","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Leh is a city and a district in the disputed territory of Jammu and Kashmir."}]}]},"chittagong":{"h":"Chittagong","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Chittagong is the second largest city in Bangladesh.","e":"Chittagong is where I live."},{"m":"Chittagong is a division in Bangladesh."},{"m":"Chittagong is also a district and Sadar Upzilla in Bangladesh."}]}]},"jerusalem":{"h":"Jerusalem","i":"/d͡ʒəˈruːsələm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Jerusalem.wav","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Jerusalem is the ancient holy city, and the capital city of Israel and Palestine."}]}]},"bengali":{"h":"Bengali","i":"/bɛŋˈɡɔːli/","a":"en-us-Bengali.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Bangla or Bengali is a language spoken in Bangladesh and the states of Tripura and West Bengal, India."}]}]},"tibet":{"h":"Tibet","i":"/tɪˈbet/","a":"en-us-Tibet.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Tibet is a province of China. The capital is Lhasa."}]}]},"charity":{"h":"charity","i":"/ˈtʃærɪti/","a":"en-us-charity.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A charity is an organisation that collects money or goods and uses them to help poor or sick people, often with the help of volunteers.","e":"The group, a Catholic charity that runs schools on Indian reservations, collected nearly $17 million from the public."},{"m":"(uncountable) Charity is the work of helping the poor and the sick.","e":"All the money raised goes to charity."},{"m":"(uncountable) Charity is the money, goods, or help that people give to the poor and the sick.","e":"Our family was poor, but my mother would never accept charity."},{"m":"(uncountable) Charity is the quality of being kind, thoughtful, and helpful.","e":"He led a life of charity."}]}]},"iran":{"h":"Iran","i":"/ɪˈrɑːn/","a":"en-us-Iran-noun.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"' Iran is a country in South-Central Asia. The capital is Tehran. It was known as Persia until 1935."}]}]},"albania":{"h":"Albania","i":"/ælˈbeɪ.ni.ə/","a":"en-us-Albania.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Albania is a country in south