al city of the state of Bihar in India."}]}]},"shiraz":{"h":"Shiraz","a":"En-Shiraz.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Shiraz is a city in Iran."}]}]},"karnataka":{"h":"Karnataka","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Karnataka is a state in southern India. Bangalore is the capital city."}]}]},"soil":{"h":"soil","i":"/sɔɪl/","a":"en-us-soil.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A mix of sand and other natural material on the surface of the earth that is used to grow plants."},{"m":"or land.","e":"The refugees were happy to return to their home soil."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To make dirty or ruin.","e":"Look at that! You soiled your shirt with mud!"}]}]},"disappointment":{"h":"disappointment","i":"/dɪsəˈpɔɪntmənt/","a":"en-us-disappointment.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Disappointment is the feeling you have when something isn't as good as you expected."},{"m":"(countable) A disappointment is someone or something that isn't as good as you expected."}]}]},"istanbul":{"h":"Istanbul","i":"/ɪstænˈbʊl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Istanbul.wav","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Istanbul is the largest city in Turkey."}]}]},"tajikistan":{"h":"Tajikistan","i":"/tɑːˈdʒiːkɪstɑːn/","a":"en-us-Tajikistan.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Tajikistan is a country in South-Central Asia, the capital city is Dushanbe."}]}]},"ankara":{"h":"Ankara","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Ankara is the capital city of Turkey."}]}]},"kyrgyzstan":{"h":"Kyrgyzstan","i":"/ˈkɪər.ɡɪˌstɑːn/","a":"en-us-Kyrgyzstan.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Kyrgyzstan is a landlocked country in South-Central Asia. The capital city is Bishkek."}]}]},"bishkek":{"h":"Bishkek","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Bishkek is the capital city of Kyrgyzstan."}]}]},"uzbekistan":{"h":"Uzbekistan","i":"/ʊzˌbɛkɪˈstɑːn/","a":"en-us-Uzbekistan.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Uzbek Republic is a landlocked country in South-Central Asia; the capital city is Tashkent."}]}]},"tashkent":{"h":"Tashkent","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Tashkent is the capital city of Uzbekistan.","e":"I used to live in Tashkent."}]}]},"kazakhstan":{"h":"Kazakhstan","i":"/ˈkæzəkstæn/","a":"en-us-Kazakhstan.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Kazakhstan is landlocked country in South-Central Asia; the capital city is Astana."}]}]},"astana":{"h":"Astana","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Nur-Sultan, formerly Astana, is the capital city of Kazakhstan."}]}]},"tatarstan":{"h":"Tatarstan","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Tatarstan is an autonomous republic in Russia; the capital city is Kazan."}]}]},"kazan":{"h":"Kazan","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Kazan is the capital city of Tatarstan."}]}]},"kashgar":{"h":"Kashgar","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Kashgar is a city in China."}]}]},"junagarh":{"h":"Junagarh","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Junagarh is a city in India."}]}]},"medina":{"h":"Medina","i":"/məˈdinə/","a":"en-us-Medina.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Medina is a city in Saudi Arabia."}]}]},"mecca":{"h":"Mecca","i":"/ˈmɛkə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Mecca.wav","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Mecca is a city in Saudi Arabia.","e":"Mecca is a holy place for Muslims, many of who travel there every year."}]}]},"manchester":{"h":"Manchester","i":"/ˈmæntʃɛstɚ/","a":"en-uk-Manchester.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Manchester is a city and borough in Northern England in the United Kingdom."}]}]},"bradford":{"h":"Bradford","i":"/ˈbrædfɚd/","a":"en-uk-Bradford.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Bradford is a city in northern England."}]}]},"jeddah":{"h":"Jeddah","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Jeddah is a port city of Saudi Arabia."}]}]},"granada":{"h":"Granada","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Granada is a province in Spain."},{"m":"Granada is the capital city of the Granada province."}]}]},"distract":{"h":"distract","i":"/dɪsˈtrækt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-distract.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you distract someone, you make them pay attention to something different than what they were paying attention to before.","e":"The crowd was distracted by a helicopter hovering over the stadium when the only goal of the game was scored."}]}]},"chat":{"h":"chat","i":"/tʃæt/","a":"en-us-chat.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If two or more people chat, they talk with each other in a casual way, sometimes by typing on a computer or cell phone.","e":"His friends dropped by frequently just to chat."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A chat is a casual conversation, sometimes by typing on a computer or cell phone.","e":"People come to the bar to have a drink and a chat."}]}]},"cheer":{"h":"cheer","i":"/t͡ʃɪə(r)/","a":"en-us-cheer.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you cheer, you shout to show that you are happy about something or to encourage someone.","e":"The band begins to play and the crowd cheers."},{"m":"If something cheers somebody, it makes them feel happier.","e":"There isn't much on the street to cheer the poor."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cheer is a shout to show that you are happy about something or to encourage someone.","e":"As the clock counted down the final seconds of the game the cheers from the crowd grew louder and louder."},{"m":"(uncountable) Cheer is a feeling of happiness.","e":"Thanksgiving is a time for families to gather with good cheer and put problems behind them."}]}]},"wales":{"h":"Wales","i":"/weɪlz/","a":"en-us-Wales.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Wales is a principality in the west of, and one of the nations of, the United Kingdom. The capital city is Cardiff."}]}]},"cheque":{"h":"cheque","i":"/tʃɛk/","a":"EN-AU ck1 cheque.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cheque is a written promise that allows the receiver to take money from a bank account. It is used instead of cash to pay for things.","e":"Do you take personal cheques?"}]}]},"dacca":{"h":"Dacca","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"The old spelling of Dhaka, capital of East Bengal, later East Pakistan."}]}]},"cooperate":{"h":"cooperate","i":"/kəʊˈɒp.ə.reɪt/","a":"en-us-cooperate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If people cooperate, they help each other and work together towards the same goal."}]}]},"melee":{"h":"melee","i":"/mɛˈleɪ/","a":"en-us-melee.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Hand-to-hand combat; very close fighting."},{"m":"A naval or armor battle at a very close range."}]}]},"ammunition":{"h":"ammunition","i":"/ˌæmjuˈnɪʃən/","a":"en-us-ammunition.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Ammunition is the supply for a weapon (like bullets)."},{"m":"(uncountable) Ammunition can be used to describe words which can hurt people."}]}]},"render":{"h":"render","i":"/rɛn.də(r)/","a":"en-us-render.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If something is rendered useless, meaningless, invisible, etc. its use, meaning, visibility, etc. is removed.","e":"She had left the phone in a bowl of water, rendering it useless."},{"m":"(transitive) If you render something to someone, you give it to or do it for them because of a promise or commitment.","e":"You should carefully render aid to those who are injured."},{"m":"If an image is rendered in some style or pose, it is shown that way.","e":"The drawing of the ranch is rendered in a similar style to that of the school."},{"m":"(intransitive) (cooking) If the fat of a piece of meat renders, the fat drips off the meat when cooking.","e":"Bacon is very fatty when raw; however, most of the fat will render during cooking."}]}]},"rendering":{"h":"rendering","i":"/ˈrɛndərɪŋ/","a":"en-us-rendering.ogg","l":"render","q":"verb"},"definitely":{"h":"definitely","i":"/dɛf.ɪnət.li/","a":"en-us-definitely.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Something that will definitely happen will happen without doubt or with great chances of occurring.","e":"The letter will definitely come this week."}]}]},"chocolate":{"h":"chocolate","i":"/ˈtʃɒklət/","a":"en-ca-chocolate.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Chocolate is a candy made from cacao beans and often used to flavour other foods such as cakes and cookies.","e":"In my opinion, the best cookies are those that contain chocolate."},{"m":"(countable) A chocolate is an individual candy that is made of or covered in chocolate.","e":"These homemade chocolates are delicious."},{"m":"(uncountable) Chocolate is a dark brown colour."}]}]},"chop":{"h":"chop","i":"/ʧɒp/","a":"en-us-chop.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you chop something, you cut it using quick downward movements.","e":"Use 1 small onion, finely chopped."},{"m":"If you chop time, money, etc., you reduce it.","e":"Through careful planning, we were able to chop the production time in half."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A chop is a quick downward cutting motion."},{"m":"Your chops is your skill with something, especially music."},{"m":"(countable) If you get the chop, you are fired your job."},{"m":"(countable) (usually plural) A chop is particular piece of meat containing a bone, especially pork chops or mutton chops."},{"m":"(countable) (usually plural) A chop is a jaw or the side of a face."},{"m":"(uncountable) Chop is irregular waves on a rive, lake, etc."}]}]},"hedge":{"h":"hedge","i":"/hedʒ/","a":"en-us-hedge.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hedge is a plant with green leaves that has been planted in a straight line to divide a space."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you hedge an area, you enclose it with [[#Noun|hedges]]."},{"m":"(transitive) If you hedge something, you obstruct or surround it."}]}]},"besides":{"h":"besides","i":"/bəˈsaɪdz/","a":"en-us-besides.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"In addition (to); as well (as).","e":"We've got a pile of homework and a part time job besides."},{"m":"Other than; except for.","e":"I don't want to go anywhere besides China."}]}]},"thus":{"h":"thus","i":"/ˈðʌs/","a":"en-us-thus.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"(formal) as a result","e":"I didn't do my homework and thus got a bad grade."},{"m":"(formal) in this way or manner","e":"If you throw the ball thus, as I’m showing you, you’ll have better luck hitting the target."},{"m":"(formal) You use thus far to mean until now, or up to this point.","e":"Things have gone well thus far. Let's hope they continue."}]}]},"citizen":{"h":"citizen","i":"/ˈsɪt.ɪ.zən/","a":"en-us-citizen.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A citizen is a person who lives in a particular place.","e":"The town has a population of 115, most of them senior citizens, with no young families."},{"m":"(countable) A citizen is a person who belongs to a particular country, usually because they were born there.","e":"Some of these Americans moved north and eventually become naturalized Canadian citizens."}]}]},"hermit":{"h":"hermit","a":"en-us-hermit.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hermit is a person who lives alone, far from other people, and does not like to interact with other people.","e":"We walked far and came to the house of the hermit who lives in the forest."},{"m":"(countable) A hermit is a religious person who lives alone and does not like to interact with other people for religious reasons."}]}]},"priest":{"h":"priest","i":"/ˈpriːst/","a":"en-us-priest.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A priest is a person who leads or performs in a religion.","e":"The priest stood in front of the people and blessed them."}]}]},"gravestone":{"h":"gravestone","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A gravestone is a stone on a grave, usually with the name of the dead person written on it.","e":"The old gravestone was smooth from many years of rain, but she could still read the name on it."}]}]},"famous":{"h":"famous","i":"/ˈfeɪməs/","a":"en-us-famous.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone or something is famous, then many people know about them.","e":"Judy Garland was a famous singer."}]}]},"rely":{"h":"rely","i":"/rɪˈlaɪ/","a":"en-us-rely.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When someone relies on something, they need it and they feel certain that it will be there.","e":"In this place, you can't rely on good weather even in the summer."},{"m":"When someone relies on another person, they need the person to do something, and they trust the person and feel certain that the person will do it.","e":"I'm relying on you to water my plants when I'm travelling."}]}]},"beak":{"h":"beak","i":"/biːk/","a":"en-us-beak.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A beak is a bird's mouth.","e":"The bird is pecking with its beak for worms in the grass."}]}]},"chlorine":{"h":"chlorine","i":"/ˈklɔriːn/","a":"en-us-chlorine.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A chemical element (symbol Cl) with an atomic number of 17."},{"m":"(uncountable) Chlorine can mean something that contains chlorine, but is not chlorine as an element","e":"Drinking water and swimming pool water is chlorinated to make it clean."}]}]},"argon":{"h":"argon","i":"/ˈɑːrɡɒn/","a":"en-us-argon.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A chemical element (symbol Ar) with an atomic number of 18."},{"m":"Argon is a gas, often used in light bulbs to change the colour of the light."}]}]},"ankle":{"h":"ankle","i":"/ˈæŋ.kəl/","a":"en-us-ankle.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The ankle is the joint between the foot and the leg.","e":"She sprained her ankle when she fell on the ice."}]}]},"election":{"h":"election","i":"/ɪˈlɛkʃ(ə)n/","a":"en-us-election.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An election is a decision, often decided by voting.","e":"The man elected to take part in the work."}]}]},"oversight":{"h":"oversight","i":"/ˈoʊvɚˌsaɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-oversight.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An oversight is something that someone does by mistake, without seeing that they are doing it.","e":"He didn't thank me, but I'm sure that was just an oversight."},{"m":"Oversight is the action of watching and making sure people do things right.","e":"We have many ordinary workers, and a manager for oversight."},{"m":"On Wikipedia, oversight is deleting pages or parts of pages so that not even administrators can see the part that was deleted.","e":"I put my email address on Wikipedia by mistake, but I asked for oversight so that no one would see it."}]}]},"gramps":{"h":"gramps","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Grandpa, grandfather.","e":"Hi gramps! How's grandma?"},{"m":"(by extension) An old man.","e":"Hey gramps, get off the road!"}]}]},"capability":{"h":"capability","i":"/keɪpəˈbɪləti/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-capability.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"We say that someone has a capability when they are capable of doing something; that means they are able to do it.","e":"He has great capabilities in using computers, but he always forgets to go to school on time."}]}]},"uncertain":{"h":"uncertain","i":"/ʌnˈsɜːtən/","a":"en-us-uncertain.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Uncertain is the opposite of certain. You don't know whether it is going to happen or not. You have doubts about it.","e":"I'm uncertain whether I should go out tonight."}]}]},"volunteer":{"h":"volunteer","i":"/ˌvɒl(ə)nˈtɪə/","a":"en-us-volunteer.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A volunteer is someone who does work because they want to, without being paid.","e":"We have one paid manager and five volunteers working on this project."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To do something voluntarily--to do it without being offered something in exchange","e":"I volunteered to do the dishes after dinner to help my mom clean up."}]}]},"clarify":{"h":"clarify","i":"/ˈklærɪfaɪ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-clarify.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you clarify something, you make it clearer.","e":"Finally, we would recommend further research to clarify the various issues."}]}]},"pakistani":{"h":"Pakistani","i":"/pakɪˈstɑːni/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A Pakistani is a person or thing that comes from Pakistan."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something or someone that is Pakistani comes from Pakistan.","e":"The Pakistani currency is the Rupee."}]}]},"pakistanis":{"h":"Pakistanis","l":"pakistani","q":"noun"},"clerk":{"h":"clerk","i":"/aːk/","a":"en-us-clerk.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A clerk is a person who keeps an organization's records.","e":"I called the city clerks office to see if they had a record of her birth."},{"m":"(countable) A sales clerk is the person in a shop who helps you find things you want to buy.","e":"A convenience store clerk was arrested for selling cigarettes to children."},{"m":"(countable) A desk clerk is the person at a hotel who registers guests.","e":"The desk clerk called a taxi for us."},{"m":"(countable) A law clerk is a person, often a junior lawyer, who is the assistant of a judge or another lawyer."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you clerk, you work as a clerk, especially as a law clerk.","e":"She clerked for the judge in 1992, and says she and her fellow clerks worked \"as many hours as we could stay awake, often past midnight and on weekends.\""}]}]},"climb":{"h":"climb","i":"/klaɪm/","a":"en-us-climb.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you climb something, you move up or down it.","e":"They climbed the stairs to the top of the tower again and went out onto the roof."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you climb into, out of, through something, etc., you move with difficulty, often using your hands and knees.","e":"The old man climbed into the back seat of her small car."},{"m":"(intransitive) If prices, profits, temperatures, etc. climb or if a road, a path, or a piece of land climbs, it goes up.","e":"This year, gas prices have climbed steadily from a low of 75 cents to a peak of almost $1.30 in August."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A climb is an upwards movement, often a slow or difficult one.","e":"It isn't far, but it's a steep climb and they were sweating when they reach the top."},{"m":"(countable) A climb down is a long slow downwards movement."}]}]},"later":{"h":"later","i":"/leɪtə/","a":"en-us-later.ogg","l":"late","q":"adverb","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Afterwards.","e":"I'll see you later."}]}]},"quadrennial":{"h":"quadrennial","i":"/kwɒˈdrɛn.i.əl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-NaomiAmethyst-quadrennial.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is quadrennial, it happens every four years."}]}]},"useless":{"h":"useless","i":"/ˈjuːs.ləs/","a":"en-us-useless.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is useless, it has no use."}]}]},"onlooker":{"h":"onlooker","i":"/ˈɒnˌlʊk.ə(r)/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-onlooker.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An onlooker is someone who watches but does not participate.","e":"I wasn't in the fight. I was only an onlooker."}]}]},"poems":{"h":"poems","i":"/ˈpəʊ.ɪmz/","a":"en-us-poems.ogg","l":"poem","q":"noun"},"owe":{"h":"owe","i":"/əʊ/","a":"en-us-owe.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you owe something you need to pay or give it to someone because of something you have been given. For example, if I ask to borrow five dollars for lunch from a friend, then I will owe that friend five dollars. It could also be something you agree to pay (like a bill) or something you lost.","e":"I owe $50 to the phone company right now."},{"m":"If you owe a person, there is something you need to pay or give to that person. That is, you owe something to that person.","e":"Thanks for the help! I really owe you for that!"},{"m":"If you owe a lot to someone or something, you have something to thank that person (or thing) for.","e":"We owe as much to good luck as to our own skills."},{"m":"If something owes to something else, what it owes to is what caused or the reason for doing it.","e":"Much of the success of early rock music owed to the ability of teenagers to buy records."}]}]},"knowledgeable":{"h":"knowledgeable","i":"/ˈnɑl.ɪd͡ʒ.ə.bəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-knowledgeable.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a person is knowledgeable that person knows many things, or a great amount about something.","e":"She is very knowledgeable when it comes to medicine."}]}]},"earn":{"h":"earn","i":"/ɜːn/","a":"en-us-earn.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you earn something you get it by working or doing something.","e":"I earn a lot more money at my new job than at my last job."},{"m":"If you think you have earned something, you think you should have it because of what you have done.","e":"After completing that project I thought I had earned some time to rest."}]}]},"hill":{"h":"hill","i":"/hɪl/","a":"en-us-hill.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hill is a piece of high ground that rises up out of lower ground. A hill is like a mountain but smaller.","e":"My house was on the top of a hill."}]}]},"hillbilly":{"h":"hillbilly","i":"/ˈhɪlˌbɪli/","a":"en-us-hillbilly.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A person who lives in the country in an area with many hills, and who has little money. Usually, this means an American from a region called Appalachia or a region called the Ozark Mountains. These people have homes and farms in the valleys between the hills.","e":"My dad is a hillbilly from eastern Kentucky."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Having to do with hillbillies, or typical of hillbillies."}]}]},"hills":{"h":"hills","i":"/hɪlz/","a":"en-us-hills.ogg","l":"hill","q":"noun"},"hillbillies":{"h":"hillbillies","l":"hillbilly","q":"noun"},"valleys":{"h":"valleys","i":"/ˈvæliz/","l":"valley","q":"noun"},"appalachia":{"h":"Appalachia","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Appalachia is a region in the eastern United States of America, named for the Appalachian Mountains.","e":"It is hard to pass through the Appalachia region because most of it is mountainous."}]}]},"kentucky":{"h":"Kentucky","i":"/kɛnˈtʌki/","a":"en-us-Kentucky.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Kentucky is a state in the United States of America.","e":"Frankfort is the capital of Kentucky."}]}]},"qualification":{"h":"qualification","i":"/ˌkwɒlɪfɪˈkeɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-qualification.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A qualification is something you might need to do something (such as a job). This might be a skill, knowing about something, or having done a similar job before.","e":"Being able to lead is an important qualification to be president."},{"m":"(countable) A qualification is something you add to an idea that limits its effect or meaning.","e":"I accept your offer, but with some qualifications."}]}]},"qualifications":{"h":"qualifications","i":"/ˌkwɑlɪfɪˈkeɪʃənz/","a":"en-us-qualifications.ogg","l":"qualification","q":"noun"},"huge":{"h":"huge","i":"/hjuːd͡ʒ/","a":"en-us-huge.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is huge it is very big. When you say this, you mean bigger than large, or bigger than what is usually called big.","e":"Wow! That dog is so huge he could be a horse."},{"m":"If something is huge it is very important or very exciting.","e":"He's moving all the way to Africa! That's huge!"}]}]},"nationalization":{"h":"nationalization","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Nationalization is when a privately owned object becomes the property of the government or the public."}]}]},"spawn":{"h":"spawn","i":"/ˈspɔːn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-spawn.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To create, in large numbers."},{"m":"To reproduce in large numbers."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The eggs of a frog are spawn. They are covered in clear jelly."}]}]},"heathen":{"h":"heathen","i":"/ˈhiːðən/","a":"en-us-heathen.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A person who has no religion and does not believe in anything spiritual.","e":"An atheist doesn't believe in God, but a heathen doesn't believe in anything."},{"m":"(by extension) A wild or immoral person.","e":"Those kids were a bunch of heathens who did nothing but party."},{"m":"(often capitalized) A pagan who tries to follow the religion of ancient Germany or Scandinavia. This religion is often called Asatru or Heathenry.","e":"He is a very serious Heathen and prays to Odin and Thor everyday."},{"m":"(often offensive) A person who is not a Christian."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Not believing in any religion or anything spiritual. This could also mean an idea that is against all religion.","e":"I found him reading some heathen book that claimed to disprove God."},{"m":"(by extension) or immoral.","e":"Everything he does is totally heathen."},{"m":"(often capitalized) Having to do with the religion of ancient Germany or Scandinavia; about Heathenry."},{"m":"(often offensive) Not Christian.","e":"\"The heathen [Aztec] gods cursed the gold....\"—from"}]}]},"scandinavia":{"h":"Scandinavia","i":"/skændɪˈneɪvi.ə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Scandinavia.wav","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"A region of Europe in the north. The called Norway, Sweden, and Denmark are part of Scandinavia. Sometime Iceland and Finland are included, but not always.","e":"The Vikings sailed from Scandinavia to attack the rest of Europe."}]}]},"thor":{"h":"Thor","i":"/θɔː/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Thor.wav","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"The god of thunder and lightning to the Vikings (a people from ancient Europe)."}]}]},"heathens":{"h":"heathens","l":"heathen","q":"noun"},"norway":{"h":"Norway","i":"/ˈnɔː.weɪ/","a":"en-us-Norway.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Norway is a country in the north of Europe, with borders to Sweden, Finland and Russia."}]}]},"shamans":{"h":"shamans","l":"shaman","q":"noun"},"sweden":{"h":"Sweden","i":"/ˈswiː.dən/","a":"en-uk-Sweden.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Sweden is a country in the north of Europe."}]}]},"denmark":{"h":"Denmark","i":"/ˈdɛn.mɑːk/","a":"en-us-Denmark.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Denmark is a country in the north of Europe.","e":"Copenhagen is the capital city of Denmark."}]}]},"iceland":{"h":"Iceland","i":"/ˈaɪs.lənd/","a":"en-us-Iceland.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Iceland is an island country in the northern Atlantic Ocean. Iceland is halfway between Europe and North America."}]}]},"finland":{"h":"Finland","i":"/ˈfɪn.lənd/","a":"en-us-Finland.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Finland is a country in the north of Europe."}]}]},"ireland":{"h":"Ireland","i":"/ˈaɪə(r)lənd/","a":"en-us-Ireland.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"An island in the Atlantic Ocean which is a little west of the Britain."},{"m":"Ireland is the official name for the Republic of Ireland, it is located in the south of the island, forms most of the island and includes 26 counties."}]}]},"graph":{"h":"graph","i":"/ɡrɑːf/","a":"en-us-graph.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A graph shows data (numbers) as a picture."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To draw a graph."}]}]},"charts":{"h":"charts","l":"chart","q":"noun"},"salary":{"h":"salary","i":"/ˈsælɚi/","a":"en-us-salary.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Your salary is the money you are paid every month for doing your job.","e":"Your salary will be paid into your bank on the first day of each month."}]}]},"clue":{"h":"clue","i":"/kluː/","a":"en-au-clue.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A clue is a piece of information that helps you answer a question or solve a problem.","e":"He said nothing, made no gesture, and gave no clue about what he was thinking."},{"m":"(informal) (singular) If you have no clue about something, you don't know at all.","e":"I'm afraid I have no clue how to get there."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(informal) If you clue somebody in to something, you give them that information that they didn't have.","e":"I had no idea what she was angry about until my sister clued me in."}]}]},"humiliation":{"h":"humiliation","i":"/hjuːˌmɪliˈeɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-humiliation.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Humiliation is the feeling you have when something very bad has happened and many people think it's your fault."},{"m":"(uncountable) Humiliation is the act of or embarrassing someone or making them feel very bad."}]}]},"embarrass":{"h":"embarrass","i":"/ɪmˈbæ.rəs/","a":"en-us-embarrass.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you embarrass someone, you make them feel discomfort or shame.","e":"The boys embarrassed him by pulling down his pants."}]}]},"mango":{"h":"mango","i":"/ˈmæŋɡəʊ/","a":"en-us-mango.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mango is a sweet tropical fruit with smooth yellow or red skin, soft yellow or orange flesh and a very large seed inside.","e":"This mango is very big."}]}]},"fluorine":{"h":"fluorine","i":"/ˈflɔːrɪn/","a":"en-us-fluorine.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Fluorine is a yellow gas that has an atomic number of 9 and the symbol F.","e":"Fluorine reacts very easily."}]}]},"morphologies":{"h":"morphologies","l":"morphology","q":"noun"},"british":{"h":"British","i":"/ˈbrɪt.ɪʃ/","a":"en-us-British.oga","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"British people or things are those that come from Britain.","e":"My dad is British, and my Mom is Indian."}]}]},"fag":{"h":"fag","i":"/fæɡ/","a":"EN-AU ck1 fag.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(UK only) A cigarette.","e":"She smokes about 10 fags a day."},{"m":"(often offensive) A homosexual male, sometimes used between homosexuals themselves. Short for faggot."}]}]},"fairy":{"h":"fairy","i":"/ˈfɛəri/","a":"en-us-fairy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(fiction, folklore, mythology) A type of human-like being with magical powers. In modern stories fairies are small with insect-like wings. In older stories they were human-size and very powerful, and sometimes dangerous.","e":"A fairy granted then each a wish."},{"m":"(offensive) A homosexual man, usually one who is very feminine.","e":"I'm not sure that fairy even knows he's male."}]}]},"queer":{"h":"queer","i":"/kwir/","a":"en-us-queer.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is queer, it is a little bit strange, it is not quite normal."},{"m":"If someone feels queer, that person is mentally strange or sick."},{"m":"(see usage notes) Another word for homosexual or for LGBT people in general. It is sometimes used as a derogatory term and some people see it as a slur."},{"m":"(see usage notes) Denoting or relating to a sexual or gender identity that does not correspond to established ideas of sexuality and gender, especially heterosexual norms."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(see usage notes above) A person who is homosexual."},{"m":"(see usage notes above) A person whose gender identity is nonbinary or differs from the sex they had or were identified as having at birth."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To queer somebody's pitch means to upset someone's plans."},{"m":"To queer something is to see it, examine it, or show it from a queer perspective."}]}]},"border":{"h":"border","i":"/bɔədə/","a":"en-us-border.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The border of a country is the edge of the country: the place where that country touches another country.","e":"You can't cross the border without identification papers."},{"m":"The border of a shape or of a picture or of part of a picture is the edge of it.","e":"She drew three pink hearts with red borders at the top of the picture."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive), If something is bordered with or in something, that goes all around it.","e":"The newspaper notice was bordered in black."},{"m":"(transitive) If one place borders on another, they are side by side.","e":"The Sea of Japan is bordered by Japan, North Korea, Russia and South Korea."}]}]},"aspirin":{"h":"aspirin","i":"/ˈæsprɪn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-aspirin.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A drug for pain."}]}]},"strict":{"h":"strict","i":"/strɪkt/","a":"en-us-strict.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Making firm rules.","e":"The father was very strict about the children coming to dinner on time."},{"m":"Following rules exactly, or giving strong punishments for not following the rules."}]}]},"coach":{"h":"coach","i":"/kəʊtʃ/","a":"en-us-coach.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A coach is a teacher of a sport.","e":"Even though his team won, first-year coach Andrew Johnson was not happy."},{"m":"(countable) A coach is a private teacher, often to help prepare for a particular test, job, or situation."},{"m":"(countable) A coach is a bus or a car of a train with seats for many people.","e":"Thomas the Tank Engine was pulling his coaches Annie and Clarabel back into Knapford Station."},{"m":"(countable) A coach is a vehicle pulled by a horse."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":", If you coach a person or a team, you teach them how to do a sport.","e":"She coaches girls gymnastics at Middlebury High School."},{"m":"(transitive) If you coach someone, you help them prepare for a particular test, job, or situation."}]}]},"unanimous":{"h":"unanimous","i":"/juːˈnanɪməs/","a":"en-uk-unanimous.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is unanimous, it is agreed on by all who are present.","e":"The vote to pass the bill was unanimous. Every member of the state congress voted to pass it."}]}]},"coast":{"h":"coast","i":"/kəʊst/","a":"en-us-coast.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The coast is the area of land closest to the sea.","e":"The hotel was near the coast and their room had a balcony from which they could see the distant ocean."},{"m":"If the coast is clear, nobody is looking, so you can do something without anyone knowing.","e":"He looked out the window to see if the coast was clear."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If a vehicle coasts, it continues to move forward without needing new energy.","e":"The car gradually coasted to a stop."}]}]},"preference":{"h":"preference","i":"/ˈprɛf(ə)r(ə)ns/","a":"en-us-preference.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A preference is something that you like more than others"}]}]},"intruder":{"h":"intruder","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An intruder is someone who enters another persons' home without permission.","e":"The intruder in the house was caught after we called the police."}]}]},"astrology":{"h":"astrology","i":"/əˈstrɒlədʒi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-astrology.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Astrology is the study of stars, planets, and their relations to predict future events."}]}]},"combine":{"h":"combine","i":"/kəmˈbaɪn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-combine (verb).wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you combine two or more things, you put them together.","e":"In a large bowl, combine 1/2 cup white sugar and cinnamon."},{"m":"(transitive) If something combines two or more things, it has both/all of them.","e":"This is a world that combines the old with the new."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A combine is a large farm vehicle the cuts grain and separates the seeds."}]}]},"messiah":{"h":"messiah","i":"/məˈsaɪ.ə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-messiah.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Jews and Christians use the word messiah to mean someone who was chosen by God to lead the people of Israel. Christians believe that Jesus was the Messiah."},{"m":"A person who is like God and who has many strong."}]}]},"conscience":{"h":"conscience","i":"/ˈkɒn.ʃəns/","a":"en-us-conscience.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The ability to feel whether what you're doing is right or wrong.","e":"Even though he stole things, he had some conscience: he didn't kill anyone."}]}]},"honour":{"h":"honour","i":"/ˈɑn.ɚ/","a":"en-us-honour.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Honour is the quality of being respected by other people."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you honour someone or something, you think highly of them; you respect them."}]}]},"honor":{"h":"honor","i":"/ˈɑn.ɚ/","a":"en-us-honor.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Honor is the quality of being respected by other people."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you honor someone or something, you think highly of them; you respect them."}]}]},"psychiatrist":{"h":"psychiatrist","i":"/ˌsaɪˈkaɪ.ə.trɪst/","a":"en-us-psychiatrist.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A psychiatrist is a doctor who helps people whose minds are sick.","e":"She went to a psychiatrist to try to learn to think about her life in a more normal way."}]}]},"fatherland":{"h":"fatherland","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The fatherland is the land of your father or mother."}]}]},"command":{"h":"command","i":"/kəˈmɑːnd/","a":"en-us-command.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Command, is the power to control people or things.","e":"The information moved from the soldiers up the chain of command right to the president."},{"m":"Command is the people or place that orders come from.","e":"This operation was planned carefully from the central command."},{"m":"(countable) A command is a direction for a computer to do something.","e":"A complicated command like \"COPY: *. *B:PRNT1 i\" could take some time for the computer to complete."},{"m":"(countable) A command is an order that somebody do something or that something happen.","e":"He gave the command to attack."},{"m":"If you have command of something, you understand it well.","e":"He has an excellent command of both French and Spanish."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you command someone to do something, you tell them to do it because you have power over them.","e":"He'd first joined the Army in 1969 and commanded a unit in Vietnam."},{"m":"(transitive) If you command attention, respect, etc., you get it because you should get it.","e":"The amazing power of weather commands respect and fear."}]}]},"nitrogen":{"h":"nitrogen","i":"/ˈnaɪtrədʒən/","a":"en-us-nitrogen.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Nitrogen is a colourless gas that has an atomic number of 7 and the symbol N.","e":"The air we breathe is mostly made of nitrogen."}]}]},"colourless":{"h":"colourless","i":"/ˈkʌlə(r).ləs/","a":"en-us-colourless.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that has no colour, and is almost invisible","e":"Air is colourless, which is why we can see through it."}]}]},"dweeb":{"h":"dweeb","i":"/dwiːb/","a":"en-au-dweeb.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A dweeb is a person who is not cool.","e":"What a dweeb -- he dresses like he is still in the 1980's."}]}]},"admission":{"h":"admission","i":"/ædˈmɪʃ.ən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Mélange a trois-admission.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An admission is when you admit (confess) something."},{"m":"Admission is when you are allowed to enter a place, an event, or a group (organization)."},{"m":"Admission is money you pay to get into a place. Examples would be paying to get into a theater of an amusement park."}]}]},"antivirus":{"h":"antivirus","i":"/ˈantɪvʌɪrəs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-antivirus.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A program for a computer that keep computer viruses out the computer. Usually, this program will take viruses out of the computer too."}]}]},"forgive":{"h":"forgive","i":"/fəˈgɪv/","a":"en-us-forgive.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you forgive something, you do not punish the person who did it.","e":"I know you stole some money from me, but I forgive your stealing."},{"m":"When you forgive a person, you do not try to punish that person for something.","e":"I know you stole some money from me, but I forgive you."}]}]},"guilty":{"h":"guilty","i":"/ˈgɪl.ti/","a":"en-us-guilty.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are guilty of something, you did it. This is usually for doing a bad thing."},{"m":"If you feel guilty you feel bad about something you did."},{"m":"If you are found guilty of a crime, a court of law said you did do that crime."}]}]},"lithium":{"h":"lithium","i":"/ˈlɪθi.əm/","a":"en-us-lithium.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Lithium is a light silver-grey metal. It has an atomic number of 3 and the symbol Li. It is the first alkali metals.","e":"Lithium reacts very easily. It even reacts with water."}]}]},"beryllium":{"h":"beryllium","i":"/bə'rɪliəm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Naomi Persephone Amethyst (NaomiAmethyst)-beryllium.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Beryllium is a light, grey metal. It has an atomic number of 4 and the symbol Be. It is the first of the alkaline earth metals.","e":"Beryllium is very poisonous."}]}]},"magnesium":{"h":"magnesium","i":"/ˌmæɡˈniziəm/","a":"en-us-magnesium.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Magnesium is a light, silver-grey metal. It has an atomic number of 12 and the symbol Mg. It is the second of the alkaline earth metals.","e":"s used to use magnesium to make a flash of light."}]}]},"photographer":{"h":"photographer","i":"/fəˈtɑɡrəfɚ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-photographer.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A photographer is a person who takes photographs as his work.","e":"We had a good photographer at the wedding."}]}]},"colorless":{"h":"colorless","i":"/ˈkʌlə(r).ləs/","a":"en-us-colourless.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that has no color, and is almost invisible","e":"Air is colorless, which is why we can see through it."}]}]},"react":{"h":"react","i":"/ri'ækt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-react.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you react to a person or event, you do something because of the person or event.","e":"When someone shouts at you, you usually react by shouting back."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you react to a medicine or other substance, something happens in your body because of it.","e":"She reacts badly to asprin. Her skin becomes red all over her body."},{"m":"(intransitive) When two or more chemicals react, they combine to form new chemical compounds.","e":"s and alkalis normally react to form salt and water."}]}]},"diagram":{"h":"diagram","i":"/ˈdaɪ.ə.ɡræm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-diagram.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A diagram is a drawing, or sketch, to show how something, such as a machine, works.","e":"You can see from this diagram that the electric switch is very simple, in fact."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you diagram something or someone, you show it using a diagram.","e":"They diagramed the building they were about to build."}]}]},"sketch":{"h":"sketch","i":"/ˈskɛtʃ/","a":"en-us-sketch.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sketch is a simple drawing.","e":"The artist made a quick sketch before he started painting the real picture."},{"m":"(countable) A sketch is a quick description of a person, or of something that happened.","e":"He gave me a sketch of the incident, stating only the main facts."},{"m":"(countable) A sketch is a short piece of acting, usually funny.","e":"The best part was the three-minute sketch about the cowboy who couldn't ride a horse."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you sketch something, you make a quick drawing of it using a pencil or a pen.","e":"I sketched his face quickly before he woke up."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you sketch something, you describe it without many details.","e":"The policeman asked me to sketch the accident while he took notes of what I said."}]}]},"thump":{"h":"thump","i":"/θʌmp/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-thump.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you thump something, you hit it, often with your closed hand."},{"m":"If something thumps, it hits something else, making a loud, low sound."},{"m":"(intransitive) If your heart thumps, it beats so strongly and quickly that you can easily notice it."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A thump is a loud, low sound made when something hits something else."},{"m":"(countable) A thump is the action of something hits something else."}]}]},"thumps":{"h":"thumps","l":"thump","q":"verb"},"commerce":{"h":"commerce","i":"/ˈkɒ.mɜs/","a":"en-us-commerce.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Commerce is the activity of buying and selling goods and services. Or broadly, it is the unmeasurable exchange of energy.","e":"The U.S. Department of Commerce reported that economic activity had dropped in 16 of the 50 states."}]}]},"compensate":{"h":"compensate","i":"/ˈkɒmpənseɪt/","a":"en-us-compensate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you compensate somebody, you give them something because they have lost something or done something for you."}]}]},"disinterested":{"h":"disinterested","i":"/dɪˈsɪnt(ə)rɛstɪd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Back ache-Disinterested.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is disinterested, they are not affected by a situation, so they can make fair decisions about it."},{"m":"If someone is disinterested, they are not interested in something; they find it boring."}]}]},"silicon":{"h":"silicon","i":"/'sIlIkən/","a":"en-us-silicon.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Silicon is a non-metal chemical element with the atomic number 14 and the symbol \"Si\".","e":"Sand is made of mostly silicon compounds."}]}]},"phosphorus":{"h":"phosphorus","i":"/ˈfɒsfərəs/","a":"en-us-phosphorus.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Phosphorus is a chemical element that has an atomic number of 15 and the symbol P.","e":"Phosphorus is used to make matches."}]}]},"compete":{"h":"compete","i":"/kəm.ˈpiːt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-compete.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you compete for something, you are working against other people to get it.","e":"He competed but failed to win a medal in the 1928 Olympics in Amsterdam."}]}]},"complicate":{"h":"complicate","i":"/ˈkɑmplɪkeɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-complicate.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you complicate a task, you make it difficult to do.","e":"My job is harder. They have complicated it by making me answer the telephone, too."},{"m":"(transitive) If you complicate an explanation, you make it difficult to understand.","e":"Just tell me the facts. Please don't complicate the account with unnecessary details."}]}]},"province":{"h":"province","i":"/ˈprɑvɪns/","a":"en-us-province.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A province is a major subdivision of a country.","e":"Canada has ten provinces and three."}]}]},"telegraph":{"h":"telegraph","i":"/ˈtɛl.ə.ɡræf/","a":"en-us-telegraph.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A telegraph is an older instrument that was used for sending words and signals to people over far distances. Most people now use the telephone.","e":"I sent my mother a message using my telegraph to tell her that I was fine."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To telegraph means to send a message using a telegraph."}]}]},"criminal":{"h":"criminal","i":"/ˈkrɪmənəl/","a":"en-us-criminal.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Criminal law, charges, investigations, and so forth are ones related to crime."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A criminal is someone who has commited a crime or been convicted of a crime.","e":"The politician said in a speech, \"don't blame society when somebody commits a crime, blame the criminal\". \""}]}]},"clout":{"h":"clout","i":"/klaʊt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-clout.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Clout is control or power over other people.","e":"The president of the United States has a lot of clout."},{"m":"(countable) A clout is a hard hit, usually with your hand.","e":"She gave him two sharp clouts on the ear."}]}]},"nowhere":{"h":"nowhere","i":"/ˈnoʊ.(h)wɛr/","a":"en-us-nowhere.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(in, at or to) no place","e":"We tried to follow his instructions but we got nowhere."}]}]},"concentrate":{"h":"concentrate","i":"/ˈkɒn.sən.treɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-concentrate.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you concentrate on something, you use most of your time and work there.","e":"We concentrated our rebuilding efforts on villages in the North of the city, where most of the damage had been done."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you concentrate on something, you think about it and not about other things.","e":"I went to a quiet room so I could concentrate."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something is concentrated somewhere, there is a lot of it in that place.","e":"The fighting was concentrated in a few small areas."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A concentrate is a liquid such as juice or chemicals from which most of the water has been removed.","e":"Instead of fresh orange juice, we usually make it from concentrate."}]}]},"zionist":{"h":"Zionist","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A Zionist is a person who supports Zionism."}]}]},"israel":{"h":"Israel","i":"/ˈɪz.reɪ.əl/","a":"en-us-Israel.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Israel is a country in the Middle East.","e":"Israel is the only Jewish country in the world."},{"m":"Israel was an ancient kingdom in the Middle East."}]}]},"palestine":{"h":"Palestine","i":"/ˈpæləˌstaɪn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Palestine.wav","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"The West Bank and Gaza Strip together; that is, the parts occupied by Israel and those under the jurisdiction of the Palestinian National Authority.","e":"Israel and Palestine both want peace."},{"m":"(geography) The region between the Mediterranean Sea and the Jordan River."},{"m":"(historical) The Roman province Palestina."},{"m":"(historical) A former British mandate in the Middle East. The capital city was Jerusalem."}]}]},"tiresome":{"h":"tiresome","i":"/ˈtaɪrsəm/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone or something is tiresome, it makes you bored or annoyed, usually because it is too long.","e":"All of this talking can get a little tiresome."}]}]},"temper":{"h":"temper","i":"/ˈtɛmpə/","a":"en-us-temper.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"If you have a temper, you often get mad quickly.","e":"Because of my temper, when I saw what he had done, I got very angry."},{"m":"One's temper can be one's nature.","e":"Count Cross-Stitch's genial temper makes him a charming house guest."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you temper a material, you toughen it by heat treatment."}]}]},"madder":{"h":"madder","l":"mad","q":"adjective"},"maddest":{"h":"maddest","l":"mad","q":"adjective"},"muzaffarabad":{"h":"Muzaffarabad","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Muzaffarabad is the state-level capital city of Azad Kashmir."}]}]},"mumbai":{"h":"Mumbai","i":"/mʊm.ˈbaɪ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Mumbai.wav","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Mumbai, formerly known as Bombay, is a city in India."}]}]},"bihar":{"h":"Bihar","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Bihar is a state in India. The capital city is Patna."}]}]},"zahedan":{"h":"Zahedan","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"The capital of the Sistan and Baluchestan province of Iran."}]}]},"tehran":{"h":"Tehran","i":"/ˈtɛ.ræn/","a":"en-Tehran.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Tehran is the capital city of Iran."}]}]},"dushanbe":{"h":"Dushanbe","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Dushanbe is the capital city of Tajikistan."}]}]},"beijing":{"h":"Beijing","i":"/beɪˈʒɪŋ/","a":"en-us-Beijing.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Beijing is the capital city of China."}]}]},"assam":{"h":"Assam","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Assam is a state in India; its capital is Dispur."}]}]},"pomegranate":{"h":"pomegranate","i":"/ˈpɒm.iˌɡræn.ɪt/","a":"en-uk-pomegranate.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A small tree, that gives fruit called pomegranates."},{"m":"A fruit with seeds that are covered in red jelly."}]}]},"juniper":{"h":"juniper","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A juniper is a shrub or tree that has pointed, needle-like leaves and strong-smelling cones."}]}]},"bustard":{"h":"bustard","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bustard is a large bird that lives on land."}]}]},"cemetery":{"h":"cemetery","i":"/ˈsɛm.ɪˌtri/","a":"en-us-cemetery.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A place where dead people are; a place for graves."}]}]},"rawalpindi":{"h":"Rawalpindi","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Rawalpindi is a city in Pakistan next to Islamabad."}]}]},"gangtok":{"h":"Gangtok","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Gangtok is the capital city of the state of Sikkim in India."}]}]},"chandigarh":{"h":"Chandigarh","i":"/ˌt͡ʃʌndɪˈɡɑː(r)/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Chandigarh.wav","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Chandigarh is a city in India that serves as the capital of two states: Punjab and Haryana."}]}]},"consume":{"h":"consume","i":"/kənˈsjuːm/","a":"en-us-consume.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you consume energy, resources, time, etc., you use it and it is no longer available.","e":"Only 10% of the energy consumed by a light bulb produces usable light."},{"m":"(transitive) If you consume alcohol, food, etc., you eat or drink it.","e":"They discovered that about half the calories consumed by an adult bat are used up during flight."},{"m":"(transitive) If a fire consumes something, it burns it until it's gone.","e":"In 1988 a fire consumed about half of the park's trees."},{"m":"(transitive) If you are consumed by a thought or idea, you cannot think about anything else.","e":"Our minds were consumed by the things we saw and dreamed of having."}]}]},"contain":{"h":"contain","i":"/kənˈteɪn/","a":"en-ca-contain.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If x contains y, y is in x.","e":"Did the envelope contain a letter?"},{"m":"(transitive) If you contain something, you stop it from getting out.","e":"Molly was so happy should could barely contain her tears."}]}]},"countryside":{"h":"countryside","i":"/ˈkʌn.triˌsaɪd/","a":"en-uk-countryside.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The countryside is the area outside the.","e":"He headed out of town and through the surrounding countryside."}]}]},"criterion":{"h":"criterion","i":"/kraɪˈtɪəriən/","a":"En-us-criterion.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (usually plural) A criterion is a principle that you use to judge something or decide about something.","e":"The only criterion used for measuring success was school grades."}]}]},"cupboard":{"h":"cupboard","i":"/ˈkʌb.əd/","a":"en-us-cupboard.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cupboard is a piece of furniture with shelves to hold dishes, towels, food, etc.","e":"He took cups, plates and saucers from the kitchen cupboards and stacked them on the table."}]}]},"deputy":{"h":"deputy","i":"/ˈdɛpjəti/","a":"en-us-deputy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A deputy is somebody one level down from another person. The deputy helps the other person or does that person's job sometimes.","e":"The sheriff posted a deputy to stay until they could get a better look in the morning."}]}]},"directory":{"h":"directory","i":"/dɪˈrɛktəri/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-directory.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A directory is a book or list of names, usually in alphabetical order with telephone numbers or addresses.","e":"He checked he number in the directory."}]}]},"disabled":{"h":"disabled","i":"[dɪsˈeɪbəɫd]","a":"en-us-disabled.oga","l":"disable","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If somebody is disabled, they cannot use part(s) of their body or mind in the same way that most people can.","e":"Two people died in the crash and the others were severely physically disabled."}]}]},"dot":{"h":"dot","i":"/dɒt/","a":"en-us-dot.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A dot is a small round mark.","e":"You forgot to put a dot over the i."},{"m":"If you do something at a particular time \"on the dot\", you do it exactly at that time.","e":"I'll be there at 5:00 on the dot."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you dot something, you put small round marks on it.","e":"Don't forget to dot the i."},{"m":"(transitive) If an area is dotted with things, the things are spread out over the area.","e":"The valley was dotted with camp fires."}]}]},"distinct":{"h":"distinct","i":"/dɪˈstɪŋkt/","a":"en-us-distinct.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If two things are distinct, they are clearly different or separate.","e":"Sports psychologists recognized that there were two distinct types of athletes who could become gold-medal winners."},{"m":"A distinct impression, advantage, possibility, etc. is one that clearly exists.","e":"I had the distinct impression that he was secretly laughing at me."},{"m":"If something is distinct, it can be clearly seen, heard, or sensed.","e":"As Gillian approached Theo's dressing room, the angry voices became more distinct."}]}]},"dozen":{"h":"dozen","i":"/ˈdʌzn̩/","a":"en-us-dozen.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A dozen is 12 of something.","e":"He ate half a dozen cookies and felt sick."},{"m":"(countable) A dozen is a large number.","e":"I've been there dozens of times."}]}]},"criminally":{"h":"criminally","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Someone behaving criminally is breaking laws or acting in a criminal manner."}]}]},"criminals":{"h":"criminals","l":"criminal","q":"noun"},"crowd":{"h":"crowd","i":"/kraʊd/","a":"en-us-crowd.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A crowd is a lot of people in one place together.","e":"The crowd cheered when the team scored another goal."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you crowd someone, you push too close to them.","e":"Don't crowd me, please. I can't see the stage."}]}]},"dare":{"h":"dare","i":"/deə(r)/","a":"en-us-dare.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you dare to do something, you have the courage to do it, even if you are afraid.","e":"The President dared to make an unpopular decision."},{"m":"If you dare someone to do something, you challenge them to do something that is a risk, or even dangerous.","e":"I dare you to climb that tree."},{"m":"If you dare not do something, you are afraid to do it.","e":"I daren't tell my parents what happened. They'll be very cross."},{"m":"You say How dare someone do something? to show that you are angry about something that someone has done.","e":"How dare you come in here without knocking?"}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A dare is a challenge to somebody.","e":"He never says \"No\" to a dare."}]}]},"sometimes":{"h":"sometimes","i":"/ˈsʌmtaɪmz/","a":"en-us-sometimes.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Things that happen sometimes only happen at certain times, or on certain occasions, but not every time.","e":"The bus sometimes arrives late, especially if it is raining."}]}]},"damn":{"h":"damn","i":"/dæm/","a":"en-us-damn.ogg","s":[{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"You say damn when you are angry or surprised about something.","e":"Damn! That hurts. Be careful."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something is damn good, damn sure, etc., it is very much that way.","e":"I want to make damn sure he knows about it."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"You use damn to show that you are angry.","e":"He doesn't know a damn thing about fixing cars."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) (usually subjunctive) You say \"damn you\" or \"damn (something)\" to show that you are angry or that you don't care.","e":"He slammed his glass down on the table.\" I am dying, God damn it, dying!\""},{"m":"(transitive) (usually passive) You say \"I'll be damned\" to show that you are surprised.","e":"You mean I was right? Well, I'll be damned!"},{"m":"(transitive) (usually passive) You say \"I'll be damned if something happens\" to show that you don't want it to happen or that you don't think it will happen."},{"m":"(transitive) (usually passive) If someone is damned, go to hell when they die.","e":"Living that way will damn your soul to Hell."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) If you don't give a damn, you don't care.","e":"Look, don't tell me about your problems. I don't give a damn."},{"m":"(countable) If something isn't worth a damn, it has no value."}]}]},"dam":{"h":"dam","i":"/dæm/","a":"en-us-dam.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A dam is like a wall used to hold back water. Usually, this is to block a river."},{"m":"(countable) A dam is a barrier like that used to hold back water, such as a dental dam."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you dam a river you block it with a dam."}]}]},"complaints":{"h":"complaints","i":"/kəmˈpleɪnts/","a":"en-us-complaints.ogg","l":"complaint","q":"noun"},"content":{"h":"content","i":"/'kɒntɛnt/","a":"en-us-content.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (usually plural) The contents of a container, such as a bag, a file, a book etc., are the things that are in it.","e":"A couple of green plastic bags had torn open, and the contents had spilled out onto the floor."},{"m":"(countable) (singular) The fat, water, alcohol, etc. content of something is the amount of that substance in something else.","e":"The red wine had a deep color and high alcohol content."},{"m":"(uncountable) Content is the feeling of being happy and satisfied.","e":"She could sleep to her heart's content."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is content, they are happy and satisfied.","e":"She had always been perfectly content to live in the city."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If somebody contents themselves with something, they accept it even though they wanted something different."}]}]},"contents":{"h":"contents","i":"/'kɒntɛnts/","a":"en-us-contents.ogg","l":"content","q":"noun"},"contribute":{"h":"contribute","i":"/kənˈtrɪbjuːt/","a":"en-us-contribute.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If x contributes to y, x is one of a number of things that together make or cause y.","e":"Unusually warm temperatures may have significantly contributed to the amount of rain we've had."},{"m":"If you contribute something, you make it available to other people.","e":"Everybody contributed $10 to pay for the present."}]}]},"spelt":{"h":"spelt","i":"/'spεlt/","l":"spell","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A kind of wheat."}]}]},"cope":{"h":"cope","i":"/kəʊp/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-cope.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you cope with a problem, you do things so that the problem does not stop you.","e":"She went to a special school and learned the skills needed to cope with her learning differences."}]}]},"crisis":{"h":"crisis","i":"/ˈkraɪsɪs/","a":"en-us-crisis.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A crisis is a situation that has become very bad or dangerous and can have bad changes to security, economic, political, social or environmental issues.","e":"The latest change in the hostage crisis came one day after Israel freed 51 prisoners from a jail in south Lebanon."},{"m":"(countable) A crisis is a serious emotional problem.","e":"My high school friends thought I was confused, that I was having an identity crisis."}]}]},"crisp":{"h":"crisp","i":"/krɪsp/","a":"en-us-crisp.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is crisp, it breaks easily and makes a cracking or snapping sound when you break or bite it.","e":"Fry the bacon until it is brown and crisp."},{"m":"If cloth or paper is crisp, it is clean or new and often stiff.","e":"The young man stood tall and straight in a crisp white shirt and dark pants."},{"m":"If the weather is crisp, it is cold and dry, often with a clear sky."},{"m":"If food tastes crisp, it has a fresh acid flavour."},{"m":"If a person is crisp, they are professional and quick, but not especially friendly."},{"m":"If a picture is crisp, it is very clear."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (usually plural) Crisps are thin, deep-fried potatoes.","e":"I ate a packet of crisps yesterday."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To make crisp."},{"m":"(intransitive) To become crisp."}]}]},"creampie":{"h":"creampie","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"; (pornography) A creampie is semen coming out of someone's vagina (or anus) after sex."}]}]},"crisps":{"h":"crisps","l":"crisp","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable), (usually plural) Crisps are thin, deep-fried potatoes."}]}]},"pornography":{"h":"pornography","i":"/pɔː(r)ˈnɒɡ.rə.fi/","a":"en-au-pornography.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Pornography is pictures or words that show or describe sex to make people feel excited."}]}]},"cock":{"h":"cock","i":"/kɒk/","a":"en-us-cock.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cock is a male chicken."},{"m":"(countable) A cock is another word for a penis.","e":"My girlfriend likes to suck my cock."},{"m":"(countable) Cock is a friendly form of address among men, without using in a derogatory or offensive manner."},{"m":"Cock is another word for stopcock."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If a gun is cocked, that means it is prepared to fire."},{"m":"(transitive) If something is cocked, that means it is turned on its side or sideways.","e":"He cocked his hat in farewell."}]}]},"porn":{"h":"porn","i":"/pɔːn/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"porn is a short word, meaning pornography","e":"My girlfriend and I like to watch porn."}]}]},"porno":{"h":"porno","i":"/ˈpɔːnəʊ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-porno.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A porno is a film that has pornography.","e":"My girlfriend and me want to make a porno in our bedroom."}]}]},"gangbang":{"h":"gangbang","i":"/ˈɡæŋ.bæŋ/","a":"en-au-gangbang.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A gangbang is sex involving more than two people.","e":"My girlfriend and I want to invite you to our home for a gangbang."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you gangbang, you have sex with a group of people. Usually this means you are one of several men having sex with the same woman.","e":"We gangbanged her all night."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you gangbang, you do crimes as part of a gang. Most often, this means doing violence (hurting people). Also, it can mean just being part of a criminal gang.","e":"If you keep gangbanging you will die young."}]}]},"gangbanger":{"h":"gangbanger","i":"/ˈɡæŋˌbæŋə/","a":"en-us-gangbanger.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A gangbanger is someone who is part of a gang of young, violent criminals.","e":"The gangbangers shot members of another gang from their car."},{"m":"A gangbanger is a person who visits a gangbang.","e":"My girlfriend and I invited Brad to our house, because he was a gangbanger, and we are all gangbangers."}]}]},"strip":{"h":"strip","i":"/strɪp/","a":"en-us-strip.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A strip is a narrow, long piece of something.","e":"A few strips of paper are used for making a chain."},{"m":"(countable) A strip (or a strip mall) is a road with many shops."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you strip, you remove your clothes.","e":"My girlfriend will strip, and Brad and me will watch and become excited."},{"m":"(transitive) If you strip paper from a wall, you remove it."}]}]},"boner":{"h":"boner","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"; If you get a boner, then your penis becomes hard.","e":"My girlfriend asked me what it was like to have a boner because she's never had one."},{"m":"; A boner is another word for a stupid person.","e":"I guess I'm the smartest person in the class because I'm the only one who isn't a complete boner."}]}]},"stroke":{"h":"stroke","i":"/strəʊk/","a":"en-us-stroke.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A stroke is when blood stops coming into your brain.","e":"I had a stroke after running so hard."},{"m":"A stroke is an action of hitting something lightly."},{"m":"A stroke is the person who sets the speed in a rowing crew.","e":"After years of training he was made stroke in the Oxford University crew."},{"m":"A stroke is something that happens without warning.","e":"She had a stroke of good luck playing cards and won 20 dollars."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you stroke something, you touch something with the hand, and move your hand gently up it.","e":"She stroked his hair lovingly."}]}]},"underpants":{"h":"underpants","i":"/ˈʌndə(r)ˌpænts/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-underpants.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Underpants are clothes which you wear under your trousers or skirt.","e":"Brad took off his underpants."}]}]},"cunnilingus":{"h":"cunnilingus","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Cunnilingus is where a woman's vagina is touched by somebody's lips or tongue, for sexual pleasure.","e":"I performed cunnilingus on my girlfriend, and she enjoyed it."}]}]},"ejaculate":{"h":"ejaculate","i":"/ɪˈdʒæk.jʊ.leɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-ejaculate (verb).wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you ejaculate, you eject semen from your penis.","e":"Men usually ejaculate during orgasm."}]}]},"horny":{"h":"horny","i":"/ˈhɔ.ni/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-horny.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is horny, it has a horn.","e":"Rhinos are horny animals."},{"m":"If you are horny, you want to have sex.","e":"You make me rather horny when you take off a lot of your clothes."}]}]},"vibrator":{"h":"vibrator","i":"/vaɪˈbreɪtə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-vibrator.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A vibrator is a machine that vibrates; they are sometimes used for massages or to increase sexual pleasure.","e":"She used her vibrator to try to have an orgasm."}]}]},"fisting":{"h":"fisting","i":"/ˈfɪstɪŋ/","a":"en-au-fisting.ogg","l":"fist","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Fisting is a sex act where the entire hand is placed inside the vagina or anus.","e":"This vibrator wasn't enough, so Brad started fisting her ass."}]}]},"critic":{"h":"critic","i":"/ˈkrɪt.ɪk/","a":"en-us-critic.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A critic is someone whose job is to judge and report about the quality of something such as books, movies, wine, restaurants, etc.","e":"Every critic in New York was at the theatre for the opening."},{"m":"(countable) A critic is someone who talks or writes about the problems with something.","e":"He is one of the most outspoken critics against the practice."}]}]},"decent":{"h":"decent","i":"/ˈdiː.sənt/","a":"en-us-decent.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is decent, it is good enough.","e":"He urged all workers to demand a living wage and decent working conditions."},{"m":"If someone is decent, they are usually honest, kind, and fair.","e":"A decent society does not ignore poor people."},{"m":"If someone is decent, they are wearing enough clothes to be seen by other people.","e":"Excuse me, may I come in? Are you decent?"}]}]},"armour":{"h":"armour","i":"/ˈɑːr.mɚ/","a":"en-us-armor.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Armour is something you wear to protect your body.","e":"It was a story of a girl who dressed in armour and fought great battles."},{"m":"(uncountable) Armour may be used to describe the hard protective layer of an animal's body.","e":"A stegosaur's body is protected by its armour."}]}]},"declare":{"h":"declare","i":"/dɪkleə(r)/","a":"en-us-declare.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you declare something, you say it publicly or officially.","e":"She was declared the winner Sunday, with 54 percent of the vote."},{"m":"(transitive) If you declare what you own or earn, you officially list those things."},{"m":"(transitive) If you declare something, you say it publicly or officially."}]}]},"decorate":{"h":"decorate","i":"/ˈdɛkəreɪt/","a":"en-us-decorate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you decorate something, you make it look nice, usually by putting something pretty on it or painting it.","e":"We're going to decorate our Christmas tree tonight."},{"m":"(transitive) If x decorates y, y looks nice because x is on or close to it.","e":"In her room, photos decorated the white walls."},{"m":"(transitive) If you decorate someone, you give them a medal for doing something brave or good.","e":"He was decorated by the president for saving several men who had been shot."}]}]},"zookeeper":{"h":"zookeeper","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A zookeeper is someone who works at a zoo and takes care of the animals.","e":"We saw the zookeeper feeding the tiger in the zoo."}]}]},"yearbook":{"h":"yearbook","i":"/ˈjɪəbʊk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-yearbook.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A book which is written newly every year, with information in it"},{"m":"(countable) A book which is written every year about a school, with information and pictures about the students in the school.","e":"Will you sign your name in my yearbook?"}]}]},"signature":{"h":"signature","i":"/ˈsɪɡnətʃə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-signature.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) When a person writes their own name with a pen, they are writing their signature.","e":"The cheque has to have my signature on it, or the bank won't give you money for it."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A signature item of a place is something that is unique and indicates the identity of it.","e":"My signature dish is herb-crusted lamb."}]}]},"easter":{"h":"Easter","i":"/ˈis.tɚ/","a":"en-us-easter.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Easter is a Christian celebration, usually in April, of the day when Christians believe that Jesus of Nazareth came back from the dead.","e":"Our church will start Easter Sunday with a sunrise service at 6 a.m."}]}]},"efficient":{"h":"efficient","i":"/ɪˈfɪʃənt/","a":"en-us-efficient.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is efficient, it can do a lot but uses very little time, energy, money, etc.","e":"He wastes a lot of time talking, and isn't very efficient at work."}]}]},"yawn":{"h":"yawn","i":"/jɔːn/","a":"en-us-yawn.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When someone yawns, they open their mouth wide and sometimes stretch their arms.","e":"I can see that you're tired, because you keep yawning."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A yawn is the action of yawning.","e":"He did three big yawns, then stood up to go upstairs to bed."}]}]},"zoology":{"h":"zoology","i":"/zəʊˈɒlədʒi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-zoology.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Zoology is the science of learning about animals.","e":"He likes animals, so he wants to study zoology in university."}]}]},"wasted":{"h":"wasted","i":"/ˈweɪstɪd/","a":"en-us-wasted.ogg","l":"waste","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"We say that something is wasted if it was not used, but should have been used, and now it can't be used.","e":"We forgot to put the food in the refrigerator to keep it cold, so it was all wasted."},{"m":"Someone is wasted if they are very thin, as if they didn't eat enough.","e":"She doesn't look healthy. She looks wasted."}]}]},"refrigerator":{"h":"refrigerator","i":"/rɪˈfrɪd͡ʒəˌreɪtə/","a":"en-us-refrigerator.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A refrigerator is a machine which keeps food cold.","e":"Put the milk in the refrigerator so it will stay fresh."}]}]},"writer":{"h":"writer","i":"/raɪtə/","a":"en-us-writer.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A writer is a person who writes books or other things that people read.","e":"She works as a writer for a magazine."}]}]},"magazine":{"h":"magazine","i":"/mæɡ.əˈziːn/","a":"en-us-magazine.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A magazine is a publication that is printed regularly (usually weekly or monthly), and is often about a topic like a hobby, sports or news.","e":"I get the magazine Cosmopolitan every month. I really like the articles it has on fashion and love."},{"m":"(countable) A magazine is a small building that an army keeps weapons in.","e":"We don't sleep too close to the magazine because it has things in it that can explode."},{"m":"(countable) A magazine is removable container that feeds ammunition into a gun."}]}]},"worker":{"h":"worker","i":"/ˈwɝkɚ/","a":"En-us-worker.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A worker is a person who works, usually for money.","e":"The workers are putting a new roof on the house."}]}]},"workhouse":{"h":"workhouse","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A place for poor people to live, but they have to work."},{"m":"(countable) A jail where the prisoners have to work."}]}]},"woodwork":{"h":"woodwork","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Woodwork is things made by people out of wood.","e":"Don't throw water at the wall: it will hurt the woodwork."}]}]},"windpipe":{"h":"windpipe","i":"/ˈwɪndpaɪp/","a":"en-au-windpipe.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The part of a person's throat that air goes through when they breathe.","e":"I can feel the cold air deep in my windpipe."},{"m":"Any tube that air goes through.","e":"There are windpipes to bring the warm air from the furnace to the whole house."}]}]},"defence":{"h":"defence","i":"/dɛˈfɛns/","a":"en-us-defence.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Defence is the process of protecting.","e":"The secretary of defence met with the president at the White House."},{"m":"(uncountable) In a court case, the defence is the person who was accused of a crime together with their lawyer.","e":"His defence lawyers say that Honecker did not shoot the gun."},{"m":", The defence is the players who are supposed to stop the other team from scoring points.","e":"I wasn't very satisfied with the play of our offense, but our defence played great."}]}]},"governor":{"h":"governor","i":"/gʌvənɚ/","a":"en-us-governor.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A governor is a person who leads a place like a state or territory.","e":"The king appointed a new governor for the province."}]}]},"rhododendron":{"h":"Rhododendron","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Rhododendron is a large genus of flowering plants. Most of them display their flowers quite aptly."}]}]},"morina":{"h":"Morina","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Morina is a genus of the Caprifoliaceae family."}]}]},"fig":{"h":"fig","i":"/fɪɡ/","a":"en-us-fig.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A fig is a tree that grows mainly in the tropics and produces fruit."},{"m":"(countable) A fig is a pear-shaped fruit with many small seeds that comes from a fig tree."}]}]},"jasmine":{"h":"jasmine","i":"/ˈdʒæzmɪn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-jasmine.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A plant of the genus that has fragrant white or yellow flowers."},{"m":"The perfume made from these plants."},{"m":"(uncountable) A yellow color."}]}]},"motor":{"h":"motor","i":"/ˈməʊtə/","a":"en-us-motor.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A machine that changes energy into motion (movement)."},{"m":"(countable) A motor car, or automobile."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you motor, you travel in a [[#Noun|motor]] vehicle."}]}]},"nasty":{"h":"nasty","i":"/ˈnaː.sti/","a":"en-us-nasty.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is nasty it is very bad.","e":"I've never camped in the Italian Alps, but the weather must be pretty nasty there."}]}]},"solution":{"h":"solution","i":"/səˈl(j)uːʃən/","a":"en-us-solution.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A solution is an answer to a problem.","e":"The solution to the math problem 4+3 is 7."},{"m":"(countable) A solution is a liquid that has something dissolved in it.","e":"The student made a solution by mixing salt and water."}]}]},"butcher":{"h":"butcher","i":"/ˈbʊtʃ.ə(r)/","a":"en-us-butcher.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A butcher is a person who slices and sells meat.","e":"I went to the butcher to buy a steak."},{"m":"(countable) A butcher is a person who kills and prepares animals as meat.","e":"The butcher killed the pig and made bacon."},{"m":"(countable) A butcher is a person who kills in a violent way.","e":"was a crazy butcher of women."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you butcher an animal, you kill it and cut it up into meat.","e":"He had to butcher the sheep to get chops for his dinner."}]}]},"delegate":{"h":"delegate","i":"/ˈdɛlɪɡət/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-delegate (noun).wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A delegate is a person authorized to act as representative for one or more other people, especially at a conference or in government.","e":"He's attending the Democratic Convention as a delegate from the great state of Ohio."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you delegate a job or the power to do that job, it is yours, but you give it to someone in a lower position.","e":"As more decisions on more complicated matters have to be made, more power has to be delegated to lower-ranking personnel."}]}]},"waterfall":{"h":"waterfall","i":"/ˈwɔːtəfɔːl/","a":"en-us-waterfall.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A waterfall is a part of a river where water falls down.","e":"Don't swim too close to the waterfall!"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If something waterfalls, it falls like a waterfall."}]}]},"whisky":{"h":"whisky","i":"/ˈwɪski/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-عُثمان (Middle river exports)-whiskey.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Whisky is a drink with alcohol in it. It is made from grain."}]}]},"delight":{"h":"delight","i":"/dəˈlaɪt/","a":"en-us-delight.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Delight is the feeling of being very happy.","e":"There was a real sense of relief when the war ended and great delight that it had stopped."},{"m":"(countable) A delight is something that makes you feel very happy.","e":"Your children are such a delight."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you delight somebody, you make them feel very happy.","e":"We delight in the beauty around us."}]}]},"pour":{"h":"pour","i":"/pɔː/","a":"en-us-pour.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you pour something, you let it flow from one place to another."},{"m":"If something pours, it flows fast from one place to another."},{"m":"If the rain pours, it is raining hard (a lot of rain is coming down fast)."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The act of pouring.","e":"Now that's a good pour of beer."}]}]},"hardly":{"h":"hardly","i":"/ˈhɑːdli/","a":"en-us-hardly.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Not much, very little.","e":"I hardly noticed the pain."},{"m":"Not at all.","e":"I'm hardly to give you medicine."}]},{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"You can use hardly show you disagree a lot and are upset.","e":"Would I do that? Hardly!"}]}]},"whitewash":{"h":"whitewash","i":"/ˈwaɪtwɒʃ/","a":"en-au-whitewash.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Someone whitewashes something when they try to hide anything that is wrong with it and try to make it look good.","e":"He tried to whitewash the thing that happened last year so that he could be elected President."},{"m":"Someone whitewashes something when they paint it with a white paint.","e":"She whitewashed the wall."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The action of whitewashing something.","e":"They didn't tell you the whole story. That was just a whitewash."},{"m":"White paint.","e":"He covered the fence with whitewash."}]}]},"zeros":{"h":"zeros","l":"zero","q":"noun"},"demand":{"h":"demand","i":"/dɪˈmɑːnd/","a":"en-us-demand.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(singular), (uncountable) Demand for something is how much people want of it.","e":"Right now we have a supply in excess of demand for crude oil, gasoline, and heating oil."},{"m":"(countable) A demand is what you say must be done or what you say you must have, a strong request.","e":"His demands for new machines were ignored by the company."},{"m":"(usually plural) The demands on someone or something are the difficult things that are required of them.","e":"I can't deal with all these demands on my time."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you demand something, you say strongly that you must receive it or that it must happen.","e":"The Lebanese Foreign Minister demanded an immediate withdrawal of Israeli forces."},{"m":"(transitive) If x demands y, x needs or requires y.","e":"The problems are real and they demand attention."}]}]},"well-off":{"h":"well-off","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When you are well-off, you have enough money or other things to be able to live well.","e":"Both parents have worked for many years, so now they're very well-off."}]}]},"yellowish":{"h":"yellowish","i":"/ˈjeləʊɪʃ/","a":"en-us-yellowish.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is yellowish it is a color that is like yellow but is not yellow.","e":"The grass is looking yellowish because there has been no rain."}]}]},"vegetable":{"h":"vegetable","i":"/ˈvedʒtəbl/","a":"en-us-vegetable.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A vegetable a part of a plant that is good for eating. This does not include grain, but does include leaves, stems, and roots. Some fruits are also called vegetables but most are not."},{"m":"; (often offensive) A vegetable is a person who has much damage to the brain and does not wake-up."}]}]},"vegetables":{"h":"vegetables","i":"/ˈved͡ʒtəbəlz/","a":"en-us-vegetables.ogg","l":"vegetable","q":"noun"},"outer":{"h":"outer","i":"/ˈaʊtɚ/","a":"en-us-outer.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"An outer thing is on the outside or toward the outside.","e":"The outer layer of the coat is water proof, the inner layer keeps you warm."}]}]},"fruits":{"h":"fruits","a":"en-us-fruits.ogg","l":"fruit","q":"noun"},"motherboard":{"h":"motherboard","i":"/ˈmʌðɚˌbɔrd/","a":"en-us-motherboard.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The motherboard is the main part of a computer."}]}]},"lexicon":{"h":"lexicon","i":"/ˈlɛk.sɪ.kən/","a":"en-us-lexicon.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The lexicon of a particular subject is all the words and phrases that are used for it."}]}]},"telescope":{"h":"telescope","i":"/ˈtɛləskəʊp/","a":"en-us-telescope.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A telescope is a machine that is made up of a tube and lenses that is used to make things that are far away look larger. Often used by astronomers.","e":"Freddy used the telescope to see the mountain fifty miles away."}]}]},"lens":{"h":"lens","i":"/lɛnz/","a":"en-us-lens.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A lens is a specially shaped piece of glass that is used in cameras or telescopes to bend light."}]}]},"earthquake":{"h":"earthquake","i":"/ˈɜːθkweɪk/","a":"en-us-earthquake.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An earthquake is a natural event that causes the ground to shake up and down, and sometimes, may destroy buildings.","e":"The earthquake ripped a crack in the road and destroyed half of the building that I live in."}]}]},"parole":{"h":"parole","i":"/pəˈroːl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-parole.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Parole is the supervised release of a prisoner before the completion of their sentence."}]}]},"perpendicular":{"h":"perpendicular","i":"/ˌpɜː.pənˈdɪk.jə.lə(r)/","a":"en-us-perpendicular.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Perpendicular means \"at a ninety degree angle to\"."}]}]},"picnic":{"h":"picnic","i":"/ˈpɪknɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-picnic.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A picnic is a meal that is eaten outside, usually not at home or at a restaurant."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If someone picnics, they eat a picnic."}]}]},"popularity":{"h":"popularity","i":"/ˌpɒp.jəˈlær.ɪ.ti/","a":"en-us-popularity.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Popularity is the quality of being either well-liked or common.","e":"Brad Pitt's popularity as an actor has never been higher."}]}]},"prequel":{"h":"prequel","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A prequel is a story, book, or movie that comes or takes place before another one."}]}]},"pretence":{"h":"pretence","i":"/ˈpriːtɛns/","a":"en-us-pretense.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Pretence is the behaviour to make people believe what the pretender is doing."}]}]},"protogalaxy":{"h":"protogalaxy","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A protogalaxy is gas and dust in outer space that will change into a galaxy."}]}]},"nomination":{"h":"nomination","i":"/ˌnɑmɪˈneɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-nomination.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Nomination The process of suggesting a candidate for either election to an office, or of a political party selecting its candidate for presidency.","e":"Senator Barry Goldwater won the Republican Party's nomination for President of the United States of America in 1964 after competing with and defeating Governor Nelson Rockefeller of New York for it."},{"m":"The giving of an honor or award."}]}]},"wrist":{"h":"wrist","i":"/rɪst/","a":"en-us-wrist.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Someone's wrist is a part of their body where the arm joins the hand.","e":"You can move your hand up and down while keeping your arm in one place by bending your wrist."}]}]},"wedge":{"h":"wedge","i":"/wɛdʒ/","a":"en-au-wedge.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A wedge is something in the shape of a triangle that someone pushes under a door or into a crack.","e":"You can break a log into two pieces by knocking a wedge into it with a hammer."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you wedge something, you force it into a narrow gap.","e":"He had wedged the package between the wall and the back of the sofa."}]}]},"lesson":{"h":"lesson","i":"/ˈlɛsn̩/","a":"en-us-lesson.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A lesson is a time when something is taught.","e":"The Math lesson starts at 5:12."}]}]},"tire":{"h":"tire","i":"/ˈtaɪ̯ə(r)/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-tyre.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A tire is the outer part of a car wheel. It is usually made of rubber","e":"The front tire on my bike needs changing."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To become tired.","e":"Running makes me tire."}]}]},"pit":{"h":"pit","i":"/ˈpɪt/","a":"en-us-pit.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pit is a big hole in the ground.","e":"Don't fall in the pit!"},{"m":"(countable) A pit is a large seed such as that in a peach.","e":"The peach pit is hard. Don't bite it."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If something is pitted, it is marked with little hollows.","e":"The metal is pitted due to the exposure to acid rain."},{"m":"(transitive) If you pit something, you remove the seed from a fruit.","e":"Please pit the cherries before giving it to the children."}]}]},"beef":{"h":"beef","i":"/biːf/","a":"en-uk-beef.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Beef is the meat of a cow.","e":"We're having ground beef for dinner."},{"m":"(countable) A beef is a complaint: something that bothers someone, or that someone keeps getting a little angry about.","e":"One of my biggest beefs about this place is that you can't get a drink of water here."}]}]},"calendar":{"h":"calendar","i":"/ˈkæl.ən.də/","a":"en-us-calendar.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A calendar is a system of measuring time.","e":"The Chinese new year is different from the western new year because the Chinese use a lunar calendar."},{"m":"(countable) A calendar is list of all the days with their dates, usually for one full year.","e":"Write his birthday on the calendar hanging on the wall."}]}]},"chorus":{"h":"chorus","i":"/ˈkɔːrəs/","a":"en-us-chorus.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A chorus is a musical group, usually in four parts.","e":"He is in the school chorus."},{"m":"(countable) A chorus is the part of a song that is repeated.","e":"I don't know many of the words, but I can sing the chorus."}]}]},"visa":{"h":"visa","i":"/ˈviː.zə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-visa.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A visa is a document that gives you permission to enter a country.","e":"His visa expired today."}]}]},"viewpoint":{"h":"viewpoint","i":"/ˈvjuː.pɔɪnt/","a":"en-us-viewpoint.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Your viewpoint is your idea of what the world is like.","e":"Jimmy's viewpoint of the war was that is was wrong."}]}]},"wreck":{"h":"wreck","i":"/ˈrɛk/","a":"en-us-wreck.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A wreck is what is left of something that has been seriously damaged.","e":"The wreck of the Titanic was found on the bottom of the sea."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you wreck something, you harm it beyond repair."}]}]},"wholesale":{"h":"wholesale","i":"/ˈhoʊlseɪl/","a":"en-us-wholesale.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Wholesale is the sale of a large amount of an item to other businesses."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"In a large quantity at a cheap price."}]}]},"well-being":{"h":"well-being","i":"/wɛlˈbiː.ɪŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Persent101-well-being.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Your well-being is your state of happiness and health.","e":"He was in a state of well-being."}]}]},"kennel":{"h":"kennel","i":"/ˈkɛnəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-kennel.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A kennel is a doghouse.","e":"On hot days the dog goes into the kennel to get out of the sun."},{"m":"(countable) A kennel is a place where pets are kept when their owners are away.","e":"The kennel at the hotel was open from 9 to 5 so guests could keep their pets safe."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you kennel something, you keep a pet in a kennel.","e":"We have to kennel our two dogs whenever we go on vacation."}]}]},"keeper":{"h":"keeper","i":"/ˈkiːpə/","a":"en-us-keeper.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A keeper is someone who keeps something.","e":"He is the keeper of the keys."}]}]},"quantity":{"h":"quantity","i":"/ˈkwɑn(t)ɪti/","a":"en-us-quantity2.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A quantity is the number or amount of something.","e":"The quantity of the candies in the tin has dropped to 17."}]}]},"quotient":{"h":"quotient","i":"/ˈkwəʊʃənt/","a":"en-us-quotient.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A quotient is the result you get when you divide one number by another.","e":"A quotient of 2 is given when you divide 6 by 3."}]}]},"victim":{"h":"victim","i":"/ˈvɪktɪm/","a":"en-us-victim.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A victim is the person hurt in a crime.","e":"The family of the murder victim cried."}]}]},"victory":{"h":"victory","i":"/ˈvɪkt(ə)ri/","a":"en-us-victory.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A victory is the act or result of winning.","e":"The had no clear victory."}]}]},"greets":{"h":"greets","l":"greet","q":"verb"},"jug":{"h":"jug","i":"/d͡ʒʌɡ/","a":"en-au-jug.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A jug is a large container for liquids, usually with a wide mouth.","e":"The jug is full of milk."}]}]},"jury":{"h":"jury","i":"/ˈdʒʊəri/","a":"en-us-jury.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A jury is a group of people who decide a court case's result.","e":"The jury says the person is not guilty."}]}]},"jam":{"h":"jam","i":"/ˈdʒæm/","a":"en-gb-Jam (fruit spread).ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Jam is a sweet spread for bread made by boiling fruit.","e":"I want blueberry jam on my toast."},{"m":"(countable) A jam is a hard situation.","e":"I'm in a jam right now. Can you help me out?"},{"m":"(countable) A jam can be a blockage; congestion.","e":"I'll be late to work today because of that traffic jam."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you jam something, it means you get it stuck or blocked in a small area; congested.","e":"The stapler that I was using jammed. Can I use that one please?"},{"m":"If you jam your finger or toe, it means it hit it against another object."},{"m":"If you jam, it means that you play music."},{"m":"If you jam a signal, it means you block it from broadcasting."}]}]},"inferno":{"h":"inferno","i":"/ɪnˈfɝnoʊ/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An inferno is a large fire.","e":"Nobody escaped the inferno last night."}]}]},"defense":{"h":"defense","i":"/dɛˈfɛns/","a":"en-us-defence.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Defense is the process of protecting.","e":"The secretary of defense met with the president at the White House."},{"m":"(uncountable), In a court case, the defense is the person who was accused of a crime together with their lawyer.","e":"His defense lawyers say that Honecker did not shoot the gun."},{"m":", The defense is the players who are supposed to stop the other team from scoring points.","e":"I wasn't very satisfied with the play of our offense, but our defense played great."}]}]},"velocity":{"h":"velocity","i":"/vəˈlɒsəti/","a":"en-us-velocity.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Something's velocity is how fast it is moving.","e":"The bullet comes out of a gun at a high velocity."},{"m":"In physics, velocity is how fast something is moving in a particular direction.","e":"The velocity of the car was 10 metres per second to the north-east when it hit the tree."}]}]},"violin":{"h":"violin","i":"/ˌvaɪəˈlɪn/","a":"en-us-violin.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A violin is a musical instrument played by moving a bow across the strings.","e":"He has played the violin from when he was 6 years old."}]}]},"jeweler":{"h":"jeweler","i":"/ˈdʒuːələ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-jeweler.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A jeweler is someone who sells jewels.","e":"The jeweler said that the jewel was worth $1000."}]}]},"joiner":{"h":"joiner","i":"/ˈdʒɔɪnɚ/","a":"en-us-joiner.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A joiner something that joins two or more things together.","e":"Glue is a good joiner."}]}]},"jealous":{"h":"jealous","i":"/ˈdʒɛləs/","a":"en-us-jealous.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"To be jealous is to want something someone else has.","e":"I'm jealous of all your free time."}]}]},"jerk":{"h":"jerk","i":"/d͡ʒɜːk/","a":"en-us-jerk.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A jerk is a quick action.","e":"The door opened with a jerk."},{"m":"(countable) A jerk is a bad or mean person.","e":"He's such a jerk for not holding the door open for his grandma."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you jerk, you make a quick action.","e":"He jerked the door open."}]}]},"meow":{"h":"meow","i":"/miˈaʊ̯/","a":"en-au-meow.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A meow is the crying sound a cat makes.","e":"He heard a soft meow from behind the sofa."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If a cat meows, it makes a crying sound.","e":"The cat meowed when it was fed."}]}]},"navy":{"h":"navy","i":"/ˈneɪvi/","a":"en-us-navy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Navy is a dark blue color.","e":"He wore a navy shirt."},{"m":"(countable) A navy is a country's water army.","e":"He was a member of the navy."}]}]},"handkerchief":{"h":"handkerchief","i":"/ˈhæŋkətʃiːf/","a":"en-us-handkerchief.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A handkerchief is a cloth, usually white, used to clean one's face of sweat, etc.","e":"The gentleman had a handkerchief in his jacket pocket."}]}]},"everything":{"h":"everything","i":"/ˈɛvriθɪŋ/","a":"en-us-everything.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"Everything is all that exists, or all things in one area.","e":"If you win, you get everything: the car and all other prizes you won!"}]}]},"sunlight":{"h":"sunlight","i":"/ˈsʌnˌlaɪt/","a":"en-us-sunlight.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Sunlight is light from the sun.","e":"The sunlight is bright today."}]}]},"runaway":{"h":"runaway","i":"/ˈrʌnəweɪ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-runaway.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A runaway is someone who runs away from home.","e":"The little boy tried to become a runaway, but only went to the end of the block before coming home."}]}]},"tradesman":{"h":"tradesman","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A tradesman is someone who does a skilled job by hand, such as carpenter or electrician.","e":"We need to hire a tradesman to install the toilet."}]}]},"manhole":{"h":"manhole","i":"/mænhəʊl/","a":"en-us-manhole.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A manhole is a large hole in a street that is used to get to the sewers.","e":"Don't fall in the manhole!"}]}]},"downfall":{"h":"downfall","i":"/ˈdaʊnfɔːl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-downfall.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A downfall is a quick fall from power or riches.","e":"The empire's downfall happened when the emperor was killed with out a prince."}]}]},"looking-glass":{"h":"looking-glass","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A looking-glass is a fancy name for a mirror","e":"Alice looked into the looking-glass so she could see herself."}]}]},"lighthouse":{"h":"lighthouse","i":"/ˈlaɪthaʊs/","a":"en-us-lighthouse.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A lighthouse is a tower built on the shore to light the way to shore for ships.","e":"The lighthouse is showing the way."}]}]},"landmark":{"h":"landmark","i":"/ˈlændmɑrk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-landmark.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A landmark is a large object used to know where one is.","e":"Big Ben is a landmark in London."}]}]},"landslip":{"h":"landslip","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A landslip is when dirt and mud fall down a hill or cliff, like a landslide.","e":"Beware very wet hills, because a landslip might happen."}]}]},"everywhere":{"h":"everywhere","i":"/ɛv.ri.(h)weə(r)/","a":"en-us-everywhere.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(at, to, or in) every place","e":"I've looked everywhere else, so it must be here."}]}]},"evergreen":{"h":"evergreen","i":"/ˈɛvəɡriːn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-evergreen.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An evergreen is a tree that stays green all year.","e":"The pine tree is an evergreen."}]}]},"earthwork":{"h":"earthwork","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An earthwork is a construction made of earth, especially to protect an area from attack.","e":"The existing walls and buildings were linked together with earthworks."}]}]},"earring":{"h":"earring","i":"/ˈɪrɪŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-earring.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An earring is a piece of jewelry worn on the ear.","e":"She wore golden earrings."}]}]},"nursery":{"h":"nursery","i":"/ˈnɝs(ə)ri/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-nursery.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A nursery is place where are kept."},{"m":"(countable) A nursery is place where young plants are grown before planting (putting in the ground) outdoors."}]}]},"nurseries":{"h":"nurseries","l":"nursery","q":"noun"},"restful":{"h":"restful","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is restful it helps your rest or relax."}]}]},"tune":{"h":"tune","i":"/tjuːn/","a":"en-uk-tune.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A tune is a piece or part of music; a song or melody.","e":"Whistling a happy tune can chase the blues away."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you tune a musical instrument you make it so it will play the right notes.","e":"You tune it by making the strings tighter or looser."},{"m":"(transitive) If you tune a radio you set the frequency to get a certain signal."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you tune-in to a show, you watch it or listen to it."}]}]},"melody":{"h":"melody","i":"/ˈmelədi/","a":"en-us-melody.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A melody is the sequence of notes (sounds) that make a piece of music."}]}]},"melodies":{"h":"melodies","l":"melody","q":"noun"},"update":{"h":"update","i":"/ˈʌpdeɪt/","a":"en-us-update.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"New information.","e":"He gave me an update on the situation in New York"},{"m":"A change from older information to newer information.","e":"I have a couple of updates to install on your laptop"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you update something, you add changes to make it newer times or new ideas."}]}]},"vestigial":{"h":"vestigial","i":"/vɛˈstɪd͡ʒɪəl/","a":"en-us-vestigial.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is vestigial, it is left over or almost gone.","e":"A horse has a vestigial toe on the side of its leg."}]}]},"valve":{"h":"valve","i":"/ˈvælv/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-valve.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A valve is part of a tube that lets liquid or gas go through one way but stops it from going through the other way.","e":"There are four valves in the heart that let blood go in one direction but stop it from going in the other direction."},{"m":"(countable) A valve is part of a tube that someone can open or close to let water or other things go through.","e":"Open this valve to let water go through the pipe."}]}]},"vitamin":{"h":"vitamin","a":"en-us-vitamin.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A vitamin is something that we need in our food to help us live, that is different from protein, carbohydrates, fat or minerals.","e":"The vitamins are named with the letters A, B, C, D, E and K."}]}]},"knocker":{"h":"knocker","a":"en-au-knocker.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A knocker is something that knocks or is used to knock.","e":"I used the knocker on the door."},{"m":"; (usually plural) Knockers are woman's breasts.","e":"Man, she has a hot set of knockers."}]}]},"breast":{"h":"breast","i":"/brɛst/","a":"en-us-breast.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (usually plural) A woman's breasts are the two soft round parts on her chest.","e":"She learned that the cancer in her breast had spread to her leg."},{"m":"(countable) Your breast is the area between your neck and your belly.","e":"A warm feeling spread in his breast as she stepped closer."},{"m":"(uncountable) Breast is bird meat that comes from the front of the bird","e":"Skinless, boneless chicken breasts have very little flavour when grilled."},{"m":"(countable) A bird's breast is the front of its body below its head.","e":"The Robin is a plump bird with bright orange-red breast."},{"m":"(countable) The breast of a jacket or shirt is the part that goes over your breast.","e":"My father pulled a cigarette from his breast pocket."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you breast a hill, mountain, etc., you come to the top of it.","e":"He breasted the hill and saw the town in front of him."}]}]},"breasts":{"h":"breasts","i":"/brɛsts/","a":"en-us-breasts.ogg","l":"breast","q":"noun"},"democrat":{"h":"democrat","i":"/ˈdɛməkræt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-democrat.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A democrat is someone who supports democracy.","e":"As a democrat, it angered him that there had been no vote."}]}]},"peking":{"h":"Peking","i":"/piːˈkɪŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Peking.wav","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Peking is the old name for Beijing."}]}]},"endearment":{"h":"endearment","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Naomi Persephone Amethyst (NaomiAmethyst)-endearment.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An endearment is something someone says to show love to someone else.","e":"I like it when he says \"darling\" and \"honey\" and other words of endearment to me."}]}]},"copyright":{"h":"copyright","i":"/ˈkɑpiˌraɪt/","a":"en-us-copyright.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Copyright is the rights given to a creator to protect their work from other uses.","e":"copyright is held by."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you copyright something, you register its copyright.","e":"She copyrighted her book."}]}]},"resided":{"h":"resided","l":"reside","q":"verb"},"postmaster":{"h":"postmaster","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A postmaster is the head of the post office.","e":"Benjamin Franklin was the first postmaster general of the U.S."}]}]},"residing":{"h":"residing","l":"reside","q":"verb"},"resides":{"h":"resides","l":"reside","q":"verb"},"ablest":{"h":"ablest","i":"/eɪ.bləst/","l":"able","q":"adjective"},"accounts":{"h":"accounts","i":"/əˈkaʊnts/","a":"en-us-accounts.ogg","l":"account","q":"noun"},"acids":{"h":"acids","l":"acid","q":"noun"},"acts":{"h":"acts","i":"/ækts/","a":"en-us-acts.ogg","l":"act","q":"verb"},"acted":{"h":"acted","i":"/ˈæk.tɪd/","a":"en-us-acted.ogg","l":"act","q":"verb"},"additions":{"h":"additions","i":"/əˈdɪʃənz/","a":"en-us-additions.ogg","l":"addition","q":"noun"},"agreements":{"h":"agreements","l":"agreement","q":"noun"},"advertisements":{"h":"advertisements","l":"advertisement","q":"noun"},"adjustments":{"h":"adjustments","l":"adjustment","q":"noun"},"amusements":{"h":"amusements","l":"amusement","q":"noun"},"angled":{"h":"angled","l":"angle","q":"verb"},"angling":{"h":"angling","l":"angle","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A kind of fishing."}]}]},"angrier":{"h":"angrier","l":"angry","q":"adjective"},"angriest":{"h":"angriest","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-NaomiAmethyst-angriest.wav","l":"angry","q":"adjective"},"upright":{"h":"upright","i":"/ˈʌpraɪt/","a":"en-us-upright.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A long or flat thing is upright when it is at a right angle to the ground. That means that one end is exactly above the other end.","e":"There was so much heavy ice on the tree that the whole tree bent down close to the ground, but after the ice melted, the tree went back upright again."},{"m":"Having good morals; doing good things.","e":"I trust her: she is a perfectly upright person."}]}]},"animals":{"h":"animals","i":"/ˈæn.ɪ.məlz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Back ache-animals.wav","l":"animal","q":"noun"},"answers":{"h":"answers","i":"/ˈæn.sɚz/","l":"answer","q":"noun"},"answered":{"h":"answered","i":"/ænsɜːd/","a":"en-us-answered.ogg","l":"answer","q":"verb"},"answering":{"h":"answering","i":"/ˈɑːn.sə.rɪŋ/","a":"en-us-answering.ogg","l":"answer","q":"verb"},"apparatuses":{"h":"apparatuses","l":"apparatus","q":"noun"},"apples":{"h":"apples","l":"apple","q":"noun"},"approvals":{"h":"approvals","l":"approval","q":"noun"},"arched":{"h":"arched","i":"/ɑrt͡ʃt/","a":"en-us-arched.ogg","l":"arch","q":"verb"},"arching":{"h":"arching","l":"arch","q":"verb"},"arguments":{"h":"arguments","i":"/ˈɑːɡjʊmənts/","a":"en-us-arguments.ogg","l":"argument","q":"noun"},"armies":{"h":"armies","i":"/ˈɑr.miz/","a":"en-us-armies.ogg","l":"army","q":"noun"},"arms":{"h":"arms","i":"/ɑrmz/","a":"en-us-arms.ogg","l":"arm","q":"noun"},"armed":{"h":"armed","i":"/ɑrmd/","a":"en-us-armed.ogg","l":"arm","q":"verb"},"arming":{"h":"arming","l":"arm","q":"verb"},"arts":{"h":"arts","i":"/ɑrts/","a":"en-us-arts.ogg","l":"art","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The arts the study of languages, literature, philosophy, and the arts."}]}]},"gunpowder":{"h":"gunpowder","i":"/ˈɡʌnˌpaʊdə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-gunpowder.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Gunpowder is a black powder that burns very quickly or explodes.","e":"The army ran out of gunpower."}]}]},"attempts":{"h":"attempts","i":"/əˈtɛmpts/","a":"en-us-attempts.ogg","l":"attempt","q":"noun"},"attempted":{"h":"attempted","i":"/əˈtɛmptɪd/","a":"en-us-attempted.ogg","l":"attempt","q":"verb"},"attempting":{"h":"attempting","i":"/əˈtɛmp.tɪŋ/","a":"en-us-attempting.ogg","l":"attempt","q":"verb"},"attractions":{"h":"attractions","a":"en-us-attractions.ogg","l":"attraction","q":"noun"},"authorities":{"h":"authorities","l":"authority","q":"noun"},"automatics":{"h":"automatics","l":"automatic","q":"noun"},"awakes":{"h":"awakes","l":"awake","q":"verb"},"awoke":{"h":"awoke","i":"/əˈwəʊk/","a":"en-us-awoke.ogg","l":"awake","q":"verb"},"awoken":{"h":"awoken","l":"awake","q":"verb"},"awaking":{"h":"awaking","l":"awake","q":"verb"},"postman":{"h":"postman","a":"En-us-postman.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A postman is someone who delivers mail.","e":"The postman dropped off the mail."}]}]},"policeman":{"h":"policeman","i":"/pəˈliːsmən/","a":"en-us-policeman.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A policeman is someone who works for the police.","e":"The policeman carried a gun."}]}]},"babies":{"h":"babies","i":"/ˈbeɪbiz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Persent101-babies.wav","l":"baby","q":"noun"},"firearm":{"h":"firearm","i":"/ˈfaɪ.ərɑrm/","a":"en-us-firearm.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A firearm is a gun.","e":"Soldiers used the firearms to shot the other side."}]}]},"desperate":{"h":"desperate","i":"/ˈdɛsp(ə)rət/","a":"en-us-desperate.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A desperate action is one that is dangerous or likely to fail, but one that you take because you have no choice.","e":"During the fire, some people tried to break through a wall in a desperate attempt to survive."},{"m":"A desperate situation is a very bad one.","e":"Trucks have not been able to reach the village for weeks, and the food situation appears desperate."},{"m":"If someone is desperate, they have a very strong want or need for something.","e":"We're desperate for money to help these people."}]}]},"determine":{"h":"determine","i":"/dɪ'tɜːmɪn/","a":"en-ca-determine.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If A determines the outcome of B, A causes B to occur in a certain way."},{"m":"(transitive) If you determine something, you conclude it by or.","e":"The autopsy will determine her cause of death."}]}]},"objected":{"h":"objected","l":"object","q":"verb"},"postmark":{"h":"postmark","i":"/ˈpəʊs(t)mɑːk/","a":"en-us-postmark.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A postmark is a stamp that shows where a letter was sent from.","e":"The postcard had an Orlando postmark on it."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you postmark something, you add a postmark to it.","e":"This letter was postmarked on the 23rd of January."}]}]},"pincushion":{"h":"pincushion","i":"/ˈpɪnˌkʊʃ(ə)n/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-pincushion.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pincushion is something you stick pins in when you are not using them.","e":"The pincushion was shaped like a hedgehog."}]}]},"plaything":{"h":"plaything","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A plaything is a toy or something else you play with.","e":"The computer has turned into a plaything."}]}]},"chemist":{"h":"chemist","i":"/ˈkɛmɪst/","a":"en-us-chemist.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A chemist is someone whose job is related to chemistry","e":"He became a chemist at age 30."},{"m":"(countable) A chemist is another name for a pharmacist (a person who gives medicine to make people feel better).","e":"The chemist gave us medicine."}]}]},"medication":{"h":"medication","i":"/mɛdɪˈkeɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-medication.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The medicine(s) that a patient takes.","e":"The patient forgot to take his medication."}]}]},"grayish":{"h":"grayish","i":"/ˈɡreɪ.ɪʃ/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is grayish, then it is moderately gray."}]}]},"diet":{"h":"diet","i":"/ˈdaɪət/","a":"en-us-diet.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A diet is the food that an animal, person, or group usually eats.","e":"Several studies have suggested that high-fat diets can directly increase the risk of this cancer."},{"m":"(countable) A diet is a controlled set of foods chosen for health purposes.","e":"Oprah Winfrey wasn't the only celebrity who transformed her body through exercise and diet last year."},{"m":"(countable) A diet of something is something your experience regularly, usually something negative.","e":"The Daily News has served up a steady diet of local news."},{"m":"(countable) A diet is a council of political leaders.","e":"This week, the Japanese parliament, the Diet, considered but did not act on a resolution apologizing for Pearl Harbor."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you diet, you limit the food you eat to lose weight.","e":"Weight lost by dieting alone almost never stays off."}]}]},"impatient":{"h":"impatient","i":"/ɪmˈpeɪʃənt/","a":"en-us-impatient.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Does not like to be delayed."},{"m":"Cannot wait to begin something."}]}]},"backs":{"h":"backs","i":"/bæks/","a":"en-us-backs.ogg","l":"back","q":"noun"},"backed":{"h":"backed","i":"/bækt/","a":"en-us-backed.ogg","l":"back","q":"verb"},"backing":{"h":"backing","i":"/ˈbæk.ɪŋ(ɡ)/","a":"en-us-backing.ogg","l":"back","q":"verb"},"chemists":{"h":"chemists","l":"chemist","q":"noun"},"entities":{"h":"entities","l":"entity","q":"noun"},"inland":{"h":"inland","i":"/ˈɪnlənd/","a":"en-us-inland.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"To be inland is to be away from the ocean.","e":"The town was built near an inland sea."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If something is or moves inland it moves away from the ocean towards the middle of the land.","e":"A terrible storm moved inland off the Pacific Ocean."}]}]},"undo":{"h":"undo","i":"/ʌnˈduː/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-undo.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you undo an action, you reverse it.","e":"We can undo the damage to the system."},{"m":"(transitive) If you undo something, unfasten it.","e":"Could you undo my buckle for me?"},{"m":"If you undo something in a computer program, you reverse a change done in the file.","e":"I had to undo all of the bad edits that my naughty little brother made."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An undo is a function in a computer program that can reverse a change done to a file.","e":"This program can do up to 20 undoes."}]}]},"undoes":{"h":"undoes","l":"undo","q":"verb"},"undid":{"h":"undid","i":"/ʌn'dɪd/","l":"undo","q":"verb"},"undone":{"h":"undone","i":"/ʌn'dɒn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-undone.wav","l":"undo","q":"verb"},"inlet":{"h":"inlet","i":"/ˈɪnlət/","a":"en-us-inlet.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An inlet is a body water that is has land on all but one side, like a bay or a cove.","e":"We went fishing in the inlet."}]}]},"anybody":{"h":"anybody","i":"/ˈɛn.i.ːbɒd.i/","a":"en-us-anybody.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"Any one person out of a number of people.","e":"I don't care who comes. Anybody will do."}]}]},"undergrowth":{"h":"undergrowth","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Undergrowth is smaller plants growing in a forest: bushes, which are smaller than the trees and which grow under the trees.","e":"She couldn't walk very fast in this forest, because she had to push through the undergrowth."}]}]},"lands":{"h":"lands","i":"/lændz/","a":"en-us-lands.ogg","l":"land","q":"noun"},"waters":{"h":"waters","i":"/ˈwɔː.təz/","a":"en-us-waters.ogg","l":"water","q":"noun"},"cyclone":{"h":"cyclone","i":"/ˈsaɪ.kloʊn/","a":"en-us-cyclone.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A storm with air going around in a circle in the same direction as the Earth. If it's big, it might be called a hurricane or typhoon.","e":"A cyclone blew part of the roof off the house."}]}]},"cyclones":{"h":"cyclones","l":"cyclone","q":"noun"},"hurricane":{"h":"hurricane","i":"/ˈhʌrɪkən/","a":"en-us-ne-hurricane.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hurricane is a type of tropical cyclone, which is a storm system that has a low pressure center, many thunderstorms, and strong winds.","e":"The hurricane was very dangerous when it hit land."}]}]},"hurricanes":{"h":"hurricanes","l":"hurricane","q":"noun"},"thunderstorm":{"h":"thunderstorm","i":"/ˈθʌn.dɚˌstɔrm/","a":"en-ca-thunderstorm.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A thunderstorm is a type of weather with rain, wind, lightning and thunder.","e":"Don't stand under a tree in a thunderstorm, because lightning might hit you."}]}]},"thunderstorms":{"h":"thunderstorms","l":"thunderstorm","q":"noun"},"tornado":{"h":"tornado","i":"/tɔː(r)ˈneɪ.dəʊ/","a":"en-us-tornado.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A strong wind that moves in a circle with a cloud shaped like a funnel.","e":"A tornado destroyed our house."}]}]},"tornadoes":{"h":"tornadoes","l":"tornado","q":"noun"},"typhoon":{"h":"typhoon","i":"/taɪˈfuːn/","a":"en-us-typhoon.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A typhoon is a kind of storm in the Western Pacific Ocean."}]}]},"typhoons":{"h":"typhoons","l":"typhoon","q":"noun"},"dig":{"h":"dig","i":"/dɪg/","a":"en-us-dig.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you dig a hole, you make it bigger by removing material, usually using a shovel or your hands.","e":"You will need to dig the hole larger than the roots of the tree you want to plant."},{"m":"If you dig somewhere for something, you look there for it.","e":"He dug in his pocket for another ten cents."},{"m":"(transitive) If you dig something, you take it out of the ground, usually using a shovel.","e":"Can you go out to the garden and dig some onions?"},{"m":"(intransitive) If you dig up dirt on someone, you find hidden information that can hurt them.","e":"Before the trial, they dug up a bunch of dirt on her."},{"m":"(transitive) If you dig a hole for yourself, you make your own problems.","e":"Mr. Bush has dug himself a hole that he can't get out of."},{"m":"(transitive), If you dig something, you like it.","e":"I really dig your new car."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A dig is a short negative comment about someone.","e":"In a dig at the teacher, he said she's lucky to be right even once in a while."},{"m":"(countable) A dig is a place where people are digging.","e":"There's a dig in the middle of the city where they found some old bones."},{"m":"Your digs is the room that you ren