pleased you were able to make it to my show."}]}]},"pleasing":{"h":"pleasing","i":"/ˈpliːzɪŋ/","a":"en-us-pleasing.ogg","l":"please","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is pleasing, it gives pleasure, happiness, enjoyment or gratification."}]}]},"bidding":{"h":"bidding","l":"bid","q":"verb"},"bidden":{"h":"bidden","l":"bid","q":"verb"},"twelves":{"h":"twelves","l":"twelve","q":"noun"},"humiliations":{"h":"humiliations","l":"humiliation","q":"noun"},"syllables":{"h":"syllables","l":"syllable","q":"noun"},"follows":{"h":"follows","i":"/ˈfɒl.əʊz/","a":"en-us-follows.ogg","l":"follow","q":"verb"},"followed":{"h":"followed","i":"/ˈfɒl.əʊd/","a":"en-us-followed.ogg","l":"follow","q":"verb"},"followings":{"h":"followings","l":"following","q":"noun"},"shaded":{"h":"shaded","l":"shade","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is shaded, it is in the shade.","e":"The bench is shaded."}]}]},"breaks":{"h":"breaks","i":"/breɪks/","a":"en-us-breaks.ogg","l":"break","q":"verb"},"broke":{"h":"broke","i":"/brəʊk/","a":"en-us-broke.ogg","l":"break","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"(informal) If you're broke, you don't have money.","e":"Sorry, I can't do anything this weekend, I'm broke."},{"m":"(informal)."}]}]},"breaking":{"h":"breaking","i":"/ˈbreɪkɪŋ/","a":"en-us-breaking.ogg","l":"break","q":"verb"},"behinds":{"h":"behinds","l":"behind","q":"noun"},"sized":{"h":"sized","l":"size","q":"verb"},"sizing":{"h":"sizing","l":"size","q":"verb"},"marries":{"h":"marries","l":"marry","q":"verb"},"marrying":{"h":"marrying","i":"/ˈmæriɪŋ/","l":"marry","q":"verb"},"friendlier":{"h":"friendlier","l":"friendly","q":"adjective"},"friendliest":{"h":"friendliest","l":"friendly","q":"adjective"},"friendlies":{"h":"friendlies","l":"friendly","q":"noun"},"banked":{"h":"banked","l":"bank","q":"verb"},"banking":{"h":"banking","i":"/ˈbæŋkɪŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-banking.wav","l":"bank","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Banking is the job or business of managing a bank."}]}]},"panned":{"h":"panned","l":"pan","q":"verb"},"panning":{"h":"panning","l":"pan","q":"verb"},"zooms":{"h":"zooms","l":"zoom","q":"verb"},"zoomed":{"h":"zoomed","l":"zoom","q":"verb"},"zooming":{"h":"zooming","i":"/ˈzuːmɪŋ/","l":"zoom","q":"verb"},"bodies":{"h":"bodies","l":"body","q":"noun"},"sheds":{"h":"sheds","l":"shed","q":"noun"},"sexes":{"h":"sexes","a":"en-us-sexes.ogg","l":"sex","q":"noun"},"mid":{"h":"mid","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"In the middle.","e":"The seat can be connected on the mid or rear position."},{"m":"A mid vowel is produced with the tongue relaxed in the middle of the mouth."}]}]},"frightening":{"h":"frightening","i":"/ˈfraɪtənɪŋ/","a":"en-uk-frightening.ogg","l":"frighten","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is frightening, it causes fear, it is scary.","e":"The ghost ride was so frightening that I screamed the entire time."}]}]},"model":{"h":"model","i":"/ˈmɒdl̩/","a":"en-us-model.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A model is a something that is made to look or act like something else, usually being smaller or simpler than the original.","e":"Mathematical models can greatly help researchers understand the behavior of real systems."},{"m":"(countable) A model is an example of something, a goal, or a way to do something.","e":"Both men and women who had public athletic role models during childhood were more likely to play sports at a higher level."},{"m":"(fashion) (art); (countable) A model is a person who puts on clothes, glasses, jewelery, etc. to show them at shows and in photographs or who poses for paintings or sculptures.","e":"High-fashion runway models are typically 5 foot 10 inches or taller."},{"m":"(countable) A model is a kind or design of car or other machine.","e":"The wireless phone will be installed in future models from GM, Toyota and Honda."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you model clothes, jewelery, etc., you wear them to show them at shows and in photographs."},{"m":"(transitive) If you model an action, you show how it is done.","e":"Parents should model the behavior they want without forcing or controlling the child."},{"m":"(transitive) If you model x on y, you try to make x like y.","e":"There's a youth baseball field modeled after Fenway Park in the old Memorial Stadium."},{"m":"(transitive) If you model something, you make a smaller, simpler copy of it.","e":"He's trying to model the human thought process on the computer."}]}]},"counts":{"h":"counts","a":"en-us-counts.ogg","l":"count","q":"verb"},"counted":{"h":"counted","a":"en-us-counted.ogg","l":"count","q":"verb"},"shedding":{"h":"shedding","l":"shed","q":"verb"},"frightens":{"h":"frightens","l":"frighten","q":"verb"},"galaxies":{"h":"galaxies","l":"galaxy","q":"noun"},"fats":{"h":"fats","l":"fat","q":"noun"},"chile":{"h":"Chile","i":"/ˈtʃɪl.iː/","a":"en-us-Chile.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Chile is a country in South America. Its capital is Santiago.","e":"I was born in Chile."}]}]},"lonelier":{"h":"lonelier","l":"lonely","q":"adjective"},"loneliest":{"h":"loneliest","l":"lonely","q":"adjective"},"crybabies":{"h":"crybabies","l":"crybaby","q":"noun"},"wheelchairs":{"h":"wheelchairs","l":"wheelchair","q":"noun"},"reduces":{"h":"reduces","l":"reduce","q":"verb"},"mortgage":{"h":"mortgage","i":"/ˈmɔː.ɡɪdʒ/","a":"en-us-mortgage.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mortgage is a loan for the purpose of paying for a house, apartment, building, etc.","e":"For five-year adjustable-rate mortgages, interest rates rose to 5.58 percent."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you mortgage your home, you borrow money and promise to give up your home if you can't pay back the money.","e":"Henderson's parents mortgaged their house in Cuthbert to buy a piano for the front parlor."},{"m":"(transitive) If you mortgage your future, you enjoy something now even though it will cause problems in the future.","e":"We're mortgaging our children's future instead of investing in it."}]}]},"impulses":{"h":"impulses","l":"impulse","q":"noun"},"enigma":{"h":"enigma","i":"/əˈnɪgmə/","a":"En-us-enigma.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An enigma is something that is mysterious, puzzling, or cannot be explained.","e":"That man is an enigma; I never know what he's going to do next."},{"m":"An enigma is a riddle, or a difficult problem."}]}]},"hawked":{"h":"hawked","l":"hawk","q":"verb"},"hawking":{"h":"hawking","l":"hawk","q":"verb"},"enigmas":{"h":"enigmas","l":"enigma","q":"noun"},"sleazy":{"h":"sleazy","i":"/sliː.zi/","a":"en-us-sleazy.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something, usually a person, that is dishonest, corrupt, shabby, dirty, and/or vulgar.","e":"That man insulted me. He is so sleazy."},{"m":"Low quality.","e":"That quilt has sleazy lining."}]}]},"riddle":{"h":"riddle","i":"/ˈrɪdəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-riddle.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A riddle is something that is, hard to solve, or difficult to define.","e":"That question is quite a riddle."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To fill with holes.","e":"The shots from his gun began to riddle the target."},{"m":"To be filled with.","e":"Your argument is riddled with errors."},{"m":"To solve or answer a riddle or question.","e":"Riddle me this...., meaning Answer the following question."},{"m":"To put something through a sieve.","e":"You have to riddle the gravel before you lay it on the road."}]}]},"riddles":{"h":"riddles","l":"riddle","q":"noun"},"xenophobia":{"h":"xenophobia","i":"/zɛnəˈfəʊbɪə/","a":"en-ca-xenophobia.oga","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The fear of strangers or foreigners.","e":"That man was afraid of the new member beacuse he had xenophobia."}]}]},"xenophobias":{"h":"xenophobias","l":"xenophobia","q":"noun"},"motorway":{"h":"motorway","i":"/ˈməʊtəweɪ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-motorway.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A motorway is a large, high-speed road.","e":"She pulled in at a motorway service station and decided on lunch."}]}]},"decreases":{"h":"decreases","l":"decrease","q":"noun"},"bicycles":{"h":"bicycles","l":"bicycle","q":"noun"},"decreased":{"h":"decreased","l":"decrease","q":"verb"},"decreasing":{"h":"decreasing","l":"decrease","q":"verb"},"muck":{"h":"muck","i":"/mʌk/","a":"en-us-muck.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Muck is any unclean wet substance.","e":"The soap sat in a soupy muck in the holder."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you muck something up, you make a mess of it or you cause problems."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you muck around, you play, or you are not serious."},{"m":"If you muck out a place where animals like cows or pigs live, you clean out the animals' waste."}]}]},"enigmatic":{"h":"enigmatic","i":"/ˌɛnɪɡˈmætɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-enigmatic.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something, or someone, that is an enigma."},{"m":"Something, or someone, that is mysterious, puzzling, or cannot be explained.","e":"That man is enigmatic; I never know what he's going to do next."}]}]},"dog-ear":{"h":"dog-ear","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To fold the corner of a book's page.","e":"I don't like to lend my books to Lisa because she dog-ears the pages."}]}]},"dog-ears":{"h":"dog-ears","l":"dog-ear","q":"verb"},"dog-earing":{"h":"dog-earing","l":"dog-ear","q":"verb"},"consults":{"h":"consults","l":"consult","q":"noun"},"consulted":{"h":"consulted","l":"consult","q":"verb"},"consulting":{"h":"consulting","l":"consult","q":"verb"},"xenophobe":{"h":"xenophobe","i":"/ˈzinəfoʊb/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-xenophobe.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A xenophobe is someone who has xenophobia."},{"m":"(countable) A xenophobe is someone who has the fear of strangers or foreigners.","e":"That xenophobe was afraid of the new member."}]}]},"khakis":{"h":"khakis","l":"khaki","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Pants made from khaki material.","e":"Should I wear my khakis or my jeans with this shirt?"}]}]},"xenophobes":{"h":"xenophobes","l":"xenophobe","q":"noun"},"respects":{"h":"respects","a":"en-us-respects.ogg","l":"respect","q":"verb"},"respected":{"h":"respected","i":"/rɪˈspɛktɪd/","a":"en-us-respected.ogg","l":"respect","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is respected, they have or deserve respect.","e":"He is respected by his peers for his outstanding writing abilities."}]}]},"fearful":{"h":"fearful","i":"/ˈfɪəfəl/","a":"en-us-fearful.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Fearful means a person who has a fear of someone or something; to be scared of someone or something.","e":"I am fearful of monsters."}]}]},"phobia":{"h":"phobia","i":"/ˈfəʊ.bi.ə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-phobia.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A phobia is a strong fear of something.","e":"I have a phobia of spiders."}]}]},"phobias":{"h":"phobias","l":"phobia","q":"noun"},"multiply":{"h":"multiply","i":"/ˈmʌltɪplaɪ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-multiply (verb).wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you multiply x by y, you add x to itself y times.","e":"Nine multiplied by eleven is ninety nine (9\\times 11 = 99)."},{"m":"If something multiplies, more and more of it exist.","e":"Problems have multiplied since the beginning of the week."},{"m":"(intransitive) If living things multiply, the have babies, or they make more of themselves.","e":"The bugs seem to be multiplying."}]}]},"rhythms":{"h":"rhythms","l":"rhythm","q":"noun"},"gangbanged":{"h":"gangbanged","l":"gangbang","q":"verb"},"weddings":{"h":"weddings","l":"wedding","q":"noun"},"multiplies":{"h":"multiplies","l":"multiply","q":"verb"},"multiplied":{"h":"multiplied","l":"multiply","q":"verb"},"multiplying":{"h":"multiplying","l":"multiply","q":"verb"},"naughty":{"h":"naughty","i":"/ˈnɔːti/","a":"en-us-naughty.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If somebody, especially a child or a pet, is naughty, they are not good.","e":"Oh! Go on you naughty boy. Silly thing. Get out."},{"m":"If an adult is naughty, they are a little bit bad, often in a fun or sexual way.","e":"He just kept putting wine in my glass. It's quite naughty, isn't it?"}]}]},"negotiate":{"h":"negotiate","i":"/nəˈgəʊ.ʃi.eɪt/","a":"en-us-negotiate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you negotiate with somebody about something, you each give your own ideas and try to reach an agreement.","e":"Owens and his boss are still negotiating."},{"m":"(transitive) If you negotiate a difficult area, you successfully move over or through it.","e":"Drivers still consider it a challenge to negotiate the long, desolate stretches of road with few services."}]}]},"neighbour":{"h":"neighbour","i":"/'neɪbə/","a":"En-us-neighbour.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A neighbour is someone who lives close to a person's home.","e":"My neighbour has an annoying cat."}]}]},"unhappy":{"h":"unhappy","i":"/ʌnˈhæpi/","a":"en-us-unhappy.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is unhappy, they are angry, sad, or depressed; to be upset.","e":"There are many unhappy people in the hospital."}]}]},"useable":{"h":"useable","i":"/ˈjuː.zə.bəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-usable.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is useable, then it can be used."}]}]},"dumps":{"h":"dumps","i":"/dʌmps/","l":"dump","q":"noun"},"hadiths":{"h":"hadiths","l":"hadith","q":"noun"},"encounters":{"h":"encounters","l":"encounter","q":"noun"},"beings":{"h":"beings","i":"/ˈbiːɪŋz/","a":"en-us-beings.ogg","l":"being","q":"noun"},"satisfy":{"h":"satisfy","i":"/ˈsætɪsfaɪ/","a":"en-us-satisfy.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you satisfy something, you fulfill it or meet its needs.","e":"Will the results of the investigation satisfy you?"}]}]},"lifts":{"h":"lifts","a":"en-us-lifts.ogg","l":"lift","q":"noun"},"moons":{"h":"moons","l":"moon","q":"noun"},"unflavored":{"h":"unflavored","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is unflavored, then it does not have any flavor."}]}]},"unflavoured":{"h":"unflavoured","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is unflavoured, then it does not have any flavour."}]}]},"members":{"h":"members","a":"en-us-members.ogg","l":"member","q":"noun"},"mayors":{"h":"mayors","l":"mayor","q":"noun"},"preliminaries":{"h":"preliminaries","l":"preliminary","q":"noun"},"boycotts":{"h":"boycotts","l":"boycott","q":"noun"},"workhouses":{"h":"workhouses","l":"workhouse","q":"noun"},"neighboring":{"h":"neighboring","a":"en-us-neighboring.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"American standard spelling of neighbouring"}]}]},"neighbouring":{"h":"neighbouring","a":"en-us-neighboring.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is neighbouring something, then it is next to it or near it.","e":"France is a country that is neighbouring Spain."}]}]},"objectives":{"h":"objectives","l":"objective","q":"noun"},"restraints":{"h":"restraints","l":"restraint","q":"noun"},"rooms":{"h":"rooms","i":"/ruːmz/","a":"en-us-rooms.ogg","l":"room","q":"noun"},"crowns":{"h":"crowns","a":"en-us-crowns.ogg","l":"crown","q":"noun"},"regards":{"h":"regards","a":"en-us-regards.ogg","l":"regard","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Regards are a kind of greeting used to pass on to another person."},{"m":"Regards are a way of signing letters or emails."}]}]},"crowning":{"h":"crowning","i":"/ˈkraʊnɪŋ/","l":"crown","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is crowning, it is at the height of what it can be.","e":"That crowning accomplishment was the best you could hope for."}]}]},"neons":{"h":"neons","l":"neon","q":"noun"},"taxes":{"h":"taxes","i":"/ˈtæksɪz/","a":"en-us-taxes.ogg","l":"tax","q":"noun"},"energies":{"h":"energies","a":"en-us-energies.ogg","l":"energy","q":"noun"},"bagels":{"h":"bagels","l":"bagel","q":"noun"},"sickos":{"h":"sickos","l":"sicko","q":"noun"},"sickoes":{"h":"sickoes","l":"sicko","q":"noun"},"admirers":{"h":"admirers","i":"/ədˈmaɪ.rɚz/","a":"en-us-admirers.ogg","l":"admirer","q":"noun"},"humours":{"h":"humours","l":"humour","q":"noun"},"opportunities":{"h":"opportunities","a":"en-us-opportunities.ogg","l":"opportunity","q":"noun"},"chances":{"h":"chances","i":"/ˈt͡ʃænsɪz/","a":"en-us-chances.ogg","l":"chance","q":"noun"},"occasionally":{"h":"occasionally","i":"/əˈkeɪʒənəli/","a":"en-us-occasionally.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something happens occasionally, then it happens sometimes, but not often.","e":"I occasionally get nosebleeds when I fly."}]}]},"breaches":{"h":"breaches","l":"breach","q":"noun"},"ammunitions":{"h":"ammunitions","l":"ammunition","q":"noun"},"kiloton":{"h":"kiloton","i":"/ˈkɪləˌtʌn/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A kiloton is a unit that is used to determine how strong an explosion caused by a bomb is. The unit is based on how many thousand tons of TNT would be needed to make the same size explosion."}]}]},"kilotons":{"h":"kilotons","l":"kiloton","q":"noun"},"adder":{"h":"adder","i":"/ˈædɚ/","a":"en-au-adder.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An adder is a short, rather massive poisonous snake with long front teeth that poison its victims by biting them.","e":"Don't walk in the bush unprotected, you may be bitten by an adder!"},{"m":"Adder can also stand for any poisonous snake.","e":"Certain poisonous snakes in North America are called adders though they are not true adders."},{"m":"Someone or something that adds. Usually a part (circuit) of computer chip.","e":"The CPU contained extra adders to increase speed."}]}]},"usable":{"h":"usable","i":"/ˈjuː.zə.bəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-usable.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is usable, then it can be used."}]}]},"nil":{"h":"nil","i":"/nɪl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-nil.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Nil is zero.","e":"Their chances of meeting again are almost nil."}]}]},"northern":{"h":"northern","i":"/ˈnɔrðɚn/","a":"en-us-northern.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is northern, it is in, from, or about the north.","e":"We couldn't go south, so we looked for a more northern route."}]}]},"unification":{"h":"unification","i":"/ˌjuːnɪfɪˈkeɪʃn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Wodencafe-unification.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Unification is when things come together or join each other to become one.","e":"The unification of East Germany and West Germany happened in 1990."}]}]},"unifications":{"h":"unifications","l":"unification","q":"noun"},"dishonest":{"h":"dishonest","i":"/dɪˈsɒnɪst/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-dishonest.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone or something is dishonest, they lie or keep secrets."},{"m":"If someone or something is dishonest, they are not honest.","e":"That man is dishonest because he lied about his age."}]}]},"mania":{"h":"mania","i":"/ˈmeɪniə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-mania.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Mania is when someone is crazy. Their mind is not working right.","e":"Drugs are one way to treat mania."},{"m":"Mania is when a person is obsessed with or feels very, very strongly about something.","e":"You're spending so much time and energy on this, it isn't normal: it's mania."}]}]},"manias":{"h":"manias","l":"mania","q":"noun"},"swallows":{"h":"swallows","l":"swallow","q":"noun"},"antiheroes":{"h":"antiheroes","l":"antihero","q":"noun"},"forces":{"h":"forces","i":"/ˈfɔr.sɪz/","a":"en-us-forces.ogg","l":"force","q":"noun"},"trays":{"h":"trays","l":"tray","q":"noun"},"concepts":{"h":"concepts","l":"concept","q":"noun"},"antiquarian":{"h":"antiquarian","i":"/ˌæn.tɪˈkwɛr.i.ən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-antiquarian.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is antiquarian, then it has something to do with or old things, usually books."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An antiquarian is a person who buys or sells old books."}]}]},"nought":{"h":"nought","i":"/nɔːt/","a":"en-us-nought.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Nought is zero.","e":"What's three quarters as a decimal? Nought point seven five, right?"}]}]},"darkness":{"h":"darkness","i":"/ˈdɑːknəs/","a":"en-us-darkness.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The state of being dark; no light."},{"m":"(uncountable)."},{"m":"(countable) The product of being dark."}]}]},"antiquarians":{"h":"antiquarians","l":"antiquarian","q":"noun"},"murders":{"h":"murders","l":"murder","q":"noun"},"whistles":{"h":"whistles","l":"whistle","q":"noun"},"contras":{"h":"contras","l":"contra","q":"noun"},"webs":{"h":"webs","l":"web","q":"noun"},"thoughts":{"h":"thoughts","i":"/θɔːts/","a":"en-us-thoughts.ogg","l":"thought","q":"noun"},"oblige":{"h":"oblige","i":"/əˈblaɪdʒ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-oblige.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive); If you are obliged to do something, a law, rule, or situation forces you to do it.","e":"She felt obliged to make conversation before leaving."},{"m":"If you oblige someone, you do something that they want you to do.","e":"We asked three experts they obliged with very clear answers."},{"m":"(formal) If you tell someone that you'd be obliged if they did something, you're asking them to do it."},{"m":"If you say, \"much obliged\", you are thanking somebody for something."}]}]},"observe":{"h":"observe","i":"/əbˈzɜːv/","a":"en-us-observe.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you observe something, you see or notice it.","e":"No problem behavior was observed among these students."},{"m":"If you observe something, you watch it carefully.","e":"The moon is really too bright to observe through a telescope."},{"m":"(transitive); (formal) If you observe something, usually a fact, you say or write it.","e":"When we were talking, he also observed that some new problems had come up."},{"m":"(transitive) If you observe a law or agreement, you follow it.","e":"Israel agreed to start moving out of West Bank towns if the Palestinians observed a cease-fire."},{"m":"(transitive) If you observe a special day, you do the traditional things that are done on that day, especially in a religion.","e":"Some 1 billion people around the world will do something to observe the anniversary of the first Earth Day in 1970."}]}]},"blasphemy":{"h":"blasphemy","a":"en-ca-blasphemy.oga","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An act of cursing God or sacred things."},{"m":"Not having respect for God or sacred things."},{"m":"Saying that you are like God."}]}]},"trumpets":{"h":"trumpets","l":"trumpet","q":"noun"},"scales":{"h":"scales","i":"/skeɪlz/","a":"en-us-scales.ogg","l":"scale","q":"noun"},"pianos":{"h":"pianos","l":"piano","q":"noun"},"geese":{"h":"geese","a":"En-us-geese.ogg","l":"goose","q":"noun"},"occupy":{"h":"occupy","i":"/ˈɒkjʊpaɪ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-occupy.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If something occupies a space, it is there, lives there, or belongs there.","e":"Her personal apartment has two bedrooms. In New York this is sometimes more space than entire families occupy."},{"m":"(transitive) If a country or army occupies another country, it controls it.","e":"We have requested the removal of armed forces from occupied in the recent war."},{"m":"(transitive) If you occupy a position, you do a job, or have a job title.","e":"Women are seeking positions that were formerly occupied by men."},{"m":"If your mind is occupied, you are thinking of something and can't concentrate on other things.","e":"I like to keep their minds occupied and keep them busy and out of trouble."},{"m":"If something occupies you or your time, it keeps you busy.","e":"Before, I ate constantly; but now, I find other things to occupy my time."}]}]},"boilerplate":{"h":"boilerplate","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Wodencafe-boilerplate.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Boilerplate is a standard text that can be reused in different pieces of writing without being changed much.","e":"You should put this boilerplate on the front of the survey you give, so that people will know why they are filling it out."}]}]},"broiler":{"h":"broiler","i":"/ˈbrɔɪlə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Wodencafe-broiler.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A broiler is an oven for broiling."},{"m":"(countable) A broiler is a chicken that is good for broiling."}]}]},"broil":{"h":"broil","i":"/brɔɪl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-broil.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you broil something you cook it with strong, direct heat."},{"m":"If something broils, it is cooked by strong, direct heat."},{"m":"If you broil, you are very hot."}]}]},"mandolin":{"h":"mandolin","i":"/ˌmandoˈlɪn/","a":"en-us-mandolin.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mandolin is a small musical instrument with eight strings; there are four sets of two strings."},{"m":"(countable) A mandolin is a kitchen tool used for slicing vegetables (usually spelled mandoline)"}]}]},"packet":{"h":"packet","i":"/ˈpæk.ɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-packet.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A packet is a small container that goods are sold in.","e":"Many seed companies sell mixed packets for summer and winter gardening."},{"m":"(countable) A packet is a small container sent in the mail.","e":"Participants were mailed a packet containing the survey and a cover letter."},{"m":"; (countable) A packet is a unit of information sent between two computers."}]}]},"broilers":{"h":"broilers","l":"broiler","q":"noun"},"packets":{"h":"packets","l":"packet","q":"noun"},"foots":{"h":"foots","i":"/fʊts/","l":"foot","q":"verb"},"footed":{"h":"footed","i":"/ˈfʊtɪd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-footed.wav","l":"foot","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is footed, it has a foot."}]}]},"footing":{"h":"footing","i":"/ˈfʊtɪŋ/","a":"en-us-footing.ogg","l":"foot","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A footing is a place for you to stand; a foundation.","e":"I almost lost my footing and fell down the hill."},{"m":"A footing is a safe position.","e":"As soon as he had obtained a footing at court, the charms of his manner... made him a favorite. –."}]}]},"footings":{"h":"footings","l":"footing","q":"noun"},"blog":{"h":"blog","i":"/blɒɡ/","a":"en-us-blog.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable); (internet) A blog is a personal website that is used as an online journal (short for weblog).","e":"Check out my blog at blogwebsite.net."},{"m":"(countable) One entry in a blog.","e":"I'll be talking about my thoughts on the new action movie in my next blog."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you blog about something, you write a blog about it."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you blog, you write a blog.","e":"My friend Mary blogs daily, but I only blog once or twice a week."}]}]},"parliament":{"h":"parliament","i":"/ˈpɑːlɪmənt/","a":"en-us-parliament.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Parliament is the elected people who work together to make and debate a country's laws.","e":"She was elected to parliament and is now the assistant minister for the environment."}]}]},"pat":{"h":"pat","i":"/pæt/","a":"en-us-pat.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you pat something, you touch it gently a number of times with your open hand.","e":"Rinse the meat with water then pat dry."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A gentle touch or tap."},{"m":"(countable) The sound made by the gentle touch."}]}]},"doubled":{"h":"doubled","l":"double","q":"verb"},"doubling":{"h":"doubling","l":"double","q":"verb"},"websites":{"h":"websites","l":"website","q":"noun"},"web-sites":{"h":"web-sites","l":"web-site","q":"noun"},"restricts":{"h":"restricts","l":"restrict","q":"verb"},"restricted":{"h":"restricted","i":"/rɪˈstrɪktɪd/","a":"en-us-restricted.ogg","l":"restrict","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is restricted, it is limited."},{"m":"If something is restricted, it is available only to certain people.","e":"You can't come in here! This is a restricted area!"},{"m":"One of the levels of the secrecy of an official document."}]}]},"restricting":{"h":"restricting","l":"restrict","q":"verb"},"reinforcing":{"h":"reinforcing","l":"reinforce","q":"verb"},"railroaded":{"h":"railroaded","l":"railroad","q":"verb"},"railroading":{"h":"railroading","l":"railroad","q":"verb"},"thankful":{"h":"thankful","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are thankful for or about something, you want to say \"thank you\" because of it."},{"m":"If you are thankful for or about something, you are grateful or full of appreciation.","e":"I am very thankful for your kindness."}]}]},"patch":{"h":"patch","i":"/pætʃ/","a":"en-us-patch.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A patch is a small area that is a different colour or material from the area around it.","e":"He'd come every other Sunday afternoon to mow the little patch of grass in front of the house."},{"m":"(countable) A patch is a piece of material that is sewn on clothes to cover a hole or for decoration.","e":"She was wearing a jacket with patches on the elbows."},{"m":"; (countable) A patch is a computer program that fixes another program."},{"m":"(countable) A patch is a length of time.","e":"Her business has hit a rough patch lately."},{"m":"(countable) An eye patch is something to cover an eye."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you patch clothing, a tire, etc., you put a piece of material on it to cover a hole."},{"m":"If you patch a number of things together, you put them together, but not very well.","e":"She was patching together part-time jobs and trying to pay the rent."},{"m":"If you patch something up, you fix it.","e":"She patched a hole in the wall where it looked like John's head had hit it."}]}]},"sections":{"h":"sections","a":"en-us-sections.ogg","l":"section","q":"noun"},"sectioned":{"h":"sectioned","l":"section","q":"verb"},"sectioning":{"h":"sectioning","l":"section","q":"verb"},"supposes":{"h":"supposes","l":"suppose","q":"verb"},"quotes":{"h":"quotes","l":"quote","q":"verb"},"quoted":{"h":"quoted","a":"en-us-quoted.ogg","l":"quote","q":"verb"},"quoting":{"h":"quoting","l":"quote","q":"verb"},"invests":{"h":"invests","l":"invest","q":"verb"},"invested":{"h":"invested","a":"en-us-invested.ogg","l":"invest","q":"verb"},"investing":{"h":"investing","l":"invest","q":"verb"},"telephones":{"h":"telephones","l":"telephone","q":"noun"},"telephoned":{"h":"telephoned","l":"telephone","q":"verb"},"telephoning":{"h":"telephoning","l":"telephone","q":"verb"},"cleverer":{"h":"cleverer","l":"clever","q":"adjective"},"cleverest":{"h":"cleverest","l":"clever","q":"adjective"},"builds":{"h":"builds","l":"build","q":"verb"},"chats":{"h":"chats","l":"chat","q":"verb"},"chatted":{"h":"chatted","l":"chat","q":"verb"},"chatting":{"h":"chatting","l":"chat","q":"verb"},"tills":{"h":"tills","l":"till","q":"verb"},"tilled":{"h":"tilled","i":"/tɪld/","l":"till","q":"verb"},"tilling":{"h":"tilling","l":"till","q":"verb"},"wedges":{"h":"wedges","l":"wedge","q":"noun"},"wedged":{"h":"wedged","l":"wedge","q":"verb"},"wedging":{"h":"wedging","l":"wedge","q":"verb"},"persuade":{"h":"persuade","i":"/pəˈsweɪd/","a":"en-us-persuade.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you persuade somebody to do something, you make them do it, usually by telling them why it's a good thing to do.","e":"She tried to persuade her mother to leave Greensburg."},{"m":"(transitive) If you persuade somebody of something, you make them believe that it's true.","e":"I was able to persuade my parents that I needed a new cell phone."}]}]},"disagreement":{"h":"disagreement","i":"/dɪsəˈɡriːmənt/","a":"en-us-disagreement.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An argument or debate.","e":"There was a disagreement about what color to paint the bedroom, but they have reached a decision."},{"m":"When something does not agree with something else.","e":"There is disagreement between the brother and sister about what color the shirt is."}]}]},"disagreements":{"h":"disagreements","l":"disagreement","q":"noun"},"fucks":{"h":"fucks","l":"fuck","q":"noun"},"russia":{"h":"Russia","i":"/ˈrʌ.ʃə/","a":"en-us-Russia.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Russia is a country in Europe and Asia. Its capital is Moscow.","e":"I was born in Russia."}]}]},"santiago":{"h":"Santiago","i":"/sæntiˈɑːɡəʊ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Santiago.wav","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Santiago is the capital city of Chile.","e":"The restaurants in Santiago have delicious food."}]}]},"restaurants":{"h":"restaurants","l":"restaurant","q":"noun"},"sturdy":{"h":"sturdy","i":"/ˈstɜːdi/","a":"en-us-sturdy.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is sturdy, it is solid, strong or firm.","e":"It was a sturdy building, able to withstand strong winds and cold weather."},{"m":"If something or someone is sturdy, they are solid in structure or personality."}]}]},"extracts":{"h":"extracts","a":"en-us-extracts.ogg","l":"extract","q":"noun"},"trusts":{"h":"trusts","l":"trust","q":"verb"},"mouths":{"h":"mouths","i":"/maʊðz/","a":"en-us-mouths.ogg","l":"mouth","q":"noun"},"boilerplates":{"h":"boilerplates","l":"boilerplate","q":"noun"},"panics":{"h":"panics","l":"panic","q":"noun"},"panicked":{"h":"panicked","l":"panic","q":"verb"},"seeded":{"h":"seeded","l":"seed","q":"verb"},"seeding":{"h":"seeding","i":"/ˈsiːdɪŋ/","l":"seed","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A numbered position going into a tournament.","e":"My college has a high seeding."}]}]},"seedings":{"h":"seedings","l":"seeding","q":"noun"},"checks":{"h":"checks","i":"/t͡ʃɛks/","l":"check","q":"verb"},"weekends":{"h":"weekends","l":"weekend","q":"noun"},"gains":{"h":"gains","l":"gain","q":"noun"},"petrol":{"h":"petrol","i":"/ˈpetrəl/","a":"en-us-petrol.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Petrol is a liquid fuel made from oil.","e":"I don't care whether the car's got a diesel engine or a petrol engine as long as it'll get me from A to B."}]}]},"explosives":{"h":"explosives","l":"explosive","q":"noun"},"plants":{"h":"plants","i":"/plɑːnts/","a":"en-us-plants.ogg","l":"plant","q":"noun"},"planted":{"h":"planted","i":"/ˈplɑːntɪd/","a":"en-us-planted.ogg","l":"plant","q":"verb"},"sturdier":{"h":"sturdier","l":"sturdy","q":"adjective"},"thorns":{"h":"thorns","l":"thorn","q":"noun"},"debates":{"h":"debates","l":"debate","q":"noun"},"seasons":{"h":"seasons","l":"season","q":"noun"},"linens":{"h":"linens","l":"linen","q":"noun"},"sheets":{"h":"sheets","a":"En-us-sheets.ogg","l":"sheet","q":"noun"},"engages":{"h":"engages","l":"engage","q":"verb"},"facing":{"h":"facing","i":"/ˈfeɪsɪŋ/","a":"en-us-facing.ogg","l":"face","q":"verb"},"faces":{"h":"faces","i":"/ˈfeɪsɪz/","a":"en-us-faces.ogg","l":"face","q":"noun"},"unaccented":{"h":"unaccented","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Someone is unaccented if they do not have an accent.","e":"I can understand her better because she is unaccented."},{"m":"A letter is unaccented if it has no diacritics.","e":"The letter \"a\" is unaccented, \"á\", \"ä\", \"â\" etc. are accented letters."},{"m":"A vowel or a syllable is unaccented if it is pronounced without stress (i.e. quickly, without emphasis); unstressed.","e":"The first syllable in the word \"about\" is unaccented."}]}]},"mandolins":{"h":"mandolins","l":"mandolin","q":"noun"},"utilities":{"h":"utilities","l":"utility","q":"noun"},"fights":{"h":"fights","i":"/faɪts/","l":"fight","q":"verb"},"fighting":{"h":"fighting","i":"/ˈfaɪtɪŋ/","a":"en-us-fighting.ogg","l":"fight","q":"verb"},"strontium":{"h":"strontium","i":"/ˈstrɒn.ti.əm/","a":"en-us-strontium.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Strontium a metallic chemical element with the atomic number of 38 and the symbol Sr."}]}]},"pigeon":{"h":"pigeon","i":"/ˈpɪdʒɪn/","a":"en-us-pigeon.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pigeon is a type of bird.","e":"Seeing a dead pigeon on the side of the road is scary."}]}]},"pigeons":{"h":"pigeons","l":"pigeon","q":"noun"},"shrub":{"h":"shrub","i":"/ʃrʌb/","a":"en-us-shrub.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A shrub is a plant. It is smaller than a tree, usually has many stems from the same base, and looks very much like a bush.","e":"I think the ball rolled under that shrub."}]}]},"shrubs":{"h":"shrubs","a":"en-us-shrubs.ogg","l":"shrub","q":"noun"},"victims":{"h":"victims","a":"en-us-victims.ogg","l":"victim","q":"noun"},"pile":{"h":"pile","i":"/paɪl/","a":"en-us-pile.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pile is a lot of things with some on the bottom and more on top.","e":"There was a neat pile of sheets and blankets at the foot of each bed."},{"m":"(countable) A pile is a long, strong post to support something like a bridge or building."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you pile something somewhere, you put a lot of it there.","e":"The table that was piled high with all sorts of fruit, cheese, cakes, and sweets."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something piles (up), there is more an more of it.","e":"I listen to the snow piling on the roof."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something piles on top of something else, it is added to it.","e":"The changes, piled on top of the problems at home were too much."},{"m":"(intransitive) If people pile on, they attack somebody who is already being attacked."},{"m":"(intransitive) If people pile in(to) a car, or some other small space, they get in quickly."},{"m":"(intransitive) If people pile out of a car, or some other small space, they get out quickly."}]}]},"whiles":{"h":"whiles","i":"/waɪlz/","l":"while","q":"verb"},"piles":{"h":"piles","i":"/paɪlz/","l":"pile","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Piles is an alternative name for hemorrhoids."}]}]},"advances":{"h":"advances","a":"en-us-advances.ogg","l":"advance","q":"noun"},"fright":{"h":"fright","i":"/fraɪt/","a":"En-ca-fright.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A strong and sudden fear."},{"m":"Fright means a person or thing that scares someone; to cause someone to have a fear.","e":"Seeing someone with a gun gave me quite a fright."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To scare someone.","e":"Seeing someone with a gun frightened me very much."}]}]},"frights":{"h":"frights","l":"fright","q":"noun"},"pint":{"h":"pint","i":"/paɪnt/","a":"en-us-pint.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pint is a unit of measurement for liquids equal to 0.568 litres in Britain and 1/8 of a gallon in the US.","e":"She had pasta for dinner and half a pint of ice cream every night for dessert."}]}]},"details":{"h":"details","i":"/ˈdiːteɪlz/","a":"en-us-details.ogg","l":"detail","q":"noun"},"detailed":{"h":"detailed","i":"/dɪˈteɪld/","a":"en-us-detailed.ogg","l":"detail","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is detailed, it has many details; it is thorough or complex.","e":"The plan that he came up with is very detailed."}]}]},"detailing":{"h":"detailing","l":"detail","q":"verb"},"delayed":{"h":"delayed","l":"delay","q":"verb"},"delaying":{"h":"delaying","l":"delay","q":"verb"},"points":{"h":"points","a":"en-us-points.ogg","l":"point","q":"noun"},"pointed":{"h":"pointed","i":"/ˈpɔɪntɪd/","a":"en-us-pointed.ogg","l":"point","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is pointed, it is sharp, it has a point.","e":"The warrior brandished a pointed spear."}]}]},"pointing":{"h":"pointing","a":"en-us-pointing.ogg","l":"point","q":"verb"},"sampled":{"h":"sampled","l":"sample","q":"verb"},"sampling":{"h":"sampling","l":"sample","q":"verb"},"fuckers":{"h":"fuckers","l":"fucker","q":"noun"},"simpler":{"h":"simpler","i":"/ˈsɪmplɚ/","l":"simple","q":"adjective"},"simplest":{"h":"simplest","i":"/ˈsɪmpləst/","l":"simple","q":"adjective"},"kids":{"h":"kids","i":"/kɪdz/","a":"en-us-kids.ogg","l":"kid","q":"noun"},"kidded":{"h":"kidded","l":"kid","q":"verb"},"kidding":{"h":"kidding","a":"en-us-kidding.ogg","l":"kid","q":"verb"},"trolls":{"h":"trolls","l":"troll","q":"noun"},"trolled":{"h":"trolled","l":"troll","q":"verb"},"trolling":{"h":"trolling","l":"troll","q":"verb"},"encountered":{"h":"encountered","i":"/ɪnˈkaʊntɚd/","a":"en-us-encountered.ogg","l":"encounter","q":"verb"},"encountering":{"h":"encountering","l":"encounter","q":"verb"},"processes":{"h":"processes","i":"/ˈprɑsɛsɪz/","a":"en-us-processes.ogg","l":"process","q":"noun"},"processed":{"h":"processed","i":"/prəˈsɛst/","a":"en-uk-process.ogg","l":"process","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something has been processed, they have underwent refinement or a similar process."}]}]},"processing":{"h":"processing","i":"/ˈprəʊsɛsɪŋ/","a":"en-us-processing.ogg","l":"process","q":"verb"},"evaluations":{"h":"evaluations","l":"evaluation","q":"noun"},"contemporaries":{"h":"contemporaries","l":"contemporary","q":"noun"},"unites":{"h":"unites","l":"unite","q":"verb"},"uniting":{"h":"uniting","l":"unite","q":"verb"},"lists":{"h":"lists","l":"list","q":"noun"},"listed":{"h":"listed","l":"list","q":"verb"},"listing":{"h":"listing","l":"list","q":"verb"},"hopefuls":{"h":"hopefuls","l":"hopeful","q":"noun"},"nights":{"h":"nights","a":"en-us-nights.ogg","l":"night","q":"noun"},"felons":{"h":"felons","l":"felon","q":"noun"},"stages":{"h":"stages","l":"stage","q":"noun"},"staged":{"h":"staged","l":"stage","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is staged, it has been planned or prepared.","e":"The prank seems to be staged, his reaction to it is too dramatic."}]}]},"staging":{"h":"staging","l":"stage","q":"verb"},"arrives":{"h":"arrives","l":"arrive","q":"verb"},"arriving":{"h":"arriving","l":"arrive","q":"verb"},"wearing":{"h":"wearing","i":"/ˈwɛrɪŋ/","a":"en-us-wearing.ogg","l":"wear","q":"verb"},"guardrail":{"h":"guardrail","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-guardrail.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A guardrail is a rail that is put on the side of a dangerous place (like a road or staircase) to make it safer."}]}]},"guardrails":{"h":"guardrails","l":"guardrail","q":"noun"},"sinkhole":{"h":"sinkhole","i":"/ˈsɪŋkhəʊl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-sinkhole.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sinkhole is a hole in the ground that is made when water erodes dirt or rock."}]}]},"sinkholes":{"h":"sinkholes","l":"sinkhole","q":"noun"},"wildfire":{"h":"wildfire","i":"/ˈwaɪldˌfaɪɚ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-wildfire.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A wildfire is a quickly-spreading fire that occurs in the wild. These fires can not be controlled.","e":"The wildfire burned down the trees in the forest."}]}]},"pitch":{"h":"pitch","i":"/pɪtʃ/","a":"en-us-pitch.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) In baseball, a pitch is when the pitcher throws the ball to the batter, who tries to hit it.","e":"Matsuzaka collected 10 strikeouts while throwing 108 pitches during a 4-1 win over Kansas City."},{"m":"(countable) In football (soccer), a pitch is the place where the game is played.","e":"She kicked the ball halfway down the pitch."},{"m":"(countable) A pitch is a level of excitement, anger, etc.","e":"The anger over the changes has pushed this feeling to a fever pitch."},{"m":"(countable) A pitch is a sound at a particular frequency, how high or low a note is.","e":"We need to listen for small changes of pitch and rhythm that lie beyond the limits of Western music."},{"m":"(countable) Somebody's pitch is how well they can produce or recognize a specific note.","e":"He has perfect pitch; at age eight he played the entire Bach Toccata in D Minor by ear."},{"m":"(countable) A pitch is an explanation to encourage somebody to do something, often to convince them to buy something.","e":"He was no good at all at fast-talking sales pitches over the telephone."},{"m":"(uncountable) Pitch is a sticky, black substance used to seal things like roofs.","e":"The night was pitch black."},{"m":"(countable) A pitch is the angle, up or down of a surface or vehicle."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you pitch something, you throw it.","e":"He pitched the ball for his dog."},{"m":"(transitive) If you pitch something, you promote or attempt to sell something.","e":"We pitched our ideas to various."},{"m":"(transitive) If you pitch a tent, you assemble it.","e":"The decided to pitch the tent over there."}]}]},"wildfires":{"h":"wildfires","l":"wildfire","q":"noun"},"staked":{"h":"staked","l":"stake","q":"verb"},"staking":{"h":"staking","l":"stake","q":"verb"},"killers":{"h":"killers","l":"killer","q":"noun"},"frequents":{"h":"frequents","l":"frequent","q":"verb"},"frequented":{"h":"frequented","a":"en-us-frequented.ogg","l":"frequent","q":"verb"},"frequenting":{"h":"frequenting","l":"frequent","q":"verb"},"chucked":{"h":"chucked","l":"chuck","q":"verb"},"chucking":{"h":"chucking","l":"chuck","q":"verb"},"relies":{"h":"relies","l":"rely","q":"verb"},"relied":{"h":"relied","a":"en-us-relied.ogg","l":"rely","q":"verb"},"relying":{"h":"relying","l":"rely","q":"verb"},"nachos":{"h":"nachos","i":"/ˈnætʃəʊz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-nachos.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Nachos are a type of food from Mexico made from tortilla chips and melted cheese. Often, nachos also have other toppings like jalapeños, onions, lettuce, tomatoes, olives, refried beans, salsa, sour cream or guacamole.","e":"Let's get some nachos as an appetizer."}]}]},"acoustic":{"h":"acoustic","i":"/əˈkuːstɪk/","a":"en-us-acoustic.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Related to hearing or sounds."},{"m":"An acoustic instrument is played without electricity.","e":"I think music from an acoustic guitar is prettier than music from an electric guitar."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) If a space has good acoustics (or sometimes acoustic) its physical structure makes it easy to hear sound in it.","e":"She hated singing in the gym because of the poor acoustics."}]}]},"flamed":{"h":"flamed","l":"flame","q":"verb"},"complemented":{"h":"complemented","l":"complement","q":"verb"},"complementing":{"h":"complementing","l":"complement","q":"verb"},"compiles":{"h":"compiles","l":"compile","q":"verb"},"compiled":{"h":"compiled","l":"compile","q":"verb"},"compiling":{"h":"compiling","l":"compile","q":"verb"},"spaces":{"h":"spaces","i":"/ˈspeɪsɪz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Back ache-spaces.wav","l":"space","q":"noun"},"spaced":{"h":"spaced","l":"space","q":"verb"},"mechanic":{"h":"mechanic","i":"/məˈkænɪk/","a":"en-us-mechanic.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mechanic is a person that can fix machines like cars and airplanes.","e":"My mechanic can fix anything."},{"m":"(uncountable) Mechanics is the way of doing something.","e":"Will you teach me the mechanics of songwriting?"}]}]},"poll":{"h":"poll","i":"/paɔl/","a":"en-us-pole.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A poll is a process of asking people for their opinions about something and counting the results.","e":"The latest Newsweek poll suggests 65% of the public is dissatisfied with the president."},{"m":"(countable); (plural) If people go to the polls, they vote in an election.","e":"Voters go to the polls eight days from now."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you poll people, you ask them for their opinion about something and you count the results.","e":"Seventy percent of those polled said that the U.S. military was making the security situation worse in Iraq."}]}]},"pray":{"h":"pray","i":"/preɪ/","a":"en-us-pray.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you pray, you make a wish or give thanks to a god believing they will pay attention or make the wish come true.","e":"I decided to pray. I prayed for somebody to help me."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you pray, you wish for something very strongly.","e":"I was hoping and praying she would get in touch with me."}]}]},"assets":{"h":"assets","i":"/'æsets/","l":"asset","q":"noun"},"patients":{"h":"patients","i":"/ˈpeɪʃəntz/","a":"en-us-patients.ogg","l":"patient","q":"noun"},"lives":{"h":"lives","i":"/lɪvz/","a":"en-us-lives-noun.ogg","l":"life","q":"noun"},"lived":{"h":"lived","a":"en-us-lived.ogg","l":"live","q":"verb"},"pregnant":{"h":"pregnant","i":"/ˈprɛgnənt/","a":"en-us-pregnant.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a female is pregnant, she has a baby growing inside her.","e":"Between 10 and 40 percent of US teen girls will get pregnant before the age of 20."},{"m":"A pregnant silence has some meaning or feeling."},{"m":"If something is pregnant with a quality, it has a lot of that quality."}]}]},"prize":{"h":"prize","i":"/praɪz/","a":"en-us-prize.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A prize is something that you receive for winning or doing well.","e":"She was the first African woman to win the Nobel Peace Prize."},{"m":"A prize horse, story, performance, etc. is very good and could win a prize.","e":"She caught this year's prize fish late yesterday evening."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive); If something is prized, people feel that it is very important and often people want it.","e":"DuMond is a world-famous artist and his pieces are highly prized by collectors."},{"m":"(transitive) If you prize something off of or away from something else, you use strong force to get it to move.","e":"He prized the doors open, dragged the two men out, and laid them on the road."}]}]},"pro":{"h":"pro","i":"/prəʊ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-pro.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pro is somebody who is very good at what they do; short for professional.","e":"She's real pro who cares about her job."},{"m":"(countable) A pro is somebody who is paid to play sports, sometimes as a teacher; short for professional.","e":"He began his career as a golf pro in Indiana, and later taught golf to Bob Hope."},{"m":"(countable) (plural) The pros and cons of a situation are the positive parts and the negative parts.","e":"What are the pros and cons of going from one method to the other?"}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If you are pro something, you support it, or you think it is a good idea.","e":"Yet when they got into the war, he was very pro the country winning the war."}]}]},"manner":{"h":"manner","i":"/ˈmænə/","a":"en-us-manner.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A manner is the way that someone or something acts or performs.","e":"My daughter quickly changed her manner when I came into her room."}]}]},"pudding":{"h":"pudding","i":"/ˈpʊd.ɪŋ/","a":"en-au-pudding.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) (UK) Pudding is a dessert made with cake, bread or rice and often fruit, usually hot.","e":"The shop had desserts-fruit cobblers, pies, bread pudding, and chocolate, pound, and carrot cakes."},{"m":"(US) Pudding is a thick desert made with milk and eggs, usually cold.","e":"Use 1 (18.25-ounce) package white cake mix with 1 (3.9-ounce) package instant chocolate pudding mix, 1 cup sugar, 1 cup vegetable oil, 1 cup water, and 4 large eggs."},{"m":"(UK) Pudding is a food made of flour, animal fat, and meat or vegetables, usually hot."}]}]},"pupil":{"h":"pupil","i":"/pjuːpəl/","a":"en-us-pupil.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pupil is a student, especially a young one.","e":"They can put their children in public school, but it costs $9,600 per pupil per year."},{"m":"(countable) Your pupil is the black circle in the middle of your eye.","e":"He checked her eyes; the pupils seemed rather large for the lighting in the room."}]}]},"reach":{"h":"reach","i":"/riːtʃ/","a":"en-us-reach.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you reach a level, you get to that level.","e":"Seven mice were born, six living long enough to reach adulthood."},{"m":"(transitive) If you reach a conclusion, agreement, etc. you keep working, talking, thinking, etc. until the ideas come together.","e":"They came to the same conclusion I had reached: it wasn't working."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you reach for something, you put your hand out to touch it.","e":"He reached in his pocket and he came out with an envelope."},{"m":"(transitive) If you reach a place, you get there.","e":"By the time we had reached our destination, it was already past midnight."},{"m":"If something reaches a place, it is long enough or tall enough to touch that place.","e":"My hair is long enough to reach my waist."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable); (singular) Your reach is the distance that you can move your body to touch something.","e":"We had to keep the tools outside of the elephants' reach so they wouldn't take them."},{"m":"If something is within reach of somewhere, you can get to it easily from there; it's close.","e":"They were within easy reach of a hospital."},{"m":"(plural) The outer reaches of a place are the parts that are furthest away from the centre or from the start.","e":"The tree is found in New Mexico and up into the upper reaches of the Colorado River system."}]}]},"recall":{"h":"recall","i":"/rɪˈkɔːl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-recall (verb).wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you recall something, you think about something you learned or experienced in the past.","e":"She recalled a childhood summer camp in the Tetons, singing around a campfire."},{"m":"(transitive) If you recall a worker, you officially ask them to come back to a job or place.","e":"The workers were recalled after a two month layoff."},{"m":"(transitive) If you recall a product, you tell stores and customers to send it back because it has a problem."},{"m":"If you recall someone, you call them again."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Recall is your ability to think about something you learned or experienced in the past.","e":"You can improve your recall by using memory tricks."},{"m":"(countable) A recall is a request to stores and customers to send back a product because it has a problem.","e":"The company is announcing the recall of fifteen different products."}]}]},"recession":{"h":"recession","i":"/rɪˈsɛʃn̩/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-recession.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A recession is a time when there is less economic activity.","e":"Spending is one reason that economists are increasingly worried about the economy moving into a recession."}]}]},"genocide":{"h":"genocide","i":"/ˈʤɛnəsaid/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-genocide.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Genocide is the killing of many people because of their ethnicity, race, religion, or culture."}]}]},"inflation":{"h":"inflation","i":"/ɪnˈfleɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-inflation.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Inflation is a general increase in the price of goods and services.","e":"Because of inflation, I can't afford to go to the movies anymore."},{"m":"(uncountable) Inflation is the process of blowing up a balloon, bag, etc.","e":"The speed of inflation of the airbag is very important in protecting you in a car crash."},{"m":"(uncountable) Inflation is any process or result of growth.","e":"With competition to enter college, grade inflation is a serious problem across the country."}]}]},"recover":{"h":"recover","i":"/rɪˈkʌvə/","a":"en-us-recover.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you recover, you get better after getting sick, or being hurt, surprised, etc.","e":"She is just about fully recovered from a broken leg."},{"m":"If something recovers, it returns to normal after a change, especially a bad change.","e":"We don't expect the economy to begin recovering until the second half of next year."},{"m":"(transitive) If you recover something that you didn't have for a time, you get it back.","e":"Five hours now after the accident, bodies were still being recovered from the train."},{"m":"(transitive) If you recover money, such as an investment, damages, etc., you get back the amount you put out or lost.","e":"He brought suit to recover damages suffered in an automobile accident."},{"m":"To cover something again."}]}]},"recognised":{"h":"recognised","i":"/ˈrɛkəɡnaɪzd/","a":"en-us-recognized.ogg","l":"recognise","q":"verb"},"recognising":{"h":"recognising","l":"recognise","q":"verb"},"recruit":{"h":"recruit","i":"/rɪˈkrut/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-recruit.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you recruit people, you try to get them to come and work or study with you or to join your group.","e":"The university will actively recruit good students from disadvantaged backgrounds."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A recruit is a person who has recently joined a company or organization.","e":"New recruits go through a ten-day training session."}]}]},"reflect":{"h":"reflect","i":"/ˈriflɛkt/","a":"en-us-reflect.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If x reflects y, x shows or matches y, or x is affected by y.","e":"These words didn't accurately reflect his thoughts."},{"m":"(transitive) If x reflects y, the light from y can be seen in x.","e":"The mirrors on the stairway reflected ladies in white, blue, and pink dresses."},{"m":"(intransitive) If light or sound reflects off something, it hits it and goes in a different direction.","e":"Sunlight was reflecting off the glass."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you reflect about something, you think about it carefully.","e":"In jail he's had time to reflect upon what he did and how many lives he touched through his actions."}]}]},"refrigerate":{"h":"refrigerate","i":"/rɪˈfrɪdʒəreɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-refrigerate.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you refrigerate something such as food or drink, you cool it in a refrigerator.","e":"Combine olive oil and pepper, stir, then coat meat with it. Cover and refrigerate overnight."}]}]},"regulate":{"h":"regulate","i":"/ˈrɛɡjəleɪt/","a":"en-us-regulate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you regulate something, you control it by making laws and rules.","e":"The industry has fought the state's attempts to regulate it."},{"m":"(transitive) If x regulates y, x causes y to function in a particular way, often at a higher or lower level.","e":"You turn this to regulate the water flow."}]}]},"jester":{"h":"jester","i":"/ˈdʒɛs.tə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-jester.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A person who jokes or jests."},{"m":"(countable) An entertainer in a medieval royal court."}]}]},"relief":{"h":"relief","i":"/rɪˈliːf/","a":"en-us-relief.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) or (singular) Relief is the good feeling you have when something bad is finished or didn't happen.","e":"Most people are just breathing a sigh of relief that he's gone."},{"m":"(uncountable) Relief is help given to people who have suffered disasters, such as an earthquake.","e":"The government recently announced it was donating $150,000 to the Red Cross for disaster relief."},{"m":"(uncountable) Pain relief is the reduction of pain.","e":"After such injuries, pain relief is often the patient's priority."},{"m":"(uncountable) Financial relief is the reduction of debt or taxes, or receiving money.","e":"Tony Blair, is encouraging leaders of the richest nations to consider debt relief as a form of aid to impoverished nations."},{"m":"(uncountable) Relief is somebody who will take over your difficult job to give you a rest.","e":"2,0000 relief fighters arrived too late to save the city."},{"m":"(uncountable) Comic relief is something funny during a serious or difficult time.","e":"A coworker who provides steady emotional support and comic relief can help you get through the day."},{"m":"A relief or bas relief is a kind of decoration in which a shape is raised above the surface."},{"m":"(uncountable) If something stands out in relief, it is very noticeable.","e":"His face and his right hand stand out in sharp relief against the blue background."}]}]},"remark":{"h":"remark","i":"/rɪˈmɑrk/","a":"en-us-remark.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A remark is your spoken opinion or observation about something.","e":"He made some very interesting remarks about what he expects in Iraq."},{"m":"(countable); (plural) Your remarks are your words.","e":"A final section provides some interpretation of the results and concluding remarks."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you remark upon something, you say what you noticed or think about it.","e":"Some visitors have remarked upon the contrast between this expensive car and the tiny, broken down house."},{"m":"If you remark something, you mark it again."}]}]},"remind":{"h":"remind","i":"/rəˈmaɪnd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-remind.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you remind somebody of something, you tell them something they already know to make them think about it again.","e":"We doctors have to constantly remind ourselves to keep it simple."},{"m":"(transitive) If x reminds you of y, x makes you think about y, usually because x and y are similar.","e":"It reminded me of the time my girlfriend broke her nose."}]}]},"stir":{"h":"stir","i":"/stɜː/","a":"en-us-stir.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you stir something, you move it in a circular movement.","e":"He needed to stir the water into the flour"},{"m":"If something is stirred up, it is caused or begins because of something else.","e":"The appointment of the new CEO stirred up controversy."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A stir can be when someone becomes excited, upset or angry.","e":"Her short dress made quite a stir when she came into the room."}]}]},"reply":{"h":"reply","i":"/rɪˈplaɪ/","a":"en-us-reply.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you reply to someone or something, you answer using words.","e":"\"Are you OK?\" she ask. \"Yes,\" I replied."},{"m":"If you reply to someone or something, you react.","e":"The Cubs replied with three points of their own to win the game."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A reply is the words you use to answer someone.","e":"\"Why?\" He received no reply. \"Did you hear me?\""}]}]},"reserve":{"h":"reserve","i":"/rɪˈzɝv/","a":"en-us-reserve.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you reserve a room, a table, seat etc. you arrange for it to be kept for you, usually for a particular date and time.","e":"This parking spot is reserved for the general manager."},{"m":"(transitive) When you're cooking, if you reserve something, you put it aside to use later.","e":"Cook pasta as directed on package and reserve 1/4 cup of pasta cooking water."},{"m":"(transitive) If you reserve something for a particular situation, you usually don't use it except in that situation.","e":"She spoke to me in a voice usually reserved for young children."},{"m":"(transitive) If you reserve the right to do something, you let people know that these are your legal rights and you may use or defend them.","e":"This program is copyrighted © 2008 by CBS Studios Inc. All Rights Reserved."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (usually plural) Reserves are extra amounts of something that are for the future.","e":"Canada has 179 billion barrels of oil reserves - second only to Saudi Arabia."},{"m":"Reserve is a feeling of holding back, controlling yourself, and not being very friendly.","e":"We listened to all this talk about change with a certain reserve."},{"m":"Reserves are extra players on a team, or fighters in an army in case somebody is hurt or needs a rest.","e":"Their best player spent a season on injured reserve after hurting his knee."},{"m":"(countable) A reserve is an area of land or water that is protected from humans.","e":"These lands (such as national parks and nature reserves) supply cities with clean drinking water."},{"m":"(countable) A reserve (or reservation) is an area of land that belongs to a group of indigenous people, such as a First Nations group in Canada."}]}]},"kidneys":{"h":"kidneys","l":"kidney","q":"noun"},"piled":{"h":"piled","i":"/paɪld/","a":"en-us-piled.ogg","l":"pile","q":"verb"},"piling":{"h":"piling","i":"/ˈpaɪlɪŋ/","l":"pile","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Piling is a type of structural support that is made of wood, steel, or other construction material."}]}]},"resist":{"h":"resist","i":"/rɪˈzɪst/","a":"en-us-resist.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you resist something, you work, push, fight, etc. against it.","e":"Unable to resist the call of the road, he left once more."}]}]},"retire":{"h":"retire","i":"/rəˈtaɪ.ə(r)/","a":"en-au-retire.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you retire, you stop working, usually because of your age.","e":"She recently retired after 25 years with the company."},{"m":"(transitive) If you retire something, you stop using it.","e":"NASA will soon be retiring the space shuttles."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you retire, you go to a quiet place, often to bed.","e":"After dinner she retired to her bedroom with a head cold."}]}]},"rome":{"h":"Rome","i":"/rəʊm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Rome.wav","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Rome is the capital city of Italy.","e":"It is noon at the U.N. headquarters in New York, 6:00 p.m. in Rome, Italy."},{"m":"Rome is the Roman Empire, an empire that existed between 27 BC and AD 476 and covered much of the southern Europe, some of West Asia, and some of northern Africa.","e":"Most of our great ideas are rooted in Greece and Rome."}]}]},"rubbish":{"h":"rubbish","i":"/ˈrʌbɪʃ/","a":"en-us-rubbish.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Rubbish is unwanted things such as plastic bags, half-eaten food, and broken toys.","e":"She's always throwing her left-over food on the ground, and not in the rubbish bin."},{"m":"(uncountable) Rubbish is a stupid or wrong idea.","e":"You're going to sing? Rubbish! Total rubbish! You can't sing."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you rubbish something, you say it's bad or stupid.","e":"It's not very good, but I didn't want to completely rubbish it."}]}]},"scare":{"h":"scare","i":"/skɛə/","a":"en-us-scare.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If someone or something scares a person, it makes them feel fear.","e":"They climbed out of the water alive--cold, wet, tired, and scared to death, but alive."},{"m":"If something scares a person off, it makes them not want to do something.","e":"The high costs often scare students off."},{"m":"If a person scares up something, they find it, even though it's rare or hard to find.","e":"She didn't think she'd be able to scare up the cash for the trip."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sudden fright.","e":"I had quite a bad scare last night--I almost hit a deer on the highway."}]}]},"scene":{"h":"scene","i":"/siːn/","a":"en-us-scene.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A scene is a place where something happened.","e":"Police found a gun near the crime scene."},{"m":"(countable) A scene is one part of a movie or play where the action happens at one time in one place.","e":"Who could forget the amazing opening scene of Star Wars?"},{"m":"(countable) A scene is the public activities of a group of people with a common interest, such as music, politics, etc.","e":"For more than a decade, she dominated the fashion scene."},{"m":"If something happens behind the scenes, it happens out of sight, in secret.","e":"It's hard to know what went on behind the scenes."},{"m":"(countable) A scene is a view of a place, especially in art.","e":"The photo was a street scene out of New York."},{"m":"(countable) A scene is a loud, public argument or demonstration."}]}]},"senior":{"h":"senior","i":"/ˈsinjɚ/","a":"en-US senior.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A senior person has a higher social position.","e":"She's a senior vice-president with the company."},{"m":"A senior citizen is somebody who is older, usually over the age of 65.","e":"By 2030, one in five Americans will be a senior citizen."},{"m":"Senior high school is usually for grades 10-12 (ages, 15-18).","e":"I studied the works of many classical writers in junior high school and senior high school."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A senior is a student in their last year of high school, college, or university.","e":"He's also attended his senior prom and heads off to college this fall."},{"m":"(countable) A senior is someone who has a higher social position."},{"m":"(countable) A senior is somebody who is older, usually over the age of 65."}]}]},"sensible":{"h":"sensible","i":"/ˈsensəbl/","a":"en-us-sensible.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A sensible person thinks clearly and makes good decisions.","e":"She wasn't talking wildy or anything; she seemed like a nice sensible lady."},{"m":"A sensible plan, action, idea, etc. is a good one because it fits the situation well.","e":"Stopping to rest seemed like a very sensible idea, so we did."}]}]},"session":{"h":"session","i":"/ˈsɛʃ(ə)n/","a":"en-au-session.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A session is the period of time of an activity.","e":"There will be a presentation by Michael Hirschorn, followed by a question-and-answer session."},{"m":"If something is in session, it's happening at that time.","e":"Some schools offer open houses, and most will invite you to observe their classes in session."}]}]},"silly":{"h":"silly","i":"/'sIlI/","a":"en-us-silly.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is silly, it shows that somebody didn't think about it carefully.","e":"Sometimes I called her \"Mommy Ruby\", even if it sounded silly."},{"m":"If something is silly, it's not important or serious.","e":"I was making silly little jokes and she was laughing."},{"m":"If you are silly, you don't think about things carefully or you are not serious.","e":"Sometimes it's hard to believe how silly students can be."}]}]},"sin":{"h":"sin","i":"/sɪn/","a":"en-us-sin.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A sin is a bad action that breaks laws or rules, especially religious ones.","e":"32 percent of Catholics said they confess their sins to a priest less than once a year."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you sin, you do something bad that breaks laws or rules, especially religious ones.","e":"I wanted him to say,' Yes, I have sinned. I'm sorry."}]}]},"flags":{"h":"flags","i":"/flæɡz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Wodencafe-flags.wav","l":"flag","q":"noun"},"flagged":{"h":"flagged","l":"flag","q":"verb"},"flagging":{"h":"flagging","l":"flag","q":"verb"},"enters":{"h":"enters","l":"enter","q":"verb"},"entered":{"h":"entered","i":"/ˈEntə(r)d/","a":"en-us-entered.ogg","l":"enter","q":"verb"},"entering":{"h":"entering","i":"/ˈɛnt.ə(r).ɪŋ/","a":"en-us-entering.ogg","l":"enter","q":"verb"},"rows":{"h":"rows","i":"/rəʊz/","a":"en-us-rows.ogg","l":"row","q":"noun"},"rowed":{"h":"rowed","i":"/rəʊd/","l":"row","q":"verb"},"rowing":{"h":"rowing","a":"en-us-rowing.ogg","l":"row","q":"verb"},"raised":{"h":"raised","i":"/reɪzd/","a":"en-us-raised.ogg","l":"raise","q":"verb"},"raising":{"h":"raising","a":"en-us-raising.ogg","l":"raise","q":"verb"},"foundered":{"h":"foundered","l":"founder","q":"verb"},"foundering":{"h":"foundering","l":"founder","q":"verb"},"keepers":{"h":"keepers","l":"keeper","q":"noun"},"journeys":{"h":"journeys","l":"journey","q":"noun"},"journeyed":{"h":"journeyed","a":"en-us-journeyed.ogg","l":"journey","q":"verb"},"journeying":{"h":"journeying","l":"journey","q":"verb"},"projects":{"h":"projects","i":"/ˈprɒdʒɛkts/","l":"project","q":"noun"},"projected":{"h":"projected","i":"/prəˈdʒɛktɪd/","l":"project","q":"verb"},"projecting":{"h":"projecting","i":"/prəˈd͡ʒɛktɪŋ/","a":"en-us-projecting.ogg","l":"project","q":"verb"},"releases":{"h":"releases","l":"release","q":"verb"},"released":{"h":"released","i":"/rɪˈliːst/","a":"en-us-released.ogg","l":"release","q":"verb"},"releasing":{"h":"releasing","l":"release","q":"verb"},"adapts":{"h":"adapts","l":"adapt","q":"verb"},"adapting":{"h":"adapting","l":"adapt","q":"verb"},"drops":{"h":"drops","i":"/drɑps/","a":"en-us-drops.ogg","l":"drop","q":"noun"},"dropped":{"h":"dropped","i":"/drɑpt/","a":"en-us-dropped.ogg","l":"drop","q":"verb"},"dropping":{"h":"dropping","i":"/ˈdrɒp.ɪŋ/","a":"en-us-dropping.ogg","l":"drop","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(usually plural) Droppings are the excrement of animals.","e":"A rabbit's droppings."}]}]},"slide":{"h":"slide","i":"/slaɪd/","a":"en-us-slide.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something slides, it moves smoothly and easily, usually over a surface.","e":"She put on the brakes and slid sideways fifteen yards before she was stopped by a pine tree."},{"m":"(intransitive) If prices, numbers, rates, etc. slide, they go down.","e":"Oil prices are expected to slide in the near future."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A slide is a structure, usually on a playground, that you slide down.","e":"He made a splash by entering the pool on a water slide."},{"m":"(countable) A slide is a small photographic image on transparent plastic.","e":"When Kodak stopped making the slide projector last fall, it was the end of an era."},{"m":"(countable) A microscope slide is a piece of glass to hold something under a microscope.","e":"She transferred each flake to a glass slide under a microscope."},{"m":"(countable) A slide is a long slow movement down.","e":"He's just an actor whose life is on a downward slide."},{"m":"(countable) A slide is a sliding part of a machine or musical instrument.","e":"His trombone slide was stuck. So he had to excuse himself to get it oiled."},{"m":"(countable) A slide is a smooth, easy movement, usually over a surface."},{"m":"(countable) A rock, snow, or mud slide is when a large amount of the material falls down a hill or mountain."}]}]},"slides":{"h":"slides","l":"slide","q":"verb"},"slid":{"h":"slid","i":"/'slɪd/","a":"en-us-slid.ogg","l":"slide","q":"verb"},"sliding":{"h":"sliding","l":"slide","q":"verb"},"losses":{"h":"losses","a":"en-us-losses.ogg","l":"loss","q":"noun"},"panicking":{"h":"panicking","l":"panic","q":"verb"},"visas":{"h":"visas","l":"visa","q":"noun"},"renders":{"h":"renders","l":"render","q":"verb"},"rendered":{"h":"rendered","i":"/ˈrɛn.dəd/","a":"en-us-rendered.ogg","l":"render","q":"verb"},"ads":{"h":"ads","i":"/ædz/","a":"en-us-adds.ogg","l":"ad","q":"noun"},"mules":{"h":"mules","a":"en-us-mules.ogg","l":"mule","q":"noun"},"saner":{"h":"saner","l":"sane","q":"adjective"},"sanest":{"h":"sanest","l":"sane","q":"adjective"},"refurbish":{"h":"refurbish","i":"/riˈfɝbɪʃ/","a":"en-us-refurbish.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you refurbish something, you remake it using new materials or restore it to its original (or better) condition.","e":"I refurbished my bedroom with brand new furniture and a new paint job."}]}]},"defeated":{"h":"defeated","i":"/dɪˈfiːtəd/","a":"en-us-defeated.ogg","l":"defeat","q":"verb"},"sod":{"h":"sod","i":"/sɒd/","a":"en-us-sod.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Sod is a layer of earth with grass growing in it.","e":"By the time I came along there was little of such unturned prairie sod In Falrweather Township."},{"m":"(countable) A sod is somebody you don't like, usually a man.","e":"I'm not having these silly old sods coming to the party. No way!"},{"m":"(countable) A sod is a person, usually a man.","e":"He's not had much sleep though, poor sod."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"You use sod to show you're not happy about something.","e":"I looked at the clock, it said twenty to eight, I thought, \"sod it! I ain't getting up.\""}]}]},"solicitor":{"h":"solicitor","i":"/səˈlɪsɪtɚ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-solicitor.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) In many areas, such as the UK, Australia, India, and Singapore, a solicitor is a type of lawyer who offers legal services to clients outside of court.","e":"I have instructed my solicitor to sell the house to any interested party."},{"m":"(countable) A solicitor is someone trying to sell things, especially door to door.","e":"Don't answer the door. It's just another solicitor."}]}]},"ships":{"h":"ships","i":"/ʃɪps/","a":"en-us-ships.ogg","l":"ship","q":"noun"},"seniors":{"h":"seniors","l":"senior","q":"noun"},"southern":{"h":"southern","i":"/ˈsʌðən/","a":"en-us-southern.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A southern place, accent, person, etc. is in, from, or about the south.","e":"The money helps everyone from a grocer in southern Lebanon to a farmer in Tajikistan."}]}]},"spare":{"h":"spare","i":"/ˈspɛə(r)/","a":"en-us-spare.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you spare (somebody) something, you make it available even though you don't have much of it.","e":"Excuse, me! Can you spare a few minutes to look at this?"},{"m":"(transitive); (infinitive only) If you have something to spare, you have something extra.","e":"She had five minutes to spare before he was due to pick her up."},{"m":"(transitive) If you spare somebody something not nice, they don't have to experience it.","e":"The phone rang, sparing me from having to give an answer."},{"m":"(transitive) If somebody is spared, they live, even though they were expected to die.","e":"The accident took the life of his wife, but spared his son."},{"m":"(transitive) If you spare no expense, effort, detail, etc., you do everything you can.","e":"They spared no expense for their wedding."},{"m":"(transitive) If you spare a thought for somebody, you think of them, usually at a time that you are happy, but they are not."},{"m":"(transitive) If you spare somebody's feelings, you try not to do or say things that will upset them.","e":"She never hid the truth to spare somebody's feelings."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A spare part, room, key, etc. is an extra one, one that is not being used.","e":"The bags were in the small backseat because the spare tire filled most of the trunk."},{"m":"Your spare time is time when you are not working and you can relax or have fun.","e":"He spends most of his spare time playing guitar with his friends."},{"m":"Spare change is coins that are not worth much and that you can give away.","e":"I often find spare change lying on the floor."},{"m":"If something is spare, it is plain and has no decoration.","e":"The room was very spare, with only a window, a single chair, and a ceiling light."},{"m":"A spare person is tall and thin."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A spare is an extra thing, such as a key, just in case it is needed.","e":"Don't worry! I've got a spare in the back room."},{"m":"(countable) A spare is a tire that you keep in your car in case one of the other tires has a problem."}]}]},"beggar":{"h":"beggar","i":"/ˈbɛɡɚ/","a":"en-us-beggar.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A beggar is a person who begs.","e":"Several beggars are seen begging for food and money in modern cities."}]}]},"beggars":{"h":"beggars","i":"/ˈbɛɡɚs/","a":"en-us-beggars.ogg","l":"beggar","q":"noun"},"accessibility":{"h":"accessibility","i":"/ækˌsɛs.əˈbɪl.ət.i/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-accessibility.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Accessibility is the property of being accessible.","e":"The accessibility of the city depends on how well it is linked by roads."}]}]},"split":{"h":"split","i":"/spliɪt/","a":"en-us-split.ogg","l":"split","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If a group of people splits or is split, the people don't agree, so the group becomes more than one group.","e":"Female voters overall are evenly split between Obama (48%) and McCain (47%)."},{"m":"(transitive) If you split something, you separate, cut, or break it into different parts.","e":"East and West Germany were split apart at the end of World War II."},{"m":"If you split your skin, you cut it by hitting it."},{"m":"(intransitive); If you split, you leave."},{"m":"A splitting headache is a very painful headache."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A split between two groups is a strong disagreement.","e":"Time brought about the split between Moscow and Beijing."},{"m":"(countable) A split in something, is a place where it breaks into two or where there is a long thing opening.","e":"The split in the wood had grown wider over the years."},{"m":"If you do the splits, you spread your legs so that your feet are pointing away from each other."},{"m":"A kind of ice cream dessert."}]}]},"cupped":{"h":"cupped","l":"cup","q":"verb"},"cupping":{"h":"cupping","l":"cup","q":"verb"},"unfair":{"h":"unfair","i":"/ʌnˈfɛə(r)/","a":"en-us-unfair.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is unfair, it is not fair.","e":"It was unfair for the boss to give larger bonuses to his friends."}]}]},"sponsor":{"h":"sponsor","i":"/ˈspɒn.sə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-sponsor.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you sponsor an event or you sponsor somebody to do an event, you give them money, usually in exchange for advertising.","e":"The contest in public school art classes is sponsored by the manufacturers of Ivory soap."},{"m":"(transitive) If a politician sponsors a law, they officially support it.","e":"Don't expect Senator Schaffer to sponsor legislation around those issues."},{"m":"(transitive) If you sponsor somebody, you agree to help them and be responsible for them.","e":"He discovered that no company would sponsor him for a work visa."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sponsor is someone who gives money to an event or to somebody to do an event, usually in exchange for advertising.","e":"Without corporate sponsors, the event will not run this year."},{"m":"(countable) A sponsor is somebody who officially supports a law.","e":"He was the only sponsor of a bill to cut $1.5 billion from government spending."},{"m":"(countable) A sponsor is somebody who agrees to help another person and be responsible for them.","e":"The United States, demanded immigrants have a sponsor willing to financially support them"}]}]},"centred":{"h":"centred","l":"centre","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is centred, it is in the centre or middle."}]}]},"centring":{"h":"centring","l":"centre","q":"verb"},"creeps":{"h":"creeps","i":"/kriːps/","l":"creep","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Fear or anxiety.","e":"Spiders give me the creeps."}]}]},"creeping":{"h":"creeping","i":"/ˈkriːpɪŋ/","a":"en-us-creeping.ogg","l":"creep","q":"verb"},"crept":{"h":"crept","i":"/'krεpt/","a":"en-us-crept.ogg","l":"creep","q":"verb"},"creeped":{"h":"creeped","i":"/kriːpt/","l":"creep","q":"verb"},"looser":{"h":"looser","l":"loose","q":"adjective"},"loosest":{"h":"loosest","l":"loose","q":"adjective"},"keener":{"h":"keener","l":"keen","q":"adjective","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A person who keens at a funeral."},{"m":"(Canada) A person who is very keen or eager; a brownnoser."}]}]},"keenest":{"h":"keenest","l":"keen","q":"adjective"},"keeners":{"h":"keeners","l":"keener","q":"noun"},"keens":{"h":"keens","l":"keen","q":"noun"},"keened":{"h":"keened","l":"keen","q":"verb"},"keening":{"h":"keening","l":"keen","q":"verb"},"socked":{"h":"socked","l":"sock","q":"verb"},"socking":{"h":"socking","i":"/ˈsɑkɪŋ/","l":"sock","q":"verb"},"translates":{"h":"translates","l":"translate","q":"verb"},"translated":{"h":"translated","i":"/ˈtrænzleɪtɪd/","a":"en-us-translated.ogg","l":"translate","q":"verb"},"translating":{"h":"translating","l":"translate","q":"verb"},"nailed":{"h":"nailed","l":"nail","q":"verb"},"nailing":{"h":"nailing","l":"nail","q":"verb"},"screened":{"h":"screened","l":"screen","q":"verb"},"screening":{"h":"screening","l":"screen","q":"verb"},"equations":{"h":"equations","l":"equation","q":"noun"},"mates":{"h":"mates","l":"mate","q":"noun"},"mated":{"h":"mated","l":"mate","q":"verb"},"mating":{"h":"mating","i":"/ˈmeɪtɪŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-mating.wav","l":"mate","q":"verb"},"bigger":{"h":"bigger","i":"/ˈbɪɡɚ/","a":"en-us-bigger.ogg","l":"big","q":"adjective"},"biggest":{"h":"biggest","i":"/ˈbɪɡɪst/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Persent101-biggest.wav","l":"big","q":"adjective"},"informs":{"h":"informs","l":"inform","q":"verb"},"informed":{"h":"informed","a":"en-us-informed.ogg","l":"inform","q":"verb"},"informing":{"h":"informing","l":"inform","q":"verb"},"stirs":{"h":"stirs","l":"stir","q":"verb"},"stirred":{"h":"stirred","a":"en-us-stirred.ogg","l":"stir","q":"verb"},"stirring":{"h":"stirring","i":"/ˈstɝɪŋ/","a":"en-us-stirring.ogg","l":"stir","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"or inspiring.","e":"He gave such a stirring speech that many people were moved to tears."},{"m":"or lively."}]}]},"democracies":{"h":"democracies","l":"democracy","q":"noun"},"rehearses":{"h":"rehearses","l":"rehearse","q":"verb"},"rehearsed":{"h":"rehearsed","l":"rehearse","q":"verb"},"spot":{"h":"spot","i":"/spɒt/","a":"en-us-spot.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A spot is a small area that's different from that area around it.","e":"I have a bald spot on my head."},{"m":"(countable) A spot is a place, position, or period of time.","e":"\"There... \" I said, pointing to a spot near Forest Hills."},{"m":"(countable) A spot is a place, especially one that you like going to.","e":"Pizza and seared halibut are among the excellent dishes at this Wine Country hot spot."},{"m":"(countable) A spot is a place in a group.","e":"A 42-35 victory that gave the Spartans a playoff spot."},{"m":"(countable) A spot is a commercial time on TV or Radio.","e":"This year, Fox is asking $2.7 million per 30-second spot, and advertisers are lined up for the opportunity."},{"m":"(countable) (British) A spot of something is a small amount of it.","e":"Would you like a spot of tea?"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you spot something, you see it, even though it may be difficult to see.","e":"I spotted Lisa shopping at the grocery store with Mike yesterday."},{"m":"If something is spotted, it has or gets spots on it.","e":"Oh no! That red wine spotted my new shirt!"},{"m":"(transitive) If you spot someone money, you give or lend it to them.","e":"Can you spot me a five for the burger?"},{"m":"(transitive) If you spot someone points in a game, you let them have points to make the game more even."},{"m":"If your spot someone doing something dangerous, you watch closely to help if needed.","e":"I can't do a cartwheel unless someone spots me."}]}]},"sails":{"h":"sails","a":"en-us-sails.ogg","l":"sail","q":"noun"},"sailed":{"h":"sailed","a":"en-us-sailed.ogg","l":"sail","q":"verb"},"sailing":{"h":"sailing","i":"/ˈseɪ.lɪŋ/","a":"en-us-sailing.ogg","l":"sail","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Sailing is a sport where people race by sailing."}]}]},"aimed":{"h":"aimed","a":"en-us-aimed.ogg","l":"aim","q":"verb"},"aiming":{"h":"aiming","l":"aim","q":"verb"},"advises":{"h":"advises","l":"advise","q":"verb"},"advised":{"h":"advised","a":"en-us-advised.ogg","l":"advise","q":"verb"},"advising":{"h":"advising","l":"advise","q":"verb"},"carps":{"h":"carps","l":"carp","q":"noun"},"carped":{"h":"carped","l":"carp","q":"verb"},"carping":{"h":"carping","l":"carp","q":"verb"},"guards":{"h":"guards","l":"guard","q":"noun"},"guarded":{"h":"guarded","i":"/ˈɡɑrdɪd/","a":"en-us-guarded.ogg","l":"guard","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"or careful."},{"m":"ed by a guard."}]}]},"guarding":{"h":"guarding","l":"guard","q":"verb"},"provinces":{"h":"provinces","a":"en-us-provinces.ogg","l":"province","q":"noun"},"explores":{"h":"explores","l":"explore","q":"verb"},"explored":{"h":"explored","l":"explore","q":"verb"},"exploring":{"h":"exploring","a":"en-us-exploring.ogg","l":"explore","q":"verb"},"coloreds":{"h":"coloreds","l":"colored","q":"noun"},"beggared":{"h":"beggared","l":"beggar","q":"verb"},"beggaring":{"h":"beggaring","l":"beggar","q":"verb"},"collapsed":{"h":"collapsed","l":"collapse","q":"verb"},"collapsing":{"h":"collapsing","l":"collapse","q":"verb"},"julys":{"h":"Julys","l":"july","q":"noun"},"stronger":{"h":"stronger","i":"/strɒŋɡə/","a":"en-us-stronger.ogg","l":"strong","q":"adjective"},"strongest":{"h":"strongest","i":"/ˈstrɒŋɡəst/","a":"en-us-strongest.ogg","l":"strong","q":"adjective"},"steep":{"h":"steep","i":"/stiːp/","a":"en-us-steep.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a hill or slope is steep, it goes up at a high angle.","e":"Be very careful; the hill is very steep and it's easy to fall and hurt yourself."},{"m":"If a price or cost of something is steep, it is very high or expensive.","e":"$500 for an old, used television set? No thanks, that's too steep for me."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To soak something in a liquid."},{"m":"To be soaked in a liquid."},{"m":"To be full of some quality.","e":"The accident is steeped in mystery."}]}]},"jail":{"h":"jail","i":"/dʒeɪl/","a":"en-us-jail.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A place where people who have done a crime or a suspected of having done a crime are kept."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To put someone in jail."}]}]},"stable":{"h":"stable","i":"/ˈsteɪ.bəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-stable.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is stable, it is unlikely to move or change.","e":"That number has remained relatively stable over the years."},{"m":"If you are stable, you are calm and don't get upset easily.","e":"I'm a lot more stable than I was as a teen."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A stable is a building for housing animals like horses and cows."}]}]},"ally":{"h":"ally","i":"/ˈæ.laɪ/","a":"en-us-ally.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Two countries are allies if they support, help, and defend each other.","e":"England and the United States have been allies for most of the last two centuries."},{"m":"(countable) Two people or groups can also be allies.","e":"We didn't like each other, but we had the same goals, so we became uneasy allies."},{"m":"(countable) An ally is anything that helps you.","e":"This little blue pill is your ally in the war against weight gain."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you ally yourself with someone, you become their ally.","e":"Some Indian groups allied themselves with the French, others with the English."},{"m":"(transitive), If two things are allied, they are related, are connected, or have many similarities.","e":"The bird was closely allied to the tits of England."}]}]},"stall":{"h":"stall","i":"/stɔːl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-stall.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A stall is a small room or area, usually for one person, animal, etc.","e":"I stepped into a shower stall and turned on the cold water."},{"m":"(countable) A stall is when something flying loses lift because it is not moving at a good angle to the air.","e":"The airplane went into a stall and started dropping."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something stalls, it stops improving or progressing.","e":"Talks between Israel and the Palestinians have stalled."},{"m":"If an engine or vehicle stalls, it stops working because there is too much load and not enough fuel.","e":"The truck was stalled in the middle of the street."},{"m":"If you stall, you purposefully slow things down or make people wait because you're not ready.","e":"\"Can you tell me again?\" she said, stalling for time."}]}]},"initiates":{"h":"initiates","l":"initiate","q":"verb"},"initiated":{"h":"initiated","l":"initiate","q":"verb"},"initiating":{"h":"initiating","l":"initiate","q":"verb"},"laboured":{"h":"laboured","a":"en-us-laboured.ogg","l":"labour","q":"verb"},"labouring":{"h":"labouring","a":"en-us-labouring.ogg","l":"labour","q":"verb"},"labored":{"h":"labored","a":"en-us-laboured.ogg","l":"labor","q":"verb"},"laboring":{"h":"laboring","a":"en-us-labouring.ogg","l":"labor","q":"verb"},"compliments":{"h":"compliments","i":"/ˈkɑmplɪmənts/","a":"en-us-compliments.ogg","l":"compliment","q":"noun"},"complimented":{"h":"complimented","l":"compliment","q":"verb"},"complimenting":{"h":"complimenting","l":"compliment","q":"verb"},"fields":{"h":"fields","a":"en-us-fields.ogg","l":"field","q":"noun"},"fielded":{"h":"fielded","l":"field","q":"verb"},"fielding":{"h":"fielding","l":"field","q":"verb"},"logs":{"h":"logs","a":"en-us-logs.ogg","l":"log","q":"noun"},"logged":{"h":"logged","l":"log","q":"verb"},"logging":{"h":"logging","l":"log","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Logging is the act or instance of cutting trees.","e":"The loggings were spread over large areas, but mainly near the few roads that existed."},{"m":"Logging is the act of making an entry in a log."}]}]},"representatives":{"h":"representatives","a":"en-us-representatives.ogg","l":"representative","q":"noun"},"chairpersons":{"h":"chairpersons","l":"chairperson","q":"noun"},"buys":{"h":"buys","l":"buy","q":"verb"},"buying":{"h":"buying","i":"/ˈbaɪ.ɪŋ/","a":"en-us-buying.ogg","l":"buy","q":"verb"},"bothers":{"h":"bothers","l":"bother","q":"verb"},"bothered":{"h":"bothered","l":"bother","q":"verb"},"bothering":{"h":"bothering","l":"bother","q":"verb"},"flats":{"h":"flats","l":"flat","q":"noun"},"unions":{"h":"unions","l":"union","q":"noun"},"sketches":{"h":"sketches","l":"sketch","q":"noun"},"sketched":{"h":"sketched","l":"sketch","q":"verb"},"sketching":{"h":"sketching","l":"sketch","q":"verb"},"minored":{"h":"minored","l":"minor","q":"verb"},"minoring":{"h":"minoring","l":"minor","q":"verb"},"majors":{"h":"majors","l":"major","q":"noun"},"majored":{"h":"majored","l":"major","q":"verb"},"majoring":{"h":"majoring","l":"major","q":"verb"},"allies":{"h":"Allies","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"The countries who fought against the Axis Powers during World War II. Some of those countries were: the United States, Russia, Britain, France, Canada, and China."}]}]},"allied":{"h":"allied","i":"/əˈlaɪd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-allied (verb).wav","l":"ally","q":"verb"},"allying":{"h":"allying","l":"ally","q":"verb"},"conducts":{"h":"conducts","l":"conduct","q":"verb"},"conducted":{"h":"conducted","i":"/kənˈdʌktɪd/","a":"en-us-conducted.ogg","l":"conduct","q":"verb"},"conducting":{"h":"conducting","i":"/kənˈdʌktɪŋ/","a":"en-us-conducting.ogg","l":"conduct","q":"verb"},"stock":{"h":"stock","i":"/stɒk/","a":"en-us-stock.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Your stock is the collection of things that you have available, usually to sell.","e":"It depend on where the store got its stock from."},{"m":"(countable) A stock is a share in a public company.","e":"ETFs are mutual funds that trade on stock exchanges, just as stocks do."},{"m":"If something is in stock it is at the store and available for sale.","e":"I think we have five more in stock."},{"m":"If something is out of stock it is not at the store and available for sale.","e":"I'm sorry, we're all out of stock."},{"m":"(uncountable) Stock is a basic soup made from boiling meat, bones, or vegetables.","e":"Add a cup of chicken stock and half a cup of cream and cook for 10 minutes."},{"m":"If you take stock of a situation, you think about it and plan what to do next."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If a store stocks a product, it has it available to be sold.","e":"They are expensive, and most stores won't stock them."},{"m":"(transitive) If you stock x with y, you fill x with y.","e":"I've stocked the fridge with beer for the party."},{"m":"If you stock up on something, you get more than you use in a short time.","e":"Residents there are stocking up on food and water for the winter."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is stock, it is the usual one with no special changes or additions.","e":"The car's engine, tires, brakes and steering are all stock."}]}]},"struggle":{"h":"struggle","i":"/ˈstrʌɡəl/","a":"en-us-struggle.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you struggle to do something difficult, you work very hard to do it.","e":"They struggled to survive in New York City on $25,000 a year."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A struggle is a fight, often long and hard, or needing a lot of effort.","e":"As long as they are not willing to make peace, there will be armed struggle."}]}]},"substantial":{"h":"substantial","i":"/səbˈstænʃəl/","a":"en-us-substantial.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is substantial, it is not small.","e":"The children spent a substantial portion of the day in free play or unstructured time."}]}]},"sue":{"h":"sue","i":"/suː/","a":"en-us-sue.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you sue someone, you take them to court to make them do something they don't want to do, often to make them pay you money.","e":"They successfully sued the company they had worked for, winning a combined award of $275,000."}]}]},"penetrate":{"h":"penetrate","i":"/ˈpɛnɪtreɪt/","a":"en-us-penetrate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you penetrate something, you enter it.","e":"The rocket was the first to penetrate space."}]}]},"tablet":{"h":"tablet","i":"/ˈtæblət/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-tablet.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A tablet is a small, hard medicine or vitamin that you take by mouth.","e":"Take only one 600-milligram tablet of calcium a day."},{"m":"(countable) A tablet is a hard surface for writing on.","e":"The agreement is not written on tablets of stone."},{"m":"(countable) A tablet is a tablet computer; a large touch-screen device.","e":"I bring a tablet to work rather than a laptop because it is more portable."}]}]},"tackle":{"h":"tackle","i":"/ˈtækəl/","a":"en-us-tackle.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you tackle a problem, issue, question, etc., you try to solve it.","e":"We want an executive who solves problems and tackles issues."},{"m":"(transitive) If you tackle a person, you jump on them and pull them to the ground, usually in sports such as American football."},{"m":"(transitive) If you tackle a person in soccer, you take the ball from them."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A tackle is an attempt to pull somebody to the ground, usually in sports such as American football.","e":"Gaines Adams put constant pressure on the Atlanta quarterback and finished the game with six tackles and two sacks."},{"m":"(countable) A tackle is an attempt to take the ball from somebody in sports such as soccer."},{"m":"(countable) A tackle is a position in American football (see diagram below).","e":"Georgia defensive tackle Kade Weston has been out the past two games with an injured knee."},{"m":"(uncountable) Fishing tackle is the equipment used to catch fish.","e":"He gathered his camp supplies including fishing tackle."},{"m":"; (singular) A block and tackle is a system of ropes and pulleys used to lift heavy weights."}]}]},"tank":{"h":"tank","i":"/tæŋk/","a":"en-au-tank.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A tank is a large, strong container for gas or liquid.","e":"The gas stove was connected to a propane tank."},{"m":"(countable) A tank is a large metal vehicle with a gun that runs on tracks.","e":"They do not have heavy weapons such as tanks and armored vehicles."},{"m":"(countable) The tank is a room, usually in a police station, for keeping people locked up.","e":"The police threw him in the holding tank with us."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If something tanks, it gets worse quickly."}]}]},"tanks":{"h":"tanks","l":"tank","q":"noun"},"tanked":{"h":"tanked","a":"en-au-tanked.ogg","l":"tank","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":".","e":"Oh man, Don is so tanked! I bet he won't remember this tomorrow!"}]}]},"tanking":{"h":"tanking","l":"tank","q":"verb"},"tackles":{"h":"tackles","l":"tackle","q":"verb"},"tackled":{"h":"tackled","l":"tackle","q":"verb"},"tackling":{"h":"tackling","l":"tackle","q":"verb"},"tablets":{"h":"tablets","l":"tablet","q":"noun"},"penetrates":{"h":"penetrates","l":"penetrate","q":"verb"},"penetrated":{"h":"penetrated","a":"en-us-penetrated.ogg","l":"penetrate","q":"verb"},"penetrating":{"h":"penetrating","a":"en-us-penetrating.ogg","l":"penetrate","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Very sharp, able to penetrate.","e":"The skunk produces a penetrating odor."}]}]},"solicitors":{"h":"solicitors","l":"solicitor","q":"noun"},"defeats":{"h":"defeats","a":"En-us-defeats.ogg","l":"defeat","q":"verb"},"defeating":{"h":"defeating","l":"defeat","q":"verb"},"refurbishes":{"h":"refurbishes","l":"refurbish","q":"verb"},"refurbished":{"h":"refurbished","l":"refurbish","q":"verb"},"refurbishing":{"h":"refurbishing","l":"refurbish","q":"verb"},"scenes":{"h":"scenes","a":"en-us-scenes.ogg","l":"scene","q":"noun"},"sins":{"h":"sins","a":"en-us-sins.ogg","l":"sin","q":"noun"},"sillier":{"h":"sillier","l":"silly","q":"adjective"},"silliest":{"h":"silliest","l":"silly","q":"adjective"},"sessions":{"h":"sessions","l":"session","q":"noun"},"scares":{"h":"scares","l":"scare","q":"verb"},"scaring":{"h":"scaring","l":"scare","q":"verb"},"rubbishes":{"h":"rubbishes","l":"rubbish","q":"verb"},"rubbished":{"h":"rubbished","l":"rubbish","q":"verb"},"rubbishing":{"h":"rubbishing","l":"rubbish","q":"verb"},"retires":{"h":"retires","l":"retire","q":"verb"},"retired":{"h":"retired","l":"retire","q":"verb"},"retiring":{"h":"retiring","l":"retire","q":"verb"},"resists":{"h":"resists","l":"resist","q":"verb"},"resisted":{"h":"resisted","i":"/rɪˈzɪstɪd/","a":"en-us-resisted.ogg","l":"resist","q":"verb"},"resisting":{"h":"resisting","i":"/rɪˈzɪstɪŋ/","a":"en-us-resisting.ogg","l":"resist","q":"verb"},"replies":{"h":"replies","l":"reply","q":"verb"},"replied":{"h":"replied","i":"/rɪˈplaɪd/","a":"en-us-replied.ogg","l":"reply","q":"verb"},"replying":{"h":"replying","i":"/rɪˈplaɪŋ/","a":"en-us-replying.ogg","l":"reply","q":"verb"},"reserves":{"h":"reserves","a":"en-us-reserves.ogg","l":"reserve","q":"verb"},"reserved":{"h":"reserved","i":"/rɪˈzɝvd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Persent101-reserved.wav","l":"reserve","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is reserved, they are quiet, and don't like to talk about their feelings.","e":"She greeted us warmly, but her fried was more reserved."}]}]},"reserving":{"h":"reserving","l":"reserve","q":"verb"},"struggles":{"h":"struggles","a":"en-us-struggles.ogg","l":"struggle","q":"verb"},"struggled":{"h":"struggled","a":"en-us-struggled.ogg","l":"struggle","q":"verb"},"struggling":{"h":"struggling","a":"en-us-struggling.ogg","l":"struggle","q":"verb"},"bellies":{"h":"bellies","l":"belly","q":"noun"},"barks":{"h":"barks","l":"bark","q":"noun"},"batters":{"h":"batters","l":"batter","q":"noun"},"beaches":{"h":"beaches","l":"beach","q":"noun"},"beached":{"h":"beached","l":"beach","q":"verb"},"beaching":{"h":"beaching","l":"beach","q":"verb"},"beams":{"h":"beams","i":"/biːmz/","a":"en-us-beams.ogg","l":"beam","q":"noun"},"beamed":{"h":"beamed","l":"beam","q":"verb"},"beaming":{"h":"beaming","l":"beam","q":"verb"},"bets":{"h":"bets","l":"bet","q":"verb"},"betting":{"h":"betting","i":"/ˈbɛtɪŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-betting.wav","l":"bet","q":"verb"},"biases":{"h":"biases","l":"bias","q":"noun"},"biasses":{"h":"biasses","l":"bias","q":"noun"},"biased":{"h":"biased","l":"bias","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Having or showing a bias.","e":"The newspaper gave a biased account of the story."}]}]},"biasing":{"h":"biasing","l":"bias","q":"verb"},"biassed":{"h":"biassed","l":"bias","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Having or showing a bias.","e":"The newspaper gave a biassed account of the story."}]}]},"biassing":{"h":"biassing","l":"bias","q":"verb"},"accords":{"h":"accords","l":"accord","q":"noun"},"accorded":{"h":"accorded","l":"accord","q":"verb"},"maniac":{"h":"maniac","i":"/ˈmeɪniˌæk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-maniac.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A maniac is someone who is crazy. Their mind is not working right.","e":"It is never safe to trust a maniac."},{"m":"A maniac is a person who has an obsession with or extreme enthusiasm for something."}]}]},"maniacs":{"h":"maniacs","l":"maniac","q":"noun"},"adjusts":{"h":"adjusts","l":"adjust","q":"verb"},"adjusting":{"h":"adjusting","l":"adjust","q":"verb"},"adopts":{"h":"adopts","l":"adopt","q":"verb"},"adopting":{"h":"adopting","l":"adopt","q":"verb"},"adulthood":{"h":"adulthood","i":"/ˈadʌlthʊd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-adulthood.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Adulthood is the state or condition of being an adult.","e":"He has just entered adulthood."}]}]},"childhood":{"h":"childhood","i":"/ˈtʃaɪld.hʊd/","a":"en-us-childhood.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Childhood is the state or condition of being an child, that is, being under 18 years of age.","e":"Childhood is the first stage of every man's life."}]}]},"addresses":{"h":"addresses","l":"address","q":"noun"},"addressed":{"h":"addressed","l":"address","q":"verb"},"addressing":{"h":"addressing","i":"/əˈdrɛsɪŋ/","a":"en-us-addressing.ogg","l":"address","q":"verb"},"admits":{"h":"admits","i":"/ədˈmɪts/","l":"admit","q":"verb"},"admitted":{"h":"admitted","i":"/ədˈmɪtɪd/","a":"en-us-admitted.ogg","l":"admit","q":"verb"},"admitting":{"h":"admitting","i":"/ədˈmɪtɪŋ/","l":"admit","q":"verb"},"affects":{"h":"affects","l":"affect","q":"verb"},"affected":{"h":"affected","i":"/əˈfɛktɪd/","a":"en-us-affected.ogg","l":"affect","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If x is affected by y, then y causes a change in x.","e":"The girls are still very affected by the loss of their father."},{"m":"If something that somebody does is affected, it is not natural or not real.","e":"The young ladies looked on with affected interest."}]}]},"affecting":{"h":"affecting","i":"/əˈfɛktɪŋ/","a":"en-us-affecting.ogg","l":"affect","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is affecting, it makes you feel strong feelings, especially sadness or pity.","e":"It was very affecting to see the tears of disappointment in his eyes."}]}]},"admires":{"h":"admires","l":"admire","q":"verb"},"admiring":{"h":"admiring","i":"/æd.'maɪ.ɚ.ɪŋ/","a":"en-us-admiring.ogg","l":"admire","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are admiring of somebody or something, you think them good or nice; you respect them.","e":"I was very admiring of these two young women who worked so hard."}]}]},"admired":{"h":"admired","i":"/ədˈmaɪrd/","a":"en-us-admired.ogg","l":"admire","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something or someone is admired, people think it is good or they like it.","e":"The Rolling Stones are a very admired band."}]}]},"positives":{"h":"positives","l":"positive","q":"noun"},"keeps":{"h":"keeps","a":"en-us-keeps.ogg","l":"keep","q":"verb"},"kept":{"h":"kept","i":"/ˈkɛpt/","a":"en-us-kept.ogg","l":"keep","q":"verb"},"keeping":{"h":"keeping","i":"/ˈkiːpɪŋ/","a":"en-us-keeping.ogg","l":"keep","q":"verb"},"scholar":{"h":"scholar","i":"/ˈskɒlə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-scholar.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A scholar is a student who studies at school or college."},{"m":"(countable) A scholar is a person who knows many things.","e":"Socrates was an ancient Greek scholar."},{"m":"(countable) A scholar is a somebody who studies for their whole life."}]}]},"scholars":{"h":"scholars","a":"en-us-scholars.ogg","l":"scholar","q":"noun"},"threat":{"h":"threat","i":"/θrɛt/","a":"en-us-threat.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A threat is something or someone that might be bad or dangerous, or cause a problem.","e":"The product posed a serious health threat and should not be used."},{"m":"(countable) A threat is the words somebody uses to tell you they will do something bad to you unless you do what they want you to.","e":"He made a lot of threats, but he didn't do anything."}]}]},"tidy":{"h":"tidy","i":"/ˈtaɪdi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-tidy.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is tidy, it is clean and everything is in its place.","e":"Her small, tidy, little house seemed very nice."},{"m":"A tidy person is somebody who keeps thing clean and organized."},{"m":"A tidy amount is not small.","e":"They're planning to sell them for a tidy profit."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you tidy something up, you pick up things and put everything back where it belongs.","e":"Give me a minute to go tidy up the room."}]}]},"threats":{"h":"threats","i":"/θrɛts/","a":"en-us-threats.ogg","l":"threat","q":"noun"},"tile":{"h":"tile","i":"/taɪl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-tile.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A tile is a hard flat building material, usually made of clay or glass.","e":"The new floor would be ceramic tile, and the tiles on the walls were being replaced."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you tile a surface, you cover it with [[#Noun|tiles]]."}]}]},"tidies":{"h":"tidies","l":"tidy","q":"verb"},"tidied":{"h":"tidied","l":"tidy","q":"verb"},"tidying":{"h":"tidying","i":"/ˈtaɪ.di.ɪŋ/","l":"tidy","q":"verb"},"tip":{"h":"tip","i":"/tɪp/","a":"en-us-tip.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The tip of something is the farthest point of it.","e":"She runs her finger down the bird's back and to the tip of its tail."},{"m":"(countable) A tip is words or ideas that help you solve a problem.","e":"Police say anonymous tips have led them to more than 20 of the stolen items."},{"m":"(countable) A tip is a small amount of money that you give to somebody to thank them for good service."},{"m":"(countable) If something is the tip of the iceberg, it is just a small part of something much bigger.","e":"The problems we've seen today are just the tip of the iceberg."},{"m":"(countable) If something is on the tip of your tongue, you feel that you know it, but you can't say it.","e":"I wanted the words to come out; They were on the tip of my tongue, but my mind still wasn't clear."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something tips, the top of it moves to one side more than the bottom.","e":"The piano tipped over as we were putting it on the truck."},{"m":"(transitive) If you tip something into something else, you pour it.","e":"He tipped the water out of the glass by accident."},{"m":"If you tip somebody, you give them money to thank them for good service."},{"m":"If you tip somebody off, you tell them about something that's going to happen.","e":"The police were tipped off by a phone call."},{"m":"(transitive) If you tip your hat, you touch it or pick it up when you meet or leave somebody."},{"m":"(transitive) If you tip your hat to somebody, you thank or congratulate them."}]}]},"tips":{"h":"tips","a":"en-us-tips.ogg","l":"tip","q":"noun"},"tipped":{"h":"tipped","l":"tip","q":"verb"},"tipping":{"h":"tipping","l":"tip","q":"verb"},"stocks":{"h":"stocks","l":"stock","q":"noun"},"stocked":{"h":"stocked","l":"stock","q":"verb"},"tidier":{"h":"tidier","l":"tidy","q":"adjective"},"tidiest":{"h":"tidiest","l":"tidy","q":"adjective"},"recognizing":{"h":"recognizing","a":"en-us-recognizing.ogg","l":"recognize","q":"verb"},"recognized":{"h":"recognized","i":"/ˈrɛkəɡnaɪzd/","a":"en-us-recognized.ogg","l":"recognize","q":"verb"},"pockets":{"h":"pockets","a":"en-us-pockets.ogg","l":"pocket","q":"noun"},"pocketed":{"h":"pocketed","l":"pocket","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a piece of clothing or some other equipment is pocketed, it has pockets."}]}]},"pocketing":{"h":"pocketing","l":"pocket","q":"verb"},"x-rayed":{"h":"X-rayed","l":"x-ray","q":"verb"},"x-raying":{"h":"X-raying","l":"x-ray","q":"verb"},"whales":{"h":"whales","i":"/weɪlz/","l":"whale","q":"noun"},"whaled":{"h":"whaled","l":"whale","q":"verb"},"whaling":{"h":"whaling","i":"/ˈweɪlɪŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-whaling.wav","l":"whale","q":"verb"},"audited":{"h":"audited","l":"audit","q":"verb"},"auditing":{"h":"auditing","l":"audit","q":"verb"},"pats":{"h":"pats","l":"pat","q":"noun"},"patted":{"h":"patted","a":"en-us-patted.ogg","l":"pat","q":"verb"},"patting":{"h":"patting","l":"pat","q":"verb"},"tory":{"h":"Tory","i":"/ˈtɔːri/","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"A Tory is a member of the Conservative party of Britain or Canada.","e":"60 Tory MPs who refused to support Mrs Thatcher for leader last week."}]}]},"tough":{"h":"tough","i":"/tʌf/","a":"en-us-tough.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is tough, it is difficult, not easy.","e":"It's important to stay healthy when the going gets tough."},{"m":"If something is tough, it doesn't change or move easily; it's not soft.","e":"The government is taking a tough stance on crime."},{"m":"If something is tough, it is not nice to experience.","e":"He should get the toughest penalty possible for this killing."},{"m":"If a person is tough, they are strong and may often fight.","e":"He was an older guy, truly tough with huge arms and a gold cross chain."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you tough something out, it is difficult, but you continue; you don't give up.","e":"Even though it rained the whole time, they toughed it out without complaining."}]}]},"toughs":{"h":"toughs","l":"tough","q":"verb"},"tougher":{"h":"tougher","l":"tough","q":"adjective"},"toughed":{"h":"toughed","l":"tough","q":"verb"},"toughing":{"h":"toughing","l":"tough","q":"verb"},"toughest":{"h":"toughest","l":"tough","q":"adjective"},"track":{"h":"track","i":"/træk/","a":"en-us-track.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A track is a line on the ground or in space that people, animals or vehicles follow.","e":"It's right where Hardy Road crosses the railroad tracks."},{"m":"(countable) A track is a single part of an audio recording that can be separated from other parts of a recording.","e":"You can make digital copies of the CD tracks and save them in MP3 format."},{"m":"(countable) A track is a mark left on the ground by somebody or something walking or driving.","e":"Phillip glanced at the policemen measuring and marking the tire tracks."},{"m":"(uncountable) If you keep track of something, you follow it or always know where it is or what's happening with it.","e":"I use a watch in order to keep track of how long I've been studying."},{"m":"(uncountable) Track is the sport of running and jumping on a track.","e":"No new records were set in the most recent track and field championships."},{"m":"(countable) If you're on track to do something, you are taking the right steps to prepare and should be able to do it in the future.","e":"Making a study plan is a good way to keep on track with your homework."},{"m":"(countable) If you're on the fast track, you are moving ahead quickly in your job."},{"m":"(countable) A track is a long, flat circular band that goes over wheels to help a vehicle move in snow, on sand, etc."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you track something down, you find it after looking for it.","e":"He was trying to track down where she lived."},{"m":"If you track something, you follow it, to see where it's going or how it's changing.","e":"I also started weighing myself weekly to track my progress."},{"m":"If you track mud, water, or some other substance somewhere, you walk and leave it there.","e":"The kids tracked mud all over my clean floors."}]}]},"treasure":{"h":"treasure","i":"/ˈtrɛʒɚ/","a":"en-us-treasure.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Treasure is a collection of valuable things, such as gold, diamonds, money, etc.","e":"Going after buried treasure is just as scary in real life as it is in the movies."},{"m":"(countable) A treasure is something or someone that is very valuable or important.","e":"As an actor, he's a national treasure."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you treasure something that belongs to you, you take good care of it; it is very important to you.","e":"We will always treasure the memories of his visits."}]}]},"treasures":{"h":"treasures","i":"/ˈtrɛʒɚz/","a":"en-us-treasures.ogg","l":"treasure","q":"noun"},"belongs":{"h":"belongs","i":"/bɪˈlɒŋz/","a":"en-us-belongs.ogg","l":"belong","q":"verb"},"tremendous":{"h":"tremendous","a":"en-us-tremendous.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is tremendous, it is very good or very big.","e":"We've put a tremendous amount of effort into solving this case."}]}]},"belonged":{"h":"belonged","i":"/bɪˈlɒŋd/","a":"en-us-belonged.ogg","l":"belong","q":"verb"},"belonging":{"h":"belonging","i":"/bɪˈlɔŋɪŋ/","a":"en-us-belonging.ogg","l":"belong","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (usually plural) Your belongings are the things that you own.","e":"Make sure you take all your belongings when you leave."}]}]},"loves":{"h":"loves","i":"/lʌvz/","a":"en-us-loves.ogg","l":"love","q":"verb"},"loved":{"h":"loved","i":"/lʌvd/","a":"en-us-loved.ogg","l":"love","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is loved by you, you feel great affection for it.","e":"John was loved by many people and he will be greatly missed."}]}]},"loving":{"h":"loving","i":"/ˈlʌvɪŋ/","a":"en-us-loving.ogg","l":"love","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"To be loving is to show love or affection towards someone.","e":"She is a loving mother."}]}]},"treasured":{"h":"treasured","i":"/ˈtrɛʒəd/","l":"treasure","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is treasured, it is considered to be important."}]}]},"treasuring":{"h":"treasuring","l":"treasure","q":"verb"},"trial":{"h":"trial","i":"/ˈtraɪəl/","a":"en-us-trial.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A trial is a meeting in court with a judge where two sides explain their positions and the judge or jury makes a decision.","e":"He was taken to jail to await trial for murder."},{"m":"(countable) A trial is a test to see if something works or not, especially in science.","e":"Several randomized clinical trials have shown that aspirin may reduce the risk of cancer."},{"m":"(uncountable) Trial and error is the process of trying things and making mistakes as you learn something.","e":"There is some trial and error to finding the right solution."},{"m":"(countable) A trial is a competition where the winners are chosen to move on to higher level competitions.","e":"She finishes in the top three at the Olympic trials in Toronto."},{"m":"(countable) A trial is a difficult experience."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you trial something, you test it to see if it works, especially in science."}]}]},"trying":{"h":"trying","i":"/ˈtraɪ.ɪŋ/","a":"en-us-trying.ogg","l":"try","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is trying, it is difficult and makes you feel bad and tired."}]}]},"tries":{"h":"tries","a":"en-us-tries.ogg","l":"try","q":"verb"},"tried":{"h":"tried","i":"/traɪd/","a":"en-us-tried.ogg","l":"try","q":"verb"},"editor":{"h":"editor","i":"/ˈɛdɪtə/","a":"en-us-editor.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An editor is someone who edits or changes the text in a document.","e":"Simple English Wiktionary welcomes all editors to edit its pages."},{"m":"(countable) An editor is a computer program that allows users to add text to a document.","e":"Simple English Wiktionary has a special editor for adding or modifying pages."}]}]},"editors":{"h":"editors","l":"editor","q":"noun"},"ultimate":{"h":"ultimate","i":"/ˈʌltɪmɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-ultimate.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"The ultimate goal, success, decision, etc. is the final one.","e":"You can't have ultimate success without a lot of little successes."},{"m":"The ultimate test, responsibility, power, etc. is the one that is more important, bigger, stronger, etc. than the others.","e":"They are trying to build the ultimate computer, one that can do anything and everything."}]}]},"variety":{"h":"variety","i":"/vəˈraɪ.ɪ.ti/","a":"en-us-variety.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (singular) A variety of things is a group of things that are not all the same.","e":"Americans can buy a wide variety of cheap products at local supermarkets."},{"m":"(uncountable) Variety is the quality of not being the same.","e":"Fruit can add variety to your salads."},{"m":"(countable) A variety is one kind of something, especially plants and animals.","e":"The shop has 25 tomato varieties."}]}]},"vast":{"h":"vast","i":"/vɑːst/","a":"en-us-vast.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is vast, it is very, very big.","e":"Tax rates will go up for the vast majority of the population."}]}]},"virtual":{"h":"virtual","i":"/ˈvɜːtʃuəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-virtual.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A virtual world, tour, address, etc. is one that is made to look like or replace a real one, usually using a computer.","e":"He is the designer of three of the top virtual reality games."},{"m":"A virtual monopoly, certainty, disappearance, etc. is a one that is close to 100%.","e":"Google has a virtual monopoly on web searches."}]}]},"ward":{"h":"ward","i":"/wɔːd/","a":"en-us-ward.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A ward is an area in a hospital that focused on one kind of medicine.","e":"We visited them in the hospital's children's ward."},{"m":"(countable) A ward is an area of a city.","e":"The lower ninth ward of New Orleans was destroyed by the flood."},{"m":"(countable) A ward is someone, usually a child, who is under the legal care of someone else."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you ward off something bad, you do something to keep it away."}]}]},"witness":{"h":"witness","i":"/ˈwɪtnəs/","a":"en-us-witness.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A witness is somebody who saw something, especially a crime.","e":"The journalist spent three years interviewing survivors and witnesses."},{"m":"(countable) A witness is somebody who tells a court what they know about a situation, especially a crime.","e":"The witness testified that Simpson was ill at the time."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you witness something, you see it.","e":"She spoke of the terrible events she witnesses during the war."},{"m":"(transitive) If something witnesses something, it experiences it."}]}]},"abbeys":{"h":"abbeys","l":"abbey","q":"noun"},"absences":{"h":"absences","l":"absence","q":"noun"},"albums":{"h":"albums","l":"album","q":"noun"},"alcoholics":{"h":"alcoholics","l":"alcoholic","q":"noun"},"basements":{"h":"basements","l":"basement","q":"noun"},"bats":{"h":"bats","i":"/bæts/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Persent101-bats.wav","l":"bat","q":"noun"},"behaves":{"h":"behaves","l":"behave","q":"verb"},"benches":{"h":"benches","l":"bench","q":"noun"},"bibles":{"h":"bibles","l":"bible","q":"noun"},"blades":{"h":"blades","l":"blade","q":"noun"},"bolts":{"h":"bolts","i":"/bəʊlts/","l":"bolt","q":"noun"},"borders":{"h":"borders","i":"/bɔrdərz/","l":"border","q":"noun"},"brakes":{"h":"brakes","i":"/breɪks/","a":"en-us-breaks.ogg","l":"brake","q":"noun"},"bucks":{"h":"bucks","l":"buck","q":"noun"},"buckets":{"h":"buckets","l":"bucket","q":"noun"},"bugs":{"h":"bugs","i":"/bʌɡz/","l":"bug","q":"noun"},"burdens":{"h":"burdens","l":"burden","q":"noun"},"bursts":{"h":"bursts","l":"burst","q":"noun"},"cans":{"h":"cans","a":"en-au-cans.ogg","l":"can","q":"noun"},"ceilings":{"h":"ceilings","l":"ceiling","q":"noun"},"classics":{"h":"classi