","i":"/ˈɔrɡənaɪzd/","a":"en-us-organized.ogg","l":"organise","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is organised, it is in a state of order."}]}]},"organising":{"h":"organising","l":"organise","q":"verb"},"capture":{"h":"capture","i":"/ˈkæp.ʃɚ/","a":"en-us-capture.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you capture a person or animal, you catch them and do not let them go free.","e":"Keith Maupin is the first American soldier captured in Iraq."},{"m":"(transitive) If an army, a team, etc. captures a place or an object, it takes control of it.","e":"The Christians captured the holy city of Jerusalem."},{"m":"(transitive) If you capture an image, a sound, or a feeling, you show it clearly in your picture, movie, art, etc.","e":"She captured the beautiful scenery of the hills with her camera."},{"m":"(transitive) If something captures your imagination, it makes you interested in it.","e":"A good science teacher captures the imagination of children with experiments."},{"m":"(transitive) If somebody captures your heart, you fall in love with them.","e":"The beautiful sight of the daffodils captured Wordsworth's heart."},{"m":"(transitive) If something captures the headlines, it is a big story in the news."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The capture of something is when you get it and do not let it go free.","e":"The capture of the thief was well planned."}]}]},"captures":{"h":"captures","l":"capture","q":"noun"},"captured":{"h":"captured","l":"capture","q":"verb"},"capturing":{"h":"capturing","l":"capture","q":"verb"},"frees":{"h":"frees","i":"/ˈfriːz/","a":"en-us-freeze.ogg","l":"free","q":"verb"},"freed":{"h":"freed","i":"/friːd/","l":"free","q":"verb"},"freeing":{"h":"freeing","i":"/ˈfriːɪŋ/","l":"free","q":"verb"},"burnt":{"h":"burnt","i":"/bɜːnt/","a":"en-us-burnt.ogg","l":"burn","q":"verb"},"origin":{"h":"origin","i":"/ˈɒr.ɪ.dʒɪn/","a":"en-us-origin.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The origin of something is its begi