n an inaccurate manner; it is done incorrectly or inexactly."}]}]},"translation":{"h":"translation","i":"/trænz'leɪʃən/","a":"en-us-translation.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Translation is the process of changing words of sentences from one language to another."},{"m":"(countable) A translation is a change of words, sentences, or texts from one language to another language."}]}]},"trainer":{"h":"trainer","i":"/ˈtreɪnə/","a":"en-au-trainer.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A trainer is a person who trains other people."},{"m":"(countable) (British) A trainer is a running shoe or sneaker."}]}]},"concrete":{"h":"concrete","i":"/ˈkɒŋkriːt/","a":"en-us-concrete.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Concrete is a type of mix that, when dried, hardens, often for sidewalks.","e":"Did you know that the sidewalk was made out of concrete?"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you concrete something, you cover it with or in [[#Noun|concrete]]."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A synonym for strong.","e":"There is no concrete evidence to say that Bill really does like salad."}]}]},"cripple":{"h":"cripple","i":"/krɪpl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-cripple.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cripple is a person whose mobility has been impaired or disabled.","e":"The cripple couldn't find a job and started to beg on the streets."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you cripple something, you damage it so that it cannot work normally.","e":"The game is crippled with a 60-minute free version until Mom buys it."},{"m":"(transitive) To injure or harm someone so that they are unable to walk or move in the usual way.","e":"The car bomb crippled five passers-by."}]}]},"cripples":{"h":"cripples","l":"cripple","q":"verb"},"crippled":{"h":"crippled","a":"En-us-crippled.ogg","l":"cripple","q":"verb"},"crippling":{"h":"crippling","l":"cripple","q":"verb"},"translations":{"h":"translations","a":"En-us-translations.ogg","l":"translation","q":"noun"},"trainers":{"h":"trainers","i":"/ˈtreɪnə(r)z/","l":"trainer","q":"noun"},"bury":{"h":"bury","i":"/ˈbɛ.ri/","a":"en-us-bury.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you bury something, you put it into the ground and cover it.","e":"John was buried near Washington, D.C."},{"m":"(transitive) If you bury a disagreement, you end it.","e":"Mary and Bill buried their disagreement over the sandwich."}]}]},"translationless":{"h":"translationless","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a text is translationless, there is no translation of it."}]}]},"translational":{"h":"translational","i":"/trænzˈleɪʃənəl/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is translational, it is related to or a translation of a text."}]}]},"misery":{"h":"misery","i":"/ˈmɪz(ə)rɪ/","a":"en-us-misery.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Misery is great unhappiness or sadness."},{"m":"(uncountable) Misery is the way of life and situation of very poor people."},{"m":"(countable) A misery is an event that causes misery; a disaster."}]}]},"miseries":{"h":"miseries","l":"misery","q":"noun"},"wretchedness":{"h":"wretchedness","i":"/ˈrɛt͡ʃɪdnəs/","a":"en-us-wretchedness.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Wretchedness is an unhappy state of pain of the mind and body."},{"m":"(uncountable) Wretchedness is a long state of very bad luck."}]}]},"buries":{"h":"buries","l":"bury","q":"verb"},"buried":{"h":"buried","i":"/ˈbɛ.rid/","a":"en-us-buried.ogg","l":"bury","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a body of a person is buried, it is put into a gravesite."},{"m":"If something or someone is buried, it is hidden; it is concealed."}]}]},"burying":{"h":"burying","l":"bury","q":"verb"},"unhappiness":{"h":"unhappiness","i":"/ʌnˈhæpinəs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-unhappiness.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Unhappiness is a feeling of not being happy.","e":"After the leader of our country died, many people had feelings of unhappiness."}]}]},"dissimulation":{"h":"dissimulation","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A dissimulation is a hiding of the truth."},{"m":"(uncountable) Dissimulation is hiding of a person's feelings or purposes."}]}]},"dissimulations":{"h":"dissimulations","l":"dissimulation","q":"noun"},"deceptively":{"h":"deceptively","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something is done deceptively, it is done in a way that could make people believe something that isn't true."}]}]},"unhappily":{"h":"unhappily","i":"/ʌnˈhapɪli/","a":"en-us-unhappily.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something is done unhappily, it is done in an unhappy manner.","e":"Charles unhappily did his homework, which he did not like too much."}]}]},"restless":{"h":"restless","i":"/ˈrɛstlɪs/","a":"en-us-restless.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are restless, you want to do something else."},{"m":"If you are restless, you are always moving and have trouble being still.","e":"He was a restless child."},{"m":"A restless time, is a time in which it is difficulty to sleep.","e":"The night before the wedding was restless."}]}]},"restlessness":{"h":"restlessness","i":"/ˈrɛstləsnəs/","a":"en-us-restlessness.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Restlessness is the feeling of not being able to be still, at rest or peace, or comfortable.","e":"The restlessness he felt grew as the vacation came nearer."}]}]},"restlessly":{"h":"restlessly","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something is done restlessly, it is done in a restless manner."}]}]},"joyous":{"h":"joyous","a":"en-us-joyous.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is joyous, they are full of joy; they are happy."}]}]},"joyously":{"h":"joyously","i":"/d͡ʒɔɪəsli/","a":"en-us-joyously.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something is done joyously, it is done in a joyful manner; it is done joyfully."}]}]},"translator":{"h":"translator","i":"/ˈtrænzleɪdər/","a":"En-uk-translator.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A translator is a person or software who is able to translate text from one language to another.","e":"Lucy is a Spanish translator for a local newspaper, where she translates the information from English into Spanish."}]}]},"translators":{"h":"translators","l":"translator","q":"noun"},"software":{"h":"software","i":"/ˈsɒftˌwɛə/","a":"en-us-software.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Software is a computer program.","e":"This wiki runs the MediaWiki software available from MediaWiki.org."}]}]},"sensitive":{"h":"sensitive","i":"/ˈsɛnsɪtɪv/","a":"en-us-sensitive.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are sensitive, you easily understand other people's feelings."},{"m":"Sensitive information, areas, issues, etc. are those that need to be handled carefully so they don't cause problems."},{"m":"Sensitive skin, materials, etc. are those that are easily damaged.","e":"An area on my arm is sensitive, so please don't touch me there."}]}]},"joyful":{"h":"joyful","i":"/ˈdʒɔɪfəl/","a":"En-us-joyful.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is joyful, they have a feeling of joy.","e":"The kids were joyful on Christmas morning because they were going to open presents."}]}]},"hastily":{"h":"hastily","i":"/ˈheɪstɪli/","a":"en-us-hastily.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something is done hastily, it is done without much thought; it is done carelessly."},{"m":"If something is done hastily, it is done quickly; it is done in a fast manner."}]}]},"scolds":{"h":"scolds","l":"scold","q":"verb"},"scolded":{"h":"scolded","l":"scold","q":"verb"},"scolding":{"h":"scolding","l":"scold","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A scolding is a series of critical comments, like those used to teach children when they do not behave."}]}]},"scoldings":{"h":"scoldings","l":"scolding","q":"noun"},"canucks":{"h":"Canucks","l":"canuck","q":"proper noun"},"canadians":{"h":"Canadians","l":"canadian","q":"noun"},"misbehave":{"h":"misbehave","i":"/mɪsbɪˈheɪv/","a":"en-us-misbehave.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If somebody misbehaves, they behave in an inappropriate or incorrect way.","e":"The child was misbehaving by throwing his toys around the room."}]}]},"misbehaves":{"h":"misbehaves","l":"misbehave","q":"verb"},"misbehaved":{"h":"misbehaved","l":"misbehave","q":"verb"},"misbehaving":{"h":"misbehaving","l":"misbehave","q":"verb"},"disputant":{"h":"disputant","i":"/dəˈspjutənt/","a":"en-ca-synth-disputant.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A disputant is a person that takes part in a dispute."}]}]},"disputants":{"h":"disputants","l":"disputant","q":"noun"},"perforation":{"h":"perforation","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A perforation is a hole made in something, usually many small holes in paper."}]}]},"perforations":{"h":"perforations","l":"perforation","q":"noun"},"literature":{"h":"literature","i":"/ˈlɪt.ə.rə.t͡ʃə(r)/","a":"en-us-literature.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Literature is the text of something written."},{"m":"(uncountable) Literature is the collection of everything written of a nation, people, group or culture.","e":"I love the Chilean literature."}]}]},"literatures":{"h":"literatures","l":"literature","q":"noun"},"chilean":{"h":"Chilean","i":"/ˈtʃɪli.ən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Chilean.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone or something is Chilean, then it is of or from Chile.","e":"Many Chilean writers have become famous all over the world."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A Chilean is a person that is from Chile.","e":"A Chilean bought my computer."}]}]},"chileans":{"h":"Chileans","l":"chilean","q":"noun"},"neapolitans":{"h":"Neapolitans","l":"neapolitan","q":"noun"},"norwegians":{"h":"Norwegians","l":"norwegian","q":"noun"},"rhododendrons":{"h":"Rhododendrons","l":"rhododendron","q":"noun"},"sundays":{"h":"Sundays","l":"sunday","q":"noun"},"saturdays":{"h":"Saturdays","l":"saturday","q":"noun"},"tuesdays":{"h":"Tuesdays","l":"tuesday","q":"noun"},"wednesdays":{"h":"Wednesdays","l":"we