 made an honorary member of The Academy of American Poets."}]}]},"academies":{"h":"academies","l":"academy","q":"noun"},"acre":{"h":"acre","i":"/ˈeɪkə/","a":"en-us-acre.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An acre is an imperial measure of area. One acre is 4,840 square yards or 4047 square metres.","e":"The lower field on his farm is more than 2 acres."}]}]},"acres":{"h":"acres","l":"acre","q":"noun"},"adore":{"h":"adore","a":"en-us-adore.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you adore someone, you love them very much.","e":"It is clear that he adores his wife."},{"m":"If you adore something, you like it a lot.","e":"I simply adore your new dress. Where did you get it?"}]}]},"adores":{"h":"adores","l":"adore","q":"verb"},"adored":{"h":"adored","a":"en-us-adored.ogg","l":"adore","q":"verb"},"adoring":{"h":"adoring","l":"adore","q":"verb"},"amplify":{"h":"amplify","i":"/ˈæmp.lɪ.faɪ/","a":"en-us-amplify.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To amplify something is to make more of it: larger, louder, or more in number."},{"m":"(transitive) if you amplify an image, you make it bigger.","e":"We can see the details of the bird more clearly if we amplify the photo."},{"m":"(transitive) If you amplify a sound, you make it louder.","e":"We will have to amplify your voice more, or the audience won't hear it."},{"m":"(transitive) If you amplify a description, you add more details and illustrations."}]}]},"amplifies":{"h":"amplifies","l":"amplify","q":"verb"},"amplified":{"h":"amplified","l":"amplify","q":"verb"},"amplifying":{"h":"amplifying","l":"amplify","q":"verb"},"disunity":{"h":"disunity","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Disunity is a situation in which people do not act together."}]}]},"disunities":{"h":"disunities","l":"disunity","q":"noun"},"disunite":{"h":"disunite","i":"/dɪsjuːˈnaɪt/","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you disunite something, you separate it; you split it up."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something is disunited, it comes apart."}]}]},"