r playing games."},{"m":"(uncountable) Allowance is an act of allowing or granting of something by someone."}]}]},"allowances":{"h":"allowances","l":"allowance","q":"noun"},"inaccuracy":{"h":"inaccuracy","i":"/ɪnˈakjʊrəsi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-inaccuracy.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Inaccuracy is a lack of accuracy; it is the state of being inaccurate."},{"m":"(countable) An inaccuracy is a piece of writing or a fact that is not accurate or is not true."}]}]},"inaccuracies":{"h":"inaccuracies","l":"inaccuracy","q":"noun"},"bush":{"h":"bush","i":"/bʊʃ/","a":"en-us-bush.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bush is a plant that is a short tree.","e":"I grow a few bushes."}]}]},"bushes":{"h":"bushes","i":"/ˈbʊʃɪz/","a":"en-us-bushes.ogg","l":"bush","q":"noun"},"certificate":{"h":"certificate","i":"/sə'tɪfɪkɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-certificate.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A certificate is a paper that acknowledges something like an award.","e":"I finally got my certificate of honor from school."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you certificate a person, you give him a [[#Noun|certificate]]."}]}]},"certificates":{"h":"certificates","l":"certificate","q":"noun"},"newt":{"h":"newt","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":", (countable) A newt is an amphibian that looks like a lizard and lives in the water when it becomes an adult"}]}]},"newts":{"h":"newts","l":"newt","q":"noun"},"cola":{"h":"cola","i":"/ˈkəʊ.lə/","l":"colon"},"incorrectness":{"h":"incorrectness","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Incorrectness is the quality of being incorrect."}]}]},"exacts":{"h":"exacts","l":"exact","q":"verb"},"exacted":{"h":"exacted","l":"exact","q":"verb"},"exacting":{"h":"exacting","l":"exact","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is exacting, they are not easy to satisfy; they request things to be done for them very often."}]}]},"convey":{"h":"convey","i":"/kənˈveɪ/","a":"en-us-convey.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If somebody conveys something, they take it from one place to another; they move it; they transport it.","e":"The ship conveyed the goods."},{"m":"(transitive) If somebody conveys something, they tell you about it; they make it known.","e":"He conveyed to me that it was wrong to steal."}]}]},"conveys":{"h":"conveys","l":"convey","q":"verb"},"conveyed":{"h":"conveyed","l":"convey","q":"verb"},"conveying":{"h":"conveying","l":"convey","q":"verb"},"merge":{"h":"merge","i":"/mɜː(r)dʒ/","a":"En-us-merge.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you merge two or more things, you combine them.","e":"The two companies will merge soon."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A merge is the point at which two different things join together."}]}]},"merges":{"h":"merges","l":"merge","q":"verb"},"merged":{"h":"merged","l":"merge","q":"verb"},"merging":{"h":"merging","l":"merge","q":"verb"},"conveyance":{"h":"conveyance","i":"/kənˈveɪəns/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-conveyance.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A conveyance is an act of conveying something."},{"m":"(countable) A conveyance is a way to transport oneself from one place to another; usually a vehicle of some sort."}]}]},"conveyances":{"h":"conveyances","l":"conveyance","q":"noun"},"nailbiter":{"h":"nailbiter","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable)"}]}]},"nailbiters":{"h":"nailbiters","l":"nailbiter","q":"noun"},"nail-biter":{"h":"nail-biter","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable)"}]}]},"nail-biters":{"h":"nail-biters","l":"nail-biter","q":"noun"},"conveyable":{"h":"conveyable","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is conveyable, it is able to be conveyed, usually between two different people.","e":"The telephone call we got was conveyable between the child and his parents."}]}]},"obscure":{"h":"obscure","i":"/əbˈskjʊə(r)/","a":"en-us-obscure.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is obscure, it is not easy to understand.","e":"The textbook the teacher was using in her class was obscure."},{"m":"If something is obscure, it is not bright in color or appearance; it is dull or dark."},{"m":"If something is obscure, it is very hard to make out a clear image of it; it is faint; it is unclear or vague."},{"m":"If something is obscure, it is hidden; it is out of sight.","e":"The Johnsons decided to have a date at an obscure retreat."},{"m":"If a place where people live is obscure, it is found far away from where most other people live."},{"m":"If something is obscure, it is not easily seen; it is inconspicuous.","e":"The ruby had an obscure flaw in it."},{"m":"If somebody is obscure, they are not known; they have no fame and are not notable."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If someone obscures something, they darken it; they make it faint."},{"m":"(transitive) If someone obscures something, they hide it from sight; they put it out of sight.","e":"The fog obscured the road ahead of Sherry while she was driving."}]}]},"obscurer":{"h":"obscurer","l":"obscure","q":"adjective"},"obscurest":{"h":"obscurest","l":"obscure","q":"adjective"},"obscures":{"h":"obscures","l":"obscure","q":"verb"},"obscured":{"h":"obscured","a":"en-us-obscured.ogg","l":"obscure","q":"verb"},"obscuring":{"h":"obscuring","l":"obscure","q":"verb"},"cannibal":{"h":"cannibal","i":"/ˈkænɪbəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-cannibal.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cannibal is someone who eats other human beings."}]}]},"roofer":{"h":"roofer","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A roofer is someone who works on repairing roofs."}]}]},"roofers":{"h":"roofers","l":"roofer","q":"noun"},"cannibals":{"h":"cannibals","l":"cannibal","q":"noun"},"baleful":{"h":"baleful","i":"/beɪlfəl/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is baleful, it warns about an evil that is about to happen; it is ominous."}]}]},"ominous":{"h":"ominous","i":"/ˈɒmɪnəs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-ominous.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is ominous, it relates to omens; it is significant."},{"m":"If something is ominous, it gives an indication that something bad is about to happen; it is threatening.","e":"The dark clouds moving into the area that we live in is an ominous sign that a bad storm is about to happen."}]}]},"omen":{"h":"omen","i":"/ˈəʊmən/","a":"en-us-omen.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An omen is a warning or a sign about a good or bad event that will happen in the future; it is an augury or foreboding."},{"m":"(countable) An omen is something of prophetic importance."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you omen something, you predict its happening with an omen."}]}]},"omens":{"h":"omens","l":"omen","q":"noun"},"omened":{"h":"omened","l":"omen","q":"verb"},"omening":{"h":"omening","l":"omen","q":"verb"},"obscene":{"h":"obscene","i":"/ɑbˈsin/","a":"en-us-obscene.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is obscene, it is offensive to morality; it is vulgar; it is depraved."},{"m":"If something is obscene, it is lewd or lustful."},{"m":"If something is obscene, it is beyond all reason."},{"m":"If something is obscene, it is disgusting, repulsive, or abominable."},{"m":"If something is obscene, it is likely to deprave or corrupt somebody."}]}]},"obscener":{"h":"obscener","l":"obscene","q":"adjective"},"obscenest":{"h":"obscenest","l":"obscene","q":"adjective"},"nonobscene":{"h":"nonobscene","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is nonobscene, it is not obscene; it is not vulgar, lewd, disgusting, lustful, or revolting.","e":"The video was nonobscene."}]}]},"obpyriform":{"h":"obpyriform","i":"/ɒbˈpɪrəˌfɔrm/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is obpyriform, it is shaped like a pear, only the top and the bottom of the design has been changed; the narrow part of the pear is on the bottom and the wider part of the pear is on top."}]}]},"obovoid":{"h":"obovoid","i":"/ɒbˈoʊvɔɪd/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is obovoid, it is ovoid in shape, with the narrow end of the at the bottom of it."}]}]},"crook":{"h":"crook","i":"/krʊk/","a":"EN-AU ck1 crook.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A crook is a person who steals things, lies, cheats, or does other things which are against the law; they are a criminal."},{"m":"(countable) A crook is a bend."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If someone crooks something, they bend it; they curve it."}]}]},"crooks":{"h":"crooks","i":"/crʊks/","l":"crook","q":"noun"},"crooking":{"h":"crooking","l":"crook","q":"verb"},"ominously":{"h":"ominously","i":"/ˈɒmɪnəsli/","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something is done ominously, it is done in an ominous manner; it is done with a lot of foreboding."}]}]},"ominousness":{"h":"ominousness","i":"/ˈɒmɪnəsnəs/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Ominousness is the state of being ominous; it is a state of foreboding."}]}]},"balefulness":{"h":"balefulness","i":"/ˈbeɪl.fəlnəs/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Balefulness is the quality of being baleful."}]}]},"balefully":{"h":"balefully","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something is done balefully, it is done in a baleful manner."}]}]},"expel":{"h":"expel","i":"/ɪkˈspɛl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-expel.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If someone is expelled, they are no longer a member of a group or organization.","e":"He was expelled from school."},{"m":"(transitive) If someone expels a person, they force them to leave a country; they deport them."},{"m":"(transitive) If someone or something is expelled, they are thrown out; they are ejected; it erupted."}]}]},"expels":{"h":"expels","l":"expel","q":"verb"},"expelling":{"h":"expelling","l":"expel","q":"verb"},"expelled":{"h":"expelled","a":"en-us-expelled.ogg","l":"expel","q":"verb"},"spontaneous":{"h":"spontaneous","a":"en-us-spontaneous.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is spontaneous, it happens without any outside cause; nothing else makes it happen.","e":"He made a spontaneous offer to help the old lady cross the street."},{"m":"If something is spontaneous, it is random."},{"m":"If something is spontaneous, it happens suddenly; it happens without any warning."},{"m":"If someone does something in a spontaneous way, it is done of their own free will or without making any plan to do so."},{"m":"If something is spontaneous, it was made without being planted by humans; it is indigenous."}]}]},"breakdown":{"h":"breakdown","i":"/ˈbreɪkdaʊn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-breakdown.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A breakdown is when something has failed, usually having to do with a machine of some sort.","e":"The car they were driving had a breakdown when the engine stopped working."},{"m":"(countable) A breakdown is when someone's state of mind has fallen apart or lapsed."},{"m":"(countable) A breakdown of something is a list or a breaking up of something into in great detail."}]}]},"breakdowns":{"h":"breakdowns","l":"breakdown","q":"noun"},"unplanned":{"h":"unplanned","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something that has happened was unplanned, it was not intended.","e":"The change in tactics used to rob the bank was unplanned."},{"m":"If something is unplanned, it was not thought of in advance."},{"m":"If something is unplanned, it does not have a structure or organization."}]}]},"pear":{"h":"pear","i":"/pɛə/","a":"en-uk-pear.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pear is an edible fruit that is made by the pear tree, looking like an apple, but with an elongated area around the stem.","e":"Sally bit into a ripe green pear, with juice coming out from either side of her mouth."}]}]},"pears":{"h":"pears","i":"/pɛəz/","l":"pear","q":"noun"},"pearlike":{"h":"pearlike","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is pearlike, it looks like a pear or some feature of one."}]}]},"peary":{"h":"peary","i":"/ˈpɛəri/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-peary.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is peary, it looks like pears; it is pearlike."},{"m":"If somethin