rd for torso."}]}]},"trunks":{"h":"trunks","a":"En-us-trunks.ogg","l":"trunk","q":"noun"},"impregnation":{"h":"impregnation","i":"/ɪmprɛɡˈneɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-impregnation.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An impregnation is a process that one or more people go through in order to become pregnant."}]}]},"impregnations":{"h":"impregnations","l":"impregnation","q":"noun"},"pregnancy":{"h":"pregnancy","i":"/ˈprɛɡnənsi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-pregnancy.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A pregnancy when a female is pregnant.","e":"She was in the third month of her pregnancy."}]}]},"pregnancies":{"h":"pregnancies","l":"pregnancy","q":"noun"},"unbearable":{"h":"unbearable","i":"/ˌənˈbe(ə)rəbəl/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A condition which is so extreme that you want to stop experiencing it is unbearable.","e":"The heat was unbearable."}]}]},"intolerable":{"h":"intolerable","i":"/ɪnˈtɑlərəbl̩/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-intolerable.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is intolerable, you can't tolerate it or stand it.","e":"What's that awful noise? It's intolerable!"}]}]},"quagmire":{"h":"quagmire","i":"/ˈkwɒɡ.maɪə(r)/","a":"en-au-quagmire.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A soft and muddy or swampy area of ground."},{"m":"A difficult or confusing situation."}]}]},"maternal":{"h":"maternal","i":"/məˈtəːnəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-maternal.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Maternal is the adjective related to the noun 'mother'.","e":"Maternal inheritance is what you inherit from your mother."}]}]},"paternal":{"h":"paternal","i":"/pəˈtɜː(r)nəl/","a":"En-us-paternal.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Paternal is the adjective related to the noun 'father'.","e":"A paternal inheritance is one which comes from your father."}]}]},"dreadful":{"h":"dreadful","i":"/ˈdrɛd.fʊl/","a":"en-us-dreadful.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something dreadful is something very bad.","e":"There has been a dreadful accident."}]}]},"rubber":{"h":"rubber","i":"/ˈrʌbə/","a":"en-us-rubber.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A material made from the sap of trees.","e":"The ball is made of rubber."},{"m":"(countable) An eraser."},{"m":"(countable) A condom."}]}]},"rubbers":{"h":"rubbers","l":"rubber","q":"noun"},"inconclusible":{"h":"inconclusible","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is inconclusible, then it cannot be finished or ended."}]}]},"par":{"h":"par","i":"/pɑː/","a":"en-us-par.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Par could mean with the same value or quality.","e":"The car was cheaper but on par with the others."},{"m":"(golf) The number of shots needed to reach the hole.","e":"He needs to make this shot for par."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(golf) To reach the hole in the number of shots needed.","e":"He has to par every hole win this game."}]}]},"pars":{"h":"pars","i":"/pɑːz/","l":"par","q":"noun"},"vet":{"h":"vet","i":"/vɛt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-vet.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A veterinarian.","e":"We took all of our pets to the vet."},{"m":"A veteran, somebody who used to be in the military.","e":"My grandfather was a World War II vet. He used to tell stories about fighting in France."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you vet someone, you investigate them carefully and critically.","e":"The FBI vets all nominees to the Federal bench."}]}]},"vets":{"h":"vets","l":"vet","q":"noun"},"terra":{"h":"Terra","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"A name for the planet earth."}]}]},"uprising":{"h":"uprising","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An uprising is a revolt by a group of people that attempts to get rid of a government or policies that the people do not like."}]}]},"freeborn":{"h":"freeborn","i":"/friːˈbɔːn/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"free and with natural rights rather than being a slave or a servant"}]}]},"uprisings":{"h":"uprisings","l":"uprising","q":"noun"},"despot":{"h":"despot","i":"/ˈdɛs.pɒt/","a":"en-ca-despot-2.oga","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A despot is a totalitarian autocrat or dictator, a person who rules without the need for a or parliament.","e":"The Domitian was a despot."}]}]},"brainy":{"h":"brainy","i":"/ˈbreɪni/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-brainy.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"(informal) Somebody brainy is intelligent, or clever.","e":"The kid is brainy."}]}]},"brainier":{"h":"brainier","l":"brainy","q":"adjective"},"brainiest":{"h":"brainiest","l":"brainy","q":"adjective"},"despots":{"h":"despots","l":"despot","q":"noun"},"dyslexia":{"h":"dyslexia","i":"/dɪsˈlɛk.si.ə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-dyslexia.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Dyslexia is a learning problem that makes it difficult to read. This may cause difficulties in writing also."},{"m":"He is not able to do well in school because he has dyslexia."}]}]},"b-movie":{"h":"B-movie","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A B-movie is a film that was made with a small amount of money and made not very well.","e":"I did not like the B-movie I saw yesterday."}]}]},"quango":{"h":"quango","i":"/kwæŋ.ɡəʊ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-quango.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A quango is a British term for a public body which runs itself, but is paid for by the government. See devolution.","e":"English Heritage is a quango because it is paid for by the government, but it manages itself."}]}]},"bride":{"h":"bride","i":"/brʌɪd/","a":"en-us-bride.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bride is a wife, the female partner in a marriage. Most used for the period of time around the marriage ceremony.","e":"Jill was the bride, and Jack was the bridegroom."}]}]},"hood":{"h":"hood","i":"/hʊd/","a":"en-us-hood.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hood is a covering for the head. It covers the top, back and sides of the head. By extension, other objects may have hoods: cars, some flowers.","e":"The monk was wearing a hood."},{"m":"A hood is another word for neighbourhood.","e":"I've lived in the hood for five years."}]}]},"ballad":{"h":"ballad","i":"/ˈbæləd/","a":"en-us-ballad.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A ballad is a slow, romantic song.","e":"Between the fast numbers, she sang ballads."}]}]},"burlesque":{"h":"burlesque","i":"/bə(r)ˈlɛsk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-burlesque.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Burlesque is a kind of humorous theatrical entertainment. Exaggeration, and vulgar songs and dance may occur.","e":"Burlesque is a vulgar copy of the respectable world."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you burlesque, you make a [[#Noun|burlesque]] parody of something."}]}]},"copes":{"h":"copes","l":"cope","q":"verb"},"coped":{"h":"coped","l":"cope","q":"verb"},"coping":{"h":"coping","l":"cope","q":"verb"},"uncoded":{"h":"uncoded","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something uncoded is not in code.","e":"The message was uncoded."}]}]},"brides":{"h":"brides","l":"bride","q":"noun"},"ballads":{"h":"ballads","l":"ballad","q":"noun"},"hoods":{"h":"hoods","l":"hood","q":"noun"},"director":{"h":"director","i":"/dɪˈrɛktə/","a":"en-us-director.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A director is a person who is in charge of something.","e":"The film director was doing a very good job."}]}]},"directors":{"h":"directors","l":"director","q":"noun"},"realtor":{"h":"realtor","i":"/ˈril.tɚ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-realtor.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(North America) (countable) A realtor is a person or business that helps people sell or rent real estate. They are a type of agent.","e":"The realtor helped us sell the house."}]}]},"realtors":{"h":"realtors","l":"realtor","q":"noun"},"appease":{"h":"appease","i":"/əˈpiːz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-appease.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To appease is to calm down an angry or dangerous person.","e":"She was so angry, but he managed to appease her."}]}]},"ridicule":{"h":"ridicule","i":"/ˈrɪdɪkjuːl/","a":"en-us-ridicule.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Ridicule is derision or mockery.","e":"Aristophanes shocked the Athenians with his ridicule of their sincerely-held beliefs."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To ridicule is to make fun of, or mock, someone or something.","e":"To ridicule a powerful man is to take a big risk."}]}]},"jest":{"h":"jest","i":"/ʤest/","a":"en-us-jest.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A jest is a joke or a prank, made in fun.","e":"It was only a jest, a piece of fun."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To jest is to joke or make fun of something.","e":"Don't jest about serious things."}]}]},"shackle":{"h":"shackle","i":"/ˈʃækəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-shackle.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A shackle is a restraint, originally leg-irons which made movement slow and difficult. By extension, it means anything that limits what people do.","e":"Laws are meant as shackles to prevent governments doing whatever they wish."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To shackle is to limit or restrain what can be done.","e":"He could scarcely move after they shackled him."}]}]},"serrated":{"h":"serrated","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A serrated knife is one with a jagged edge.","e":"We cut bread with a serrated bread knife."}]}]},"snout":{"h":"snout","i":"/snaʊt/","a":"en-us-snout.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The snout is the front part of the head of a mammal.","e":"Dogs have big snouts, but we have almost none."}]}]},"snouts":{"h":"snouts","l":"snout","q":"noun"},"treachery":{"h":"treachery","i":"/ˈtrɛtʃəri/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-treachery.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Treachery is behaviour which cannot be trusted: to break faith or betray.","e":"King John was known for his treachery."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Treacherous","e":"His behaviour was treacherous."}]}]},"inhibit":{"h":"inhibit","i":"/ɪnˈhɪbɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-inhibit.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To inhibit is to stop something happening, or to make it happen less.","e":"She wanted to kiss him, but was inhibited by the onlookers."}]}]},"insolence":{"h":"insolence","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Insolence is the quality of insulting arrogance, and offensiveness.","e":"When Brummel said \"Who's your fat friend?\" the Prince of Wales thought it was insolence."}]}]},"slaughter":{"h":"slaughter","i":"/ˈslɔːtə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-slaughter.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The killing of animals is slaughter.","e":"We kill cows in a slaughter-house."},{"m":"(uncountable) The mass killing of men is slaughter.","e":"The end of a battle is often a slaughter of men."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To slaughter is to kill many.","e":"To slaughter is to kill many men or animals."}]}]},"triumph":{"h":"triumph","i":"/ˈtraɪ.ʌmpf/","a":"en-us-triumph.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A triumph is a great success.","e":"His discovery of the electron was a great triumph."},{"m":"(countable) A Triumph was the ceremonial entry of a victorious general into Rome.","e":"When Caesar returned to Rome he qualified for a Triumph."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) To triumph is to gain a victory or be successful.","e":"He triumphed over adversity."}]}]},"cognate":{"h":"cognate","i":"/ˈkɒɡ.neɪt/","a":"en-us-cognate.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) One related by blood or origin with another, especially a person sharing an ancestor with another."},{"m":"(countable) A word related to one in another language."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Related by blood; having a common ancestor."},{"m":"Related in origin, as certain words in genetically related languages descended from the same ancestral root; for example, English name and Latin nmen from Indo-European *n-men-."},{"m":"Related or analogous in nature, character, or function."}]}]},"mats":{"h":"mats","i":"/mæts/","l":"mat","q":"noun"},"quangos":{"h":"quangos","l":"quango","q":"noun"},"burlesques":{"h":"burlesques","l":"burlesque","q":"noun"},"trombone":{"h":"trombone","i":"/ˌtrɒmˈbəʊn/","a":"en-us-trombone.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A trombone is a musical instrument that uses the slide to play notes.","e":"He picked up the trombone and started playing the national anthem."}]}]},"trombones":{"h":"trombones","l":"trombone"},"insist":{"h":"insist","i":"/ɪnˈsɪst/","a":"En-us-insist.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) To insist means to get your own way without listening to other people's comments.","e":"He insisted on eating out. His wife, therefore, had no choice but to also do so."}]}]},"substitute":{"h":"substitute","i":"/ˈsʌbstɪtʃuːt/","a":"en-us-substitute.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A substitute is a person on standby for a sport team or school teacher.","e":"Although he was only a substitute for the team, but he played very well during yesterday's match."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you substitute x for y, you don't use y and use x instead.","e":"You may substitute fresh lime juice for lemon juice"}]}]},"voucher":{"h":"voucher","i":"/ˈvaʊtʃə(r)/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-voucher.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A voucher is a special piece of paper which can be used to get discounts on products.","e":"The insurance company was celebrating its 50th anniversary, therefore every new customer was given a $10 voucher."}]}]},"appeases":{"h":"appeases","l":"appease","q":"verb"},"appeased":{"h":"appeased","l":"appease","q":"verb"},"appeasing":{"h":"appeasing","l":"appease","q":"verb"},"ridicules":{"h":"ridicules","l":"ridicule","q":"verb"},"ridiculed":{"h":"ridiculed","l":"ridicule","q":"verb"},"ridiculing":{"h":"ridiculing","l":"ridicule","q":"verb"},"laboratory":{"h":"laboratory","i":"/ˈlæbrəˌtɔri/","a":"en-uk-laboratory-2.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A laboratory is a place for scientists to experiment on new things.","e":"The little child entered the laboratory by mistake."}]}]},"dial":{"h":"dial","i":"/ˈdaɪəɫ/","a":"en-au-dial.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A dial is a circular scale which a needle moves to show a measurement of something."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To dial means to use a telephone to do a call.","e":"I picked up the phone to dial my boss."}]}]},"drip":{"h":"drip","i":"/drɪp/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-drip.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A drip is a small amount of water.","e":"The tap is spoiled. Water just keeps coming down drip by drip."},{"m":"(countable) A drip is an uninteresting person."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If something is dripping, it is falling one drop at a time.","e":"My pen has been dripping throughout the day."}]}]},"intact":{"h":"intact","a":"en-us-intact.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Intact means untouched or at least not spoilt.","e":"Yellowstone is a still a mostly intact ecosystem."}]}]},"cinema":{"h":"cinema","i":"/ˈsɪn.ɪ.mə/","a":"en-us-cinema.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cinema is a building that shows movies.","e":"The cinema in my town has two screens and has four showings every day."}]}]},"scribble":{"h":"scribble","i":"/ˈskrɪbəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-scribble.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you scribble something, you write it or draw it quickly.","e":"I scribbled the licence plate number on a piece of paper before the car drove away."}]}]},"huddle":{"h":"huddle","i":"/ˈhʌdəl/","a":"en-us-huddle.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A huddle is a group of people that are tight and not orderly."},{"m":"(countable) In football, a huddle is a short meeting of all the players from one team that are on the field to plan their next play."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) to crowd together, usually when unhappy or afraid","e":"The girls huddled together to get warm."},{"m":"(intransitive) to bend your legs to your chest and lean over, getting into a position like an embryo in a womb"}]}]},"huddling":{"h":"huddling","l":"huddle","q":"verb"},"huddled":{"h":"huddled","i":"/ˈhʌdl̩d/","l":"huddle","q":"verb"},"clinic":{"h":"clinic","i":"/ˈklɪnɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-clinic.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A clinic is a place to see the doctor for health checkups or to buy medicine.","e":"He felt ill yesterday, so he had to visit the clinic to buy some medicine."}]}]},"clinics":{"h":"clinics","l":"clinic","q":"noun"},"clip":{"h":"clip","i":"/klɪp/","a":"en-us-clip.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A clip is a small item to hold things on to another.","e":"We need more clips to hang the laundry."},{"m":"(countable) Clip is another word for video.","e":"The clip that we saw just now was very touching."},{"m":"(countable) A clip is a container that is attached to a gun and holds the bullets for the gun, to be inserted into the magazine. Bullets leave the clip and go into the gun for firing."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To use a clipper to hold something tightly.","e":"It is important to clip your laundry properly on a windy day."},{"m":"If you clip something, you cut it with scissors or shears.","e":"She clipped my hair with her scissors."},{"m":"If you clip a video, you process it by removing a certain, usually wanted, part of the video.","e":"He clipped the part of the video where it shows nothing."}]}]},"pane":{"h":"pane","i":"/peɪn/","a":"en-us-pane.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pane is a sheet of glass in a window."},{"m":"A pane is a layer in a GUI."},{"m":"Another spelling of peen."}]}]},"contest":{"h":"contest","i":"/ˈkɒn.tɛst/","a":"en-us-contest.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A contest is where people do a quiz or play a game to win a prize.","e":"He took part in the contest as he wanted to win the first prize."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you contest a position, you engage in a competition for a position of power."},{"m":"(transitive) If you contest a decision, you oppose it."}]}]},"hooray":{"h":"hooray","i":"/həˈreɪ/","a":"en-uk-Hooray.ogg","s":[{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"You use \"hooray\" to show happiness, especially when you have won something.","e":"Hooray! Dad is bring us to the theme park."}]}]},"hint":{"h":"hint","i":"/hɪnt/","a":"en-us-hint.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hint is a clue to a question or a puzzle.","e":"I really need a hint to solve this question. It is too difficult for me."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To suggest.","e":"He hinted that he wanted to marry another man."}]}]},"faint":{"h":"faint","i":"/fɛɪnt/","a":"en-us-faint.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) When someone faints, they suddenly become unconscious and cannot be woken up easily.","e":"Get help quick! Someone has fainted here!"}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is faint, it is not clear, very small.","e":"The writing was faint."}]}]},"offspring":{"h":"offspring","i":"/ˈɒfsprɪŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-offspring.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An offspring is either the sons, daughters, or immediate descendants of a human, animal or plant.","e":"That lioness just gave birth to two offspring!"}]}]},"dip":{"h":"dip","i":"/dɪp/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-dip.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A dip is a lower section of a road or geological feature.","e":"There is a dip in the road ahead."},{"m":"A dip is a short swim to refresh oneself.","e":"I’m going for a dip before breakfast."},{"m":"A dip is a sauce for [[#Verb|dipping]].","e":"This onion dip is just scrumptious."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To dip is an act when something is placed into a liquid.","e":"I slowly dipped the towel into the bowl of water."}]}]},"drown":{"h":"drown","i":"/draʊn/","a":"en-us-drown.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To drown is an action where someone is struggling in water.","e":"I remembered when I was young, I nearly drowned in the lake near my house."},{"m":"(transitive) The effect of drowning can also be produced intentionally."},{"m":"(transitive) If you drown something, you lose, make hard to find or unnoticeable in a great mass.","e":"The CIA collects so much information that the actual answers it should seek are often drowned in the flood of reports."}]}]},"drill":{"h":"drill","i":"/drɪl/","a":"en-us-drill.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A drill is an object used to dig a hole.","e":"He used the drill to make a hole on the wall."},{"m":"A practice before a major event is called a drill.","e":"Our school often conduct fire drills to train us in case of a real fire."},{"m":"(countable) A drill is a type of primate."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you drill a hole, you use a drill to make a hole in something.","e":"We must drill six holes in the wood for the screws."},{"m":"If you drill some information into someone's head, you make them review it again and again until they remember it.","e":"My teacher tried all ways to drill the mathematical concept into my head."}]}]},"drift":{"h":"drift","i":"/drɪft/","a":"en-us-drift.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"An action when an object moves towards the earth slowly.","e":"The plane ran out of fuel, therefore it had to drift slowly down to the nearby airport."}]}]},"lap":{"h":"lap","i":"/læp/","a":"en-us-lap.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The thighs. Usually used when one is sitting down.","e":"The baby was tired, so he rested down on his mother's lap."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"An animal laps when it uses its tongue to drink milk or water."}]}]},"leak":{"h":"leak","i":"/liːk/","a":"en-us-leak.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A hole in a tube. Usually used for gas tubes and water pipes.","e":"Quick! Get a plumber! I have found a leak in this pipe."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"An action when someone reveals a secret to the public.","e":"Don't tell him about this. He will leak it out."}]}]},"oral":{"h":"oral","i":"/ˈɔː.rəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-oral.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Oral history, arguments, etc. are spoken, not written."},{"m":"Oral sex is sex using the mouth."},{"m":"Oral health, cancer, etc. is issues of the mouth."},{"m":"Oral medicine is medicine you put in your mouth and swallow."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An oral is an examination that is spoken, usually for the languages."}]}]},"offend":{"h":"offend","i":"/əˈfɛnd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-offend.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"An act when someone makes another person unhappy. To offend someone is to make them feel disgust.","e":"Don't offend him. It's not nice. He may fight back."}]}]},"magnet":{"h":"magnet","i":"/ˈmæɡnɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-magnet.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A magnet is a natural object which can attract magnetic objects such as steel or iron.","e":"Never place magnets near credit cards, or all the info in it will be lost."}]}]},"millimetre":{"h":"millimetre","i":"/ˈmɪləˌmitɚ/","a":"en-us-millimetre.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A millimetre is one tenth of a centimetre.","e":"The smallest measurement of a ruler is the millimetre. You need another tool to measure objects smaller than that."}]}]},"mobile":{"h":"mobile","i":"/ˈmoʊbəl/","a":"en-uk-mobile.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mobile is a small device that can be used to call someone."},{"m":"(countable) A mobile is a hanging sculpture."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something capable of being moved is said to be mobile."},{"m":"If something is mobile, it can be used on a mobile device.","e":"The mobile version of the website is simpler than the desktop version."}]}]},"drills":{"h":"drills","l":"drill","q":"noun"},"drilling":{"h":"drilling","l":"drill","q":"verb"},"fade":{"h":"fade","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When something fades, it slowly disappears.","e":"The mysterious figure slowly faded into the darkness."}]}]},"drilled":{"h":"drilled","l":"drill","q":"verb"},"disgrace":{"h":"disgrace","i":"/dɪsˈɡreɪs/","a":"en-us-disgrace.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A shame to someone or a group of people.","e":"The worst thing in life is being a disgrace."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To bring disgrace or shame to yourself or someone else","e":"The journalist disgraced the Congressman by telling the public of his sex scandal."}]}]},"duo":{"h":"duo","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Two people","e":"The duo were like brothers, never being separated."}]}]},"flute":{"h":"flute","i":"/fluːt/","a":"en-us-flute.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A flute is a musical instrument that you blow into to make sound.","e":"He played the flute so much better than his seniors that he became the best player in the band."}]}]},"deserve":{"h":"deserve","i":"/dɪˈzɜːv/","a":"en-us-deserve.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When someone deserve something, it means he is good enough to have the privilege of getting something special.","e":"You deserve a gift from me since you often treat me well."}]}]},"gesture":{"h":"gesture","i":"/ˈd͡ʒest͡ʃə/","a":"en-us-gesture.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hand sign for friendly communication.","e":"Our old neighbor gestured to us across the road."}]}]},"glow":{"h":"glow","i":"/ɡləʊ/","a":"en-us-glow.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"A small amount of light.","e":"The lamp glowed in the dark road."}]}]},"headline":{"h":"headline","i":"/ˈhɛd.laɪn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-headline.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A headline is something that is on a front cover page. Especially on newspapers.","e":"His marriage hit the headlines yesterday."}]}]},"housewife":{"h":"housewife","i":"/ˈhaʊs.waɪf/","a":"en-us-housewife.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A housewife is a woman in a household who does all or many of the chores such as cooking, cleaning, and caring for children.","e":"By and large, mothers and housewives are the only workers who do not have regular time off. – Anne Morrow Lindbergh"}]}]},"hesitate":{"h":"hesitate","i":"/ˈhɛzɪteɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-hesitate.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When someone hesitates, they have doubts about something and therefore do not act, or stop the action.","e":"He hesitated for a while before signing the contract."}]}]},"dispose":{"h":"dispose","i":"/dɪˈspəʉzd/","a":"en-us-dispose.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you dispose something, it means that you throw away that thing.","e":"That toy was so torn and tattered that I disposed it away immediately."}]}]},"leap":{"h":"leap","i":"/liːp/","a":"en-us-leap.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A leap is a jump.","e":"The clown took a leap through the hoop."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) When you leap, you jump from one place to another.","e":"The frog leaped from one end of the pond to the other."}]}]},"mask":{"h":"mask","i":"/mɑːsk/","a":"en-us-mask.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mask is something you wear over your face for protection, or to disguise yourself.","e":"The health ministry recommended wearing masks when going outdoors due to the forest fires in the next town."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you mask A, you cover or disguise A with B."}]}]},"melt":{"h":"melt","i":"/mɛlt/","a":"en-us-melt.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) Melting is a process of an object changing from the solid state to the liquid state without a change in temperature.","e":"The ice melted under the hot sun."}]}]},"menu":{"h":"menu","i":"/ˈmɛnjuː/","a":"en-us-menu.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A menu is a small book for displaying the type of food sold in a restaurant.","e":"We collected the menu from the waiter after we sat down in the fast food restaurant."},{"m":"(countable) A menu is also a home page of games, similar to main menu","e":"After I turned on the game console, I was brought to the menu."}]}]},"multiple":{"h":"multiple","i":"/ˈmʌltɪpl̩/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-multiple.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Multiple items are more than one item.","e":"We ran into multiple problems, but we solved them all."},{"m":"A muliple thing is one with many parts.","e":"The bone had a multiple break."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A constant product of a number.","e":"3, 6, 9 and 12 are multiples of 3."}]},{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"Multiple items are more than one item.","e":"Multiple of the people were confused."}]}]},"miracle":{"h":"miracle","i":"/ˈmɪrəkəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-miracle.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (Christianity) A miracle is an amazing thing that happened that seemed very unlikely to happen.","e":"Thanks to a miracle, Jane recovered from the final stage of cancer."}]}]},"litre":{"h":"litre","i":"/ˈliː.tə/","a":"en-uk-litre.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A litre is a measurement of water. 1000 millilitres = 1 litre.","e":"To make this cake, you need to first mix 1 litre of water with a spoonful of flour."}]}]},"litter":{"h":"litter","i":"/ˈlɪtə(r)/","a":"en-us-litter.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Litter is rubbish that is left alone on the floor.","e":"When you are in Singapore, you hardly see litter on the floor."},{"m":"(countable) A litter is the whole group of live young born at the same time.","e":"A litter of piglets."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) To litter is the act of throwing [[#Noun|litter]] on the floor.","e":"Littering is an offence under the Public Health Act."}]}]},"inherit":{"h":"inherit","i":"/ɪnˈhɛrɪt/","a":"en-us-inherit.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) Getting the characteristics of its parents.","e":"He inherited the double eyelids of his mother."},{"m":"(transitive) Getting the fortune of someone.","e":"She inherited her father's billion dollar fortune."}]}]},"infect":{"h":"infect","i":"/ɪnˈfɛkt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-infect.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When someone is infected by something, they come into contact with something (bacteria, virus, etc.) that causes sickness.","e":"Don't go near him, or he will infect you with his illness."}]}]},"inject":{"h":"inject","i":"/ɪnˈdʒɛkt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-inject.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"An act of getting something (usually medicine) into the blood of someone.","e":"The nurse injected a medicine into my body which is useful for my immunity."},{"m":"Adding more of something.","e":"My mother injected more money into my insurance."}]}]},"interfere":{"h":"interfere","i":"/ˌɪntɚˈfɪr/","a":"en-us-interfere.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"An act of minding other people's business.","e":"He is a busybody who goes around interfering with other people's business."}]}]},"sausage":{"h":"sausage","i":"/ˈsɒsɪd͡ʒ/","a":"en-us-sausage.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sausage is a piece of food that is made of chicken, pork and other meats.","e":"Sausages are mass-produced in factories."}]}]},"scan":{"h":"scan","i":"/skæn/","a":"en-us-scan.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"An act of looking through something quickly.","e":"I scanned through the page to find the information I was looking for."}]}]},"scratch":{"h":"scratch","i":"/skrætʃ/","a":"en-us-scratch.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A scratch is a mark made by a sharp object against another object.","e":"I found a scratch on my car, so I had to get paint to cover it."},{"m":"If something is made from scratch, then it was made without anything that existed or was prepared before.","e":"It took us all afternoon to make the pizzas from scratch."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you scratch you use a sharp object to make a mark on another object."},{"m":"If you scratch you rub a part of your body, because you feel an itch.","e":"I scratched my back as it felt very itchy."}]}]},"seal":{"h":"seal","i":"/siːl/","a":"en-us-seal.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mammal that lives in watch.","e":"We saw seals at the theme park performing tricks."},{"m":"(countable) A form of signature to represent a person or a company/service.","e":"Place this seal on your website and it will be trusted by your visitors."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you seal something, you close it tightly.","e":"I sealed the bag tightly before putting it into my suitcase."},{"m":"(transitive) If you seal, you hunt seals.","e":"Many countries have made it illegal to seal."}]}]},"sew":{"h":"sew","i":"/səʊ/","a":"en-us-sew.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"An act of using thread to make clothes or to mend clothes.","e":"I have a hobby of sewing. This is why I have a collection of colorful clothes."}]}]},"shell":{"h":"shell","i":"/ʃɛl/","a":"en-us-shell.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hard object that can be found on beaches.","e":"I have a collection of colorful shells at home which I have collected when I visit the beach."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"An act of bombing.","e":"The shelling of the South Korean island is a major event that happened in 2010."}]}]},"shelter":{"h":"shelter","i":"/ˈʃɛltə/","a":"en-us-shelter.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A shelter is a place which can protect someone from the rain and sun.","e":"There is no shelter nearby. I wonder how we can get out of this heavy rain."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you shelter someone or something, you provide it with cover."}]}]},"shield":{"h":"shield","i":"/ʃiːld/","a":"en-us-shield.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A piece of metal that is used for defense.","e":"A soldier carried a sword and a shield to fight in the past."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you shield something, you protect or defend it."}]}]},"skip":{"h":"skip","i":"/skɪp/","a":"en-au-skip.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"An act of overlooking something on purpose.","e":"This question has an error. Just skip it."},{"m":"A word similar to jump","e":"Squealer skipped from side to side."}]}]},"slap":{"h":"slap","i":"/slæp/","a":"en-ca-slap.oga","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you slap someone, you use something to hit another person, usually with something flat.","e":"Jane's boyfriend cheated her and she slapped him when she heard about it."}]}]},"slice":{"h":"slice","i":"/slaɪs/","a":"en-us-slice.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A slice is a piece of something that has been [[#Verb|sliced]].","e":"I like to have my sandwich with a couple slices of ham it in."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"An act of cutting meat using a small knife.","e":"I sliced the fish and placed it into another bowl."}]}]},"slim":{"h":"slim","i":"/ˈslɪm/","a":"en-us-slim.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When someone is slim, they are thin and not fat.","e":"She is so slim that she looks like a wooden stick."}]}]},"smack":{"h":"smack","i":"/smæk/","a":"en-au-smack.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"An act of slapping someone hard.","e":"I smacked him for talking back to me."}]}]},"snap":{"h":"snap","i":"/snæp/","a":"en-us-snap.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"An act of breaking something.","e":"He snapped the ruler into two by accident."}]}]},"sneak":{"h":"sneak","i":"/sniːk/","a":"en-au-sneak.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you sneak, you walk into a place quietly, usually to avoid being noticed by other people of that place.","e":"The burglar sneaked into the room while we were sleeping and stole a bag of."}]}]},"sniff":{"h":"sniff","i":"/snɪf/","a":"en-au-sniff.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"An act of breathing to find out what the smell is.","e":"The dog sniffed the floor to find for any bones."}]}]},"soak":{"h":"soak","i":"/səʊk/","a":"en-au-soak.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"An act of putting a piece of cloth or something made of thread or silk into a basin of water.","e":"I soaked my dirty clothes into the soap water."}]}]},"sore":{"h":"sore","i":"/sɔː/","a":"en-us-sore.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A feeling of the muscles being very tired.","e":"My arm is sore after all the exercises."}]}]},"spark":{"h":"spark","i":"/spɑːk/","a":"en-us-spark.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A spark is something that is created by rubbing two objects quickly. Used for starting fires with fuels.","e":"This lighter does not work anymore. It does not produce any sparks."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Spark means to cause.","e":"His strange attire sparked comment."}]}]},"speculate":{"h":"speculate","i":"/ˈspɛk.jʊˌleɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-speculate.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) When you speculate, you guess about the truth when you don't have all the important information.","e":"I speculated that Tom and Jerry's marriage would not last a year."},{"m":"(intransitive) (money) If you speculate, you make risky investments with the hope of making a large profit.","e":"He lost a lot of money by speculating in stocks."}]}]},"spill":{"h":"spill","i":"/spɪl/","a":"en-us-spill.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"An act of accidentally hitting a cup of water and the water makes a mess on something.","e":"(transitive) I accidentally spilled coffee on my shirt."}]}]},"squeeze":{"h":"squeeze","i":"/skwiːz/","a":"en-us-squeeze.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you squeeze something, you press it very tightly in your hand.","e":"I squeezed orange juice from the orange with my bare hands!"}]}]},"stack":{"h":"stack","i":"/stæk/","a":"en-au-stack.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pile of something similar.","e":"There is a stack of books outside. Are those yours?"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you stack something, you put something similar on top of one another to form a pile.","e":"I stacked up the books at one side."}]}]},"stain":{"h":"stain","i":"/steɪn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-stain.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A stain is an ugly mark on a surface.","e":"There is an ugly stain on my shirt."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you stain something, you discolor it by spilling or other contact with a fluid or substance.","e":"to stain the hand with dye"},{"m":"If you stain someone's reputation, you taint or tarnish it."}]}]},"stare":{"h":"stare","i":"/stɛər/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-stare.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When someone is looking at you for a very long time, he is staring at you.","e":"Why are so many people staring at me?"}]}]},"supper":{"h":"supper","i":"/ˈsʌpɚ/","a":"en-us-supper.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A meal taken at night, after dinner. It is usually eating snacks and not eating heavy meals.","e":"It is not good to have suppers too often. It is very unhealthy."}]}]},"sweat":{"h":"sweat","i":"/swɛt/","a":"en-us-sweat.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A salty water that is produced naturally by the body.","e":"It is so hot that my whole body is covered with sweat!"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"A natural occurrence of the body to allow the body to cool by salty water (see above).","e":"You are sweating so much!"}]}]},"sweep":{"h":"sweep","i":"/swiːp/","a":"en-us-sweep.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you sweep the floor, you use the broom to clean it.","e":"The road cleaner swept the roads clean."}]}]},"tunnel":{"h":"tunnel","i":"/ˈtʌn(ə)l/","a":"en-us-tunnel.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A tunnel is a big hole for vehicles to drive in.","e":"This tunnel collapsed a few years ago due to construction faults."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you tunnel, you make a tunnel."}]}]},"tease":{"h":"tease","i":"/tiːz/","a":"en-us-tease.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) An act of making fun of somebody. Usually for enjoyment and is not a personal attack.","e":"We were good friends that often tease each other."},{"m":"(transitive) If you tease a person, you entice or tempt them."}]}]},"photocopy":{"h":"photocopy","i":"/ˈfəʊtəʊkɒpi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-photocopy.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A duplicate of the original.","e":"Please submit a photocopy of your birth certificate."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you photocopy something, you make a duplicate of the original.","e":"It is illegal to photocopy more than 10% of a book."}]}]},"numerous":{"h":"numerous","i":"/ˈnumərəs/","a":"en-us-numerous.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is numerous, it is in large amount.","e":"Why are there numerous ants here?"}]}]},"rip":{"h":"rip","i":"/rɪp/","a":"en-us-rip.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) An act of tearing something.","e":"In anger, I ripped the page and threw it in his face."}]}]},"gasp":{"h":"gasp","i":"/ˈɡæsp/","a":"en-ca-synth-gasp.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) To gasp is the act of drawing in the breath suddenly, as if surprised.","e":"The audience gasped as the rabbit came out of the magician's hat."}]}]},"jig":{"h":"jig","i":"/dʒɪɡ/","a":"en-au-jig.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A jig is a light, quick musical dance or movement."},{"m":"(countable) A jig is a device that is used in manufacturing or woodworking and is used to control the location and movement of the workpiece."}]}]},"brisk":{"h":"brisk","i":"/brɪsk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-brisk.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Very active and quick.","e":"We took a brisk walk yesterday."}]}]},"cot":{"h":"cot","i":"/kɒt/","a":"en-us-cot.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cot is a simple bed, one that can be portable or used only for a short time, such as when camping."},{"m":"(countable) A cot is a crib (child's bed).","e":"The baby was sleeping in the cot."}]}]},"glance":{"h":"glance","i":"/ɡlɑːns/","a":"en-us-glance.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) To look for a short moment (at something).","e":"She glanced at her reflection as she passed the mirror."}]}]},"glancing":{"h":"glancing","i":"/ˈɡlɑːnsɪŋ/","a":"en-us-glancing.ogg","l":"glance","q":"verb"},"glanced":{"h":"glanced","i":"/ɡlɑːnst/","a":"en-us-glanced.ogg","l":"glance","q":"verb"},"glances":{"h":"glances","i":"/ˈɡlɑːnsɪz/","a":"en-us-glances.ogg","l":"glance","q":"verb"},"seduce":{"h":"seduce","i":"/sɪˈdjuːs/","a":"en-uk-seduce.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To seduce is to trick someone to do something wrong."},{"m":"(transitive) To seduce is to persuade someone to be a part of a sexual relationship."},{"m":"(transitive) To seduce is to charm or attract someone."}]}]},"seducing":{"h":"seducing","l":"seduce","q":"verb"},"seduces":{"h":"seduces","l":"seduce","q":"verb"},"seduced":{"h":"seduced","l":"seduce","q":"verb"},"consequent":{"h":"consequent","i":"/ˈkɑn.sɪ.kwənt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-consequent.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"happening as a result of sth.","e":"The warming of the Earth and the consequent climatic changes affect us all."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If x is consequent on y, x happens as a result of y.","e":"The flooding of the river was consequent on the heavy rain."}]}]},"chunk":{"h":"chunk","i":"/ʧʌŋk/","a":"en-us-chunk.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A chunk is a part of something that has been separated.","e":"The statue broke into chunks."}]}]},"curl":{"h":"curl","i":"/kəːl/","a":"en-us-curl.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A curl is a piece or lock of curling hair.","e":"She had beautiful golden-brown hair falling in curls on her shoulder."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something curls, it moves in a rounded or spiral shape.","e":"She curled her fingers around the pencil."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you curl, you do a sport called curling.","e":"I curl at my local club every weekend."}]}]},"curls":{"h":"curls","a":"en-us-curls.ogg","l":"curl","q":"noun"},"nervous":{"h":"nervous","i":"/ˈnɜː.vəs/","a":"en-us-nervous.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are nervous, you are tense and worried about something.","e":"I am nervous about my examinations."},{"m":"Related to the nerves.","e":"Nervous system."}]}]},"dread":{"h":"dread","i":"/drɛd/","a":"en-us-dread.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Dread is the feeling of fear of meeting, facing, or dealing with something.","e":"The idea of giving a speech in front of everyone filled her with dread."},{"m":"A dread is a long matted string of hair."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you dread something, you have a strong fear of meeting, facing, or dealing with it.","e":"He dreaded the moment that she would leave him."}]}]},"dreads":{"h":"dreads","l":"dread","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) (plural) If you wear your hair in dreads, you grow it into long matted strings.","e":"She had the longest dreads I'd ever seen."}]}]},"dreaded":{"h":"dreaded","l":"dread","q":"verb"},"dreading":{"h":"dreading","l":"dread","q":"verb"},"nip":{"h":"nip","i":"/nɪp/","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To pinch, bite, or clip (something).","e":"The small dog nipped at her fingers affectionately."}]}]},"nipped":{"h":"nipped","l":"nip","q":"verb"},"nipping":{"h":"nipping","l":"nip","q":"verb"},"chunks":{"h":"chunks","l":"chunk","q":"noun"},"criticism":{"h":"criticism","i":"/ˈkrɪtɪsɪzəm/","a":"en-us-criticism.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Critique or the expression thereof.","e":"Their marriage received a lot of criticism from their families."}]}]},"criticisms":{"h":"criticisms","l":"criticism","q":"noun"},"singapore":{"h":"Singapore","i":"/ˈsɪŋəpɔː/","a":"en-us-Singapore.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Singapore is a small country in Southeast Asia.","e":"Singapore is a small country although it is well known in many countries."}]}]},"antioxidant":{"h":"antioxidant","i":"/ˌæntiˈɒksɪdənt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-antioxidant.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An antioxidant is something that slows or stops the oxidation of another chemical."},{"m":"(countable) An antioxidant is a vitamin that can fights the harmful effects of oxidation in animal and human tissues.","e":"There are many helpful antioxidants in tea."}]}]},"antioxidants":{"h":"antioxidants","l":"antioxidant","q":"noun"},"concert":{"h":"concert","i":"/ˈkɒnsət/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-concert.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A concert is a musical performance, usually of several selections.","e":"The concert included a Mozart serenade and a Tchaikovsky symphony."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To concert something is to plan it or to arrange it."}]}]},"concerts":{"h":"concerts","l":"concert","q":"noun"},"concerted":{"h":"concerted","l":"concert","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is done with a concerted effort, it means that the action was an effort done by many people doing the same thing together.","e":"This project was a concerted effort by my team."}]}]},"concerting":{"h":"concerting","l":"concert","q":"verb"},"dine":{"h":"dine","i":"/daɪn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-dine.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you dine, then you eat dinner.","e":"We usually dine at four o'clock, because that is when we get hungry."}]}]},"dines":{"h":"dines","l":"dine","q":"verb"},"dined":{"h":"dined","a":"En-us-dined.ogg","l":"dine","q":"verb"},"dining":{"h":"dining","i":"/ˈdaɪnɪŋ(ɡ)/","a":"en-us-dining.ogg","l":"dine","q":"verb"},"diner":{"h":"diner","i":"/ˈdaɪnə(r)/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-diner.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A diner is a place where people go to eat. It is like a cheap restaurant.","e":"The diner downtown was always busy late at night."},{"m":"(countable) A diner is a person who dines.","e":"The waitress made sure to keep the diners coffee cup full."}]}]},"diners":{"h":"diners","l":"diner","q":"noun"},"frustrate":{"h":"frustrate","i":"/frəˈstreɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-frustrate.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you frustrate someone, then you make him annoyed or upset.","e":"He is frustrated because his car is broken and doesn't start."}]}]},"frustrates":{"h":"frustrates","l":"frustrate","q":"verb"},"frustrated":{"h":"frustrated","i":"/frəsˈtreɪt.ɪd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-frustrated.wav","l":"frustrate","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A frustrated person is someone who is agitated as they are unable to perform an action they want to do."}]}]},"frustrating":{"h":"frustrating","i":"/frʌˈstreɪ̯tɪŋ/","l":"frustrate","q":"verb"},"tyre":{"h":"tyre","i":"/taɪə(r)/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-tyre.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A tyre is the outer part of a car wheel. It is usually made of rubber."}]}]},"tyres":{"h":"tyres","l":"tyre","q":"noun"},"leaks":{"h":"leaks","l":"leak","q":"noun"},"stains":{"h":"stains","l":"stain","q":"noun"},"pamphlet":{"h":"pamphlet","i":"/ˈpæmflət/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-pamphlet.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pamphlet is a small book of printed information that is usually not bound between hard covers.","e":"The protesters passed out pamphlets explaining their cause."}]}]},"distress":{"h":"distress","i":"/dɪˈstrɛs/","a":"en-us-distress.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) Distress means someone who is intensely upset, worried, anxious, or is suffering from physical or emotional pain."},{"m":"Distress means a situation involving financial difficulties, poverties, or economic declines."},{"m":"Distress means to make items look old, weathered, worn, or torn on purpose."},{"m":"Distress means to be in danger.","e":"Three ships were in distress that night."}]}]},"distresses":{"h":"distresses","l":"distress","q":"verb"},"distressed":{"h":"distressed","i":"/dɪˈstrɛst/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Flame, not lame-distressed.wav","l":"distress","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Distressed means to be intensely upset, worried, anxious, or to suffer from physical or emotional pain.","e":"I was distressed after the sad loss."},{"m":"Distressed means to experience financial difficulty, poverty, or economic decline."},{"m":"Distressed means items that are made to look old, weathered, worn, or torn on purpose."},{"m":"Distressed means someone who is in danger."}]}]},"distressing":{"h":"distressing","l":"distress","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is distressing, it causes a person to be distressed."}]}]},"miserable":{"h":"miserable","a":"en-us-miserable.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"In a state of misery: very sad, ill, or poor."}]}]},"pamphlets":{"h":"pamphlets","l":"pamphlet","q":"noun"},"nosed":{"h":"nosed","l":"nose","q":"verb"},"nosing":{"h":"nosing","l":"nose","q":"verb"},"disguise":{"h":"disguise","i":"/dɪsˈɡaɪz/","a":"en-us-disguise.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Disguise is a thing (e.g. clothing) used to hide one's identity or pretend to be another.","e":"That cape and mask completed his disguise."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To change the appearance of (a person or thing) so as to hide, or to assume an identity.","e":"Spies often disguise themselves."},{"m":"(transitive) To not reveal (something secret).","e":"He disguised his true intentions."}]}]},"disguises":{"h":"disguises","l":"disguise","q":"noun"},"disguised":{"h":"disguised","i":"/dɪsˈɡaɪzd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-disguised.wav","l":"disguise","q":"verb"},"disguising":{"h":"disguising","l":"disguise","q":"verb"},"enclosure":{"h":"enclosure","i":"/ɛnˈkloʊʒər/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-enclosure.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An area closed partially or entirely by barriers.","e":"He faced punishment for creating the fenced enclosure in a public park."}]}]},"enclosures":{"h":"enclosures","l":"enclosure","q":"noun"},"dormant":{"h":"dormant","i":"/ˈdɔrmənt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-dormant.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is dormant, it means that it is not active.","e":"That is a dormant volcano."}]}]},"activate":{"h":"activate","i":"/ˈæktɪˌveɪt/","a":"en-us-activate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To activate means to make something active.","e":"The machine activated the screensaver because it was idle."}]}]},"activates":{"h":"activates","l":"activate","q":"verb"},"activated":{"h":"activated","l":"activate","q":"verb"},"activating":{"h":"activating","l":"activate","q":"verb"},"buffer":{"h":"buffer","i":"/ˈbʌfə(r)/","a":"en-au-buffer.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A buffer is a physical object at the end of a train line which stops the train going any further.","e":"Trains stop at the buffers."},{"m":"A buffer (figurative) is an end-zone.","e":"That is a buffer to prevent war. No military people may cross it."},{"m":"A buffer (computer software) is a zone that can be read and written to. It usually holds back data until it is fine to be used.","e":"Let's try to turn off the buffering setting in the game's video settings."}]}]},"buffers":{"h":"buffers","l":"buffer","q":"noun"},"tolerance":{"h":"tolerance","a":"En-us-tolerance.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Your tolerance for drugs, alcohol, danger, pain, etc. is your ability to take them without a bad effect."},{"m":"(uncountable) Tolerance is the ability to accept the opinions, beliefs and customs of other people."}]}]},"rips":{"h":"rips","l":"rip","q":"verb"},"ripped":{"h":"ripped","i":"/rɪpt/","l":"rip","q":"verb"},"ripping":{"h":"ripping","l":"rip","q":"verb"},"racist":{"h":"racist","i":"/ˈreɪsɪst/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-racist.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A racist is someone who believes that people of difference races should be treated differently.","e":"He is a racist. He keeps on saying bad things about the blacks and Arabs."}]}]},"mission":{"h":"mission","i":"/ˈmɪʃ(ə)n/","a":"en-us-mission.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mission is a quest given by someone to gain something.","e":"The Interpol is on a mission to find the international terrorists."}]}]},"equator":{"h":"equator","i":"/ɪˈkweɪ.tə/","a":"en-uk-equator.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The equator is the line that separates the Northern Hemisphere and Southern Hemisphere equally. A Latin word for \"even-maker\", since the days and nights are even throughout the year.","e":"The climate around the equator is very humid."}]}]},"port":{"h":"port","i":"/poʊrt/","a":"en-uk-a port.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A port is a place for ships to stop to trade or refuel.","e":"The port was bombed by the Japanese during World War II."},{"m":"(countable) A port is a socket in a computer where a device can be plugged in."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If a ship ports, it turns to a [[#Noun|port]]."},{"m":"If you port a software, you transfer it from one system to another."},{"m":"If you port your weapon, you carry it diagonally across the body with the barrel near the left shoulder."}]}]},"poke":{"h":"poke","i":"/pəʊk/","a":"en-au-poke.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To poke is the act of using one finger to touch someone else, usually to attract his/her attention.","e":"She did not even notice me poking her."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A poke is the an act of [[#Noun|poking]] someone or something."},{"m":"(Hawaii) Poke is a dish made of slices or cubes of raw fish or other seafood. It is mixed with sesame oil, seaweed, sea salt, herbs, spices, or other flavorful ingredients."}]}]},"pole":{"h":"pole","i":"/pəʊl/","a":"en-us-pole.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pole is a long stick that is used for grabbing for support.","e":"Grab the pole there to keep your balance on this old bus."},{"m":"(countable) A pole is the northernmost or the southernmost point of Earth."}]}]},"pokes":{"h":"pokes","l":"poke","q":"verb"},"poked":{"h":"poked","l":"poke","q":"verb"},"poking":{"h":"poking","l":"poke","q":"verb"},"equators":{"h":"equators","l":"equator","q":"noun"},"poles":{"h":"poles","a":"En-us-poles.ogg","l":"pole","q":"noun"},"pronounce":{"h":"pronounce","i":"/prəˈnaʊns/","a":"en-us-pronounce.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To pronounce something is the act of saying a word.","e":"He wanted me to pronounce that word."}]}]},"pronounces":{"h":"pronounces","l":"pronounce","q":"verb"},"pronounced":{"h":"pronounced","a":"en-us-pronounced.ogg","l":"pronounce","q":"verb"},"pr