erything!"}]}]},"sucks":{"h":"sucks","l":"suck","q":"verb"},"sucking":{"h":"sucking","l":"suck","q":"verb"},"sucked":{"h":"sucked","l":"suck","q":"verb"},"guilt":{"h":"guilt","i":"/ɡɪlt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-guilt.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"If someone feels guilt, they feel responsibility for doing something wrong."}]}]},"surround":{"h":"surround","i":"/səˈraʊnd/","a":"en-us-surround.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you surround something, you confine that object on all sides of it.","e":"The police surrounded the burglars to prevent them from escaping."}]}]},"surrounds":{"h":"surrounds","l":"surround","q":"verb"},"surrounded":{"h":"surrounded","a":"En-us-surrounded.ogg","l":"surround","q":"verb"},"surrounding":{"h":"surrounding","i":"/səˈraʊndɪŋ/","a":"en-us-surrounding.ogg","l":"surround","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"The surrounding area is the area that surrounds something."}]}]},"fierce":{"h":"fierce","i":"/fɪəs/","a":"en-us-fierce.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something or someone is fierce, then they are violent or aggressive.","e":"The dinosaur was fierce."}]}]},"fiercer":{"h":"fiercer","l":"fierce","q":"adjective"},"fiercest":{"h":"fiercest","l":"fierce","q":"adjective"},"entail":{"h":"entail","i":"/ɛnˈteɪl/","a":"en-us-entail.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If x entails y, y is involved in x as an important part.","e":"I accept the office of the President and all of the responsibilities it entails."}]}]},"appropriation":{"h":"appropriation","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An appropriation is money to be used for a specific purpose, usually by a government.","e":"The appropriations for new roads this year came to $1,000,000."},{"m":"(uncountable) Appropriation is the act of taking something for your own benefit."}]}]},"entails":{"h":"entails","l":"entail","q":"verb"},"entailed":{"h":"entailed","l":"entail","q":"verb"},"entailing":{"h":"entailing","l":"entail","q":"verb"},"appropriations":{"h":"appropriations","l":"appropriation","q":"noun"},"prerogative":{"h":"prerogative","i":"/prɪˈrɒɡ.ə.tɪv/","a":"en-us-prerogative.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A prerogative is a right that someone has because of their job, age, skill, etc.","e":"He used his presidential prerogative to end the war."}]}]},"abundant":{"h":"abundant","i":"/əˈbʌn.dn̩t/","a":"en-us-abundant.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is abundant, then there is a lot of it.","e":"The abundant fruit trees provided a steady supply of food for the monkeys."}]}]},"abundance":{"h":"abundance","i":"/əˈbʌn.dn̩s/","a":"en-us-abundance.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) If there is an abundance of something, then there is plenty of it.","e":"Harry was pleasantly surprised by the abundance of food on the Thanksgiving table."}]}]},"abundances":{"h":"abundances","l":"abundance","q":"noun"},"prerogatives":{"h":"prerogatives","l":"prerogative","q":"noun"},"fond":{"h":"fond","i":"/fɒnd/","a":"en-us-fond.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"To be fond of someone or something means to like someone or something very much.","e":"I am quite fond of having fruit for dessert."}]}]},"ambition":{"h":"ambition","i":"/æmˈbɪ.ʃən/","a":"en-us-ambition.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"If you have ambition, then you have a want to accomplish (complete) a task.","e":"That young man is full of ambition and will make a great leader someday."}]}]},"scarce":{"h":"scarce","i":"/ˈskɛəs/","a":"en-us-scarce.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is scarce, then there is almost nothing to very little left.","e":"Scientists predict that there will be a scarce supply of oil in the next fifty years."}]}]},"fonder":{"h":"fonder","l":"fond","q":"adjective"},"fondest":{"h":"fondest","l":"fond","q":"adjective"},"ambitions":{"h":"ambitions","l":"ambition","q":"noun"},"constitutionals":{"h":"constitutionals","l":"constitutional","q":"noun"},"intense":{"h":"intense","i":"/ɪnˈtɛns/","a":"en-us-intense.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Intense means strong or extreme.","e":"The intense heat of the day has gone, and a cooler evening is here."},{"m":"Intense activity involves doing a lot in a short time.","e":"The practice involved a mixture of long, slow stretching and intense jumping and running."}]}]},"dual":{"h":"dual","i":"/djʊəl/","a":"en-uk-dual.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A dual role, purpose, identity, etc. is one that has two parts, functions, or aspects.","e":"Mr. Gonzalez holds dual citizenship in Mexico and the United States."}]}]},"directly":{"h":"directly","i":"/dɪˈrɛk(t)li/","a":"en-us-directly.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something happens directly, it happens with nothing in between.","e":"I don't think we'll be directly affected by these changes."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"right after; as soon as.","e":"I'll pay him a visit directly I've finished my tea."}]}]},"postcard":{"h":"postcard","i":"/ˈpoʊstˌkɑrd/","a":"en-us-postcard.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A postcard is a piece of paper with a message on it mailed without an envelope.","e":"I sent a postcard to my friend when I was on vacation."}]}]},"postcards":{"h":"postcards","l":"postcard","q":"noun"},"indefinite":{"h":"indefinite","i":"/ɪnˈdɛfɪnɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-indefinite.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a time is indefinite, it is not known how long it is.","e":"She'll be staying with us for an indefinite period of time. Perhaps even a few months."}]}]},"refresh":{"h":"refresh","i":"/riˈfrɛʃ/","a":"en-us-refresh.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you are refreshed, you feel good or are relaxed.","e":"That glass of lemonade really refreshed me!"},{"m":"Refreshing something means to make it reload or redo a task.","e":"Hitting the \"Refresh\" button on an Internet browser makes it redo the loading of the page."}]}]},"merchant":{"h":"merchant","i":"/ˈmɝtʃənt/","a":"en-us-merchant.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A merchant is someone who sells goods.","e":"The merchant at the market made a fortune today!"}]}]},"merchants":{"h":"merchants","i":"/ˈmɝtʃənts/","a":"en-us-merchants.ogg","l":"merchant","q":"noun"},"refreshes":{"h":"refreshes","l":"refresh","q":"verb"},"refreshed":{"h":"refreshed","l":"refresh","q":"verb"},"refreshing":{"h":"refreshing","l":"refresh","q":"verb"},"lounge":{"h":"lounge","i":"/laʊndʒ/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A lounge is a waiting room in an office, airport."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you lounge, you are resting.","e":"Quit lounging around and get back to work!"}]}]},"lounges":{"h":"lounges","l":"lounge","q":"noun"},"lounged":{"h":"lounged","l":"lounge","q":"verb"},"lounging":{"h":"lounging","l":"lounge","q":"verb"},"reception":{"h":"reception","i":"/rɪˈsɛp.ʃn̩/","a":"en-us-reception.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A reception of something is how well it is doing.","e":"The reception of this video game is pretty good. I recommend buying it."},{"m":"(countable) A reception is a party-like social affair for meeting someone important or special.","e":"A reception was held in the civic center for the winners of the county art competition."}]}]},"receptions":{"h":"receptions","l":"reception","q":"noun"},"console":{"h":"console","a":"en-us-console-noun.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A console is a receptor of information.","e":"That video game console I bought was expensive!"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you console someone, you try to make them feel better.","e":"When my friend found his cassette broken, I tried to console him."}]}]},"consoles":{"h":"consoles","l":"console","q":"noun"},"consoled":{"h":"consoled","l":"console","q":"verb"},"consoling":{"h":"consoling","l":"console","q":"verb"},"ambivalent":{"h":"ambivalent","i":"/æmˈbɪv.ə.lənt/","a":"en-us-ambivalent.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are ambivalent, then you do not have a preference.","e":"I'm ambivalent about what to do because I see good reasons for both options."}]}]},"alliance":{"h":"alliance","i":"/əˈlaɪ.əns/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-alliance.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An alliance is a form of partnership between two or more. An alliance can be in the form of a coalition. It can also be an agreement or a form of friendship.","e":"The alliance was between Germany and Russia."}]}]},"neologism":{"h":"neologism","i":"/niːˈɒləd͡ʒɪzəm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-neologism.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A neologism is a newly made-up term or word.","e":"Neologisms usually do not fit Wikimedia's Criteria For Inclusion."}]}]},"synthesis":{"h":"synthesis","i":"/ˈsɪnθɪsɪs/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A synthesis is the combination of simpler components to form something more complex.","e":"Our chemistry teacher explained us the ammonia synthesis today."},{"m":"(countable) In logic, synthesis is the use of deduction to get from the general case to the particular."},{"m":"(countable) In philosophy, synthesis is the thesis and antithesis are combined to form the synthesis."},{"m":"(countable) In rhetoric, synthesis is an good arrangement of elements of a text, especially for euphony."}]}]},"neologisms":{"h":"neologisms","l":"neologism","q":"noun"},"alliances":{"h":"alliances","l":"alliance","q":"noun"},"syntheses":{"h":"syntheses","l":"synthesis","q":"noun"},"gentle":{"h":"gentle","i":"/ˈdʒɛntl̩/","a":"en-us-gentle.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A gentle person is kind and careful not to cause damage, pain, or surprise.","e":"He used to fight all the time, but I have become much kinder and gentler."},{"m":"If a movement or moving thing is gentle, it moves slowly and softly.","e":"There is a gentle breeze and one red leaf falls."},{"m":"A gentle slope or curve changes slowly from flat or straight.","e":"The slope was gentle enough that even my grandmother climbed it easily."},{"m":"A gentle voice is quiet and often friendly."},{"m":"A gentle smile is small and friendly."},{"m":"A gentle heat is not very hot."}]}]},"gentler":{"h":"gentler","l":"gentle","q":"adjective"},"gentlest":{"h":"gentlest","l":"gentle","q":"adjective"},"dignity":{"h":"dignity","i":"/ˈdɪɡnɪti/","a":"en-us-dignity.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Dignity is a human quality that makes a person worthy of respect.","e":"The man went to war to try and regain some of his dignity."}]}]},"pedestrian":{"h":"pedestrian","i":"/pəˈdɛst.ri.ən/","a":"en-us-pedestrian.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A person who is walking or traveling by foot.","e":"The pedestrian crossed the road when all the cars had stopped."}]}]},"pedestrians":{"h":"pedestrians","l":"pedestrian","q":"noun"},"moist":{"h":"moist","i":"/mɔɪst/","a":"en-us-moist.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is moist it is a little bit wet or damp.","e":"She wiped the baby's mouth with the moist cloth."}]}]},"moister":{"h":"moister","l":"moist","q":"adjective"},"moistest":{"h":"moistest","l":"moist","q":"adjective"},"tentative":{"h":"tentative","i":"/ˈtɛntətɪv/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-tentative.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is tentative, he is hesitant or uncertain.","e":"The child was tentative about crossing the road."}]}]},"gland":{"h":"gland","i":"/ɡlænd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-gland.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A gland is a cell, group of cells, or an organ that makes a special substance, like a hormone.","e":"The gland that produces sweat is called the sweat gland."}]}]},"glands":{"h":"glands","l":"gland","q":"noun"},"inner":{"h":"inner","i":"/ˈɪnɚ/","a":"en-au-inner.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"An inner item is located close to the center.","e":"The inner city was crowded and dirty."},{"m":"Relating to the mind or spirit."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A part inside another part."}]}]},"fume":{"h":"fume","i":"/fjuːm/","a":"en-us-fume.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A fume is a gas or a vapor that has a strong smell, or is dangerous to inhale.","e":"A strong fume was coming from the car's exhaust."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something is fuming, there are fumes coming out of it.","e":"The engine of the car was fuming."},{"m":"If someone is fuming, they are very angry.","e":"He's still fuming from the argument."}]}]},"fumes":{"h":"fumes","i":"/fjuːmz/","l":"fume","q":"noun"},"unhealthy":{"h":"unhealthy","i":"/ʌnˈhɛl.θi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-unhealthy.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is unhealthy, it is harmful to one’s health."},{"m":"If a person or an animal is unhealthy, they are sick."},{"m":"Unhealthy means not having or showing good health."},{"m":"Unhealthy means not doing well; not successful."},{"m":"Unhealthy means not normal."}]}]},"inferior":{"h":"inferior","i":"/ɪnˈfɪə.ri.ə/","a":"en-us-inferior.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is inferior, it is not very good.","e":"Even with her good grades, she often felt inferior to the other students."},{"m":"If x is inferior to y, x is under y.","e":"His skills are inferior to mine."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An inferior of x is something or someone that is inferior to x."}]}]},"unaided":{"h":"unaided","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"without the help or aid someone or something","e":"The unaided eye cannot see objects smaller than a grain of sand."}]}]},"oklahoma":{"h":"Oklahoma","i":"/ˌoʊk.ləˈhoʊ.mə/","a":"en-us-Oklahoma.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Oklahoma is one of the 50 states in the United States of America.","e":"Betty and Joe moved to Oklahoma."}]}]},"russian":{"h":"Russian","i":"/ˈrʌʃ(ə)n/","a":"en-us-Russian.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone or something is Russian, they are from Russia.","e":"The president met with Russian President Medvedev, to talk about U.S. and Russian cooperation."},{"m":"If something is Russian, it is typical of Russia.","e":"There aren't many Russian restaurants in Toronto."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Russian is the main language of Russia.","e":"I studied Russian for two years, but in Moscow nobody understood me."},{"m":"(countable) A Russian is a person from the country Russia.","e":"Bill talked to a Russian man who was visiting."}]}]},"russians":{"h":"Russians","l":"russian","q":"noun"},"killjoy":{"h":"killjoy","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A killjoy is a person who ruins fun, or stops people from having fun.","e":"Stop being a killjoy and join the party!"}]}]},"killjoys":{"h":"killjoys","l":"killjoy","q":"noun"},"thirsty":{"h":"thirsty","i":"/ˈθɜː(r)st.i/","a":"en-us-thirsty.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When you are thirsty, you feel like you need to have a drink.","e":"After eating dinner, I was very thirsty."}]}]},"thirstier":{"h":"thirstier","l":"thirsty","q":"adjective"},"thirstiest":{"h":"thirstiest","l":"thirsty","q":"adjective"},"underscore":{"h":"underscore","i":"/ˈʌn.də(r)ˌskɔː(r)/","a":"en-us-underscore.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An underline that goes under text is called an underscore","e":"Bob put an underscore under his title to make it stand out."}]}]},"underscores":{"h":"underscores","l":"underscore","q":"noun"},"tab":{"h":"tab","i":"/tæb/","a":"en-au-tab.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A tab is a small flap or strip of material attached to something."},{"m":"(countable) (informal) A tab is a tablet, especially one containing illegal drugs."},{"m":"A march."},{"m":"(countable) A student of Cambridge University."}]}]},"tabs":{"h":"tabs","l":"tab","q":"noun"},"exploits":{"h":"exploits","a":"en-us-exploits.ogg","l":"exploit","q":"noun"},"exploited":{"h":"exploited","l":"exploit","q":"verb"},"exploiting":{"h":"exploiting","l":"exploit","q":"verb"},"simultaneous":{"h":"simultaneous","i":"/sɪm.əlˈteɪ̯n.i.əs/","a":"en-us-simultaneous.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If events are simultaneous, they happen at exactly the same time.","e":"often plans simultaneous attacks in different places."}]}]},"partition":{"h":"partition","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A partition is a physical barrier which separates a space into two parts.","e":"Our office is divided up by partitions."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"The act of separating something into two or more pieces or parts."},{"m":"The act of dividing a place or area into two or more parts.","e":"The partition of India divided the British Indian Empire into India and Pakistan."}]}]},"partitions":{"h":"partitions","l":"partition","q":"noun"},"thwart":{"h":"thwart","i":"/θwɔːt/","a":"en-uk-thwart.oga","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To thwart is to prevent, frustrate or spoil a person or purpose.","e":"The police were planning to arrest him, but he managed to thwart them."}]}]},"forethought":{"h":"forethought","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Forethought is thought for the future: to take care, protect and anticipate.","e":"It was good foresight to have the roof mended before the winter."}]}]},"thwarts":{"h":"thwarts","l":"thwart","q":"verb"},"thwarted":{"h":"thwarted","l":"thwart","q":"verb"},"thwarting":{"h":"thwarting","l":"thwart","q":"verb"},"forethoughts":{"h":"forethoughts","l":"forethought","q":"noun"},"ethnicity":{"h":"ethnicity","i":"/ɛθˈnɪsɪti/","a":"en-us-ethnicity.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A person's ethnicity describes the common characteristics of the cultural group they belong to.","e":"Lucy's family has Italian ethnicity."}]}]},"ethnicities":{"h":"ethnicities","l":"ethnicity","q":"noun"},"pier":{"h":"pier","i":"/pɪə/","a":"en-us-pier.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pier is a raised place over the water for walking or tying boats to that connects to land."}]}]},"piers":{"h":"piers","l":"pier","q":"noun"},"wig":{"h":"wig","i":"/wɪɡ/","a":"en-us-wig.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A wig is a type of artificial hair. It can be worn by actors to change their hairstyle without affecting their original hairstyle, by people who do not have hair, or just to look better.","e":"She took off her blond wig to reveal a bald head"}]}]},"wigs":{"h":"wigs","l":"wig","q":"noun"},"clash":{"h":"clash","i":"/klaʃ/","a":"en-us-clash.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If two individuals or groups clash, they get into a fight.","e":"The Reds clashed with the police during the riot."}]}]},"clashes":{"h":"clashes","l":"clash","q":"verb"},"clashing":{"h":"clashing","l":"clash","q":"verb"},"clashed":{"h":"clashed","l":"clash","q":"verb"},"troop":{"h":"troop","i":"/truːp/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-troop.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A troop is a soldier. This word is mostly used in the plural.","e":"The enemy's troops are coming, get ready!"}]}]},"troops":{"h":"troops","i":"/truːps/","a":"en-us-troops.ogg","l":"troop","q":"noun"},"precedents":{"h":"precedents","l":"precedent","q":"noun"},"blurt":{"h":"blurt","i":"/ˈblɜːt/","a":"en-us-blurt.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you blurt something out, then you are speaking quickly without thinking.","e":"Even though the teacher asked students not to say the answer out loud, Tim blurted \"the Revolutionary War!\" to the whole class."}]}]},"blurts":{"h":"blurts","l":"blurt","q":"verb"},"blurted":{"h":"blurted","l":"blurt","q":"verb"},"blurting":{"h":"blurting","l":"blurt","q":"verb"},"discombobulate":{"h":"discombobulate","i":"/ˌdɪs.kəmˈbɒb.jəˌleɪt/","a":"en-us-discombobulate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If someone is discombobulated, they are confused.","e":"Jim was discombobulated with the math problem."}]}]},"ailurophilia":{"h":"ailurophilia","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) ailurophilia is a love for cats."}]}]},"unbosom":{"h":"unbosom","i":"/ʌnˈbʊz.əm/","a":"en-au-unbosom.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you unbosom yourself, you tell somebody a secret or your feelings.","e":"Jackie unbosomed herself to her diary."}]}]},"unbosoms":{"h":"unbosoms","l":"unbosom","q":"verb"},"unbosomed":{"h":"unbosomed","l":"unbosom","q":"verb"},"unbosoming":{"h":"unbosoming","l":"unbosom","q":"verb"},"discombobulating":{"h":"discombobulating","l":"discombobulate","q":"verb"},"discombobulated":{"h":"discombobulated","l":"discombobulate","q":"verb"},"discombobulates":{"h":"discombobulates","l":"discombobulate","q":"verb"},"inners":{"h":"inners","l":"inner","q":"noun"},"anecdote":{"h":"anecdote","i":"/ˈæ.nɪk.doʊt/","a":"en-us-anecdote.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An anecdote is a story, often told orally, and often amusing.","e":"He told us a good anecdote at dinner."}]}]},"aggression":{"h":"aggression","i":"/əˈɡrɛʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-aggression.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Aggression is a forceful and unprovoked attack, either verbal or physical.","e":"When he shouted at her, it was a kind of aggression."}]}]},"courtship":{"h":"courtship","i":"/ˈkɔːt.ʃɪp/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Mélange a trois-courtship.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Courtship is the period leading up to mating or marriage. The term can be applied to humans and animals.","e":"After a long courtship they got married."}]}]},"armament":{"h":"armament","i":"/ˈɑː(r)məmənt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-armament.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Armament is weaponry.","e":"Armies have plenty of armament."}]}]},"armaments":{"h":"armaments","l":"armament","q":"noun"},"anecdotes":{"h":"anecdotes","l":"anecdote","q":"noun"},"courtships":{"h":"courtships","l":"courtship","q":"noun"},"aggressions":{"h":"aggressions","l":"aggression","q":"noun"},"wikipedia":{"h":"Wikipedia","i":"/ˌwɪkɪˈpiːdiə/","a":"en-us-Wikipedia.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Wikipedia is an online encyclopedia that is among the top 10 websites in the world.","e":"Wikipedia is owned by the Wikimedia Foundation."}]}]},"wikipedias":{"h":"Wikipedias","l":"wikipedia","q":"noun"},"vagrant":{"h":"vagrant","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A vagrant is a person who does not have a home or job.","e":"I always see the same vagrant walking around at the bus stop."},{"m":"(countable) A vagrant is an animal that is found outside the places where it usually lives.","e":"The laughing gull usually lives in the Americas. It is a rare vagrant to Europe."}]}]},"vagrants":{"h":"vagrants","l":"vagrant","q":"noun"},"coordinate":{"h":"coordinate","i":"/koʊˈɔrdənət/","a":"en-us-coordinate-noun.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (cartography) Coordinates are a set of numbers that tells others where you are on a map."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you coordinate with someone, you work with him/her to finish an activity."}]}]},"coordinates":{"h":"coordinates","l":"coordinate","q":"noun"},"coordinated":{"h":"coordinated","l":"coordinate","q":"verb"},"coordinating":{"h":"coordinating","l":"coordinate","q":"verb"},"poop":{"h":"poop","i":"/puːp/","a":"en-ca-poop.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) (childish) When you poop, you push feces out of your anus.","e":"He is pooping in the toilet."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Poop is a term for feces.","e":"She had to clean up the dog poop, that was found on the floor."}]}]},"poops":{"h":"poops","i":"/puːps/","l":"poop","q":"verb"},"pooped":{"h":"pooped","i":"/pupt/","l":"poop","q":"verb"},"pooping":{"h":"pooping","i":"/ˈpuːpɪŋ/","l":"poop","q":"verb"},"spray":{"h":"spray","i":"/spreɪ/","a":"en-us-spray.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A spray is a fine and gentle mist of liquid.","e":"I need to get a spray to freshen up the house."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) When you spray something, you target at something and give out mist of liquid at that thing.","e":"The firemen got the hose and sprayed at the burning house."}]}]},"sprays":{"h":"sprays","l":"spray","q":"noun"},"sprayed":{"h":"sprayed","l":"spray","q":"verb"},"spraying":{"h":"spraying","l":"spray","q":"verb"},"grind":{"h":"grind","i":"/ˈɡraɪnd/","a":"en-us-grind.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you grind something, you use a machine to break it into smaller pieces.","e":"I used the grinder to grind the coffee beans."},{"m":"(transitive) If you grind someone, you rub your body against theirs in a sexual way."}]}]},"grinded":{"h":"grinded","i":"/ˈɡraɪndɪd/","l":"grind","q":"verb"},"pillage":{"h":"pillage","i":"/ˈpɪl.ɪdʒ/","a":"en-us-pillage.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) When you pillage something, you steal or loot money/goods, especially during a war.","e":"The barbarians pillaged every city."}]}]},"pillages":{"h":"pillages","l":"pillage","q":"verb"},"pillaged":{"h":"pillaged","l":"pillage","q":"verb"},"pillaging":{"h":"pillaging","l":"pillage","q":"verb"},"grower":{"h":"grower","i":"/ˈɡroʊɚ/","a":"en-au-grower.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A grower is someone, especially a farmer, who grows things like carrots.","e":"He was a carrot grower until a hurricane hit the plantation."},{"m":"(countable) A grower is something that grows.","e":"That plant is a fast grower! A few days ago, it was only half of its height!"}]}]},"growers":{"h":"growers","l":"grower","q":"noun"},"handy":{"h":"handy","i":"/ˈhæn.di/","a":"en-us-handy.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is handy, it is easy to use, or useful."},{"m":"If something is handy, then it is close by, or within reach.","e":"Do you have a pen handy?"}]}]},"handier":{"h":"handier","l":"handy","q":"adjective"},"handiest":{"h":"handiest","l":"handy","q":"adjective"},"jagged":{"h":"jagged","i":"/ˈd͡ʒæɡɪd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-jagged (adj).wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is jagged, it is unevenly cut.","e":"This piece of paper is jagged and it looks very ugly."}]}]},"jaggeder":{"h":"jaggeder","l":"jagged","q":"adjective"},"jaggedest":{"h":"jaggedest","l":"jagged","q":"adjective"},"rattle":{"h":"rattle","i":"/ˈræt.l̩/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-rattle.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you rattle something, you make sounds by shaking the object.","e":"I rattled the tin to find out if there were still biscuits left in it."}]}]},"rattles":{"h":"rattles","l":"rattle","q":"verb"},"rattled":{"h":"rattled","a":"En-us-rattled.ogg","l":"rattle","q":"verb"},"rattling":{"h":"rattling","l":"rattle","q":"verb"},"backspace":{"h":"backspace","i":"/ˈbækˌspeɪs/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A backspace is a key on the keyboard of a computer or typewriter that erases the letter before the cursor.","e":"I pressed backspace because I accidentally typed the wrong letter."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) When you backspace, you erase the letter before the cursor.","e":"No, that's wrong. Backspace here, and delete this word too."}]}]},"backspaces":{"h":"backspaces","l":"backspace","q":"noun"},"backspaced":{"h":"backspaced","l":"backspace","q":"verb"},"backspacing":{"h":"backspacing","l":"backspace","q":"verb"},"database":{"h":"database","i":"/ˈdeɪtəˌbeɪs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-database.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A database is a collection of information arranged neatly.","e":"I have a huge database of all the employees in my company."}]}]},"databases":{"h":"databases","l":"database","q":"noun"},"opium":{"h":"opium","i":"/ˈoʊpi.əm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-opium.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Opium is a yellow-brown, addictive drug.","e":"China used to sell lots of opium which resulted in many deaths."},{"m":"(countable) Anything that numbs."}]}]},"disregard":{"h":"disregard","i":"/dɪsrɪˈɡɑːd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-disregard.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you disregard something, you ignore it.","e":"The criminal disregarded the law when he stole."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(singular) Disregard is the lack of care or attention to something.","e":"His actions showed a total disregard for the law."}]}]},"disregarded":{"h":"disregarded","l":"disregard","q":"verb"},"disregarding":{"h":"disregarding","l":"disregard","q":"verb"},"doorstep":{"h":"doorstep","i":"/ˈdɔː(r)stɛp/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-doorstep.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A doorstep is the area in front of a door.","e":"We bought a new mat to replace the old one at our doorstep."}]}]},"doorsteps":{"h":"doorsteps","l":"doorstep","q":"noun"},"transform":{"h":"transform","i":"/trænzˈfɔːm/","a":"en-us-transform.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you transform something, you change it into a different thing totally.","e":"The powerful magician transformed the hamster into a rabbit."}]}]},"transforms":{"h":"transforms","l":"transform","q":"verb"},"transformed":{"h":"transformed","a":"En-us-transformed.ogg","l":"transform","q":"verb"},"transforming":{"h":"transforming","l":"transform","q":"verb"},"luggage":{"h":"luggage","i":"/ˈlʌɡɪd͡ʒ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-luggage.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Luggage is a bag that contains a traveller's belongings.","e":"Alan just lost his green luggage and is asking the staff at the airport for help."}]}]},"slash":{"h":"slash","i":"/slaʃ/","a":"en-au-slash.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A slash is a very quick cut of an object, usually with a sharp blade."},{"m":"The symbol \"/\", also known as a in computing."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you slash an object, you cut it violently with a sharp blade, such as a knife or a sword.","e":"The samurai slashed the watermelon into two in the blink of an eye."},{"m":"(transitive) To reduce something by a huge amount.","e":"That shop had to slash its prices for their closing down sales."}]}]},"tavern":{"h":"tavern","i":"/ˈtævən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-tavern.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A tavern is building that has a bar, where alcoholic drinks are sold.","e":"At the end of the week my friends and I go and relax at the tavern in the city."}]}]},"taverns":{"h":"taverns","l":"tavern","q":"noun"},"suicide":{"h":"suicide","i":"/ˈs(j)uːɪˌsaɪd/","a":"en-uk-suicide.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Suicide means to kill oneself on purpose; to take one’s own life.","e":"Sadly, Joe committed suicide last Thursday."}]}]},"suicides":{"h":"suicides","l":"suicide","q":"noun"},"nobelium":{"h":"nobelium","i":"/noʊˈbɛliəm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Naomi Persephone Amethyst (NaomiAmethyst)-nobelium.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Nobelium is a chemical element (symbol No) with an atomic number of 102. It was named after."}]}]},"festivity":{"h":"festivity","i":"/fɛˈstɪvəti/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-festivity.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A festivity is a lively and enjoyable celebration."}]}]},"festivities":{"h":"festivities","l":"festivity","q":"noun"},"strap":{"h":"strap","i":"/stræp/","a":"en-au-strap.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A strap is a long and narrow strip of either leather or cloth usually used to tie things together.","e":"Since we had no strings, we had to use the red strap to tie our tent."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you strap something, you use a strap to tie around an object and fasten it.","e":"I strapped the loose strap around my bag."}]}]},"straps":{"h":"straps","l":"strap","q":"noun"},"strapped":{"h":"strapped","l":"strap","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you're strapped (for cash), you don't have much money at the time."}]}]},"strapping":{"h":"strapping","l":"strap","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A strapping young person looks strong, healthy, and muscular."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Strapping is a narrow material used to hold things together."},{"m":"(countable) A strapping is a punishment where somebody is hit with a strap of leather."}]}]},"activist":{"h":"activist","i":"/ˈæk.tɪ.vɪst/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-activist.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An activist is someone who is trying to change a situation, especially one that is political or environmental.","e":"He is an activist for Greenpeace."}]}]},"activists":{"h":"activists","l":"activist","q":"noun"},"lobby":{"h":"lobby","i":"/lɒbi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-lobby.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A lobby is the entrance of a building.","e":"Please wait in the lobby for the tour guide."},{"m":"(countable) A lobby is a group of people who try to change the policy of a government.","e":"The U.S. anti-gun lobby is trying to change gun laws."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you lobby something, you attempt to change a decision or policy.","e":"The group lobbied to have the law repealed."}]}]},"lobbies":{"h":"lobbies","l":"lobby","q":"noun"},"uzi":{"h":"uzi","i":"/ˈuːzi/","a":"en-ca-uzi.oga","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An uzi is a type of submachine gun.","e":"The police were carrying uzis."}]}]},"uzis":{"h":"uzis","l":"uzi","q":"noun"},"contained":{"h":"contained","i":"/kənˈteɪnd/","a":"en-us-contained.ogg","l":"contain","q":"verb"},"teammate":{"h":"teammate","i":"/ˈtiːmˌmeɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-teammate.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A teammate is a person who is on the same team.","e":"I passed the ball to my teammate so he could score the goal."}]}]},"teammates":{"h":"teammates","l":"teammate","q":"noun"},"lobbied":{"h":"lobbied","l":"lobby","q":"verb"},"lobbying":{"h":"lobbying","l":"lobby","q":"verb"},"strappings":{"h":"strappings","l":"strapping","q":"noun"},"reasonable":{"h":"reasonable","i":"/ˈriː.zən.ə.bəl/","a":"en-us-reasonable.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A reasonable amount or number is not too much or too big.","e":"The hotel has good food, and the prices are reasonable."},{"m":"If something is reasonable, it is fair and sensible.","e":"It seems like a reasonable idea to me."}]}]},"unprincipled":{"h":"unprincipled","i":"/ʌnprínsəpld/","a":"en-us-unprincipled.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are unprincipled, you act as you like without considering rules or the feelings of others.","e":"A murder is unprincipled, and conscienceless."},{"m":"If an action is unprincipled, it is done without considering the rules or the feelings of others."}]}]},"tumble":{"h":"tumble","i":"/tʌmbəl/","a":"en-us-tumble.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you tumble, you fall down over and over again.","e":"Tie your shoes so that you won't tumble down the stairs."}]}]},"tumbles":{"h":"tumbles","l":"tumble","q":"verb"},"tumbled":{"h":"tumbled","l":"tumble","q":"verb"},"tumbling":{"h":"tumbling","a":"En-us-tumbling.ogg","l":"tumble","q":"verb"},"boast":{"h":"boast","i":"/bəʊst/","a":"en-us-boast.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To boast means to brag about yourself. Usually about what you do, and the good things about you.","e":"After the game Joe started to boast about his skill as a goalie."}]}]},"boasts":{"h":"boasts","l":"boast","q":"verb"},"boasted":{"h":"boasted","i":"/ˈboʊstɪd/","l":"boast","q":"verb"},"boasting":{"h":"boasting","l":"boast","q":"verb"},"republican":{"h":"republican","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A republican is a person who prefers a republic"}]}]},"republicans":{"h":"republicans","l":"republican","q":"noun"},"analyst":{"h":"analyst","i":"/ˈænəlɪst/","a":"en-us-analyst.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An analyst is a person who researches or a topic.","e":"The company called for a business analyst to help plan the budget."}]}]},"analysts":{"h":"analysts","l":"analyst","q":"noun"},"announcement":{"h":"announcement","i":"/ʌˈnaʊs.mɛnt/","a":"en-us-announcement.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An announcement is something that informs people about a topic or an issue.","e":"The announcement in the airport told people that some airplanes would not arrive on time."}]}]},"announcements":{"h":"announcements","l":"announcement","q":"noun"},"apologize":{"h":"apologize","i":"/əˈpɑləd͡ʒaɪz/","a":"en-us-apologize.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you apologize, then you say you are sorry.","e":"He apologized because he had accidentally bumped into someone."}]}]},"apologizes":{"h":"apologizes","l":"apologize","q":"verb"},"apologizing":{"h":"apologizing","l":"apologize","q":"verb"},"apologise":{"h":"apologise","i":"/əˈpɑləd͡ʒaɪz/","a":"en-us-apologize.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you apologise, then you say you are sorry.","e":"He apologised because he had accidentally bumped into someone."}]}]},"apologises":{"h":"apologises","l":"apologise","q":"verb"},"apologised":{"h":"apologised","l":"apologise","q":"verb"},"apologising":{"h":"apologising","l":"apologise","q":"verb"},"assignment":{"h":"assignment","i":"/əˈsʌɪnm(ə)nt/","a":"en-us-assignment.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An assignment is a task that is given to somebody for them to complete.","e":"The teacher gave Joe an assignment to complete while he is away on vacation."}]}]},"assignments":{"h":"assignments","l":"assignment","q":"noun"},"cloudy":{"h":"cloudy","i":"/ˈklaʊdi/","a":"en-us-cloudy.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When the sky is cloudy, it is covered with clouds.","e":"The sky quickly became cloudy and it started to rain."}]}]},"cloudier":{"h":"cloudier","l":"cloudy","q":"adjective"},"cloudiest":{"h":"cloudiest","l":"cloudy","q":"adjective"},"referee":{"h":"referee","i":"/ˌrɛf.əˈriː/","a":"en-us-referee.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A referee is someone who ensures that the rules are followed during a game.","e":"That referee was hit by the ball during the football game."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you referee a game or a match, you make sure that the rules are followed during the game or match.","e":"Both teachers refereed the volleyball match yesterday."}]}]},"referees":{"h":"referees","l":"referee","q":"noun"},"joked":{"h":"joked","l":"joke","q":"verb"},"joking":{"h":"joking","l":"joke","q":"verb"},"scuppernong":{"h":"scuppernong","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A scuppernong is a green grape grown in the Southern parts of the United States."}]}]},"scuppernongs":{"h":"scuppernongs","l":"scuppernong","q":"noun"},"melancholy":{"h":"melancholy","i":"/ˈmɛl.ənˌkɑl.i/","a":"En-us-melancholy.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Someone who is melancholy is very sad."},{"m":"Something that is melancholy makes you feel very sad.","e":"The news was very melancholy, all about people dying and losing their jobs."}]}]},"sleeve":{"h":"sleeve","i":"/sliːv/","a":"en-us-sleeve.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sleeve is the part of a shirt that covers the arm.","e":"The sleeve on my shirt is too long for my size."}]}]},"sleeves":{"h":"sleeves","l":"sleeve","q":"noun"},"catapult":{"h":"catapult","i":"/ˈkæ.tə.pʌlt/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A catapult is an object that can be used to throw or launch objects such as stones.","e":"That child used the catapult to hit his friend."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you catapult something, it means that you throw an object through the air.","e":"That small stone was being catapulted towards the road."}]}]},"catapults":{"h":"catapults","l":"catapult","q":"noun"},"catapulted":{"h":"catapulted","l":"catapult","q":"verb"},"catapulting":{"h":"catapulting","l":"catapult","q":"verb"},"opia":{"h":"opia","l":"opium","q":"noun"},"opiums":{"h":"opiums","l":"opium","q":"noun"},"gerent":{"h":"gerent","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A gerent is a manager, leader, or ruler.","e":"The gerent was the manager of the store."}]}]},"gerents":{"h":"gerents","l":"gerent","q":"noun"},"lurid":{"h":"lurid","i":"/ˈlʊrɪd/","a":"en-us-lurid.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is lurid, it causes shock or horror.","e":"The earthquake was described lurid detail."},{"m":"If a colour is lurid, it is pale and not nice.","e":"The pages of the book turned to a lurid color over time."}]}]},"scalar":{"h":"scalar","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A scalar is a real number or the magnitude of a vector."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Scalar in mathematics means to have a magnitude and no direction."}]}]},"clauses":{"h":"clauses","l":"clause","q":"noun"},"euphonious":{"h":"euphonious","i":"/juˈfoʊniəs/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is euphonious, it is pleasing to hear.","e":"The translator changed his pronunciation of the word to make it sound euphonious."}]}]},"converter":{"h":"converter","i":"/kənˈvɜː(r)tə(r)/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-converter.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A converter is something that converts one object into another object."}]}]},"converters":{"h":"converters","l":"converter","q":"noun"},"awareness":{"h":"awareness","a":"en-us-awareness.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Awareness is the state of consciousness, or the state when someone is awake. It means that a person can sense changes in their environment and respond to it.","e":"I gradually passed from sleep to full awareness."},{"m":"(uncountable) Awareness is the state or quality of being aware of something."}]}]},"fichu":{"h":"fichu","i":"/ˈfɪʃ(j)uː/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-fichu.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A fichu is a triangular scarf worn by women that is tied at the breast.","e":"Women in the 1800s commonly wore fichus."}]}]},"fichus":{"h":"fichus","l":"fichu","q":"noun"},"reciprocate":{"h":"reciprocate","i":"/rɪˈsɪprəˌkeɪt/","a":"en-us-reciprocate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) To go with alternating forward and backward motion.","e":"A reciprocating engine is so called because its pistons reciprocate: they go forward and backward."},{"m":"(transitive) When someone reciprocates something, it means that they give something back in return for something they get. This thing can be an object, or a feeling.","e":"She did not reciprocate his love for her."}]}]},"reciprocates":{"h":"reciprocates","l":"reciprocate","q":"verb"},"reciprocated":{"h":"reciprocated","l":"reciprocate","q":"verb"},"reciprocating":{"h":"reciprocating","l":"reciprocate","q":"verb"},"trader":{"h":"trader","i":"/ˈtreɪdə(r)/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-trader.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A trader is someone who tries to make a profit by buying something at a low price and then selling it at a higher price.","e":"Many traders often come to this market to sell their goods."}]}]},"traders":{"h":"traders","l":"trader","q":"noun"},"fricassee":{"h":"fricassee","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-fricassee.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Fricassee is meat or poultry that is cut into pieces and served in its own fat or juices.","e":"The beef fricassee was a very good meal."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To cook meat in the above-mentioned way."}]}]},"fricassees":{"h":"fricassees","l":"fricassee","q":"noun"},"fricasseed":{"h":"fricasseed","l":"fricassee","q":"verb"},"fricasseeing":{"h":"fricasseeing","l":"fricassee","q":"verb"},"nosy":{"h":"nosy","i":"/ˈnəʊziː/","a":"en-us-nosy.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are nosy, you are curious in a negative way.","e":"He is always too interested in what I am doing. He's such a nosy boy"}]}]},"yellowjacket":{"h":"yellowjacket","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A yellowjacket is a type of wasp.","e":"The yellowjacket stung me."}]}]},"yellowjackets":{"h":"yellowjackets","l":"yellowjacket","q":"noun"},"raincoat":{"h":"raincoat","i":"/ˈreɪnkoʊt/","a":"en-us-raincoat.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A raincoat is a waterproof coat that is worn to prevent rain water from entering and wetting the user.","e":"It has been raining a lot these days, do bring a raincoat in case."}]}]},"raincoats":{"h":"raincoats","l":"raincoat","q":"noun"},"binturong":{"h":"binturong","i":"/ˈbɪntjʊrɒŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-binturong.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A binturong is sort of like a bearcat.","e":"The binturong climbed a tree."}]}]},"binturongs":{"h":"binturongs","l":"binturong","q":"noun"},"nosier":{"h":"nosier","l":"nosy","q":"adjective"},"nosiest":{"h":"nosiest","l":"nosy","q":"adjective"},"scalars":{"h":