r some rest and relaxation."}]}]},"captive":{"h":"captive","i":"/ˈkæptɪv/","a":"en-us-captive.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A captive is a prisoner, usually in a war.","e":"Put the captives back in jail."}]}]},"captivity":{"h":"captivity","i":"/kæpˈtɪvɪti/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-captivity.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Captivity is the condition of being kept as a prisoner.","e":"You will be put into captivity until you tell us the truth."}]}]},"cargo":{"h":"cargo","i":"/ˈkɑːɡəʊ/","a":"en-us-cargo.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Cargo is goods carried on a ship or airplane.","e":"Tie up the cargo so that it does not fall off the ship."}]}]},"carpenter":{"h":"carpenter","i":"/ˈkɑː.pən.tə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-carpenter.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A carpenter is a person who creates and repairs wooden houses and other objects.","e":"The carpenter will build us new cabinets."}]}]},"carpentry":{"h":"carpentry","i":"/ˈkɑː.pɪn.tri/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-carpentry.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The activity or job of making or repairing wooden houses and things."}]}]},"carrot":{"h":"carrot","i":"/ˈkær.ət/","a":"en-us-carrot.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A long root eaten as a vegetable. It is usually orange in color."},{"m":"A shade of orange similar to the flesh of most carrots (also called carrot orange)."}]}]},"cartoon":{"h":"cartoon","i":"/kɑrˈtuːn/","a":"en-us-cartoon.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cartoon is a movie using animation."},{"m":"(countable) A cartoon is a funny humorous drawing in a comic or newspaper or magazine."}]}]},"carve":{"h":"carve","i":"/kɑrv/","a":"en-us-carve.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you carve wood or stone, you cut it into a designed shape."},{"m":"If you carve cooked meat, you cut into slices for eating."}]}]},"darling":{"h":"darling","i":"/ˈdɑrlɪŋ/","a":"en-us-darling.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A kind of name to be used 