 your own desire to do something"},{"m":"satisfy what someone wants","e":"\"I will indulge you by playing one of my finest ukulele songs, The Wailing Guitar.\""}]}]},"lodge":{"h":"lodge","i":"/lɒd͡ʒ/","a":"en-us-lodge.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A building in an outdoorsy setting, where people can rent a room","e":"\"We stayed in Hodge's Lodge during our hunting trip.\""},{"m":"(countable) A place where a hired servant, like a butler or gardener, lives separately from the main house"},{"m":"(countable) A hotel or inn"},{"m":"(countable) The place where a beaver lives"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"be stuck and hardly able to move","e":"\"That stick is lodged between those two boulders, and I can't get it out.\""},{"m":"provide one's own residence for housing"},{"m":"place something somewhere"}]}]},"somewhere":{"h":"somewhere","i":"/ˈsʌm.wɛr/","a":"en-us-somewhere.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"(in, at or to) a place, but you do not say or know exactly where","e":"I know somewhere we can go."}]}]},"residence":{"h":"residence","i":"/ˈrɛz.ɪ.dəns/","a":"en-us-residence.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The place where someone lives"},{"m":"Where someone officially lives","e":"\"He has residence in the Great State of Malarkus.\""}]}]},"nuisance":{"h":"nuisance","i":"/ˈnuː.səns/","a":"en-us-nuisance.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (usually singular) A nuisance is something or someone that bothers or annoys people."}]}]},"routine":{"h":"routine","i":"/ruːˈtiːn/","a":"en-us-routine.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Done like it is a routine. Hackneyed, shop-worn.","e":"He showed little interest in the flute sonata and played it in a routine manner."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The normal way of doing something"},{"m":"A set of actions used to perform a trick","e":"s all use the same routine to pull the rabbit out of the hat."}]}]},"show-off":{"h":"show-off","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A show-off is a person who does things to get other people to notice them."}]}]},"splendid":{"h":"splendid","i":"/ˈsplɛndɪd/","a":"en-us-splendid.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is splendid, it is very impressive and magnificent."}]}]},"tender":{"h":"tender","i":"/ˈtɛn.də(r)/","a":"en-us-tender.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"sensitive, painful when touched"},{"m":"(of food) soft and easy to chew"},{"m":"loving, gentle"},{"m":"a means of paying for something"}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A tender is an offer to do something at a fixed price."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) (formal) to formally offer or show something to someone.","e":"As company secretary, you must tender the proposal."},{"m":"(intransitive) to make a formal offer to do a job or provide goods or services for a particular price.","e":"We are unable to tender competitively for the contract."}]}]},"frisbee":{"h":"Frisbee","i":"/ˈfrɪzbi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Frisbee.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A Frisbee is a plastic disc that is thrown to make it fly."}]}]},"cooper":{"h":"cooper","i":"/ˈkuːpə(r)/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-cooper.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cooper is someone who fixes barrels and tubs."}]}]},"babysitter":{"h":"babysitter","i":"/ˈbeɪbiˌsɪtɚ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-babysitter.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A babysitter is someone who looks after young children while their parents are out.","e":"I had to be a babysitter and take care of my younger brother as my parents went overseas."}]}]},"puissance":{"h":"puissance","i":"/ˈpjuːɪ.s(ə)ns/","a":"en-uk-puissance.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A puissance is the power, might, force or strength of someone or something."}]}]},"steward":{"h":"steward","i":"/ˈstjuː.əd/","a":"en-us-steward.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A steward is someone whose regular job is to take care of something for someone else.","e":"King Ragnar was busy with the war, so his steward was kept busy mending all the ills of the nation at home."},{"m":"(countable) A steward is a male flight attendant."}]}]},"conflate":{"h":"conflate","i":"/kənˈfleɪt/","a":"en-us-conflate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To bring things together and merge them into a single entity, sometimes wrongly","e":"When she conflated two ideas, it was like mixing apples and oranges."}]}]},"stewards":{"h":"stewards","l":"steward","q":"noun"},"quota":{"h":"quota","i":"/ˈkwoʊtə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-quota.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A quota is a limit to the numbers or amounts which are allowed.","e":"Fishermen always try to land more than their quota."}]}]},"bicolour":{"h":"bicolour","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is bicolour, it has two colours."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A bicolour refers to a flower, cat etc. that has two colours."}]}]},"momentary":{"h":"momentary","i":"/ˈmoʊmənˌtɛri/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-momentary.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is momentary, it lasts for a very brief amount of time.","e":"I took a momentary glimpse at the commotion."}]}]},"precisely":{"h":"precisely","i":"/prɪˈsaɪsli/","a":"en-us-precisely.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"When something happens precisely, it happens in an exact and precise manner.","e":"The egg flew out the window and landed precisely on Mr. Norton's bald head."}]}]},"slippery":{"h":"slippery","i":"/ˈslɪpəri/","a":"en-us-slippery.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Tending or liable to cause slipping or sliding.","e":"A slippery road can be dangerous."}]}]},"unformed":{"h":"unformed","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is unformed, it does not have a definite form."},{"m":"Something that is not well developed."},{"m":"Something that is not formed or made.","e":"My opinion is unformed until I have some time to think about it."}]}]},"fugitive":{"h":"fugitive","i":"/ˈfjuːd͡ʒɪtɪv/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-fugitive.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A fugitive is a person who has escaped from a place or is in hiding, especially to avoid arrest or persecution."}]}]},"hierarchy":{"h":"hierarchy","i":"/ˈhaɪ.ə.rɑː(r).ki/","a":"en-us-hierarchy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A hierarchy is a body of officials organized in ranks so that each is above or below another."},{"m":"Any group of objects ranked so that every one is above or below another."}]}]},"televise":{"h":"televise","i":"/ˈtɛlɪvaɪz/","a":"en-us-televise.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you televise a show, you broadcast it by television.","e":"The media corporation televised the ball game for everyone to see."}]}]},"modular":{"h":"modular","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is modular, it is made up of different modules."}]}]},"module":{"h":"module","i":"/ˈmɒdjuːl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-module.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A module is a part of a system. It can often be changed at any time."},{"m":"(countable) In computing, a module is a section of a program."}]}]},"modules":{"h":"modules","l":"module","q":"noun"},"regularly":{"h":"regularly","i":"/ˈrɛɡjəlɚli/","a":"en-us-regularly.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Regularly is when something is done often.","e":"I go there quite regularly."}]}]},"pauses":{"h":"pauses","a":"En-us-pauses.ogg","l":"pause","q":"verb"},"paused":{"h":"paused","a":"En-us-paused.ogg","l":"pause","q":"verb"},"pausing":{"h":"pausing","l":"pause","q":"verb"},"apostles":{"h":"apostles","l":"apostle","q":"noun"},"shoves":{"h":"shoves","i":"/ʃʌvz/","l":"shove","q":"verb"},"shoved":{"h":"shoved","i":"/ʃʌvd/","l":"shove","q":"verb"},"shoving":{"h":"shoving","i":"/ˈʃʌvɪŋ/","l":"shove","q":"verb"},"sincerer":{"h":"sincerer","l":"sincere","q":"adjective"},"sincerest":{"h":"sincerest","l":"sincere","q":"adjective"},"strides":{"h":"strides","l":"stride","q":"noun"},"hassles":{"h":"hassles","l":"hassle","q":"noun"},"hassled":{"h":"hassled","l":"hassle","q":"verb"},"hassling":{"h":"hassling","l":"hassle","q":"verb"},"indulges":{"h":"indulges","l":"indulge","q":"verb"},"indulged":{"h":"indulged","a":"En-us-indulged.ogg","l":"indulge","q":"verb"},"indulging":{"h":"indulging","l":"indulge","q":"verb"},"lodges":{"h":"lodges","l":"lodge","q":"noun"},"lodged":{"h":"lodged","a":"En-us-lodged.ogg","l":"lodge","q":"verb"},"lodging":{"h":"lodging","i":"/ˈlɑd͡ʒɪŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Persent101-lodging.wav","l":"lodge","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A place to live."}]}]},"residences":{"h":"residences","l":"residence","q":"noun"},"nuisances":{"h":"nuisances","l":"nuisance","q":"noun"},"routines":{"h":"routines","l":"routine","q":"noun"},"coward":{"h":"coward","i":"/ˈkaʊəd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-coward.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A coward is a person who does not have courage."}]}]},"cowards":{"h":"cowards","l":"coward","q":"noun"},"bonnet":{"h":"bonnet","i":"/ˈbɒn.ɪt/","a":"en-us-bonnet.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bonnet is a brimless hat of cloth or straw worn by women and children that covers the hair and ears but not the forehead and is tied under the chin"},{"m":"(countable) chiefly Scottish: A seamless woven cap worn by Scottish men and boys; a Tam o'Shanter"},{"m":"(countable) British: An automobile hood"},{"m":"(countable) British: A metal covering or cowl for a heater, a ventilator, a fireplace, etc.","e":"A baby bonnet is sometimes given as a gift to the parents of a newborn."}]}]},"bonspiel":{"h":"bonspiel","i":"/ˈbɒnspiːl/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(Scotland, Canada) A tournament in the sport of curling."}]}]},"biceps":{"h":"biceps","i":"/ˈbaɪsɛp/","a":"en-us-biceps.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The biceps is a muscle in the human upper arm."}]}]},"thigh":{"h":"thigh","i":"/θaɪ/","a":"en-us-thigh.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The thigh is the part of the human leg between the hip and the knee."}]}]},"tint":{"h":"tint","i":"/tɪnt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-tint.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"In color theory, a tint is the mixture of a color with white, which increases lightness."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you tint something, you color or shade it.","e":"The windows of the car are tinted."}]}]},"fastidious":{"h":"fastidious","i":"/fæˈstɪdi.əs/","a":"en-us-fastidious.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Fastidious means to be very particular about one thing or another; \"picky\"","e":"He is so fastidious about personal cleanliness that he bathes three times a day."}]}]},"bonnets":{"h":"bonnets","l":"bonnet","q":"noun"},"frisbees":{"h":"frisbees","l":"frisbee","q":"noun"},"thighs":{"h":"thighs","l":"thigh","q":"noun"},"tints":{"h":"tints","i":"/tɪnts/","a":"en-us-tints.ogg","l":"tint","q":"noun"},"fugitives":{"h":"fugitives","l":"fugitive","q":"noun"},"conflates":{"h":"conflates","l":"conflate","q":"verb"},"conflated":{"h":"conflated","l":"conflate","q":"verb"},"conflating":{"h":"conflating","l":"conflate","q":"verb"},"preach":{"h":"preach","i":"/priːt͡ʃ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-preach.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When someone preaches, he gives a speech or sermon before a group of people. This speech is usually related to religion.","e":"Reverend Mather preached a one-hour sermon on the Book of John in church today"}]}]},"preaches":{"h":"preaches","l":"preach","q":"verb"},"preached":{"h":"preached","l":"preach","q":"verb"},"preaching":{"h":"preaching","i":"/ˈpriːtʃɪŋ/","a":"en-us-preaching.ogg","l":"preach","q":"verb"},"sermon":{"h":"sermon","i":"/ˈsɜː.mən/","a":"en-us-sermon.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sermon is a speech that has to do with religion.","e":"Reverend Mather preached a one-hour sermon on the Book of John in church today"},{"m":"(countable) A sermon can also be a speech one person gives to criticize other people.","e":"After George came home at 2 AM, his mom gave him a sermon about staying out late."}]}]},"postpone":{"h":"postpone","i":"/poʊstˈpoʊn/","a":"en-us-postpone.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you postpone something, it means to cancel a plan or event with the intention of at a later date.","e":"She will postpone the picnic if weather reports indicate rain."}]}]},"sermons":{"h":"sermons","l":"sermon","q":"noun"},"replacement":{"h":"replacement","i":"/rɪˈpleɪsmənt/","a":"en-us-replacement.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A replacement is something that stands in for something else.","e":"I'll be the replacement security guard for the guy who quit."}]}]},"coda":{"h":"coda","a":"en-us-coda.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A coda is a short passage at the end of a piece of music, sometimes summarizing the main themes or bringing the piece to a brilliant conclusion. A very short coda is called a 'codetta'."}]}]},"athlete":{"h":"athlete","i":"/ˈæθ.liːt/","a":"en-us-athlete.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An athlete is person involved in a sporting activity.","e":"The athlete gets ready for her race."},{"m":"(countable) (US) A person who actively participates in physical sports, or a person who is highly skilled in sports. (Known in British English as a \"sportsperson\".)"},{"m":"(countable) A physically fit person."}]}]},"codas":{"h":"codas","l":"coda","q":"noun"},"athletes":{"h":"athletes","l":"athlete","q":"noun"},"televises":{"h":"televises","l":"televise","q":"verb"},"televised":{"h":"televised","l":"televise","q":"verb"},"televising":{"h":"televising","l":"televise","q":"verb"},"hierarchies":{"h":"hierarchies","l":"hierarchy","q":"noun"},"bicolours":{"h":"bicolours","l":"bicolour","q":"noun"},"bonspiels":{"h":"bonspiels","l":"bonspiel","q":"noun"},"postpones":{"h":"postpones","l":"postpone","q":"verb"},"postponed":{"h":"postponed","a":"en-us-postponed.ogg","l":"postpone","q":"verb"},"postponing":{"h":"postponing","l":"postpone","q":"verb"},"replacements":{"h":"replacements","l":"replacement","q":"noun"},"coopers":{"h":"coopers","l":"cooper","q":"noun"},"babysitters":{"h":"babysitters","l":"babysitter","q":"noun"},"quotas":{"h":"quotas","l":"quota","q":"noun"},"incites":{"h":"incites","l":"incite","q":"verb"},"incited":{"h":"incited","l":"incite","q":"verb"},"inciting":{"h":"inciting","l":"incite","q":"verb"},"traits":{"h":"traits","l":"trait","q":"noun"},"trances":{"h":"trances","l":"trance","q":"noun"},"startles":{"h":"startles","l":"startle","q":"noun"},"startled":{"h":"startled","i":"/ˈstɑrt.l̩d/","a":"en-us-startled.ogg","l":"startle","q":"verb"},"startling":{"h":"startling","l":"startle","q":"verb"},"dazzles":{"h":"dazzles","l":"dazzle","q":"verb"},"dazzled":{"h":"dazzled","a":"En-us-dazzled.ogg","l":"dazzle","q":"verb"},"dazzling":{"h":"dazzling","a":"En-us-dazzling.ogg","l":"dazzle","q":"verb"},"aromas":{"h":"aromas","l":"aroma","q":"noun"},"survivals":{"h":"survivals","l":"survival","q":"noun"},"bloodshed":{"h":"bloodshed","i":"/ˈblʌdˌʃɛd/","a":"en-us-bloodshed.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Bloodshed refers to bleeding. Usually during a gun shootout between police and robbers, lots of bloodshed can occur.","e":"There were lots of bloodshed on the site of the riots."}]}]},"bloodsheds":{"h":"bloodsheds","l":"bloodshed","q":"noun"},"precision":{"h":"precision","i":"/prɪˈsɪ.ʒ(ə)n/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-precision.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Precision is how exact an action or measurement is.","e":"Please remember to give your precision in 3 significant figures."}]}]},"precisions":{"h":"precisions","l":"precision","q":"noun"},"outing":{"h":"outing","i":"/ˈaʊtɪŋ/","a":"en-uk-outing.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An outing is a short trip, such as a picnic, or a shopping trip.","e":"My latest outing was a trip to the beach."},{"m":"Telling another person's secrets, breaking trust."}]}]},"outings":{"h":"outings","l":"outing","q":"noun"},"pesticides":{"h":"pesticides","l":"pesticide","q":"noun"},"scrap":{"h":"scrap","i":"/skræp/","a":"en-us-scrap.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A scrap of paper or fabric is a small piece that is left unused after something is made.","e":"After Timmy cut up a magazine for his art project, there were scraps of paper everywhere."},{"m":"(countable) A scrap of food is something that isn't eaten","e":"Timmy ate most of his dinner, but left scraps of ham on his plate."},{"m":"Scrap metal or parts are pieces of junk that can be reused.","e":"There was a big pile of scrap metal in One-Eyed Joe's Junkyard."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you scrap a project or plan, you stop working on it before it is completed.","e":"Plans for a 100-story skyscraper were scrapped when the company ran out of money."},{"m":"(transitive) When you scrap a car that can't be used anymore, you sell it to a junkyard, which will destroy the car after removing any parts that can be sold.","e":"Jim's car had to be scrapped after it got in an accident."}]}]},"scraps":{"h":"scraps","l":"scrap","q":"noun"},"scrapped":{"h":"scrapped","l":"scrap","q":"verb"},"scrapping":{"h":"scrapping","l":"scrap","q":"verb"},"toss":{"h":"toss","i":"/tɒs/","a":"en-au-toss.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A toss is also known as a throw of a ball."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you toss something, you throw the object to another person.","e":"I am here! Toss the ball to me!"}]}]},"tosses":{"h":"tosses","l":"toss","q":"noun"},"tossed":{"h":"tossed","a":"En-us-tossed.ogg","l":"toss","q":"verb"},"tossing":{"h":"tossing","l":"toss","q":"verb"},"timetable":{"h":"timetable","i":"/ˈtaɪmˌteɪbəl/","a":"en-us-timetable.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A timetable is a kind of schedule with times of when the events are going to happen, usually used by schools to schedule lesson times.","e":"Check the timetable to know what the next lesson is."}]}]},"timetables":{"h":"timetables","l":"timetable","q":"noun"},"hangover":{"h":"hangover","a":"en-us-hangover.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A hangover is a group of symptoms that can include headache. It can be caused by drinking alcohol, or by other things."}]}]},"hangovers":{"h":"hangovers","l":"hangover","q":"noun"},"backcloth":{"h":"backcloth","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A backcloth or backdrop is a piece of stage scenery typically covering the rear of the stage.","e":"The backcloth was painted to represent a forest."}]}]},"backcloths":{"h":"backcloths","l":"backcloth","q":"noun"},"biedermeier":{"h":"Biedermeier","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Biedermeier is a period in European history between 1815 and 1848, and refers to a style in the arts, literature, and interior design of this period.","e":"That chair is in the Biedermeier style."}]}]},"degenerate":{"h":"degenerate","i":"/dɪˈdʒɛnərət/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-degenerate.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A degenerate is a person who loses all moral values","e":"He became a degenerate after becoming a junkie and losing his moral values."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Degenerate is to break down, to crumble, erode.","e":"She was a junkie and her health degenerated day by day."}]}]},"degenerates":{"h":"degenerates","l":"degenerate","q":"noun"},"degenerated":{"h":"degenerated","l":"degenerate","q":"verb"},"degenerating":{"h":"degenerating","l":"degenerate","q":"verb"},"chimera":{"h":"chimera","i":"/kʌɪˈmɪərə/","a":"en-au-chimera.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (mythology) A fabulous creature with parts from different animals. Can be spelt chimera or chimaera.","e":"A griffin is a chimaera with the body of a lion and the wings and head of an eagle."},{"m":"(countable) (genetics) a chimera is an organism with genetically different cells, for example, cells from two different zygotes."},{"m":"(countable) (genetics) DNA or DNA products which have been put together from different genes or different organisms."},{"m":"(countable) Chimaera, a cartilaginous marine fish in the order, with a blunt snout, long tail, and a spine before the first dorsal fin.","e":"The Axolotl is a chimera because its body has both larval and adult tissues."}]}]},"chimeras":{"h":"chimeras","l":"chimera","q":"noun"},"hotdog":{"h":"hotdog","i":"/ˈhɒtdɒɡ/","a":"en-au-hotdog.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hotdog is a type of sausage, most often a weiner or frankfurter.","e":"For lunch, I had an all-beef hotdog with ketchup and mustard."}]}]},"hotdogs":{"h":"hotdogs","l":"hotdog","q":"noun"},"archive":{"h":"archive","i":"/ˈɑːkaɪv/","a":"en-us-archive.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An archive is a collection of historical information, usually kept for people in the future to see.","e":"The police keeps an archive of the files of the criminals."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you archive something, you store and preserve it for people in the future to see. A person who archives things as a job is known as an archivist.","e":"I just archived my family's photo collection so that we can see it in the future."}]}]},"archives":{"h":"archives","l":"archive","q":"noun"},"archived":{"h":"archived","l":"archive","q":"verb"},"archiving":{"h":"archiving","l":"archive","q":"verb"},"archivist":{"h":"archivist","i":"/ˈɑː(r)kəvɪst/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An archivist is someone that archives things as a job and gets paid to do so.","e":"The Internet Archive is an organisation that employs archivists."}]}]},"archivists":{"h":"archivists","l":"archivist","q":"noun"},"futurology":{"h":"futurology","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Futurology is the scientific study of the future. A person that studies the future is known as a futurologist.","e":"Futurology has helped us to predict what is going to happen to mankind in the future."}]}]},"futurologist":{"h":"futurologist","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A futurologist is a scientist that studies the future.","e":"When I grow up, I want to be a futurologist and help mankind find out what is going to happen in the future."}]}]},"futurologists":{"h":"futurologists","l":"futurologist","q":"noun"},"whiteboard":{"h":"whiteboard","i":"/ˈwaɪtbɔːd/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A whiteboard is a large piece of either plastic or glass which words can be written on using a whiteboard marker.","e":"We drew on the class whiteboard until the teacher walked in and scolded us."}]}]},"whiteboards":{"h":"whiteboards","l":"whiteboard","q":"noun"},"disintegrate":{"h":"disintegrate","i":"/dɪsˈɪntɪɡreɪt/","a":"en-us-disintegrate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When something disintegrates, it means to fall apart, to crumble, to erode.","e":"The 100-year-old shirt disintegrated into scraps and dust."}]}]},"disintegrates":{"h":"disintegrates","l":"disintegrate","q":"verb"},"disintegrated":{"h":"disintegrated","l":"disintegrate","q":"verb"},"disintegrating":{"h":"disintegrating","l":"disintegrate","q":"verb"},"ethereal":{"h":"ethereal","a":"En-us-ethereal.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is heavenly, unearthly, of the ether (air).","e":"The ballerina had an ethereal aura."}]}]},"extraordinary":{"h":"extraordinary","i":"/ɪksˈtrɔː(r)dɪnəri/","a":"en-us-extraordinary.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is above the everyday, above the ordinary, more than ordinary, spectacular.","e":"We've been having an extraordinary spell of pleasant weather."}]}]},"prolong":{"h":"prolong","i":"/proʊˈlɔŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-prolong.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you prolong something, you lengthen it in time.","e":"Let's hope a blizzard will not prolong our visit with your mother."}]}]},"balletomane":{"h":"balletomane","i":"/ˈbalɪtəʊˌmeɪn/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A balletomane is a ballet fan.","e":"She is a balletomane and attends the ballet often."}]}]},"fulfill":{"h":"fulfill","i":"/fʊlˈfɪl/","a":"en-us-fulfil.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you fulfill something, you meet expectations.","e":"He fulfilled his promises."}]}]},"penultimate":{"h":"penultimate","i":"/pɪˈnʌltɪmət/","a":"en-us-penultimate.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is penultimate, it is in the second-to-last position in a series.","e":"Y is the penultimate letter in the alphabet."}]}]},"designer":{"h":"designer","i":"/dɪˈzaɪnɚ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-designer.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A designer is someone who designs something.","e":"The costume designer quit before the show opened."}]}]},"effeminacy":{"h":"effeminacy","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Effeminacy is the feminine traits displayed by a human male."}]}]},"fulfills":{"h":"fulfills","l":"fulfill","q":"verb"},"fulfilled":{"h":"fulfilled","a":"En-us-fulfilled.ogg","l":"fulfill","q":"verb"},"fulfilling":{"h":"fulfilling","l":"fulfill","q":"verb"},"prolongs":{"h":"prolongs","l":"prolong","q":"verb"},"prolonged":{"h":"prolonged","i":"/prəʊˈlɒŋd/","l":"prolong","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is prolonged, it is lengthy in duration."}]}]},"prolonging":{"h":"prolonging","l":"prolong","q":"verb"},"cornice":{"h":"cornice","i":"/ˈkɔːnɪs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-cornice.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cornice is a decorative horizontal molding."}]}]},"birdcage":{"h":"birdcage","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A birdcage is a cage for a pet bird (or birds) usually portable and found in the home.","e":"I keep a parakeet in a birdcage."}]}]},"orchestrate":{"h":"orchestrate","i":"/ˈɔː(r).kə.streɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-orchestrate.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"A musical term meaning to assign specific instruments.","e":"\"\" is orchestrated for celesta and bass clarinet."},{"m":"If you orchestrate something, you plan or manipulate it.","e":"Nancy and Rhonda orchestrated the break-up between Ron and Wanda."}]}]},"rancor":{"h":"rancor","i":"/ˈræŋ.kɚ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-rancour.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Anger, resentment or ill-will."}]}]},"thrill":{"h":"thrill","i":"/θrɪl/","a":"en-us-thrill.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A thrill is an intense excitement.","e":"My trip to Alaska was the thrill of my life."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Giving intense excitement.","e":"Try to thrill me by telling me something new."}]}]},"thrilled":{"h":"thrilled","l":"thrill","q":"verb"},"virginal":{"h":"virginal","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is virginal, it is fresh, new and unspoiled, very much like a virgin.","e":"The young lady had a virginal charm that was endearing."}]}]},"prowess":{"h":"prowess","i":"/ˈpraʊɪs/","a":"en-au-prowess.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The prowess of somebody represents the person's great ability, usually referring to the physical ability.","e":"I couldn't match Tom's prowess playing tennis."}]}]},"uranian":{"h":"Uranian","i":"/jʊˈreɪnɪən/","a":"en-uk-Uranian.oga","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A person of a third sex — originally, someone with \"a female psyche in a male body\" who is sexually attracted to men. Also known as homosexual."}]}]},"tendril":{"h":"tendril","i":"/ˈtɛn.drəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-tendril.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A tendril is a leaf, petiole, or stem with a threadlike shape used by a plant to grow upward by wrapping itself about an object."}]}]},"mystique":{"h":"mystique","i":"/mɪˈstiːk/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A mystique is a mystery, a mysterious aura."}]}]},"abiotic":{"h":"abiotic","i":"/ˌeɪ.baɪˈɑt.ɪk/","a":"en-ca-abiotic.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is abiotic, it is not a living thing, not alive and is not made by an organism. Abiotic refers to things that are not alive, like light, water, air, nutrients, minerals, and soil.","e":"is often done by abiotic means, such as wind or water."}]}]},"unconventional":{"h":"unconventional","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is unconventional, it is non traditional, not the expected, not the norm.","e":"John and Jane had unconventional attitudes about marriage."}]}]},"delicacy":{"h":"delicacy","i":"/ˈdɛlɪkəsi/","a":"en-us-delicacy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A delicacy is an exotic, tasty, or rare food item.","e":"Fried fish brains with pickled banana peel is a delicacy for some gourmands."},{"m":"Something that is delicate, tender.","e":"The delicacy of your touch pleases me."}]}]},"delicacies":{"h":"delicacies","l":"delicacy","q":"noun"},"emit":{"h":"emit","i":"/iˈmɪt/","a":"en-us-emit.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something emits gas, light, sound, etc., it sends it out.","e":"The sun emits hot rays."}]}]},"perfume":{"h":"perfume","i":"/ˈpɜːfjuːm/","a":"en-us-perfume.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A perfume is something that gives out a scent, odor, aroma.","e":"Her perfume smelled like lily of the valley."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To make a place smell nice.","e":"The flowers perfumed the room with a delicious scent."}]}]},"saccharine":{"h":"saccharine","i":"/ˈsækərɪn/","a":"en-au-saccharine.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is saccharine is too sweet, too syrupy, too cute.","e":"Strawberry shortcake is a saccharine character."}]}]},"controversial":{"h":"controversial","i":"/kɒn.trə.ˈvɜː.ʃəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-controversial.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is causing debate, causing talk and discussion.","e":"The latest book about UFOs has been very controversial."}]}]},"orchestral":{"h":"orchestral","i":"/ˌɔrˈkɛstrəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-orchestral.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is of an orchestra.","e":"The orchestral sound was brilliant."}]}]},"urinate":{"h":"urinate","i":"/ˈjʊərɪneɪt/","a":"en-us-urinate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When a person or animal urinates, it passes urine to empty the bladder.","e":"I drink a lot of water and need to urinate several times a day."}]}]},"coil":{"h":"coil","i":"/kɔɪl/","a":"en-us-coil.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A coil is a long object in circular piles \"wound continuously round one point\".","e":"s are usually stored as coils."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you coil something, you wind it cylindrically or spirally around a common center.","e":"The machine coils the wire at a very high speed."}]}]},"balletomanes":{"h":"balletomanes","l":"balletomane","q":"noun"},"designers":{"h":"designers","l":"designer","q":"noun"},"cornices":{"h":"cornices","l":"cornice","q":"noun"},"birdcages":{"h":"birdcages","l":"birdcage","q":"noun"},"orchestrates":{"h":"orchestrates","l":"orchestrate","q":"verb"},"orchestrated":{"h":"orchestrated","l":"orchestrate","q":"verb"},"orchestrating":{"h":"orchestrating","l":"orchestrate","q":"verb"},"thrills":{"h":"thrills","l":"thrill","q":"noun"},"thrilling":{"h":"thrilling","l":"thrill","q":"verb"},"uranians":{"h":"Uranians","l":"uranian","q":"noun"},"tendrils":{"h":"tendrils","l":"tendril","q":"noun"},"mystiques":{"h":"mystiques","l":"mystique","q":"noun"},"emits":{"h":"emits","l":"emit","q":"verb"},"emitted":{"h":"emitted","l":"emit","q":"verb"},"emitting":{"h":"emitting","l":"emit","q":"verb"},"perfumes":{"h":"perfumes","l":"perfume","q":"noun"},"perfumed":{"h":"perfumed","l":"perfume","q":"verb"},"perfuming":{"h":"perfuming","l":"perfume","q":"verb"},"urinates":{"h":"urinates","l":"urinate","q":"verb"},"urinated":{"h":"urinated","l":"urinate","q":"verb"},"urinating":{"h":"urinating","l":"urinate","q":"verb"},"coils":{"h":"coils","l":"coil","q":"noun"},"choreography":{"h":"choreography","i":"/ˌkɔr.iˈɒɡ.rə.fi/","a":"en-au-choreography.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Choreography is the art of designing dances.","e":"The choreography for \"\" was completed in three or four rehearsals."}]}]},"choreograph":{"h":"choreograph","i":"/ˈkɔrjəɡræf/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-choreograph.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you choreograph a dance or a set of movements, you design a them.","e":"Will Susie choreograph this year's Dance Revue?"}]}]},"rehearsal":{"h":"rehearsal","i":"/rɪˈhɜː(r)səl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-rehearsal.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A rehearsal is a practice session before a performance.","e":"A rehearsal gives the director a chance to correct mistakes."}]}]},"freshness":{"h":"freshness","i":"/ˈfrɛʃnəs/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Freshness refers to the newness, originality of something.","e":"The freshness of the director's interpretation shed a whole new light on the play."}]}]},"improvisation":{"h":"improvisation","i":"/ɪmprəvaɪˈzeɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-improvisation.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Improvisation refers to a performance without a script, plan, direction, or rehearsal.","e":"Tom and Jerry's improvisation at the party was a success."},{"m":"Making something better, improving it to make something better."}]}]},"virtuosity":{"h":"virtuosity","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Great expertise, a virtuoso is a highly skilled expert with great technical skills.","e":"Claude's virtuosity at the piano can not be bettered."}]}]},"expressiveness":{"h":"expressiveness","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The act of showing expression, usually emotional expression.","e":"Her fervent and moving expressiveness led me to reconsider sending her to the guillotine."}]}]},"adagio":{"h":"adagio","i":"/əˈdɑːdʒiəʊ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-adagio.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An adagio is a slow movement in music.","e":"The second movement of a symphony is sometimes an adagio."},{"m":"(countable) An adagio is a type of marking in music meaning to play slowly.","e":"There is an adagio mark at bar 12."}]}]},"anguish":{"h":"anguish","i":"/ˈæŋ.ɡwɪʃ/","a":"en-us-anguish.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Anguish refers to the emotional pain and despair someone can experience.","e":"My anguish over a break-up with my lover could not be soothed."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you feel anguished, you are suffering in pain."}]}]},"discard":{"h":"discard","i":"/dɪsˈkɑːd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-discard (verb).wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you discard something, you throw away, to get rid of something.","e":"Will you please discard those old love letters?"},{"m":"If you discard a playing card, you take the playing card out of your hand."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Something that is thrown away.","e":"That tattered old song sheet is a discard."}]}]},"dispense":{"h":"dispense","i":"/dɪsˈpɛns/","a":"en-us-dispense.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When something dispenses an object, it means that it is the object, to distribute it."},{"m":"To throw away, or ignore.","e":"She made us all feel relaxed and comfortable by dispensing with the old formalities."}]}]},"virtuoso":{"h":"virtuoso","i":"/ˌvɜ.tʃuˈəʊ.səʊ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-virtuoso.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A virtuoso is someone with great expertise in a particular field, usually a musician or someone in the arts.","e":"Lotte is virtuoso on the Jew's harp."}]}]},"choreographies":{"h":"choreographies","l":"choreography","q":"noun"},"choreographs":{"h":"choreographs","l":"choreograph","q":"verb"},"choreographed":{"h":"choreographed","l":"choreograph","q":"verb"},"choreographing":{"h":"choreographing","l":"choreograph","q":"verb"},"rehearsals":{"h":"rehearsals","l":"rehearsal","q":"noun"},"improvisations":{"h":"improvisations","l":"improvisation","q":"noun"},"adagios":{"h":"adagios","l":"adagio","q":"noun"},"anguishes":{"h":"anguishes","l":"anguish","q":"noun"},"discards":{"h":"discards","l":"discard","q":"verb"},"discarded":{"h":"discarded","i":"/dɪsˈkɑrdɪd/","l":"discard","q":"verb"},"discarding":{"h":"discarding","l":"discard","q":"verb"},"dispenses":{"h":"dispenses","l":"dispense","q":"verb"},"dispensed":{"h":"dispensed","l":"dispense","q":"verb"},"dispensing":{"h":"dispensing","l":"dispense","q":"verb"},"virtuosos":{"h":"virtuosos","l":"virtuoso","q":"noun"},"virtuosi":{"h":"virtuosi","l":"virtuoso","q":"noun"},"trifle":{"h":"trifle","i":"/ˈtraɪfəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Naomi Persephone Amethyst (NaomiAmethyst)-trifle.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Something of little worth, notice, or importance","e":"This issue is a mere trifle."},{"m":"A British dessert of cake, fruit, cream, and custard.","e":"Mary Anne, you may serve the trifle."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Toying with.","e":"Are you trifling with my affections?"}]}]},"reconstruct":{"h":"reconstruct","i":"/ˌriːkənˈstrʌkt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-reconstruct.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you reconstruct something, you rebuild it.","e":"Will the police reconstruct the events leading to the crime?"}]}]},"revive":{"h":"revive","i":"/rɪˈvaɪv/","a":"en-us-revive.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To revive is to restore to life.","e":"The drowned swimmer was revived by paramedics."}]}]},"booklet":{"h":"booklet","i":"/ˈbʊk.lət/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-booklet.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A booklet is a small book, including audio CDs."}]}]},"persona":{"h":"persona","i":"/pɝˈsoʊnə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-persona.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A persona is an assumed identity or role; an identity or role that somebody assumes."},{"m":"A social role."},{"m":"A character played by an actor."},{"m":"The mask or appearance one presents to the world."},{"m":"An imaginary person representing a particular type of client or customer."}]}]},"booklets":{"h":"booklets","l":"booklet","q":"noun"},"revives":{"h":"revives","l":"revive","q":"verb"},"revived":{"h":"revived","l":"revive","q":"verb"},"reviving":{"h":"reviving","l":"revive","q":"verb"},"reconstructed":{"h":"reconstructed","l":"reconstruct","q":"verb"},"reconstructing":{"h":"reconstructing","l":"reconstruct","q":"verb"},"reconstructs":{"h":"reconstructs","l":"reconstruct","q":"verb"},"trifles":{"h":"trifles","l":"trifle","q":"noun"},"trifling":{"h":"trifling","i":"/ˈtraɪfliŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-trifling.wav","l":"trifle","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A trifling matter is something that is not important."}]}]},"trifled":{"h":"trifled","l":"trifle","q":"verb"},"superstar":{"h":"superstar","i":"/ˈsuːpə(r)ˌstɑː(r)/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-superstar.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A superstar is an extremely successful, high-profile performer or sportsperson.","e":"Venus and Serena Williams are sports superstars."}]}]},"machinist":{"h":"machinist","i":"/mə.ˈʃi.nɪst/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An individual who operates machinery such as flying machines and trap doors back stage in a theatre.","e":"The machinist was injured when the trap door failed to open."}]}]},"backstage":{"h":"backstage","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"In the area in a theatre behind the stage.","e":"I met the stars backstage after the show."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The area in a theatre behind the stage."}]}]},"hideous":{"h":"hideous","i":"/ˈhɪd.iː.ʌs/","a":"en-us-hideous.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When someone is hideous, it means the person is very ugly.","e":"Medusa was a hideous monster."}]}]},"jilt":{"h":"jilt","i":"/dʒɪlt/","a":"en-us-jilt.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To not marry, to break an engagement suddenly, to leave one standing at the altar.","e":"John has warned Jill he will jilt her if she doesn't stop seeing Rory."}]}]},"maiden":{"h":"maiden","i":"/ˈmeɪdən/","a":"en-us-maiden.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A maiden is a female human whose hymen (\"cherry\") is intact and unbroken.","e":"Jill was a maiden when she met John."}]}]},"supernatural":{"h":"supernatural","i":"/ˌs(j)uːpəˈnatʃ(ə)rəl/","a":"en-us-supernatural.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is supernatural, it is something of the other world, spooky, scary or that is not natural or normal.","e":"I love stories about ghost, goblins, and supernatural creatures."}]}]},"bride-to-be":{"h":"bride-to-be","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A bride-to-be is a woman who is about to be married","e":"Jill is a bride-to-be. She will marry in a month."}]}]},"jilting":{"h":"jilting","l":"jilt","q":"verb"},"jilts":{"h":"jilts","l":"jilt","q":"verb"},"jilted":{"h":"jilted","l":"jilt","q":"verb"},"superstars":{"h":"superstars","l":"superstar","q":"noun"},"maidens":{"h":"maidens","a":"En-us-maidens.ogg","l":"maiden","q":"noun"},"brides-to-be":{"h":"brides-to-be","l":"bride-to-be","q":"noun"},"radiant":{"h":"radiant","i":"/ˈreɪdi.ənt/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is radiant is shining brightly, glowing brilliantly.","e":"Her radiant face told us she was very happy."}]}]},"commentator":{"h":"commentator","i":"/ˈkɑmənˌteɪtər/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-commentator.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A commentator is someone who comments, opines, or makes remarks upon a topic, subject, or issue.","e":"The news commentator explained the issue clearly."}]}]},"strangeness":{"h":"strangeness","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The state or quality of being strange, odd, or weird.","e":"The strangeness of his manner created amusement for his neighbors."}]}]},"incarnation":{"h":"incarnation","i":"/ˌɪŋkɑː(r)ˈneɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-incarnation.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A person or thing regarded as embodying or exhibiting some quality, idea, or the like.","e":"The leading dancer is the incarnation of grace."}]}]},"revel":{"h":"revel","i":"/ˈrɛv.əl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-revel.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A revel is a party, a festival, merrymaking, a gay time.","e":"Shakespeare wrote, \"Our revels now are ended\"."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To make merry; to have a gay, lively time.","e":"We revelled in the first warm day of spring."}]}]},"liberation":{"h":"liberation","i":"/ˌlɪbəˈreɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-liberation.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Liberation is the process or result of becoming free.","e":"The country was very different after liberation from minority white rule in 1994."}]}]},"sensation":{"h":"sensation","i":"/sɛnˈseɪʃən/","a":"en-us-sensation.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A sensation is a feeling one experiences.","e":"I have a tingling sensation in my arm."},{"m":"A sensation is a widespread reaction of interest or excitement.","e":"Her debut created a sensation among theatre-goers."}]}]},"insipid":{"h":"insipid","i":"/ɪnˈsɪp.ɪd/","a":"en-us-insipid.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is unappetizingly flavorless.","e":"The diners were disappointed with the plain, insipid soup they were served."},{"m":"Flat; lacking character or definition.","e":"The textbook had a very insipid presentation of the controversy."},{"m":"Cloyingly sweet or sentimental.","e":"Greeting cards contain some of the most insipid words ever written."}]}]},"abjection":{"h":"abjection","i":"/æbˈd͡ʒɛk.ʃn̩/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-abjection.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The act of bringing down or humbling.","e":"The abjection of the king and his realm."},{"m":"The state of being rejected or cast out.","e":"An abjection from the beatific regions where God, and his angels and saints, dwell forever."},{"m":"A low or downcast condition; meanness of spirit; abasement; degradation."}]}]},"transcendence":{"h":"transcendence","i":"/træn(t)ˈsɛndəns/","a":"en-us-transcendence.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The act of surpassing usual limits."},{"m":"(uncountable) The state of being beyond the range of normal perception."},{"m":"(uncountable) The state of being free from the constraints of the material world, as in the case of a deity."}]}]},"deprivation":{"h":"deprivation","i":"/dɛp.rɪ.veɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-deprivation.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The act of, dispossessing, or; the act of deposing or divesting of some dignity."},{"m":"(uncountable) The state of being deprived; privation; loss; want; bereavement."},{"m":"(countable) The taking away from a clergyman's benefice, or other spiritual promotion or dignity."},{"m":"The lack of something.","e":"He was suffering from deprivation of sleep."}]}]},"vivify":{"h":"vivify","i":"/ˈvɪvɪfʌɪ/","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you vivify something, you bring it to life; to restore vitality."}]}]},"mediocre":{"h":"mediocre","i":"/ˌmiːdɪˈəʊkə/","a":"en-us-mediocre.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Ordinary; not extraordinary; not special, exceptional, or great; of medium quality","e":"I'm pretty good at tennis but only mediocre at ping pong."}]}]},"exotic":{"h":"exotic","i":"/ɪɡˈzɒtɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-exotic.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is foreign, with the connotation of excitingly foreign.","e":"Vera's make up gave her an exotic appearance."},{"m":"If something is exotic, it is not native to the ecosystem.","e":"Palm trees would be considered an exotic species in Antarctica."}]}]},"tunic":{"h":"tunic","i":"/tjuːnɪk/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A garment worn with or without sleeves, and of various lengths reaching from the hips to the ankles. It is worn over the torso."}]}]},"sentimental":{"h":"sentimental","i":"/ˌsɛntiˈmɛntl̩/","a":"en-us-sentimental.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is sentimental, then it involves sentiment or relates to it in some way.","e":"I'm in a sentimental mood."}]}]},"eject":{"h":"eject","i":"/ɪˈdʒɛkt/","a":"en-us-eject.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To eject can mean to force (a person or people) to leave.","e":"The man started a fight and was ejected from the bar."},{"m":"(transitive) To be ejected can also mean to be thrown out of something quickly.","e":"A man from Montreal was ejected from his car because he was in an accident."},{"m":"(transitive) To eject someone can mean to make (a sports player) leave the field because they are behaving in a bad way."},{"m":"(transitive) To eject can mean to make something come out of a machine.","e":"Press that button to eject the video tape."},{"m":"(intransitive) To eject can also mean to exit an aircraft when it is flying.","e":"The pilot could not control the plane and had to eject."},{"m":"(intransitive) To eject can mean to come out of a machine."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A button on a machine that ejects something from the machine.","e":"When the DVD is finished, press eject."}]}]},"costumier":{"h":"costumier","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A costumier is a maker or supplier of theatrical costumes."}]}]},"ejects":{"h":"ejects","l":"eject","q":"verb"},"ejected":{"h":"ejected","l":"eject","q":"verb"},"ejecting":{"h":"ejecting","l":"eject","q":"verb"},"stencil":{"h":"stencil","i":"/ˈstɛnsɪl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-stencil.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A stencil is a utensil that contains a perforated sheet through which ink can be forced to create a printed pattern onto a surface.","e":"They will use stencils to put the design onto the wall."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To print with a stencil.","e":"The designs were stenciled onto the wall."}]}]},"embroider":{"h":"embroider","i":"/ɪmˈbrɔɪdɚ/","a":"en-us-embroider.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To stitch a decorative design on fabric with needle and thread of various colors.","e":"Jane embroidered a colorful design at the hem of her tunic."},{"m":"To add imaginary detail to a narrative to make it more interesting or acceptable.","e":"Jane always embroiders her stories of past dates with fabulous details."}]}]},"tarnish":{"h":"tarnish","i":"/ˈtɑrnɪʃ/","a":"en-us-tarnish.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The discoloration of some metals when exposed to air","e":"The tarnish on the silver tea pot must be removed."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To discolor a metal due to exposure to the air","e":"Silver tea pots tarnish easily."},{"m":"To soil, sully, damage or compromise","e":"The rumors tarnished Jane's reputation."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Damaged, sullied, soiled, compromised"},{"m":"John's tarnished reputation cost him the respect of his co-workers."}]}]},"sequin":{"h":"sequin","i":"/ˈsiː.kwɪn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-sequin.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A sequin is a spangle sewn onto clothing.","e":"The sequins on her costume were falling off."}]}]},"priesthood":{"h":"priesthood","i":"/ˈpristˌhʊd/","a":"en-us-priesthood.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Clergymen as a group; the clergy.","e":"John felt called to enter the priesthood after much prayer."}]}]},"anticipation":{"h":"anticipation","i":"/æn.tɪs.ɪˈpeɪ.ʃən/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Anticipation is looking forward to or expecting something, expectancy, the eagerness associated with waiting for something to occur.","e":"He waited with great anticipation for Christmas to arrive."},{"m":"The act of anticipating, taking up, placing, or considering something beforehand, or before the proper time in natural order.","e":"Often the anticipation of a shot is worse than the pain of the needle stick."}]}]},"anticipations":{"h":"anticipations","l":"anticipation","q":"noun"},"priesthoods":{"h":"priesthoods","l":"priesthood","q":"noun"},"embroiders":{"h":"embroiders","l":"embroider","q":"verb"},"embroidered":{"h":"embroidered","a":"En-us-embroidered.ogg","l":"embroider","q":"verb"},"sequins":{"h":"sequins","l":"sequin","q":"noun"},"stencils":{"h":"stencils","l":"stencil","q":"noun"},"tarnishes":{"h":"tarnishes","l":"tarnish","q":"noun"},"tarnished":{"h":"tarnished","l":"tarnish","q":"verb"},"tarnishing":{"h":"tarnishing","l":"tarnish","q":"verb"},"stenciled":{"h":"stenciled","l":"stencil","q":"verb"},"stenciling":{"h":"stenciling","l":"stencil","q":"verb"},"embroidering":{"h":"embroidering","l":"embroider","q":"verb"},"tunics":{"h":"tunics","l":"tunic","q":"noun"},"deprivations":{"h":"deprivations","l":"deprivation","q":"noun"},"transcendences":{"h":"transcendences","l":"transcendence","q":"noun"},"vivifies":{"h":"vivifies","l":"vivify","q":"verb"},"vivified":{"h":"vivified","l":"vivify","q":"verb"},"vivifying":{"h":"vivifying","l":"vivify","q":"verb"},"abjections":{"h":"abjections","l":"abjection","q":"noun"},"revels":{"h":"revels","l":"revel","q":"noun"},"liberations"