something very closely.","e":"He mimicked the unusual way his friend walked."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A mimic is a person who copies others very closely.","e":"She was an excellent mimic."},{"m":"A mimic is a person who acts in a mime.","e":"She was the best mimic in the theatre company."}]}]},"mimics":{"h":"mimics","l":"mimic","q":"verb"},"mimicked":{"h":"mimicked","l":"mimic","q":"verb"},"mimicking":{"h":"mimicking","l":"mimic","q":"verb"},"tolerations":{"h":"tolerations","l":"toleration","q":"noun"},"trusses":{"h":"trusses","l":"truss","q":"noun"},"titanium":{"h":"titanium","i":"/taɪˈteɪni.əm/","a":"en-us-titanium.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Titanium is a metallic (meaning made of metal) element with an atomic number of 22 and the symbol Ti.","e":"Titanium is a strong and light metal which is used to build airplanes."}]}]},"dysprosium":{"h":"dysprosium","i":"/dɪsˈproʊziəm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Naomi Persephone Amethyst (NaomiAmethyst)-dysprosium.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Dysprosium is a metallic (meaning made of metal) element with an atomic number of 66 and the symbol Dy.","e":"It takes a lot of heat to melt dysprosium."}]}]},"bismuth":{"h":"bismuth","i":"/ˈbɪz.məθ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-bismuth.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Bismuth is a metallic (meaning made of metal) element with an atomic number of 83.","e":"Bismuth is very heavy and weighs the same as lead."}]}]},"palladium":{"h":"palladium","i":"/pəˈleɪdiəm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-palladium.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Palladium is a metallic (meaning made of metal) element with an atomic number of 46.","e":"Palladium is often used to make surgical tools for doctors."},{"m":"A palladium is a sacred object with the power to protect a city or country.","e":"The palladium at the city of Troy was a statue of Athena."}]}]},"rite":{"h":"rite","i":"/raɪt/","a":"en-us-rite.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A rite is the proper way of performing a ceremony.","e":"Her body was buried according to the rites of the church."}]}]},"solvation":{"h":"solvation","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Solvation is a chemical process when molecules in a solute react with those in the solvent.","e":"Water is often used as a solvent during solvation."}]}]},"molecule":{"h":"molecule","i":"/ˈmɒləkjuːl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-molecule.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A molecule is the smallest part of a substance.","e":"A water molecule is made of two hydrogen atoms and one oxygen atom."}]}]},"molecules":{"h":"molecules","l":"molecule","q":"noun"},"rites":{"h":"rites","i":"/raɪts/","a":"en-us-rites.ogg","l":"rite","q":"noun"},"solute":{"h":"solute","i":"/ˈsɒljuːt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-solute.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"In chemistry, a solute is something that is dissolved into another substance.","e":"Sugar is a solute when it is added to a cup of hot coffee."}]}]},"solutes":{"h":"solutes","l":"solute","q":"noun"},"prematurely":{"h":"prematurely","i":"/ˌpriːməˈtjʊə(r)li/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-prematurely.wav","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something happens prematurely, it means it happened too soon, before it was ready.","e":"He left the hospital prematurely, before his wounds had healed."}]}]},"atomic":{"h":"atomic","i":"/əˈtɔm.ɪk/","a":"en-us-atomic.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Atomic means it is about atoms, which are very small.","e":"The force of an atomic bomb comes from breaking an atom into pieces."}]}]},"proton":{"h":"proton","i":"/ˈprəʊ.tɒn/","a":"en-us-proton.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A proton is a particle that is part of the nucleus of an atom and has a positive charge.","e":"s think that a proton is made up of quarks."}]}]},"protons":{"h":"protons","l":"proton","q":"noun"},"particle":{"h":"particle","i":"/ˈpɑːtɪk(ə)l/","a":"en-us-particle.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A particle is a very small, tiny piece.","e":"His eye hurt because a particle of dust had got into it."},{"m":"(countable) A particle is a type of complement in a verb phrase, coming either between a verb and a direct object or after the object.","e":"In I picked it up and I picked up the bit, the preposition up functions as a particle."}]}]},"particles":{"h":"particles","l":"particle","q":"noun"},"palladia":{"h":"palladia","l":"palladium","q":"noun"},"harry":{"h":"harry","i":"/hæri/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-harry.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To harry is to annoy, harass and cause distress over and over again.","e":"The teacher was harried by a group of bad boys."},{"m":"(transitive) To harry means to attack or raid a town in a war.","e":"The Viking raiders would harry English towns that were close to the sea."}]}]},"harries":{"h":"harries","l":"harry","q":"verb"},"harried":{"h":"harried","a":"En-us-harried.ogg","l":"harry","q":"verb"},"harrying":{"h":"harrying","l":"harry","q":"verb"},"molecular":{"h":"molecular","i":"/məˈlɛkjʊlə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-molecular.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is molecular, it is about molecules.","e":"Molecular weight is the mass of a molecule."}]}]},"viking":{"h":"Viking","i":"/ˈvaɪkɪŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Viking.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A Viking was a person from Scandinavia from 793 AD-1066 AD. They were famous as warriors, pirates, explorers and traders.","e":"The Vikings sailed in ships called longboats."}]}]},"vikings":{"h":"Vikings","l":"viking","q":"noun"},"explorer":{"h":"explorer","i":"/ɛkˈsplɔːrə(r)/","a":"en-us-explorer.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An explorer is a person who is trying to discover new things and places.","e":"was a famous explorer."}]}]},"explorers":{"h":"explorers","l":"explorer","q":"noun"},"raider":{"h":"raider","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A raider is a person who takes part in quick surprise attacks on an enemy.","e":"People living near the sea were scared of being attacked by Viking raiders."}]}]},"raiders":{"h":"raiders","l":"raider","q":"noun"},"metalloid":{"h":"metalloid","i":"/ˈmɛtəlɔɪd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-metalloid.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A metalloid is an element that is not a metal, but looks or acts like a metal.","e":"is a metalloid because it looks like metal, but it is not as strong."},{"m":"(countable) A metalloid is an element that can be mixed with metal to make an alloy.","e":"is a metalloid which makes cast iron when mixed with iron."}]}]},"metalloids":{"h":"metalloids","l":"metalloid","q":"noun"},"revival":{"h":"revival","i":"/rɪˈvaɪvəl/","a":"en-GB-revival.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A revival is when something is brought back into use, or restored.","e":"There was a revival of the music of Mozart on his 200th birthday."}]}]},"revivals":{"h":"revivals","l":"revival","q":"noun"},"alloy":{"h":"alloy","i":"/ˈæ.lɔɪ/","a":"en-us-alloy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An alloy is made by mixing one metal with another metal or a metalloid.","e":"is an alloy made by mixing iron and carbon together."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To alloy means to mix metals together to make an alloy."},{"m":"To alloy ideas means to combine them together."},{"m":"To alloy means to mix an item with something else that makes it less pure and not as valuable."}]}]},"alloys":{"h":"alloys","l":"alloy","q":"noun"},"alloyed":{"h":"alloyed","l":"alloy","q":"verb"},"alloying":{"h":"alloying","l":"alloy","q":"verb"},"rove":{"h":"rove","i":"/rəʊv/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-rove.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To rove is to travel about a large area without a plan or destination.","e":"He roved through the fields looking for wild flowers."}]}]},"roves":{"h":"roves","l":"rove","q":"verb"},"roved":{"h":"roved","l":"rove","q":"verb"},"roving":{"h":"roving","l":"rove","q":"verb"},"juggalo":{"h":"juggalo","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"a juggalo is someone who likes clowns"}]}]},"juggalos":{"h":"juggalos","l":"juggalo","q":"noun"},"dolphin":{"h":"dolphin","i":"/ˈdɒlf.ɪn/","a":"en-us-dolphin.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A dolphin is an animal that lives in water, usually colored gray.","e":"We went to the zoo to see the dolphins."}]}]},"impregnable":{"h":"impregnable","i":"/ɪmˈprɛɡnəbəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-impregnable.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is impregnable, it cannot be beaten. Used in contexts of physical force, but in metaphor, for any situation where a position or person cannot be defeated.","e":"The Welsh found that Edward's castles were impregnable."}]}]},"francium":{"h":"francium","i":"/ˈfrænsi.əm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-francium.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Francium is a heavy, radioactive, metal element with an atomic number of 87.","e":"Francium is made from actinium or thorium."}]}]},"spaz":{"h":"spaz","i":"/spæz/","a":"en-au-spaz.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Someone that is physically or mentally disabled."}]}]},"authentic":{"h":"authentic","i":"/ɔ.ˈθɛn.tɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-authentic.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Of the same origin as claimed; genuine.","e":"The experts confirmed it was an authentic signature."},{"m":"Conforming to reality and therefore worthy of trust, reliance, or belief.","e":"The report was completely authentic."},{"m":"Having authority."}]}]},"tungsten":{"h":"tungsten","i":"/ˈtʌŋstən/","a":"en-us-tungsten.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Tungsten is a metal and element with an atomic number of 74 and the symbol W.","e":"Tungsten is used in light bulbs because it can get very hot and not melt."}]}]},"soar":{"h":"soar","i":"/sɔː/","a":"en-us-sore.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To fly high with little or no effort."},{"m":"Figurative use:"}]}]},"hover":{"h":"hover","i":"/ˈhɒ.və(r)/","a":"en-us-hover.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To hover is to hang in the air, almost in one place","e":"The kestrel hovered, with rapidly beating wings."},{"m":"Figurative uses:","e":"He hovered between this and that."}]}]},"streamline":{"h":"streamline","i":"/ˈstriːmlʌɪn/","a":"en-us-streamline.oga","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you streamline something, you make it into a shape that allows it to move through a fluid easily using little energy.","e":"Streamlining helps animals swim though water and fly through air."}]}]},"hovers":{"h":"hovers","l":"hover","q":"verb"},"hovered":{"h":"hovered","l":"hover","q":"verb"},"hovering":{"h":"hovering","l":"hover","q":"verb"},"soars":{"h":"soars","l":"soar","q":"verb"},"soared":{"h":"soared","l":"soar","q":"verb"},"soaring":{"h":"soaring","l":"soar","q":"verb"},"glides":{"h":"glides","l":"glide","q":"verb"},"glided":{"h":"glided","a":"en-us-glided.ogg","l":"glide","q":"verb"},"gliding":{"h":"gliding","l":"glide","q":"verb"},"glider":{"h":"glider","i":"/ˈɡlaɪdə(r)/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-glider.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A glider is an aircraft which can fly without an engine.","e":"The glider soared through the sky using the warm air currents."}]}]},"gliders":{"h":"gliders","l":"glider","q":"noun"},"glacial":{"h":"glacial","i":"/ˈɡleɪ.ʃ(ɪ)əl/","a":"en-us-glacial.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"To be glacial, something needs to be like a glacier such as cold, freezing or very slow moving.","e":"He moved at glacial speed towards the exam room."}]}]},"overnight":{"h":"overnight","i":"/əʊvə(r)ˈnaɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-overnight.wav","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Period from midnight to dawn.","e":"She went on an overnight trip to visit her mother."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you overnight somewhere, you spend the night there.","e":"I overnighted at my friend's house after my home was broken into."}]}]},"chromium":{"h":"chromium","i":"/ˈkroʊmi.əm/","a":"en-us-chromium.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Chromium is a metal and element with an atomic number of 24 and the symbol Cr.","e":"Chromium is used to make stainless steel because it keeps its shine and does not rust."}]}]},"holmium":{"h":"holmium","i":"/ˈhoʊmiəm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Naomi Persephone Amethyst (NaomiAmethyst)-holmium.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Holmium is a metal and element with an atomic number of 67 and the symbol Ho.","e":"Holmium is very magnetic."}]}]},"chrome":{"h":"chrome","i":"/krəʊm/","a":"en-us-chrome.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Chrome is chromium or something made with an alloy of chronium.","e":"Many car parts are made with chrome because it is very bright and shines."},{"m":"chrome is a name of Google browser, also as Google chrome.","e":"I surf the Internet by Google chrome."}]}]},"cocktail":{"h":"cocktail","i":"/ˈkɒkteɪl/","a":"en-au-cocktail.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cocktail is an alcoholic drink made from a spirit or several spirits mixed with fruit juice, lemonade, or cream.","e":"Her favourite cocktail was a \"Pink Lady\" made with gin, grenadine syrup, cream and an egg."}]}]},"cocktails":{"h":"cocktails","l":"cocktail","q":"noun"},"cobalt":{"h":"cobalt","i":"/ˈkəʊ.bɒlt/","a":"en-us-cobalt.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Cobalt is a metal and element with an atomic number of 27 and the symbol Co.","e":"Cobalt is used to make magnetic alloys."}]}]},"magnetic":{"h":"magnetic","i":"/mæɡˈnɛtɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-magnetic.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Magnetic means that something is or acts like a magnet."}]}]},"dodgy":{"h":"dodgy","i":"/ˈdɒd͡ʒ.i/","a":"EN-AU ck1 dodgy.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is dodgy is risky and probably not going to work.","e":"He came up with a dodgy plan to make a lot of money."}]}]},"dodgier":{"h":"dodgier","l":"dodgy","q":"adjective"},"dodgiest":{"h":"dodgiest","l":"dodgy","q":"adjective"},"dodge":{"h":"dodge","i":"/dɒdʒ/","a":"en-us-dodge.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To dodge is to move quickly to avoid being hit.","e":"He had to dodge to the left so the ball missed him."},{"m":"To dodge is to be clever and cunning to avoid questions.","e":"The President dodged questions about unemployment during the debate."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A dodge is a plan to trick or avoid.","e":"The investment plan was a dodge to avoid paying tax."}]}]},"dodges":{"h":"dodges","l":"dodge","q":"verb"},"dodged":{"h":"dodged","l":"dodge","q":"verb"},"dodging":{"h":"dodging","l":"dodge","q":"verb"},"wobble":{"h":"wobble","i":"/ˈwɑbəl/","a":"en-us-wobble.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To wobble is to move from side to side, or shake unevenly.","e":"During the earthquake, the tall building wobbled."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An uneven or shaky movement is a wobble.","e":"She was scared and her voice had a wobble."}]}]},"wobbles":{"h":"wobbles","a":"En-us-wobbles.ogg","l":"wobble","q":"verb"},"wobbled":{"h":"wobbled","a":"En-us-wobbled.ogg","l":"wobble","q":"verb"},"wobbling":{"h":"wobbling","a":"En-us-wobbling.ogg","l":"wobble","q":"verb"},"maggot":{"h":"maggot","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A maggot is a type of insect."}]}]},"maggots":{"h":"maggots","l":"maggot","q":"noun"},"fatass":{"h":"fatass","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A fatass is a slang term for someone who is overweight.","e":"That man is a total fatass! He is occupying two seats instead of one."}]}]},"skunk":{"h":"skunk","i":"/skʌŋk/","a":"en-au-skunk.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A skunk is an animal that releases a strong odor when frightened."}]}]},"skunks":{"h":"skunks","l":"skunk","q":"noun"},"gypsy":{"h":"Gypsy","i":"/ˈd͡ʒɪp.si/","a":"en-us-gypsy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A Gypsy is a person who belongs to a nomadic group from Europe.","e":"Many Gypsies lived in brightly colored and decorated horse pulled wagons."},{"m":"Someone who lives a wandering life is sometimes called a gypsy."}]}]},"horsefeathers":{"h":"horsefeathers","a":"En-us-horsefeathers.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Something that is nonsense and does not make any sense at all."}]}]},"analog":{"h":"analog","i":"/ˈænəlɒɡ/","a":"en-us-analog.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A variable used in a technical system is continuous, and does not have one of a finite number of different values."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) something that has an analogy to something else"}]}]},"digital":{"h":"digital","i":"/ˈdɪd͡ʒɪtəɫ/","a":"en-us-digital.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Having to do with digits (fingers or toes); performed with a finger."},{"m":"Property of representing values as discrete numbers rather than a continuous spectrum."}]}]},"indestructible":{"h":"indestructible","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Not able to be destroyed."},{"m":"Being resistant to harm as to be unable to be destroyed.","e":"Because diamonds are so hard, they are almost indestructible."}]}]},"posh":{"h":"posh","i":"/pɑʃ/","a":"en-uk-posh.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Posh is something that is high class, elegant and fashionable.","e":"He spoke with a posh voice."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Posh is to act in an elegant or high class way.","e":"He liked to talk posh."}]}]},"posher":{"h":"posher","l":"posh","q":"adjective"},"poshest":{"h":"poshest","l":"posh","q":"adjective"},"heather":{"h":"heather","i":"/ˈhɛðɚ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Naomi Persephone Amethyst (NaomiAmethyst)-heather.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Heather is a small evergreen shrub, Calluna vulgaris, with pink or purple flowers.","e":"He liked to walk through the heather which grew on the hills near the farm."}]}]},"heathers":{"h":"heathers","l":"heather","q":"noun"},"likeness":{"h":"likeness","i":"/ˈlaɪknəs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-likeness.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A likeness is a similarity between things.","e":"His face had a likeness to Prince Charles."},{"m":"A likeness is a picture, sculpture or something that is made to look like something else.","e":"Her drawing was a good likeness of his face."}]}]},"elegant":{"h":"elegant","i":"/ˈɛl.ə.ɡənt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-elegant.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"To be elegant something has beauty and is graceful.","e":"She looked elegant in her new dress."},{"m":"A answer that is elegant, is clever and simple.","e":"He came up with an elegant answer to a complex problem."}]}]},"weathers":{"h":"weathers","l":"weather","q":"verb"},"weathered":{"h":"weathered","l":"weather","q":"verb"},"weathering":{"h":"weathering","l":"weather","q":"verb"},"dislike":{"h":"dislike","i":"/dɪsˈlaɪk/","a":"en-us-dislike.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If a person dislikes someone or something, they do not like someone or something.","e":"He had to eat cabbage although he really disliked its strong smell."}]}]},"dessert":{"h":"dessert","i":"/dɪˈzɜːt/","a":"en-us-dessert.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A dessert is a sweet food dish usually served at the end of a meal.","e":"After the roast duck, we had a plum pudding for dessert."}]}]},"desserts":{"h":"desserts","l":"dessert","q":"noun"},"plaster":{"h":"plaster","i":"/ˈplɑːstə/","a":"en-us-plaster.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Plaster is a mix of lime or gypsum and sand which becomes hard when water is added.","e":"Builders use plaster to put a smooth coating on walls and ceilings."},{"m":"(countable) A bandage or medical dressing is also called a plaster.","e":"The doctor put a plaster over the deep cut on the boy's arm."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To plaster is to put a mix of lime, sand and water on a surface.","e":"She plastered the new wall in the bedroom."},{"m":"To plaster is to put a dressing on a wound."},{"m":"To plaster can mean to cover, hide or stick something completely as if you were using plaster.","e":"He got very angry when his new car was plastered with bird droppings."},{"m":"To plaster can mean to use force or cause damage.","e":"The city was plastered with bombs during the war."}]}]},"plasters":{"h":"plasters","l":"plaster","q":"noun"},"plastered":{"h":"plastered","l":"plaster","q":"verb"},"plastering":{"h":"plastering","l":"plaster","q":"verb"},"plasterer":{"h":"plasterer","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A plasterer is a person who puts a smooth coat of plaster on to walls and ceilings.","e":"The painters had to wait for the plasterer to finish before they could paint the wall."}]}]},"plasterers":{"h":"plasterers","l":"plasterer","q":"noun"},"gypsum":{"h":"gypsum","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Gypsum is a mineral used to make plaster, paint and fertilizer. It can be colorless, pink or yellow."}]}]},"bandage":{"h":"bandage","i":"/ˈbændɪdʒ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-bandage.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bandage is a long piece of material used to cover a wound, or protect an injury.","e":"The vet wrapped the cat's injured leg with a bandage."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To bandage is to use material to cover or protect an injury.","e":"The doctor bandaged the boy's broken arm so that it would not move."}]}]},"bandages":{"h":"bandages","l":"bandage","q":"noun"},"bandaged":{"h":"bandaged","l":"bandage","q":"verb"},"bandaging":{"h":"bandaging","l":"bandage","q":"verb"},"gypsies":{"h":"Gypsies","l":"gypsy","q":"noun"},"fashionable":{"h":"fashionable","i":"/ˈfæʃənəbl̩/","a":"en-us-fashionable.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is fashionable, it is the latest popular style or fashion.","e":"He wore fashionable new sunglasses."}]}]},"generator":{"h":"generator","i":"/ˈdʒɛnəreɪtə(r)/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-generator.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A generator is a machine that makes electrical energy from mechanical energy."}]}]},"generators":{"h":"generators","l":"generator","q":"noun"},"likeable":{"h":"likeable","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Someone or something that is likeable means it is easy to like someone or something.","e":"He was a very likeable person."}]}]},"sixpence":{"h":"sixpence","i":"/ˈsɪks.pəns/","a":"en-us-sixpence.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A sixpence was a coin with the value of six.","e":"She gave the boy sixpence to buy sweets."}]}]},"sixpences":{"h":"sixpences","l":"sixpence","q":"noun"},"saint":{"h":"saint","i":"/seɪnt/","a":"en-us-saint.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A saint is a religious person who has done such good things, that after their death they have a special place in heaven.","e":"Mother Theresa did such good work with poor people in India, the Catholic Church has named her a saint."}]}]},"saints":{"h":"saints","a":"En-us-saints.ogg","l":"saint","q":"noun"},"superb":{"h":"superb","a":"En-us-superb.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"To be superb, something must be the very best, grand, excellent and the very best quality.","e":"The food at the restaurant was superb."}]}]},"vanadium":{"h":"vanadium","i":"/vəˈneɪdi.əm/","a":"en-us-vanadium.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Vanadium is white, soft, metal element with an atomic number of 23 and the symbol V.","e":"Vanadium is added to steel to make it stronger."}]}]},"goodly":{"h":"goodly","i":"/ˈɡʊdli/","a":"en-us-goodly.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Goodly means large, a big amount.","e":"He bet a goodly sum of money at the races."}]}]},"goodlier":{"h":"goodlier","l":"goodly","q":"adjective"},"goodliest":{"h":"goodliest","l":"goodly","q":"adjective"},"burglar":{"h":"burglar","i":"/ˈbɜːɡlə(r)/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-burglar.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A burglar is a person who goes into people's houses to take things.","e":"The burglar stole money and jewellery from my house."}]}]},"burglars":{"h":"burglars","l":"burglar","q":"noun"},"bandit":{"h":"bandit","i":"/ˈbændɪt/","a":"en-au-bandit.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bandit is person, usually in a group, who uses guns to rob people.","e":"The bandits took their money and horses as they came home from the market."}]}]},"bandits":{"h":"bandits","l":"bandit","q":"noun"},"passport":{"h":"passport","i":"/ˈpɑːspɔːt/","a":"en-us-passport.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A passport is an official document that a person, and allows them to leave and come back to a country."}]}]},"passports":{"h":"passports","l":"passport","q":"noun"},"steer":{"h":"steer","i":"/stɪə(r)/","a":"en-us-steer.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To steer is use a rudder, wheel, or paddle to decide which way something will travel.","e":"The driver gripped the wheel tightly to steer the car around a corner."},{"m":"To steer is to set a direction.","e":"He was able to steer the group through the difficult changes."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A steer is a young bull or ox that has been castrated and raised for beef."}]}]},"steers":{"h":"steers","l":"steer","q":"verb"},"steered":{"h":"steered","l":"steer","q":"verb"},"steering":{"h":"steering","l":"steer","q":"verb"},"castrate":{"h":"castrate","i":"/ˈka.streɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-castrate.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To castrate is to remove the testicles from a male, making him unable to produce children.","e":"The young bulls were castrated so they would grow more meat."},{"m":"To castrate is to take away energy and vigor, to make it easier to handle or control."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A castrate is a male that has had his testicles removed."}]}]},"castrates":{"h":"castrates","l":"castrate","q":"verb"},"castrated":{"h":"castrated","l":"castrate","q":"verb"},"castrating":{"h":"castrating","l":"castrate","q":"verb"},"castrato":{"h":"castrato","i":"/kæsˈtrɑː.təʊ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-castrato.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A castrato is a male soprano singer who has been castrated while still a boy to keep his voice high pitched."}]}]},"castratos":{"h":"castratos","l":"castrato","q":"noun"},"castration":{"h":"castration","i":"/kæˈstreɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-castration.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Castration is the removal of the testicles of a male animal."}]}]},"castrations":{"h":"castrations","l":"castration","q":"noun"},"soprano":{"h":"soprano","i":"/səˈprænoʊ/","a":"en-us-soprano.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A soprano is the highest pitched voice range of a woman or a young boy.","e":"The soprano range is from middle C to the A which is 13 notes above."},{"m":"A soprano is a person who has a voice in the soprano range.","e":"The sopranos in the choir struggled to sing the high notes in tune."},{"m":"A soprano is a musical instrument in the soprano range.","e":"The soprano saxophone is often used in Irish music."}]}]},"sopranos":{"h":"sopranos","l":"soprano","q":"noun"},"saxophone":{"h":"saxophone","i":"/ˈsæksəfoʊn/","a":"en-us-saxophone.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The saxophone is a musical instrument made of metal which has a single reed mouthpiece.","e":"The saxophone was invented by Adolphe Sax in 1846."}]}]},"saxophones":{"h":"saxophones","l":"saxophone","q":"noun"},"saxophonist":{"h":"saxophonist","i":"/ˈsæksəˌfoʊnɪst/","a":"en-us-saxophonist.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A saxophonist is a person who plays the saxophone.","e":"John Coltrane is a famous jazz saxophonist."}]}]},"saxophonists":{"h":"saxophonists","l":"saxophonist","q":"noun"},"cellist":{"h":"cellist","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable); A cellist is someone who plays the cello.","e":"Pablo Casals was a famous cellist."}]}]},"cellists":{"h":"cellists","l":"cellist","q":"noun"},"cello":{"h":"cello","i":"/ˈtʃɛləʊ/","a":"en-us-cello.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cello is a stringed instrument in the violin family, larger than a viola but smaller than a double bass.","e":"A cello is played while sitting, with the instrument held between the knees."}]}]},"cellos":{"h":"cellos","l":"cello","q":"noun"},"mandolinist":{"h":"mandolinist","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable); A mandolinist is a person who plays the mandolin.","e":"Fred Tackett is the mandolinist in the band Little Feat."}]}]},"mandolinists":{"h":"mandolinists","l":"mandolinist","q":"noun"},"violoncello":{"h":"violoncello","i":"/ˌvaɪələnˈtʃɛləʊ/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A violoncello is a large four stringed instrument in the violin family."}]}]},"violoncellos":{"h":"violoncellos","l":"violoncello","q":"noun"},"violoncellist":{"h":"violoncellist","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A violoncellist is the full name for a cellist, a person who plays the violoncello or cello."}]}]},"violoncellists":{"h":"violoncellists","l":"violoncellist","q":"noun"},"graphic":{"h":"graphic","i":"/ˈɡræfɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-graphic.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Graphic means something is very clearly described, so that you can easily imagine what it looks like.","e":"People were upset by the graphic violence in the movie because it looked so real."},{"m":"Graphic means writing or other written symbols.","e":"The ancient Egyptians used graphic symbols called hieroglyphs to write."},{"m":"Graphic is to show information using a graph.","e":"His diagrams gave a graphic view of the increase in crime."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A graphic is a picture used to help give meaning to writing.","e":"The railway station had a graphic of a man on the door of the male toilets."},{"m":"A graphic is an image made on a computer.","e":"The new video game was popular because it had great graphics."}]}]},"graphics":{"h":"graphics","i":"/ˈɡræfɪks/","a":"en-us-graphics.oga","l":"graphic","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Graphics is images produced and displayed by a computer."}]}]},"distraught":{"h":"distraught","i":"/dɪsˈtrɔːt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-distraught.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"To be distraught, you are very upset, emotional and even frantic.","e":"The little boy was distraught because he could not find his mother in the busy store."}]}]},"windmill":{"h":"windmill","i":"/ˈwɪnd.mɪl/","a":"en-us-windmill.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A windmill is a type of engine that converts the energy of wind into rotational energy by means of vanes called \"sails\" or \"blades\". This rotational energy is then used for different purposes such as generating electricity, to mill grains, etc."}]}]},"namesake":{"h":"namesake","i":"/ˈneɪmseɪk/","a":"en-us-namesake.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A namesake is one who is named after another, or for whom another is named.","e":"She was named Kylie after her namesake Kylie Minogue, a singer her mother really liked."},{"m":"A namesake is a person with the same name as another."},{"m":"A namesake can be a ship or a building that is named after someone or something."}]}]},"namesakes":{"h":"namesakes","l":"namesake","q":"noun"},"lotion":{"h":"lotion","a":"En-us-lotion.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A lotion is a cream or ointment used on the skin to clean, heal or protect.","e":"She used a sunscreen lotion so she would not get sunburnt while on the beach."}]}]},"windmills":{"h":"windmills","l":"windmill","q":"noun"},"lotions":{"h":"lotions","l":"lotion","q":"noun"},"eponym":{"h":"eponym","i":"/ˈɛpənɪm/","a":"en-us-eponym.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An eponym is something that is named after a person's name.","e":"A spoonerism is an eponym, named after the Reverend William Archibald Spooner (1844–1930) who used to make the mistake when he spoke."}]}]},"eponyms":{"h":"eponyms","l":"eponym","q":"noun"},"emotional":{"h":"emotional","i":"/ɪˈməʊʃənəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-emotional.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Emotional is when your feelings control what you do, rather than reason.","e":"His reasons for buying the old house were emotional."},{"m":"To be emotional, you show more emotion than is usual.","e":"She became quite emotional when her small child was missing."},{"m":"Emotional can be used to describe how the emotions affect things.","e":"The music was quite emotional and made everyone feel very sad."}]}]},"organist":{"h":"organist","i":"/ˈɔːɡənɪst/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Wodencafe-organist.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) An organist is a person who plays the organ.","e":"The Bach fugues were some of the organist's best pieces."}]}]},"organists":{"h":"organists","l":"organist","q":"noun"},"fugue":{"h":"fugue","i":"/ˈfjuːɡ/","a":"En-us-fugue.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A fugue is a musical form using a theme which is repeated in a complex pattern.","e":"The composer Bach wrote many enjoyable fugues."}]}]},"fugues":{"h":"fugues","l":"fugue","q":"noun"},"violist":{"h":"violist","i":"/ˈvaɪ.əl.ɪst/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-violist (viol).wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A violist is a person who plays the viola or the viol.","e":"The violist stood up and played a solo."}]}]},"violists":{"h":"violists","l":"violist","q":"noun"},"racquet":{"h":"racquet","i":"/ˈrækɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Eleanorrrrrrrrrr-racquet.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A racquet is a sporting device with a handle joined to a frame covered in tightly stretched strings. It is used in tennis, squash and in badminton to hit a shuttlecock.","e":"She bought a new tennis racquet before the tournament."}]}]},"racquets":{"h":"racquets","l":"racquet","q":"noun"},"penance":{"h":"penance","i":"/ˈpɛn.əns/","a":"en-us-penance.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A penance is an action you do as a punishment. You do penance when you have done something wrong and want to compensate for it.","e":"His penance was to pray for two days and not eat"}]}]},"penances":{"h":"penances","l":"penance","q":"noun"},"outrage":{"h":"outrage","i":"/ˈaʊt.reɪd͡ʒ/","a":"en-us-outrage.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An outrage is a very violent act.","e":"He kicked a puppy which was an outrage."},{"m":"An outrage can be an act that offends many people.","e":"Burning the US flag was an outrage."},{"m":"Outrage is a feeling of anger towards people who have been violent or offensive.","e":"He was outraged by by the attack on the old lady."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To outrage someone is to be very violent or cause great offence.","e":"He outraged Muslims when he burned copies of the Koran."}]}]},"outrages":{"h":"outrages","l":"outrage","q":"noun"},"outraged":{"h":"outraged","l":"outrage","q":"verb"},"outraging":{"h":"outraging","l":"outrage","q":"verb"},"whoop":{"h":"whoop","i":"/wuːp/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-whoop.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To whoop is to call out a noise in excitement.","e":"The crowd whooped as the football player ran towards the goal."},{"m":"To whoop is to make a hooting noise like a bird.","e":"She could hear the whooping calls of the birds in the forest."},{"m":"To whoop is to make the gasping noise that is known as whooping cough.","e":"The doctor recognised the whooping sound of his coughing."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A whoop is a shout made by someone who is excited.","e":"You could clearly hear his excited whoops."}]}]},"whoops":{"h":"whoops","l":"whoop","q":"verb"},"whooped":{"h":"whooped","l":"whoop","q":"verb"},"whooping":{"h":"whooping","l":"whoop","q":"verb"},"lever":{"h":"lever","i":"/ˈliː.vɚ/","a":"en-uk-lever.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A lever is a simple tool, a bar resting on a fixed point. If one end of the bar is pushed, the force is used at the other end.","e":"A see-saw in a children's' playground is a simple lever."},{"m":"(countable) A lever is a long handle used to operate a machine.","e":"The signalman pulled on the lever to change the railway signals."},{"m":"Lever is to use something to do something else.","e":"He used his charm as a lever to get past the guards at the gate."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To lever is to move or lift something with lever.","e":"She used a long pole to lever the large rock out of the way."}]}]},"levers":{"h":"levers","l":"lever","q":"noun"},"levered":{"h":"levered","l":"lever","q":"verb"},"levering":{"h":"levering","l":"lever","q":"verb"},"playground":{"h":"playground","i":"/ˈpleɪɡraʊnd/","a":"en-us-playground.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A playground is a place where people go to play.","e":"The playground had swings and slides for children."}]}]},"playgrounds":{"h":"playgrounds","l":"playground","q":"noun"},"leverage":{"h":"leverage","i":"/ˈlɛv(ə)rɪdʒ/","a":"en-us-leverage.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Leverage is the action caused by using a lever.","e":"She was able to use the iron bar to get leverage on the heavy rock."},{"m":"Leverage is the power to be able to use something to get something done.","e":"She was able to use her position on the council as leverage to get a better price from the company."},{"m":"Leverage is the act of using the value of investment shares to borrow money to buy more shares.","e":"Increasing the amount of leverage was seen to be too risky."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) Leverage is to provide leverage.","e":"He was able to leverage the company's money to buy more shares."},{"m":"(transitive) Leverage is to improve something to make it better.","e":"We need to leverage our good reputation to increase our sales."}]}]},"leverages":{"h":"leverages","l":"leverage","q":"noun"},"leveraged":{"h":"leveraged","l":"leverage","q":"verb"},"leveraging":{"h":"leveraging","l":"leverage","q":"verb"},"signalman":{"h":"signalman","i":"/ˈsɪɡnəl.mən/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A signalman is a person who works on the railway and changes the railway signals.","e":"The signalman changed the light from red to green to let the train continue."},{"m":"(countable) A signalman is a sailor who sends signals from the ship.","e":"The signalman waved his semaphore flags to send a message to the admiral's ship."}]}]},"signalmen":{"h":"signalmen","l":"signalman","q":"noun"},"semaphore":{"h":"semaphore","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Semaphore is a system of sending messages using lights, mechanical signals or flags.","e":"Railways use semaphore to send messages to trains."},{"m":"Semaphore is a system of sending messages using two flags to show each alphabet letter.","e":"Sailors use semaphore flags to send messages between ships."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To semaphore is to send a message using a semaphore system.","e":"The sailor semaphored the nearby ship."}]}]},"semaphores":{"h":"semaphores","l":"semaphore","q":"noun"},"semaphored":{"h":"semaphored","l":"semaphore","q":"verb"},"semaphoring":{"h":"semaphoring","l":"semaphore","q":"verb"},"retail":{"h":"retail","i":"/ˈriˌteɪl/","a":"en-us-retail.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Retail is selling things, usually in small amounts.","e":"She owned a retail store, selling clothes in the main street."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To retail is to sell in small amounts.","e":"By buying CD players in bulk, he made a profit retailing them."}]}]},"retails":{"h":"retails","l":"retail","q":"noun"},"retailed":{"h":"retailed","l":"retail","q":"verb"},"retailing":{"h":"retailing","l":"retail","q":"verb"},"orifice":{"h":"orifice","i":"/ˈɒrɪfɪs/","a":"en-us-orifice.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An orifice is an opening into the body.","e":"The mouth is an orifice."}]}]},"orifices":{"h":"orifices","l":"orifice","q":"noun"},"admiral":{"h":"admiral","i":"/ˈæd.mə.rəl/","a":"en-us-admiral.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An admiral is the person in charge of a navy or fleet of ships, like a general in the army.","e":"Horatio Nelson is a famous British admiral."},{"m":"(countable) An admiral is a high rank naval officer who is allowed to fly his own flag.","e":"We could easily recognize the admiral's ship because of his flag."}]}]},"admirals":{"h":"admirals","l":"admiral","q":"noun"},"badminton":{"h":"badminton","i":"/ˈbæd.mɪn.tən/","a":"en-us-badminton.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Badminton is a sport where players hit a shuttlecock over a high net using racquets.","e":"He played six games of badminton."}]}]},"shuttlecock":{"h":"shuttlecock","i":"/ˈʃʌtl̩kɑk/","a":"en-us-shuttlecock.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(badminton) A shuttlecock is an object that is made with a cork and feathers. It is used in badminton and it is also called a birdie.","e":"She hit the shuttlecock high into the air."}]}]},"shuttlecocks":{"h":"shuttlecocks","l":"shuttlecock","q":"noun"},"horrendous":{"h":"horrendous","i":"/həˈrɛndəs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-horrendous.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Horrendous is something that is large and so dreadful or horrible that it makes you tremble with fear.","e":"She heard a horrendous noise as the truck smashed into the wall."}]}]},"tremble":{"h":"tremble","i":"/ˈtrɛmbl̩/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-tremble.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To tremble is to vibrate a little bit.","e":"The building trembled during the earthquake."},{"m":"To tremble is to shake with fear, anxiety or excitement.","e":"She was trembling with fear while waiting her turn to speak at the meeting."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A tremble is the act of slightly shaking.","e":"He felt a tremble in his body as he turned into the dark street."}]}]},"trembles":{"h":"trembles","l":"tremble","q":"verb"},"trembled":{"h":"trembled","i":"/ˈtrɛmbl̩d/","a":"en-us-trembled.ogg","l":"tremble","q":"verb"},"trembling":{"h":"trembling","i":"/ˈtrɛmblɪŋ/","a":"en-us-trembling.ogg","l":"tremble","q":"verb"},"anxiety":{"h":"anxiety","i":"/ˌæŋ(ɡ)ˈzaɪ.ə.ti/","a":"en-us-anxiety.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Anxiety is a fear of what might happen in the future.","e":"The thought of going to the dentist filled him with anxiety."}]}]},"anxieties":{"h":"anxieties","l":"anxiety","q":"noun"},"anxious":{"h":"anxious","i":"/ˈaŋ(k)ʃəs/","a":"en-us-anxious.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"To be anxious, you are or scared about what might happen in the future.","e":"He had an anxious wait at the hospital before seeing the doctor."}]}]},"postulate":{"h":"postulate","i":"/ˈpɒstjʊlət/","a":"en-us-postulate-noun.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To postulate is to suggest or accept that something is true.","e":"Maharishi Kanad postulated that atoms are smallest particles."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A postulate is a thing that is suggested or assumed to be true."}]}]},"symmetrical":{"h":"symmetrical","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Symmetrical means having the property of symmetry.","e":"The building was symmetrical."}]}]},"symmetry":{"h":"symmetry","i":"/ˈsɪmɪtri/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-symmetry.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A balance or harmony of parts."},{"m":"(countable) A division of the body would produce two parts which are mirror images of each other."},{"m":"An arrangement of parts around a central point.","e":"An orange has symmetry: it is a sphere with segments arranged around a common central line."}]}]},"asymmetrical":{"h":"asymmetrical","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Asymmetrical means not being symmetrical.","e":"An asymmetrical painting is one which is not balanced by the frame of the picture."}]}]},"postulates":{"h":"postulates","l":"postulate","q":"verb"},"postulated":{"h":"postulated","l":"postulate","q":"verb"},"postulating":{"h":"postulating","l":"postulate","q":"verb"},"bullshat":{"h":"bullshat","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Bullshat is an alternative past tense of the word bullshit.","e":"I bullshat my essay."}]}]},"recipient":{"h":"recipient","i":"/rəˈsɪp.i.ənt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-recipient.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A recipient is someone who receives, such as one who receives money, goods or awards.","e":"He was a recipient of the special award for bravery."},{"m":"A recipient is person receiving donor organs or tissues.","e":"She was the recipient of a new heart after a long operation."},{"m":"The part of an alembic or other still in which the distilled liquid is collected.","e":"The green colored liquid slowly dripped into the recipient."}]}]},"recipients":{"h":"recipients","l":"recipient","q":"noun"},"receptionist":{"h":"receptionist","i":"/rɪˈsɛpʃənɪst/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-receptionist.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A receptionist is a person who works in an office to answer the telephone and welcome visitors.","e":"The receptionist at the doctor's office greeted me with a friendly smile."}]}]},"receptionists":{"h":"receptionists","l":"receptionist","q":"noun"},"sewage":{"h":"sewage","i":"/ˈsuː.ɪd͡ʒ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-sewage.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Sewage is the waste, like feces, urine and dirty water, from houses and factories.","e":"A complex system of pipes was built to take away the sewage."}]}]},"feces":{"h":"feces","i":"/ˈfiːsiːz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-feces.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Feces are the solid waste from the intestines, also called excrement, shit or poo.","e":"The street was dirty, with dog feces all over the footpath."}]}]},"urine":{"h":"urine","i":"/ˈjʊrɪn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-urine.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Urine is the liquid waste from the bladder, also called piss or wee.","e":"The doctor tested the man's urine to see if he had diabetes."}]}]},"diabetes":{"h":"diabetes","i":"/ˌdaɪəˈbiːtiːz/","a":"en-au-diabetes.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Diabetes is a disease which causes people to become very thirsty and urinate a lot.","e":"Doctors can test for diabetes by checking the amount of glucose in a person's urine."}]}]},"diabetic":{"h":"diabetic","i":"/daɪəˈbɛtɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-diabetic.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A diabetic is a person with the disease called diabetes.","e":"The diabetic had to test his blood sugar levels every day."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Diabetic is something for or about the disease called diabetes.","e":"To control his blood sugar levels, he could only eat special diabetic sweets."}]}]},"diabetics":{"h":"diabetics","l":"diabetic","q":"noun"},"sewer":{"h":"sewer","i":"/ˈs(j)uːə/","a":"en-us-sewer.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sewer is a pipe, or system of pipes, that removes wastes from buildings.","e":"They were not able to use the toilet after the sewer was blocked."},{"m":"(countable) A sewer in medieval times was a person who served food at meals."},{"m":"(countable) A sewer is a person who sews with needle and thread.","e":"She was a sewer of quality clothing."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To sewer is to put in pipes to take away sewage and wastes.","e":"The new house needed to be sewered before the family could move in."}]}]},"sewers":{"h":"sewers","l":"sewer","q":"noun"},"sewered":{"h":"sewered","l":"sewer","q":"verb"},"sewering":{"h":"sewering","l":"sewer","q":"verb"},"sewerage":{"h":"sewerage","i":"/ˈsuː.rɪd͡ʒ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-sewerage.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Sewerage is a system of pipes to take away sewage and other wastes from buildings.","e":"The toilet needed to be joined to the sewerage before it could be used."}]}]},"medieval":{"h":"medieval","i":"/ˌmɛd.i.ˈiː.vəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-medieval.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Medieval means something belongs to the, the time from about 400 AD to 1400 AD.","e":"She liked to collect medieval books, with their beautiful pictures and handwriting."}]}]},"leisure":{"h":"leisure","i":"/ˈlɛʒə(r)/","a":"en-uk-leisure.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Leisure is time that is free from work or other duties, when a person can relax and do what they enjoy.","e":"He looked forward to the holidays when he could read at his leisure."}]}]},"rigour":{"h":"rigour","i":"/rɪɡɚ/","a":"en-us-rigor.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Rigour is strict care and completeness in making sure something is correct.","e":"The army demands a lot of rigour in training new recruits."},{"m":"(usually plural) The rigours of something are its difficult parts or its problems.","e":"She did not enjoy the rigorus of giving birth."}]}]},"rigours":{"h":"rigours","l":"rigour","q":"noun"},"rigorous":{"h":"rigorous","i":"/ˈrɪɡərəs/","a":"en-us-rigorous.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"To be rigorous someone needs to be very strict, exact and not change the rules.","e":"To make herself fit, she kept to a rigorous program of exercise."},{"m":"Something that is rigorous is very difficult and unpleasant.","e":"He found the walk through the snow was quite rigorous."}]}]},"unpleasant":{"h":"unpleasant","i":"/ʌnˈplezənt/","a":"en-us-unpleasant.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something unpleasant is nasty, bad, offensive, the opposite of pleasant.","e":"The coffee tasted unpleasant as if the milk had gone bad."}]}]},"glucose":{"h":"glucose","i":"/ˈɡluːkoʊz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-glucose.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Glucose is a type of monosaccharide (sugar) found in plants and animals, formula C6H12O6.","e":"Glucose is main source of energy for the body."}]}]},"dextrin":{"h":"dextrin","i":"/ˈdɛkstrɪn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-dextrin.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Dextrin is a sticky substance that is made by heating starch.","e":"Dextrin is used to make food thick and to make glue."}]}]},"dextrins":{"h":"dextrins","l":"dextrin","q":"noun"},"starch":{"h":"starch","i":"/stɑrtʃ/","a":"en-us-starch.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Starch is a carbohydrate found in seeds, fruits, roots, and tubers.","e":"Potatoes and rice are a good source of starch."},{"m":"Starch is a white powder made from carbohydrates and added to clothes during washing to make them stiff.","e":"She added starch to the washing to stiffen the shirt collars."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To starch is to add a powder to washing to make the material stiff.","e":"His freshly washed clothes had been starched and were so hard that it was difficult to put them on."}]}]},"starches":{"h":"starches","l":"starch","q":"noun"},"starched":{"h":"starched","l":"starch","q":"verb"},"starching":{"h":"starching","l":"starch","q":"verb"},"carbohydrate":{"h":"carbohydrate","i":"/kɑːbəʊˈhaɪdreɪt/","a":"en-us-carbohydrate.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A carbohydrate is made up of carbon, hydrogen and oxygen. They are made by plants and are the main source of energy for animals.","e":"es are a good source of carbohydrates."}]}]},"carbohydrates":{"h":"carbohydrates","l":"carbohydrate","q":"noun"},"dextrose":{"h":"dextrose","i":"/ˈdɛkstrəʊz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-dextrose.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Dextrose is a type of glucose, a sugar found in honey and fruit.","e":"Dextrose is sometimes called grape sugar."}]}]},"dextroses":{"h":"dextroses","l":"dextrose","q":"noun"},"maltose":{"h":"maltose","i":"/ˈmɔːltəʊz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-maltose.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Maltose is a sugar made when starch is digested.","e":"Maltose is sometimes called malt sugar."}]}]},"maltoses":{"h":"maltoses","l":"maltose","q":"noun"},"confectionery":{"h":"confectionery","i":"/kənˈfɛkʃənəri/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-confectionery.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Confectionery is name for candy, lollies and other sweets.","e":"The children went to the candy store to look at the confectionery."},{"m":"A confectionery is the name for a shop where candy is sold.","e":"She opened a new confectionery to sell sweets."}]}]},"lolly":{"h":"lolly","a":"en-au-lolly.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A lolly is a sweet, a hard type of candy.","e":"He liked to suck on a lolly while working."},{"m":"(UK) (informal) A lolly is a shortened word for a lollipop."}]}]},"lollies":{"h":"lollies","l":"lolly","q":"noun"},"lollipop":{"h":"lollipop","a":"En-us-lollipop.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A lollipop is a piece of hard candy on a stick.","e":"The little boy's face was a sticky mess from eating a lollipop."}]}]},"lollipops":{"h":"lollipops","l":"lollipop","q":"noun"},"confection":{"h":"confection","i":"/kənˈfɛkʃən/","a":"en-us-confection.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A confection is a food which made with a lot of sugar.","e":"His favorite confection was a meringue covered in chocolate."},{"m":"A confection is something made by mixing together a lot of different things.","e":"His story was a confection of lies and half truths."}]}]},"confections":{"h":"confections","l":"confection","q":"noun"},"confectionaries":{"h":"confectionaries","l":"confectionery","q":"noun"},"confectioner":{"h":"confectioner","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A confectioner is a person who makes or sells sweets.","e":"The confectioner spent the morning making lollipops."}]}]},"confectioners":{"h":"confectioners","l":"confectioner","q":"noun"},"mathematician":{"h":"mathematician","i":"/ˈmæθ(.ə)ˌmə.tɪʃ.ən/","a":"en-us-mathematician.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mathematician is a person who studies mathematics.","e":"Sir Isaac Newton is regarded as one of the greatest mathematicians."}]}]},"mathematicians":{"h":"mathematicians","l":"mathematician","q":"noun"},"lablet":{"h":"lablet","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A lablet is a laptop that converts to a touchscreen tablet. More commonly known as a convertible laptop."},{"m":"A lablet in the area of micro- or nanosystems is an autonomously powered programmable electronic particle capable of acting as a microscopic chemical laboratory."}]}]},"spazzes":{"h":"spazzes","l":"spaz","q":"noun"},"fatasses":{"h":"fatasses","l":"fatass","q":"noun"},"analogs":{"h":"analogs","l":"analog","q":"noun"},"dislikes":{"h":"dislikes","l":"dislike","q":"verb"},"disliked":{"h":"disliked","l":"dislike","q":"verb"},"disliking":{"h":"disliking","l":"dislike","q":"verb"},"lablets":{"h":"lablets","l":"lablet","q":"noun"},"apostrophe":{"h":"apostrophe","i":"/əˈpɒs.trə.fi/","a":"en-us-apostrophe.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An apostrophe is a punctuation mark which is used to show that part of a word is missing, to show that something belongs to someone, or added after plurals of numbers, letters and abbreviations.","e":"In the phrase \"John's sentence\", there is an apostrophe after John but before the \"s\" to show that the sentence belongs to John."}]}]},"apostrophes":{"h":"apostrophes","l":"apostrophe","q":"noun"},"timber":{"h":"timber","i":"/ˈtɪmbə/","a":"en-us-timber.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Timber is trees and forests used as a source of wood.","e":"They walked into the tall timber to find a place to camp."},{"m":"Timber is wood used for building.","e":"He went to the timber yard to buy the wood for his house."},{"m":"Timber is a piece of wood used in building.","e":"She carefully chose a timber that had an interesting pattern."},{"m":"Timber is wood used as a frame in building ships.","e":"During the battle he could feel the ship's timbers shiver."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To timber is to use wood as a support or frame.","e":"The miners had to timber the shaft in the gold mine to make it safe."}]}]},"timbers":{"h":"timbers","l":"timber","q":"noun"},"timbered":{"h":"timbered","l":"timber","q":"verb"},"timbering":{"h":"timbering","l":"timber","q":"verb"},"timbre":{"h":"timbre","i":"/ˈtæm.bə/","a":"en-us-timbre.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Timbre is the qualities of a sound that make sounds different.","e":"Even if a flute and saxophone play the same note, they sound different because of the timbre."}]}]},"timbres":{"h":"timbres","l":"timbre","q":"noun"},"spy":{"h":"spy","i":"/spaɪ/","a":"en-us-spy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A spy is a person whose job is to get secret information.","e":"James Bond is a famous spy from the books by Ian Fleming."},{"m":"(countable) A spy is a person who watches other people secretly.","e":"The princess was concerned that a spy with a camera would take photos when she went near the pool."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To spy is to gather information secretly.","e":"He was not a rich businessman, he was really spying for the CIA."},{"m":"To spy is to watch someone secretly.","e":"He spied on the people who entered the Russian embassy."},{"m":"To spy is to see something.","e":"I thought I could spy someone on top of the mountain."}]}]},"spies":{"h":"spies","l":"spy","q":"noun"},"spied":{"h":"spied","l":"spy","q":"verb"},"spying":{"h":"spying","a":"En-us-spying.ogg","l":"spy","q":"verb"},"kimono":{"h":"kimono","i":"/kəˈmoʊnoʊ/","a":"en-us-kimono.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A kimono is a Japanese item of clothing."}]}]},"chequebook":{"h":"chequebook","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A chequebook is a book containing blank cheques given to people with bank accounts.","e":"He took his chequebook to the auction so that he could pay for any items he bought."}]}]},"gown":{"h":"gown","i":"/ɡaʊn/","a":"en-us-gown.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A gown is a long formal dress for women.","e":"She wore a beautiful white gown and carried a bunch of flowers."},{"m":"A gown is a long, loose item of clothing to be worn in bed.","e":"She wore a gown to bed."},{"m":"A gown is a protective item worn by doctors during operations.","e":"The doctor put on his gown before going into the operating theatre."},{"m":"A gown is a ceremonial robe worn by scholars or church men.","e":"At the graduation the students looked impressive in their black gowns."},{"m":"Gown is the members of a university.","e":"The gown defeated the town at the annual golf match."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To gown is to put on or wear a gown.","e":"The nurse assisted the doctor to gown before the operation."}]}]},"robe":{"h":"robe","i":"/rəʊb/","a":"en-us-robe.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A robe is a long loose item of clothing.","e":"The young people wore white robes to the church for their confirmation."},{"m":"(countable) A robe is a long item of clothing used to show rank or importance.","e":"The judge looked splendid in his red robe."},{"m":"(countable) A robe is a dressing gown or bathrobe.","e":"He put on his robe after his bath and watched TV."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To robe is to put on or wear a robe.","e":"The king was robed before his coronation."}]}]},"garb":{"h":"garb","i":"/ɡɑː(r)b/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-garb.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A garb is a style or fashion of clothing."},{"m":"A garb is an outer layer of clothes."},{"m":"A garb is an outer layer or guise, worn to hide or disguise."},{"m":"A garb is clothes worn by a special group or profession."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To garb is to cover, as if you were using a layer of clothes."}]}]},"kilt":{"h":"kilt","i":"/kɪlt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-kilt.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A kilt is a knee length skirt, with pleats, and usually with a tartan pattern and worn by men in the Scottish highlands.","e":"The piper played his bagpipes and wore a traditional highland kilt."},{"m":"A kilt is a similar skirt worn by women.","e":"The school's winter uniform for girls was a kilt and a blazer."}]}]},"whatsoever":{"h":"whatsoever","i":"/ˌwɒtsəʊˈɛvə(r)/","a":"en-us-whatsoever.ogg","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"Whatever.","e":"Most studies find no relationship whatsoever."}]}]},"whosoever":{"h":"whosoever","i":"/ˈhuːsəʊɛvə/","a":"en-us-whosoever.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"Whichever person; whoever.","e":"Whosoever comes back first will be the winner."}]}]},"kimonos":{"h":"kimonos","l":"kimono","q":"noun"},"yukata":{"h":"yukata","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A yutaka is a kimono for wearing in summer.","e":"patterns are common for womens' yukata and geometric patterns for mens' yukata."}]}]},"yukatas":{"h":"yukatas","l":"yukata","q":"noun"},"chequebooks":{"h":"chequebooks","l":"chequebook","q":"noun"},"auction":{"h":"auction","i":"/ˈɔːkʃən/","a":"en-us-auction.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An auction is a sale where the goods are sold to the person who offers the most money.","e":"She wanted to sell her house at auction because she hoped to get a higher price."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To auction is to sell goods to the person who offers the most money.","e":"He auctioned the house on Saturday morning."}]}]},"auctions":{"h":"auctions","l":"auction","q":"noun"},"auctioned":{"h":"auctioned","l":"auction","q":"verb"},"auctioning":{"h":"auctioning","l":"auction","q":"verb"},"auctioneer":{"h":"auctioneer","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An auctioneer is a person who sells items at an auction.","e":"The auctioneer sold the house to the highest bidder."}]}]},"auctioneers":{"h":"auctioneers","l":"auctioneer","q":"noun"},"gowns":{"h":"gowns","i":"/ɡaʊnz/","l":"gown","q":"noun"},"gowned":{"h":"gowned","l":"gown","q":"verb"},"gowning":{"h":"gowning","l":"gown","q":"verb"},"robes":{"h":"robes","l":"robe","q":"noun"},"robed":{"h":"robed","l":"robe","q":"verb"},"robing":{"h":"robing","l":"robe","q":"verb"},"garbs":{"h":"garbs","l":"garb","q":"noun"},"garbed":{"h":"garbed","l":"garb","q":"verb"},"garbing":{"h":"garbing","l":"garb","q":"verb"},"kilts":{"h":"kilts","l":"kilt","q":"noun"},"bagpipe":{"h":"bagpipe","i":"/ˈbæɡˌpaɪp/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bagpipe, is a musical instrument which has an air-filled bag, a double-reed pipe for playing melodies, and between one and four drone pipes.","e":"There are different types of bagpipes including the Scottish great highland pipes, the Irish uilleann pipes and the Northumberland pipes."}]}]},"bagpipes":{"h":"bagpipes","i":"/ˈbæɡ.pɑɪps/","a":"en-us-bagpipes.ogg","l":"bagpipe","q":"noun"},"bagpiper":{"h":"bagpiper","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bagpiper is a person who plays the bagpipes.","e":"We had a bagpiper at our Scottish wedding."}]}]},"bagpipers":{"h":"bagpipers","l":"bagpiper","q":"noun"},"piper":{"h":"piper","i":"/ˈpaɪ.pə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-piper.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A piper is a person who plays the bagpipes.","e":"The piper played on the castle wall to signal the end of the day."},{"m":"A piper is a person who plays the pipes."},{"m":"Piper is a large family of climbing tropical plants.","e":"A pepper vine is part of the genus Piper."}]}]},"pipers":{"h":"pipers","l":"piper","q":"noun"},"tartan":{"h":"tartan","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Tartan is a pattern of colored lines and stripes crossing at right angles.","e":"Clans, or large family groups in Scotland have their own tartans."},{"m":"Tartan is a material having the tartan pattern.","e":"They selected a big roll of tartan to make the kilts."}]}]},"tartans":{"h":"tartans","l":"tartan","q":"noun"},"floral":{"h":"floral","i":"/ˈflɔrəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-floral.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Floral is something to do with flowers or like a flower.","e":"The material had a floral pattern."}]}]},"personality":{"h":"personality","i":"/pɜːsəˈnælətɪ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-personality.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A quality that make a person (or thing) distinct from another.","e":"My teacher complained to me about my personality."},{"m":"(countable) A celebrity.","e":"Usain Bolt has made himself a personality."}]}]},"personalities":{"h":"personalities","l":"personality","q":"noun"},"pity":{"h":"pity","i":"/ˈpɪti/","a":"en-us-pity.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A feeling of sympathy at the distress or suffering of someone or something.","e":"It's a pity her friend died."},{"m":"Something regrettable."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) The action of feeling pity for someone or something.","e":"We pity her not being able to come with the rest of us."}]}]},"pities":{"h":"pities","i":"/ˈpɪtiz/","l":"pity","q":"noun"},"pitied":{"h":"pitied","i":"/ˈpɪtid/","a":"en-us-pitied.ogg","l":"pity","q":"verb"},"pitying":{"h":"pitying","l":"pity","q":"verb"},"keyed":{"h":"keyed","l":"key","q":"verb"},"keying":{"h":"keying","l":"key","q":"verb"},"locksmith":{"h":"locksmith","i":"/ˈlɑksmɪθ/","a":"en-au-locksmith.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A locksmith is a person who makes or repairs locks and keys.","e":"He had to get a locksmith to open his car after he had locked his keys inside it."}]}]},"locksmiths":{"h":"locksmiths","l":"locksmith","q":"noun"},"supervise":{"h":"supervise","i":"/ˈsuːpə(r)vaɪz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-supervise.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To direct or manage; to be in charge","e":"The principal said that our class will need a teacher to supervise us if we go on the field trip."}]}]},"supervises":{"h":"supervises","l":"supervise","q":"verb"},"supervised":{"h":"supervised","l":"supervise","q":"verb"},"supervising":{"h":"supervising","l":"supervise","q":"verb"},"atlases":{"h":"atlases","l":"atlas","q":"noun"},"atlantes":{"h":"atlantes","i":"/ətˈlantiːz/","l":"atlas","q":"noun"},"environmentalist":{"h":"environmentalist","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An environmentalist is a person who works to protect the environment from being damaged.","e":"John Muir was a famous environmentalist who worked to create National Parks in America."}]}]},"environmentalists":{"h":"environmentalists","l":"environmentalist","q":"noun"},"thermostat":{"h":"thermostat","i":"/ˈθɝməstæt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-thermostat.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A thermostat is a device that can tell if the temperature changes, and can then turn other machines on or off.","e":"My hot water system has a thermostat that turns the gas boiler on if the water is cold, and turns it off if the water gets too hot."}]}]},"thermostats":{"h":"thermostats","l":"thermostat","q":"noun"},"intellectual":{"h":"intellectual","i":"/ˌɪntəˈlɛk(t)ʃʊəl/","a":"en-us-intellectual.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An intellectual is an intelligent person, or a person who has learned a lot about a subject.","e":"Smith is an intellectual person in medicine."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A person who is intelligent, or has learned a lot about a subject."},{"m":"A person who is able to think clearly about difficult things."}]}]},"intellectuals":{"h":"intellectuals","l":"intellectual","q":"noun"},"overtake":{"h":"overtake","i":"/ˈəʊvə(r).teɪk/","a":"en-us-overtake.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To overtake is to catch up to and then pass or do better than something.","e":"He had to really increase his speed to overtake her car on the freeway."},{"m":"(transitive) If something overtakes you, you are not ready, you are surprised, and overwhelmed by it.","e":"The government's reforms were overtaken by the mass demonstrations which called for big changes in the laws."}]}]},"anus":{"h":"anus","i":"/ˈeɪ.nəs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-anus.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The anus is the opening in the butt where waste from the intestines leaves the body.","e":"He used paper to clean around his anus before leaving the toilet."}]}]},"overtakes":{"h":"overtakes","l":"overtake","q":"verb"},"overtook":{"h":"overtook","i":"/oʊ.vɚ.tʊk/","a":"en-us-overtook.ogg","l":"overtake","q":"verb"},"overtaken":{"h":"overtaken","i":"/ˈovərteɪkən/","a":"en-us-overtaken.ogg","l":"overtake","q":"verb"},"overtaking":{"h":"overtaking","l":"overtake","q":"verb"},"anuses":{"h":"anuses","l":"anus","q":"noun"},"willow":{"h":"willow","i":"/ˈwɪl.əʊ/","a":"en-us-willow.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Willows are trees and shrubs belonging to the genus Salix.","e":"Salix alba caerulea is a tree called the cricket bat willow."},{"m":"Willow is the wood from a willow tree.","e":"Cricket bats are made from willow."},{"m":"A willow can be a bat made from the wood of a willow tree used in cricket and baseball.","e":"He struck the ball with the willow and sent it to the boundary."},{"m":"A willow is machine with rotating metal spikes use to clean raw materials for making textiles."}]}]},"willows":{"h":"willows","l":"willow","q":"noun"},"incidental":{"h":"incidental","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is incidental, it happened by chance or has occurred by accident."}]}]},"footage":{"h":"footage","i":"/ˈfʊtɪd͡ʒ/","a":"en-us-footage.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (video) A footage is the raw and unedited video that is originally recorded on a video camera.","e":"I have got a rare footage of the towers collapsing in the 9/11 attacks."}]}]},"footages":{"h":"footages","l":"footage","q":"noun"},"uniqueness":{"h":"uniqueness","i":"/juːˈniːkːnəs/","a":"en-us-uniqueness.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The state or quality of being unique or one-of-a-kind."}]}]},"suburban":{"h":"suburban","i":"/səˈbɜː(r)bən/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"To be suburban, something is about or characteristic of a suburb.","e":"He led a quiet, suburban life."}]}]},"suburb":{"h":"suburb","i":"/ˈsʌbɜː(r)b/","a":"en-au-suburb.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A suburb is the area around a city where people live.","e":"Carlton is an inner suburb, close to the city of Melbourne."}]}]},"suburbs":{"h":"suburbs","l":"suburb","q":"noun"},"uniquenesses":{"h":"uniquenesses","l":"uniqueness","q":"noun"},"tolled":{"h":"tolled","l":"toll","q":"verb"},"tolling":{"h":"tolling","l":"toll","q":"verb"},"great-grandchild":{"h":"great-grandchild","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The son or daughter of someone's grandchild."}]}]},"great-grandchildren":{"h":"great-grandchildren","l":"great-grandchild","q":"noun"},"tone":{"h":"tone","i":"/təʊn/","a":"en-us-tone.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A specific pitch.","e":"\"What's your favourite tone?\" asked the teacher of music."},{"m":"The character of a sound, especially the timbre of an instrument or voice.","e":"He needed more practice to get proper control of the tone on his oboe."},{"m":"General character, mood, or trend.","e":"I don't like the tone of your tenant."},{"m":"The pitch of a word that distinguishes a difference in meaning, for example in Chinese."},{"m":"The manner in which speech or writing is expressed."},{"m":"The quality or shade of a colour.","e":"She was surprised at how many tones of sage green there were in the paint shop."},{"m":"The definition and firmness of a muscle or organ."},{"m":"The state of a living body or of any of its organs or parts in which the functions are healthy and performed with due vigor."},{"m":"Normal tension or responsiveness to stimuli."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To give a particular tone to (something)."},{"m":"(transitive) To change the colour of (something).","e":"The landlord asked the painter to tone the border a bit."},{"m":"(transitive) To make (something) firmer.","e":"He found doing more sit ups helped to tone his muscles."}]}]},"tones":{"h":"tones","a":"En-us-tones.ogg","l":"tone","q":"noun"},"toned":{"h":"toned","i":"/təʊnd/","l":"tone","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A toned person is someone who is physically fit."}]}]},"toning":{"h":"toning","l":"tone","q":"verb"},"tome":{"h":"tome","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A tome is a large book.","e":"The lawyer had many legal tomes on his shelves."}]}]},"tomes":{"h":"tomes","l":"tome","q":"noun"},"potter":{"h":"potter","i":"/ˈpɒtə/","a":"en-us-potter.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A potter is someone who creates pots or other pottery.","e":"He went to the potter because he wanted a new vase for his flowers."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you potter, you walk aimlessly or for no reason. (putter) (Often potter around, potter about)","e":"He was bored so he pottered around."},{"m":"If you potter, you do small things. (same as putter, potter around)","e":"I pottered around yesterday, sharpening some pencils and sorting out my collection."}]}]},"potters":{"h":"potters","l":"potter","q":"noun"},"pottered":{"h":"pottered","l":"potter","q":"verb"},"pottering":{"h":"pottering","l":"potter","q":"verb"},"intrigue":{"h":"intrigue","i":"/ˈɪntriːɡ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-intrigue (noun).wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An intrigue is when someone plots (plans) to do something in a secret and complicated way; a conspiracy, secret scheme.","e":"After hearing that the politician had planned an intrigue, the citizens were outraged."},{"m":"(uncountable) Intrigue is the activity of making a secret plan or conspiracy.","e":"There was a lot of intrigue in the secret organization."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If something or someone intrigues you, it interests you.","e":"That article on the creation of the universe intrigued the reader."}]}]},"intrigues":{"h":"intrigues","l":"intrigue","q":"noun"},"intrigued":{"h":"intrigued","l":"intrigue","q":"verb"},"intriguing":{"h":"intriguing","i":"/ɪnˈtriːɡɪŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-intriguing.wav","l":"intrigue","q":"verb"},"pottery":{"h":"pottery","i":"/ˈpɑtəri/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-pottery.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Pottery is items made from clay and then baked to make them hard.","e":"The archaeologist found broken pottery at the site of the ancient village."},{"m":"A pottery is a place where a potter makes things from clay.","e":"He worked hard at the pottery making tall vases."}]}]},"potteries":{"h":"potteries","l":"pottery","q":"noun"},"archaeologist":{"h":"archaeologist","i":"/ˌɑː.kiˈɒl.ə.d͡ʒɪst/","a":"en-us-archaeologist.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An archaeologist is a person who studies people and by looking at the things they have left behind.","e":"Archaeologists dug around the pyramids looking for clues to show how they were built."}]}]},"archaeologists":{"h":"archaeologists","l":"archaeologist","q":"noun"},"archaeology":{"h":"archaeology","i":"/ˌɑː(r).kiˈɒl.ə.dʒi/","a":"en-us-archaeology.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Archaeology is the study of people and by looking at what they have left behind.","e":"To understand the ancient burials, we needed someone who was skilled in archaeology."}]}]},"archaeological":{"h":"archaeological","i":"/ˌɑːkɪəˈlɒdʒɪk(ə)l/","a":"en-us-archaeological.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Archaeological describes things that are about or related to archaeology.","e":"The Valley of the Kings in Egypt is an important archaeological site."}]}]},"willy":{"h":"willy","i":"/ˈwɪli/","a":"en-us-willie.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A willy is a word, often used by or around children, for penis.","e":"Richard said his willy was the biggest in the class."}]}]},"willies":{"h":"willies","l":"willy","q":"noun"},"repayment":{"h":"repayment","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A repayment the act of giving back money, or a part of the money, that you have borrowed.","e":"He had to make three more repayments before he owned the car."}]}]},"repayments":{"h":"repayments","l":"repayment","q":"noun"},"asterisk":{"h":"asterisk","i":"/ˈæstərɪsk/","a":"en-us-asterisk.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An asterisk is the sign * used for several purposes including to mark footnotes and other notes, to indicate multiplication (e.g., 3*3), and (on the Internet) to signify that something should be in bold (e.g., *IMPORTANT*).","e":"s put asterisks before reconstructed words."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you asterisk something, you mark it with an [[#Noun|asterisk]] (*).","e":"I asterisked that sentence because I wanted to leave a footnote at the bottom."}]}]},"asterisks":{"h":"asterisks","l":"asterisk","q":"noun"},"asterisked":{"h":"asterisked","l":"asterisk","q":"verb"},"asterisking":{"h":"asterisking","l":"asterisk","q":"verb"},"spam":{"h":"spam","i":"/spæm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-spam.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) (internet) Spam refers to random messages on the Internet. If you receive many messages that advertise things or were sent without you asking for them, you are getting spam.","e":"There are many online computer programs that send spam to users."},{"m":"(countable) (internet) A spam is a single random message. A single occurrence of spam.","e":"He received 65 spams to his e-mail account yesterday."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) (internet) If you spam someone, you send many random electronic messages ([[#Noun|spam]]) to that person.","e":"I hate it when people spam my forum."},{"m":"(intransitive) (internet) If you spam, you send spam.","e":"I don't like the guy who spams people every day."}]}]},"spams":{"h":"spams","l":"spam","q":"noun"},"spamming":{"h":"spamming","l":"spam","q":"verb"},"spammed":{"h":"spammed","l":"spam","q":"verb"},"cab":{"h":"cab","i":"/kæb/","a":"en-us-cab.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cab is a car that you can hire (pay for) for single trips. (Often taxi cab)"}]}]},"cabs":{"h":"cabs","l":"cab","q":"noun"},"suspicious":{"h":"suspicious","i":"/səˈspɪʃəs/","a":"en-us-suspicious.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone or something is suspicious, you do not trust that person, you suspect that he is doing something shady, or that something odd is happening.","e":"The man who is inspecting that window seems suspicious."},{"m":"If you are suspicious, you don't trust people. You suspect something or are distrustful.","e":"Don't be suspicious of that man; I don't think he's doing anything shady."}]}]},"dishonesty":{"h":"dishonesty","i":"/dɪsˈɒnɪ.stɪ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-dishonesty.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Dishonesty is the quality of not being honest. If you have dishonesty, you do not tell the truth. You are not honest."},{"m":"(countable) A dishonesty is an act which is not honest."}]}]},"dishonesties":{"h":"dishonesties","l":"dishonesty","q":"noun"},"template":{"h":"template","i":"/ˈtɛmp.lət/","a":"en-us-template.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A template is a model or base which you can use as a starting point to make other objects.","e":"I used the template with holes for letters to write that message neatly."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you template something, you make it or set it up using a template."},{"m":"(transitive) If you template something, you make a guide or pattern for creating it.","e":"He templated a circle by writing rules for making circles and providing an example circle to copy."}]}]},"templates":{"h":"templates","l":"template","q":"noun"},"templated":{"h":"templated","l":"template","q":"verb"},"templating":{"h":"templating","l":"template","q":"verb"},"caption":{"h":"caption","i":"/ˈkæp.ʃn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-caption.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A caption is a title or description of an image or illustration.","e":"Look at the caption under the illustration to learn more."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you caption an image or a text, you add a caption (description or title) to it.","e":"Only once the drawing is done will the letterer caption it."}]}]},"captions":{"h":"captions","l":"caption","q":"noun"},"captioned":{"h":"captioned","l":"caption","q":"verb"},"captioning":{"h":"captioning","l":"caption","q":"verb"},"spite":{"h":"spite","i":"/spaɪt/","a":"en-us-spite.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Ill will or hatred toward another, accompanied with the disposition to annoy, harass, irritate, or thwart; a desire to harass, injure or vex; petty malice; grudge; rancor.","e":"They were so filled with spite for their coach that they lost most of their matches."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To treat maliciously; to try to injure or thwart.","e":"He soon married again, to spite his ex-wife."},{"m":"(transitive) To fill with spite; to offend; to harass.","e":"After calling a foul on one of the players, the referee was spited by him."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"Notwithstanding; despite."}]}]},"spites":{"h":"spites","l":"spite","q":"noun"},"spited":{"h":"spited","l":"spite","q":"verb"},"spiting":{"h":"spiting","l":"spite","q":"verb"},"prisoner":{"h":"prisoner","i":"/ˈprɪzən/","a":"en-us-prisoner.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A prisoner is a person imprisoned, while on trial or serving a sentence.","e":"The prisoners were let out of their cells each afternoon so they could exercise."},{"m":"(countable) Any person held against his or her will is a prisoner.","e":"He kept his mother as a prisoner in her bedroom until she agreed to change her will."}]}]},"prisoners":{"h":"prisoners","i":"/ˈprɪzənɚz/","a":"en-us-prisoners.ogg","l":"prisoner","q":"noun"},"scientific":{"h":"scientific","i":"/ˈsaɪənˌtɪfɪk/","a":"en-ca-scientific.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Of, or having to do with science."},{"m":"Having the quality of being derived from, or similar to, the scientific method."}]}]},"thorough":{"h":"thorough","i":"/ˈθʌ.rə/","a":"en-uk-thorough.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"not to miss or omit any detail.","e":"The thorough investigation by the police led to the arrest of the criminals."},{"m":"complete; absolute","e":"It is a thorough pleasure to see the building finished."}]}]},"plonk":{"h":"plonk","i":"/plɒŋk/","a":"en-au-plonk.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Plonk is a cheap wine.","e":"He had a headache after a night on the plonk."},{"m":"A plonk is the noise something makes if dropped, especially into liquid.","e":"She heard the plonk of the coins as she dropped them into the wishing well."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To plonk is to drop something heavily, or sit down heavily.","e":"He was so tired he just plonked on the sofa when he got home."}]}]},"plonks":{"h":"plonks","l":"plonk","q":"noun"},"plonked":{"h":"plonked","l":"plonk","q":"verb"},"plonking":{"h":"plonking","l":"plonk","q":"verb"},"therapy":{"h":"therapy","i":"/ˈθɛr.ə.pi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-therapy.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Therapy is the treatment of impairment, injury, disease, or disorder.","e":"My grandfather's therapy will start at the hospital at noon tomorrow."},{"m":"power or quality."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To treat with a therapy."},{"m":"(intransitive) To undergo a therapy."}]}]},"therapies":{"h":"therapies","l":"therapy","q":"noun"},"therapied":{"h":"therapied","l":"therapy","q":"verb"},"therapying":{"h":"therapying","l":"therapy","q":"verb"},"terrify":{"h":"terrify","i":"/ˈtɛrɪfaɪ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-terrify.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you terrify someone, you frighten the person greatly; to fill with terror.","e":"The dogs terrify the cats."}]}]},"terrifies":{"h":"terrifies","l":"terrify","q":"verb"},"terrified":{"h":"terrified","a":"En-us-terrified.ogg","l":"terrify","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Being terrified means being very scared."}]}]},"terrifying":{"h":"terrifying","i":"/ˈtɛrɪfaɪ.ɪŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-terrifying.wav","l":"terrify","q":"verb"},"terrific":{"h":"terrific","i":"/təˈrɪfɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-terrific.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"(informal) Frighteningly good.","e":"She's a terrific tennis player."},{"m":"(informal) or awesome.","e":"The aircraft landed at a terrific speed."},{"m":"; causing terror","e":"The lightning was followed by a terrific clap of thunder."},{"m":"(informal) great or intense.","e":"The racing cars drive at terrific speeds."}]}]},"heavily":{"h":"heavily","i":"/ˈhɛvɪli/","a":"en-us-heavily.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Heavily is a quality of heavy, a great weight, load, effort, or to a large amount.","e":"He dragged himself heavily out of the water and onto the boat."}]}]},"tragedy":{"h":"tragedy","i":"/ˈtrædʒɪdi/","a":"en-us-tragedy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A tragedy is a disaster that usually involves someone getting injured or dying and can affect the lives of many others.","e":"The 9/11 attacks was a tragedy in the history of United States."},{"m":"(countable) A tragedy is play or written work in which the main character is destroyed by his own weakness or things that he can not deal with.","e":"In Shakepeare's tragedy Macbeth, Macbeth is destroyed by his own ambition and greed."}]}]},"tragedies":{"h":"tragedies","l":"tragedy","q":"noun"},"salvation":{"h":"salvation","i":"/sælˈveɪʃən/","a":"en-us-salvation.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) (religion) Salvation is the state of being saved from hell or a punishment of sin."},{"m":"(uncountable) Someone's or something's salvation is the act of saving them from harm or from an unpleasant situation."}]}]},"sophisticated":{"h":"sophisticated","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is sophisticated, it is very complicated and difficult to understand for someone who is not knowledgeable in that area.","e":"This key is very sophisticated, is it a key to a secret passage?"},{"m":"When something is sophisticated it is very high class, very refined, cultured, the very best quality.","e":"She was a very sophisticated young woman, who always looked stunning, in beautifully designed dresses."}]}]},"socialist":{"h":"socialist","i":"/ˈsəʊʃəlɪst/","a":"en-gb-socialist.oga","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A socialist is someone who practices socialism, a type of government that makes the goods produced in a country owned by the people.","e":"Russia used to be a socialist country during the period when the country was called the Union of Soviet Socialist Republics."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"The level of socialism that a person practices."}]}]},"socialists":{"h":"socialists","l":"socialist","q":"noun"},"tragic":{"h":"tragic","i":"/'træd͡ʒɪk/","a":"en-au-tragic.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When an event is tragic, it is causing a lot of pain and suffering for those involved in that event. We would call such event a tragedy as well.","e":"s are people who want to make tragic events happen and make the innocent people suffer so as to tell the government something."}]}]},"nowt":{"h":"nowt","i":"/naʊt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-nowt.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(Northern England) Nowt means nothing, something that is empty and does not contain anything.","e":"There is nowt in this box."}]}]},"stronghold":{"h":"stronghold","i":"/ˈstrɔŋhoʊld/","a":"en-us-stronghold.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A stronghold is a fortress."},{"m":"(countable) A stronghold is a place of refuge, survival or domination by a particular group or idea.","e":"The soldiers attacked the enemy stronghold on the hill."}]}]},"socialism":{"h":"socialism","i":"/ˈsoʊʃəlɪzəm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-socialism.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Socialism is any ideology that wants everyone to publicly own all things that are used to make other things, like and farms. In this system, the economy is run to benefit all the people and not simply to make profit.","e":"Karl Marx said socialism was the first step in moving from capitalism to communism."}]}]},"socialisms":{"h":"socialisms","l":"socialism","q":"noun"},"argentina":{"h":"Argentina","i":"/ˌɑː.dʒənˈtiː.nə/","a":"en-us-Argentina.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Argentina is a country in South America.","e":"The capital city of Argentina is Buenos Aires."}]}]},"argentinian":{"h":"Argentinian","i":"/ɑr.ˌdʒɨn.ˈtɪ.ni.ən/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An Argentinian is a citizen of Argentina.","e":"The musical \"Evita\" was written about the life of a famous Argentinian, Eva Perón."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is Argentinian, it about or comes from Argentina.","e":"The tango is a famous Argentinian dance."}]}]},"argentinians":{"h":"Argentinians","l":"argentinian","q":"noun"},"delete":{"h":"delete","i":"/dɪˈliːt/","a":"en-us-delete.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A key that may be pressed to [[#Verb|delete]] something (including text or files) from a computer.","e":"I lost the files when I accidentally hit delete."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you delete something, you remove or get rid of, or erase it, especially written or printed material, or data on a computer.","e":"I will delete the first paragraph of my essay from the file."},{"m":"(transitive) If you delete something, you conceal hide or conceal it."}]}]},"deletes":{"h":"deletes","l":"delete","q":"verb"},"deleted":{"h":"deleted","l":"delete","q":"verb"},"deleting":{"h":"deleting","l":"delete","q":"verb"},"argentine":{"h":"Argentine","i":"/ˈɑː.dʒən.taɪn/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Argentina is sometimes called \"the Argentine\"."},{"m":"(countable) An Argentine is a person from Argentina, also called an Argentinian."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Argentine is something from, or is like something from Argentina.","e":"She loved the excitement in dancing an Argentine tango."}]}]},"argentines":{"h":"Argentines","l":"argentine","q":"noun"},"mosaic":{"h":"mosaic","i":"/məʊˈzeɪk/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A mosaic is a picture or design made with small coloured pieces.","e":"The Romans used mosaics to decorate the floors of their houses."},{"m":"A mosaic can be something that is like a mosaic as it is made up of many pieces.","e":"This mosaic is made of images taken by the Mariner 10 spacecraft."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To mosaic you would make a picture or design using many small pieces.","e":"He was tired after mosaicking around the edge of the pool to make it look Roman."}]}]},"mosaics":{"h":"mosaics","l":"mosaic","q":"noun"},"mosaicked":{"h":"mosaicked","l":"mosaic","q":"verb"},"mosaicking":{"h":"mosaicking","l":"mosaic","q":"verb"},"blunt":{"h":"blunt","i":"/blʌnt/","a":"en-us-blunt.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is blunt, it has a thick end and is not sharp."},{"m":"(speech) Very direct in one's words, usually in a negative manner and in a rude way."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A blunt is a type of cigarette."}]}]},"blunts":{"h":"blunts","l":"blunt","q":"noun"},"cannabis":{"h":"cannabis","i":"/ˈkænəbɪs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-cannabis.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Cannabis is a type of plant from Central Asia."},{"m":"A type of drug taken from the cannabis plant parts."}]}]},"hash":{"h":"hash","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Hash is a kind of chopped meat and vegetable that are mixed together."},{"m":"A symbol (\"#\"), also known as the number sign."},{"m":"A type of drug."}]}]},"barley":{"h":"barley","i":"/ˈbɑː(r)li/","a":"en-us-barley.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Barley is a kind of grain."}]}]},"caveman":{"h":"caveman","i":"/ˈkeɪvˌmæn/","a":"en-us-caveman.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A caveman is someone who lives in caves."}]}]},"hound":{"h":"hound","i":"/haʊnd/","a":"en-us-hound.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hound is a breed of dog that has a good sense of smell for hunting other animals."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you hound someone, you harass or pester them persistently."}]}]},"hounds":{"h":"hounds","i":"/haʊndz/","a":"en-us-hounds.ogg","l":"hound","q":"noun"},"pathetic":{"h":"pathetic","i":"/pəˈθɛtɪk/","a":"en-us-pathetic.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Arousing pity, sympathy, or compassion.","e":"The student's pathetic pleas for an extension stirred the teacher's heart."}]}]},"tractor":{"h":"tractor","i":"/ˈtræktə/","a":"en-us-tractor.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A vehicle used on farms for pulling equipment, preparing the fields, and so on.","e":"The mechanic just fixed the old tractor so the that Mr. Brown, the farmer can plough his fields."},{"m":"(countable) A truck (or lorry) for pulling a semi-trailer or trailer."},{"m":"(countable) Any piece of machinery or thing that pulls something."},{"m":"(countable) An airplane where the propeller is located in front of the fuselage."}]}]},"tractors":{"h":"tractors","l":"tractor","q":"noun"},"usage":{"h":"usage","i":"/ˈjuːsid͡ʒ/","a":"En-us-usage.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The way or the amount of using; use.","e":"I learnt the usage of some verbs while studying the language."},{"m":"(countable) A habit or accepted practice."}]}]},"usages":{"h":"usages","l":"usage","q":"noun"},"tummy":{"h":"tummy","i":"/ˈtʌm.i/","a":"en-au-tummy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (childish language) stomach","e":"Tommy told his mother that his tummy was full."},{"m":"(countable) A belly that is sticking out."}]}]},"tummies":{"h":"tummies","l":"tummy","q":"noun"},"noon":{"h":"noon","i":"/nuːn/","a":"en-us-noon.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"12:00 pm; the middle of the daylight; the middle of the calendar day."}]}]},"noons":{"h":"noons","l":"noon","q":"noun"},"audition":{"h":"audition","i":"/ɔːˈdɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-audition.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An audition is a performance by an someone hoping to become a performer in order to show suitability or talent.","e":"The music club had it's auditions on Tuesday."},{"m":"(uncountable) Audition is the sense of hearing.","e":"His audition was poor."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To audition is to evaluate one or more performers through an [[#Noun|audition]].","e":"We auditioned many singers for the part in our new show."},{"m":"(intransitive) To audition is to take part in an [[#Noun|audition]].","e":"Many singers auditioned for the part in our new show."}]}]},"auditions":{"h":"auditions","l":"audition","q":"noun"},"auditioned":{"h":"auditioned","l":"audition","q":"verb"},"auditioning":{"h":"auditioning","l":"audition","q":"verb"},"cavemen":{"h":"cavemen","l":"caveman","q":"noun"},"posthumous":{"h":"posthumous","i":"/ˈpɒs.tʃə.məs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-posthumous.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"To be posthumous, a person was born after the death of their father.","e":"Posthumous orphans never knew their fathers."},{"m":"Posthumous is something that happens to a person after their death.","e":"The posthumous Medal of Honor was given to the family of the soldier who died in battle."}]}]},"leaderships":{"h":"leaderships","l":"leadership","q":"noun"},"leadership":{"h":"leadership","i":"/ˈlidɚʃɪp/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-leadership.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Leadership is the capacity of someone to lead.","e":"I doubt that even his leadership can help us."},{"m":"(countable) Leadership means a group of leaders.","e":"The leadership of the football club has decided to have them suspended for rough play."},{"m":"Leadership is the office or status of a leader.","e":"She really wanted the leadership of the gardening club."}]}]},"cautious":{"h":"cautious","i":"/ˈkɔːʃəs/","a":"en-us-cautious.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Someone who is cautious is careful, uses or exercises caution, and is tentative.","e":"He took a few cautious steps out the door when he heard the sirens."}]}]},"performer":{"h":"performer","i":"/pɚˈfɔrmɚ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-performer.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A performer is someone who entertains people with music, dance or acting.","e":"Freddie Mercury, the lead singer of Queen, was a great performer."}]}]},"performers":{"h":"performers","l":"performer","q":"noun"},"oftentimes":{"h":"oftentimes","a":"En-us-oftentimes.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"To do something oftentimes means you do it many times.","e":"Oftentimes we met each other on the way home from school."}]}]},"prominent":{"h":"prominent","i":"/ˈprɑmɪnənt/","a":"en-us-prominent.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is prominent sticks out and is easily seen.","e":"The most prominent feature of the garden was the large fountain in the center of the pond."},{"m":"A person who is prominent is one who is important and famous.","e":"He was described as being one of Canada's prominent writers."}]}]},"caution":{"h":"caution","i":"/ˈkɔːʃ(ə)n/","a":"en-us-caution.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Caution is being careful and planning ways to avoid danger or being hurt.","e":"He used caution as he climbed the old wooden steps."},{"m":"A caution is a warning about what might happen in the future.","e":"The doctor gave me a caution about eating too much."},{"m":"A caution can be a legal warning and that a repeat of the action could end up as an arrest.","e":"The police gave the boy a caution after he was caught stealing from the shop."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To caution is to give a warning or advice.","e":"His mother cautioned him about staying out too late at night."}]}]},"cautions":{"h":"cautions","l":"caution","q":"noun"},"cautioned":{"h":"cautioned","l":"caution","q":"verb"},"cautioning":{"h":"cautioning","l":"caution","q":"verb"},"coincidence":{"h":"coincidence","i":"/kəʊˈɪnsɪdəns/","a":"en-us-coincidence.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A coincidence is when two things are in the same place or space, they coincide.","e":"The scientist studied the beam of electrons and timed examples of coincidence."},{"m":"A coincidence is when two things happen by chance, but it seems like it was really planned.","e":"It is a strange coincidence that William Shakespeare was born and died on 23 April."}]}]},"palace":{"h":"palace","i":"/ˈpælɪs/","a":"en-us-palace.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A palace is the home of a king or queen.","e":"Elizabeth II of England lives in a palace in London, called Buckingham Palace."},{"m":"(countable) A palace is a big, very grand house, often the home of someone important like a president or bishop.","e":"During the revolution, soldiers guarded the gates of the president's palace."}]}]},"palaces":{"h":"palaces","a":"En-us-palaces.ogg","l":"palace","q":"noun"},"weightlessness":{"h":"weightlessness","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Weightlessness is the feeling of having very little or no weight.","e":"Astronauts train for space flights in planes that make steep dives to create a sense of weightlessness."}]}]},"reusable":{"h":"reusable","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is reusable can be used more than once.","e":"I have to remember to take my own reusable bags as the shops no longer put things into plastic bags."}]}]},"specialist":{"h":"specialist","i":"/ˈspɛʃəlɪst/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-specialist.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A specialist is a person who is highly skilled in one type of activity or study.","e":"His army training had made him a bomb disposal specialist."},{"m":"(countable) A specialist is a doctor who is skilled in treating one part of the body.","e":"It hurt so much when she swallowed food that she was sent to a throat specialist."}]}]},"applicant":{"h":"applicant","i":"/ˈæp.lə.kɪnt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-applicant.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An applicant is a person who makes an application for something, often a job.","e":"The job applicants had to have an interview with the head of the company."}]}]},"terrorist":{"h":"terrorist","i":"/ˈtɛrərɪst/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-terrorist.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A terrorist is a person who uses terror and violence to get political change.","e":"The car bomb at the busy market was the work of a terrorist."}]}]},"specialists":{"h":"specialists","l":"specialist","q":"noun"},"applicants":{"h":"applicants","l":"applicant","q":"noun"},"terrorists":{"h":"terrorists","l":"terrorist","q":"noun"},"mudra":{"h":"mudra","a":"En-us-mudra.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Mudra are hand and body positions used in classical Indian dancing.","e":"She moved her hands into a calming mudra."}]}]},"mudras":{"h":"mudras","l":"mudra","q":"noun"},"dissent":{"h":"dissent","i":"/dɪˈsɛnt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-dissent.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Dissent is a difference of opinion.","e":"In his dissent he pointed out what was wrong with the decision."},{"m":"Dissent can be a public protest to show disagreement with government.","e":"The people marched in the street, showing their dissent to the changes to the law."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To dissent is to disagree or have a different opinion.","e":"The judge strongly dissented the decision of the Supreme Court."},{"m":"To dissent can be to take action to show disagreement."}]}]},"dissents":{"h":"dissents","l":"dissent","q":"noun"},"dissented":{"h":"dissented","l":"dissent","q":"verb"},"dissenting":{"h":"dissenting","l":"dissent","q":"verb"},"telecom":{"h":"telecom","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Telecom is short for telecommunications.","e":"He bought shares in cable, internet and telecom companies."}]}]},"telecoms":{"h":"telecoms","l":"telecom","q":"noun"},"telecommunication":{"h":"telecommunication","i":"/ˌtɛlɪkəmjuːnɪˈkeɪʃ(ə)n/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-telecommunication.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Telecommunication is the science of sending messages over a distance using radio, television, telegraph, computers, cable and telephone.","e":"Telecommunication has made it possible to speak directly to people in other countries."},{"m":"A telecommunication is a message received by using radio, television, telegraph, computers, cable and telephone.","e":"The CIA was able to read the company's telecommunications using a spy satellite."}]}]},"telecommunications":{"h":"telecommunications","l":"telecommunication","q":"noun"},"ephemeral":{"h":"ephemeral","a":"En-us-ephemeral.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is ephemeral is only temporary, it does not last long.","e":"\"Here today and gone tomorrow\" is a phrase which describes an ephemeral situation."}]}]},"lignotuber":{"h":"lignotuber","i":"/ˈlɪgnəʊˌtjuːbə(r)/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A lignotuber is a large root buried in the ground that can produce one or more tree trunks.","e":"Many Australian eucalypt trees have lignotubers which let the tree regrow after a bushfire."}]}]},"rooted":{"h":"rooted","i":"/ˈruːtɪd/","a":"en-us-rooted.ogg","l":"root","q":"verb"},"rooting":{"h":"rooting","l":"root","q":"verb"},"moor":{"h":"moor","i":"/moː/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-moor.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To moor a ship or boat is to tie it to a dock, jetty, or hold it in place with an anchor.","e":"The big ship was moored at the long jetty."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (usually plural) A moor is open ground, often with peat soils, swampy, covered in grass or low shrubs.","e":"The search for the missing boy led them right across the moors."}]}]},"moors":{"h":"moors","a":"En-us-moors.ogg","l":"moor","q":"verb"},"moored":{"h":"moored","l":"moor","q":"verb"},"mooring":{"h":"mooring","l":"moor","q":"verb"},"santa":{"h":"Santa","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Santa is short for Santa Claus, the person who brings children presents at Christmas.","e":"The children were excited at Christmas because they hoped Santa would leave them presents."}]}]},"editable":{"h":"editable","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is editable you can change or edit it.","e":"This page is editable, like all Wiktionary pages."}]}]},"swede":{"h":"swede","i":"/swiːd/","a":"en-au-swede.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A swede is a yellow root vegetable, like a turnip.","e":"He really enjoyed a dinner of fish with boiled swedes and peas."}]}]},"swedes":{"h":"Swedes","l":"swede","q":"noun"},"santas":{"h":"Santas","l":"santa","q":"noun"},"lignotubers":{"h":"lignotubers","l":"lignotuber","q":"noun"},"mistily":{"h":"mistily","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Mistily refers to being full of or covered with something; in a misty manner."}]}]},"downtown":{"h":"downtown","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"In or in the direction of the center of a city or town.","e":"The bus is headed downtown."},{"m":"(basketball) Outside the three-point line, or generally far from the basket.","e":"He took a shot from way downtown!"}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Either the lower, or the business center, of a city or town.","e":"The downtown was badly damaged in the war."}]}]},"banners":{"h":"banners","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The plural form of banner; more than one banner."}]}]},"decimals":{"h":"decimals","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The plural form of decimal; more than one decimal."}]}]},"rockhole":{"h":"rockhole","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A hole in an outcrop of solid bedrock that holds surface water."},{"m":"Any depression or opening in an area of bedrock sticking out of the ground. Often found in granite outcrops."}]}]},"rockholes":{"h":"rockholes","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The plural form of rockhole; more than one rockhole."}]}]},"bedrock":{"h":"bedrock","i":"/ˈbɛdrɒk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-bedrock.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The solid rock that sits below the ground surface (and sometimes sticks out of the ground)."}]}]},"downtowns":{"h":"downtowns","l":"downtown","q":"noun"},"banquets":{"h":"banquets","l":"banquet","q":"noun"},"watts":{"h":"watts","l":"watt","q":"noun"},"aerosols":{"h":"aerosols","l":"aerosol","q":"noun"},"banisters":{"h":"banisters","l":"banister","q":"noun"},"adverts":{"h":"adverts","l":"advert","q":"noun"},"wasps":{"h":"wasps","l":"wasp","q":"noun"},"washbasins":{"h":"washbasins","l":"washbasin","q":"noun"},"wardens":{"h":"wardens","l":"warden","q":"noun"},"passages":{"h":"passages","a":"En-us-passages.ogg","l":"passage","q":"noun"},"fabrics":{"h":"fabrics","l":"fabric","q":"noun"},"fables":{"h":"fables","l":"fable","q":"noun"},"elves":{"h":"elves","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The plural form of elf; more than one elf."}]}]},"easels":{"h":"easels","l":"easel","q":"noun"},"dalmatians":{"h":"dalmatians","l":"dalmatian","q":"noun"},"daisies":{"h":"daisies","l":"daisy","q":"noun"},"canes":{"h":"canes","l":"cane","q":"noun"},"canaries":{"h":"canaries","l":"canary","q":"noun"},"rafts":{"h":"rafts","l":"raft","q":"noun"},"pastries":{"h":"pastries","l":"pastry","q":"noun"},"caned":{"h":"caned","l":"cane","q":"verb"},"caning":{"h":"caning","l":"cane","q":"verb"},"trope":{"h":"trope","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Something which is common in popular culture or in a type of literature, such as ‘once upon a time’ is the first lline of a story"},{"m":"A figure of speech in which words or phrases are used with a special meaning, like a metaphor"},{"m":"A short section at the end of the melody in some early music."},{"m":"A phrase or verse added to the mass when sung by a choir."}]}]},"tropes":{"h":"tropes","l":"trope","q":"noun"},"accessory":{"h":"accessory","i":"/əkˈsɛsəri/","a":"en-us-accessory.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An accessory is an extra item, not needed, but which adds to the whole.","e":"She bought a number of accessories including a bag, hat, and gloves, to match her new dress."},{"m":"(countable) An accessory is a person who helps someone to break the law.","e":"Because she helped him hide the body after the murder, she was charged with being an accessory to the crime."}]}]},"accessories":{"h":"accessories","l":"accessory","q":"noun"},"arbitration":{"h":"arbitration","i":"/ˌɑː.bɪˈtreɪ.ʃən/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Arbitration is a way of settling a dispute. An independent person listens to arguments from all participants in the dispute, and then makes a decision.","e":"The two neighbors had to go to arbitration to decide who had to pay for the new fence."}]}]},"arbitrations":{"h":"arbitrations","l":"arbitration","q":"noun"},"coalition":{"h":"coalition","i":"/koʊəˈlɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-coalition.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A temporary group that is formed for a particular reason.","e":"The two governments formed a coalition to help their workers."}]}]},"coalitions":{"h":"coalitions","l":"coalition","q":"noun"},"intimidate":{"h":"intimidate","i":"/ɪnˈtɪmɪdeɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-intimidate.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To make fearful; to inspire or affect with fear; to stop or block others by threats","e":"He's trying to intimidate you. If you ignore him, hopefully he'll stop."}]}]},"steamroller":{"h":"steamroller","i":"/ˈstimˌroʊlɚ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Flame, not lame-steamroller.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A steamroller is a steam-powered heavy road-making machine.","e":"A steamroller was used to make the road smooth and hard."},{"m":"(countable) A modern steamroller is a petrol or diesel-powered heavy road making machine."},{"m":"(uncountable) A figure of speech for anything that rolls over someone or something else."}]}]},"devalue":{"h":"devalue","i":"/diːˈvæljuː/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-devalue.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To lower or remove the value of something.","e":"The bully tried to devalue his critics."},{"m":"(money) To lose value.","e":"The government wanted to devalue the Australian dollar in relation to the euro."}]}]},"arm-twisting":{"h":"arm-twisting","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The use of personal pressure to persuade"},{"m":"The use of political pressure to gain support"}]}]},"premise":{"h":"premise","i":"/ˈprɛ.mɪs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-premise.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A premise is a set of ideas from which you can put forward an answer or reach conclusion.","e":"A basic premise of Christianity is to treat other people like you want to be treated."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you premise, you make an argument based on findings."}]}]},"premises":{"h":"premises","i":"/ˈprɛmɪsɪz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-premises.wav","l":"premise","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Premises is the land, and all the structures built on it.","e":"This organization will be moving its headquarters to a new premises."}]}]},"intimidates":{"h":"intimidates","l":"intimidate","q":"verb"},"intimidated":{"h":"intimidated","l":"intimidate","q":"verb"},"intimidating":{"h":"intimidating","l":"intimidate","q":"verb"},"steamrollers":{"h":"steamrollers","l":"steamroller","q":"noun"},"devalues":{"h":"devalues","l":"devalue","q":"verb"},"devalued":{"h":"devalued","l":"devalue","q":"verb"},"devaluing":{"h":"devaluing","l":"devalue","q":"verb"},"blunter":{"h":"blunter","l":"blunt","q":"adjective"},"bluntest":{"h":"bluntest","l":"blunt","q":"adjective"},"hashes":{"h":"hashes","l":"hash","q":"noun"},"sheer":{"h":"sheer","i":"/ˈʃɪə/","a":"en-us-sheer.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To sheer is to turn sharply or change direction quickly.","e":"The lion hoped that one of the deer would sheer off from the herd so he could catch it."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Sheer is total, complete, without anything to hold it back.","e":"When people heard the air raid siren they ran around in sheer panic."},{"m":"Something that is sheer is very steep, almost vertical.","e":"They came to the edge of the cliff, with a sheer drop into the valley below."},{"m":"Sheer material is so thin you can almost see through it.","e":"She wore her high heel shoes and her sheer silk stockings."}]}]},"sheers":{"h":"sheers","l":"sheer","q":"verb"},"sheered":{"h":"sheered","l":"sheer","q":"verb"},"sheering":{"h":"sheering","l":"sheer","q":"verb"},"scrape":{"h":"scrape","i":"/skreɪp/","a":"en-us-scrape.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To scrape is to drag something with force across a surface.","e":"She was worried the heavy table would scrape the polished floor as it was being moved."},{"m":"To scrape is to make something smooth by rubbing.","e":"He could scrape off the rough edges to make the stone smooth."},{"m":"To scrape is to save or collect things with difficulty.","e":"After I lost my job, I had to really scrape to have enough money for the rent."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A scrape is the noise made by forced rubbing.","e":"He could hear the scrape of the table being dragged across the floor."},{"m":"A scrape is a wound made by rubbing.","e":"She had a nasty scrape on her knee after falling on the path."},{"m":"A scrape is a fight.","e":"The two boys got into a bit of a scrape during the football match."}]}]},"scrapes":{"h":"scrapes","l":"scrape","q":"verb"},"scraped":{"h":"scraped","l":"scrape","q":"verb"},"scraping":{"h":"scraping","l":"scrape","q":"verb"},"puppet":{"h":"puppet","a":"En-us-puppet.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A puppet is a doll or animal figure that is moved by strings.","e":"Another name for a string puppet is a marionette."},{"m":"A puppet is a doll or animal figure that is moved by a hand place inside it.","e":"Mr. Punch is a famous glove puppet from the \"Punch and Judy\" puppet show."},{"m":"A puppet is a doll or animal figure that is moved with long sticks.","e":"The play had a large dragon puppet with four men using long sticks to make it flap its wings."},{"m":"A puppet is a person whose actions are controlled by other people.","e":"The new President was simply a puppet of the army generals."}]}]},"puppets":{"h":"puppets","l":"puppet","q":"noun"},"tread":{"h":"tread","i":"/trɛd/","a":"en-us-tread.ogg","l":"tread","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A tread is a step, as in walking.","e":"The old man moved with heavy tread across the road."},{"m":"A tread is a mark made by someone taking a step.","e":"The police searched the crime scene for tread marks."},{"m":"Tread is the part of a wheel, tyre, or a shoe that touches the road.","e":"The car left tread marks across the lawn."},{"m":"Tread is the surface pattern on a tyre.","e":"The car was not safe as there was very little tread left on the tyre."},{"m":"The tread on a stair is the part on which you put your foot.","e":"The wooden staircase had to be fixed by replacing the rotten treads."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To tread is to take a step.","e":"The wooden bridge did not look safe so I had to tread carefully."},{"m":"To tread is to stand on, or crush.","e":"To make wine you need to tread on the grapes to squeeze out the juice."}]}]},"treads":{"h":"treads","l":"tread","q":"noun"},"hartal":{"h":"hartal","i":"/ˈhɑː.tɑːl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-hartal.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"In India, a hartal is closing a shop or not working as part of a political protest.","e":"The hartal was a large disservice to Srivijaya, who wanted to go shopping at the bazaar."}]}]},"trod":{"h":"trod","l":"tread","q":"verb"},"trodden":{"h":"trodden","i":"/ˈtrɑdən/","a":"en-us-trodden.ogg","l":"tread","q":"verb"},"treading":{"h":"treading","l":"tread","q":"verb"},"hartals":{"h":"hartals","l":"hartal","q":"noun"},"spectacle":{"h":"spectacle","i":"/ˈspɛktəkl̩/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Mélange a trois-spectacle.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A spectacle is something that you see that is unusual or notable.","e":"I will never forget the spectacle of watching trying to carry all his bags home from the station."},{"m":"A spectacle is a display or event on a grand scale.","e":"The opening ceremony of the Olympic Games was quite a spectacle."},{"m":"To make a spectacle of yourself you do something stupid that other people can see.","e":"While trying to impress the boys, she fell over in her high heel shoes, making a real spectacle of herself."}]}]},"spectacles":{"h":"spectacles","i":"/ˈspɛktəkl̩z/","a":"en-us-spectacles.ogg","l":"spectacle","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Spectacles are a pair of eyeglasses.","e":"She could not read the newspaper without her spectacles."}]}]},"token":{"h":"token","i":"/ˈtəʊkən/","a":"en-us-token.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A token is an individual symbol, representing something else.","e":"A postage stamp is a token to show you have paid the postal charge."},{"m":"(countable) A token can be a plastic or metal disc used instead of a coin.","e":"He had to put a token in the ticket machine to enter the station."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A token is a small amount, purely symbolic.","e":"He was not interested in winning, so he only made a token effort."}]}]},"tokens":{"h":"tokens","a":"En-us-tokens.ogg","l":"token","q":"noun"},"ream":{"h":"ream","i":"/riːm/","a":"en-au-ream.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A ream is a measure of paper; there are 500 sheets in a ream.","e":"He was sent to the storeroom to bring back a ream of paper."},{"m":"(usually plural) A ream is a lot of written work.","e":"He had to complete reams for his mid term essay."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To ream is to make a hole, or make a hole bigger."},{"m":"To ream is to remove material from a hole with a reamer."},{"m":"When you ream a lemon, you squeeze out the juice with a reamer."}]}]},"reams":{"h":"reams","l":"ream","q":"noun"},"reamed":{"h":"reamed","l":"ream","q":"verb"},"reaming":{"h":"reaming","l":"ream","q":"verb"},"coincidences":{"h":"coincidences","l":"coincidence","q":"noun"},"sergeant":{"h":"sergeant","i":"/ˈsɑː.d͡ʒənt/","a":"en-us-sergeant.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sergeant is a noncomissioned officer in the army, higher in rank than a corporal but lower in rank than a staff sergeant.","e":"She was wearing a huge army overcoat which had sergeant stripes at the shoulder."},{"m":"(countable) A sergeant is an officer in the police force, higher in rank than a constable but lower than an inspector.","e":"He was a police sergeant with over twenty years experience."}]}]},"sergeants":{"h":"sergeants","l":"sergeant","q":"noun"},"tide":{"h":"tide","i":"/taɪd/","a":"en-us-tide.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The tide is the regular rising and falling of sea levels caused by the moon.","e":"After getting the ship stuck on sand, the crew had to wait until high tide so it would refloat."},{"m":"A tide may be something that rises and falls as if it were the sea.","e":"The politicians knew that one day the tide of public opinion would agree with them."},{"m":"Tide is a period of time or a season; usually used with another word.","e":"She always looked forward to Whitsun tide."}]}]},"tides":{"h":"tides","a":"En-us-tides.ogg","l":"tide","q":"noun"},"tack":{"h":"tack","i":"/tæk/","a":"en-us-tack.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A tack is a small, sharp nail with a large flat head.","e":"He needed a tack to hold the carpet edge down."},{"m":"A tack is the direction of a boat sailing against the wind.","e":"The boat sailed across the bay on a southerly tack."},{"m":"A tack is a course or direction to follow.","e":"Our ideas caused so much anger we were forced to change tack."},{"m":"Tack is items that are used for horse riding.","e":"The saddles were kept in the tack room."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To tack is to use small nails to hold something.","e":"She had to tack the new rules on the notice board."},{"m":"To tack is to put something together.","e":"We might be able to tack together a few ideas."},{"m":"To tack is to sew something together with large loose stitches.","e":"The tailor quickly began to tack the hem of her dress."},{"m":"To tack is to sail a zigzag course against the wind.","e":"We had to tack our way along the coast."}]}]},"tacks":{"h":"tacks","i":"/tæks/","l":"tack","q":"noun"},"tacked":{"h":"tacked","l":"tack","q":"verb"},"tacking":{"h":"tacking","l":"tack","q":"verb"},"supplement":{"h":"supplement","i":"/ˈsʌpləmənt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-supplement.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A supplement is extra text that is added to the end of a book.","e":"At the back of the book was a supplement with maps showing where the story took place."},{"m":"A supplement is a small insert or magazine added to a newspaper.","e":"He read the sport supplement that came with the Sunday paper."},{"m":"A supplement is an extra that is added to something.","e":"His hotel bill included an internet connection supplement."},{"m":"A supplement is a loosely attached expression set off by intonation and usually punctuation, presenting supplementary, non-integrated content."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To supplement is to add something extra.","e":"The doctor told him to supplement his new diet with vitamins."}]}]},"supplements":{"h":"supplements","l":"supplement","q":"noun"},"supplemented":{"h":"supplemented","l":"supplement","q":"verb"},"supplementing":{"h":"supplementing","l":"supplement","q":"verb"},"brute":{"h":"brute","i":"/bruːt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-bruit.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A brute is an animal.","e":"He told her he would not come to the house unless she tied up her brute."},{"m":"(countable) A person who behaves like an animal is a brute.","e":"The brute just pushed his way to the front of the line."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Brute is strong, like an animal, without thought or reason.","e":"He used brute strength to move the large rock."}]}]},"brutes":{"h":"brutes","l":"brute","q":"noun"},"historian":{"h":"historian","i":"/hɪˈstɔərɪən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-historian.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A historian is a person who studies or writes about history.","e":"Herodotus (484 – c. 420 BC), was a famous historian who wrote about."}]}]},"historians":{"h":"historians","l":"historian","q":"noun"},"machinery":{"h":"machinery","i":"/məˈʃiːnəri/","a":"en-us-machinery.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The group of machines that make up a production apparatus in a plant."},{"m":"The working parts of a machine as a group."},{"m":"The group of parts of something which allows it to function."}]}]},"machineries":{"h":"machineries","l":"machinery","q":"noun"},"zoroastrianism":{"h":"Zoroastrianism","i":"/ˌzɒrəʊˈæstrɪəˌnɪzəm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Zoroastrianism.wav","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Zoroastrianism is a religion founded by Zoroaster."}]}]},"monotheistic":{"h":"monotheistic","i":"/ˌmɒnə(ʊ)θɪˈɪstɪk/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Monotheistic is believing in a single god.","e":"Christianity is a monotheistic religion."}]}]},"denomination":{"h":"denomination","i":"/dɪˌnɒmɪˈneɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-denomination.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A denomination is a class or society of people.","e":"You are a Christian? What is your denomination?"}]}]},"ignosticism":{"h":"ignosticism","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Ignosticism is the idea that religions assume too much about the idea of God.","e":"In ignosticism people ask \"What is meant by 'God'?\""}]}]},"coving":{"h":"coving","i":"/ˈkəʊvɪŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-coving.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The coving is a concave surface that joins a ceiling and a wall.","e":"The coving on the old house was very decorative."}]}]},"fireworks":{"h":"fireworks","l":"firework","q":"noun"},"covings":{"h":"covings","l":"coving","q":"noun"},"actionable":{"h":"actionable","i":"/ˈæk.ʃə.nə.bəl/","a":"en-us-actionable.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is actionable, then it can be acted on.","e":"The general wanted details of where the enemy were; he needed actionable information."}]}]},"infotainment":{"h":"infotainment","i":"/ˌɪnfəʊˈteɪnmənt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-infotainment.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Infotainment is a mix of information and entertainment, usually used negatively.","e":"He had to keep the story light and amusing, it was just infotainment, not serious news."}]}]},"denominations":{"h":"denominations","l":"denomination","q":"noun"},"arrangement":{"h":"arrangement","i":"/əˈreɪnd͡ʒmənt/","a":"en-us-arrangement.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Arrangement is the manner of being arranged.","e":"The arrangement of furniture in the office was important for getting things done efficiently."},{"m":"An arrangement is a collection of things that have been arranged.","e":"In the vase was a beautiful flower arrangement."},{"m":"An arrangement is a plans for some activity.","e":"We made arrangements to meet after work."},{"m":"An arrangement is an agreement.","e":"We came to an arrangement about who would wash the dishes."},{"m":"An arrangement is an adaptation of a piece of music.","e":"wrote a piano arrangement of an English folk song called \"Country Gardens\""}]}]},"accountable":{"h":"accountable","i":"/ʌˈkaʊntəbl̩/","a":"en-us-accountable.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are accountable for something that people are not happy about, you need to explain or apologize for it.","e":"Governments must be accountable for the way they spend people's taxes."}]}]},"arrangements":{"h":"arrangements","i":"/əˈreɪnd͡ʒmənts/","a":"en-us-arrangements.ogg","l":"arrangement","q":"noun"},"excitements":{"h":"excitements","l":"excitement","q":"noun"},"negatively":{"h":"negatively","i":"/ˈnɛɡətɪvli/","a":"en-us-negatively.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"In a negative manner rather than a positive one.","e":"His idea for cutting wages was received negatively by the workers."}]}]},"bred":{"h":"bred","i":"/brɛd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-bred.wav","l":"breed","q":"verb"},"liability":{"h":"liability","i":"/laɪəˈbɪlɪti/","a":"en-us-liability.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A liability is something for which you are liable or responsible.","e":"The airline admitted liability for loosing the suitcase."},{"m":"A liability is when you owe money to someone else.","e":"The company had a liability of more than 10 million dollars."},{"m":"A liability is a weakness or problem that holds you back from doing things.","e":"He worked as a writer, but found his bad spelling was a real liability."}]}]},"liabilities":{"h":"liabilities","l":"liability","q":"noun"},"pertains":{"h":"pertains","l":"pertain","q":"verb"},"pertained":{"h":"pertained","l":"pertain","q":"verb"},"arab":{"h":"Arab","i":"/ˈærəb/","a":"en-us-Arab.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Of or relating to [[#Noun|Arabs]] and their nations.","e":"I am not familiar with that Arab tradition."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A Semitic person, whose ancestors were from Arabia."},{"m":"(countable) A member of a community that speaks Arabic.","e":"An Arab was fishing from the river."},{"m":"(countable) A particular breed of horse."}]}]},"arabs":{"h":"Arabs","l":"arab","q":"noun"},"prune":{"h":"prune","i":"/pruːn/","a":"en-au-prune.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A prune is a dried plum.","e":"He placed a prune in the middle of a plate of cheese and biscuits."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you prune a bush or shrub, you cut off parts of the plant.","e":"After a rose has finished flowering, you should prune it."},{"m":"(transitive) If you prune something, you cut it back, as if it were a plant.","e":"I was running out of money, so I had to prune my budget."}]}]},"prunes":{"h":"prunes","i":"/pruːnz/","l":"prune","q":"noun"},"pruned":{"h":"pruned","i":"/pruːnd/","l":"prune","q":"verb"},"pruning":{"h":"pruning","i":"/ˈpruːnɪŋ/","l":"prune","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Pruning means removing excess material from a tree or shrub."}]}]},"tittle":{"h":"tittle","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A tittle is a small mark, like the little dot over i or j.","e":"Don't forget to dot your is by adding tittles!"},{"m":"(countable) A tittle is a small amount of something, like a crumb or a speck."}]}]},"tittles":{"h":"tittles","l":"tittle","q":"noun"},"niobium":{"h":"niobium","i":"/naɪˈoʊbiəm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-niobium.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An element with atomic number 41 and the symbol Nb. It was formerly known as columbium (Cb), but is now called \"niobium\"."}]}]},"masochism":{"h":"masochism","i":"/ˈmæs.ə.kɪ.zəm/","a":"en-us-masochism.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Masochism is the feeling of sexual pleasure from pain or other abuse.","e":"He had to seek medical help for his love of masochism."}]}]},"masochist":{"h":"masochist","i":"/ˈmæ.səˌkʰɪst/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-masochist.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A masochist is a person who likes pain, or enjoys being punished."}]}]},"sadist":{"h":"sadist","i":"/ˈseɪdɪst/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-sadist.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sadist is someone who enjoys causing pain or cruelty to others."}]}]},"masochists":{"h":"masochists","l":"masochist","q":"noun"},"sadists":{"h":"sadists","l":"sadist","q":"noun"},"preview":{"h":"preview","i":"/ˈpriːvjʉː/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-preview.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A preview is a showing of a work like a movie, play, or painting, before the public are able to see it.","e":"We went to a preview of the new art show which opens next week."},{"m":"(countable) A preview can be a short sample from a movie, used as an advertisement before the movie is ready to be shown to the public.","e":"I had to see the movie, as the preview made it look so exciting."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you preview something, you get to see it before everyone else.","e":"We went to a special movie night, to preview the latest horror movie."}]}]},"previews":{"h":"previews","l":"preview","q":"noun"},"previewed":{"h":"previewed","l":"preview","q":"verb"},"previewing":{"h":"previewing","l":"preview","q":"verb"},"bulletproof":{"h":"bulletproof","i":"/bʊl.ɪtpruːf/","a":"en-au-bulletproof.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A bulletproof material is something that can resist a direct shot by a bullet fired from a gun.","e":"The police officers are wearing bulletproof vests."},{"m":"If an idea or concept is bulletproof, it is unbreakable, very tough."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you bulletproof something, you make it able to resist bullets.","e":"The engineers are trying to bulletproof the president's vehicle now."},{"m":"(transitive) If you bulletproof something, you make it resistant to failure.","e":"We have to bulletproof this program before we let the users at it; check every input, catch every possible flaw … it must not fail in use."}]}]},"bulletproofs":{"h":"bulletproofs","l":"bulletproof","q":"verb"},"bulletproofed":{"h":"bulletproofed","l":"bulletproof","q":"verb"},"bulletproofing":{"h":"bulletproofing","l":"bulletproof","q":"verb"},"missile":{"h":"missile","i":"/ˈmɪsaɪl/","a":"en-us-missile.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An object intended to be launched at a target."},{"m":"(countable) A self-propelled object whose path can be changed after having been launched."}]}]},"missiles":{"h":"missiles","l":"missile","q":"noun"},"sprig":{"h":"sprig","i":"/sprɪɡ/","a":"en-us-sprig.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sprig is the young growth of a plant, sometimes sprouts.","e":"Sprigs of clover were pushing through the soil."},{"m":"Sprigs are cuttings from a mature plant.","e":"She used sprigs of holly to decorate the room."}]}]},"sprigs":{"h":"sprigs","l":"sprig","q":"noun"},"welterweight":{"h":"welterweight","i":"/ˈwɛltəweɪt/","a":"en-us-welterweight.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Welterweight is a division in boxing and other sports, based on the person's weight."},{"m":"A welterweight is a boxer or wrestler in the welterweight division."},{"m":"A welterweight was a weight of 28 pounds carried by racehorses as a handicap."}]}]},"primate":{"h":"primate","i":"/ˈpraɪmeɪt/","a":"en-us-primate.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A primate is a family of mammals, with well developed hands and feet, short noses, and large brains.","e":"Humans and apes are examples of a primate."},{"m":"(religion) A primate is the highest ranking bishop in a country.","e":"The Archbishop of Canterbury is the Primate of all England."}]}]},"primates":{"h":"primates","l":"primate","q":"noun"},"fascism":{"h":"fascism","i":"/ˈfæʃɪz(ə)m/","a":"en-us-fascism.oga","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) (historical) A political system that needs absolute obedience and control of the market and the people by companies and government joined together under the cult leadership of the dictator and a devoted military hierarchy where people are above one another.","e":"Adolf Hitler and the Nazis set up a government based on fascism."},{"m":"Used today to describe any kind of authoritarian system that violates the rights of ordinary, unarmed people."}]}]},"welterweights":{"h":"welterweights","l":"welterweight","q":"noun"},"retard":{"h":"retard","i":"/rɪˈtɑː(r)d/","a":"en-us-retard (delay sense).ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To retard something is to hold it back, or slow it down.","e":"He cut back the shrub to retard its growth."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A retard in music is an instruction to slow down the tempo."},{"m":"See retardation. The state of being delayed."},{"m":"(countable) A retard is someone who is mentally disabled or a very slow learner.","e":"I've been showing my co-worker for a whole year how to properly seal the bags together and he still doesn't do it right, god what a retard."}]}]},"retards":{"h":"retards","l":"retard","q":"verb"},"retarded":{"h":"retarded","l":"retard","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Less advanced in mental, physical, or social development than is usual for one's age."}]}]},"retarding":{"h":"retarding","l":"retard","q":"verb"},"quaquaversal":{"h":"quaquaversal","a":"En-us-quaquaversal.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If it is quaquaversal then it is going in all directions at the same time.","e":"A quaquaversal beard."}]}]},"archaic":{"h":"archaic","i":"/ɑː.ˈkeɪ.ɪk/","a":"en-us-archaic.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is archaic, it is very old, ancient, or no longer used.","e":"There was no hot water because of the archaic plumbing."}]}]},"molest":{"h":"molest","i":"/məˈlɛst/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-molest.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you molest someone, you annoy, harass, or disturb them.","e":"She needed to sit somewhere quiet where her children would not molest her."},{"m":"(transitive) To molest someone is to force unwanted sexual contact on them.","e":"He was trying to molest the woman."},{"m":"(transitive) To molest means to sexually abuse a child.","e":"She was sent to jail because she kept trying to molest children."}]}]},"molests":{"h":"molests","l":"molest","q":"verb"},"molested":{"h":"molested","l":"molest","q":"verb"},"molesting":{"h":"molesting","l":"molest","q":"verb"},"molester":{"h":"molester","i":"/məˈlɛstə(r)/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A molester is someone who tries to have unwanted sexual contact with others.","e":"He was a well known child molester."}]}]},"molesters":{"h":"molesters","l":"molester","q":"noun"},"molestation":{"h":"molestation","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Molestation is the act of annoying, disturbing, or molesting others.","e":"Molestation in the office would lead to immediate dismissal."},{"m":"Molestation is the act of forcing unwanted sexual contact on others.","e":"The result of child molestation left her with emotional problems."}]}]},"molestations":{"h":"molestations","l":"molestation","q":"noun"},"rally":{"h":"rally","i":"/ˈræ.li/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-rally.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A rally is a large meeting where people gather to protest to support or oppose something."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you rally, you recover in health or consciousness."}]}]},"rallies":{"h":"rallies","l":"rally","q":"noun"},"rallied":{"h":"rallied","l":"rally","q":"verb"},"rallying":{"h":"rallying","l":"rally","q":"verb"},"phototropic":{"h":"phototropic","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When someone or an animal is phototropic, it has the tendency to move towards or away from light."}]}]},"scar":{"h":"scar","i":"/skɑr/","a":"en-ca-scar.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A scar is the mark left behind when a wound has healed.","e":"He still has a scar on his hand where he cut himself with scissors as a boy."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If an injury scars it leaves a mark after it heals.","e":"He was careful when shaving as he did not want to scar his face."},{"m":"If something scars someone, it makes them feel bad for a very long time.","e":"Her death scarred her children."}]}]},"outlet":{"h":"outlet","i":"/ˈaʊtlɛt/","a":"en-us-outlet.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (electronics) An outlet is the thing on the wall you plug electronics into."},{"m":"(countable) A store of a large company selling their products."}]}]},"scars":{"h":"scars","l":"scar","q":"noun"},"scarred":{"h":"scarred","l":"scar","q":"verb"},"scarring":{"h":"scarring","l":"scar","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The presence of scars."}]}]},"scarrings":{"h":"scarrings","l":"scarring","q":"noun"},"faulty":{"h":"faulty","i":"/ˈfɔːlti/","a":"en-us-faulty.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is faulty it is not working, or has gone wrong.","e":"The car would not start because the battery was faulty."}]}]},"faultier":{"h":"faultier","l":"faulty","q":"adjective"},"faultiest":{"h":"faultiest","l":"faulty","q":"adjective"},"hesitation":{"h":"hesitation","i":"/hɛzɪˈteɪʃən/","a":"en-us-hesitation.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A hesitation is a pause in speaking, usually because you are nor sure of what to say.","e":"There was a hesitation in his reading as he turned the page."},{"m":"Hesitation is the act of hesitating."}]}]},"hesitations":{"h":"hesitations","l":"hesitation","q":"noun"},"belated":{"h":"belated","i":"/bɪˈleɪtɪd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-belated.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is belated, it refers to being at a later time as compared to the actual time of the event.","e":"Your birthday was yesterday, but well, happy belated birthday!"}]}]},"cisgender":{"h":"cisgender","i":"/sɪsˈdʒɛndə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Flame, not lame-cisgender.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"appearing or attempting to be a member of their birth sex."},{"m":"having one's gender identity match their biological sex."}]}]},"cisgenders":{"h":"cisgenders","l":"cisgender","q":"noun"},"cisgendered":{"h":"cisgendered","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"of, relating to, or being someone whose birth sex matches the sex they act and/or appear as."}]}]},"arse":{"h":"arse","i":"/ɑːs/","a":"en-uk-arse.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"; British version of ass."},{"m":"An unpleasant person, usually male.","e":"You stupid arse!"}]}]},"arses":{"h":"arses","l":"arse","q":"noun"},"staircase":{"h":"staircase","a":"En-us-staircase.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A staircase is a set of steps between two different levels.","e":"She climbed the staircase to reach the upper floor of the house."}]}]},"staircases":{"h":"staircases","l":"staircase","q":"noun"},"brew":{"h":"brew","i":"/bruː/","a":"en-us-brew.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To brew is boil, infuse and ferment hops and malt to make beer.","e":"He grew hops so he could use them to brew his own beer."},{"m":"(transitive) Brew is to put leaves into very hot water to make a drink.","e":"He used the best tea leaves to brew his tea."},{"m":"To brew is to come up with a plan."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A brew is a drink made by putting the ingredients into hot water.","e":"He made a strong brew of tea."},{"m":"A brew is something made by a process of mixing, like beer.","e":"High prices and high unemployment created a brew of discontent among the people."}]}]},"brews":{"h":"brews","i":"/bruːz/","l":"brew","q":"verb"},"brewed":{"h":"brewed","l":"brew","q":"verb"},"brewing":{"h":"brewing","l":"brew","q":"verb"},"ramp":{"h":"ramp","i":"/ræmp/","a":"en-us-ramp.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A ramp is a sloped surface that connects two levels.","e":"If you are handicapped, you might have to take a ramp to get onto the sidewalk."},{"m":"(countable) A ramp is a large parking area in an airport for aircraft, for loading and unloading or for storage (see also apron)"}]}]},"ramps":{"h":"ramps","l":"ramp","q":"noun"},"barf":{"h":"barf","i":"/bɑːf/","a":"en-au-barf.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(informal); (uncountable) Barf is vomit.","e":"There is barf all over the floor!"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(informal) To barf is to vomit.","e":"He was sick, so he barfed."}]}]},"barfs":{"h":"barfs","l":"barf","q":"verb"},"barfed":{"h":"barfed","l":"barf","q":"verb"},"barfing":{"h":"barfing","l":"barf","q":"verb"},"discomfort":{"h":"discomfort","i":"/dɪsˈkʌmfət/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-discomfort.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A feeling of being embarrassed or worried.","e":"His bad singing caused us discomfort."},{"m":"(uncountable) Pain or another unpleasant physical feeling.","e":"She had some discomfort in her knees."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you discomfort a person or animal, you make them feel worried, embarrassed, or a little ill.","e":"Her strange behaviour discomforted us."}]}]},"phlogiston":{"h":"phlogiston","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(historical) An ancient Greek idea of energy, which was used up when things burned. For example, burning wood would use up the phlogiston in the wood and the air (which actually had no oxygen). When the air or the wood had lost their phlogiston they could not be used. Scientists now know this idea is wrong."}]}]},"wherewithal":{"h":"wherewithal","i":"/ˈwɛə.wɪ.ðɔːl/","a":"en-us-wherewithal.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Wherewithal is a tool with which you are able to do something, often money. It can also be the series of steps you go through to do something.","e":"He didn't have any wherewithal to carry out his difficult ideas."}]}]},"propulsion":{"h":"propulsion","i":"/prəˈpʌlʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-propulsion.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Propulsion is a force that makes something move, by pushing it or pulling on it.","e":"The rocket needed a lot of propulsion from the engine to fly upwards."}]}]},"bribe":{"h":"bribe","i":"/braɪb/","a":"en-us-bribe.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bribe is a reward that is given to someone, so that they do something they normally would not. It's different from payment in that a bribe is usually for something illegal, or against some rules.","e":"He gave the judge a bribe so that he would win the contest."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you bribe someone, you give a reward so that they do something they normally wouldn't.","e":"s that the police were bribed to cover up the investigation surfaced after the event."}]}]},"description":{"h":"description","i":"/dɪˈskrɪpʃən/","a":"en-us-description.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A description is a phrase or sentence that tells you what something is, or what something is like. A dictionary has descriptions of words, and a biography has descriptions of events in a person's life.","e":"After coming back from Costa Rica, he gave me a long description of the swimming and sight-seeing he did there."}]}]},"contraction":{"h":"contraction","i":"/kənˈtræk.ʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-contraction.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A contraction is when something pulls together and gets smaller. It is the act of contracting.","e":"The cold weather made the bridge contract and break."},{"m":"(countable) A contraction is a word made of two other words, with letters and spaces removed, and an apostrophe added. It is different from a compound word, because a compound word doesn't have any letters removed. Most are informal.","e":"In English class, we learned the contractions we've and you're."},{"m":"(countable) A contraction is when a muscle is used and pulls together to move some part of the body. Specifically, when giving birth, it means the uterus contracting.","e":"When she felt the contractions, she knew she was going into labor."}]}]},"swampy":{"h":"swampy","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a place is swampy, the ground is like a swamp. It is usually wet, soggy, or the water might be deep enough to wade through. Usually the place will be shady and with lots of trees.","e":"The hike led through some swampy sections, unfortunately."}]}]},"descriptions":{"h":"descriptions","l":"description","q":"noun"},"contractions":{"h":"contractions","l":"contraction","q":"noun"},"bribes":{"h":"bribes","l":"bribe","q":"noun"},"discomforts":{"h":"discomforts","l":"discomfort","q":"verb"},"discomforted":{"h":"discomforted","l":"discomfort","q":"verb"},"discomforting":{"h":"discomforting","l":"discomfort","q":"verb"},"aunty":{"h":"aunty","i":"/ˈæn.ti/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A fun word for aunt; a different way of spelling auntie."}]}]},"incident":{"h":"incident","a":"en-us-incident.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An incident is an event or occurrence.","e":"What happened before was sure an unusual incident."},{"m":"An incident is a small event that has something to do with other events."}]}]},"incidents":{"h":"incidents","a":"En-us-incidents.ogg","l":"incident","q":"noun"},"outlets":{"h":"outlets","l":"outlet","q":"noun"},"wherewithals":{"h":"wherewithals","l":"wherewithal","q":"noun"},"poker":{"h":"poker","i":"/ˈpoʊkɚ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-poker.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Poker is a group of card games that involve trying to get a good hand of cards. Usually there is some betting, and people give or take cards to try to build a better hand.","e":"The three of us play poker every Friday night, and the loser buys drinks."},{"m":"(countable) A poker, which people also call a fire poker or fire iron, is something people use in a fire. They use it to move around the ashes so that the fire keeps burning well, and they use it to move coals back to the middle of the fire.","e":"The fire is dying down, so can you hand me the poker?"}]}]},"pokers":{"h":"pokers","l":"poker","q":"noun"},"swifter":{"h":"swifter","l":"swift","q":"adjective"},"swiftest":{"h":"swiftest","l":"swift","q":"adjective"},"tamer":{"h":"tamer","l":"tame","q":"adjective"},"tamest":{"h":"tamest","l":"tame","q":"adjective"},"baggier":{"h":"baggier","l":"baggy","q":"adjective"},"baggiest":{"h":"baggiest","l":"baggy","q":"adjective"},"fluffier":{"h":"fluffier","l":"fluffy","q":"adjective"},"fluffiest":{"h":"fluffiest","l":"fluffy","q":"adjective"},"grumpier":{"h":"grumpier","l":"grumpy","q":"adjective"},"grumpiest":{"h":"grumpiest","l":"grumpy","q":"adjective"},"hornier":{"h":"hornier","l":"horny","q":"adjective"},"horniest":{"h":"horniest","l":"horny","q":"adjective"},"swampier":{"h":"swampier","l":"swampy","q":"adjective"},"swampiest":{"h":"swampiest","l":"swampy","q":"adjective"},"paycheck":{"h":"paycheck","i":"/ˈpeɪ.t͡ʃɛk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-paycheck.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Money received (normally in the form of a check) in return for work performed during the previous pay period.","e":"My paycheck was pleasantly high this week!"}]}]},"paychecks":{"h":"paychecks","l":"paycheck","q":"noun"},"tremolando":{"h":"tremolando","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(Italian) A tremolando is a rapid repetition of the same note, or an alternation between two or more notes.","e":"Molly played the notes tremolando, much to the surprise of her friends."}]}]},"tremolandos":{"h":"tremolandos","l":"tremolando","q":"noun"},"allergy":{"h":"allergy","i":"/ˈæl.ər.d͡ʒi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-allergy.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An allergy is when your immune system reacts badly to something that isn't bad for other people.","e":"I have a peanut allergy."}]}]},"allergies":{"h":"allergies","l":"allergy","q":"noun"},"taxonomy":{"h":"taxonomy","i":"/tækˈsɒnəmi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-taxonomy.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Taxonomy is the classification of living things into groups."},{"m":"Taxonomy is dividing things into categories and groups."}]}]},"taxonomies":{"h":"taxonomies","l":"taxonomy","q":"noun"},"odor":{"h":"odor","i":"/ˈəʊ.də/","a":"en-us-odour.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Something's odor is its smell, usually a bad smell.","e":"The football players had an odor after their match, and I had to hold my breath as they walked past."}]}]},"rebuild":{"h":"rebuild","i":"/ri'bɪld/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-rebuild.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you rebuild something, you build it again.","e":"He had to completely rebuild his house after the tornado destroyed it."}]}]},"rebuilds":{"h":"rebuilds","l":"rebuild","q":"verb"},"rebuilding":{"h":"rebuilding","l":"rebuild","q":"verb"},"disciple":{"h":"disciple","i":"/dɪˈsaɪ.pəl/","a":"en-us-disciple.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A disciple is a person who believes in and helps spread the teachings of another person.","e":"There were 12 disciples who spread the teachings of Jesus Christ."}]}]},"disciples":{"h":"disciples","a":"En-us-disciples.ogg","l":"disciple","q":"noun"},"temple":{"h":"temple","i":"/ˈtɛmp(ə)l/","a":"en-uk-temple.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A temple is a building used for religious activities."},{"m":"(countable) A temple is a Mormon church."},{"m":"The temple is the flat area on the side of your head."}]}]},"temples":{"h":"temples","i":"/ˈtɛmpl̩z/","a":"en-us-temples.ogg","l":"temple","q":"noun"},"microscope":{"h":"microscope","i":"/ˈmaɪ.krəˌskəʊp/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-microscope.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A microscope is a device that makes tiny things easy to see.","e":"The scientist used a microscope to look at the blood cells."}]}]},"forge":{"h":"forge","i":"/fɔːd͡ʒ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-forge.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A forge is a fire or furnace used to heat metal.","e":"The blacksmith worked at his forge, shaping horseshoes."},{"m":"A forge is a place where metal is shaped and tempered."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To forge metal is to heat it and then shape it."},{"m":"To forge something is to fake it.","e":"He was arrested for forging documents."},{"m":"To forge is to shape or adapt something with a lot of care.","e":"He was able to forge close friendships with the rest of the team."}]}]},"lively":{"h":"lively","i":"/ˈlaɪvli/","a":"en-us-lively.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Someone that is lively is full of life and energy.","e":"She had a lively conversation with her new boyfriend."}]}]},"utter":{"h":"utter","i":"/ˈʌtə/","a":"en-us-utter.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To utter is to say something.","e":"Don't utter that name again!"},{"m":"To utter is to put something into circulation.","e":"He tried to utter a fake bank note at the shop."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Utter is total or complete.","e":"His attempt to fly was an utter failure."}]}]},"distant":{"h":"distant","i":"/ˈdɪstənt/","a":"en-us-distant.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Distant is far away; at a distance.","e":"She liked to travel to distant places."},{"m":"A distant person is someone who is hard to get to know.","e":"My best friend is so quiet and distant, even I don't know him too well sometimes."}]}]},"forges":{"h":"forges","l":"forge","q":"noun"},"forged":{"h":"forged","i":"/fɔːdʒd/","l":"forge","q":"verb"},"forging":{"h":"forging","l":"forge","q":"verb"},"utters":{"h":"utters","l":"utter","q":"verb"},"uttered":{"h":"uttered","i":"/ˈʌtɚd/","a":"en-us-uttered.ogg","l":"utter","q":"verb"},"uttering":{"h":"uttering","l":"utter","q":"verb"},"livelier":{"h":"livelier","l":"lively","q":"adjective"},"liveliest":{"h":"liveliest","l":"lively","q":"adjective"},"microscopes":{"h":"microscopes","l":"microscope","q":"noun"},"intuition":{"h":"intuition","a":"en-us-intuition.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Intuition is knowing something or how to do it without thinking about it.","e":"She just had a sense, an intuition, that something was wrong."}]}]},"neptunium":{"h":"neptunium","i":"/nɛpˈtjuːniəm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-neptunium.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Neptunium is a chemical element with atomic number 93 and symbol Np."}]}]},"accumulate":{"h":"accumulate","i":"/əˈkjuːmjʊˌleɪt/","a":"en-us-accumulate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you accumulate something, you bring it together.","e":"He worried that the paperwork would accumulate on his desk if he took a day off work."}]}]},"wisdom":{"h":"wisdom","i":"/ˈwɪzdəm/","a":"en-us-wisdom.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Wisdom is the skillful use of knowledge and insight to make a good decision."}]}]},"capitalism":{"h":"capitalism","i":"/ˈkapɪt(ə)lɪz(ə)m/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-capitalism.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Capitalism is an economic system in which ordinary people own land and businesses and use them to increase their wealth.","e":"East Germany changed from the Soviet Union's type of socialism to the Western type of capitalism after the fall of the Berlin Wall."}]}]},"accumulates":{"h":"accumulates","l":"accumulate","q":"verb"},"accumulated":{"h":"accumulated","l":"accumulate","q":"verb"},"accumulating":{"h":"accumulating","l":"accumulate","q":"verb"},"faux":{"h":"faux","i":"/fəʊ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-faux.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is a faux, it is a fake and not real.","e":"She was wearing faux leather."}]}]},"bossy":{"h":"bossy","i":"/ˈbɔsi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-bossy.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A bossy person often tells others what to do.","e":"Mary is so bossy, always telling me what to do."}]}]},"prescient":{"h":"prescient","a":"En-uk-prescient.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Prescient people are able to know what will happen in the future."}]}]},"bossier":{"h":"bossier","l":"bossy","q":"adjective"},"bossiest":{"h":"bossiest","l":"bossy","q":"adjective"},"implausible":{"h":"implausible","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is not likely to happen.","e":"A third world war is implausible now that so many countries are closely linked economically."}]}]},"improbable":{"h":"improbable","i":"/ɪmˈprɑbəbl̩/","a":"en-GB-improbable.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is improbable is not likely to happen.","e":"He needs to consider every outcome, even the most improbable ones."}]}]},"unimportant":{"h":"unimportant","i":"/ˌʌnɪmˈpɔːtənt/","a":"en-us-unimportant.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something unimportant is not important, it is minor or petty.","e":"He had to know the starting time, but the other details were unimportant."}]}]},"eager":{"h":"eager","i":"/ˈiɡɚ/","a":"en-us-eager.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"To be eager is to hardly be able to wait to do something.","e":"They were eager to see the new movie."}]}]},"critical":{"h":"critical","i":"/ˈkrɪtɪkəl/","a":"en-us-critical.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that criticizes or includes criticism.","e":"A critical review."},{"m":"If something is critical, it is very important.","e":"It's critical that my package arrives on time."},{"m":"If a person is in critical condition, they are badly injured.","e":"He got hit by a car and is in critical condition."}]}]},"protection":{"h":"protection","i":"/prəˈtɛkʃən/","a":"en-us-protection.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Protection is keeping something or someone safe.","e":"She ran away from her abusive husband to her brother for protection."},{"m":"A device used for safe sex e.g. condom.","e":"I used protection so I wouldn't get her pregnant."}]}]},"pest":{"h":"pest","i":"/pɛst/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-pest.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pest is an insect that spreads disease or bothers people in some way.","e":"We had to call pest control to get rid of this infestation in my house."},{"m":"(countable) A pest is an annoying, bothersome person.","e":"My little brother is so annoying, he's such a pest."}]}]},"shortage":{"h":"shortage","i":"/ˈʃɔː(r)tɪdʒ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-shortage.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A shortage is when there is too little of something.","e":"There has been a shortage of food because of the drought."}]}]},"surplus":{"h":"surplus","i":"/ˈsɝˌplʌs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-surplus.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A surplus is when there is more of a good than is strictly needed."}]}]},"surplusses":{"h":"surplusses","l":"surplus","q":"noun"},"shortages":{"h":"shortages","l":"shortage","q":"noun"},"odors":{"h":"odors","l":"odor","q":"noun"},"intuitions":{"h":"intuitions","l":"intuition","q":"noun"},"capitalisms":{"h":"capitalisms","l":"capitalism","q":"noun"},"protections":{"h":"protections","l":"protection","q":"noun"},"pests":{"h":"pests","l":"pest","q":"noun"},"distinctive":{"h":"distinctive","i":"/dɪˈstɪŋktɪv/","a":"en-us-distinctive.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Distinctive is something that's noticeable because it's different.","e":"She knew it was him as soon as she heard his distinctive laugh."}]}]},"fastening":{"h":"fastening","i":"/fɑːsənɪŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-fastening.wav","l":"fasten","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A fastening holds something in place.","e":"She felt the fastening on the back of her dress become loose."}]}]},"fastenings":{"h":"fastenings","l":"fastening","q":"noun"},"nucleus":{"h":"nucleus","i":"/ˈnjuː.kli.əs/","a":"en-us-nucleus.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A nucleus is the central part of something, such as a cell or an atom.","e":"Our cells store their genetic information in their nucleus."}]}]},"assault":{"h":"assault","i":"/əˈsɔːlt/","a":"en-us-assault.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you assault someone, you attack and hurt that person.","e":"He punched someone and got arrested for assault."}]}]},"crab":{"h":"crab","i":"/kræb/","a":"en-us-crab.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A crab is a sea animal with a shell and pincers."}]}]},"evaporate":{"h":"evaporate","i":"/ɪˈvæpəreɪt/","a":"en-us-evaporate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To evaporate is to turn from liquid into air.","e":"If you leave a pot of water on a hot stove, the water will evaporate."}]}]},"deprive":{"h":"deprive","i":"/dɪˈpraɪv/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-deprive.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To deprive is to keep something from someone.","e":"The mafia mastermind was deprived of the use of telephones in prison."}]}]},"imitate":{"h":"imitate","i":"/ˈɪmɪteɪt/","a":"en-us-imitate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To imitate is to copy what someone else says or does.","e":"The monkey imitated every action I made."}]}]},"onion":{"h":"onion","i":"/ˈʌnjən/","a":"en-us-onion.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An onion is a vegetable. They can make you cry when you cut them.","e":"She liked eating onions, but they made her cry."}]}]},"nuclei":{"h":"nuclei","l":"nucleus","q":"noun"},"nucleuses":{"h":"nucleuses","l":"nucleus","q":"noun"},"assaults":{"h":"assaults","l":"assault","q":"verb"},"assaulted":{"h":"assaulted","l":"assault","q":"verb"},"assaulting":{"h":"assaulting","l":"assault","q":"verb"},"crabs":{"h":"crabs","l":"crab","q":"noun"},"evaporates":{"h":"evaporates","l":"evaporate","q":"verb"},"evaporated":{"h":"evaporated","l":"evaporate","q":"verb"},"evaporating":{"h":"evaporating","l":"evaporate","q":"verb"},"deprives":{"h":"deprives","l":"deprive","q":"verb"},"deprived":{"h":"deprived","l":"deprive","q":"verb"},"depriving":{"h":"depriving","l":"deprive","q":"verb"},"imitates":{"h":"imitates","l":"imitate","q":"verb"},"imitated":{"h":"imitated","a":"En-us-imitated.ogg","l":"imitate","q":"verb"},"imitating":{"h":"imitating","l":"imitate","q":"verb"},"troublemaker":{"h":"troublemaker","i":"/ˈtrʌblˌmeɪkə/","a":"en-us-troublemaker.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A troublemaker is someone who causes problems or makes trouble.","e":"John was not liked by many people because he was a troublemaker."}]}]},"trajectory":{"h":"trajectory","i":"/trəˈdʒɛktərɪ/","a":"en-us-trajectory.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Trajectory is the path that something like an arrow takes when it is shot into the air."}]}]},"momentum":{"h":"momentum","i":"/ˌmoʊˈmɛntəm/","a":"en-us-momentum.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The momentum is the way something keeps going after you stop pushing it.","e":"The rock rolled down the hill. It had too much momentum. Nobody could stop it."}]}]},"troublemakers":{"h":"troublemakers","l":"troublemaker","q":"noun"},"trajectories":{"h":"trajectories","l":"trajectory","q":"noun"},"momentums":{"h":"momentums","l":"momentum","q":"noun"},"bale":{"h":"bale","i":"/beɪ̯l/","a":"en-us-bale.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bale is a large bundle, or package, tied with wire, rope, or string.","e":"The farmer used the straw bale to feed his sheep."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you bale, you create a bale from hay.","e":"The hay was baled so it would be easier to transport."}]}]},"bales":{"h":"bales","i":"/beɪlz/","a":"en-us-bales.ogg","l":"bale","q":"noun"},"backwoods":{"h":"backwoods","i":"/ˈbakˌwʊdz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Wodencafe-backwoods.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Backwoods are an area of forest or woodlands, far from any towns.","e":"The family enjoyed camping in the backwoods."}]}]},"birthright":{"h":"birthright","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A birthright is a right, or possession, you get when you are born.","e":"The prince knew he would be king one day, it was his birthright."}]}]},"birthrights":{"h":"birthrights","l":"birthright","q":"noun"},"bluebell":{"h":"bluebell","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A bluebell is a small blue flowering bulb of the genus Hyacinthoides.","e":"He went into the garden to pick a bluebell."}]}]},"bluebells":{"h":"bluebells","l":"bluebell","q":"noun"},"brushwood":{"h":"brushwood","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Brushwood is wood from branches or shrubs.","e":"They collected brushwood for a small camp fire."}]}]},"cleavage":{"h":"cleavage","i":"/ˈkliːvɪdʒ/","a":"en-au-cleavage.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Cleavage is the gap between a woman's breasts.","e":"Her low cut dress showed her cleavage."},{"m":"Cleavage is a when something is split into two parts.","e":"There was a cleavage in the group between those who wanted to wait and those who wanted to leave."}]}]},"cleavages":{"h":"cleavages","l":"cleavage","q":"noun"},"packings":{"h":"packings","l":"packing","q":"noun"},"foreshorten":{"h":"foreshorten","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To foreshorten is to make shorter.","e":"His use of tobacco would foreshorten his life by ten years."},{"m":"An artist can foreshorten lines on a drawing to make it look like it has depth."}]}]},"foil":{"h":"foil","i":"/fɔɪl/","a":"en-us-foil.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A foil is a sword used in the sport of fencing.","e":"He struck his opponent three times with his foil."},{"m":"Foil is a very thin sheet of metal.","e":"He wrapped his sandwich in aluminium foil."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To foil is to stop somebody who is trying to do something.","e":"The guard was able to foil the bad man from hurting the little girl."}]}]},"generalize":{"h":"generalize","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you generalize you speak in general, or in vague terms."},{"m":"To infer or induce from specific cases to more general cases or principles."},{"m":"To spread throughout the body and become part of the body's system."}]}]},"generalization":{"h":"generalization","i":"/dʒɛn(ə)rəlʌɪˈzeɪʃ(ə)n/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-generalization.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The process of forming general concepts from specific instances by abstracting common properties."},{"m":"The process of reasoning from detailed facts to general principles."}]}]},"foreshortens":{"h":"foreshortens","l":"foreshorten","q":"verb"},"foreshortened":{"h":"foreshortened","l":"foreshorten","q":"verb"},"foreshortening":{"h":"foreshortening","l":"foreshorten","q":"verb"},"foils":{"h":"foils","i":"/fɔɪlz/","l":"foil","q":"noun"},"foiled":{"h":"foiled","i":"/fɔɪld/","l":"foil","q":"verb"},"foiling":{"h":"foiling","i":"/ˈfɔɪlɪŋ/","l":"foil","q":"verb"},"generalizes":{"h":"generalizes","l":"generalize","q":"verb"},"generalized":{"h":"generalized","l":"generalize","q":"verb"},"generalizing":{"h":"generalizing","l":"generalize","q":"verb"},"generalizations":{"h":"generalizations","l":"generalization","q":"noun"},"climber":{"h":"climber","i":"/ˈklaɪm.ə(r)/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A climber is someone who climbs.","e":"She was a famous mountain climber."},{"m":"A social climber is a person who tries to get a higher position in society."},{"m":"A plant that climbs is called a climber.","e":"is a climber, used to cover walls."}]}]},"climbers":{"h":"climbers","l":"climber","q":"noun"},"cusp":{"h":"cusp","i":"/kʌsp/","a":"en-us-cusp.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A cusp is a pointed end."},{"m":"A point on a tooth is a cusp.","e":"The cusp on his back tooth had broken."},{"m":"The point on a crescent is a cusp.","e":"They could see the cusp of the moon."},{"m":"When two curved lines meet, they create a cusp."},{"m":"A cusp is a point from which everything changes.","e":"The scientist was at the cusp of a great discovery."}]}]},"cusps":{"h":"cusps","l":"cusp","q":"noun"},"chef":{"h":"chef","i":"/ʃɛf/","a":"en-au-chef.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A chef is a person who is paid to cook.","e":"The restaurant had a really good chef."},{"m":"(countable) A chef is the person in charge of a large kitchen.","e":"The chef wrote out the menus for the coming week."}]}]},"onions":{"h":"onions","i":"/ˈʌnjəns/","a":"en-us-onions.ogg","l":"onion","q":"noun"},"consignment":{"h":"consignment","i":"/kənˈsʌɪnm(ə)nt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-consignment.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A consignment is goods sent for sale.","e":"The shop got a consignment of new books."}]}]},"consignments":{"h":"consignments","l":"consignment","q":"noun"},"contour":{"h":"contour","i":"/ˈkɒntʊə(r)/","a":"en-us-contour.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Contour is the outline of a shape.","e":"He liked the contour of her body."},{"m":"A contour is a line that shows the outline of the shape.","e":"I started with a contour drawing of the mountains."},{"m":"A contour line joins places of the same height on a map.","e":"Tightly spaced contour lines mean steep slopes."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To contour is to draw or create the outline of a shape.","e":"He would contour the seat so that it would fit the human shape and be comfortable to sit on."}]}]},"contours":{"h":"contours","l":"contour","q":"noun"},"contoured":{"h":"contoured","l":"contour","q":"verb"},"contouring":{"h":"contouring","l":"contour","q":"verb"},"locality":{"h":"locality","i":"/loʊˈkælɪti/","a":"en-us-locality.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The fact or quality of having a position in space."},{"m":"The features or surroundings of a particular place."},{"m":"The situation or position of an object."},{"m":"An area or district considered as the site of certain."},{"m":"Limitation to a county, district, or place."}]}]},"localities":{"h":"localities","l":"locality","q":"noun"},"gesticulate":{"h":"gesticulate","i":"/dʒɛsˈtɪkjʊleɪt/","a":"en-us-gesticulate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you gesticulate you wave your hands to communicate with others.","e":"When he was excited he would gesticulate wildly."}]}]},"skate":{"h":"skate","i":"/skeɪt/","a":"en-us-skate.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An ice skate is a steel blade, which are worn on the feet to travel across ice."},{"m":"(countable) A roller skate has wheels, which are worn on the feet, to travel across smooth surfaces."},{"m":"(countable) A skate board is a small piece of wood with wheels on the bottom."},{"m":"(countable) A skate is a type of ray with a flat body."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To skate is to travel using roller skates, ice skates, or a skate board.","e":"I loved to ice skate during the winter."}]}]},"skates":{"h":"skates","l":"skate","q":"noun"},"skated":{"h":"skated","l":"skate","q":"verb"},"skating":{"h":"skating","l":"skate","q":"verb"},"gesticulates":{"h":"gesticulates","l":"gesticulate","q":"verb"},"gesticulated":{"h":"gesticulated","l":"gesticulate","q":"verb"},"gesticulating":{"h":"gesticulating","l":"gesticulate","q":"verb"},"creeper":{"h":"creeper","i":"/ˈkripɚ/","a":"en-au-creeper.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A creeper is something that creeps."},{"m":"(countable) A creeper is a climbing plant.","e":"The fence was covered with Virginia creeper."},{"m":"(countable) A mechanic's creeper is a board with wheels on it. People can lie on them to move around while working under cars.","e":"He was at work on the creeper and only his legs could be seen sticking out from under the car."},{"m":"(countable) A creeper is a pervert.","e":"This creeper at the park kept asking for my number even though I didn't know him."}]}]},"creepers":{"h":"creepers","l":"creeper","q":"noun"},"ambitious":{"h":"ambitious","i":"/æmˈbɪʃ.əs/","a":"en-us-ambitious.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Someone who is ambitious always wants to do or to be something positive.","e":"Robert, a very ambitious man from our department, nominated himself to be the new supervisor."}]}]},"cunning":{"h":"cunning","i":"/ˈkʌnɪŋ/","a":"en-us-cunning.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Cunning is the skill of being very clever, usually to trick or fool someone else.","e":"His new plan to attack the castle showed great cunning."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is cunning uses skills to trick or deceive others.","e":"The cunning fox was able to climb over the fence into the hen house."}]}]},"wonderful":{"h":"wonderful","i":"/ˈwʌn.də.fl/","a":"en-us-wonderful.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something wonderful is exciting, excellent, and creates feelings of wonder.","e":"The newly discovered continent was full of strange and wonderful creatures."}]}]},"reconnoitre":{"h":"reconnoitre","i":"/ˌrɛkəˈnɔɪtə/","a":"en-us-reconnoiter.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you reconnoitre, you perform a reconnaissance of an area.","e":"Our scout will reconnoitre the path ahead of our troops."}]}]},"reconnoitres":{"h":"reconnoitres","l":"reconnoitre","q":"verb"},"reconnoitred":{"h":"reconnoitred","l":"reconnoitre","q":"verb"},"reconnoitring":{"h":"reconnoitring","l":"reconnoitre","q":"verb"},"punishable":{"h":"punishable","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"To be punishable someone must do, or have done, something that needs to be punished.","e":"Spitting on the floor was a punishable offence."}]}]},"gull":{"h":"gull","i":"/ˈɡʌl/","a":"en-us-gull.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A gull is a seabird with big wings."}]}]},"indian":{"h":"Indian","i":"/ˈɪndɪən/","a":"en-us-Indian.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An Indian is a person from India or a person whose family is from India."},{"m":"(countable) An Indian is a person having descents of Native Americans."}]}]},"indians":{"h":"Indians","l":"indian","q":"noun"},"chennai":{"h":"Chennai","i":"/ˈtʃenaɪ/","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Chennai is the name of a city in the southern part of India"}]}]},"vijayawada":{"h":"Vijayawada","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Vijayawada is a city in the southern part of India"}]}]},"visakhapatnam":{"h":"Visakhapatnam","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Visakhapatnam is a city in the southern part of India."}]}]},"warangal":{"h":"Warangal","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Warangal is a city in the southern part of India"}]}]},"guntur":{"h":"Guntur","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Guntur is a city in the southern part of India"}]}]},"tirumala":{"h":"Tirumala","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Tirumala is a city in the southern part of India"}]}]},"humanitarian":{"h":"humanitarian","i":"/hjʊˌmæ.nɪˈtɛː.rɪ.ən/","a":"en-us-humanitarian.mp3","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Concerned and interested about the welfare of people. Trying to reduce the grieving and pain of people."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A person with such interests and concerns."}]}]},"microscopic":{"h":"microscopic","i":"/ˌmaɪkrəˈskɑpɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-microscopic.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is microscopic, it is very small. It is too small to be seen with the eye."}]}]},"urea":{"h":"urea","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The main nitrogen-containing substance in the urine of mammals."}]}]},"hetero":{"h":"hetero","i":"/ˈhɛ.tɚ.oʊ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-hetero.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"One who is attracted to members of the opposite sex."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is hetero, they are attracted to members of the opposite sex."}]}]},"breeder":{"h":"breeder","i":"/ˈbriːdə(r)/","a":"en-au-breeder.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A breeder is a person who breeds plants or animals.","e":"I met a plant breeder at the seedling farm."},{"m":"(countable) A breeder is an animal kept for breeding.","e":"The champion bull was kept at the farm as a breeder."},{"m":"(countable) A breeder is a person attracted to members of the opposite sex."}]}]},"aisle":{"h":"aisle","i":"/aɪ̯l/","a":"en-us-aisle.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An aisle is the space between two sets of seats."}]}]},"aisles":{"h":"aisles","i":"/aɪlz/","l":"aisle","q":"noun"},"carter":{"h":"carter","i":"/ˈkɑrtɚ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-carter.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A carter is a person who drives carts or wagons.","e":"The carter had a team of four horses to pull his heavy cart."}]}]},"clothier":{"h":"clothier","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A clothier is a person who makes and sells clothes.","e":"I went to the clothier to get a new suit."}]}]},"cooker":{"h":"cooker","i":"/ˈkʊkɚ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-cooker.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cooker is a stove, or a pot, used to cook food.","e":"We bought a new gas cooker."},{"m":"(countable) A cooker is a person who cooks."},{"m":"(countable) (Australia) A cooker is a person who makes drugs."}]}]},"carters":{"h":"carters","l":"carter","q":"noun"},"clothiers":{"h":"clothiers","l":"clothier","q":"noun"},"cookers":{"h":"cookers","l":"cooker","q":"noun"},"breeders":{"h":"breeders","l":"breeder","q":"noun"},"fuse":{"h":"fuse","i":"/fjuːz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-fuse.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A fuse is a length of cord that will burn and is used to set off explosives.","e":"After lighting the fuse, the miners moved away to a safe area."},{"m":"A fuse is a switch used to set off an explosive.","e":"The soldier carefully set the fuse on the bomb."},{"m":"A fuse is a thin piece of wire that will melt if it gets too hot.","e":"We lost power after after the faulty toaster made the fuse melt."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To fuse is to melt with heat."},{"m":"Fuse is to mix or join two or more things together."}]}]},"debit":{"h":"debit","i":"/ˈdɛb.ɪt/","a":"en-us-debit.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A debit is a written record of a debt in an account book.","e":"I wrote the amount he owed into the debit column of the account book."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To debit is to add a debt to an account.","e":"The bank agreed to debit his account for the cost of his new suit."}]}]},"debiting":{"h":"debiting","l":"debit","q":"verb"},"depict":{"h":"depict","i":"/dɪˈpɪkt/","a":"en-us-depict.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To depict is to show, illustrate, or represent someone or something.","e":"Smoking is depicted as harmful to your health"}]}]},"depicts":{"h":"depicts","l":"depict","q":"verb"},"depicted":{"h":"depicted","l":"depict","q":"verb"},"depicting":{"h":"depicting","l":"depict","q":"verb"},"cheerful":{"h":"cheerful","i":"/ˈt͡ʃɪrfəl/","a":"en-us-cheerful.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A person that is cheerful is happy and optimistic.","e":"He is a very cheerful guy. He is always laughing and talking to the others."}]}]},"shipwreck":{"h":"shipwreck","i":"/ˈʃɪprɛk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-shipwreck.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A shipwreck is the remains of a ship that has sunk or run aground. It can no longer be used.","e":"The \"Titanic\" shipwreck is very deep in the ocean."},{"m":"When a ship sinks or runs aground, it is called a shipwreck.","e":"The sinking of the \"Titanic\" was a shipwreck."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Shipwreck is to destroy a ship in an accident.","e":"They were shipwrecked on a small island."}]}]},"optimistic":{"h":"optimistic","i":"/ˌɒptɪˈmɪstɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-optimistic.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A person who is optimistic expects the best in all possible ways.","e":"He is very optimistic about his plans that they will succeed."}]}]},"pessimistic":{"h":"pessimistic","i":"/ˌpɛ.səˈmɪs.tɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-pessimistic.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A pessimistic person is always expecting the worst to happen."}]}]},"negligent":{"h":"negligent","i":"/ˈnɛɡ.lɪ.dʒənt/","a":"en-us-negligent.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Negligent is being careless, without giving enough or proper attention."},{"m":"due to negligence."}]}]},"culpable":{"h":"culpable","i":"/ˈkʌlpəbəl/","a":"en-us-culpable.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Culpable is to deserve blame, especially as something wrong","e":"I am culpable for stealing your money."}]}]},"unsuspicious":{"h":"unsuspicious","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Not suspicious.","e":"The unsuspicious crowd never thought that he was lying."}]}]},"aeolian":{"h":"aeolian","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-NaomiAmethyst-aeolian.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is aeolian is formed or caused by wind.","e":"Sanddunes are made by the wind: they are aeolian in origin."}]}]},"co-dependent":{"h":"co-dependent","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Co-dependent is a relationship in which a person allows another person to control them."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A co-dependent person does not act to meet their own needs; a doormat."}]}]},"amend":{"h":"amend","i":"/əˈmɛnd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-amend.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you amend a law, statement, or piece of writing, you change it to make it better or fix a mistake.","e":"Pakistan has amended a law to give new powers to army courts."}]}]},"amended":{"h":"amended","l":"amend","q":"verb"},"amends":{"h":"amends","l":"amend","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Amends are the apologies or payment given to a person due to loss or injury.","e":"Making amends is an important step after a fight."}]}]},"debits":{"h":"debits","l":"debit","q":"noun"},"debited":{"h":"debited","a":"en-us-debited.ogg","l":"debit","q":"verb"},"amending":{"h":"amending","l":"amend","q":"verb"},"jet":{"h":"jet","i":"/dʒɛt/","a":"en-au-jet.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A jet is a stream of gas or liquid forced through a small opening.","e":"A jet of water burst through the broken pipe."},{"m":"(countable) A jet is the opening where a stream of gas or liquid can be forced.","e":"The gas stove would not work because the jet was blocked."},{"m":"(countable) A jet is an aircraft powered by a jet engine.","e":"The jet landed at the airport."},{"m":"(countable) Jet is a hard, black coal, that is used for jewellery.","e":"She was wearing her mother's jet necklace."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Jet is a deep, black color.","e":"She had jet black hair."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To jet is to travel by a jet powered aircraft.","e":"We had to jet from Rome to London."}]}]},"jets":{"h":"jets","i":"/dʒɛts/","l":"jet","q":"noun"},"jetted":{"h":"jetted","l":"jet","q":"verb"},"jetting":{"h":"jetting","l":"jet","q":"verb"},"stub":{"h":"stub","i":"/stʌb/","a":"en-us-stub.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A stub is a short piece of something left when the rest has been used.","e":"He chewed on the stub of his pencil."},{"m":"(countable) A stub is the part of a ticket or cheque that you keep.","e":"He put the ticket stub into his pocket and entered the theatre."},{"m":"(countable) A stub is something short and blunt.","e":"They cut off the branch, leaving a small stub."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To stub is to put out something burning by crushing it.","e":"Before entering the building, he had to stub out his cigarette."},{"m":"If you stub your toe, you hit it hard against something.","e":"I was scared walking in bare feet, because I could stub my toe."},{"m":"To stub is to pull out by the roots.","e":"The farmer needed to stub his field before he could plant a new crop."}]}]},"stubs":{"h":"stubs","l":"stub","q":"noun"},"stubbed":{"h":"stubbed","l":"stub","q":"verb"},"stubbing":{"h":"stubbing","l":"stub","q":"verb"},"mint":{"h":"mint","i":"/mɪnt/","a":"En-us-mint.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Mint is a plant that can be eaten in the genus Mentha which has very strong-smelling leaves.","e":"We had a mint sauce to pour on the roast lamb."},{"m":"A green colour, like that of mint."},{"m":"Mint is a lolly or candy flavored with the mint plant.","e":"She sucked on a mint to make her breathe smell nice."},{"m":"A mint is a place where money is made.","e":"There was a high fence around the mint."},{"m":"A mint is a lot of money.","e":"He made a mint selling his house at the right time."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To mint is to make coins and money.","e":"The government need to mint extra coins."},{"m":"To mint is to invent or make something.","e":"He was able to make people smile when he would mint a new word."}]}]},"mints":{"h":"mints","i":"/mɪnts/","l":"mint","q":"noun"},"minted":{"h":"minted","l":"mint","q":"verb"},"minting":{"h":"minting","l":"mint","q":"verb"},"grill":{"h":"grill","i":"/ɡrɪl/","a":"en-us-grill.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A grill is a cooking surface which has parallel metal bars.","e":"I like steak when it is cooked on a grill."},{"m":"A grill is food cooked on a grill.","e":"The most popular meal at the hotel was the mixed grill."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To grill is cook on hot metal bars.","e":"He thought he would grill the steak."},{"m":"To grill is to question intensely.","e":"The police would grill the suspect for hours."}]}]},"grills":{"h":"grills","l":"grill","q":"noun"},"grilled":{"h":"grilled","i":"/ɡrɪld/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-grilled.wav","l":"grill","q":"verb"},"grilling":{"h":"grilling","l":"grill","q":"verb"},"premium":{"h":"premium","i":"/ˈprimiəm/","a":"en-us-premium.oga","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A premium is an amount of money paid for insurance.","e":"He had to pay a higher premium after his house burnt down."},{"m":"Premium is something that high quality and in short supply.","e":"We had to pay a premium price for a glass of water in the desert."},{"m":"A premium is a bonus or reward."}]}]},"premiums":{"h":"premiums","l":"premium","q":"noun"},"resent":{"h":"resent","i":"/riˈzɛnt/","a":"en-us-resent.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Resent is to be angry or bitter about something.","e":"I resent having to do homework when I could be outside playing."}]}]},"resents":{"h":"resents","l":"resent","q":"verb"},"resented":{"h":"resented","l":"resent","q":"verb"},"resenting":{"h":"resenting","l":"resent","q":"verb"},"alternate":{"h":"alternate","i":"/ˈɒlˌtɜː(r).nət/","a":"en-us-alternate-noun-adj.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To alternate is change between two positions.","e":"She would alternate between laughing and crying without warning."},{"m":"To alternate is to take turns.","e":"My wife and I would alternate doing the dishes."},{"m":"To alternate, something changes regularly and repeatedly.","e":"The traffic lights would alternate from red to green."}]}]},"alternates":{"h":"alternates","l":"alternate","q":"verb"},"alternated":{"h":"alternated","l":"alternate","q":"verb"},"alternating":{"h":"alternating","l":"alternate","q":"verb"},"architect":{"h":"architect","i":"/ˈɑːkɪtɛkt/","a":"en-us-architect.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An architect is a person who designs and plans buildings.","e":"We had an architect design our new house."}]}]},"architects":{"h":"architects","l":"architect","q":"noun"},"cage":{"h":"cage","i":"/keɪdʒ/","a":"en-us-cage.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cage is a structure made with wire or bars, to hold an animal.","e":"The bird lived in a large wire cage near the window."},{"m":"(countable) A cage is a something that holds things in, to protect or to keep imprisoned.","e":"Your heart is inside your rib cage."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Cage is to place something in a wire or barred structure so that they can not get out.","e":"We had to cage the lion to keep it from escaping."}]}]},"caged":{"h":"caged","l":"cage","q":"verb"},"cages":{"h":"cages","l":"cage","q":"verb"},"caging":{"h":"caging","l":"cage","q":"verb"},"hack":{"h":"hack","i":"/hæk/","a":"en-au-hack.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hack is someone who works hard, but does not get great results.","e":"He thinks he's a great rapper but he's just a hack."},{"m":"(countable) A hack is a horse that is hired to others.","e":"I rode a hack into the valley."},{"m":"(countable) A hack is a way to gain access to parts of a computer program.","e":"He got really high scores in that computer game but we knew he was using a hack."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To hack is to cut something roughly.","e":"He decided to hack the tree in half."},{"m":"(transitive) To hack is to break into a computer or make programs do things they wouldn't normally do.","e":"I was worried someone could hack into my e-mail account and get my credit card number."}]}]},"fantastic":{"h":"fantastic","i":"/fænˈtæstɪk/","a":"en-us-fantastic.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Existing in or constructed from fantasy; of or relating to fantasy; fanciful.","e":"He told fantastic stories of dragons and goblins."},{"m":"Not believable; maybe only possible in fantasy.","e":"The events were so fantastic that all the audience went silent."},{"m":"; marvelous; excellent; really good or great (used especially as an intensifier).","e":"\"I had a simply fantastic vacation, and I can't wait to tell you all about it!\""}]}]},"fantasy":{"h":"fantasy","i":"/ˈfæntəsi/","a":"en-us-fantasy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"That which comes from one's imagination."},{"m":"The literary genre of magic and fictive medieval technology."},{"m":"The drug."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(literary) To fantasize (about)"},{"m":"To have a fancy for; to be pleased with; to like."}]}]},"fantasies":{"h":"fantasies","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The plural of fantasy; more than one fantasy."}]}]},"fantasied":{"h":"fantasied","l":"fantasy","q":"verb"},"fantasying":{"h":"fantasying","l":"fantasy","q":"verb"},"subscribes":{"h":"subscribes","l":"subscribe","q":"verb"},"subscribed":{"h":"subscribed","l":"subscribe","q":"verb"},"subscribing":{"h":"subscribing","l":"subscribe","q":"verb"},"subscribe":{"h":"subscribe","i":"/səbˈskraɪb/","a":"en-us-subscribe.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To sign up to have copies of a publication, such as a newspaper or a magazine, delivered for a period of time.","e":"Would you like to subscribe or subscribe a friend to our new magazine, Lexicography Illustrated?"},{"m":"To pay for the provision of a service, such as Internet access or a cell phone plan."},{"m":"To believe or agree with a theory or an idea.","e":"I don’t subscribe to that theory."},{"m":"To pay money to be a member of an organization."},{"m":"To contribute or promise to contribute money to a common fund.","e":"1913: Theodore Roosevelt, —... under no circumstances could I ever again be nominated for any public office, as no corporation would subscribe to a campaign fund if I was on the ticket, and that they would subscribe most heavily to beat me;"},{"m":"To agree to buy shares in a company.","e":"1776: Adam Smith, The Wealth of Nations — The capital which had been subscribed to this bank, at two different subscriptions, amounted to one hundred and sixty thousand pounds, of which eighty per cent only was paid up."},{"m":"To write one's name at the bottom of a document, to sign."},{"m":"To sign away; to give up."},{"m":"To admit to being inferior or in the wrong."}]}]},"hacks":{"h":"hacks","l":"hack","q":"noun"},"hacked":{"h":"hacked","l":"hack","q":"verb"},"hacking":{"h":"hacking","l":"hack","q":"verb"},"subscription":{"h":"subscription","i":"/səbˈskrɪpʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-subscription.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Having access to a resource for a period of time.","e":"I have a monthly subscription to The Daily Telegraph newspaper."},{"m":"The formal acceptance of something, especially when verified with a signature."},{"m":"The signing of one's name."}]}]},"subscriptions":{"h":"subscriptions","l":"subscription","q":"noun"},"infusion":{"h":"infusion","i":"/ɪnˈfjuːʒən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-infusion.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A product made of a liquid which has had other ingredients in it to extract useful qualities.","e":"An extract of many ingredients makes a refreshing infusion."},{"m":"The act of soaking a substance in liquid so as to extract medicinal or herbal qualities."},{"m":"The act of installing a quality into a person."},{"m":"The act of dipping into a fluid."}]}]},"infusions":{"h":"infusions","l":"infusion","q":"noun"},"loudness":{"h":"loudness","i":"/laʊdnəs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-loudness.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Loudness depends on the amplitde of a sound wave."},{"m":"(uncountable) Loudness is how loud or soft any kind of sound is."}]}]},"loudnesses":{"h":"loudnesses","l":"loudness","q":"noun"},"acidity":{"h":"acidity","i":"/əˈsɪdɪti/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-acidity.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The quality or state of being acid."},{"m":"The quality of sour; sourness to the taste, as in the acidity of lemon juice.","e":"Empty stomachs lead to acidity and leave a sour taste in the mouth."},{"m":"Excessive acid quality, as in gastric secretions."}]}]},"acidities":{"h":"acidities","l":"acidity","q":"noun"},"pathology":{"h":"pathology","i":"/pəˈθɒlədʒi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-pathology.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The branch of medicine concerned with the study of the nature of disease and its causes, processes, development, and consequences."},{"m":"Any bad status of health."}]}]},"pathologies":{"h":"pathologies","l":"pathology","q":"noun"},"adjuster":{"h":"adjuster","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"One who adjusts, especially for the insurance industry's employment title \"claims adjuster.\""}]}]},"adjusters":{"h":"adjusters","l":"adjuster","q":"noun"},"lifestyle":{"h":"lifestyle","i":"/ˈlaɪfˌstaɪl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-lifestyle.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A lifestyle is a way of living.","e":"His lifestyle was not a good example for young people."},{"m":"(marketing) the totality of the likes and dislikes of a particular section of the market, especially when expressed in terms of the products and services that they would buy; a marketing strategy based on the self-image of such a group"}]}]},"lifestyles":{"h":"lifestyles","l":"lifestyle","q":"noun"},"ureas":{"h":"ureas","l":"urea","q":"noun"},"heteros":{"h":"heteros","l":"hetero","q":"noun"},"humanitarians":{"h":"humanitarians","l":"humanitarian","q":"noun"},"deck":{"h":"deck","i":"/dɛk/","a":"en-us-deck.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A deck is the floor of a ship.","e":"The sailors had to clean the top deck."},{"m":"(countable) A deck is the space between the floors of a ship.","e":"The cannons were lined up in the gun deck."},{"m":"(countable) A deck is something that is like the floor of a ship.","e":"We sat on the top deck of the bus."},{"m":"(countable) A deck is the outside floor of a house or building without a roof.","e":"We went out onto the observation deck at the top of the tall building."},{"m":"(countable) A deck is the surface of a bridge.","e":"The bridge was closed while the deck was being repaired."},{"m":"(countable) A deck is a pack of playing cards.","e":"Before playing poker, you need to shuffle the deck."},{"m":"(countable) A deck is a packet of drugs."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you deck something, you dress it up.","e":"We had to deck out the room with ribbons for the party."},{"m":"If you deck someone, you knock them down to the floor.","e":"He was so angry, I thought he would deck me."}]}]},"decks":{"h":"decks","l":"deck","q":"noun"},"decked":{"h":"decked","l":"deck","q":"verb"},"decking":{"h":"decking","l":"deck","q":"verb"},"typist":{"h":"typist","i":"/ˈtaɪpɪst/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-typist.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A typist is a person who writes things using a typewriter.","e":"He was a good typist, and could write more than 40 words per minute."}]}]},"typists":{"h":"typists","l":"typist","q":"noun"},"alleviate":{"h":"alleviate","i":"/əˈli.vi.eɪt/","a":"en-us-alleviate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you alleviate pain, suffering, or an unpleasant condition, you make it less intense or severe.","e":"Nowadays, a great deal can be done to alleviate back pain."}]}]},"alleviates":{"h":"alleviates","l":"alleviate","q":"verb"},"alleviated":{"h":"alleviated","l":"alleviate","q":"verb"},"alleviating":{"h":"alleviating","l":"alleviate","q":"verb"},"rooster":{"h":"rooster","i":"/ˈruːstə/","a":"en-us-rooster.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A rooster is an adult male chicken.","e":"The rooster crowed loudly every morning."}]}]},"roosters":{"h":"roosters","l":"rooster","q":"noun"},"shipwrecks":{"h":"shipwrecks","l":"shipwreck","q":"noun"},"shipwrecked":{"h":"shipwrecked","l":"shipwreck","q":"verb"},"shipwrecking":{"h":"shipwrecking","l":"shipwreck","q":"verb"},"durrie":{"h":"durrie","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A durrie is a cotton carpet from India.","e":"The durrie was so pretty that we hung it on the wall."},{"m":"A durrie is an Australian word for cigarette.","e":"Hey mate, have you got a spare durrie?"}]}]},"durries":{"h":"durries","l":"durrie","q":"noun"},"node":{"h":"node","i":"/nəʊd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-node.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A node is a center point, where parts meet.","e":"The railway station was the town's transport node where all the buses stopped."},{"m":"A node is a swelling or a lump.","e":"The doctor examined his armpit to feel the lymph node."},{"m":"A node is a swelling on a plant which becomes a new branch or leaf."},{"m":"A node is the point on a wave where the amplitude is zero."},{"m":"A node is the point on an orbit where it crosses a plane."},{"m":"A node is a computer in the context of a network."}]}]},"nodes":{"h":"nodes","l":"node","q":"noun"},"dental":{"h":"dental","i":"/ˈdɛntəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-dental.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Dental describes anything to do with the teeth.","e":"I use dental floss to clean between my teeth."}]}]},"miscreant":{"h":"miscreant","i":"/ˈmɪs.kri.ənt/","a":"en-us-miscreant.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A miscreant is an evil doer."}]}]},"cynical":{"h":"cynical","i":"/ˈsɪnɪkəl/","a":"en-us-cynical.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is cynical, they have a negative attitude towards life.","e":"He is a cynical person who seems to complain about everything."}]}]},"deficit":{"h":"deficit","i":"/ˈdɛfɪsɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-deficit.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A deficit is a lack or shortage of something, such as money."}]}]},"hypothesize":{"h":"hypothesize","i":"/hʌɪˈpɒθɪsʌɪz/","a":"en-us-hypothesize.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To hypothesize is to make a guess, a hypothesis, based on the available evidence.","e":"The detective hypothesized that the criminal could have escaped through the heating vents."}]}]},"patriotism":{"h":"patriotism","i":"/ˈpætri.əˌtɪzəm/","a":"en-us-patriotism.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Patriotism is love, support, and defense of one's country.","e":"Americans get a burst of patriotism every year on July 4 when they celebrate Independence Day."}]}]},"abortion":{"h":"abortion","i":"/əˈbɔr.ʃn̩/","a":"en-us-abortion.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"If a woman has an abortion, her pregnancy is ended deliberately.","e":"She's had two abortions."}]}]},"absurd":{"h":"absurd","i":"/əbˈzɜːd/","a":"en-us-absurd.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something absurd is ridiculous and stupid.","e":"Saying that a fish cannot swim in water is just absurd."}]}]},"accelerator":{"h":"accelerator","i":"/æk.ˈsɛl.ə.ˌreɪ.tɚ/","a":"en-us-accelerator.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An accelerator is the pedal in a vehicle which you step on to make it go faster.","e":"He took his foot off the accelerator and the car started to slow down."}]}]},"acquaintance":{"h":"acquaintance","i":"/əˈkweɪntəns/","a":"en-us-acquaintance.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An acquaintance is someone you know slightly but not well.","e":"He's an old acquaintance of mine."}]}]},"acquit":{"h":"acquit","i":"/əˈkwɪt/","a":"en-au-acquit.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If someone is acquitted of a crime, they have been tried in a court and found not guilty.","e":"He was acquitted of murder but found guilty of manslaughter."}]}]},"miscreants":{"h":"miscreants","l":"miscreant","q":"noun"},"deficits":{"h":"deficits","l":"deficit","q":"noun"},"hypothesizes":{"h":"hypothesizes","l":"hypothesize","q":"verb"},"hypothesized":{"h":"hypothesized","l":"hypothesize","q":"verb"},"hypothesizing":{"h":"hypothesizing","l":"hypothesize","q":"verb"},"abortions":{"h":"abortions","l":"abortion","q":"noun"},"agriculture":{"h":"agriculture","i":"/ˈæɡrɪˌkʌltʃə/","a":"en-uk-agriculture.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Agriculture is farming and the methods that are used to raise and look after crops and animals.","e":"Ukraine is strong both in industry and agriculture."}]}]},"airmail":{"h":"airmail","i":"/ˈɛə.meɪl/","a":"en-au-airmail.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Airmail is the system of sending letters, parcels, and goods by air.","e":"Goods are generally shipped by airmail."}]}]},"allergic":{"h":"allergic","i":"[ə.ˈlɜː.dʒɪk]","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-allergic.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"No people are allergic to Earth at all.","e":"No humans are allergic to the other planet at all."}]}]},"aloud":{"h":"aloud","i":"/əˈlaʊd/","a":"en-us-aloud.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"When you say something, read, or laugh aloud, you speak or laugh so that other people can hear you.","e":"When we were children, our father read aloud to us."},{"m":"If you think aloud, you express your thoughts as they occur to you, rather than thinking first and then speaking.","e":"He really must be careful about thinking aloud. Who knew what he might say?"}]}]},"ambassador":{"h":"ambassador","i":"/æmˈbæs.ə.də(r)/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-ambassador.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An ambassador is an important official who lives in a foreign country and represents his or her own country's interests there.","e":"The German ambassador to Poland lives in Warsaw."}]}]},"ambassadors":{"h":"ambassadors","l":"ambassador","q":"noun"},"acquaintances":{"h":"acquaintances","a":"en-us-acquaintances.ogg","l":"acquaintance","q":"noun"},"acquits":{"h":"acquits","l":"acquit","q":"verb"},"acquitted":{"h":"acquitted","l":"acquit","q":"verb"},"acquitting":{"h":"acquitting","l":"acquit","q":"verb"},"beware":{"h":"beware","i":"/biˈwɛɚ/","a":"en-us-beware.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Be careful or cautious.","e":"Beware of the dog because it bites."}]}]},"rajshahi":{"h":"Rajshahi","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Rajshahi is a division in Bangladesh."},{"m":"Rajshahi is also a district and sadar upzilla in Bangladesh"}]}]},"khulna":{"h":"Khulna","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Khulna is a division in Bangladesh."},{"m":"Khulna is also a district and sadar upzilla in Bangladesh"}]}]},"sylhet":{"h":"Sylhet","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Sylhet is a division in Bangladesh."},{"m":"Sylhet also is a district and a sadar upzilla in Bangladesh"}]}]},"rangpur":{"h":"Rangpur","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Rangpur is a division of Bangladesh."},{"m":"Rangpur is also a district and Sadar Upzilla in Bangladesh"}]}]},"barisal":{"h":"Barisal","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Barisal is a division of Bangladesh."},{"m":"Barisal is also a district and Sadar Upzilla in Bangladesh"}]}]},"magura":{"h":"Magura","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Magura is a district in Bangladesh.","e":"I live in Magura."}]}]},"jessore":{"h":"Jessore","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Jessore is a district in Bangladesh.","e":"I live in Jessore."}]}]},"mymensingh":{"h":"Mymensingh","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Mymensingh is a district in Bangladesh","e":"I live in Mymensingh."}]}]},"bewares":{"h":"bewares","l":"beware","q":"verb"},"bewared":{"h":"bewared","l":"beware","q":"verb"},"bewaring":{"h":"bewaring","l":"beware","q":"verb"},"ample":{"h":"ample","i":"/ˈæm.pəl/","a":"en-us-ample.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If there is an ample amount of something, there is enough of it and usually some extra.","e":"There'll be ample opportunity to relax, swim and soak up some sun."},{"m":"If you describe someone's figure as ample, you mean that they are large in a pleasant or attractive way.","e":"... a young mother with a baby resting against her ample bosom."}]}]},"apparently":{"h":"apparently","i":"/əˈpær.ənt.liː/","a":"en-us-apparently.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"You use apparently to indicate that the information you are giving is something that you have heard or seen, but you are not certain that it is true.","e":"Oil prices fell this week to their lowest level in fourteen months, apparently because of over-production."}]}]},"approximately":{"h":"approximately","i":"/əˈprɑk.sɪ.mət.li/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-PerfectSoundWhatever-approximately.wav","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Approximately is close to, but not exactly.","e":"Approximately $150 million is to be spent on improvements."}]}]},"arabic":{"h":"Arabic","i":"/ˈæ.rə.bɪk/","a":"en-us-Arabic.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Arabic is a language that is spoken in the Middle East and in parts of North Africa.","e":"She is learning Arabic."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is Arabic belongs or relates to the language, writing, or culture of the Arabs."},{"m":"An Arabic numeral is one of the written figures such as 1, 2, 3, or 4.","e":"The clock is available with either Roman or Arabic numerals."}]}]},"archbishop":{"h":"archbishop","i":"/ˌɑː(r)tʃˈbɪʃəp/","a":"en-us-archbishop.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) In the Roman Catholic, Orthodox, and Anglican Churches, an archbishop is a bishop of the highest rank, who is in charge of all the bishops and priests in a certain country or region.","e":"A new archbishop was recently appointed."}]}]},"architecture":{"h":"architecture","i":"/ˈɑː.kɪ.ˌtɛk.tʃə/","a":"en-us-architecture.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Architecture is the art of planning, designing, and constructing buildings.","e":"He studied classical architecture and design in Rome."},{"m":"The architecture of a building is the style in which it is designed and constructed."},{"m":"The architecture of something is its structure."}]}]},"arena":{"h":"arena","i":"/əˈriːnə/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An arena is a place where sports, entertainments, and other public events take place. It has seats around it where people sit and watch.","e":"We went to the arena to watch the football game."},{"m":"You can refer to a field of activity, especially one where there is a lot of conflict or action, as an arena of a particular kind.","e":"Oil speculation proved a natural arena for his skills."}]}]},"armchair":{"h":"armchair","i":"/ˈɑː(r)mtʃɛə(r)/","a":"en-us-armchair.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An armchair is a big comfortable chair which has a support on each side for your arms.","e":"She was sitting in an armchair with blankets wrapped round her."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"An armchair critic, fan, or traveller knows about a particular subject from reading or hearing about it rather than from practical experience.","e":"This great book is ideal for both the travelling supporter and the armchair fan."}]}]},"gorgeous":{"h":"gorgeous","i":"/ˈɡɔːdʒəs/","a":"en-us-gorgeous.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"(of a person or place) Gorgeous is very beautiful.","e":"All my classmates agreed that Bella was absolutely gorgeous."},{"m":"Very enjoyable, pleasant, tasty etc.","e":"Israeli hummus is absolutely gorgeous."}]}]},"grocery":{"h":"grocery","i":"/ˈɡrəʊs(ə)ri/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Back ache-grocery.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Groceries are food and other household that you buy in a store.","e":"I'm going to pick up some groceries. Do you need anything?"},{"m":"(countable) A grocery is a shop or store that sells groceries.","e":"I'm going to the grocery to get some milk."}]}]},"charlatan":{"h":"charlatan","i":"/ˈʃɑrlətən/","a":"en-ca-charlatan.oga","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A charlatan is someone who fools another person.","e":"Do not pay that charlatan any more money."}]}]},"charlatans":{"h":"charlatans","l":"charlatan","q":"noun"},"arenas":{"h":"arenas","l":"arena","q":"noun"},"armchairs":{"h":"armchairs","l":"armchair","q":"noun"},"archbishops":{"h":"archbishops","l":"archbishop","q":"noun"},"abbreviate":{"h":"abbreviate","i":"/ə.ˈbriː.vi.eɪt/","a":"en-us-abbreviate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you abbreviate something, especially a word or a piece of writing, you make it shorter.","e":"Alexander abbreviated his first name to Alec."}]}]},"aboriginal":{"h":"aboriginal","i":"/ˌæb.əˈrɪd͡ʒ.n̩.l̩/","a":"en-uk-aboriginal.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An Aboriginal is an Australian aborigine.","e":"He remained fascinated by the Aboriginals tales."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Aboriginal means belonging or relating to the Australian Aborigines.","e":"They saw the Aboriginal rock art in the Northern Territory."},{"m":"The aboriginal people or animals of a place are ones that have been there from the earliest known times or that were there before people or animals from other countries arrived.","e":"Most Canadians acknowledge that the aboriginal people have had a rotten deal."}]}]},"aborigine":{"h":"aborigine","i":"/ˌæb.əˈrɪdʒ.ɪ.ni/","a":"en-us-aborigine.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Aborigines are members of the tribes that were living in Australia when Europeans arrived there."}]}]},"aborigines":{"h":"aborigines","l":"aborigine","q":"noun"},"aboriginals":{"h":"aboriginals","l":"aboriginal","q":"noun"},"abbreviates":{"h":"abbreviates","l":"abbreviate","q":"verb"},"abbreviated":{"h":"abbreviated","i":"/əˈbriːvieɪtɪd/","a":"en-us-abbreviated.ogg","l":"abbreviate","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) If something is abbreviated, it is shortened.","e":"The abbreviated book cost less because it wasn't as big."}]}]},"abbreviating":{"h":"abbreviating","l":"abbreviate","q":"verb"},"abound":{"h":"abound","i":"/əˈbaʊnd/","a":"en-us-abound.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If things abound, or if a place abounds with things, there are very large numbers of them.","e":"The book abounds with close-up images from space."}]}]},"abounds":{"h":"abounds","l":"abound","q":"verb"},"abounded":{"h":"abounded","l":"abound","q":"verb"},"abounding":{"h":"abounding","l":"abound","q":"verb"},"poncho":{"h":"poncho","i":"/ˈpɒn.tʃəʊ/","a":"en-us-poncho.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A poncho is a simple garment, like a blanket, with a hole for the head to go through.","e":"He bought a poncho on his last trip to Bolivia."}]}]},"resilience":{"h":"resilience","i":"/rɪˈzɪl.ɪ.əns/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-resilience.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Resilience is the mental strength to recover from misfortune.","e":"He needed resilience to continue working after the death of his wife."},{"m":"Resilience is elasticity, how much something can stretch.","e":"The scientists measured the resilience of the metal beam."}]}]},"ponchos":{"h":"ponchos","l":"poncho","q":"noun"},"absent-minded":{"h":"absent-minded","i":"/ˌæb.sn̩tˈmaɪn.dɪd/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Someone who is absent-minded forgets things or does not pay attention to what they are doing, often because they are thinking about something else.","e":"In his later life he became even more absent-minded."}]}]},"abstraction":{"h":"abstraction","i":"/əbˈstræk.ʃn̩/","a":"en-us-abstraction.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An abstraction is a general idea rather than one relating to a particular object, person, or situation.","e":"Is it worth fighting a big war, in the name of an abstraction like sovereignty?"},{"m":"Abstraction is the state of being very deep in thought.","e":"Andrew noticed her abstraction and asked, 'What's bothering you?'"},{"m":"Abstraction is the use of shapes and patterns in art.","e":"Her paintings grew larger, and the images changed from abstraction to realism."}]}]},"emigrant":{"h":"emigrant","i":"/ˈɛmɪɡrənt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-emigrant.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An emigrant is a person who has left their own country to live in another country.","e":"In the 1840's about 30,000 emigrants left Ireland every year."}]}]},"grocer":{"h":"grocer","i":"/ˈɡrəʊsə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-grocer.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A grocer is a person who sells groceries (foodstuffs and household items) retail from a grocery.","e":"John worked as a grocer when he was young."}]}]},"grocers":{"h":"grocers","l":"grocer","q":"noun"},"emigrants":{"h":"emigrants","a":"En-us-emigrants.ogg","l":"emigrant","q":"noun"},"compassionate":{"h":"compassionate","i":"/kəmˈpæʃənət/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-compassionate.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone or something is compassionate, they feel or show pity, sympathy, and understanding for people who are suffering.","e":"The nurse was a very caring, compassionate person."}]}]},"infection":{"h":"infection","i":"/ɪnˈfɛkʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Wodencafe-infection.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An infection is when germs enter the body and make it sick.","e":"He had a serious infection from the cut on his arm."},{"m":"An infection is the state of being infected.","e":"The doctor had to treat a person with a scabies infection."}]}]},"infections":{"h":"infections","l":"infection","q":"noun"},"acclaim":{"h":"acclaim","i":"/ə.ˈkleɪm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-acclaim.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If someone or something is acclaimed, they are praised enthusiastically.","e":"The group's debut album was immediately acclaimed a hip hop classic."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Acclaim is public praise for someone or something.","e":"All this equipment has received international acclaim from the specialist hi-fi press."}]}]},"accomplish":{"h":"accomplish","i":"/əˈkʌm.plɪʃ/","a":"en-us-accomplish.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you accomplish something, you succeed in doing or completing something.","e":"They are skeptical about how much will be accomplished by legislation."}]}]},"accomplished":{"h":"accomplished","i":"/ə.ˈkɑm.plɪʃt/","a":"en-us-accomplished.ogg","l":"accomplish","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is accomplished at something, they are very good at it.","e":"She is an accomplished painter."}]}]},"accomplishes":{"h":"accomplishes","l":"accomplish","q":"verb"},"accomplishing":{"h":"accomplishing","l":"accomplish","q":"verb"},"acclaims":{"h":"acclaims","i":"/əˈkleɪmz/","l":"acclaim","q":"verb"},"acclaimed":{"h":"acclaimed","i":"/əˈkleɪmd/","l":"acclaim","q":"verb"},"acclaiming":{"h":"acclaiming","i":"/əˈkleɪmɪŋ/","l":"acclaim","q":"verb"},"deposit":{"h":"deposit","i":"/dɪˈpɒzɪt/","a":"en-us-deposit.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you deposit something, you put it down in a place."},{"m":"If you deposit money, you put it into a bank account.","e":"I deposited £50 in my bank account."},{"m":"If you deposit a coin or a note, you put it into a machine to buy something."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A deposit is something put down or left behind."},{"m":"A deposit is money or other valuables left in a bank to be kept safe.","e":"I put my jewelry in my safe deposit."},{"m":"A deposit is a part payment for an item.","e":"I paid a £50 deposit for my new television."},{"m":"A deposit is a security left when borrowing something."},{"m":"A deposit is a layer of matter that is found under a surface."}]}]},"deposits":{"h":"deposits","l":"deposit","q":"verb"},"deposited":{"h":"deposited","l":"deposit","q":"verb"},"depositing":{"h":"depositing","l":"deposit","q":"verb"},"superposition":{"h":"superposition","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Superposition means one on top of the other, \"placed above\".","e":"The superposition of rock strata means they are found one on top of the other."}]}]},"lateral":{"h":"lateral","i":"/ˈlæt.rəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-lateral.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"An object's lateral refers to the side of it.","e":"The lateral extension of the wall was 30 metres."}]}]},"cross-contamination":{"h":"cross-contamination","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Cross-contamination is the transfer of disease-causing microorganisms, such as bacteria and viruses, from one food to another."}]}]},"resemble":{"h":"resemble","i":"/rɪˈzɛmb(ə)l/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-AcpoKrane-resemble.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If two things resemble each other, it means they are similar or look like one another.","e":"Modern computers do not resemble computers from the 1970's."}]}]},"resembles":{"h":"resembles","a":"en-us-resembles.ogg","l":"resemble","q":"verb"},"resembled":{"h":"resembled","i":"/rɪˈzɛmbl̩d/","a":"en-us-resembled.ogg","l":"resemble","q":"verb"},"resembling":{"h":"resembling","i":"/rɪˈzɛmblɪŋ/","a":"en-us-resembling.ogg","l":"resemble","q":"verb"},"enumeration":{"h":"enumeration","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A detailed account, in which each thing is specially noticed."}]}]},"construe":{"h":"construe","i":"/kənˈstruː/","a":"en-us-construe.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To translate and explain the meaning of something.","e":"This court must construe according to the law."}]}]},"disparage":{"h":"disparage","i":"/dɪsˈpærɪd͡ʒ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-disparage.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you disparage someone, you make fun of or degrade them.","e":"The Constitution shall not disparage others and put them in a bad light."}]}]},"inoperative":{"h":"inoperative","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is inoperative, it is not working or not functioning, usually because it is idle or has broken down."},{"m":"Something that is not in effect.","e":"This article shall be inoperative unless it shall have been ratified as an amendment to the Constitution by the legislatures of the several States."}]}]},"patriotisms":{"h":"patriotisms","l":"patriotism","q":"noun"},"accelerators":{"h":"accelerators","l":"accelerator","q":"noun"},"resiliences":{"h":"resiliences","l":"resilience","q":"noun"},"enumerations":{"h":"enumerations","l":"enumeration","q":"noun"},"construes":{"h":"construes","l":"construe","q":"verb"},"construing":{"h":"construing","l":"construe","q":"verb"},"construed":{"h":"construed","l":"construe","q":"verb"},"disparages":{"h":"disparages","l":"disparage","q":"verb"},"disparaged":{"h":"disparaged","l":"disparage","q":"verb"},"disparaging":{"h":"disparaging","l":"disparage","q":"verb"},"scarcity":{"h":"scarcity","i":"/ˈskɛrsɪti/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-scarcity.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The fact of being scarce"}]}]},"invert":{"h":"invert","a":"en-us-invert.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To turn something upside down; to flip."}]}]},"turk":{"h":"Turk","i":"/tɝk/","a":"en-au-Turk.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A Turk is someone who is from Turkey or someone who is part of the Turkic ethnic groups.","e":"My father is a Turk, but my family has never visited Turkey."}]}]},"intuitive":{"h":"intuitive","i":"/ɪnˈtjuːɪtɪv/","a":"en-us-intuitive.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is intuitive, you can learn or understand it without thinking about it much."}]}]},"stringent":{"h":"stringent","i":"/ˈstrɪndʒənt/","a":"en-us-stringent.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If the requirements of something is stringent, it is strict.","e":"They have stringent quality requirements what is acceptable."}]}]},"farinaceous":{"h":"farinaceous","i":"/ˌfærəˈneɪʃəs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-farinaceous.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Containing a lot of flour"}]}]},"disorder":{"h":"disorder","i":"/dɪsˈɔː(r)də(r)/","a":"en-us-disorder.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"of order; a condition of not being arranged in an orderly manner.","e":"The children left the room in disorder."},{"m":"A disturbance of civic peace or of public order.","e":"The class was thrown into disorder when the teacher left the room"},{"m":"A physical or psychical dysfunction and, or, malfunction.","e":"Bulimia is an eating disorder."}]}]},"disorders":{"h":"disorders","l":"disorder","q":"noun"},"hypobole":{"h":"hypobole","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A hypobole is an understatement to create emphasis or effect. It is the opposite of hyperbole."}]}]},"hypoboles":{"h":"hypoboles","l":"hypobole","q":"noun"},"autism":{"h":"autism","i":"/ˈɔːtɪzəm/","a":"en-uk-autism.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Autism is a disorder where a person has difficulty with communication & social interaction, have repetitive behaviors, have intense interests, and how they learn and behave.","e":"Because their child continually rocked back and forward without speaking, the parents thought it might be autism."}]}]},"suzerain":{"h":"suzerain","i":"/ˈs(j)uz(ə)rən/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A dominant nation or state which has at least some control over the subordinate state."},{"m":"A feudal overlord."}]}]},"suzerains":{"h":"suzerains","l":"suzerain","q":"noun"},"loaf":{"h":"loaf","i":"/ləʊf/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(also loaf of bread) A block of bread after baking."},{"m":"Any solid block of food, such as meat."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) To do nothing, to be idle.","e":"loaf about, loaf around."}]}]},"banish":{"h":"banish","i":"/ˈbænɪʃ/","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To send someone away and to forbid him from returning.","e":"The king banished the rebels."}]}]},"inscription":{"h":"inscription","i":"/ɪnˈskrɪpʃən/","a":"en-us-inscription.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An inscription is the words cut into or printed on a stone or other surface.","e":"The inscription says he died 100 years ago."}]}]},"vernacular":{"h":"vernacular","i":"/vəˈnækjələ/","a":"en-us-vernacular.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Vernacular refers to the language spoken by the people in their own country.","e":"The Bible was translated from Latin into the vernacular."}]}]},"inverts":{"h":"inverts","l":"invert","q":"verb"},"inverted":{"h":"inverted","l":"invert","q":"verb"},"inverting":{"h":"inverting","l":"invert","q":"verb"},"turks":{"h":"Turks","l":"turk","q":"proper noun"},"autisms":{"h":"autisms","l":"autism","q":"noun"},"loaves":{"h":"loaves","l":"loaf","q":"noun"},"loafs":{"h":"loafs","l":"loaf","q":"verb"},"loafed":{"h":"loafed","l":"loaf","q":"verb"},"loafing":{"h":"loafing","l":"loaf","q":"verb"},"banished":{"h":"banished","i":"/ˈbænɪʃt/","a":"en-us-banished.ogg","l":"banish","q":"verb"},"banishing":{"h":"banishing","l":"banish","q":"verb"},"inscriptions":{"h":"inscriptions","l":"inscription","q":"noun"},"gulls":{"h":"gulls","l":"gull","q":"noun"},"upstage":{"h":"upstage","i":"/ʌpˈsteɪd͡ʒ/","a":"en-us-upstage.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The part of a stage that is farthest from the audience or camera."}]},{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"toward or at the back of a stage.","e":"The actor turned and walked upstage."},{"m":"away from a camera."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"At the back of a stage.","e":"The play had no upstage props."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To make people pay attention to you instead of to another person.","e":"The dog did tricks and upstaged the speaker."},{"m":"(transitive) To force other actors to face away from the audience by moving upstage."}]}]},"upstages":{"h":"upstages","l":"upstage","q":"verb"},"upstaged":{"h":"upstaged","l":"upstage","q":"verb"},"disposable":{"h":"disposable","i":"/dɪsˈpəʊzəbl̩/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-disposable.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A disposable is an object that is designed to be used once and then thrown away."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is disposable, it is made to be used for a short time and then thrown away.","e":"He wiped his mouth with a disposable wipe."}]}]},"ridge":{"h":"ridge","i":"/rɪdʒ/","a":"en-us-ridge.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A ridge is a long narrow hilltop or mountain."},{"m":"(countable) A ridge is a long narrow elevation on the bottom of an ocean."},{"m":"(countable) A ridge is a highest point on a roof forming a horizontal line."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you ridge something, you make it into a ridge or add ridges to it."}]}]},"ridges":{"h":"ridges","a":"En-us-ridges.ogg","l":"ridge","q":"noun"},"shoreland":{"h":"shoreland","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The land at the shore of a lake, sea, etc."},{"m":"Where the water meets land."}]}]},"tactic":{"h":"tactic","i":"/ˈtæktɪk/","a":"en-us-tactic.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A tactic is an action or plan to achieve a specific goal."},{"m":"A tactic is a maneuver used against an enemy."}]}]},"tactics":{"h":"tactics","l":"tactic","q":"noun"},"nightfall":{"h":"nightfall","a":"En-us-nightfall.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Nightfall is the end of the day; the beginning of night."},{"m":"Nightfall is when it becomes completely dark outside because the sun went down.","e":"Nightfall was 45 minutes after sunset this evening."}]}]},"nightfalls":{"h":"nightfalls","l":"nightfall","q":"noun"},"throne":{"h":"throne","i":"[θrəʊn]","a":"en-us-throne.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A ceremonial chair for a sovereign, bishop or leader."},{"m":"The position of a sovereign or leader itself.","e":"The King is the only person that can sit on the throne."}]}]},"thrones":{"h":"thrones","l":"throne","q":"noun"},"sovereign":{"h":"sovereign","i":"/ˈsɒv.rɪn/","a":"en-us-sovereign.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A country that is sovereign is able to control itself without the influence of other countries.","e":"Taiwan is recognized as a sovereign state by few countries."},{"m":"Something that is sovereign has supreme power."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sovereign is a monarch or the ruler of a country."},{"m":"(countable) A sovereign is a person who is not a subject to a ruler or nation."},{"m":"(countable) A sovereign is a gold coin formerly used in the United Kingdom."}]}]},"sovereigns":{"h":"sovereigns","l":"sovereign","q":"noun"},"monarch":{"h":"monarch","i":"/ˈmɒnək/","a":"en-us-monarch.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A monarch is the leader of a kingdom or empire.","e":"The monarch of England is."},{"m":"(countable) A monarch butterfly is a kind of orange and black butterfly, Danaus plexippus."}]}]},"deathbed":{"h":"deathbed","i":"/ˈdɛθˌbɛd/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Someone's deathbed is the bed on which they died."},{"m":"If someone is on their deathbed, they are in the last hours of their life."}]}]},"deathbeds":{"h":"deathbeds","l":"deathbed","q":"noun"},"royalty":{"h":"royalty","i":"/ˈrɔɪəlti/","a":"en-us-royalty.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The rank, status, power or authority of a monarch."},{"m":"A member of a royal family."}]}]},"overlord":{"h":"overlord","i":"/ˈəʊvə(r)lɔː(r)d/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-overlord.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A ruler of other rulers.","e":"The duke of 's overlord was the king of France."},{"m":"(countable) A person with great power or authority."}]}]},"overlords":{"h":"overlords","l":"overlord","q":"noun"},"aberrant":{"h":"aberrant","i":"/əˈbɛr.n̩t/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-aberrant.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A person who is unusual or weird"}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is aberrant, it is straying from the right or usual course; wandering."},{"m":"Something that is varying from ordinary type; abnormal; exceptional."}]}]},"mince":{"h":"mince","i":"/mɪns/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-mince.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Mince is meat that has been chopped into very small pieces.","e":"That mince that I just gave you was pork."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To mince something, you chop it into very small piece to make mince."}]}]},"mushroom":{"h":"mushroom","i":"/ˈmʌʃˌruːm/","a":"en-us-mushroom.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mushroom is a fungus that grows on soil or on dying wood.","e":"While in the forest, make sure to look on dead trees for mushrooms!"}]}]},"revert":{"h":"revert","i":"/rɨˈvɝt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-revert.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you revert, you are undoing an action."}]}]},"flush":{"h":"flush","i":"/ˈflʌʃ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-flush.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To flush is to have your skin turn red from fever or emotion.","e":"The sick boy's face was flushed."},{"m":"To flush is to clean with a sudden flow of water.","e":"Heavy rain would flush the rubbish out of the drain."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"To be flush is to be level or even.","e":"The tiles had to be flush with each other so that people would not trip over them."},{"m":"(game) Flush cards are all of the same suit.","e":"In poker he was dealt five hearts, a flush."}]}]},"wrinkle":{"h":"wrinkle","i":"/ˈrɪŋkl̩/","a":"en-us-wrinkle.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A wrinkle is a line or crease on old and fragile skin, usually caused by old age or tiredness.","e":"My grandfather had a lot of wrinkles on his face."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To wrinkle is to make lines, creases, or folds on a smooth surface.","e":"When he smiled, his face wrinkled."}]}]},"duchy":{"h":"duchy","i":"/ˈdʌtʃi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-duchy.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A dominion or region ruled by a duke or duchess.","e":"She ruled the duchy while the duke was away."}]}]},"duchess":{"h":"duchess","i":"/ˈdʌtʃ.əs/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The female spouse or widow of a duke."},{"m":"The female ruler of a duchy (where women can reign)."}]}]},"duchesses":{"h":"duchesses","l":"duchess","q":"noun"},"interregnum":{"h":"interregnum","i":"/ˌɪntərˈrɛɡnəm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-interregnum.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The period of time between the end of a sovereign's reign and the beginning of the reign of another sovereign."},{"m":"A period of time during which normal executive leadership is suspended or interrupted."}]}]},"hostage":{"h":"hostage","i":"/ˈhɒs.tɪd͡ʒ/","a":"en-us-hostage.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A person given as a pledge or security for the performance of an action or act; that upon completion of that act the person is to be released."}]}]},"hostages":{"h":"hostages","l":"hostage","q":"noun"},"livery":{"h":"livery","i":"/ˈlɪv.ə.ri/","a":"en-us-livery.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Livery is the formal dress of an upper class servant, usually suggesting the 18th century with gold braid, gold buttons, waistcoat, pumps, powdered wig.","e":"The Queen's footmen wear livery on formal occasions."}]}]},"coachman":{"h":"coachman","i":"/ˈkoʊt͡ʃmən/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A coachman is the person who drives a coach.","e":"The family tipped the coachman when they arrived at their destination."}]}]},"adoption":{"h":"adoption","i":"/əˈdɑp.ʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-adoption.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An act of adopting a child by different parents so that the child becomes one of their own.","e":"The dog was available for adoption, so I decided to take it."}]}]},"archer":{"h":"archer","i":"/ˈɑrtʃɚ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-archer.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An archer is a person who shoots an arrow from a bow or a bolt from a crossbow."}]}]},"archers":{"h":"archers","l":"archer","q":"noun"},"crossbow":{"h":"crossbow","i":"/ˈkrɒsbəʊ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-crossbow.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mechanical bow, which fires bolts."}]}]},"crossbows":{"h":"crossbows","l":"crossbow","q":"noun"},"disloyalty":{"h":"disloyalty","i":"/dɪsˈlɔɪ.(j)əɫ.ti/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An act of being disloyal; a betrayal."},{"m":"(uncountable) The quality of being disloyal."}]}]},"disloyal":{"h":"disloyal","i":"[dɪsˈlɔɪ(j)əɫ]","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-disloyal.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Failing to be loyal.","e":"It would be disloyal to let him go alone."},{"m":"A lack of loyalty."}]}]},"illegitimate":{"h":"illegitimate","i":"/ɪlɪˈdʒɪtɪmət/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-illegitimate.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Against the law; illegal.","e":"They set up an illegitimate government."},{"m":"Born to unmarried parents.","e":"He was an illegitimate child."}]}]},"scattered":{"h":"scattered","i":"/ˈskætɚd/","a":"en-us-scattered.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A group of items that are distributed randomly.","e":"Her toys were scattered all over the floor."},{"m":"(meteorology) occasional.","e":"The weather forecast says scattered showers this morning."}]}]},"randomly":{"h":"randomly","i":"/ˈrændm̩li/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-randomly.wav","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Doing an action in a random way.","e":"He fired randomly at all the targets."}]}]},"kite":{"h":"kite","i":"/kaɪt/","a":"en-us-kite.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A kite is an object made of light material that can use the wind to fly. They are held by a long string.","e":"We went to the beach to fly a kite this summer."},{"m":"(countable) A kite is a bird of prey.","e":"Most kites eat dead animals, but some catch and eat mice and squirrels."}]}]},"moron":{"h":"moron","i":"/ˈmɔːrɒn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-moron.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A moron is someone who is an idiot or is stupid.","e":"It is not nice to call someone a moron."}]}]},"aaqib":{"h":"Aaqib","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Aaqib is a male given name."}]}]},"reliable":{"h":"reliable","i":"/rɪˈlaɪəbəl/","a":"en-us-reliable.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something or someone that is reliable can be trusted or believed.","e":"I told you computers are reliable, they finished the task in just 10 minutes when we took 5 hours for!"}]}]},"vijay":{"h":"Vijay","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Vijay is a male given name."}]}]},"bleach":{"h":"bleach","i":"/bliːt͡ʃ/","a":"en-us-bleach.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) Bleaching something means to make it become white or even colorless.","e":"She bleached her brown hair so she could impersonate the blonde Marilyn Monroe in the talent show."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Bleach is a chemical used to make things white.","e":"I used a cup of bleach in the washing machine."}]}]},"franc":{"h":"franc","i":"/fræŋk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-franc.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Franc is a unit of French currency before it was replaced by the euro."}]}]},"gravy":{"h":"gravy","i":"/ˈɡreɪvi/","a":"en-us-gravy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A thick sauce made from the fats or juices from meat and vegetables.","e":"I added some gravy over my plate of rice to make it tastier."},{"m":"Gravy is an extra benefit or bonus.","e":"To fulfill a dream, to be allowed to sweat over lonely labor, to be given a chance to create, is the meat and potatoes of life. The money is the gravy. -- Bette Davis"}]}]},"syrup":{"h":"syrup","i":"/ˈsɪ.rəp/","a":"en-us-syrup.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Syrup is a thick, sticky, sweet liquid made from sugar, water and flavourings.","e":"I poured syrup on my waffles and pancakes."}]}]},"avocado":{"h":"avocado","i":"/ævəˈkɑːdəʊ/","a":"en-us-avocado.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An avocado is a type of fruit that is yellowish-green and mushy inside.","e":"Avocados grow in South Africa."},{"m":"A dark chartreuse colour, like the colour of the meat of an avocado."}]}]},"lychee":{"h":"lychee","i":"/ˈlaɪ̯t͡ʃiː/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-lychee.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A lychee is a fruit, that comes from China. It is small with thick rough reddish skin, white flesh and a large seed inside.","e":"Lychees are very sweet."},{"m":"(uncountable) Lychee is a soft pink-red colour."}]}]},"avocados":{"h":"avocados","l":"avocado","q":"noun"},"illegitimacy":{"h":"illegitimacy","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The state or condition of being illegitimate."}]}]},"incomprehensible":{"h":"incomprehensible","i":"/ˌɪnkɑmprəˈhɛnsɪbəl/","a":"en-us-incomprehensible.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is incomprehensible, it is very difficult or impossible to understand.","e":"Alan's story was incomprehensible and made almost everyone confused by what he was saying."}]}]},"prosperous":{"h":"prosperous","i":"/ˈprɑs.pə.rəs/","a":"en-us-prosperous.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is prosperous is financially successful.","e":"Trading Babe Ruth was far more prosperous for the Yankees than for the Red Sox."},{"m":"A person or thing that is prosperous has a lot of money.","e":"He was raised in a very prosperous household."}]}]},"overload":{"h":"overload","i":"/əʊvəˈləʊd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-overload.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To load many items in something that it exceeds the limit.","e":"The lift was too overloaded that it refused to close the doors until someone got out of it."}]}]},"characterize":{"h":"characterize","i":"/ˈkɛrəktəraɪz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-characterize.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To see someone or something a particular way (often negative)."},{"m":"To determine the characteristics of someone or something."}]}]},"characterizes":{"h":"characterizes","l":"characterize","q":"verb"},"characterized":{"h":"characterized","l":"characterize","q":"verb"},"characterizing":{"h":"characterizing","l":"characterize","q":"verb"},"hijab":{"h":"hijab","i":"/hɪˈdʒɑːb/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-hijab.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A hijab is a piece of material worn by Muslim women to cover their hair and neck."}]}]},"unreliable":{"h":"unreliable","i":"/(ˌ)ʌn.rɪˈlaɪ.ə.bl̩/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-unreliable.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something or someone is unreliable, it cannot be trusted.","e":"He is an unreliable source of this murder case as he is a good friend of the suspect and would then try to defend him."}]}]},"georgia":{"h":"Georgia","i":"/ˈdʒɔː.dʒə/","a":"en-us-Georgia.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Georgia is a country in Eastern Europe or West Asia."},{"m":"Georgia is a state in the southern United States."}]}]},"virginia":{"h":"Virginia","i":"/vɚˈdʒɪn.jə/","a":"en-us-Virginia.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Virginia is a state in the United States of America (USA).","e":"Richmond is the capital of Virginia."}]}]},"colonization":{"h":"colonization","i":"/ˌkɑː.lə.nəˈzeɪ.ʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-colonization.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Colonization is when a new colony is created by a country elsewhere.","e":"The British colonization in the 17th-18th century made the British Empire one of the largest in the world."}]}]},"gobbledygook":{"h":"gobbledygook","i":"/ˈɡɒb(ə)ldɪˌɡuːk/","a":"en-us-gobbledygook.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Something that is useless, incomprehensible or even nonsense writing.","e":"Paggyita's story of the Yang Ying was gobbledygook, none of it was even true."}]}]},"mao":{"h":"Mao","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Mao is a common Chinese surname."}]}]},"patty":{"h":"patty","i":"/ˈpæti/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-patty.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A patty is a flat circular piece of ground meat."}]}]},"crew":{"h":"crew","i":"/kruː/","a":"en-us-crew.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A group of people working together to operate something such as a ship, factory, airplane, etc."}]}]},"thingy":{"h":"thingy","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An item whose name is unknown."}]}]},"jaunt":{"h":"jaunt","i":"/ˈdʒɔːnt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-jaunt.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) When you take a jaunt, you take a short trip, usually for pleasure.","e":"We took a jaunt to the beach."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you jaunt, you take a short trip, usually for pleasure."}]}]},"falooda":{"h":"falooda","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Falooda is a cold and sweet drink that is rather popular in Southern Asia."}]}]},"enactment":{"h":"enactment","i":"/ɛnˈæktmənt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-enactment.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A piece of legislation that has been authorized by a legislative person.","e":"The enactment of this law will be a great step backward for our country."}]}]},"inappropriate":{"h":"inappropriate","i":"/ˌɪnəˈprəʊpri.ət/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-inappropriate.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something that is inappropriate, it is not appropriate, something that is not needed.","e":"Your act of throwing food away was inappropriate."}]}]},"advisory":{"h":"advisory","i":"/ədˈvaɪzəri/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-advisory.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An advisory is a warning. Usually this is used for weather reports.","e":"The Weather Department issued a tornado advisory."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something contains an advice, it is advisory; you are suggested, but not forced to do it."}]}]},"reassign":{"h":"reassign","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If someone reassigns something, they change a persons job from one thing to another, usually through someone of higher power than them.","e":"Mrs. Bullium reassigned Caper from being a software developer to becoming a system administrator."}]}]},"unoccupied":{"h":"unoccupied","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"(of a house) If something is unoccupied, it is not occupied.","e":"The tenant left, making the house unoccupied."},{"m":"(of a person) If someone is unoccupied, they are not busy; they are free to do something.","e":"My dad is unoccupied and is free to get us some ice cream."}]}]},"spotless":{"h":"spotless","i":"/ˈspɒtləs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Flame, not lame-spotless.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is spotless, it has no spots on it; it is not dirty.","e":"You did a good job cleaning the house! It is spotless!"}]}]},"welsh":{"h":"Welsh","i":"/wɛlʃ/","a":"en-us-welsh.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Welsh is a language that is spoken in Wales.","e":"I spoke Welsh."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is Welsh is related to Wales, its people or its culture."}]}]},"wintry":{"h":"wintry","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If it is wintry, it feels like winter and the cold.","e":"It feels wintry even when it is just autumn."}]}]},"halal":{"h":"halal","i":"/həˈlɑːl/","a":"en-us-halal.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Food that Muslims can eat according to the Islamic religious practice."}]}]},"tights":{"h":"tights","i":"/taɪts/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-tights.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(plural) Tights are pants worn by females that cover from the waist down to the feet."}]}]},"tenderhearted":{"h":"tenderhearted","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When someone is tenderhearted, the person is kind, gentle and cares about other people's troubles or distress."}]}]},"maturity":{"h":"maturity","i":"/məˈt͡ʃʊərəti/","a":"en-us-maturity.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Maturity is the stage of being fully grown or developed; the stage of being mature. This means being able to reproduce."}]}]},"abdul":{"h":"Abdul","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Abdul means servant in Arabic which is derived from the word Abd."}]}]},"greedy":{"h":"greedy","i":"/ˈɡriːdi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-greedy.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A greedy person is someone who wants money or other items for himself and does not like to share.","e":"My aunt is greedy because she keeps talking about money."}]}]},"projectile":{"h":"projectile","i":"/prə(ʊ)ˈdʒɛktʌɪl/","a":"en-us-projectile.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An object that is fired from a weapon."},{"m":"(countable) An object that is propelled by force.","e":"An object that is thrown is called a projectile."}]}]},"recite":{"h":"recite","i":"/rɪˈsaɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-recite.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To say something you have memorized","e":"I will recite my poem tomorrow."}]}]},"patiently":{"h":"patiently","i":"/ˈpeɪʃəntli/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-patiently.wav","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Doing something patiently means to do it in a patient manner.","e":"Jimmy waited patiently for his mother to bring him his favorite toy."}]}]},"akmal":{"h":"Akmal","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Akmal is an Islamic male given name."}]}]},"rebellion":{"h":"rebellion","i":"/rɪˈbɛli.ən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-rebellion.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Armed resistance to an established government or ruler.","e":"The government is doing its best to stop rebellion in the country."},{"m":"(countable) Defiance of authority or control; the act of rebeling.","e":"Having a tattoo was Mathilda's personal rebellion against her parents."},{"m":"(countable) An organized, forceful subversion of the law of the land in an attempt to replace it with another form of government.","e":"The army general led a successful rebellion and became president of the country."}]}]},"rebellions":{"h":"rebellions","l":"rebellion","q":"noun"},"irresponsible":{"h":"irresponsible","i":"/ˌɪrɪˈspɒnsəbl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Jjamesryan-irresponsible.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When someone is irresponsible, he/she is not responsible and does not care about anything that goes wrong.","e":"My uncle's friend is irresponsible. He does not care about the damage he caused because of him in public, causing his company to suffer because of this."}]}]},"spectacular":{"h":"spectacular","i":"/spɛkˈtæk.jʊ.lə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-spectacular.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is spectacular, it is very amazing and, making people surprised and excited about it.","e":"The bridge is spectacular! I have never seen something like it before!"}]}]},"thingies":{"h":"thingies","l":"thingy","q":"noun"},"rahman":{"h":"Rahman","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Rahman is an Islamic male given name."}]}]},"repeater":{"h":"repeater","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-repeater.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (electronics) An electronic device that takes in a weak signal and makes it stronger."}]}]},"marshmallow":{"h":"marshmallow","i":"/mɑːʃˈmaləʊ/","a":"en-us-marshmallow.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A marshmallow is a plant from Africa (Althaea officinalis).","e":"The root of the marshmallow plant is used to make confections."},{"m":"(countable) A marshmallow is a sweet, fluffy food that is white in color and cylindrical in shape.","e":"The kids love having marshmallows in hot chocolate drinks"}]}]},"marshmallows":{"h":"marshmallows","l":"marshmallow","q":"noun"},"irrational":{"h":"irrational","i":"/ɪˈræʃ.(ə.)nəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-irrational.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is irrational is it not rational, or it is nonsensical.","e":"That decision was completely irrational."}]}]},"livid":{"h":"livid","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When someone is livid, he/she is very angry, sometimes can even become irrational.","e":"My friend is livid because someone stole his candy bar."}]}]},"repeaters":{"h":"repeaters","l":"repeater","q":"noun"},"tsunami":{"h":"tsunami","i":"/suːˈnɑːmi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-tsunami.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A tsunami is a very large water wave formed in the ocean and can destroy buildings and people, usually due to an earthquake or volcanic eruption."}]}]},"nonviolent":{"h":"nonviolent","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is nonviolent, it is not violent and usually peaceful.","e":"Mahatma Gandhi and his protesters protested in a nonviolent way."}]}]},"delicious":{"h":"delicious","i":"/dɪˈlɪʃəs/","a":"en-us-delicious.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When a food is delicious, it is tasty or tastes very nice.","e":"The lasagna the school cooks is delicious and the children loved it a lot."}]}]},"insightful":{"h":"insightful","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is insightful, then it has insight; it gives you a better understanding of a topic or concept."}]}]},"obituary":{"h":"obituary","i":"/əˈbɪtjʊərɪ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-obituary.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An obituary is a death notice with information of someone who has died, usually published in a newspaper or in a booklet, given to people at funerals.","e":"His obituary was published yesterday, but did not have the cause of his death."}]}]},"obituaries":{"h":"obituaries","l":"obituary","q":"noun"},"infamous":{"h":"infamous","i":"/ˈɪnfəməs/","a":"en-us-infamous.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Someone or something that is infamous is well-known, but for bad reasons. They are famous, but are hated and considered to be bad."}]}]},"pineapple":{"h":"pineapple","a":"En-us-pineapple.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A pineapple is a large green-and-brown fruit with yellow flesh.","e":"I was looking forward to eating my pineapple, but I had a lot of trouble cutting it open."}]}]},"pineapples":{"h":"pineapples","l":"pineapple","q":"noun"},"mega":{"h":"mega","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Mega is another word for huge or large","e":"This ant experiment will be mega cool!"}]}]},"meaningful":{"h":"meaningful","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"useful; It is useful","e":"Your contributions to Wiktionary are meaningful."}]}]},"thingamabob":{"h":"thingamabob","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Thingamabob is used for (usually) weird inventions or things; doohickey"}]}]},"thingamabobs":{"h":"thingamabobs","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"More than one thingamabob"}]}]},"custody":{"h":"custody","i":"/ˈkʌstədiː/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-custody.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Custody is the act of taking care of something or somebody as it relates to the law, usually children.","e":"The court gave custody to the childrens' father."},{"m":"(uncountable) Custody is the brief watching over or taking care of a persons' things.","e":"The bank has taken custody of the house while I finish paying the money owed on my loan."},{"m":"(uncountable) Custody is when someone is watched over or put in prison, usually while waiting for a trial","e":"Until the trial, the judge ordered the defendant to stay in police custody because of the risk of him running away."}]}]},"unappreciated":{"h":"unappreciated","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Unappreciated means to not being appreciated","e":"He felt unappreciated when the teacher yelled at him."}]}]},"cabby":{"h":"cabby","i":"/ˈkæ.bi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-cabby.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) One who drives a vehicle for hire such as a taxi cab driver.","e":"The cabby sped through rush hour traffic."}]}]},"ajar":{"h":"ajar","i":"/əˈd͡ʒɑː/","a":"en-us-ajar.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a door or window is ajar, it is slightly open."}]}]},"cabbies":{"h":"cabbies","l":"cabby","q":"noun"},"quadrilateral":{"h":"quadrilateral","i":"/ˌkwɒd.rəˈlæt.ər.əl/","a":"en-ca-quadrilateral.oga","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A quadrilateral is a geometric shape having four sides.","e":"A rectangle is a quadrilateral."}]}]},"quadrilaterals":{"h":"quadrilaterals","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"More than one quadrilateral; plural of quadrilateral"}]}]},"pentagon":{"h":"pentagon","i":"/ˈpɛn.tə.ɡɑn/","a":"en-ca-pentagon.oga","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pentagon (⬟) is a shape that has five sides."}]}]},"pentagons":{"h":"pentagons","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"More than one pentagon; plural of pentagon"}]}]},"paranoid":{"h":"paranoid","i":"/ˈpɛr.ə.ˌnɔɪd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-paranoid.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When someone is being paranoid, they feel and have fear about something.","e":"Stop being so paranoid; nobody's following us."}]}]},"eerie":{"h":"eerie","i":"/ˈɪəri/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is eerie, it is weird or unusual.","e":"My friends said that the swamp was eerie at night."}]}]},"unhelpful":{"h":"unhelpful","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is unhelpful, it is not useful or helpful.","e":"Most of his contributions are unhelpful."}]}]},"dodo":{"h":"dodo","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A dodo is an extinct bird of the Aves family from Mauritius."}]}]},"dodos":{"h":"dodos","l":"dodo","q":"noun"},"hijabs":{"h":"hijabs","l":"hijab","q":"noun"},"syrups":{"h":"syrups","l":"syrup","q":"noun"},"flushes":{"h":"flushes","l":"flush","q":"verb"},"flushed":{"h":"flushed","a":"En-us-flushed.ogg","l":"flush","q":"verb"},"flushing":{"h":"flushing","l":"flush","q":"verb"},"administrator":{"h":"administrator","i":"/ədˈmɪnɪstreɪtə/","a":"en-us-administrator.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An administrator is a person who takes authority over someone or something.","e":"Congratulations to Max, he is now an administrator of Wiktionary!"}]}]},"disallow":{"h":"disallow","i":"/dɪsəˈlaʊ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-disallow.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you disallow, you do not let it happen; you do not allow this to happen.","e":"Please disallow his request for adminship."}]}]},"popsicle":{"h":"popsicle","i":"/ˈpɒpsɪkl̩/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-popsicle.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A frozen flavored ice or ice cream treat on a stick.","e":"My mother gave me a popsicle."}]}]},"popsicles":{"h":"popsicles","l":"popsicle","q":"noun"},"ferocious":{"h":"ferocious","i":"/fəˈrəʊʃəs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-ferocious.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When someone is ferocious, they are livid, scary or mad.","e":"Tigers are ferocious."}]}]},"scooter":{"h":"scooter","i":"/ˈskuːtə(r)/","a":"en-us-scooter.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A scooter is a child's vehicle that has two wheels and a footboard mostly pushed by the foot. Some scooters are electrical, meaning that they do not need to be pushed."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you scooter, you ride on a [[#Noun|scooter]]."}]}]},"toddler":{"h":"toddler","a":"En-us-toddler.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A toddler is a very young child, about two or three years old."}]}]},"stubborn":{"h":"stubborn","i":"/ˈstʌbɚn/","a":"en-us-stubborn.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Refusing to move or to change one's opinion; obstinate."},{"m":"Hard and not easy to handle.","e":"He is very stubborn about his beliefs."}]}]},"stubborner":{"h":"stubborner","l":"stubborn","q":"adjective"},"stubbornest":{"h":"stubbornest","l":"stubborn","q":"adjective"},"administrators":{"h":"administrators","l":"administrator","q":"noun"},"threatening":{"h":"threatening","i":"/ˈθrɛt.n̩.ɪŋ/","a":"en-us-threatening.ogg","l":"threaten","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Threatening means something is bad or has threat.","e":"She goes around the block threatening to commit suicide."}]}]},"humbug":{"h":"humbug","i":"/ˈhʌmbʌɡ/","a":"en-au-humbug.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A cheat, swindle, or trick.","e":"I was the victim of a humbug."},{"m":"(countable) (Britain) A humbug is a type of hard sweet that is peppermint flavoured with a striped pattern."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To humbug means to cheat, swindle, or trick.","e":"Don't humbug me."}]}]},"humbugged":{"h":"humbugged","l":"humbug","q":"verb"},"humbugging":{"h":"humbugging","i":"/ˈhʌmbʌɡɪŋ/","l":"humbug","q":"verb"},"humbugs":{"h":"humbugs","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"More than one humbug"}]}]},"revulsion":{"h":"revulsion","i":"/rɪˈvʌlʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-revulsion.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Loathing, aversion, disgust, abhorrence.","e":"I was overcome with revulsion when I heard of what happened."}]}]},"lynch":{"h":"lynch","i":"/lɪntʃ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-lynch.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To lynch someone is to hang them and is usually done by a mob of people.","e":"Do not lynch her, it is against the law!"}]}]},"flapjack":{"h":"flapjack","i":"/ˈflæpd͡ʒæk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Flame, not lame-flapjack.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A flapjack is a pancake."}]}]},"mushrooms":{"h":"mushrooms","l":"mushroom","q":"noun"},"baffle":{"h":"baffle","i":"/ˈbæfl̩/","a":"en-us-baffle.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you are baffled by something, it shows that it is confusing.","e":"I am baffled by this puzzle and I cannot solve it."}]}]},"councilman":{"h":"councilman","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A councilman is a male member of a council, usually a city council."}]}]},"marshal":{"h":"marshal","i":"/ˈmɑːʃəl/","a":"en-us-marshall.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A marshal is a kind of law enforcement official in the USA, usually a federal one.","e":"M.N. Harriman was the first law enforcement marshal in Anderson, Indiana."}]}]},"determination":{"h":"determination","i":"/dɪˌtɜːmɪˈneɪʃən/","a":"en-us-determination.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The act of determining, or the state of being determined."},{"m":"Bringing to an end; termination; limit."},{"m":"Direction or tendency to a certain end; impulsion."},{"m":"The quality of mind which reaches definite conclusions; decision of character; resoluteness."},{"m":"(countable) The state of decision; a judicial decision, or ending of controversy."},{"m":"(countable) That which is determined upon; result of deliberation; purpose; conclusion formed; fixed resolution."}]}]},"determinations":{"h":"determinations","l":"determination","q":"noun"},"cha-cha":{"h":"cha-cha","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Cha-cha refers to the famous Latin American dance."}]}]},"attacker":{"h":"attacker","i":"/əˈtækɚ/","a":"en-us-attacker.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An attacker is someone who attacks someone else, usually out of violence.","e":"A hacker is an attacker that tries to enter other people's systems illegally."},{"m":"(countable) An attacker is a player who tries to score goals or points for their own team."}]}]},"attackers":{"h":"attackers","l":"attacker","q":"noun"},"reopen":{"h":"reopen","i":"/riːˈəʊp(ə)n/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-reopen.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you reopen something, you open it again.","e":"The store will reopen tomorrow after being closed for repairs."}]}]},"reopened":{"h":"reopened","l":"reopen","q":"verb"},"reopens":{"h":"reopens","l":"reopen","q":"verb"},"reopening":{"h":"reopening","l":"reopen","q":"verb"},"lynching":{"h":"lynching","i":"/lɪntʃɪŋ/","l":"lynch","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A lynching is an act of violence given to somebody by a mob of people."}]}]},"lynchings":{"h":"lynchings","l":"lynching","q":"noun"},"rumormonger":{"h":"rumormonger","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) If you are a rumormonger, you are a person who spreads or repeats rumors and gossip.","e":"Rumormongers made my campaign for re-election a living hell."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you rumormonger, you spread rumors or gossip.","e":"He rumormongered about the campaign every chance he had."}]}]},"showman":{"h":"showman","i":"/ˈʃəʊ.mən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Flame, not lame-showman.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A showman is a person who organizes a show or theatrical event.","e":"P. T. Barnum was an American showman."}]}]},"impresario":{"h":"impresario","i":"/ˌɪmprɪˈsɑːrɪəʊ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-impresario.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An impresario is a person who organizes shows, theatrical events and performers."}]}]},"provoke":{"h":"provoke","i":"/prəˈvəʊk/","a":"en-us-provoke.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To cause or to bring about a reaction.","e":"Your bad behavior provoked me to drop out of the club."},{"m":"To make angry or to annoy.","e":"Don't provoke your parents into taking away your privileges by behaving badly."}]}]},"devious":{"h":"devious","i":"/ˈdiːvi.əs/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When someone is devious, that person is not honest and frank.","e":"Paul is being devious about the missing funds in the company's reserves, something is not right here."}]}]},"pew":{"h":"pew","i":"/pjuː/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-pew.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bench-like piece of furniture in a house of worship for members of the congregation.","e":"I sat in the front pew of the church for my grandson's wedding."}]}]},"embellish":{"h":"embellish","i":"/ɪmˈbɛlɪʃ/","a":"en-us-embellish.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you embellish something, you decorate it.","e":"The picture frame was embellished with tiny gold angels."}]}]},"shorelands":{"h":"shorelands","l":"shoreland","q":"noun"},"monarchs":{"h":"monarchs","a":"En-us-monarchs.ogg","l":"monarch","q":"noun"},"royalties":{"h":"royalties","l":"royalty","q":"noun"},"minces":{"h":"minces","l":"mince","q":"noun"},"minced":{"h":"minced","l":"mince","q":"verb"},"mincing":{"h":"mincing","l":"mince","q":"verb"},"reverts":{"h":"reverts","l":"revert","q":"verb"},"reverted":{"h":"reverted","l":"revert","q":"verb"},"reverting":{"h":"reverting","l":"revert","q":"verb"},"wrinkles":{"h":"wrinkles","l":"wrinkle","q":"noun"},"duchies":{"h":"duchies","l":"duchy","q":"noun"},"interregnums":{"h":"interregnums","i":"/ˌɪntərˈrɛɡnəmz/","l":"interregnum","q":"noun"},"interregna":{"h":"interregna","i":"/ˌɪntərˈrɛɡnə/","l":"interregnum","q":"noun"},"coachmen":{"h":"coachmen","l":"coachman","q":"noun"},"liveries":{"h":"liveries","l":"livery","q":"noun"},"adoptions":{"h":"adoptions","l":"adoption","q":"noun"},"disloyalties":{"h":"disloyalties","l":"disloyalty","q":"noun"},"kites":{"h":"kites","i":"/kaɪts/","l":"kite","q":"noun"},"bleached":{"h":"bleached","l":"bleach","q":"verb"},"bleaching":{"h":"bleaching","l":"bleach","q":"verb"},"francs":{"h":"francs","l":"franc","q":"noun"},"gravies":{"h":"gravies","l":"gravy","q":"noun"},"lychees":{"h":"lychees","l":"lychee","q":"noun"},"overloaded":{"h":"overloaded","l":"overload","q":"verb"},"overloading":{"h":"overloading","l":"overload","q":"verb"},"overloads":{"h":"overloads","l":"overload","q":"verb"},"colonizations":{"h":"colonizations","l":"colonization","q":"noun"},"gobbledygooks":{"h":"gobbledygooks","l":"gobbledygook","q":"noun"},"patties":{"h":"patties","l":"patty","q":"noun"},"northman":{"h":"Northman","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A person from Scandinavia, especially one who raided into Britain and western Europe between the eighth and eleventh centuries; a Viking.","e":"A common medieval prayer was: \"From the fury of the Northmen deliver us, O Lord.\""}]}]},"northmen":{"h":"Northmen","l":"northman","q":"noun"},"norse":{"h":"Norse","i":"/nors/","a":"en-us-Norse.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Of, or relating to the people, language and culture of Scandinavia."},{"m":"Of, or relating to the North Germanic group of languages."}]},{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"A collective term for Scandinavian (historically Norwegian) people.","e":"His ancestors were Norse."},{"m":"People who speak of any of the North Germanic languages.","e":"He is Norse from his language."},{"m":"The ancient language spoken by Vikings, from which modern Scandinavian languages are derived. Icelandic is the most closely related modern version, having changed little due to Iceland's isolation.","e":"He can speak Old Norse."}]}]},"toddlers":{"h":"toddlers","l":"toddler","q":"noun"},"colonisation":{"h":"colonisation","i":"/ˌkɒl.ə.naɪˈzeɪ.ʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-colonization.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Colonisation is when a new colony is created by a country elsewhere.","e":"The British colonisation in the 17th-18th century made the British Empire one of the largest in the world."}]}]},"colonisations":{"h":"colonisations","l":"colonisation","q":"noun"},"publicize":{"h":"publicize","i":"/ˈpʌblɪˌsaɪz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-publicise.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you publicize something, you make it known to the public.","e":"The trial was publicized for entertainment."}]}]},"publicizes":{"h":"publicizes","l":"publicize","q":"verb"},"publicized":{"h":"publicized","l":"publicize","q":"verb"},"publicizing":{"h":"publicizing","l":"publicize","q":"verb"},"publicise":{"h":"publicise","i":"/ˈpʌblɪˌsaɪz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-publicise.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you publicise something, you make it known to the public.","e":"The trial was publicised for entertainment."}]}]},"publicises":{"h":"publicises","l":"publicise","q":"verb"},"publicised":{"h":"publicised","l":"publicise","q":"verb"},"publicising":{"h":"publicising","l":"publicise","q":"verb"},"lynches":{"h":"lynches","l":"lynch","q":"verb"},"lynched":{"h":"lynched","l":"lynch","q":"verb"},"principality":{"h":"principality","i":"/prɪnsɪˈpælɪti/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A principality is the process of being a ruler, prince, or other person of power."},{"m":"A principality is an area that is ruled by a prince or princess.","e":"Wales was a principality ruled by the son of the English King until it joined England in 1542."},{"m":"A principality is the state of being principal; pre-eminence."}]}]},"principalities":{"h":"principalities","l":"principality","q":"noun"},"princeps":{"h":"princeps","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A princeps can be a leader, first in importance.","e":"William I Longsword was the princeps of Normandy."},{"m":"(countable) A princeps can mean a prince or sovereign."},{"m":"(countable) princeps can mean a chief or director."}]}]},"crews":{"h":"crews","l":"crew","q":"noun"},"jaunts":{"h":"jaunts","l":"jaunt","q":"noun"},"faloodas":{"h":"faloodas","l":"falooda","q":"noun"},"enactments":{"h":"enactments","l":"enactment","q":"noun"},"advisories":{"h":"advisories","l":"advisory","q":"noun"},"greedier":{"h":"greedier","l":"greedy","q":"adjective"},"greediest":{"h":"greediest","l":"greedy","q":"adjective"},"reassigns":{"h":"reassigns","l":"reassign","q":"verb"},"reassigned":{"h":"reassigned","l":"reassign","q":"verb"},"reassigning":{"h":"reassigning","l":"reassign","q":"verb"},"wintrier":{"h":"wintrier","l":"wintry","q":"adjective"},"wintriest":{"h":"wintriest","l":"wintry","q":"adjective"},"reassignment":{"h":"reassignment","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A reassignment is assigning something to someone more than once."}]}]},"reassignments":{"h":"reassignments","l":"reassignment","q":"noun"},"principes":{"h":"principes","l":"princeps","q":"noun"},"maturities":{"h":"maturities","l":"maturity","q":"noun"},"projectiles":{"h":"projectiles","l":"projectile","q":"noun"},"recites":{"h":"recites","l":"recite","q":"verb"},"recited":{"h":"recited","l":"recite","q":"verb"},"reciting":{"h":"reciting","l":"recite","q":"verb"},"tsunamis":{"h":"tsunamis","l":"tsunami","q":"noun"},"angelology":{"h":"angelology","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Angelology is the study of angels.","e":"To begin angelology, you should read the Bible."}]}]},"angelologies":{"h":"angelologies","l":"angelology","q":"noun"},"faithful":{"h":"faithful","i":"/ˈfeɪθ.fəl/","a":"en-us-faithful.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone or something is faithful, they are loyal to a person or cause.","e":"My dog follows me everywhere I go. He is very faithful."},{"m":"If someone is faithful, they have faith in something.","e":"People who go to church are faithful to their God."},{"m":"If someone is faithful, they are able to be relied on; they are able to be trusted.","e":"My assistant does anything I ask him to. He is very faithful to me."},{"m":"If something is faithful, it is close to something real.","e":"That painting is a very faithful copy of the Mona Lisa."},{"m":"If someone is faithful, they have only had sex with their partner; they have not had sex with other people.","e":"They have been faithful to each other since they got married."}]}]},"rescuer":{"h":"rescuer","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A rescuer is someone that rescues someone or something.","e":"The fireman that saved me from that fire was my rescuer."}]}]},"rescuers":{"h":"rescuers","l":"rescuer","q":"noun"},"infectible":{"h":"infectible","i":"/ɪnˈfɛk.tɨ.bəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-infectible.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is infectible, it is able to become infected."}]}]},"diabolic":{"h":"diabolic","i":"/ˌdaɪəˈbɒlɪk/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone or something is diabolic, it shows evil that is usually shown by a devil.","e":"This video game has a diabolic plotline."},{"m":"If someone or something is diabolic, it is very evil or cruel."}]}]},"diabolical":{"h":"diabolical","i":"[ˌdaɪəˈbɒlɪkəɫ]","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-diabolical.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone or something is diabolical, it is very evil or cruel.","e":"That math test was diabolical! I only knew the answers to three of the questions!"},{"m":"If someone or something is diabolical, it is related to the devil; it is satanic."}]}]},"anytime":{"h":"anytime","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"Anytime is any time at all.","e":"I have no plans this weekend; I can paint the house anytime."}]}]},"rainy":{"h":"rainy","i":"/ˈreɪni/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-rainy.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If it is rainy, it is a wet day with rain.","e":"It was a rainy day, so he stayed inside where it was warm and dry."}]}]},"rainier":{"h":"rainier","l":"rainy","q":"adjective"},"rainiest":{"h":"rainiest","l":"rainy","q":"adjective"},"suitable":{"h":"suitable","i":"/ˈsuːtəbl/","a":"en-us-suitable.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something suitable is right for a particular purpose.","e":"He had to find a suitable pair of shoes for running."}]}]},"outbid":{"h":"outbid","i":"/aʊtˈbɪd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-outbid.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To outbid means that one has offered the most money for an object, thus \"outbidding\" one's rivals.","e":"I outbid all those interested in the property."}]}]},"prurient":{"h":"prurient","i":"/ˈprʊər.i.ənt/","a":"en-us-prurient.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is prurient, they are uneasy with desire, usually having to do with lust."},{"m":"If someone is prurient, they appeal to desires of sex."},{"m":"If someone is prurient, they are curious, usually in an inappropriate way."}]}]},"pruriently":{"h":"pruriently","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something is done pruriently, it is done in a prurient way."}]}]},"treaty":{"h":"treaty","i":"/ˈtriː.ti/","a":"en-us-treaty.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A treaty is a formal agreement between two or more states.","e":"Both countries signed the peace treaty."}]}]},"treaties":{"h":"treaties","l":"treaty","q":"noun"},"noble":{"h":"noble","i":"/ˈnəʊbəl/","a":"en-us-noble.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A noble is an aristocrat; a member of the highest social class.","e":"This house was occupied by nobles in the 16th century."},{"m":"(countable) A noble was a medieval gold coin of England in the 14th and 15th centuries, usually valued at 6s 8d."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Noble qualities are those admired by others.","e":"It was very noble of him to defend his friend."}]}]},"nobles":{"h":"nobles","i":"/ˈnoʊbl̩z/","l":"noble","q":"noun"},"tabernacle":{"h":"tabernacle","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Dwelling place, tent"},{"m":"A house of worship"}]}]},"invitation":{"h":"invitation","i":"/ɪn.vɪˈteɪ.ʃən/","a":"en-us-invitation.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) If you receive an invitation, you are being asked to attend an event.","e":"The wedding invitations were mailed a week ago."}]}]},"glimpse":{"h":"glimpse","i":"/ɡlɪmps/","a":"en-us-glimpse.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) When you catch a glimpse of something, you see it only for a moment.","e":"I caught a glimpse of baby as his parents left the hospital."}]}]},"curiosity":{"h":"curiosity","i":"/ˌkjʊərɪˈɒsɪti/","a":"en-us-curiosity.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) When you have a curiosity about something, you have an interest in it.","e":"My curiosity about Prince William's personal life deepens every day."},{"m":"(countable) An unusual or rare object of interest; an oddity","e":"Did you buy that little curiosity at Harrod's?"}]}]},"profitable":{"h":"profitable","i":"/ˈprɑfɪtəbl̩/","a":"en-us-profitable.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is profitable, it means it is money-making or it produces other good results.","e":"Our product was a profitable one for years, and we retired as millionaires."}]}]},"venture":{"h":"venture","i":"/ˈvɛn.t͡ʃɚ/","a":"en-us-venture.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A venture is an undertaking.","e":"My venture into television production was successful."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To venture is to do an."}]}]},"saloon":{"h":"saloon","i":"/səˈlun/","a":"en-us-saloon.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A saloon was a place in the American Old West where you could drink and play cards.","e":"drinks were offered in saloons as well as card games and roulette."}]}]},"likenesses":{"h":"likenesses","l":"likeness","q":"noun"},"resemblance":{"h":"resemblance","i":"/rəzˈɛmbləns/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-resemblance.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A resemblance is something that resembles or looks like something else; likeness."},{"m":"A resemblance is a comparison."}]}]},"resemblances":{"h":"resemblances","l":"resemblance","q":"noun"},"obtainable":{"h":"obtainable","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something or someone is obtainable, it is able to be obtained or gotten.","e":"Finishing the project before the deadline is an obtainable goal."}]}]},"obtainment":{"h":"obtainment","i":"/əbˈteɪn.mənt/","a":"en-us-obtainment.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An obtainment is an act of obtaining something or someone; it is the attaining of something or someone."}]}]},"obtainments":{"h":"obtainments","l":"obtainment","q":"noun"},"fealty":{"h":"fealty","i":"/ˈfiəlti/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Fealty is being loyal to one's lord or superior."}]}]},"fealties":{"h":"fealties","l":"fealty","q":"noun"},"baptisms":{"h":"baptisms","l":"baptism","q":"noun"},"confounder":{"h":"confounder","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A confounder is someone that confounds."}]}]},"confounders":{"h":"confounders","l":"confounder","q":"noun"},"synthetic":{"h":"synthetic","i":"/sɪnˈθetɪk/","a":"en-us-synthetic.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is synthetic, it is artificial, fake, man-made or not genuine."}]}]},"mastermind":{"h":"mastermind","i":"/ˈmɑː.stə.mʌɪnd/","a":"en-us-mastermind.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) If you are the mastermind behind something like a product or concept, you are the genius who creates, manages, or controls it.","e":"Ray Kroc was the mastermind behind the fast food concept."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you mastermind something you create, manage, or control it.","e":"Ray Kroc masterminded the fast foods concept."}]}]},"condescension":{"h":"condescension","i":"/kɑndiˈsɛnʃən/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"If you treat someone with condescension, you are lowering yourself to interact with them.","e":"The salesman treated the buyer with condescension because of their race."}]}]},"scamp":{"h":"scamp","i":"/skæmp/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A scamp is someone who likes mischief and playful tricks.","e":"My six year old son is a scamp. He farts in front of company then runs away laughing."}]}]},"sentiment":{"h":"sentiment","i":"/ˈsɛn.tɪ.mənt/","a":"en-us-sentiment.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (usually plural) Sentiments are thoughts or beliefs that are based on emotion more than on reason.","e":"Her sentiments about that gangster are sorely misplaced."}]}]},"entertainer":{"h":"entertainer","i":"/ɛntəˈteɪnə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-entertainer.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An entertainer is a person who entertains or amuses other people.","e":"There will be many entertainers at the State Fair this year."}]}]},"mourner":{"h":"mourner","i":"/ˈmɔrnɚ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-mourner.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mourner is a person who grieves at a funeral or a burial, or at someone's death.","e":"The mourners left the cemetery before the storm broke."}]}]},"sentiments":{"h":"sentiments","i":"/ˈsɛn.tɪ.mənts/","a":"en-us-sentiments.ogg","l":"sentiment","q":"noun"},"premieres":{"h":"premieres","l":"premiere","q":"noun"},"premiered":{"h":"premiered","l":"premiere","q":"verb"},"premiering":{"h":"premiering","l":"premiere","q":"verb"},"entertainers":{"h":"entertainers","l":"entertainer","q":"noun"},"mourners":{"h":"mourners","l":"mourner","q":"noun"},"showmen":{"h":"showmen","l":"showman","q":"noun"},"impresarios":{"h":"impresarios","l":"impresario","q":"noun"},"scamps":{"h":"scamps","l":"scamp","q":"noun"},"narrative":{"h":"narrative","i":"/ˈnærətɪv/","a":"en-us-narrative.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A narrative tells events in a set order.","e":"This narrative about the Indian capture of an American pioneer woman in the 1800s is thrilling."}]}]},"narratives":{"h":"narratives","l":"narrative","q":"noun"},"elegy":{"h":"elegy","i":"/ˈɛlɪdʒi/","a":"en-uk-elegy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An elegy is a sad poem about death.","e":"This elegy on the death of is very moving."}]}]},"statuette":{"h":"statuette","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A statuette is a small statue.","e":"Put that statuette on the bookcase."}]}]},"elegies":{"h":"elegies","l":"elegy","q":"noun"},"evocation":{"h":"evocation","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An evocation is meant to suggest or bring out something in the imagination."},{"m":"(countable) The calling forth or summoning of a spirit.","e":"The witch's evocation of the evil spirit caused everyone to tremble."}]}]},"caboose":{"h":"caboose","i":"/kəˈbuːs/","a":"en-au-caboose.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A caboose is the last car on a railway train. In past days, they were usually painted a bright red.","e":"I love trains! I always wanted to ride in the caboose when I was a kid!"}]}]},"bunk":{"h":"bunk","i":"/bʌŋk/","a":"en-au-bunk.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bunk is a small bed.","e":"I shared a bunk with my brother at summer cap."},{"m":"(uncountable) Bunk is nonsense.","e":"Your story about getting a million dollar job is a lot of bunk!"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Bunk means to occupy or sleep in a small bed.","e":"Will you bunk with me at baseball camp?"}]}]},"bunkhouse":{"h":"bunkhouse","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bunkhouse is a structure that has many small beds. A bunkhouse can often be found on a western ranch or at a truck stop.","e":"Cowboys sleep in a bunkhouse."}]}]},"intention":{"h":"intention","i":"/ɪnˈtɛnʃən/","a":"en-us-intention.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An intention is a plan to do something.","e":"I have no intention of getting married until I'm thirty."}]}]},"intentions":{"h":"intentions","a":"En-us-intentions.ogg","l":"intention","q":"noun"},"statuettes":{"h":"statuettes","l":"statuette","q":"noun"},"ventures":{"h":"ventures","l":"venture","q":"noun"},"bleaches":{"h":"bleaches","l":"bleach","q":"verb"},"wrinkled":{"h":"wrinkled","i":"/ˈrɪŋkl̩d/","a":"en-us-wrinkled.ogg","l":"wrinkle","q":"verb"},"wrinkling":{"h":"wrinkling","l":"wrinkle","q":"verb"},"cabooses":{"h":"cabooses","l":"caboose","q":"noun"},"bunkhouses":{"h":"bunkhouses","l":"bunkhouse","q":"noun"},"cyclist":{"h":"cyclist","i":"/ˈsaɪ.klɪst/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-cyclist.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cyclist is a person who rides on a bicycle or motorcycle.","e":"The cyclist rode up the hill."}]}]},"cyclists":{"h":"cyclists","l":"cyclist","q":"noun"},"rotunda":{"h":"rotunda","i":"/rə(ʊ)ˈtʌndə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-rotunda.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A rotunda is a circular building (sometimes covered with a dome), or a round room within a building.","e":"The Pantheon is Rome is a rotunda."}]}]},"rotundas":{"h":"rotundas","l":"rotunda","q":"noun"},"aggravate":{"h":"aggravate","i":"/ˈæɡ.rə.veɪ̯t/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Mélange a trois-aggravate.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To aggravate is to make something worse.","e":"The doctor said eating too much would aggravate his condition."}]}]},"aggravates":{"h":"aggravates","l":"aggravate","q":"verb"},"aggravated":{"h":"aggravated","l":"aggravate","q":"verb"},"aggravating":{"h":"aggravating","l":"aggravate","q":"verb"},"son-in-law":{"h":"son-in-law","i":"/ˈsʌnɪnˌlɔː/","a":"en-us-son-in-law.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A son-in-law is the husband of one's daughter or child.","e":"He made his son-in-law a partner in his business."}]}]},"sons-in-law":{"h":"sons-in-law","l":"son-in-law","q":"noun"},"hearty":{"h":"hearty","i":"/ˈhɑrti/","a":"en-us-hearty.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Hearty means to have good health and vigor.","e":"My grandfather was a hearty man who enjoyed outdoor sports."}]}]},"drollery":{"h":"drollery","i":"/ˈdrəʊləri/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-drollery.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Drollery is something that is said or done to cause laughter.","e":"Your drollery is misplaced and unwanted at this funeral."},{"m":"(uncountable) Drollery is an amusing quality in someone or something.","e":"Mr. Crump's drollery is a welcome relief from all this seriousness."}]}]},"genteel":{"h":"genteel","i":"/dʒɛnˈtiːl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-genteel.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Genteel means refined and showing the polite manners and traditions of society.","e":"Crook your pinkie when you drink tea. People will think you have a genteel background."}]}]},"incredulous":{"h":"incredulous","i":"/ɪnˈkrɛdjʊləs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-incredulous.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Incredulous means doubting.","e":"I'm an incredulous person and don't believe your story."},{"m":"Incredulous means too fantastic to be believed or trusted.","e":"Your incredulous story will never be printed in the newspaper."}]}]},"dastardly":{"h":"dastardly","i":"/ˈdɑːstədli/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-dastardly.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Dastardly means to show a lack of courage.","e":"Your dastardly act should cause you great shame!"}]}]},"mountebank":{"h":"mountebank","i":"/ˈmaʊntəˌbæŋk/","a":"en-us-mountebank.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mountebank is a fake, a phony, or someone who claims credentials he does not have, especially in the medical professions.","e":"My doctor is a mountebank."}]}]},"fleet":{"h":"fleet","i":"/fliːt/","a":"en-us-fleet.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A fleet is a large group of something, especially ships and aircraft.","e":"The fleet of warships left port at dawn."}]}]},"constancy":{"h":"constancy","i":"/ˈkɑnstənsi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-constancy.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Constancy is steadfastness, faithfulness, loyalty","e":"His constancy to our cause is heartening."}]}]},"generosity":{"h":"generosity","i":"/ˌd͡ʒɛnəˈrɑsəti/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-generosity.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Generosity is the quality or state of being generous.","e":"His generosity with the lottery winnings made it possible for me to go to college."}]}]},"genial":{"h":"genial","i":"/ˈdʒiːnɪəl/","a":"en-us-genial.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Genial means having a and relaxed manner.","e":"Whipslake Turdley is a genial dinner host."}]}]},"heartier":{"h":"heartier","l":"hearty","q":"adjective"},"heartiest":{"h":"heartiest","l":"hearty","q":"adjective"},"drolleries":{"h":"drolleries","l":"drollery","q":"noun"},"fad":{"h":"fad","i":"/fæd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-fad.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A fad is a brief but popular trend or interest.","e":"Hula hoops were a fad in the 1950s."}]}]},"sparked":{"h":"sparked","l":"spark","q":"verb"},"sparking":{"h":"sparking","l":"spark","q":"verb"},"fads":{"h":"fads","l":"fad","q":"noun"},"constancies":{"h":"constancies","l":"constancy","q":"noun"},"generosities":{"h":"generosities","l":"generosity","q":"noun"},"sportsperson":{"h":"sportsperson","i":"/spɔrtspɝsən/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sportsperson is a man or a woman who practices one or more sports.","e":"Golfers, footballers, swimmers are sportspersons."}]}]},"renew":{"h":"renew","i":"/rɪˈnjuː/","a":"en-us-renew.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Renew means to refresh.","e":"My energies were renewed after taking a nap."},{"m":"Renew means to re-negotiate.","e":"The studio renewed the actor's contract."},{"m":"Renew means to reissue a library book.","e":"Customer: Librarian, may I renew this book for another week?"}]}]},"renews":{"h":"renews","l":"renew","q":"verb"},"renewed":{"h":"renewed","a":"En-us-renewed.ogg","l":"renew","q":"verb"},"renewing":{"h":"renewing","l":"renew","q":"verb"},"veto":{"h":"veto","i":"/ˈviːtəʊ/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A veto is a political right to reject a decision or law."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you veto, you exercise a [[#Noun|veto]] against a decision or law."}]}]},"yacht":{"h":"yacht","i":"/jɑːt/","a":"en-us-yacht.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A yacht is a large boat used mostly for pleasure or racing.","e":"The Queen had a yacht called \"Britannia\"."}]}]},"discharge":{"h":"discharge","i":"/dɪsˈtʃɑːdʒ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-discharge (verb).wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To discharge something is to release it or let it go, especially all at once.","e":"Discharging steam prevented pressure from building."},{"m":"When a gun goes off, it is said to discharge.","e":"He took aim and discharged his gun."},{"m":"When you are discharged, you are allowed to leave.","e":"I was honorably discharged at the end of the war."},{"m":"When a debt or obligation is been met or is ended, it is discharged.","e":"We made the last payment, and the loan was discharged."},{"m":"Discharge is the opposite of charge for things like batteries and reservoirs.","e":"I forgot to plug in my phone and the battery totally discharged."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The act of discharging is also called a discharge.","e":"There was a discharge of steam when he opened the oven door."},{"m":"Something released (in a discharge) is also called a discharge.","e":"The puddle of water was discharge from the pump, not from a leak in the pipe."},{"m":"A discharge is a substance (other than blood) coming from a wound or part of your body, usually because of infection.","e":"There was a discharge coming from the wound."}]}]},"tuition":{"h":"tuition","i":"/tuˈɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-tuition.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Tuition is the money you pay to go to a school, college, university, or educational program.","e":"The tuition to the Lovely Ladies Modeling School is more than I thought it would be."}]}]},"fraternity":{"h":"fraternity","i":"/frəˈtɜː(r)nəti/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-fraternity.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A fraternity is a social organization for men at colleges.","e":"Sigma Chi is a fraternity."}]}]},"callus":{"h":"callus","i":"/ˈkæləs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-callus.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A callus is an area of dry, hardened skin.","e":"A carpenter gets calluses on his hands from using a hammer all the time."}]}]},"polymer":{"h":"polymer","i":"/ˈpɒl.ɨ.mə/","a":"en-us-polymer.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A polymer is a compound made up of many repeated smaller simple monomers. Polymers can be natural or man-made.","e":"is a natural polymer, and nylon is a man-made polymer."}]}]},"eulogy":{"h":"eulogy","i":"/ˈjuːlədʒi/","a":"en-uk-eulogy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A eulogy is a speech, or writing, which praises someone who has died.","e":"Writing an eulogy isn't easy."}]}]},"calluses":{"h":"calluses","l":"callus","q":"noun"},"eulogies":{"h":"eulogies","l":"eulogy","q":"noun"},"polymers":{"h":"polymers","l":"polymer","q":"noun"},"monomer":{"h":"monomer","i":"/ˈmɒnəmə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-monomer.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A monomer is a simple compound that can join with others to make a polymer.","e":"is a monomer."}]}]},"monomers":{"h":"monomers","l":"monomer","q":"noun"},"cellulose":{"h":"cellulose","i":"/ˈsɛljʊləʊz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-cellulose.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Cellulose is a polymer made up of glucose, which makes the walls of plant cells.","e":"Cellulose is used to make paper and cellophane."}]}]},"cellophane":{"h":"cellophane","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Cellophane is a clear, flexible, material made from cellulose. It is used to wrap up things to keep them dry.","e":"I bought a box of cigarettes which were covered in cellophane."}]}]},"cellophanes":{"h":"cellophanes","l":"cellophane","q":"noun"},"cobbler":{"h":"cobbler","i":"/ˈkɒblə/","a":"en-us-cobbler.oga","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cobbler is a person who makes and repairs shoes."},{"m":"(countable) A cobbler is a type of dessert made with fruit."}]}]},"filicide":{"h":"filicide","i":"/ˈfɪ.lɪ.sʌɪd/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Filicide is when a person kills their own child.","e":"A psychological overview of filicide - the murder of his family by a father."}]}]},"ogle":{"h":"ogle","i":"/ˈəʊɡəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-ogle.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you ogle, you stare at someone with sex on one's mind.","e":"The man on the bench in the shopping mall ogled the young female shoppers as they passed."}]}]},"rife":{"h":"rife","i":"/raɪf/","a":"en-us-rife.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If x is rife with y, then y is common or widespread in x, especially when y is unpleasant or bad.","e":"is rife in big city slums."}]}]},"sweetheart":{"h":"sweetheart","i":"/ˈswiːtˌhɑːt/","a":"en-us-sweetheart.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sweetheart is someone you love in a romantic way.","e":"My sweetheart gave me a box of candy on Valentine's Day."}]}]},"adultery":{"h":"adultery","i":"/əˈdʌltəri/","a":"en-us-adultery.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Adultery is the act of having sex between a married person and someone who is not that person's wife or husband.","e":"He found out that his wife had committed adultery and divorced her."}]}]},"elector":{"h":"elector","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An elector is someone that can vote in an election.","e":"The elections are coming soon, please do not forget to register yourself as an elector."},{"m":"In the history of Germany an elector was a prince or archbishop who had the right to vote for the emperor who ruled over the.","e":"The Archbishop of Mainz was an elector in 1340."},{"m":"In the United States, an elector is a delegate who has the right to vote in the for the.","e":"Bob was an elector in the last presidential election."}]}]},"electors":{"h":"electors","l":"elector","q":"noun"},"assimilate":{"h":"assimilate","i":"/əˈsɪm.ɪ.leɪt/","a":"en-us-assimilate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To assimilate is to mix with other people, to absorb into their community."}]}]},"libertine":{"h":"libertine","i":"/ˈlɪb.ə.tiːn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-libertine.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A libertine is someone (usually a man) who has no regard for the morals of his time, especially sexual morals.","e":"Don Juan is the classic libertine."}]}]},"rake":{"h":"rake","i":"/reɪk/","a":"en-us-rake.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A rake is a garden tool used to gather leaves, grass clippings, and other garden debris.","e":"He mowed the grass, then used a rake to gather the clippings."},{"m":"(countable) A rake is someone (usually a man) who has little regard for morals, especially sexual morals.","e":"Don Juan was a rake."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you rake something, you use a [[#Noun|rake]] on something, such as leaves, in order to loosen or gather them together.","e":"We raked all the leaves into a pile."}]}]},"analytic":{"h":"analytic","i":"/ˌænəˈlɪtɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-analytic.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is analytic, that person has the ability to analyze."}]}]},"analytical":{"h":"analytical","i":"/ˌæn.əˈlɪt.ɪ.kəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-analytical.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When someone is analytical, that person is skilled in using analysis."},{"m":"An analytical method or technique breaks down an object or idea into its smaller parts.","e":"The old analytical approach to science was done, and a new approach is needed."}]}]},"analytically":{"h":"analytically","i":"/æn.əˈlɪt.ɪk.əl.li/","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"When someone studies something analytically, that person studies it in an analytical manner."}]}]},"precious":{"h":"precious","i":"/ˈprɛʃəs/","a":"en-us-precious.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is precious, it is something that you have a fond affection for."},{"m":"When something is precious, it has a high worth or cost."}]}]},"repent":{"h":"repent","i":"/rɪˈpɛnt/","a":"en-us-repent.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) In religion, repent means to be sorry for one's sins and to seek forgiveness; to regret one's sins and to start a better life based on religious principles.","e":"I repent my sins and ask forgiveness."},{"m":"Repent means to regret","e":"I repent skipping school last week."}]}]},"appeasement":{"h":"appeasement","i":"/əˈpɪiz.mənt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-appeasement.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Appeasement is to be appeased and is the policy of giving in to demands in the hope of maintaining peace.","e":"Both Britain and France adopted the appeasement policy towards Germany hoping that war can be avoided."}]}]},"twerk":{"h":"twerk","i":"/twɛrk/","a":"en-au-twerk.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Twerk is a kind of dance where the dancer rapidly moves or shakes their buttocks, especially while bent down with their buttocks."}]}]},"poo":{"h":"poo","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Poo refers to the feces produced from the anus."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(childish) When you poo, you take a shit, to defecate."}]}]},"birch":{"h":"birch","i":"/bɝtʃ/","a":"en-us-birch.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A birch is a tree or shrub of the genus, comprising species with a smooth, laminated outer bark and close-grained wood."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you birch a person, you punish them with a rod made of [[#Noun|birch]] wood."}]}]},"clawed":{"h":"clawed","l":"claw","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is clawed, it has a claw."}]}]},"seduction":{"h":"seduction","i":"/sɪˈdʌk.ʃn̩/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-seduction.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Seduction is process of.","e":"The villain in the play used seduction to ruin the helpless young maid."}]}]},"anglophone":{"h":"Anglophone","i":"/ˈæŋɡləˌfəʊn/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A person who can speak the English language."}]}]},"fremescent":{"h":"fremescent","i":"/frɪˈmɛsənt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-fremescent.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"ing and roaring.","e":"The dog was becoming fremescent."}]}]},"tonic":{"h":"tonic","i":"/ˈtɒnɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-tonic.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A drink that supposedly can make you stronger.","e":"Ben wanted bigger muscles, so he drank a glass of Beauregard's strength tonic"},{"m":"Tonic water, a drink made with quinine that is used in cocktails","e":"Devon went to the bar and ordered a gin and tonic"},{"m":"The keynote of a song (the note that says what other notes will be sharp or flat)"}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Pertaining to the keynote of a song"}]}]},"tonics":{"h":"tonics","l":"tonic","q":"noun"},"extort":{"h":"extort","i":"/ɪkˈstɔː(r)t/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-extort.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you extort a person, you threaten to hurt or kill them unless they give you something, such as money or information","e":"The criminals extorted $300 from Jack in a dark alley."}]}]},"extorts":{"h":"extorts","l":"extort","q":"verb"},"extorted":{"h":"extorted","l":"extort","q":"verb"},"extorting":{"h":"extorting","l":"extort","q":"verb"},"threaten":{"h":"threaten","i":"/ˈθrɛt.n̩/","a":"en-us-threaten.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To make a threat against someone; to say that you are going to do something harmful to that person","e":"After Joe ran off with Fred's wife, Fred threatened to kill him."}]}]},"threatens":{"h":"threatens","l":"threaten","q":"verb"},"threatened":{"h":"threatened","i":"/ˈθrɛt.n̩d/","a":"en-us-threatened.ogg","l":"threaten","q":"verb"},"harmful":{"h":"harmful","i":"/ˈhɑrmfl̩/","a":"en-us-harmful.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that causes harm, something that can cause injury, damage, or loss."}]}]},"euphemism":{"h":"euphemism","i":"/ˈjuː.fəˌmɪ.z(ə)m/","a":"en-us-euphemism.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Euphemism is the substitution of a mild, indirect, or vague expression for one thought to be offensive, harsh, or blunt."},{"m":"(countable) An euphemism is a word or a phrase used to replace another to make it less offensive.","e":"\"To pass away” is a euphemism for \"to die\"."}]}]},"euphemisms":{"h":"euphemisms","l":"euphemism","q":"noun"},"magnify":{"h":"magnify","i":"/ˈmaɡnɪfaɪ/","a":"en-au-magnify.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you magnify something, you make it bigger, or you make it seem bigger.","e":"I need to magnify the words in my book because the letters are too small."}]}]},"magnifies":{"h":"magnifies","l":"magnify","q":"verb"},"magnified":{"h":"magnified","l":"magnify","q":"verb"},"magnifying":{"h":"magnifying","l":"magnify","q":"verb"},"magnifiable":{"h":"magnifiable","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is magnifiable, it can be."}]}]},"resistance":{"h":"resistance","i":"/rɪˈzɪstəns/","a":"en-us-resistance.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Resistance is the act of something, usually to oppose a change."},{"m":"Resistance is the amount of force pushing against an object.","e":"As I run, the resistance of the air slows me down by a bit, making it harder for me to run faster."},{"m":"Resistance is electrical resistance, which is the opposition to the flow of an electrical current."},{"m":"A resistance is an illegal organization that tries to use force to fight for freedom and human rights."}]}]},"resistances":{"h":"resistances","l":"resistance","q":"noun"},"gooses":{"h":"gooses","l":"goose","q":"verb"},"goosed":{"h":"goosed","l":"goose","q":"verb"},"goosing":{"h":"goosing","l":"goose","q":"verb"},"hayride":{"h":"hayride","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hayride is a ride in a wagon filled with hay. It is typically held in the evenings around Halloween for a group of people who tell stories, sing, drink cider, et cetera.","e":"We took a hayride around Old MacDonald's farm looking for ghosts."}]}]},"refrain":{"h":"refrain","i":"/rɪˈfreɪn/","a":"en-us-refrain.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A refrain is part of a song. It is also called the chorus. The words (lyrics) of the refrain are the same words sung over and over after each verse in the song.","e":"I don't know the words but I can hum along during the refrain."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To refrain means to control or hold back.","e":"Stop making jokes! Will you refrain yourself?"}]}]},"anglophones":{"h":"Anglophones","l":"anglophone","q":"noun"},"refrains":{"h":"refrains","l":"refrain","q":"noun"},"refrained":{"h":"refrained","l":"refrain","q":"verb"},"refraining":{"h":"refraining","l":"refrain","q":"verb"},"hayrides":{"h":"hayrides","l":"hayride","q":"noun"},"cider":{"h":"cider","i":"/ˈsaɪ̯.dɚ/","a":"en-us-cider.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A beverage made from the juice of apples or other fruit. It often, but not always, is alcoholic.","e":"At the harvest dance, everybody drank a mug of cider."}]}]},"ciders":{"h":"ciders","l":"cider","q":"noun"},"tabernacles":{"h":"tabernacles","l":"tabernacle","q":"noun"},"worship":{"h":"worship","i":"/ˈwɜːʃɪp/","a":"en-us-worship.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"or devotion to a god or other higher power."},{"m":"The things you do to show that belief or devotion."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To participate in religious services.","e":"Methodists worship God by praying and singing hymns."}]}]},"worships":{"h":"worships","l":"worship","q":"noun"},"worshiped":{"h":"worshiped","l":"worship","q":"verb"},"worshiping":{"h":"worshiping","l":"worship","q":"verb"},"obsequious":{"h":"obsequious","i":"/əbˈsiːkwi.əs/","a":"en-us-obsequious.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are obsequious, you are obedient."},{"m":"An obsequious person likes to please people or to obey instructions excessively."}]}]},"dipstick":{"h":"dipstick","i":"/ˈdɪpstɪk/","a":"en-au-dipstick.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A dipstick is a tool. The most familiar dipstick is the one used to measure the amount of oil in a car's engine. Another dipstick is made of litmus paper. It is dipped into urine to test for ketosis."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you dipstick a person, you check their understanding of something."},{"m":"(engineering) If you dipstick a car, you measure the level of a fluid using a [[#Noun|dipstick]]."}]}]},"shrug":{"h":"shrug","i":"/ʃrʌɡ/","a":"En-us-shrug.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you shrug your shoulders, you raise and then lower them in order to say you do not know or are not interested.","e":"Where's Dad?\" \"How should I know?\" replied my brother, shrugging."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A shrug is the action of raising your shoulders and then lowering them in order to say you don't know or are not interested.","e":"Liam responded with an uninterested shrug."}]}]},"gem":{"h":"gem","a":"En-us-gem.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A gem is a piece of mineral that is used in jewelry because it looks pretty."},{"m":"A gem is anything beautiful, even if it is not a rock or mineral.","e":"Randy Johnson's one-hitter against the Padres was a gem of a game."}]}]},"gems":{"h":"gems","l":"gem","q":"noun"},"jewelry":{"h":"jewelry","i":"/ˈʤuː.əl.ri/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-jewellery.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(usually uncountable) Things that you wear such as rings, necklaces, brooches and bracelets, made of metals and sometimes with valuable gemstones."}]}]},"ski":{"h":"ski","i":"/skiː/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-ski.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A ski is a long piece of wood, metal or other material designed so a person who wears them on his feet can quickly move through snow"},{"m":"(countable) A ski is one of a pair of long flat runners under an airplane that are used for landing on snow."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you ski, you travel through snow on skis","e":"I skied down the hill at Green Diamond Lodge"}]}]},"runway":{"h":"runway","i":"/ˈrʌnweɪ/","a":"en-us-runway.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A runway is a roadway where an airplane takes off or lands."}]}]},"runways":{"h":"runways","l":"runway","q":"noun"},"expressway":{"h":"expressway","i":"/eksˈprɛs.weɪ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Persent101-expressway.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An expressway is a large road of two or more lanes in each direction designed for cars to travel quickly."}]}]},"expressways":{"h":"expressways","l":"expressway","q":"noun"},"macaroni":{"h":"macaroni","i":"/mak.əˈrəʊ.ni/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-macaroni.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Macaroni is a type of curved pasta.","e":"He had macaroni and cheese for dinner."}]}]},"serum":{"h":"serum","i":"/ˈsɪərəm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-serum.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Serum is any clear liquid from an animal or plant"}]}]},"footprint":{"h":"footprint","i":"/ˈfʊtprɪnt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-footprint.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mark made in something by the foot"},{"m":"(uncountable) The impact that a famous or notable person makes on a specific field.","e":"The star left her footprint on the Hollywood Walk of Fame."}]}]},"footprints":{"h":"footprints","l":"footprint","q":"noun"},"max":{"h":"max","i":"/mæks/","a":"en-us-max.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A common shortening of the word maximum."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To reach the maximum.","e":"John maxed out his credit cards to get his business started."}]}]},"skis":{"h":"skis","l":"ski","q":"noun"},"skied":{"h":"skied","l":"ski","q":"verb"},"skiing":{"h":"skiing","i":"/ˈski.ɪŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-skiing.wav","l":"ski","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Skiing is a sport where people race each other on skis through snow"}]}]},"skier":{"h":"skier","i":"/ˈskiːə(r)/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-skier.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A skier is a person who skis.","e":"Steve moved to Aspen because he was a good skier and liked to ski every weekend."}]}]},"skiers":{"h":"skiers","l":"skier","q":"noun"},"allege":{"h":"allege","i":"/əˈlɛdʒ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-allege.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you allege something, you claim that it happened, even if it might not have. Usually, the word \"allege\" is used with doing something wrong.","e":"John alleged that Joe dragged him out of his car and beat him."}]}]},"alleges":{"h":"alleges","l":"allege","q":"verb"},"alleged":{"h":"alleged","i":"/əˈlɛdʒd/","a":"en-us-alleged.ogg","l":"allege","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A person is alleged if it is claimed that they did something that may or may not be true","e":"Alleged criminal."}]}]},"alleging":{"h":"alleging","l":"allege","q":"verb"},"interchange":{"h":"interchange","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An interchange is where two freeways connect with each other with ramps.","e":"Interstate 5 connects to Routes 22 and 57 at the Orange Crush Interchange"}]}]},"interchanges":{"h":"interchanges","l":"interchange","q":"noun"},"intersection":{"h":"intersection","i":"/ˈɪntərˌsɛkʃən/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An intersection is where two or more streets meet and cross."}]}]},"intersections":{"h":"intersections","l":"intersection","q":"noun"},"stifle":{"h":"stifle","i":"/ˈstaɪfl̩/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-stifle.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you stifle a good thing, you keep it from continuing.","e":"The traditions at the company stifle the change we need."}]}]},"malaria":{"h":"malaria","i":"/məˈlɛə.ri.ə/","a":"en-us-malaria.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Malaria is a sickness found mostly in Africa and is caused by mosquitoes","e":"The family was saved from getting malaria because of mosquito nets given to them"}]}]},"mew":{"h":"mew","i":"/mjuː/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-mew.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An old word for prison or a cage"}]}]},"liqueur":{"h":"liqueur","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An alcoholic drink that is flavored and made sweet.","e":"I used a cherry liqueur in the cake"}]}]},"patent":{"h":"patent","i":"/ˈpætənt/","a":"en-uk-patent.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A patent is a way of protecting an invention from being stolen.","e":"Thomas Edison had over 2000 patents."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To patent means to get a patent on an invention","e":"Thomas Edison patented the light bulb and the phonograph."}]}]},"phonograph":{"h":"phonograph","i":"/ˈfəʊnəˌɡrɑːf/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-phonograph.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A phonograph is an old way of playing recorded music.","e":"The phonograph was replaced by CDs and tapes in the 1980s."}]}]},"catarrh":{"h":"catarrh","i":"/kəˈtɑr/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-catarrh.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Puffiness in the nose and throat caused by illness.","e":"He was out of work for a week because of catarrhs"}]}]},"patents":{"h":"patents","l":"patent","q":"noun"},"patented":{"h":"patented","l":"patent","q":"verb"},"patenting":{"h":"patenting","l":"patent","q":"verb"},"turnpike":{"h":"turnpike","i":"/ˈtɜː(r)npaɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-turnpike.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A turnpike is a road (now usually a freeway) that charges tolls for use."},{"m":"(countable) A turnpike is also the gate placed in a road to stop travellers until they pay tolls."}]}]},"turnpikes":{"h":"turnpikes","l":"turnpike","q":"noun"},"soda":{"h":"soda","i":"/ˈsəʊdə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-soda.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Soda is the chemical compound (also known as baking soda)"},{"m":"(uncountable) Soda is carbonated water."},{"m":"Soda is a drink that is sweet and contains carbonated water."},{"m":"Soda is a bottle, can or glass of a soft drink.","e":"Jimmy went to the lunch counter and ordered a soda."}]}]},"sodas":{"h":"sodas","l":"soda","q":"noun"},"maxes":{"h":"maxes","l":"max","q":"noun"},"maxed":{"h":"maxed","l":"max","q":"verb"},"maxing":{"h":"maxing","l":"max","q":"verb"},"reimburse":{"h":"reimburse","i":"/ˌriːɪmˈbɜː(r)s/","a":"en-us-reimburse.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you reimburse someone, you give money back to the person, usually as a compensation.","e":"Acme Inc. reimbursed Joe for his business trip to Calcutta."}]}]},"remuneration":{"h":"remuneration","i":"/rɪˌmjuːnəˈreɪʃən/","a":"en-au-remuneration.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A remuneration is a reward for providing goods or services","e":"Having led the company to become listed in the NASDAQ stock market, I was given a remuneration by the company."}]}]},"necklace":{"h":"necklace","i":"/ˈnɛkləs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-necklace.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A necklace is a piece of jewelry that is worn around the neck. Usually, it is a string of metal, gems or beads.","e":"Stephanie's necklace consisted of a series of gold bands and a large diamond."},{"m":"(uncountable) Necklace can also be the name given to an item that is shaped like a necklace.","e":"The Emerald Necklace is a series of parks in"}]}]},"necklaces":{"h":"necklaces","l":"necklace","q":"noun"},"reimburses":{"h":"reimburses","l":"reimburse","q":"verb"},"reimbursed":{"h":"reimbursed","l":"reimburse","q":"verb"},"reimbursing":{"h":"reimbursing","l":"reimburse","q":"verb"},"adjuration":{"h":"adjuration","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An adjuration can be a serious promise.","e":"We made an adjuration never to leave one another."},{"m":"An adjuration can be a serious piece of advice.","e":"My friend's adjuration was to change jobs before the situation worsened."}]}]},"solemn":{"h":"solemn","i":"/ˈsɒləm/","a":"en-us-solemn.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When an event is solemn, it is very serious and dignified."}]}]},"grin":{"h":"grin","i":"/grɪn/","a":"en-us-grin.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A grin is a small smile, or a smile where you can see the teeth."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you grin, you smile a little bit, or with your teeth visible."}]}]},"grins":{"h":"grins","l":"grin","q":"noun"},"grinned":{"h":"grinned","l":"grin","q":"verb"},"grinning":{"h":"grinning","a":"En-us-grinning.ogg","l":"grin","q":"verb"},"adjurations":{"h":"adjurations","l":"adjuration","q":"noun"},"intonation":{"h":"intonation","i":"/ɪntɵˈneɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-intonation.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Intonation is act of or chanting.","e":"I could hear the intonations of the priest in the church."},{"m":"Intonation is the rise and fall in the pitch of a voice.","e":"I could tell from his intonation that he was a German speaker."},{"m":"Intonation is the ability to play or sing a musical note in tune.","e":"He needed to work on his intonation as he was often out of tune on the higher notes."}]}]},"intonations":{"h":"intonations","l":"intonation","q":"noun"},"intone":{"h":"intone","i":"/ɪnˈtoʊn/","a":"en-us-intone.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"Intone is to sing, chant or recite without many changes in pitch.","e":"I could hear the priest intone the prayer."},{"m":"To intone is to sing the opening phrase of a plainsong."},{"m":"To intone is to speak carefully, choosing a particular pitch or changes of pitch.","e":"He intoned the bad news in a slow, sad way."}]}]},"intones":{"h":"intones","l":"intone","q":"verb"},"intoned":{"h":"intoned","l":"intone","q":"verb"},"intoning":{"h":"intoning","l":"intone","q":"verb"},"plainsong":{"h":"plainsong","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Plainsong is medieval religious music, sung in unison without instruments. It is also called Gregorian chant.","e":"The monks sang plainsong during the service in the church."}]}]},"plainsongs":{"h":"plainsongs","l":"plainsong","q":"noun"},"chant":{"h":"chant","i":"/tʃɑːnt/","a":"en-us-chant.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To chant is to sing or recite in a simple, rhythmic way.","e":"The crowd at the cricket game began to chant \"Aussie Aussie Aussie, Oi Oi Oi\"."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A chant is a simple repeated phrase."}]}]},"chants":{"h":"chants","l":"chant","q":"verb"},"chanted":{"h":"chanted","l":"chant","q":"verb"},"chanting":{"h":"chanting","l":"chant","q":"verb"},"thermal":{"h":"thermal","i":"/ˈθɝməl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-thermal.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Thermal is about, or using, heat.","e":"He swam in the thermal pool."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A thermal is a rising mass of warm air.","e":"We could see the bird soaring in the thermal."}]}]},"thermals":{"h":"thermals","l":"thermal","q":"noun"},"cold-hearted":{"h":"cold-hearted","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When someone is cold-hearted, that person does not have any sympathy or feeling of warmth. Usually used to imply that a person is cruel and heartless."}]}]},"warm-hearted":{"h":"warm-hearted","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When someone is warm-hearted, that person is sympathetic and kind."},{"m":"Someone that is friendly, cordial and generous."}]}]},"warm-heartedly":{"h":"warm-heartedly","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"When someone behaves warm-heartedly, it is in a warm-hearted, considerate or friendly manner."}]}]},"rhapsodic":{"h":"rhapsodic","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something rhapsodic is filled with great pleasure and delight."}]}]},"autodidact":{"h":"autodidact","i":"/ˌɔːtoʊˈdaɪdækt/","a":"en-us-autodidact.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An autodidact is a person who has taught himself or herself a particular subject."}]}]},"autodidacts":{"h":"autodidacts","l":"autodidact","q":"noun"},"reciprocity":{"h":"reciprocity","i":"/ˌrɛsəˈprɑsəti/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-reciprocity.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Reciprocity is a relationship in which a something is given, and something is expected back in return."},{"m":"(uncountable) Reciprocity is a relationship which means quid pro quo or \"fair trade\".","e":"You scratch my back, and I'll scratch your back: that's reciprocity."}]}]},"reciprocities":{"h":"reciprocities","l":"reciprocity","q":"noun"},"antarctic":{"h":"Antarctic","i":"/ænˈtɑː(k)tɪk/","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"The Antarctic, is the area around the south pole."}]}]},"advertiser":{"h":"advertiser","i":"/ˈædvə(r)ˌtaɪzə(r)/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-advertiser.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An advertiser is a person or a company that tells the public about a product or a service, usually on TV, the Internet, newspapers, etc., to make them to buy it or know about it."}]}]},"applicable":{"h":"applicable","i":"/ˈæplɪkəbəl/","a":"en-us-applicable.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is applicable, it is related or applies to the person or situation.","e":"Please complete all applicable sections of this form."}]}]},"blacken":{"h":"blacken","i":"/ˈblækən/","a":"en-us-blacken.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When something is blackened, it is made darker."},{"m":"(transitive) Blackened meat or fish is seasoned in spices, mostly in Cajun cooking."}]}]},"employable":{"h":"employable","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When a person is employable, they have the skills that a job needs."}]}]},"grandma":{"h":"grandma","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Grandma (informal for grandmother) is the mother of your father or mother."}]}]},"brit":{"h":"Brit","i":"/brɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Brit.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A Brit is a citizen of Britain."}]}]},"christendom":{"h":"Christendom","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"All the Christian people or countries in the world are a part of Christendom."}]}]},"rewrite":{"h":"rewrite","i":"/riːˈraɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-rewrite (verb).wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you rewrite something that has been written, you change it to improve it or to add new information."}]}]},"outbreak":{"h":"outbreak","a":"En-us-outbreak.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) If there is an outbreak, a disease suddenly appears in an area and spreads.","e":"It was the first measles outbreak in the area in thirty years."},{"m":"(countable) If there is an outbreak of something, it suddenly increases.","e":"There's been a recent outbreak of broken windows in the street."}]}]},"unaffected":{"h":"unaffected","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something or someone is unaffected by something, they are not changed by it.","e":"He was unaffected by the change in weather and continued to walk as it started to rain."}]}]},"handwritten":{"h":"handwritten","i":"/ˌhandˈrɪtn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-handwritten.wav","l":"handwrite","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is handwritten, it was done with a writing tool (such as a pen or a pencil) onto a piece of paper.","e":"Her essay was handwritten."}]}]},"unpack":{"h":"unpack","i":"/ʌnˈpæk/","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To unpack something means to remove items from a package or container, usually referring to a bag or a luggage.","e":"The first thing you should do once you arrive home from camping is to unpack your bags."}]}]},"selfish":{"h":"selfish","i":"/ˈsɛlf.ɪʃ/","a":"en-us-selfish.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When someone is selfish, that person regards himself/herself as the standard in making decisions.","e":"John is very selfish and only thinks about himself."}]}]},"heater":{"h":"heater","i":"/ˈhitɚ/","a":"en-us-heater.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A heater is a machine that makes air or water hotter."}]}]},"brownie":{"h":"brownie","i":"/ˈbraʊni/","a":"EN-AU ck1 brownie.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A brownie is a small, short, chocolate cake that is often cut into squares and sometimes contains nuts.","e":"There was a plate of fresh brownies on the kitchen table."}]}]},"macho":{"h":"macho","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone or something is macho, they are tough, strong, and like the traditional idea of a man.","e":"He always tried to be the most macho man in any room."}]}]},"machismo":{"h":"machismo","i":"/mɑːˈtʃiz.moʊ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-machismo.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Machismo is an exaggerated way of being a man by being tough and virile.","e":"In an action movie I expect the hero will show machismo."}]}]},"kilo":{"h":"kilo","i":"/ˈkiːləʊ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-kilo.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Kilo is an abbreviation of kilogram (also kg).","e":"After my diet, I had lost a kilo."},{"m":"(countable) Kilo is an abbreviation of kilometer (also km).","e":"After walking for ten minutes, I had gone one kilo."}]}]},"brownies":{"h":"brownies","l":"brownie","q":"noun"},"habitual":{"h":"habitual","i":"/həˈbɪtʃuəl/","a":"en-us-habitual.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A habitual behaviour is done regularly, often without planning or making a decision to it.","e":"In our changing world, the old habitual ways of doing business will not work any more."}]}]},"kilos":{"h":"kilos","l":"kilo","q":"noun"},"relativity":{"h":"relativity","i":"/rɛləˈtɪvɪti/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-relativity.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Relativity is the connection between time, space, and movement in the universe."}]}]},"vibration":{"h":"vibration","i":"/vaɪˈbreɪʃən/","a":"en-us-vibration.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A vibration is a fast motion back and forth such as an earthquake, sound, or the motion of a motor."},{"m":"(countable) If someone feels a good or bad vibration, they feel that the social situation is good or bad."}]}]},"podcast":{"h":"podcast","i":"/ˈpɒdkɑːst/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-podcast.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A podcast is a series of related digital files (music, talk, or video) that are placed on the internet at regular times."}]}]},"festival":{"h":"festival","i":"/ˈfɛstɪv(ə)l/","a":"en-us-festival.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A festival is an organized event that contains a number of performances and usually happens every year.","e":"Many actors are in town for the Toronto international film festival."},{"m":"(countable) A festival is a period of celebration that marks a special occasion, often religious traditions.","e":"Next week our town celebrates the annual winter festival."}]}]},"butterfly":{"h":"butterfly","i":"/ˈbʌtə(r)flaɪ/","a":"en-ca-butterfly.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A butterfly is an insect with large, often colourful wings."}]}]},"campus":{"h":"campus","i":"/ˈkæmpəs/","a":"en-us-campus.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A campus is the grounds and the building(s) of a college or university."}]}]},"vibrations":{"h":"vibrations","l":"vibration","q":"noun"},"additive":{"h":"additive","i":"/ˈæ.dɪ.tɪv/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-additive.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An additive is a substance which is added to another substance to improve its quality."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is additive, it involves addition."}]}]},"ageless":{"h":"ageless","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is ageless, it does not get old or go out of style."}]}]},"americanized":{"h":"Americanized","l":"americanize","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something is Americanized, it has been influenced by the United States of America."}]}]},"unemployed":{"h":"unemployed","i":"/ˌʌnɪmˈplɔɪd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-unemployed.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is unemployed, they want to work but do not have a job."}]}]},"businesswoman":{"h":"businesswoman","i":"/ˈbɪznəswʊmən/","a":"en-us-businesswoman.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A businesswoman is a woman whose profession is business."}]}]},"activism":{"h":"activism","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Activism is the process of people working to change a specific social or political issue, often through protest."}]}]},"convict":{"h":"convict","i":"/kənˈvɪkt/","a":"en-us-convict-verb.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If a judge or a jury convicts someone, they officially decide the person is guilty of a crime.","e":"If he is convicted of all charges, he is facing between eight and 25 years in prison."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A convict is a person who has been found guilty of a crime and received a jail sentence."}]}]},"ageist":{"h":"ageist","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An ageist is someone who discriminates against others due to their age."}]}]},"approachable":{"h":"approachable","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are approachable you are a friendly and welcoming person that other people feel comfortable talking to."}]}]},"sociable":{"h":"sociable","i":"/ˈsoʊʃəbəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-sociable.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A sociable person is friendly and likes to be with other people."}]}]},"unanswerable":{"h":"unanswerable","i":"/ʌnˈɑːnsərəb(ə)l/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"An unanswerable question cannot be answered; it does not have a solution."}]}]},"drinker":{"h":"drinker","i":"/ˈdrɪŋkə(r)/","a":"en-au-drinker.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A drinker is a person who drinks alcohol regularly, and sometimes drinks too much of it."},{"m":"(countable) A coffee drinker drinks coffee regularly; a tea drinker drinks tea regularly."}]}]},"documentary":{"h":"documentary","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A documentary is a type of movie or TV program that gives real information about a specific topic or event."}]}]},"infant":{"h":"infant","i":"/ˈɪn.fənt/","a":"En-us-infant.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An infant is a newborn or a baby; a young child in the first stage of their life."}]}]},"forbearance":{"h":"forbearance","i":"/fɔrbεrəns/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Naomi Persephone Amethyst (NaomiAmethyst)-forbearance.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) If you say that someone has shown forbearance, you admire them for behaving in a calm and sensible way about something that they have a right to be very upset or angry about.","e":"His unfailing forbearance under great provocation shocked me."}]}]},"creature":{"h":"creature","i":"/ˈkriːt͡ʃə/","a":"en-us-creature.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A creature is a large animal, especially a created (mythical) nonhuman.","e":"Those creatures only come out at night."}]}]},"caller":{"h":"caller","i":"/ˈkɔːlə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-caller.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A caller is a person making a call, usually over the phone.","e":"The operator gave directions to the caller."}]}]},"divider":{"h":"divider","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A divider is an object or person that stands between two things.","e":"I use a divider in my notebook for my subjects."}]}]},"unopened":{"h":"unopened","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"An unopened object can be opened but it has not been opened.","e":"I was holding the unopened can of tuna while looking for a can-opener."}]}]},"roomy":{"h":"roomy","i":"/ˈruːmi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-roomy.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A spacious or large enclosure is often referred to as roomy.","e":"That one-bedroom basement apartment was very roomy."}]}]},"ophiolatry":{"h":"ophiolatry","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The love of snakes"}]}]},"gyneolatry":{"h":"gyneolatry","i":"/ˌdʒaɪniˈɒlətri/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Gyneolatry is the love of women."}]}]},"selenolatry":{"h":"selenolatry","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The love of the Moon"}]}]},"arborolatry":{"h":"arborolatry","i":"/ɑrbɚˈɑlətri/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Arborolatry is the love of trees."}]}]},"symbololatry":{"h":"symbololatry","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The love of symbols"}]}]},"anthropolatry":{"h":"anthropolatry","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Anthropolatry is the love of humans."}]}]},"bardolatry":{"h":"bardolatry","i":"/ˈbɑː(r).dɒlətrɪi/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The excessive love of."}]}]},"bibliolatry":{"h":"bibliolatry","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Bibliolatry is the love of the Bible."},{"m":"(uncountable) Bibliolatry is the excessive love of a book."}]}]},"jezebel":{"h":"Jezebel","i":"/ˈdʒɛzəˌbɛl/","a":"en-au-Jezebel.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An evil woman."}]}]},"slut":{"h":"slut","i":"/slʌt/","a":"en-au-slut.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A woman who loves sex."},{"m":"(countable) A woman who has sex with many men."}]}]},"fenestra":{"h":"fenestra","i":"/fɪˈnɛstrə/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A fenestra is a small natural opening."}]}]},"semiannual":{"h":"semiannual","a":"En-us-semiannual.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Happening two times each year.","e":"The club meets every month for a business meeting and has semiannual parties, usually in June and December."}]}]},"yiddishism":{"h":"Yiddishism","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A Yiddishism is a word from the Yiddish language that has become an English word.","e":"Schmooze is an example of a Yiddishism"}]}]},"abyssinia":{"h":"Abyssinia","i":"/ˌæb.ɪˈsɪn.i.ə/","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Abyssinia is an old name for the country of Ethiopia."}]}]},"regicide":{"h":"regicide","i":"/ˈredʒəsaɪd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-regicide.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The killing of a king"}]}]},"crafty":{"h":"crafty","i":"/ˈkræfti/","a":"en-us-crafty.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Being crafty means to be very clever and skilful, usually to trick, fool or deceive someone else."}]}]},"belch":{"h":"belch","i":"/ˈbɛltʃ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-belch.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When something belches, it releases in large amounts (normally smoke)"}]}]},"belches":{"h":"belches","l":"belch","q":"verb"},"belched":{"h":"belched","l":"belch","q":"verb"},"belching":{"h":"belching","l":"belch","q":"verb"},"plagiarize":{"h":"pla