uilding, statue, etc., that honors a person or event."}]}]},"monuments":{"h":"monuments","l":"monument","q":"noun"},"mainland":{"h":"mainland","a":"En-us-mainland.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The mainland is a large area of land that forms a country or a continent. It does not include islands."}]}]},"mainlands":{"h":"mainlands","l":"mainland","q":"noun"},"reform":{"h":"reform","i":"/ˌriːˈfɔrm/","a":"en-us-reform.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A reform is a change to an institution's rules or ways something works to improve it.","e":"We have implemented additional reforms to make it easier to apply."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you reform something, you improve it by removing or correcting faults, problems, etc."}]}]},"reforms":{"h":"reforms","l":"reform","q":"verb"},"reformed":{"h":"reformed","l":"reform","q":"verb"},"reforming":{"h":"reforming","l":"reform","q":"verb"},"navigate":{"h":"navigate","i":"/ˈnæv.ɪ.ɡeɪt/","a":"en-us-navigate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you navigate a ship or airplane somewhere, you plan where it should go and drive it there."}]}]},"navigates":{"h":"navigates","l":"navigate","q":"verb"},"navigated":{"h":"navigated","l":"navigate","q":"verb"},"navigating":{"h":"navigating","l":"navigate","q":"verb"},"amalgamate":{"h":"amalgamate","i":"/əˈmælɡəˌmeɪt/","a":"en-au-amalgamate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When two things amalgamate, they join and combine together.","e":"John and Peter amalgamated their businesses to form a larger company."}]}]},"amalgamated":{"h":"amalgamated","l":"amalgamate","q":"verb"},"amalgamating":{"h":"amalgamating","l":"amalgamate","q":"verb"},"amalgamation":{"h":"amalgamation","i":"/əˌmælɡəˈmeɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-amalgamation.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Amalgamation is the act of.","e":"The amalgamation of was in 1998."},{"m":"(countable) An amalgamation of organizations is the organization that is formed when two or more organizations get together."}]}]},"amalgamations":{"h":"amalgamations","l":"amalgamation","q":"noun"},"kwanzaa":{"h":"Kwanzaa","i":"/ˈkwɑnzə/","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Kwanzaa is an African-American cultural festival, celebrated from December 26 to January 1."}]}]},"pony":{"h":"pony","i":"/ˈpəʊni/","a":"en-au-pony.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pony is a breed of horses that are small in size even when full grown."}]}]},"ponies":{"h":"ponies","a":"En-us-ponies.ogg","l":"pony","q":"noun"},"coral":{"h":"coral","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Coral is a hard material formed on the bottom of the sea by the skeletons of small creatures."},{"m":"(uncountable) Coral is an orange pink colour. &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"}]}]},"corals":{"h":"corals","l":"coral","q":"noun"},"conversion":{"h":"conversion","i":"/kənˈvɜːʃ(ə)n/","a":"en-us-conversion.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Conversion is the act or process of changing from one form to another."}]}]},"conversions":{"h":"conversions","l":"conversion","q":"noun"},"ferry":{"h":"ferry","i":"/ˈfɛri/","a":"en-us-ne-ferry.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A ferry is a boat that carries across a short stretch of water, usually going back and forth on the same route."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you ferry people or things, you carry them for a short distance between places on a boat or other vehicle."}]}]},"ferries":{"h":"ferries","l":"ferry","q":"verb"},"ferried":{"h":"ferried","l":"ferry","q":"verb"},"ferrying":{"h":"ferrying","l":"ferry","q":"verb"},"pumpkin":{"h":"pumpkin","i":"/ˈpʌmpkɪn/","a":"en-us-pumpkin.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pumpkin is a round, orange colored vegetable."},{"m":"(uncountable) The color of a pumpkin."}]}]},"pumpkins":{"h":"pumpkins","l":"pumpkin","q":"noun"},"summertime":{"h":"summertime","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The summertime is the time or season of summer."}]}]},"summertimes":{"h":"summertimes","l":"summertime","q":"noun"},"buttercup":{"h":"buttercup","i":"/ˈbʌt.ə.kʌp/","a":"en-us-buttercup.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A buttercup is an herb that has small yellow flowers that are shaped like cups."},{"m":"A buttercup is a plant of the genus Narcissus; it is a daffodil."}]}]},"buttercups":{"h":"buttercups","l":"buttercup","q":"noun"},"episode":{"h":"episode","i":"/ˈɛpɪsəʊd/","a":"en-us-episode.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An episode is an event or a short period of time that is important or unusual.","e":"She remembered an especially strange episode that occurred when she was a teenager."},{"m":"(countable) An episode is a part of a dramatic work such as a television or radio program.","e":"This television series has 10 episodes and will be shown over the next 10 weeks."}]}]},"episodes":{"h":"episodes","l":"episode","q":"noun"},"rotor":{"h":"rotor","i":"/ˈroʊ.tɚ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-rotor.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A rotor is a rotating part of an electrical or mechanical device."}]}]},"rotors":{"h":"rotors","l":"rotor","q":"noun"},"connecticut":{"h":"Connecticut","i":"/kəˈnɛtɪkət/","a":"en-us-Connecticut.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Connecticut is one of the states in the United States.","e":"Hartford is the capital of Connecticut."}]}]},"spike":{"h":"spike","i":"/spaɪk/","a":"en-us-spike.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A spike is a very large nail."},{"m":"A spike is a very large increase in something.","e":"The price of spiked yesterday."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you spike something, you fasten it with spikes, or long, large nails."},{"m":"If you spike a drink, you secretly add alcohol or another substance into it.","e":"She spiked my lemonade with vodka!"},{"m":"If something spikes, it increases sharply.","e":"Traffic accidents spiked in December when there was ice on the roads."}]}]},"spikes":{"h":"spikes","l":"spike","q":"noun"},"turtle":{"h":"turtle","a":"En-us-turtle.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A turtle is an aquatic reptile. A turtle has horny toothless jaws, and a bony shell.","e":"Pet turtles make good pets."}]}]},"turtles":{"h":"turtles","l":"turtle","q":"noun"},"fallow":{"h":"fallow","i":"/ˈfæləʊ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-fallow.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Fallow land is land that has been readied for seeding, but not seeded last year."},{"m":"If something is fallow, it is not active or developed."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Fallow is land that has been reading for seeding, but not seeding last year."},{"m":"(uncountable) Fallow is land that has not been farmed on."},{"m":"(countable) A fallow is an area of fallow land."},{"m":"(countable) A fallow is an act of readying the land, but not seeding it last year."}]}]},"fallows":{"h":"fallows","l":"fallow","q":"noun"},"fallowness":{"h":"fallowness","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Fallowness is the state of being fallow."}]}]},"spiritual":{"h":"spiritual","i":"/ˈspɪrɪtʃʊəl/","a":"en-us-spiritual.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something or someone is spiritual, it is of or about God; they are sacred."},{"m":"If something is spiritual, it is of or about the spirit or soul."},{"m":"If something is spiritual, it is of or about spirits or the supernatural."},{"m":"If something or someone is spiritual, they are made up of spirit; it is not material."},{"m":"If something is spiritual, it is about the mind; it is about intellect."},{"m":"If something is spiritual, it is not about time; it is related to sacred things."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A spiritual is a job, office, or matter that is sacred in nature."},{"m":"A spiritual is a Christian folk song."}]}]},"spirituals":{"h":"spirituals","l":"spiritual","q":"noun"},"spirituality":{"h":"spirituality","i":"/ˌspɪr.ə.t͡ʃuˈæl.ə.tɪ/","a":"en-us-spirituality.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Spirituality is the state of being spiritual."}]}]},"thunderclap":{"h":"thunderclap","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A thunderclap is sudden, loud thunder that was caused by lightning hitting the ground nearby; it is a shock of thunder.","e":"Thunderclaps that make them quake."}]}]},"thunderclaps":{"h":"thunderclaps","l":"thunderclap","q":"noun"},"thunderous":{"h":"thunderous","i":"/ˈθʌn.dər.əs/","a":"en-au-thunderous.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something or someone is thunderous, it is very loud, like thunder.","e":"After winning the duel in the arena, thunderous cheers greeted the hero from the audience."}]}]},"thunderously":{"h":"thunderously","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something is done thunderously, it is done very loudly; it is very thunderous."}]}]},"thunderousness":{"h":"thunderousness","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Thunderousness is the state of being thunderous; it is roaring loudness."}]}]},"thundery":{"h":"thundery","i":"/ˈθʌndəri/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If it is thundery out, it is stormy with thunder.","e":"After waking up, the merchant decided not to open his store because of how thundery it was outside."}]}]},"stormy":{"h":"stormy","i":"/ˈstɔrmi/","a":"en-us-stormy.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If it is stormy out, it is rainy and windy.","e":"The weatherman predicted that it would be stormy outside today."},{"m":"If something is stormy, it is of or about storms."},{"m":"If something is stormy, it is rough; it is violent.","e":"The fisherman had to bring his boat into the dock because of the stormy waves."}]}]},"stormier":{"h":"stormier","l":"stormy","q":"adjective"},"stormiest":{"h":"stormiest","l":"stormy","q":"adjective"},"tempestuous":{"h":"tempestuous","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If it is tempestuous outside, it is very windy; it is blustery; it is stormy."},{"m":"If something is tempestuous, it is of or about tempests."}]}]},"tempestuously":{"h":"tempestuously","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something is done tempestuously, it is done in a stormy or tempestuous way."}]}]},"tempestuousness":{"h":"tempestuousness","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Tempestuousness is the quality of being tempestuous; storminess; tumultuousness."}]}]},"storminess":{"h":"storminess","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Storminess is the state or quality of being stormy."},{"m":"(countable) A storminess is how strong or severe a storm is."}]}]},"storminesses":{"h":"storminesses","l":"storminess","q":"noun"},"stormless":{"h":"stormless","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If it is stormless outside, it is without a storm or stormy weather."}]}]},"stormlessness":{"h":"stormlessness","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Stormlessness is the lack of storms; it is calm."}]}]},"spiritlessly":{"h":"spiritlessly","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something is done spiritlessly, it is done in a spiritless way; it is done without any energy or motivation."}]}]},"ablaze":{"h":"ablaze","i":"/əˈbleɪz/","a":"en-us-ablaze.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something or someone is ablaze, it is on fire; it is burning strongly.","e":"After many tries, the camper finally looked down at the stack of wood that was now ablaze."},{"m":"If something is ablaze, it is glowing with a bright light and color."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something is ablaze, it is done very passionately."},{"m":"If something is ablaze, it is done in a blaze; it is on fire.","e":"Twitter was ablaze with tweets after Apple showed its' newest IPhone."}]}]},"gleamings":{"h":"gleamings","l":"gleaming","q":"noun"},"bluster":{"h":"bluster","i":"/ˈblʌs.tə/","a":"en-us-bluster.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Bluster is smug formal talk."},{"m":"(countable) A bluster is a gust of wind."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To bluster is to speak or protest loudly."},{"m":"To bluster is to speak or act in a threatening way."},{"m":"To bluster is to blow in strong and sudden gusts."}]}]},"blusters":{"h":"blusters","l":"bluster","q":"noun"},"blustered":{"h":"blustered","l":"bluster","q":"verb"},"blustering":{"h":"blustering","l":"bluster","q":"