magazine who offers opinions and a point of view."}]}]},"columnists":{"h":"columnists","l":"columnist","q":"noun"},"pursuit":{"h":"pursuit","i":"/pəˈsjuːt/","a":"en-us-pursuit.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pursuit is an act of going after something, to pursue it.","e":"The pursuit of happiness is never ending, as people are not satisfied with what already have."}]}]},"pursuits":{"h":"pursuits","l":"pursuit","q":"noun"},"headquarters":{"h":"headquarters","i":"/ˌhɛd.ˈkwɔː.təz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-headquarters.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A headquarters is the main building in control of whatever is going on in an organization."},{"m":"A headquarters is a military command center that controls and commands troops."}]}]},"individuality":{"h":"individuality","i":"/ˌɪndɪvɪd͡ʒuˈælɪti/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Individuality refers to the traits that you have that makes you different from others, something that is unique to yourself or your group and is part of your identity."},{"m":"(countable) A person."}]}]},"brainwash":{"h":"brainwash","i":"/ˈbreɪnwɒʃ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-brainwash.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you are brainwashed by something, you have been persuaded or convinced that something is real.","e":"North Korean citizens are being brainwashed by the media in their country about the West being evil."}]}]},"brainwashes":{"h":"brainwashes","l":"brainwash","q":"verb"},"brainwashed":{"h":"brainwashed","l":"brainwash","q":"verb"},"brainwashing":{"h":"brainwashing","l":"brainwash","q":"verb"},"dirts":{"h":"dirts","l":"dirt","q":"noun"},"equilibrium":{"h":"equilibrium","i":"/ɛkwɪˈlɪbrɪəm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-equilibrium.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"When something is at equilibrium, it is balanced and different types of influences are the same, hence having no net change.","e":"The population of the ants in this area has reached an equilibrium."},{"m":"When an object is at equilibrium, it is at rest or continuous motion and all the forces acting on it cancels out to become zero."},{"m":"When a system is in equilibrium, the rates of the forward and backward reactions are the same, hence causing no change in the concentration of the reactants and products.","e":"When a weak acid is added into water, an equilibrium mixture is obtained."}]}]},"equilibriums":{"h":"equilibriums","l":"equilibrium","q":"noun"},"equilibria":{"h":"equilibria","l":"equilibrium","q":"noun"},"irritable":{"h":"irritable","i":"/ˈɪrɪtəbl̩/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-irritable.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a person is irritable, they are grumpy, angry, cross and/or disagreeable","e":"When Brian is irritable, he is difficult to get along with."}]}]},"absents":{"h":"absents","l":"absent","q":"verb"},"absented":{"h":"absented","l":"absent","q":"verb"},"absenting":{"h":"absenting","l":"absent","q":"verb"},"socialisation":{"h":"socialisation","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Socialisation is the process of learning how to behave in one's own society."}]}]},"socialisations":{"h":"socialisations","l":"socialisation","q":"noun"},"emigration":{"h":"emigration","i":"/ˌɛmɪˈɡreɪʃn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-emigration.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Emigration of people is to leave one's country or area to go live in another and to stay in the new place permanently."}]}]},"emigrations":{"h":"emigrations","l":"emigration","q":"noun"},"lexeme":{"h":"lexeme","a":"en-us-lexeme.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Lexeme is the head-words in a dictionary and some words are made based on these lexemes. They are units of meaning, independent of any inflectional endings, or whether it is one word or several. The largest English dictionaries have about half a million lexemes, although the numbers can be higher.","e":"\"Come in\" is a lexeme, so is \"raining cats and dogs\"."}]}]},"lexemes":{"h":"lexemes","a":"En-us-lexemes.ogg","l":"lexeme","q":"noun"},"proactivity":{"h":"proactivity","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Proactivity is thinking ahead, taking charge of situations, and prevents something before it happens."}]}]},"elopement":{"h":"elopement","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Elopement refers to running away from home and is done in secret, hidden from anyone. It is an act of."}]}]},"elopements":{"h":"elopements","l":"elopement","q":"noun"},"gaelic":{"h":"Gaelic","i":"/ˈɡeɪlɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Gaelic.wav","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Gaelic is a family of languages in the British Isles that have mostly died out that includes Scottish (the native language of the Scottish Highlands), Manx (the language of the Isle of Man) and Irish (the language of Ireland).","e":"Most Irish people speak Gaelic."}]}]},"dashiki":{"h":"dashiki","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A Dashiki is a loose, brightly colored African garment that covers the top half of the body. It is worn mostly by men in West Africa."}]}]},"dashikis":{"h":"dashikis","l":"dashiki","q":"noun"},"barebacking":{"h":"barebacking","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Barebacking is when two or more people have sexual intercourse without using a condom."}]}]},"bowline":{"h":"bowline","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A bowline is a simple knot which creates a loop at the end of a rope. When it is used, it will not slip or jam."}]}]},"bowlines":{"h":"bowlines","l":"bowline","q":"noun"},"beret":{"h":"beret","i":"/ˈbɛreɪ/","a":"en-us-beret.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A beret is a soft, round type of hat and usually made of felt or a similar material. Berets are worn as part of the uniform of many military and police units across the world. Many other organizations also wear berets for different purposes."}]}]},"berets":{"h":"berets","l":"beret","q":"noun"},"talon":{"h":"talon","i":"/ˈtælən/","a":"en-us-talon.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A talon is a big, sharp claw of an animal, usually found on birds of prey, such as the eagle, hawk, falcon, owl, or buzzard."}]}]},"talons":{"h":"talons","l":"talon","q":"noun"},"alkaliphile":{"h":"alkaliphile","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An alkaliphile is an organism that can live in extremely alkaline conditions that are harmful to most life on Earth, usually with pH levels of 9.0 or above. These organisms are a form of extremophiles"}]}]},"alkaliphiles":{"h":"alkaliphiles","l":"alkaliphile","q":"noun"},"psychoanalysis":{"h":"psychoanalysis","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Psychoanalysis is a method of psychotherapy and science of the mind based on finding a connection among patients' dreams and thoughts, speaking whatever came to the patients' mind.","e":"Charles Socarides was an American psychoanalyst and psychiatrist who treated people for sexual issues by performing psychoanalysis."}]}]},"onanism":{"h":"onanism","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Onanism is an act of masturbation."},{"m":"(uncountable) Onanism is when you ejaculate outside the vagina during sex."}]}]},"bleacher":{"h":"bleacher","i":"/ˈbli.t͡ʃɚ/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bleacher is used to seat people watching sports events, usually simply built from metal supports and wooden planks."}]}]},"bleachers":{"h":"bleachers","l":"bleacher","q":"noun"},"freemasonry":{"h":"Freemasonry","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Freemasonry in full Free and Accepted Masons, is an originally secret fraternal organization, founded in England, and first revealing itself in 1717 in London.","e":"Peter Myers stated, \"I oppose Freemasonry in all its forms, due to its ritual content and because secrecy enables a few people at the top to manipulate the rest.\""}]}]},"onanisms":{"h":"onanisms","l":"onanism","q":"noun"},"individualities":{"h":"individualities","l":"individuality","q":"noun"},"scientology":{"h":"Scientology","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Scientology is a religion and a set of beliefs based on the writings and teachings of L. Ron Hubbard."}]}]},"thelarche":{"h":"thelarche","i":"/θiˈlɑr.ki/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Thelarche refers to the development of breasts in girls during puberty."}]}]},"antinatalism":{"h":"antinatalism","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Antinatalism is a philosophy that supports preventing new people from being born, and for the human race to finally disappear."}]}]},"neurology":{"h":"neurology","i":"/n(j)uˈrɒləd͡ʒi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-neurology.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Neurology is the treatment of the nervous system by a medical doctor called a neurologist."}]}]},"tsar":{"h":"tsar","i":"/(t)sɑː/","a":"en-us-tsar.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The tsar is the title of the Emperors of Russia before 1917.","e":"Our tsar Alexander I of Russia saved us from Napoleon in 1812."}]}]},"mormon":{"h":"Mormon","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A Mormon is a member of an American Christian religious group, officially called The Church of Jesus Christ of Latterday Saints.","e":"73 percent of Mormons believe that \"working to help the poor\" is \"essential to being a good Mormon.\""}]},{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"The ancient American prophet who, according to Mormonism, wrote the Book of Mormon."}]}]},"soviet":{"h":"Soviet","i":"/ˈsəʊ.vi.ət/","a":"en-us-Soviet.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"A Soviet is an elected council in a communist country."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A Soviet is a citizen of the Union of Soviet Socialist Republics."}]}]},"tsars":{"h":"tsars","l":"tsar","q":"noun"},"mormons":{"h":"Mormons","l":"mormon","q":"noun"},"soviets":{"h":"Soviets","l":"soviet","q":"noun"},"elohim":{"h":"Elohim","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Elohim is a Hebrew name for God."},{"m":"Elohim is also the name of the chief God of the Mormon religion."}]}]},"psychotherapy":{"h":"psychotherapy","i":"/ˌsaɪkoʊˈθɛrəpi/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Psychotherapy is a method of psychological help where a patient tries to solve his mental problems by talking about them with a psychotherapist.","e":"John used psychotherapy to help him with his depression."}]}]},"psychotherapies":{"h":"psychotherapies","l":"psychotherapy","q":"noun"},"confederation":{"h":"confederation","i":"/kənfɛdəˈreɪʃən/","a":"en-us-confederation.oga","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A confederation is a group of states that surrender some of their autonomy to a federal state that they are members of.","e":"The Union of Soviet Socialist Republics and the European Union are examples of confederations."}]}]},"lucifer":{"h":"Lucifer","i":"/ˈluːsɪfə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Lucifer.wav","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Lucifer is another name for the Devil among Christians.","e":"Some Christians have claimed that Albert Pike, a Masonic author, stated that Lucifer was God, but the claim is not proven."},{"m":"Another name for the planet Venus."},{"m":"The spirit brother of Jesus Christ in Mormonism."}]}]},"snack":{"h":"snack","i":"/snæk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-snack.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A snack is a small amount of food or a small meal.","e":"The snacks I ate were potato chips and candy."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you snack, you are eating a light meal.","e":"While waiting for the movie to start, I snacked on some popcorn."}]}]},"snacks":{"h":"snacks","l":"snack","q":"noun"},"confederations":{"h":"confederations","l":"confederation","q":"noun"},"chronic":{"h":"chronic","i":"/ˈkrɒnɪk/","a":"en-au-chronic.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is chronic, it happens all the time.","e":"Michelle is a chronic worrier who gets upset about everything."},{"m":"If something is chronic, it has happened for a long time.","e":"My father has chronic back pain since he was injured at work 5 years ago."},{"m":"If something is chronic, it is difficult to stop.","e":"My brother is a chronic smoker and is unable to quit."}]}]},"wail":{"h":"wail","i":"/weɪl/","a":"en-us-wail.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you wail, you cry intensely, usually in anguish or grief.","e":"The mother wailed when her child died."},{"m":"Wailing is when something makes a noise that sounds like crying.","e":"The wind wailed through the trees during the storm."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A wail is a long, loud, high-pitched cry of sorrow or grief.","e":"The dog's wails were painful to hear."}]}]},"meaningless":{"h":"meaningless","i":"/ˈmiːnɪŋləs/","a":"en-us-meaningless.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is meaningless, it has no meaning. It is not important.","e":"The child's scribbles were meaningless."},{"m":"When something is meaningless, it has no meaning. It has no purpose.","e":"After his wife left him, his life felt meaningless."}]}]},"snacked":{"h":"snacked","l":"snack","q":"verb"},"snacking":{"h":"snacking","l":"snack","q":"verb"},"wails":{"h":"wails","l":"wail","q":"verb"},"wailed":{"h":"wailed","l":"wail","q":"verb"},"wailing":{"h":"wailing","i":"/ˈweɪlɪŋ/","a":"en-us-wailing.ogg","l":"wail","q":"verb"},"fantasize":{"h":"fantasize","i":"/ˈfæntəˌsaɪz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-fantasize.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you fantasize about something, you imagine and dream about it.","e":"I fantasized going to Hawaii with my friends."}]}]},"fantasizes":{"h":"fantasizes","l":"fantasize","q":"verb"},"fantasized":{"h":"fantasized","l":"fantasize","q":"verb"},"fantasizing":{"h":"fantasizing","l":"fantasize","q":"verb"},"rhodesia":{"h":"Rhodesia","i":"/rəʊˈdiːʃə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Rhodesia.wav","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Rhodesia was a country in Africa."}]}]},"cult":{"h":"cult","i":"/kʌlt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-cult.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cult is a group that practices coercion and brainwashing on its followers."},{"m":"(countable) A cult refers to a religious group that claims to be part of one religion, while rejecting foundations beliefs of that religion.","e":"The Nation of Islam is a cult of Islam because it rejects the Koran's teachings but still claims to be Islamic."}]}]},"enlarge":{"h":"enlarge","i":"/ɪnˈlɑːd͡ʒ/","a":"en-us-enlarge.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you enlarge something, you make it larger.","e":"I used a magnifying glass to enlarge the text on the document."},{"m":"(transitive) When you enlarge something, you increase and expand the size of it, giving it a greater scope.","e":"Learning knowledge in school enlarges my mind about the world around me."},{"m":"(intransitive) To talk a lot about a certain subject and to elaborate about it.","e":"The speaker enlarged about the topic on politics."}]}]},"enlarges":{"h":"enlarges","l":"enlarge","q":"verb"},"enlarged":{"h":"enlarged","a":"En-us-enlarged.ogg","l":"enlarge","q":"verb"},"enlarging":{"h":"enlarging","l":"enlarge","q":"verb"},"cults":{"h":"cults","l":"cult","q":"noun"},"condominium":{"h":"condominium","i":"/kɒn.dəˈmɪn.ɪ.əm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-condominium.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A condominium is a colony that is jointly ruled by two nations.","e":"New Hebridges was a condominium of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland and France"},{"m":"A condominium is where a person has their own housing unit but its are shared with other people living in the same estate."}]}]},"manxman":{"h":"Manxman","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A Manxman is someone from the Isle of Man."}]}]},"manxmen":{"h":"Manxmen","l":"manxman","q":"noun"},"condominiums":{"h":"condominiums","l":"condominium","q":"noun"},"populous":{"h":"populous","i":"/ˈpɒpjʊləs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-populous.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is populous, it means that there is a large population.","e":"China is the most populous country in the world."},{"m":"When a language is populous, it is spoken by many people."},{"m":"A populous place is a place where many people live in it, a place that is densely populated."}]}]},"marketings":{"h":"marketings","l":"marketing","q":"noun"},"forcefully":{"h":"forcefully","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"When you do something forcefully, you do it in a powerful and forceful manner.","e":"The dictator executed all his opponents forcefully."}]}]},"execute":{"h":"execute","i":"/ˈɛksɪˌkjuːt/","a":"en-us-execute.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you execute someone, you kill someone due to the crimes that the person has committed.","e":"The smuggler was found guilty with delivering drugs across the border and was executed."},{"m":"(transitive) When you execute an action, you carry it out.","e":"The soldiers executed the orders given by their superior."},{"m":"(transitive) When you execute a program, you start, launch or run it.","e":"I executed the program to begin my installation of the new web browser."}]}]},"executes":{"h":"executes","l":"execute","q":"verb"},"executed":{"h":"executed","l":"execute","q":"verb"},"executing":{"h":"executing","l":"execute","q":"verb"},"satisfaction":{"h":"satisfaction","i":"/sætɪsˈfækʃən/","a":"en-us-satisfaction.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Satisfaction is a feeling when a need or want has been fulfilled or achieved.","e":"He enjoyed the dish with great satisfaction and wants to order it again the next time he comes to this restaurant."},{"m":"Satisfaction refers to the happiness and pleasure from fulfilling a need or a want.","e":"The satisfaction that you have when you managed to beat all your opponents to win a prize is very rewarding."}]}]},"satisfactions":{"h":"satisfactions","l":"satisfaction","q":"noun"},"frown":{"h":"frown","i":"/fraʊn/","a":"en-us-frown.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A frown is a facial expression whereby the eyebrows are brought closer together and wrinkles form on the forehead. A frown usually happens when a person is unhappy, sad or worried, but can also be very focused on doing something.","e":"A frown appeared on his face when he heard the news of someone else spreading rumors about him."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) When you frown, you have a [[#Noun|frown]] on your face, usually due to sadness or anger.","e":"The teacher frowned when he saw his student sleeping in his class."},{"m":"(intransitive) When you frown about something, you are not happy about something and do not like it.","e":"Making a lot of noise in a library is frowned upon."}]}]},"frowns":{"h":"frowns","i":"/fraʊnz/","l":"frown","q":"noun"},"frowned":{"h":"frowned","i":"/fraʊnd/","l":"frown","q":"verb"},"frowning":{"h":"frowning","i":"/ˈfraʊnɪŋ/","l":"frown","q":"verb"},"broadcaster":{"h":"broadcaster","i":"/ˈbrɔdˌkæstɚ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-broadcaster.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A broadcaster is an organization that does broadcasting.","e":"The British Broadcasting Corporation (BBC) is a broadcaster in the United Kingdom."},{"m":"(countable) A broadcaster is a person with a job of doing broadcasting."}]}]},"broadcasters":{"h":"broadcasters","l":"broadcaster","q":"noun"},"celebration":{"h":"celebration","i":"/ˌsɛlɪˈbreɪʃən/","a":"en-uk-celebration.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A celebration is a gathering of people for fun and entertainment, usually like a party.","e":"We held a birthday celebration for Jane last Sunday."}]}]},"celebrations":{"h":"celebrations","l":"celebration","q":"noun"},"hinted":{"h":"hinted","i":"/ˈhɪntɪd/","l":"hint","q":"verb"},"hinting":{"h":"hinting","i":"/ˈhɪntɪŋ/","l":"hint","q":"verb"},"laps":{"h":"laps","l":"lap","q":"verb"},"lapped":{"h":"lapped","l":"lap","q":"verb"},"lapping":{"h":"lapping","l":"lap","q":"verb"},"orals":{"h":"orals","l":"oral","q":"noun"},"fades":{"h":"fades","l":"fade","q":"verb"},"sweeps":{"h":"sweeps","l":"sweep","q":"verb"},"mohammedan":{"h":"Mohammedan","i":"/məˈhæm.ɪ.dən/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A Mohammedan is a follower of Islam, the religion founded by the prophet Mohammed."}]}]},"mohammedans":{"h":"Mohammedans","l":"mohammedan","q":"noun"},"pissy":{"h":"pissy","i":"/ˈpɪsi/","a":"en-au-pissy.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is pissy, it is covered in piss."},{"m":"When something is pissy, it smells like piss.","e":"Ew, the bathroom smells pissy, who pee'd in here?"}]}]},"asexual":{"h":"asexual","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When someone is asexual, the person does not have any interest in having sex."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An asexual is a person that does not have any sexual desire or attraction, a person with asexuality."}]}]},"pissier":{"h":"pissier","l":"pissy","q":"adjective"},"pissiest":{"h":"pissiest","l":"pissy","q":"adjective"},"asexuals":{"h":"asexuals","l":"asexual","q":"noun"},"sodomy":{"h":"sodomy","i":"/ˈsɒdəmi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-sodomy.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Sodomy refers to any of several types of sexual acts that people in the past sometimes considered to be unnatural. Anal sex or sexual interaction with animals are considered to be a sodomy."}]}]},"encyclopediae":{"h":"encyclopediae","l":"encyclopedia","q":"noun"},"simples":{"h":"simples","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Naomi Persephone Amethyst (NaomiAmethyst)-simples.wav","l":"simple","q":"noun"},"simpled":{"h":"simpled","l":"simple","q":"verb"},"simpling":{"h":"simpling","l":"simple","q":"verb"},"worded":{"h":"worded","l":"word","q":"verb"},"wording":{"h":"wording","l":"word","q":"verb"},"rainbowed":{"h":"rainbowed","l":"rainbow","q":"verb"},"rainbowing":{"h":"rainbowing","l":"rainbow","q":"verb"},"neurologist":{"h":"neurologist","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A neurologist is a doctor who treats patients with problems in their nervous systems.","e":"Sigmund Freud was a neurologist who treated neurotic patients through psychotherapy and founded psychoanalysis."}]}]},"neurologists":{"h":"neurologists","l":"neurologist","q":"noun"},"contentment":{"h":"contentment","i":"/kənˈtɛntmənt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-contentment.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Contentment is a feeling of being happy and.","e":"The mother sighed with contentment when she held her baby."},{"m":"A contentment is something that causes a feeling of happiness and satisfaction.","e":"Cicero found contentment in a garden or a library."}]}]},"contentments":{"h":"contentments","l":"contentment","q":"noun"},"overs":{"h":"overs","l":"over","q":"noun"},"sexuality":{"h":"sexuality","i":"/sɛkʃuˈælɪti/","a":"en-au-sexuality.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Sexuality refers to the ability to have sexual feelings and experiences."},{"m":"A person's sexuality is their sexual orientation; either heterosexual, homosexual, bisexual or asexual.","e":"His sexuality is heterosexual."}]}]},"gratification":{"h":"gratification","i":"/ˌɡrætɪfɪˈkeɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-gratification.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Gratification is a feeling of pleasure and satisfaction.","e":"The artist felt gratification when he saw his art in the gallery."},{"m":"Gratification is something that.","e":"Eating chocolate gives me great gratification."}]}]},"gun-shy":{"h":"gun-shy","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone or something is gun-shy, they are afraid of guns.","e":"Although her father was a hunter, the little girl was gun-shy."},{"m":"If someone or something is gun-shy, they are scared of the sound guns make.","e":"The dog was gun-shy of fireworks and thunder."},{"m":"If someone or something is gun-shy, they are fearful or wary, especially because of past experience.","e":"After crashing the car, I was gun-shy of driving."}]}]},"sexualities":{"h":"sexualities","l":"sexuality","q":"noun"},"gratifications":{"h":"gratifications","l":"gratification","q":"noun"},"birded":{"h":"birded","l":"bird","q":"verb"},"birding":{"h":"birding","l":"bird","q":"verb"},"languaged":{"h":"languaged","l":"language","q":"verb"},"languaging":{"h":"languaging","l":"language","q":"verb"},"kittened":{"h":"kittened","l":"kitten","q":"verb"},"kittening":{"h":"kittening","l":"kitten","q":"verb"},"habitat":{"h":"habitat","i":"/ˈhæbɪtæt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-habitat.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A habitat is a natural place that a plant or an animal lives in."}]}]},"polyarchy":{"h":"polyarchy","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A polyarchy is a type of government where power is in the hands of a few people."}]}]},"monarchy":{"h":"monarchy","i":"/ˈmɒnəki/","a":"en-us-monarchy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A monarchy is a form of government in which one person officially is the ruler of the state and the ruler's position is passed down through his family.","e":"Belgium is a monarchy."}]}]},"defender":{"h":"defender","i":"/dɪˈfɛndə(r)/","a":"en-us-defender.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A defender is someone who defends someone else, usually from violence."},{"m":"(countable) A defender is a player who tries to stop the other teams from goals or points."}]}]},"supporter":{"h":"supporter","i":"/səˈpɔː.tə/","a":"en-au-supporter.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A supporter is someone that supports a cause or a movement, usually because the person believes in it."},{"m":"(countable) A supporter is someone who likes and follows a sports team or a sportsperson, usually as a fan.","e":"The team managed to get more than a thousand supporters to cheer for them at the latest match."},{"m":"(countable) A supporter is something that supports something else, usually a structure such as a building."}]}]},"correctly":{"h":"correctly","i":"/kəˈrɛktli/","a":"en-us-correctly.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If you do something correctly, then you do it as it is supposed to be done, doing it in a correct way."}]}]},"massage":{"h":"massage","i":"/məˈsɑʒ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-massage.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A massage is an act of rubbing, kneading or hitting the skin. It is a form of therapy as it allows the person to relax or recover from aches."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you massage someone, you [[#Noun|massage]] the person's body so that the person can relax."}]}]},"uncommon":{"h":"uncommon","i":"/ʌnˈkɒmən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-uncommon.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is uncommon it does not occur or appear very often.","e":"It is uncommon for a divorced couple to forgive one another."}]}]},"skilled":{"h":"skilled","i":"/skɪld/","a":"en-us-skilled.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When someone is skilled, it means they are very good or talented at doing something.","e":"You seem to be very skilled in sewing! Who taught you so well?"}]}]},"entirely":{"h":"entirely","i":"/ɪnˈtaɪəli/","a":"en-us-entirely.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Entirely refers to the full extent of doing something. It is another word for totally or completely.","e":"It is entirely up to you on how you intend to get help for your project. I am only here to give advice."},{"m":"When something is done entirely by a group of people, it is exclusive to them only.","e":"This project was done entirely by me, I did not ask for help from anyone else."}]}]},"soften":{"h":"soften","i":"/ˈsɒfən/","a":"en-us-soften.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you soften something, then you make it soft or softer.","e":"You will have to use this to beat the flour to soften it before we can use it to make our cake."},{"m":"When you soften your words, you make it less harsh and less critical.","e":"Seeing that she was about to cry, I softened my tone and criticism about her project."}]}]},"sunset":{"h":"sunset","i":"/ˈsʌnˌsɛt/","a":"en-us-sunset.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"It is the part of the day when the sun disappears on the western horizon."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you sunset something, you stop using it and phase it out.","e":"We will be sunsetting this version of the software as it has became very old and no one is maintaining it."}]}]},"slavery":{"h":"slavery","i":"/ˈsleɪvəri/","a":"en-us-slavery.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Slavery is the act of using or owning human beings as an object or as slaves, usually using them to do forced labor. It is a crime in most places in the world."}]}]},"rug":{"h":"rug","i":"/rʌɡ/","a":"en-au-rug.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A rug is a piece of cloth used to cover the floor, just like a carpet.","e":"My sister bought a new rug for the living room."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you rug something, you pull it in a very rough way and the thing may spoil due to this.","e":"Stop rugging the rope! It may tear apart and we cannot use it again."}]}]},"unfortunate":{"h":"unfortunate","i":"/ʌnˈfɔːtjʊnət/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-unfortunate.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something (usually an event) is unfortunate, it is not good and is a misfortune. It is considered to be unlucky that such a thing happened.","e":"It is unfortunate that the Prince was murdered."}]}]},"affectionate":{"h":"affectionate","i":"/əˈfɛkʃənət/","a":"en-us-affectionate.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A person who is affectionate likes to touch other people in a friendly way, usually due to love or affection."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you affectionate with someone, you show your love and affection to another person."}]}]},"purr":{"h":"purr","i":"/pɜː(r)/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-purr.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A purr is the sound a cat makes when it is relaxed."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If a cat purrs, it makes a sound showing that it is relaxed.","e":"It was a lazy afternoon and the cat purred before going to sleep on the sofa."}]}]},"kiddy":{"h":"kiddy","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(informal) A kiddy refers to a child."}]}]},"hiya":{"h":"hiya","s":[{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"You say \"hiya\" when you greet somebody in an informal situation."}]}]},"hazard":{"h":"hazard","i":"/ˈhæzəd/","a":"en-us-hazard.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hazard is something that poses a danger.","e":"Please look out for the hazard ahead while you are driving along the highway."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you hazard, you take a risk or a chance in doing something."}]}]},"habitats":{"h":"habitats","l":"habitat","q":"noun"},"polyarchies":{"h":"polyarchies","l":"polyarchy","q":"noun"},"hazards":{"h":"hazards","l":"hazard","q":"noun"},"viceroy":{"h":"viceroy","i":"/ˈvaɪsˌrɔɪ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-viceroy.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A viceroy is a person who governs a region as the representative of the king.","e":"When Ireland was under English rule, the English King governed the island through a viceroy."}]}]},"viceroys":{"h":"viceroys","l":"viceroy","q":"noun"},"anal":{"h":"anal","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Anal sex, cancer, bleeding, etc. are things relating to or situated near the anus."},{"m":"When someone is anal, the person is being very critical.","e":"Why are you so anal about her project? This is just her first time planning one."}]}]},"ontology":{"h":"ontology","i":"/ɒnˈtɒləd͡ʒi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-ontology.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(philosophy) Ontology is a part of philosophy under the branch of metaphysics which studies the nature of being, becoming, existence and reality."}]}]},"uncommoner":{"h":"uncommoner","l":"uncommon","q":"adjective"},"uncommonest":{"h":"uncommonest","l":"uncommon","q":"adjective"},"monarchies":{"h":"monarchies","l":"monarchy","q":"noun"},"defenders":{"h":"defenders","a":"En-us-defenders.ogg","l":"defender","q":"noun"},"supporters":{"h":"supporters","i":"/səˈpɔː.təz/","a":"en-us-supporters.ogg","l":"supporter","q":"noun"},"massages":{"h":"massages","l":"massage","q":"noun"},"massaged":{"h":"massaged","l":"massage","q":"verb"},"massaging":{"h":"massaging","l":"massage","q":"verb"},"softens":{"h":"softens","l":"soften","q":"verb"},"softened":{"h":"softened","l":"soften","q":"verb"},"softening":{"h":"softening","l":"soften","q":"verb"},"congolese":{"h":"Congolese","i":"/ˌkɒŋ.ɡəˈliːz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Congolese.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A Congolese is a person from the Republic of the Congo or Democratic Republic of the Congo.","e":"King Leopold II of Belgium was a Congolese monarch."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Congolese refers to the people and culture of the Republic of the Congo or Democratic Republic of the Congo."}]}]},"sunsets":{"h":"sunsets","l":"sunset","q":"noun"},"sunsetted":{"h":"sunsetted","l":"sunset","q":"verb"},"sunsetting":{"h":"sunsetting","l":"sunset","q":"verb"},"coitus":{"h":"coitus","i":"/ˈkəʊ.ɪ.təs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-coitus.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A coitus is when a person has sexual intercourse. The penis is inserted inside the vagina and usually until orgasm happens."}]}]},"slaveries":{"h":"slaveries","l":"slavery","q":"noun"},"affectionates":{"h":"affectionates","l":"affectionate","q":"verb"},"affectionated":{"h":"affectionated","l":"affectionate","q":"verb"},"affectionating":{"h":"affectionating","l":"affectionate","q":"verb"},"rugs":{"h":"rugs","l":"rug","q":"noun"},"rugged":{"h":"rugged","a":"En-us-rugged.ogg","l":"rug","q":"verb"},"rugging":{"h":"rugging","l":"rug","q":"verb"},"purrs":{"h":"purrs","l":"purr","q":"noun"},"purred":{"h":"purred","l":"purr","q":"verb"},"purring":{"h":"purring","l":"purr","q":"verb"},"kiddies":{"h":"kiddies","l":"kiddy","q":"noun"},"hazarded":{"h":"hazarded","l":"hazard","q":"verb"},"hazarding":{"h":"hazarding","l":"hazard","q":"verb"},"anals":{"h":"anals","l":"anal","q":"noun"},"ontologies":{"h":"ontologies","l":"ontology","q":"noun"},"fatuous":{"h":"fatuous","i":"/ˈfæt.ju.əs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-fatuous.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is fatuous, it is stupid, silly and foolish.","e":"It is fatuous to think that both men and women have the same muscle strength."}]}]},"onomasiology":{"h":"onomasiology","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Onomasiology is the branch of linguistics concerned with \"how do you express X?\". It gives the words for a given concept. A thesaurus is often used for this job."}]}]},"eolian":{"h":"eolian","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Eolian refers to something that occurs in nature. It is related to the wind and its ability to change the surface of the Earth and other planets."}]}]},"gamine":{"h":"gamine","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A gamine refers to a woman that is boyish, elegant and wide-eyed woman who is seen to be mischievous or sexually appealing.","e":"Some examples of women who are gamines include Audrey Hepburn, Elizabeth Hartman, Bridget Fonda and Jennifer Jason Leigh."}]}]},"gamines":{"h":"gamines","l":"gamine","q":"noun"},"hallam":{"h":"Hallam","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Hallam is a town in Victoria, Australia."}]}]},"handbag":{"h":"handbag","a":"en-uk-handbag.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(mainly Commonwealth) A handbag is a small bag used by women (and sometimes men) to carry a few small personal items.","e":"For my sister's birthday, I bought her a brown handbag and she really liked it."}]}]},"handbags":{"h":"handbags","l":"handbag","q":"noun"},"theosophy":{"h":"theosophy","i":"[θɪˈɒsəfɪ]","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(religion) A theosophy is a religious belief that knowledge of God can be obtained through mysticism and that it is possible to directly talk to the spiritual world, it especially refers to the beliefs of Helena Blavatsky's Theosophical Society."}]}]},"theosophies":{"h":"theosophies","l":"theosophy","q":"noun"},"pedal":{"h":"pedal","i":"/ˈpɛdəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-pedal (noun, verb).wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pedal is a kind of lever that is used by the foot to control a machine. A bicycle, a piano and a car all have pedals in them.","e":"He pressed his foot down on the pedal of the car and it started to go faster."},{"m":"A pedal is a foot or a foot-like part of the body."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you pedal something, you step on a [[#Noun|pedal]] that is linked to a wheel so that it can move in circles.","e":"He tried the pedal his bicycle in the woods, but a wheel was stuck in the mud."},{"m":"(intransitive) When you pedal, you are trying to control and operate a bicycle.","e":"He tried to pedal across the countryside but became breathless halfway through."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is related to the foot."}]}]},"pedals":{"h":"pedals","l":"pedal","q":"noun"},"pedaled":{"h":"pedaled","l":"pedal","q":"verb"},"pedaling":{"h":"pedaling","l":"pedal","q":"verb"},"pedalled":{"h":"pedalled","l":"pedal","q":"verb"},"pedalling":{"h":"pedalling","l":"pedal","q":"verb"},"feasible":{"h":"feasible","i":"/ˈfiːzəbəl/","a":"en-us-feasible.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is feasible, it is something that can be done, something that is possible to be done.","e":"The government did a study of this area and found that it is feasible to build a new building here."}]}]},"commonplace":{"h":"commonplace","i":"/ˈkɑmənˌpleɪs/","a":"en-us-commonplace.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is commonplace, it happens repeatedly, regularly or frequently; usual.","e":"Almost no one visits the library anymore. Using the Internet for research has become commonplace."},{"m":"Something that is ordinary, uninteresting, or not special.","e":"Almost everyone has mobile phones now. They are commonplace."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A commonplace is a place that is ordinary and common."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you commonplace, you are making a commonplace book, a personal notebook used to write quotes."}]}]},"commonplaces":{"h":"commonplaces","l":"commonplace","q":"noun"},"commonplaced":{"h":"commonplaced","l":"commonplace","q":"verb"},"commonplacing":{"h":"commonplacing","l":"commonplace","q":"verb"},"bolshevik":{"h":"Bolshevik","i":"/ˈbɒlʃəvɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Bolshevik.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A Bolshevik is a member of the, the political party that overthrew the Russian government in 1917.","e":"The Russian people got rid of their government and Russia had Bolshevik rule for 70 years."},{"m":"Bolshevik is used to describe the Communist Party that ruled the Russian Soviet Federative Socialist Republic and the Union of Soviet Socialist Republics."},{"m":"Something that is related to the Bolshevik Party or Bolshevism."}]}]},"menshevik":{"h":"Menshevik","i":"/ˈmɛnʃəvɪk/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A Menshevik refers to a person that is part of the moderate wing of the during the time of the in Russia."}]}]},"bolsheviks":{"h":"Bolsheviks","l":"bolshevik","q":"noun"},"mensheviks":{"h":"Mensheviks","l":"menshevik","q":"noun"},"niggardly":{"h":"niggardly","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When someone is niggardly, the person does not give away money or other things. The person is mean and stingy.","e":"The economics teacher said people were being niggardly with their money."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"When you do something niggardly, you do it in an uptight way, usually sparingly or stingily."}]}]},"attractiveness":{"h":"attractiveness","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Attractiveness is how attractive something or someone is."},{"m":"(countable) Attractiveness is the result of being attractive."}]}]},"coffin":{"h":"coffin","i":"/ˈkɒfɪn/","a":"en-us-coffin.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A coffin is a box used to keep the dead body of a person.","e":"The family of Mary were very hurt to see her laying in her coffin."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you coffin a dead person, you place his or her body into a [[#Noun|coffin]]."}]}]},"casket":{"h":"casket","i":"/ˈkæs.kɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-casket.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A casket is another word for a coffin, a box used to place the bodies of dead people.","e":"We went to pick out a casket for our late grandmother."},{"m":"(countable) A casket is a small box to place items, usually jewellery."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you casket something, you put it into a [[#Noun|casket]]."}]}]},"kikes":{"h":"kikes","l":"kike","q":"noun"},"scots":{"h":"Scots","i":"/skɒts/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Persent101-Scots.wav","l":"scot","q":"proper noun","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Scots refers to a language that is closely related to English and is spoken in some parts of Scotland."}]}]},"jahbulon":{"h":"Jahbulon","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Jahbulon is a God mentioned in a degree of Freemasonry."}]}]},"antimasonry":{"h":"antimasonry","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Antimasonry refers to the political, religious or economic opposition to Freemasonry.","e":"Antimasonry is more common than anti-Semitism, it is more tolerated by the liberal establishment to criticize Masonry than Judaism."}]}]},"anti-semitism":{"h":"anti-Semitism","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Political, religious, or economic opposition to Judaism.","e":"Anti-Semitism and racial discrimination are less common than they once were."},{"m":"Ethnic or racial hatred against Jews."},{"m":"Ethnic or racial hatred against the Semitic races in general."}]}]},"jewry":{"h":"Jewry","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The Jewish people, the world Jewish population as a whole, Jewish populations in specific locations.","e":"Hitler's regime murdered Jewry in Europe."},{"m":"Jewry is the land of Judea."}]}]},"mormonism":{"h":"Mormonism","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"An American Christian religion that was founded by the prophet Joseph Smith."}]}]},"jesuit":{"h":"Jesuit","i":"/ˈdʒɛzuɪt/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A member of a Roman Catholic fraternity of priests called the Society of Jesus that was founded by St. Ignatius Loyola."}]}]},"vatican":{"h":"Vatican","i":"/ˈvæ.tɪ.kən/","a":"en-us-Vatican.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Vatican is short for Vatican City, a country in Europe, located in Rome, Italy where the Pope of the Roman Catholic Church is the absolute monarch."},{"m":"Vatican is the official residence of the Pope of the Roman Catholic Church inside the Vatican City."},{"m":"Vatican is the Pope's government in the Vatican City.","e":"The Global Christian Forum unites Christian groups through a Vatican council."}]}]},"restorationism":{"h":"restorationism","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Restorationism is the belief that Christianity should be restored to what Jesus' original church was like in the view of restorationists, and that modern Christians churches such as the Roman Catholic Church are incorrect."}]}]},"manx":{"h":"Manx","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Manx is the native language of the Isle of Man, a member of the Gaelic language family, now largely extinct."}]}]},"shrieve":{"h":"shrieve","i":"/ʃriːv/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-shrieve.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A shrieve is an obsolete word for sheriff."}]}]},"baphomet":{"h":"Baphomet","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Baphomet refers to the deity that the Knights Templar, witches, and pagans were accused of worshiping by the Roman Catholic Church, and which some modern Satanic and occult movements worship today."}]}]},"malthusianism":{"h":"Malthusianism","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Malthusianism refers to the idea made by Thomas Malthus of lowering human population growth. It is a belief that the world's population will grow faster than the available food supply that is required for living.","e":"Many environmentalists believe Malthusianism will help protect wildlife."}]}]},"barnacle":{"h":"barnacle","i":"/ˈbɑːnəkl̩/","a":"en-au-barnacle.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sea crustacean of the subclass that attaches itself to surfaces in water like tidal rocks or ships.","e":"The barnacle attached itself to the submarine while it came up on top of the water."}]}]},"neotrogla":{"h":"neotrogla","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A genus of barklice, about the size of fleas, found in dry caves in Brazil."}]}]},"elks":{"h":"Elks","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Elks is the name of an American fraternity and social club."}]}]},"coca-cola":{"h":"Coca-Cola","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Coca-Cola is a brand of carbonated non-alcoholic cola drink."}]}]},"windbaggery":{"h":"windbaggery","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Windbaggery refers to the behavior of a windbag, which is excessive speaking and talking nonsense."}]}]},"blather":{"h":"blather","i":"/blæðə(r)/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-blather.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you blather, you talk rapidly without making any sense."}]}]},"cheapskate":{"h":"cheapskate","i":"/ˈt͡ʃipˌskeɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-cheapskate.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cheapskate is a person who avoids giving money."}]}]},"miser":{"h":"miser","i":"/ˈmaɪzə(r)/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-miser.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A miser refers to a person who prefers to hold on to their own money and not spend it, someone who is cheap.","e":"He is such a miser! I only asked him to treat me to an ice cream but he insists on not doing so."}]}]},"hoard":{"h":"hoard","i":"/hɔrd/","a":"en-us-hoard.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To have a fixation on collecting things into a large collection.","e":"Ebenezer Scrooge was a man who would hoard money."}]}]},"amass":{"h":"amass","i":"/əˈmæs/","a":"en-us-amass.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To collect into a mass or heap, to gather a large number of things, to gain possession of a lot of things."}]}]},"dyke":{"h":"dyke","i":"/daɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-dyke.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A dyke is a female homosexual."}]}]},"aryan":{"h":"Aryan","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A division of the Caucasian race."},{"m":"(theosophy, Germanic mysticism, Nazism) A member of an alleged non-Jewish Caucasian master race."},{"m":"A racist of European ancestry."}]}]},"pushy":{"h":"pushy","i":"/ˈpʊʃ.i/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-pushy.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When someone is pushy, the person is forceful and is determined in doing certain things his or her way.","e":"Please stop being so pushy about your way of working on this project!"}]}]},"binoculars":{"h":"binoculars","i":"/ˈbɪnˌɒk.jʊ.lə(r)z/","a":"en-us-binoculars.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Binoculars is a device that is used to zoom in using a series of lenses so that items that are far away can be made bigger and seen more clearly."}]}]},"crackpot":{"h":"crackpot","a":"en-us-crackpot.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(informal) A crackpot is someone that is crazy and foolish, someone that is eccentric.","e":"That person must be a crackpot for giving an idea that does not work!"},{"m":"(informal) A crackpot refers to a person that is addicted to crack cocaine. A crackpot is a drug addict."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is crackpot, it is crazy and foolish.","e":"This is such a crackpot idea. It is not possible for it to work in real life."}]}]},"creepy":{"h":"creepy","i":"/ˈkripi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-creepy.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is creepy, it produces a nervous and uneasy feeling, as if something is crawling on your skin."},{"m":"Something that is strange, eccentric and repelling."}]}]},"wikipedian":{"h":"Wikipedian","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A Wikipedian is an editor of Wikipedia, usually referring to someone that is very knowledgable about using the website."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is Wikipedian, it is related to Wikipedia."}]}]},"anglican":{"h":"Anglican","i":"/ˈæŋ.ɡlɪ.kən/","a":"en-us-Anglican.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is Anglican, it is related to the Church of England or the other churches that are part of the Anglican Communion."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An Anglican is a member of an Anglican church."}]}]},"thelema":{"h":"Thelema","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Thelema is a spiritual philosophy that tells a person to act on his or her true will in order to achieve spiritual growth."}]}]},"foreskin":{"h":"foreskin","i":"/ˈfɔːskɪn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-foreskin.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The foreskin is the fold of skin that naturally covers and protects the head of the penis."}]}]},"homologous":{"h":"homologous","i":"/həˈmɒləɡəs/","a":"en-us-homologous.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Homologous means when an organ in one kind of animal or sex of animal is similar to a different organ in a different kind of animal or sex of animal, and shares a common origin with it.","e":"The female clitoris and the male penis are homologous."}]}]},"circumcision":{"h":"circumcision","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A circumcision is the removal of the foreskin of the penis.","e":"The circumcision of men penis is a tradition in some religions."}]}]},"circumcisions":{"h":"circumcisions","l":"circumcision","q":"noun"},"foreskins":{"h":"foreskins","l":"foreskin","q":"noun"},"guild":{"h":"guild","i":"/ɡɪld/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-guild.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A guild is group of traders including of merchants, craftspeople, or artisans, especially in the Middle Ages."}]}]},"appendage":{"h":"appendage","i":"/əˈpɛndɪdʒ/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"On an organism, an appendage is an external body part that sticks out from the body.","e":"Unlike most mammals, humans have only two appendages for walking."},{"m":"An appendage is a part that is joined to something larger than itself."}]}]},"burial":{"h":"burial","i":"/ˈbɛrɪəl/","a":"en-us-burial.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A burial is the act of burying a dead human."}]}]},"broker":{"h":"broker","i":"/ˈbrəʊkə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-broker.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A broker is a person who helps a buyer and seller do a trade. A broker is usually not involved in the trade and is not biased towards either the buyer or seller."},{"m":"(countable) A broker is an agent that helps to relay and exchange messages."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you broker, you act as [[#Noun|the person]] who helps a buyer and seller do a trade."}]}]},"champagne":{"h":"champagne","i":"/ʃæmˈpeɪn/","a":"en-us-champagne.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A champagne is a wine made from grapes grown in a part of France called Champagne."},{"m":"(countable) A glass of champagne."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is champagne, it has the pale-gold color, similar to how [[#Noun|champagne]] looks like.","e":"The color of champagne"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) When you champagne, you are drinking [[#Noun|champagne]]."},{"m":"(transitive) When you champagne something, you add [[#Noun|champagne]] to it."}]}]},"correlation":{"h":"correlation","i":"/kɔrəˈleɪʃən/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(statistics) Correlation is a measure of the linear relationship between two random variables. If the correlation is higher than zero, the variables are likely to change in the same direction. If the correlation is lower than zero, the variables are likely to change in the opposite directions."},{"m":"Correlation refers to the relationship between two or more objects or events, although they may not be related to each other."}]}]},"appendages":{"h":"appendages","l":"appendage","q":"noun"},"retry":{"h":"retry","i":"/riˈtraɪ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-retry.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A retry is another try.","e":"I know that you can still master this if you just retry."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you retry at something, you try it again.","e":"I did not do this right the first time, but I am going to retry."}]}]},"kike":{"h":"kike","i":"/kaɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-kike.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Kike is a highly offensive and derogatory term meaning a Jew."},{"m":"(countable) Kike is a highly offensive term meaning an obnoxious or contemptible person, especially one who is not willing to give money."}]}]},"nativelike":{"h":"nativelike","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is nativelike, it refers to the characteristic of a native speaker of a language.","e":"Even though he was not born in an English-speaking country, his English is nativelike."}]}]},"nan":{"h":"nan","i":"/næn/","a":"en-us-nan.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Nan is a friendly and affectionate name for a grandmother."}]}]},"chancellor":{"h":"chancellor","i":"/ˈtʃɑːnsələ/","a":"en-au-chancellor.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A chancellor is a senior state or legal official."},{"m":"(countable) (education) A chancellor is the head of a university."}]}]},"great-grandparent":{"h":"great-grandparent","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A great-grandparent of a person refers to the parent of their grandparents."}]}]},"great-grandfather":{"h":"great-grandfather","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Great-grandfather refers to the father of one's grandparent."}]}]},"great-grandmother":{"h":"great-grandmother","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Great-grandmother refers to the mother of one's grandparent."}]}]},"gregarious":{"h":"gregarious","i":"/ɡrɪˈɡɛə.rɪ.əs/","a":"en-us-gregarious.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When someone is gregarious, the person likes to spend most of their time with other people and being in crowds."},{"m":"An animal is gregarious if they travel together in herds or packs.","e":"Spotted hyenas are gregarious because they are always with others of their species."}]}]},"philately":{"h":"philately","i":"/fɪˈlæt.ə.li/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Philately refers to stamp collecting."},{"m":"Philately is the study of postage stamps, postal routes, postal history, etc."}]}]},"sunniphobia":{"h":"Sunniphobia","i":"/ˈsʌniˈfəʊ.bi.ə/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Sunniphobia refers to the fear of or hating someone who is a Sunni Muslim."}]}]},"sunni":{"h":"Sunni","i":"/ˈsʊni/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Sunni.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A Sunni is a member of the Sunnism branch of Islam and their beliefs are based on the Qur'an and the.","e":"Sunnis makes up 75% of the total number of Muslims in the world.."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When someone or something is Sunni, it is related to Sunnism.","e":"May I ask if your whole family is Sunni?"}]}]},"sunnism":{"h":"Sunnism","i":"/sʌnɪ.zəm/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Sunnism refers to the Sunni Islam, an orthodox and the largest branch of Islam","e":"Sunnism is often practiced in Middle East."}]}]},"shi'ism":{"h":"Shi'ism","i":"/ʃɪ.zəm/","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Shi'ism refers to the branch of Islam that follows Ali, the cousin of prophet Muhammad.","e":"Shi'ism is often practiced in Middle East."}]}]},"perpetual":{"h":"perpetual","i":"/pɚˈpɛtʃuəl/","a":"en-us-perpetual.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is perpetual, it is something that will last forever or for a very long time."},{"m":"When something is perpetual, it will keep doing the same thing without being interrupted."}]}]},"civilization":{"h":"civilization","i":"/ˌsɪv.ɪ.laɪˈzeɪ.ʃən/","a":"en-us-civilization.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A civilization is an organized culture encompassing many, often on the scale of a nation or a people; a stage or system of political or technical development."}]}]},"admittedly":{"h":"admittedly","i":"/ədˈmɪtɪdli/","a":"en-us-admittedly.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Admittedly means is acknowledged to be true; by general admission; confessedly.","e":"Admittedly, vandalism is a bit of problem."}]}]},"mensheviki":{"h":"Mensheviki","l":"menshevik","q":"noun"},"attractivenesses":{"h":"attractivenesses","l":"attractiveness","q":"noun"},"coffins":{"h":"coffins","l":"coffin","q":"noun"},"coffined":{"h":"coffined","l":"coffin","q":"verb"},"coffining":{"h":"coffining","l":"coffin","q":"verb"},"caskets":{"h":"caskets","l":"casket","q":"noun"},"casketed":{"h":"casketed","l":"casket","q":"verb"},"casketing":{"h":"casketing","l":"casket","q":"verb"},"