 is any waste or worthless material.","e":"The dross should be separated from the melted silver and thrown away."}]}]},"drosses":{"h":"drosses","l":"dross","q":"noun"},"poverty":{"h":"poverty","i":"/ˈpɒvəti/","a":"en-us-poverty.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Poverty is the condition of being poor."},{"m":"(uncountable) Poverty is the condition of not having enough."}]}]},"philosophise":{"h":"philosophise","i":"/fɪˈlɒsəfʌɪz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-philosophize.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you philosophise, you use philosophy to think about something or discover a truth."}]}]},"outright":{"h":"outright","i":"/aʊtˈraɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-outright (adv).wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"An outright lie, victory, rejection, etc. is a complete and total one.","e":"The report was full of fake photos and outright lies."},{"m":"Outright theft, attacks, racism, etc. are clear and direct.","e":"The outright racism in his speech was shocking."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If you do something outright, you do it without hiding your feelings or purpose.","e":"I told him outright, that I would not go to his party."},{"m":"If you do something outright, you do it entirely and completely.","e":"She rejected his idea outright."}]}]},"portrayal":{"h":"portrayal","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A portrayal refers to a painting or other artwork portraying something such as a person, a landscape, or an event happening."},{"m":"A portrayal refers to the way in which a person, area or event is described when discussing it.","e":"The witness has a very interesting portrayal of how the incident happened."}]}]},"protestor":{"h":"protestor","i":"/prəˈtestər/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-protester.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A protestor is a person who protests."}]}]},"racialism":{"h":"racialism","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The belief that there are different biological races."}]}]},"enraged":{"h":"enraged","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When someone is enraged, the person is filled with rage and anger."}]}]},"harassment":{"h":"harassment","i":"/həˈræsmənt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-harassment.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Harassment refers to repeatedly annoying a person or a few people until they become and stressed.","e":"His mother constantly harassed him about his grades."},{"m":"Harassment refers to a crime whereby a person keeps repeatedly annoying someone else even though he/she has been told to stop.","e":"He kept asking questions to the woman, and she got frustrated and reported him for harassment."}]}]},"overlooked":{"h":"overlooked","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is overlooked, it is not noticed or is missed out."}]}]},"overlooking":{"h":"overlooking","a":"en-us-overlooking.ogg","l":"overlook","q":"verb"},"forenoon":{"h":"forenoon","i":"/ˈfɔːnuːn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-forenoon.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Period from sunrise to midday."}]}]},"probations":{"h":"probations","l":"probation","q":"noun"},"protester":{"h":"protester","i":"/prəˈtestər/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-protester.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A protester is a person who is protesting against something. A protester can either be one person or publicly as a group.","e":"The protesters occupied the streets and resulted in cars being unable to move."},{"m":"A protester is someone that does not agree with the bill or note."}]}]},"protesters":{"h":"protesters","l":"protester","q":"noun"},"portrayals":{"h":"portrayals","l":"portrayal","q":"noun"},"precaution":{"h":"precaution","i":"/priːˈkɔː.ʃən/","a":"en-us-precaution.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Precaution refers to previous care and caution taken to ensure safety.","e":"The father of the family took a gun out of his closet as a precaution against intruders during the night."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you precaution someone, you warn the person of possible danger."},{"m":"(transitive) When you 