."}]}]},"patronize":{"h":"patronize","i":"/ˈpeɪtrənaɪz/","a":"en-au-patronize.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you patronize someone, you become a patron and you often support him/her.","e":"He patronized the downtown restaurant."},{"m":"When you patronize someone, you talk to the person as if he/she is worse off than you and you do not treat the person with much respect."},{"m":"When you patronize a business, you become a regular customer."}]}]},"rustle":{"h":"rustle","i":"/ˈrʌsəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-rustle.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A rustle is a soft noise similar to leaf movement."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If a person rustles, he moves quietly with soft vibrational or snapping noises."}]}]},"penalize":{"h":"penalize","i":"/ˈpiː.nəl.aɪz/","a":"en-au-penalize.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) When you penalize someone, you punish the person, usually due to the person breaking a rule."},{"m":"(transitive) When you penalize a player, you cause the player to be disadvantaged."}]}]},"offhand":{"h":"offhand","i":"/ˌɔfˈhænd/","a":"en-us-offhand.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"An offhand comment, manner, joke, etc. is one that is made without careful thought.","e":"He punched the buttons with a casual, offhand style."}]}]},"offhandedly":{"h":"offhandedly","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is done or being made offhandedly, it is done or being made without thinking and planning."}]}]},"rehabilitations":{"h":"rehabilitations","l":"rehabilitation","q":"noun"},"remedial":{"h":"remedial","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A below average class to improve one's skill before advancing to the next level of the class.","e":"He had to take remedial mathematics because he was so bad at mathematics."}]}]},"reverend":{"h":"reverend","i":"/ˈrɛvrənd/","a":"en-us-reverend.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(informal) A reverend is a religious person who is the head of his church."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something 