as.","e":"The way he spoke in front of the crowd was very operatic."}]}]},"oceanic":{"h":"oceanic","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is oceanic, it is related to the ocean."},{"m":"When an animal or plant is oceanic, it lives in the open sea and is pelagic."},{"m":"When something is oceanic, it is similar to the ocean in terms of its size."}]}]},"reviewer":{"h":"reviewer","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A reviewer is a person who writes reviews things, such as books or movies, for a newspaper or other publications."}]}]},"reviewers":{"h":"reviewers","l":"reviewer","q":"noun"},"rehabilitate":{"h":"rehabilitate","i":"/riː(h)əˈbɪlɪteɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-rehabilitate.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you rehabilitate, you restore a person who committed crimes to legal and socially acceptable activities so that he can become a productive member of society."},{"m":"When you rehabilitate, you help a person with physical or mental disabilities overcome those so that he can successful."}]}]},"winder":{"h":"winder","i":"/ˈwaɪndɚ/","a":"en-au-winder.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A textile worker, or machine, that winds cloth."}]}]},"pantomimes":{"h":"pantomimes","l":"pantomime","q":"noun"},"rogue":{"h":"rogue","i":"/ˈrəʊ̯ɡ/","a":"en-us-rogue.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A rogue is an unprincipled, unreliable, and deceitful person. They do not listen to authority and do not follow rules or laws."},{"m":"(role-playing games) A common class in role-playing games is the rogue, a class all about stealth and stealing."}]}]},"rogues":{"h":"rogues","l":"rogue","q":"noun"},"negligently":{"h":"negligently","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"When something is done negligently, it means that the person doing it is neglecting something that he is supposed to be doing or neglecting another person's needs."}]}]},"participative":{"h":"participative","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something or someone is participative, it can participate or is able to participate in something."}]}]},"ripen":{"h":"ripen","i":"/ˈraɪpən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-ripen.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When a fruit or grain ripens, it becomes softer, sweeter, and ready to eat.","e":"As the summer ends, the grapes ripen to a perfect sweetness, ideal for picking."},{"m":"When a cheese ripens, it ages under controlled conditions and slowly develops its flavor, texture, and smell.","e":"This type of cheddar ripens best in a cool, dark room."}]}]},"obsession":{"h":"obsession","i":"/əbˈsɛʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-obsession.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) To have an obsession with someone or something means to have a strong and compulsive interest in or worry about someone or something; to have a fixation with/on someone or something."}]}]},"obsessions":{"h":"obsessions","l":"obsession","q":"noun"},"petitioners":{"h":"petitioners","l":"petitioner","q":"noun"},"obsessional":{"h":"obsessional","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Obsessional means when a person is obsessive about someone or something."}]}]},"probationers":{"h":"probationers","l":"probationer","q":"noun"},"patronizes":{"h":"patronizes","l":"patronize","q":"verb"},"interpenetrations":{"h":"interpenetrations","l":"interpenetration","q":"noun"},"nana":{"h":"nana","i":"/ˈnɑːnə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-nana (banana).wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(informal) Nana is a nickname that a person uses to call his/her grandmother."},{"m":"Nana refers to a nanny."},{"m":"Nana refers to a fool.","e":"You look like a nana if you wear that costume!"},{"m":"Nana is a short form of banana."}]}]},"nanas":{"h":"nanas","l":"nana","q":"noun"},"obsessionally":{"h":"obsessionally","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Obsessionally means in an obsessive manner or to an obsessive degree."}]}]},"obsessive":{"h":"obsessive","i":"/əbˈsɛsɪv/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-obsessive.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"To be obsessive about someone or something means tending to cause an obsession."}]}]},"obsessiveness":{"h":"obsessiveness","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Obsessivness means how obsessive a person is about someone or something."}]}]},"obsessively":{"h":"obsessively","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Obsessively means in an obsessive manner or to an obsessive degree."}]}]},"opting":{"h":"opting","l":"opt","q":"verb"},"opts":{"h":"opts","l":"opt","q":"verb"},"optimistically":{"h":"optimistically","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"The word optimistically means something is being done in an optimistic way."}]}]},"patronizers":{"h":"patronizers","l":"patronizer","q":"noun"},"ornamental":{"h":"ornamental","i":"/ˌɔːnəˈmɛntl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-ornamental.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Serving to ornament; characterized by ornament; beautifying; embellishing."}]}]},"panto":{"h":"panto","i":"/pæn.təʊ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-panto.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(UK) (informal) Panto is a short form of pantomime."},{"m":"(rail transport) (informal) (countable) Panto is a short form of pantograph."}]}]},"pantos":{"h":"pantos","l":"panto","q":"noun"},"ornamentally":{"h":"ornamentally","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Ornamentally means that something is being done in an ornamental manner."}]}]},"ornamentation":{"h":"ornamentation","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Ornamentation refers to the act of decorating something."}]}]},"owt":{"h":"owt","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(Northern England)Owt means anything."}]}]},"overladen":{"h":"overladen","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is overladen, it means that it is overloaded and is packed far more than what it can hold.","e":"The tray was overladen with food and the waiter was not able to carry it on one hand."},{"m":"When someone is overladen, the person is overly burdened and unable to cope with the workload.","e":"The student was overladen with homework to complete."}]}]},"outstandingly":{"h":"outstandingly","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"When something is done outstandingly, it is being done in a very outstanding and remarkable manner."}]}]},"patronise":{"h":"patronise","i":"/ˈpeɪtrənaɪz/","a":"en-au-patronize.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you patronise someone, you become a patron and you often support him/her.","e":"He patronised the downtown restaurant."},{"m":"When you patronise someone, you talk to the person as if he/she is worse off than you and you do not treat the person with much respect."},{"m":"When you patronise a business, you become a regular customer."}]}]},"patronises":{"h":"patronises","l":"patronise","q":"verb"},"extortion":{"h":"extortion","i":"/ɪkˈstɔːʃn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-extortion.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Extortion refers to a person to give you money or other property by making threats to the person."}]}]},"rapidity":{"h":"rapidity","i":"/rəˈpɪdɪti/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Rapidity refers to a person or an object being very fast or in a rapid state."},{"m":"Rapidity is a measure of velocity of something compared to the speed of light."}]}]},"protestations":{"h":"protestations","l":"protestation","q":"noun"},"raffle":{"h":"raffle","i":"/ˈræfl̩/","a":"en-us-raffle.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A raffle is a gambling contest where people can buy tickets to get a chance to win money or some other award."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you raffle something, you offer it as a prize in a contest."}]}]},"portuguese":{"h":"Portuguese","i":"/ˌpɔː.t͡ʃəˈɡiːz/","a":"en-us-Portuguese.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is Portuguese, it is related to the [[#Proper noun|Portuguese]] language or the culture and people of Portugal."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A person who is Portuguese is a native, inhabitant or citizen of Portugal."}]},{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Portuguese refers to the language that is spoken in Portugal and Brazil."}]}]},"resolve":{"h":"resolve","i":"/rɪˈzɒlv/","a":"en-us-resolve.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To resolve means to create a solution for a problem.","e":"He was able to resolve the argument with his boss by to her the next day and talking to her about what happened."},{"m":"To resolve means to make a serious decision to do something.","e":"The President said: \"I resolve to protect our country from terrorists.\""}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"If a person has resolve, they have determination. They know what they want and will not let anything keep them from getting it.","e":"Her resolve to stay on her diet was so strong that she didn't even eat any cake at her own birthday party."}]}]},"porch":{"h":"porch","a":"en-us-porch.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A porch is a covered and enclosed entrance into a building. It is similar to an extended roof that covers an area in front of an entrance."},{"m":"A porch is also known as a portico, which is a covered walkway into a building."}]}]},"porches":{"h":"porches","l":"porch","q":"noun"},"imperishable":{"h":"imperishable","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When something is imperishable, it is something that cannot decay or be destroyed. It is not perishable and can last for a very long time."}]}]},"primaries":{"h":"primaries","l":"primary","q":"noun"},"fascists":{"h":"fascists","l":"fascist","q":"noun"},"provisionals":{"h":"provisionals","l":"provisional","q":"noun"},"saleswomen":{"h":"saleswomen","l":"saleswoman","q":"noun"},"poachers":{"h":"poachers","l":"poacher","q":"noun"},"pedestrianisation":{"h":"pedestrianisation","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Pedestrianisation refers to making a street become only usable by people (pedestrians) instead of being used by vehicles such as cars."}]}]},"pedestrianization":{"h":"pedestrianization","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Pedestrianization refers to making a street become only usable by people (pedestrians) instead of being used by vehicles such as cars."}]}]},"persistently":{"h":"persistently","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"When something is done 