(countable) A massotherapist is someone who does massotherapy.","e":"The athlete visited a massotherapist for his muscles."}]}]},"similarly":{"h":"similarly","i":"/ˈsɪməlɚli/","a":"en-us-similarly.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"You use, similarly to show that two ideas are partly the same.","e":"Canadians sell more TV programs abroad than almost any other country. Similarly, Canadian songwriters sell more of their music abroad than they do in Canada."}]}]},"catsup":{"h":"catsup","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Another word for ketchup."}]}]},"hog":{"h":"hog","i":"/hɒɡ/","a":"en-us-hog.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hog is a pig.","e":"We keep cows, chickens, and hogs."},{"m":"(countable) A hog is somebody who doesn't share.","e":"Give me that. Don't be such a hog."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you hog something, keep it to yourself and don't share it.","e":"John is always hogging the TV remote."}]}]},"tawdry":{"h":"tawdry","i":"/ˈtɔːdri/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-tawdry.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is tawdry, it looks nice but is actually of bad quality. It is showy yet cheap.","e":"I can only afford to wear tawdry jewelry."}]}]},"rebuke":{"h":"rebuke","i":"/riˈbjuːk/","a":"en-us-rebuke.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you rebuke someone, you tell them that they did something bad.","e":"Sohan rebuked his children for their mistakes."}]}]},"rebukes":{"h":"rebukes","l":"rebuke","q":"verb"},"rebuked":{"h":"rebuked","l":"rebuke","q":"verb"},"rebuking":{"h":"rebuking","l":"rebuke","q":"verb"},"macaw":{"h":"macaw","i":"/məˈkɔː/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-macaw.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A macaw is a parrot with a long tail that lives in South America.","e":"My pet macaw keeps squawking all the time."}]}]},"skinhead":{"h":"skinhead","i":"/ˈskɪn.hɛd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Flame, not lame-skinhead.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A skinhead is someone who has shaved his or her head."},{"m":"(countable) Members of racist (white supremacy) skinhead groups, who often have shaved heads, are called skinheads."}]}]},"squad":{"h":"squad","i":"/ˈskwɒd/","a":"en-au-squad.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A squad is a group of people.","e":"The England cricket squad won their last match."}]}]},"depot":{"h":"depot","i":"/ˈdɛpəʊ/","a":"en-us-depot.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A depot is an area where equipment or goods are stored."},{"m":"(countable) A depot is an area where vehicles are stored."}]}]},"depots":{"h":"depots","l":"depot","q":"noun"},"batsman":{"h":"batsman","i":"/ˈbætsmən/","a":"en-au-batsman.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (cricket) A batsman is a role in cricket whose skill is to bat.","e":"The batsman hit the ball."}]}]},"scrum":{"h":"scrum","i":"/skrʌm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-scrum.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(rugby) (countable) A scrum is a group of players huddling together in order to gain possession of the ball in a game of rugby."}]}]},"bowler":{"h":"bowler","i":"/ˈbəʊ.lə/","a":"en-us-bowler.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (cricket) A bowler is a role in cricket which involves bowling the ball to the batsman.","e":"The bowler bowls the ball and hits the stumps."},{"m":"(countable) (bowls) A bowler is the player who rolls the ball in a game of bowls."},{"m":"(countable) (bowling) A bowler is the player in a game of bowling."}]}]},"smartphone":{"h":"smartphone","i":"/ˈsmɑːtfəʊn/","a":"en-us-smartphone.oga","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A smartphone is a mobile personal computer with a mobile operating system with features useful for mobile or handheld use."}]}]},"laser":{"h":"laser","i":"/ˈleɪz.ə(r)/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-laser.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A laser is a device that emits light through a process of optical amplification based on the stimulated emission of electromagnetic radiation."},{"m":"The term laser originated as an acronym for \"light amplification by stimulated emission of radiation\"."}]}]},"goad":{"h":"goad","i":"/ɡəʊd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-goad.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you goad someone, you annoy or bother them to get them to do something.","e":"My frequent questions will goad her into telling me the full story."},{"m":"If you goad goad an animal, you poke it with a sharp stick to make it move."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A goad is a spiked stick used to drive animals."},{"m":"A goad can be anything that is used to get a response from someone.","e":"The poor test results were a goad for him to begin working harder."}]}]},"dyspraxia":{"h":"dyspraxia","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Dyspraxia is a disability in the brain that interferes with movement.","e":"My dyspraxia makes my writing very messy."}]}]},"fiscal":{"h":"fiscal","i":"/ˈfɪskəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-fiscal.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Fiscal policy, problems, health, etc. all relate to how a company or government manages money.","e":"The fiscal year at Apple ends in September."}]}]},"jewries":{"h":"Jewries","l":"jewry","q":"noun"},"dyspraxias":{"h":"dyspraxias","l":"dyspraxia","q":"noun"},"unsurprised":{"h":"unsurprised","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is unsurprised about something, they expected it."}]}]},"talker":{"h":"talker","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A talker is a person who talks a lot or talks in a special way.","e":"He's bald and thin, and he's a fast talker."}]}]},"unaccountable":{"h":"unaccountable","i":"/ˌʌnəˈkaʊntəbl̩/","a":"en-us-unaccountable.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is unaccountable, it is surprising and you cannot explain it."},{"m":"If someone is unaccountable, they don't have to explain their actions or decisions."}]}]},"therapist":{"h":"therapist","i":"/ˈθɛrəpɪst/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-therapist.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A therapist is someone who is skilled in a particular type of therapy."}]}]},"handbook":{"h":"handbook","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A handbook is a book informing people about rules or giving instructions about how to perform a task."}]}]},"handbooks":{"h":"handbooks","l":"handbook","q":"noun"},"reinforcement":{"h":"reinforcement","i":"/ˌriːɪnˈfɔː(r)smənt/","a":"en-us-reinforcement.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A reinforcement is something that makes something more strong."},{"m":"A reinforcement in behavioral psychology is a reward designed to make encouraged behavior more likely to continue."}]}]},"reinforcements":{"h":"reinforcements","l":"reinforcement","q":"noun"},"prayer":{"h":"prayer","i":"/prɛə(r)/","a":"en-us-prayer.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A prayer is when a person tries to communicate with a god he believes in and make requests for help to the god or give him devotion and praise."}]}]},"prayers":{"h":"prayers","l":"prayer","q":"noun"},"locus":{"h":"locus","i":"/ˈləʊkəs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-locus.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A locus is a place or location."},{"m":"A locus is a set of points that meets some condition."}]}]},"secrecy":{"h":"secrecy","i":"/ˈsiːkrəsi/","a":"en-us-secrecy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Secrecy is the state or quality of something being secret."}]}]},"defendant":{"h":"defendant","i":"/dɪˈfɛnd.ənt/","a":"en-us-defendant.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A defendant is a person being prosecuted for breaking the law."}]}]},"moonlight":{"h":"moonlight","i":"/ˈmunˌlaɪt/","a":"en-us-moonlight.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Moonlight is light coming from the moon."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If a person moonlights, they work a second job, often in the evening or during the night."}]}]},"housekeeping":{"h":"housekeeping","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Housekeeping is work done to keep a place such as a restaurant, hotel or home clean."}]}]},"pyramid":{"h":"pyramid","i":"/ˈpɪrəmɪd/","a":"en-us-pyramid.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pyramid is an ancient kind of religious monument shaped with four triangles meeting at the top and being supported by a square or rectangle as its floor.","e":"We went to the pyramids of Giza in Egypt."},{"m":"(countable) A pyramid is a 3D shape with a polygon base connected to a point."}]}]},"forgiveness":{"h":"forgiveness","i":"/fɚˈɡɪvnəs/","a":"en-us-forgiveness.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Forgiveness is when a person forgives another person for his bad action."}]}]},"gunboat":{"h":"gunboat","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A gunboat is a boat carrying guns."}]}]},"magistrate":{"h":"magistrate","i":"/ˈmædʒɪstreɪt/","a":"En-us-magistrate.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A magistrate is a judicial officer with limited power to enforce the law."}]}]},"statutory":{"h":"statutory","i":"/ˈstætjʊt(ə)rɪ/","a":"en-us-statutory.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Statutory rules are government rules imposed by statute.","e":"The minimum statutory legal age for sexual activity in France is 15 years old."}]}]},"flourish":{"h":"flourish","i":"/ˈflʌr.ɪʃ/","a":"en-us-flourish.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If something flourishes, it thrives or grows well or successfully.","e":"The plants flourished in the greenhouse."}]}]},"statute":{"h":"statute","i":"/ˈstætʃuːt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-statute.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A statute is a law.","e":"The Statute of Kilkenny forbid English from marrying Irish or using Irish language."}]}]},"statutes":{"h":"statutes","l":"statute","q":"noun"},"literary":{"h":"literary","i":"/ˈlɪtərəri/","a":"en-us-literary.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something literary is something of or related to literature.","e":"He was a literary expert, knowing vast amounts of information on the works of Charles Dickens and other authors."}]}]},"magnificent":{"h":"magnificent","i":"/mæɡˈnɪfəsənt/","a":"en-us-magnificent.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is magnificent, it is very wonderful, beautiful or impressive in appearance."}]}]},"pubescent":{"h":"pubescent","i":"/pjʊˈbɛs(ə)nt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-pubescent.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pubescent is a person who is going through puberty."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something pubescent is something during the beginning and early stages of puberty."},{"m":"Something pubescent is something of or related to puberty."}]}]},"scramble":{"h":"scramble","i":"/ˈskræmbl̩/","a":"en-us-scramble.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you scramble, you climb quickly and with difficulty, often using your hands to help you.","e":"They scrambled like spiders up the rocks."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you scramble to do something, you do quickly and with difficulty.","e":"She scrambled out of her car."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you scramble for something, you compete or fight with others to get it.","e":"When the new show was announced everyone scrambled for tickets."},{"m":"(transitive) (food) If you scramble food, you mix and then cook it.","e":"He scrambled some eggs."},{"m":"(transitive) If something is scrambled, it is mixed up.","e":"Sometimes using email can scramble the message."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A scramble is when someone is hurrying or doing something really fast."}]}]},"inasmuch":{"h":"inasmuch","i":"/ˌɪnəzˈmʌt͡ʃ/","a":"en-us-inasmuch.ogg","s":[{"p":"preposition","d":[{"m":"If x is true inasmuch as y, x is true because or only at the same level as y is true.","e":"The Knights of Columbus is a secret society inasmuch as having oaths makes a group a secret society."}]}]},"treasury":{"h":"treasury","i":"/ˈtrɛʒəri/","a":"en-us-treasury.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A treasury is a government department handling money."},{"m":"A treasury is a place treasure or money is held."}]}]},"hanger":{"h":"hanger","i":"/hæŋə(r)/","a":"en-au-hanger.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hanger is a device to hang clothing on."}]}]},"dyscalculia":{"h":"dyscalculia","i":"/ˌdɪskælˈkjuːli.ə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-dyscalculia.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Dyscalculia is when a person has a mathematical disability."}]}]},"sundae":{"h":"sundae","i":"/ˈsʌndeɪ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-sundae1.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A sundae is a type of ice cream dessert.","e":"I had a sundae after lunch today."}]}]},"extinction":{"h":"extinction","i":"/ɪkˈstɪŋkʃ(ə)n/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-extinction.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The extinction of a type of plant, animal, job, etc is when it does not exist anymore."}]}]},"loyalty":{"h":"loyalty","i":"/ˈlɔɪəlti/","a":"en-us-loyalty.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Loyalty is the quality or state of a person or group of persons being loyal to someone or something.","e":"The Germans exhibited great loyalty to Hitler during his rule in Germany."}]}]},"housework":{"h":"housework","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Housework is work done in your own home for your family, such as cleaning and cooking."}]}]},"earnest":{"h":"earnest","i":"/ˈɝnɪst/","a":"en-us-earnest.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is earnest, they are serious and truly believe in what they say or do."}]}]},"annoyance":{"h":"annoyance","i":"/əˈnɔɪəns/","a":"en-us-annoyance.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An annoyance is something or someone that makes a person angry or bothered."}]}]},"discontent":{"h":"discontent","i":"/ˌdɪskənˈtɛnt/","a":"en-us-discontent.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Discontent is the feeling you have when you are not happy with your own life."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you are discontented, you are not satisfied."}]}]},"fisher":{"h":"fisher","i":"/ˈfɪʃə/","a":"en-us-fisher.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A fisher is a person who catches fish."},{"m":"(countable) A fisher is a boat used for catching fish."},{"m":"(countable) A fisher is an animal."}]}]},"hoax":{"h":"hoax","i":"/hoʊks/","a":"en-us-hoax.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A hoax is anything done on purpose to trick or fool people."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you hoax someone, you mislead them on purpose by making them believe something which has been made up to trick or fool them."}]}]},"catalan":{"h":"Catalan","i":"/ˈkæ.tə.ˌlæn/","a":"en-us-Catalan.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Catalan is the language in Catalonia."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A Catalan is a person or thing that comes from Catalonia."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something or someone that is Catalan comes from Catalonia.","e":"My friend Matías is Catalan."}]}]},"catalans":{"h":"Catalans","l":"catalan","q":"noun"},"skater":{"h":"skater","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A skater is a person who skates.","e":"He likes winter sports and he's a good ice skater."}]}]},"skaters":{"h":"skaters","l":"skater","q":"noun"},"mexican":{"h":"Mexican","i":"/ˈmɛksɪk(ə)n/","a":"en-au-Mexican.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A Mexican is a person or thing that comes from Mexico."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something or someone that is Mexican comes from Mexico.","e":"The Mexican currency is the Peso."}]}]},"mexicans":{"h":"Mexicans","l":"mexican","q":"noun"},"millimeter":{"h":"millimeter","i":"/ˈmɪləˌmitɚ/","a":"en-us-millimetre.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A millimeter is one tenth of a centimeter.","e":"The smallest measurement of a ruler is the millimeter. You need another tool to measure objects smaller than that."}]}]},"millimeters":{"h":"millimeters","l":"millimeter","q":"noun"},"euphonium":{"h":"euphonium","i":"/juːˈfəʊnɪəm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-euphonium.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A euphonium is a musical instrument that plays notes that are between tenor and bass, such as a baritone.","e":"The euphonium looks similar to the tuba."}]}]},"euphoniums":{"h":"euphoniums","l":"euphonium","q":"noun"},"piccolo":{"h":"piccolo","i":"/fluːt/","a":"en-us-flute.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A piccolo is a musical i