de street in a town or city.","e":"Turn right at Sunset Boulevard."}]}]},"boulevards":{"h":"boulevards","l":"boulevard","q":"noun"},"tortoises":{"h":"tortoises","l":"tortoise","q":"noun"},"snails":{"h":"snails","l":"snail","q":"noun"},"slang":{"h":"slang","i":"/slæŋ/","a":"en-us-slang.ogg","l":"sling","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Slang is an informal way of speaking that is used mostly within certain social groups.","e":"I have trouble understanding my kids' slang."}]}]},"lilac":{"h":"lilac","i":"/ˈlaɪlək/","a":"en-us-lilac.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Lilac is a brightly-coloured flower.","e":"There were lilacs in my garden."},{"m":"(uncountable) Lilac is a pinkish-purple colour."}]}]},"lilacs":{"h":"lilacs","l":"lilac","q":"noun"},"punt":{"h":"punt","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A punt is a type of boat.","e":"We sailed on a punt."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you punt, you guess on something.","e":"I will take a punt on B as the answer to your question."}]}]},"punts":{"h":"punts","l":"punt","q":"noun"},"punted":{"h":"punted","l":"punt","q":"verb"},"punting":{"h":"punting","l":"punt","q":"verb"},"paintbrush":{"h":"paintbrush","i":"/ˈpeɪntˌbrʌʃ/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A paintbrush is a brush that people use for painting.","e":"This paintbrush is used for small details."}]}]},"paintbrushes":{"h":"paintbrushes","l":"paintbrush","q":"noun"},"choreographer":{"h":"choreographer","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A choreographer is a person who choreographs dances.","e":"The choreographer worked on all the dances in the movie."}]}]},"choreographers":{"h":"choreographers","l":"choreographer","q":"noun"},"cookbooks":{"h":"cookbooks","l":"cookbook","q":"noun"},"loci":{"h":"loci","i":"/ˈləʊsaɪ/","l":"locus","q":"noun"},"manga":{"h":"manga","i":"/ˈmɑŋɡə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-manga.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Manga is a style of Japanese comic books.","e":"The manga was turned into an anime movie last year."}]}]},"bittersweet":{"h":"bittersweet","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A bittersweet feeling is both sad and happy.","e":"He remembered the bittersweet memories in the school."},{"m":"If a food or drink is bittersweet is sweet but has a bitter aftertaste."}]}]},"nocturnal":{"h":"nocturnal","i":"/nɒkˈtɜː(r)nəl/","a":"en-us-nocturnal.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"When someone is nocturnal, they are active and awake at night.","e":"s are nocturnal animals."}]}]},"companion":{"h":"companion","i":"/kəmˈpænjən/","a":"en-us-companion.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A companion is somebody who you spend time with, usually because you enjoy being with them.","e":"In some places, it's best to travel with a companion."},{"m":"(countable) If x is a companion to y, x and y go together.","e":"Pain is a natural companion to art."}]}]},"fishers":{"h":"fishers","l":"fisher","q":"noun"},"mackerel":{"h":"mackerel","i":"/ˈmækrəl/","a":"en-us-mackerel.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mackerel is a type of pelagic fish.","e":"We cooked mackerel for dinner."}]}]},"mackerels":{"h":"mackerels","l":"mackerel","q":"noun"},"archery":{"h":"archery","i":"/ɑrtʃəriː/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-archery.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Archery is an activity where people use bows to shoot arrows.","e":"Archery is an Olympic sport."}]}]},"dime":{"h":"dime","i":"/daɪm/","a":"en-au-dime.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (US, Canada) A dime is a metal coin that is worth ten cents.","e":"Ten dimes is one dollar."}]}]},"dimes":{"h":"dimes","l":"dime","q":"noun"},"radius":{"h":"radius","i":"/ˈreɪdi.əs/","a":"en-us-radius.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"; (countable) A radius is a straight line between the centre of a circle and its circumference.","e":"To find the area of a circle, you have to know the length of the radius."}]}]},"radii":{"h":"radii","l":"radius","q":"noun"},"radiuses":{"h":"radiuses","l":"radius","q":"noun"},"classification":{"h":"classification","i":"/ˌklæsɪfɪˈkeɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-classification.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A classification the system of groups that are based on the characteristics of the group members.","e":"Linnaeus was known for his system of plant classification, which ordered plants according to their sexual parts."},{"m":"(uncountable) Classification is the process of organizing things into groups based on their characteristics.","e":"The information that was originally on our website was based on an earlier classification."},{"m":"(countable) A classification is one group of things that have similar characteristics.","e":"The raises are going out mostly to employees in different skill classifications."}]}]},"classifications":{"h":"classifications","l":"classification","q":"noun"},"lukewarm":{"h":"lukewarm","i":"/ˌluːkˈwɔːm/","a":"en-us-lukewarm.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is lukewarm is slightly warm.","e":"Wash the dishes in lukewarm water."}]}]},"steadfast":{"h":"steadfast","i":"/ˈstɛdfæst/","a":"En-us-steadfast.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something or someone that is steadfast is very determined.","e":"Your steadfast loyalty won't help you."}]}]},"repetition":{"h":"repetition","i":"/rɛpəˈtɪʃən/","a":"en-us-repetition.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Repetition is the same thing happening more than one time, usually many times, especially in speaking or writing.","e":"The article is too long because of all the repetition."},{"m":"(countable) A repetition is the second, third, fourth, etc. time that something happens.","e":"With this exercise, aim for 3 sets of 20 repetitions."}]}]},"cupcake":{"h":"cupcake","i":"/ˈkʌpkeɪk/","a":"en-au-cupcake.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cupcake is a small cake that is baked in a small cup.","e":"They baked cupcakes for the bake sale."}]}]},"cupcakes":{"h":"cupcakes","l":"cupcake","q":"noun"},"vibe":{"h":"vibe","i":"/vaɪb/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-vibe.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(informal); (countable) A vibe is a person's emotions or feelings because of their surroundings.","e":"I'm getting bad vibes from this place."}]}]},"vibes":{"h":"vibes","l":"vibe","q":"noun"},"sob":{"h":"sob","i":"/sɒb/","a":"en-us-sob.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you sob, you cry very loudly.","e":"She went to bed sobbing."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sob is a sound you make when you cry."}]}]},"sobs":{"h":"sobs","l":"sob","q":"verb"},"sobbed":{"h":"sobbed","l":"sob","q":"verb"},"sobbing":{"h":"sobbing","l":"sob","q":"verb"},"radish":{"h":"radish","i":"/ˈradɪʃ/","a":"en-us-radish.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A radish is a type of root vegetable that is small and red.","e":"Put the radishes in the salad."}]}]},"radishes":{"h":"radishes","l":"radish","q":"noun"},"persimmon":{"h":"persimmon","i":"/pɜːˈsɪmən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-persimmon.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A persimmon is a sweet, orange fruit.","e":"Would you like to eat a persimmon or a tangerine?"},{"m":"(countable) A persimmon is the tree that the fruit grows on."}]}]},"persimmons":{"h":"persimmons","l":"persimmon","q":"noun"},"chipped":{"h":"chipped","l":"chip","q":"verb"},"chipping":{"h":"chipping","l":"chip","q":"verb"},"ritual":{"h":"ritual","i":"/ˈrɪ.tʃu.əl/","a":"en-us-ritual.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A ritual is a ceremony that always follows the same steps.","e":"The annual ritual to honour the gods was tomorrow."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is ritual is related to a ritual or rite."}]}]},"inquire":{"h":"inquire","i":"/ɪnˈkwaɪr/","a":"en-us-inquire.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you inquire about something, you ask about it.","e":"I was telling everybody that inquired about him that he was dead."},{"m":"If you inquire into something, you investigate it.","e":"In order to move forward you need to inquire into the nature of the problem."}]}]},"straightens":{"h":"straightens","l":"straighten","q":"verb"},"straightened":{"h":"straightened","l":"straighten","q":"verb"},"straightening":{"h":"straightening","l":"straighten","q":"verb"},"customary":{"h":"customary","i":"/ˈkʌst(ə)mri/","a":"en-us-customary.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is customary, it is usual.","e":"Before the meeting, there were the customary greetings and exchange of gifts."}]}]},"doorknob":{"h":"doorknob","i":"/ˈdɔː.nɒb/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-doorknob.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A doorknob is a round handle on a drawer or a door that you turn to open.","e":"The door has a doorknob, not a handle."}]}]},"doorknobs":{"h":"doorknobs","l":"doorknob","q":"noun"},"exaggeration":{"h":"exaggeration","i":"/ɪɡˌzæd͡ʒəˈreɪʃən/","a":"en-us-exaggeration.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An exaggeration is when someone says something is better or worse than it really is.","e":"Your sentence is an exaggeration."}]}]},"exaggerations":{"h":"exaggerations","l":"exaggeration","q":"noun"},"citrus":{"h":"citrus","i":"/ˈsɪ.trəs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-citrus.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A citrus is a tree that can grow oranges, lemons, limes, and grapefruits.","e":"We can't grow citrus trees in Canada."},{"m":"A citrus is a fruit that comes from a citrus tree."}]}]},"citruses":{"h":"citruses","l":"citrus","q":"noun"},"mercy":{"h":"mercy","i":"/ˈmɜːsi/","a":"en-us-mercy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Mercy is the quality of kindness and forgiveness that stops you from harming or punishing somebody who you could harm or punish.","e":"The king would always prefer to show mercy, even to his enemies."},{"m":"(countable) A mercy is a situation that it makes you feel lucky, usually because something worse didn't happen.","e":"It was a small mercy that the storm didn't last long."},{"m":"A mercy mission or journey is one to help people who are in great need.","e":"They took food and set out on a mercy mission to find survivors."},{"m":"If you are at the mercy of somebody or something, you have no control over your situation.","e":"I hope the trip will be nice, but we're at the mercy of the weather."}]},{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"You use mercy or mercy me to show surprise.","e":"Mercy! You haven't come here alone, have you?"}]}]},"empties":{"h":"empties","l":"empty","q":"verb"},"emptying":{"h":"emptying","l":"empty","q":"verb"},"grasps":{"h":"grasps","l":"grasp","q":"verb"},"grasping":{"h":"grasping","l":"grasp","q":"verb"},"cape":{"h":"cape","i":"/keɪp/","a":"en-us-cape.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cape is a long piece of cloth tied around the neck and worn down the back."},{"m":"(countable) A cape is a long piece of land that sticks out into a sea or lake."}]}]},"capes":{"h":"capes","l":"cape","q":"noun"},"oblations":{"h":"oblations","l":"oblation","q":"noun"},"variant":{"h":"variant","i":"/ˈvɛəri.ənt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-variant.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A varient of something is a bit different than the original.","e":"The anthem is a varient of Beethoven's \"Ode to Joy\"."}]}]},"variants":{"h":"variants","l":"variant","q":"noun"},"anthem":{"h":"anthem","i":"/ˈæn.θəm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-anthem.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An anthem is a type of song.","e":"Please stand for the national anthem."}]}]},"anthems":{"h":"anthems","l":"anthem","q":"noun"},"memo":{"h":"memo","i":"/ˈmɛməʊ̯/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-memo.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (informal) A memo is a short message or note.","e":"I have an urgent memo from the CEO."}]}]},"memos":{"h":"memos","l":"memo","q":"noun"},"agonic":{"h":"agonic","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A shape, line, etc. that is agonic doesn't have an angle."},{"m":"Something that is agonic has a lot of agony."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An agonic is an agonic line."}]}]},"agon":{"h":"agon","i":"/ˈæ.ɡəʊn/","a":"en-au-agon.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An agon is a fight or argument in books, between the main character and their enemy.","e":"The agon in is between the kids and It."},{"m":"(uncountable) Agon is a game that is played on a hexagonal board.","e":"Agon was played in Britain."}]}]},"agons":{"h":"agons","l":"agon","q":"noun"},"agones":{"h":"agones","l":"agon","q":"noun"},"agonics":{"h":"agonics","l":"agonic","q":"noun"},"alpenglow":{"h":"alpenglow","i":"/ˈæl.pən.ɡloʊ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-alpenglow.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An alpenglow is a red glow that shines from mountains.","e":"The alpenglow can be seen at sunrise or sunset."}]}]},"alpenglows":{"h":"alpenglows","l":"alpenglow","q":"noun"},"indelible":{"h":"indelible","i":"/ɪnˈdɛləbl/","a":"en-us-indelible.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A stain, smear, etc. that is indelible is hard to remove.","e":"This stain on my shirt is indelible."}]}]},"oniochalasia":{"h":"oniochalasia","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Oniochalasia is when a person buys things to relax themselves."}]}]},"problematic":{"h":"problematic","i":"/ˌprɒblɛˈmætɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-problematic.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is problematic, it is causing a problem.","e":"Rush hour at the train station was very problematic."}]}]},"tripod":{"h":"tripod","i":"/ˈtraɪpɒd/","a":"en-au-tripod.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A tripod is a stand that supports cameras.","e":"I put my camera on the tripod so that I can capture better pictures."},{"m":"(countable) A tripod is a seat or table that has three legs."}]}]},"tripods":{"h":"tripods","l":"tripod","q":"noun"},"humble":{"h":"humble","i":"/ˈhʌmbəl/","a":"en-us-humble.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are humble, you are aware of your own weaknesses and do not want or accept recognition of your good qualities or successes.","e":"You can tell he's very quiet and humble and he keeps to himself."},{"m":"A humble place or thing is ordinary and not special.","e":"In my humble opinion, we need to make these changes quickly."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you humble someone, you easily beat them, even though they have a strong advantage.","e":"The weak will grow strong, and the mighty will be humbled."},{"m":"If you are humbled, you are shown that you are not as important or good as you thought you were.","e":"I was also honored and deeply humbled to see the great work that my students are doing."}]}]},"disband":{"h":"disband","i":"/dɪsˈbænd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-disband.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If a company, group, etc. disbands, it breaks up.","e":"disbanded in 1970."}]}]},"disbands":{"h":"disbands","l":"disband","q":"verb"},"disbanded":{"h":"disbanded","l":"disband","q":"verb"},"disbanding":{"h":"disbanding","l":"disband","q":"verb"},"armory":{"h":"armory","i":"/ˈɑrməri/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-armoury.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An armory is where weapons are kept."},{"m":"An armory is a collection of weapons."},{"m":"An armory is a place where weapons are made."}]}]},"armories":{"h":"armories","l":"armory","q":"noun"},"misconception":{"h":"misconception","i":"/ˌmɪskənˈsɛp.ʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-misconception.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A misconception is a wrong idea.","e":"You're under the misconception that you're better than him."}]}]},"misconceptions":{"h":"misconceptions","l":"misconception","q":"noun"},"veil":{"h":"veil","i":"/veɪl/","a":"en-us-veil.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A veil is a thin piece of cloth that hides a woman's face.","e":"Her hair fell over her face like a veil."},{"m":"(countable) A veil is something that hides important information about a situation.","e":"The election lifted the thin veil and fully exposed the truth about America."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you veil something, you make it hard to see or understand."}]}]},"veils":{"h":"veils","l":"veil","q":"noun"},"prescribe":{"h":"prescribe","i":"/prɪˈskrʌɪb/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-prescribe.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If a doctor prescribes you a medicine or treatment, they tell you what medicine or treatment to use.","e":"The doctor will prescribe me some tablets."},{"m":"(transitive) If someone prescribes a rule or a way to do something, they are telling people to follow that rule or do something a certain way.","e":"We have to follow what the law prescribes."}]}]},"prescribing":{"h":"prescribing","l":"prescribe","q":"verb"},"councilmen":{"h":"councilmen","l":"councilman","q":"noun"},"mansion":{"h":"mansion","i":"/ˈmæn(t)ʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-mansion.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mansion is a large house that is usually really expensive.","e":"The rich live in mansions."}]}]},"mansions":{"h":"mansions","l":"mansion","q":"noun"},"cultivate":{"h":"cultivate","i":"/ˈkʌltɪveɪt/","a":"en-us-cultivate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you cultivate a crop, you grow it.","e":"By 3,600 years ago, farmers were cultivating cereals at a high altitude."},{"m":"(transitive) If you cultivate land, you grow crops on it.","e":"The government gave farmers the right to cultivate more than one million hectares of unused farmland."},{"m":"(transitive) If you cultivate a relationship, an image, or a skill, you develop it.","e":"An additional important strategy noted was the importance of cultivating relationships with people."}]}]},"harmonious":{"h":"harmonious","i":"/hɑrˈmoʊni.əs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-harmonious.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is harmonious, it sounds pleasant and tuneful.","e":"The music sounded harmonious."}]}]},"cultivating":{"h":"cultivating","l":"cultivate","q":"verb"},"ballot":{"h":"ballot","i":"/ˈbalət/","a":"en-au-ballot.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A ballot is a piece of paper or a card that is used in voting.","e":"The ballot listed three candidates."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you ballot, you vote or decide by [[#Noun|ballot]].","e":"to ballot for a candidate"},{"m":"If you ballot, you draw lots."}]}]},"ballots":{"h":"ballots","l":"ballot","q":"noun"},"origami":{"h":"origami","i":"/ˌɔrəˈɡɑmi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-origami.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Origami is a type of art where people fold paper.","e":"Origami came from Japan."},{"m":"(countable) Origami is a piece of art that is made of folded paper.","e":"I can fold origami cranes."}]}]},"origamis":{"h":"origamis","l":"origami","q":"noun"},"discriminatory":{"h":"discriminatory","i":"/dɪsˈkrɪmɪnət(ə)rɪ/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is discriminatory discriminates against someone or something.","e":"The laws are discriminatory towards Asians."}]}]},"aftermath":{"h":"aftermath","i":"/ˈæf.tɚˌmæθ/","a":"en-us-aftermath.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The aftermath of a flood, shooting, etc. is what happens after it. It is usually bad, not good.","e":"The aftermath of the flood was devastating."}]}]},"aftermaths":{"h":"aftermaths","l":"aftermath","q":"noun"},"drought":{"h":"drought","i":"/draʊt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-drought.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A drought is when there is less water in an area than normal.","e":"The drought in California began in 2012."}]}]},"droughts":{"h":"droughts","l":"drought","q":"noun"},"collector":{"h":"collector","i":"/kəˈlɛktɚ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-collector.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A collector is somebody who collects things, usually things that are rare and interesting.","e":"A collector would be willing to pay a lot of money for that painting."},{"m":"(countable) A ticket collector is somebody who checks your ticket on a bus or train.","e":"After you get on the bus, be ready to show your ticket to the collector."},{"m":"(countable) A debt collector is somebody who tries to make people pay their debts when payment is late.","e":"Life was very difficult when a debt collector started calling daily."}]}]},"paraphrase":{"h":"paraphrase","i":"/ˈparəfreɪz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-paraphrase.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you paraphrase something, you say it again in different words.","e":"When paraphrasing books, don't copy everything in it; instead, use your own words."}]}]},"paraphrases":{"h":"paraphrases","l":"paraphrase","q":"verb"},"paraphrased":{"h":"paraphrased","l":"paraphrase","q":"verb"},"paraphrasing":{"h":"paraphrasing","l":"paraphrase","q":"verb"},"integers":{"h":"integers","l":"integer","q":"noun"},"earbud":{"h":"earbud","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable); (usually plural) An earbud is a small headphone that you put in your ear.","e":"I use earbuds for listening to music."}]}]},"earbuds":{"h":"earbuds","l":"earbud","q":"noun"},"sabotage":{"h":"sabotage","i":"/ˈsæbətɑʒ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-sabotage.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If a building, event, etc. are sabotaged, they are damaged so that they can't work properly.","e":"Her rival sabotaged the concert."}]}]},"sabotages":{"h":"sabotages","l":"sabotage","q":"verb"},"sabotaged":{"h":"sabotaged","l":"sabotage","q":"verb"},"sabotaging":{"h":"sabotaging","l":"sabotage","q":"verb"},"favela":{"h":"favela","i":"/faˈvɛlə/","a":"en-ca-favela.oga","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A favela is a neighbourhood where many poorer people live.","e":"6% of people in Brazil live in favelas."}]}]},"favelas":{"h":"favelas","l":"favela","q":"noun"},"slum":{"h":"slum","i":"/slʌm/","a":"en-us-slum.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A slum is a neighbourhood where many poorer people live.","e":"The slums of Rio de Janeiro don't have proper sewage treatment."}]}]},"slums":{"h":"slums","l":"slum","q":"noun"},"novella":{"h":"novella","i":"/nəˈvɛlə/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A novella is a short form of a book. It has between 7,500 and 40,000 words.","e":"by has 30,000 words and would be considered a novella."}]}]},"novellas":{"h":"novellas","l":"novella","q":"noun"},"sleeted":{"h":"sleeted","l":"sleet","q":"verb"},"sleeting":{"h":"sleeting","l":"sleet","q":"verb"},"earthworm":{"h":"earthworm","i":"/ˈɜː(r)θˌwɜː(r)m/","a":"en-us-earthworm.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An earthworm is a type of worm that lives in the ground.","e":"When it was raining, the earthworms came out."}]}]},"earthworms":{"h":"earthworms","l":"earthworm","q":"noun"},"enthrall":{"h":"enthrall","i":"/ɪnˈθrɔːl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-enthrall.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If someone is enthralled, they get a huge fascination with a person or thing.","e":"The singer was able to enthrall audiences with her unique voice."}]}]},"enthralled":{"h":"enthralled","l":"enthrall","q":"verb"},"enthralling":{"h":"enthralling","l":"enthrall","q":"verb"},"enthralls":{"h":"enthralls","l":"enthrall","q":"verb"},"confront":{"h":"confront","i":"/kʌnˈfrʌnt/","a":"en-us-confront.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you are confronted with something, you come face to face with it.","e":"The man confronted the burglar."}]}]},"confronts":{"h":"confronts","l":"confront","q":"verb"},"confronted":{"h":"confronted","l":"confront","q":"verb"},"confronting":{"h":"confronting","l":"confront","q":"verb"},"enclose":{"h":"enclose","i":"/ɪnˈkləʊz/","a":"en-ca-synth-enclose.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) When you enclose something, you force it into a certain area and keep it there.","e":"The sheep flock was enclosed by the fence."},{"m":"When you enclose something with a letter, you put it in the same envelope as the letter."}]}]},"holler":{"h":"holler","i":"/ˈhɑ.lər/","a":"en-us-holler.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you holler, you yell or scream as loud as you can.","e":"Hollering at your enemy will not help you."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A holler is a loud yell or scream.","e":"Give a holler to call Jim."}]}]},"cucumber":{"h":"cucumber","i":"/ˈkjuːˌkʌmbər/","a":"en-us-cucumber.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cucumber is a type of vine."},{"m":"(countable) A cucumber is a vegetable that is grown on a vine.","e":"There are cucumbers in the salad."}]}]},"hollers":{"h":"hollers","l":"holler","q":"verb"},"hollered":{"h":"hollered","l":"holler","q":"verb"},"hollering":{"h":"hollering","l":"holler","q":"verb"},"cucumbers":{"h":"cucumbers","l":"cucumber","q":"noun"},"encloses":{"h":"encloses","l":"enclose","q":"verb"},"enclosed":{"h":"enclosed","i":"/ənˈkloʊzd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-enclosed.wav","l":"enclose","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If A is enclosed within B, A surrounded by B."}]}]},"enclosing":{"h":"enclosing","l":"enclose","q":"verb"},"imaginative":{"h":"imaginative","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are imaginative, you have many new and interesting ideas.","e":"As an artist, she's wildly imaginative, and each new show is completely different."},{"m":"An imaginative action, idea, or creation is one that is new and interesting.","e":"As the boys grew up, the tree was the centre of many hours of imaginative play."}]}]},"stiffen":{"h":"stiffen","i":"/ˈstɪfən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-stiffen.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you stiffen, you stop moving and make your muscles hard.","e":"The mouse stiffened when the shadow went by."},{"m":"(intransitive) If your muscles or joints stiffen, they become painful to move.","e":"By the morning after the accident, my hand had stiffened so much that I couldn't move it."},{"m":"(transitive) If you stiffen something, you make it stronger or harder so that it is more difficult to bend.","e":"We'll have to stiffen the airplane wing or it could break in flight."}]}]},"stiffening":{"h":"stiffening","l":"stiffen","q":"verb"},"fumed":{"h":"fumed","i":"/fjuːmd/","l":"fume","q":"verb"},"fuming":{"h":"fuming","i":"/ˈfjuːmɪŋ/","l":"fume","q":"verb"},"compulsion":{"h":"compulsion","i":"/kəmˈpʌl.ʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-compulsion.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"If you have a compulsion to do something, you really want to do it even though there is no good reason."},{"m":"If someone is under compulsion to do something, they are being forced to do it."}]}]},"irresistible":{"h":"irresistible","i":"/ˌɪrɪˈzɪstəbl̩/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is irresistible, it's so good that it can't be ignored.","e":"That pie is irresistible!"}]}]},"compulsions":{"h":"compulsions","l":"compulsion","q":"noun"},"hasten":{"h":"hasten","i":"/ˈheɪs.ən/","a":"en-us-hasten.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you hasten to do something, you try to do it very soon and very quickly.","e":"After the play ended, she hastened to leave."},{"m":"If you hasten an event, you try to make it happen very soon and very quickly.","e":"We've known for a long time that loneliness hastens death, but haven't been able to explain how."}]}]},"talkative":{"h":"talkative","i":"/ˈtɔːkətɪv/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-talkative.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are talkative, you like talking or you talk a lot.","e":"The class is talkative during recess."}]}]},"transversal":{"h":"transversal","i":"/trænsˈvɜːsəl/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable); A transversal is a line that goes through multiple lines.","e":"Euclid's paralell postulate uses a transversal."}]}]},"transversals":{"h":"transversals","l":"transversal","q":"noun"},"topple":{"h":"topple","i":"/ˈtɑpl̩/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-topple.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you topple something, you push it over or defeat it.","e":"Germany toppled Canada in the hockey match."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something topples, it falls over or it looks like it might fall over.","e":"The pile of pennies began to topple"}]}]},"curling":{"h":"curling","i":"/ˈkərlɪŋ/","a":"en-us-curling.ogg","l":"curl","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Curling is a type of sport where people slide stones across ice.","e":"Curling came from Scotland."}]}]},"standoff":{"h":"standoff","a":"en-us-standoff.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A standoff is a competition between two sides in which neither side is making progress.","e":"A standoff between the protesters and the police began."}]}]},"godspeed":{"h":"Godspeed","i":"/ɡɒdˈspiːd/","s":[{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"You say Godspeed when you want something to go well."}]}]},"azalea":{"h":"azalea","i":"/əˈzeɪliə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-azalea.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An azalea is a type of plant that grows flowers.","e":"I have, roses, and azaleas in my garden."}]}]},"playstation":{"h":"PlayStation","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"PlayStation is a brand of gaming console."}]}]},"bungs":{"h":"bungs","l":"bung","q":"noun"},"bunged":{"h":"bunged","l":"bung","q":"verb"},"bunging":{"h":"bunging","l":"bung","q":"verb"},"churn":{"h":"churn","i":"/tʃɜː(r)n/","a":"en-us-churn.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you churn something, you stir it quickly and multiple times.","e":"To make butter, we churn the milk."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something churns, it moves around a lot.","e":"I was so nervous my stomach was churning."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A churn is a machine that [[#Verb|churns]] things.","e":"Put the milk in the butter churn."}]}]},"churns":{"h":"churns","l":"churn","q":"verb"},"churned":{"h":"churned","l":"churn","q":"verb"},"churning":{"h":"churning","l":"churn","q":"verb"},"pry":{"h":"pry","i":"/praɪ/","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you pry, you ask too much about a person's private affairs.","e":"I don't mean to pry, but are you single?"}]}]},"excellence":{"h":"excellence","i":"/ˈɛksələns/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-excellence.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Excellence is the quality of being very, very good.","e":"We're aiming for more than quality. We're aiming for excellence."}]}]},"tighten":{"h":"tighten","i":"/ˈtaɪ.tən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-tighten.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you tighten something, you make it tighter.","e":"Can you tighten the lid on the jar so it doesn't leak?"}]}]},"perfection":{"h":"perfection","i":"/pɚˈfɛkʃən/","a":"en-us-perfection.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Perfection is the state or quality of having no mistakes, problems, or negative aspects.","e":"I don't expect perfection from teachers, but I do expect honesty and hard work."},{"m":"(uncountable) Perfection is the process of making something perfect.","e":"In the perfection of the show, a number of significant changes were made."}]}]},"waist":{"h":"waist","i":"/weɪst/","a":"en-us-waste.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Your waist is the narrow point between your hips and your chest.","e":"She turned and slipped her arms around his waist."}]}]},"kangaroo":{"h":"kangaroo","i":"/kaŋ.ɡəˈruː/","a":"en-us-kangaroo.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A kangaroo is a jumping animal with a pouch that is native to Australia."}]}]},"buffalo":{"h":"buffalo","i":"/ˈbʌf.əl.əʊ/","a":"en-us-buffalo.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A buffalo is a type of large mammal.","e":"Buffalo used to live in the plains of North America."}]}]},"darken":{"h":"darken","i":"/ˈdɑrkən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-darken.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something darkens, there is less light.","e":"In the evening, he went walking and watched the sky darken."},{"m":"(intransitive) If your mood, face, or eyes darkens, you become less happy.","e":"As he told her the story, he could see her face darken."}]}]},"heighten":{"h":"heighten","i":"/ˈhaɪ̯.tən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-heighten.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If a sense, awareness, or risk heightens, it increases or becomes stronger.","e":"The music heightened the tension in the film."}]}]},"loosen":{"h":"loosen","i":"/ˈluːsn̩/","a":"en-us-loosen.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you loosen something, you make it looser.","e":"Can you loosen the lid on this jar for me."},{"m":"(intransitive) If somebody loosens up, they become more relaxed.","e":"She loosened up after she'd had a glass of wine."},{"m":"If your joints or muscles loosen up, they start to move more easily.","e":"I took a deep breath, and I could feel the muscles in my chest loosen."},{"m":"(transitive) If you loosen somebody's tongue, you make them talk about something they would not talk about before.","e":"But what truly loosened my tongue was knowing I was on home ground."}]}]},"thirst":{"h":"thirst","i":"/θɜːst/","a":"en-us-thirst.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Thirst is the feeling that you want to drink.","e":"She took a long drink to ease her thirst."},{"m":"(uncountable) Thirst is the state of not having enough to drink.","e":"When the river stopped running, the animals began to die of thirst."},{"m":"(countable) If you have a thirst for something, you want a lot of it regularly.","e":"Their thirst for knowledge was too much for the small school library."}]}]},"kangaroos":{"h":"kangaroos","l":"kangaroo","q":"noun"},"sweeten":{"h":"sweeten","i":"/ˈswiːtən/","a":"en-us-sweeten.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you sweeten something, you make it sweeter.","e":"They offer me hot milk sweetened with sugar."},{"m":"If you sweeten a deal or an offer, you make it better for the other person.","e":"I might agree to that if you sweetened the deal."}]}]},"heavenly":{"h":"heavenly","i":"/ˈhɛvənli/","a":"en-us-heavenly.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Heavenly things are related to heaven in some religions.","e":"Every day, we thank our heavenly father for all that we have."},{"m":"If something is heavenly, it is extremely pleasant.","e":"The smell of that coffee is heavenly."},{"m":"Heavenly things are related to outer space or located there.","e":"In 1609, Galileo made his first observations of heavenly bodies with a telescope."}]}]},"attentive":{"h":"attentive","i":"/əˈtɛntɪv/","a":"en-us-attentive.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a person or animal is attentive, it is trying hard to notice things.","e":"An attentive audience, both young and old, was listening for any change."}]}]},"buffaloes":{"h":"buffaloes","l":"buffalo","q":"noun"},"patriotic":{"h":"patriotic","i":"/ˈpæt.ri.ɒ.tɪk/","a":"en-us-patriotic.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are patriotic, you love, support, and believe in your country.","e":"During the war, it was common to hear patriotic songs on the radio."}]}]},"bison":{"h":"bison","i":"/ˈbaɪ̯sən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-bison.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bison is a large animal related to cows.","e":"The Yellowstone animals make up the last wild bison herd."}]}]},"porcupine":{"h":"porcupine","i":"/'pɔːʳkjʊpaɪn/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A porcupine is an animal (a rodent) with sharp needles all over its body."}]}]},"macaque":{"h":"macaque","i":"/məˈkæk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-macaque.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A macaque is a small monkey.","e":"We saw macaques in the zoo."}]}]},"ounce":{"h":"ounce","i":"/aʊns/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-ounce.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An ounce (oz) is a unit of weight equal to 1/16 of a pound or 28.35 grams.","e":"Add 1/2 cup shaved Parmesan cheese (about 2 ounces)."},{"m":"(countable) An ounce is a very small amount of something.","e":"He was still in great shape, with not an ounce of fat on him."},{"m":"(countable) A fluid ounce (fl oz) is a unit of volume equal to 1/20 of a pint or 0.028 litres in Britain, and 1/16 of a pint or 0.030 litres in the US."}]}]},"indoor":{"h":"indoor","i":"/ˈɪndɔː/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-indoor.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"An indoor event happens in a building, not outside.","e":"The gym has an indoor swimming pool."}]}]},"redden":{"h":"redden","i":"/ˈrɛdn̩/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-redden.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something reddens, it becomes more red.","e":"There were still tears in his reddened eyes."},{"m":"If a person or a person's face reddens, they are embarrassed.","e":"His face reddened as he realized nobody was laughing at his jokes."}]}]},"woolen":{"h":"woolen","i":"/wʊl/","a":"en-us-wool.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A woolen fabric is made of wool.","e":"She wore a woolen sweater."}]}]},"fraud":{"h":"fraud","i":"/frɔːd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-fraud.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Fraud is a trick for the purpose of gaining money or other valuables illegally.","e":"He faces punishment for the fraud that lost $1 million."}]}]},"elucidate":{"h":"elucidate","i":"/əˈluː.sɪ.de͡ɪt/","a":"en-uk-elucidate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you elucidate something, you clarify or make something clear.","e":"George was able to elucidate his son on proper procedures to cook."}]}]},"persuasion":{"h":"persuasion","i":"/pəˈsweɪʒ(ə)n/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-persuasion.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Persuasion is the process of making somebody agree with you or do what you want them to do.","e":"A great leader has vision and the power of persuasion."},{"m":"(countable) A religious or political persuasion is a belief system.","e":"He was of a religious persuasion that said \"no work on Sundays.\""}]}]},"volley":{"h":"volley","i":"/ˈvɒli/","a":"en-au-volley.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A volley of bullets, arrows, etc. is a group of them fired at the same time.","e":"The army fired a volley of bullets."},{"m":"A volley is when a ball is hit before it touches the ground."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"; (transitive) If a ball is volleyed, it is hit before it touches the ground.","e":"The tennis player volleyed the ball over the net."}]}]},"omission":{"h":"omission","i":"/oʊˈmɪʃ ən/","a":"En-ca-omission.oga","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An omission is a failure to do or include something.","e":"The story is misleading because of all the lies and omissions."}]}]},"gaiety":{"h":"gaiety","i":"/ˈɡeɪ.ɪ.ti/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-gaiety.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Gaiety is the feeling or atmosphere of fun and happiness.","e":"The air was full of gaiety and sunshine and the sense of singing birds."}]}]},"scorn":{"h":"scorn","i":"/skɔːn/","a":"en-us-scorn.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Scorn is a strong feeling, attitude, or comment that something has very low quality or low value.","e":"The teacher was often the object of the students' scorn."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you scorn something, you you show that you strongly think it has very low quality or low value.","e":"They began to consider ideas they had previously scorned."}]}]},"scent":{"h":"scent","i":"/sɛnt/","a":"en-us-scent.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A scent is a smell.","e":"The scent of fresh bread filled the house."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If x sents y, x gives y a smell.","e":"The flowers scented the room."},{"m":"(transitive) If you scent something such as danger or a story, you have a feeling that it exists.","e":"When the president didn't appear, the newspapers scented a story."},{"m":"(transitive) If an animal scents something, it smells it.","e":"The deer ran when they scented the hunter."}]}]},"volleys":{"h":"volleys","l":"volley","q":"noun"},"volleyed":{"h":"volleyed","l":"volley","q":"verb"},"volleying":{"h":"volleying","l":"volley","q":"verb"},"discord":{"h":"discord","i":"/ˈdɪskɔrd/","a":"en-us-discord.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Discord is disagreement and bad feelings between people.","e":"The idea created discord among them."},{"m":"Discord is when notes in music don't sound good when played at the same time."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you discord, you disagree with someone."}]}]},"conquer":{"h":"conquer","i":"/ˈkɒŋkə/","a":"en-us-conquer.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If one side conquers in a war, it wins.","e":"Alexander conquered most of Europe and North Africa."},{"m":"(transitive) If you conquer a problem, a fear, a disease, etc. you overcome it.","e":"With the help of a councilor, she was able to conquer her fear of flying."}]}]},"sometime":{"h":"sometime","i":"/ˈsʌmˌtaɪm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-sometime.wav","s":[{"p":"determiner","d":[{"m":"You use sometime for a time in the future or the past that is unknown or undecided.","e":"We should get together sometime soon."},{"m":"A sometime editor, president, minister, etc. is someone who used to be in that position.","e":"Downey's uncle is a sometime actor and screenwriter."},{"m":"A sometime actor, friend, teacher, etc. is someone who is not usually in that position.","e":"Jackson was a teacher and sometime actor who appeared in many TV commercials."}]}]},"bearskin":{"h":"bearskin","i":"/ˈbɛə.skɪn/","a":"en-us-bearskin.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bearskin is the fur of a bear."},{"m":"(countable) A bearskin is a hat that is worn by British soldiers for special occasions."}]}]},"ostrich":{"h":"ostrich","i":"/ˈɒs.trɪt͡ʃ/","a":"en-us-ostrich.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An ostrich is a large bird that cannot fly.","e":"The ostrich can run up to speeds of 70 kilometres per hour."}]}]},"ostriches":{"h":"ostriches","l":"ostrich","q":"noun"},"reindeer":{"h":"reindeer","i":"/ˈreɪndɪr/","a":"en-us-reindeer.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A reindeer is a type of deer that lives in the Arctic.","e":"Rudolph the red-nosed reindeer had a very shiny nose."}]}]},"gorilla":{"h":"gorilla","i":"/ɡəˈrɪl.ə/","a":"en-us-gorilla.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A gorilla is an ape that lives in Africa.","e":"Gorillas are related to chimpanzees, orangutans and humans."}]}]},"gorillas":{"h":"gorillas","l":"gorilla","q":"noun"},"reindeers":{"h":"reindeers","l":"reindeer","q":"noun"},"dissatisfaction":{"h":"dissatisfaction","i":"/dɪsˌsætɪsˈfækʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-dissatisfaction.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Dissatisfaction is the feeling that something are not as good as it should be.","e":"She has recently expressed some dissatisfaction with the amount of progress."}]}]},"rivalry":{"h":"rivalry","i":"/ˈraɪ.vəl.ri/","a":"en-us-rivalry.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A rivalry is a situation in which two groups see themselves as being in long-term competition.","e":"The rivalry between and heated up this weekend."}]}]},"impound":{"h":"impound","i":"/ɪmˈpaʊ̯nd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-impound.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If something is impounded, it is taken away and put in a pound.","e":"The car was impounded for seven days."},{"m":"(transitive) If documents, vehicles, etc. is impounded, a court holds on to it.","e":"The court impounded a document to keep it safe."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An impound is a place where things are [[#Verb|impounded]]."}]}]},"flamingo":{"h":"flamingo","i":"/fləˈmɪŋɡoʊ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-flamingo.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A flamingo is a pink bird that lives near water.","e":"We saw flamingoes in the Zoo."}]}]},"complication":{"h":"complication","i":"/ˈkɒmplɪkeɪʃən/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A complication is something that makes your job more difficult.","e":"When the switch broke, it added a new complication."},{"m":"(uncountable) Complication is the process of making something more difficult.","e":"Let's aim for simplification, not complication."}]}]},"congratulations":{"h":"congratulations","i":"/kənˌɡræt͡ʃəˈleɪʃ(ə)nz/","a":"en-uk-congratulations.ogg","s":[{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"You say congratulations when a happy event happens, such as somebody winning a game, getting a new job, or passing a test at school.","e":"So you can drive now. Congratulations!"}]}]},"disappearance":{"h":"disappearance","i":"/dɪsəˈpɪərəns/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-disappearance.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The disappearance of something is when it is gone and we can't find it or it doesn't exist anymore.","e":"Detroit Police say they are still investigating the children's disappearance."}]}]},"koala":{"h":"koala","i":"/koʊ.ˈɑː.lə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-koala.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A koala is a small mammal that climbs trees and lives in Australia.","e":"Koalas usually eat eucalyptus leaves."}]}]},"heptadecagon":{"h":"heptadecagon","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A heptadecagon is a shape that has 17 sides and 17 angles."}]}]},"avoidance":{"h":"avoidance","i":"/əˈvɔɪdn̩s/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-avoidance.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Avoidance is the process of staying away from or not doing something.","e":"Tax avoidance is also high among business owners."}]}]},"octagon":{"h":"octagon","i":"/ˈɒktəɡ(ə)n/","a":"en-us-octagon.mp3","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An octagon (⯄) is a shape that has 8 sides and 8 angles."}]}]},"rejoice":{"h":"rejoice","i":"/rɪˈd͡ʒɔɪs/","a":"en-us-rejoice.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you rejoice, you act in a way that shows that you feel very happy about something.","e":"An event like this gives everyone an great opportunity and reason to rejoice and celebrate."}]}]},"dissatisfied":{"h":"dissatisfied","i":"/dɪsˈsætɪsˌfaɪd/","a":"en-us-dissatisfied.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are dissatisfied with something, it is not as good as you think it should be.","e":"I was very dissatisfied with the results of the test."}]}]},"inclusive":{"h":"inclusive","i":"/ɪnˈkluːsɪv/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is inclusive, it is open to all the people or all the things that it could be open to.","e":"Our school has a very inclusive culture so that nobody feels left out."},{"m":"If a price is inclusive, it is the total price and there are no other charges.","e":"It's $127, inclusive of tax and delivery."},{"m":"You use inclusive at the end of a list to say that the first and last items also belong.","e":"The race is open to anyone 16 to 24 inclusive."}]}]},"walkout":{"h":"walkout","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-walkout.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A walkout is when workers suddenly stop working.","e":"Teachers in Oklahoma are going to do a walkout."},{"m":"(countable) A walkout is when many people leave a place to protest something.","e":"Students took part in a high school walkout to protest gun laws."}]}]},"metronome":{"h":"metronome","i":"/ˈmɛtrəˌnoʊm/","a":"en-us-metronome.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A metronome is something that musicians use to make sure they are playing on time.","e":"Set your metronome to 104."}]}]},"homemade":{"h":"homemade","i":"/ˌ(h)əʊmˈmeɪ̯d/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Homemade bread, sweaters, cookies, etc. are made at home.","e":"We always have homemade cookies for lunch."}]}]},"well-known":{"h":"well-known","i":"/ˌwɛlˈnoʊn/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a person or thing is well-known, many people know it or know about it.","e":"That area is well-known for their restaurants."}]}]},"procession":{"h":"procession","i":"/prəˈsɛʃən/","a":"en-us-procession.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A procession is a number of individuals moving together in one direction.","e":"A funeral procession snaked through the streets of Toronto."}]}]},"chimpanzee":{"h":"chimpanzee","i":"/tʃɪmˈpæn.zi/","a":"en-us-chimpanzee.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A chimpanzee is an ape that lives in Africa."}]}]},"jealousy":{"h":"jealousy","i":"/ˈdʒɛləsi/","a":"en-us-jealousy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Jealousy is the bad feeling you get when somebody else has something that you want.","e":"I felt great jealousy towards them and their successes"},{"m":"(uncountable) Jealousy is the bad feeling you get when somebody you're interested in shows interest in another, or when the other person shows interest in them.","e":"Men act violently out of sexual jealousy more than women."}]}]},"messy":{"h":"messy","i":"/ˈmɛsi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-messy.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is messy is very chaotic and not organized.","e":"His sister's bedroom can be a bit messy at times."}]}]},"homecoming":{"h":"homecoming","i":"/ˈhoʊm.ˌkʌmɪŋ/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Homecoming is the event of returning home after a long time away, and the celebrations that go with it.","e":"Everyone was at the house for her homecoming."},{"m":"Homecoming is the yearly event of returning to the school that you went to, and the celebrations that go with it.","e":"Did you see the homecoming game?"}]}]},"conform":{"h":"conform","i":"/kənˈfɔːm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-conform.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If you conform to something, you behave in that manner, especially as a result of social pressure.","e":"He changed his clothes to conform to local tastes."}]}]},"cockatoo":{"h":"cockatoo","i":"/kɒkəˈtuː/","a":"en-au-cockatoo.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cockatoo is a kind of parrot from Australia."}]}]},"gruelling":{"h":"gruelling","i":"/ˈɡrʊə.lɪŋ/","a":"en-us-gruelling.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is gruelling is very tiring and difficult.","e":"The climb lasted a gruelling twenty minutes."}]}]},"grueling":{"h":"grueling","i":"/ˈɡrʊə.lɪŋ/","a":"en-us-gruelling.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is grueling is very tiring and difficult.","e":"It took five grueling hours to finish running the marathon."}]}]},"werewolf":{"h":"werewolf","i":"/ˈwɛːwʊlf/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-werewolf.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A werewolf is a mythical creature that is sometimes human and sometimes a Wolf."}]}]},"whiten":{"h":"whiten","i":"/ˈ(h)waɪtn̩/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-whiten.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you whiten something, you make it white or lighter in colour.","e":"I got my teeth whitened at the dentist."}]}]},"cultivation":{"h":"cultivation","i":"/ˌkʌltɪˈveɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-cultivation.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Cultivation is the process of growing or improving something, especially in farming.","e":"There is a long history of rice cultivation in the region."}]}]},"companionship":{"h":"companionship","i":"/kəmˈpænjənˌʃɪp/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-companionship.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Companionship is the state of having a friend with you.","e":"She keeps a dog for companionship."}]}]},"weekday":{"h":"weekday","i":"/ˈwiːkdeɪ/","a":"en-us-weekday.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The weekdays are Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, & Friday.","e":"I can't sleep late on a weekday."}]}]},"modesty":{"h":"modesty","i":"/ˈmɒd.ə.sti/","a":"en-us-modesty.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Modesty is the attitude of not talking about or not trying to make people notice your abilities and achievements.","e":"Two things were obvious: his intellectual honesty and the modesty with which he spoke."},{"m":"(uncountable) If you dress with, modesty you cover most of your body and do not wear sexy clothes or bright colours.","e":"There were also all sorts of rules about modesty in dress, you know, no pants for women."}]}]},"brighten":{"h":"brighten","i":"/ˈbraɪtən/","a":"en-uk-Brighton.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something brightens, it becomes brighter, less dark.","e":"As the sun came up, the room brightened."},{"m":"(intransitive) If someone brightens, they become.","e":"She brightened when she thought about the holiday plans."},{"m":"(transitive) If you brighten someone or something, you make it brighter.","e":"Having the grandchildren visit brightened their day."}]}]},"airstrike":{"h":"airstrike","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An airstrike is an attack by the military that is done by using airplanes or missiles.","e":"President Trump ordered airstrikes against Syria."}]}]},"tusk":{"h":"tusk","i":"/ˈtʌsk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-tusk.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A tusk is a long tooth that goes outside of the mouth of an animal.","e":"Elephant tusks were a large part of the ivory trade."}]}]},"ambient":{"h":"ambient","i":"/ˈæm.biː.ənt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Mélange a trois-ambient.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is ambient is in the background and is on all sides of an object.","e":"The cup of tea cooled down to the ambient temperature."},{"m":"Music that is ambient is very relaxing and peaceful."}]}]},"moderation":{"h":"moderation","i":"/ˌmɑdəˈreɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-moderation.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Moderation is the quality of doing things at a reasonable level, not too much or too little, too hard or too gently, etc.","e":"It's OK to have some sweets, as long as you do so in moderation."}]}]},"deafen":{"h":"deafen","i":"/ˈdɛfən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-deafen.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If a sound deafens you, it is so loud that it makes you lose your hearing.","e":"The flash temporarily blinded him, and he was deafened by the roar."},{"m":"A deafening silence is failure to get a reply or reaction when one is needed or expected.","e":"My request for additional funds was met with a deafening silence."}]}]},"punctual":{"h":"punctual","i":"/ˈpʌŋktjʊəl/","a":"En-us-punctual.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are punctual, you generally do things on time, not late.","e":"Bobbie, always punctual, walked into the restaurant at exactly 7:00."}]}]},"hurrah":{"h":"hurrah","i":"/həˈrɑː/","s":[{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"You use \"hurrah\" when you are happy and want to cellebrate.","e":"Hurrah! We won."}]}]},"uppermost":{"h":"uppermost","i":"/ˈʌpəməʊst/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"The uppermost point, layer, floor, etc. is the one at the top of something very high.","e":"Birds sat in the uppermost branchs of the tree."},{"m":"If something is uppermost in your mind, it's the main thing you're thinking about.","e":"The changes at school were uppermost in her mind."}]}]},"troupe":{"h":"troupe","i":"/truːp/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-troupe.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A theatre, circus, etc. troupe is a group of dancers, actors, or singers that perform on tour.","e":"The Haiyuza theatre troupe is on tour!"}]}]},"conqueror":{"h":"conqueror","i":"/ˈkɒŋkərə/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A conqueror is a country, army, or leader who wins a war and takes complete control of the area.","e":"The first Spanish conquerors defeated the native Americans by infecting them with diseases."}]}]},"hindrance":{"h":"hindrance","i":"/ˈhɪndr(ə)ns/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-hindrance.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hindrance is something that makes something more difficult.","e":"He long hair was a hinderance, always falling in her face."}]}]},"stethoscope":{"h":"stethoscope","i":"/ˈstɛθəskəʊp/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-stethoscope.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A stethoscope is a tool that doctors and nurses use to listen to sounds inside the body.","e":"The doctor checked the patient's abdomen with a stethoscope."}]}]},"saucer":{"h":"saucer","i":"/ˈsɔː.sə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-saucer.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A saucer is a small plate that goes under a cup.","e":"His tea arrived in a small white cup with two packets of sugar on the saucer."}]}]},"madden":{"h":"madden","i":"/ˈmædən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-madden.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you madden a person or animal, you make them angry or crazy.","e":"She fought like a maddened animal."}]}]},"motherhood":{"h":"motherhood","i":"/ˈmʌðəhʊd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-motherhood.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Motherhood is the state of being a mother.","e":"Balancing marriage, motherhood and her career will not be easy."}]}]},"sadden":{"h":"sadden","i":"/ˈsædən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-sadden.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If something saddens you, it makes you feel less happy.","e":"I was saddened by the news of his illness."}]}]},"headdress":{"h":"headdress","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A headdress is anything that is worn on the head, but especially something very decorative."}]}]},"possessor":{"h":"possessor","i":"/pəˈzɛsə/","a":"en-us-possessor.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A possessor of something is someone who has it.","e":"You are now the proud possessor of a university degree."}]}]},"motherly":{"h":"motherly","i":"/ˈmʌðəli/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-motherly.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you act in a motherly way, you are caring and helpful, like a mother.","e":"She spoke in a soft motherly voice."}]}]},"bribery":{"h":"bribery","i":"/ˈbraɪbəri/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Bribery is the crime of paying someone in power to use their power to help you.","e":"The company was under investigation for bribery in the awarding of a government contract."}]}]},"cultivator":{"h":"cultivator","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cultivator is a tool or machine that breaks up the earth for farming or gardening.","e":"He drove the cultivator around the fields before seeding."},{"m":"(countable) (formal) A cultivator is a person who helps plants grow."}]}]},"alas":{"h":"alas","s":[{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"You use \"alas\" to express regret.","e":"I thought you'd be here, but alas!"}]}]},"inceldom":{"h":"inceldom","i":"/ˈɪnsɛldəm/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Inceldom is when someone is an incel.","e":"Her inceldom made her feel lonely."}]}]},"scrutinize":{"h":"scrutinize","i":"/ˈskruːtɨnaɪz/","a":"en-au-scrutinize.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you scrutinize something, you look into it very carefully.","e":"The group scrutinizes the government's actions."}]}]},"scrutinise":{"h":"scrutinise","i":"/ˈskruːtɨnaɪz/","a":"en-au-scrutinize.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you scrutinise something, you look into it very carefully.","e":"The group scrutinises the government's actions."}]}]},"shotgun":{"h":"shotgun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A shotgun is a type of gun."},{"m":"The shotgun seat in a car is the seat that is next to the driver seat."}]}]},"cancan":{"h":"cancan","i":"/ˈkænˌkæn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-cancan.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The cancan is a dance where people stand in a line and kick their legs high in the air."}]}]},"foreshadow":{"h":"foreshadow","i":"/fɔːˈʃadəʊ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-foreshadow.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If an event is foreshadowed, it is hinted that it will happen.","e":"The downfall of the company was foreshadowed by the stock market crash."}]}]},"heptadecagons":{"h":"heptadecagons","l":"heptadecagon","q":"noun"},"postscript":{"h":"postscript","i":"/ˈpoʊst.skrɪpt/","a":"En-us-postscript.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A postscript is a message that is put at the end of a letter and is put after the author's signature.","e":"He added a postscript to the end of the letter."},{"m":"(countable) A postscript is something that is added to a story or play after it is finished.","e":"The author explained in the postscript of the book why she wrote the book."}]}]},"skidmark":{"h":"skidmark","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"a mark made by a tire"}]}]},"sawgrass":{"h":"sawgrass","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Sawgrass is a type of grass in the species, it has long sedges with saw-like sharp, serrated edges,"}]}]},"chainsaw":{"h":"chainsaw","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A chainsaw is a tool used to cut wood.","e":"He used the chainsaw to cut through the tree."}]}]},"versatile":{"h":"versatile","i":"/ˈvɝsətl̩/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-versatile.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is versatile is able to change easily and do different things.","e":"The writer is versatile because he can write romance stories, science fiction stories, and action stories."}]}]},"flank":{"h":"flank","i":"/flæŋk/","a":"en-us-flank.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If an attacking group flanks someone, it comes from both sides."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A flank is the part of the body between the ribs and the hip."}]}]},"nonagon":{"h":"nonagon","i":"/ˈnɑn.ə.ɡɑn/","a":"en-ca-nonagon.oga","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A nonagon is a shape with nine sides."}]}]},"heptagon":{"h":"heptagon","i":"/ˈhɛp.tə.ɡɒn/","a":"en-ca-heptagon.oga","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A heptagon is a shape with seven sides."}]}]},"cuboid":{"h":"cuboid","i":"/ˈkjuːbɔɪd/","a":"en-us-cuboid.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cuboid is a 3D shape with rectangular sides."}]}]},"hexagon":{"h":"hexagon","i":"/ˈhɛk.sə.ɡən/","a":"en-ca-hexagon.oga","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hexagon (⬢) is a shape with six sides."}]}]},"commend":{"h":"commend","i":"/kəˈmɛnd/","a":"en-us-commend.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you commend someone, you praise or give them credit for something good.","e":"The president commended the soldier for their bravery."}]}]},"billboard":{"h":"billboard","i":"/ˈbɪlbɔːd/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A billboard is a large advertisement that is usually beside a road or highway.","e":"On the side of the road, we saw a billboard shoes."}]}]},"valedictorian":{"h":"valedictorian","i":"/vælədɪkˈtɔrɪən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-valedictorian.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The valedictorian of a class is a student that says the valedictory speech. They usually have the highest marks of the class.","e":"The highest placing person in the exam was chosen as the valedictorian."}]}]},"valedictory":{"h":"valedictory","i":"/ˌvælɪˈdɪktəri/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-valedictory.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A valedictory is a farewell speech.","e":"The valedictorian delivered the valedictory speech."}]}]},"farewell":{"h":"farewell","i":"/fɛrˈwɛl/","a":"en-us-farewell.ogg","s":[{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"You use farewell when you are or departing.","e":"Farewell! I will miss you."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A farewell is when a person says \"farewell\" to someone else. This means to wish for happiness and safety."}]}]},"quindecagon":{"h":"quindecagon","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A quindecagon is a shape with fifteen sides."}]}]},"ruthlessness":{"h":"ruthlessness","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Ruthlessness is the property of being ruthless."}]}]},"ruthless":{"h":"ruthless","i":"/ˈruːθləs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-ruthless.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A ruthless person tries to achieve their goals despite knowing that it will cause pain or damage."},{"m":"A ruthless action is carried out despite knowing that it will cause pain or damage."}]}]},"humanity":{"h":"humanity","i":"/hjuˈmænɪti/","a":"en-us-humanity.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Humanity is human-kind, all humans."},{"m":"(uncountable) Humanity is what makes people human.","e":"Have we lost all humanity?"}]}]},"haggle":{"h":"haggle","i":"/ˈhæɡəl/","a":"en-us-haggle.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you haggle, you bargain to find a price that is acceptable for the seller and the buyer.","e":"I haggled on the price for the shoes."}]}]},"novice":{"h":"novice","i":"/ˈnɒvɪs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-novice.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A novice is a person who is new to a field or activity.","e":"I was once a novice at football."}]}]},"den":{"h":"den","i":"/dɛn/","a":"en-us-den.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A den is a place where a wild animal lives.","e":"The wolf went back to his den to sleep after a day of hunting."},{"m":"(countable) A den is a small cave in the side of a hill."}]}]},"flick":{"h":"flick","i":"/flɪk/","a":"en-us-flick.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A flick is a fast movement.","e":"With a quick flick of his wrist, he threw the ball."},{"m":"(countable); (informal) A flick is a movie or movie theatre.","e":"The newest flick is."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you flick something, you move it or hit it very quickly.","e":"She flicked his hair affectionately."}]}]},"dale":{"h":"dale","i":"/deɪl/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A dale is a big valley that is very broad and open.","e":"It took the hiker a day to walk through the dale."}]}]},"dean":{"h":"dean","i":"/diːn/","a":"en-us-dean.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A dean is the head of a department of a university or college.","e":"The dean welcomed the students to another year of study at Humber College."}]}]},"incels":{"h":"incels","l":"incel","q":"noun"},"genitalia":{"h":"genitalia","i":"/ˈdʒɛnɪˈteɪli.ə/","a":"en-us-genitalia.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Genitalia are the body parts used for sex and reproduction, especially the parts on the outside of the body.","e":"His pants were down, and his genitalia were clearly visible."}]}]},"hendecagon":{"h":"hendecagon","i":"/hɛnˈdɛkəɡ(ə)n/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Flame, not lame-hendecagon.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hendecagon is a shape with eleven sides."}]}]},"untied":{"h":"untied","l":"untie","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A string, rope, etc. that is untied is not tied.","e":"Your shoelaces are untied."}]}]},"deaf-mute":{"h":"deaf-mute","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"(now offensive): A person who can not hear and can not speak (excluding sign lenguage). In modern times some people consider the word offensive and prefer just deaf."}]}]},"deafmute":{"h":"deafmute","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"(now offensive): A person who can not hear and can not speak (excluding sign lenguage). In modern times some people consider the word offensive and prefer just deaf."}]}]},"timeout":{"h":"timeout","i":"/ˈtaɪm.aʊt/","a":"en-us-time-out.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) In sports a timeout is when the coach asks for a short stop in the game to talk with the team.","e":"The coach of the home team is asking for a timeout."},{"m":"(countable) A timeout is a short period to relax from a situation that causes stress.","e":"I need a timeout from this meeting."}]}]},"time-out":{"h":"time-out","i":"/ˈtaɪm.aʊt/","a":"en-us-time-out.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) In sports a time-out is when the coach asks for a short stop in the game to talk with the team.","e":"The coach of the home team is asking for a time-out."},{"m":"(countable) A time-out is a short period to relax from a situation that causes stress.","e":"I need a time-out from this meeting."}]}]},"weld":{"h":"weld","i":"/wɛld/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-weld.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If two things are welded together, they are joined together, usually using metal.","e":"The workers welded a piece of steel to the bridge."},{"m":"(transitive) If you weld two things, you bring them together very closely."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A weld is the piece of metal that joins two things together."}]}]},"ratings":{"h":"ratings","l":"rating","q":"noun"},"assuage":{"h":"assuage","i":"/əˈsweɪdʒ/","a":"en-us-assuage.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you assuage a feeling, you make it less intense.","e":"We tried to assuage her anger about the damage."}]}]},"boomerang":{"h":"boomerang","i":"/ˈbuːməræŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-boomerang.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A boomerang is a curved weapon made of wood that you can throw and it returns to you."}]}]},"surreptitiously":{"h":"surreptitiously","i":"/sʌrəpˈtɪʃəsli/","a":"en-us-surreptitiously.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you do something surreptitiously, you do it in secret.","e":"As they were speaking, he surreptitiously took the diamond."}]}]},"amulet":{"h":"amulet","i":"/ˈæm.jə.lɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-amulet.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An amulet is an object a person keeps because he thinks it gives him good luck."}]}]},"defiant":{"h":"defiant","i":"/dɪˈfaɪ(j)ənt/","a":"en-us-defiant.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are defiant, you refuse to do what you are told to do."}]}]},"defiance":{"h":"defiance","i":"/dɪˈfaɪ(j)əns/","a":"en-us-defiance.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Defiance is the state or act of to do what you are told to do."}]}]},"idolize":{"h":"idolize","i":"/ˈaɪdəlaɪz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-idolize.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When you idolize something, you love and admire it very strongly.","e":"He idolized his mother."}]}]},"compulsive":{"h":"compulsive","i":"/kəmˈpʌlsɪv/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-compulsive.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is compulsive, they are doing something a lot and unable to stop doing it.","e":"Her compulsive was causing a lot of problems in her life."},{"m":"If something is compulsive, it’s uncontrollable."}]}]},"daunting":{"h":"daunting","i":"/ˈdɔːntɪŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-daunting.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is daunting, you feel that should not try it because it will be very difficult.","e":"The from the bottom of the hill, the ride up looked daunting."}]}]},"regolith":{"h":"regolith","i":"/ˈrɛɡəlɪθ/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A regolith is a layer of loose material such as dust, soil, and broken rock which covers solid rock. It can be found on planets and the moon."}]}]},"expedition":{"h":"expedition","i":"/ɛkspəˈdɪʃən/","a":"en-us-expedition.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An expedition is a long trip that people go on for a specific reason.","e":"The expedition across the lasted two weeks."}]}]},"intently":{"h":"intently","i":"/ɪnˈtɛntli/","a":"en-us-intently.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If you do something intently, you are very focused on doing it.","e":"He listened intently to his grandfather's stories."}]}]},"contronym":{"h":"contronym","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A contronym is a word with two different meanings, which are the opposite of each other. The meaning can only be understood in the context of the sentence."}]}]},"fistfight":{"h":"fistfight","i":"/ˈfɪstˌfaɪt/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A fistfight is a fight that is fought using bare fists.","e":"The two men got into a fistfight behind the bar."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you fistfight, you fight using your bare fists."}]}]},"thrive":{"h":"thrive","i":"/θraɪv/","a":"en-us-thrive.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To thrive is to grow or develop well or vigorously.","e":"In its new place on the windowsill, the plant is sure to thrive and bloom regularly."}]}]},"prick":{"h":"prick","i":"/prɪk/","a":"en-au-prick.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A prick is a short pain from a small sharp object like a needle."},{"m":"(countable) A prick is an annoying or rude person, usually a man.","e":"Nobody cares, prick."},{"m":"(countable) A prick is a penis."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you prick something, it means that you pierce or poke it slightly.","e":"John hardly felt the needle prick his arm when the nurse gave him an injection."}]}]},"gorge":{"h":"gorge","i":"/ɡɔːdʒ/","a":"en-uk-gorge.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A gorge is a narrow valley and normally has steep rocky walls and a stream.","e":"The Kali Gandaki Gorge is the deepest in the world."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If a person gorge themselves, they eat greedily and in large.","e":"They gorged themselves on chocolate and cake."}]}]},"tributary":{"h":"tributary","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A tributary is a river or stream that flows into a larger body of water, such as a river or lake."},{"m":"A tributary is a state that pays another state, often in return for protection."}]}]},"myometrium":{"h":"myometrium","i":"/ˌmaɪəʊˈmiːtriəm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-myometrium.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The myometrium is the thick wall of the uterus made of smooth muscle.","e":"The cells of the myometrium get larger during pregnancy."}]}]},"menstruation":{"h":"menstruation","i":"/ˌmɛnstrʊˈeɪʃn/","a":"menstruation US.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Menstruation is the flow of blood and fluid out through the vagina.","e":"She had her first menstruation at age 13."}]}]},"enterprise":{"h":"enterprise","i":"/ˈɛntəˌpraɪz/","a":"en-us-enterprise.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An enterprise is a business or company.","e":"The enterprise grew every year and now earns millions."}]}]},"citation":{"h":"citation","i":"/ˌsaɪˈteɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-citation.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A citation is a notice given to a person who has to go to court."},{"m":"(countable) A citation is the paper notice given to a person who has to go to court."},{"m":"(countable) A citation is the act of citing a section of a book, or from another person, in their own words."}]}]},"blender":{"h":"blender","i":"/ˈblɛndɚ/","a":"en-us-blender.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A blender is an appliance used to crush food into smaller pieces.","e":"I used the blender to make your smoothie."}]}]},"pentadecagon":{"h":"pentadecagon","i":"/ˌpɛntəˈdɛkəɡən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Rho9998-pentadecagon.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pentadecagon is a shape with 15 sides."}]}]},"scoff":{"h":"scoff","i":"/skɒf/","a":"en-us-scoff.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you scoff at someone or at something, you laugh at someone or something with contempt."},{"m":"If you scoff your food, you eat it very quickly."}]}]},"denominator":{"h":"denominator","i":"/dɪˈnɒmɪneɪtə(r)/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-denominator.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The denominator is the lower number of the fraction.","e":"In the fraction 3/4, the numerator is 3 and the denominator is 4."}]}]},"voyages":{"h":"voyages","l":"voyage","q":"noun"},"hmm":{"h":"hmm","s":[{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"You use hmm when you are thinking about what to say or what to do.","e":"Hmm... What should I do?"}]}]},"hype":{"h":"hype","i":"/haɪp/","a":"en-au-hype.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(usually singular) Hype is excitement for something that is upcoming in the future.","e":"After a storm of hype, the group's debut album was finally released."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If someone hypes about something, they are promoting or advertising heavily.","e":"They started to hype about the new album weeks before its release date."}]}]},"garrison":{"h":"garrison","i":"/ˈɡarɪs(ə)n/","a":"en-us-garrison.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A garrison is a group of soldiers who stay in a place, such as a fort, usually to defend it from a possible attack."}]}]},"slime":{"h":"slime","i":"/slaɪm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-slime.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Slime is a moist soft, sticky substance."},{"m":"(uncountable) Slime is mucus-resembling or viscous substance."}]}]},"peel":{"h":"peel","i":"/piːl/","a":"en-au-peel.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you peel a fruit, you remove its skin.","e":"I am going to peel this banana."},{"m":"If you peel something thin and flat off, you remove it.","e":"After peeling off this old wallpaper, I can add new wallpaper."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Peel is the peeled skin of a fruit.","e":"Banana peels are slippery."}]}]},"deduce":{"h":"deduce","i":"/dɪˈdjuːs/","a":"en-us-deduce.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If someone deduces something, the person reaches a conclusion based on a logical process."}]}]},"lightbulb":{"h":"lightbulb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Another word for light bulb."}]}]},"consequently":{"h":"consequently","i":"/ˈkɒnsɪˌkwɛntli/","a":"en-us-consequently.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"(formal) The word consequently is used show what happened as a result or consequence of an event.","e":"He did not wake up early in the morning. Consequently, he was late to work."}]}]},"consecutive":{"h":"consecutive","i":"/kɒnsɛkjʊtɪv/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-consecutive.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Consecutive events follow one another with no other in between.","e":"We were given homework over five consecutive days."}]}]},"turd":{"h":"turd","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Turd is feces."}]}]},"faeces":{"h":"faeces","i":"/ˈfiːsiːz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-feces.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Faeces are the solid waste from the intestines, also called excrement, shit or poo.","e":"The street was dirty, with dog faeces all over the footpath."}]}]},"beep":{"h":"beep","i":"/biːp/","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something beeps, it makes a short high-pitched sound; it is a sound that sounds like \"beep\".","e":"He is an impatient driver. He kept beeping at the car in front of him."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A beep is a short high-pitched sound that sounds like \"beep\"."}]}]},"blister":{"h":"blister","i":"/ˈblɪstɚ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-blister.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A blister is a painful bump on skin that is caused by excessive rubbing or because of extreme heat."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If someone blisters, they develop a blister."}]}]},"dubious":{"h":"dubious","i":"/ˈdjuːbi.əs/","a":"en-us-dubious.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A dubious decision or opinion is one that you don't believe is honest, safe, or reliable."},{"m":"If you are dubious about something, you are not sure if you should believe or trust it."}]}]},"secondhand":{"h":"secondhand","i":"/ˈsɛk(ə)nd hand/","a":"en-us-secondhand.oga","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A secondhand item is one that was owned by somebody before.","e":"That car retailer sells secondhand cars."}]}]},"fluctuate":{"h":"fluctuate","i":"/ˈflʌktʃʊeɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-fluctuate.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If something fluctuates, it changes often but not regularly.","e":"The price of gasoline has been fluctuating wildly."}]}]},"writ":{"h":"writ","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A writ is a document form a court that says you have to do something.","e":"The writ was given to tell information to everyone."}]}]},"filth":{"h":"filth","i":"/fɪlθ/","a":"en-au-filth.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Filth is the dirt that appears on objects."},{"m":"(uncountable) Filth is someone or something that is disgusting."}]}]},"stew":{"h":"stew","i":"/stʃʉː/","a":"en-au-stew.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Stew is a dish that is made with meat and/or vegetables cooked in liquid."},{"m":"(by extension) A stew is an add-on to staple foods such as rice and pasta, usually in the form of soup, vegetables etc."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(cooking) If you stew something, it means that you cook by slowly boiling or simmering.","e":"I'm going to stew some meat."},{"m":"(transitive) If you stew tea, it means that you brewed it for too long that the flavour becomes too strong."}]}]},"shorthand":{"h":"shorthand","i":"/ˈʃɔːthænd/","a":"en-uk-shorthand.oga","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Shorthand is a shortened or simplified way of referring to something."}]}]},"prong":{"h":"prong","i":"/prɒŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-prong.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A prong is a pointed end of a fork.","e":"The broccoli was stuck on one prong of my fork."}]}]},"deflect":{"h":"deflect","i":"/dɪˈflɛkt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-deflect.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you deflect something, you hit it to change its direction.","e":"I was able to deflect the ball coming at me."}]}]},"spine":{"h":"spine","i":"/spaɪn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-spine.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Your spine is the set of bones down the middle of your back."},{"m":"(countable) Spines are sharp, pointy parts on an animal or a plant."},{"m":"(countable) The spine of a book is the narrow, hard part that joins the pages together."}]}]},"interrogation":{"h":"interrogation","i":"/ɪnˌter.əˈɡeɪ.ʃən/","a":"en-us-interrogation.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Interrogation is the process of asking someone questions to get information from them.","e":"The police use interrogation to investigate people suspected of crimes."}]}]},"mortar":{"h":"mortar","i":"/'mɔːtə/","a":"en-us-mortar.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mortar is kind of large gun that fires explosive shells."},{"m":"(uncountable) Mortar is a type of paste used to stick bricks together."},{"m":"(countable) A mortar is a bowl used with a pestle to crush food or drugs into smaller pieces."}]}]},"mortars":{"h":"mortars","l":"mortar","q":"noun"},"denominators":{"h":"denominators","l":"denominator","q":"noun"},"blunder":{"h":"blunder","i":"/ˈblʌn.də(r)/","a":"en-us-blunder.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A blunder is a major mistake."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) A blunder means to make a clumsy or stupid mistake.","e":"She made a blunder while preparing the customer's order."}]}]},"skewer":{"h":"skewer","i":"/ˈskjuːə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-skewer.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A skewer is a long piece of wood or metal used to hold pieces of food, typically meat, while cooking.","e":"He used a skewer to put pieces of meat together for his kebab."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If someone skewers pieces of food, they pierce them through a skewer.","e":"He skewered pieces of meat to make his kebab."},{"m":"(informal) If you skewer someone, you criticize them strongly, often in a humorous way."}]}]},"inflict":{"h":"inflict","i":"/ɪnˈflɪkt/","a":"en-us-inflict.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you inflict something on someone, you cause an unpleasant situation for them."}]}]},"toasty":{"h":"toasty","i":"/ˈtoʊsti/","a":"en-us-toasty.oga","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is toasty is cooked in a way that resembles toast.","e":"These roasted marshmallows look toasty."},{"m":"(informal) If you feel toasty, you feel comfortably warm.","e":"I am feeling toasty with that new fireplace."}]}]},"brandy":{"h":"brandy","i":"/ˈbrændi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-brandy.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Brandy is a type of spirit produced by distilled wine."}]}]},"smear":{"h":"smear","i":"/smɪə(r)/","a":"en-uk-smear.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you smear a substance on a surface, you spread it by rubbing."},{"m":"If you smear a person, you say bad things about them, that are false.","e":"There is a online campaign to smear the president."}]}]},"spoonbill":{"h":"spoonbill","i":"/ˈspunˌbɪl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-spoonbill.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A spoonbill is a type of water bird with a spoon-shaped beak."}]}]},"contempt":{"h":"contempt","i":"/kənˈtɛmpt/","a":"en-us-contempt.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Contempt is the feeling that a person or a thing is useless or deserves to be looked down upon."},{"m":"(uncountable) If you treat someone with contempt, you treat them as inferior or worthless."}]}]},"bling":{"h":"bling","i":"/blɪŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-bling.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Bling is expensive clothes or jewelry of high prestige."}]}]},"pricey":{"h":"pricey","i":"/ˈpraɪsi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-pricey.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"(informal) If something is pricey, it costs a lot of money."}]}]},"rip-off":{"h":"rip-off","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (informal) A rip-off is something that costs much more than it is actually worth.","e":"$200 for a pair of shoes!? That is a rip-off."},{"m":"(countable) (informal) A rip-off of something is a poor imitation of it.","e":"This cheap company produces rip-offs of the popular Nike shoes."}]}]},"swindle":{"h":"swindle","i":"/ˈswɪnd(ə)l/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-swindle.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you swindle someone out of money, you trick them into giving you the money."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A swindle is the deception of money-related items."}]}]},"nah":{"h":"nah","s":[{"p":"interjection","d":[{"m":"You use \"nah\" as a casual way of saying \"no\".","e":"Nah, I'm not gonna make a funny prank at the teacher. You should do it if you are wanting me to do that."}]}]},"goosebumps":{"h":"goosebumps","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Goosebumps are bumps on your skin that appear whenever you are cold."}]}]},"wonky":{"h":"wonky","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is wonky it is not straight or level."}]}]},"obese":{"h":"obese","i":"/oʊˈbis/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-obese.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Someone who is obese is extremely fat.","e":"The man with the obese belly walked to the nearest McDonalds."}]}]},"necromancer":{"h":"necromancer","i":"/ˈnekrə(ʊ)ˌmænsə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-necromancer.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A necromancer is someone who summons dead people."}]}]},"skillful":{"h":"skillful","i":"/ˈskɪlfəl/","a":"en-us-skilful.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A skillful person is someone who is skilled in doing something."}]}]},"chaotic":{"h":"chaotic","i":"/keɪˈɒtɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-chaotic.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Someone or something that is chaotic is unpredictable."},{"m":"Someone who is chaotic is crazy."}]}]},"rip-offs":{"h":"rip-offs","l":"rip-off","q":"noun"},"pixel":{"h":"pixel","i":"/ˈpɪksəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-pixel.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pixel is a unit of a computer image.","e":"If you look close enough at an image on the computer, you can see pixels on the picture. They are shaped like squares."}]}]},"shuffle":{"h":"shuffle","i":"/ˈʃʌfəl/","a":"en-us-shuffle.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you shuffle, you drag your feet along the floor without lifting them up.","e":"He shuffled out of the room."},{"m":"If you shuffle something, you rearrange something in a random order.","e":"The dealer will shuffle the playing cards to make the game fair."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"If you make a shuffle, you drag your feet along the floor without lifting them up.","e":"The sad young girl left with a tired shuffle."},{"m":"A shuffle is the rearrangement of something in a random order.","e":"You don't do very good shuffles. Why not make me do it instead?"}]}]},"periodic":{"h":"periodic","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is periodic happens regularly."}]}]},"twit":{"h":"twit","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(informal) A twit is a stupid person."}]}]},"smudge":{"h":"smudge","i":"/smʌdʒ/","a":"en-us-smudge.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A smudge is a dirty mark.","e":"He rubbed the smudge off the glass."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you smudge something, you rub something in or make it dirty.","e":"The painter accidentally smudged his painting."}]}]},"jimmy":{"h":"jimmy","i":"/ˈd͡ʒɪmi/","a":"en-us-jimmy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (US) A jimmy is a crowbar used by burglars to open windows and doors."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) (informal) If you jimmy a lock, you pry it open with something such as a crowbar."}]}]},"wally":{"h":"Wally","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Wally is a nickname given to the male given name for Waldo."}]}]},"greg":{"h":"Greg","i":"/ɡrɛɡ/","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Greg is a male given name; it is often, but not always, a shortened form of Gregory."}]}]},"boiler":{"h":"boiler","i":"/ˈbɔɪlə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-boiler.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A boiler is a large container where water is heated, usually for the purpose of heating a building.","e":"The water from the boiler heats the whole building."}]}]},"trump":{"h":"trump","i":"/trʌmp/","a":"en-us-trump.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"In a game of cards, a trump is a card of the most powerful suit."},{"m":"If you have a trump card (or just a trump), you have something that gives you an advantage."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If someone or something trumps another, it matters more or is more powerful."}]}]},"overwhelm":{"h":"overwhelm","i":"/ˌəʊvəˈʍɛlm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-overwhelm.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you are overwhelmed by a feeling, you feel it very strongly, and you cannot deal with it."},{"m":"If a problem overwhelms you, it's too difficult for you to solve or deal with."},{"m":"If one army overwhelms another, they completely defeat them.","e":"The team was able to overwhelm their opponents and win first place"}]}]},"overwhelmed":{"h":"overwhelmed","a":"en-us-overwhelmed.ogg","l":"overwhelm","q":"verb"},"jude":{"h":"Jude","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Jude is a male and female given name."}]}]},"victor":{"h":"Victor","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Victor is a male given name."}]}]},"hayden":{"h":"Hayden","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Hayden is a male given name."}]}]},"miguel":{"h":"Miguel","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Miguel is a Spanish male given name."},{"m":"Miguel is a surname."}]}]},"tucker":{"h":"tucker","i":"/ˈtʌkə/","a":"en-au-tucker.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) (Australia, New Zealand) Tucker is food."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you tucker someone, you make a person tired."}]}]},"matteo":{"h":"Matteo","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Matteo is a male given name from Italy."}]}]},"preston":{"h":"Preston","i":"/ˈprɛs.tən/","a":"en-uk-Preston.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Preston is a city in Lancashire in the United Kingdom."}]}]},"alejandro":{"h":"Alejandro","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Alejandro is a Spanish male given name."}]}]},"maximus":{"h":"Maximus","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Maximus is a male given name."}]}]},"gunn":{"h":"Gunn","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Gunn is a surname."},{"m":"Gunn is a male given name."}]}]},"kaden":{"h":"Kaden","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Kaden is a male given name."}]}]},"holst":{"h":"Holst","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Holst is a surname."}]}]},"lukas":{"h":"Lukas","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Lukas is a male given name."}]}]},"johnson":{"h":"johnson","i":"/ˈd͡ʒɑnsən/","a":"en-au-johnson.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A johnson is another word for a penis.","e":"You're just asking to get a look at my johnson."}]}]},"aidan":{"h":"Aidan","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Aidan is a male given name."}]}]},"milo":{"h":"Milo","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Milo is a male given name."}]}]},"javier":{"h":"Javier","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Javier is a male given name."}]}]},"jaden":{"h":"Jaden","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Jaden is a male given name."}]}]},"jorge":{"h":"Jorge","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Jorge is a male given name."}]}]},"lisa":{"h":"Lisa","i":"/ˈliːsə/","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Lisa is a female given name."}]}]},"annie":{"h":"Annie","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Annie is a female given name."}]}]},"yoshi":{"h":"Yoshi","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Yoshi is a Japanese male given name."}]}]},"adequacy":{"h":"adequacy","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Adequacy is the property of being good enough or sufficient.","e":"The fire department was sent to see adequacy of the escape plan."}]}]},"reignite":{"h":"reignite","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something is reignited, it is set on fire again.","e":"The cigarette reignited the campfire."},{"m":"If an argument, debate, etc. is reignited, it starts again.","e":"The mayor reignited talks of a new subway."}]}]},"mainstream":{"h":"mainstream","i":"/ˈmeɪnstriːm/","a":"en-us-mainstream.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is mainstream is used or accepted by a lot of people.","e":"The news story wasn't covered by the mainstream media."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The mainstream is something that is common or accepted by a lot of people."}]}]},"app":{"h":"app","i":"/æp/","a":"en-us-app.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An app is a computer application.","e":"There are various apps on the internet that you can download or purchase."}]}]},"clam":{"h":"clam","i":"/klæm/","a":"en-us-clam.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A clam is a type of shellfish with a hard shell and a small opening that allows the flow of nutrients in and out of it."},{"m":"(US) (usually plural) A clam is a dollar."},{"m":"A clam is a vagina."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If a person clams, they dig for [[#Noun|clams]]."}]}]},"squid":{"h":"squid","i":"/skwɪd/","a":"en-us-squid.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A squid is a cephalopod (a type of sea creature) with a large head and ten legs.","e":"The squid is not able to grow a leg after it is severed."}]}]},"calculus":{"h":"calculus","i":"/ˈkæl.kjʊ.ləs/","a":"calculus-pron.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Calculus is a branch of mathematics that involves understanding mathematical functions.","e":"One use of calculus is for finding and maximization."}]}]},"apps":{"h":"apps","l":"app","q":"noun"},"overwhelms":{"h":"overwhelms","l":"overwhelm","q":"verb"},"overwhelming":{"h":"overwhelming","i":"/ˌoʊvɚˈ(h)wɛlmɪŋ/","a":"en-us-overwhelming.ogg","l":"overwhelm","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If evidence or numbers are overwhelming they are far more than needed.","e":"The police believed their evidence against Curtis was overwhelming."},{"m":"If you feel that something is overwhelming you feel that it is too much for you.","e":"Parts of this job are probably very overwhelming for him."}]}]},"conforms":{"h":"conforms","l":"conform","q":"verb"},"conforming":{"h":"conforming","l":"conform","q":"verb"},"conformed":{"h":"conformed","l":"conform","q":"verb"},"elucidates":{"h":"elucidates","l":"elucidate","q":"verb"},"frauds":{"h":"frauds","l":"fraud","q":"noun"},"elucidated":{"h":"elucidated","l":"elucidate","q":"verb"},"elucidating":{"h":"elucidating","l":"elucidate","q":"verb"},"garrisons":{"h":"garrisons","l":"garrison","q":"noun"},"legion":{"h":"legion","i":"/ˈliːdʒən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-legion.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A legion is large number","e":"The film won him a legion of followers."},{"m":"A legion is a part of the Roman army with 3000 to 6000 soldiers","e":"Caesar and his legions defeated the Gauls."}]}]},"legions":{"h":"legions","l":"legion","q":"noun"},"thrash":{"h":"thrash","i":"/θræʃ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-thrash.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you thrash someone or something, you beat it violently.","e":"She thrashed him across the head and shoulders."},{"m":"If you thrash a person, you defeat them."}]}]},"conventional":{"h":"conventional","i":"/kənˈvɛnʃənəl/","a":"en-us-conventional.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is conventional is what is generally done, believed, or ordinary.","e":"The conventional temperature is at 22C."}]}]},"clams":{"h":"clams","l":"clam","q":"noun"},"thrashed":{"h":"thrashed","l":"thrash","q":"verb"},"goads":{"h":"goads","l":"goad","q":"verb"},"decrucify":{"h":"decrucify","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) To decrucify is to remove from a cross.","e":"Jesus was later decrucified to be put in a tomb."}]}]},"drainage":{"h":"drainage","i":"/ˈdreɪnədʒ/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"To use a drainage is engage in the action or process of draining something.","e":"The pot has holes in the base for good drainage"}]}]},"conspire":{"h":"conspire","i":"/kənˈspaɪə(r)/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-conspire.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If people are conspiring, they are making secret plans together, usually to cause harm.","e":"The group was caught conspiring to overthrow the leader."}]}]},"conspiring":{"h":"conspiring","l":"conspire","q":"verb"},"conspired":{"h":"conspired","l":"conspire","q":"verb"},"