ou store it in a [[#Noun|hangar]]."}]}]},"hangaring":{"h":"hangaring","l":"hangar","q":"verb"},"hangars":{"h":"hangars","l":"hangar","q":"noun"},"hangared":{"h":"hangared","l":"hangar","q":"verb"},"heaters":{"h":"heaters","l":"heater","q":"noun"},"councilor":{"h":"councilor","i":"/ˈkaʊns(ɪ)lə/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A councilor is a member of a council.","e":"Half of the councilors voted against expanding the metro."}]}]},"councilors":{"h":"councilors","l":"councilor","q":"noun"},"powdery":{"h":"powdery","i":"/ˈpaʊdəri/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-powdery.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is powdery, it is made up of fine particles that resembles powder."}]}]},"verdures":{"h":"verdures","l":"verdure","q":"noun"},"lush":{"h":"lush","i":"/lʌʃ/","a":"en-us-lush.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"(of vegetation) If vegetation is lush, it is dense and abundant in growth."},{"m":"If something is lush, it is very rich and provides great sensory pleasure."},{"m":"(British) If a person is lush, he or she is sexually, attractive.","e":"Boys with long hair are lush!"},{"m":"(British, Canada) If something is lush, it is, cool or fantastic.","e":"Your voice is lush, Lucy! I could listen to it all day!"}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A lush is a habitual heavy drinker."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you lush, you drink liquor to excess."}]}]},"lushes":{"h":"lushes","l":"lush","q":"noun"},"lushed":{"h":"lushed","l":"lush","q":"verb"},"lushing":{"h":"lushing","l":"lush","q":"verb"},"lushest":{"h":"lushest","l":"lush","q":"adjective"},"lusher":{"h":"lusher","l":"lush","q":"adjective"},"luxuriant":{"h":"luxuriant","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is luxuriant, it is abundant in growth or detail."}]}]},"liquor":{"h":"liquor","i":"/ˈlɪk.ə(r)/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-liquor.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Liquor is a liquid that is obtained by cooking meat or vegetables."},{"m":"(US) Liquor is any alcoholic drink that is made through fermentation and distillation."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you liquor something, you dress it with oil or grease."},{"m":"(transitive) If someone liquors, they drink excess [[#Noun|liquor]]."}]}]},"liquors":{"h":"liquors","l":"liquor","q":"noun"},"liquoring":{"h":"liquoring","l":"liquor","q":"verb"},"liquored":{"h":"liquored","l":"liquor","q":"verb"},"licker":{"h":"licker","i":"/ˈlɪkɚ/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A licker is someone or something that licks."}]}]},"lickers":{"h":"lickers","l":"licker","q":"noun"},"sensory":{"h":"sensory","i":"/ˈsɛnsəri/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-sensory.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is sensory, it is related to sensations or physical senses."}]}]},"medicate":{"h":"medicate","i":"/ˈmɛdɪkeɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-medicate.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you medicate, you prescribe or administer medication to someone."}]}]},"medicates":{"h":"medicates","l":"medicate","q":"verb"},"medicated":{"h":"medicated","l":"medicate","q":"verb"},"medicating":{"h":"medicating","l":"medicate","q":"verb"},"capsule":{"h":"capsule","i":"/ˈkæps(ə)l/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-capsule.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A capsule is a small case or container, usually circular or cylindrical in shape."},{"m":"(countable) A capsule is a tough, fibrous layer surrounding an organ such as the kidney or liver"},{"m":"(countable) A capsule is a membrane that surrounds the eyeball."},{"m":"(countable) (pharmacy) A capsule is a small container containing a dose of medicine."},{"m":"(countable) A capsule is a dry fruit that releases its seeds by bursting open when ripe."},{"m":"(countable) (winemaking) A capsule is a foil or plastic covering the cork of a wine bottle."}]}]},"capsules":{"h":"capsules","l":"capsule","q":"noun"},"membrane":{"h":"membrane","i":"/ˈmembreɪn/","a":"en-us-membrane.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A membrane is a thin layer of cells or tissue that acts as a boundary or lining that separates two environments."}]}]},"membranes":{"h":"membranes","l":"membrane","q":"noun"},"fibrous":{"h":"fibrous","i":"/ˈfaɪbrəs/","a":"en-us-fibrous.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is fibrous, it is related to or contains fibre."}]}]},"cylindrical":{"h":"cylindrical","i":"/sɪˈlɪndrɪkəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-cylindrical.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is cylindrical, it is shaped like a cylinder."}]}]},"maelstrom":{"h":"maelstrom","i":"/ˈmeɪ.jəlˌstrəm/","a":"en-us-maelstrom.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A maelstrom is a large and violent whirlpool."},{"m":"(countable) A maelstrom is any violent or turbulent situation."}]}]},"maelstroms":{"h":"maelstroms","l":"maelstrom","q":"noun"},"figurative":{"h":"figurative","i":"/ˈfɪɡjʊrətɪv/","a":"en-us-figurative.oga","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a word has a figurative meaning, it is used as a metaphor, simile as opposed to literal."}]}]},"whirlpool":{"h":"whirlpool","i":"/ˈwɝlpul/","a":"en-au-whirlpool.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A whirlpool is a swirling body of water."},{"m":"(countable) A whirlpool is a hot tub or jacuzzi."}]}]},"whirlpools":{"h":"whirlpools","l":"whirlpool","q":"noun"},"turbulent":{"h":"turbulent","i":"/ˈtɜːbjələnt/","a":"en-us-turbulent.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something becomes turbulent, it was violently disturbed or agitated.","e":"It is dangerous to sail in turbulent seas."},{"m":"If something isturbulent, it is being in, or causing disturbance or unrest.","e":"The mid-19th century was a turbulent time in American history."}]}]},"jacuzzi":{"h":"jacuzzi","i":"/dʒəˈkuːzi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-jacuzzi.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A jacuzzi is a large bath with a system of underwater jets of water to massage the body."}]}]},"jacuzzis":{"h":"jacuzzis","l":"jacuzzi","q":"noun"},"swirl":{"h":"swirl","i":"/swɜːl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-swirl.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something is swirling, it is move in a twisting or spiraling pattern."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A swirl is something that is moving in a twisting or spiraling pattern."}]}]},"swirls":{"h":"swirls","l":"swirl","q":"verb"},"swirled":{"h":"swirled","l":"swirl","q":"verb"},"swirling":{"h":"swirling","l":"swirl","q":"verb"},"spiraled":{"h":"spiraled","l":"spiral","q":"verb"},"spiralled":{"h":"spiralled","l":"spiral","q":"verb"},"spiraling":{"h":"spiraling","l":"spiral","q":"verb"},"spiralling":{"h":"spiralling","l":"spiral","q":"verb"},"agitate":{"h":"agitate","i":"/ˈæ.dʒɪ.teɪt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Mélange a trois-agitate.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you agitate someone, you make them feel troubled or nervous."},{"m":"If something is agitated, it moves with a violent, irregular action.","e":"The wind agitates the sea"},{"m":"(transitive) If someone is agitated, they are disturbed or excited over something.","e":"He was greatly agitated by the news."}]}]},"agitates":{"h":"agitates","l":"agitate","q":"verb"},"agitated":{"h":"agitated","i":"/ˈæd͡ʒɪteɪtɪd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Persent101-agitated.wav","l":"agitate","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"An agitated person is someone who is angry and annoyed."}]}]},"agitating":{"h":"agitating","l":"agitate","q":"verb"},"theorist":{"h":"theorist","i":"/ˈθɪərɪst/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-theorist.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A theorist is a person who constructs, especially in the arts or sciences."}]}]},"theorists":{"h":"theorists","l":"theorist","q":"noun"},"sloppy":{"h":"sloppy","i":"/ˈslɒpi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-sloppy.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is sloppy, very wet and contains too much liquid.","e":"The dog tracked sloppy mud through the kitchen!"},{"m":"If something is sloppy, it is messy; not neat, elegant, or careful.","e":"The carpenter did a sloppy job of building the staircase."},{"m":"If something is sloppy, it is not precise or loose.","e":"A sloppy measurement; a sloppy fit!"}]}]},"sloppier":{"h":"sloppier","l":"sloppy","q":"adjective"},"sloppiest":{"h":"sloppiest","l":"sloppy","q":"adjective"},"slop":{"h":"slop","i":"/slɒp/","a":"en-us-slop.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Slop is a liquid or semi-solid."},{"m":"Slops are scraps used as food for animals, especially pigs or hogs."},{"m":"Slops are domestic liquid waste."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you slop, you accidentally spill or dump liquid, over the edge of a container.","e":"I slopped water all over my shirt."},{"m":"(transitive) If you slop, you feed pigs."}]}]},"slops":{"h":"slops","l":"slop","q":"noun"},"slopped":{"h":"slopped","l":"slop","q":"verb"},"slopping":{"h":"slopping","l":"slop","q":"verb"},"smoker":{"h":"smoker","i":"/ˈsmoʊkɚ/","a":"en-au-smoker.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A smoker is a person who smokes tobacco regularly."},{"m":"A smoker is a person or device that smokes fish or meat."},{"m":"A smoker is a device that releases smoke to distract bees."}]}]},"smokers":{"h":"smokers","l":"smoker","q":"noun"},"smoky":{"h":"smoky","i":"/ˈsmoʊki/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-smoky.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a place is smoky, it is filled with smoke.","e":"A smoky cabin."},{"m":"If a something has a smoky color, it has the color similar to that of smoke."},{"m":"If a something has a smoky flavor, it has a taste or odor like smoke.","e":"A smoky whisky."}]}]},"smokey":{"h":"smokey","i":"/ˈsmoʊki/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-smoky.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a place is smokey, it is filled with smoke.","e":"A smokey cabin."},{"m":"If a something has a smokey color, it has the color similar to that of smoke."},{"m":"If a something has a smokey flavor, it has a taste or odor like smoke.","e":"A smokey whisky."}]}]},"smokier":{"h":"smokier","l":"smoky","q":"adjective"},"smokiest":{"h":"smokiest","l":"smokey","q":"adjective"},"brownish":{"h":"brownish","i":"/ˈbraʊnɪʃ/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is brownish, then it is moderately brown."}]}]},"veteran":{"h":"veteran","i":"/ˈvɛ.tə.rən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-veteran.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A veteran is a person with long experience of a particular activity."},{"m":"(countable) A veteran is a person who has served in the army, especially an old soldier who has seen long service."}]}]},"veterans":{"h":"veterans","l":"veteran","q":"noun"},"petal":{"h":"petal","i":"/ˈpɛtl̩/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-petal.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A petal is one of the component parts of the corolla of a flower."}]}]},"petals":{"h":"petals","l":"petal","q":"noun"},"corolla":{"h":"corolla","i":"/kəˈroʊlə/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A corolla is the petals of a flower that encloses the reproductive organ or the flower."}]}]},"corollas":{"h":"corollas","l":"corolla","q":"noun"},"corollae":{"h":"corollae","l":"corolla","q":"noun"},"haggard":{"h":"haggard","i":"/ˈhæɡ.əd/","a":"en-au-haggard.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a person looks haggard, they look exhausted from fatigue, worry or suffering.","e":"Staring his eyes, and haggard was his look."}]}]},"fatigue":{"h":"fatigue","i":"/fəˈtiːɡ/","a":"en-us-fatigue.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Fatigue is the extreme tiredness which is the result of having mental or physical exertion or illness."},{"m":"(engineering) Fatigue is the material failure, such as cracking or separation, caused by stress on the material.","e":"failures due to fatigue have been the subject of engineering efforts for more than 150 years."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you fatigue a person, you make them exhausted."}]}]},"fatigues":{"h":"fatigues","l":"fatigue","q":"noun"},"intransitive":{"h":"intransitive","i":"/ɪnˈtrænsətɪv/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-intransitive.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Having no object, as with a verb like faint or a clause like I fainted."}]}]},"attributive":{"h":"attributive","i":"/ə.ˈtrɪ.bju.tɪv/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-attributive.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"An attributive modifier is a modifier of a noun, usually occurring before the noun in English.","e":"In a big tree, the adjective big is attributive, but in the tree is big, it is predicative."}]}]},"predicative":{"h":"predicative","i":"/prɪˈdɪk.ə.tɪv/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"The predicative use is the use of an adjective or other expression as predicative complement or predicative adjunct.","e":"The clause I am hot illustrates the predicative use of the adjective hot."}]}]},"pandemic":{"h":"pandemic","i":"/pænˈdɛmɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-pandemic.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is pandemic, it is spread over a wide geographical area and affecting a large proportion of the population."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pandemic is an outbreak of a [[#Adjective|pandemic]] disease."}]}]},"pandemics":{"h":"pandemics","l":"pandemic","q":"noun"},"geographic":{"h":"geographic","i":"/d͡ʒiəˈɡræfɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-geographic.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is geographic, it is determined by the physical features of an area."}]}]},"echelon":{"h":"echelon","i":"/ˈɛʃəlɒn/","a":"en-au-echelon.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An echelon is a level or rank in an organization, profession, or society."},{"m":"(countable) An echelon is a formation of troops, ships in diagonal parallel rows."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you echelon, you form troops into an [[#Noun|echelon]]."}]}]},"echelons":{"h":"echelons","l":"echelon","q":"noun"},"echeloned":{"h":"echeloned","l":"echelon","q":"verb"},"echeloning":{"h":"echeloning","l":"echelon","q":"verb"},"procedural":{"h":"procedural","i":"/prəˈsiːdʒ(ə)rəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-procedural.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is procedural, it is related to or done according to a procedure.","e":"The judge dismissed the case on procedural grounds: it wasn't the facts or the law, but just that they hadn't filed the correct forms."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A procedural is a type of literature, film, or television program that involves a sequence of technical detail."}]}]},"procedurals":{"h":"procedurals","l":"procedural","q":"noun"},"understudy":{"h":"understudy","i":"/ˈʌndɚˌstʌdi/","a":"en-us-ncalif-undertusdy.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An understudy is a person who [[#Noun|understudies]]."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you understudy, you study or know a role so as to be able to replace the normal performer when required."}]}]},"understudies":{"h":"understudies","l":"understudy","q":"noun"},"understudied":{"h":"understudied","l":"understudy","q":"verb"},"understudying":{"h":"understudying","l":"understudy","q":"verb"},"immigrant":{"h":"immigrant","i":"/ˈɪmɪɡrənt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-immigrant.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An immigrant is a person who comes to live permanently in a foreign country."}]}]},"immigrants":{"h":"immigrants","l":"immigrant","q":"noun"},"caterpillar":{"h":"caterpillar","i":"/ˈkætəpɪlə(r)/","a":"en-us-caterpillar.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A caterpillar is the larva of a butterfly or moth.","e":"The bird just ate that green caterpillar."}]}]},"caterpillars":{"h":"caterpillars","l":"caterpillar","q":"noun"},"moth":{"h":"moth","i":"/mɒθ/","a":"en-us-moth.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Moths are nocturnal insects with two pairs of broad and dull wings covered in microscopic scales."}]}]},"moths":{"h":"moths","l":"moth","q":"noun"},"chariot":{"h":"chariot","i":"/ˈt͡ʃærɪət/","a":"en-us-chariot.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A two-wheeled horse-drawn vehicle, used in and Early warfare."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you are charioting, you are riding in a [[#Noun|chariot]]."}]}]},"chariots":{"h":"chariots","l":"chariot","q":"noun"},"charioted":{"h":"charioted","l":"chariot","q":"verb"},"charioting":{"h":"charioting","l":"chariot","q":"verb"},"charioteer":{"h":"charioteer","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A charioteer is a person who drives a chariot."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you charioteer people, you drive people in a chariot."},{"m":"(intransitive) If you charioteer, you drive a chariot."}]}]},"charioteers":{"h":"charioteers","l":"charioteer","q":"noun"},"chug":{"h":"chug","i":"/tʃʌɡ/","a":"en-us-chug.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A chug is a dull and fairly quick explosive sound, as if made by a laboring engine."},{"m":"A chug is a large gulp of drink.","e":"He drank his beer in three chugs."},{"m":"A chug is a homemade Cuban boat, built to carry emigrants to the USA, and often abandoned upon arrival."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you chug, you make dull explosive sounds."},{"m":"(transitive) If you chug, you move or travel while making such sounds.","e":"We were chugging along a back road when the engine cut out."},{"m":"(transitive) If you chug, you drink a large amount (especially of beer) in a single action/without breathing. People usually chant this at the person who is drinking.","e":"Chug! Chug! Chug!"}]}]},"chugs":{"h":"chugs","i":"/tʃʌɡz/","l":"chug","q":"noun"},"chugged":{"h":"chugged","i":"/tʃʌɡd/","l":"chug","q":"verb"},"chugging":{"h":"chugging","i":"/ˈtʃʌɡɪŋ/","l":"chug","q":"verb"},"gulp":{"h":"gulp","i":"/ɡʌlp/","a":"en-au-gulp.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A gulp is an act of eating or drinking."},{"m":"A gulp is the sound of swallowing, sometimes indicating fear."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you gulp, you swallow (drink or food) quickly or in large mouthfuls, and usually can be heard.","e":"He does not swallow, but he gulps it down."},{"m":"If you gulp, you react nervously by swallowing."}]}]},"gulps":{"h":"gulps","l":"gulp","q":"noun"},"gulped":{"h":"gulped","l":"gulp","q":"verb"},"gulping":{"h":"gulping","l":"gulp","q":"verb"},"mettle":{"h":"mettle","i":"/ˈmɛt.l̩/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-mettle.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Your mettle is your ability to deal with difficult situations well."}]}]},"snooze":{"h":"snooze","i":"/snuːz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-snooze.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you snooze, you sleep for a short period of time.","e":"The boss caught him snoozing at his desk."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A snooze is a brief period of sleep.","e":"The cat enjoys taking a snooze on a sunny windowsill."},{"m":"(informal) The snooze button on an alarm clock."}]}]},"snoozes":{"h":"snoozes","l":"snooze","q":"verb"},"snoozed":{"h":"snoozed","l":"snooze","q":"verb"},"snoozing":{"h":"snoozing","l":"snooze","q":"verb"},"doze":{"h":"doze","i":"/doʊz/","a":"en-us-doze.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you doze, you sleep lightly or briefly.","e":"I didn’t sleep very well, but I think I may have dozed a bit."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A doze is a light, short sleep or nap.","e":"I felt much better after a short doze."}]}]},"dozes":{"h":"dozes","l":"doze","q":"verb"},"dozed":{"h":"dozed","l":"doze","q":"verb"},"dozing":{"h":"dozing","l":"doze","q":"verb"},"lightly":{"h":"lightly","i":"/ˈlaɪtli/","a":"en-us-lightly.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something is placed lightly, it is placed gently."},{"m":"If it is raining lightly, it is raining in small amounts or in low density."},{"m":"If something can be taken lightly, it is not serious or solemn.","e":"It is not something that should be taken lightly."}]}]},"conglomerate":{"h":"conglomerate","i":"/kənˈɡlɒm(ə)rət/","a":"en-au-conglomerate.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A conglomerate is a corporation formed by the combination of several smaller corporations whose activities are not related to the corporation's primary activity."},{"m":"A conglomerate is a rock that consists of gravel or pebbles embedded in a matrix."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is conglomerate it is clustered together into a mass.","e":"conglomerate flowers."},{"m":"If something is conglomerate it is composed of fragments of rock, pebbles, or stones cemented together."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If something is conglomerated, it is combined together into a larger mass."},{"m":"(transitive) If something is conglomerated, it is combined together into a larger corporation."}]}]},"conglomerates":{"h":"conglomerates","l":"conglomerate","q":"noun"},"conglomerated":{"h":"conglomerated","l":"conglomerate","q":"verb"},"conglomerating":{"h":"conglomerating","l":"conglomerate","q":"verb"},"embed":{"h":"embed","i":"/ɪmˈbɛd/","a":"en-us-embed.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you embed something, you put it firmly and deeply in a surrounding mass.","e":"To embed something in clay, mortar, or sand"},{"m":"(transitive) If you embed a person, you attach someone, usually a journalist, to a military unit during a conflict.","e":"We wanted to embed our reporter with the Fifth Infantry Division, but the Army would have none of it."},{"m":"(transitive) If you embed data, you put it within another document or data file.","e":"The instructions showed how to embed a chart from the spreadsheet within the word processor document."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An embed is a journalist who is attached to a military unit during a conflict."}]}]},"embeds":{"h":"embeds","l":"embed","q":"verb"},"embedded":{"h":"embedded","l":"embed","q":"verb"},"embedding":{"h":"embedding","l":"embed","q":"verb"},"elusive":{"h":"elusive","i":"/ɪˈluːsɪv/","a":"en-us-elusive-illusive.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something or someone is elusive, they are difficult to find, catch, or achieve.","e":"The elusive criminal was arrested."}]}]},"illusive":{"h":"illusive","i":"/ɪˈluːsɪv/","a":"en-us-elusive-illusive.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is illusive, it is subject to or related to an illusion. It is often used in the sense of a goal or outcome that is not achievable.","e":"Testing software completely is an illusive goal."}]}]},"mole":{"h":"mole","i":"/məʊl/","a":"en-us-mole.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mole is a small animal that digs in the ground."}]}]},"moles":{"h":"moles","l":"mole","q":"noun"},"affiliated":{"h":"affiliated","l":"affiliate","q":"verb"},"affiliating":{"h":"affiliating","l":"affiliate","q":"verb"},"apprehend":{"h":"apprehend","i":"/æ.priˈhɛnd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Mélange a trois-apprehend.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If someone is apprehended, they are taken or seized by legal process.","e":"Officers apprehended the suspect two streets away from the bank."},{"m":"(transitive) If you apprehend something, you are able to understand or perceive it."}]}]},"apprehends":{"h":"apprehends","l":"apprehend","q":"verb"},"apprehended":{"h":"apprehended","l":"apprehend","q":"verb"},"apprehending":{"h":"apprehending","l":"apprehend","q":"verb"},"array":{"h":"array","i":"/əˈreɪ/","a":"en-us-array.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A collection or assortment of things."},{"m":"(programming) A basic data structure for storing multiple instances of data, typically all of the same type. It occupies a contiguous chunk of memory."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you array someone, you dress someone in something.","e":"He was arrayed in his finest robes and jewels."},{"m":"If you array something, you display or arrange it in a particular way."}]}]},"arrays":{"h":"arrays","l":"array","q":"noun"},"arrayed":{"h":"arrayed","l":"array","q":"verb"},"arraying":{"h":"arraying","l":"array","q":"verb"},"astound":{"h":"astound","i":"/əˈstaʊnd/","a":"en-us-astound.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you are astounded, you are shocked or greatly surprised."}]}]},"astounds":{"h":"astounds","l":"astound","q":"verb"},"astounded":{"h":"astounded","l":"astound","q":"verb"},"astounding":{"h":"astounding","l":"astound","q":"verb"},"anglo":{"h":"anglo","i":"/ˈæŋ.ɡloʊ/","a":"EN-AU ck1 anglo.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An anglo is an English person or person of English ancestry.","e":"Back when we went to the World Cup in South Africa, we saw many anglos waving English flags."},{"m":"(countable) (informal) An anglo is an American, especially a white one (regardless of actual ethnicity), whose native language is English.","e":"I'm not an \"anglo\"; my grandparents are from."}]}]},"anglos":{"h":"anglos","l":"anglo","q":"noun"},"ancestry":{"h":"ancestry","i":"/ˈæn.sɛs.tri/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-ancestry.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Ancestry is a person's family or ethnic descent."},{"m":"Ancestry is the origin or background of something."}]}]},"ancestries":{"h":"ancestries","l":"ancestry","q":"noun"},"backfire":{"h":"backfire","i":"/bækˈfaɪə(r)/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-backfire.wav","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If an engine backfires, it experiences a premature ignition of fuel or exhaust gases, making a popping sound."},{"m":"If something backfires, it failed in a manner that brings an opposite and undesirable effect to what was intend.","e":"His attempt to make money by importing luxury cars backfired horribly when fuel prices tripled."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A backfire is a premature explosion in the cylinder of a gas or oil engine during the exhaust or the compression stroke, tending to drive the piston in the wrong direction."},{"m":"A backfire is an explosion in the exhaust passages of an."}]}]},"backfires":{"h":"backfires","l":"backfire","q":"verb"},"backfired":{"h":"backfired","l":"backfire","q":"verb"},"backfiring":{"h":"backfiring","l":"backfire","q":"verb"},"ignition":{"h":"ignition","i":"/ɪɡˈnɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-ignition.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Ignition is the act of something."},{"m":"Ignition is a system for combustion in a combustion engine."},{"m":"An ignition is a receptacle for a key used to start the engine in a vehicle."}]}]},"ignitions":{"h":"ignitions","l":"ignition","q":"noun"},"receptacle":{"h":"receptacle","i":"/rɪˈsɛp.tə.kl̩/","a":"en-au-receptacle.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A receptacle is a container."},{"m":"(countable) A receptacle is the part of the flower stalk to which the floral parts are attached.."},{"m":"(countable) A receptacle is an organ that receives and holds a secretion."},{"m":"(countable) (electricity) A receptacle is an electrical socket for the connection of a plug (typically by the plug's prongs) to supply portable appliances or equipment."}]}]},"receptacles":{"h":"receptacles","l":"receptacle","q":"noun"},"stalk":{"h":"stalk","i":"/stɔːk/","a":"en-us-ne-stalk.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The stalk of a plant is the stem or main axis of a plant, which supports the seed-carrying parts."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you stalk, you approach slowly and quietly in order not to be discovered when getting closer."},{"m":"(transitive) If you stalk someone, you try to follow or contact someone constantly, often resulting in harassment.","e":"My ex-girlfriend is stalking me."}]}]},"stalks":{"h":"stalks","l":"stalk","q":"noun"},"stalked":{"h":"stalked","l":"stalk","q":"verb"},"stalking":{"h":"stalking","l":"stalk","q":"verb"},"stork":{"h":"stork","i":"/stɔrk/","a":"en-us-stork.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A stork is a large bird with long legs and a long beak of the family."},{"m":"(folklore) A stork is a mythical bringer of babies to families, or good news."}]}]},"storks":{"h":"storks","l":"stork","q":"noun"},"folklore":{"h":"folklore","i":"/ˈfəʊk.lɔː/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-folklore.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Folklore is the tales, legends and superstitions of a particular ethnic population."}]}]},"folklores":{"h":"folklores","l":"folklore","q":"noun"},"superstition":{"h":"superstition","i":"/ˌs(j)uː.pə(r)ˈstɪ.ʃən/","a":"en-us-superstition.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Superstition is a person's belief(s) in something which is not based on human reason or scientific knowledge, that events may be influenced by one's behaviour in some magical or mystical way."}]}]},"superstitions":{"h":"superstitions","l":"superstition","q":"noun"},"superstitious":{"h":"superstitious","i":"/ˌs(j)uː.pəˈstɪ.ʃəs/","a":"en-us-superstitious.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A superstitious person has or shows a belief in superstitions."}]}]},"mystical":{"h":"mystical","i":"/ˈmɪstɪkəl/","a":"en-us-mystical.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is mystical, it inspires a sense of spiritual mystery, awe, and fascination."}]}]},"awe":{"h":"awe","i":"/ɔː/","a":"en-uk-awe.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Awe is a feeling of fear and reverence."},{"m":"Awe is a feeling of amazement."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If someone is awed, fear and reverence is inspired in them."}]}]},"awes":{"h":"awes","l":"awe","q":"verb"},"awed":{"h":"awed","l":"awe","q":"verb"},"awing":{"h":"awing","l":"awe","q":"verb"},"reverence":{"h":"reverence","i":"/ˈrɛv.ə.rəns/","a":"en-us-reverence.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Reverence is the deep respect for someone or something."},{"m":"Reverence is an act of showing respect, such as a bow."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If something is reverenced, it is treated with deep respect."}]}]},"reverences":{"h":"reverences","l":"reverence","q":"noun"},"reverenced":{"h":"reverenced","l":"reverence","q":"verb"},"reverencing":{"h":"reverencing","l":"reverence","q":"verb"},"secretion":{"h":"secretion","i":"/sɪˈkriːʃ(ə)n/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-secretion.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Secretion is any substance that is secreted by an organism"},{"m":"(uncountable) Secretion is the act of a substance, especially from a gland"}]}]},"secretions":{"h":"secretions","l":"secretion","q":"noun"},"pollinate":{"h":"pollinate","i":"/ˈpɒlɪneɪt/","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If a flower is pollinated, pollen is to the stigma."}]}]},"pollinates":{"h":"pollinates","l":"pollinate","q":"verb"},"pollinated":{"h":"pollinated","l":"pollinate","q":"verb"},"pollinating":{"h":"pollinating","l":"pollinate","q":"verb"},"erotic":{"h":"erotic","i":"/ɪˈrɑtɪk/","a":"en-us-erotic.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is erotic, it is related to or tends to arouse sexual desire or excitement.","e":"I had an erotic dream last night."}]}]},"outgoing":{"h":"outgoing","i":"/aʊtˈɡəʊɪŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-outgoing.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a person is outgoing, they are talkative, friendly, and social, especially when meeting new people easily and comfortably.","e":"Tom is very outgoing and enjoys meeting people; his brother, on the other hand, is painfully shy."},{"m":"Going out, on its way out.","e":"Is there any outgoing post?"}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Outgoing is the act of leaving or going out."}]}]},"outgoings":{"h":"outgoings","l":"outgoing","q":"noun"},"comfortably":{"h":"comfortably","i":"/ˈkʌmftɚbli/","a":"en-us-comfortably.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something is done comfortably, it is done in a comfortable manner without effort or difficulty.","e":"I snuggled comfortably into the blankets."}]}]},"bracelet":{"h":"bracelet","i":"/ˈbreɪslət/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-bracelet.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bracelet is a band or chain worn around the wrist as jewelry or an ornament."},{"m":"(countable) A bracelet is the strap of a wrist watch, used to secure it around the wrist."},{"m":"(countable) A handcuff."}]}]},"bracelets":{"h":"bracelets","l":"bracelet","q":"noun"},"bandwagon":{"h":"bandwagon","i":"/ˈbændˌwæɡ.ən/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bandwagon is a large wagon used to carry a band of musicians in a parade."},{"m":"A bandwagon is a current movement that attracts wide support."}]}]},"bandwagons":{"h":"bandwagons","l":"bandwagon","q":"noun"},"balloted":{"h":"balloted","l":"ballot","q":"verb"},"ba