 importance or value.","e":"These trivia take up too much of the day."},{"m":"(countable) A trivia is a quiz game that involves obscure facts.","e":"I joined the trivia club this semester!"}]}]},"trivias":{"h":"trivias","l":"trivia","q":"noun"},"bristle":{"h":"bristle","i":"/ˈbrɪs.l̩/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-bristle.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bristle is a stiff or coarse hair.","e":"the bristles of a pig"},{"m":"Bristles are the hair or straws that make up a brush, broom, or similar item."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something bristles, it rises or stand erect, like [[#Noun|bristles]].","e":"His hair did bristle upon his head."},{"m":"If someone bristles, they are on guard to react with fear, suspicion, or distance.","e":"The employees bristled at the prospect of working through the holidays."}]}]},"bristles":{"h":"bristles","l":"bristle","q":"noun"},"bristled":{"h":"bristled","l":"bristle","q":"verb"},"bristling":{"h":"bristling","l":"bristle","q":"verb"},"stumble":{"h":"stumble","i":"/ˈstʌmbəl/","a":"en-us-stumble.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A stumble is a fall or trip."},{"m":"(countable) A stumble is an error or blunder."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you stumble, you trip or fall.","e":"He stumbled up the dark avenue."},{"m":"(transitive) If you stumble, you make a mistake or have trouble.","e":"I always stumble over verbs in Spanish."}]}]},"stumbles":{"h":"stumbles","l":"stumble","q":"noun"},"stumbled":{"h":"stumbled","l":"stumble","q":"verb"},"stumbling":{"h":"stumbling","l":"stumble","q":"verb"},"jurisdiction":{"h":"jurisdiction","i":"/d͡ʒʊrɪsˈdɪkʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-jurisdiction.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Jurisdiction is the power or right to exercise authority."},{"m":"Jurisdiction is the authority of a sovereign power to govern or legislate."},{"m":"Jurisdiction is the limits or territory within which authority may be exercised."}]}]},"jurisdictions":{"h":"jurisdictions","l":"juri