h a scourge."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you scourge someone, you cause suffering to them."},{"m":"If you scourge something, you hit it with a [[#Noun|scourge]] (whip)."}]}]},"scourges":{"h":"scourges","l":"scourge","q":"noun"},"scourged":{"h":"scourged","l":"scourge","q":"verb"},"scourging":{"h":"scourging","l":"scourge","q":"verb"},"graffiti":{"h":"graffiti","i":"/ɡrəˈfiːti/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-graffiti.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Graffiti are drawings or words that are drawn illegally on something in a public place."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) IF you graffiti something, you mark it with a surface with such drawings."}]}]},"graffitis":{"h":"graffitis","l":"graffiti","q":"noun"},"graffitied":{"h":"graffitied","l":"graffiti","q":"verb"},"graffitiing":{"h":"graffitiing","l":"graffiti","q":"verb"},"scour":{"h":"scour","i":"/ˈskaʊə/","a":"en-us-scour.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you scour something, you clean or polish something by scrubbing it hard with an abrasive or cleaning agent.","e":"He scoured the burnt food from the pan."},{"m":"To (cause livestock to) suffer from diarrhoea.","e":"If a lamb is scouring, do not delay treatment."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Scour is the action of rubbing something hard to clean or brighten it.","e":"Give the pot a good scour."}]}]},"scours":{"h":"scours","l":"scour","q":"noun"},"scoured":{"h":"scoured","l":"scour","q":"verb"},"scouring":{"h":"scouring","l":"scour","q":"verb"},"kitchenware":{"h":"kitchenware","i":"/ˈkɪtʃɪnwɛː/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Kitchenware are utensils that are used in a kitchen.","e":"The new chef reorganized the area where we keep the pots, pans, and other kitchenware."}]}]},"ox":{"h":"ox","i":"/ˈɑks/","a":"en-ca-ox.oga","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An ox is an adult male of the cattle family whose sex organs have been removed.","e":"The stones had been carried up in wagons pulled by teams of oxen."}]}]},"mews":{"h"