,"e":"She has produced 10 new songs recorded with orchestral or big-band accompaniment."},{"m":"Accompaniment is something that is together with something else.","e":"The prime minister has taken this trip without the usual accompaniment of the press."}]}]},"accompaniments":{"h":"accompaniments","l":"accompaniment","q":"noun"},"academics":{"h":"academics","i":"/ˌækəˈdɛmɪks/","l":"academic","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Academics is the part of school related to learning.","e":"This class was strong in every aspect of their schooling, including academics, athletics and extracurricular activities."}]}]},"academically":{"h":"academically","i":"/ˌæk.əˈdɛm.ɪk.ə.li/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-academically.wav","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If you are academically gifted, talented, or successfully, you are very good at school subjects and learning."},{"m":"If you write or speak academically, you do so in a way that many people find boring or hard to understand because it uses a lot of difficult vocabulary or complicated ideas."}]}]},"coerce":{"h":"coerce","i":"/koʊˈɝs/","a":"en-us-coerce.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you coerces someone into doing something, you use power to make them do it, though they may not want to.","e":"She was coerced into giving the bully her lunch money."}]}]},"coerces":{"h":"coerces","l":"coerce","q":"verb"},"coerced":{"h":"coerced","l":"coerce","q":"verb"},"coercing":{"h":"coercing","l":"coerce","q":"verb"},"disinherit":{"h":"disinherit","i":"/ˌdɪsɪnˈhɛrɪt/","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you disinherit your family member or someone else, you prevent them from inheriting your property, usually because you feel that they've done something wrong.","e":"The Duke is seeking to disinherit his eldest son over the incident."}]}]},"disinherits":{"h":"disinherits","l":"disinherit","q":"verb"},"disinherited":{"h":"disinherited","l":"disinherit","q":"verb"},"disinheriting":{"h":"disinheriting","l":"disinherit","q":"verb"},"clarification":{"h":"clarification","i":"/ˌklærɪfɪˈkeɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-clarification.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) If you ask someone for a clarification, you are asking them to make a statement or situation less."}]}]},"clarifications":{"h":"clarifications","l":"clarification","q":"noun"},"clairvoyant":{"h":"clairvoyant","i":"/ˌklɛəˈvɔɪ.ənt/","a":"en-us-clairvoyant.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If you are clairvoyant, you are able to see things that cannot be perceived by the normal senses or able to foresee the future."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A clairvoyant is a person who is able to see things that cannot be perceived by the normal senses or able to foresee the future."}]}]},"clairvoyants":{"h":"clairvoyants","l":"clairvoyant","q":"noun"},"clairvoyance":{"h":"clairvoyance","i":"/klɛrˈvɔɪəns/","a":"en-ca-clairvoyance.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Clairvoyance is the power to see the future."}]}]},"fructose":{"h":"fructose","i":"/ˈfrʌk.təʊz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-fructose.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Fructose is a type of monosaccharide (sugar), formula C6H12O6."}]}]},"galactose":{"h":"galactose","i":"/ɡəˈlaktəʊz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-galactose.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Galactose is a type of monosaccharide (sugar) found in dairy products, formula C6H12O6."}]}]},"monosaccharide":{"h":"monosaccharide","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (biochemistry) A monosaccharide is a simple sugar, such as glucose, fructose or galactose, that cannot be broken up into a simpler form."}]}]},"monosaccharides":{"h":"monosaccharides","l":"monosaccharide","q":"noun"},"disaccharide":{"h":"disaccharide","i":"/daɪˈsækəraɪd/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (biochemistry) A disaccharide is a sugar, such as sucrose, maltose and lactose, that is made of two monosaccharides."}]}]},"disaccharides":{"h":"disaccharides","l":"disaccharide","q":"noun"},"inquest":{"h":"inquest","i":"/ˈɪŋkw