r a newspaper or any other broadcasting organization."}]}]},"correspondents":{"h":"correspondents","l":"correspondent","q":"noun"},"limitation":{"h":"limitation","i":"/lɪmɪˈteɪʃən/","a":"en-us-limitation.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A limitation is a restriction that is caused by something or by a certain circumstance.","e":"Getting into his wheelchair after his amputation, it felt like a limitation you could roll in."},{"m":"A limitation is a time period after which some legal action may no longer be continued."}]}]},"limitations":{"h":"limitations","l":"limitation","q":"noun"},"helm":{"h":"helm","i":"/hɛlm/","a":"en-us-helm.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A helm is a steering wheel of a ship."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you helm a boat, you are in charge of steering it."},{"m":"If you helm an organization, you lead them in doing something."}]}]},"helms":{"h":"helms","l":"helm","q":"noun"},"helmed":{"h":"helmed","l":"helm","q":"verb"},"helming":{"h":"helming","l":"helm","q":"verb"},"censor":{"h":"censor","i":"/ˈsɛnsə/","a":"en-us-censor.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (Ancient Rome) A censor is one of the two magistrates first did a census of citizens."},{"m":"(countable) A censor is an official person who hides offensive information from the public."},{"m":"(countable) A censor is a college or university official whose job may be different things."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you censor something, you review or remove information from others, especially offensive or private information. Often refers to types of media, such as books, movies, and television."}]}]},"phonetic":{"h":"phonetic","i":"/fəˈnɛtɪk/","a":"en-us-phonetic.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A phonetic alphabet, system, difference, etc. relates to the basic language sounds (or movements, in the case of sign language).","e":"If you're learning a number of languages, it's useful to learn the International Phonetic Alphabet (IPA)."}]}]},"censors":{"h":"censors","l