{"m":"Organizational is relating to the action of something.","e":"Our leader has different kinds of organizational skills for developing a project."}]}]},"renewal":{"h":"renewal","i":"/rɪˈnjuːəl/","a":"en-us-renewal.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Renewal is the process or situation of starting again after a pause.","e":"They fear the renewal of fighting if an agreement is not reached soon."},{"m":"The renewal of a contract, license, or other document is the act of making it valid for a longer time.","e":"The renewal of his vehicle insurance is good for five more years."}]}]},"announcers":{"h":"announcers","l":"announcer","q":"noun"},"organisational":{"h":"organisational","i":"/ˌɔːɡənʌɪˈzeɪʃən(ə)l/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Organisational structure, culture, change, etc. are those things as they relate to an organisation.","e":"In the new organisational structure, my department is under a new director."},{"m":"Organisational skills, efforts, etc. are those things as they relate to organising.","e":"I need to improve my organisational skills to get things done on time."}]}]},"renewals":{"h":"renewals","l":"renewal","q":"noun"},"namely":{"h":"namely","i":"/ˈneɪmli/","a":"en-us-namely.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"You use namely to specifically name who or what you are talking about.","e":"Some of the students — namely Paul, Alice and Jake — seem to have problems with their projects."}]}]},"lawless":{"h":"lawless","i":"/ˈlɔːləs/","a":"en-us-lawless.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A lawless place is not well controlled by laws and rules.","e":"Orin's area is a lawless region where peace never really took hold."},{"m":"A lawless action is one that is illegal.","e":"Thomas's drugs business was completely lawless, for which he was penalized."}]}]},"bulgaria":{"h":"Bulgaria","i":"/bʌlˈɡɛə.ri.ə/","a":"en-uk-Bulgaria.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Bulgaria is a country in southeast Europe."}]}]},"emu":{"h":"emu","i":"/ˈiːmjuː/","a":"en-au-emu.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An emu is a flightless bird that is native to Australia."}]}]},"adaptor":{"h":"adaptor","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An adaptor is an adapter."}]}]},"adapter":{"h":"adapter","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An adapter is a device that allows two different standards to work together.","e":"This monitor won't work for you computer without an adapter."},{"m":"(countable) An adapter is a person who changes or changes something to suit a new situation.","e":"In creating her movies, she is an able adapter of novels and short stories."}]}]},"emus":{"h":"emus","l":"emu","q":"noun"},"midday":{"h":"midday","i":"/mɪdˈdeɪ/","a":"en-us-midday.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"12:00 pm; the middle of the daylight; the middle of the calendar day."}]}]},"middays":{"h":"middays","l":"midday","q":"noun"},"rector":{"h":"rector","i":"/ˈrɛktɚ/","a":"en-us-rector.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A rector is a clerk who is in charge of a church or parish.","e":"By then the church had replaced him with the first of several rectors."},{"m":"(countable) A rector is a headmaster in educational institutions, e.g. a university.","e":"One of my friends has been a rector at various universities in the United States."}]}]},"rectors":{"h":"rectors","l":"plural","q":"noun"},"amplification":{"h":"amplification","i":"/ˌæmplɪfɪˈkeɪʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-amplification.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Amplification is the process or result of increasing a signal, such as a sound wave, light, etc.","e":"Most of the music classrooms have some type of sound amplification system."}]}]},"atelier":{"h":"atelier","i":"/əˈtɛl.jeɪ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-atelier.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An atelier is the name for a workshop of an artist."}]}]},"sleepy":{"h":"sleepy","i":"/ˈsliːpi/","a":"en-us-sleepy.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is sleepy, that person feels like they need to sleep; they are tired.","e":"My son woke me up at four in the morning, and I had to work until eight at night! Now I'm very sleepy."},{"m":"If a place is sleepy, it is quiet; there is not a lot happening there.","e":"After I moved to the big city, I missed my sleepy hometown."}]}]},"sleepier":{"h":"sleepier","l":"sleepy","q":"adjective"},"sleepiest":{"h":"sleepiest","l":"sleepy","q":"adjective"},"wryer":{"h":"wryer","l":"wry","q":"adjective"},"wryest":{"h":"wryest","l":"wry","q":"adjective"},"amplifications":{"h":"amplifications","l":"amplification","q":"noun"},"wrier":{"h":"wrier","l":"wry","q":"adjective"},"wriest":{"h":"wriest","l":"wry","q":"adjective"},"cordage":{"h":"cordage","i":"/ˈkɔːdɪdʒ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-cordage.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Cordage is a set of ropes and cords, especially when used for a ship's rigging.","e":"The cordage of the ship stretched during the storm."},{"m":"Cordage is the amount of wood measured in cords."}]}]},"cordages":{"h":"cordages","l":"cordage","q":"noun"},"herder":{"h":"herder","i":"/ˈhɜːdə/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A herder is someone who herds animals.","e":"The herder brought the sheep to the barn."}]}]},"godmother":{"h":"godmother","i":"/ˈɡɒdmʌðə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-godmother.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A godmother is a woman present at the baptism of a child."}]}]},"digger":{"h":"digger","i":"/ˈdɪɡɚ/","a":"EN-AU ck1 digger.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A digger a person or animal that digs.","e":"The man was a digger."}]}]},"drover":{"h":"drover","i":"/drəʊ.və/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A drover is a person who herds cattle or sheep"}]}]},"jiggly":{"h":"jiggly","i":"/ˈd͡ʒɪɡ.əˌli/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is jiggly, it jiggles."}]}]},"dolt":{"h":"dolt","i":"/dɒlt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-dolt.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A dolt is a dumb person."}]}]},"hooky":{"h":"hooky","i":"/ˈhʊk