danese is the co-official language of Indonesia in West Java province."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A Sundanese is a person from the Indonesian island of Java."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is related to the cultural land of Sundanese in western Java."},{"m":"Something that is related to the Sundanese people."},{"m":"Something that is related to the Sundanese language."}]}]},"betawi":{"h":"Betawi","i":"/bətʌwɪ/","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Betawi is an indigenous language of the Indonesian island of Java.","e":"Betawi is the co-official language of Indonesia in Jakarta province."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A Betawi is a person from the Indonesian island of Java."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is related to the cultural land of Betawi in northwestern Java."},{"m":"Something that is related to the Betawi people."},{"m":"Something that is related to the Betawi language."}]}]},"osing":{"h":"Osing","i":"/ɔsɪŋ/","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"Osing is an indigenous language of the Indonesian island of Java.","e":"Osing is the co-official language of Indonesia in Banyuwangi."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An Osing is a person from the Indonesian island of Java."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is related to the cultural land of Osing in easternmost Java."},{"m":"Something that is related to the Osing people."},{"m":"Something that is related to the Osing language."}]}]},"osings":{"h":"Osings","l":"osing","q":"noun"},"northeastern":{"h":"northeastern","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A northeastern state, corner, city, etc. is in the northeast.","e":"Maine is in the northeastern United States."}]}]},"uncharacteristic":{"h":"uncharacteristic","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Not characteristic.","e":"That was uncharacteristic of him."}]}]},"emaciate":{"h":"emaciate","i":"/ɪˈmeɪsɪeɪt/","a":"en-us-emaciate.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you emaciate a person, you make them extremely thin."}]}]},"emaciating":{"h":"emaciating","l":"emaciate","q":"verb"},"emaciates":{"h":"emaciates","l":"emaciate","q":"verb"},"emaciated":{"h":"emaciated","l":"emaciate","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"An emaciated person is someone who is extremely thin and weak, specially if it is because of hunger or illness."}]}]},"incest":{"h":"incest","i":"/ˈɪnsɛst/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-incest.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Incest is the act of having sex with a close relative, like your sibling or your parent. Sex with your first cousin is also usually considered incest. Incest is taboo and illegal in most places."}]}]},"mailman":{"h":"mailman","i":"/ˈmeɪl.mən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Sapaa-mailman.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mailman is someone who delivers mail. Mailman usually refers to a man, but it can also be a gender-neutral term."}]}]},"gender-neutral":{"h":"gender-neutral","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is gender-neutral applies to men, women, and people with other.","e":"is a gender-neutral word for chairman and chairwoman."}]}]},"divisor":{"h":"divisor","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The divisor is the number that another number is divided by.","e":"In the equation \"48 ÷ 6 = 8\", the divisor is 6."},{"m":"The divisors of a number are all the numbers which evenly divide into it.","e":"The divisors of 12 are 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, and 12."}]}]},"wasteful":{"h":"wasteful","i":"/ˈweɪstfəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-wasteful.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is wasteful is something that is a waste of good resources, time, or.","e":"Throwing away fresh food is wasteful."}]}]},"spotter":{"h":"spotter","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A spotter is someone who observes something."},{"m":"(weightlifting, gymnastics, climbing) A spotter is someone who watches another person who is performing an activity, for the purpose of being there to help them if they can't complete the activity."}]}]},"allegory":{"h":"allegory","i":"/ˈæl.ɪˌɡɔː.ri/","a":"en-us-allegory.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An allegory is a fictional story that is meant to metaphorically represent things, people, or events in the real world.","e":"is a famous allegory for totalitarianism."}]}]},"questionably":{"h":"questionably","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"The word questionably describes something that is questionable (dubious).","e":"The fool was questionably dressed."},{"m":"If something is said questionably it is said in a questioning manner."}]}]},"coverage":{"h":"coverage","i":"/ˈkʌv.ər.ɪdʒ/","a":"en-us-nn-coverage.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Coverage is the amount something or someone is covered."},{"m":"Coverage is the amount of space or time given to an event in newspapers or television."},{"m":"Coverage is the area a mobile phone (cellphone) network or radio network provides to."}]}]},"profound":{"h":"profound","i":"/prəˈfaʊnd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Naomi Persephone Amethyst (NaomiAmethyst)-profound.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is profound is deep, having great depths, reaching far below the surface.","e":"The explorers became trapped in a profound cave."},{"m":"Something that is profound is deep in an intellectual sense. It means something that reaches figuratively deep into a subject, or has great depth of meaning."}]}]},"inconceivable":{"h":"inconceivable","i":"/ɪn.kənˈsiː.və.bl̩/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-inconceivable.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is inconceivable is unable to be believed."},{"m":"Something that is inconceivable is something that is impossible to imagine or think about.","e":"You can't imagine a color you've never seen before, that's inconceivable!"}]}]},"preposterous":{"h":"preposterous","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is preposterous is ridiculous or unbelievable."}]}]},"adaptability":{"h":"adaptability","i":"/ədæptəˈbɪlɪti/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-adaptability.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Adaptability is the ability to change yourself and your behaviors to match changes in your life and your environment.","e":"Thanks to evolution, animals have high adaptability."}]}]},"incestuous":{"h":"incestuous","i":"/ɪnˈsɛstjuəs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-incestuous.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"An act that is incestuous is an act of incest. A person who is incestuous is someone who participates in incest.","e":"Having sex with your sister is incestuous."}]}]},"incessantly":{"h":"incessantly","i":"/ɪnˈsɛs.ənt.li/","a":"en-us-incessantly.ogg","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"To do something incessantly is to do something without pause, especially when it annoys other people."}]}]},"skinship":{"h":"skinship","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Skinship is the act of two or more people spending time together while naked in order to strengthen a social bond."}]}]},"taqueria":{"h":"taqueria","i":"/ˌtɑkəˈriːə/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-taqueria.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A taqueria is a restaurant that sells tacos."}]}]},"taquerias":{"h":"taquerias","l":"taqueria","q":"noun"},"notification":{"h":"notification","i":"/ˌnəʊtɪfɪˈkeɪʃən/","a":"en-us-notification.oga","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A notification is a message that you of something."}]}]},"notifications":{"h":"notifications","l":"notification","q":"noun"},"hoe":{"h":"hoe","i":"/həʊ/","a":"en-au-hoe.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hoe is a agricultural tool used to level ground and break roots."},{"m":"(countable) A hoe is an insulting term that describes a sexually promiscuous woman."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To hoe is to use a hoe, especially when using it to dig or to level ground."},{"m":"To hoe is to act sexually promiscuous, or in other words, to act like a whore."}]}]},"hoes":{"h":"hoes","l":"hoe","q":"noun"},"hoed":{"h":"hoed","l":"hoe","q":"verb"},"hoeing":{"h":"hoeing","l":"hoe","q":"verb"},"sine":{"h":"sine","i":"/saɪn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-sine.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) The sine is the ratio of the side opposite an angle to the length of the hypotenuse."}]}]},"spherical":{"h":"spherical","i":"/sfɛrɪkəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-spherical.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is spherical is shaped like a sphere.","e":"A basketball is spherical."}]}]},"oddly":{"h":"oddly","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"To do something oddly is to do it in an odd manner."}]}]},"godless":{"h":"godless","i":"/ˈɡɒdləs/","a":"en-au-godless.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something or someone who doesn't have a god."}]}]},"encouragement":{"h":"encouragement","i":"[ɪnˈkʌrɪd͡ʒmənt]","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-encouragement.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"You give encouragement to someone to help motivate them or make them feel better about something.","e":"\"I wasn't feeling brave enough to run a marathon, but my mother gave me some encouragement.\""}]}]},"droplet":{"h":"droplet","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A droplet is a small glob of a liquid.","e":"On a rainy day, my window is covered in water droplets."}]}]},"droplets":{"h":"droplets","l":"droplet","q":"noun"},"sentry":{"h":"sentry","i":"/ˈsɛntri/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-sentry.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sentry is a guard, usually one who is stationed at the entrance of a place, especially a military base."}]}]},"sentries":{"h":"sentries","l":"sentry","q":"noun"},"hive":{"h":"hive","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A hive is a home for honeybees. Honeybees make their own hives, but humans who farm honey usually make artificial hives for bees."},{"m":"(countable) The group of all honeybees in a hive are also collectively called a hive."},{"m":"(countable) A very busy place crowded with people is sometimes called a hive."}]}]},"hives":{"h":"hives","l":"hive","q":"noun","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Hives are itchy, red areas on your skin. People usually get hives from an allergic reaction."}]}]},"subclass":{"h":"subclass","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A subclass is a group of things which are all also in a larger group.","e":"Volcanoes are a subclass of mountains."}]}]},"subclasses":{"h":"subclasses","l":"subclass","q":"noun"},"handful":{"h":"handful","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A handful of something is the amount of it you can hold in the palm of one hand."},{"m":"If a person or a group of people are called a handful, it means they're demanding and difficult to watch over.","e":"\"Those rowdy kids are a handful!\""}]}]},"slur":{"h":"slur","i":"/slɜː(r)/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-slur.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A slur is an offensive and bigoted word used to describe a specific group of people as a way of insulting them.","e":"is a slur used to describe mentally disabled people."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you slur your speech, it means the way you pronounce words is difficult for other people to understand."}]}]},"slurs":{"h":"slurs","l":"slur","q":"noun"},"slurred":{"h":"slurred","l":"slur","q":"verb"},"slurring":{"h":"slurring","l":"slur","q":"verb"},"bigoted":{"h":"bigoted","i":"/ˈbɪɡətɪd/","a":"en-us-bigoted.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A bigoted person is a bigot.","e":"Racists, sexists and homophobes are all bigoted."},{"m":"A bigoted statement or opinion is one that bigots are likely to say or agree with."}]}]},"bigot":{"h":"bigot","i":"/ˈbɪɡət/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-bigot.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bigot is someone who has bad and unfair opinions about large groups of people, especially groups of people defined by something inherent to them, like race, gender, or sexuality."}]}]},"giver":{"h":"giver","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A giver is someone who gives something to another person or people.","e":"Santa Claus is a giver of gifts."}]}]},"givers":{"h":"givers","l":"giver","q":"noun"},"sedentary":{"h":"sedentary","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Being sedentary means not moving very often, staying still most of the time."}]}]},"marimba":{"h":"marimba","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A marimba is a musical instrument made of wooden bars that are struck with mallets to produce sound. It is similar to a xylophone, but a marimba is bigger."}]}]},"croissant":{"h":"croissant","i":"/ˈk(r)wæsɒ̃/","a":"Croissant (UK).wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A croissant is a buttery pastry sold at bakeries and cafés."}]}]},"croissants":{"h":"croissants","l":"croissant","q":"noun"},"labyrinth":{"h":"labyrinth","i":"/ˈlæb.ə.rɪnθ/","a":"en-us-labyrinth.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A labyrinth is a maze, a structure made of a complicated network of paths."},{"m":"A place that is very difficult to navigate is sometimes called a labyrinth."}]}]},"footstep":{"h":"footstep","i":"/ˈfʊtstɛp/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-footstep.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A footstep is the act of taking a single step while walking.","e":"Footsteps in snow make footprints."}]}]},"footsteps":{"h":"footsteps","l":"footstep","q":"noun"},"sucker":{"h":"sucker","i":"/ˈsʌk.ə/","a":"en-au-sucker.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A sucker is something that sucks, in the sense that it sucks fluid from something.","e":"s are blood-suckers."},{"m":"(countable) A sucker is someone who is easy to trick or deceive. They are gullible."},{"m":"(countable) (regional) A sucker is another word for a lollipop. It can also mean any candy that you suck on."},{"m":"(countable) If someone is a sucker for something or someone, they are very attracted to it.","e":"I'm always a sucker for horror stories."}]}]},"suckers":{"h":"suckers","l":"sucker","q":"noun"},"oneself":{"h":"oneself","i":"/wʌnˈsɛlf/","a":"en-us-oneself.ogg","s":[{"p":"pronoun","d":[{"m":"Oneself is a word that stands in for words like \"myself\", \"himself\", and \"herself\". It is meant to refer to people in general, nobody in particular.","e":"It's a good idea to check oneself in the mirror before going outside."}]}]},"adventurer":{"h":"adventurer","i":"/ædˈvɛn.t͡ʃɚ.ɚ/","a":"en-us-adventurer.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An adventurer is someone who goes on an adventure, especially someone who frequently goes on adventures."}]}]},"adventurers":{"h":"adventurers","l":"adventurer","q":"noun"},"hourglass":{"h":"hourglass","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An hourglass is a glass device used as a timer. It contains sand which slowly falls down from a top section into a bottom section."},{"m":"Someone with an hourglass figure has a slim waist, wide hips, and a broad chest (large breasts). This word is almost always applied to women."}]}]},"hourglasses":{"h":"hourglasses","l":"hourglass","q":"noun"},"cubical":{"h":"cubical","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something cubical is shaped like a cube.","e":"The is named after its cubical shape."}]}]},"cubicle":{"h":"cubicle","i":"/ˈkjubɪkəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-cubicle.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A cubicle is a sectioned-off part of a room, especially in a workplace."}]}]},"workplace":{"h":"workplace","i":"/ˈwəːkpleɪs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-workplace.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A workplace is any place where people work."}]}]},"workplaces":{"h":"workplaces","l":"workplace","q":"noun"},"middle-aged":{"h":"middle-aged","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is middle-aged, they are around 50 years old.","e":"My father is middle-aged."}]}]},"huger":{"h":"huger","l":"huge","q":"adjective"},"hugest":{"h":"hugest","l":"huge","q":"adjective"},"mailmen":{"h":"mailmen","l":"mailman","q":"noun"},"reconsideration":{"h":"reconsideration","i":"/ˌriːkənˌsɪdəˈreɪʃ(ə)n/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) Reconsideration is when you consider something again."}]}]},"half-sister":{"h":"half-sister","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A half-sister is a female half-sibling."}]}]},"half-brother":{"h":"half-brother","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A half-brother is a male half-sibling."}]}]},"half-sibling":{"h":"half-sibling","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A half-sibling is a sibling you share only one parent with."}]}]},"nationally":{"h":"nationally","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something is done nationally it applies to the whole nation.","e":"The speech was broadcasted nationally."}]}]},"wordy":{"h":"wordy","i":"/ˈwɝdi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-wordy.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is wordy it has a lot of words, probably too many words."}]}]},"upside":{"h":"upside","i":"/ˈʌpˌsaɪd/","a":"en-us-upside.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An upside is a good aspect of a situation that is otherwise bad."}]}]},"upsides":{"h":"upsides","l":"upside","q":"noun"},"doubtful":{"h":"doubtful","i":"/ˈdaʊtfəl/","a":"en-us-doubtful.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is doubtful it is probably not true.","e":"The fool made many doubtful claims."},{"m":"If someone is doubtful they are doubting something or someone.","e":"The teacher was doubtful of his bad students."}]}]},"technically":{"h":"technically","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Based on exact facts which go against common knowledge or intuition but are still true.","e":"He was technically an American, even though everyone thought he was Canadian."},{"m":"Based on a technicality; true only under a very specific set of rules.","e":"It was 7PM, but it was before sunset, so technically it wasn't nighttime."},{"m":"Having (or using) skills or talent.","e":"She was technically gifted at playing the piano; she was very good at it."},{"m":"Relating to technology.","e":"It is technically impossible for humans to go to Mars; we don't have the technology to do it."}]}]},"technicality":{"h":"technicality","i":"/ˌtɛknɪˈkælɪti/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-technicality.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A technicality is a minor rule, law, or other detail which is usually unimportant but can sometimes have big consequences.","e":"She was fired on a technicality."}]}]},"technicalities":{"h":"technicalities","l":"technicality","q":"noun"},"imperfect":{"h":"imperfect","i":"/ɪmˈpɜː(r)fɪkt/","a":"en-us-imperfect.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is imperfect has flaws; it is not perfect."}]}]},"overvalued":{"h":"overvalued","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is overvalued is valued too much, too highly.","e":"The painting was overvalued; it sold for $100 but was only worth $20."}]}]},"overdressed":{"h":"overdressed","l":"overdress","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Someone who is overdressed is dressed in clothes that are too fancy."},{"m":"Someone who is overdressed is wearing more pieces of clothing than they should be."}]}]},"overstatement":{"h":"overstatement","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An overstatement is a description that makes something out to be more than it actually is; an exaggeration."}]}]},"overstatements":{"h":"overstatements","l":"overstatement","q":"noun"},"undersized":{"h":"undersized","i":"/ʌndəˈsʌɪzd/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is undersized is too small."}]}]},"undervalued":{"h":"undervalued","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is undervalued is valued too little."}]}]},"drifter":{"h":"drifter","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A drifter is someone who travels from place to place without staying anywhere for very long."}]}]},"drifters":{"h":"drifters","l":"drifter","q":"noun"},"unexposed":{"h":"unexposed","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is unexposed is covered; it is not exposed."},{"m":"If you're unexposed to something, you haven't seen or dealt with it before."}]}]},"equivalence":{"h":"equivalence","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"If there is equivalence between things, they are equal."}]}]},"equivalences":{"h":"equivalences","l":"equivalence","q":"noun"},"featherless":{"h":"featherless","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is featherless doesn't have any feathers."}]}]},"frostily":{"h":"frostily","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Something that is done frostily is done coldly; it is done in a frosty manner."}]}]},"grossly":{"h":"grossly","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Something that is done grossly is done in a gross way."}]}]},"humourous":{"h":"humourous","i":"/ˈhjuːmərəs/","a":"en-uk-humorous.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a person is humourous, they cause laughter and amusement for others.","e":"The waiters were so humourous, one even did a back flip for us, when we asked him."}]}]},"mender":{"h":"mender","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A mender is someone or something that mends (repairs)."},{"m":"A doctor is sometimes called a mender, because they mend people."}]}]},"informational":{"h":"informational","i":"/ˌɪnfə(r)ˈmeɪʃənəl/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is informational is educational, it provides information."}]}]},"fairness":{"h":"fairness","i":"/ˈfɛər.nəs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-fairness.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Fairness is the act of treating people or things fairly."},{"m":"A woman's beauty is her fairness."}]}]},"uneaten":{"h":"uneaten","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is uneaten has not been eaten; something can be completely uneaten or it can be partially uneaten."}]}]},"airhead":{"h":"airhead","i":"/ˈɛːhɛd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-airhead.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An airhead is a stupid person."}]}]},"airheads":{"h":"airheads","l":"airhead","q":"noun"},"nads":{"h":"nads","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Someone's nads are their testicles."},{"m":"If you have the nads to do something, you have the courage to do it."}]}]},"insurmountable":{"h":"insurmountable","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"An obstacle that is insurmountable is impossible or very difficult to overcome.","e":"This mountain is an insurmountable obstacle in our path."}]}]},"surmountable":{"h":"surmountable","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"An obstacle that is surmountable is able to be overcome; it can be moved past or gotten over."}]}]},"girly":{"h":"girly","i":"/ˈɡɝli/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-girly.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is girly is for girls, or like a girl.","e":"\"That flowery shirt is so girly!\""}]}]},"manly":{"h":"manly","i":"/ˈmænli/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-manly.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is manly is for men, or like a man.","e":"\"That truck is so manly!\""}]}]},"practicable":{"h":"practicable","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Able to be practiced."},{"m":"Able to be put into practice. In other words, it can be done."}]}]},"default":{"h":"default","i":"/dɪˈfɔːlt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-default1.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"The default option or setting is the one that is there without any input. It is what you are given if you do not ask for anything specific."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A default is one such option or setting."},{"m":"If someone loses a competition because they were unable to compete, they lose by default."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"To default is to take on a default value."}]}]},"electoral":{"h":"electoral","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is electoral has to do with elections or electing."}]}]},"menders":{"h":"menders","l":"mender","q":"noun"},"deceitful":{"h":"deceitful","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A deceitful person is someone who does not tell the truth."}]}]},"rouge":{"h":"rouge","i":"/ruːʒ/","a":"en-us-rouge.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Red makeup put onto the cheeks of the face is called rouge."}]}]},"stupidly":{"h":"stupidly","i":"/ˈstjuːpɪdli/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Wodencafe-stupidly.wav","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Something done in a stupid (dumb, unintelligent) way."},{"m":"Something that shouldn't have been done; it was a stupid decision to do it at all."}]}]},"unsaid":{"h":"unsaid","l":"unsay","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that was unsaid wasn't said; it wasn't spoken, but it might have been written down or thought of."}]}]},"unsaved":{"h":"unsaved","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that was left unsaved was not saved."}]}]},"unshared":{"h":"unshared","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something unshared hasn't been shared."}]}]},"sickly":{"h":"sickly","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A sickly person is someone who is sick, especially someone who is sick very frequently.","e":"He was a sickly child."},{"m":"Something that appears sickly appears diseased and unhealthy."},{"m":"Something that gives off a sickly light doesn't give off very much light; it is dim but not completely dark."},{"m":"A sickly action or activity is one that lacks intensity and vigor; it is done weakly.","e":"He flashed me a sickly smile."},{"m":"Something that is sickly is associated with poor moral or mental well-being."},{"m":"Something that is sickly is disgusting, especially something that makes you nauseous.","e":"The house was filled with a sickly smell; it smelled like a rotting corpse."},{"m":"Something sickly sweet is too sweet; it is overly sweet."}]},{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Something done sickly is done in a sick way.","e":"She sickly coughed into her arm."}]}]},"substandard":{"h":"substandard","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is substandard is below standards; it is not good enough."}]}]},"xxx":{"h":"XXX","s":[{"p":"numeral","d":[{"m":"The number thirty (30) in Roman numerals."}]}]},"scarlet":{"h":"scarlet","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) A bright red color with an orange hue."},{"m":"Cloth of a scarlet color.","e":"Her household is clothed with scarlet."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something with such a color.","e":"She had scarlet hair; her hair was bright red."},{"m":"A person who is scarlet is sinful or whorish.","e":"a scarlet woman"},{"m":"(Ireland) A scarlet person is blushing, embarrassed, or mortified."}]}]},"territorial":{"h":"territorial","i":"/ˌtɛr.ɪˈtɔː.ri.əl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-territorial.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A territorial person or animal is one that is very protective of its territory.","e":"Wolves are territorial animals."},{"m":"Relating to territory."}]}]},"rizz":{"h":"rizz","i":"/ˈrɪz/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-rizz.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The ability to attract a love interest."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you rizz someone, you attempt to seduce them."}]}]},"rizzes":{"h":"rizzes","l":"rizz","q":"verb"},"rizzed":{"h":"rizzed","l":"rizz","q":"verb"},"rizzing":{"h":"rizzing","l":"rizz","q":"verb"},"fungus":{"h":"fungus","i":"/ˈfʌŋ.ɡəs/","a":"en-us-fungus.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) (mycology) A fungus is a member of the Fungi kingdom of organisms. Fungi are plant-like organisms that lack chlorophyll. Common examples of fungi include mushrooms and mold."}]}]},"fungi":{"h":"fungi","i":"/ˈfʌnd͡ʒaɪ/","a":"en-us-fungi.ogg","l":"fungus","q":"noun"},"funguses":{"h":"funguses","l":"fungus","q":"noun"},"bullish":{"h":"bullish","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A bullish person is muscular and strong; they are \"built like a bull\"."},{"m":"A bullish person is aggressive and overly confident."}]}]},"cryptography":{"h":"cryptography","i":"[kr̥ɪpˈtʰɒɡrəfiː]","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-cryptography.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Cryptography is the field of study related to communication security. It is about making sure messages are sent securely without being read by anyone other than who is supposed to read it, and making sure the message doesn't get changed as it is sent, as well as solving other related problems."}]}]},"breastfeeding":{"h":"breastfeeding","i":"/ˈbrɛstˌfidɪŋ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Flame, not lame-breastfeeding.wav","l":"breastfeed","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Breastfeeding is the act of feeding a baby milk from the breasts."}]}]},"breastfed":{"h":"breastfed","l":"breastfeed","q":"verb"},"breastfeeds":{"h":"breastfeeds","l":"breastfeed","q":"verb"},"ghastly":{"h":"ghastly","i":"/ˈɡɑːs(t).li/","a":"en-us-ghastly.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is ghastly is gross and scary."}]}]},"buggies":{"h":"buggies","l":"buggy","q":"noun"},"censorships":{"h":"censorships","l":"censorship","q":"noun"},"clockwise":{"h":"clockwise","i":"/ˈklɒkwaɪz/","a":"en-us-clockwise.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Clockwise is the direction that the hands of a clock turn in."}]}]},"openness":{"h":"openness","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The state of being open, literally or figuratively."}]}]},"unsay":{"h":"unsay","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(almost always in the subjunctive) To unsay something is to make it so that it was never said. This isn't possible in real life, so when this word is used, it's usually someone wishing they could do it.","e":"I wish I could unsay the insults I said to you last night."}]}]},"unsays":{"h":"unsays","l":"unsay","q":"verb"},"unsaying":{"h":"unsaying","l":"unsay","q":"verb"},"perseverance":{"h":"perseverance","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Perseverance is the ability to continue and not give up at something, even when it is difficult, or people tell you that you can't do it, or you have failed at it before."}]}]},"booger":{"h":"booger","i":"/ˈbʊɡɚ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-booger.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(childish) Snot; both dried flakes of snot and liquid globs."}]}]},"boogers":{"h":"boogers","l":"booger","q":"noun"},"matricide":{"h":"matricide","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Matricide is the act of killing one's own mother."}]}]},"patricide":{"h":"patricide","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Patricide is the act of killing one's own father."}]}]},"distressingly":{"h":"distressingly","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Done in a way that causes discomfort and unease; it causes distress."}]}]},"watchlist":{"h":"watchlist","i":"/ˈwɔt͡ʃˌlɪst/","a":"en-us-watchlist.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A watchlist is a list of things being watched; things on a watchlist are given extra attention and monitoring."}]}]},"watchlists":{"h":"watchlists","l":"watchlist","q":"noun"},"amicably":{"h":"amicably","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"In an amicable (friendly, kind) manner.","e":"He smiled at me amicably."}]}]},"ultraviolet":{"h":"ultraviolet","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"(science) waves (light) that are ultraviolet are higher in frequency than violet waves. They are outside of the visible spectrum and can't be seen with your eyes."}]}]},"superiority":{"h":"superiority","i":"/sʊuˌpɪə(r).iˈɒ.rɪ.ti/","a":"en-us-superiority.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) If you have superiority over someone, you are superior to them and probably have authority over them."}]}]},"realism":{"h":"realism","i":"/ˈri.əlɪzm/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-realism.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Realism is the quality of being real, as opposed to stylized or fictional."}]}]},"morality":{"h":"morality","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Morality is the ability to tell the difference between things that are just and things that are evil.","e":"Without morality, everybody would be killing each other constantly."},{"m":"(countable) A morality is a set of rules and beliefs that say what actions are appropriate for people in a society to do."},{"m":"(countable) Your morality is your own personal set of beliefs for what is okay for you and other people to do.","e":"In my morality, it is always wrong to kill someone, no matter what."},{"m":"(uncountable) Morality is the field of moral philosophy."}]}]},"burdensome":{"h":"burdensome","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is burdensome is a burden; it is something that literally or figuratively weighs you down."}]}]},"mariner":{"h":"mariner","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A mariner is another word for a sailor."}]}]},"mariners":{"h":"mariners","l":"mariner","q":"noun"},"sos":{"h":"SOS","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) An SOS is a distress signal sent with; it tells anyone who is listening to send help."}]}]},"dolly":{"h":"dolly","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(childish, cute) Another word for a doll."}]}]},"dollies":{"h":"dollies","l":"dolly","q":"noun"},"dismissively":{"h":"dismissively","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If you say or do something dismissively, you do it with disregard for someone else, as a way of rejecting or ignoring them."}]}]},"undented":{"h":"undented","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is undented, it has no dents."}]}]},"dented":{"h":"dented","l":"dent","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is dented, it has one or more dents in it."}]}]},"denting":{"h":"denting","l":"dent","q":"verb"},"accelerant":{"h":"accelerant","i":"/əkˈsɛlər(ə)nt/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-accelerant.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An accelerant is something that causes something else to accelerate.","e":"is an accelerant; it makes your heart rate accelerate."}]}]},"accelerants":{"h":"accelerants","l":"accelerant","q":"noun"},"caffeine":{"h":"caffeine","i":"/ˈkæfiːn/","a":"en-us-caffeine.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Caffeine is a mild drug that acts as a stimulant in the body, making you more jittery and excited. It is in coffee and some teas."}]}]},"caffeinated":{"h":"caffeinated","i":"/ˈkafɪneɪtɪd/","a":"en-au-caffeinated.ogg","l":"caffeinate","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is caffeinated contains caffeine."}]}]},"decaffeinated":{"h":"decaffeinated","i":"/diːˈkæfiːneɪtəd/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Flame, not lame-decaffeinated.wav","l":"decaffeinate","q":"verb","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Something that is decaffeinated has had all the caffeine in it removed."}]}]},"decaf":{"h":"decaf","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"Short for decaffeinated.","e":"\"I enjoy decaf coffee.\""}]}]},"caffeinate":{"h":