nd how you've hurt me."}]}]},"unwisely":{"h":"unwisely","i":"/ʌnˈwaɪzli/","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If you do something unwisely, you do what good judgment says not to do.","e":"He unwisely drove back home after having some drinks at the party."}]}]},"spadeful":{"h":"spadeful","i":"/ˈspeɪdful/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-spadeful.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A spadeful of something is the amount of it you can fit on a spade.","e":"She lifted a spadeful of dirt and tossed it onto the wheelbarrow."}]}]},"boringly":{"h":"boringly","i":"/ˈbɔːrɪŋli/","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something is done boringly, it is done a way that does not make people interested.","e":"The novel's plot is boringly predictable, and the characters are bland and one-dimensional."}]}]},"frustratingly":{"h":"frustratingly","i":"/frəˈstreɪtɪŋli/","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something is done frustratingly, it is done in a way that makes people upset, because it stops them from doing or achieving something.","e":"In some countries, the process of getting a visa can be frustratingly long."}]}]},"bomber":{"h":"bomber","i":"/ˈbɑmɚ/","a":"en-au-bomber.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A bomber is a person that sets bombs.","e":"The bomber was caught by the police before he could detonate the explosives."},{"m":"(countable) A bomber is an aircraft that drops bombs.","e":"Several bombers were spotted flying over international waters."}]}]},"bombers":{"h":"bombers","l":"bomber","q":"noun"},"spadefuls":{"h":"spadefuls","l":"spadeful","q":"noun"},"hepatitis":{"h":"hepatitis","i":"/ˌhepəˈtaɪtɪs/","a":"en-us-hepatitis.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Hepatitis is the inflammation of the liver. It is usually caused by a viral infection.","e":"Hepatitis may cause liver failure if it is left untreated."}]}]},"hepatitises":{"h":"hepatitises","l":"hepatitis","q":"noun"},"hepatitides":{"h":"hepatitides","l":"hepatitis","q":"noun"},"aver":{"h":"aver","i":"/əˈvɜː/","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you aver something, you say that it must be true.","e":"The defendant averred that they did not know that the document was forged."}]}]},"avers":{"h":"avers","l":"aver","q":"verb"},"averred":{"h":"averred","l":"aver","q":"verb"},"averring":{"h":"averring","l":"aver","q":"verb"},"inadequacy":{"h":"inadequacy","i":"/ɪˈnædɪ(ə)kwəsi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-inadequacy.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The inadequacy of something is the fact of its being not good enough for some purpose.","e":"The inadequacy of the measuring equipment is thought to be the cause of most of the errors."}]}]},"inadequacies":{"h":"inadequacies","l":"inadequacy","q":"noun"},"inadequately":{"h":"inadequately","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If you did something inadequately, you did not do it well enough for some purpose.","e":"Investigation revealed that the staff were inadequately trained."}]}]},"impossibility":{"h":"impossibility","i":"/ɪmˌpɒsəˈbɪləti/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-impossibility.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"The impossibility of something is the quality of it being impossible.","e":"The law of conservation of energy proves the impossibility of perpetual motion."},{"m":"(countable) An impossibility is something that cannot happen.","e":"Getting to work on time in such heavy traffic is an impossibility."}]}]},"coexist":{"h":"coexist","i":"/koʊɪɡˈzɪst/","a":"en-us-coexist.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(intransitive) If two or more things coexist, they exist together or at the same time.","e":"At a certain temperature and pressure, liquid water, solid ice, and water vapor can coexist."},{"m":"(intransitive) If two or more groups of people coexist, they live together without fighting.","e":"Neighbors who had previously coexisted peacefully turned against each other."}]}]},"impossibly":{"h":"impossibly","i":"/ɪmˈpɒsəbli/","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something is impossibly difficult, expensive, far, etc. it is so much so that it i