 it personally."},{"m":"If you know someone personally, you know them and they know you.","e":"Sure, I know of her, but I don't know her personally."},{"m":"If something is true personally, it is true of your personality and character.","e":"Even though I'm on TV every day, I'm shy personally."},{"m":"If something applies personally, it applies to your private life at home, not what happens at work or in society.","e":"He was totally in control of his life, personally and professionally."}]}]},"deterrents":{"h":"deterrents","l":"deterrent","q":"noun"},"gendarmerie":{"h":"gendarmerie","i":"/ˈʒɒn.dɑː.mə.ri/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-gendarmerie.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A gendarmerie is a military body that is in charge with police duties among the civilian population."}]}]},"gendarmeries":{"h":"gendarmeries","l":"gendarmerie","q":"noun"},"ossuary":{"h":"ossuary","i":"/ˈɒsjʊəri/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-ossuary.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An ossuary is a container or room in which the bones of dead people are placed."}]}]},"ossuaries":{"h":"ossuaries","l":"ossuary","q":"noun"},"divest":{"h":"divest","i":"/daɪˈvɛst/","a":"en-us-divest.ogg","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you divest someone of something, you remove it from them.","e":"After being convicted, the judge was divested of his powers."},{"m":"(transitive) (finance) If you divest a property or investment, you sell it off.","e":"The church has decided to divest itself of all its properties."}]}]},"divests":{"h":"divests","l":"divest","q":"verb"},"divested":{"h":"divested","l":"divest","q":"verb"},"divesting":{"h":"divesting","l":"divest","q":"verb"},"snappy":{"h":"snappy","i":"/ˈsnæpi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-snappy.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"(informal) If a person is snappy, they are irritable and more likely to speak harshly."},{"m":"(informal) A snappy person is someone who is tidy and sharp."}]}]},"snappier":{"h":"snappier","l":"snappy