ʃən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-exposition.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An exposition is a detailed explanation or description of an idea or theory, especially in a piece of writing.","e":"The essay includes a thorough exposition of the author's argument."},{"m":"(countable) An exposition is a show of goods, artwork, or cultural displays to the public.","e":"The art gallery's annual exposition attracted visitors from around the world."},{"m":"Exposition is the action of something to something.","e":"The exposition of the paint to the light caused it to fade."}]}]},"expositions":{"h":"expositions","l":"exposition","q":"noun"},"tort":{"h":"tort","i":"/tɔːt/","a":"en-uk-tort.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A tort is a wrongful act that leads to a legal liability."}]}]},"torts":{"h":"torts","l":"tort","q":"noun"},"torte":{"h":"torte","i":"/tɔːt/","a":"en-uk-tort.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A torte is a rich, dense cake made with many eggs and very little flour."}]}]},"tortes":{"h":"tortes","l":"torte","q":"noun"},"torten":{"h":"torten","l":"torte","q":"noun"},"wrongful":{"h":"wrongful","i":"/ˈrɒŋfəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-wrongful.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A wrongful act is one that is violates somebody's rights.","e":"His wrongful conviction for the crime was eventually overturned."},{"m":"A wrongful act is one that is illegal.","e":"He was charged for the wrongful death of the cyclist."},{"m":"A wrongful heir, possessor, etc. is one that has no right to be in that position.","e":"The wrongful heir claimed the throne, causing a dispute."}]}]},"unwritten":{"h":"unwritten","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"An unwritten rule or understanding is one that is generally known or understood without being stated explicitly.","e":"It's an unwritten rule that you lock the gate when you leave the swimming pool."},{"m":"An unwritten language is one which is not usually written down, usually because it has no writing system.","e":"Svan is a largely unwritten language many scholars believe predates Georgian."},{"m":"An unwritten paper, article, or book, is one for which somebody has an idea but which has not yet been written.","e":"I'm afraid we'll never see the last book in the series, which is still unwritten."}]}]},"unwrittenness":{"h":"unwrittenness","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) The unwrittenness of a rule, language, or book is the state of not being or having been written."}]}]},"igloo":{"h":"igloo","i":"/ˈɪɡluː/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-igloo.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) An igloo is a hut made of ice or snow."}]}]},"igloos":{"h":"igloos","l":"igloo","q":"noun"},"monetisation":{"h":"monetisation","i":"/ˌmʌnətaɪˈzeɪʃən/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Monetisation is the process of converting something into money.","e":"The central bank's monetisation of its debt increased the money supply."},{"m":"Monetisation is the process of earning money from an activity or asset, often applied to digital content, websites, or services.","e":"The monetisation of the website's traffic through advertisements and subscriptions allowed it to become profitable."}]}]},"monetization":{"h":"monetization","i":"/ˌmʌnətaɪˈzeɪʃən/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Monetization is the process of converting something into money.","e":"The central bank's monetization of its debt increased the money supply."},{"m":"Monetization is the process of earning money from an activity or asset, often applied to digital content, websites, or services.","e":"The monetization of the website's traffic through advertisements and subscriptions allowed it to become profitable."}]}]},"monetizations":{"h":"monetizations","l":"monetization","q":"noun"},"monetisations":{"h":"monetisations","l":"monetisation","q":"noun"},"pettings":{"h":"pettings","l":"petting","q":"noun"},"testable":{"h":"testable","i":"/ˈtɛs.tə.bəl/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is testable, it is susceptible to being test