true.","e":"The two products are essentially the same."}]}]},"historically":{"h":"historically","i":"/hɪˈstɒrɪkəli/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-historically.wav","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"Historically means reference with past events.","e":"The building is historically significant."},{"m":"Historically means in the past.","e":"Historically, people have traveled by horse and carriage."}]}]},"anklet":{"h":"anklet","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A anklet is a band or chain worn around the ankle as jewelry or an ornament."}]}]},"anklets":{"h":"anklets","l":"anklet","q":"noun"},"precedences":{"h":"precedences","l":"precedence","q":"noun"},"yoke":{"h":"yoke","i":"/joʊk/","a":"En-au-yoke.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"A yoke is a wooden frame or bar with loops or bows at either end, used for joining two oxen or other animals together to pull a plough or vehicle.","e":"The farmer used a yoke to connect the oxen."},{"m":"If someone has to live under the yoke of something bad, they have to lives that are controlled by it.","e":"The people struggled to free themselves from the yoke of slavery."},{"m":"A yoke is something that connects two parts and keeps them together.","e":"The yoke of marriage binds two people together."},{"m":"In engineering, a yoke is a crosspiece that connects two parts of a mechanism.","e":"The yoke of the airplane controls its pitch and roll."},{"m":"A yoke is a fitted part of a garment, usually around the neck and shoulders, that provides support and shape.","e":"The dress had a lace yoke around the neckline."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you yoke animals, such as oxen, to something that they pull, you put a yoke on them, so they can pull it.","e":"The farmer yoked the oxen to the plough."},{"m":"If you yoke two things together, you join or link them together closely.","e":"The new policy yokes education with economic development."},{"m":"If someone is yoked to something bad, they have to lives that are controlled by it.","e":"The workers felt yoked to their desks."}]}]},"yokes":{"h":"yokes","l":"yoke","q":"noun"},"yoked":{"h":"yoked","l":"yoke","q":"verb"},"yoking":{"h":"yoking","l":"yoke","q":"verb"},"quilt":{"h":"quilt","i":"/kwɪlt/","a":"en-us-quilt.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A quilt is a bed cover made of two layers of cloth with a filling of wool, cotton, or down held together by patterned stitching."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If you quilt, you construct a [[#Noun|quilt]]."}]}]},"quilts":{"h":"quilts","l":"quilt","q":"noun"},"loom":{"h":"loom","i":"/luːm/","a":"en-us-loom.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A loom is a machine used for weaving thread or yarn into cloth.","e":"She used a loom to make the fabric for her dress."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"If something looms, it appears as a large, often threatening shape.","e":"A large ship loomed on the horizon."},{"m":"If something is looming, usually something bad, it seems likely to happen soon.","e":"A crisis is looming for the company."}]}]},"looms":{"h":"looms","l":"loom","q":"noun"},"loomed":{"h":"loomed","l":"loom","q":"verb"},"looming":{"h":"looming","l":"loom","q":"verb"},"quantum":{"h":"quantum","i":"/ˈkwɒn.təm/","a":"en-US quantum (enunciated).ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A quantum is the smallest amount of a physical quantity that can exist independently.","e":"Energy is transferred in small packets called quanta."},{"m":"Quantum physics/computing/mechanics, etc. is related to quanta in sense 1.","e":"Particles like electrons behave differently at the quantum level."},{"m":"A quantum change is a very large one.","e":"There has been a quantum shift in the way people think about this."},{"m":"A quantum change is one that is sudden and non-continuous, moving from one state another without any intermediate states.","e":"A quantum leap occurs abruptly, without gradual transition."},{"m":"(countable) The quantum of something is its total amount.","e":"The court decided the quantum of damages to be paid."}]}]},"quanta":{"h":"quanta","l":"quantum","q":"noun"},"annum":{"h":"annum","i":"/ˈæn.əm/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Annum is a Latin word for year, often used in business.","e":"The interest rate is 5% per annum."}]}]},"charitable":{"h":"charitable","i":"/ˈtʃærɪtəbəl/","a":"en-us-charitable.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A charitable person or act shows kindness by giving money or help to people who need it.","e":"She is very charitable and often donates to the hospital."},{"m":"A charitable event or organization is one related to helping people in need.","e":"They organized a charitable event to raise funds for the homeless."},{"m":"A charitable attitude or interpretation is one that assumes people are trying their best.","e":"His charitable attitude towards her mistakes was appreciated."}]}]},"brow":{"h":"brow","i":"/braʊ/","a":"en-us-brow.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Your brow is the bump out above your eye, also the hair and skin there.","e":"She raised her brow in surprise."}]}]},"brows":{"h":"brows","i":"/braʊz/","l":"brow","q":"noun"},"topical":{"h":"topical","i":"/ˈtɒpɪkəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-topical.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is topical, it is related to the things that are happening now or a particular subject.","e":"The news covered several topical issues including the environment and politics."},{"m":"A topical medicine is put on a part of the body.","e":"The doctor prescribed a topical cream for the rash."}]}]},"japanophile":{"h":"Japanophile","i":"/dʒəˌpænə(ʊ)ˈfaɪl/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A Japanophile is a person who loves the country, culture, or people of Japan, even relating the Japanophilia culture."}]}]},"japanophiles":{"h":"Japanophiles","l":"japanophile","q":"noun"},"neuter":{"h":"neuter","i":"/ˈnjuːtə/","a":"en-us-neuter.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A neuter word or form is neither male nor female.","e":"In English, it is a neuter pronoun."}]},