mething warily, they do it in a way that shows that they have a lack of trust."}]}]},"suspiciously":{"h":"suspiciously","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If someone does something suspiciously, they do it in a way that makes others think they are hiding something or doing something wrong.","e":"He glanced around suspiciously before entering the room."},{"m":"If someone does something suspiciously, they do it because they think something is wrong or not trustworthy.","e":"She stared at the stranger suspiciously when he approached her."}]}]},"skeptically":{"h":"skeptically","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If someone looks at or thinks about something skeptically, they wonder if or doubt that it is true or correct.","e":"She listened skeptically to his explanation because it sounded unlikely."}]}]},"distrustfully":{"h":"distrustfully","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If a person does something distrustfully, they do it in a distrustful way."}]}]},"skeptical":{"h":"skeptical","i":"/ˈskɛptɪkəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-skeptical.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone is skeptical, they doubt that something is true or correct.","e":"Many people were skeptical of his claim to have seen a UFO."},{"m":"If someone has a skeptical attitude, they question ideas or beliefs rather than accepting them easily.","e":"The scientist took a skeptical approach and asked for more evidence."}]}]},"sceptical":{"h":"sceptical","i":"/ˈskɛptɪkəl/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-skeptical.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If a person is sceptical, they have or expresses doubt."}]}]},"distrustful":{"h":"distrustful","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A distrustful person is someone who shows distrust or is skeptical and suspicious."}]}]},"parcook":{"h":"parcook","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you parcook something, you cook it partially."}]}]},"parcooks":{"h":"parcooks","l":"parcook","q":"verb"},"parcooked":{"h":"parcooked","l":"parcook","q":"verb"},"parboil":{"h":"parboil","