on."}]}]},"unionises":{"h":"unionises","l":"unionise","q":"verb"},"unionised":{"h":"unionised","l":"unionise","q":"verb"},"unionising":{"h":"unionising","l":"unionise","q":"verb"},"sociality":{"h":"sociality","i":"/ˌsoʊʃiˈæləti/","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Sociality is the tendency or ability to form relationships and live with others in a group.","e":"The sociality of humans has helped them build large, complex societies."},{"m":"(countable) A sociality is a specific form of social behaviour or group organization.","e":"The different socialities of animals, like packs or colonies, show how they cooperate."}]}]},"socialities":{"h":"socialities","l":"sociality","q":"noun"},"legendary":{"h":"legendary","i":"/ˈlɛdʒənˌdɛri/","a":"en-us-legendary.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"A legendary person, place, or event is famous and remembered in stories, whether real or fictional.","e":"The legendary King Arthur is said to have ruled Britain."},{"m":"If something is legendary, it is very famous or well-known for being impressive or extraordinary.","e":"The athlete's performance in the game was truly legendary."}]}]},"mechanically":{"h":"mechanically","i":"/məˈkænɪkli/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-mechanically.wav","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something happens mechanically, it happens in a way that uses machines or tools.","e":"The parts of the clock move mechanically."},{"m":"If someone acts mechanically, they do something automatically, without thinking or feeling.","e":"She nodded mechanically during the long meeting."}]}]},"notably":{"h":"notably","i":"/ˈnoʊtəbli/","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something is notably done, it is worth noticing or is important that it was done.","e":"The artist's work was notably praised for its originality."},{"m":"You use notably to introduce a clear or important example.","e":"Many countries were represented at the event, notably France and Germany."}]}]},"prospective":{"h":"prospective","i":"/prəˈspɛktɪv/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-prospective.wav","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone or something is a prospective event, outcome, or situation, it is expected or likely to happen in the future.","e":"They are preparing for a prospective change in regulations."},{"m":"If someone is a prospective customer, student, etc., they are being considered or are considering joining or buying.","e":"The university welcomed prospective students during the open house."}]},{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A prospective is someone who might join, buy, or participate in something.","e":"The salesperson spoke to several prospectives at the trade show."}]}]},"regularity":{"h":"regularity","i":"/ˌrɛɡjəˈlærɪti/","a":"en-us-regularity.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Regularity is the state or quality of happening in a steady, predictable pattern.","e":"The regularity of the train schedule makes commuting easier."},{"m":"(countable) A regularity is something that happens repeatedly in the same way.","e":"He noticed several regularities in the data during his analysis."}]}]},"timeless":{"h":"timeless","i":"/ˈtaɪmləs/","a":"en-us-timeless.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is timeless, it never goes out of style or loses its importance.","e":"The story's message is timeless and still relevant today."},{"m":"If something is timeless, it exists outside of time or is not affected by time.","e":"The beauty of the mountains seemed timeless."}]}]},"prospectives":{"h":"prospectives","l":"prospective","q":"noun"},"regularities":{"h":"regularities","l":"regularity","q":"noun"},"kneecap":{"h":"kneecap","i":"/ˈniːˌkæp/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-kneecap.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A kneecap is the round bone that covers and protects the knee joint.","e":"She fell and bruised her kneecap while running."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you kneecap someone, you injure their kneecap, often by shooting or hitting it.","e":"The gang threatened to kneecap him if he didn’t pay."}]}]},"genetically":{"h":"genetically","i":"/dʒəˈnɛtɪkli/","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something happens genetically, it happens in a way that relates to genes or heredity.","e":"The disease is genetically passed down from parents to children."},{"m":"If something is changed or influenced genetically, it is done by altering genes.","e":"The crops were modified genetically to grow faster."}]}]},"enormously":{"h":"enormously","i":"/ɪˈnɔːrməsli/","s":[{"p":"adverb","d":[{"m":"If something is enormously popular, important, successful, etc., it is very much so.","e":"The project was enormously successful."},{"m":"If something grows, varies, or changes enormously it does so a lot.","e":"The city has grown enormously since I was last here."}]}]},"kneecaps":{"h":"kneecaps","l":"kneecap","q":"noun"},"kneecapped":{"h":"kneecapped","l":"kneecap","q":"verb"},"kneecapping":{"h":"kneecapping","l":"kneecap","q":"verb"},"kabuki":{"h":"kabuki","i":"/kəˈbuːki/","a":"en-us-kabuki.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Kabuki is a classical form of Japanese theatre, mixing dramatic performance with traditional dance."}]}]},"genetical":{"h":"genetical","i":"/d͡ʒəˈnɛtɪkəl/","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is genetical, it is related to genes or heredity."}]}]},"heredity":{"h":"heredity","i":"/hɪˈrɛdɪti/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-heredity.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Heredity is the transmission of the physical and genetic qualities of parents to their offspring."}]}]},"vermilion":{"h":"vermilion","i":"/vəˈmɪl.jən/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-vermilion.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Vermilion is a vivid red synthetic pigment made of"},{"m":"Vermilion is a bright orange-red colour."}]}]},"vermilions":{"h":"vermilions","l":"vermilion","q":"noun"},"taupe":{"h":"taupe","i":"/təʊp/","a":"en-us-taupe.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"Taupe is a dark brownish-grey colour."}]}]},"taupes":{"h":"taupes","l":"taupe","q":"noun"},"crochet":