e used for driving on rough roads."}]}]},"jeeps":{"h":"jeeps","l":"jeep","q":"noun"},"secs":{"h":"secs","l":"sec","q":"noun"},"stooge":{"h":"stooge","i":"/stuːd͡ʒ/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-stooge.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A stooge is someone who lets them be used for another person's benefit knowingly."},{"m":"(countable) A stooge is a secret informant for police."}]}]},"stooges":{"h":"stooges","l":"stooge","q":"noun"},"dependency":{"h":"dependency","i":"/dɪˈpɛndənsi/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-dependency.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(uncountable) Dependency is the state of needing someone or something for support or help.","e":"His dependency on his parents is starting to worry them."},{"m":"(countable) A dependency is a place that is controlled by another country or government.","e":"Greenland is a dependency of Denmark."},{"m":"(countable) In linguistics, a dependency is a relationship between two parts of a sentence, where one part depends on the other.","e":"In the sentence \"She likes swimming,\" there is a dependency between \"likes\" and \"swimming.\""}]}]},"formidable":{"h":"formidable","i":"/ˈfɔːrmɪdəbl/","a":"en-us-formidable.ogg","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If someone or something is formidable, they cause fear, respect, or admiration because they are powerful, strong, or impressive.","e":"The boxer faced a formidable opponent in the championship match."},{"m":"If something is formidable, it is very difficult or challenging.","e":"Climbing the mountain was a formidable task."}]}]},"pouch":{"h":"pouch","i":"/paʊtʃ/","a":"en-us-pouch.ogg","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A pouch is a small bag or pocket used for carrying things.","e":"He kept his coins in a leather pouch."},{"m":"(countable) A pouch is a pocket-like part of an animal's body, used to carry young or store food.","e":"A kangaroo carries its baby in a pouch."}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you pouch something, you put it in a pouch or small bag.","e":"She pouched the seeds before planting them."},{"m":"(intransitive) If something pouches, it bulges outward like a pouch.","e":"The fabric pouched where it was stitched poorly."}]}]},"dependencies":{"h":"dependencies","l":"dependency","q":"noun"},"pouches":{"h":"pouches","l":"pouch","q":"noun"},"pouched":{"h":"pouched","l":"pouch","q":"verb"},"pouching":{"h":"pouching","l":"pouch","q":"verb"},"yoga":{"h":"yoga","i":"/ˈjoʊ.ɡə/","a":"en-us-yoga.ogg","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"A group of exercises from India that include stretching, breathing, and relaxing.","e":"She practices yoga every morning to relax and stay fit."},{"m":"A way of thinking and living that helps people feel calm and healthy."}]}]},"suntan":{"h":"suntan","i":"/ˈsʌnˌtæn/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-NaomiAmethyst-suntan.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A suntan is darker skin caused by spending time in the sun"}]},{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"When a person suntans, they obtain a [[#Noun|suntan]]."}]}]},"suntans":{"h":"suntans","l":"suntan","q":"noun"},"suntanned":{"h":"suntanned","l":"suntan","q":"verb"},"suntanning":{"h":"suntanning","l":"suntan","q":"verb"},"transship":{"h":"transship","i":"/trænzˈʃɪp/","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you transship something, you transfer it from one vessel to another for onward shipment."}]}]},"transships":{"h":"transships","l":"transship","q":"verb"},"transshipped":{"h":"transshipped","l":"transship","q":"verb"},"transshipping":{"h":"transshipping","l":"transship","q":"verb"},"transload":{"h":"transload","i":"/trænzˈloʊd/","s":[{"p":"verb","d":[{"m":"(transitive) If you transload something, you transfer it from one vessel to another for onward shipment."}]}]},"transloads":{"h":"transloads","l":"transload","q":"verb"},"transloaded":{"h":"transloaded","l":"transload","q":"verb"},"transloading":{"h":"transloading","l":"transload","q":"verb"},"parley":{"h":"parley","i":"/ˈpɑrli/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-parley.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","