 a large, deep, round metal pot used for heating or boiling liquids over an open fire. It is usually made of heavy metals like cast iron or copper."}]}]},"oculus":{"h":"oculus","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"An oculus (plural: oculi) is a round, eye-like opening or design element, most commonly found at the center of a dome or in a wall."},{"m":"A circular window or opening, famously seen at the top of the Pantheon dome in Rome, which lets in natural light and air."},{"m":"The Latin word for \"eye,\" used in medical terms relating to vision or eye structures."},{"m":"A brand name for virtual reality (VR) headsets, originally developed by Oculus VR (now part of Meta)."}]}]},"serendipity":{"h":"serendipity","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"It means the occurrence of finding valuable, pleasant, or agreeable things by chance, luck, or unexpected good fortune."}]}]},"perjurer":{"h":"perjurer","i":"/ˈpərdʒərər/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-perjurer.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A perjurer is someone who makes a very serious promise that something is true, but he is actually lying."}]}]},"perjurers":{"h":"perjurers","l":"perjurer","q":"noun"},"cauldrons":{"h":"cauldrons","l":"cauldron","q":"noun"},"precipice":{"h":"precipice","i":"/ˈprɛsɪpɪs/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-precipice.wav","s":[{"p":"noun","d":[{"m":"(countable) A precipice is a very steep cliff."}]}]},"precipices":{"h":"precipices","l":"precipice","q":"noun"},"transatlantic":{"h":"transatlantic","s":[{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"(geography) If something is transatlantic, it is beyond or crosses to the other side of the Atlantic Ocean."}]}]},"atlantic":{"h":"Atlantic","i":"/ətˈlæn.tɪk/","a":"LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Atlantic.wav","s":[{"p":"proper noun","d":[{"m":"The Atlantic Ocean."}]},{"p":"adjective","d":[{"m":"If something is Atlantic, it is related to the Atlantic Ocean."},{"m":"If something is Atlantic, it is related to the locations beside or are in the vicinity of the Atlantic Ocean."}]}]},"swo